ivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD1","text":"Distinctiones personales non dividunt intellectum divinum in plures actus, conceptus aut voces, sed unum actum sub relatione originis personaliter determinant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD2","text":"Nomen personale potest simul originem aeternam et ordinem ad creaturas significare, dummodo relatio ad creaturas ex essentia et intellectione consequenter, non ex proprietate personali principaliter, derivetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A7","CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD3","text":"Pluralitas creaturarum et idearum non pluralitatem verbi producit, quia obiecta multa in una divina auto-intellectione continentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4","text":"Creatio in verbo fundatur ut expressio operativa cognitionis divinae, non ut causa quae cognitionem divinam informet aut verbum constituat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A10","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD5","text":"Eadem nativitas filii per nomina filius, splendor, imago et verbum sub rationibus diversis intelligitur, sine multiplicatione rerum vel proprietatum in divinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX1","text":"Cognitio divina non recipit formam, specificationem aut principium ab obiectis creatis; creatura est intellecta ex essentia divina, non causa intellectionis divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX2","text":"Processio verbi divina non est emissio localis, exterior prolatio, nec separatio subsistentis a principio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A2","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX3","text":"Persona divina non est individuum additum essentiae communi per accidens; ipsa relatio originis in natura subsistente personaliter distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX4","text":"Aeternitas divina non excludit omnem respectum ad creaturas, sed excludit tantum respectum qui mutationem vel novam actionem externam in Deo postularet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A7","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX5","text":"Analogia verbi humani non transfert in Deum discursum, successionem, imperfectionem conceptus aut distinctionem realem inter intellegere et esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A1","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX1","text":"Nulla distantia ponitur inter perfectam Dei sui cognitionem et cognitionem creaturarum, quia creaturae in unica Dei intellectione sui comprehenduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX2","text":"Nulla regio intelligibilium creatorum independens a divina essentia admittitur, quae verbum multiplicare, modificare aut temporaliter determinare possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX3","text":"Nulla communis actio dicendi tribus personis tribuitur, quia communitas naturae non absorbet asymmetricam originis Patris ad Verbum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_26:A5","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX4","text":"Nulla creatura efficitur principium divini sermonis, etiamsi tota creatura in verbo expressa atque per verbum operabilis sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS1","text":"Usus vocis distinguuntur → conceptus interior ut significatio propria isolatur → usus vocales, imaginarii et effectuales ad secundarium vel figurativum ordinem reducuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS2","text":"Conceptus interior procedit a cognoscente → processio originem importat → origo in divinis personam distinguit → verbum personaliter dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS3","text":"Processio per intellectum → generatio divina → persona procedens est filius → verbum est proprium nomen filii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS4","text":"Identitas divini esse et intelligere → verbum non est accidens → verbum subsistit → processio non separat verbum a Patre nec introducit mutationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS5","text":"Unica Dei auto-intellectio continet creaturas → unum verbum omnia exprimit → creaturas factive respicit → relatio ad creaturas aeterna manet quia actio est immanens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS6","text":"Distinctio entis et non-entis in ordine factivo → entia verbo exprimuntur et fieri possunt → non-entia verbo exprimuntur tantum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF1","text":"Ambiguitas semantica verbi → segregatio usus proprii a figurativo → conceptus interior procedens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF2","text":"Conceptus procedens → relatio originis → nomen personale, non essentiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF3","text":"Processio intellectualis → generatio → identificatio verbi cum filio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF4","text":"Identitas esse et intellegere divini → subsistentia verbi → exclusio accidentis et prolationis exterioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF5","text":"Una cognitio Dei sui et creaturarum → unum verbum expressive universale → creaturarum ratio operativa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF6","text":"Distinctio actionis immanentis et transeuntis → relatio aeterna ad creaturas → exclusio temporalitatis nominis verbi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME1","text":"Praedicata intellectualia dividuntur inter ea quae essentiam absolute significant et illud quod originem conceptus significat; verbum ad secundum ordinem transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter nomen personale et respectum ad creaturas dissolvitur, quia relatio personalis potest esse primaria et relatio creaturalis consequens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter aeternum et ad-creaturam-relatum restringitur: temporale est quod actionem externam consequitur, non omne quod creaturas intelligibiliter respicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME4","text":"Idea et verbum diversis principiis numerantur: idea per respectus creaturarum multiplicatur, verbum per actum dicentis unum manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME5","text":"Non-entia a campo factibilium separantur, quamvis intra campum divinae cognitionis et expressionis contineantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT1","text":"Surface — Nomen verbi personaliter dicitur, filio proprie convenit, et creaturas significative atque operative respicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT2","text":"Structural — Ratio originis, non sola ratio cognitionis, praedicatum intellectuale in nomen personale convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur per mutationem ordinis significationis: idem nomen potest proprie, improprie, figurative, principaliter et consequenter dici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Divina simplicitas excludit distinctionem realem esse-intellegere et successionem cogitationis, sed admittit relationes originis aeternas et ordinem aeternum ad creaturas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT1","text":"Systema restitui potest ex nexus conceptus procedentis, originis personalis, generationis intellectualis et identitatis divini esse cum intellegere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT2","text":"Inferentia verbum personale → filius proprie pendet a praemissa iam statuta quod processio intellectualis divina generatio sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT3","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi distinguitur intellegere commune a dicere originem verbi importans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in compositione relationis personalis primariae cum relatione creaturarum consequente intra unum nomen, quia distinctio ex ordine significationis potius quam ex pluralitate rei servatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT5","text":"Tensionem continet unicum verbum omnia exprimens et pluralitas idearum creaturarum; solutio prioritati semanticae verbi super ideam innititur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT6","text":"Distinctio entium factorum et non-entium tantum expressorum clausuram servat, sed modum positivum quo non-entia in verbo continentur ulterius non determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T160912405837Z_e55b0680","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 34","source_sha256":"9db87b74ea0c6e111c25615de43557c6cbb70b00877917b6c672ba34e4cf6e7a","sha256":"1ca788d2511711ff2bc3fa92ea4291cb6ad57a2b70a5bdf0c3c48fdcb1b47050","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:09:12.406838+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AS1","text":"The question determines whether the name Word in divine matters is personal, proper to the Son, and related to creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","text":"The ambiguity of the term word is resolved by distinguishing the interior concept, the signifying utterance, the image of an utterance, and figurative use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AS3","text":"A word properly so called is a concept of the intellect proceeding from the one understanding; procession therefore imports origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AS4","text":"Since the divine persons are distinguished by origins, a word properly so called signifies not the common essence but the proceeding person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AS5","text":"Divine intellectual procession is generation; therefore word is a proper name of the Son, not an addition of a new property.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AS6","text":"The one Word, proceeding from the one divine intellection, expresses the Father and represents known creatures and regards them operatively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AS7","text":"The relation of the Word to creatures remains eternal, because it follows the intellectual action remaining in God, not temporal action passing over into an effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A1","text":"A word properly so called is the interior concept of the intellect, not an exterior utterance nor the thing signified by an utterance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A2","text":"The intellectual concept, as a word, proceeds from the knowledge of the conceiver.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","text":"The divine persons are distinguished according to origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","text":"In God, to be and to understand are the same; whatever belongs to the divine nature subsists.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A5","text":"To understand directly imports a relation to the thing understood, whereas to speak principally imports a relation to the conceived word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A6","text":"Divine procession by way of intellect is generation, and the person thus proceeding is the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A7","text":"The name word principally signifies a relation to the speaker, but can consequently include a relation to creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","text":"God knows Himself and all creatures by one act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A9","text":"The conceived word represents everything actually understood; the unity of the act of understanding grounds the unity of the word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A10","text":"God's knowledge of Himself is cognoscitive only, but of creatures it is cognoscitive and productive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A11","text":"A relation to creatures arising from an action remaining in the agent is not from time, although a relation arising from an action passing into an external effect is said to be from time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:A12","text":"The Word of God expresses beings and regards them operatively; but it expresses and manifests non-beings, not constituting them productively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX1","text":"The divine Word is not an exterior utterance, an image of an utterance, or an effect commanded by a word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX2","text":"A word spoken metaphorically does not eliminate the necessity of a word properly so called, because the metaphor itself presupposes manifestation through a word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX3","text":"Word is not an essential name common to the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX4","text":"Word is not inquiring or mutable thought, because in God there is no successive search for truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX5","text":"Divine speaking is not simply the same as divine understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX6","text":"The Word of the Son is not an accident, a power of the soul, or an effect separated from the divine nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX7","text":"The Word is not multiplied according to the multitude of creatures or ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX8","text":"The relation of the Word to creatures does not signify procession of the Word from creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:NX9","text":"The relation of the Word to creatures is not the temporal relation of a creator to an effect already produced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D1","text":"The divine Word, properly taken, is a personal name, because a proceeding concept imports origin and the character of origin distinguishes persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A1","CH_GGVC_P_26:A2","CH_GGVC_P_26:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D2","text":"The Father alone is properly the speaker, because He alone is the principle from which the Word personally proceeds; yet the whole Trinity is understood and spoken in the Word as the thing understood.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_26:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D3","text":"The divine Word subsists, because the divine concept does not fall outside divine being, which is subsistent understanding itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D4","text":"Word is a proper name of the Son, because the same intellectual procession that constitutes the Word constitutes filial generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A2","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D5","text":"The Son understands essentially, but is not a speaker as producing the Word, because understanding belongs commonly to the nature, whereas speaking designates the origin of the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A5","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D6","text":"The name word adds no new personal property, but signifies the same filial nativity under the aspect of immaterial generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","text":"The one Word expresses the Father and creatures, because one divine knowledge comprehends itself and all other things by one act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D8","text":"The Word regards creatures operatively without temporal change in God, because productive intelligibility follows eternal knowledge and immanent action.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A10","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:D9","text":"Non-beings are contained in the Word as knowable and manifestable, not as effects to be produced.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:A10","CH_GGVC_P_26:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD1","text":"Personal distinctions do not divide the divine intellect into several acts, concepts, or utterances, but personally determine one act under the relation of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD2","text":"A personal name can simultaneously signify eternal origin and an ordering to creatures, provided that the relation to creatures is derived consequently from essence and intellection, not principally from personal property.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A7","CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD3","text":"The plurality of creatures and ideas does not produce a plurality of words, because many objects are contained in one divine self-intellection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4","text":"Creation is grounded in the Word as the operative expression of divine knowledge, not as a cause that informs divine knowledge or constitutes the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A10","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SD5","text":"The same nativity of the Son is understood under diverse aspects through the names Son, splendor, image, and word, without multiplication of things or properties in divine matters.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX1","text":"Divine knowledge receives no form, specification, or principle from created objects; the creature is understood from the divine essence, not as a cause of divine intellection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX2","text":"Divine procession of the Word is not local emission, exterior utterance, or separation of a subsistent from its principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A2","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX3","text":"The divine person is not an individual added accidentally to the common essence; the relation of origin itself personally distinguishes in the subsisting nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX4","text":"Divine eternity does not exclude every relation to creatures, but excludes only a relation that would require change or a new external action in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A7","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX5","text":"The analogy of the human word does not transfer to God discursiveness, succession, imperfection of concept, or a real distinction between understanding and being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A1","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX1","text":"No distance is posited between God's perfect knowledge of Himself and knowledge of creatures, because creatures are comprehended in God's one intellection of Himself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX2","text":"No region of created intelligibles independent of the divine essence is admitted that could multiply, modify, or temporally determine the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX3","text":"No common act of speaking is attributed to the three persons, because the community of nature does not absorb the asymmetry of the Father's origin toward the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_26:A5","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX4","text":"No creature becomes a principle of divine speech, even though the whole of creation is expressed in the Word and operable through the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS1","text":"Uses of the term are distinguished → the interior concept as proper signification is isolated → vocal, imaginary, and effectual uses are reduced to a secondary or figurative order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS2","text":"The interior concept proceeds from the knower → procession imports origin → origin in divine matters distinguishes person → word is said personally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS3","text":"Procession through intellect → divine generation → the proceeding person is the Son → word is a proper name of the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS4","text":"Identity of divine being and understanding → the Word is not an accident → the Word subsists → procession neither separates the Word from the Father nor introduces change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS5","text":"God's one self-intellection contains creatures → one Word expresses all things → it regards creatures productively → the relation to creatures remains eternal because the action is immanent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:FGS6","text":"Distinction of being and non-being in the productive order → beings are expressed by the Word and can come to be → non-beings are expressed by the Word only.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF1","text":"Semantic ambiguity of word → separation of proper from figurative use → proceeding interior concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF2","text":"Proceeding concept → relation of origin → personal, not essential, name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF3","text":"Intellectual procession → generation → identification of the Word with the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF4","text":"Identity of divine being and understanding → subsistence of the Word → exclusion of accident and exterior utterance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF5","text":"One knowledge of God of Himself and creatures → one expressively universal Word → operative intelligibility of creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:AF6","text":"Distinction of immanent and transitive action → eternal relation to creatures → exclusion of temporality from the name Word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME1","text":"Intellectual predicates are divided between those that signify essence absolutely and that which signifies the origin of a concept; word is assigned to the second order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME2","text":"The opposition between a personal name and relation to creatures is dissolved, because the personal relation can be primary and the creaturely relation consequent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME3","text":"The opposition between eternal and related-to-creatures is restricted: temporal is that which follows external action, not everything that intelligibly regards creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME4","text":"Idea and word are numbered by different principles: idea is multiplied through relations to creatures, while word remains one through the act of the speaker.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ME5","text":"Non-beings are separated from the field of producibles, although they are contained within the field of divine knowledge and expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT1","text":"Surface — The name word is said personally, properly belongs to the Son, and regards creatures significantly and operatively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT2","text":"Structural — The character of origin, not the character of knowledge alone, converts an intellectual predicate into a personal name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved through a change in the order of signification: the same name can be said properly, improperly, figuratively, principally, and consequently.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Divine simplicity excludes a real distinction between being and understanding and the succession of thought, but admits eternal relations of origin and an eternal ordering to creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT1","text":"The system can be reconstructed from the nexus of proceeding concept, personal origin, intellectual generation, and the identity of divine being with understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT2","text":"The inference personal word → Son properly depends on the already established premise that divine intellectual procession is generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT3","text":"The structure is strongest where common understanding is distinguished from speaking, which imports the origin of the Word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains in combining the primary personal relation with the consequent relation to creatures within one name, because the distinction is preserved from the order of signification rather than from a plurality of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT5","text":"There is a tension between the one Word expressing all things and the plurality of ideas of creatures; the solution rests on the semantic priority of word over idea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0070","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT6","text":"The distinction between produced beings and merely expressed non-beings preserves closure, but does not further determine the positive mode by which non-beings are contained in the Word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_26:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_26@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_26:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 35","title":"First Part · Question 34","context":"Chapter 35","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 34"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 34","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 35","order":36,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_27"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_27@R001","sha256":"f9cb132a117f07e9c7673d0dcf54f85fe62b1b3ae6280558ce591ea450ac308e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat utrum nomen imaginis in divinis ad essentiam communem vel ad relationem personalem pertineat, et utrum filium solum proprie designet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2","text":"Argumentatio conceptum imaginis a similitudine indeterminata ad similitudinem originatam restringit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS3","text":"Origo similis in specie, quia processionem importat, nomen imaginis ex ordine essentiali ad ordinem personalem transfert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS4","text":"Processiones filii et spiritus sancti non ex sola natura accepta, sed ex propria ratione verbi et amoris distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS5","text":"Filius, quia procedit ut verbum cui similitudo speciei essentialiter competit, imago patris proprie et perfecte dicitur; spiritus sanctus, licet similis, hoc nomine proprie non constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS6","text":"Motus argumenti est: similitudo communis → origo expressiva → nomen personale → distinctio processionum → proprietas filii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A1","text":"De ratione imaginis est similitudo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A2","text":"Similitudo ad rationem imaginis non sufficit nisi sit in specie rei vel in signo speciei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","text":"Similitudo specifica ad rationem imaginis non sufficit nisi ex origine procedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","text":"Imago proprie est quod ab alio procedit ut ei simile in specie vel in signo speciei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A5","text":"In divinis ea quae processionem sive originem important sunt personalia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A6","text":"Imitatio in divinis assimilationem significat, non temporalem posterioritatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A7","text":"Acceptio eiusdem naturae divinae non determinat per se rationem personalis nominis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","text":"Processio ut verbum essentialiter includit similitudinem speciei ad principium a quo procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A9","text":"Processio ut amor similitudinem speciei non ex propria ratione importat, etiamsi amor divinus eam habeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A10","text":"Imago eiusdem naturae secundum speciem est perfecta; imago in natura altera est imperfecta et secundum participationem dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX1","text":"Quaelibet similitudo non est imago.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX2","text":"Color vel proprietas accidentaliter similis, sine figura vel signo speciei, imaginem non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX3","text":"Duae res specie similes, si altera ex altera non procedit, relationem imaginis non habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX4","text":"Exemplar, id ad cuius similitudinem alterum procedit, non proprie imago dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX5","text":"Forma vel species, prout essentialiter dicitur, non coincidit simpliciter cum imagine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX6","text":"Imitatio divina ordinem temporis, anterioritatis vel posterioritatis non inducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX7","text":"Similitudo spiritus sancti cum patre et filio non infert ipsum esse imaginem proprie dictam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX8","text":"Homo non est imago Dei eodem modo quo filius est imago patris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D1","text":"Nomen imaginis in divinis personaliter dicitur, quia definitio eius originem similis importat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D2","text":"Relativitas imaginis non ex sola similitudine, sed ex origine qua imago ad exemplar refertur, constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A1","CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D3","text":"Argumentum quod imago temporalem imitationem postulat deficit, quia assimilatio divina sine successione intelligitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D4","text":"Spiritus sanctus non fit imago proprie dicta ex hoc solo quod naturam et similitudinem divinam a principio recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A7","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D5","text":"Filius est imago patris proprie, quia processio eius ut verbum originem cum similitudine specifica per se coniungit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D6","text":"Homo dicitur imago Dei secundum similitudinem imperfectam in natura altera, atque ideo dicitur ad imaginem tendere potius quam imago perfecta esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SD1","text":"Nomina divina personalia non distribuuntur ex communitate naturae, sed ex formali ratione qua unaquaeque processio constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A5","CH_GGVC_P_27:A7","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SD2","text":"Similitudo divina non est criterium sufficiens distinctionis personalis, quia aequalitas, inaequalitas et similitudo secundum relationes personales non mensurantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A1","CH_GGVC_P_27:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SD3","text":"Unus effectus processionalis potest a pluribus personis, inquantum sunt unum principium, procedere sine multiplicatione imaginum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A5","CH_GGVC_P_27:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SD4","text":"Vocabulum imaginis analogice ordinatur: proprie ad filium, latius apud Graecos ad perfectam similitudinem, participative ad hominem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit opinionem quod omnia praedicata fundata in natura divina communi aequaliter personaliter attribuantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit reductionem imaginis ad relationem staticam similitudinis, quia imago originem expressivam requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit symmetriam inter verbum et amorem, quia solum verbum similitudinem specificam ex sua propria ratione importat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit univocam applicationem imaginis ad filium, spiritum sanctum et hominem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX5","text":"Systema excludit temporalem genealogiam intra Trinitatem, etiam ubi vocabula imitationis et originis adhibentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio ordinatur circa impossibilitatem definiendi personas divinas per proprietates essentiales communes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio respuit possibilitatem quod processio divina sit mera communicatio naturae sine propria ratione intelligibili vel volitiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX3","text":"Perfecta imago non admittit statum tendentem ad perfectionem; ideo filius non potest dici ad imaginem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX4","text":"Conceptus imaginis servatur a dissolutione in nomen generalis similitudinis per exclusionem omnis similitudinis non-originatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS1","text":"Similitudo indeterminata → restrictio ad speciem vel signum speciei → exclusio similitudinum accidentalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS2","text":"Similitudo specifica → exigentia originis expressae → constitutio relationis imaginis ad exemplar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS3","text":"Origo divina → personalitas → imago personaliter dicta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS4","text":"Communicatio naturae → distinctio processionalis verbi et amoris → similitudo essentialis verbo propria → imago filio propria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS5","text":"Imago perfecta eiusdem naturae → filius; imago participata alterius naturae → homo ad imaginem; similitudo sine ratione verbi → spiritus sanctus non proprie imago.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AF1","text":"Ambiguitas essentiae et personae → definitio restricta imaginis → origo ut differentia constitutiva → personalitas imaginis → distinctio verbi et amoris → proprietas filii → subordinatio imaginis humanae ad perfectionem filii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME1","text":"Similitudo dividitur in similitudinem genericam, similitudinem specificam et similitudinem originatam; sola ultima rationem imaginis perfecte complet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME2","text":"Distinctio essentiale/personale reconfiguratur: natura communicata est communis, ratio processionis est nomen personale distribuens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME3","text":"Oppositio filius/spiritus sanctus non describitur per maiorem vel minorem naturae similitudinem, sed per diversos modos processionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4","text":"Relatio creatoris et creaturae sub imagine filii ordinatur: homo imago est participata et tendens, filius imago est perfecta et subsistens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME5","text":"Diversitas usus Graeci et Latini explicatur ut diversitas extensionis vocabuli imaginis, non ut discrepantia circa naturam divinam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT1","text":"Surface — Quaestio immediate determinat utrum imago sit nomen personale et utrum filio proprie conveniat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT2","text":"Structural — Definitio imaginis componitur ex similitudine specifica et origine expressiva, quarum secunda nomen ad relationem processionalem ligat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones non per negationem auctoritatis solvuntur, sed per restrictionem formalem termini imaginis et distinctionem modorum processionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Processio divina est originaria et relativa sine successione temporali; distinctio personalis consistit in ratione originis, non in inaequalitate naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de similitudine, origine et personalitate sufficiunt ad restitutionem conclusionis quod imago in divinis nomen personale est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de verbo et amore sufficiunt ad restitutionem proprietatis filii sine negatione similitudinis spiritus sancti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT3","text":"Systema maxime cohaeret ubi similitudo originata distinguitur a similitudine simpliciter sumpta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter usum Graecorum, qui imaginem pro perfecta similitudine dicunt, et usum Latinorum, qui imaginem proprie ad processionem verbi restringunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT5","text":"Argumenta quae impossibilitatem imaginis spiritus sancti ex mediatione filii, imagine imaginis, vel unitate duorum principiorum deducunt reiciuntur, sed ratio finalis eorum insufficentiae in distinctione verbi et amoris condensatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus si imago non ut praedicatum similitudinis, sed ut relatio originis similis, et filius non ut simillimus tantum, sed ut procedens per modum verbi intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T160933607083Z_0dadfeaf","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 35","source_sha256":"f9cb132a117f07e9c7673d0dcf54f85fe62b1b3ae6280558ce591ea450ac308e","sha256":"0ba6278fd39db7968375f1b8f4d6151833cd2fd09f495eb87bd26b38cdfec6d4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:09:33.608028+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS1","text":"The question investigates whether the name of image in the divine pertains to the common essence or to personal relation, and whether it properly designates the Son alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2","text":"The argument restricts the concept of image from indeterminate likeness to originated likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS3","text":"Origin similar in species, because it imports procession, transfers the name of image from the essential order to the personal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS4","text":"The processions of the Son and the Holy Spirit are distinguished not from nature taken alone, but from the proper account of word and love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS5","text":"The Son, because he proceeds as a word to which likeness of species essentially belongs, is properly and perfectly called the image of the Father; the Holy Spirit, though similar, is not properly constituted by this name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AS6","text":"The movement of the argument is: common likeness → expressive origin → personal name → distinction of processions → propriety of the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A1","text":"Likeness belongs to the account of image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A2","text":"Likeness does not suffice for the account of image unless it is in the species of the thing or in a sign of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","text":"Specific likeness does not suffice for the account of image unless it proceeds from an origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","text":"An image properly is that which proceeds from another as similar to it in species or in a sign of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A5","text":"In the divine, those things that import procession or origin are personal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A6","text":"Imitation in the divine signifies assimilation, not temporal posteriority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A7","text":"The reception of the same divine nature does not of itself determine the account of a personal name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","text":"Procession as word essentially includes likeness of species to the principle from which it proceeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A9","text":"Procession as love does not import likeness of species from its proper account, even though divine love possesses it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:A10","text":"An image of the same nature according to species is perfect; an image in another nature is imperfect and is said according to participation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX1","text":"Not every likeness is an image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX2","text":"A color or property accidentally similar, without figure or a sign of species, does not constitute an image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX3","text":"Two things similar in species, if one does not proceed from the other, do not have the relation of image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX4","text":"The exemplar, that to whose likeness another proceeds, is not properly called an image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX5","text":"Form or species, insofar as it is said essentially, does not simply coincide with image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX6","text":"Divine imitation does not entail an order of time, priority, or posteriority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX7","text":"The likeness of the Holy Spirit with the Father and the Son does not entail that he himself is an image properly so called.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:NX8","text":"Man is not the image of God in the same way that the Son is the image of the Father.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D1","text":"The name of image in the divine is said personally, because its definition imports the origin of one similar.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D2","text":"The relativity of image is constituted not from likeness alone, but from the origin by which the image is referred to the exemplar.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A1","CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D3","text":"The argument that image requires temporal imitation fails, because divine assimilation is understood without succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D4","text":"The Holy Spirit does not become an image properly so called merely from receiving divine nature and likeness from the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A7","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D5","text":"The Son is properly the image of the Father, because his procession as word joins origin with specific likeness through itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:D6","text":"Man is called the image of God according to an imperfect likeness in another nature, and therefore is said rather to tend toward the image than to be a perfect image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SD1","text":"Personal divine names are not distributed from community of nature, but from the formal account by which each procession is constituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A5","CH_GGVC_P_27:A7","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SD2","text":"Divine likeness is not a sufficient criterion of personal distinction, because equality, inequality, and likeness are not measured according to personal relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A1","CH_GGVC_P_27:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SD3","text":"One processional effect can proceed from several persons, insofar as they are one principle, without a multiplication of images.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A5","CH_GGVC_P_27:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SD4","text":"The term image is ordered analogically: properly to the Son, more broadly among the Greeks to perfect likeness, and participatively to man.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the opinion that all predicates founded in the common divine nature are attributed equally personally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the reduction of image to a static relation of likeness, because image requires expressive origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX3","text":"The system excludes symmetry between word and love, because word alone imports specific likeness from its own proper account.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the univocal application of image to the Son, the Holy Spirit, and man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX5","text":"The system excludes a temporal genealogy within the Trinity, even where terms of imitation and origin are employed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX1","text":"The argument is ordered around the impossibility of defining the divine persons through common essential properties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX2","text":"The argument rejects the possibility that divine procession is a mere communication of nature without a proper intelligible or volitional account.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX3","text":"A perfect image does not admit a state tending toward perfection; therefore the Son cannot be said to be unto the image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX4","text":"The concept of image is preserved from dissolution into a name of general likeness by the exclusion of every non-originated likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS1","text":"Indeterminate likeness → restriction to species or a sign of species → exclusion of accidental likenesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS2","text":"Specific likeness → requirement of expressed origin → constitution of the relation of image to exemplar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS3","text":"Divine origin → personality → image said personally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS4","text":"Communication of nature → processional distinction of word and love → essential likeness proper to word → image proper to the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:FGS5","text":"Perfect image of the same nature → Son; participated image of another nature → man unto the image; likeness without the account of word → the Holy Spirit not properly image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:AF1","text":"Ambiguity of essence and person → restricted definition of image → origin as constitutive difference → personality of image → distinction of word and love → propriety of the Son → subordination of human image to the perfection of the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME1","text":"Likeness is divided into generic likeness, specific likeness, and originated likeness; the last alone perfectly completes the account of image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME2","text":"The essential/personal distinction is reconfigured: communicated nature is common; the account of procession is the personal name that distributes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME3","text":"The opposition Son/Holy Spirit is not described through greater or lesser likeness of nature, but through diverse modes of procession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4","text":"The relation of creator and creature is ordered under the image of the Son: man is a participated and tending image; the Son is a perfect and subsisting image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ME5","text":"The diversity of Greek and Latin usage is explained as a diversity in the extension of the term image, not as a discrepancy concerning divine nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT1","text":"Surface — The question immediately determines whether image is a personal name and whether it properly belongs to the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT2","text":"Structural — The definition of image is composed of specific likeness and expressive origin, the second of which binds the name to processional relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved not through the negation of authority, but through a formal restriction of the term image and a distinction of the modes of procession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Divine procession is originary and relative without temporal succession; personal distinction consists in the account of origin, not in inequality of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning likeness, origin, and personality suffice to reconstruct the conclusion that image in the divine is a personal name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning word and love suffice to reconstruct the propriety of the Son without denying the likeness of the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT3","text":"The system is most coherent where originated likeness is distinguished from likeness taken simply.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains between the usage of the Greeks, who call image perfect likeness, and the usage of the Latins, who properly restrict image to the procession of word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT5","text":"Arguments that deduce the impossibility of the image of the Holy Spirit from the mediation of the Son, image of image, or unity of two principles are rejected, but the final reason for their insufficiency is condensed in the distinction of word and love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if image is understood not as a predicate of likeness but as a relation of the origin of one similar, and the Son not merely as most similar but as proceeding in the mode of word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_27:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_27@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_27:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 36","title":"First Part · Question 35","context":"Chapter 36","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 35"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 35","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 36","order":37,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_28"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_28@R001","sha256":"9e1ca655aa5f055c482943cdd69ad5cd69ff76c7554a7d2b99231cab2b292bb2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quomodo nomen, origo et principium Spiritus Sancti concipienda sint salva unitate essentiae et distinctione trium personarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS2","text":"Spiritus Sanctus est nomen accommodatum personae procedenti per modum amoris, quae a Patre et Filio procedit, a Patre per Filium, atque ab utroque tamquam ab uno principio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est dialectica, semantica et metaphysico-reconstructiva, quia ex regulis nominationis, relationis, originis et praedicationis doctrinam personae restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS4","text":"Motus primus transit a communitate significationis vocum ad proprietatem nominis ex accommodatione usus ecclesialis et scripturarii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS5","text":"Motus secundus transit ab unitate essentiae ad distinctionem relationibus oppositis, inde ad necessitatem processionis Spiritus Sancti a Filio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS6","text":"Motus finalis transit ab origine virtutis spirativae in Filio ad formulam per Filium, deinde ab unitate eiusdem virtutis et proprietatis ad unum principium Spiritus Sancti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","text":"In divinis quidquid absolute dicitur ad unitatem essentiae pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","text":"Personae divinae solis relationibus ab invicem distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","text":"Relationes personas divinas distinguunt tantum quatenus sibi opponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","text":"In divinis non dantur relationes oppositae praeter relationes originis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","text":"Ex Patre sunt duae processiones, Filii per modum intellectus ut Verbi et Spiritus Sancti per modum voluntatis ut Amoris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","text":"Processio per modum amoris eiusque relationes proprium nomen naturale non habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","text":"Voces spiritus et sanctus secundum proprias significationes toti Trinitati communes sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","text":"Usus Scripturae et Ecclesiae dictionem Spiritus Sanctus personae procedenti per modum amoris accommodat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A9","text":"Nomen accommodatum potest pro relativo poni quamvis secundum formam lexicalem relative non dicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A10","text":"Filius non est a Spiritu Sancto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","text":"Amor procedit a verbo mentali, quia nihil amatur nisi secundum conceptionem mentis apprehendatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","text":"Plura ab uno sine ordine procedere possunt tantum ubi materialiter distinguuntur; multiplicitas immaterialis ordinem originis requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","text":"Filius a Patre habet quod Spiritus Sanctus ab eo procedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A14","text":"Praepositio per causam vel principium in ordine actionis et processionis designat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","text":"Una eademque numero virtus spirativa est in Patre et Filio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A16","text":"Generatio Filii et processio Spiritus Sancti suis principiis coaeternae sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A17","text":"Pater et Filius unum sunt in omnibus in quibus eos oppositio relationis non distinguit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","text":"Nomen substantivum numerum secundum formam significatam accipit, nomen autem adiectivum secundum supposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX1","text":"Spiritus Sanctus non est nomen proprium ex vi separatarum vocum, quae tribus personis communes manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX2","text":"Defectus formae grammaticae relativae non impedit quin nomen personam sola relatione distinctam significet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX3","text":"Personae divinae non distinguuntur secundum aliquid absolutum neque secundum pluralitatem essentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX4","text":"Processio a Patre non significat processionem a solo Patre ad exclusionem Filii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","text":"Absentia formulae verbatim expressae non efficit doctrinam extraneam Scripturae, si eius sensus in Scriptura continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6","text":"Explicatio posterior symboli non constituit doctrinam novam, si id quod implicite continebatur contra errorem supervenientem declarat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX7","text":"Quies vel mansio Spiritus Sancti in Filio processionem ab eo non excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX8","text":"Verbum divinum non accipitur ad similitudinem verbi vocalis, sed verbi mentalis a quo amor procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX9","text":"Perfecta processio Spiritus Sancti a Patre processionem a Filio non reddit superfluam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX10","text":"Formula per Filium non importat instrumentum, virtutem secundam, inaequalitatem causalitatis aut successionem temporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX11","text":"Unum principium non significat unam personam neque duo principia sub una appellatione collecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D1","text":"Dictiones communiter acceptae totam Trinitatem significant, sed tamquam una dictio ex usu acceptae proprium nomen personae Amoris constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","text":"Proprietas nominis Spiritus Sancti est referentialis et relationalis per accommodationem, non exclusiva ex nativa significatione vocum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_28:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","text":"Si Spiritus Sanctus a Filio non esset, relationes Filii et Spiritus Sancti ad Patrem mutuo oppositae non essent, unde distinctio eorum personalis tolleretur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D4","text":"Cum mutua oppositio originis requiratur et Filius a Spiritu Sancto non sit, Spiritus Sanctus necessario est a Filio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D5","text":"Processio Amoris a Verbo ordinem personalem confirmat quo Spiritus Sanctus a Filio procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D6","text":"Duae personae ab uno Patre procedentes non possunt ut productiones immateriales omnino parallelae manere; earum ordo determinatur Spiritu Sancto a Filio existente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:A10","CH_GGVC_P_28:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","text":"Pater per Filium spirat Spiritum Sanctum, quia Filius a Patre recipit ipsam rationem qua principium processionis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","text":"In ordine virtutis nullum medium inter Patrem, Filium et processionem interponitur, sed in ordine suppositorum Spiritus Sanctus a Patre etiam per Filium procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A14","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D9","text":"Spiritus Sanctus aequaliter a Patre et Filio procedit, quamvis Pater principaliter nominetur quia Filius virtutem spirativam ab eo habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D10","text":"Ordo quo Filius a Patre et Spiritus Sanctus a Patre per Filium procedunt est ordo originis sine priori et posteriori temporali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","text":"Pater et Filius sunt unum principium Spiritus Sancti propter unam virtutem et proprietatem spirativam in qua relative non opponuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A17","CH_GGVC_P_28:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D12","text":"Secundum solutionem praelatam Pater et Filius sunt duo spirantes propter pluralitatem suppositorum, sed non duo spiratores propter unam spirationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD1","text":"Identitas personalis in divinis non ex essentia communi neque ex qualitatibus absolutis, sed ex topologia relationum originis oppositarum constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD2","text":"Processio Spiritus Sancti a Filio non est additamentum externum doctrinae Trinitatis, sed condicio distinctionis Filii et Spiritus intra exemplar relationale admissum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD3","text":"Processiones intellectus et voluntatis eandem structuram ordinis exprimunt ac relationes originis: Verbum a Patre, Amor a Patre per Verbum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:D5","CH_GGVC_P_28:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD4","text":"Formula a Patre per Filium coniungit asymmetriam originis virtutis cum aequalitate virtutis spirativae et effectus processionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD5","text":"Systema numeros diversos secundum diversa strata distribuit: una essentia, tres personae, duae processiones, una virtus spirativa, unum principium et duo supposita spirantia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD6","text":"Explicatio doctrinalis legitima transit ab implicito ad explicitum cum error novus distinctionem antea non requisitam facit, dummodo sensus prior servetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX1","text":"Systema falsitatem requirit individuationis personarum per proprietates absolutas, quia talis differentia unitatem essentiae destrueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX2","text":"Sola diversitas modorum quibus Filius et Spiritus Sanctus ad Patrem referuntur non sufficit, nisi inter eos relatio originis opposita constituatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX3","text":"Excluditur exemplar duarum processionum immaterialium omnino parallelarum et mutuo inordinatarum ab eodem principio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","CH_GGVC_P_28:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX4","text":"Excluditur virtus spirativa Filii numero alia vel instrumentalis respectu virtutis Patris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX5","text":"Excluditur translatio ordinis originis in successionem temporalem, mutationem vel inceptionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A16","CH_GGVC_P_28:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX6","text":"Essentia communis simpliciter non potest esse tota ratio spirationis, quia tunc Spiritus Sanctus, eiusdem essentiae, a seipso procederet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0105","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX7","text":"Excluditur regula univoca qua numerus suppositorum semper numerum principiorum, proprietatum vel actionum determinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0107","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX1","text":"Possibilitas Filii et Spiritus Sancti ut duarum personarum sine relatione originis inter se praecluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX2","text":"Nullum tertium instrumentum, medium reale aut potestas derivata numero alia inter Patrem, Filium et Spiritum Sanctum admittitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX3","text":"Oppositio simplicis immediationis et mediationis praecluditur, quia immediatio secundum virtutem et mediatio secundum supposita simul affirmantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX4","text":"Una arithmetica indiscriminata essentiae, personae, proprietatis et actus inadmissibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX5","text":"Doctrina ad solam formulam Scripturae verbatim expressam claudi non potest, quia sensus implicitus et explicatio contra errorem structuram argumenti sustinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS1","text":"Defectus nominis naturaliter proprii → communitas vocum → accommodatio usus → nomen personale Spiritus Sancti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_28:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS2","text":"Unitas essentiae → exclusio differentiarum absolutarum → distinctio relationibus → oppositio originis → necessitas Spiritus Sancti a Filio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS3","text":"Processio intellectus ut Verbum → apprehensio mentalis → processio voluntatis ut Amor → ordo Spiritus Sancti ad Filium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS4","text":"Duae personae ab uno principio → exclusio distinctionis materialis → requisitus ordo originis → Spiritus Sanctus a Filio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","CH_GGVC_P_28:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS5","text":"Filius recipit virtutem spirativam a Patre → per designat principium derivatum → Pater spirat per Filium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A14","CH_GGVC_P_28:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS6","text":"Una virtus spirativa → nulla mediatio virtutis → distinctus ordo suppositorum → processio immediata a Patre et per Filium sine inaequalitate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS7","text":"Absentia oppositionis in proprietate spirativa → una forma significata → unum principium → pluralitas suppositorum manet sine multiplicatione spirationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A17","CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF1","text":"Communitas lexicalis → accommodatio ecclesialis → proprietas nominis → significatio personae Amoris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D1","CH_GGVC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF2","text":"Una essentia → relationes ut principium distinctionis → oppositio originis → Spiritus Sanctus a Filio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF3","text":"Verbum mentale → amor → ordo processionum → confirmatio processionis Spiritus Sancti a Filio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF4","text":"Virtus Filii a Patre → Pater per Filium → una virtus → aequalis et coaeterna processio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A16","CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF5","text":"Non-oppositio Patris et Filii ut spirantium → unitas proprietatis → unum principium → distinctio suppositorum sine duplici spiratore.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A17","CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME1","text":"Proprietas nominis a significatione lexicali exclusiva ad usum referentialem relatione fundatum transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D1","CH_GGVC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME2","text":"Processio a Filio ex formula controversa in condicionem structuralem distinctionis Filii et Spiritus Sancti reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME3","text":"Formula per Filium ab imagine instrumentalis mediationis ad ordinem originis inter supposita sub una virtute transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME4","text":"Oppositio inter immediationem et mediationem dissolvitur distinctione ordinis virtutis ab ordine suppositorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME5","text":"Numerus personarum, principiorum, proprietatum et actuum secundum formas diversas praedicationis distribuitur, non secundum unam rationem numeralem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX7","CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME6","text":"Relatio inter symbolum prius et explicationem posteriorem ab oppositione novitatis et traditionis ad distinctionem impliciti et expliciti transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — Disputantur proprietas nominis Spiritus Sancti, processio a Filio, processio a Patre per Filium et unitas principii spirativi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — Nomina, personae et processiones ordinantur per accommodationem semanticam, relationes oppositas, virtutem communem et regulas praedicationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — Controversia reformulatur ita ut formulae a Patre, a Filio et per Filium non ut aemulae, sed ut diversi gradus eiusdem ordinis originis legantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Realitas divina praesupponitur una secundum essentiam, pluralis secundum relationes originis, ordinata sine materia, successione temporali vel inaequalitate virtutis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad quattuor conclusiones principales restituendas: nomen proprium accommodatum, processionem a Filio, processionem per Filium et unum principium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT2","text":"Restitutio intra systema cohaeret, si concedantur doctrinae antea probatae de duabus processionibus, distinctione relationibus et exclusivitate relationum originis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT3","text":"Firmissima commissura est deductio processionis a Filio ex necessitate oppositionis relationis inter Filium et Spiritum Sanctum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT4","text":"Ratio ex pluralitate immateriali ad necessarium ordinem originis compressa manet, quia impossibilitas cuiuslibet alterius ordinis hic potius assumitur quam integre demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","CH_GGVC_P_28:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT5","text":"Compositio immediationis cum processione per Filium cohaeret per distinctionem virtutis et suppositorum, sed ab huius distinctionis stabilitate pendet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT6","text":"Formula unius principii pendet a metaphysica grammatica qua numerus substantivorum ex forma significata, non simpliciter ex numero suppositorum, sumitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT7","text":"Proprietas nominis et legitimatio explicationis doctrinalis usum ecclesialem atque sensum implicitum requirunt, quorum criteria intra hanc quaestionem non plene elaborantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT8","text":"Restitutio verum motum argumenti servat: nomen per accommodationem, persona per relationem, processio per ordinem originis, unitas principii per identitatem virtutis et proprietatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS5","CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161004000030Z_2f64d7b1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 36","source_sha256":"9e1ca655aa5f055c482943cdd69ad5cd69ff76c7554a7d2b99231cab2b292bb2","sha256":"087bd52830b5a6e179adc4e8bb491576b78808e1ce1d7df5830499d0b4d21a7f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:10:04.002525+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS1","text":"The question determines how the name, origin, and principle of the Holy Spirit are to be conceived while preserving the unity of essence and the distinction of three persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS2","text":"Holy Spirit is a name accommodated to the person proceeding by way of love, who proceeds from the Father and the Son, from the Father through the Son, and from both as from one principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS3","text":"The argumentation is dialectical, semantic, and metaphysically reconstructive, because from the rules of naming, relation, origin, and predication it reconstructs the doctrine of person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS4","text":"The first movement proceeds from the commonality of the meaning of the terms to the propriety of the name through the accommodation of ecclesial and scriptural usage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS5","text":"The second movement proceeds from the unity of essence to distinction by opposed relations, thence to the necessity of the procession of the Holy Spirit from the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AS6","text":"The final movement proceeds from the origin of the spirative power in the Son to the formula through the Son, then from the unity of that same power and property to the one principle of the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","text":"In divine things, whatever is said absolutely pertains to the unity of essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","text":"The divine persons are distinguished from one another solely by relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","text":"Relations distinguish the divine persons only insofar as they are opposed to one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","text":"In divine things there are no opposed relations besides relations of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","text":"From the Father there are two processions: that of the Son by way of intellect as Word, and that of the Holy Spirit by way of will as Love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","text":"The procession by way of love and its relations do not have a proper natural name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","text":"The terms spirit and holy, according to their proper significations, are common to the whole Trinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","text":"The usage of Scripture and the Church accommodates the expression Holy Spirit to the person proceeding by way of love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A9","text":"An accommodated name can be used for a relative, although according to lexical form it is not said relatively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A10","text":"The Son is not from the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","text":"Love proceeds from the mental word, because nothing is loved unless it is apprehended according to a conception of the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","text":"Many can proceed from one without order only where they are materially distinguished; immaterial multiplicity requires an order of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","text":"The Son has from the Father that the Holy Spirit proceeds from him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A14","text":"The preposition through designates a cause or principle in the order of action and procession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","text":"One and the same numerically spirative power is in the Father and the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A16","text":"The generation of the Son and the procession of the Holy Spirit are coeternal with their principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A17","text":"The Father and the Son are one in all things in which opposition of relation does not distinguish them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","text":"A substantive noun receives number according to the signified form, whereas an adjective receives it according to the supposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX1","text":"Holy Spirit is not a proper name by virtue of the separate terms, which remain common to the three persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX2","text":"The lack of a relative grammatical form does not prevent a name from signifying a person distinguished solely by relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX3","text":"The divine persons are not distinguished according to anything absolute, nor according to a plurality of essences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX4","text":"Procession from the Father does not signify procession from the Father alone, to the exclusion of the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","text":"The absence of a verbatim expressed formula does not render a doctrine alien to Scripture, if its meaning is contained in Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6","text":"A later explanation of the creed does not constitute a new doctrine if it declares against a supervening error what was implicitly contained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX7","text":"The resting or abiding of the Holy Spirit in the Son does not exclude procession from him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX8","text":"The divine Word is not understood according to the likeness of a vocal word, but of the mental word from which love proceeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX9","text":"The perfect procession of the Holy Spirit from the Father does not render procession from the Son superfluous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX10","text":"The formula through the Son does not imply an instrument, a second power, inequality of causality, or temporal succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:NX11","text":"One principle does not signify one person, nor two principles gathered under one designation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D1","text":"Terms taken commonly signify the whole Trinity, but, taken as one expression by usage, they constitute a proper name of the person of Love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","text":"The propriety of the name Holy Spirit is referential and relational by accommodation, not exclusive by the native signification of the terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_28:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","text":"If the Holy Spirit were not from the Son, the relations of the Son and the Holy Spirit to the Father would not be mutually opposed, whence their personal distinction would be removed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D4","text":"Since mutual opposition of origin is required, and the Son is not from the Holy Spirit, the Holy Spirit is necessarily from the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D5","text":"The procession of Love from the Word confirms the personal order by which the Holy Spirit proceeds from the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D6","text":"Two persons proceeding from one Father cannot remain as wholly parallel immaterial productions; their order is determined by the Holy Spirit being from the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:A10","CH_GGVC_P_28:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","text":"The Father spirates the Holy Spirit through the Son, because the Son receives from the Father the very ground by which he is the principle of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","text":"In the order of power no medium is interposed between the Father, the Son, and the procession; but in the order of supposita the Holy Spirit proceeds from the Father also through the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A14","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D9","text":"The Holy Spirit proceeds equally from the Father and the Son, although the Father is named principally because the Son has spirative power from him.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D10","text":"The order by which the Son proceeds from the Father and the Holy Spirit from the Father through the Son is an order of origin without temporal prior and posterior.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","text":"The Father and the Son are one principle of the Holy Spirit by reason of the one spirative power and property in which they are not relatively opposed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A17","CH_GGVC_P_28:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:D12","text":"According to the preferred solution, the Father and the Son are two spirating persons on account of the plurality of supposita, but not two spirators on account of the one spiration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD1","text":"Personal identity in divine things is constituted not from common essence nor from absolute qualities, but from the topology of opposed relations of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD2","text":"The procession of the Holy Spirit from the Son is not an external addition to the doctrine of the Trinity, but a condition of the distinction of the Son and the Spirit within the admitted relational model.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD3","text":"The processions of intellect and will express the same structure of order as the relations of origin: Word from the Father, Love from the Father through the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:D5","CH_GGVC_P_28:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD4","text":"The formula from the Father through the Son joins the asymmetry of the origin of power with the equality of spirative power and of the effect of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD5","text":"The system distributes diverse numbers according to diverse strata: one essence, three persons, two processions, one spirative power, one principle, and two spirating supposita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SD6","text":"Legitimate doctrinal explanation proceeds from the implicit to the explicit when a new error makes necessary a distinction not previously required, provided the prior meaning is preserved.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX1","text":"The system requires the falsity of individuating persons through absolute properties, because such difference would destroy the unity of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX2","text":"The mere diversity of the ways in which the Son and the Holy Spirit are referred to the Father is insufficient, unless an opposed relation of origin between them is constituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX3","text":"The model of two wholly parallel and mutually unordered immaterial processions from the same principle is excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","CH_GGVC_P_28:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX4","text":"A spirative power of the Son numerically other than, or instrumental with respect to, the power of the Father is excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX5","text":"The translation of the order of origin into temporal succession, change, or beginning is excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A16","CH_GGVC_P_28:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX6","text":"The common essence simply cannot be the whole ground of spiration, because then the Holy Spirit, being of the same essence, would proceed from himself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0105","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX7","text":"A univocal rule by which the number of supposita always determines the number of principles, properties, or actions is excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0107","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX1","text":"The possibility of the Son and the Holy Spirit as two persons without a relation of origin between them is precluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX2","text":"No third instrument, real medium, or numerically other derived power between the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit is admitted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX3","text":"The opposition of simple immediacy and mediation is precluded, because immediacy according to power and mediation according to supposita are affirmed simultaneously.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX4","text":"One undifferentiated arithmetic of essence, person, property, and act is inadmissible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX5","text":"Doctrine cannot be confined to the sole formula of Scripture expressed verbatim, because implicit meaning and explanation against error sustain the structure of the argument.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS1","text":"Lack of a naturally proper name → commonality of terms → accommodation of usage → personal name of the Holy Spirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_28:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS2","text":"Unity of essence → exclusion of absolute differences → distinction by relations → opposition of origin → necessity of the Holy Spirit from the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS3","text":"Procession of intellect as Word → mental apprehension → procession of will as Love → order of the Holy Spirit to the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS4","text":"Two persons from one principle → exclusion of material distinction → required order of origin → Holy Spirit from the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","CH_GGVC_P_28:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS5","text":"The Son receives spirative power from the Father → through designates a derived principle → the Father spirates through the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A14","CH_GGVC_P_28:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS6","text":"One spirative power → no mediation of power → distinct order of supposita → immediate procession from the Father and through the Son without inequality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS7","text":"Absence of opposition in the spirative property → one signified form → one principle → plurality of supposita remains without multiplication of spiration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A17","CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF1","text":"Lexical commonality → ecclesial accommodation → propriety of the name → signification of the person of Love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D1","CH_GGVC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF2","text":"One essence → relations as principle of distinction → opposition of origin → Holy Spirit from the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF3","text":"Mental Word → love → order of processions → confirmation of the procession of the Holy Spirit from the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF4","text":"Power of the Son from the Father → Father through the Son → one power → equal and coeternal procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A16","CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:AF5","text":"Non-opposition of the Father and the Son as spirating → unity of property → one principle → distinction of supposita without a double spirator.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A17","CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME1","text":"The propriety of the name is transferred from exclusive lexical signification to relation-grounded referential usage.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D1","CH_GGVC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME2","text":"Procession from the Son is reclassified from a controversial formula into a structural condition of the distinction of the Son and the Holy Spirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME3","text":"The formula through the Son is transferred from an image of instrumental mediation to an order of origin among supposita under one power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME4","text":"The opposition between immediacy and mediation is dissolved by distinguishing the order of power from the order of supposita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME5","text":"The number of persons, principles, properties, and acts is distributed according to diverse forms of predication, not according to one numerical account.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX7","CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ME6","text":"The relation between the earlier creed and the later explanation is transferred from the opposition of novelty and tradition to the distinction of implicit and explicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — The propriety of the name Holy Spirit, procession from the Son, procession from the Father through the Son, and the unity of the spirative principle are disputed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — Names, persons, and processions are ordered through semantic accommodation, opposed relations, common power, and rules of predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — The controversy is reformulated so that the formulas from the Father, from the Son, and through the Son are read not as rivals but as diverse levels of the same order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:D9","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Divine reality is presupposed as one according to essence, multiple according to relations of origin, ordered without matter, temporal succession, or inequality of power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct four principal conclusions: an accommodated proper name, procession from the Son, procession through the Son, and one principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_28:A13","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_28:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction coheres within the system if the previously proved doctrines concerning the two processions, distinction by relations, and the exclusivity of relations of origin are granted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4","CH_GGVC_P_28:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT3","text":"The strongest joint is the deduction of procession from the Son from the necessity of opposition of relation between the Son and the Holy Spirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D3","CH_GGVC_P_28:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT4","text":"The argument from immaterial plurality to a necessary order of origin remains compressed, because the impossibility of any other order is here assumed rather than fully demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A12","CH_GGVC_P_28:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT5","text":"The combination of immediacy with procession through the Son coheres through the distinction of power and supposita, but depends on the stability of this distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D8","CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT6","text":"The formula of one principle depends on a metaphysical grammar by which the number of substantives is taken from the signified form, not simply from the number of supposita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A18","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0117","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT7","text":"The propriety of the name and the legitimation of doctrinal explanation require ecclesial usage and implicit meaning, the criteria of which are not fully elaborated within this question.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the argument: name through accommodation, person through relation, procession through order of origin, unity of principle through identity of power and property.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS5","CH_GGVC_P_28:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_28:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_28@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_28:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 37","title":"First Part · Question 36","context":"Chapter 37","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 36"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 36","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 37","order":38,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_29"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_29@R001","sha256":"9bdd2050422cdff3e074ab240e346fa743fe0b1b6c14bb03691ccc3c8e1c9539","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS1","text":"Quaestio discernit utrum «amor» sit nomen personale Spiritus Sancti vel nomen essentiale omnibus personis commune.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS2","text":"Solutio instituit distinctionem semanticam inter amorem ut habitudinem amantis ad amatum et amorem ut rem procedentem per modum voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS3","text":"Ex analogia verbi intellecti et amoris procedentis sequitur quod amor, personaliter acceptus, Spiritum Sanctum nominat sicut verbum Filium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS4","text":"Quaestio secunda ablativum «Spiritu Sancto» resolvit, ne Spiritus Sanctus tamquam principium formale vel efficiens dilectionis essentialis statuatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS5","text":"Propositio «Pater et Filius diligunt se Spiritu Sancto» vera fit solum cum diligere notionaliter significat productionem amoris procedentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A1","text":"In divinis sunt duae processiones: Verbi per intellectum et Amoris per voluntatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A2","text":"Processio per modum intellectus proprie designatur verbo; processio per modum voluntatis indiget vocabulis analogice extensis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","text":"Amor potest essentialiter significare habitudinem amantis ad rem amatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","text":"Amor potest personaliter significare rem procedentem per modum amoris cum habitudine ad principium spirans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A5","text":"In Deo amor et verbum subsistunt, quia in Deo nullum accidens est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A6","text":"Spiritus Sanctus procedit a Patre et Filio ut amor mutuus eorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A7","text":"Actus diligendi in divinis dupliciter accipitur: essentialiter ut actus communis, notionaliter ut spiratio amoris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","text":"Denominatio per effectum procedentem licet cum ille effectus in intellectu actionis determinate includitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A9","text":"Diligere notionaliter est producere amorem, sicut dicere est producere verbum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A10","text":"Amor procedens habet habitudinem ad rem amatam, etiam cum res amata est ipse Pater, Filius vel creatura.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX1","text":"Amor personaliter dictus non est mera actio transiens ab amante in obiectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX2","text":"Spiritus Sanctus non est medium originis inter Patrem et Filium, sed tertia persona ab utroque procedens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX3","text":"Spiritus Sanctus non est principium quo Pater et Filius essentialiter diligunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX4","text":"Amor essentialis non est proprium nomen Spiritus Sancti, quia essentialiter omnibus personis convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX5","text":"Spiritus Sanctus, quamvis amet essentialiter, non spirat amorem notionaliter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX6","text":"Non omnis actus notionalis denominari potest per personam procedentem; hoc valet tantum ubi effectus determinatus in ratione actus continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","text":"«Amor» est nomen proprium Spiritus Sancti quando significat amorem procedentem, non quando dilectionem essentialem significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_29:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D2","text":"Spiritus Sanctus est nexus Patris et Filii secundum relationem amoris mutui, non secundum positionem medii originarii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D3","text":"Amor divinus non implicat accidens in Deo, quia relatio ad amatum in amore subsistente manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A5","CH_GGVC_P_29:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D4","text":"Pater et Filius diligunt se Spiritu Sancto veraciter, si ablativus significat effectum formalem amoris notionaliter producti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A7","CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D5","text":"Non licet dicere Patrem spirare Spiritu Sancto vel generare Filio, quia spirare et generare non includunt determinate personam productam in ratione denominationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D6","text":"Amor procedens se extendit ad creaturas secundarie, quia bonitas divina, quam procedens amor exprimit, est principium amoris creaturarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SD1","text":"Proprietates personales non constituuntur per rem essentialiter diversam, sed per modum processionis quo eadem divina realitas relative significatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A1","CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_29:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SD2","text":"Ambiguitas nominum trinitariorum non est defectus marginalis sermonis, sed locus in quo distinctio inter essentiam, relationem, originem et personam formaliter exercetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A2","CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_29:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SD3","text":"Actio notionalis non describit productionem extrinsecam, sed relationem immanentem in qua persona procedens simul est terminus processionis et principium denominationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A5","CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit opinionem quod nomen univoce et simpliciter essentiale personalem distinctionem immediate destruere debeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit exemplar causale creaturarum, in quo amor esset accidens transiens, a descriptione processionum divinarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit reflexionem symmetricam omnium actuum notionalium, quia persona procedens participat actum essentialiter sine fieri principio processionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio circumagit impossibilitatem comprehendendi processionem voluntatis per vocabula proprie instituta, unde analogia et translatio semantica necessariae fiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio excludit omnem conceptionem personae divinae quae subsistentiam, relationem et originem tamquam res separabiles disponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:FGS1","text":"Processio intellectualis et processio voluntaria → distinctio Verbi et Amoris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:FGS2","text":"Amor ut relatio essentialis / Amor ut procedens subsistens → nomen commune / nomen personale Spiritus Sancti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:FGS3","text":"Diligere essentiale / diligere notionale → exclusio Spiritus Sancti ut principii dilectionis / affirmatio Spiritus Sancti ut amoris producti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:FGS4","text":"Effectus determinate inclusus in actu → denominatio Patris et Filii per Spiritum Sanctum → veritas propositionis ablativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AF1","text":"Ambiguitas nominis amoris → distinctio essentialis et personalis → analogia Verbi et Amoris → Spiritus Sanctus ut Amor procedens → distinctio dilectionis essentialis et notionalis → ablativus effectus formalis → Pater et Filius diligentes Spiritu Sancto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ME1","text":"Nomen amoris reclassificatur ex attributo affectivo simpliciter communi in terminum bivalens, essentialem vel personalem secundum modum significationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter nexus et persona solvitur: idem Spiritus Sanctus est nexus relationis et persona tertia secundum diversa respecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ME3","text":"Ablativus trinitarius reclassificatur ex indice causae efficientis in denominationem per terminum formaliter effectum actionis notionalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus statuit utrum Amor sit proprium nomen Spiritus Sancti et utrum Pater ac Filius se Spiritu Sancto diligant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT2","text":"Structural — Distinctiones essentiae, personae, relationis, originis et actus notionalis ordinant usum nominum divinorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur per translationem quaestionis ex grammatica superficiali ad rationem significationis et denominationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Processiones divinae sunt immanentes, subsistentes et a successione actionis transiens immunes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad inferendum proprietatem personalem Amoris, si duplex significatio nominis et duplex acceptio diligendi servantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT2","text":"Structura firmissime nititur analogia inter Verbum intellectus et Amorem voluntatis, quae transitum a processione ad nomen personale permittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT3","text":"Systema manet dependens a distinctione inter rem significatam et modum significandi, quam non ex principiis huius quaestionis plene demonstrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in extensione vocabulorum voluntatis, quia ipsa vocabulorum inopia simul necessitatem et indeterminationem analogiae producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT5","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, quia ex difficultate semantica procedit ad distinctionem processionum, deinde ad regulam denominationis ablativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161023381303Z_7961bb11","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 37","source_sha256":"9bdd2050422cdff3e074ab240e346fa743fe0b1b6c14bb03691ccc3c8e1c9539","sha256":"746228d77d8b854953b29e495e9ffec915684b52e8b2fa5c2b29348b266a7d10","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:10:23.382373+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS1","text":"The question distinguishes whether “love” is a personal name of the Holy Spirit or an essential name common to all persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS2","text":"The solution establishes a semantic distinction between love as the relation of the lover to the beloved and love as a thing proceeding according to the mode of will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS3","text":"From the analogy of the understood word and proceeding love, it follows that love, taken personally, names the Holy Spirit as word names the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS4","text":"The second question resolves the ablative “by the Holy Spirit,” lest the Holy Spirit be established as the formal or efficient principle of essential love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AS5","text":"The proposition “The Father and the Son love one another by the Holy Spirit” is true only when to love signifies notionally the production of proceeding love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A1","text":"In God there are two processions: that of the Word through intellect and that of Love through will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A2","text":"Procession according to the mode of intellect is properly designated by word; procession according to the mode of will requires analogically extended terms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","text":"Love can signify essentially the relation of the lover to the thing loved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","text":"Love can signify personally the thing proceeding according to the mode of love, with a relation to the spirating principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A5","text":"In God love and word subsist, because in God there is no accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A6","text":"The Holy Spirit proceeds from the Father and the Son as their mutual love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A7","text":"The act of loving in God is taken in two ways: essentially, as a common act; notionally, as the spiration of love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","text":"Denomination through a proceeding effect is permissible when that effect is determinately included in the intelligibility of the action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A9","text":"To love notionally is to produce love, just as to speak is to produce a word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:A10","text":"Proceeding love bears a relation to the thing loved, even when the thing loved is the Father himself, the Son, or a creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX1","text":"Love, when spoken of personally, is not a mere action passing from the lover into an object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX2","text":"The Holy Spirit is not a medium of origin between the Father and the Son, but the third person proceeding from both.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX3","text":"The Holy Spirit is not the principle by which the Father and the Son love essentially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX4","text":"Essential love is not a proper name of the Holy Spirit, because it belongs essentially to all persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX5","text":"The Holy Spirit, although he loves essentially, does not spirate love notionally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:NX6","text":"Not every notional act can be denominated through the proceeding person; this holds only where a determinate effect is contained in the intelligibility of the act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","text":"“Love” is a proper name of the Holy Spirit when it signifies proceeding love, not when it signifies essential love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_29:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D2","text":"The Holy Spirit is the bond of the Father and the Son according to the relation of mutual love, not according to the position of an intermediary origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D3","text":"Divine love does not imply an accident in God, because the relation to the beloved remains in subsistent love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A5","CH_GGVC_P_29:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D4","text":"The Father and the Son truly love one another by the Holy Spirit, if the ablative signifies the formal effect of notionally produced love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A7","CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D5","text":"It is not permissible to say that the Father spirates by the Holy Spirit or generates by the Son, because to spirate and to generate do not determinately include the produced person in the intelligibility of denomination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:D6","text":"Proceeding love extends secondarily to creatures, because divine goodness, which proceeding love expresses, is the principle of love for creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SD1","text":"Personal properties are not constituted by something essentially diverse, but by the mode of procession through which the same divine reality is signified relatively.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A1","CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_29:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SD2","text":"The ambiguity of Trinitarian names is not a marginal defect of speech, but the locus in which the distinction among essence, relation, origin, and person is formally exercised.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A2","CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_29:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SD3","text":"Notional action does not describe extrinsic production, but an immanent relation in which the proceeding person is at once the terminus of procession and the principle of denomination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A5","CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the opinion that a name univocally and simply essential must immediately destroy personal distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX2","text":"The system excludes from the description of divine processions the causal model of creatures, in which love would be a passing accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a symmetric reflection of all notional acts, because the proceeding person participates in the act essentially without becoming the principle of procession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1","text":"The argument revolves around the impossibility of comprehending the procession of will through properly instituted terms, whence analogy and semantic transference become necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX2","text":"The argument excludes every conception of a divine person that disposes subsistence, relation, and origin as separable things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:FGS1","text":"Intellectual procession and volitional procession → distinction of Word and Love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:FGS2","text":"Love as essential relation / Love as proceeding subsistent → common name / personal name of the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:FGS3","text":"Essential loving / notional loving → exclusion of the Holy Spirit as the principle of loving / affirmation of the Holy Spirit as produced love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:FGS4","text":"Effect determinately included in the act → denomination of the Father and the Son through the Holy Spirit → truth of the ablative proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:AF1","text":"Ambiguity of the name love → essential and personal distinction → analogy of Word and Love → the Holy Spirit as proceeding Love → distinction of essential and notional loving → ablative of formal effect → the Father and the Son loving by the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ME1","text":"The name love is reclassified from a simply common affective attribute into a bivalent term, essential or personal according to its mode of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ME2","text":"The opposition between bond and person is resolved: the same Holy Spirit is the bond of relation and the third person according to diverse respects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ME3","text":"The Trinitarian ablative is reclassified from an indicator of efficient cause into denomination through the formally effected terminus of notional action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text establishes whether Love is a proper name of the Holy Spirit and whether the Father and the Son love one another by the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT2","text":"Structural — The distinctions of essence, person, relation, origin, and notional act order the use of divine names.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved by translating the question from superficial grammar to the intelligibility of signification and denomination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Divine processions are immanent, subsistent, and free from the succession of passing action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to infer the personal property of Love, if the twofold signification of the name and the twofold understanding of loving are retained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT2","text":"The structure relies most firmly on the analogy between the Word of intellect and the Love of will, which permits the transition from procession to personal name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT3","text":"The system remains dependent on the distinction between the thing signified and the mode of signifying, which it does not fully demonstrate from the principles of this question.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains in the extension of the terms of will, because the very paucity of terms produces both the necessity and the indeterminacy of analogy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from semantic difficulty to the distinction of processions, then to the rule of ablative denomination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_29:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_29@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_29:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 38","title":"First Part · Question 37","context":"Chapter 38","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 37"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 37","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 38","order":39,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_30"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_30@R001","sha256":"4d081b087a224b18a68c3fefd812d18f0b253cab5a849d97c5292748ab5b0b2c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat utrum «donum» in divinis nomen personale esse possit et utrum Spiritui Sancto proprie conveniat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS2","text":"Argumentatio objectiones ex indistinctione essentiali, subiectione, temporalitate et communicabilitate vocis ortas convertit in distinctionem modorum quibus aliquid dicitur esse alicuius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS3","text":"«Donum» personaliter significat aptitudinem ad dandum, fundatam in origine divinae personae a dante, non actum temporalem dationis neque relationem servilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS4","text":"Capacitas recipiendi personam divinam restringitur ad creaturam rationalem Deo coniunctam, quae libere Deo frui et eius effectu uti potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS5","text":"Proprietas nominis «donum» Spiritui Sancto attribuitur quia eius processio est processio amoris, et amor est primum donum gratuitum ex quo alia dona procedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS6","text":"Motus argumentationis est: difficultas vocis relativae → distinctio relationum possessionis et originis → aeternitas aptitudinis donabilis → identificatio processionis amoris cum ratione primi doni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","text":"Donum importat aptitudinem ad hoc quod donetur, non necessario dationem in actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A2","text":"Quod donatur refertur et ad dantem, cuius est, et ad recipientem, cuius per dationem fit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","text":"In divinis relatio qua persona est alicuius per originem distinguit personam a principio dante sine divisione essentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A4","text":"Relatio doni ad dantem, prout nomen personale est, originem tantum significat et subiectionem non significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","text":"Persona divina a creatura haberi potest solum ut obiectum liberi usus vel fruitionis, non sicut res subiecta dominio creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","text":"Sola creatura rationalis Deo coniuncta capax est libere Deum vere cognoscendi et recte amandi; ideo sola potest personam divinam habere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A7","text":"Creatura rationalis ad habendam personam divinam propria virtute pervenire non potest; talis habitio necessario est desuper data.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A8","text":"Donum proprie est datio irreddibilis, cuius ratio est gratuita donatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","text":"Amor est principium gratuitae donationis et primum donum per quod alia dona gratuita donantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A10","text":"Spiritus Sanctus procedit ut amor; ideo processio eius rationem primi doni constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A11","text":"Nomen personale proprium determinatur ex modo processionis proprio, etiamsi effectus vel communicatio significata aliis personis aliquo modo conveniat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX1","text":"«Donum» non definitur per dationem temporaliter iam perfectam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX2","text":"«Donum» personale non est nomen essentiae secundum identitatem, neque nomen creaturae secundum possessionem vel servitutem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX3","text":"Relatio doni personalis ad dantem non est subiectio personae divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX4","text":"Respectus ad creaturam non efficit nomen personale necessario temporale neque necessario essentiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX5","text":"Motio creaturae a persona divina non aequivalet habitioni divinae personae per liberam fruitionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX6","text":"Filius, quamvis detur, non dicitur proprie donum ex ipso actu dationis; proprium nomen sequitur modum processionis, non solam missionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX7","text":"Donum ante dationem non est donum recipientis; post dationem, eius esse potest ut datum vel spiritus, non tamen ut nomen originis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D1","text":"Persona divina potest ab aeterno dici donum, quia aptitudo donabilis aeternaliter competit, licet effectus dationis in creatura sit temporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D2","text":"Nomen «donum» distinguit Spiritum Sanctum a dante personaliter solum ubi «esse alicuius» per originem intelligitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A2","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","CH_GGVC_P_30:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D3","text":"Donatio divina creaturae non est translatio possessionis, sed concessio participationis qua creatura rationalis libere cognoscit et amat Deum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","CH_GGVC_P_30:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D4","text":"Spiritus Sanctus est principium donationum gratuitarum non solum quia donatur, sed quia procedit ut amor qui donationem gratuitam radicaliter constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A8","CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D5","text":"Communicabilitas Filii per missionem non destruit proprietatem nominis «donum» Spiritus Sancti, quia missio sequitur amorem dantis, dum proprietas sequitur processionem personae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10","CH_GGVC_P_30:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D6","text":"Nomen «donum Dei» retinet primatum originis divinae etiam postquam donum in creatura datum efficitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:A2","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1","text":"Donum personale unit ordinem intratrinitarium originis et ordinem oeconomicum participationis, ita ut relatio ad creaturam manifestationem processionis aeternae, non causam eius, constituat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SD2","text":"Gratia donativa describitur ut elevatio libertatis rationalis ad fruitionem Dei, non ut mera passiva impressio divinae motionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","CH_GGVC_P_30:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SD3","text":"Proprietates personales non abstrahuntur ex effectibus creaturis communiter apparentibus, sed ex rationibus originis quae effectuum distributionem ordinate fundant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10","CH_GGVC_P_30:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4","text":"Amor, ut primum donum, obtinet structuram generativam: ipse gratuitatem donationis fundat et per ipsum pluralitas donorum participatorum distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A8","CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX1","text":"Falsa esse debet aequatio omnis relationis ad creaturam cum temporalitate vel accidentalitate in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX2","text":"Falsa esse debet aequatio donationis cum alienatione rei a dante vel cum dominio recipientis super datum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX3","text":"Falsa esse debet opinio quod receptivitas creaturae ad Deum ex sola capacitate naturali aut ex sola motione divina sufficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX4","text":"Falsa esse debet opinio quod idem effectus missionis vel dationis nomen personale proprium omnibus personis communicet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX5","text":"Falsa esse debet reductio amoris ad effectum inter dona numerandum; amor ponitur potius ut principium quo ratio doni constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit divinam communicationem quae aut originem personalem supprimat aut creaturam in possessorem Dei convertat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit aeternitatem divinam clausam intra se et incapacem relationis donabilis ad creaturam, sed etiam excludit Deum cui relatio creaturae principium constitutivum sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit gratuitatem quae retributionem quaerat, quia talis datio rationem proprii doni destrueret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:FGS1","text":"Aptitudo donabilis → relatio originis ad dantem → nomen personale aeternum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:FGS2","text":"Persona divina donabilis → creatura rationalis Deo coniuncta → participatio gratuita → liber usus et fruitio Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:FGS3","text":"Donatio irreddibilis → gratuitum velle bonum → amor ut primum donum → processio Spiritus ut ratio proprii nominis «donum».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:FGS4","text":"Communis dabilitas personarum vel effectuum → distinctio modorum processionis → restrictio nominis proprii ad Spiritum Sanctum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AF1","text":"Ambiguitas doni inter essentiam, creaturam et personam → distinctio identitatis, possessionis et originis → donum personale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AF2","text":"Respectus ad creaturam → distinctio aptitudinis a datione actuali → aeternitas nominis «donum» cum temporalitate missionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AF3","text":"Capacitas rationalis ad fruitionem → necessitas donationis desuper → persona divina ut donum participabile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AF4","text":"Donum gratuitum → amor ut primum donum → Spiritus procedens ut amor → «donum» ut nomen proprium Spiritus Sancti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ME1","text":"Vocabulum relativum «donum» reclassificatur: non est simpliciter nomen effectus creati aut actus temporalis, sed potest esse nomen personale fundatum in origine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter aeternitatem divinam et donationem creaturae dissolvitur per distinctionem inter aptitudinem aeternam et dationem temporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ME3","text":"Relatio creaturae ad personam divinam describitur sub forma fruitionis liberae et participatae, non sub forma dominii, servitutis aut merae motionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ME4","text":"Processio amoris fit principium classificatorium quo Spiritus Sanctus distinguitur a Filio, etiam ubi uterque in oeconomia divina datur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus determinat an «donum» sit nomen personale et an Spiritui Sancto proprie attribuatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT2","text":"Structural — Textus distinguit relationem originis, identitatis et possessionis, atque aptitudinem donandi ab actu dationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones non removentur per negationem relationis, sed per specificationem cuius relationis nomen personale sit capax.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Processio aeterna Spiritus ut amor fundat nomen personale aeternum, dum donatio participata in creatura contingit temporaliter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de aptitudine, origine, fruitione rationali, gratuitate et processione amoris sufficiunt ad conclusionem quod «donum» sit nomen personale proprium Spiritus Sancti restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT2","text":"Nexus inter nomen personale et relationem ad creaturam stabilitur per distinctionem aptitudinis a datione actuali; hic est cardo quo aeternitas nominis servatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT3","text":"Systema maxime cohaeret ubi aequivocationem «esse alicuius» in identitatem, possessionem et originem dividit, quia haec divisio objectiones heterogeneas sub una regula disponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in eo quod nomen ad creaturam ordinatum personale dicitur sine essentialitate, quamvis essentia divina in intellectu personae includatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT5","text":"Tensio persistit inter gratuitam donationem quae recipiens quodammodo accipit et negationem cuiuslibet dominii recipientis; textus eam per fruitionem et usum liberum, non per definitionem possessionis exhaustivam, moderatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat si distinctio semantica relationum antecedit deductionem pneumatologicam ex amore ut primo dono.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161047735053Z_6599b018","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 38","source_sha256":"4d081b087a224b18a68c3fefd812d18f0b253cab5a849d97c5292748ab5b0b2c","sha256":"8e9f330b1ba0fdc46813ba85b664acd8ab55c32bea1c60779692854b3b79cea9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:10:47.736136+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS1","text":"The question examines whether “gift” can be a personal name in the divine, and whether it properly belongs to the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS2","text":"The argument converts objections arising from essential indistinction, subjection, temporality, and the communicability of the term into a distinction among the ways in which something is said to be another's.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS3","text":"“Gift” personally signifies an aptitude for being given, founded upon the origin of the divine person from the giver, not the temporal act of giving nor a servile relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS4","text":"The capacity to receive a divine person is restricted to the rational creature united to God, which can freely enjoy God and make use of His effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS5","text":"The propriety of the name “gift” is attributed to the Holy Spirit because His procession is a procession of love, and love is the first gratuitous gift from which other gifts proceed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AS6","text":"The movement of the argument is: difficulty of the relative term → distinction of relations of possession and origin → eternity of donable aptitude → identification of the procession of love with the character of the first gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","text":"Gift implies an aptitude for being given, not necessarily actual giving.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A2","text":"What is given is related both to the giver, whose it is, and to the recipient, whose it becomes through giving.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","text":"In the divine, the relation by which a person is another's through origin distinguishes the person from the giving principle without division of the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A4","text":"The relation of gift to the giver, insofar as it is a personal name, signifies origin alone and does not signify subjection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","text":"A divine person can be possessed by a creature only as the object of free use or enjoyment, not as a thing subject to the creature's dominion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","text":"Only the rational creature united to God is capable of freely knowing God truly and loving Him rightly; therefore only it can possess a divine person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A7","text":"The rational creature cannot attain possession of a divine person by its own power; such possession is necessarily given from above.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A8","text":"A gift properly is an irrecompensable giving, whose character is gratuitous donation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","text":"Love is the principle of gratuitous donation and the first gift through which other gratuitous gifts are given.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A10","text":"The Holy Spirit proceeds as love; therefore His procession constitutes the character of the first gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:A11","text":"A proper personal name is determined from the proper mode of procession, even if the signified effect or communication belongs in some way to other persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX1","text":"“Gift” is not defined by giving already temporally completed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX2","text":"Personal “gift” is not a name of essence according to identity, nor a name of creature according to possession or servitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX3","text":"The relation of the personal gift to the giver is not the subjection of the divine person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX4","text":"Reference to the creature does not render the personal name necessarily temporal or necessarily essential.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX5","text":"The motion of a creature by a divine person is not equivalent to possession of the divine person through free enjoyment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX6","text":"The Son, although He is given, is not properly called gift from the very act of giving; the proper name follows the mode of procession, not mission alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:NX7","text":"Before being given, a gift is not the gift of the recipient; after being given, it can be his as given or as spirit, yet not as a name of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D1","text":"A divine person can be called gift from eternity, because donable aptitude belongs eternally, although the effect of giving in the creature is temporal.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D2","text":"The name “gift” distinguishes the Holy Spirit personally from the giver only where “to be another's” is understood through origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A2","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","CH_GGVC_P_30:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D3","text":"Divine donation to the creature is not a transfer of possession, but the granting of a participation by which the rational creature freely knows and loves God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","CH_GGVC_P_30:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D4","text":"The Holy Spirit is the principle of gratuitous donations not only because He is given, but because He proceeds as love, which radically constitutes gratuitous donation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A8","CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D5","text":"The communicability of the Son through mission does not destroy the propriety of the name “gift” of the Holy Spirit, because mission follows the love of the giver, whereas propriety follows the procession of the person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10","CH_GGVC_P_30:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:D6","text":"The name “gift of God” retains the primacy of divine origin even after the gift is made given in the creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:A2","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1","text":"Personal gift unites the intratrinitarian order of origin and the economic order of participation, such that relation to the creature constitutes a manifestation of eternal procession, not its cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SD2","text":"Donative grace is described as the elevation of rational freedom to the enjoyment of God, not as a mere passive impression of divine motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","CH_GGVC_P_30:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SD3","text":"Personal properties are not abstracted from effects commonly appearing in creatures, but from the accounts of origin that orderly ground the distribution of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10","CH_GGVC_P_30:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4","text":"Love, as the first gift, possesses a generative structure: it grounds the gratuity of donation, and through it a plurality of participated gifts is distributed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A8","CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX1","text":"The equation of every relation to the creature with temporality or accidentality in God must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX2","text":"The equation of donation with alienation of a thing from the giver or with the recipient's dominion over what is given must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX3","text":"The opinion that the creature's receptivity toward God is sufficiently accounted for by natural capacity alone or by divine motion alone must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX4","text":"The opinion that the same effect of mission or giving communicates a proper personal name to all persons must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX5","text":"The reduction of love to an effect to be numbered among gifts must be false; love is posited rather as the principle by which the character of gift is constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX1","text":"The system excludes a divine communication that either suppresses personal origin or converts the creature into a possessor of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX2","text":"The system excludes a divine eternity closed within itself and incapable of a donable relation to the creature, but also excludes a God for whom relation to the creature is a constitutive principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX3","text":"The system excludes a gratuity that seeks recompense, because such a giving would destroy the character of a proper gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:FGS1","text":"Donable aptitude → relation of origin to the giver → eternal personal name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:FGS2","text":"Donable divine person → rational creature united to God → gratuitous participation → free use and enjoyment of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:FGS3","text":"Irrecompensable donation → gratuitous willing of good → love as first gift → procession of the Spirit as the character of the proper name “gift.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:FGS4","text":"Common givability of persons or effects → distinction of modes of procession → restriction of the proper name to the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AF1","text":"Ambiguity of gift between essence, creature, and person → distinction of identity, possession, and origin → personal gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AF2","text":"Reference to the creature → distinction of aptitude from actual giving → eternity of the name “gift” together with the temporality of mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AF3","text":"Rational capacity for enjoyment → necessity of donation from above → divine person as participable gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:AF4","text":"Gratuitous gift → love as first gift → Spirit proceeding as love → “gift” as the proper name of the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ME1","text":"The relative term “gift” is reclassified: it is not simply the name of a created effect or temporal act, but can be a personal name founded in origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ME2","text":"The opposition between divine eternity and donation to the creature is dissolved through the distinction between eternal aptitude and temporal giving.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ME3","text":"The relation of the creature to the divine person is described under the form of free and participated enjoyment, not under the form of dominion, servitude, or mere motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ME4","text":"The procession of love becomes the classificatory principle by which the Holy Spirit is distinguished from the Son, even where each is given in the divine economy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines whether “gift” is a personal name and whether it is properly attributed to the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT2","text":"Structural — The text distinguishes the relation of origin, identity, and possession, and aptitude for giving from the act of giving.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are not removed through denial of relation, but through specification of which relation a personal name can bear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The eternal procession of the Spirit as love grounds the eternal personal name, while participated donation occurs temporally in the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning aptitude, origin, rational enjoyment, gratuity, and the procession of love suffice to restore the conclusion that “gift” is the proper personal name of the Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT2","text":"The nexus between the personal name and relation to the creature is established through the distinction of aptitude from actual giving; this is the hinge by which the eternity of the name is preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT3","text":"The system is most coherent where it divides the equivocation of “to be another's” into identity, possession, and origin, because this division orders heterogeneous objections under one rule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains in that a name ordered to the creature is called personal without essentiality, although the divine essence is included in the understanding of the person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT5","text":"A tension persists between gratuitous donation, by which the recipient receives in some way, and the denial of any dominion of the recipient; the text moderates it through enjoyment and free use, not through an exhaustive definition of possession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if the semantic distinction of relations precedes the pneumatological deduction from love as the first gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_30:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_30@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_30:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 39","title":"First Part · Question 38","context":"Chapter 39","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 38"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 38","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 39","order":40,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_31"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_31@R001","sha256":"ffe0e60fb79c5c7ca345ddc63a43d9923c83ff02ee43b90208efbaa65bab5273","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quomodo unitas essentiae divinae cum distinctione personarum componatur et quibus regulis haec compositio praedicetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS2","text":"Essentia et persona sunt idem secundum rem, sed personae per oppositiones relationum realiter distinguuntur, essentia indivisa manente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est ontologico-semantica et reconstructiva: distinctionem realem personarum ex relationibus, distinctiones locutionum ex modis significandi deducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS4","text":"Motus procedit ab identitate essentiae et personae ad regulas numeri, suppositionis et praedicationis, deinde ad distinctionem inter proprietatem et appropriationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS5","text":"Clausura systematis essentialia communia in instrumenta manifestationis personarum convertit, sine partitione essentiae vel conversione appropriatorum in propria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0182","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","text":"In Deo essentia et suppositum seu persona sunt idem secundum rem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","text":"Una eademque essentia numero in tribus personis subsistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","text":"Persona divina relationem subsistentem in natura divina significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","text":"Relatio divina ab essentia non differt re, sed ratione tantum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A5","text":"Relationes oppositae virtute oppositionis realiter distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","text":"Intellectus humanus divina nominat secundum modum ex creaturis acceptum, non secundum modum ipsarum rerum divinarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","text":"Veritas locutionis dependet et a re significata et a modo significandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A8","text":"Essentia divina, quantum ad modum significandi, ut forma trium personarum significatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","text":"Numerus nominis substantivi sequitur formam significatam, numerus autem adiectivi supposita quibus forma attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","text":"Nomen concretum Deus essentiam ut in habente significat, ideoque pro essentia vel, ex determinatione contextus, pro una pluribusve personis supponere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","text":"Nomen abstractum essentia formam abstractam significat et naturalem suppositionem pro persona non habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A12","text":"Nomina personalia substantiva de essentia per identitatem realem praedicantur, non sicut inferiora de universali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","text":"Attributa essentialia ex creaturis certius cognoscuntur quam proprietates personales, quae demonstratione probari non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","text":"Appropriatio est attributio manifestativa communis essentialis ad personam, non constitutio proprietatis exclusivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A15","text":"Appropriatio personam manifestat per similitudinem vel per dissimilitudinem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0159","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","text":"Consideratio creaturae quattuor ordines praebet: esse, unitatem, virtutem causalem et habitudinem ad effectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A17","text":"Ordo personalis distinguit principium non de principio, principium de principio et nexum a duobus procedentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0183","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX1","text":"Essentia et persona non sunt duae res in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX2","text":"Distinctio personarum non est multiplicatio vel divisio essentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX3","text":"Relationes divinae non sunt accidentia vel res essentiae assistentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX4","text":"Nomina suppositum et hypostasis realem subiectionem personae sub essentia non significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX5","text":"Nomina essentialia substantive sumpta pluralitatem deorum vel substantiarum non admittunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX6","text":"Tres personae ex una essentia vel de una essentia esse non dicuntur, quia talis constructio distinctionem causae materialis vel efficientis insinuaret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX7","text":"Actus et proprietates personales nomini abstracto essentiae non attribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX8","text":"Attributum appropriatum non soli personae appropriatae convenit neque ei magis quam aliis convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX9","text":"Trinitas personarum ex creaturis demonstrari non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX10","text":"Essentia et operatio personis non appropriantur, quia earum communitas nullam similitudinem determinatam cum proprietatibus personalibus praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0182","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D1","text":"Unitas essentiae et pluralitas personarum simul servantur, quia relatio secundum essentiam est idem realiter, secundum oppositionem autem personam realiter distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D2","text":"De essentia et persona diversa affirmari vel negari possunt sine contradictione, quia identitas realis distinctionem rationis non tollit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D3","text":"Formula tres personae unius essentiae legitima est, quia genitivus essentiam secundum rationem formae designat, non causam a personis distinctam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D4","text":"Unitas essentiae strictius unitatem divinam exprimit quam unitas naturae, quia essentia unum esse, natura autem etiam solam convenientiam operationis significare potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D5","text":"Nomina essentialia substantive sumpta de tribus personis singulariter praedicantur, adiective autem sumpta pluraliter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D6","text":"Locutio Deus genuit Deum vera est, quia nomen concretum pro patre et filio supponere potest, una deitate numero permanente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D7","text":"Locutio essentia genuit essentiam falsa est, quia nomen abstractum personam non importat et generationem intra essentiam distinctam significaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D8","text":"Locutiones essentia est tres personae et Deus est Trinitas verae sunt, quando subiectum pro essentia supponit et praedicatio per identitatem fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0145","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D9","text":"Appropriatio potest personas manifestare sine distributione attributorum essentialium, quia munus eius epistemicum est, non constitutivum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D10","text":"Sub ratione esse, aeternitas patri, species filio et usus Spiritui Sancto appropriantur secundum similitudines principii non principiati, imaginis perfectae et amoris seu doni.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A15","CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0180","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0181","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D11","text":"Sub ratione unitatis, unitas patri, aequalitas filio et connexio Spiritui Sancto appropriantur secundum ordinem absoluti principii, respectus ad alterum et nexus duorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0182","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D12","text":"Sub ratione virtutis causalis, potentia patri, sapientia filio et bonitas Spiritui Sancto appropriantur secundum similitudines principii, verbi et amoris atque per remotionem defectuum creatorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A15","CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0184","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0185","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D13","text":"Sub ratione habitudinis ad effectus, ex quo patri, per quem filio et in quo Spiritui Sancto appropriantur secundum efficientiam, rationem formalem operationis et continentiam gubernantem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0186","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0187","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD1","text":"Identitas realis nominum divinorum substituibilitatem universalem non efficit, quia modus significandi ambitum suppositionis et praedicationis regit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","CH_GGVC_P_31:D6","CH_GGVC_P_31:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD2","text":"Unum et tria non de eodem sub eadem ratione dicuntur: unitas ad essentiam, pluralitas ad relationes oppositas pertinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5","CH_GGVC_P_31:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","text":"Grammatica theologica instrumentum conservationis ontologicae fit, quia locutiones admittuntur vel excluduntur secundum quod unitatem essentiae aut distinctionem relationum servant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD4","text":"Nomen Deus structuram duplicem habet: quasi singulare est propter formam non multiplicatam, quasi commune propter eandem formam in pluribus suppositis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD5","text":"Appropriatio constituit mediationem inter cognitionem naturalem attributorum essentialium et cognitionem revelatam proprietatum personalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A15","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD6","text":"Quattuor modi considerandi ens creatum in matricem trinitariam convertuntur, non quia structuram Trinitatis demonstrent, sed quia ordinem personalem manifestent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17","CH_GGVC_P_31:D10","CH_GGVC_P_31:D11","CH_GGVC_P_31:D12","CH_GGVC_P_31:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet identitatem rei sufficere ad substitutionem nominum in omni contextu praedicativo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem pluralitatem suppositorum multiplicationem formae vel naturae requirere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet nomen Deus ad personas se habere sicut universale ad singularia creata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A12","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet attributionem communis ad personam divisionem, maiorem possessionem vel causalitatem essentialis attributi importare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet modos creatos significandi compositiones creatas in Deo secundum rem constituere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:A8","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX1","text":"Modus cognoscendi et nominandi Deum secundum ipsum modum divinum intellectui creato indisponibilis manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX2","text":"Nulla quarta res inter essentiam et personas admittitur quae unitatem colligat vel pluralitatem recipiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX3","text":"Compositio, divisio substantialis et causalitas essentiae sunt solutiones praeclusae contradictionis apparentis inter unum et tria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4","text":"Ex creaturis nulla via demonstrativa ad proprietates personales patet; remanet tantum manifestatio analogica post positionem fidei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0159","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS1","text":"Simplicitas divina → identitas realis essentiae et personae → relatio subsistens → oppositio relationum → distinctio realis personarum sine distinctione essentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS2","text":"Cognitio ex creaturis → modus significandi creatus → distinctio substantivi et adiectivi atque concreti et abstracti → determinatio numeri, suppositionis et praedicationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:A8","CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS3","text":"Locutio divina → examen rei significatae → examen modi significandi → determinatio suppositi → admissio si essentia una et relatio personalis distincta servantur → reiectio si essentia dividitur, generatur vel causaliter separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS4","text":"Proprietates personales indemonstrabiles + attributa essentialia manifestiora → comparatio per similitudinem vel dissimilitudinem → appropriatio → manifestatio personae sine conversione communis in proprium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS5","text":"Esse → aeternitas, species, usus; unitas → unitas, aequalitas, connexio; virtus → potentia, sapientia, bonitas; effectus → ex quo, per quem, in quo; singulae triades ad patrem, filium et Spiritum Sanctum ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17","CH_GGVC_P_31:D10","CH_GGVC_P_31:D11","CH_GGVC_P_31:D12","CH_GGVC_P_31:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0182","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0184","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0186","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0187","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AF1","text":"Identitas essentiae et personae → oppositio relationum → unitas essentiae cum tribus personis → regula numeri essentialium → suppositio concreti → exclusio abstracti → praedicatio per identitatem → appropriatio communium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0143","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AF2","text":"Difficultas ontologica → resolutio relationalis → translatio in semanticam → probatio locutionum singularium → distinctio proprii et appropriati → ordinatio quattuor matricum trinitariarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0143","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter unam essentiam et tres personas solvitur per distributionem unitatis et pluralitatis ad diversos ordines formales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME2","text":"Pluralitas divina ex principiis essentialibus ad oppositiones relationum subsistentium transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME3","text":"Numerus grammaticalis desinit esse index simplex numeri rerum et secundum substantivum vel adiectivum diversimode ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME4","text":"Praedicatio essentiae et personae extra exemplar universalis et singularis reclassificatur ut praedicatio per identitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0147","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME5","text":"Appropriatio ex distributione ontologica attributorum in operationem epistemicam manifestationis convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME6","text":"Quattuor ordines considerationis creaturae fiunt tabula ordinans attributa communia circa proprietates personales sine demonstratione Trinitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT1","text":"Surface — Locutiones de una essentia, tribus personis, uno Deo, generatione et appropriatione secundum regulas grammaticales admittuntur vel excluduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT2","text":"Structural — Identitas essentiae et relationis cum oppositione reali relationum mechanismum unitatis substantialis et distinctionis personalis constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Modus significandi et suppositio fiunt instrumenta ad errores divisionis essentiae, polytheismi et confusionis personarum inhibendos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Realitas divina simplex et aeterna praesupponitur, dum ordo personarum per originem relationalem, non per partitionem essentiae, disponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendam compositionem ontologiae relationum, semanticae nominum et doctrinae appropriationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT2","text":"Distinctio relationum, processiones personales et simplicitas divina hic non integre probantur, sed ex quaestionibus prioribus assumuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT3","text":"Regula modi significandi necessaria est, sed criterium eius contextuale manet nec in calculum semanticum completum reducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT4","text":"Systema interne cohaeret si identitas realis, distinctio rationis et oppositio relationalis stricte separantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT5","text":"Firmissima commissura est resolutio pluralitatis personarum per relationes subsistentes oppositas, essentia numero una permanente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT6","text":"Fragilior commissura est asymmetria qua Deus pro essentia vel persona supponit, dum essentia de persona praedicari potest sed pro persona supponere nequit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT7","text":"Matrices appropriationis similitudinibus selectivis nituntur, quarum vis manifestativa constat, sed quarum necessitas non semper univoce determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0186","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0187","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT8","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: quaestionem ontologicam per relationes solvit, solutionem in regulas locutionis transfert, deinde eas in ordinem manifestationis trinitariae extendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161116630990Z_61fd8bae","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 39","source_sha256":"ffe0e60fb79c5c7ca345ddc63a43d9923c83ff02ee43b90208efbaa65bab5273","sha256":"b2d58090693465827da9bc0bb91377f294d0eadec7a5d2275ddc42aa421ec313","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:11:16.632046+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS1","text":"The question determines how the unity of the divine essence is reconciled with the distinction of persons and by what rules this reconciliation is predicated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS2","text":"Essence and person are the same in reality, but the persons are really distinguished through the oppositions of relations, while the essence remains undivided.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS3","text":"The argumentation is ontological-semantic and reconstructive: it derives the real distinction of persons from relations, and distinctions of expressions from modes of signifying.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS4","text":"The movement proceeds from the identity of essence and person to the rules of number, supposition, and predication, then to the distinction between property and appropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AS5","text":"The system's closure converts common essentials into instruments for the manifestation of persons, without partitioning the essence or converting appropriated attributes into proper ones.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0182","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","text":"In God, essence and supposit or person are the same in reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","text":"One and the same essence numerically subsists in three persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","text":"A divine person signifies a subsisting relation in the divine nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","text":"A divine relation does not differ from the essence in reality, but only in reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A5","text":"Opposed relations are really distinguished by virtue of opposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","text":"The human intellect names divine things according to a mode received from creatures, not according to the mode of the divine things themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","text":"The truth of an expression depends both on the thing signified and on the mode of signifying.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A8","text":"The divine essence, as regards the mode of signifying, is signified as the form of the three persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","text":"The number of a substantive noun follows the signified form, whereas the number of an adjective follows the supposits to which the form is attributed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","text":"The concrete name God signifies the essence as existing in a possessor and thus can stand for the essence or, as determined by context, for one or more persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","text":"The abstract name essence signifies an abstract form and does not naturally have supposition for a person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A12","text":"Personal substantive names are predicated of the essence through real identity, not as inferiors of a universal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","text":"Essential attributes are known more certainly from creatures than personal properties, which cannot be proved by demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","text":"Appropriation is the manifestative attribution of a common essential attribute to a person, not the constitution of an exclusive property.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A15","text":"Appropriation manifests a person through likeness or through unlikeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0159","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","text":"Consideration of the creature provides four orders: being, unity, causal power, and relation to effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:A17","text":"The personal order distinguishes a principle not from a principle, a principle from a principle, and a nexus proceeding from two.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0183","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX1","text":"Essence and person are not two things in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX2","text":"The distinction of persons is not a multiplication or division of the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX3","text":"Divine relations are not accidents or things adjunct to the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX4","text":"The names supposit and hypostasis do not signify a real subordination of the person to the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX5","text":"Essential names taken substantively do not admit a plurality of gods or substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX6","text":"The three persons are not said to be from one essence or of one essence, because such a construction would insinuate a distinction of material or efficient cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX7","text":"Personal acts and properties are not attributed to the abstract name essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX8","text":"An appropriated attribute belongs neither to the appropriated person alone nor to that person more than to the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX9","text":"The Trinity of persons cannot be demonstrated from creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:NX10","text":"Essence and operation are not appropriated to persons, because their commonality affords no determinate likeness to personal properties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0182","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D1","text":"The unity of essence and the plurality of persons are simultaneously preserved, because relation is really the same according to essence, but really distinguishes the person according to opposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D2","text":"Different things can be affirmed or denied of essence and person without contradiction, because real identity does not remove distinction of reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D3","text":"The formula three persons of one essence is legitimate, because the genitive designates the essence under the aspect of form, not a cause distinct from the persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D4","text":"The unity of essence expresses divine unity more strictly than unity of nature, because essence signifies one being, whereas nature can also signify merely an agreement of operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D5","text":"Essential names taken substantively are predicated singularly of the three persons, but when taken adjectivally, plurally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D6","text":"The expression God begot God is true, because the concrete name can stand for the Father and the Son, while one numerically identical deity remains.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D7","text":"The expression essence begot essence is false, because the abstract name does not import a person and would signify generation within a distinct essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D8","text":"The expressions essence is three persons and God is the Trinity are true when the subject stands for the essence and predication occurs through identity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0145","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D9","text":"Appropriation can manifest persons without distributing essential attributes, because its function is epistemic, not constitutive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D10","text":"Under the aspect of being, eternity is appropriated to the Father, species to the Son, and use to the Holy Spirit, according to likenesses of the principle not principled, the perfect image, and love or gift.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A15","CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0180","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0181","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D11","text":"Under the aspect of unity, unity is appropriated to the Father, equality to the Son, and connection to the Holy Spirit, according to the order of absolute principle, relation to another, and nexus of two.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0182","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D12","text":"Under the aspect of causal power, power is appropriated to the Father, wisdom to the Son, and goodness to the Holy Spirit, according to likenesses of principle, word, and love, and through the removal of creaturely defects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A15","CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0184","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0185","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:D13","text":"Under the aspect of relation to effects, from whom is appropriated to the Father, through whom to the Son, and in whom to the Holy Spirit, according to efficiency, the formal principle of operation, and governing containment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0186","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0187","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD1","text":"The real identity of divine names does not effect universal substitutability, because the mode of signifying governs the scope of supposition and predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","CH_GGVC_P_31:D6","CH_GGVC_P_31:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD2","text":"One and three are not said of the same thing under the same aspect: unity pertains to essence, plurality to opposed relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5","CH_GGVC_P_31:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","text":"Theological grammar becomes an instrument of ontological preservation, because expressions are admitted or excluded according as they preserve the unity of essence or the distinction of relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD4","text":"The name God has a double structure: it is as though singular on account of the non-multiplied form, and as though common on account of the same form in several supposits.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD5","text":"Appropriation constitutes a mediation between natural knowledge of essential attributes and revealed knowledge of personal properties.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A15","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SD6","text":"The four modes of considering created being are converted into a Trinitarian matrix, not because they demonstrate the structure of the Trinity, but because they manifest the personal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17","CH_GGVC_P_31:D10","CH_GGVC_P_31:D11","CH_GGVC_P_31:D12","CH_GGVC_P_31:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX1","text":"It must be false that identity of the thing suffices for the substitution of names in every predicative context.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX2","text":"It must be false that every plurality of supposits requires a multiplication of form or nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the name God relates to the persons as a universal to created singulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A12","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX4","text":"It must be false that attribution of a common attribute to a person imports division, greater possession, or causality of the essential attribute.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX5","text":"It must be false that created modes of signifying constitute created compositions in God in reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:A8","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX1","text":"The mode of knowing and naming God according to the divine mode itself remains unavailable to the created intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX2","text":"No fourth thing between essence and persons is admitted that gathers unity together or receives plurality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX3","text":"Composition, substantial division, and causality of essence are precluded solutions to the apparent contradiction between one and three.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4","text":"From creatures no demonstrative path to personal properties is open; only analogical manifestation remains after the positing of faith.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0159","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS1","text":"Divine simplicity → real identity of essence and person → subsisting relation → opposition of relations → real distinction of persons without distinction of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS2","text":"Knowledge from creatures → created mode of signifying → distinction of substantive and adjective, and of concrete and abstract → determination of number, supposition, and predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:A8","CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS3","text":"Divine expression → examination of the thing signified → examination of the mode of signifying → determination of the supposit → admission if one essence and distinct personal relation are preserved → rejection if the essence is divided, generated, or causally separated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS4","text":"Indemonstrable personal properties + more manifest essential attributes → comparison through likeness or unlikeness → appropriation → manifestation of the person without conversion of the common into the proper.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:FGS5","text":"Being → eternity, species, use; unity → unity, equality, connection; power → potency, wisdom, goodness; effects → from whom, through whom, in whom; the individual triads are ordered to the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:A17","CH_GGVC_P_31:D10","CH_GGVC_P_31:D11","CH_GGVC_P_31:D12","CH_GGVC_P_31:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0182","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0184","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0186","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0187","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AF1","text":"Identity of essence and person → opposition of relations → unity of essence with three persons → rule of the number of essentials → supposition of the concrete → exclusion of the abstract → predication through identity → appropriation of common attributes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0143","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:AF2","text":"Ontological difficulty → relational resolution → translation into semantics → proof of singular expressions → distinction of proper and appropriated → ordering of four Trinitarian matrices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0143","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME1","text":"The opposition between one essence and three persons is resolved by distributing unity and plurality to different formal orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME2","text":"Divine plurality is transferred from essential principles to the oppositions of subsisting relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME3","text":"Grammatical number ceases to be a simple index of the number of things and is ordered differently according to substantive or adjective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME4","text":"The predication of essence and person outside the model of universal and singular is reclassified as predication through identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0147","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME5","text":"Appropriation is converted from an ontological distribution of attributes into an epistemic operation of manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ME6","text":"The four orders of consideration of the creature become a table ordering common attributes around personal properties without demonstrating the Trinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT1","text":"Surface — Expressions concerning one essence, three persons, one God, generation, and appropriation are admitted or excluded according to grammatical rules.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT2","text":"Structural — The identity of essence and relation together with the real opposition of relations constitutes the mechanism of substantial unity and personal distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Mode of signifying and supposition become instruments for preventing errors of division of the essence, polytheism, and confusion of persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Simple and eternal divine reality is presupposed, while the order of persons is arranged through relational origin, not through partition of the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore the composition of the ontology of relations, the semantics of names, and the doctrine of appropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT2","text":"The distinction of relations, personal processions, and divine simplicity are not fully proved here, but are assumed from prior questions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT3","text":"The rule of the mode of signifying is necessary, but its criterion remains contextual and is not reduced to a complete semantic calculus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT4","text":"The system coheres internally if real identity, distinction of reason, and relational opposition are strictly separated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT5","text":"The strongest joint is the resolution of the plurality of persons through opposed subsisting relations, while the essence remains numerically one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT6","text":"The weaker joint is the asymmetry by which God stands for essence or person, whereas essence can be predicated of person but cannot stand for person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT7","text":"The matrices of appropriation rest on selective likenesses, whose manifestative force is established, but whose necessity is not always univocally determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0186","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0187","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: it resolves the ontological question through relations, transfers the solution into rules of expression, and then extends them into an order of Trinitarian manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_31:P0179","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_31@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_31:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 40","title":"First Part · Question 39","context":"Chapter 40","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 39"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 39","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 40","order":41,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_32"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_32@R001","sha256":"b4fcf54d8ce96c87ad74b1899b242a49746f92e080979a78f27b70f34e26c56d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat utrum relationes divinae sint ipsae personae, utrum eas distinguant et constituant, utrum hypostases sine relationibus personalibus intelligi possint, et quem ordinem intelligibilem habeant respectu actuum notionalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS2","text":"Argumentatio ab unitate essentiae et simplicitate divina procedit ad identitatem realem relationis, essentiae et personae, servata differentia secundum modum significandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS3","text":"Relatio personalis non solum personam manifestat, sed ut relatio subsistens ipsam hypostasim distinguit et constituit; relatio autem non personalis cum pluribus personis communicari potest sine constitutione personae propriae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS4","text":"Cum essentia divina sit una et indivisa, distinctio personalis neque ex essentia neque ex aliquo absoluto oriri potest; ideo relatio sola principium distinctionis fit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS5","text":"Origo, quia significatur ut actus vel via a persona aut ad personam, non potest primum principium constitutivum hypostasis esse; relatio significata ut forma internam distinctionem praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS6","text":"Abstractio relationis personalis non relinquit hypostasim divinam distinctam, quia relatio personalis non advenit supposito praeexistenti, sed secum fert suppositum constitutum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS7","text":"Quaestio de prioritate solvitur per divisionem formalem: relatio ut relatio actum fundantem praesupponit, sed relatio ut constitutiva personae originantis actui ipsi praeintelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A1","text":"Simplicitas divina excludit compositionem formae et materiae atque subiecti et accidentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A2","text":"Quidquid realiter est in Deo est divina essentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","text":"Relatio, secundum quod res est in divinis, est ipsa essentia divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A4","text":"Essentia divina et persona divina sunt idem re.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","text":"Identitas realis in divinis compatitur differentiam secundum rationem et modum significandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A6","text":"Proprietas personalis significat relationem quae est ipsa persona subsistens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","text":"Relatio personalis distinguit et constituit hypostasim, quia hypostasis divina nihil praeter essentiam et relationem intelligibilem continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A8","text":"Proprietas non personalis est idem cum personis per identitatem essentiae, sed non est persona per se subsistens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A9","text":"Personae divinae conveniunt in essentia indivisa neque distinguuntur secundum esse absolutum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","text":"Origo significatur ut actus vel via a re aut ad rem, non ut principium intrinsecum quo res constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A11","text":"Relatio subsistens secum fert distinctionem correlativorum; relatio autem accidentalis distinctionem suppositorum praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A12","text":"Hypostasis divina significat substantiam individuam distinctam, cuius ratio distinctionis est relatio personalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A13","text":"Omnis hypostasis naturae rationalis est persona; hypostasis divina sine proprietate personali non manet ut hypostasis distincta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A14","text":"Prioritas secundum intellectum variatur secundum id quod relatio vel origo significat: actum, viam, relationem, vel personam constitutam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX1","text":"Relationes divinae non sunt assistentes extra personas neque merae denominationes loquendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX2","text":"Identitas relationis et personae non est identitas secundum omnem modum praedicationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX3","text":"Proprietas divina non est accidens in subiecto distincto, quamvis significetur ad modum formae in supposito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX4","text":"Essentia communis non dividitur ut ex eius partitione personae constituantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX5","text":"Personae divinae non distinguuntur seipsis secundum aliquod absolutum principium individuale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX6","text":"Origo sola non est principium primum distinctionis vel constitutionis hypostasis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX7","text":"Verba et participia notionalia non praedicantur de proprietatibus, quia actus sunt suppositorum, proprietates autem significantur ut formae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX8","text":"Remota relatione personali, non remanet hypostasis divina distincta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX9","text":"Innascibilitas, quia negative dicitur, non constituit neque distinguit hypostasim Patris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX10","text":"Nullus ordo simpliciter univocus inter omnes relationes et actus notionales admittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D1","text":"Paternitas est ipse Pater, filiatio est ipse Filius, et processio est ipse Spiritus Sanctus, quia proprietates personales sunt relationes subsistentes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A1","CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","CH_GGVC_P_32:A4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D2","text":"Spiratio communis potest esse eadem realiter cum Patre et Filio sine eo quod sit una persona subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A2","CH_GGVC_P_32:A4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D3","text":"Multiplicatio relationum in una persona vel communicatio unius relationis pluribus personis non destruit identitatem realem relationis et personae, quia numeratio sequitur modos significandi, non solam identitatem realem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_32:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D4","text":"Proprietates determinant et distinguunt personas, non essentiam, quia in essentia sunt per identitatem realem, in personis autem etiam secundum modum formae in supposito.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D5","text":"Distinctio personalis est distinctio minima et unitati divinae propinquissima, quia sola relatio distinguit sine divisione essentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:A9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D6","text":"Origo potest distinctionem manifestare, sed non eam primitus efficere, quia originans et originatum iam exigunt terminos quos sola relatio intrinsece distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_32:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D7","text":"Abstractio universalitatis a proprietatibus personalibus relinquit essentiam communem, non hypostasim Patris, Filii vel Spiritus Sancti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A12","CH_GGVC_P_32:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D8","text":"Abstractio proprietatum non personalium a persona non destruit intellectum hypostasis, quia tales proprietates non constituunt personam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A8","CH_GGVC_P_32:A12","CH_GGVC_P_32:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D9","text":"Paternitas ut relatio generationem praesupponit, sed paternitas ut persona Patris constituta generationem activam praecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A6","CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_32:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D10","text":"Nativitas, quia est via ad personam Filii, filiationem etiam constitutivam secundum intellectum praecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_32:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD1","text":"Pluralitas Trinitatis non est pluralitas essentiarum, substantiarum absolutarum, vel partium divini esse, sed pluralitas relationum subsistentium intra essentiam unam indivisam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD2","text":"Persona divina non est essentia prius individuata cui relatio postea accidat, sed ipsa essentia subsistens sub ratione relationis personaliter distinctivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD3","text":"Eadem res divina potest esse simul fundamentum unitatis essentialis et ratio distinctionis personalis, quia identitas realis non tollit pluralitatem formalium modorum significandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","text":"Argumentatio semantica de praedicatione, inesse, multiplicari et agere non est exterior doctrinae ornamentum, sed instrumentum quo identitas realis a confusione rationum significandi custoditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD5","text":"Relatio divina non sub eadem ratione ponitur ante et post actum notionalem; duplex ordo intelligibilis impedit ut circulus inter personam, relationem et actionem simpliciter statuatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX1","text":"Systema negat substratum hypostaticum prae-relationale quod post remotionem paternitatis, filiationis vel processionis manere posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX2","text":"Systema negat principium individuationis divinum ex materia, forma absoluta, accidente, vel differentia essentiali derivari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX3","text":"Systema negat relationem subsistentem explicari posse per exemplar relationis creaturae accidentaliter fundatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX4","text":"Systema negat originem posse personam originantem constituere, quia actus originans supponit personam a qua procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX5","text":"Systema negat negationem originis, ut innascibilitatem, vicem gerere posse relationis positivae et constitutivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX6","text":"Systema negat distinctionem divinam per unam regulam prioritatis explicari posse, quia actus, origo, relatio et persona diversis rationibus intelliguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX1","text":"Impossibilis est pluralitas personarum quae vel unitatem essentiae dividat vel eam tamquam commune genus super individua absoluta disponat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX2","text":"Impossibilis est persona divina quae sit primum quid absolutum et relationem habeat tantum ut proprietatem secundariam vel dignitatem additam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX3","text":"Impossibile est personam divinam intelligere sine correlativo, quia relatio subsistens non solum ad aliud refertur, sed simul distinctionem correlativorum fert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX4","text":"Impossibilis est reductio mysterii personalis ad nudam negationem, originem sine termino constituto, vel essentiam sine distinctione relativa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS1","text":"Essentia una et communis + pluralitas personarum data → necessitas principii distinctionis quod essentiam non dividat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS2","text":"Exclusio materiae, accidentis et differentiae absolutae → exclusio omnium principiorum distinctionis non relationalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS3","text":"Relatio ut res divina = essentia; essentia = persona → relatio realiter idem est cum persona.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS4","text":"Relatio personalis ut forma subsistens → constitutio et distinctio hypostasis; relatio communis ut essentiae participatio → identitas cum pluribus personis sine persona propria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS5","text":"Relatio personalis sublata per intellectum → sublata ratio hypostasis distinctae; proprietas non personalis sublata → hypostasis intelligibiliter manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS6","text":"Relatio ut relatio fundata in actu → actus prior; relatio ut persona constituens agentem → persona relativa prior actui; origo passiva ut via ad personam → origo prior persona procedente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AF1","text":"Identitas relationis et personae apparenter negata per differentias praedicationis → distinctio rei et rationis → identitas realis salva differentia significandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AF2","text":"Unitas essentiae communis → quaesitio distinctionis intrinsecae → exclusio originis ut principii primi → relatio subsistens ut principium distinctionis et constitutionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AF3","text":"Abstractio proprietatis personalis → examinatio residui hypostatici → remanet essentia communis, non persona vel hypostasis distincta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AF4","text":"Apparens prioritas actus super relationem → divisio relationis ut relatio et ut constitutiva personae → ordo intelligibilis multiplex et non contradictorius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0077","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME1","text":"Relatio reclassificatur ab accidente vel signo exteriori ad modum subsistentiae personalis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME2","text":"Distinctio inter proprietatem personalem et non personalem fit decisiva: prima personam constituit, altera essentiam communem in pluribus personis significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter unitatem essentiae et pluralitatem personarum dissolvitur, quia unitas ad essentiam, pluralitas ad relationes subsistentes refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME4","text":"Origo et relatio distinguuntur ut via sive actus et forma sive constitutivum, ita ut eadem realitas sub diversis rationibus diversa munera argumentativa habeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME5","text":"Abstractio intelligibilis dividitur in abstractionem quae commune relinquit et particulare tollit, atque abstractionem quae formas non constitutivas separare potest sine sublatione suppositi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME6","text":"Prioritas in divinis reordinatur non ut successio simplex, sed ut ordo secundum rationem rei significatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus determinat quomodo relationes, proprietates, hypostases, personae et actus notionales de divinis dicenda sint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT2","text":"Structural — Simplicitas divina prohibet compositionem et distinctionem absolutam, ideo relatio subsistens unicum principium personale distinctionis efficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur per separationem identitatis realis a modo significandi, ne regulae praedicationis creaturalis directe ad divina transferantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Personae non habent successionem constitutivam ex actibus, sed ordines intelligibiles diversos secundum relationem, originem activam, originem passivam et suppositum agens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de simplicitate, identitate essentiae et relationis, differentia secundum rationem, atque constitutione hypostasis per relationem sufficiunt ad conclusionem principalem de relationibus personalibus restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT2","text":"Ratio distinctionis personalis firmissime consistit in coniunctione essentiae indivisae cum necessitate principii distinctivi intrinseci, quod non potest esse absolutum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT3","text":"Commissura principalis systematis est transitus a relatione divina ut essentia ad relationem ut forma in supposito, qui per modum significandi explicatur sine introductione compositionis realis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT4","text":"Tensio ordinativa manet inter relationem quae ut relatio actum fundantem praesupponit et eandem relationem quae ut constitutiva personae actum originantem praecedit; textus eam per distinctionem rationum significandi ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT5","text":"Negatio originis ut principii constitutivi est cohaerens tantum si origo stricte retinetur ut via inter terminos et relatio ut principium intrinsecum terminorum distinctivum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, si identitas realis, distinctio rationalis, constitutio relationalis, impossibilitas hypostasis prae-relationalis, et pluralitas ordinum intelligibilium simul retinentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161146511696Z_9ec819dd","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 40","source_sha256":"b4fcf54d8ce96c87ad74b1899b242a49746f92e080979a78f27b70f34e26c56d","sha256":"5fba38b574ddb1dbeac6cda4c16f9e0128dc87005474916bde83e3014b88332c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:11:46.512747+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS1","text":"The question examines whether the divine relations are the persons themselves, whether they distinguish and constitute them, whether hypostases can be understood without personal relations, and what intelligible order they have with respect to notional acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS2","text":"The argument proceeds from the unity of essence and divine simplicity to the real identity of relation, essence, and person, while preserving the difference according to mode of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS3","text":"A personal relation not only manifests the person, but, as a subsisting relation, distinguishes and constitutes the hypostasis itself; a non-personal relation, however, can be shared with several persons without constituting a proper person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS4","text":"Since the divine essence is one and undivided, personal distinction can arise neither from essence nor from anything absolute; therefore relation alone becomes the principle of distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS5","text":"Origin, because it is signified as an act or way from a person or toward a person, cannot be the first constitutive principle of a hypostasis; relation, signified as a form, provides intrinsic distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS6","text":"The abstraction of a personal relation does not leave a distinct divine hypostasis, because a personal relation does not accrue to a pre-existing suppositum, but carries with itself the constituted suppositum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AS7","text":"The question of priority is resolved through a formal division: relation as relation presupposes the founding act, but relation as constitutive of the originating person is understood prior to the act itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A1","text":"Divine simplicity excludes composition of form and matter, and of subject and accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A2","text":"Whatever is really in God is the divine essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","text":"Relation, insofar as it is a thing in the divine, is the divine essence itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A4","text":"The divine essence and the divine person are the same in reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","text":"Real identity in the divine is compatible with difference according to notion and mode of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A6","text":"A personal property signifies a relation that is the subsisting person itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","text":"A personal relation distinguishes and constitutes the hypostasis, because a divine hypostasis contains nothing beyond essence and intelligible relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A8","text":"A non-personal property is the same as the persons through identity of essence, but is not a person subsisting through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A9","text":"The divine persons agree in undivided essence and are not distinguished according to absolute being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","text":"Origin is signified as an act or way from a thing or toward a thing, not as an intrinsic principle by which a thing is constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A11","text":"A subsisting relation carries with itself the distinction of correlatives; an accidental relation, however, presupposes the distinction of supposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A12","text":"A divine hypostasis signifies a distinct individual substance, whose principle of distinction is personal relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A13","text":"Every hypostasis of rational nature is a person; a divine hypostasis without a personal property does not remain as a distinct hypostasis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:A14","text":"Priority according to understanding varies according to what relation or origin signifies: act, way, relation, or constituted person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX1","text":"Divine relations are not adjuncts external to the persons, nor mere denominations of speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX2","text":"The identity of relation and person is not identity according to every mode of predication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX3","text":"A divine property is not an accident in a distinct subject, although it is signified in the manner of a form in a suppositum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX4","text":"The common essence is not divided such that persons are constituted from its partition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX5","text":"The divine persons are not distinguished by themselves according to any absolute individual principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX6","text":"Origin alone is not the first principle of the distinction or constitution of a hypostasis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX7","text":"Notional verbs and participles are not predicated of properties, because acts belong to supposita, whereas properties are signified as forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX8","text":"With personal relation removed, no distinct divine hypostasis remains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX9","text":"Unbegottenness, because it is stated negatively, neither constitutes nor distinguishes the hypostasis of the Father.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:NX10","text":"No simply univocal order among all relations and notional acts is admitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D1","text":"Paternity is the Father himself, filiation is the Son himself, and procession is the Holy Spirit himself, because personal properties are subsisting relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A1","CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","CH_GGVC_P_32:A4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D2","text":"Common spiration can be really the same as the Father and the Son without being one subsisting person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A2","CH_GGVC_P_32:A4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D3","text":"The multiplication of relations in one person or the communication of one relation to several persons does not destroy the real identity of relation and person, because enumeration follows modes of signification, not real identity alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_32:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D4","text":"Properties determine and distinguish persons, not essence, because in essence they are through real identity, whereas in persons they are also according to the mode of a form in a suppositum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D5","text":"Personal distinction is the least distinction and the closest to divine unity, because relation alone distinguishes without division of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:A9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D6","text":"Origin can manifest distinction, but cannot primarily effect it, because the originator and the originated already require terms that relation alone intrinsically distinguishes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_32:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D7","text":"The abstraction of universality from personal properties leaves the common essence, not the hypostasis of the Father, Son, or Holy Spirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A12","CH_GGVC_P_32:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D8","text":"The abstraction of non-personal properties from a person does not destroy the understanding of hypostasis, because such properties do not constitute the person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A8","CH_GGVC_P_32:A12","CH_GGVC_P_32:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D9","text":"Paternity as relation presupposes generation, but paternity as the constituted person of the Father precedes active generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A6","CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_32:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:D10","text":"Nativity, because it is a way toward the person of the Son, precedes even constitutive filiation according to understanding.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_32:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD1","text":"The plurality of the Trinity is not a plurality of essences, absolute substances, or parts of divine being, but a plurality of subsisting relations within one undivided essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD2","text":"A divine person is not an essence first individuated to which relation subsequently accrues, but the essence itself subsisting under the notion of a personally distinctive relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD3","text":"The same divine reality can simultaneously be the foundation of essential unity and the principle of personal distinction, because real identity does not remove a plurality of formal modes of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","text":"Semantic argumentation concerning predication, inherence, multiplication, and acting is not an external ornament of doctrine, but the instrument by which real identity is preserved from confusion of notions of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SD5","text":"Divine relation is not posited under the same notion before and after the notional act; a twofold intelligible order prevents a simple circle between person, relation, and action from being established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX1","text":"The system denies a pre-relational hypostatic substrate that could remain after the removal of paternity, filiation, or procession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX2","text":"The system denies that a divine principle of individuation is derived from matter, absolute form, accident, or essential difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX3","text":"The system denies that a subsisting relation can be explained through the model of a creaturely relation founded accidentally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX4","text":"The system denies that origin can constitute the originating person, because the originating act presupposes the person from whom it proceeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX5","text":"The system denies that the negation of origin, such as unbegottenness, can take the place of a positive and constitutive relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX6","text":"The system denies that divine distinction can be explained through one rule of priority, because act, origin, relation, and person are understood according to diverse notions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX1","text":"Impossible is a plurality of persons that either divides the unity of essence or disposes it as a common genus over absolute individuals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX2","text":"Impossible is a divine person that is first an absolute something and has relation only as a secondary property or added dignity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX3","text":"It is impossible to understand a divine person without a correlative, because a subsisting relation not only refers to another, but simultaneously carries the distinction of correlatives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX4","text":"Impossible is the reduction of the personal mystery to bare negation, origin without a constituted term, or essence without relative distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS1","text":"One common essence + a given plurality of persons → necessity of a principle of distinction that does not divide essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS2","text":"Exclusion of matter, accident, and absolute difference → exclusion of all non-relational principles of distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS3","text":"Relation as divine reality = essence; essence = person → relation is really the same as person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS4","text":"Personal relation as subsisting form → constitution and distinction of hypostasis; common relation as participation in essence → identity with several persons without a proper person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS5","text":"Personal relation removed by understanding → the notion of distinct hypostasis removed; non-personal property removed → hypostasis remains intelligibly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS6","text":"Relation as relation founded in act → act prior; relation as person constituting the agent → relative person prior to act; passive origin as way toward person → origin prior to the person proceeding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AF1","text":"Identity of relation and person apparently denied by differences of predication → distinction of reality and notion → real identity preserved with difference of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AF2","text":"Unity of common essence → inquiry into intrinsic distinction → exclusion of origin as first principle → subsisting relation as principle of distinction and constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AF3","text":"Abstraction of personal property → examination of the hypostatic remainder → common essence remains, not a distinct person or hypostasis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:AF4","text":"Apparent priority of act over relation → division of relation as relation and as constitutive of person → a multiple and non-contradictory intelligible order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0077","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME1","text":"Relation is reclassified from an accident or external sign to a mode of divine personal subsistence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME2","text":"The distinction between personal and non-personal property becomes decisive: the former constitutes the person, the latter signifies the common essence in several persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME3","text":"The opposition between unity of essence and plurality of persons is dissolved, because unity is referred to essence and plurality to subsisting relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME4","text":"Origin and relation are distinguished as way or act and form or constitutive, such that the same reality has different argumentative functions under diverse notions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME5","text":"Intelligible abstraction is divided into abstraction that leaves the common and removes the particular, and abstraction that can separate non-constitutive forms without removal of the suppositum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ME6","text":"Priority in the divine is reordered not as simple succession, but as an order according to the notion of the thing signified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines how relations, properties, hypostases, persons, and notional acts are to be spoken of concerning the divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT2","text":"Structural — Divine simplicity prohibits composition and absolute distinction; therefore subsisting relation becomes the sole personal principle of distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved by separating real identity from mode of signification, lest rules of creaturely predication be transferred directly to the divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The persons do not have constitutive succession from acts, but diverse intelligible orders according to relation, active origin, passive origin, and the acting suppositum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning simplicity, the identity of essence and relation, difference according to notion, and the constitution of hypostasis through relation suffice for reconstructing the principal conclusion concerning personal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT2","text":"The basis of personal distinction rests most firmly in the conjunction of undivided essence with the necessity of an intrinsic distinctive principle, which cannot be absolute.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT3","text":"The principal juncture of the system is the transition from divine relation as essence to relation as form in a suppositum, which is explained through mode of signification without introducing real composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT4","text":"An ordering tension remains between relation which, as relation, presupposes the founding act and the same relation which, as constitutive of person, precedes the originating act; the text orders it through the distinction of notions of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT5","text":"The denial of origin as a constitutive principle is coherent only if origin is strictly retained as a way between terms and relation as the intrinsic principle distinguishing the terms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if real identity, rational distinction, relational constitution, the impossibility of a pre-relational hypostasis, and the plurality of intelligible orders are retained together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_32:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_32@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_32:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 41","title":"First Part · Question 40","context":"Chapter 41","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 40"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 40","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 41","order":42,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_33"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_33@R001","sha256":"41f9ce211f669e2754b26a51b2df56013733740fcc0dea07ebdb572dd817dd30","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quomodo actus originis personis divinis attribuantur sine mutatione, passione vel compositione divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS2","text":"Eadem inquisitio examinat causalitatem, necessitatem, terminum substantialem, potentiam et numerum terminorum actuum notionalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS3","text":"Actus notionales ad originem personalem significandam requiruntur, quamvis relationibus personalibus secundum rem identificentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS4","text":"Processiones divinae naturales et per se necessariae sunt, non productiones voluntariae rerum quae aliter esse possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS5","text":"Generatio communicat totam naturam consubstantialem, dum potentia generandi essentiam directe et relationem personalem indirecte significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6","text":"Argumentatio a purificatione praedicationis actionis progreditur ad distinctionem generationis a creatione, deinde ad potentiam et clausuram numeri personarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A1","text":"Personae divinae relationibus originis distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A2","text":"Omnis origo per aliquem actum designatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A3","text":"Actiones designantes processum creaturae sunt essentiales, actiones autem designantes processum personae a persona sunt notionales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A4","text":"Actus notionalis et relatio personalis idem sunt secundum rem, sed differunt secundum modum significandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A5","text":"Remoto motu, actio notionalis solum ordinem originis importat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","text":"Natura est principium eius quod aliter esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A7","text":"Voluntas, ut principium productivum, est principium eius quod aliter esse potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A8","text":"Intellectio et amor quibus Deus seipsum intelligit et amat naturales sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A9","text":"Voluntas Patris generationi Filii concomitatur, sed eam non principiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A10","text":"Generatio Filii est necessaria per se, non per coactionem neque propter finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A11","text":"Vera filiatio generationem de principio consubstantiali requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","text":"Natura divina tota et indivisa genito communicatur sine transmutatione vel partitione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A13","text":"Communicata eadem natura, distinctio personarum sola origine manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A14","text":"Potentia activa significat id quo agens agit tamquam principium actus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A15","text":"Principium actus notionalis potentiam respectu personae procedentis fundat, quamvis persona procedens non fiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A16","text":"Potentia generandi divinam essentiam in recto et relationem personalem in obliquo significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","text":"Relationes subsistentes eiusdem rationis sine distinctione materiali multiplicari non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A18","text":"Deus omnia uno et simplici actu intelligit et vult.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX1","text":"Praedicatio actionis de Deo non ideo semper ad essentiam pertinet quod actio genus praedicamentale sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX2","text":"Actus notionalis non est res tertia praeter substantiam et relationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX3","text":"Actio notionalis motum, passionem realem et mutationem excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX4","text":"Voluntas non est principium productivum generationis Filii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX5","text":"Naturalis necessitas generationis neque coactionem neque voluntatem contrariam importat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX6","text":"Filius non est factus, creatus ex nihilo vel metaphorice tantum filius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX7","text":"Generatio de substantia Patris principium materiale, divisionem substantiae et transmutationem excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX8","text":"Essentia divina non generat tamquam suppositum generans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX9","text":"Potentia notionalis neque potentia passiva neque possibilitas necessario opposita est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX10","text":"Potentia generandi non significat principaliter relationem personalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX11","text":"Unus actus notionalis eiusdem modi ad plures personas procedentes non terminatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX12","text":"Unicitas Filii et Spiritus Sancti non provenit ex impotentia principii producentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D1","text":"Distinctio personalis nequit intelligibiliter exprimi nisi personis actus notionales attribuantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A1","CH_GGVC_P_33:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D2","text":"Eadem vox actionis essentialiter vel notionaliter praedicatur secundum terminum processionis ad extra vel ad intra.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A3","CH_GGVC_P_33:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D3","text":"Actus notionales relationes originis sub forma actionis significant, non accidentia aut eventus motus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A4","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D4","text":"Pater vult se Filium generare, sed Filium natura potius quam voluntate ut principio producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A7","CH_GGVC_P_33:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D5","text":"Processio per modum intellectus vel voluntatis naturalis manet quando Deus naturaliter seipsum intelligit vel amat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D6","text":"Generatio divina est necessaria ut non potens non esse, sed non necessaria ut violenta, coacta vel fini subordinata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D7","text":"Filius de substantia Patris genitus est, quia processio ex nihilo factionem constitueret et veram filiationem tolleret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A11","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D8","text":"Praepositio de in generatione divina principium consubstantiale, non materiam, significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A11","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D9","text":"Pater generat per naturam divinam tamquam principium quo, non per paternitatem neque per essentiam tamquam suppositum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A14","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D10","text":"Potentia notionalis cum necessitate processionis compatitur, quia principium actus significat potius quam indifferentiam ad opposita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A10","CH_GGVC_P_33:A14","CH_GGVC_P_33:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D11","text":"Potentia secundum essentiam tribus personis communis est, sed potentia generandi active sumpta Patri propria est propter relationem connotatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A13","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D12","text":"Unicitas Filii et Spiritus Sancti sequitur ex immaterialitate relationum subsistentium, simplicitate actuum divinorum et determinatione naturae ad unum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","CH_GGVC_P_33:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD1","text":"Praedicatio actionis de Deo salvatur per purificationem motus et passionis, non per abrogationem ordinis originis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D1","CH_GGVC_P_33:D2","CH_GGVC_P_33:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2","text":"Libertas divina a coactione non requirit contingentiam intradivinam neque electionem inter generationem et non-generationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D4","CH_GGVC_P_33:D5","CH_GGVC_P_33:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD3","text":"Fecunditas intradivina non producit alteram naturam, sed eandem naturam totam secundum distinctum ordinem originis communicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D7","CH_GGVC_P_33:D8","CH_GGVC_P_33:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD4","text":"Potentia divina perfectionem principii iam actu operantis significat, non capacitatem nondum impletam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D9","CH_GGVC_P_33:D10","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD5","text":"Communitas essentiae et incommunicabilitas relationis simul impediunt et divisionem naturae et permutationem munerum personalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D9","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD6","text":"Numerus personarum non augetur per maiorem potentiam, quia perfectio processionis terminum unicum potius quam pluralitatem effectuum exigit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D10","CH_GGVC_P_33:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX1","text":"Praedicamenta ex rebus sensibilibus accepta de Deo univoce transferri non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX2","text":"Identitas secundum rem identitatem rationis et modi significandi non requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX3","text":"Libertas non necessario consistit in indifferentia ad opposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX4","text":"Causalitas originis non requirit productionem rei essentialiter alienae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX5","text":"Potentia perfecta carentiam actus, futuritionem vel mutabilitatem non implicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX6","text":"Communitas essentiae permutationem relationum personalium non inducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX7","text":"Pluralitas numerica formarum immaterialium sine principio individuationis materiali admitti non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX8","text":"Maior numerus productorum maiorem perfectionem principii producentis non demonstrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX1","text":"Processio divina nullum ante et post, transitum vel intervallum temporale recipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX2","text":"In Deo nulla possibilitas notionalis remanet quae actu non sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX3","text":"In communicatione naturae divinae nullum substratum externum, residuum non communicatum vel pars translata datur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX4","text":"Personae divinae non sunt subiecta quibus actiones et relationes tamquam accidentia adveniunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX5","text":"Nulla processio eiusdem modi terminum personalem additum ultra unicum Verbum et unicum Amorem admittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS1","text":"Distinctio personalis → relatio originis → necessitas actus originem significantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS2","text":"Actio sensibilis − motus − passio → ordo originis → identitas realis cum relatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS3","text":"Processio ad extra → communitas tribus personis → actio essentialis; processio ad intra → distinctio personarum → actio notionalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS4","text":"Effectus aliter possibilis → voluntas ut principium → creatio; terminus aliter impossibilis → natura ut principium → generatio vel processio naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS5","text":"Vera filiatio → principium consubstantiale → communicatio totius naturae → distinctio sola origine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS6","text":"Actus → principium quo → potentia → essentia in recto et relatio in obliquo → communitas essentialis cum proprietate personali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS7","text":"Immaterialitas relationis subsistentis + simplicitas intellectionis et voluntatis + determinatio naturae ad unum → unus Filius et unus Spiritus Sanctus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AF1","text":"Suspecta praedicatio actionis → origo personalis tamquam explanandum → actus purificatus in relationem → distinctio naturae et voluntatis → distinctio generationis et creationis → potentia ut principium quo → coordinatio essentiae et relationis → unicitas terminorum processionalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME1","text":"Actio divina ex categoria eventus mutabilis in signum relationis originis reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME2","text":"Oppositio voluntarii et necessarii dissolvitur per distinctionem concomitantiae, principii productivi, necessitatis per se et coactionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME3","text":"Generatio et creatio non amplius ut gradus eiusdem productionis, sed ut consubstantialitas et productio ex nihilo distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4","text":"Potentia ex possibilitate ad opposita in principium quo actus reordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME5","text":"Communitas essentiae et proprietas personalis per distinctionem significationis rectae et obliquae simul cogitari possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME6","text":"Unicitas personae procedentis ex limitatione potentiae in effectum immaterialitatis, simplicitatis et perfectionis convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7","text":"Discrimen inter identitatem realem et diversitatem rationis fit instrumentum generale ad simplicitatem divinam cum distinctione personali conciliandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT1","text":"Surface — Sex decisiones statuuntur de attributione, modalitate, principio substantiali, existentia, significatione et termino actuum notionalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT2","text":"Structural — Relationes originis, communicatio naturae et principium quo structuram internam processionum constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Distinctiones inter naturam et voluntatem, generationem et creationem, essentiam et relationem conclusionem Arianam sine negatione actionis divinae excludunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Systema realitatem simplicem, immutabilem, necessario actualem et temporaliter non successivam praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad sex articulorum conclusiones conditionaliter restituendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT2","text":"Restitutio doctrinis antecedentibus de relationibus subsistentibus, simplicitate divina et duobus modis processionis dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT3","text":"Firmissima commissura est reductio actionis sine motu ad ordinem originis et distinctio generationis consubstantialis a creatione ex nihilo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT4","text":"Cohaerentia interna maxime distinctione inter identitatem realem et diversitatem modi significandi sustentatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT5","text":"Communitas potentiae essentialis et exclusio actus generativi a Filio tensionem relinquunt quae distinctione inter rectum, obliquum et adiunctum notionale continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0124","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT6","text":"Probatio unicitatis principiis de individuatione materiali et determinatione naturae ad unum nititur, quae in hac quaestione non denuo demonstrantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT7","text":"Argumentum ab identitate esse et posse ad exclusionem plurium filiorum circulare videretur, nisi rationibus independentibus ex relatione, processione et immaterialitate compleretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT8","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: a licentia praedicationis notionalis ad purificationem causalitatis, deinde ad significationem potentiae et clausuram numeri personarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161213015946Z_c7c782dd","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 41","source_sha256":"41f9ce211f669e2754b26a51b2df56013733740fcc0dea07ebdb572dd817dd30","sha256":"a059051c5c964a4e0fd254b6b9fe3fe295e341b5008888a51641973a3f681d2f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:12:13.018022+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS1","text":"The question determines how acts of origin are attributed to the divine persons without divine change, passivity, or composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS2","text":"The same inquiry examines causality, necessity, substantial terminus, power, and the number of termini of notional acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS3","text":"Notional acts are required to signify personal origin, although they are identical in reality with personal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS4","text":"Divine processions are natural and necessary through themselves, not voluntary productions of things that can be otherwise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS5","text":"Generation communicates the whole consubstantial nature, whereas the power of generating signifies essence directly and personal relation indirectly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6","text":"The argument proceeds from the purification of the predication of action to the distinction of generation from creation, then to power and the closure of the number of persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A1","text":"The divine persons are distinguished by relations of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A2","text":"Every origin is designated through some act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A3","text":"Actions designating the procession of a creature are essential, whereas actions designating the procession of a person from a person are notional.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A4","text":"A notional act and a personal relation are the same in reality, but differ according to the mode of signifying.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A5","text":"Once motion is removed, a notional action imports only an order of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","text":"Nature is the principle of that which cannot be otherwise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A7","text":"Will, as a productive principle, is the principle of that which can be otherwise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A8","text":"The understanding and love by which God understands and loves Himself are natural.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A9","text":"The will of the Father accompanies the generation of the Son, but does not originate it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A10","text":"The generation of the Son is necessary through itself, not through coercion nor for the sake of an end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A11","text":"True filiation requires generation from a consubstantial principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","text":"The divine nature, whole and undivided, is communicated to the begotten without transmutation or division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A13","text":"Once the same nature is communicated, the distinction of persons remains by origin alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A14","text":"Active power signifies that by which an agent acts as the principle of an act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A15","text":"The principle of a notional act grounds a power with respect to the proceeding person, although the proceeding person is not made.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A16","text":"The power of generating signifies the divine essence directly and the personal relation indirectly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","text":"Subsisting relations of the same account cannot be multiplied without material distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:A18","text":"God understands and wills all things by one simple act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX1","text":"The predication of action concerning God does not therefore always pertain to the essence because action is a predicamental genus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX2","text":"A notional act is not a third thing besides substance and relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX3","text":"Notional action excludes motion, real passivity, and change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX4","text":"Will is not the productive principle of the generation of the Son.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX5","text":"The natural necessity of generation imports neither coercion nor a contrary will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX6","text":"The Son is not made, created from nothing, or Son merely metaphorically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX7","text":"Generation from the substance of the Father excludes a material principle, division of substance, and transmutation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX8","text":"The divine essence does not generate as a generating suppositum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX9","text":"Notional power is neither passive power nor possibility opposed to necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX10","text":"The power of generating does not principally signify the personal relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX11","text":"One notional act of the same mode does not terminate in several proceeding persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:NX12","text":"The uniqueness of the Son and the Holy Spirit does not arise from the impotence of the productive principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D1","text":"Personal distinction cannot be intelligibly expressed unless notional acts are attributed to the persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A1","CH_GGVC_P_33:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D2","text":"The same term for action is predicated essentially or notionally according to whether the terminus of procession is ad extra or ad intra.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A3","CH_GGVC_P_33:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D3","text":"Notional acts signify relations of origin under the form of action, not accidents or events of motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A4","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D4","text":"The Father wills Himself to generate the Son, but produces the Son by nature rather than by will as principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A7","CH_GGVC_P_33:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D5","text":"Procession through the mode of intellect or natural will remains natural when God naturally understands or loves Himself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D6","text":"Divine generation is necessary as unable not to be, but not necessary as violent, coerced, or subordinated to an end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D7","text":"The Son is begotten from the substance of the Father, because procession from nothing would constitute making and remove true filiation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A11","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D8","text":"The preposition de in divine generation signifies a consubstantial principle, not matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A11","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D9","text":"The Father generates through the divine nature as the principle by which, not through paternity nor through essence as suppositum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A14","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D10","text":"Notional power is compatible with the necessity of procession, because it signifies the principle of act rather than indifference to opposites.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A10","CH_GGVC_P_33:A14","CH_GGVC_P_33:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D11","text":"Power according to essence is common to the three persons, but the power of generating, taken actively, is proper to the Father on account of the connoted relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A13","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:D12","text":"The uniqueness of the Son and the Holy Spirit follows from the immateriality of subsisting relations, the simplicity of divine acts, and the determination of nature to one.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","CH_GGVC_P_33:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD1","text":"The predication of action concerning God is preserved by purifying motion and passivity, not by abolishing the order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D1","CH_GGVC_P_33:D2","CH_GGVC_P_33:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2","text":"Divine freedom from coercion does not require intradivine contingency or a choice between generation and non-generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D4","CH_GGVC_P_33:D5","CH_GGVC_P_33:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD3","text":"Intradivine fecundity does not produce another nature, but communicates the same whole nature according to a distinct order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D7","CH_GGVC_P_33:D8","CH_GGVC_P_33:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD4","text":"Divine power signifies the perfection of a principle already operating in act, not a capacity not yet fulfilled.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D9","CH_GGVC_P_33:D10","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD5","text":"Community of essence and incommunicability of relation together prevent both division of nature and interchange of personal offices.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D9","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SD6","text":"The number of persons is not increased through greater power, because the perfection of procession requires a single terminus rather than a plurality of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D10","CH_GGVC_P_33:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX1","text":"Predicaments taken from sensible things cannot be transferred univocally to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX2","text":"Identity in reality does not require identity of account and mode of signifying.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX3","text":"Freedom does not necessarily consist in indifference to opposites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX4","text":"Causality of origin does not require the production of a thing essentially alien.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX5","text":"Perfect power does not imply privation of act, futurity, or mutability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX6","text":"Community of essence does not induce interchangeability of personal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX7","text":"Numerical plurality of immaterial forms without a material principle of individuation cannot be admitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX8","text":"A greater number of products does not demonstrate greater perfection of the productive principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX1","text":"Divine procession admits no before and after, transition, or temporal interval.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX2","text":"In God no notional possibility remains that is not in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX3","text":"In the communication of the divine nature there is no external substratum, uncommunicated remainder, or transferred part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX4","text":"The divine persons are not subjects to which actions and relations accrue as accidents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX5","text":"No procession of the same mode admits an additional personal terminus beyond the one Word and the one Love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS1","text":"Personal distinction → relation of origin → necessity of an act signifying origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS2","text":"Sensible action − motion − passivity → order of origin → real identity with relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS3","text":"Procession ad extra → community to the three persons → essential action; procession ad intra → distinction of persons → notional action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS4","text":"Effect possibly otherwise → will as principle → creation; terminus impossibly otherwise → nature as principle → generation or natural procession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS5","text":"True filiation → consubstantial principle → communication of the whole nature → distinction by origin alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS6","text":"Act → principle by which → power → essence directly and relation indirectly → essential community with personal property.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:FGS7","text":"Immateriality of subsisting relation + simplicity of understanding and will + determination of nature to one → one Son and one Holy Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:AF1","text":"Suspect predication of action → personal origin as that to be explained → act purified into relation → distinction of nature and will → distinction of generation and creation → power as principle by which → coordination of essence and relation → uniqueness of processional termini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME1","text":"Divine action is reclassified from the category of mutable event into a sign of the relation of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME2","text":"The opposition of voluntary and necessary is dissolved through the distinction of accompaniment, productive principle, necessity through itself, and coercion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME3","text":"Generation and creation are no longer distinguished as grades of the same production, but as consubstantiality and production from nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4","text":"Power is reordered from possibility toward opposites into the principle by which of act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME5","text":"Community of essence and personal property can be conceived together through the distinction of direct and indirect signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME6","text":"The uniqueness of the proceeding person is converted from a limitation of power into an effect of immateriality, simplicity, and perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7","text":"The distinction between real identity and diversity of account becomes a general instrument for reconciling divine simplicity with personal distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT1","text":"Surface — Six decisions are established concerning the attribution, modality, substantial principle, existence, signification, and terminus of notional acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT2","text":"Structural — Relations of origin, communication of nature, and the principle by which constitute the internal structure of processions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Distinctions between nature and will, generation and creation, essence and relation exclude the Arian conclusion without denying divine action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The system presupposes a simple, immutable, necessarily actual, and temporally non-successive reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore conditionally the conclusions of the six articles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction depends on prior doctrines concerning subsisting relations, divine simplicity, and the two modes of procession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT3","text":"The strongest joint is the reduction of action without motion to an order of origin and the distinction of consubstantial generation from creation from nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence is chiefly sustained by the distinction between real identity and diversity of mode of signifying.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT5","text":"The community of essential power and the exclusion of generative act from the Son leave a tension contained by the distinction between the direct, the indirect, and the notional adjunct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0110","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0124","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT6","text":"The proof of uniqueness rests on principles concerning material individuation and the determination of nature to one, which are not demonstrated anew in this question.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT7","text":"The argument from the identity of being and power to the exclusion of several sons would appear circular unless supplemented by independent accounts from relation, procession, and immateriality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: from the admissibility of notional predication to the purification of causality, then to the signification of power and the closure of the number of persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_33:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_33@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_33:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 42","title":"First Part · Question 41","context":"Chapter 42","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 41"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 41","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 42","order":43,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_34"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_34@R001","sha256":"2bb17bd6dd130c96b77bd5505dd4c990b3d25b2f49c83df2d0aab2115ba23987","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS1","text":"Quaeritur quomodo personae divinae inter se comparari possint secundum aequalitatem, durationem, ordinem, magnitudinem, praesentiam mutuam et potentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS2","text":"Unitas numerica essentiae plenam aequalitatem personarum exigit, dum relationes originis earum distinctionem conservant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS3","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica, reconstructiva et polemica est, quia modos creatos comparationis purgat et excludit subordinationem personarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","text":"Categoriae quantitatis, generationis, ordinis, continentiae et potentiae ad divina transferuntur solum post remotionem dimensionis, successionis, mutationis, distantiae et defectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS5","text":"Motus procedit ab obiectionibus ex exemplaribus creatis ad distinctionem essentiae et relationis, deinde ad consequentias consubstantialitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS6","text":"Asymmetria originis constituit ordinem sine prioritate, distinctionem sine separatione et receptionem sine inferioritate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A1","text":"In divinis nihil realiter consideratur praeter essentiam communem et relationes personales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","text":"Tres personae unam numero essentiam divinam communicant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","text":"Personae distinguuntur relationibus originis realiter oppositis, quae in divinis subsistunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","text":"Quaelibet persona est sua essentia, et tota perfectio divinae naturae in qualibet persona est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A5","text":"Quantitas divina est quantitas virtutis, quae perfectionem naturae eiusque effectus in esse et operatione significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A6","text":"Aequalitas secundum quantitatem virtutis paritatem perfectionis significat, similitudinem includit et maius vel minus excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A7","text":"Principium in divinis dicitur secundum originem absque prioritate durationis, naturae vel intellectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","text":"Aeternitas principium durationis excludit, non principium originis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A9","text":"Pater Filium natura generat, non voluntaria temporis electione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A10","text":"Natura Patris ab aeterno perfecte actuosa est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","text":"Generatio divina neque successiva neque materialis neque transmutativa est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A12","text":"Vera generatio naturalis perfectionem naturae generantis genito communicat, nisi defectus principii vel transmutatio receptionem impediat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0082","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A13","text":"Relationes mutuo definitae simul sunt natura et intellectu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","text":"Processio intelligibilis interior in principio originante manet et essentialem distantiam non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A15","text":"Potentia agendi perfectionem naturae consequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A16","text":"Pluralitas personarum vel notionum perfectionem divinae naturae non auget.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","text":"Eadem perfectio absoluta sub diversis modis relativis dandi et accipiendi possidetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A18","text":"Aequalitas et similitudo non addunt relationem realem distinctam, sed unitatem essentiae cum relationibus personalibus intellectu coniungunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX1","text":"Aequalitas divina non fundatur in quantitate dimensiva, loco, tempore vel numero personarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX2","text":"Communicatio formae sola non sufficit ad aequalitatem, quia formam inaequaliter participari licet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX3","text":"Nulla persona divina maior, minor, perfectior vel minus perfecta altera est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX4","text":"Aequalitas non est relatio realis communis superaddita relationibus personalibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX5","text":"Nullus modus processionis creatae divinam generationem perfecte repraesentat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX6","text":"Generari in divinis non significat incipere esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX7","text":"Generatio aeterna neque fieri imperfectum neque instans temporale continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX8","text":"Ordo originis neque essentiam ordinat neque prius et posterius inter personas constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX9","text":"Distinctio relationum inaequalitatem vel dissimilitudinem essentialem non infert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX10","text":"Personae et relationes divinae non sunt universalia, partes vel quantitates addibiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX11","text":"Esse unius personae in altera non est continentia localis nec abolitio oppositionis relativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX12","text":"Exitus personae procedentis non est discessus exterior vel distantia essentialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX13","text":"Locutiones de mandato, auditione, demonstratione vel non agere a se defectum potentiae divinae Filii non significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX14","text":"Non posse generare alium Filium non est impotentia Filii, quia generare relationem, non actum absolutum, significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX15","text":"Minuitas et subiectio Christi secundum humanam naturam aequalitatem eius divinam non tollunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D1","text":"Unitas numerica essentiae et plenitudo perfectionis necessario excludunt inaequalitatem personarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A5","CH_GGVC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D2","text":"Aequalitas personarum explicatur per nullam praecessionem aeternitatis, nullum excessum magnitudinis et nullam superationem potentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A5","CH_GGVC_P_34:A6","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D3","text":"Nomina aequalitatis reciproce de Patre et Filio dicuntur, sed verbum coaequandi directionem receptionis a Patre ad Filium retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_34:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D4","text":"Filius Patri coaeternus est, quia generans ab aeterno perfectus actione non successiva naturaliter generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A9","CH_GGVC_P_34:A10","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D5","text":"In personis est ordo originis sine ulla prioritate naturae, intellectus vel durationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A7","CH_GGVC_P_34:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D6","text":"Filius ab aeterno Patri aequalis est in magnitudine, quia generatione non defectiva totam perfectionem naturae accipit sine incremento successivo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A10","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","CH_GGVC_P_34:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","text":"Personae mutuo insunt secundum essentiae identitatem, relationum correlationem et processionis interioritatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A13","CH_GGVC_P_34:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D8","text":"Filius Patri aequalis est in potentia, quia eadem perfectio naturae eandem virtutem agendi secum fert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D9","text":"Omnes personae simul non sunt maius aliquid quam una persona, quia tota perfectio indivisa in qualibet est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D10","text":"Pater et Filius eandem omnipotentiam habent, quamvis generare et generari secundum diversas relationes dicantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A15","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D11","text":"Eadem principia quae coeternitatem, magnitudinem et potentiam Filii constituunt Spiritum Sanctum utrique coaeternum et aequalem constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A7","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","CH_GGVC_P_34:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD1","text":"Omnis perfectio absoluta communis est personis, dum omnis distinctio personalis ad relationem originis restringitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A1","CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","text":"Asymmetria originis ordinem constituit, sed in hierarchiam ontologicam converti non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A7","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A13","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_34:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD3","text":"Aequalitas, coaeternitas, paritas magnitudinis, praesentia mutua et aequalitas potentiae sunt manifestationes coordinatae eiusdem consubstantialitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:D1","CH_GGVC_P_34:D4","CH_GGVC_P_34:D6","CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","CH_GGVC_P_34:D8","CH_GGVC_P_34:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD4","text":"Pluralitas personalis ordinem relationum multiplicat, non quantitatem esse vel perfectionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD5","text":"Cognitio processionum divinarum per compositionem similitudinum partialium procedit, quia nullum exemplar creatum sine defectu transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A5","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","CH_GGVC_P_34:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD6","text":"Argumenta ab incommunicabili relatione ad minorem essentiam vel potentiam illicitam mutationem ab absoluto ad relativum efficiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A15","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_34:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD7","text":"Vita intradivina causalitatem originis sine processu temporali, mutatione vel exteriori effectu praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A10","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","CH_GGVC_P_34:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX1","text":"Omnis derivatio ab alio posterioritatem vel inferioritatem non implicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX2","text":"Distinctio realis personarum diversas essentias vel substantias non requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX3","text":"Relatio realis in divinis accidens subiecto personali superadditum non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX4","text":"Numerus personarum essentiam numerabilem vel divisibilem non reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX5","text":"Causalitas originis ad productionem efficientem extra producentem reduci non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX6","text":"Inapplicabilitas actus relativi potentiae absolutae defectum non demonstrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX7","text":"Catalogus modorum creatorum essendi, generandi vel continendi categorias divinas non exhaurit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX8","text":"Accipere naturam ab alio dependentiam defectivam non significat, ubi natura tota et aeternaliter communicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX1","text":"Nullum tempus ante generationem Filii concipi potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX2","text":"Nulla persona divina ante vel extra relationem originis qua distinguitur subsistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX3","text":"Nulla tertia relatio inter relationes personales mediationem realem praestat, quia talis mediatio regressum infinitum produceret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX4","text":"Nulla mensura extrinseca essentiae divinae personas secundum gradus perfectionis ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX5","text":"Nullum spatium ontologicum extra essentiam est in quod processio divina exeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX6","text":"Inadmissibilia sunt tam distinctio per essentias inaequales quam unitas quae relationes personales absorbeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS1","text":"Essentia numerice una et tota in singulis + relationes originis subsistentes et oppositae → personae distinctae sine divisione naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS2","text":"Praedicatum creaturale → discretio perfectionis a defectu → remotio dimensionis, successionis, mutationis vel distantiae → applicatio analogica ad divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS3","text":"Una essentia → una quantitas virtutis → nullum maius vel minus → aequalitas personarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS4","text":"Generatio naturalis + natura generantis aeternaliter perfecta + actio non successiva → nulla posterioritas geniti → coaeternitas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS5","text":"Principium originis + oppositio relationum → ordo; remotio prioritatis → ordo naturae sine hierarchia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS6","text":"Communicatio plena naturae → aequalitas perfectionis → aequalitas magnitudinis → aequalitas potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS7","text":"Identitas essentiae + simultas correlativorum + processio interior → mutuum esse personarum in se invicem sine confusione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS8","text":"Inaequalitas personarum → diversitas quantitatis divinae → diversitas essentiae → pluralitas deorum → impossibilitas → necessitas aequalitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS9","text":"Eadem perfectio absoluta + diversae relationes dantis et accipientis → actus relativi non convertibiles sine inaequalitate potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AF1","text":"Comparatio personarum → obiectiones ex quantitate et processione creatis → distinctio essentiae, relationis et originis → remotio defectuum creatorum → aequalitas necessaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AF2","text":"Aequalitas generalis → exclusio posterioritatis temporalis → constitutio ordinis originis → aequalitas magnitudinis → mutua praesentia → aequalitas potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AF3","text":"Origo ab alio → asymmetria relativa → nulla prioritas essentialis → nulla distantia → nulla inferioritas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME1","text":"Aequalitas a mensuratione dimensionali ad exclusionem excessus in perfectione virtuali transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME2","text":"Axis originis ab axe perfectionis separatur, ut esse ab alio non amplius esse minus significet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME3","text":"Oppositio personarum in campo relationum collocatur, communitas autem in campo essentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME4","text":"Ordo a prioritate temporali vel naturali ad puram ordinationem originis reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME5","text":"Esse in alio a continentia locali ad identitatem essentiae, correlationem et processionem interiorem transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME6","text":"Potentia absoluta a proprietate relativa distinguitur, ne diversitas actuum personalium gradus omnipotentiae efficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME7","text":"Pluralitas personarum desinit esse pluralitas additiva magnitudinis vel perfectionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME8","text":"Exemplaria creata ex normis exhaustivis in similitudines partiales et corrigendas convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei tractat aequalitatem, coaeternitatem, ordinem, magnitudinem, mutuum esse et potentiam personarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis omnia problemata per matricem essentiae communis, relationum oppositarum et originis interioris ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus obiectiones solvit detegendo translationes illicitas a modis creatis et a relativis ad absoluta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis ponit subsistentiam relationum, plenitudinem indivisam essentiae et aeternitatem sine successione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT1","text":"Axiomata proposita sex conclusiones quaestionis ex una matrice essentiae, relationis et originis restituere sufficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT2","text":"Structura interne cohaeret quatenus perfectiones absolutae communes et proprietates relativae distinctivae constanter separantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT3","text":"Firmissima deductio est transitus ab una essentia et plena perfectione ad aequalitatem magnitudinis et potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT4","text":"Identitas essentiae cum perfectione, subsistentia relationum et unitas Dei ex tractatu antecedenti assumuntur potius quam hic demonstrantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilior manet quod aequalitas et ordo ex relationibus realibus constituuntur, quamvis aequalitas relationem additam et ordo prioritatem non significent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT6","text":"Solutiones de reciproco aequali, non reciproco coaequari et eadem potentia sine facultate generandi rigida distinctione absoluti et relativi nituntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT7","text":"Usus plurium similitudinum creatarum defectus singulorum exemplarium compensat, sed criterium compositionis ex doctrina iam constituta dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT8","text":"Auctoritates et distinctiones Christologicae difficultates locales claudunt, sed nucleus demonstrativus in consubstantialitate et origine non successiva consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT9","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: modos creatos excludit, principia divina distinguit et ex eis aequalitatem sine confusione atque ordinem sine inaequalitate generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161242121216Z_3f7d3347","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 42","source_sha256":"2bb17bd6dd130c96b77bd5505dd4c990b3d25b2f49c83df2d0aab2115ba23987","sha256":"06f31416784f83f9854600448211c949b0fb31c65ae971a26d023f0ec721c5cd","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:12:42.122935+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS1","text":"It is asked how the divine persons can be compared with one another according to equality, duration, order, magnitude, mutual presence, and power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS2","text":"The numerical unity of the essence requires the full equality of the persons, while relations of origin preserve their distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, reconstructive, and polemical, because it purges created modes of comparison and excludes the subordination of the persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","text":"The categories of quantity, generation, order, containment, and power are transferred to the divine only after the removal of dimension, succession, change, distance, and defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS5","text":"The movement proceeds from objections based on created models to the distinction of essence and relation, then to the consequences of consubstantiality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AS6","text":"The asymmetry of origin establishes order without priority, distinction without separation, and reception without inferiority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A1","text":"In the divine, nothing is considered really except the common essence and the personal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","text":"The three persons share one divine essence numerically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","text":"The persons are distinguished by really opposed relations of origin, which subsist in the divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","text":"Each person is its essence, and the whole perfection of the divine nature is in each person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A5","text":"Divine quantity is quantity of power, which signifies the perfection of nature and of its effects in being and operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A6","text":"Equality according to quantity of power signifies parity of perfection, includes likeness, and excludes greater and lesser.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A7","text":"Principle in the divine is said according to origin without priority of duration, nature, or intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","text":"Eternity excludes a principle of duration, not a principle of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A9","text":"The Father generates the Son by nature, not by a voluntary choice in time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A10","text":"The nature of the Father is perfectly actual from eternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","text":"Divine generation is neither successive, nor material, nor transmutative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A12","text":"True natural generation communicates the perfection of the generating nature to the generated, unless a defect of the principle or transmutation impedes reception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0082","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A13","text":"Mutually defined relations are simultaneous by nature and intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","text":"An interior intelligible procession remains in the originating principle and does not establish essential distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A15","text":"The power of acting follows upon the perfection of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A16","text":"The plurality of persons or notions does not increase the perfection of the divine nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","text":"The same absolute perfection is possessed under diverse relative modes of giving and receiving.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:A18","text":"Equality and likeness do not add a distinct real relation, but unite in intellect the unity of essence with the personal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX1","text":"Divine equality is not founded upon dimensional quantity, place, time, or the number of persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX2","text":"The communication of form alone does not suffice for equality, because a form may be participated unequally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX3","text":"No divine person is greater, lesser, more perfect, or less perfect than another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX4","text":"Equality is not a common real relation superadded to the personal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX5","text":"No mode of created procession perfectly represents divine generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX6","text":"To be generated in the divine does not signify to begin to be.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX7","text":"Eternal generation contains neither imperfect becoming nor a temporal instant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX8","text":"The order of origin neither orders the essence nor establishes before and after among the persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX9","text":"The distinction of relations does not entail inequality or essential dissimilarity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX10","text":"The divine persons and relations are not universals, parts, or addible quantities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX11","text":"The being of one person in another is neither local containment nor the abolition of relative opposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX12","text":"The going forth of the proceeding person is not an outward departure or essential distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX13","text":"Expressions concerning command, hearing, showing, or not acting from oneself do not signify a defect of the Son's divine power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX14","text":"Not being able to generate another Son is not impotence in the Son, because to generate signifies a relation, not an absolute act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:NX15","text":"The lowliness and subjection of Christ according to human nature do not remove His divine equality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D1","text":"The numerical unity of the essence and the fullness of perfection necessarily exclude inequality among the persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A5","CH_GGVC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D2","text":"The equality of the persons is explained through no precedence in eternity, no excess in magnitude, and no superiority in power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A5","CH_GGVC_P_34:A6","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D3","text":"Names of equality are said reciprocally of the Father and the Son, but the word coequalizing retains the direction of reception from the Father to the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_34:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D4","text":"The Son is coeternal with the Father, because the generator, perfect from eternity, naturally generates by non-successive action.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A9","CH_GGVC_P_34:A10","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D5","text":"Among the persons there is an order of origin without any priority of nature, intellect, or duration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A7","CH_GGVC_P_34:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D6","text":"The Son is equal to the Father from eternity in magnitude, because by non-defective generation He receives the whole perfection of nature without successive increase.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A10","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","CH_GGVC_P_34:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","text":"The persons mutually inhere according to identity of essence, correlation of relations, and interiority of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A13","CH_GGVC_P_34:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D8","text":"The Son is equal to the Father in power, because the same perfection of nature entails the same power of acting.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D9","text":"All the persons together are not something greater than one person, because the whole undivided perfection is in each.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D10","text":"The Father and the Son have the same omnipotence, although generating and being generated are said according to diverse relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A15","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:D11","text":"The same principles that establish the Son's coeternity, magnitude, and power establish the Holy Spirit as coeternal and equal to both.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A7","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","CH_GGVC_P_34:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD1","text":"Every absolute perfection is common to the persons, while every personal distinction is restricted to a relation of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A1","CH_GGVC_P_34:A2","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","text":"The asymmetry of origin establishes order, but cannot be converted into an ontological hierarchy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A7","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A13","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_34:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD3","text":"Equality, coeternity, parity of magnitude, mutual presence, and equality of power are coordinated manifestations of the same consubstantiality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:D1","CH_GGVC_P_34:D4","CH_GGVC_P_34:D6","CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","CH_GGVC_P_34:D8","CH_GGVC_P_34:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD4","text":"Personal plurality multiplies the order of relations, not the quantity of being or perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD5","text":"Knowledge of the divine processions proceeds through the composition of partial likenesses, because no created model is transferred without defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A5","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","CH_GGVC_P_34:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD6","text":"Arguments from an incommunicable relation to a lesser essence or power effect an illicit transition from the absolute to the relative.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A15","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_34:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SD7","text":"Intradivine life presupposes causality of origin without temporal process, change, or external effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_34:A10","CH_GGVC_P_34:A11","CH_GGVC_P_34:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX1","text":"Not every derivation from another implies posteriority or inferiority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX2","text":"The real distinction of the persons does not require diverse essences or substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX3","text":"A real relation in the divine is not an accident superadded to a personal subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX4","text":"The number of persons does not render the essence numerable or divisible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX5","text":"Causality of origin cannot be reduced to efficient production outside the producer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX6","text":"The inapplicability of a relative act to absolute power does not demonstrate a defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX7","text":"The catalogue of created modes of being, generating, or containing does not exhaust the divine categories.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX8","text":"Receiving nature from another does not signify defective dependence where nature is communicated wholly and eternally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX1","text":"No time before the generation of the Son can be conceived.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX2","text":"No divine person subsists before or apart from the relation of origin by which it is distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX3","text":"No third relation provides real mediation between the personal relations, because such mediation would produce an infinite regress.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX4","text":"No extrinsic measure of the divine essence orders the persons according to degrees of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX5","text":"There is no ontological space outside the essence into which divine procession goes forth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX6","text":"Both distinction through unequal essences and unity that absorbs the personal relations are inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS1","text":"Essence numerically one and whole in each + subsistent and opposed relations of origin → distinct persons without division of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS2","text":"Created predicate → discernment of perfection from defect → removal of dimension, succession, change, or distance → analogical application to the divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS3","text":"One essence → one quantity of power → no greater or lesser → equality of persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS4","text":"Natural generation + eternally perfect nature of the generator + non-successive action → no posteriority of the generated → coeternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS5","text":"Principle of origin + opposition of relations → order; removal of priority → order of nature without hierarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS6","text":"Full communication of nature → equality of perfection → equality of magnitude → equality of power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS7","text":"Identity of essence + simultaneity of correlatives + interior procession → mutual being of the persons in one another without confusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS8","text":"Inequality of persons → diversity of divine quantity → diversity of essence → plurality of gods → impossibility → necessity of equality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS9","text":"The same absolute perfection + diverse relations of giver and receiver → relative acts not convertible without inequality of power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AF1","text":"Comparison of persons → objections from created quantity and procession → distinction of essence, relation, and origin → removal of created defects → necessary equality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AF2","text":"General equality → exclusion of temporal posteriority → establishment of the order of origin → equality of magnitude → mutual presence → equality of power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:AF3","text":"Origin from another → relative asymmetry → no essential priority → no distance → no inferiority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME1","text":"Equality is transferred from dimensional measurement to the exclusion of excess in virtual perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME2","text":"The axis of origin is separated from the axis of perfection, so that being from another no longer signifies being less.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME3","text":"The opposition of persons is situated in the field of relations, while community is situated in the field of essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME4","text":"Order is reclassified from temporal or natural priority to the pure ordering of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME5","text":"Being in another is transferred from local containment to identity of essence, correlation, and interior procession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME6","text":"Absolute power is distinguished from relative property, lest diversity of personal acts produce degrees of omnipotence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME7","text":"The plurality of persons ceases to be an additive plurality of magnitude or perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ME8","text":"Created models are converted from exhaustive norms into partial and corrigible likenesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT1","text":"The surface level treats the equality, coeternity, order, magnitude, mutual being, and power of the persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT2","text":"The structural level orders all problems through the matrix of common essence, opposed relations, and interior origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level resolves objections by detecting illicit transfers from created modes and from relatives to absolutes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level posits the subsistence of relations, the undivided fullness of essence, and eternity without succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT1","text":"The proposed axioms suffice to reconstruct the six conclusions of the question from one matrix of essence, relation, and origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT2","text":"The structure coheres internally insofar as common absolute perfections and distinctive relative properties are consistently separated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT3","text":"The strongest deduction is the transition from one essence and full perfection to equality of magnitude and power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT4","text":"The identity of essence with perfection, the subsistence of relations, and the unity of God are assumed from the preceding treatment rather than demonstrated here.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT5","text":"A more fragile joint remains: equality and order are constituted by real relations, although equality does not signify an added relation and order does not signify priority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT6","text":"The solutions concerning reciprocal equality, non-reciprocal coequalizing, and the same power without the capacity to generate rest upon a rigid distinction of absolute and relative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT7","text":"The use of several created likenesses compensates for the defects of individual models, but the criterion of composition depends upon doctrine already established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT8","text":"Authorities and Christological distinctions close local difficulties, but the demonstrative core consists in consubstantiality and non-successive origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: it excludes created modes, distinguishes divine principles, and from them generates equality without confusion and order without inequality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_34:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_34@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_34:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 43","title":"First Part · Question 42","context":"Chapter 43","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 42"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 42","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 43","order":44,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_35"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_35@R001","sha256":"a59bbdbb39ff75c4da4b1413db29f44cc29ea570b6f5ff6650e805a37d9f2b44","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quomodo personae divinae mitti possint sine minoratione, separatione, motu locali aut mutatione divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","text":"Missio divina constituitur ex processione originis et novo modo praesentiae in creatura, cuius novitas in recipiente creato ponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica et reconstructiva, quia notionem missionis creatae in rationes analogice transferibiles dividit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS4","text":"Obiectiones ex imperio, distantia et motu locali sumptae resolvuntur per distinctionem originis a termino temporali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS5","text":"Ex definitione missionis proceditur ad gratiam sanctificantem, inhabitationem, personas mittibiles et modos innovationis recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS6","text":"Postremo missio visibilis ut manifestatio selectiva missionis invisibilis constituitur, atque actus mittendi secundum principium personae vel effectus distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","text":"Ratio missionis coniungit habitudinem missi ad mittentem cum habitudine ad terminum ad quem mittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","text":"Habitudo ad mittentem in divinis est processio originis aeterna inter personas aequales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","text":"Terminus missionis divinae est novus modus existendi personae divinae in creatura.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","text":"Novitas huius termini provenit ex mutatione creaturae, non personae divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","text":"Deus communiter omnibus rebus inest per essentiam, potentiam et praesentiam sicut causa effectibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","text":"Modus specialis praesentiae in creatura rationali constituitur cum Deus cognoscitur et amatur atque in ea sicut in templo inhabitat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","text":"Sola gratia gratum faciens creaturae rationali facultatem fruendi divina persona confert et specialem inhabitationem constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","text":"Donum gratiae creatae animam ad personam divinam habendam disponit, sed ipsum donum a persona divina causatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","text":"In dono gratiae gratum facientis ipsa persona missa datur et inhabitat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","text":"Per gratiam gratum facientem tota Trinitas mentem inhabitat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A11","text":"Pater non est ab alio; Filius et Spiritus Sanctus ab alio sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A12","text":"Missio invisibilis Filii attenditur secundum illuminationem intellectus in amorem prorumpentem, missio autem Spiritus Sancti secundum inflammationem affectus per caritatem; ambae tamen in una radice gratiae communicant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A13","text":"Missio invisibilis ad creaturam rationalem requirit simul inhabitationem gratiae et innovationem per gratiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A14","text":"Innovatio missionis potest esse initium inhabitationis, augmentum gratiae, novus actus vel status, aut extensio cognitionis per novam revelationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A15","text":"Missio visibilis invisibilem praesentiam per creaturam visibilem selecte manifestat ad utilitatem Ecclesiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A16","text":"Filius visibiliter mittitur ut auctor sanctificationis in natura humana personaliter assumpta; Spiritus Sanctus ut indicium sanctificationis in signo formato non assumpto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","text":"Persona mittens, ut principium personae missae, mittit tantum secundum ordinem originis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A18","text":"Persona mittens, ut principium effectus temporalis missionis, est tota Trinitas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX1","text":"Missio divina neque imperium neque consilium importat, ideoque nullam inaequalitatem personarum constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX2","text":"Missio divina non est motus localis, discessus, separatio aut acquisitio loci prius vacui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX3","text":"Missio non est mera processio aeterna, nec eius temporalitas mutationem intrinsecam Dei ponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX4","text":"Praesentia communis Dei in omnibus rebus nondum est missio invisibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX5","text":"Persona divina non datur tantum per dona creata, nec sola cognitio, miraculum, prophetia aut gratia gratis data missionem simpliciter constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX6","text":"Pater, quamvis inhabitet et se liberaliter communicet, mitti non potest quia non est ab alio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX7","text":"Filius non mittitur secundum quamlibet perfectionem intellectus, sed solum secundum cognitionem quae in amorem procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX8","text":"Missio visibilis Spiritus Sancti non est assumptio hypostatica, visio imaginaria prophetica aut usus rei praeexistentis ut signi sacramentalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0138","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0139","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX9","text":"Neque omnis missio invisibilis signo visibili manifestatur, neque omnis apparitio divina missio visibilis est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX10","text":"Sacramenta gratiam instrumentaliter continent, sed non sunt termini ad quos persona divina mittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX11","text":"Ministerium angelicum in formando signo non constituit missionem Angeli, neque minister humanus Spiritum Sanctum dat ut causa gratiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0145","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D1","text":"Processio originis missionem divinam sine imperio, auctoritate dominativa aut minoratione personae missae constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D2","text":"Quia persona divina iam communiter adest, novus modus praesentiae neque separationem a mittente neque transitum localem requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D3","text":"Relatione originis manente una et aeterna, missio temporaliter praedicatur ex termino novo in creatura; geminatio processionis est ex terminis, non ex duplicata origine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D4","text":"Missio invisibilis non ex omnipraesentia, sed ex cognitione, amore et fruitione Dei per gratiam constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D5","text":"Gratia creata est dispositio ad habendam personam, non substitutum personae; persona causat donum et in dono ipsa datur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D6","text":"Inhabitatio et missio non convertuntur: tota Trinitas inhabitat, sed solis Filio et Spiritui Sancto convenit mitti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","CH_GGVC_P_35:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D7","text":"Missiones invisibiles Filii et Spiritus Sancti sunt distinctae secundum originem et effectus appropriatos, sed inseparabiles secundum radicem gratiae et praesentiam personarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","CH_GGVC_P_35:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D8","text":"Omnis creatura rationalis in qua inhabitatio gratiae vere innovatur missionem invisibilem recipit, quamvis novitas initio, augmento, novo statu aut extensione revelationis perfici possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A13","CH_GGVC_P_35:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D9","text":"Missio visibilis Filii et Spiritus Sancti communicat in manifestatione invisibilis, sed differt ut praesentia auctoris personaliter assumens et praesentia signati in signo transitorio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A15","CH_GGVC_P_35:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D10","text":"Filius, secundum principium personae, a solo Patre mittitur, Spiritus Sanctus a Patre et Filio; secundum principium effectus autem quaelibet persona divina personam mittibilem mittere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD1","text":"Praedicatio temporalis de persona immutabili fundatur in relatione ad effectum creatum temporaliter novum, non in acquisitione realitatis novae a persona divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD2","text":"Gratia sanctificans est commissura inter donum creatum et donum increatum: qualitas creata recipiens disponit, sed terminus fruitionis est ipsa persona divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","text":"Unitas operationis Trinitatis distinctionem missionum non delet, quia communitas gratiae cum distinctione originum et appropriationum componitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","CH_GGVC_P_35:A11","CH_GGVC_P_35:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD4","text":"Tempus missionis non est series mutationum in Deo, sed ordo diversarum innovationum recipientis: initii, intensionis, status, actus vel extensionis cognitionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_35:A13","CH_GGVC_P_35:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD5","text":"Ordo visibilis est oeconomia signorum selectiva et ecclesialiter ordinata, non necessaria duplicatio exterior cuiuslibet inhabitationis interioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A15","CH_GGVC_P_35:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD6","text":"Actus mittendi est relatio dupliciter typata: secundum originem restringitur ad principia personalia, secundum effectum extenditur ad causalitatem communem Trinitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","text":"Univocitas missionis creatae et divinae falsa esse debet; aliter imperium, distantia et motus localis in divinas personas transferrentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet omnem praedicationem temporalem de Deo mutationem realem in Deo exigere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet praesentiam divinam unum tantum modum habere, quia praesentia causalis communis ab inhabitatione rationali distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet donum gratiae creatum totam donationem divinam exhaurire.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet operationem communem Trinitatis omnem distinctionem personalem in effectibus oeconomicis evacuare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","CH_GGVC_P_35:A11","CH_GGVC_P_35:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet auctoritatem mittentis uno tantum sensu dici, quia principium personae et principium effectus diversos ambitus agentium constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX1","text":"Absentia localis personae divinae, quam adventus missionis suppleret, impossibilis habetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX2","text":"Intrinsecum fieri temporale in Deo praecluditur; omnis novitas missionis ad creaturam transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX3","text":"Missio personae innascibilis praecluditur, quia mitti sine esse ab alio intra hoc systema intelligi nequit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX4","text":"Fruitio personae divinae per facultatem naturalem, cognitionem nudam aut charisma sine sanctificatione indisponibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX5","text":"Ordo visibilis a gratia, inhabitatione, processione personali et utilitate Ecclesiae separatus inadmissibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A15","CH_GGVC_P_35:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX6","text":"Nulla creatura est principium sufficiens effectus gratiae quo persona divina simpliciter dari dicitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS1","text":"Definitio operativa ponitur: missio = habitudo ad principium + habitudo ad terminum novum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS2","text":"Applicatio ad divina procedit: processio originis aequalis et aeterna + novus terminus in creatura → missio temporalis sine mutatione divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS3","text":"Constitutio missionis invisibilis procedit: praesentia communis → praesentia rationalis per cognitionem et amorem → gratia sanctificans → inhabitatio et fruitio → donatio personae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS4","text":"Distributio personalis procedit: inhabitatio communis Trinitati + esse ab alio proprium Filio et Spiritui Sancto → Pater inhabitat sed non mittitur; Filius et Spiritus inhabitatione missibili gaudent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS5","text":"Distributio effectuum procedit: una radix gratiae → illuminatio intellectus in amorem et inflammatio affectus → missiones distinctae sed inseparabiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS6","text":"Manifestatio exterior procedit: missio invisibilis + modus humanus per sensibilia cognoscendi + utilitas Ecclesiae → missio visibilis selectiva → Filius ut auctor assumens, Spiritus ut signatum in signo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS7","text":"Determinatio mittentis procedit: principium personae → ordo originis; principium effectus → causalitas totius Trinitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AF1","text":"Primus motus est: objectiones ex missione creata → divisio rationis missionis → processio originis → terminus novus → temporalitas ex creatura.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AF2","text":"Secundus motus est: praesentia communis → praesentia specialis rationalis → gratia gratum faciens → donatio personae → exclusio missionis Patris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AF3","text":"Tertius motus est: inhabitatio Filii et Spiritus Sancti → distinctio illuminationis et caritatis → inseparabilitas missionum → varietas innovationum recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AF4","text":"Quartus motus est: invisibile manifestandum → creatura visibilis → distinctio auctoris et indicii → utilitas ecclesialis → duplex ratio mittentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME1","text":"Missio ex motu, distantia et subordinatione in relationem originis cum termino creato reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME2","text":"Vocabula originis in tria genera distribuuntur: processio et exitus sine termino determinato, generatio et spiratio termino aeterno, missio et datio termino temporali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME3","text":"Praesentia divina ex oppositione simplici praesentiae et absentiae in modos causalitatis communis et inhabitationis rationalis distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME4","text":"Gratia ex effectu creato separato in medium dispositionis ad fruitionem ipsius personae divinae reordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME5","text":"Inhabitatio a missione distinguitur, unde tota Trinitas inhabitat, sed Pater non mittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME6","text":"Intellectus et affectus non ut facultates separatae, sed ut effectus appropriati missionum inseparabilium ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME7","text":"Visibilia distinguuntur in naturam personaliter assumptam, signa specialiter formata, visiones imaginarias, sacramenta et apparitiones non missionales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME8","text":"Mittens non amplius uno ordine classificatur, sed vel ut principium personae vel ut principium effectus temporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — Quaeritur quibus personis, quibus recipientibus, quo tempore et quibus modis missio visibilis vel invisibilis conveniat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — Mechanismus consistit in coniunctione originis personalis, gratiae sanctificantis, innovationis recipientis et manifestationis signalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — Obiectiones dissolvuntur non negando missionem, sed notionem eius analogice dividendo et terminos originis, praesentiae, donationis atque causalitatis distinguendo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Realitas divina manet immutabilis et ubique praesens, dum tempus, novitas et multiplicatio modorum missionis ex relatione ad creaturam rationalem oriuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad octo articulorum conclusiones principales ex definitione missionis restituendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT2","text":"Structura firmissima est distinctio inter processionem originis aeternam et terminum temporalem ex mutatione creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT3","text":"Notio novi modi existendi pendet ex doctrina praevia de praesentia divina et gratia, quae hic adhibetur potius quam integre demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT4","text":"Reciprocitas qua persona gratiam causat et gratia ad personam habendam disponit circulum formalem vitat, sed commissuram causalitatis creatae et increatae presupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT5","text":"Distinctio missionum personalium nititur originibus et appropriationibus, quia effectus gratiae manent communes et inseparabiles; hic est nexus structuraliter delicatissimus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT6","text":"Terminus inter apparitionem visibilem et missionem visibilem pendet ex formatione speciali signi et intentione significandi inhabitationem, quae non ex sola specie visibili discernuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT7","text":"Duplex significatio mittentis formulas alioquin repugnantes conciliat, sed unitatem univocam praedicati mittendi relinquit intentionaliter divisam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0160","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT8","text":"Contradictio interna directa post distinctiones non remanet, et restitutio motum a missione analogice definita ad gratiam, manifestationem et causalitatem mittentis servat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0163","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161315731335Z_2c053e18","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 43","source_sha256":"a59bbdbb39ff75c4da4b1413db29f44cc29ea570b6f5ff6650e805a37d9f2b44","sha256":"10cd77f294f2c1b1def6fca10ac6ad35c17bf87a31284071ffc4db94e1f32d07","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:13:15.732300+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS1","text":"The text asks how the divine persons can be sent without diminution, separation, local motion, or divine change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","text":"Divine mission is constituted by procession of origin and a new mode of presence in the creature, the newness of which is posited in the created recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical and reconstructive, because it divides the notion of created mission into analogically transferable intelligibilities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS4","text":"Objections drawn from command, distance, and local motion are resolved through the distinction of origin from a temporal terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS5","text":"From the definition of mission one proceeds to sanctifying grace, indwelling, sendable persons, and modes of innovation of the recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AS6","text":"Finally, visible mission is constituted as a selective manifestation of invisible mission, and the act of sending is distinguished according to the principle of the person or of the effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","text":"The intelligibility of mission joins the relation of the sent one to the sender with the relation to the terminus to which it is sent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","text":"The relation to the sender in divine matters is the eternal procession of origin among equal persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","text":"The terminus of divine mission is a new mode of existence of the divine person in the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","text":"The newness of this terminus proceeds from a change in the creature, not in the divine person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","text":"God is commonly present to all things through essence, power, and presence, as a cause is present to its effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","text":"A special mode of presence in the rational creature is constituted when God is known and loved and dwells in it as in a temple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","text":"Only grace making pleasing confers on the rational creature the capacity to enjoy the divine person and constitutes special indwelling.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","text":"The gift of created grace disposes the soul to possess the divine person, but the gift itself is caused by the divine person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","text":"In the gift of grace making pleasing, the very person sent is given and dwells within.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","text":"Through grace making pleasing, the whole Trinity dwells in the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A11","text":"The Father is not from another; the Son and the Holy Spirit are from another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A12","text":"The invisible mission of the Son is considered according to the illumination of the intellect bursting forth into love, but the mission of the Holy Spirit according to the inflaming of the affect through charity; yet both share one root in grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A13","text":"Invisible mission to a rational creature requires simultaneously indwelling by grace and innovation through grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A14","text":"The innovation of mission can be the beginning of indwelling, an increase of grace, a new act or state, or an extension of knowledge through a new revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A15","text":"Visible mission selectively manifests invisible presence through a visible creature for the benefit of the Church.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A16","text":"The Son is visibly sent as the author of sanctification in a human nature personally assumed; the Holy Spirit as an indication of sanctification in a formed sign not assumed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","text":"The sending person, as principle of the person sent, sends only according to the order of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:A18","text":"The sending person, as principle of the temporal effect of mission, is the whole Trinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX1","text":"Divine mission imports neither command nor counsel, and therefore constitutes no inequality of persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX2","text":"Divine mission is not local motion, departure, separation, or acquisition of a previously empty place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX3","text":"Mission is not mere eternal procession, nor does its temporality posit an intrinsic change in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX4","text":"God's common presence in all things is not yet invisible mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX5","text":"The divine person is not given only through created gifts, nor does knowledge alone, miracle, prophecy, or grace gratuitously given simply constitute mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX6","text":"The Father, although he dwells within and communicates himself freely, cannot be sent because he is not from another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX7","text":"The Son is not sent according to any perfection of intellect whatsoever, but only according to knowledge that proceeds into love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX8","text":"The visible mission of the Holy Spirit is not hypostatic assumption, an imaginary prophetic vision, or the use of a pre-existing thing as a sacramental sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0138","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0139","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX9","text":"Neither is every invisible mission manifested by a visible sign, nor is every divine appearance a visible mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX10","text":"The sacraments contain grace instrumentally, but they are not termini to which the divine person is sent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:NX11","text":"Angelic ministry in forming the sign does not constitute the mission of an Angel, nor does a human minister give the Holy Spirit as the cause of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0145","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D1","text":"Procession of origin constitutes divine mission without command, dominative authority, or diminution of the person sent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D2","text":"Because the divine person is already commonly present, a new mode of presence requires neither separation from the sender nor local transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D3","text":"With the relation of origin remaining one and eternal, mission is predicated temporally from a new terminus in the creature; the doubling of procession is from termini, not from a doubled origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D4","text":"Invisible mission is constituted not from omnipresence, but from knowledge, love, and enjoyment of God through grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D5","text":"Created grace is a disposition for possessing the person, not a substitute for the person; the person causes the gift and in the gift is itself given.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D6","text":"Indwelling and mission are not convertible: the whole Trinity dwells within, but only the Son and the Holy Spirit are fittingly sent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","CH_GGVC_P_35:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D7","text":"The invisible missions of the Son and the Holy Spirit are distinct according to origin and appropriated effects, but inseparable according to the root of grace and the presence of the persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","CH_GGVC_P_35:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D8","text":"Every rational creature in which the indwelling of grace is truly innovated receives an invisible mission, although the newness can be effected by beginning, increase, a new state, or extension of revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A13","CH_GGVC_P_35:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D9","text":"The visible mission of the Son and the Holy Spirit shares in the manifestation of the invisible, but differs as the presence of the author personally assuming and the presence of that signified in a transitory sign.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A15","CH_GGVC_P_35:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:D10","text":"The Son, according to the principle of the person, is sent by the Father alone; the Holy Spirit by the Father and the Son; but according to the principle of the effect, any divine person can send a sendable person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD1","text":"Temporal predication of the immutable person is founded on a relation to a temporally new created effect, not on the acquisition of a new reality by the divine person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD2","text":"Sanctifying grace is the joint between the created gift and the uncreated gift: the created quality disposes the recipient, but the terminus of enjoyment is the divine person itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","text":"The unity of the operation of the Trinity does not erase the distinction of missions, because the commonality of grace is combined with the distinction of origins and appropriations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","CH_GGVC_P_35:A11","CH_GGVC_P_35:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD4","text":"The time of mission is not a series of changes in God, but an order of diverse innovations of the recipient: beginning, intensification, state, act, or extension of knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_35:A13","CH_GGVC_P_35:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD5","text":"The visible order is a selective economy of signs ordered ecclesially, not a necessary exterior duplication of every interior indwelling.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A15","CH_GGVC_P_35:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SD6","text":"The act of sending is a relation typed in two ways: according to origin it is restricted to personal principles; according to effect it extends to the common causality of the Trinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","text":"The univocity of created and divine mission must be false; otherwise command, distance, and local motion would be transferred to the divine persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX2","text":"It must be false that every temporal predication of God requires a real change in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX3","text":"It must be false that divine presence has only one mode, because common causal presence is distinguished from rational indwelling.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the created gift of grace exhausts the whole divine donation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the common operation of the Trinity evacuates every personal distinction in economic effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A10","CH_GGVC_P_35:A11","CH_GGVC_P_35:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX6","text":"It must be false that the authority of the sender is said in only one sense, because the principle of the person and the principle of the effect constitute diverse domains of agents.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX1","text":"The local absence of the divine person, which the advent of mission would supply, is held to be impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX2","text":"Temporal becoming intrinsic to God is precluded; all newness of mission is transferred to the creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX3","text":"The mission of an unbegotten person is precluded, because being sent without being from another cannot be understood within this system.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX4","text":"Enjoyment of the divine person through natural capacity, bare knowledge, or charisma without sanctification is unavailable.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX5","text":"A visible order separated from grace, indwelling, personal procession, and the benefit of the Church is inadmissible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A15","CH_GGVC_P_35:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX6","text":"No creature is a sufficient principle of the effect of grace by which the divine person is said to be given simply.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS1","text":"An operative definition is posited: mission = relation to principle + relation to a new terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS2","text":"Application to divine matters proceeds: equal and eternal procession of origin + new terminus in the creature → temporal mission without divine change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS3","text":"The constitution of invisible mission proceeds: common presence → rational presence through knowledge and love → sanctifying grace → indwelling and enjoyment → gift of the person.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS4","text":"Personal distribution proceeds: indwelling common to the Trinity + being from another proper to the Son and the Holy Spirit → the Father dwells within but is not sent; the Son and the Spirit enjoy sendable indwelling.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS5","text":"The distribution of effects proceeds: one root of grace → illumination of the intellect into love and inflaming of the affect → distinct but inseparable missions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS6","text":"Exterior manifestation proceeds: invisible mission + the human mode of knowing through sensibles + benefit of the Church → selective visible mission → the Son as assuming author, the Spirit as that signified in a sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS7","text":"Determination of the sender proceeds: principle of the person → order of origin; principle of the effect → causality of the whole Trinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AF1","text":"The first movement is: objections from created mission → division of the intelligibility of mission → procession of origin → new terminus → temporality from the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AF2","text":"The second movement is: common presence → special rational presence → grace making pleasing → gift of the person → exclusion of the Father's mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AF3","text":"The third movement is: indwelling of the Son and the Holy Spirit → distinction of illumination and charity → inseparability of missions → variety of innovations of the recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:AF4","text":"The fourth movement is: the invisible to be manifested → visible creature → distinction of author and indication → ecclesial benefit → twofold intelligibility of the sender.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0147","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME1","text":"Mission is reclassified from motion, distance, and subordination into a relation of origin with a created terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME2","text":"Terms of origin are distributed into three kinds: procession and going forth without a determinate terminus, generation and spiration with an eternal terminus, mission and giving with a temporal terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME3","text":"Divine presence is distinguished from the simple opposition of presence and absence into modes of common causality and rational indwelling.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME4","text":"Grace is reordered from a separate created effect into a means of disposition for enjoyment of the divine person itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME5","text":"Indwelling is distinguished from mission, whence the whole Trinity dwells within, but the Father is not sent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME6","text":"Intellect and affect are ordered not as separate faculties, but as appropriated effects of inseparable missions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME7","text":"Visible things are distinguished into a nature personally assumed, specially formed signs, imaginary visions, sacraments, and non-missional appearances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ME8","text":"The sender is no longer classified according to one order, but either as principle of the person or as principle of the temporal effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — It is asked to which persons, which recipients, at what time, and in which modes visible or invisible mission is fitting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — The mechanism consists in the conjunction of personal origin, sanctifying grace, innovation of the recipient, and sign-manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — Objections are dissolved not by denying mission, but by dividing its notion analogically and distinguishing the terms of origin, presence, donation, and causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Divine reality remains immutable and everywhere present, while time, newness, and the multiplication of modes of mission arise from relation to the rational creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal conclusions of eight articles from the definition of mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT2","text":"The most robust structure is the distinction between eternal procession of origin and a temporal terminus from the change of the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT3","text":"The notion of a new mode of existence depends on prior doctrine concerning divine presence and grace, which is applied here rather than demonstrated integrally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT4","text":"The reciprocity by which the person causes grace and grace disposes toward possessing the person avoids a formal circle, but presupposes the joint of created and uncreated causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT5","text":"The distinction of personal missions rests on origins and appropriations, because the effects of grace remain common and inseparable; here lies the structurally most delicate nexus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT6","text":"The boundary between visible appearance and visible mission depends on the special formation of the sign and the intention of signifying indwelling, which are not discerned from visible appearance alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT7","text":"The twofold signification of sender reconciles otherwise conflicting formulations, but leaves the univocal unity of the predicate of sending intentionally divided.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0160","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT8","text":"No direct internal contradiction remains after the distinctions, and the reconstruction preserves the movement from analogically defined mission to grace, manifestation, and the causality of the sender.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_35:P0163","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_35@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_35:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 44","title":"First Part · Question 43","context":"Chapter 44","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 43"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 43","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 44","order":45,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_36"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_36@R001","sha256":"f4d322db39e719800d9e2006e1648807ff2a98c6055bd56c534b2e89733589c9","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat utrum omne ens, inclusa materia prima, a Deo procedat ut a causa efficiente, exemplari et finali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS2","text":"Argumentatio a distinctione inter esse per essentiam et esse per participationem incipit, ut dependentia omnium entium a primo esse inferatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3","text":"Productio universalis entis distinguitur a mutatione particulari, ut materia prima, quam fieri particulariter non contingit, ab emanatione universali non eximatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS4","text":"Determinatio formarum creatarum ad sapientiam divinam reducitur, ita ut exemplaria sint rationes in Deo, non res separatae extra Deum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS5","text":"Finis universalis rerum ponitur bonitas divina communicata et participata, unde causalitas efficiens, exemplaris et finalis in uno primo principio formaliter distinguitur, realiter non dividitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A1","text":"Deus est ipsum esse per se subsistens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A2","text":"Ipsum esse subsistens non potest esse nisi unum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","text":"Omne ens aliud a Deo esse participat neque est suum esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A4","text":"Quod per participationem convenit causatur ab eo cui essentialiter convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A5","text":"Causa entium inquantum entia sunt causat quidquid ad esse eorum quocumque modo pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A6","text":"Emanatio ab universali principio essendi non est fieri particulare ex subiecto in formam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A7","text":"Primum principium passivum, ut imperfectum, ab primo principio activo et perfectissimo causatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","text":"Determinata forma effectus requirit exemplar quod formam determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A9","text":"Rationes exemplares omnium rerum sunt in sapientia divina et realiter non differunt ab essentia divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A10","text":"Omne agens agit propter finem, alioquin effectus determinatus non sequeretur nisi casualiter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","text":"Primum agens non agit ad finem acquirendum, sed ad communicandam suam perfectionem sive bonitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A12","text":"Omne bonum creatum est participatio similitudinis divinae bonitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A13","text":"Deus est causa efficiens, exemplaris et finalis omnium rerum, quamvis hae rationes causalitatis in intellectu nostro ordine distinguantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX1","text":"Habitudo ad causam non pertinet ad rationem entis simpliciter, sed ens participatum sine causalitate esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX2","text":"Necessitas essendi non excludit causalitatem, quia necessarium potest causam suae necessitatis habere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX3","text":"Abstractio mathematica secundum rationem non constituit rem abstractam secundum esse neque eam a causa agente separat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX4","text":"Materia prima non est principium increatum Deo ex aequo coordinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX5","text":"Creatio materiae non significat productionem materiae nudae sine forma, sed causalitatem divinam totius eius esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX6","text":"Exemplaria non sunt species subsistentes extra Deum neque universalia separata a singularibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX7","text":"Causalitas finalis divina non procedit ex indigentia, utilitate vel acquisitione divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8","text":"Distinctio causae efficientis et finalis in Deo non inducit prius et posterius reale in primo principio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D1","text":"Omne ens quod non est ipsum esse subsistens ab uno primo ente causatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A1","CH_GGVC_P_36:A2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","CH_GGVC_P_36:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D2","text":"Materia prima, licet pura potentia secundum suam rationem, ab universali causa entium creatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A5","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D3","text":"Materia prima creatur ut pars compositi actualis et non ut ens separatim creatum in pura potentialitate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","text":"Multiplicitas idearum est multiplicitas respectuum participationis creaturae, non multiplicitas realium formarum in Deo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D5","text":"Similitudo creaturae ad Deum est repraesentativa rationis divinae, non aequalitas naturae vel identitas speciei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D6","text":"Universale intellectum ex singularibus abstrahi potest sine subsistentia universalis extra singularia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D7","text":"Omnis appetitio boni, etiam naturalis et cognitione carens, ad Deum ut finem ordinate tendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A10","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D8","text":"Unitas primi principii compatitur pluralitatem rationum causalium, quia pluralitas est in ordine intellectus nostri, non in re divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SD1","text":"Causalitas divina occupat totum campum entis: originem esse, determinatio formalis, communicatio boni et ordinatio ad finem ab eodem principio dependent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:D1","CH_GGVC_P_36:D2","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D7","CH_GGVC_P_36:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2","text":"Quaestio de causis rerum transfertur a mutationibus intra ens ad dependentiam ipsius entis secundum omnem gradum perfectionis et potentialitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A5","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6","CH_GGVC_P_36:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3","text":"Diversitas creaturarum non minuit unitatem causae primae, quia diversae participationes unius esse et bonitatis constituunt gradus entium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","CH_GGVC_P_36:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SD4","text":"Teleologia universalis non requirit cognitionem explicitam Dei in rebus, quia ratio finis fundatur in participatione boni, non in conscientia finis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A10","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12","CH_GGVC_P_36:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX1","text":"Non datur esse creatum quod causaliter autonomum sit ab ipso esse subsistente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX2","text":"Non datur potentia prima quae extra causalitatem perfectionis primae subsistat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX3","text":"Non datur determinatio formarum quae ultimam rationem sui ordinis extra sapientiam divinam habeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX4","text":"Non datur universale separatum quod simul sit obiectum scientiae et exemplar ontologicum singularium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX5","text":"Non datur finis ultimus rerum qui sit alienus a bonitate divina vel in divino defectu fundatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX1","text":"Nulla regio ontologica neutra manet inter Deum et creaturam, quia quidquid quocumque modo ad esse pertinet sub causalitate universali cadit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX2","text":"Dualismus ultimus inter actum divinum et potentiam materialem excluditur, quia principium passivum ipsum effectus primi principii activi est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX3","text":"Finis rerum non potest consistere in autorealizatione divina neque in cognitione creaturarum explicita, sed in communicatione et participatione bonitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS1","text":"Esse per participationem → dependentia ab esse per essentiam → causalitas universalis omnium entium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS2","text":"Causalitas entis inquantum ens → distinctio ab alteratione particulari → inclusio materiae primae intra creationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS3","text":"Determinatio formarum naturalium → requisitum exemplar → rationes rerum in sapientia divina → exclusio exemplarium separatorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS4","text":"Actio determinata → finis → communicatio bonitatis primi agentis → perfectio creaturae ut similitudo divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS5","text":"Efficere, exemplare et finalizare → distinctio secundum rationem → unitas realis primi principii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF1","text":"Ens participatum → primum esse subsistens → causalitas efficiens universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF2","text":"Causalitas universalis → imminutio privilegii materiae → creatio materiae primae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF3","text":"Formae determinatae → sapientia ordinans → ideae divinae ut exemplaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF4","text":"Idea divina → repraesentatio creaturalis → recusatio formarum et universalium separatorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF5","text":"Bonum participatum → appetitus creaturae → bonitas divina ut finis → unitas causarum in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME1","text":"Ens non amplius classificatur solum per genera, formas aut motus, sed per modum participationis esse et dependentiae causalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME2","text":"Creatio reclassificatur ut emanatio universalis essendi, non ut species mutationis quae subiectum praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME3","text":"Materia prima reclassificatur ex principio contrario Deo in effectum imperfectum causae perfectissimae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME4","text":"Idea reclassificatur ex re separata in ratione divina existente respectu creaturarum participabilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME5","text":"Appetitus boni reclassificatur ex actu necessario cognitivo in structuram universalem ordinationis rerum ad bonitatem divinam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus statuit Deum esse causam efficientem, exemplarem et finalem omnium entium, materia prima inclusa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT2","text":"Structural — Ratio participationis ordinat ens creatum, materiam, formas et bonum sub unica relatione dependentiae ad primum principium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur mutando genus quaestionis: a definitione ad consequentiam participationis, a fieri particulari ad emanationem universalem, ab abstractione intellectus ad modum essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Causalitas divina fundatur in esse et ordine perfectionis, non in successione temporali neque in prioritate reali inter rationes causales divinas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de esse subsistente, participatione et causalitate essentiali sufficiunt ad conclusionem quod omne ens creatum a Deo dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter emanationem universalem et fieri particulare sufficit ad materiam primam intra ambitum creationis includendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT3","text":"Axiomata de exemplari et sapientia divina explicant determinationem formarum, sed relatio precisa inter pluralitatem idearum et simplicitatem divinam hic per respectus affirmatur potius quam ulterius explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT4","text":"Axiomata teleologica systema claudunt, quia bonum participatum simul rationem finis creaturae et rationem communicationis divinae constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in transitu ab eo quod ens participatum est ad necessitatem causae ab eo cui esse essentialiter convenit, quia haec regula causalitatis est principium portans et non intra quaestionem independententer probatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT6","text":"Tensionem moderatur distinctio inter rationes causales multas et unitatem realem divinam, sed haec distinctio postulat ne ordo intellectus nostri in compositionem realem primi principii transferatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161337941007Z_7bd22745","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 44","source_sha256":"f4d322db39e719800d9e2006e1648807ff2a98c6055bd56c534b2e89733589c9","sha256":"7927bef48929cf7f0e10d31a5904284299c049c0bbb9cb3b89088d85a2d8a18b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:13:37.942062+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS1","text":"The question investigates whether every being, including prime matter, proceeds from God as from an efficient, exemplary, and final cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS2","text":"The argument begins from the distinction between being through essence and being through participation, so as to infer the dependence of all beings upon the first being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3","text":"The universal production of being is distinguished from particular change, so that prime matter, which cannot come to be particularly, is not exempted from universal emanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS4","text":"The determination of created forms is referred back to divine wisdom, such that exemplars are ideas in God, not separate things outside God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AS5","text":"The universal end of things is posited as divine goodness communicated and participated, whence efficient, exemplary, and final causality are formally distinguished in one first principle, but not really divided.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A1","text":"God is subsistent being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A2","text":"Subsistent being itself can be only one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","text":"Every being other than God participates in being and is not its own being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A4","text":"What belongs through participation is caused by that to which it belongs essentially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A5","text":"The cause of beings insofar as they are beings causes whatever pertains in any way to their being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A6","text":"Emanation from the universal principle of being is not particular coming-to-be from a subject into a form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A7","text":"The first passive principle, as imperfect, is caused by the first active and most perfect principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","text":"The determinate form of an effect requires an exemplar that determines the form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A9","text":"The exemplary ideas of all things are in divine wisdom and do not really differ from the divine essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A10","text":"Every agent acts for an end; otherwise, a determinate effect would follow only accidentally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","text":"The first agent does not act in order to acquire an end, but in order to communicate its perfection or goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A12","text":"Every created good is a participation in the likeness of divine goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:A13","text":"God is the efficient, exemplary, and final cause of all things, although these notions of causality are distinguished in an order within our intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX1","text":"Relation to a cause does not belong to the notion of being simply, but participated being cannot exist without causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX2","text":"Necessity of being does not exclude causality, because a necessary thing can have a cause of its necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX3","text":"Mathematical abstraction according to notion does not constitute a thing abstract according to being, nor does it separate it from an agent cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX4","text":"Prime matter is not an uncreated principle coordinated with God as an equal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX5","text":"The creation of matter does not signify the production of bare matter without form, but the divine causality of its whole being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX6","text":"Exemplars are not subsisting species outside God, nor universals separated from singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX7","text":"Divine final causality does not proceed from divine need, utility, or acquisition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8","text":"The distinction of efficient and final cause in God does not introduce a real before and after in the first principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D1","text":"Every being that is not subsistent being itself is caused by one first being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A1","CH_GGVC_P_36:A2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","CH_GGVC_P_36:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D2","text":"Prime matter, although it is pure potency according to its notion, is created by the universal cause of beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A5","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D3","text":"Prime matter is created as a part of an actual composite and not as a being created separately in pure potentiality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","text":"The multiplicity of ideas is a multiplicity of relations of the creature's participation, not a multiplicity of real forms in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D5","text":"The creature's likeness to God is representative of the divine idea, not equality of nature or identity of species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D6","text":"A universal understood can be abstracted from singulars without the subsistence of a universal outside singulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D7","text":"Every appetite for the good, even a natural one lacking cognition, tends in an ordered way toward God as end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A10","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:D8","text":"The unity of the first principle is compatible with a plurality of causal notions, because the plurality is in the order of our intellect, not in the divine reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SD1","text":"Divine causality occupies the whole field of being: the origin of being, formal determination, communication of good, and ordering to an end depend on the same principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:D1","CH_GGVC_P_36:D2","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D7","CH_GGVC_P_36:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2","text":"The question of the causes of things is transferred from changes within being to the dependence of being itself according to every degree of perfection and potentiality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A5","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6","CH_GGVC_P_36:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3","text":"The diversity of creatures does not diminish the unity of the first cause, because diverse participations in one being and goodness constitute the grades of beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","CH_GGVC_P_36:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SD4","text":"Universal teleology does not require explicit cognition of God in things, because the notion of end is founded on participation in the good, not on consciousness of the end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A10","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12","CH_GGVC_P_36:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX1","text":"There is no created being that is causally autonomous from subsistent being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX2","text":"There is no first potency that subsists outside the causality of first perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX3","text":"There is no determination of forms that has the ultimate reason for its order outside divine wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX4","text":"There is no separate universal that is at once an object of knowledge and an ontological exemplar of singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX5","text":"There is no ultimate end of things that is alien to divine goodness or founded upon a divine defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX1","text":"No ontologically neutral region remains between God and creature, because whatever pertains in any way to being falls under universal causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX2","text":"An ultimate dualism between divine act and material potency is excluded, because the passive principle itself is an effect of the first active principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX3","text":"The end of things cannot consist in divine self-realization or in the explicit cognition of creatures, but in the communication and participation of goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS1","text":"Being through participation → dependence on being through essence → universal causality of all beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS2","text":"Causality of being insofar as it is being → distinction from particular alteration → inclusion of prime matter within creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS3","text":"Determination of natural forms → required exemplar → ideas of things in divine wisdom → exclusion of separate exemplars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS4","text":"Determinate action → end → communication of the goodness of the first agent → perfection of the creature as divine likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:FGS5","text":"To effect, exemplify, and bring to an end → distinction according to notion → real unity of the first principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF1","text":"Participated being → first subsistent being → universal efficient causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF2","text":"Universal causality → removal of matter's privilege → creation of prime matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF3","text":"Determinate forms → ordering wisdom → divine ideas as exemplars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF4","text":"Divine idea → creaturely representation → rejection of separate forms and universals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:AF5","text":"Participated good → creaturely appetite → divine goodness as end → unity of causes in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME1","text":"Being is no longer classified solely through genera, forms, or motions, but through the mode of participation in being and causal dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME2","text":"Creation is reclassified as universal emanation of being, not as a species of change that presupposes a subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME3","text":"Prime matter is reclassified from a principle contrary to God into an imperfect effect of the most perfect cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME4","text":"Idea is reclassified from a separate thing into that which exists in the divine notion with respect to participable creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ME5","text":"The appetite for the good is reclassified from a necessarily cognitive act into a universal structure of the ordering of things toward divine goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text establishes that God is the efficient, exemplary, and final cause of all beings, including prime matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT2","text":"Structural — The notion of participation orders created being, matter, forms, and good under a single relation of dependence upon the first principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The objections are resolved by changing the kind of question: from definition to the consequence of participation, from particular coming-to-be to universal emanation, from the abstraction of the intellect to the mode of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Divine causality is founded in being and the order of perfection, not in temporal succession nor in real priority among divine causal notions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning subsistent being, participation, and essential causality suffice for the conclusion that every created being depends on God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT2","text":"The distinction between universal emanation and particular coming-to-be suffices to include prime matter within the scope of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT3","text":"The axioms concerning the exemplar and divine wisdom explain the determination of forms, but the precise relation between the plurality of ideas and divine simplicity is here affirmed through relations rather than further explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT4","text":"The teleological axioms close the system, because participated good simultaneously constitutes the notion of the creature's end and the notion of divine communication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains in the transition from what is participated being to the necessity of a cause from that to which being belongs essentially, because this rule of causality is a load-bearing principle and is not independently proved within the question.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT6","text":"The distinction between many causal notions and real divine unity moderates the tension, but this distinction requires that the order of our intellect not be transferred into the real composition of the first principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_36:P0083","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_36@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_36:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 45","title":"First Part · Question 44","context":"Chapter 45","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 44"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 44","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 45","order":46,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_37"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_37@R001","sha256":"c2c713a7dbbc29e5e622bd23e2b2cbd0a9a6eeb5d4f35c224ee2e255f34a48fb","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS1","text":"Quaestio modum emanationis universi entis a primo principio determinat secundum rationem, possibilitatem, realitatem, subiectum, agentem, ordinem trinitarium, repraesentationem et habitudinem ad naturam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS2","text":"Creatio est productio totius esse ex nullo ente praesupposito, a solo Deo, communiter quidem toti Trinitati sed secundum ordinem processionum personalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, reconstructiva et polemica, quia categorias causalitatis particularis corrigit antequam eas ad primam emanationem applicet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS4","text":"Motus initialis a distinctione emanationis particularis et universalis procedit ad necessitatem productionis ex nihilo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS5","text":"Deinde creatio a mutatione eximitur et in relationem realem creaturae ad principium sui esse resolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS6","text":"Ex ratione esse distribuuntur subiectum creationis et potestas creandi: subsistentia proprie creantur, solus autem Deus esse absolute producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS7","text":"Argumentatio clauditur distinctione operationis divinae communis, ordinis personalis, vestigii creati et operationis naturalis creationem praesupponentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","text":"Creatio nominat emanationem totius esse a causa universali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A2","text":"Nihil in entibus esse potest quod non sit a Deo, causa universali totius esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","text":"Productio totius esse nullum ens tamquam materiam vel subiectum praesupponere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A4","text":"Mutatio requirit aliquid idem quod aliter se habeat prius et posterius, actu vel saltem potentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","text":"Motu ab actione et passione remoto, remanent relationes causae et effectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","text":"Creatio passive accepta est relatio realis creaturae ad Creatorem ut principium sui esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A7","text":"Denominatio creandi relationem ad Creatorem cum novitate seu inceptione importat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A8","text":"Illud proprie fit et creatur cui proprie convenit esse, id est subsistens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A9","text":"Formae et accidentia non sunt subsistentia, sed principia quibus aliquid est vel tale est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","text":"Effectus universaliores ad causas universaliores et priores reducuntur; esse absolute est effectus universalissimus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A11","text":"Causa instrumentalis actionem causae principalis participat solum operando dispositive per aliquid sibi proprium in subiecto praesupposito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A12","text":"Productio ex nulla potentia praesupposita requirit virtutem infinitam, qua nulla creatura simpliciter pollet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A13","text":"Creare Deo convenit secundum esse divinum, quod est essentia tribus personis communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A14","text":"Processiones Verbi et Amoris sunt rationes productionis creaturarum, quatenus scientiam et voluntatem essentiales includunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A15","text":"Effectus causam repraesentat vel per vestigium causalitatis vel per imaginem similitudinis formalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A16","text":"Quaelibet creatura subsistentiam, determinationem formalem et ordinem ad aliud habet; creatura rationalis insuper verbo intellectus et amore voluntatis operatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A17","text":"Agens naturale compositum ex principiis creatis producit, dum forma non per se fit sed in composito actuari incipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0151","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX1","text":"Creatio non est productio entis particularis ex ente particulari praesupposito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX2","text":"Nihilum non est materia, subiectum aut causa ex qua ens constituatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX3","text":"Principium «ex nihilo nihil fieri» causalitatem particularem circumscribit, non primam emanationem ab universali principio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX4","text":"Creatio non est motus, mutatio aut pertransitus per medium inter nihilum et ens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX5","text":"Creatio non est tertium quod inter Creatorem et creaturam subsistat neque relationem ulteriorem ad sui constitutionem requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX6","text":"Formae, accidentia et alia non subsistentia non creantur proprie, sed concreantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX7","text":"Nulla creatura creare potest neque propria virtute neque instrumentaliter sive per ministerium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX8","text":"Creatio non est actio uni personae divinae propria vel inter personas divisa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX9","text":"Vestigium non est imago formae causae nec plenam rationem causae repraesentat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX10","text":"Formae naturales neque actu latentes in materia neque per creationem ab agente separato singulis generationibus infunduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX11","text":"Creatio operibus naturae non admiscetur, et tamen effectus naturales propter principia creata creaturae esse non desinunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","text":"«Ex nihilo» vel ordinem ad non esse praecedens significat vel omnem habitudinem causae materialis negat; neutro sensu nihilum in causam convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D2","text":"Si Deus causa universalis totius esse est, creatio non tantum possibilis sed necessaria est ad universalitatem causalitatis divinae servandam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A2","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D3","text":"Quia creatio nullum subiectum mutabile praesupponit, fieri et factum esse in ea simul sunt, iar «fieri» dependentiam ab alio potius quam processum successivum significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_37:A4","CH_GGVC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D4","text":"Actio creandi in Deo est ipsa essentia cum relatione ad creaturam secundum rationem, dum creatio in creatura est relatio realis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_37:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D5","text":"Creatura, postquam est, relationis creationis subiectum est, sed non per totam durationem dicitur creari, quia nomen inceptionem includit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_37:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D6","text":"Esse est ratio obiectiva creationis, sed subiectum proprie creatum est subsistens, quod cum omnibus suis principiis simul producitur; formae et accidentia tantum concreantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_37:A8","CH_GGVC_P_37:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D7","text":"Esse absolute, nullo subiecto disposito, causari non potest a causa secunda; ideo creatio soli causae primae infinitae competit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A11","CH_GGVC_P_37:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D8","text":"Una virtus creandi tribus personis communis est, sed ordinate attribuitur Patri ut principio non de principio, Filio ut principio de principio, et Spiritui Sancto ut ab utroque procedenti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A13","CH_GGVC_P_37:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D9","text":"Omnis creatura Trinitatem vestigialiter repraesentat per substantiam, formam et ordinem; rationalis creatura eam etiam per modum imaginis repraesentat in verbo et amore.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A15","CH_GGVC_P_37:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D10","text":"Operatio naturalis creationem principiorum praesupponit et compositum producit, non novam productionem totius esse ex nihilo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_37:A9","CH_GGVC_P_37:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD1","text":"Ordo causalitatis secundum amplitudinem effectus constituitur: causae particulares determinant ens iam datum, causa autem universalis ipsum esse producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D2","CH_GGVC_P_37:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2","text":"Creatio non est eventus intra ordinem entium, sed habitudo ontologica qua totus ordo entium a principio universali dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","CH_GGVC_P_37:D3","CH_GGVC_P_37:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD3","text":"Causalitas creata realis manet, sed intra agrum iam creatum operatur; nullo gradu ad productionem esse absolute ascendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D7","CH_GGVC_P_37:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD4","text":"Unitas operationis divinae ad extra cum ordine personali componitur, quia essentia communis causat, processiones autem rationem et ordinem causalitatis determinant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD5","text":"Mundus creatus simul est ordo causaliter activus et ordo repraesentativus: natura effectus secundarios producit, dum structura cuiusque creaturae principium trinitarium vestigialiter refert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D9","CH_GGVC_P_37:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit campum entis neutrum in quo Deus et creatura tamquam causae eiusdem ordinis operarentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX2","text":"Categoriae motus, successionis et subiecti non possunt univoce a mutatione particulari ad originem totius esse transferri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX3","text":"Nulla materia, potentia vel natura ontologice independens causalitati divinae substrata esse potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX4","text":"Participatio essendi creaturae potestatem producendi esse absolute non confert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX5","text":"Relatio Creatoris ad creaturam non est realiter symmetrica relationi creaturae ad Creatorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX6","text":"Distinctio personarum divinarum distinctionem trium operationum creatricium requirere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX7","text":"Forma non potest tamquam res subsistens inter materiam, compositum et agentem reificari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX1","text":"Inter Creatorem et creaturam nullum tertium ontologicum admittitur quod productionem esse mediet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX2","text":"Creaturae omnis forma sui fundationis absolutae praecluditur, quia etiam principia quibus agit esse participant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX3","text":"Potestas creandi neque horizontaliter distribui neque ministerialiter delegari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX4","text":"Inter nihilum et ens nullum intervallum, medium aut processum reale constitui potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX5","text":"Vestigium creatum plenam cognitionem distinctionum personalium ex sola similitudine effectus praebere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0131","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS1","text":"Schema causale est: effectus particularis → causa particularis cum subiecto praesupposito; effectus universalissimus → causa prima universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS2","text":"Ordo definitionis est: totum esse producitur → nullum ens praesupponitur → materia negatur → creatio ex nihilo constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS3","text":"Ordo categoricus est: nullum subiectum prius → nulla mutatio realis → sola habitudo causae et effectus → relatio creationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A4","CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS4","text":"Ordo subiecti est: esse proprie convenit subsistenti → subsistens proprie creatur → formae et accidentia concreantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A8","CH_GGVC_P_37:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS5","text":"Clausura agentis est: esse absolute est effectus proprius causae primae → instrumentum nullum subiectum disponere potest → nulla creatura creat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A11","CH_GGVC_P_37:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS6","text":"Schema trinitarium est: essentia communis → una virtus creandi → processiones Verbi et Amoris → ordo personalis attributionum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A13","CH_GGVC_P_37:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS7","text":"Schema repraesentationis est: causalitas communis → vestigium in substantia, forma et ordine; similitudo actuum spiritualium → imago in intellectu et voluntate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A15","CH_GGVC_P_37:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS8","text":"Schema naturae est: principia creata → actio naturalis in materia → compositum productum → forma actuata per accidens → nulla creatio admixta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A9","CH_GGVC_P_37:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0151","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AF1","text":"Emanatio particularis et universalis distinguuntur → creatio ex nihilo definitur → possibilitas in necessitatem causalitatis universalis convertitur → mutatio in relationem resolvitur → subsistens ut subiectum assignatur → soli Deo actio reservatur → communitas trinitaria cum ordine personali componitur → effectus ut vestigium vel imago legitur → creatio ab operatione naturae distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME1","text":"Causae non amplius sola efficientia localis, sed amplitudine effectus quem producunt classificari possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME2","text":"«Ex nihilo» ex imagine materiae vel distantiae transfertur ad negationem omnis entis praesuppositi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME3","text":"Creatio ex genere mutationum in genus relationis ontologicae reponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME4","text":"Distinctio inter subsistens et principium quo aliquid est determinat quae proprie creentur et quae tantum concreentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME5","text":"Causalitas secundaria agnoscitur intra ordinem entium, sed ab origine ipsius esse absolute separatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME6","text":"Oppositio inter operationem divinam communem et attributionem personalem solvitur distinctione essentiae, processionis et appropriationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME7","text":"Repraesentatio creaturae bifariam describitur, ut vestigium causalitatis omnibus commune ab imagine spirituali rationalium distinguatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME8","text":"Creatio et natura non ut actiones concurrentes, sed ut fundamentum ontologicum et operatio ex principiis fundatis ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT1","text":"Surface — Determinantur significatio creationis, subiectum eius, agens et praesentia eius in operibus naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT2","text":"Structural — Universitas effectus, praesuppositio subiecti et subsistentia ordinant distributionem causalitatis, relationis et productionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur detegendo translationem illicitam categoriarum causalitatis particularis ad productionem universalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Esse creatum constituitur ut dependentia realis sine mutatione, cum simultaneitate fieri et factum esse atque cum ratione novitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad octo determinationes quaestionis ex una distinctione inter productionem totius esse et mutationem entis particularis restituendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT2","text":"Firmissima compages est nexus inter universalitatem effectus, universalitatem causae et exclusionem omnis subiecti praesuppositi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT3","text":"Distinctio inter mutationem et relationem cohaeret cum definitione creationis, quia idem principium excludit tum materiam priorem tum successionem realem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT4","text":"Nexus inter ordinem ad non esse praecedens et simplicem negationem materiae dupliciter traditur, nec hic plene determinatur utrum novitas sit temporalis an tantum secundum intellectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT5","text":"Relatio creationis creaturam iam existentem ut subiectum requirit, quamvis eadem creatura per hanc relationem ad principium sui esse referatur; distinctio prioritatis subiecti et prioritatis obiecti commissuram sustinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT6","text":"Probatio virtutis infinitae distinctionem requirit inter medium infinitum, quod negatur, et improportionem nullius potentiae ad potentiam, quae ad magnitudinem virtutis adhibetur; haec distinctio implicita manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0097","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT7","text":"Communitas operationis creatricis et causalitas processionum personalium componuntur per distinctionem essentiae communis et rationum productionis, sed sensus causalitatis personalis hac distinctione continendus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0114","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT8","text":"Vestigium Trinitatis affirmatur, dum inquisitio plena Trinitatis ex creaturis negatur; cohaerentia pendet a distinctione vestigii causalitatis, imaginis et appropriationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0131","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT9","text":"Restitutio motum verum textus servat: universalitas causae → ex nihilo → relatio → subsistentia → exclusivitas divina → ordo trinitarius → repraesentatio → praesuppositio creationis in natura.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161410305792Z_e655b5a4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 45","source_sha256":"c2c713a7dbbc29e5e622bd23e2b2cbd0a9a6eeb5d4f35c224ee2e255f34a48fb","sha256":"c74b1294ec4f489ad35ae47e1c38c63824859b6e1d447ba27d0baa6e36ce52a8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:14:10.306737+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS1","text":"The question determines the mode of the emanation of universal being from the first principle according to its account, possibility, reality, subject, agent, Trinitarian order, representation, and relation to nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS2","text":"Creation is the production of the whole of being from no presupposed being, by God alone, indeed common to the whole Trinity but according to the order of the personal processions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, reconstructive, and polemical, because it corrects the categories of particular causality before applying them to the first emanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS4","text":"The initial movement proceeds from the distinction between particular and universal emanation to the necessity of production from nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS5","text":"Then creation is exempted from change and resolved into the real relation of the creature to the principle of its being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS6","text":"From the account of being are distributed the subject of creation and the power to create: subsistents are properly created, whereas God alone produces being absolutely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AS7","text":"The argumentation closes with the distinction of the common divine operation, personal order, created vestige, and natural operation presupposing creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","text":"Creation names the emanation of the whole of being from a universal cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A2","text":"Nothing can be in beings that is not from God, the universal cause of the whole of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","text":"The production of the whole of being cannot presuppose any being as matter or subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A4","text":"Change requires something identical that is disposed otherwise before and after, actually or at least potentially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","text":"When motion is removed from action and passion, the relations of cause and effect remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","text":"Creation, taken passively, is the real relation of the creature to the Creator as the principle of its being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A7","text":"The designation of being created imports a relation to the Creator together with novelty or inception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A8","text":"That is properly made and created to which being properly belongs, that is, a subsistent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A9","text":"Forms and accidents are not subsistents, but principles by which something is or is such.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","text":"More universal effects are reduced to more universal and prior causes; being absolutely is the most universal effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A11","text":"An instrumental cause participates in the action of the principal cause only by operating dispositively through something proper to itself in a presupposed subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A12","text":"Production from no presupposed potency requires an infinite power, which no creature simply possesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A13","text":"To create belongs to God according to the divine being, which is the essence common to the three persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A14","text":"The processions of Word and Love are accounts of the production of creatures, insofar as they include essential knowledge and will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A15","text":"The effect represents the cause either through a vestige of causality or through an image of formal likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A16","text":"Every creature has subsistence, formal determination, and order to another; the rational creature moreover operates by the word of intellect and the love of will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:A17","text":"A natural agent, composed of created principles, produces, while form is not made through itself but begins to be actualized in the composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0151","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX1","text":"Creation is not the production of a particular being from a presupposed particular being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX2","text":"Nothingness is not matter, a subject, or a cause from which a being is constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX3","text":"The principle «ex nihilo nihil fieri» circumscribes particular causality, not the first emanation from the universal principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX4","text":"Creation is not motion, change, or passage through an intermediary between nothingness and being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX5","text":"Creation is not a third thing subsisting between Creator and creature, nor does it require a further relation for its constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX6","text":"Forms, accidents, and other non-subsistents are not properly created, but co-created.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX7","text":"No creature can create, neither by its own power nor instrumentally or through ministry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX8","text":"Creation is not an action proper to one divine person or divided among the persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX9","text":"A vestige is not an image of the form of the cause, nor does it represent the full account of the cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX10","text":"Natural forms neither lie actually hidden in matter nor are infused by creation from a separate agent in individual generations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:NX11","text":"Creation is not mixed into the works of nature, and yet natural effects do not cease to be creatures by reason of created principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","text":"«Ex nihilo» either signifies an order to preceding non-being or denies every relation of material cause; in neither sense is nothingness converted into a cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D2","text":"If God is the universal cause of the whole of being, creation is not only possible but necessary for preserving the universality of divine causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A2","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D3","text":"Because creation presupposes no mutable subject, coming-to-be and having-been-made are simultaneous in it, and «fieri» signifies dependence on another rather than a successive process.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_37:A4","CH_GGVC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D4","text":"The action of creating in God is the essence itself with a relation to the creature according to reason, whereas creation in the creature is a real relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_37:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D5","text":"Once it exists, the creature is the subject of the relation of creation, but it is not said to be created throughout its entire duration, because the name includes inception.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_37:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D6","text":"Being is the objective account of creation, but the properly created subject is the subsistent, which is produced simultaneously with all its principles; forms and accidents are only co-created.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_37:A8","CH_GGVC_P_37:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D7","text":"Being absolutely, with no subject disposed, cannot be caused by a secondary cause; therefore creation belongs to the first infinite cause alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A11","CH_GGVC_P_37:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D8","text":"One power of creating is common to the three persons, but it is orderly attributed to the Father as principle not from a principle, to the Son as principle from a principle, and to the Holy Spirit as proceeding from both.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A13","CH_GGVC_P_37:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D9","text":"Every creature represents the Trinity vestigially through substance, form, and order; the rational creature also represents it by way of image in word and love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A15","CH_GGVC_P_37:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:D10","text":"Natural operation presupposes the creation of principles and produces the composite, not a new production of the whole of being from nothing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_37:A9","CH_GGVC_P_37:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD1","text":"The order of causality is constituted according to the scope of the effect: particular causes determine an already given being, whereas the universal cause produces being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D2","CH_GGVC_P_37:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2","text":"Creation is not an event within the order of beings, but the ontological relation by which the whole order of beings depends on the universal principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","CH_GGVC_P_37:D3","CH_GGVC_P_37:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD3","text":"Created causality remains real, but operates within the already created field; at no level does it rise to the production of being absolutely.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D7","CH_GGVC_P_37:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD4","text":"The unity of divine operation ad extra is combined with personal order, because the common essence causes, whereas the processions determine the account and order of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SD5","text":"The created world is at once a causally active order and a representative order: nature produces secondary effects, while the structure of each creature vestigially refers to the Trinitarian principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D9","CH_GGVC_P_37:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX1","text":"The system excludes a neutral field of being in which God and creature would operate as causes of the same order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX2","text":"The categories of motion, succession, and subject cannot be transferred univocally from particular change to the origin of the whole of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX3","text":"No matter, potency, or nature ontologically independent of divine causality can underlie it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX4","text":"The creature's participation in being does not confer the power to produce being absolutely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX5","text":"The relation of the Creator to the creature is not really symmetrical with the relation of the creature to the Creator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX6","text":"The distinction of the divine persons cannot require the distinction of three creative operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX7","text":"Form cannot be reified as a subsisting thing between matter, composite, and agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX1","text":"Between Creator and creature no third ontological entity is admitted that mediates the production of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX2","text":"Every form of absolute self-foundation is precluded to the creature, because even the principles by which it acts participate in being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX3","text":"The power to create can neither be distributed horizontally nor delegated ministerially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX4","text":"Between nothingness and being no interval, intermediary, or real process can be constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX5","text":"The created vestige cannot provide full knowledge of the personal distinctions from the likeness of the effect alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0131","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS1","text":"The causal schema is: particular effect → particular cause with a presupposed subject; most universal effect → universal first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS2","text":"The order of definition is: the whole of being is produced → no being is presupposed → matter is denied → creation from nothing is constituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS3","text":"The categorical order is: no prior subject → no real change → only the relation of cause and effect → relation of creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A4","CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS4","text":"The order of the subject is: being properly belongs to a subsistent → a subsistent is properly created → forms and accidents are co-created.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A8","CH_GGVC_P_37:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS5","text":"The closure concerning the agent is: being absolutely is the proper effect of the first cause → no instrument can dispose a subject → no creature creates.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A11","CH_GGVC_P_37:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS6","text":"The Trinitarian schema is: common essence → one power of creating → processions of Word and Love → personal order of attributions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A13","CH_GGVC_P_37:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS7","text":"The schema of representation is: common causality → vestige in substance, form, and order; likeness of spiritual acts → image in intellect and will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A15","CH_GGVC_P_37:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:FGS8","text":"The schema of nature is: created principles → natural action in matter → produced composite → form actualized per accidens → no creation mixed in.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A9","CH_GGVC_P_37:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0151","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:AF1","text":"Particular and universal emanation are distinguished → creation from nothing is defined → possibility is converted into the necessity of universal causality → change is resolved into relation → the subsistent is assigned as subject → action is reserved to God alone → Trinitarian commonality is combined with personal order → the effect is read as vestige or image → creation is distinguished from the operation of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME1","text":"Causes can no longer be classified by local efficiency alone, but by the scope of the effect they produce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME2","text":"«Ex nihilo» is transferred from the image of matter or distance to the negation of every presupposed being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME3","text":"Creation is relocated from the genus of changes to the genus of ontological relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME4","text":"The distinction between a subsistent and the principle by which something is determines what is properly created and what is only co-created.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME5","text":"Secondary causality is acknowledged within the order of beings, but separated from the origin of being itself absolutely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME6","text":"The opposition between common divine operation and personal attribution is resolved by the distinction of essence, procession, and appropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME7","text":"The representation of the creature is described in two ways, so that the vestige of causality common to all is distinguished from the spiritual image of rational creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ME8","text":"Creation and nature are ordered not as concurrent actions, but as ontological foundation and operation from founded principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT1","text":"Surface — The meaning of creation, its subject, agent, and its presence in the works of nature are determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT2","text":"Structural — The universality of the effect, the presupposition of a subject, and subsistence order the distribution of causality, relation, and production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved by detecting the illicit transfer of the categories of particular causality to universal production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Created being is constituted as real dependence without change, with the simultaneity of coming-to-be and having-been-made and with the account of novelty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore the eight determinations of the question from one distinction between the production of the whole of being and the change of a particular being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT2","text":"The strongest framework is the nexus between the universality of the effect, the universality of the cause, and the exclusion of every presupposed subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT3","text":"The distinction between change and relation coheres with the definition of creation, because the same principle excludes both prior matter and real succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT4","text":"The nexus between order to preceding non-being and the simple negation of matter is conveyed in two ways, nor is it fully determined here whether novelty is temporal or only according to intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT5","text":"The relation of creation requires the already existing creature as subject, although the same creature is referred through this relation to the principle of its being; the distinction between priority of subject and priority of object sustains the juncture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT6","text":"The proof of infinite power requires a distinction between an infinite intermediary, which is denied, and the disproportion of no potency to potency, which is employed for the magnitude of power; this distinction remains implicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0097","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT7","text":"The commonality of creative operation and the causality of the personal processions are combined through the distinction between common essence and accounts of production, but the sense of personal causality must be contained by this distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0109","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0113","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0114","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT8","text":"A vestige of the Trinity is affirmed, while full inquiry into the Trinity from creatures is denied; coherence depends on the distinction among vestige of causality, image, and appropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0127","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0131","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the text's true movement: universality of cause → ex nihilo → relation → subsistence → divine exclusivity → Trinitarian order → representation → presupposition of creation in nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_37:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_37@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_37:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 46","title":"First Part · Question 45","context":"Chapter 46","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 45"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 45","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 46","order":47,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_38"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_38@R001","sha256":"dc9a6328be00cdef168aa1ff36c9bc60b5cc46220207221d7972f34979c6786f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS1","text":"Quaeritur utrum universitas creaturarum initium durationis habuerit, utrum hoc initium ratione demonstrari possit, et quo sensu creatio facta sit «in principio».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS2","text":"Nihil praeter Deum ab aeterno fuit, sed haec mundi novitas sola fide tenetur, non demonstratione naturali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, dialectico-polemica et reconstructiva: objectiones ex physicis praesuppositionibus resolvit, fines demonstrationis statuit, deinde formulam revelatam metaphysice explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS4","text":"Argumenta pro aeternitate mundi a materia, motu, tempore et causalitate naturali ad voluntatem divinam et creationem non mutativam transferuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS5","text":"Argumenta pro demonstrabili mundi novitate reducuntur ad distinctionem inter causalitatem creativam cognoscibilem et contingentem determinationem voluntatis divinae sola revelatione manifestam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS6","text":"Locutio «in principio» tripliciter explicatur ut aeternitas mundi, dualitas principiorum et mediatio creaturarum spiritualium in prima productione corporalium excludantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A1","text":"Nihil praeter Deum ab aeterno fuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","text":"Voluntas Dei est causa essendi rerum creatarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","text":"Deus absolute necessario nihil vult praeter seipsum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","text":"Effectus agentis voluntarii sequitur formam ab agente praeconceptam et praedefinitam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","text":"Duratio mundi pendet a determinatione voluntatis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","text":"Creatio est productio totius esse rei nullo subiecto praesupposito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","text":"Creatio neque motus neque mutatio neque terminus motus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","text":"Agens universale rem simul cum tempore eius producit, neque materiam aut tempus actioni suae praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A9","text":"Ingenerabilitas et incorruptibilitas excludunt inceptionem per generationem naturalem, non productionem per creationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A10","text":"Principium demonstrationis de re est quod quid est rei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A11","text":"Ratio speciei abstrahit ab hic et nunc.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A12","text":"Voluntas divina circa creaturas naturali ratione investigari non potest, quia creaturae non sunt obiecta absolute necessario volita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A13","text":"Contingens determinatio voluntatis divinae homini per revelationem manifestari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","text":"Aeternitas divina est esse totum simul sine successione, non duratio successiva mundi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A15","text":"Processus infinitus causarum efficientium per se est impossibilis, sed multiplicatio causarum per accidens non eadem impossibilitate excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A16","text":"Tempus non est nisi secundum nunc et a primo nunc incipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","text":"«In principio» designat principium temporis, principium exemplare in Filio et prioritatem primae creationis ante omnem causalitatem creatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A18","text":"Caelum empyreum, materia corporalis, tempus et natura angelica simul creata sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX1","text":"Aeternitas mundi neque ex aeternitate Dei necessario sequitur neque demonstrative probatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX2","text":"Mundi novitas non est conclusio scientiae naturalis vel metaphysicae demonstrativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX3","text":"Rationes Aristotelis pro aeternitate non sunt demonstrationes simpliciter, sed contradictiones secundum quid contra modos impossibiles inceptionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX4","text":"Possibilitas mundi ante eius esse non requirit materiam praeexistentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX5","text":"Incorruptibilitas rei non excludit eius creationem, sed tantum inceptionem secundum generationem naturalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX6","text":"Prima productio mobilis non est mutatio ex statu antecedente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","text":"Ante mundum non fuit vacuum, locus, spatium vel tempus reale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX8","text":"Voluntas divina aeterna neque mutationem antecedentem neque effectum aeternum requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9","text":"Prioritas Dei ad mundum non est prioritas intra tempus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX10","text":"Ex eo quod mundus a Deo factus est non sequitur Deum mundo duratione priorem esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX11","text":"Apud defensores mundi aeterni, «ex nihilo» significat «non de aliquo», non necessario «post nihilum».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX12","text":"Intellectus divinus non incipit agere per deliberationem successivam sicut intellectus humanus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX13","text":"Initia artium, habitationum et ordinum particularium non probant initium totius mundi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX14","text":"Coextensio successiva mundi cum omni tempore non aequaret mundum aeternitati divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX15","text":"Argumenta ex pertransitu infiniti, successione generationum vel multitudine animarum non universaliter demonstrant mundi novitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX16","text":"Creatio «in principio temporis» non significat creationem a primo instanti temporaliter mensuratam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX17","text":"Prima creatio nec duo principia boni et mali nec creaturas spirituales tamquam causas intermedias corporalium admittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D1","text":"Cum Deus creaturas non necessario velit et duratio mundi ex eius voluntate dependeat, mundum semper fuisse non est necessarium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D2","text":"Aeternitas et sufficientia causae voluntariae effectum aeternum non inferunt, quia effectus producitur secundum praedefinitionem voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D3","text":"Argumenta quae omnem inceptionem ad generationem, motum vel mutationem reducunt creationem non attingunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D4","text":"Materia, locus et tempus non possunt tamquam condiciones exteriores adhiberi ad primam creationem impediendam, quia ipsi intra totum productum continentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D5","text":"Ex natura specifica mundi vel rerum mundanarum initium durationis demonstrari non potest, quia principia specifica ab indice temporali abstrahunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A10","CH_GGVC_P_38:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D6","text":"Ex parte causae agentis mundi novitas demonstrari non potest, quia determinatio voluntatis divinae circa creaturas non est rationaliter necessaria, sed revelabilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A12","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","text":"Mundi initium est credibile ex revelatione, non demonstrabile vel scientifice scibile ex principiis naturalibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D5","CH_GGVC_P_38:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D8","text":"Causalitas creativa et initium temporale non sunt eadem ratio; sola dependentia a creatore non excludit dialectice effectum semper a causa dependentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D9","text":"Etiam posita duratione mundi sine principio, mundus Deo non aequaretur, quia successio temporalis et aeternitas tota simul sunt modi durationis diversi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D10","text":"Obiectiones ex infinito praeterito non concludunt universaliter: pertransitus inter duos terminos finitos est finitus, generantes constituunt seriem per accidens, et argumentum ex animabus solum mundum humanum respicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D11","text":"Primus nunc non recipit creationem quasi mensura temporalis, sed est terminus a quo tempus simul cum rebus incipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D12","text":"Triplex sensus «in principio» constituit unam doctrinam: tempus initium habet, omnia per unum principium exemplare fiunt, et prima universitas creatorum nullo creato agente mediante producitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D13","text":"Esse mundi post non esse causam creatricem manifestius indicat; novitas igitur rationem convenientiae manifestativae habet, non necessitatem demonstrativam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","text":"Ratio naturalis cognoscere potest dependentiam mundi a creatore, sed non determinare utrum effectus creatus semper fuerit an initium temporale habuerit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:D5","CH_GGVC_P_38:D6","CH_GGVC_P_38:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD2","text":"Prioritas creatoria Dei est causaliter et aeternaliter ordinans, non positio Dei in tempore antecedente mundum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","text":"Creatio claudit totum ordinem physicum intra effectum: materia, spatium, motus et tempus non sunt condiciones creationis, sed partes ordinis creati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4","text":"Initium temporis est limes originarius successionis, non eventus positus post tempus vacuum vel statum mundi antecedentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A16","CH_GGVC_P_38:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5","text":"Actualis mundi novitas non ex principiis metaphysicis deducitur: metaphysica eius possibilitatem et non-necessitatem tuetur, revelatio autem eius veritatem determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A1","CH_GGVC_P_38:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD6","text":"Exegesis «in principio» simul temporalem, exemplarem et causalem unitatem creationis instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7","text":"Defensio fidei debet limites demonstrationis servare, ne rationes probabiles vel infirmas pro necessariis offerat et ita materiam irrisionis praebeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX1","text":"Non omnis possibilitas fundatur in potentia passiva vel receptaculo materiali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX2","text":"Generatio naturalis non est forma exhaustiva omnis productionis in esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A9","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX3","text":"Non omnis actio voluntaria supponit tempus, mutationem vel condicionem exteriorem exspectatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX4","text":"Sufficientia causae non est convertibilis cum necessitatione naturali effectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX5","text":"Dependentia causalis non includit necessario successionem temporalem causae et effectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D8","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6","text":"Veritas revelata non requirit ut in conclusionem demonstrativam convertatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX7","text":"Ex mutationibus localibus vel ex condicione particularis speciei non licet statum totius creationis universaliter inferre.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX15","CH_GGVC_P_38:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX8","text":"Infinitum temporale, infinitum causale per se et infinitum per accidens non constituunt unam structuram logicam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A15","CH_GGVC_P_38:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX9","text":"Praedicata temporalia de Deo et mundo non accipiuntur secundum unam mensuram durationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX1","text":"Nullum metatempus, spatium vacuum vel receptaculum materiale extra creationem praesto est in quo initium mundi collocetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX2","text":"Nullum principium creatum, malum vel spirituale, cum Deo primam productionem entium participat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:A18","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX3","text":"Nulla via rationalis ex sola essentia mundi vel causalitate Dei transit ad contentum liberum decreti quo mundus initium accepit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX4","text":"Nullus status mundi antecedens est ex quo creatio per mutationem ad primum statum temporalem procedat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:D11","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX5","text":"Nulla communis linea durationis Deum et mundum continet qua eorum prioritas vel aequalitas univoce metiatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX6","text":"Fides non debet certitudinem suam a pseudodemonstrationibus mutuari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS1","text":"Voluntas divina causalis → sola sui necessaria voluntas → contingentia volendi creaturas → effectus secundum praedefinitionem → nulla necessitas mundi aeterni.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_38:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS2","text":"Praesuppositio materiae, motus vel temporis → restrictio ad generationem naturalem et agentem particulare → distinctio creationis et agentis universalis → dissolutio contradictionis circa primum initium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:A9","CH_GGVC_P_38:D3","CH_GGVC_P_38:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS3","text":"Quidditas abstrahens ab hic et nunc → nulla demonstratio ex mundo → voluntas contingens naturaliter inaccessibilis → nulla demonstratio ex causa → revelatio → fides de novitate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A10","CH_GGVC_P_38:A11","CH_GGVC_P_38:A12","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13","CH_GGVC_P_38:D5","CH_GGVC_P_38:D6","CH_GGVC_P_38:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS4","text":"Creatio non mutativa + tempus coproductum + esse temporis secundum nunc → absentia prioris processus → primus nunc ut origo successionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:A16","CH_GGVC_P_38:D11","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS5","text":"«In principio» → initium temporis / exemplar in Filio / prioritas primae creationis → exclusio aeternitatis mundi / dualismi / mediationis creatae → quattuor naturae simul creatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:A18","CH_GGVC_P_38:D12","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS6","text":"Univocatio aeternitatis vel infiniti → distinctio aeternitatis a successione et causarum per se a seriebus per accidens → defectus demonstrationum ex aequalitate, transitu vel regressu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:A15","CH_GGVC_P_38:D9","CH_GGVC_P_38:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AF1","text":"Quaestio de duratione creaturarum → dissolutio necessitatis mundi aeterni → delimitatio demonstrationis → collocatio novitatis in fide → explicatio triplex «in principio».","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AF2","text":"Argumenta ex materia, motu, tempore et causa aeterna → detectio praesuppositionum naturalium → distinctio creationis → possibilitas initii sine mutatione Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AF3","text":"Conatus demonstrandi novitatem → examen mundi, causae et infiniti → defectus necessitatis → revelatio ut principium cognitionis → cautio apologetica.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS6","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AF4","text":"Difficultas creationis in primo instanti → distinctio creationis a motu → coproductio temporis → primus nunc → triplex ordinatio temporalis, exemplaris et causalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME1","text":"Aeternitas et novitas mundi desinunt esse conclusiones immediate derivabiles ex causalitate divina; status earum distribuitur inter possibilitatem metaphysicam et determinationem revelatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME2","text":"«Creatum» et «temporaliter inceptum» fiunt rationes distinctae, quamvis in mundo revelato coniungantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D8","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME3","text":"Materia, spatium, motus et tempus reclassificantur ex condicionibus universalis causalitatis in effectus internos creationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME4","text":"Prioritas Dei transfertur ex ordine chronologico in ordinem causalitatis et aeternitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME5","text":"Oppositiones inter finitum et infinitum dividuntur secundum per se et per accidens, successionem et totalitatem, universale et particulare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D9","CH_GGVC_P_38:D10","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME6","text":"Locutio «in principio» ex indice temporali simplici convertitur in nodum temporalis originis, causalitatis exemplaris et immediationis creativae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D12","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME7","text":"Defensio doctrinalis reordinatur: demonstrandum est quod fides contradictionem non continet, non fingendum quod omne fide creditum ratione necessaria probetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Investigantur initium mundi, demonstrabilitas huius initii et significatio creationis «in principio».","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Argumentatio nititur distinctionibus inter creationem et mutationem, agentem universalem et particularem, causalitatem voluntariam et necessitatem naturalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Terminus inter rationem et fidem constituitur ut veritas revelata ab infirmis pseudodemonstrationibus defendatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Tempus est effectus creatus, aeternitas est tota simul, et primum nunc est origo successionis sine tempore antecedente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:A16","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendas tres operationes principales: non-necessitatem aeternitatis, indemonstrabilitatem novitatis et interpretationem triplicem «in principio».","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A1","CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A10","CH_GGVC_P_38:A12","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT2","text":"Structura firmissima est distinctio creationis a motu coniuncta cum distinctione agentis voluntarii ab agente naturali; ea plerasque objectiones physicas uno principio dissolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT3","text":"Actualis mundi novitas ex axiomatibus metaphysicis non derivatur; revelatio manet praemissa irreducibilis quae assertionem centralem determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A1","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT4","text":"Commissura terminologica manet inter creationem ut dependentiam nullo subiecto praesupposito et «ex nihilo» ut esse post non esse; mundus aeternus priorem rationem dialectice retinere potest, non secundam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_38:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT5","text":"Ratio quod mundi novitas creatorem manifestius ostendat est convenientia explicativa, non demonstratio; argumentatio corrueret si haec convenientia in necessitatem converteretur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT6","text":"Responsiones de infinito maxime vim objectionum restringunt, sed neque aeternitatem mundi probant neque omnem difficultatem de infinitate actuali universaliter solvunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D10","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT7","text":"Triplex expositio «in principio» a principiis exegeticis et appropriationibus trinitariis pendet quae ex analysi naturali durationis non deducuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT8","text":"Systema interne cohaeret si possibilitas metaphysica, veritas revelata, causalitas creativa et initium temporale distincta servantur; restitutio hunc motum a physicis objectionibus ad limites rationis et inde ad ordinationem revelatam servat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161441531917Z_0e95e71b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 46","source_sha256":"dc9a6328be00cdef168aa1ff36c9bc60b5cc46220207221d7972f34979c6786f","sha256":"33cdf29fa6b2b4d6b3fa730e9a455852300d8e6f46882d0a441c34aa1b5ce1a2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:14:41.532853+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS1","text":"It is asked whether the universe of creatures had a beginning of duration, whether this beginning can be demonstrated by reason, and in what sense creation was made “in the beginning”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS2","text":"Nothing besides God existed from eternity, but this newness of the world is held by faith alone, not by natural demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, dialectical-polemical, and reconstructive: it resolves objections from physical presuppositions, establishes the limits of demonstration, and then metaphysically explains the revealed formula.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS4","text":"Arguments for the eternity of the world are transferred from matter, motion, time, and natural causality to the divine will and non-mutative creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS5","text":"Arguments for the demonstrability of the world's newness are reduced to the distinction between knowable creative causality and the contingent determination of the divine will, manifest through revelation alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AS6","text":"The expression “in the beginning” is explained in three ways so that the eternity of the world, the duality of principles, and the mediation of spiritual creatures in the first production of corporeal things are excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A1","text":"Nothing besides God existed from eternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","text":"The will of God is the cause of the being of created things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","text":"God wills nothing besides Himself with absolute necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","text":"The effect of a voluntary agent follows the form pre-conceived and pre-defined by the agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","text":"The duration of the world depends on the determination of the divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","text":"Creation is the production of the whole being of a thing, with no subject presupposed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","text":"Creation is neither motion nor change nor the terminus of motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","text":"The universal agent produces a thing simultaneously with its time, and presupposes neither matter nor time to its action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A9","text":"Ungenerability and incorruptibility exclude inception through natural generation, not production through creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A10","text":"The principle of demonstration concerning a thing is the whatness of the thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A11","text":"The account of the species abstracts from here and now.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A12","text":"The divine will concerning creatures cannot be investigated by natural reason, because creatures are not objects willed with absolute necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A13","text":"The contingent determination of the divine will can be made manifest to man through revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","text":"Divine eternity is being all at once without succession, not the successive duration of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A15","text":"An infinite process of essentially ordered efficient causes is impossible, but the multiplication of accidentally ordered causes is not excluded by the same impossibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A16","text":"Time exists only according to the now and begins from the first now.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","text":"“In the beginning” designates the beginning of time, the exemplary principle in the Son, and the priority of first creation before every created causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:A18","text":"The empyrean heaven, corporeal matter, time, and angelic nature were created simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX1","text":"The eternity of the world neither follows necessarily from the eternity of God nor is demonstratively proven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX2","text":"The newness of the world is not a conclusion of demonstrative natural science or metaphysics.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX3","text":"Aristotle's arguments for eternity are not demonstrations simply speaking, but contradictions in a qualified sense against impossible modes of inception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX4","text":"The possibility of the world before its being does not require pre-existing matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX5","text":"The incorruptibility of a thing does not exclude its creation, but only inception according to natural generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX6","text":"The first production of a movable thing is not a change from an antecedent state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","text":"Before the world there was no real void, place, space, or time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX8","text":"The eternal divine will requires neither antecedent change nor an eternal effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9","text":"God's priority to the world is not priority within time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX10","text":"From the fact that the world was made by God it does not follow that God is prior to the world in duration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX11","text":"For defenders of the eternal world, “ex nihilo” means “not from something,” not necessarily “after nothing.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX12","text":"The divine intellect does not begin to act through successive deliberation as the human intellect does.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX13","text":"The beginnings of arts, dwellings, and particular orders do not prove a beginning of the whole world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX14","text":"The successive coextension of the world with all time would not make the world equal to divine eternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX15","text":"Arguments from the traversal of the infinite, the succession of generations, or the multitude of souls do not universally demonstrate the newness of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX16","text":"Creation “in the beginning of time” does not signify creation measured temporally from the first instant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:NX17","text":"First creation admits neither two principles of good and evil nor spiritual creatures as intermediate causes of corporeal things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D1","text":"Since God does not will creatures necessarily and the duration of the world depends on His will, it is not necessary that the world has always existed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D2","text":"The eternity and sufficiency of a voluntary cause do not entail an eternal effect, because the effect is produced according to the predefinition of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D3","text":"Arguments that reduce every inception to generation, motion, or change do not reach creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D4","text":"Matter, place, and time cannot be employed as external conditions to impede first creation, because they themselves are contained within the produced whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D5","text":"The beginning of duration cannot be demonstrated from the specific nature of the world or of worldly things, because specific principles abstract from temporal index.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A10","CH_GGVC_P_38:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D6","text":"The newness of the world cannot be demonstrated on the part of the efficient cause, because the determination of the divine will concerning creatures is not rationally necessary, but revealable.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A12","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","text":"The beginning of the world is believable through revelation, not demonstrable or scientifically knowable from natural principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D5","CH_GGVC_P_38:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D8","text":"Creative causality and temporal beginning are not the same account; dependence on a creator alone does not dialectically exclude an effect always dependent on its cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D9","text":"Even if the world's duration without a beginning is posited, the world would not be equal to God, because temporal succession and eternity all at once are diverse modes of duration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D10","text":"Objections from the infinite past do not conclude universally: traversal between two finite termini is finite, generators constitute a series per accidens, and the argument from souls concerns only the human world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D11","text":"The first now does not receive creation as though it were a temporal measure, but is the terminus from which time begins simultaneously with things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D12","text":"The threefold sense of “in the beginning” establishes one doctrine: time has a beginning, all things are made through one exemplary principle, and the first universality of creatures is produced through no created intermediate agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:D13","text":"The being of the world after non-being indicates a creative cause more manifestly; therefore, newness has the character of manifestative fittingness, not demonstrative necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","text":"Natural reason can know the dependence of the world on a creator, but cannot determine whether the created effect has always existed or has had a temporal beginning.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:D5","CH_GGVC_P_38:D6","CH_GGVC_P_38:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD2","text":"God's creative priority is causally and eternally ordering, not the placement of God in time antecedent to the world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","text":"Creation encloses the entire physical order within the effect: matter, space, motion, and time are not conditions of creation but parts of the created order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4","text":"The beginning of time is the originating boundary of succession, not an event posited after empty time or an antecedent state of the world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A16","CH_GGVC_P_38:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5","text":"The actual newness of the world is not deduced from metaphysical principles: metaphysics maintains its possibility and non-necessity, whereas revelation determines its truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A1","CH_GGVC_P_38:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD6","text":"The exegesis of “in the beginning” establishes at once the temporal, exemplary, and causal unity of creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7","text":"The defense of faith must preserve the limits of demonstration, lest it offer probable or weak reasons as necessary and thereby provide matter for mockery.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX1","text":"Not every possibility is founded upon passive potency or a material receptacle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX2","text":"Natural generation is not the exhaustive form of every production into being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A9","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX3","text":"Not every voluntary action presupposes time, change, or awaits an external condition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX4","text":"The sufficiency of a cause is not convertible with the natural necessitation of an effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX5","text":"Causal dependence does not necessarily include the temporal succession of cause and effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D8","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6","text":"Revealed truth does not require that it be converted into a demonstrative conclusion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX7","text":"From local changes or from the condition of a particular species, one may not universally infer the state of the whole creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX15","CH_GGVC_P_38:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX8","text":"Temporal infinity, essentially ordered causal infinity, and infinity per accidens do not constitute one logical structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A15","CH_GGVC_P_38:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX9","text":"Temporal predicates concerning God and the world are not taken according to one measure of duration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX1","text":"No meta-time, empty space, or material receptacle outside creation is available in which the beginning of the world may be located.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX2","text":"No created principle, evil or spiritual, participates with God in the first production of beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:A18","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX3","text":"No rational path proceeds from the essence of the world alone or the causality of God to the free content of the decree by which the world received a beginning.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX4","text":"There is no antecedent state of the world from which creation proceeds by change to the first temporal state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:D11","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX5","text":"No common line of duration contains God and the world, by which their priority or equality is measured univocally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX6","text":"Faith ought not borrow its certainty from pseudo-demonstrations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS1","text":"Causal divine will → necessary will of itself alone → contingency of willing creatures → effect according to predefinition → no necessity of an eternal world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_38:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS2","text":"Presupposition of matter, motion, or time → restriction to natural generation and particular agent → distinction of creation and universal agent → dissolution of the contradiction concerning first beginning.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:A9","CH_GGVC_P_38:D3","CH_GGVC_P_38:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS3","text":"Whatness abstracting from here and now → no demonstration from the world → contingent will naturally inaccessible → no demonstration from the cause → revelation → faith concerning newness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A10","CH_GGVC_P_38:A11","CH_GGVC_P_38:A12","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13","CH_GGVC_P_38:D5","CH_GGVC_P_38:D6","CH_GGVC_P_38:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS4","text":"Non-mutative creation + co-produced time + being of time according to the now → absence of prior process → first now as origin of succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:A16","CH_GGVC_P_38:D11","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS5","text":"“In the beginning” → beginning of time / exemplar in the Son / priority of first creation → exclusion of eternity of the world / dualism / created mediation → four natures created simultaneously.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:A18","CH_GGVC_P_38:D12","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS6","text":"Univocation of eternity or infinity → distinction of eternity from succession and of causes per se from series per accidens → failure of demonstrations from equality, traversal, or regress.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:A15","CH_GGVC_P_38:D9","CH_GGVC_P_38:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AF1","text":"Question concerning the duration of creatures → dissolution of the necessity of an eternal world → delimitation of demonstration → placement of newness in faith → threefold explanation of “in the beginning”.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AF2","text":"Arguments from matter, motion, time, and eternal cause → detection of natural presuppositions → distinction of creation → possibility of a beginning without change in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AF3","text":"Attempt to demonstrate newness → examination of world, cause, and infinity → failure of necessity → revelation as principle of knowledge → apologetic caution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS6","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:AF4","text":"Difficulty of creation in the first instant → distinction of creation from motion → co-production of time → first now → threefold temporal, exemplary, and causal ordering.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME1","text":"The eternity and newness of the world cease to be conclusions immediately derivable from divine causality; their status is distributed between metaphysical possibility and revealed determination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME2","text":"“Created” and “temporally begun” become distinct accounts, although they are conjoined in the revealed world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D8","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME3","text":"Matter, space, motion, and time are reclassified from conditions of universal causality into internal effects of creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME4","text":"The priority of God is transferred from chronological order into the order of causality and eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME5","text":"Oppositions between finite and infinite are divided according to per se and per accidens, succession and totality, universal and particular.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D9","CH_GGVC_P_38:D10","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME6","text":"The expression “in the beginning” is transformed from a simple temporal index into a nexus of temporal origin, exemplary causality, and creative immediacy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D12","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ME7","text":"Doctrinal defense is reordered: it must be demonstrated that faith contains no contradiction, not feigned that everything believed by faith is proven by necessary reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — The beginning of the world, the demonstrability of this beginning, and the meaning of creation “in the beginning” are investigated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The argumentation rests on distinctions between creation and change, universal and particular agent, voluntary causality and natural necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The boundary between reason and faith is established so that revealed truth may be defended from weak pseudo-demonstrations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Time is a created effect, eternity is all at once, and the first now is the origin of succession without antecedent time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:A16","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the three principal operations: the non-necessity of eternity, the indemonstrability of newness, and the threefold interpretation of “in the beginning”.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A1","CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A10","CH_GGVC_P_38:A12","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT2","text":"The firmest structure is the distinction of creation from motion conjoined with the distinction of voluntary agent from natural agent; by one principle it dissolves most physical objections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT3","text":"The actual newness of the world is not derived from metaphysical axioms; revelation remains the irreducible premise that determines the central assertion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A1","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT4","text":"A terminological juncture remains between creation as dependence with no subject presupposed and “ex nihilo” as being after non-being; an eternal world can dialectically retain the former account, not the latter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_38:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT5","text":"The reason that the world's newness shows the creator more manifestly is explanatory fittingness, not demonstration; the argumentation would collapse if this fittingness were converted into necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D7","CH_GGVC_P_38:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT6","text":"The responses concerning the infinite chiefly restrict the force of objections, but neither prove the eternity of the world nor universally resolve every difficulty concerning actual infinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D10","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT7","text":"The threefold exposition of “in the beginning” depends on exegetical principles and Trinitarian appropriations that are not deduced from the natural analysis of duration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT8","text":"The system coheres internally if metaphysical possibility, revealed truth, creative causality, and temporal beginning are kept distinct; the reconstruction preserves this movement from physical objections to the limits of reason and thence to revealed ordering.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_38:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_38:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_38@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_38:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 47","title":"First Part · Question 46","context":"Chapter 47","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 46"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 46","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 47","order":48,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_39"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_39@R001","sha256":"ad096c4ff85e52c3e804c3d8a510b7ba2ca1ca9a03eb567d149078d1f770855a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat utrum multitudo, distinctio, inaequalitas et unitas mundi ex divina causalitate ordinante procedant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS2","text":"Argumentatio causalitates materiales, fortuitas, secundarias et poenales removet, ut principium distinctionis ad primum agentem reducatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS3","text":"Multitudo rerum ponitur effectus intentionis divinae bonitatem suam communicantis et creaturaliter repraesentantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS4","text":"Inaequalitas derivatur ex primatu distinctionis formalis et ex perfectione universi per gradus bonitatis constituti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS5","text":"Unitas mundi non ex singularitate numerica nuda, sed ex ordine omnium ad invicem et ad Deum demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS6","text":"Motus textus procedit a pluralitate apparenter contraria unitati divinae ad pluralitatem ordinatam, inaequalem et universaliter unificatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A1","text":"Deus est primum agens voluntarium et sapiens, non agens naturaliter ad unum effectum necessario contractum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A2","text":"Creatio, etiam ipsius materiae, soli Deo competit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","text":"Deus creaturas producit ut bonitas divina eis communicetur et per eas repraesentetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","text":"Nulla creatura singularis divinam bonitatem perfecte repraesentare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A5","text":"Distinctio rerum procedit ex intentione et sapientia primi agentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A6","text":"Materia est propter formam; distinctio rerum principaliter per formas proprias constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A7","text":"Distinctio formalis principalior est distinctione materiali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","text":"Diversitas formarum gradus bonitatis et inaequalitatem rerum requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","text":"Perfectio universi requirit multitudinem graduum bonitatis, non unum tantum gradum creaturalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A10","text":"Bonitas totius universi est ratio proportionata qua singulae creaturae diversimode bonae constituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","text":"Omnia a Deo facta ordinantur et ad invicem et ad ipsum Deum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","text":"Unitas mundi consistit in unitate ordinis omnium rerum ad unum principium et finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A13","text":"Multitudo materialis per se nullum terminum certum habet et ideo finis intentus esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A14","text":"Mundus ex tota materia sua constat, cuius partes naturaliter ad unum ordinem et ad unum medium referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX1","text":"Distinctio rerum non ex motu fortuito materiae explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX2","text":"Materia non est principium ultimum distinctionis, quia ipsa creata est et propter formas disponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX3","text":"Secunda agentia non producunt per creationem universitatem rerum nec eius complementum fortuito constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX4","text":"Multiplicitas creaturarum non repugnat unitati divinae, quia Deus per formas intellectas multa efficere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX5","text":"Unitas exemplaris divini non exigit unicum effectum, quia creatura exemplar primum perfecte non adaequat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX6","text":"Inaequalitas creaturarum non procedit ex meritis vel peccatis creaturis praecedentibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX7","text":"Mundus corporalis non est apparatus poenalis ad animas lapsas puniendas constitutus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX8","text":"Optimitas agentis non exigit ut quaelibet pars sit optima simpliciter, sed ut totum sit optimum secundum modum creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX9","text":"Plures mundi non inferuntur ex infinita Dei potentia, quia possibilitas potentiae non determinat intentionem finis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX10","text":"Pluralitas materialis non est perfectio per se intendenda, quia in infinitum indeterminate procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D1","text":"Universum, non creatura singularis, est perfectior participatio et repraesentatio divinae bonitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D2","text":"Pluralitas creaturarum est complementum repraesentativum: quod uni deest, ab alia creatura suppletur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D3","text":"Inaequalitas non est defectus ordinis creati, sed conditio qua distinctio formalis perfectionem universi auget.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A6","CH_GGVC_P_39:A7","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D4","text":"Bonitas singularum creaturarum mensuratur per proportionem ad bonitatem totius, non per identitatem dignitatis inter singula.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D5","text":"Iustitia retributiva merita praesupponit; constitutio initialis rerum ex ordine totius, non ex meritis praecedentibus, explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D6","text":"Unus mundus sequitur ex eo quod omnia entia creata sub eodem ordine reciproco et theocentrico comprehenduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D7","text":"Multiplicatio mundorum non est melior simpliciter, quia sola multiplicatio materialis finem determinatum non constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SD1","text":"Perfectionem creatam textus a perfectione partis ad coordinationem totius transfert: universum est unitas pluralitatem graduatam includens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SD2","text":"Diversitas, inaequalitas et unitas non sunt tres quaestiones separatae, sed tres effectus unius sapientiae quae bonitatem divinam finite distribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SD3","text":"Causalitas divina ordinans causam fortuitam et causam poenalem submovet, quia ordo universalis anteponitur concursui partium et historiae meritorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SD4","text":"Unitas mundi est teleologica et relationalis: mundus unus est quia omnia in unum ordinem conveniunt, non quia pluralitas absoluta materialiter prohiberi possit sola definitione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","CH_GGVC_P_39:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod ens creatum finitum possit divinam bonitatem simpliciter et exhaustive exhibere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod formae creaturae sint differentiae aequivalentes sine ordine perfectionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod materia sit principium per se sufficiens ordinis, distinctionis aut causalitatis cosmicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod inaequalitas originaria iustificationem ex culpa, merito vel dispositione praevia exigat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet quod collectio rerum sine ordine reciproco et ad Deum relata mundus proprie dicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet quod augmentum numerale rerum sit per se augmentum perfectionis finaliter intentum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX1","text":"Unitas divina non potest intellegi ut uniformitas effectus, alioquin causalitas intellectiva et voluntaria Dei in necessitatem naturalem redigeretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX2","text":"Perfectionem universi textus extra aequalitatem absolutam collocat: aequalitas omnium dissolveret gradus quibus totum perficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX3","text":"Mundus intelligibilis non potest fundari in casu, quia casus neque totalem ordinem neque terminum finalem universi rationabiliter constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX4","text":"Plures totalitates cosmicae independentes excluduntur, quia creatio divina omnia ordinat ad invicem et ad unum Deum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:FGS1","text":"Bonitas divina simplex et communicabilis → repraesentatio creaturalis finita et insufficiens → pluralitas creaturarum diversa → complementum repraesentativum universi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:FGS2","text":"Primatus formae super materiam → distinctio formalis → gradus perfectionis → inaequalitas → perfectio proportionata totius.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A6","CH_GGVC_P_39:A7","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:FGS3","text":"Creatio omnium a Deo → ordo mutuus rerum → ordinatio ad unum Deum → unitas mundi → exclusio pluralitatis materialis ut finis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","CH_GGVC_P_39:A13","CH_GGVC_P_39:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF1","text":"Unitas Dei apparenter contra multitudinem → distinctio inter agens naturale et agens voluntarium → pluralitas intentionaliter intellecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF2","text":"Defectus repraesentationis singularis → communicatio distributa bonitatis divinae → universum ut repraesentatio perfectior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF3","text":"Distinctio per formas → ordinatio graduum formarum → inaequalitas necessaria perfectioni universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF4","text":"Obiectio ex aequalitate et iustitia → separatio constitutionis a retributione → inaequalitas ex bono totius, non ex merito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF5","text":"Possibilitas plurium mundorum → definitio mundi per unitatem ordinis → unus mundus sub una gubernatione et uno fine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME1","text":"Multitudo rerum reclassificatur ex dispersione numerica in instrumentum positivum repraesentationis bonitatis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME2","text":"Inaequalitas reclassificatur ex iniustitia primae distributionis in structuram formalem perfectionis universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME3","text":"Distinctio materialis subordinatur distinctioni formali, ita ut materia non iam principium explicativum primarium sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME4","text":"Bonitas rerum non per comparationem singularum ad maximum absolutum, sed per proportionem partium ad totum ordinatum aestimatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME5","text":"Unitas mundi reclassificatur ex unitate numerali in unitatem ordinis, relationis et finis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME6","text":"Pluralitas possibilis secundum potentiam divinam separatur a pluralitate actu intenta secundum sapientiam et finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus affirmat multitudinem, distinctionem, inaequalitatem et unitatem mundi a Deo procedere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT2","text":"Structural — Formae, gradus bonitatis, materia disposita et ordo mutuus constituunt mechanismum quo universum diversum tamen unum efficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Quaestio a comparatione singularum rerum ad normam aequalitatis transfertur ad rationem boni totius ordinati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Ens creatum finitum bonitatem divinam divisive participat; propter finitudinem participativam pluralitas et gradatio rerum requiruntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de causalitate divina, repraesentatione imperfecta et primatu formae sufficiunt ad restitutionem rationis multitudinis et inaequalitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de ordine mutuo et ordine ad Deum sufficiunt ad restitutionem conclusionis de unitate mundi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT3","text":"Structura maxime cohaeret ubi imperfectio repraesentationis singularis pluralitatem creaturarum necessario generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT4","text":"Commissura principalis manet inter potentiam divinam plures mundos producendi et assumptionem quod omnia creata necessario sub unico ordine actuali comprehendantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT5","text":"Commissura altera manet in transitu a gradibus formalibus ad iudicium quod haec gradatio universum simpliciter perfectius efficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6","text":"Argumentatio inaequalitatem originariam a merito separat, sed criterium intrinsecum distributionis singularum formarum in sapientia divina positum ulterius non resolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, si distinctio, inaequalitas et unitas tractantur ut effectus coordinati unius intentionis sapientis, non ut conclusiones independentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161504289245Z_641b1b8d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 47","source_sha256":"ad096c4ff85e52c3e804c3d8a510b7ba2ca1ca9a03eb567d149078d1f770855a","sha256":"699514b0eb484e8fe06d2dbb46c48933a7f8deb27be0f749f45a9cf0ca2c4698","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:15:04.290449+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS1","text":"The question investigates whether the multitude, distinction, inequality, and unity of the world proceed from divine ordering causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS2","text":"The argument removes material, fortuitous, secondary, and penal causalities, so that the principle of distinction may be traced back to the first agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS3","text":"The multitude of things is posited as an effect of the divine intention communicating and creaturely representing its goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS4","text":"Inequality is derived from the primacy of formal distinction and from the perfection of the universe constituted through degrees of goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS5","text":"The unity of the world is demonstrated not from bare numerical singularity, but from the order of all things to one another and to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AS6","text":"The movement of the text proceeds from plurality apparently contrary to divine unity to an ordered, unequal, and universally unified plurality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A1","text":"God is the first voluntary and wise agent, not an agent acting naturally and necessarily restricted to one effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A2","text":"Creation, even of matter itself, belongs to God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","text":"God produces creatures so that the divine goodness may be communicated to them and represented through them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","text":"No single creature can perfectly represent divine goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A5","text":"The distinction of things proceeds from the intention and wisdom of the first agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A6","text":"Matter is for the sake of form; the distinction of things is principally constituted through their proper forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A7","text":"Formal distinction is more principal than material distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","text":"The diversity of forms requires degrees of goodness and inequality among things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","text":"The perfection of the universe requires a multitude of degrees of goodness, not merely one creaturely degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A10","text":"The goodness of the whole universe is the proportionate reason by which individual creatures are constituted good in diverse ways.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","text":"All things made by God are ordered both to one another and to God himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","text":"The unity of the world consists in the unity of the order of all things to one principle and end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A13","text":"Material multitude, considered in itself, has no determinate limit and therefore cannot be an intended end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:A14","text":"The world consists of all its matter, whose parts are naturally referred to one order and one center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX1","text":"The distinction of things is not explained by the fortuitous motion of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX2","text":"Matter is not the ultimate principle of distinction, because it is itself created and disposed for the sake of forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX3","text":"Secondary agents do not produce the totality of things by creation, nor do they fortuitously constitute its completion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX4","text":"The multiplicity of creatures is not contrary to divine unity, because God can produce many things through understood forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX5","text":"The unity of the divine exemplar does not require a single effect, because a creature does not perfectly equal the first exemplar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX6","text":"The inequality of creatures does not proceed from merits or sins preceding the creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX7","text":"The corporeal world is not a penal apparatus constituted to punish fallen souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX8","text":"The excellence of the agent does not require that every part be best simply, but that the whole be best according to the mode of a creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX9","text":"A plurality of worlds is not inferred from God's infinite power, because the possibility of power does not determine the intention of the end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:NX10","text":"Material plurality is not a perfection to be intended for its own sake, because it proceeds indeterminately to infinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D1","text":"The universe, not a single creature, is a more perfect participation and representation of divine goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D2","text":"The plurality of creatures is a representative complement: what is lacking to one is supplied by another creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D3","text":"Inequality is not a defect of the created order, but the condition by which formal distinction increases the perfection of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A6","CH_GGVC_P_39:A7","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D4","text":"The goodness of individual creatures is measured by proportion to the goodness of the whole, not by equality of dignity among individuals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D5","text":"Retributive justice presupposes merits; the initial constitution of things is explained from the order of the whole, not from preceding merits.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D6","text":"One world follows from the fact that all created beings are comprehended under the same reciprocal and theocentric order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:D7","text":"The multiplication of worlds is not better simply, because material multiplication alone does not constitute a determinate end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SD1","text":"The text transfers created perfection from the perfection of the part to the coordination of the whole: the universe is a unity including graded plurality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SD2","text":"Diversity, inequality, and unity are not three separate questions, but three effects of one wisdom that distributes divine goodness finitely.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SD3","text":"Divine ordering causality removes fortuitous and penal causality, because universal order is preferred to the concurrence of parts and the history of merits.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SD4","text":"The unity of the world is teleological and relational: the world is one because all things converge in one order, not because absolute plurality can be materially prohibited by definition alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","CH_GGVC_P_39:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX1","text":"It must be false that a finite created being can exhibit divine goodness simply and exhaustively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the forms of creatures are equivalent differences without an order of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX3","text":"It must be false that matter is a principle per se sufficient for order, distinction, or cosmic causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX4","text":"It must be false that original inequality requires justification from fault, merit, or prior disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX5","text":"It must be false that a collection of things without reciprocal order and without reference to God is properly called a world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX6","text":"It must be false that the numerical increase of things is per se an increase of perfection intended as an end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX1","text":"Divine unity cannot be understood as uniformity of effect, otherwise God's intellective and voluntary causality would be reduced to natural necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX2","text":"The text locates the perfection of the universe outside absolute equality: equality of all things would dissolve the degrees by which the whole is perfected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX3","text":"The intelligible world cannot be founded upon chance, because chance reasonably constitutes neither the total order nor the final end of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX4","text":"Several independent cosmic totalities are excluded, because divine creation orders all things to one another and to one God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:FGS1","text":"Simple and communicable divine goodness → finite and insufficient creaturely representation → diverse plurality of creatures → representative complement of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:FGS2","text":"Primacy of form over matter → formal distinction → degrees of perfection → inequality → proportionate perfection of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A6","CH_GGVC_P_39:A7","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:FGS3","text":"Creation of all things by God → mutual order of things → ordination to one God → unity of the world → exclusion of material plurality as an end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","CH_GGVC_P_39:A13","CH_GGVC_P_39:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF1","text":"Unity of God apparently against multitude → distinction between natural agent and voluntary agent → intentionally understood plurality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF2","text":"Defect of singular representation → distributed communication of divine goodness → universe as a more perfect representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF3","text":"Distinction through forms → ordering of degrees of forms → inequality necessary for the perfection of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF4","text":"Objection from equality and justice → separation of constitution from retribution → inequality from the good of the whole, not from merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:AF5","text":"Possibility of several worlds → definition of world through unity of order → one world under one governance and one end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME1","text":"The multitude of things is reclassified from numerical dispersion into a positive instrument for representing divine goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME2","text":"Inequality is reclassified from an injustice of the first distribution into a formal structure of universal perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME3","text":"Material distinction is subordinated to formal distinction, such that matter is no longer the primary explanatory principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME4","text":"The goodness of things is assessed not by comparison of individual things with an absolute maximum, but by the proportion of the parts to the ordered whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME5","text":"The unity of the world is reclassified from numerical unity into unity of order, relation, and end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ME6","text":"Plurality possible according to divine power is separated from plurality actually intended according to wisdom and end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text affirms that the multitude, distinction, inequality, and unity of the world proceed from God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT2","text":"Structural — Forms, degrees of goodness, disposed matter, and mutual order constitute the mechanism by which the universe is made diverse yet one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The question is transferred from comparing individual things according to a norm of equality to the rationale of the good of the ordered whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — A finite created being participates divisively in divine goodness; because of participative finitude, plurality and gradation of things are required.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT1","text":"Axioms concerning divine causality, imperfect representation, and the primacy of form suffice for reconstructing the rationale of multitude and inequality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT2","text":"Axioms concerning mutual order and order to God suffice for reconstructing the conclusion concerning the unity of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT3","text":"The structure is most coherent where the imperfection of singular representation necessarily generates a plurality of creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT4","text":"The principal joint remains between the divine power to produce several worlds and the assumption that all created things are necessarily comprehended under a single actual order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT5","text":"Another joint remains in the transition from formal degrees to the judgment that this gradation makes the universe simply more perfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6","text":"The argument separates original inequality from merit, but does not further resolve the intrinsic criterion of the distribution of individual forms posited in divine wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if distinction, inequality, and unity are treated as coordinated effects of one wise intention, not as independent conclusions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_39:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_39@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_39:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 48","title":"First Part · Question 47","context":"Chapter 48","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 47"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 47","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 48","order":49,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_40"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_40@R001","sha256":"cf0946f8197be53473f7b638956b37e9ea34fee07b87899e6b6e344969509a57","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS1","text":"Quaeritur quomodo malum possit in rebus inveniri, agere, bonum corrumpere et moraliter dividi, si natura positiva non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS2","text":"Quaestio a supposita natura mali ad privationem boni debiti in subiecto bono transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS3","text":"Primatus boni ex appetibilitate esse et perfectionis fundamentum totius argumentationis praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS4","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, privativa, cosmologica et moraliter divisiva, cum objectionibus per distinctiones modi essendi, causalitatis et ordinis solutis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS5","text":"Motus procedit a definitione mali ad eius praesentiam in rebus, subiectum, limites corruptionis, divisionem voluntariam et comparationem culpae cum poena.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS6","text":"Malum est defectus realis sed non res subsistens; bono inhaeret, per bonum operatur, sub providentia per accidens ordinatur, atque in ordine voluntario perfectius in culpa quam in poena invenitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","text":"Esse, perfectio et potentia ad perfectionem ordinata rationem boni habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","text":"Malum, inquantum malum, est privatio boni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","text":"Sola absentia boni quod subiectum natum est et debet habere rationem mali constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","text":"Privatio est negatio in subiecto capaci perfectionis oppositae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","text":"Perfectio universi inaequalitatem rerum et impletionem graduum bonitatis requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","text":"Inter gradus bonitatis creatae sunt bona defectibilia, quorum potentia deficiendi interdum in defectum exit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A7","text":"Agens facit quod melius est in toto, non necessario quod melius est in unaquaque parte nisi secundum ordinem partis ad totum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","text":"Providentia naturas salvat potius quam destruit, ideo defectus rerum defectibilium non omnes impedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","text":"Omnis actio efficiens ex forma procedit, et omne quod appetitur ut finis aliquam perfectionem praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A10","text":"Bonum malo directe oppositum per illud malum totaliter aufertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","text":"Bonum quod est subiectum mali neque totaliter tollitur neque per malum secundum substantiam diminuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A12","text":"Habilitas subiecti ad actum per malum remitti potest, sed dum radix substantialis manet totaliter non aboletur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","text":"Actus primus est forma et integritas rei, actus secundus est operatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A14","text":"Actus morales speciem ex fine, qui est obiectum voluntatis, recipiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A15","text":"In rebus voluntariis sub providentia et iustitia consideratis, privatio formae vel integritatis rationem poenae habet, privatio autem debitae operationis voluntariae rationem culpae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","text":"Bonitas hominis simpliciter in bona operatione et bono usu rerum per voluntatem consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","text":"Poena privat voluntatem aliquo bono quo utitur, culpa autem ipsum actum voluntatis deordinat et bono divino in se considerato opponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A18","text":"Deus est auctor mali poenae, non mali culpae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX1","text":"Malum non est res, forma, natura aut entitas positiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX2","text":"Malum non est pura negatio neque simpliciter nihil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX3","text":"Malum non est genus simpliciter, sed privatio sub ratione contrarietatis potest genus contrariorum nominari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX4","text":"Malum qua malum non est differentia specifica moralis; specificatio provenit ex bono indebito privationi debiti finis adiuncto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX5","text":"Malum qua privatio non est causa efficiens neque causa finalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX6","text":"Malum non appetitur neque intenditur sub ratione mali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX7","text":"Malum non est pars aut proprietas naturalis entis cui inest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX8","text":"Malum qua malum neque perfectionem universi constituit neque ordini eius per se subicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX9","text":"Non omnis limitatio vel carentia creaturae est malum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX10","text":"Poena et culpa non dividunt malum simpliciter, sed malum in rebus voluntariis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0104","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX11","text":"Poena, etiam si gratiam vel gloriam privat, non habet maiorem rationem mali quam culpa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","text":"Malum non potest esse ens positivum, quia quidquid positivum esse vel perfectionem habet sub ratione boni cadit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","text":"Malum necessario in bono sicut in subiecto est, quia privatio subiectum perfectibile requirit et tale subiectum bonitatem saltem potentialem habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D3","text":"Malum potest vere dici esse in re sine hoc quod entitas praedicamentalis sit, quia veritas propositionis de privatione in subiecto reificationem privationis non requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D4","text":"Malum realiter invenitur ubi bonum defectibile a debita perfectione actu deficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D5","text":"Malum formaliter corrumpere dicitur ut ipsa corruptio, sed efficienter agit aut finaliter movet tantum virtute boni adiuncti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","text":"Eventus mali a providentia propter ordinem totius permitti potest, quamvis malum ipsum perfectionem universi per se non constituat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A7","CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D7","text":"Malum totum bonum consumere non potest, quia consumpto subiecto simul desineret privatio cuius subiectum erat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A10","CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D8","text":"Divisio mali in poenam et culpam est exhaustiva tantum intra ordinem voluntarium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_40:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D9","text":"Malum morale speciem accipit a fine positivo sed indebito, dum ratio mali ex privatione ordinis ad finem debitum provenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D10","text":"Culpa plus de ratione mali habet quam poena, quia corrumpit usum voluntarium quo agens simpliciter bonus vel malus constituitur et ipsi bono divino contrariatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A15","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","text":"Bonum et malum non sunt principia aequalia: bonum est ontologice primum, malum autem relationem dependentiae ad bonum debitum, subiectum bonum et causam positivam semper retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD2","text":"Nullum principium causale pure malum dari potest, quia omnis efficacia et omnis appetibilitas ex forma vel perfectione mutuatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:D5","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3","text":"Perfectio totius compatibilis est cum defectu partium, sed non quia malum perfectivum sit; perfectivus est ordo graduum et bonorum quibus defectus permissus accidentaliter subservit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:A7","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD4","text":"Incrementum mali aptitudinem ad perfectionem indefinite debilitare potest, sed ipsa persistentia mali persistentiam alicuius naturae bonae praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12","CH_GGVC_P_40:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD5","text":"Gravitas moralis non secundum quantitatem boni amissi, sed secundum corruptionem operationis voluntariae et ordinis ad bonum divinum mensuratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD6","text":"Providentia potest defectum permittere et poenam efficere sine causalitate culpae, quia actum positivum causat, deordinationem autem qua deordinatio est non producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX1","text":"Systema falsitatem oppositionis symmetricae inter bonum et malum requirit; malum contrariatur bono tantum ut privatio dependens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX2","text":"Praedicatio qua dicitur malum esse non potest sine distinctione in entitatem positivam converti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX3","text":"Perfectio universi non significat uniformem maximizationem cuiusque partis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX4","text":"Providentia perfecta non significat eliminationem omnis defectibilitatis vel omnis effectus causarum secundarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX5","text":"Qualitas moralis agentis non ex bonis possessis vel amissis simpliciter, sed ex usu voluntario eorum constitui debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX6","text":"Dependentia, finitas et incapacitas perfectionis alienae non possunt per se ut mala classificari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX1","text":"Malum purum, subsistens, efficax et ab omni bono seiunctum est impossibile.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX2","text":"Subiectum omnino bono destitutum malum sustinere non potest, quia cum bono subiecti etiam ipsa privatio tolleretur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_40:D7","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX3","text":"Universus creatus ex solis rebus indefectibilibus plenitudinem graduum bonitatis huius systematis implere non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX4","text":"Deus culpam ut culpam causare, intendere aut velle non potest, quamvis actum positivum sustentet et defectum permittat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:A18","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX5","text":"Malum neque omnino extra bonum et ordinem consistere neque ut pars intrinseca perfectionis admitti potest; locus eius est dependentia privativa et ordinatio per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS1","text":"Modulus epistemicus alterum oppositorum per alterum cognoscit et rationem mali ex ratione boni elicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS2","text":"Modulus ontologicus procedit: esse et perfectio sunt bona → malum non est natura positiva → malum est privatio boni debiti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS3","text":"Modulus subiectivus procedit: privatio requirit potentiam → potentia ad perfectionem est bonum → malum in bono inest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","CH_GGVC_P_40:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS4","text":"Modulus cosmologicus procedit: plenitudo graduum → bona defectibilia → defectus actualis → malum reale sine natura mali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS5","text":"Modulus causalis procedit: actio ex forma et appetitus ex perfectione → efficacia boni adiuncti → malum neque agit neque appetitur per se.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS6","text":"Modulus corruptionis distinguit bonum oppositum totaliter ablatum, bonum subiecti permanens et habilitatem diminutam sed non annihilatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A10","CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS7","text":"Modulus voluntarius procedit: actus primus et secundus → privatio integritatis et operationis → poena et culpa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_40:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS8","text":"Modulus aestimativus procedit: bonitas agentis in usu voluntario → culpa corrumpit usum et ordinem divinum → culpa est peior poena.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AF1","text":"Motus metaphysicus est: supposita natura mali → primatus boni → privatio boni debiti → subiectum bonum → existentia privativa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AF2","text":"Motus cosmologicus est: inaequalitas universi → defectibilitas creata → defectus actualis → permissio providentiae → ordinatio per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AF3","text":"Motus voluntarius est: forma et operatio → poena et culpa → usus voluntatis → oppositio ad bonum divinum → maior malitia culpae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS7","CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME1","text":"Malum ex classe rerum vel naturarum in classem privationum relationalium transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME2","text":"Existentia dividitur inter entitatem rei et veritatem praedicationis, ita ut malum reale sine reificatione intelligi possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME3","text":"Oppositio boni et mali ex contrariis aequipollentibus in dependentiam asymmetricam reordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME4","text":"Ager providentiae ab eliminatione defectus ad conservationem naturarum defectibilium et ordinationem totius transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A7","CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME5","text":"Corruptio boni non iam ut subtractio uniformis, sed ut relatio triplex inter oppositum, subiectum et habilitatem describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A10","CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME6","text":"Aestimatio mali voluntarii a quantitate damni ad ordinem operationis et usum voluntatis transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface. Sex quaestiones determinant naturam mali, eius praesentiam, subiectum, vim corruptivam, divisionem et gradum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural. Mechanismus principalis est privatio boni debiti in subiecto bono, causaliter dependens a forma positiva et cosmologice inclusa per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","CH_GGVC_P_40:D5","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic. Quaestio originis rei malae substituitur quaestione condicionum defectus, permissionis providentis et imputabilitatis voluntariae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_40:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_40:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal. Malum praesupponit potentiam priorem, perfectionem debitam, defectum actualem et persistentiam subiecti; in ordine morali actus secundus perfectioni primae aestimative praeponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12","CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam progressionem a primatu boni ad rationem privativam mali et ad eius specificationem voluntariam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_40:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT2","text":"Systema firmissimum est in nexu inter privationem, bonum debitum, subiectum perfectibile et dependentiam causalitatis mali a bono.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT3","text":"Cohaerentia interna distinctionibus inter negationem et privationem, entitatem et praedicationem, totum et partem, atque ordinem per se et per accidens sustinetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D3","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT4","text":"Transitus a possibilitate defectus ad assertionem quod defectibilia interdum actu deficiant non plene demonstratur, sed tamquam consequentia naturae defectibilis assumitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter negationem mali ut perfectionis universi et usum eventuum malorum ad perfectionem totius; solutio pendet ex distinctione boni adiuncti et ordinis per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT6","text":"Divisio per poenam et culpam cohaeret tantum intra dominium voluntarium et sub praesuppositione providentiae ac iustitiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A15","CH_GGVC_P_40:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT7","text":"Praelatio malitiae culpae nititur hierarchia qua operatio voluntaria et ordo ad bonum divinum possessioni vel privationi bonorum praeponuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT8","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus: ontologia privativa → cosmologia permissionis → analysis corruptionis → taxonomia voluntaria → primatus mali culpae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_40:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_40:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161534185150Z_2e2df44e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 48","source_sha256":"cf0946f8197be53473f7b638956b37e9ea34fee07b87899e6b6e344969509a57","sha256":"a0cf91eb03c3a627cec450b8b75dfe5fd160526f70bad7d0f63e582ee6b8ea74","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:15:34.186960+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS1","text":"It is asked how evil can be found in things, act, corrupt good, and be divided morally, if it is not a positive nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS2","text":"The question is transferred from a supposed nature of evil to the privation of due good in a good subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS3","text":"The primacy of good, based on the desirability of being and perfection, provides the foundation of the entire argumentation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS4","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, privative, cosmological, and morally divisive, with objections resolved through distinctions of mode of being, causality, and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS5","text":"The movement proceeds from the definition of evil to its presence in things, its subject, the limits of corruption, voluntary division, and the comparison of fault with punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AS6","text":"Evil is a real defect but not a subsistent thing; it inheres in good, operates through good, is ordered per accidens under providence, and in the voluntary order is found more perfectly in fault than in punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","text":"Being, perfection, and potency ordered to perfection have the character of good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","text":"Evil, insofar as it is evil, is the privation of good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","text":"Only the absence of a good that a subject is naturally fitted and ought to have constitutes the character of evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","text":"Privation is a negation in a subject capable of the opposite perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","text":"The perfection of the universe requires the inequality of things and the fulfillment of degrees of goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","text":"Among the degrees of created goodness are defectible goods, whose potency for failing sometimes issues in defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A7","text":"An agent brings about what is better in the whole, not necessarily what is better in each part except according to the order of the part to the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","text":"Providence preserves natures rather than destroys them; therefore it does not prevent every defect of defectible things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","text":"Every efficient action proceeds from form, and everything desired as an end provides some perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A10","text":"The good directly opposed to evil is totally removed by that evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","text":"The good that is the subject of evil is neither totally removed nor diminished by evil according to substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A12","text":"The subject's aptitude for act can be weakened by evil, but so long as the substantial root remains, it is not totally abolished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","text":"First act is the form and integrity of a thing; second act is operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A14","text":"Moral acts receive their species from the end, which is the object of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A15","text":"In voluntary matters considered under providence and justice, privation of form or integrity has the character of punishment, whereas privation of due voluntary operation has the character of fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","text":"The goodness of a human being simply consists in good operation and the good use of things through the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","text":"Punishment deprives the will of some good that it uses, whereas fault disorders the very act of the will and is opposed to the divine good considered in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:A18","text":"God is the author of the evil of punishment, not of the evil of fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX1","text":"Evil is not a thing, form, nature, or positive entity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX2","text":"Evil is neither pure negation nor simply nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX3","text":"Evil is not a genus simply speaking, but privation under the aspect of contrariety may be called a genus of contraries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX4","text":"Evil as evil is not a moral specific difference; specification arises from an undue good conjoined to the privation of a due end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX5","text":"Evil as privation is neither an efficient cause nor a final cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX6","text":"Evil is neither desired nor intended under the aspect of evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX7","text":"Evil is not a natural part or property of the being in which it inheres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX8","text":"Evil as evil neither constitutes the perfection of the universe nor is subject to its order per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX9","text":"Not every limitation or lack in a creature is evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX10","text":"Punishment and fault do not divide evil simply speaking, but evil in voluntary matters.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0104","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:NX11","text":"Punishment, even if it deprives one of grace or glory, does not have a greater character of evil than fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","text":"Evil cannot be a positive being, because whatever has positive being or perfection falls under the aspect of good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","text":"Evil necessarily exists in good as in a subject, because privation requires a perfectible subject, and such a subject has at least potential goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D3","text":"Evil can truly be said to be in a thing without being a predicamental entity, because the truth of a proposition concerning privation in a subject does not require the reification of privation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D4","text":"Evil is really found where a defectible good actually falls short of due perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D5","text":"Evil is said formally to corrupt as corruption itself, but it acts efficiently or moves finally only by the power of an accompanying good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","text":"An evil event can be permitted by providence for the sake of the order of the whole, although evil itself does not per se constitute the perfection of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A7","CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D7","text":"Evil cannot consume all good, because once the subject had been consumed, the privation whose subject it was would simultaneously cease.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A10","CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D8","text":"The division of evil into punishment and fault is exhaustive only within the voluntary order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_40:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D9","text":"Moral evil receives its species from a positive but undue end, while its character of evil arises from the privation of order to the due end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:D10","text":"Fault has more of the character of evil than punishment, because it corrupts the voluntary use by which an agent is constituted simply good or bad and is contrary to the divine good itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A15","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","text":"Good and evil are not equal principles: good is ontologically first, whereas evil always retains a relation of dependence upon due good, a good subject, and a positive cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD2","text":"No purely evil causal principle can be given, because every efficacy and every desirability is borrowed from form or perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:D5","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3","text":"The perfection of the whole is compatible with the defect of parts, but not because evil is perfective; what is perfective is the order of degrees and goods, which permitted defect serves accidentally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:A7","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD4","text":"The increase of evil can indefinitely weaken aptitude for perfection, but the very persistence of evil presupposes the persistence of some good nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12","CH_GGVC_P_40:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD5","text":"Moral gravity is measured not according to the quantity of good lost, but according to the corruption of voluntary operation and of order to the divine good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SD6","text":"Providence can permit defect and effect punishment without causality of fault, because it causes the positive act but does not produce the disorder insofar as it is disorder.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX1","text":"The system requires the falsity of symmetrical opposition between good and evil; evil is contrary to good only as a dependent privation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX2","text":"The predication by which evil is said to be cannot be converted into a positive entity without distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX3","text":"The perfection of the universe does not mean the uniform maximization of every part.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX4","text":"Perfect providence does not mean the elimination of every defectibility or of every effect of secondary causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX5","text":"The moral quality of an agent must be constituted not simply by goods possessed or lost, but by their voluntary use.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX6","text":"Dependence, finitude, and incapacity for another's perfection cannot per se be classified as evils.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX1","text":"Pure, subsistent, efficacious evil, separated from every good, is impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX2","text":"A subject wholly deprived of good cannot sustain evil, because with the good of the subject, privation itself would also be removed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_40:D7","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX3","text":"A created universe composed solely of indefectible things cannot fulfill the fullness of degrees of goodness of this system.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX4","text":"God cannot cause, intend, or will fault as fault, although He sustains the positive act and permits the defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:A18","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX5","text":"Evil can neither subsist wholly outside good and order nor be admitted as an intrinsic part of perfection; its place is privative dependence and ordering per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS1","text":"The epistemic module knows one of the opposites through the other and derives the account of evil from the account of good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS2","text":"The ontological module proceeds: being and perfection are goods → evil is not a positive nature → evil is privation of due good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS3","text":"The subjective module proceeds: privation requires potency → potency for perfection is good → evil inheres in good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","CH_GGVC_P_40:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS4","text":"The cosmological module proceeds: fullness of degrees → defectible goods → actual defect → real evil without a nature of evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS5","text":"The causal module proceeds: action from form and appetite from perfection → efficacy of accompanying good → evil neither acts nor is desired per se.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A9","CH_GGVC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS6","text":"The corruption module distinguishes the opposed good totally removed, the enduring good of the subject, and aptitude diminished but not annihilated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A10","CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS7","text":"The voluntary module proceeds: first and second act → privation of integrity and operation → punishment and fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_40:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS8","text":"The evaluative module proceeds: the agent's goodness in voluntary use → fault corrupts use and divine order → fault is worse than punishment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AF1","text":"The metaphysical movement is: supposed nature of evil → primacy of good → privation of due good → good subject → privative existence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AF2","text":"The cosmological movement is: inequality of the universe → created defectibility → actual defect → permission of providence → ordering per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:AF3","text":"The voluntary movement is: form and operation → punishment and fault → use of the will → opposition to the divine good → greater malice of fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS7","CH_GGVC_P_40:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME1","text":"Evil is transferred from the class of things or natures to the class of relational privations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME2","text":"Existence is divided between the entity of a thing and the truth of predication, so that real evil can be understood without reification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME3","text":"The opposition of good and evil is reordered from equipollent contraries into asymmetric dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME4","text":"The scope of providence is transferred from the elimination of defect to the preservation of defectible natures and the ordering of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A7","CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME5","text":"The corruption of good is no longer described as uniform subtraction, but as a threefold relation among opposite, subject, and aptitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A10","CH_GGVC_P_40:A11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ME6","text":"The evaluation of voluntary evil is transferred from the quantity of harm to the order of operation and the use of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface. Six questions determine the nature of evil, its presence, its subject, its corruptive power, its division, and its degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural. The principal mechanism is the privation of due good in a good subject, causally dependent on positive form and cosmologically included per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","CH_GGVC_P_40:D5","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic. The question of the origin of an evil thing is replaced by the question of the conditions of defect, provident permission, and voluntary imputability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_40:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_40:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal. Evil presupposes prior potency, due perfection, actual defect, and the persistence of the subject; in the moral order second act is evaluatively preferred to first perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12","CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the progression from the primacy of good to the privative account of evil and to its voluntary specification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_40:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT2","text":"The system is strongest in the nexus among privation, due good, a perfectible subject, and the dependence of evil's causality upon good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A4","CH_GGVC_P_40:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence is sustained by distinctions between negation and privation, entity and predication, whole and part, and order per se and per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D3","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT4","text":"The transition from the possibility of defect to the assertion that defectible things sometimes actually fail is not fully demonstrated, but is assumed as a consequence of defectible nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains between the denial that evil belongs to the perfection of the universe and the use of evil events for the perfection of the whole; the solution depends on the distinction between accompanying good and order per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_40:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT6","text":"The division through punishment and fault coheres only within the voluntary domain and under the presupposition of providence and justice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A15","CH_GGVC_P_40:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT7","text":"The preference for the malice of fault rests on a hierarchy in which voluntary operation and order to the divine good are preferred to the possession or privation of goods.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17","CH_GGVC_P_40:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: privative ontology → cosmology of permission → analysis of corruption → voluntary taxonomy → primacy of the evil of fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_40:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_40:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_40:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_40@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_40:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 49","title":"First Part · Question 48","context":"Chapter 49","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 48"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 48","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 49","order":50,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_41"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_41@R001","sha256":"5ba77251373b6eaa4f2e109b658fedd17a44b10d8e35be8ff052486136f33789","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat quomodo malum causam habere possit, si omne ens est bonum et Deus est summum bonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","text":"Quaestio causae mali reconstituitur per distinctionem inter defectum, subiectum, causalitatem per se et causalitatem per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS3","text":"Malum causam requirit quia est defectus boni debiti, sed causare convenit enti et igitur bono; ideo malum non causatur nisi accidentaliter a bono.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS4","text":"Causalitas divina dividitur: Deus causat bonum entitatis, ordinem universi, corruptiones consequentes et malum poenae, non autem defectum actionis neque malum culpae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS5","text":"Dualismus primi boni et primi mali dissolvitur quia malum non est ens per essentiam, non est causa per se, et sine bono subiecto consistere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS6","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysico-causalis et anti-dualistica: a defectu particulari ascendit ad ordinem universalem et ad principium primum essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","text":"Omne ens, inquantum ens est, bonum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","text":"Causalitas convenit solum enti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A3","text":"Malum est defectus boni quod natum est et debet inesse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A4","text":"Malum est in bono sicut in subiecto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A5","text":"Malum formalem causam non habet, quia est privatio formae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A6","text":"Malum finalem causam non habet, quia est privatio ordinis ad finem debitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","text":"Malum per modum causae agentis non causatur per se, sed per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","text":"Defectus in actione procedit ex defectu alicuius principii agentis, instrumenti, materiae vel dispositionis receptivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A9","text":"In voluntariis defectus actionis procedit ex voluntate quae actu regulae suae non subicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A10","text":"In Deo nullus defectus est, quia Deus est summa perfectio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A11","text":"Bonum ordinis universi requirit ut quaedam res deficere possint et interdum deficiant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A12","text":"Malum poenae ad ordinem iustitiae pertinet, quo peccatoribus poena infertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A13","text":"Causae particulares contrariae reducuntur ad causam universalem communem essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A14","text":"Malum bonum diminuere potest, sed bonum totaliter consumere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX1","text":"Malum non est res positiva per se subsistens, sed privatio boni debiti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX2","text":"Malum non habet causam formalem neque finalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX3","text":"Malum non habet causam agentem per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX4","text":"Deus non est causa mali quod consistit in defectu actionis vel in culpa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX5","text":"Malum non opponitur summo bono sicut privatio habitui in eodem subiecto, quia summum bonum est actus purus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX6","text":"Non est summum malum neque primum principium malorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX7","text":"Incrementum mali non est accessus ad terminum positivum perfectum, sed recessus a termino boni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D1","text":"Bonum est causa materialis mali, quia bonum est subiectum in quo privatio boni inest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D2","text":"Bonum causat malum accidentaliter vel inducendo formam cui privatio alterius formae consequitur, vel deficiendo in actione propter impedimentum aut indispositionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D3","text":"In rebus naturalibus malus effectus praesupponit defectum in agente vel materia, nisi corruptio consequatur perfectionem agentis respectu contrarii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D4","text":"In actu voluntario entitas et motus actionis a causa prima derivari possunt, sed obliquitas moralis procedit ex defectu causae secundae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:A9","CH_GGVC_P_41:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D5","text":"Deus causat corruptiones rerum non ut privationes per se intentae, sed ut consequentias boni ordinis universi et formarum a se productarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_41:A10","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D6","text":"Deus est auctor mali poenae ratione iustitiae, non mali culpae ratione defectus agentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A9","CH_GGVC_P_41:A10","CH_GGVC_P_41:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D7","text":"Regressus causarum mali non terminatur in malo primo, sed in bono ex quo malum consequitur per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_41:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D8","text":"Malum integrum est impossibile, quia destructo omni bono destruitur ipsum subiectum mali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A4","CH_GGVC_P_41:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1","text":"Causalitas mali est asymmetrica: bonum potest accidentaliter producere defectum, sed malum non potest causaliter fundare bonum neque se ipsum ut primum principium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A4","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SD2","text":"Attributio causae divinae dividenda est secundum id quod in effectu est entitas, perfectio et ordo, atque secundum id quod est defectus et inordinatio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SD3","text":"Malum locale non definit bonitatem rei simpliciter, quia iudicium bonitatis ordinandum est ad naturam rei et ad ordinem totius universi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11","CH_GGVC_P_41:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4","text":"Contrarietas rerum non imponit dualitatem principiorum, quia contraria communicant in esse et sub causa universali conveniunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod defectus habeat eandem dignitatem ontologicam atque forma vel perfectio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod causalitas universalis transferat ad causam primam omnem rationem defectus quae in causa secunda invenitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod experientia nocivi particularis sufficiat ad naturam rei simpliciter malam declarandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod privatio participationis reducenda sit ad ens quod malum per essentiam participetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet quod frequentia defectuum humanorum convertat malum in principium naturale vel universale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit possibilitatem mali absoluti, quia malum sine bono subiecto neque esse neque intelligi potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit symmetriam metaphysicam boni et mali, quia bonum tendit ad perfectionem positivam, malum autem significat recessum privativum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit causam primam quae sit deficiens, quia primitas causalis requirit causalitatem per se, quam malum habere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX4","text":"Systema excludit non esse ut terminum positivum intentum a Deo, quia corruptio divinae causalitatis sub ordine boni consequitur, non ut per se finis intenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS1","text":"Bonum debitum → defectus eius → malum ut privatio → necessitas causae trahentis vel impedientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS2","text":"Causa ut ens → ens ut bonum → impossibilitas causae mali per se → bonum ut causa mali per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS3","text":"Forma intenta ab agente → privatio formae contrariae consequens → corruptio accidentaliter causata; defectus principii vel materiae → defectus effectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS4","text":"Causa prima perfecta → causatio entitatis et ordinis → corruptio consequens et poena iusta → exclusio causalitatis divinae culpae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS5","text":"Malum ut privatio in bono → impossibilitas mali per essentiam → impossibilitas summi mali → reductio omnium causarum ad unum principium bonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AF1","text":"Defectus boni debiti → inquisitio causae → distinctio causalitatis per se et per accidens → bonum ut unica radix causalis mali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AF2","text":"Bonum causans → distinctio entitatis a defectu → Deus ut causa ordinis, corruptionis consequentis et poenae → Deus non causa culpae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AF3","text":"Contrarietas particularium effectuum → error dualisticus → reductio contrariorum ad causam communem → negatio primi principii mali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME1","text":"Malum reclassificatur ab ente contrario bono ad defectum internum boni debiti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME2","text":"Causa mali reclassificatur ab agente malo per se ad bonum causans accidentaliter vel ad principium deficiens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME3","text":"Relatio Dei ad malum dividitur in causationem entitatis, ordinis, corruptionis consequentis et poenae, contra attributionem causalitatis culpae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME4","text":"Contrarietas cosmica reclassificatur a conflictu principiorum primorum ad diversitatem causarum particularium sub unitate causae universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME5","text":"Iudicium de malo transfertur ab effectu nocivo respectu particulari ad ordinem rei secundum se et ad ordinem universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus distinguit malum naturae, malum culpae et malum poenae secundum diversos modos defectus et causalitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ALT2","text":"Structural — Malum explicatur per relationem inter formam, materiam, potentiam, agentem, finem, impedimentum et ordinem iustitiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio prohibet inferre naturam simpliciter malam ex noxa particulari et prohibet inferre dualismum ex contrarietate particulari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Bonum habet rationem entis et perfectionis; malum habet rationem privationis, dependentiae a subiecto bono et recessus a termino perfecto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de convertibilitate entis et boni, de malo ut privatione, et de causalitate per accidens sufficiunt ad reconstruendam negationem causae mali per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter entitatem actionis et defectum actionis sufficit ad reconstruendam negationem causalitatis divinae culpae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT3","text":"Axiomata de ordine universi et de iustitia explicant quomodo corruptio et poena Deo attribuantur sine attributione mali per se intenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT4","text":"Structura firmissima est in asymmetria ontologica boni et mali, ex qua sequuntur impossibilitas summi mali et reductio causarum mali ad bonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in transitu ab eo quod corruptio ordinem universi consequitur ad eo quod haec corruptio causaliter Deo attribuitur, quia causalitas per accidens simul affirmatur et limitatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT6","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in ordine voluntario, ubi defectus actualis non-subiectionis regulae culpa non dicitur, sed culpa ex actione cum tali defectu secuta dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat si causalitas particularis, causalitas universalis et diversitas mali naturae, culpae atque poenae non confunduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161557163079Z_72726cba","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 49","source_sha256":"5ba77251373b6eaa4f2e109b658fedd17a44b10d8e35be8ff052486136f33789","sha256":"17bf52d1bae7b596b8d4b37e6c62cc1db750262918f12550e579c3f374fd269d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:15:57.164029+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS1","text":"The question investigates how evil can have a cause, if every being is good and God is the highest good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","text":"The question of the cause of evil is reconstructed through the distinction between defect, subject, causality per se, and causality per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS3","text":"Evil requires a cause because it is a defect of due good, but causing belongs to being and therefore to good; thus evil is caused only accidentally by good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS4","text":"Divine causality is divided: God causes the good of being, the order of the universe, consequent corruptions, and the evil of punishment, but not the defect of action nor the evil of fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS5","text":"The dualism of a first good and a first evil is dissolved because evil is not being through essence, is not a cause per se, and cannot subsist without a good subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AS6","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical-causal and anti-dualistic: from particular defect it ascends to universal order and to the first principle of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","text":"Every being, insofar as it is being, is good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","text":"Causality belongs only to being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A3","text":"Evil is the defect of a good which is naturally apt and ought to be present.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A4","text":"Evil is in good as in a subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A5","text":"Evil has no formal cause, because it is the privation of form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A6","text":"Evil has no final cause, because it is the privation of order toward the due end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","text":"Evil is not caused per se in the mode of an efficient cause, but per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","text":"A defect in action proceeds from a defect in some principle of the agent, instrument, matter, or receptive disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A9","text":"In voluntary matters, a defect of action proceeds from a will that is not actually subjected to its rule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A10","text":"There is no defect in God, because God is supreme perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A11","text":"The good of the order of the universe requires that certain things be able to fail and sometimes do fail.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A12","text":"The evil of punishment belongs to the order of justice, by which punishment is inflicted upon sinners.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A13","text":"Contrary particular causes are reduced to a common universal cause of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:A14","text":"Evil can diminish good, but it cannot consume good totally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX1","text":"Evil is not a positive thing subsisting per se, but a privation of due good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX2","text":"Evil has neither a formal nor a final cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX3","text":"Evil has no efficient cause per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX4","text":"God is not the cause of evil consisting in a defect of action or in fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX5","text":"Evil is not opposed to the highest good as privation to habit in the same subject, because the highest good is pure act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX6","text":"There is no highest evil or first principle of evils.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:NX7","text":"The increase of evil is not an approach to a perfect positive terminus, but a recession from the terminus of good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D1","text":"Good is the material cause of evil, because good is the subject in which the privation of good inheres.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D2","text":"Good causes evil accidentally either by inducing a form upon which the privation of another form follows, or by failing in action because of an impediment or indisposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D3","text":"In natural things, an evil effect presupposes a defect in the agent or matter, unless corruption follows upon the perfection of the agent with respect to the contrary.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D4","text":"In a voluntary act, the being and motion of the action can be derived from the first cause, but moral crookedness proceeds from a defect of the secondary cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:A9","CH_GGVC_P_41:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D5","text":"God causes corruptions of things not as privations intended per se, but as consequences of the good order of the universe and of the forms produced by Him.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_41:A10","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D6","text":"God is the author of the evil of punishment by reason of justice, not of the evil of fault by reason of a defect in the agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A9","CH_GGVC_P_41:A10","CH_GGVC_P_41:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D7","text":"The regress of the causes of evil does not terminate in a first evil, but in a good from which evil follows per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_41:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:D8","text":"Complete evil is impossible, because once every good is destroyed, the very subject of evil is destroyed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A4","CH_GGVC_P_41:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1","text":"The causality of evil is asymmetrical: good can accidentally produce a defect, but evil cannot causally ground good or itself as a first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A4","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SD2","text":"The attribution of divine causality must be divided according to what in the effect is being, perfection, and order, and according to what is defect and disorder.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SD3","text":"Local evil does not define the goodness of a thing simply, because the judgment of goodness must be ordered to the nature of the thing and to the order of the whole universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11","CH_GGVC_P_41:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4","text":"The contrariety of things does not entail a duality of principles, because contraries share in being and concur under a universal cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX1","text":"It must be false that defect has the same ontological dignity as form or perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX2","text":"It must be false that universal causality transfers to the first cause every account of defect found in the secondary cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the experience of a particular harmful thing suffices to declare a thing evil simply.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the privation of participation is to be reduced to a being that participates in evil through essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the frequency of human defects converts evil into a natural or universal principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility of absolute evil, because evil can neither be nor be understood without a good subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX2","text":"The system excludes the metaphysical symmetry of good and evil, because good tends toward positive perfection, whereas evil signifies privative recession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX3","text":"The system excludes a first cause that is defective, because causal primacy requires causality per se, which evil cannot possess.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX4","text":"The system excludes non-being as a positive terminus intended by God, because corruption follows from divine causality under the order of good, not as an end intended per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS1","text":"Due good → its defect → evil as privation → necessity of a cause drawing away or impeding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS2","text":"Cause as being → being as good → impossibility of a cause of evil per se → good as cause of evil per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS3","text":"Form intended by the agent → consequent privation of the contrary form → corruption caused accidentally; defect of principle or matter → defect of effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS4","text":"Perfect first cause → causation of being and order → consequent corruption and just punishment → exclusion of divine causality of fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:FGS5","text":"Evil as privation in good → impossibility of evil through essence → impossibility of the highest evil → reduction of all causes to one good principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AF1","text":"Defect of due good → inquiry into cause → distinction of causality per se and per accidens → good as the sole causal root of evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AF2","text":"Good causing → distinction of being from defect → God as cause of order, consequent corruption, and punishment → God not cause of fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:AF3","text":"Contrariety of particular effects → dualistic error → reduction of contraries to a common cause → denial of a first principle of evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME1","text":"Evil is reclassified from a being contrary to good into an internal defect of due good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME2","text":"The cause of evil is reclassified from an evil agent per se into good causing accidentally or into a defective principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME3","text":"God's relation to evil is divided into causation of being, order, consequent corruption, and punishment, against the attribution of causality of fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME4","text":"Cosmic contrariety is reclassified from a conflict of first principles into a diversity of particular causes under the unity of the universal cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ME5","text":"The judgment concerning evil is transferred from a harmful effect in a particular respect to the order of the thing in itself and to the order of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text distinguishes evil of nature, evil of fault, and evil of punishment according to diverse modes of defect and causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ALT2","text":"Structural — Evil is explained through the relation among form, matter, potency, agent, end, impediment, and the order of justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argumentation forbids inferring a nature evil simply from a particular harm and forbids inferring dualism from particular contrariety.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Good has the character of being and perfection; evil has the character of privation, dependence upon a good subject, and recession from a perfect terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning the convertibility of being and good, evil as privation, and causality per accidens suffice to reconstruct the denial of a cause of evil per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT2","text":"The distinction between the being of action and the defect of action suffices to reconstruct the denial of divine causality of fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT3","text":"The axioms concerning the order of the universe and justice explain how corruption and punishment are attributed to God without attributing evil intended per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT4","text":"The firmest structure lies in the ontological asymmetry of good and evil, from which follow the impossibility of the highest evil and the reduction of the causes of evil to good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains in the transition from the claim that corruption follows the order of the universe to the claim that this corruption is causally attributed to God, because causality per accidens is simultaneously affirmed and limited.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT6","text":"A fragile joint remains in the voluntary order, where the actual defect of non-subjection to the rule is not called fault, but fault is said to follow from an action with such a defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if particular causality, universal causality, and the diversity of evil of nature, fault, and punishment are not confused.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_41:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_41@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_41:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 50","title":"First Part · Question 49","context":"Chapter 50","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 49"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 49","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 50","order":51,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_42"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_42@R001","sha256":"37e2ddad9069c1309119b1981a97b39c34fae7bf8bbe5fffcdfe40dcea63601a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS1","text":"Quaestio est an creatura pure spiritualis possit esse incorporea, immaterialis, multiplex, specie distincta atque naturaliter incorruptibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS2","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica, reconstructiva et polemica ab operatione intellectuali ad constitutionem substantiae ascendit, simul positiones corporeistas et universaliter hylemorphicas removens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3","text":"Ex perfectione universi et modo causandi divino infertur necessitas alicuius creaturae intellectualis atque incorporeae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4","text":"Ex immaterialitate intelligendi proceditur ad omnimodam immaterialitatem substantiae angelicae, deinde ad compositionem actus et potentiae secundum essentiam et esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS5","text":"Ex absentia materiae multiplicitas angelica in distinctionem formarum et specierum convertitur, non in multiplicationem individuorum eiusdem speciei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS6","text":"Ex forma subsistente naturalis incorruptibilitas deducitur, quam dependentia causalis et conservativa a Deo non tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A1","text":"Perfectio universi est id quod Deus praecipue intendit in rerum creatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A2","text":"Perfecta assimilatio effectus ad causam requirit ut effectus causam imitetur secundum id quo causa effectum producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A3","text":"Deus creaturas producit per intellectum et voluntatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A4","text":"Intelligere non potest esse actus corporis neque virtutis corporeae, quia omne corpus ad hic et nunc determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","text":"Operatio uniuscuiusque rei modum substantiae eius sequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","text":"Intelligere est operatio penitus immaterialis, quia actus ab obiecto rationem accipit et intelligibile apprehenditur inquantum a materia abstrahitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A7","text":"Ea quae intellectus distinguit non propter hoc in re distincta sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","text":"In forma creata subsistente, essentia sive quod est ad esse sive quo est comparatur ut potentia ad actum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","text":"Omnis creatura finita est simpliciter, quia esse eius ad determinatam naturam limitatur nec absolute subsistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A10","text":"Multitudo transcendens ex distinctione formarum oriri potest sine divisione continui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A11","text":"Quanto creaturae perfectiores sunt, tanto in maiori excessu a Deo producuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A12","text":"In rebus incorporeis excessus secundum multitudinem, sicut in corporibus secundum magnitudinem, attendi potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","text":"Quae specie conveniunt et numero differunt, forma conveniunt atque materialiter distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A14","text":"Nihil corrumpitur nisi per separationem formae a materia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A15","text":"Quod alicui secundum se convenit ab eo separari non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A16","text":"Necessitati et incorruptibilitati creatae non repugnat quod esse ab alia causa dependeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX1","text":"Angelus Deo comparatus materialis aut corporeus dicitur solum relative, non quia naturam corpoream participet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX2","text":"Motus angelicus non est necessario motus corporis, quia intelligere et velle motus aequivoce nominantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX3","text":"Circumscriptio essentialis creaturae non est circumscriptio localis corporum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","text":"Una materia universalis substantiarum spiritualium et corporalium esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX5","text":"Substantia intellectualis non habet materiam cuiuscumque generis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX6","text":"Compositio logica generis et differentiae in rebus immaterialibus non significat compositionem realem materiae et formae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX7","text":"Receptio formae intelligibilis ab intellectu non est receptio materialis qua subiectum constituitur in specie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX8","text":"Carentia materiae Angelum neque actum purum neque infinitum simpliciter efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX9","text":"Numerus Angelorum non est quantitas discreta ex divisione continui causata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX10","text":"Substantiae immateriales non sunt propter substantias corporales, nec earum numerus ex motibus aut corporibus caelestibus mensuratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX11","text":"Multitudo angelica non consistit in pluribus individuis eiusdem speciei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX12","text":"Immortalitas naturalis Angeli non est omnimoda immutabilitas, quae per gratiam tantum perficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX13","text":"Dependentia a conservatione divina non constituit principium intrinsecum corruptionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","text":"Perfectio universi requirit ut existant creaturae intellectuales et propter intellectualitatem incorporeae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A1","CH_GGVC_P_42:A2","CH_GGVC_P_42:A3","CH_GGVC_P_42:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D2","text":"Omnis substantia intellectualis est secundum substantiam omnino immaterialis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","text":"Angelus est forma subsistens et non compositum ex materia et forma.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","text":"Ablata compositione materiae et formae, in Angelo remanet compositio potentiae et actus secundum essentiam et esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D5","text":"Angelus est finitus secundum esse receptum, sed infinitus secundum quid quatenus forma eius in materia non recipitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","text":"Substantiae immateriales multitudine substantias materiales quasi incomparabiliter excedunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A1","CH_GGVC_P_42:A11","CH_GGVC_P_42:A12","CH_GGVC_P_42:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","text":"Multitudo angelica causatur ex distinctione formarum, non ex divisione materiae vel quantitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","text":"Duo Angeli eiusdem speciei esse non possunt; unusquisque Angelus propriam speciem habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D9","text":"Gradus diversi naturae intellectivae in Angelis diversitates specificas, non solam intensionem unius formae, constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","text":"Angelus, quia forma subsistens, nullum principium intrinsecum corruptionis habet atque naturaliter incorruptibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A14","CH_GGVC_P_42:A15","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","text":"Incorruptibilitas naturalis Angeli cum continua dependentia essendi a Deo componitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A16","CH_GGVC_P_42:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD1","text":"Eadem immaterialitas quae modum operationis angelicae constituit etiam principium individuationis materialis excludit et corruptionem naturalem impedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD2","text":"Abundantia angelica est abundantia formarum et specierum unicarum, non aggregatio individuorum sub una forma communi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD3","text":"Materia desinit esse nota universalis finitudinis creatae, quia receptio esse sufficit ad potentiam, limitationem et distinctionem a Deo constituendas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD4","text":"Propinquitas naturae angelicae ad unitatem divinam minuit compositionem internam, non multitudinem substantiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD5","text":"Modus compositivus intellectus humani condicionem cognitionis exprimit, non compositionem rei angelicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A7","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD6","text":"Incorruptibilitas angelica est necessitas naturalis causata, inferior tamen immutabilitati divinae et perfectae immutabilitati per gratiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX1","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem positionis secundum quam nihil est nisi quod sensu aut imaginatione apprehenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX2","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem isomorphiae inter distinctiones intellectus et compositiones rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX3","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem hylemorphismi universalis, quo omnis receptio, potentia et limitatio materiae tribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX4","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem positionis secundum quam omnis pluralitas divisionem quantitatis praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX5","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem ordinis teleologici quo substantiae spirituales propter effectus corporeos tantum existerent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX6","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem aequationis inter esse causatum et esse intrinsece corruptibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX7","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem consequentiae qua maior propinquitas ad unum minorem multitudinem substantiarum necessario inferret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX1","text":"Apprehensio directa et adaequata substantiae angelicae intellectui humano indisponibilis est; cognitio eius per modum rerum compositarum procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX2","text":"Nullum subiectum materiale vel quasi materiale relinquitur quo plures substantiae spirituales sub eadem specie individuentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3","text":"Spiritui creato aseitas praeclusa est: etiam forma subsistens esse non habet absolute subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX4","text":"Omnimoda immutabilitas naturae angelicae non competit, quamvis corruptio substantialis naturaliter impossibilis sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX5","text":"Ordo angelicus in functiones cosmologicas corporum resolvi non potest, quia nobilius non ordinatur ad corporale sicut ad finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS1","text":"Machina perfectionis progreditur hoc ordine: intentio perfectionis universi → assimilatio ad causam intellectualem → creatura intellectualis → creatura incorporea.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A1","CH_GGVC_P_42:A2","CH_GGVC_P_42:A3","CH_GGVC_P_42:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS2","text":"Machina substantiae progreditur hoc ordine: obiectum a materia abstractum → operatio immaterialis → substantia immaterialis → exclusio omnis materiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS3","text":"Machina finitudinis progreditur hoc ordine: forma subsistens → esse receptum → essentia ut potentia ad esse → finitas sine materia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS4","text":"Machina multitudinis progreditur hoc ordine: pluralitas transcendens → distinctio formarum → excessus incorporeus secundum multitudinem → multitudo materialem excedens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A10","CH_GGVC_P_42:A11","CH_GGVC_P_42:A12","CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS5","text":"Machina distinctionis progreditur hoc ordine: absentia materiae → impossibilitas individuationis intra eandem speciem → gradus formales distincti → unus Angelus per speciem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS6","text":"Machina incorruptionis progreditur hoc ordine: forma subsistens → nulla separatio formae a materia → nullum principium intrinsecum dissolutionis → incorruptibilitas naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A14","CH_GGVC_P_42:A15","CH_GGVC_P_42:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS7","text":"Clausura causalis progreditur hoc ordine: esse receptum → dependentia a causa conservante → necessitas causata → incorruptibilitas sine aseitate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A16","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF1","text":"Perfectio universi → assimilatio ad Deum causantem per intellectum et voluntatem → creatura intellectualis → incorporeitas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF2","text":"Immaterialitas intelligendi → immaterialitas substantiae → exclusio materiae et formae → compositio essentiae et esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF3","text":"Pluralitas non quantitativa → distinctio formarum → multitudo immaterialis corporalia excedens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF4","text":"Absentia materiae individuantis → impossibilitas plurium individuorum unius speciei → multiplicatio specierum secundum gradus intellectuales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF5","text":"Forma subsistens → impossibilitas dissolutionis intrinsecae → incorruptibilitas naturalis → dependentia conservativa sine corruptibilitate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1","text":"Ager entis ultra sensibile et imaginabile extenditur, ita ut incorporeum fiat obiectum ontologicum et non mera privatio corporis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME2","text":"Finitas a materia seiungitur et in limitatione esse recepti reponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME3","text":"Multitudo a quantitate et divisione continui seiungitur atque ut distinctio transcendens formarum describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME4","text":"Genus, differentia et receptio a compositionibus realibus materiae, formae et subiecti distinguuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A7","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME5","text":"Unitas primaria ordinis angelici a specie communi ad formam subsistentem unicam transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME6","text":"Hierarchia spiritualis ab ordine instrumentali ad corpora liberatur et secundum proprios gradus perfectionis constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME7","text":"Incorruptibilitas ab aseitate et omnimoda immutabilitate distinguitur, unde necessitas creata et causata cogitari potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ALT1","text":"Surface — Angeli statuuntur creaturae incorporeae, immateriales, numerosissimae, specie singillatim distinctae et naturaliter incorruptibiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ALT2","text":"Structural — Modus operationis substantiam manifestat, materia individuationem eiusdem speciei praebet, et compositio materiae et formae corruptionem possibilem reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio oppositiones dissolvit distinguendo motum intellectualem a motu corporeo, circumscriptionem essentialem a locali, receptionem intellectualem a materiali et necessitatem causatam ab aseitate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Spiritus creatus est forma subsistens supra corruptionem naturalem, sed esse receptum habet, a Deo conservatur et omnimodam immutabilitatem naturaliter non possidet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT1","text":"Corpus axiomatum sufficit ad quinque conclusiones principales restituendas: incorporeitatem, immaterialitatem, multitudinem, distinctionem specificam et incorruptibilitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT2","text":"Nexus firmissimus est ille qui ab operatione immateriali ad substantiam immaterialem et a forma subsistente ad absentiam principii corruptionis procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:A14","CH_GGVC_P_42:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT3","text":"Initium argumenti ab antecedentibus demonstrationibus pendet, praesertim a thesi quod Deus per intellectum et voluntatem producat et perfectionem universi principaliter intendat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT4","text":"Excessus multitudinis angelicae non demonstratur eadem necessitate ac immaterialitas, sed analogia inter magnitudinem corporum perfectorum et multitudinem substantiarum incorporearum sustentatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT5","text":"Unicitas specifica cuiusque Angeli stricte sequitur ex immaterialitate et principio individuationis materialis, sed distinctio graduum intellectualium in species ulterius non demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT6","text":"Distinctio inter compositionem intellectam et compositionem realem impedit projectionem modorum cognitionis humanae in substantias angelicas, sed cognitionem earum indirectam relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A7","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT7","text":"Nulla contradictio formalis manet inter incorruptibilitatem et conservationem divinam, dummodo corruptibilitas per principium intrinsecum dissolutionis definiatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A16","CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT8","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: operatio intellectualis constituit immaterialitatem; immaterialitas reordinat finitudinem, multitudinem et speciem; forma subsistens naturalem incorruptibilitatem claudit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161628170595Z_8f996b5b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 50","source_sha256":"37e2ddad9069c1309119b1981a97b39c34fae7bf8bbe5fffcdfe40dcea63601a","sha256":"b46d57048c3bfa53987214eaa11928796407ce3030a1798f6f74bfe08d734460","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:16:28.171691+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS1","text":"The question is whether a purely spiritual creature can be incorporeal, immaterial, multiple, specifically distinct, and naturally incorruptible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS2","text":"The metaphysical, reconstructive, and polemical argument ascends from intellectual operation to the constitution of substance, while simultaneously excluding corporealist and universally hylomorphic positions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3","text":"From the perfection of the universe and the divine mode of causing, the necessity of some intellectual and incorporeal creature is inferred.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4","text":"From the immateriality of understanding one proceeds to the complete immateriality of angelic substance, then to the composition of act and potency according to essence and being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS5","text":"From the absence of matter, angelic multiplicity is converted into a distinction of forms and species, not into a multiplication of individuals of the same species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AS6","text":"From subsisting form, natural incorruptibility is deduced, which causal and conserving dependence upon God does not remove.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A1","text":"The perfection of the universe is what God chiefly intends in the creation of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A2","text":"The perfect assimilation of an effect to its cause requires that the effect imitate the cause according to that by which the cause produces the effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A3","text":"God produces creatures through intellect and will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A4","text":"Understanding cannot be an act of a body or of a corporeal power, because every body is determined to here and now.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","text":"The operation of each thing follows the mode of its substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","text":"Understanding is an entirely immaterial operation, because the act receives its character from the object and the intelligible is apprehended insofar as it is abstracted from matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A7","text":"Things distinguished by the intellect are not thereby distinct in reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","text":"In a created subsisting form, essence, or quod est, stands in relation to being, or quo est, as potency to act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","text":"Every creature is simply finite, because its being is limited to a determinate nature and does not subsist absolutely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A10","text":"Transcendent multitude can arise from the distinction of forms without division of a continuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A11","text":"The more perfect creatures are, the more they are produced by God in excess.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A12","text":"In incorporeal things, excess according to multitude can be considered, just as in bodies according to magnitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","text":"Things that agree in species and differ in number agree in form and are distinguished materially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A14","text":"Nothing is corrupted except through the separation of form from matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A15","text":"What belongs to something through itself cannot be separated from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:A16","text":"It is not incompatible with created necessity and incorruptibility that being depend upon another cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX1","text":"An angel, when compared with God, is called material or corporeal only relatively, not because it participates in a corporeal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX2","text":"Angelic motion is not necessarily bodily motion, because understanding and willing are called motions equivocally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX3","text":"The essential circumscription of a creature is not the local circumscription of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","text":"There cannot be one universal matter of spiritual and corporeal substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX5","text":"An intellectual substance has no matter of any kind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX6","text":"The logical composition of genus and difference in immaterial things does not signify a real composition of matter and form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX7","text":"The reception of an intelligible form by the intellect is not material reception by which a subject is constituted in a species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX8","text":"The lack of matter does not make an Angel either pure act or simply infinite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX9","text":"The number of Angels is not a discrete quantity caused by the division of a continuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX10","text":"Immaterial substances do not exist for corporeal substances, nor is their number measured by motions or heavenly bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX11","text":"Angelic multitude does not consist in several individuals of the same species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX12","text":"The natural immortality of an Angel is not complete immutability, which is perfected only through grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:NX13","text":"Dependence upon divine conservation does not constitute an intrinsic principle of corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","text":"The perfection of the universe requires that intellectual creatures exist and, on account of their intellectuality, incorporeal ones.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A1","CH_GGVC_P_42:A2","CH_GGVC_P_42:A3","CH_GGVC_P_42:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D2","text":"Every intellectual substance is wholly immaterial according to its substance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","text":"An Angel is a subsisting form and not a composite of matter and form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","text":"Once the composition of matter and form is removed, there remains in an Angel a composition of potency and act according to essence and being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D5","text":"An Angel is finite according to received being, but infinite in a certain respect insofar as its form is not received in matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","text":"Immaterial substances exceed material substances in multitude as though incomparably.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A1","CH_GGVC_P_42:A11","CH_GGVC_P_42:A12","CH_GGVC_P_42:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","text":"Angelic multitude is caused by the distinction of forms, not by the division of matter or quantity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","text":"Two Angels of the same species cannot exist; each Angel has its own species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D9","text":"The diverse grades of intellectual nature in Angels constitute specific diversities, not merely an intensification of one form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","text":"An Angel, because it is a subsisting form, has no intrinsic principle of corruption and is naturally incorruptible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A14","CH_GGVC_P_42:A15","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","text":"The natural incorruptibility of an Angel is compatible with the continuous dependence of its being upon God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A16","CH_GGVC_P_42:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD1","text":"The same immateriality that constitutes the mode of angelic operation also excludes the material principle of individuation and prevents natural corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD2","text":"Angelic abundance is an abundance of forms and unique species, not an aggregation of individuals under one common form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD3","text":"Matter ceases to be the universal mark of created finitude, because the reception of being suffices to constitute potency, limitation, and distinction from God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD4","text":"The proximity of angelic nature to divine unity diminishes internal composition, not the multitude of substances.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD5","text":"The compositional mode of the human intellect expresses the condition of cognition, not the composition of the angelic thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A7","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SD6","text":"Angelic incorruptibility is caused natural necessity, yet inferior to divine immutability and to perfect immutability through grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX1","text":"The system requires the falsity of the position according to which nothing exists except what is apprehended by sense or imagination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX2","text":"The system requires the falsity of an isomorphism between distinctions of the intellect and compositions of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX3","text":"The system requires the falsity of universal hylomorphism, by which every reception, potency, and limitation are attributed to matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX4","text":"The system requires the falsity of the position according to which every plurality presupposes a division of quantity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX5","text":"The system requires the falsity of the teleological order by which spiritual substances would exist only for corporeal effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX6","text":"The system requires the falsity of the equation between caused being and intrinsically corruptible being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX7","text":"The system requires the falsity of the consequence by which greater proximity to unity would necessarily entail a lesser multitude of substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX1","text":"Direct and adequate apprehension of angelic substance is unavailable to the human intellect; knowledge of it proceeds by the mode of composite things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX2","text":"No material or quasi-material subject remains by which several spiritual substances might be individuated under the same species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3","text":"Aseity is precluded from a created spirit: even a subsisting form does not have being as absolutely subsisting.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX4","text":"Complete immutability does not belong to angelic nature, although substantial corruption is naturally impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX5","text":"The angelic order cannot be reduced to cosmological functions of bodies, because what is nobler is not ordered to the corporeal as to an end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS1","text":"The engine of perfection proceeds in this order: intention of the perfection of the universe → assimilation to the intellectual cause → intellectual creature → incorporeal creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A1","CH_GGVC_P_42:A2","CH_GGVC_P_42:A3","CH_GGVC_P_42:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS2","text":"The engine of substance proceeds in this order: object abstracted from matter → immaterial operation → immaterial substance → exclusion of all matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS3","text":"The engine of finitude proceeds in this order: subsisting form → received being → essence as potency to being → finitude without matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS4","text":"The engine of multitude proceeds in this order: transcendent plurality → distinction of forms → incorporeal excess according to multitude → multitude exceeding the material.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A10","CH_GGVC_P_42:A11","CH_GGVC_P_42:A12","CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS5","text":"The engine of distinction proceeds in this order: absence of matter → impossibility of individuation within the same species → distinct formal grades → one Angel per species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS6","text":"The engine of incorruption proceeds in this order: subsisting form → no separation of form from matter → no intrinsic principle of dissolution → natural incorruptibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A14","CH_GGVC_P_42:A15","CH_GGVC_P_42:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:FGS7","text":"The causal closure proceeds in this order: received being → dependence upon a conserving cause → caused necessity → incorruptibility without aseity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A16","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF1","text":"Perfection of the universe → assimilation to God causing through intellect and will → intellectual creature → incorporeality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF2","text":"Immateriality of understanding → immateriality of substance → exclusion of matter and form → composition of essence and being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF3","text":"Non-quantitative plurality → distinction of forms → immaterial multitude exceeding corporeal things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF4","text":"Absence of individuating matter → impossibility of several individuals of one species → multiplication of species according to intellectual grades.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:AF5","text":"Subsisting form → impossibility of intrinsic dissolution → natural incorruptibility → conserving dependence without corruptibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1","text":"The field of being extends beyond the sensible and imaginable, such that the incorporeal becomes an ontological object and not a mere privation of body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME2","text":"Finitude is separated from matter and located in the limitation of received being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME3","text":"Multitude is separated from quantity and the division of the continuum and is described as a transcendent distinction of forms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME4","text":"Genus, difference, and reception are distinguished from real compositions of matter, form, and subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A7","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME5","text":"The primary unity of the angelic order is transferred from common species to unique subsisting form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME6","text":"The spiritual hierarchy is freed from an instrumental order to bodies and is constituted according to its proper grades of perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ME7","text":"Incorruptibility is distinguished from aseity and complete immutability, whence created and caused necessity can be conceived.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ALT1","text":"Surface — Angels are established as incorporeal, immaterial, exceedingly numerous creatures, individually distinct in species and naturally incorruptible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ALT2","text":"Structural — The mode of operation manifests substance, matter provides individuation within the same species, and the composition of matter and form makes corruption possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument dissolves oppositions by distinguishing intellectual motion from bodily motion, essential circumscription from local circumscription, intellectual reception from material reception, and caused necessity from aseity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — A created spirit is a subsisting form above natural corruption, but has received being, is conserved by God, and does not naturally possess complete immutability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT1","text":"The body of axioms suffices to reconstruct five principal conclusions: incorporeality, immateriality, multitude, specific distinction, and incorruptibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT2","text":"The strongest connection is that which proceeds from immaterial operation to immaterial substance and from subsisting form to the absence of a principle of corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:A14","CH_GGVC_P_42:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT3","text":"The beginning of the argument depends on antecedent demonstrations, especially on the thesis that God produces through intellect and will and principally intends the perfection of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT4","text":"The excess of angelic multitude is not demonstrated with the same necessity as immateriality, but is sustained by an analogy between the magnitude of perfect bodies and the multitude of incorporeal substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT5","text":"The specific uniqueness of each Angel strictly follows from immateriality and the material principle of individuation, but the distinction of intellectual grades into species is not further demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT6","text":"The distinction between understood composition and real composition prevents the projection of modes of human cognition onto angelic substances, but leaves their knowledge indirect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A7","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT7","text":"No formal contradiction remains between incorruptibility and divine conservation, provided that corruptibility is defined through an intrinsic principle of dissolution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A16","CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: intellectual operation establishes immateriality; immateriality reorders finitude, multitude, and species; subsisting form concludes natural incorruptibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_42:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_42@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_42:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 51","title":"First Part · Question 50","context":"Chapter 51","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 50"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 50","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 51","order":52,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_43"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_43@R001","sha256":"ba07aaebd96c3c568a1aaae685700412872d0b1ad1ad767227bec76a30c3efe3","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinatur utrum apparentiae corporales Angelorum eorum naturam corpoream, corporibus naturaliter unitam, exigant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS2","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica-exegetica distinguit corpus quod naturam intellectualem constituit ab corpore quod ad manifestationem temporaliter assumitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","text":"Intelligere, cum non sit actus corporis, substantiam intellectualem perfectam a necessitate corporis ad cognitionem acquirendam liberat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","text":"Apparitiones Angelorum a pluribus exteriori visione perceptae non ad solam imaginationem propheticam reduci possunt; corpus igitur aliquando exterius adest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","text":"Corpus assumptum Angelo unitur non ut formae vivificanti, sed ut instrumento mobili quod proprietates intelligibiles sensibiliter repraesentat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS6","text":"Opera quae viventia videri faciunt resolvuntur in effectus materiales Angelis possibiles et in actus vitales proprios, quos corpus non vivens exercere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS7","text":"Motus argumentationis procedit ab incorporeitate essentiali ad corporalitatem apparentem, deinde ab apparentia vitali ad significationem non-vitalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A1","text":"Intelligere non est actus corporis neque virtutis corporeae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A2","text":"Unio corporis non pertinet per se ad rationem substantiae intellectualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","text":"Substantia intellectualis corpori unitur propter imperfectionem cognitionis quae sensibilia requirit ad scientiam acquirendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A4","text":"Ubi in eodem genere invenitur imperfectum, ibi praeexistit perfectum eiusdem generis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A5","text":"Sunt substantiae intellectuales perfectae quae scientiam ex sensibilibus acquirere non indigent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","text":"Angeli sunt substantiae intellectuales perfectae et a corporibus naturaliter separatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A7","text":"Quod ab omnibus videri potest visione exteriori, corpus extra videntem positum requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","text":"Angelus corpus assumit formando materiam corporalem ut proprietates intelligibiles eius sensibiliter repraesententur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A9","text":"Corpus assumptum non unitur Angelo ut formae vivificanti, sed ut mobili motori repraesentato subiecto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","text":"Vita est principium potentiale operum vitalium; cuius est potentia, eius est actio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","text":"Corpora ab Angelis assumpta non vivunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A12","text":"Effectus communes operibus viventium, ut sonus vel motus, fieri possunt sine actu vitali proprio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","text":"Organa sensibilia corporis assumpti ad sensum exercendum non ordinantur, sed ad virtutes spirituales significandas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A14","text":"Angelus, cum in corpore assumpto sit ut motor in mobili, per accidens movetur ad motum corporis et sic localiter determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX1","text":"Angelus non est animal compositum ex anima et corpore, quamvis metaphorice rationale animal appelletur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX2","text":"Corpus Angelicum non est pars naturalis naturae Angelicae neque instrumentum cognitionis Angelicae necessarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX3","text":"Apparitiones Angelorum non sunt universaliter visiones imaginariae privatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX4","text":"Assumptio corporis non est unio formalis corporis ad Angelum nec quaelibet motio corporis ab Angelo effecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX5","text":"Figura humana corporis assumpti non probat corpus esse vivum neque Angelum per illud sentire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX6","text":"Locutio, ambulatio et manducatio Angelica non sunt, proprie loquendo, opera vitae animalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX7","text":"Comestio apparens non est vera nutritio, quia cibus in corpus assumptum converti non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX8","text":"Angeli sancti nec per corpora assumpta generant nec in concubitum cadere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX9","text":"Deus non localiter movetur cum corporibus quibus adest, quia non sicut Angelus loco determinato continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D1","text":"Perfectio intellectualis Angelorum corpus naturale excludit, dum imperfectio animae humanae unionem corporis explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A2","CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A4","CH_GGVC_P_43:A5","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D2","text":"Apparitiones Angelicas communiter visibiles oportet corporales esse, etiamsi Angeli ipsi corporei non sint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D3","text":"Corpus assumptum est medium apparitionis ad homines, non supplementum naturae Angelicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D4","text":"Aer condensatus figurari et colorari potest; ideo materia aerea apta est ad corpus apparens formandum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D5","text":"Veritas apparitionis non requirit ut corpus apparens vere vivat, sed ut similitudines corporales ad spiritualia significanda ordinate serventur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D6","text":"Angelus sonos vocibus similes formare et corpus apparens movere potest, sed nec proprie loquitur nec motu vitali procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A9","CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D7","text":"Oculi et cetera membra corporis assumpti sunt signa virtutum Angelicarum, non instrumenta cognitionis sensitivae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D8","text":"Angelus per accidens localiter movetur cum corpore assumpto, quia praesentia eius corpori mobili determinatur; haec ratio Deo non competit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A9","CH_GGVC_P_43:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D9","text":"Relatio de filiis Dei et filiabus hominum non Angelos sanctos generantes demonstrat, sed ad filios Seth et filias stirpis Cain refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD1","text":"Incorporeitas ontologica et visibilitas empirica conciliantur per distinctionem inter naturam Angelicam et corpus episodice repraesentativum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A7","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD2","text":"Corpus in systemate non tantum res physica est, sed dispositio semiotica qua spirituale ad humanam cognitionem sensibilem traducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD3","text":"Praedicata vitae in strata dividuntur: effectus physicus exterior conceditur, principium vitale formale negatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD4","text":"Hierarchia corporum et locorum stabilitur: anima humana corpore indiget, Angelus corpus assumere potest sine eo indigendo, Deus nec corpore nec loco determinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A9","CH_GGVC_P_43:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD5","text":"Apparitiones Veteris Testamenti ordinantur ut signa anticipantia assumptionem veri corporis humani a Verbo Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem cognitionem intellectualem a sensibilibus et organis corporeis necessario pendere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet quidquid externe videtur eo ipso esse vivum, animatum vel naturae apparentis participem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet relationem moventis ad mobile sufficere ad unionem substantialem vel ad assumptionem formalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet veritatem Scripturae requirere identitatem literalem inter figuram sensibilem et rem spiritualem significatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem motum localem vel sonum vocis ex principio intrinseco vitali procedere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem generationem humano modo apparentem filiationem substantivam agentis apparentis efficere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX1","text":"Natura spiritualis perfecta non potest per corpus definiri, compleri aut ex visibili figura ontologice colligi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX2","text":"Sensibile non est terminus ultimus cognitionis spiritualis, sed signum ordinatum ad id quod sensum excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX3","text":"Angelus non potest simul esse forma vivificans corporis assumpti et substantia intellectualis ab eo separata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX4","text":"Distantia inter praesentiam Angelicam et omnipraesentiam divinam servanda est; praesentia creata necessario aliquam determinationem habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX5","text":"Apparentia anthropomorphica non licet in anthropologiam Angelorum convertere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS1","text":"Intelligere incorporeum → corpus non essentiale substantiae intellectuali → imperfectio cognitiva explicat unionem animae humanae → perfectio Angelica separat Angelum a corpore naturali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS2","text":"Visio exterior communis → obiectum corporale extra videntem → Angelus incorporeus tamen corpus interdum assumit → corpus fit medium apparitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS3","text":"Corpus assumptum ut mobile repraesentans → membra et actiones similitudinem humanam praebent → principium vitae deest → effectus communes conceduntur, actus vitales proprii negantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS4","text":"Corporalitas repraesentativa → significatio virtutum Angelicarum et societatis futurae → figurae Veteris Testamenti ordinantur ad apparitionem Verbi in carne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS5","text":"Motor in mobili → motus localis per accidens Angelo attribuitur → praesentia Angelica a stabilitate omnipraesentiae divinae distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AF1","text":"Apparentia corporalis Angelorum → distinctio naturae et accidentis → intellectio incorporea → Angelus naturaliter incorporeus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AF2","text":"Visio Angelorum communis et exterior → exclusio visionis mere imaginariae → necessitas corporis exterioris → assumptio temporalis corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AF3","text":"Corpus assumptum → unio motoria repraesentativa → apparens vita → divisio effectus communis et actus vitalis → negatio vitae, sensus, nutritionis et generationis propriae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AF4","text":"Motus corporis assumpti → motus per accidens Angeli → determinatio localis creaturae → contrastus cum omnipraesentia divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME1","text":"Corpus reclassificatur ab elemento necessario substantiae intellectualis ad medium contingens cognitionis humanae et manifestationis Angelicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME2","text":"Apparentia dividitur in visionem imaginariam privatam et visionem corpoream publice communicabilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME3","text":"Figura humana reclassificatur ab indicio vitae realis ad signum visibile proprietatum spiritualium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME4","text":"Actiones Angelorum resolvuntur in tres ordines: effectus physici, signa sensibilia et actus vitales formaliter exclusi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME5","text":"Praesentia localis distinguitur inter Deum ubique praesentem et Angelum qui per relationem ad mobilem corporis situm determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME6","text":"Narrationes scripturales de Angelis non tamquam descriptio biologiae Angelicae, sed tamquam ordinatio figurativa ad realitatem spiritualem et christologicam leguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT1","text":"Surface — Quaeritur utrum Angeli corpora naturalia habeant, corpora assumant, et per corpora assumpta opera vitae exerceant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT2","text":"Structural — Relatio intellectualis substantiae ad corpus pendet ex modo cognitionis, ex genere unionis, et ex praesentia vel absentia principii vitae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Testimonia Scripturae per distinctionem visionis, figurae, signi et rei significatae interpretantur, ne apparentia sensibilis in assertionem ontologicam convertatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Ordo entium disponitur secundum perfectionem intellectualem et modum praesentiae; apparitiones Angelicae temporales ad futuram societatem hominum cum Angelis atque ad incarnationem Verbi referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de incorporeitate intellectus, imperfectione cognitiva animae, perfectione Angelica et principio vitae sufficiunt ad conclusionem principalem de Angelis naturaliter incorporeis restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de visione exteriori et corpore assumpto sufficiunt ad conciliandam apparitionem publicam cum incorporeitate, sed validitas transitūs a visione communi ad corpus praesens supponitur potius quam ulterius demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT3","text":"Commissura principalis systematis est distinctio inter corpus quod similitudinem vitae efficit et corpus quod vita caret; haec firmatur per principium potentiae et actus, sed limites singulorum effectuum apparentium casu per casum definiendi manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT4","text":"Systema maxime cohaeret ubi unio formalis, motio externa et significatio sensibilis separantur; sic idem corpus potest moveri, apparere et significare sine animatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT5","text":"Tensionem retinet doctrina qua corpus Angelicum simul materialiter reale, sensibiliter publicum et vitaliter inane ponitur, quia criterium quo simulatio exterior a vera operatione vitali discernitur metaphysice, non empirice, stabilitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT6","text":"Exceptio de daemonibus semine humano assumpto non destruit negationem generationis Angelicae, sed distinctionem inter causalitatem materialem seminis humani et apparentem causalitatem daemonis necessario servat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum verum textus conservat: essentia intellectualis → necessitas vel superfluitas corporis → corporis assumptio repraesentativa → negatio vitae propriae in apparentia corporali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161658518207Z_288a13c2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 51","source_sha256":"ba07aaebd96c3c568a1aaae685700412872d0b1ad1ad767227bec76a30c3efe3","sha256":"7a25b0d3c9c9f294e712258979e528d78172992be01b707d0da34031c48f44d0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:16:58.520646+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS1","text":"The question examines whether the bodily appearances of Angels require a bodily nature naturally united to bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS2","text":"The metaphysical-exegetical argument distinguishes a body that constitutes an intellectual nature from a body temporarily assumed for manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","text":"Understanding, since it is not an act of a body, frees a perfect intellectual substance from the necessity of a body for acquiring knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","text":"Appearances of Angels perceived by several through external vision cannot be reduced to prophetic imagination alone; therefore a body is sometimes externally present.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","text":"An assumed body is united to an Angel not as to an animating form, but as a movable instrument that sensibly represents intelligible properties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS6","text":"Works that make living things appear to be such are resolved into material effects possible to Angels and into proper vital acts, which a non-living body cannot perform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AS7","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from essential incorporeality to apparent corporeality, then from vital appearance to non-vital signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A1","text":"Understanding is not an act of a body or of a bodily power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A2","text":"The union of a body does not belong per se to the account of an intellectual substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","text":"An intellectual substance is united to a body on account of the imperfection of cognition that requires sensibles in order to acquire knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A4","text":"Where the imperfect is found in the same genus, there the perfect of that same genus pre-exists.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A5","text":"There are perfect intellectual substances that do not need to acquire knowledge from sensibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","text":"Angels are perfect intellectual substances and naturally separate from bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A7","text":"What can be seen by all through external vision requires a body situated outside the seer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","text":"An Angel assumes a body by forming bodily matter so that its intelligible properties may be sensibly represented.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A9","text":"An assumed body is united to an Angel not as to an animating form, but as a movable subject represented by a mover.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","text":"Life is the potential principle of vital works; to whom the power belongs, to that one the action belongs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","text":"Bodies assumed by Angels do not live.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A12","text":"Effects common to the works of living things, such as sound or motion, can occur without a proper vital act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","text":"The sensory organs of an assumed body are not ordered to the exercise of sensation, but to signifying spiritual powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:A14","text":"An Angel, since it is in an assumed body as a mover in a movable thing, is moved per accidens by the body's motion and is thus locally determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX1","text":"An Angel is not an animal composed of soul and body, although it is metaphorically called a rational animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX2","text":"An Angelic body is neither a natural part of Angelic nature nor a necessary instrument of Angelic cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX3","text":"Appearances of Angels are not universally private imaginative visions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX4","text":"The assumption of a body is neither the formal union of a body to an Angel nor every motion of a body effected by an Angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX5","text":"The human figure of an assumed body does not prove that the body is alive or that the Angel senses through it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX6","text":"Angelic speech, walking, and eating are not, properly speaking, works of animal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX7","text":"Apparent eating is not true nutrition, because food cannot be converted into an assumed body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX8","text":"Holy Angels neither generate through assumed bodies nor can fall into intercourse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:NX9","text":"God is not locally moved with the bodies to which He is present, because He is not contained in a determinate place as an Angel is.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D1","text":"The intellectual perfection of Angels excludes a natural body, whereas the imperfection of the human soul explains union with a body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A2","CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A4","CH_GGVC_P_43:A5","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D2","text":"Angelic appearances commonly visible must be bodily, even if Angels themselves are not bodily.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D3","text":"An assumed body is a medium of appearance to human beings, not a supplement to Angelic nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D4","text":"Condensed air can be shaped and colored; therefore aerial matter is suited to forming an apparent body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D5","text":"The truth of an appearance does not require that the apparent body truly live, but that bodily likenesses be fittingly preserved for signifying spiritual things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D6","text":"An Angel can form sounds like voices and move an apparent body, but it neither properly speaks nor proceeds by vital motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A9","CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D7","text":"The eyes and other members of an assumed body are signs of Angelic powers, not instruments of sensitive cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D8","text":"An Angel is moved locally per accidens with an assumed body, because its presence is determined by a movable body; this account does not apply to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A9","CH_GGVC_P_43:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:D9","text":"The account of the sons of God and the daughters of men does not demonstrate that holy Angels generate, but refers to the sons of Seth and the daughters of the line of Cain.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD1","text":"Ontological incorporeality and empirical visibility are reconciled through the distinction between Angelic nature and an episodically representative body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A7","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD2","text":"In the system, a body is not merely a physical thing, but a semiotic arrangement through which the spiritual is conveyed to human sensible cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD3","text":"Predicates of life are divided into strata: an external physical effect is conceded, a formal vital principle is denied.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD4","text":"A hierarchy of bodies and places is established: the human soul needs a body, an Angel can assume a body without needing it, God is determined by neither body nor place.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A9","CH_GGVC_P_43:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SD5","text":"Appearances of the Old Testament are ordered as signs anticipating the assumption of a true human body by the Word of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A8","CH_GGVC_P_43:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX1","text":"It must be false that all intellectual cognition necessarily depends on sensibles and bodily organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX2","text":"It must be false that whatever is externally seen is thereby alive, animate, or a participant in the nature it appears to possess.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the relation of mover to movable is sufficient for substantial union or formal assumption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the truth of Scripture requires literal identity between a sensible figure and the spiritual thing signified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX5","text":"It must be false that every local motion or vocal sound proceeds from an intrinsic vital principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX6","text":"It must be false that every generation appearing in a human manner produces substantial filiation of the apparent agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX1","text":"A perfect spiritual nature cannot be defined or completed through a body, or ontologically inferred from a visible figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX2","text":"The sensible is not the ultimate terminus of spiritual cognition, but a sign ordered to that which exceeds sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX3","text":"An Angel cannot simultaneously be the animating form of an assumed body and an intellectual substance separate from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX4","text":"The distance between Angelic presence and divine omnipresence must be preserved; created presence necessarily has some determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX5","text":"An anthropomorphic appearance must not be converted into an anthropology of Angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS1","text":"Incorporeal understanding → body non-essential to intellectual substance → cognitive imperfection explains the union of the human soul → Angelic perfection separates the Angel from a natural body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS2","text":"Common external vision → bodily object outside the seer → incorporeal Angel nevertheless sometimes assumes a body → body becomes medium of appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS3","text":"Assumed body as representative movable thing → members and actions provide human likeness → principle of life is absent → common effects are conceded, proper vital acts denied.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS4","text":"Representative corporeality → signification of Angelic powers and future society → figures of the Old Testament are ordered to the appearance of the Word in flesh.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:FGS5","text":"Mover in movable thing → local motion is attributed to an Angel per accidens → Angelic presence is distinguished from the stability of divine omnipresence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AF1","text":"Bodily appearance of Angels → distinction of nature and accident → incorporeal understanding → Angel naturally incorporeal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AF2","text":"Common and external vision of Angels → exclusion of merely imaginative vision → necessity of an external body → temporal assumption of a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AF3","text":"Assumed body → representative motor union → apparent life → division between common effect and vital act → denial of proper life, sensation, nutrition, and generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:AF4","text":"Motion of the assumed body → motion of the Angel per accidens → local determination of the creature → contrast with divine omnipresence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME1","text":"Body is reclassified from a necessary element of intellectual substance to a contingent medium of human cognition and Angelic manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME2","text":"Appearance is divided into private imaginative vision and publicly communicable bodily vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME3","text":"Human figure is reclassified from an indication of real life to a visible sign of spiritual properties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME4","text":"The actions of Angels are resolved into three orders: physical effects, sensible signs, and formally excluded vital acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME5","text":"Local presence is distinguished between God, present everywhere, and an Angel, who is determined through relation to the mobile position of a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ME6","text":"Scriptural narratives concerning Angels are read not as descriptions of Angelic biology, but as figurative ordering toward spiritual and christological reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT1","text":"Surface — It is asked whether Angels have natural bodies, assume bodies, and perform works of life through assumed bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT2","text":"Structural — The relation of intellectual substance to body depends on the mode of cognition, the kind of union, and the presence or absence of the principle of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Testimonies of Scripture are interpreted through the distinction of vision, figure, sign, and thing signified, lest sensible appearance be converted into an ontological assertion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The order of beings is arranged according to intellectual perfection and mode of presence; temporal Angelic appearances are referred to the future society of humans with Angels and to the incarnation of the Word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT1","text":"Axioms concerning the incorporeality of intellect, the cognitive imperfection of the soul, Angelic perfection, and the principle of life suffice to reconstruct the principal conclusion concerning Angels as naturally incorporeal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT2","text":"Axioms concerning external vision and an assumed body suffice to reconcile public appearance with incorporeality, but the validity of the transition from common vision to a present body is presumed rather than further demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT3","text":"The principal joint of the system is the distinction between a body that produces the likeness of life and a body that lacks life; this is supported through the principle of potency and act, but the limits for defining individual apparent effects case by case remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT4","text":"The system is most coherent where formal union, external motion, and sensible signification are separated; thus the same body can be moved, appear, and signify without animation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT5","text":"The doctrine retains a tension in which an Angelic body is posited as materially real, sensibly public, and vitally empty at once, because the criterion by which external simulation is distinguished from true vital operation is established metaphysically, not empirically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT6","text":"The exception concerning demons assuming human seed does not destroy the denial of Angelic generation, but necessarily preserves the distinction between the material causality of human seed and the apparent causality of the demon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: intellectual essence → necessity or superfluity of body → representative assumption of body → denial of proper life in bodily appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_43:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_43@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_43:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 52","title":"First Part · Question 51","context":"Chapter 52","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 51"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 51","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 52","order":53,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_44"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_44@R001","sha256":"a772bfe3f69ba015d15844a55d1e6970eb3c3c2f169d69a1786323a591de681f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat quo sensu substantia incorporea possit esse in loco, cum condiciones localitatis corporalis ei non conveniant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","text":"Argumentatio locum Angeli a commensuratione quantitativa separat et eum per applicationem virtutis ad corpus reconstituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS3","text":"Finitas virtutis angelicae limitat applicationem eius ad unum ens determinatum, unde Angelus definitive in uno loco esse dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","text":"Distinctio inter corpus, Angelum et Deum tres modos praesentiae producit: circumscriptivum, definitivum et ubiquum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS5","text":"Coexistentia plurium Angelorum in eodem loco negatur non ex repletione spatii, sed ex impossibilitate plurium causarum completarum immediatarum eiusdem rei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","text":"Angelus est substantia incorporea immunis a quantitate dimensiva et situ corporali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","text":"Corpus est in loco per contactum quantitatis dimensivae, Angelus autem per applicationem virtutis suae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A3","text":"Virtus substantiae incorporeae contingens corpus continet corpus potius quam a loco contineatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","text":"Virtus angelica est finita et ad unum ens particulare determinatum se extendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A5","text":"Totum corpus cui virtus Angeli immediate applicatur rationem unius loci Angeli accipit, sive corpus sit divisibile sive indivisibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A6","text":"Deus, cuius virtus infinita est causa universalis omnium, omnia contingit et ubique est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","text":"Duae causae completae non possunt esse immediatae unius eiusdemque rei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A8","text":"Angelus est in loco per modum continentis perfecti, inquantum virtus eius immediate locum contingit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX1","text":"Angelus non est in loco circumscriptive, quia nec loco commensuratur nec situm quantitativum habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX2","text":"Angelus non est in loco ut contentum a continente corporali, sed ut continens corpus per virtutem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX3","text":"Incorporeitas Angeli non significat absentiam omnis localitatis, sed exclusionem localitatis corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX4","text":"Indivisibilitas Angeli non est indivisibilitas puncti positum habentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX5","text":"Angelus non est simul in pluribus locis nec ubique, quia virtus eius non est infinita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX6","text":"Plures Angeli non sunt simul in eodem loco, etsi Angeli locum corporaliter non replent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX7","text":"Communicatio loci inter Angelum et corpus non probat communicationem loci inter duos Angelos, quia eorum habitudines causales non sunt eiusdem generis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX8","text":"Communicatio corporis inter animam et Daemonem non constituit exemplum duarum formarum vel causarum immediatarum completarum eiusdem corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D1","text":"Angelus localiter praesens nec mensuratur loco nec in continuo situm accipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D2","text":"Corpus extensum potest uni Angelo respondere ut unus locus, si tota extensio unicae applicationi immediatae virtutis subiacet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D3","text":"Determinatio Angeli ad unum locum non exigit locum punctalem, sed unicum terminum applicationis virtutis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D4","text":"Deus est ubique, Angelus definitive in uno loco, corpus circumscriptive in loco; differentia localitatis sequitur differentiam virtutis et quantitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D5","text":"Exclusio plurium Angelorum ab eodem loco fundatur in exclusivitate causalitatis immediatae completae, non in impenetrabilitate materiali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D6","text":"Effectus vel motus qui ad Angelum referuntur non demonstrant praesentiam eius in pluribus locis, nisi applicatio immediata virtutis ad plura distincta stabilita sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SD1","text":"Localitas angelica transmutatur ex relatione geometrica corporis ad relationem causalem virtutis ad corpus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A3","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SD2","text":"Finitas metaphysica virtutis Angelicae fit principium distributionis localis: esse finitum causaliter est esse definitive determinatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SD3","text":"Numerus substantiarum spiritualium non auget capacitatem unius loci, quia pluralitas causarum immediatarum completarum non componitur in unam causalitatem localem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SD4","text":"Distinctio praesentiae divinae ab angelica prohibet ut imminutio localitatis corporalis directe convertatur in omnipraesentiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem praesentiam localem sub unica forma extensionis, situs et commensurationis comprehendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet incorporeitatem per se infinitatem virtualem vel multipraesentiam inferre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet indivisibile metaphysicum necessario indivisibilem partem spatii occupare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet absentiam repletionis corporalis sufficere ad compresentialitatem substantiarum spiritualium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet duas causalitates immediatas completas eiusdem termini sine subordinatione vel aggregatione consistere posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit spatium tamquam receptaculum neutrum quod per se praesentiam Angelicam definiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit aequivocationem inter transcendentiam quantitatis et transcendentiam omnis termini creati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit paritatem ultimam inter Deum, Angelum et corpus, quia eorum modi essendi in loco ex inaequalitate essentiae, virtutis et quantitatis oriuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS1","text":"Incorporeitas Angelica → negatio commensurationis, situs et continentiae corporalis → recusatio definitionis corporalis loci.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS2","text":"Negatio localitatis corporalis → applicatio virtutis ad corpus → praesentia definitiva ut continentia virtualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS3","text":"Applicatio virtualis + finitas virtutis → unus terminus determinatus → unus locus Angelicus, etiam si terminus est corpus continuum extensum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS4","text":"Unus locus ut terminus causalitatis immediatae + impossibilitas plurium causarum completarum immediatarum → exclusio plurium Angelorum ab eodem loco.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS5","text":"Infinitas divina contra finitatem angelicam et quantitatem corporalem → triplex typologia praesentiae: ubique, definitive, circumscriptive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AF1","text":"Negatio apparentis localitatis incorporei → aequivocatio loci → praesentia per virtutem continentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AF2","text":"Praesentia per virtutem → comparatio finiti Angeli cum Deo infinito → determinatio Angeli ad unum locum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AF3","text":"Determinatio ad unum locum → locus ut terminus causalitatis immediatae → exclusio coexistentiae plurium Angelorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME1","text":"Locus desinit esse categoria univoce corporalis et distinguitur secundum modum praesentiae causalis vel quantitativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME2","text":"Continuum corporale potest localiter unum esse respectu virtutis Angelicae, quamvis geometrice plures partes contineat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter esse localiter et esse incorporealiter dissolvitur: incorporeitas non tollit locum, sed mutat rationem essendi in loco.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME4","text":"Quaestio de co-localitate transfertur ab occupando spatio ad causaliter continendo eundem terminum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME5","text":"Omnipraesentia classificatur ut proprietas exclusiva causalitatis universalis infinitae, non ut gradus amplificatus praesentiae angelicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT1","text":"Surface — Angelus est in loco, non tamen sicut corpus; non est simul in pluribus locis; nec plures Angeli sunt simul in eodem loco.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT2","text":"Structural — Praesentia localis Angelica constituitur per contactum immediatum virtutis finitae cum corpore, non per extensionem substantiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones ex puncto, repletione loci, anima et corpore, vel pluralitate effectuum solvuntur per distinctionem generis causalitatis, non per additionem exceptionum spatialium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Finitas et infinitas essentiae determinat modum praesentiae: creatura spiritualis habet terminum virtualem, Deus nullum terminum creatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de incorporeitate, applicatione virtutis, finitate et causalitate immediata sufficiunt ad tres conclusiones articulorum generandas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT2","text":"Firmissimum nodum systematis constituit translatio loci ab extensione corporali ad terminum applicationis virtualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT3","text":"Probatio unius loci Angelici pendet ex identitate inter ens determinatum, terminum virtutis et rationem unius loci; criterium unitatis termini non ulterius resolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT4","text":"Probatio exclusionis plurium Angelorum pendet ex eo quod praesentia Angelica semper causalitas immediata completa intelligatur; distinctiones inter causalitatem cooperantem, remotam et completam tantum exemplis indicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT5","text":"Tensio manet inter facultatem virtutis Angelicae corpus maius vel minus voluntarie terminandi et necessitatem determinati unius loci, quia extensio termini variabilis est sed unitas eius praesupponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, quia a negatione localitatis corporalis procedit ad praesentiam virtualem, a finitate virtuali ad determinationem localem, et ab exclusivitate causali ad negationem co-localitatis Angelicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161721332839Z_c2986c4b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 52","source_sha256":"a772bfe3f69ba015d15844a55d1e6970eb3c3c2f169d69a1786323a591de681f","sha256":"a58b7c60e41d6b8c189caa927b3aa15fe7306d5c034f6410720df0be0eed418a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:17:21.333957+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS1","text":"The question investigates in what sense an incorporeal substance can be in a place, since the conditions of bodily locality do not befit it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","text":"The argument separates the Angel's place from quantitative commensuration and reconstitutes it through the application of power to a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS3","text":"The finitude of angelic power limits its application to one determinate being, whence the Angel is said to be definitively in one place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","text":"The distinction among body, Angel, and God produces three modes of presence: circumscriptive, definitive, and ubiquitous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AS5","text":"The coexistence of several Angels in the same place is denied not on account of the filling of space, but on account of the impossibility of several complete immediate causes of the same thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","text":"An Angel is an incorporeal substance exempt from dimensional quantity and bodily position.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","text":"A body is in a place through contact of dimensional quantity, whereas an Angel is there through the application of its power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A3","text":"The power of an incorporeal substance touching a body contains the body rather than being contained by the place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","text":"Angelic power is finite and extends to one determinate particular being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A5","text":"The whole body to which an Angel's power is immediately applied assumes the character of one place of the Angel, whether the body is divisible or indivisible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A6","text":"God, whose infinite power is the universal cause of all things, touches all things and is everywhere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","text":"Two complete causes cannot be immediate causes of one and the same thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:A8","text":"An Angel is in a place in the mode of a perfect container, insofar as its power immediately touches the place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX1","text":"An Angel is not in a place circumscriptively, because it is neither commensurated with the place nor has quantitative position.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX2","text":"An Angel is not in a place as something contained by a bodily container, but as containing the body through power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX3","text":"The incorporeality of an Angel does not signify the absence of every locality, but the exclusion of bodily locality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX4","text":"The indivisibility of an Angel is not the indivisibility of a point having position.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX5","text":"An Angel is neither simultaneously in several places nor everywhere, because its power is not infinite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX6","text":"Several Angels are not simultaneously in the same place, even though Angels do not bodily fill a place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX7","text":"The sharing of a place between an Angel and a body does not prove the sharing of a place between two Angels, because their causal relations are not of the same kind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:NX8","text":"The sharing of a body between a soul and a Demon does not constitute an example of two complete immediate forms or causes of the same body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D1","text":"An Angel locally present is neither measured by place nor receives position in a continuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D2","text":"An extended body can correspond to one Angel as one place, if the whole extension is subject to one immediate application of power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D3","text":"The determination of an Angel to one place does not require a punctual place, but a single terminus of the application of power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D4","text":"God is everywhere, an Angel definitively in one place, a body circumscriptively in a place; the difference of locality follows the difference of power and quantity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D5","text":"The exclusion of several Angels from the same place is grounded in the exclusivity of complete immediate causality, not in material impenetrability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:D6","text":"Effects or motions attributed to an Angel do not demonstrate its presence in several places, unless the immediate application of power to several distinct things has been established.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SD1","text":"Angelic locality is transformed from the geometrical relation of a body into the causal relation of power to a body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A3","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SD2","text":"The metaphysical finitude of Angelic power becomes a principle of local distribution: to be causally finite is to be definitively determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SD3","text":"The number of spiritual substances does not increase the capacity of one place, because a plurality of complete immediate causes is not composed into one local causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SD4","text":"The distinction of divine from angelic presence prevents the diminution of bodily locality from being directly converted into omnipresence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX1","text":"It must be false that every local presence is comprehended under a single form of extension, position, and commensuration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX2","text":"It must be false that incorporeality of itself entails virtual infinity or multipresence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX3","text":"It must be false that a metaphysical indivisible necessarily occupies an indivisible part of space.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the absence of bodily filling suffices for the compresence of spiritual substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX5","text":"It must be false that two complete immediate causalities of the same terminus can subsist without subordination or aggregation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SNX1","text":"The system excludes space as a neutral receptacle that of itself defines Angelic presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SNX2","text":"The system excludes an equivocation between transcendence of quantity and transcendence of every created terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:SNX3","text":"The system excludes an ultimate parity among God, Angel, and body, because their modes of being in a place arise from the inequality of essence, power, and quantity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS1","text":"Angelic incorporeality → negation of commensuration, position, and bodily containment → rejection of a bodily definition of place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS2","text":"Negation of bodily locality → application of power to a body → definitive presence as virtual containment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS3","text":"Virtual application + finitude of power → one determinate terminus → one Angelic place, even if the terminus is an extended continuous body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS4","text":"One place as the terminus of immediate causality + impossibility of several complete immediate causes → exclusion of several Angels from the same place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:FGS5","text":"Divine infinity against angelic finitude and bodily quantity → threefold typology of presence: everywhere, definitively, circumscriptively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AF1","text":"Negation of the apparent locality of the incorporeal → equivocation of place → presence through containing power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AF2","text":"Presence through power → comparison of finite Angel with infinite God → determination of the Angel to one place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:AF3","text":"Determination to one place → place as the terminus of immediate causality → exclusion of the coexistence of several Angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME1","text":"Place ceases to be a univocally bodily category and is distinguished according to the mode of causal or quantitative presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME2","text":"A bodily continuum can be locally one with respect to Angelic power, although geometrically it contains several parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME3","text":"The opposition between being locally and being incorporeally is dissolved: incorporeality does not remove place, but changes the account of being in a place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME4","text":"The question of co-locality is transferred from occupying space to causally containing the same terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ME5","text":"Omnipresence is classified as an exclusive property of infinite universal causality, not as an amplified degree of angelic presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT1","text":"Surface — An Angel is in a place, yet not as a body is; it is not simultaneously in several places; nor are several Angels simultaneously in the same place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT2","text":"Structural — Angelic local presence is constituted through the immediate contact of finite power with a body, not through the extension of substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections from a point, the filling of a place, soul and body, or plurality of effects are resolved through a distinction in the kind of causality, not through the addition of spatial exceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The finitude and infinity of essence determine the mode of presence: a spiritual creature has a virtual terminus, God no created terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning incorporeality, application of power, finitude, and immediate causality suffice to generate the three conclusions of the articles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT2","text":"The strongest node of the system consists in the translation of place from bodily extension to the terminus of virtual application.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT3","text":"The proof of one Angelic place depends on the identity among determinate being, the terminus of power, and the account of one place; the criterion of the unity of the terminus is not further resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT4","text":"The proof excluding several Angels depends on Angelic presence always being understood as complete immediate causality; distinctions among cooperating, remote, and complete causality are indicated only by examples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT5","text":"A tension remains between the capacity of Angelic power voluntarily to delimit a greater or lesser body and the necessity of one determinate place, because the extension of the terminus is variable but its unity is presupposed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the negation of bodily locality to virtual presence, from virtual finitude to local determination, and from causal exclusivity to the negation of Angelic co-locality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_44:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_44@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_44:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 53","title":"First Part · Question 52","context":"Chapter 53","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 52"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 52","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 53","order":54,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_45"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_45@R001","sha256":"3a79558fd266d6d2e2d6fb26753b98bbf4c74271ccc8ebc5c013f82e7e54da11","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat quomodo Angelus, substantia incorporea et indivisibilis, localiter moveri possit sine subiectione ad mensuras motus corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS2","text":"Argumentatio motum localem Angelicum ab motu corporis separat per analogiam aequivocam ipsius esse-in-loco.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","text":"Motus Angelicus resolvitur in successionem contactuum virtualium ad loca diversa, non in translationem magnitudinis contentae sub loco.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4","text":"Distinctio inter motum continuum et non continuum determinat utrum medium spatialiter pertranseatur atque utrum tempus continuum vel discretum mensuret motum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS5","text":"Contra hypothesim motus instantanei, prioritas et posterioritas dispositionum localium tempus requirunt, quamvis illud tempus a motu caeli non dependeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","text":"Motus Angelicus ab indigentia propria liberatur et ad applicationem voluntariam virtutis atque ad indigentiam creaturae ministratae refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A1","text":"Esse in loco corpori et Angelo aequivoce convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","text":"Corpus est in loco ut contentum et loco commensuratum; Angelus est in loco ut continens per contactum virtutis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A3","text":"Angelus simul in pluribus locis esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A4","text":"Motus localis Angeli est successio contactuum virtualium ad diversa loca, non simultanea praesentia in eis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A5","text":"Virtus Angelica applicari potest loco divisibili, quamvis substantia Angeli non sit quantitativa nec partibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","text":"Angelus potest motu continuo successive partes loci dimittere et occupare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","text":"Angelus potest motu non continuo totum locum simul dimittere et toti alteri loco simul applicari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A8","text":"Motus continuus exigit ordinem prioris et posterioris secundum magnitudinem atque transitum per medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A9","text":"Motus non continuus non consumit infinita media loca et ideo transire potest de extremo in extremum sine medio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A10","text":"Motus secundum applicationem virtutis est actus existentis in actu, non actus imperfecti secundum potentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","text":"Motus Angelicus habet prius et posterius dispositionum localium et propterea in tempore est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A12","text":"Continuitas temporis sequitur continuitatem motus; motus discontinuus successione nunc mensuratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A13","text":"Tempus motus Angelici non mensuratur motu caeli nec ab eo dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A14","text":"Velocitas motus Angelici ex determinatione voluntatis, non ex quantitate virtutis motricis, pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A15","text":"Motus Angelicus propter indigentiam alterius fieri potest, etiamsi Angelus nulla indigentia propria moveatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX1","text":"Angelus non est in loco ut corpus contentum, circumscriptum aut magnitudine loco aequatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX2","text":"Indivisibilitas Angelica non impedit motum, quia partialitas motus continui ad locum et applicationem virtutis, non ad substantiam, refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX3","text":"Motus localis Angelicus non est necessario continuus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX4","text":"Transitus Angelicus non est necessario per medium, nisi motus sub ratione continuitatis accipiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX5","text":"Motus Angelicus non est ex se signum imperfectionis, potentiae passivae aut indigentiae Angelicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX6","text":"Motus non continuus non est motus instantaneus, quia distincta ubi successive posita prius et posterius servant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX7","text":"Tempus Angelicum non est idem cum tempore continuo quod motum caelestem et mutabilitatem corporalem mensurat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX8","text":"Cogitatio animae de rebus distantibus non est exemplar sufficiens motus localis Angelici, quia intentio cognitiva non est applicatio essentiae ad locum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D1","text":"Leges motus localis corporalis non universaliter transferuntur ad omne ens quod localiter dici potest moveri.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A1","CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D2","text":"Eadem mutatio localis Angelica duas species recipit: continuam, quae medium percurrit, et non continuam, quae extrema sine medio succedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A8","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D3","text":"Infinitas locorum mediorum impedimentum fit solum motui discontinuo qui omnia media actu percurrere deberet; motus continuus illa media potentia continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A8","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D4","text":"In motu continuo Angelus diversis partibus locorum applicatur sine divisione substantiae suae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A5","CH_GGVC_P_45:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D5","text":"Motus Angelicus est actio actualis virtutis ad effectum externum ordinata, non processus quo Angelus perfectionem sibi absentem acquirat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A10","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D6","text":"Hypothesis qua Angelus toto tempore in termino a quo quiesceret et solo ultimo nunc ad terminum ad quem transiret motum proprium destruit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D7","text":"Motus Angelicus temporaliter ordinatus manet, sed ratio temporis eius variatur cum ratione continuitatis motus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D8","text":"Celeritas Angelica non ex superioritate metaphysica virtutis ad corpora mensuratur, sed ex modo voluntarie constituto quo virtus loco applicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SD1","text":"Locus et tempus non funguntur ut mensurae ontologice uniformes omnium entium, sed secundum modum quo ens loco applicatur et mutationem ordinat diversimode constituuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A1","CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SD2","text":"Motus Angelicus systematice medius constituitur inter motum corporalem continuum et mutationem pure instantaneam: potest discontinuus esse, sed extra tempus esse non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SD3","text":"Superioritas Angelica ad locum non tollit relationem localem, sed relationem localem sub potestate applicationis virtualis et voluntariae reponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SD4","text":"Causalitas motus Angelici ministerialis est: actio localis eius ex perfectione propria procedit, sed ad defectum vel necessitatem alterius ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A10","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem praesentiam localem extensionem quantitativam, circumscriptionem et continentiam materialem necessario importare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A1","CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem motum aut ex indigentia moventis aut ex imperfectione potentiae passivae nasci.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A10","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet continuitatem esse condicionem essentialem omnis motus, temporis et transitus localis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet tempus caeleste esse mensuram universalem cui omnis mutatio creata subiciatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet absentiam medii localis idem valere ac absentiam omnis ordinis temporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A9","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio excludit univocam cosmologiam in qua corpus, Angelus et omnis mutatio eodem ordine quantitativo spatii temporisque comprehendantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio pariter excludit spiritualismum qui actionem Angelicam a successione, relatione locali et omni temporali distinctione penitus liberaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX3","text":"Angelus non describitur neque ut corpus subtus locum neque ut actus omnino extra locum et tempus, sed ut agens cuius praesentia localis virtualiter ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS1","text":"Aequivocatio loci → corpus continetur et commensuratur; Angelus continet per contactum virtutis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS2","text":"Contactus virtualis successivus + exclusio multilocationis simultaneae → motus Angelicus localis constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS3","text":"Applicatio virtutis ad locum divisibilem → partialitas localis sine partitione substantiae possibilis fit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS4","text":"Modus dimittendi et occupandi locum → motus continuus per medium vel motus non continuus sine medio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS5","text":"Successio dispositionum localium → prius et posterius → tempus motus proprium, continuum vel non continuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS6","text":"Motus per se, non terminus motus alterius → motus instantaneus excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS7","text":"Actus virtutis voluntarie determinatus + indigentia alterius → motus ministerialis sine indigentia Angelica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF1","text":"Indivisibilitas et beatitudo videntur motum excludere → esse-in-loco Angelico a corporeo distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF2","text":"Contactus virtutis substituit commensurationem magnitudinis → motus ut successio ubi constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF3","text":"Successio ubi dupliciter disponitur → continuus transitus per medium / discontinuus transitus sine medio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF4","text":"Successio localis retinet prius et posterius → motus Angelicus temporaliter mensuratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF5","text":"Tempus a continuitate motus determinatur, non a caelo → tempus Angelicum proprium et non necessario continuum constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF6","text":"Motus ab indigentia propria separatur → applicatio virtutis voluntaria in ministerium alterius ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME1","text":"Locus reclassificatur ab recipiente quantitativo corporis ad terminum contactus virtualis Angeli.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME2","text":"Motus reclassificatur ab unica translatione continua ad genus quod continuitatem vel discontinuationem recipere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter motum temporalem et motum instantaneum dissolvitur per tertium: motum discontinuum temporaliter successivum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME4","text":"Partialitas localis distinguitur a divisione substantiae, ita ut applicatio virtutis divisibilis sit sine compositione Angeli.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME5","text":"Causa motus dividitur inter indigentiam moventis et finem ministrandi indigentiae alterius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME6","text":"Tempus corporale caeleste desinit esse index universalis omnis mutationis localis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus decernit Angelum localiter moveri posse, medium aliquando pertransire, atque motum eius in tempore esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT2","text":"Structural — Motus explicatur per applicationem et successionem contactuum virtutis, non per extensionem substantiae vel loci commensurationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones physicae non simpliciter negantur, sed ad condicionem propriam motus corporalis et continui restringuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Modus essendi Angeli supra locum contentivum fundat modum motus et temporis proprium, qui successionem admittit sine dependentia a motu caeli.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de aequivocatione loci, contactu virtutis et exclusione multilocationis simultaneae sufficiunt ad rationem motus localis Angelici restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT2","text":"Distinctio motus continui et non continui sufficienter generat differentiam transitus per medium et sine medio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT3","text":"Axiomata de prioritate et posterioritate sufficiunt ad reiectionem motus instantanei atque ad positionem temporis proprii Angelici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT4","text":"Systema maxime cohaeret ubi leges physicae corporales non negantur absolute, sed ad motum commensuratum et continuum limitantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter applicationem Angelicam totius virtutis ad terminum novum simul factam et necessitatem plurium nunc successivorum ad motum temporalem constituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT6","text":"Commissura altera manet quia tempus non continuum successione nunc definitur, cum ratio unitatis et mensurabilitatis huius successionis ulterius non explicetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0058","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: ex distinctione ontologica loci procedit ad bifurcationem motus, deinde ad rationem medii, temporis et finis ministerialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161745887596Z_f1eeeb95","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 53","source_sha256":"3a79558fd266d6d2e2d6fb26753b98bbf4c74271ccc8ebc5c013f82e7e54da11","sha256":"1fbef26406d0b670c45954bfe841cd2337265d7f3386cc945c7a725f46513059","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:17:45.888539+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS1","text":"The question examines how an Angel, an incorporeal and indivisible substance, can be moved locally without being subject to the measures of bodily motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS2","text":"The argument separates Angelic local motion from bodily motion through the equivocal analogy of being-in-a-place itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","text":"Angelic motion is resolved into a succession of virtual contacts with different places, not into the translation of a magnitude contained under place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4","text":"The distinction between continuous and non-continuous motion determines whether the spatial medium is traversed and whether continuous or discrete time measures the motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS5","text":"Against the hypothesis of instantaneous motion, the priority and posteriority of local dispositions require time, although that time does not depend on the motion of the heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","text":"Angelic motion is freed from a proper need and referred to the voluntary application of power and to the need of the creature being ministered to.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A1","text":"Being in a place belongs equivocally to a body and to an Angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","text":"A body is in a place as contained and commensurated with the place; an Angel is in a place as containing through contact of power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A3","text":"An Angel cannot be in several places simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A4","text":"The local motion of an Angel is a succession of virtual contacts with different places, not simultaneous presence in them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A5","text":"Angelic power can be applied to a divisible place, although the substance of the Angel is neither quantitative nor divisible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","text":"By continuous motion, an Angel can successively leave and occupy parts of a place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","text":"By non-continuous motion, an Angel can leave a whole place all at once and be applied all at once to another whole place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A8","text":"Continuous motion requires an order of prior and posterior according to magnitude and passage through a medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A9","text":"Non-continuous motion does not traverse infinitely many intermediate places and can therefore pass from extreme to extreme without a medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A10","text":"Motion according to the application of power is the act of what exists in act, not the act of the imperfect according to potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","text":"Angelic motion has a prior and a posterior of local dispositions and is therefore in time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A12","text":"The continuity of time follows the continuity of motion; discontinuous motion is measured by a succession of nows.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A13","text":"The time of Angelic motion is not measured by the motion of the heaven nor dependent upon it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A14","text":"The velocity of Angelic motion depends on the determination of the will, not on the quantity of motive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:A15","text":"Angelic motion can occur because of another's need, even though the Angel is moved by no need of its own.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX1","text":"An Angel is not in a place as a body contained, circumscribed, or equalized to the place in magnitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX2","text":"Angelic indivisibility does not impede motion, because the partiality of continuous motion refers to place and to the application of power, not to substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX3","text":"Angelic local motion is not necessarily continuous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX4","text":"Angelic passage is not necessarily through a medium, unless the motion is understood under the aspect of continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX5","text":"Angelic motion is not of itself a sign of imperfection, passive potency, or Angelic need.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX6","text":"Non-continuous motion is not instantaneous motion, because distinct where's successively posited preserve prior and posterior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX7","text":"Angelic time is not identical with continuous time, which measures heavenly motion and bodily mutability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:NX8","text":"The soul's thought about distant things is not a sufficient model of Angelic local motion, because cognitive intention is not the application of essence to a place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D1","text":"The laws of bodily local motion are not universally transferred to every being that can be said to be moved locally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A1","CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D2","text":"The same Angelic local change admits two species: continuous, which traverses the medium, and non-continuous, which succeeds from extreme to extreme without a medium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A8","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D3","text":"The infinity of intermediate places becomes an impediment only to discontinuous motion that would have to traverse all intermediates actually; continuous motion contains those intermediates in potency.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A8","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D4","text":"In continuous motion, an Angel is applied to diverse parts of places without division of its substance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A5","CH_GGVC_P_45:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D5","text":"Angelic motion is an actual action of power ordered toward an external effect, not a process by which an Angel acquires a perfection absent from itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A10","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D6","text":"The hypothesis according to which an Angel would rest at the terminus from which throughout the whole time and pass to the terminus to which only at the final now destroys motion properly so called.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D7","text":"Angelic motion remains temporally ordered, but the character of its time varies with the character of the continuity of the motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:D8","text":"Angelic speed is not measured by the metaphysical superiority of power over bodies, but by the voluntarily established manner in which power is applied to place.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SD1","text":"Place and time do not function as ontologically uniform measures of all beings, but are constituted differently according to the manner in which a being is applied to place and orders change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A1","CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SD2","text":"Angelic motion is systematically constituted as intermediate between continuous bodily motion and purely instantaneous change: it can be discontinuous, but it cannot be outside time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SD3","text":"Angelic superiority with respect to place does not remove local relation, but places local relation under the power of virtual and voluntary application.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SD4","text":"The causality of Angelic motion is ministerial: its local action proceeds from its own perfection, but is ordered to another's defect or need.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A10","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX1","text":"It must be false that every local presence necessarily entails quantitative extension, circumscription, and material containment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A1","CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX2","text":"It must be false that every motion arises either from the need of the mover or from the imperfection of passive potency.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A10","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX3","text":"It must be false that continuity is an essential condition of every motion, time, and local passage.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX4","text":"It must be false that heavenly time is the universal measure to which every created change is subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the absence of a local medium is equivalent to the absence of every temporal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A9","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX1","text":"The argument excludes a univocal cosmology in which body, Angel, and every change are comprehended under the same quantitative order of space and time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX2","text":"The argument likewise excludes a spiritualism that would wholly free Angelic action from succession, local relation, and every temporal distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX3","text":"An Angel is described neither as a body under place nor as an act wholly outside place and time, but as an agent whose local presence is virtually ordered.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS1","text":"Equivocation of place → a body is contained and commensurated; an Angel contains through contact of power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS2","text":"Successive virtual contact + exclusion of simultaneous multilocation → Angelic local motion is constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS3","text":"Application of power to a divisible place → local partiality without partition of substance becomes possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS4","text":"Manner of leaving and occupying place → continuous motion through a medium or non-continuous motion without a medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS5","text":"Succession of local dispositions → prior and posterior → proper time of motion, continuous or non-continuous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS6","text":"Motion in itself, not the terminus of another motion → instantaneous motion is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:FGS7","text":"Voluntarily determined act of power + another's need → ministerial motion without Angelic need.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF1","text":"Indivisibility and beatitude appear to exclude motion → Angelic being-in-a-place is distinguished from bodily being-in-a-place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF2","text":"Contact of power replaces commensuration of magnitude → motion as a succession of where's is constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF3","text":"Succession of where's is arranged in two ways → continuous passage through a medium / discontinuous passage without a medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF4","text":"Local succession retains prior and posterior → Angelic motion is measured temporally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF5","text":"Time is determined by the continuity of motion, not by the heaven → Angelic time proper and not necessarily continuous is constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:AF6","text":"Motion is separated from a proper need → voluntary application of power is ordered to the ministry of another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME1","text":"Place is reclassified from the quantitative receptacle of a body to the terminus of an Angel's virtual contact.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME2","text":"Motion is reclassified from a single continuous translation to a genus that can admit continuity or discontinuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME3","text":"The opposition between temporal motion and instantaneous motion is dissolved through a third: temporally successive discontinuous motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME4","text":"Local partiality is distinguished from division of substance, so that the application of power may be divisible without composition in the Angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME5","text":"The cause of motion is divided between the need of the mover and the end of ministering to another's need.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ME6","text":"Bodily heavenly time ceases to be the universal index of every local change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines that an Angel can be moved locally, can sometimes traverse a medium, and that its motion is in time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT2","text":"Structural — Motion is explained through the application and succession of contacts of power, not through extension of substance or commensuration with place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Physical objections are not simply denied, but restricted to the proper condition of bodily and continuous motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The Angel's mode of being above containment by place grounds a proper mode of motion and time, which admits succession without dependence on the motion of the heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning the equivocation of place, contact of power, and exclusion of simultaneous multilocation suffice to restore the account of Angelic local motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT2","text":"The distinction of continuous and non-continuous motion sufficiently generates the difference between passage through a medium and passage without a medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT3","text":"The axioms concerning priority and posteriority suffice for the rejection of instantaneous motion and for the positing of Angelic proper time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT4","text":"The system is most coherent where bodily physical laws are not denied absolutely, but limited to commensurated and continuous motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains between the Angelic application of its whole power to a new terminus effected all at once and the necessity of several successive nows for constituting temporal motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT6","text":"Another joint remains because non-continuous time is defined by a succession of nows, while the account of the unity and measurability of this succession is not further explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0058","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the motion of the text: from the ontological distinction of place it proceeds to the bifurcation of motion, then to the account of the medium, time, and ministerial end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_45:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_45@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_45:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 54","title":"First Part · Question 53","context":"Chapter 54","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 53"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 53","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 54","order":55,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_46"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_46@R001","sha256":"8acdafff3854ae85cd107e84183b59bae2f1fe98ce92da45c46cf85d6eea11b6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS1","text":"Quaestio constituitur utrum in Angelo substantia, esse, intelligere et virtus intellectiva realiter identificari possint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2","text":"Argumentatio metaphysico-diagnostica distinctionem Creatoris et creaturae assumit: solus Deus est actus purus, cui substantia, esse et agere identice conveniunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS3","text":"Ex finitudine creaturae infertur quod operatio intellectualis neque substantia neque esse Angeli est, et quod virtus operativa ab essentia distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS4","text":"Distinctio intellectus agentis et possibilis reducitur ad condiciones cognoscendi per phantasmata et intelligibilia tantum potentia existentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS5","text":"Cum Angelus careat corpore naturaliter sibi unito et intelligibilia sua naturaliter actu cognoscibilia habeat, facultates sensitivae atque intellectus agens et possibilis ei proprie non attribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS6","text":"Voces de sensu, experientia, memoria, phantasia et illuminatione angelica conservantur tantum secundum similitudinem effectus vel obiecti, non secundum identitatem potentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","text":"In omni creatura essentia ab esse differt et ad esse comparatur sicut potentia ad actum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","text":"Solus Deus est actus purus; ideo solius Dei substantia est suum esse et suum agere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A3","text":"Actio est actualitas virtutis, sicut esse est actualitas substantiae vel essentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A4","text":"Actualitas non potest identice convenire ei quod potentiam admixtam retinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A5","text":"Proprius actus propriae potentiae respondet; diversitas actuum diversitatem potentiarum requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","text":"Esse creaturae determinatur ad unum genus et speciem, sed intelligere et velle, secundum obiecta verum et bonum, ad ens universaliter se habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A7","text":"Essentia Angeli est ratio totius esse sui, non autem ratio totius intelligere sui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A8","text":"Intellectus possibilis requirit cognoscentem qui respectu intelligibilium naturalium quandoque est in potentia, et intellectus agens requirit intelligibilia extra animam quae sunt tantum potentia intelligibilia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","text":"Angeli naturaliter corpora sibi unita non habent; potentiae autem sensitivae operationes per organa corporea exercent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A10","text":"Nomen potentiae vel actus non sufficienter demonstrat eius rationem metaphysicam, quia praedicatio potest esse per concomitantiam, analogiam vel aequivocationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX1","text":"Angelus non est suum intelligere, quia creatura non est actualitas pura suae operationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX2","text":"Intelligere Angeli non est esse eius, quia operatio cognoscitiva secundum obiectum universalitatem habet quam esse creatum non habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX3","text":"Virtus intellectiva Angeli non est eius essentia, quamvis Angelus sit forma simplex.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX4","text":"Illuminatio Angeli inferioris non est operatio intellectus agentis, quia intellectus agens intelligibilia potentia abstrahendo facit actu intelligibilia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX5","text":"Potentia Angeli ad mysteria supernaturalia non est intellectus possibilis proprie dictus, quia haec potentia non est ad cognoscibilia naturalia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX6","text":"Sensus, imaginatio et memoria sensitiva Angelis non competunt ut facultates propriae, quia organum corporale requirunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX7","text":"Actio immanens intelligendi non est medium reale inter intelligentem et intellectum, sed effectus unionis obiecti cum intelligente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D1","text":"In Angelo substantia, esse, virtus intellectiva et intelligere ordinantur ut principia distincta, non ut unum actus subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A3","CH_GGVC_P_46:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D2","text":"Simplicitas angelica non destruit compositionem metaphysicam potentiae et actus quae ex distinctione essentiae et esse sequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D3","text":"Eadem essentia angelica potest esse principium essendi et intelligendi secundum rationes diversas, quin esse et intelligere identica fiant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","CH_GGVC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D4","text":"Si Angelus esset suum intelligere subsistens, distinctio Dei, Angelorum et graduum cognitionis tolleretur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D5","text":"Intellectus agens et possibilis sunt distinctiones conditionales cognitionis humanae, non partes universales omnis naturae intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A8","CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D6","text":"Cognitio angelica est totaliter intellectualis, quia sola intellectus et voluntas inter potentias animae operationes sine organo corporali habent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D7","text":"Attributiones sensus, experientiae, memoriae et phantasiae Angelis non describunt structuram facultatum eorum, sed similitudinem apprehensionis vel cognitionis singularium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SD1","text":"Hierarchia entium constituitur per modum participationis actus: Deus est actus infinitus per essentiam, Angelus vero intellectualis creatura finita per participationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SD2","text":"Intellectualitas angelica maximam perfectionem creatam designat, non autosufficientiam divinam, quia etiam in Angelo actus cognoscendi ab essentia et esse distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D1","CH_GGVC_P_46:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SD3","text":"Differentiae facultatum non ex vocabulario psychologico, sed ex condicionibus ontologicis obiecti, potentiae et organi corporis determinandae sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A5","CH_GGVC_P_46:A8","CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SD4","text":"Illuminatio hierarchica inter Angelos potest manere sine processu abstractionis, quia transmissio vel receptio cognitionis non eadem est ac reductio intelligibilis de potentia ad actum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_46:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omnis forma simplex sit actus purus et ideo incapax accidentis vel potentiae operativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod perfectio intellectualis creaturae eius dependentiam ab actu essendi et distinctionem principiorum internorum absorbeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omnis receptio cognitionis sit passivitas intellectus possibilis, vel quod omnis illuminatio sit actio intellectus agentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod praedicata cognitionis univoce transferantur inter hominem corporeum et substantiam separatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit creaturam quae sit ipsum intelligere subsistens, quia talis positio distinctionem inter Deum, Angelos et gradus cognitionis destrueret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit cognitionem creatam quae simul sit infinita secundum essentiam et determinata secundum speciem, quia infinitas simpliciter soli esse divino convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit facultatem cognoscitivam cuius ratio independenter a suo obiecto, a suo actu et a condicione corporali definiri possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS1","text":"Creatura participans esse et potentiam → negatio identitatis essentiae, esse et operationis → distinctio substantiae, virtutis et actus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A3","CH_GGVC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS2","text":"Esse creatum determinatum + intelligere obiecto universali apertum → negatio identitatis esse et intelligere → essentia eadem sub diversis rationibus principium essendi et cognoscendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","CH_GGVC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS3","text":"Absentia cognitionis naturaliter potentialis + absentia intelligibilium materialium tantum potentia → negatio intellectus agentis et possibilis proprie dictorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS4","text":"Absentia corporis naturaliter uniti + necessitas organorum pro potentiis sensitivis → exclusio sensus et imaginationis → affirmatio cognitionis angelicae totaliter intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS5","text":"Distantia inter proprietatem metaphysicam et usum sermonis → reinterpretatio praedicatorum sensitivi generis per analogiam, concomitantiam vel aequivocationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AF1","text":"Identitas angelica postulata → oppositio actus puri divini et creaturae participantis → separatio essentiae, esse, virtutis et operationis → determinatio condicionum intellectus agentis et possibilis → remotio facultatum organicarum → cognitio angelica totaliter intellectualis et terminis analogicis descripta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ME1","text":"Angelus reclassificatur non ut intellectus subsistens, sed ut substantia intellectualis creata cuius cognitio est operatio propria potentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ME2","text":"Oppositio simplex inter cognitionem activam et passivam dissolvitur, quia intellectus agens et possibilis definiuntur per mechanismum abstractionis humanum, non per omnem illuminationem et receptionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D5","CH_GGVC_P_46:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ME3","text":"Distinctio inter cognitionem intellectualem et sensitivam fit distinctio ontologica inter operationem sine organo et operationem per organum, non mera distinctio graduum experientiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ME4","text":"Vocabula psychologica transferuntur ex indicationibus facultatum in indicationes similitudinum, ita ut sensus, memoria et phantasia angelica analogice tantum intelligantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus negat Angelum esse suum intelligere, suum esse, suam potentiam intellectivam, vel subiectum facultatum sensitivarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT2","text":"Structural — Distinctiones internæ Angeli generantur ex compositione essentiae et esse, ex ordine potentiae ad actum, et ex dependentia potentiarum a propriis actibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio impedit ut nomina traditionalia, sicut intellectus agens, sensus vel memoria, pro probationibus ontologicis sine examine rationis propria accipiantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Deus solus est actus infinitus et subsistens; creaturae, etiam intellectuales, actus suos participant et cognitionem suam sub distinctionibus essentiae, potentiae et operationis exercent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam conclusionem principalem quod Angelus nec suum intelligere nec suum esse nec suam virtutem intellectivam est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A3","CH_GGVC_P_46:A5","CH_GGVC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT2","text":"Systema maxime cohaeret ubi distinctio Dei actus puri et creaturae potentiam retinentis simul fundamentum praebet distinctionibus substantiae, esse et operationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT3","text":"Transitus a simplicitate angelica ad capacitatem accidentis sustentatur per distinctionem inter formam simplicem puram et formam simplicem quae non est suum esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter potentiam Angeli ad mysteria supernaturalia et negationem intellectus possibilis, quam textus servat restringendo nomen ad potentiam respectu cognoscibilium naturalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT5","text":"Commissura altera manet in principio quod intelligere subsistens unum tantum esse potest, quo imminutio distinctionis Dei et Angelorum vel graduum cognitionis prohibetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia ab ontologia actus procedit ad theoriam potentiarum, inde ad determinationem condicionum cognitionis angelicae et ad disciplinam analogicam sermonis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161808966796Z_6725e220","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 54","source_sha256":"8acdafff3854ae85cd107e84183b59bae2f1fe98ce92da45c46cf85d6eea11b6","sha256":"aec791fe2528f50d9ba75ee50ac25c3e4a6d7c82e1e5a3a4d7464ab90d29b7bb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:18:08.971456+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS1","text":"The question is posed whether in an Angel substance, being, understanding, and intellectual power can be really identified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2","text":"The metaphysical-diagnostic argument assumes the distinction between Creator and creature: God alone is pure act, to whom substance, being, and acting belong identically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS3","text":"From the finitude of the creature it is inferred that intellectual operation is neither the substance nor the being of the Angel, and that operative power is distinct from essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS4","text":"The distinction between agent and possible intellect is reduced to the conditions of knowing through phantasms and intelligibles existing only potentially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS5","text":"Since the Angel lacks a body naturally united to it and has its intelligibles naturally knowable in act, sensitive faculties as well as agent and possible intellect are not properly attributed to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AS6","text":"Terms concerning sense, experience, memory, phantasy, and angelic illumination are retained only according to likeness of effect or object, not according to identity of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","text":"In every creature essence differs from being and is related to being as potency to act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","text":"God alone is pure act; therefore the substance of God alone is its own being and its own acting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A3","text":"Action is the actuality of power, just as being is the actuality of substance or essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A4","text":"Actuality cannot belong identically to that which retains potency mixed in.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A5","text":"A proper act corresponds to a proper power; diversity of acts requires diversity of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","text":"The being of a creature is determined to one genus and species, but understanding and willing, according to the objects true and good, are related to being universally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A7","text":"The essence of the Angel is the principle of its whole being, but not the principle of its whole understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A8","text":"The possible intellect requires a knower that is at times in potency with respect to natural intelligibles, and the agent intellect requires intelligibles outside the soul that are intelligible only potentially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","text":"Angels do not naturally have bodies united to them; sensitive powers, however, exercise operations through bodily organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:A10","text":"The name of a power or act does not sufficiently demonstrate its metaphysical nature, because predication can be by concomitance, analogy, or equivocation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX1","text":"The Angel is not its own understanding, because a creature is not the pure actuality of its operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX2","text":"The understanding of the Angel is not its being, because cognitive operation has, according to its object, a universality that created being does not have.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX3","text":"The intellectual power of the Angel is not its essence, although the Angel is a simple form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX4","text":"The illumination of an inferior Angel is not an operation of the agent intellect, because the agent intellect, by abstracting intelligibles in potency, makes them intelligible in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX5","text":"The Angel's potency for supernatural mysteries is not the possible intellect properly so called, because this potency is not for natural knowables.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX6","text":"Sense, imagination, and sensitive memory do not belong to Angels as proper faculties, because they require a bodily organ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:NX7","text":"The immanent action of understanding is not a real medium between the one understanding and the thing understood, but an effect of the union of the object with the one understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D1","text":"In the Angel, substance, being, intellectual power, and understanding are ordered as distinct principles, not as one subsisting act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A3","CH_GGVC_P_46:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D2","text":"Angelic simplicity does not destroy the metaphysical composition of potency and act that follows from the distinction of essence and being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D3","text":"The same angelic essence can be the principle of being and understanding according to diverse aspects, without being and understanding becoming identical.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","CH_GGVC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D4","text":"If the Angel were its own subsisting understanding, the distinction of God, Angels, and degrees of cognition would be removed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D5","text":"Agent and possible intellect are conditional distinctions of human cognition, not universal parts of every intellectual nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A8","CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D6","text":"Angelic cognition is wholly intellectual, because only intellect and will among the powers of the soul have operations without a bodily organ.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:D7","text":"Attributions of sense, experience, memory, and phantasy to Angels do not describe the structure of their faculties, but likeness of apprehension or cognition of singulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SD1","text":"The hierarchy of beings is constituted through the mode of participation in act: God is infinite act through essence, whereas the Angel is a finite intellectual creature through participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SD2","text":"Angelic intellectuality designates the greatest created perfection, not divine self-sufficiency, because even in the Angel the act of knowing is distinct from essence and being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D1","CH_GGVC_P_46:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SD3","text":"Differences of faculties are to be determined not from psychological vocabulary, but from the ontological conditions of object, power, and bodily organ.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A5","CH_GGVC_P_46:A8","CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SD4","text":"Hierarchical illumination among Angels can remain without a process of abstraction, because the transmission or reception of cognition is not the same as the reduction of the intelligible from potency to act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_46:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:DNX1","text":"It must be false that every simple form is pure act and therefore incapable of accident or operative potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the intellectual perfection of a creature absorbs its dependence on the act of being and the distinction of its internal principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:DNX3","text":"It must be false that every reception of cognition is passivity of the possible intellect, or that every illumination is an action of the agent intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:DNX4","text":"It must be false that predicates of cognition are transferred univocally between the corporeal human being and the separate substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SNX1","text":"The system excludes a creature that is subsisting understanding itself, because such a position would destroy the distinction between God, Angels, and degrees of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SNX2","text":"The system excludes created cognition that is at once infinite according to essence and determined according to species, because infinity simply belongs to divine being alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:SNX3","text":"The system excludes a cognitive faculty whose nature can be defined independently of its object, its act, and bodily condition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS1","text":"Creature participating in being and potency → negation of the identity of essence, being, and operation → distinction of substance, power, and act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A3","CH_GGVC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS2","text":"Determined created being + understanding open to a universal object → negation of the identity of being and understanding → the same essence, under diverse aspects, principle of being and knowing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","CH_GGVC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS3","text":"Absence of naturally potential cognition + absence of material intelligibles only in potency → negation of agent and possible intellect properly so called.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS4","text":"Absence of a naturally united body + necessity of organs for sensitive powers → exclusion of sense and imagination → affirmation of angelic cognition as wholly intellectual.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS5","text":"Distance between metaphysical property and linguistic usage → reinterpretation of predicates of the sensitive kind through analogy, concomitance, or equivocation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:AF1","text":"Postulated angelic identity → opposition between divine pure act and participating creature → separation of essence, being, power, and operation → determination of the conditions of agent and possible intellect → removal of organic faculties → angelic cognition wholly intellectual and described in analogical terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ME1","text":"The Angel is reclassified not as a subsisting intellect, but as a created intellectual substance whose cognition is the proper operation of a power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ME2","text":"The simple opposition between active and passive cognition is dissolved, because agent and possible intellect are defined by the human mechanism of abstraction, not by every illumination and reception.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D5","CH_GGVC_P_46:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ME3","text":"The distinction between intellectual and sensitive cognition becomes an ontological distinction between operation without an organ and operation through an organ, not a mere distinction of degrees of experience.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ME4","text":"Psychological terms are transferred from indications of faculties to indications of likenesses, such that angelic sense, memory, and phantasy are understood only analogically.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text denies that the Angel is its own understanding, its own being, its own intellectual power, or the subject of sensitive faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT2","text":"Structural — The Angel's internal distinctions are generated from the composition of essence and being, from the order of potency to act, and from the dependence of powers on their proper acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument prevents traditional names, such as agent intellect, sense, or memory, from being taken as ontological proofs without examination of their proper nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — God alone is infinite and subsisting act; creatures, even intellectual ones, participate in their acts and exercise their cognition under the distinctions of essence, potency, and operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal conclusion that the Angel is neither its own understanding nor its own being nor its own intellectual power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A3","CH_GGVC_P_46:A5","CH_GGVC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT2","text":"The system is most coherent where the distinction between God as pure act and the creature retaining potency simultaneously provides a foundation for the distinctions of substance, being, and operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT3","text":"The transition from angelic simplicity to the capacity for accident is sustained through the distinction between a pure simple form and a simple form that is not its own being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains between the Angel's potency for supernatural mysteries and the negation of possible intellect, which the text preserves by restricting the name to potency with respect to natural knowables.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT5","text":"Another juncture remains in the principle that there can be only one subsisting understanding, by which the diminution of the distinction of God and Angels or of degrees of cognition is prevented.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_46:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the ontology of act to the theory of powers, thence to the determination of the conditions of angelic cognition and to the analogical discipline of language.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_46:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_46:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_46@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_46:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 55","title":"First Part · Question 54","context":"Chapter 55","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 54"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 54","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 55","order":56,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_47"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_47@R001","sha256":"5c1767c2e6de8a3950800dea91bd073570a82a794c2b14f4a780a3082b915061","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat utrum cognitio angelica fundetur in essentia cognoscentis, in speciebus rebus acceptis, an in speciebus connaturalibus gradu hierarchico diversis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2","text":"Angelus omnia per essentiam suam cognoscere nequit, quia potentia eius intellectiva ad ens commune se extendit, essentia vero eius finita ad rationem determinatam contrahitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS3","text":"Species angelicae non a rebus sensibilibus recipiuntur, sed cum natura intellectuali ab influxu divino connaturaliter dantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS4","text":"Superioritas angelica mensuratur minore multitudine specierum et maiore universalitate mediorum, quibus plura propria cognoscuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS5","text":"Motus argumentationis procedit ab insufficientia essentiae finitae ad necessitatem specierum, ab immaterialitate angelica ad earum originem connaturalem, et ab propinquitate ad Deum ad gradationem universalitatis cognoscitivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A1","text":"Id quo intellectus intelligit est forma intellectus actu intelligentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A2","text":"Forma intellectiva potentiam perfecte perficit solum si continet omnia ad quae illa potentia se extendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A3","text":"Obiectum intellectus est ens vel verum commune.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A4","text":"Essentia angelica est finita et determinata ad genus et speciem, ideoque omnes rationes rerum proprias non comprehendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A5","text":"Sola essentia divina, quia infinita est, omnia perfecte et secundum proprias rationes comprehendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A6","text":"Modus essendi substantiae determinat modum quo perfectionem intelligibilem consequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A7","text":"Substantia intellectualis corpori unita perfectionem intelligibilem successive ex rebus accipit, quia esse eius corpori affine est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","text":"Angelus, a corpore omnino absolutus et immaterialiter subsistens, species intelligibiles connaturales habet ad omnia quae naturaliter cognoscere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","text":"Species angelicae a Deo procedunt simul cum natura intellectuali, quia similitudines rerum primario in Deo sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","text":"Quanto intellectus creatus Deo propinquior est, tanto plura intelligibilia per pauciora media cognoscere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A11","text":"Medium universale excellens potest esse ratio propria plurium, si in se continet unde diversa secundum proprias rationes similentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX1","text":"Cognitio angelica non est comprehensio omnium per essentiam angelicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX2","text":"Locutio qua Angelus res cognoscere dicitur secundum naturam suam non designat essentiam suam tamquam medium cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX3","text":"Identitas intellectus in actu et intellecti in actu non significat identitatem substantiae intelligentis cum similitudine qua intelligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX4","text":"Praesentia rerum in essentia angelica non est praesentia perfecta neque praesentia secundum proprias rationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX5","text":"Cognitio angelica non oritur ex abstractione specierum a rebus sensibilibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX6","text":"Universalitas specierum angelicarum non requirit originem per abstractionem a singularibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX7","text":"Cognoscere per medium universale non est necessario cognoscere rem solum secundum naturam universalem et imperfectam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX8","text":"Motus localis Angeli non ordinatur ad acquisitionem cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D1","text":"Intellectus angelicus indiget speciebus intelligibilibus distinctis ab essentia sua, quia obiectum eius excedit continentiam essentiae finitae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A1","CH_GGVC_P_47:A2","CH_GGVC_P_47:A3","CH_GGVC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D2","text":"Angelus per essentiam suam potest habere cognitionem communem aliorum entium, sed non cognitionem propriam et perfectam eorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A4","CH_GGVC_P_47:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D3","text":"Species angelicae sunt similitudines creaturarum causatae a Deo, non imagines ab ipsis creaturis impressae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D4","text":"Abstrahere formas materiales directe in esse intelligibile est Angelo impossibile secundum ordinem positum, quia transitio requireret medium imaginationis quo caret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A6","CH_GGVC_P_47:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D5","text":"Etiam si Angelus abstrahere posset, abstractione non indigeret, quia species connaturales iam habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D6","text":"Cognitio angelica secundum locum aequaliter se habet ad propinquum et distans.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D7","text":"Angelus movetur localiter ad operationem in loco exercendam, non ut obiectum cognoscibile sibi praesens fiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D8","text":"Superior Angelus per formas universaliores potest singula propria cognoscere, quia universalitas medii eius est eminentia comprehensiva, non carentia determinationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","CH_GGVC_P_47:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SD1","text":"Perfectio cognitionis angelicae definitur per compressionem mediorum cognoscitivorum: idem ambitus intelligibilium per pauciora et universaliora principia continetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","CH_GGVC_P_47:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SD2","text":"Creatura intellectualis finita non potest facere ex sua essentia principium exhaustivum cognitionis rerum, quia finita determinatio entis non aequat universalitatem obiecti intellectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A2","CH_GGVC_P_47:A3","CH_GGVC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SD3","text":"Ordo cognitionis angelicae est causaliter divinus et ontologice praevia experientiae rerum, quia rationes creaturarum in intelligentia angelica ab origine naturae eius insunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SD4","text":"Locus et distantia ad cognitionem angelicam non pertinent essentialiter, sed ad ordinem effectuum quos Angelus in rebus localibus operatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D6","CH_GGVC_P_47:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem doctrinam quae cognitionem intellectualem perfectam ex sola praesentia substantiae cognoscentis deducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem doctrinam quae experientiam sensibilem vel abstractionem ponit fontem necessarium omnis cognitionis intellectualis creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet universalitatem cognitionis esse identicam cognitioni vagae, genericae vel minus propriae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet perfectionem cognitivam crescere necessario per multiplicationem formarum cognoscitivarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet cognitionem rei pendere a propinquitate locali inter cognoscens et cognitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX1","text":"Nulla essentia creata potest in una forma simplicissima possidere plenitudinem omnium rationum rerum eo modo quo essentia divina infinita eas continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX2","text":"Cognitio angelica nec a rebus autonomice producitur nec ex essentia angelica absolute fundatur, sed a Deo ut causa rationum rerum dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX3","text":"Identitas plena inter esse, intelligere et causare creaturas soli Deo reservatur; in Angelo essentia, species et obiecta cognita structuraliter distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:FGS1","text":"Obiectum intellectus universale + essentia angelica finita → insufficientia essentiae ut medii totalis → necessitas specierum intelligibilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:FGS2","text":"Immateralitas angelica + separatio a corpore + completio naturalis potentiae intellectivae → species connaturales a Deo datae → exclusio acquisitionis sensibilis et abstractionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:FGS3","text":"Propinquitas ad Deum + imminutio simplicitatis in intellectibus creatis → superior cognoscit per pauciora → species superioris universaliores et tamen propriae cognitionis capaces.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AF1","text":"Ambitus universalis intellectus → finitas essentiae angelicae → distinctio essentiae et specierum → cognitio per similitudines rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AF2","text":"Distinctio animae corpori unitae et Angeli separati → diversitas acquisitionis intelligibilis → species ab experientia receptae in anima, connaturales in Angelo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AF3","text":"Unitas divinae cognitionis → imminutio simplicitatis in creaturis → hierarchia mediorum universalium → cognitio superior per pauciora et eminentiora.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME1","text":"Essentia cognoscentis et medium cognitionis separantur, ita ut immaterialitas substantiae non sufficiat ad identitatem eius cum omnibus formis cognitis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter cognitionem causantem et cognitionem a rebus causatam dissolvitur per tertium ordinem: species creaturarum a Deo in intellectu angelico causatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME3","text":"Universalitas reclassificatur non ut imminutio cognitionis singularis, sed ut virtus medii eminentis ad plures rationes proprias extendendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME4","text":"Hierarchia angelica reclassificatur ut gradus simplicitatis cognoscitivae potius quam mera superioritas dignitatis vel multitudinis notitiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME5","text":"Motus localis ab officio epistemico separatur et ad efficaciam operativam refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus definit utrum Angelus cognoscat per essentiam, per species receptas, vel per species connaturales, atque utrum species superiorum universaliores sint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT2","text":"Structural — Cognitio constituitur ex proportione inter ambitum potentiae intellectivae, capacitatem formae cognoscitivae, modum essendi substantiae et originem specierum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Difficultas de perfectione cognitionis resolvitur distinguendo universalitatem obiecti cogniti ab universalitate medii quo res cognoscitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Ordo essendi fundat ordinem cognoscendi: rationes rerum sunt primario in Deo, consequenter in natura intellectuali angelica, et deinde res in propriis generibus producuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de forma intellectiva, finitate essentiae angelicae, origine divina specierum et simplicitate hierarchica sufficiunt ad restituendam conclusionem tripartitam quaestionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT2","text":"Systema cohaeret quia eadem regula proportionis inter potentiam et formam explicat et necessitatem specierum et gradum earum universalitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT3","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter assertionem quod essentia angelica alia communiter continet et negationem quod eas proprie cognoscere possit, quia criterium transitūs a cognitione communi ad cognitionem propriam non ulterius formalizatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter species connaturales et species a Deo acceptas, quia textus originem divinam affirmat simulque acquisitionem temporalem vel experimentalem negat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5","text":"Tensionem continet doctrina universalitatis eminentis, quia propriae cognitionis pluralitas ex una forma universali dependet ab excellentia cuius mensura intrinseca non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia ex limite essentiae creatae ad dependentiam a Deo et ex dependentia ad hierarchiam simplicitatis cognoscitivae procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161831602358Z_7470caa7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 55","source_sha256":"5c1767c2e6de8a3950800dea91bd073570a82a794c2b14f4a780a3082b915061","sha256":"7abee43f1a756439ace29243d8a522cdd4ee2a45430edaf1b455f2ac3b346633","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:18:31.603936+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS1","text":"The question determines whether angelic cognition is grounded in the essence of the knower, in species received from things, or in connatural species differing by hierarchical grade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2","text":"An angel cannot know all things through its essence, because its intellective power extends to being in common, whereas its finite essence is contracted to a determinate ratio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS3","text":"Angelic species are not received from sensible things, but are connaturally given with the intellectual nature through divine influx.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS4","text":"Angelic superiority is measured by a smaller multitude of species and a greater universality of means, through which more proper things are known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from the insufficiency of finite essence to the necessity of species, from angelic immateriality to their connatural origin, and from proximity to God to the gradation of cognitive universality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A1","text":"That by which the intellect understands is the form of the intellect actually understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A2","text":"An intellective form perfectly perfects a power only if it contains all that to which that power extends.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A3","text":"The object of the intellect is being or truth in common.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A4","text":"Angelic essence is finite and determined to genus and species, and therefore does not comprehend all the proper rationes of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A5","text":"The divine essence alone, because it is infinite, comprehends all things perfectly and according to their proper rationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A6","text":"The mode of being of a substance determines the mode by which it acquires intelligible perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A7","text":"An intellectual substance united to a body receives intelligible perfection successively from things, because its being is akin to a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","text":"An angel, wholly separate from a body and subsisting immaterially, has connatural intelligible species for all that it can naturally know.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","text":"Angelic species proceed from God together with the intellectual nature, because the likenesses of things are primarily in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","text":"The closer a created intellect is to God, the more intelligibles it can know through fewer means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:A11","text":"An excellent universal medium can be the proper ratio of many things if it contains in itself that whereby diverse things are likened according to their proper rationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX1","text":"Angelic cognition is not the comprehension of all things through angelic essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX2","text":"The expression by which an angel is said to know things according to its nature does not designate its essence as the medium of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX3","text":"The identity of the intellect in act and the intelligible in act does not signify the identity of the understanding substance with the likeness by which it understands.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX4","text":"The presence of things in angelic essence is neither perfect presence nor presence according to their proper rationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX5","text":"Angelic cognition does not arise from the abstraction of species from sensible things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX6","text":"The universality of angelic species does not require an origin through abstraction from singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX7","text":"To know through a universal medium is not necessarily to know a thing only according to a universal and imperfect nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:NX8","text":"An angel's local motion is not ordered toward the acquisition of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D1","text":"The angelic intellect requires intelligible species distinct from its essence, because its object exceeds the containment of finite essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A1","CH_GGVC_P_47:A2","CH_GGVC_P_47:A3","CH_GGVC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D2","text":"Through its essence, an angel can have common cognition of other beings, but not their proper and perfect cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A4","CH_GGVC_P_47:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D3","text":"Angelic species are likenesses of creatures caused by God, not images impressed by the creatures themselves.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D4","text":"Directly abstracting material forms into intelligible being is impossible for an angel according to the established order, because the transition would require the intermediary of imagination, which it lacks.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A6","CH_GGVC_P_47:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D5","text":"Even if an angel could abstract, it would not need abstraction, because it already has connatural species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D6","text":"Angelic cognition is equally related, with respect to place, to what is near and what is distant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D7","text":"An angel moves locally in order to exercise an operation in a place, not so that a knowable object may become present to it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:D8","text":"A higher angel can know particular proper things through more universal forms, because the universality of its medium is comprehensive eminence, not a lack of determination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","CH_GGVC_P_47:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SD1","text":"The perfection of angelic cognition is defined by the compression of cognitive means: the same range of intelligibles is contained through fewer and more universal principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","CH_GGVC_P_47:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SD2","text":"A finite intellectual creature cannot make its essence into an exhaustive principle of cognition of things, because a finite determination of being does not equal the universality of the intellect's object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A2","CH_GGVC_P_47:A3","CH_GGVC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SD3","text":"The order of angelic cognition is causally divine and ontologically prior to the experience of things, because the rationes of creatures are present in angelic intelligence from the origin of its nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A8","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SD4","text":"Place and distance do not pertain essentially to angelic cognition, but to the order of effects that an angel works in local things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D6","CH_GGVC_P_47:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX1","text":"Every doctrine that derives perfect intellectual cognition from the mere presence of the knowing substance must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX2","text":"Every doctrine that posits sensible experience or abstraction as the necessary source of all created intellectual cognition must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX3","text":"It must be false that universality of cognition is identical with vague, generic, or less proper cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX4","text":"It must be false that cognitive perfection necessarily increases through the multiplication of cognitive forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX5","text":"It must be false that cognition of a thing depends on local proximity between knower and known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX1","text":"No created essence can possess in one most simple form the fullness of all the rationes of things in the manner in which the infinite divine essence contains them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX2","text":"Angelic cognition is neither autonomously produced by things nor absolutely grounded in angelic essence, but depends on God as the cause of the rationes of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX3","text":"Full identity among being, understanding, and causing creatures is reserved to God alone; in an angel, essence, species, and known objects are structurally distinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:FGS1","text":"Universal object of intellect + finite angelic essence → insufficiency of essence as a total medium → necessity of intelligible species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:FGS2","text":"Angelic immateriality + separation from body + natural completion of intellective power → connatural species given by God → exclusion of sensible acquisition and abstraction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:FGS3","text":"Proximity to God + diminution of simplicity in created intellects → the higher knows through fewer means → the species of the higher are more universal and yet capable of proper cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AF1","text":"Universal scope of the intellect → finitude of angelic essence → distinction of essence and species → cognition through likenesses of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AF2","text":"Distinction between the soul united to a body and the separate angel → diversity of intelligible acquisition → species received from experience in the soul, connatural in the angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:AF3","text":"Unity of divine cognition → diminution of simplicity in creatures → hierarchy of universal means → higher cognition through fewer and more eminent means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME1","text":"The essence of the knower and the medium of cognition are separated, such that the immateriality of a substance does not suffice for its identity with all known forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME2","text":"The opposition between cognition causing and cognition caused by things is dissolved through a third order: species of creatures caused by God in the angelic intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME3","text":"Universality is reclassified not as a diminution of singular cognition, but as the power of an eminent medium to extend to several proper rationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME4","text":"Angelic hierarchy is reclassified as a degree of cognitive simplicity rather than mere superiority of dignity or multitude of cognitions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ME5","text":"Local motion is separated from an epistemic office and referred to operative efficacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines whether an angel knows through essence, through received species, or through connatural species, and whether the species of higher angels are more universal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT2","text":"Structural — Cognition is constituted by the proportion between the scope of intellective power, the capacity of cognitive form, the mode of being of substance, and the origin of species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The difficulty concerning the perfection of cognition is resolved by distinguishing the universality of the known object from the universality of the medium by which the thing is known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The order of being grounds the order of knowing: the rationes of things are primarily in God, consequently in the angelic intellectual nature, and then things are produced in their proper genera.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning intellective form, the finitude of angelic essence, the divine origin of species, and hierarchical simplicity suffice to restore the threefold conclusion of the question.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT2","text":"The system coheres because the same rule of proportion between power and form explains both the necessity of species and the degree of their universality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT3","text":"A fragile joint remains between the assertion that angelic essence contains other things commonly and the negation that it can know them properly, because the criterion of transition from common cognition to proper cognition is not further formalized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains between connatural species and species received from God, because the text affirms a divine origin while at the same time denying temporal or experiential acquisition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5","text":"The doctrine of eminent universality contains a tension, because the plurality of proper cognition from one universal form depends upon an excellence whose intrinsic measure is not explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0058","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the limit of created essence to dependence on God, and from dependence to the hierarchy of cognitive simplicity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_47:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_47@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_47:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 56","title":"First Part · Question 55","context":"Chapter 56","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 55"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 55","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 56","order":57,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_48"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_48@R001","sha256":"9bbf4dbc9473e4c47b1ac0937daba3cb02e0051bcb3689b744999d9216366a06","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS1","text":"Quaestio cognitionis angelicae ad res immateriales reducitur ad tres relationes: angelus ad seipsum, ad alium angelum, ad Deum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS2","text":"Argumentatio cognitionem non ex mera distantia obiecti, sed ex modo unionis obiecti intelligibilis cum potentia cognoscitiva constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS3","text":"Angelus seipsum cognoscit, quia substantia eius immaterialis est forma subsistens et intelligibilis actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS4","text":"Angelus alium angelum cognoscit per similitudines intelligibiles a Deo impressas, quae rem cognitam intentionaliter, non naturaliter, praesentem faciunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS5","text":"Cognitio naturalis Dei ab angelo possibilis est per similitudinem divinam naturae angelicae impressam, sed non per visionem essentiae divinae neque per comprehensionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS6","text":"Motus argumentationis est distinctivus et reconstructivus: potentia/passio → forma intelligibilis actu → triplex modus praesentiae cogniti → gradatio cognitionis sui, alterius et Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A1","text":"Actio quae manet in agente requirit obiectum agenti unitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A2","text":"Obiectum cognitum unitum potentiae cognoscitivae est principium formale ipsius cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A3","text":"Motus, receptio et passio ad cognitionem pertinent solum secundum quod potentia cognoscitiva est in potentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A4","text":"Forma intelligibilis actu, si subsistit per se, potest esse principium quo seipsam intelligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A5","text":"Immaterialitas, non singularitas ut talis, removet impedimentum intelligibilitatis quod materia corporalis inducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A6","text":"Angelus est forma subsistens, immaterialis et intelligibilis actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","text":"Deus mentibus angelicis impressit similitudines rerum corporalium et spiritualium quas in esse naturali produxit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A8","text":"Uniuscuiusque angeli propria species simul habet esse naturale et intelligibile; species aliarum rerum in eo habent esse intelligibile tantum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A9","text":"Species rei in intellectu cognoscentis ab ipsa re distinguitur secundum esse naturale et intentionale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A10","text":"Nulla similitudo creata sufficit ad repraesentandam essentiam divinam sicut est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A11","text":"Natura angelica est imago Dei et speculum creatum similitudinem divinam repraesentans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A12","text":"Infinitas distantiae inter creaturam et Deum excludit comprehensionem et visionem naturalem essentiae, non omnem cognitionem Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX1","text":"Cognitio angelica non definitur per mutationem ab obiecto receptam, cum intellectus actu formatus absque receptione praevia cognoscere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX2","text":"Singularitas immaterialis non est inintelligibilis; sola singularitas materialiter individuata impedimentum cognitionis intellectualis praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX3","text":"Cognitio sui non est cognitio perfecta virtutis angelicae secundum ordinem sapientiae divinae incomprehensibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX4","text":"Cognitio alterius angeli non requirit causalitatem inter angelos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX5","text":"Species intelligibilis alterius angeli non est ipse angelus cognitus, quamvis utrumque sit immateriale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX6","text":"Cognitio naturalis Dei non est visio divinae essentiae facie ad faciem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX7","text":"Cognitio Dei ab intellectu creato non est comprehensio, quia Deus supra omnem cognitionem comprehensivam manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D1","text":"Angelus seipsum intelligit per propriam substantiam, quia forma eius subsistens est sibi praesens ut intelligibile actu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A1","CH_GGVC_P_48:A2","CH_GGVC_P_48:A4","CH_GGVC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D2","text":"Intellectus angelicus, quantum ad cognitionem sui, non indiget motu ab obiecto, quia forma intelligibilis non solum potentia sed actu in eo est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A3","CH_GGVC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D3","text":"Angelus alium angelum proprie cognoscit per speciem intentionalem eius, non tantum sub genere communi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8","CH_GGVC_P_48:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D4","text":"Diversitas graduum perfectionis inter naturas angelicas cognitionem mutuam non impedit, quia affinitas naturae spiritualis cum distinctione ordinis manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D5","text":"Si Deus plures creaturas universi institueret, species intelligibiles mentibus angelicis proportionatas etiam ampliare deberet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D6","text":"Cognitio naturalis Dei ab angelo est media inter cognitionem per essentiam praesentem et cognitionem ex creaturis acceptam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11","CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D7","text":"Cognitio naturalis Dei magis ad cognitionem specularem accedit quam ad visionem essentiae, quia natura angelica similitudinem divinam creaturaliter repraesentat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1","text":"Ordo cognitionis angelicae est ordo graduum praesentiae: identitas formalis sui, similitudo intentionalis aliorum, similitudo creaturalis Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A6","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8","CH_GGVC_P_48:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SD2","text":"Immaterialitas non simpliciter aequat cognitionem perfectam, sed constituit conditionem intelligibilitatis cuius perfectio ulterior ex proportione similitudinis pendet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A5","CH_GGVC_P_48:A6","CH_GGVC_P_48:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SD3","text":"Universum creatum et apparatus specierum angelicarum sub una dispositione divina coordinantur, ita ut extensio unius extensionem alterius requirat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SD4","text":"Finitas creaturae non inducit ignorantiam absolutam Dei, sed cognitionem analogicam sine adaequatione obiecti divini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11","CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet omnem cognitionem intellectualem necessario ab exteriori agente moveri; aliter intellectus angelicus sui cognitionem exercere non posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet singularitatem per se opponere universalitati intelligibili; aliter substantia angelica, quia singulariter subsistit, intelligibilis actu non esset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet cognitionem alterius spiritualis aut per identitatem essentiae aut per causalitatem reduci; species intentionalis tertium medium constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet dilemmata cognitionis divinae inter visionem essentiae et ignorantiam totalem exhaustiva esse; cognitio naturalis similitudinis medium statum tenet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX1","text":"Nulla creatura potest divinae essentiae fieri cognitivamente coextensiva per naturam suam, quia repraesentatio creata semper infra infinitam rem repraesentatam manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX2","text":"Non admittitur cognitio quae omne obiectum eodem modo attingat: ipsum, alium et Deum diversis modis praesentiae et similitudinis cognosci necesse est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX3","text":"Non admittitur autonomia completa intellectus creati, quia species rerum et ipsa proportio universi ad cognitionem angelicam a dispositione divina dependent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS1","text":"Actio immanens → obiectum potentiae unitum → species ut principium formale → distinctio potentiae et actus cognoscentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS2","text":"Forma subsistens immaterialis → intelligibilitas actualis → praesentia substantiae sibi → cognitio angelica sui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS3","text":"Similitudines divinitus impressae → esse intelligibile aliarum naturarum → praesentia intentionalis → cognitio angelica aliorum angelorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS4","text":"Imago divina creata → similitudo finita Dei → cognitio naturalis analogica → exclusio visionis essentiae et comprehensionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS5","text":"Ordo universi divinitus dispositus → numerus rerum cognoscendarum → proportio specierum impressarum → sufficiens capacitas cognitionis angelicae ad universum institutum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AF1","text":"Difficultas de immaterialibus cognoscendis → distinctio actionis transeuntis et immanentis → cognitio ut praesentia formalis → sui cognitio per formam subsistentem → alterius cognitio per speciem intentionalem → Dei cognitio per similitudinem creatam → clausura per negationem visionis comprehensivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter singulare et intelligibile resolvitur: materia individuans, non subsistentia singularis, est principium inintelligibilitatis corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter rem absentem et rem cognitam resolvitur per esse intentionale speciei, quod obiectum cognitum in intellectu praesentat sine identitate naturali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME3","text":"Cognitio non ordinatur binarie inter immediatam essentiae visionem et cognitionem sensibilem, sed tripliciter secundum praesentiam essentiae, similitudinis directae et similitudinis in alio relucentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME4","text":"Infinitas divina reclassificatur non ut terminus omnis cognitionis, sed ut terminus adaequationis, comprehensionis et visionis naturalis essentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME5","text":"Providentia divina reclassificatur ut principium commune constitutionis rerum et conditionum cognoscibilitatis earum in intellectibus angelicis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT1","text":"Surface — Angelus cognoscit seipsum, alios angelos et Deum per sua naturalia, sed non eodem cognitionis gradu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT2","text":"Structural — Cognitio nascitur ex proportione inter potentiam, speciem, modum essendi obiecti et modum praesentiae eius in cognoscente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur per translationem quaestionis ab impedimentis physicis et causalibus ad differentias inter actum, similitudinem, esse naturale et esse intentionale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Cognoscibilitas creaturarum et species angelicae ex ordine divino universi dependent; cognitio naturalis finita intra ordinem creatum constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de actione immanente, forma intelligibili et immaterialitate sufficiunt ad conclusionem de cognitione angelica sui restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de speciebus divinitus impressis et de esse intentionale sufficiunt ad cognitionem mutuam angelorum sine identitate essentiarum aut causalitate reciproca explicandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT3","text":"Axiomata de similitudine creata et insufficientia eius ad essentiam divinam repraesentandam sufficiunt ad cognitionem naturalem Dei affirmandam simulque visionem comprehensivam negandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT4","text":"Structura maxime cohaeret ubi eadem distinctio inter esse naturale et esse intelligibile transit a cognitione alterius angeli ad cognitionem Dei per similitudinem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter species omnium rerum angelis impressas et possibilitatem creaturae novae, quae per dispositionem divinam hypotheticam, non per mutationem cognitivam angelorum, solvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT6","text":"Tensio moderata manet in cognitione Dei naturali, quae specie immediate accepta assimilatur sed simul cognitioni speculari propior declaratur; textus eam per gradum similitudinis, non per univocam categoriam, stabilit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T161855227633Z_88409f01","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 56","source_sha256":"9bbf4dbc9473e4c47b1ac0937daba3cb02e0051bcb3689b744999d9216366a06","sha256":"c6fcf5f587c2bccf2756cdf21f940f520f736c55766fa808414a67ad3626bc57","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:18:55.228622+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS1","text":"The question of angelic knowledge concerning immaterial things is reduced to three relations: the angel to itself, to another angel, and to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS2","text":"The argument establishes knowledge not from the mere distance of the object, but from the mode of union of the intelligible object with the cognitive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS3","text":"An angel knows itself because its substance is an immaterial, subsisting form and intelligible in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS4","text":"An angel knows another angel through intelligible likenesses impressed by God, which make the known thing present intentionally, not naturally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS5","text":"Natural knowledge of God by an angel is possible through a divine likeness impressed upon angelic nature, but not through vision of the divine essence or through comprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AS6","text":"The movement of the argument is distinctive and reconstructive: power/passion → intelligible form in act → threefold mode of the presence of the known → gradation of knowledge of self, another, and God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A1","text":"An action remaining in the agent requires an object united to the agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A2","text":"The known object united to the cognitive power is the formal principle of cognition itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A3","text":"Motion, reception, and passion pertain to knowledge only insofar as the cognitive power is in potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A4","text":"An intelligible form in act, if it subsists through itself, can be the principle by which it understands itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A5","text":"Immateriality, not singularity as such, removes the impediment to intelligibility introduced by corporeal matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A6","text":"An angel is a subsisting, immaterial form and intelligible in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","text":"God impressed upon angelic minds likenesses of corporeal and spiritual things which He produced in natural being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A8","text":"The proper species of each angel simultaneously has natural and intelligible being; the species of other things in it have intelligible being only.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A9","text":"The species of a thing in the intellect of the knower is distinguished from the thing itself according to natural and intentional being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A10","text":"No created likeness suffices to represent the divine essence as it is.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A11","text":"Angelic nature is an image of God and a created mirror representing the divine likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:A12","text":"The infinity of the distance between creature and God excludes comprehension and natural vision of the essence, not all knowledge of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX1","text":"Angelic knowledge is not defined by a change received from the object, since an intellect formed in act can know without prior reception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX2","text":"Immaterial singularity is not unintelligible; only materially individuated singularity presents an impediment to intellectual knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX3","text":"Knowledge of self is not perfect knowledge of angelic power according to the order of incomprehensible divine wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX4","text":"Knowledge of another angel does not require causality between angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX5","text":"The intelligible species of another angel is not the known angel itself, although both are immaterial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX6","text":"Natural knowledge of God is not vision of the divine essence face to face.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:NX7","text":"Knowledge of God by a created intellect is not comprehension, because God remains above every comprehensive knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D1","text":"An angel understands itself through its own substance, because its subsisting form is present to itself as intelligible in act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A1","CH_GGVC_P_48:A2","CH_GGVC_P_48:A4","CH_GGVC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D2","text":"The angelic intellect, as regards knowledge of itself, does not require motion from the object, because the intelligible form is not only potentially but actually in it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A3","CH_GGVC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D3","text":"An angel properly knows another angel through its intentional species, not merely under a common genus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8","CH_GGVC_P_48:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D4","text":"The diversity of degrees of perfection among angelic natures does not impede mutual knowledge, because affinity of spiritual nature remains together with distinction of order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D5","text":"If God were to institute more creatures of the universe, He would also have to enlarge the intelligible species proportioned to angelic minds.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D6","text":"Natural knowledge of God by an angel is intermediate between knowledge through the essence present and knowledge received from creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11","CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:D7","text":"Natural knowledge of God approaches mirror-like knowledge more closely than vision of the essence, because angelic nature represents the divine likeness creaturely.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1","text":"The order of angelic knowledge is an order of degrees of presence: formal identity of self, intentional likeness of others, and creaturely likeness of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A6","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8","CH_GGVC_P_48:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SD2","text":"Immateriality does not simply amount to perfect knowledge, but constitutes a condition of intelligibility whose further perfection depends on the proportion of likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A5","CH_GGVC_P_48:A6","CH_GGVC_P_48:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SD3","text":"The created universe and the apparatus of angelic species are coordinated under one divine disposition, such that the extension of one requires the extension of the other.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A7","CH_GGVC_P_48:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SD4","text":"The finitude of the creature does not entail absolute ignorance of God, but analogical knowledge without adequation to the divine object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11","CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX1","text":"It must be false that every intellectual knowledge is necessarily moved by an external agent; otherwise the angelic intellect could not exercise knowledge of itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX2","text":"It must be false that singularity through itself opposes intelligible universality; otherwise angelic substance, because it subsists singularly, would not be intelligible in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX3","text":"It must be false that knowledge of another spiritual being is reduced either to identity of essence or to causality; the intentional species constitutes a third medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the alternatives of divine knowledge between vision of the essence and total ignorance are exhaustive; natural knowledge through likeness holds a middle state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX1","text":"No creature can become cognitively coextensive with the divine essence through its own nature, because created representation always remains beneath the infinite thing represented.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX2","text":"Knowledge that attains every object in the same mode is not admitted: self, another, and God must be known through diverse modes of presence and likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX3","text":"Complete autonomy of the created intellect is not admitted, because the species of things and the very proportion of the universe for angelic knowledge depend on divine disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS1","text":"Immanent action → object united to the power → species as formal principle → distinction of the power and act of the knower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS2","text":"Immaterial subsisting form → actual intelligibility → presence of substance to itself → angelic knowledge of self.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS3","text":"Divinely impressed likenesses → intelligible being of other natures → intentional presence → angelic knowledge of other angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS4","text":"Created divine image → finite likeness of God → analogical natural knowledge → exclusion of vision of the essence and comprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:FGS5","text":"Divinely disposed order of the universe → number of things to be known → proportion of impressed species → sufficient capacity of angelic knowledge for the instituted universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:AF1","text":"Difficulty concerning the knowledge of immaterial things → distinction between transitive and immanent action → knowledge as formal presence → knowledge of self through subsisting form → knowledge of another through intentional species → knowledge of God through created likeness → closure through the negation of comprehensive vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME1","text":"The opposition between the singular and the intelligible is resolved: individuating matter, not singular subsistence, is the principle of corporeal unintelligibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME2","text":"The opposition between the absent thing and the known thing is resolved through the intentional being of the species, which presents the known object in the intellect without natural identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME3","text":"Knowledge is not ordered binarily between immediate vision of the essence and sensible knowledge, but triply according to the presence of the essence, of direct likeness, and of likeness shining forth in another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME4","text":"Divine infinity is reclassified not as the terminus of all knowledge, but as the terminus of adequation, comprehension, and natural vision of the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ME5","text":"Divine providence is reclassified as the common principle of the constitution of things and of the conditions of their knowability in angelic intellects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT1","text":"Surface — An angel knows itself, other angels, and God through its natural powers, but not in the same degree of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT2","text":"Structural — Knowledge arises from the proportion between power, species, the mode of being of the object, and the mode of its presence in the knower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved by transferring the question from physical and causal impediments to the differences among act, likeness, natural being, and intentional being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The knowability of creatures and angelic species depend on the divine order of the universe; finite natural knowledge is constituted within the created order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning immanent action, intelligible form, and immateriality suffice to reconstruct the conclusion concerning angelic knowledge of self.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning divinely impressed species and intentional being suffice to explain the mutual knowledge of angels without identity of essences or reciprocal causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT3","text":"The axioms concerning created likeness and its insufficiency for representing the divine essence suffice to affirm natural knowledge of God while denying comprehensive vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT4","text":"The structure coheres most strongly where the same distinction between natural being and intelligible being passes from knowledge of another angel to knowledge of God through likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains between the species of all things impressed upon angels and the possibility of a new creature, which is resolved through a hypothetical divine disposition, not through a cognitive change in angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT6","text":"A moderate tension remains in natural knowledge of God, which is assimilated to a species immediately received yet at the same time declared closer to mirror-like knowledge; the text stabilizes it by degree of likeness, not by a univocal category.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_48:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_48@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_48:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 57","title":"First Part · Question 56","context":"Chapter 57","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 56"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 56","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 57","order":58,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_49"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_49@R001","sha256":"036d22ae40dc204892df6839d0b319436374b7a88979d0d6e4930f790ac20206","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quid intellectus angelicus de rebus materialibus, singularibus, futuris, interioribus voluntatis et mysteriis gratiae cognoscere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS2","text":"Difficultas non resolvitur ex oppositione simplici inter spiritum et materiam, sed ex modo quo res cognita in cognoscente esse potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","text":"Angelus materialia et singularia cognoscit per species intelligibiles sibi a Deo inditas, quae inferiora eminenter repraesentant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS4","text":"Cognitio angelica limitatur ubi obiectum nondum est in se, ubi pendet a libera voluntate creata, vel ubi ex sola Dei voluntate procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS5","text":"Argumentatio metaphysico-epistemica procedit ab extensione cognitionis superioris ad determinationem praerogativarum divinarum, quae omnem intellectum creatum circumscribunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","text":"In ordine entium, quod in inferioribus est partialiter et multipliciter, in superioribus continetur eminenter, simplicius et perfectius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A2","text":"Quod est in cognoscente, est in eo secundum modum cognoscentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","text":"Angelus res materiales naturaliter non accipit a rebus sensibilibus, sed cognoscit per species intelligibiles sibi connaturales et actu intelligibiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A4","text":"Essentia rei materialis potest esse in intellectu intentionaliter sine esse reali quod habet in re.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","text":"Species angelicae a divina essentia derivatae repraesentant res secundum principia formalia et secundum principia individuationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","text":"Virtus cognoscitiva superior est magis una et ad plura extensa quam virtus inferior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A7","text":"Futurum in causis necessariis cognoscitur certo, in causis ut in pluribus coniecturaliter, et in causis ut in paucioribus non cognoscitur per cognitionem causalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","text":"Intellectus creatus deficit ab aeternitate divina et successionem conceptionum intelligibilium habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","text":"Cogitatio actualis et affectio voluntatis, quatenus a sola voluntate rationali dependent, soli Deo directe patent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A10","text":"Mysteria gratiae ex pura Dei voluntate dependent et ideo naturalem cognitionem angelicam excedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","text":"Cognitio beatifica angelorum consistit in visione Verbi et rerum in Verbo, sed divinam sapientiam non comprehendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","text":"Revelatio mysteriorum distribuitur secundum voluntatem Dei, gradum hierarchicum angelorum et congruentiam officiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX1","text":"Res materialis non est in intellectu angelico secundum suum esse reale, sed secundum speciem intelligibilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX2","text":"Cognitio angelica materialium non est sensibilis, imaginaria nec abstrahens a rebus materialibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX3","text":"Cognoscere singulare in causis universalibus non est cognoscere ipsum singulare ut hic et nunc.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX4","text":"Distantia temporalis futuri non assimilatur distantiae localis rei iam existentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX5","text":"Esse supra tempus motuum corporalium non est esse in aeternitate quae totum tempus simul comprehendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX6","text":"Cognoscere effectus corporales cogitationis non est cognoscere ipsam cogitationem ut actum intellectus vel affectionem ut actum voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX7","text":"Videre divinam sapientiam non est comprehendere omnia quae in ipsa latent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0099","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D1","text":"Materialia possunt perficere intellectum angelicum non secundum inferioritatem sui esse materialis, sed secundum actum specierum intelligibilium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A2","CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D2","text":"Angelus cognoscit singularia ut singularia, quia species eius universales includunt similitudinem principiorum individuantium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","CH_GGVC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D3","text":"Angelus cognoscit praesentia et praeterita secundum naturas iam existentes et futura secundum ordinem causarum, non autem futura contingentia ut in seipsis futura sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A7","CH_GGVC_P_49:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D4","text":"Angelus de futuris necessariis certitudinem et de futuris frequentibus coniecturam habet perfectiorem quam homo, quia causas universalius et subtilius cognoscit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D5","text":"Angelus ex actibus exterioribus et immutationibus corporalibus interiores dispositiones conicere potest, sed usum actualem specierum intelligibilium ab ipsa voluntate dependentem non penetrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D6","text":"Mysteria gratiae angelis non naturaliter patent, sed in visione beatifica revelantur mensurate, inaequaliter et hierarchice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A10","CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D7","text":"Mysterium incarnationis omnibus angelis in communi revelatur ut principium ministeriorum, sed conditiones eius particulares successive et non omnibus aequaliter manifestantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD1","text":"Carentia sensus et imaginationis non constituit defectum angelicum, quia superior modus cognoscendi continet quod inferiores vires diversimode attingunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD2","text":"Singularitas non excluditur ab intelligibilitate simpliciter, sed tantum ab eo intellectu cuius universalitas oritur per abstractionem a condicionibus materialibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","CH_GGVC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD3","text":"Fines cognitionis angelicae distribuuntur secundum quattuor modos obiecti: res iam existentes, effectus causaliter signati, actus liberi interiores, et secreta ex sola Dei voluntate pendentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A7","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_49:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD4","text":"Providentia et administratio angelica requirunt cognitionem singularium, sed non convertunt administratores creatos in possessores cognitionis divinae totalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5","text":"Visio beatifica instituit cognitionem dynamicam potius quam possessionem staticam omnium divinorum, quia revelatio ulterior officiis et ordini hierarchico subiacet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod excellentia cognitionis creatae ad omniscientiam per se sufficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod universalitas speciei, sine repraesentatione principiorum individuantium, singularitatem ut talem exhibere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omne intelligibile sit omni intellectui creato statim praesens, quia futurum, actus voluntarius et mysterium gratiae diversos modos indisponibilitatis servant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX1","text":"Nullus intellectus creatus habet situm cognoscitivum ex quo tota temporalitas, inclusis futuris contingentibus, simul praesens fiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX2","text":"Voluntas divina non reducitur ad ordinem naturalium specierum nec visio creata divinam essentiam ita exhaurit ut omne secretum eius necessario pateat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0099","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS1","text":"Ordo hierarchicus entium → continentia eminentior superioris → praesentia intentionalis inferioris in specie intelligibili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS2","text":"Species angelica divinitus derivata → repraesentatio formae et materiae → cognitio naturae materialis et singularitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS3","text":"Discrimen causae et rei in se → certitudo necessarii, coniectura frequenti, ignorantia fortuiti → exclusio futuri ut futuri ab intellectu creato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS4","text":"Discrimen effectus exterioris et actus voluntarii interioris → cognitio signorum corporum → clausura secreti cordis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS5","text":"Discrimen naturae et liberae voluntatis Dei → impotentia cognitionis naturalis → revelatio beatifica graduata et ministerialiter ordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF1","text":"Materialitas inferior → species intelligibilis angelica → cognitio materialium sine sensu nec abstractione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF2","text":"Singularitas materialis → similitudo causaliter plena in specie → cognitio singularis ut hic et nunc.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF3","text":"Futurum in causis → cognitio causalis graduata → reservatio futuri in se aeternitati divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF4","text":"Cogitatio in effectu → coniectura ex signis → exceptio actus intellectus et voluntatis soli Deo subiecti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF5","text":"Mysterium ex sola voluntate Dei → defectus cognitionis naturalis → visio Verbi et revelatio hierarchica mensurata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME1","text":"Oppositio materiae et intellectus dissolvitur, quia impedimentum non est materialitas obiecti sed incongruentia modi quo obiectum cognoscibiliter adest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME2","text":"Oppositio universalis et singularis reformatur, quia universale angelicum non est universale abstractum quod individuationem excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME3","text":"Discrimen praesentis et futuri non est mera distantia temporalis, sed discrimen inter naturam iam existentem et rem nondum in proprio esse constitutam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME4","text":"Interioritas mentis non per invisibilitatem corporalem definitur, sed per dependentiam actus actualis a voluntate libera.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME5","text":"Mysteria gratiae reclassificantur non ut obiecta naturaliter altiora, sed ut secreta voluntatis divinae quae sola revelatione communicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus distribuit obiecta cognitionis angelicae in materialia, singularia, futura, cogitationes cordium et mysteria gratiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT2","text":"Structural — Cognitio determinatur per ordinem entium, modum recipientis, species innatas, causalitatem et dependentiam a voluntate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio concedit superioritatem angelicam ubi analogia hierarchica valet, sed eam sistit ubi obiectum reservatur aeternitati, libertati vel revelationi divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Realitas cognoscibilis dividitur inter esse actuale rerum, ordinem causalem, successionem intellectus creati et aeternitatem divinam simul totum tempus continens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de ordine hierarchico, modo cognoscentis et speciebus innatis sufficiunt ad restitutionem cognitionis angelicae materialium et singularium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de causalitate, successione et aeternitate sufficiunt ad explicandum cur cognitio futurorum sit graduata nec divinae praescientiae aequetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT3","text":"Axiomata de dominio voluntatis et de voluntate divina sufficiunt ad distinguenda secreta cordis et mysteria gratiae ab obiectis naturaliter cognoscibilibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in transitu a specie universali ad cognitionem singularis, quia repraesentatio principiorum individuantium asseritur, dum mechanismus eius intra hanc quaestionem ad expositionem priorem remittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT5","text":"Tensionem regit distinctio inter superioritatem angelicam et praerogativas divinas: principium quod superior cognoscit quod inferior cognoscit non valet sine limite ubi obiectum ex sola libertate vel aeternitate divina cognoscibile est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, quia ab amplificatione cognitionis angelicae per ordinem hierarchicum ad restrictionem eius per contingentiam, voluntatem et revelationem divinam progreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T162503661168Z_66ab9f5c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 57","source_sha256":"036d22ae40dc204892df6839d0b319436374b7a88979d0d6e4930f790ac20206","sha256":"af2733218567bd07dafe599b0a32e92347d7679f494919123d6517aa94165dbb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:25:03.662221+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS1","text":"The question determines what the angelic intellect can know concerning material things, singulars, future things, the interior acts of the will, and the mysteries of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS2","text":"The difficulty is not resolved by a simple opposition between spirit and matter, but by the mode in which the known thing can be in the knower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","text":"The angel knows material and singular things through intelligible species implanted in it by God, which eminently represent lower things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS4","text":"Angelic knowledge is limited where the object is not yet in itself, where it depends upon a created free will, or where it proceeds from God's will alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AS5","text":"The metaphysical-epistemic argument proceeds from the extension of higher knowledge to the determination of divine prerogatives, which circumscribe every created intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","text":"In the order of beings, what is in lower things partially and multiply is contained in higher things eminently, more simply, and more perfectly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A2","text":"What is in a knower is in it according to the mode of the knower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","text":"The angel does not naturally receive material things from sensible things, but knows through intelligible species connatural to it and actually intelligible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A4","text":"The essence of a material thing can be in the intellect intentionally without the real being that it has in the thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","text":"Angelic species derived from the divine essence represent things according to formal principles and according to principles of individuation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","text":"A higher cognitive power is more unified and extends to more things than a lower power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A7","text":"The future in necessary causes is known certainly, in causes that occur for the most part conjecturally, and in causes that occur in the minority is not known through causal knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","text":"Created intellect falls short of divine eternity and has a succession of intelligible conceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","text":"Actual thought and the affection of the will, insofar as they depend upon rational will alone, lie open directly to God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A10","text":"The mysteries of grace depend on God's pure will and therefore exceed natural angelic knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","text":"The beatific knowledge of angels consists in the vision of the Word and of things in the Word, but does not comprehend divine wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","text":"The revelation of mysteries is distributed according to the will of God, the hierarchical rank of angels, and the suitability of offices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX1","text":"A material thing is not in the angelic intellect according to its real being, but according to an intelligible species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX2","text":"Angelic knowledge of material things is neither sensible nor imaginative nor abstracted from material things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX3","text":"To know a singular in universal causes is not to know the singular itself as here and now.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX4","text":"The temporal distance of the future is not assimilated to the local distance of an already existing thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX5","text":"To be above the time of bodily motions is not to be in eternity, which comprehends all time simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX6","text":"To know the bodily effects of thought is not to know thought itself as an act of intellect or affection as an act of will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:NX7","text":"To see divine wisdom is not to comprehend all that lies hidden within it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0099","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D1","text":"Material things can perfect the angelic intellect not according to the inferiority of their material being, but according to the act of intelligible species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A2","CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D2","text":"The angel knows singulars as singulars, because its universal species include the likeness of individuating principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","CH_GGVC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D3","text":"The angel knows present and past things according to natures already existing, and future things according to the order of causes, but not future contingents as they are in themselves future.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A7","CH_GGVC_P_49:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D4","text":"The angel has certainty concerning necessary future things and conjecture concerning frequent future things more perfect than that of man, because it knows causes more universally and subtly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D5","text":"From exterior acts and bodily changes, the angel can conjecture interior dispositions, but it does not penetrate the actual use of intelligible species dependent upon the will itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D6","text":"The mysteries of grace do not lie naturally open to angels, but are revealed in beatific vision in a measured, unequal, and hierarchical manner.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A10","CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:D7","text":"The mystery of the Incarnation is revealed to all angels in common as a principle of ministries, but its particular conditions are manifested successively and not equally to all.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD1","text":"The lack of sense and imagination does not constitute an angelic defect, because a higher mode of knowing contains what lower powers attain in diverse ways.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD2","text":"Singularity is not excluded from intelligibility simply speaking, but only from that intellect whose universality arises through abstraction from material conditions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","CH_GGVC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD3","text":"The limits of angelic knowledge are distributed according to four modes of object: things already existing, causally determined effects, free interior acts, and secrets dependent upon God's will alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A7","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_49:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD4","text":"Angelic providence and administration require knowledge of singulars, but do not transform created administrators into possessors of total divine knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5","text":"Beatific vision establishes dynamic knowledge rather than static possession of all divine things, because further revelation is subject to offices and hierarchical order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX1","text":"It must be false that the excellence of created knowledge suffices of itself for omniscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the universality of a species, without the representation of individuating principles, can present singularity as such.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX3","text":"It must be false that every intelligible is immediately present to every created intellect, because the future, voluntary act, and mystery of grace retain diverse modes of unavailability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX1","text":"No created intellect has a cognitive standpoint from which all temporality, including future contingents, becomes simultaneously present.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX2","text":"The divine will is not reduced to the order of natural species, nor does created vision exhaust the divine essence such that every one of its secrets necessarily lies open.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0099","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS1","text":"Hierarchical order of beings → more eminent containment of the higher → intentional presence of the lower in an intelligible species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS2","text":"Angelic species divinely derived → representation of form and matter → knowledge of material nature and singularity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS3","text":"Distinction between cause and thing in itself → certainty of the necessary, conjecture of the frequent, ignorance of the fortuitous → exclusion of the future as future from created intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS4","text":"Distinction between exterior effect and interior act of will → knowledge of bodily signs → closure of the secret of the heart.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:FGS5","text":"Distinction between nature and the free will of God → incapacity of natural knowledge → graded and ministerially ordered beatific revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF1","text":"Lower materiality → angelic intelligible species → knowledge of material things without sense or abstraction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF2","text":"Material singularity → causally complete likeness in the species → knowledge of the singular as here and now.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF3","text":"Future in causes → graded causal knowledge → reservation of the future in itself to divine eternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF4","text":"Thought in effect → conjecture from signs → exception of acts of intellect and will subject to God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:AF5","text":"Mystery from God's will alone → deficiency of natural knowledge → vision of the Word and measured hierarchical revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME1","text":"The opposition between matter and intellect is dissolved, because the impediment is not the materiality of the object but the incongruity of the mode in which the object is present cognoscibly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME2","text":"The opposition between universal and singular is reformulated, because the angelic universal is not an abstract universal that excludes individuation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME3","text":"The distinction between present and future is not mere temporal distance, but the distinction between a nature already existing and a thing not yet constituted in its proper being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME4","text":"The interiority of the mind is defined not by bodily invisibility, but by the dependence of an actual act upon free will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ME5","text":"The mysteries of grace are reclassified not as naturally higher objects, but as secrets of the divine will communicated by revelation alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text distributes the objects of angelic knowledge into material things, singulars, future things, thoughts of hearts, and mysteries of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT2","text":"Structural — Knowledge is determined by the order of beings, the mode of the recipient, innate species, causality, and dependence upon will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument grants angelic superiority where hierarchical analogy holds, but halts it where the object is reserved to eternity, freedom, or divine revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Knowable reality is divided among the actual being of things, the causal order, the succession of created intellect, and divine eternity containing all time simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning hierarchical order, the mode of the knower, and innate species suffice for the reconstruction of angelic knowledge of material things and singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning causality, succession, and eternity suffice to explain why knowledge of future things is graded and is not equal to divine foreknowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT3","text":"The axioms concerning the dominion of will and the divine will suffice to distinguish secrets of the heart and mysteries of grace from naturally knowable objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains in the transition from universal species to knowledge of the singular, because the representation of individuating principles is asserted, while its mechanism within this question is referred back to an earlier exposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT5","text":"The distinction between angelic superiority and divine prerogatives governs the tension: the principle that a superior knows what an inferior knows does not hold without a limit where the object is knowable from divine freedom or eternity alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the amplification of angelic knowledge through hierarchical order to its restriction through contingency, will, and divine revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_49:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_49@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_49:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 58","title":"First Part · Question 57","context":"Chapter 58","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 57"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 57","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 58","order":59,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_50"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_50@R001","sha256":"97abc1d1eb4a14851acf9386ddf644bd7db39d834265153d39f1bbad862572b1","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS1","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo perfectio naturae angelicae actum, simultaneitatem, processum, veritatem et obiecta cognitionis determinet sine intellectu angelico cum intellectu divino confundendo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS2","text":"Intellectus angelicus naturalia non addiscit neque ratiocinando acquirit, sed per species connaturales immediate et simpliciter cognoscit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS3","text":"Simultaneitas cognitionis non ex numero rerum, sed ex unitate speciei et obiecti intelligibilis pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS4","text":"Falsitas non pertinet per se ad apprehensionem quidditatis, sed accidentaliter oritur cum iudicium de ordine supernaturali a divina sapientia abstrahitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS5","text":"Distinctio cognitionis matutinae et vespertinae ordinem rerum in Verbo et in propria natura exprimit; earum identitas vel diversitas secundum medium cognitionis determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS6","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, distinctiva et reconstructiva: ab aequivocationibus potentiae et motus procedit ad mechanismos speciei, luminis intellectualis, voluntatis et medii cognoscendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A1","text":"Potentia intellectiva dicitur vel ante possessionem habitus et speciei, vel post eorum possessionem sine actuali consideratione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","text":"Omnis potentia intellectus angelici ad naturaliter cognoscibilia speciebus intelligibilibus connaturalibus totaliter completur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","text":"Intellectus angelicus potest esse receptivus revelationum supernaturalium nondum datarum et potest naturaliter nota non actu considerare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A4","text":"Visio Verbi et eorum quae in Verbo videntur, quatenus beatitudinem constituit, semper est in actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","text":"Unitas operationis intellectualis unitatem obiecti formaliter intellecti requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","text":"Plura per unam speciem cognita unum intelligibile constituunt, plura autem per diversas species cognita ut distincta intelligibilia manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","text":"Essentia divina est unica species qua omnia in Verbo cognoscuntur, species autem innatae pluralitatem intelligibilium secundum suos ambitus distribuunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","text":"Discursus est transitus a prius noto ad posterius cognitum quod antea ignotum erat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","text":"Intellectus angelicus in principiis naturaliter cognitis statim intuetur quidquid in eis cognosci potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A10","text":"Compositio et divisio oriuntur ex eo quod intellectus in prima apprehensione subiecti non statim cognoscit quid ei attribuendum vel removendum sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A11","text":"Angelus in apprehensione quidditatis simul cognoscit quidquid ex ea naturaliter attribui vel removeri potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A12","text":"Intellectus quidditatis per se verus est; falsitas ei tantum per accidens ex indebita compositione vel ordinatione accidit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A13","text":"Quidditas rei est principium cognoscendi proprietates naturales, non autem eventus ex ordinatione supernaturali Dei dependentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","text":"Voluntas recta iudicium naturale divinae ordinationi subiicit, voluntas autem perversa illud ab ordine divinae sapientiae abstrahit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","text":"Ordo cognitionis matutinae et vespertinae respondet esse rerum in Verbo ut principio, esse earum in propria natura ut termino, et relationi huius termini ad principium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A16","text":"Esse rerum in propria natura cognoscitur a substantiis angelicis vel per Verbum vel per species innatas, non per cognitionem a rebus acceptam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A17","text":"Distinctio essentialis cognitionum medium cognoscendi sequitur: cognitio vespertina per Verbum cum matutina essentialiter convenit, per species innatas ab ea differt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A18","text":"Operationes eiusdem potentiae simul esse possunt si una ad alteram ordinatur, et imperfectum a perfecto non evacuatur nisi perfectioni opponatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX1","text":"Intellectus angelicus respectu naturalium numquam est potentia nuda speciebus carens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX2","text":"Motus mentis angelicae non est necessario actus imperfecti, sed potest actum perfecti significare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX3","text":"Desiderium angelicum non requirit absentiam rei desideratae, sed potest absentiam fastidii vel expectationem novae revelationis significare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX4","text":"Angelus neque simpliciter unum tantum neque indiscrete omnia simul intelligit; simultaneitas ab unitate intelligibilis determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX5","text":"Cognoscere unum per aliud non constituit discursum nisi alterum ex priori cognito tamquam antea ignotum acquiratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX6","text":"Facultas cognoscendi syllogismum, causam vel effectum non importat acquisitionem veritatis per syllogizare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX7","text":"Cognitio propositionum affirmativarum et negativarum non probat intellectum angelicum componendo et dividendo operari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX8","text":"Nescientia supernaturalium non est ignorantia naturalium nec per se causa falsitatis; error daemonis ad iudicium de ordine supernaturali restringitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX9","text":"Cognitio matutina et vespertina non designat dies solares neque necessariam admixtionem tenebrarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0103","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX10","text":"Nox cognitionis non sequitur vesperam bonorum Angelorum, quia cognitio creaturae ad Deum ut principium refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX11","text":"Cognitio rerum in propria natura non sumitur a rebus ipsis, nec esse rerum in intellectu angelico tertium genus cognitionis praeter matutinum et vespertinum constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0107","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX12","text":"Cognitio vespertina neque cognitioni matutinae opponitur neque adventu eius necessario evacuatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D1","text":"Intellectus angelicus potest simul naturaliter perfectus, quoad considerationem variabilis, supernaturalium receptivus et in visione beatifica perpetuo actualis esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A1","CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D2","text":"In cognitione per Verbum omnia simul cognoscuntur, in cognitione autem per species innatas simul cognoscuntur tantum quae sub eadem specie uniuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D3","text":"Angelus ordinem syllogisticum et causalitatem cognoscere potest, sed veritatem ex principiis vel causis tamquam prius ignotam non acquirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D4","text":"Angelus compositiones, divisiones et enuntiationes ut obiecta simplicis intellectus cognoscit, non ut operationes quibus ad cognitionem perveniat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A10","CH_GGVC_P_50:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D5","text":"Angeli boni errorem vitant quia limites cognitionis naturalis sub ordine divino servant; daemones de naturalibus non falluntur, sed de supernaturalibus falli possunt cum ex sola condicione naturali iudicant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:A13","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D6","text":"Metaphora matutini et vespertini structuram principii, processionis et termini exprimit, non oppositionem veritatis et falsitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D7","text":"Eadem res secundum proprium esse duplici medio cognosci potest, unde cognitio vespertina vel idem actus cum matutina vel actus ab ea distinctus est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A16","CH_GGVC_P_50:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D8","text":"Cognitio matutina et vespertina simul manere possunt, quia cognitio creaturae ad cognitionem Verbi ordinatur et eius imperfectio perfectioni visionis non opponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_50:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","text":"Perfectio intellectus angelici est relativa ad ambitum naturae: naturalem privationem excludit, sed receptivitatem supernaturalem non tollit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2","text":"Simplicitas actus cognoscendi magnam pluralitatem propositionum, relationum et consequentiarum continere potest sine successione aut compositione operativa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A10","CH_GGVC_P_50:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3","text":"Error angelicus non est defectus specierum naturalium, sed deordinatio iudicii qua voluntas ambitum naturae ultra competentiam eius extendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:A13","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD4","text":"Cognitio angelica naturalem successionem acquisitivam excludit, sed novitatem revelationum supernaturalium recipere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5","text":"Cognitio creaturae structuram processionis et reditus habet: res a Verbo ad proprium esse procedit, cognoscitur in utroque ordine, atque cognitio termini ad principium refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_50:A16","CH_GGVC_P_50:A17","CH_GGVC_P_50:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX1","text":"Modi intellectus humani non sunt mensura univoca intellectus angelici; potentia, motus, discursus et compositio analogice distinguenda sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX2","text":"Superioritas intellectus non consistit in intensiore usu operationis inferioris, sed in immediata possessione termini quem inferior per illam operationem acquirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX3","text":"Complexitas cogniti non requirit complexitatem actus cognoscentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX4","text":"Ignorantia limitis supernaturalis non sufficit ad falsitatem; deordinatio iudicii ad illud quod naturaliter determinari nequit requiritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX5","text":"Obiectum cognitum, medium cognitionis et principium a quo cognitio accipitur non sunt idem nec ad unam distinctionem reducuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX1","text":"Intellectus creatus non potest sibi ipsi esse ultimum principium intelligibilitatis; etiam perfecta cognitio naturalis a Verbo ontologice dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2","text":"Perfectio angelica omniscientiam excludit: completudo naturalis cum indigentia revelationis supernaturalis componitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX3","text":"Inter principium naturale et consequentias eius nullum intervallum acquisitivum constituit cognitionem angelicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX4","text":"Bonis Angelis praecluditur terminatio definitiva in creatura tamquam in ultimo cognoscibili; talis fixatio structuram noctis constitueret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS1","text":"Schema actualitatis est: species connaturales → exclusio primae potentiae naturalis; habitus sine consideratione → secunda potentia; revelatio nondum data → receptivitas; visio beatifica → actus continuus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A1","CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS2","text":"Schema simultaneitatis est: unitas speciei → unitas intelligibilis → unus actus simultaneus; diversitas specierum → distincta intelligibilia → non-simultaneitas; essentia divina ut una species → omnia simul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS3","text":"Schema non-discursus est: principium cognitum + consequentiae immediate visae → nulla acquisitio ignoti → nullus transitus discursivus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS4","text":"Schema simplicitatis et veritatis est: quidditas apprehensa → naturalia praedicata simul cognita → nulla compositio acquisitiva → veritas per se; extensio ad ordinem supernaturalem sine regula divina → falsitas per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A10","CH_GGVC_P_50:A11","CH_GGVC_P_50:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:A13","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS5","text":"Schema diei angelici est: esse in Verbo ut principium → cognitio matutina; esse in propria natura ut terminus → cognitio vespertina; relatio termini ad Deum → reditus ad mane sine nocte.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS6","text":"Schema identitatis est: proprium esse cognitum per Verbum → eadem cognitio secundum essentiam, diversa secundum cognitum; proprium esse cognitum per species innatas → cognitio distincta; ordinatio alterius ad alteram → simultaneitas sine repugnantia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A16","CH_GGVC_P_50:A17","CH_GGVC_P_50:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AF1","text":"Aequivocatio potentiae → distinctio ambituum naturalis et supernaturalis → determinatio actus angelici → regula simultaneitatis secundum unitatem speciei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AF2","text":"Perfectio luminis intellectualis → consequentiae visae in principiis → exclusio discursus → praedicata visa in quidditate → exclusio compositionis et divisionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AF3","text":"Veritas quidditatis → limitatio ad naturalia → interventus voluntatis in iudicio supernaturali → distinctio matutini et vespertini → determinatio identitatis secundum medium → compatibilitas utriusque cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME1","text":"Potentia intellectualis ex oppositione simplici actus et privationis in matricem primae potentiae, secundae potentiae, receptivitatis supernaturalis et actus beatifici transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter unum et multa in distinctionem inter pluralitatem rerum et unitatem formalem intelligibilis convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME3","text":"Syllogismus, propositio, affirmatio et negatio ab operationibus necessariis ad obiecta simpliciter cognoscibilia reclassificantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME4","text":"Falsitas ab imperfectione naturali intellectus ad coniunctionem limitis cognoscitivi, iudicii et ordinationis voluntatis transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME5","text":"Vocabula temporalia matutini et vespertini in tabulam ontologicam principii, processionis, termini et reditus convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME6","text":"Quaestio utrum cognitiones sint unae vel diversae solvitur per separationem duarum axium: rei cognitae et medii cognoscendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei: determinantur potentia, simultaneitas, discursus, compositio, falsitas atque cognitio matutina et vespertina in Angelis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis: modum cognitionis regunt species intelligibiles, unitas obiecti, perfectio luminis, ambitus quidditatis, voluntas et medium cognoscendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus: praedicata ex cognitione humana desumpta secundum differentiam inter obiectum cognitum et modum cognoscendi purgantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis: esse creatum a Verbo ad propriam naturam procedit, dum intellectus angelicus naturalem successionem acquisitivam excludit et novam revelationem recipere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad septem determinationes restituendas, quia potentiam, simultaneitatem, processum, veritatem et duplicem cognitionis medium comprehendunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT2","text":"Praemissae de speciebus innatis, visione Verbi et perfectione luminis angelici ex tractatu antecedente assumuntur neque hic integre demonstrantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT3","text":"Cohaerentia interna distinctionibus ambitus, medii et modi operationis conservatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT4","text":"Firmissima commissura est derivatio simultaneitatis, non-discursus et non-compositionis ex unitate intelligibilis et immediata continentia consequentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT5","text":"Apparens oppositio inter completam actualitatem naturalem et non-actualem considerationem solvitur distinctione primae et secundae potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT6","text":"Ambitus vocabuli Angelus partitionem inter Angelos beatos, bonos et daemones requirit; aliter visio perpetua Verbi cum errore daemonico componi non posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT7","text":"Transitus a voluntate perversa ad falsum iudicium explicatur per subtractionem a divina sapientia, sed mechanismus causalitatis voluntatis in intellectum compressus manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT8","text":"Coexistentia cognitionis per Verbum et per species innatas possibilis ostenditur per ordinationem actuum, sed necessitas functionalis duplicis medii ulterius non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT9","text":"Structura matutini et vespertini ab interpretatione Augustiniana sex dierum dependet; argumentum eius exegeseos hic assumitur potius quam probatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT10","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: distinctiones initiales modos humanos cognitionis removent, principia intellectualia operationes angelicas determinant, et ordo ontologicus ultimam cognitionum classificationem generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T163823006504Z_18e44574","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 58","source_sha256":"97abc1d1eb4a14851acf9386ddf644bd7db39d834265153d39f1bbad862572b1","sha256":"8b7d104e5453425d2e25159af410429b09c8204602b128b182def97e9354e0e3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:38:23.009036+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS1","text":"The central question is how the perfection of angelic nature determines act, simultaneity, process, truth, and the objects of knowledge without confusing the angelic intellect with the divine intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS2","text":"The angelic intellect does not learn natural things or acquire them by reasoning, but knows them immediately and simply through connatural species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS3","text":"The simultaneity of knowledge depends not on the number of things, but on the unity of the species and of the intelligible object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS4","text":"Falsity does not pertain per se to the apprehension of quiddity, but arises accidentally when judgment concerning the supernatural order is abstracted from divine wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS5","text":"The distinction between morning and evening knowledge expresses the order of things in the Word and in their proper nature; their identity or diversity is determined according to the medium of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AS6","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, distinctive, and reconstructive: it proceeds from equivocations concerning potency and motion to the mechanisms of species, intellectual light, will, and the medium of knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A1","text":"Intellective potency is spoken of either before the possession of habit and species, or after their possession without actual consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","text":"Every potency of the angelic intellect with respect to naturally knowable things is wholly completed by connatural intelligible species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","text":"The angelic intellect can be receptive of supernatural revelations not yet given and can fail actually to consider naturally known things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A4","text":"The vision of the Word and of those things seen in the Word, insofar as it constitutes beatitude, is always in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","text":"The unity of an intellectual operation requires the unity of the formally understood object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","text":"Many things known through one species constitute one intelligible, whereas many things known through diverse species remain distinct intelligibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","text":"The divine essence is the one species through which all things are known in the Word, whereas innate species distribute a plurality of intelligibles according to their respective scopes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","text":"Discursus is a transition from what is known first to what is known later and was previously unknown.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","text":"The angelic intellect immediately intuits in naturally known principles whatever can be known in them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A10","text":"Composition and division arise from the fact that the intellect, in its first apprehension of the subject, does not immediately know what is to be attributed to it or removed from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A11","text":"In the apprehension of quiddity, the angel simultaneously knows whatever can naturally be attributed to or removed from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A12","text":"The intellect of quiddity is per se true; falsity befalls it only per accidens through improper composition or ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A13","text":"The quiddity of a thing is a principle for knowing natural properties, but not events dependent on God's supernatural ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","text":"A right will subjects natural judgment to divine ordering, whereas a perverse will abstracts it from the order of divine wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","text":"The order of morning and evening knowledge corresponds to the being of things in the Word as principle, their being in their proper nature as terminus, and the relation of this terminus to the principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A16","text":"The being of things in their proper nature is known by angelic substances either through the Word or through innate species, not through knowledge received from things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A17","text":"The essential distinction of cognitions follows the medium of knowing: evening knowledge through the Word essentially agrees with morning knowledge, while through innate species it differs from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:A18","text":"The operations of the same potency can exist simultaneously if one is ordered to the other, and the imperfect is not eliminated by the perfect unless it is opposed to the perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX1","text":"With respect to natural things, the angelic intellect is never bare potency lacking species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX2","text":"The motion of the angelic mind is not necessarily an act of the imperfect, but can signify the act of the perfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX3","text":"Angelic desire does not require the absence of the desired thing, but can signify the absence of weariness or the expectation of a new revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX4","text":"The angel understands neither simply only one thing nor indiscriminately all things at once; simultaneity is determined by the unity of the intelligible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX5","text":"To know one thing through another does not constitute discursus unless the latter is acquired from what was known first as something previously unknown.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX6","text":"The capacity to know a syllogism, cause, or effect does not entail the acquisition of truth through syllogizing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX7","text":"Knowledge of affirmative and negative propositions does not prove that the angelic intellect operates by composing and dividing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX8","text":"Ignorance of supernatural things is not ignorance of natural things nor per se a cause of falsity; the demon's error is restricted to judgment concerning the supernatural order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX9","text":"Morning and evening knowledge do not designate solar days or a necessary admixture of darkness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0103","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX10","text":"The night of knowledge does not follow the evening of the good Angels, because knowledge of the creature is referred to God as principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX11","text":"Knowledge of things in their proper nature is not taken from the things themselves, nor does the being of things in the angelic intellect constitute a third kind of knowledge besides morning and evening knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0107","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:NX12","text":"Evening knowledge neither is opposed to morning knowledge nor is necessarily eliminated by its advent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D1","text":"The angelic intellect can simultaneously be naturally perfect, variable with respect to consideration, receptive of supernatural things, and perpetually actual in the beatific vision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A1","CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D2","text":"In knowledge through the Word all things are known simultaneously, whereas in knowledge through innate species only those things united under the same species are known simultaneously.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D3","text":"The angel can know syllogistic order and causality, but does not acquire truth from principles or causes as something previously unknown.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D4","text":"The angel knows compositions, divisions, and enunciations as objects of simple understanding, not as operations through which it arrives at knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A10","CH_GGVC_P_50:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D5","text":"Good angels avoid error because they preserve the limits of natural knowledge under divine order; demons are not mistaken concerning natural things, but can be mistaken concerning supernatural things when they judge from natural condition alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:A13","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D6","text":"The metaphor of morning and evening expresses the structure of principle, procession, and terminus, not the opposition of truth and falsity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D7","text":"The same thing according to its proper being can be known through a double medium, whence evening knowledge is either the same act as morning knowledge or an act distinct from it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A16","CH_GGVC_P_50:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:D8","text":"Morning and evening knowledge can remain simultaneously, because knowledge of the creature is ordered to knowledge of the Word and its imperfection is not opposed to the perfection of vision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_50:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","text":"The perfection of the angelic intellect is relative to the scope of nature: it excludes natural privation but does not remove supernatural receptivity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2","text":"The simplicity of the act of knowing can contain a great plurality of propositions, relations, and consequences without succession or operative composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A10","CH_GGVC_P_50:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3","text":"Angelic error is not a defect of natural species, but a disordering of judgment by which the will extends the scope of nature beyond its competence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:A13","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD4","text":"Angelic knowledge excludes natural acquisitive succession, but can receive the novelty of supernatural revelations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5","text":"Knowledge of the creature has a structure of procession and return: the thing proceeds from the Word to its proper being, is known in both orders, and knowledge of the terminus is referred to the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_50:A16","CH_GGVC_P_50:A17","CH_GGVC_P_50:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX1","text":"The modes of the human intellect are not a univocal measure of the angelic intellect; potency, motion, discursus, and composition must be distinguished analogically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX2","text":"The superiority of intellect does not consist in a more intense use of an inferior operation, but in immediate possession of the terminus that the inferior acquires through that operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX3","text":"The complexity of what is known does not require complexity in the act of knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX4","text":"Ignorance of the supernatural limit does not suffice for falsity; a disordering of judgment concerning that which cannot be naturally determined is required.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX5","text":"The known object, the medium of knowledge, and the principle from which knowledge is received are not the same and cannot be reduced to one distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX1","text":"The created intellect cannot be for itself the ultimate principle of intelligibility; even perfect natural knowledge depends ontologically on the Word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2","text":"Angelic perfection excludes omniscience: natural completeness is compatible with the need for supernatural revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX3","text":"No acquisitive interval constitutes angelic knowledge between a natural principle and its consequences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX4","text":"For the good Angels, definitive termination in the creature as in the ultimate knowable is precluded; such fixation would constitute the structure of night.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS1","text":"The schema of actuality is: connatural species → exclusion of first natural potency; habit without consideration → second potency; revelation not yet given → receptivity; beatific vision → continuous act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A1","CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS2","text":"The schema of simultaneity is: unity of species → unity of intelligible → one simultaneous act; diversity of species → distinct intelligibles → non-simultaneity; divine essence as one species → all things simultaneously.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS3","text":"The schema of non-discursus is: known principle + immediately seen consequences → no acquisition of the unknown → no discursive transition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS4","text":"The schema of simplicity and truth is: apprehended quiddity → natural predicates simultaneously known → no acquisitive composition → truth per se; extension to the supernatural order without divine rule → falsity per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A10","CH_GGVC_P_50:A11","CH_GGVC_P_50:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:A13","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS5","text":"The schema of the angelic day is: being in the Word as principle → morning knowledge; being in proper nature as terminus → evening knowledge; relation of the terminus to God → return to morning without night.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:FGS6","text":"The schema of identity is: proper being known through the Word → the same knowledge according to essence, different according to what is known; proper being known through innate species → distinct knowledge; ordering of one to the other → simultaneity without incompatibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A16","CH_GGVC_P_50:A17","CH_GGVC_P_50:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AF1","text":"Equivocation of potency → distinction of natural and supernatural scopes → determination of angelic act → rule of simultaneity according to unity of species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AF2","text":"Perfection of intellectual light → consequences seen in principles → exclusion of discursus → predicates seen in quiddity → exclusion of composition and division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:AF3","text":"Truth of quiddity → limitation to natural things → intervention of will in supernatural judgment → distinction of morning and evening → determination of identity according to medium → compatibility of both cognitions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME1","text":"Intellectual potency is transferred from the simple opposition of act and privation into a matrix of first potency, second potency, supernatural receptivity, and beatific act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME2","text":"The opposition between one and many is converted into the distinction between the plurality of things and the formal unity of the intelligible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME3","text":"Syllogism, proposition, affirmation, and negation are reclassified from necessary operations into objects simply knowable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME4","text":"Falsity is transferred from a natural imperfection of the intellect to the conjunction of cognitive limit, judgment, and the ordering of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME5","text":"The temporal terms morning and evening are converted into an ontological map of principle, procession, terminus, and return.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ME6","text":"The question whether cognitions are one or diverse is resolved by separating two axes: the known thing and the medium of knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT1","text":"Surface level: potency, simultaneity, discursus, composition, falsity, and morning and evening knowledge in Angels are determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT2","text":"Structural level: intelligible species, unity of object, perfection of light, scope of quiddity, will, and medium of knowing govern the mode of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic level: predicates drawn from human knowledge are purified according to the difference between the known object and the mode of knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT4","text":"Ontological and temporal level: created being proceeds from the Word to its proper nature, while the angelic intellect excludes natural acquisitive succession and can receive new revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct seven determinations, because they encompass potency, simultaneity, process, truth, and the double medium of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT2","text":"The premises concerning innate species, vision of the Word, and the perfection of angelic light are assumed from the preceding treatise and are not fully demonstrated here.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence is preserved through distinctions of scope, medium, and mode of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT4","text":"The firmest joint is the derivation of simultaneity, non-discursus, and non-composition from the unity of the intelligible and the immediate containment of consequences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT5","text":"The apparent opposition between complete natural actuality and non-actual consideration is resolved by the distinction between first and second potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT6","text":"The scope of the term Angel requires a partition between blessed Angels, good angels, and demons; otherwise perpetual vision of the Word could not be reconciled with demonic error.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT7","text":"The transition from perverse will to false judgment is explained through abstraction from divine wisdom, but the mechanism of the will's causality in the intellect remains compressed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT8","text":"The coexistence of knowledge through the Word and through innate species is shown possible through the ordering of acts, but the functional necessity of the double medium is not further explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT9","text":"The structure of morning and evening depends on the Augustinian interpretation of the six days; the argument of this exegesis is assumed here rather than proved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: initial distinctions remove human modes of knowledge, intellectual principles determine angelic operations, and ontological order generates the final classification of cognitions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_50:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_50@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_50:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 59","title":"First Part · Question 58","context":"Chapter 59","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 58"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 58","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 59","order":60,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_51"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_51@R001","sha256":"3262c182361ed8c67112ea53399e0240acd75dfeb44f4931cf484edde0d2a3fa","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat utrum natura intellectualis angelica voluntatem exigat, et quomodo voluntas ad naturam, intellectum, libertatem atque passiones comparetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS2","text":"Argumentatio appetitum secundum gradum cognitionis distinguit: sine cognitione, cum cognitione particulari, et cum cognitione universalis boni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3","text":"Ex cognitione angelica universalis rationis boni infertur voluntas, quae est appetitus intellectualis boni universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS4","text":"Ex distinctione inter esse cognitum in cognoscente et inclinationem ad rem exteriorem infertur voluntatem creatam nec essentiam nec intellectum esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS5","text":"Ex intellectu universale bonum iudicante infertur liberum arbitrium angelicum, quamvis electio angelica discursiva deliberatione careat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS6","text":"Ex obiecto voluntatis ut bono communi et ex absentia appetitus sensitivi infertur voluntatem angelicam indivisam manere, sine irascibili et concupiscibili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A1","text":"Omnia inclinantur in bonum secundum modum sibi proprium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A2","text":"Modus appetitus sequitur modum cognitionis: appetitus naturalis cognitione caret, sensitivus bonum particulare cognoscit, intellectualis rationem boni universalem cognoscit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A3","text":"Voluntas est inclinatio appetitus intellectualis in bonum sub ratione universali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A4","text":"Angelus per intellectum cognoscit ipsam universalem rationem boni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A5","text":"Essentia rei intra rem continetur; inclinatio ad rem exteriorem per principium essentiae superadditum exercetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A6","text":"Cognitio rem extrinsecam in cognoscente habet; voluntas ad rem extrinsecam inclinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","text":"Potentiae distinguuntur secundum rationes formales obiectorum, non secundum distinctiones materiales rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A8","text":"Solum intellectus universalem rationem boni cognoscens iudicio libero agit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A9","text":"Electio angelica veritatem operabilem subito accipit, non per inquisitionem consilii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A10","text":"Perfectio intellectus angelici requirit determinationem ad omne verum naturaliter cognoscibile; perfectio voluntatis non requirit indifferentiam ad ea quae infra angelum sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A11","text":"Irascibilis et concupiscibilis ad appetitum sensitivum pertinent, qui bonum particulare respicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A12","text":"Nomina passionum in Angelis aut metaphorice dicuntur aut simplices actus voluntatis significant, non passiones sensitivas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX1","text":"Voluntas angelica non est appetitus superior voluntate, quia intellectus et ratio eundem obiectum universale appetibile proponunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX2","text":"Voluntas non definitur sola carentia boni possessi, quia appetitus etiam ad bona iam habita et ad alios actus extenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX3","text":"Motus voluntatis angelicae non est motus corporeus vel imperfectivus, sed actus perfecti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX4","text":"Voluntas creaturae non est eius essentia, quia bonum infinitum extra cuiuslibet creaturae essentiam manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX5","text":"Voluntas angelica non est intellectus, quamvis bonum et verum secundum rem convertantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX6","text":"Liberum arbitrium angelicum non requirit deliberationem inquisitivam nec indeterminationem intellectualem circa veritates naturales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX7","text":"Libertas ut remotio coactionis per se magis et minus non recipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX8","text":"In Angelis non sunt irascibilis et concupiscibilis neque passiones sensitivae quas temperantia et fortitudo humana regulant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D1","text":"In Angelis necesse est esse voluntatem, quia cognitio universalis boni appetitum proportionalem universalem requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A2","CH_GGVC_P_51:A3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D2","text":"Voluntas angelica est potentia realiter ab essentia distincta, quia in bonum extra essentiam creatam tendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D3","text":"Voluntas angelica realiter ab intellectu distinguitur, quia cognoscere et appetere contrarias habitudines ad rem extrinsecam constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A6","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D4","text":"Conversio realis boni et veri distinctionem voluntatis et intellectus non destruit, quia potentiae a rationibus formalibus obiecti distinguuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D5","text":"Angelus liberum arbitrium habet, quia iudicium de particularibus bonis ex universali ratione boni exercet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A4","CH_GGVC_P_51:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D6","text":"Libertatem angelicam cognitio non-discursiva non tollit, sed modum electionis ab electione humana distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A8","CH_GGVC_P_51:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D7","text":"Determinatio intellectualis ad verum naturale cum libertate voluntatis componitur, quia perfectio cognitionis et amplitudo inclinationis ad inferiora diversis regulis mensurantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A6","CH_GGVC_P_51:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D8","text":"Appetitus angelicus indivisus manet et voluntas vocatur, quia bonum commune, non bonum sensibile particulare, formaliter respicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","CH_GGVC_P_51:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D9","text":"Amor, gaudium, temperantia et fortitudo Angelis attribui possunt solum secundum actus voluntatis divino bono conformes vel divinae voluntati firmiter exsequentes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A11","CH_GGVC_P_51:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1","text":"Simplicitas angelica non implicat identitatem omnium principiorum, sed compatitur pluralitatem potentiarum quae diversis modis ad intra et ad extra ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A6","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2","text":"Solus Deus voluntatem, intellectum et essentiam identice habet, quia solus in se ens et bonum universale continet; omnis creatura intellectualis excentricam ordinationem ad bonum infinitum retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SD3","text":"Libertas non ex ignorantia, fluctuatione aut defectu determinationis procedit, sed ex cognitione universalis boni et iudicio quod ad particularia applicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A4","CH_GGVC_P_51:A8","CH_GGVC_P_51:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SD4","text":"Virtutes angelicae non sunt habitus moderantes passiones, sed formae voluntatis ordinate conformatae regulae divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A11","CH_GGVC_P_51:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod creatura intellectualis in propria essentia bonum universale totaliter contineat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod cognitio perfecta determinata et libertas appetitiva sibi mutuo opponantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod electio essentialiter ex discursu, consilio inquisitivo vel ignorantiae superatione oriatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod omnis amor, gaudium, spes, fortitudo vel temperantia passionem sensitivam significet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod multiplicatio potentiarum ex multitudine materialium obiectorum, potius quam ex rationibus formalibus, procedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit absolutam autonomiam creaturae, quia voluntas creata semper ad bonum quod propriam essentiam excedit ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit anthropomorphismum psychologicum, quo vita angelica per passiones corpori et sensui proprias explicaretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit oppositionem simplicem inter necessitatem cognitivam et libertatem moralem, quia ad diversa obiecta et diversa perfectionis criterIa referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS1","text":"Ordinatio omnium ad bonum → distinctio graduum cognitionis → distinctio proportionalis appetituum → intellectus angelicus cognoscens bonum universale → voluntas angelica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS2","text":"Bonum infinitum extra essentiam creatam → inclinatio voluntatis ad extrinsecum → voluntas ≠ essentia → cognitio in cognoscente et inclinatio ad rem → voluntas ≠ intellectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS3","text":"Intellectus universalis → iudicium liberum → electio sine consilio discursivo → libertas angelica eminenter exercita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS4","text":"Obiectum formale boni communis → absentia boni sensibilis particularis → absentia appetitus sensitivi → absentia irascibilis et concupiscibilis → voluntas indivisa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS5","text":"Translatio nominum passionum ad actus voluntatis → attributio analogica amoris, gaudii et virtutum → exclusio passionum angelicarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AF1","text":"Gradus cognitionis → species appetitus → intellectus angelicus → voluntas angelica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AF2","text":"Exterioritas boni infiniti creaturae → distinctio essentiae et voluntatis → distinctio cognitionis et inclinationis → distinctio intellectus et voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AF3","text":"Cognitio universalis boni → iudicium liberum → electio immediata → libertas sine discursu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AF4","text":"Bonum universale ut obiectum voluntatis → indivisio appetitus intellectualis → exclusio potentiarum sensitivarum → reinterpretatio affectuum et virtutum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME1","text":"Appetitus reclassificatur non per solam praesentiam desiderii, sed per rationem boni cogniti et modum cognitionis ipsum antecedentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME2","text":"Simplicitas angelica reclassificatur ut simplicitas compatibilis cum distinctione reali essentiae, intellectus et voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME3","text":"Libertas reclassificatur ut capacitas intellectualis iudicii universalis, non ut oscillatio inter contraria neque ut deliberatio discursiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME4","text":"Affectus et virtutes reclassificantur secundum dualem sermonis ordinem: passiones sensitivae in Angelis negantur, actus voluntatis et conformitas divina affirmantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME5","text":"Distinctio boni et veri efficax fit non in ordine rei, sed in ordine rationum formalium quibus potentiae specificantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus attribuit Angelis voluntatem et liberum arbitrium, dum irascibilem, concupiscibilem et passiones sensitivas negat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT2","text":"Structural — Distinctiones potentiarum ex obiectis formalibus, et distinctiones essentiae atque voluntatis ex oppositione interioritatis et exterioritatis, producuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones ex motu, imperfectione, simplicitate, deliberatione et affectibus solvuntur per mutationem sensus terminorum: motus, appetitus, electio, libertas et passio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creatura intellectualis definitur per non-identitatem sui et boni infiniti, dum Deus solus identitatem essentiae, intellectus et voluntatis habet; angelus autem intelligit et eligit sine successione discursiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam conclusionem principalem, quia nexus cognitionis universalis, appetitus intellectualis et voluntatis totam primam determinationem generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT2","text":"Distinctio voluntatis ab essentia et intellectu firmissime sustinetur per duplicem oppositionem inter bonum infinitum extra creaturam et differentiam cognitionis ab inclinatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT3","text":"Argumentum de libero arbitrio internam tensionem retinet: libertas ex iudicio universali derivatur, sed electio angelica deliberatione carens ulteriorem rationem mediationis non accipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT4","text":"Compositio inter intellectum naturaliter determinatum et voluntatem liberam stabilitur per distinctionem superioris boni, quod indeterminationem non admittit, ab inferioribus, circa quae voluntas non determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT5","text":"Reinterpretatio passionum et virtutum cohaeret si sermo analogicus servatur; fragilis manet ubi eadem vocabula interdum actus voluntatis, interdum passiones sensitivas significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: taxonomia cognitionis et appetitus → distinctio potentiarum → libertas intellectualis → exclusio psychologiae sensitivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T163847617182Z_60a282dc","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 59","source_sha256":"3262c182361ed8c67112ea53399e0240acd75dfeb44f4931cf484edde0d2a3fa","sha256":"6d44caba5b12f67240684cc4f7609a319c7981247dd508bb13f6b2f7b6b83d8c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:38:47.619934+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS1","text":"The question determines whether angelic intellectual nature requires a will, and how will is related to nature, intellect, freedom, and passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS2","text":"The argument distinguishes appetite according to the grade of cognition: without cognition, with particular cognition, and with cognition of universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3","text":"From the angelic cognition of the universal notion of good, will is inferred, which is the intellectual appetite of universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS4","text":"From the distinction between being known in the knower and inclination toward an external thing, it is inferred that created will is neither essence nor intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS5","text":"From the intellect judging universal good, angelic free choice is inferred, although angelic choice lacks discursive deliberation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AS6","text":"From the object of will as common good and from the absence of sensitive appetite, it is inferred that angelic will remains undivided, without irascible and concupiscible powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A1","text":"All things are inclined toward the good according to their proper mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A2","text":"The mode of appetite follows the mode of cognition: natural appetite lacks cognition, sensitive appetite knows particular good, intellectual appetite knows the universal notion of good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A3","text":"Will is the inclination of intellectual appetite toward good under a universal notion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A4","text":"Through intellect, an angel knows the very universal notion of good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A5","text":"The essence of a thing is contained within the thing; inclination toward an external thing is exercised through a principle added to the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A6","text":"Cognition has the external thing in the knower; will is inclined toward the external thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","text":"Powers are distinguished according to the formal notions of their objects, not according to material distinctions among things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A8","text":"Only an intellect knowing the universal notion of good acts by free judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A9","text":"Angelic choice apprehends practical truth immediately, not through the inquiry of deliberation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A10","text":"The perfection of angelic intellect requires determination to every naturally knowable truth; the perfection of will does not require indifference toward those things that are beneath the angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A11","text":"The irascible and concupiscible belong to sensitive appetite, which regards particular good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:A12","text":"Names of passions in Angels are either used metaphorically or signify simple acts of will, not sensitive passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX1","text":"Angelic will is not an appetite higher than will, because intellect and reason propose the same universal appetible object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX2","text":"Will is not defined by the mere lack of a possessed good, because appetite also extends to goods already possessed and to other acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX3","text":"The movement of angelic will is not bodily or imperfective movement, but the act of a perfect being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX4","text":"The will of a creature is not its essence, because infinite good remains outside the essence of every creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX5","text":"Angelic will is not intellect, although good and true are convertible in reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX6","text":"Angelic free choice requires neither inquisitive deliberation nor intellectual indetermination concerning natural truths.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX7","text":"Freedom as the removal of coercion does not in itself admit of more and less.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:NX8","text":"In Angels there are neither irascible and concupiscible powers nor sensitive passions regulated by human temperance and fortitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D1","text":"In Angels there must be will, because cognition of universal good requires a proportionate universal appetite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A2","CH_GGVC_P_51:A3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D2","text":"Angelic will is a power really distinct from essence, because it tends toward good outside created essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D3","text":"Angelic will is really distinct from intellect, because knowing and appetizing constitute contrary relations to an external thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A6","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D4","text":"The real convertibility of good and true does not destroy the distinction between will and intellect, because powers are distinguished by the formal notions of their object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D5","text":"An angel has free choice because it exercises judgment concerning particular goods from the universal notion of good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A4","CH_GGVC_P_51:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D6","text":"Non-discursive cognition does not remove angelic freedom, but distinguishes the mode of choice from human choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A8","CH_GGVC_P_51:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D7","text":"Intellectual determination to natural truth is compatible with freedom of will, because the perfection of cognition and the extent of inclination toward inferior things are measured by different rules.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A6","CH_GGVC_P_51:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D8","text":"Angelic appetite remains undivided and is called will, because it formally regards common good, not particular sensible good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","CH_GGVC_P_51:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:D9","text":"Love, joy, temperance, and fortitude can be attributed to Angels only according to acts of will conformed to divine good or firmly executing the divine will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A11","CH_GGVC_P_51:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1","text":"Angelic simplicity does not imply the identity of all principles, but is compatible with a plurality of powers ordered in diverse ways inwardly and outwardly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A6","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2","text":"God alone has will, intellect, and essence identically, because He alone contains in Himself universal being and good; every intellectual creature retains an eccentric ordination to infinite good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SD3","text":"Freedom does not proceed from ignorance, fluctuation, or a defect of determination, but from cognition of universal good and judgment applied to particulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A4","CH_GGVC_P_51:A8","CH_GGVC_P_51:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SD4","text":"Angelic virtues are not habits moderating passions, but forms of will orderly conformed to the divine rule.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A11","CH_GGVC_P_51:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX1","text":"It must be false that an intellectual creature totally contains universal good in its own essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX2","text":"It must be false that perfect determinate cognition and appetitive freedom are mutually opposed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX3","text":"It must be false that choice essentially arises from discourse, inquisitive deliberation, or the overcoming of ignorance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX4","text":"It must be false that every love, joy, hope, fortitude, or temperance signifies a sensitive passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the multiplication of powers proceeds from a multitude of material objects rather than from formal notions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the absolute autonomy of the creature, because created will is always ordered to a good that exceeds its own essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX2","text":"The system excludes psychological anthropomorphism, by which angelic life would be explained through passions proper to body and sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX3","text":"The system excludes a simple opposition between cognitive necessity and moral freedom, because they are referred to different objects and different criteria of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS1","text":"Ordination of all things to good → distinction of grades of cognition → proportionate distinction of appetites → angelic intellect knowing universal good → angelic will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS2","text":"Infinite good outside created essence → inclination of will toward the external → will ≠ essence → cognition in the knower and inclination toward the thing → will ≠ intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS3","text":"Universal intellect → free judgment → choice without discursive deliberation → angelic freedom exercised eminently.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS4","text":"Formal object of common good → absence of particular sensible good → absence of sensitive appetite → absence of irascible and concupiscible powers → undivided will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:FGS5","text":"Transfer of the names of passions to acts of will → analogical attribution of love, joy, and virtues → exclusion of angelic passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AF1","text":"Grades of cognition → species of appetite → angelic intellect → angelic will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AF2","text":"Externality of infinite good to the creature → distinction of essence and will → distinction of cognition and inclination → distinction of intellect and will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AF3","text":"Cognition of universal good → free judgment → immediate choice → freedom without discourse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:AF4","text":"Universal good as object of will → indivision of intellectual appetite → exclusion of sensitive powers → reinterpretation of affections and virtues.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME1","text":"Appetite is reclassified not through the mere presence of desire, but through the notion of the known good and the prior mode of cognition itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME2","text":"Angelic simplicity is reclassified as simplicity compatible with the real distinction of essence, intellect, and will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME3","text":"Freedom is reclassified as the intellectual capacity for universal judgment, not as oscillation between contraries nor as discursive deliberation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME4","text":"Affections and virtues are reclassified according to a twofold order of speech: sensitive passions in Angels are denied, while acts of will and divine conformity are affirmed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ME5","text":"The distinction between good and true becomes effective not in the order of the thing, but in the order of formal notions by which powers are specified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text attributes will and free choice to Angels, while denying irascible and concupiscible powers and sensitive passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT2","text":"Structural — Distinctions of powers are produced from formal objects, and distinctions of essence and will from the opposition of interiority and exteriority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections from movement, imperfection, simplicity, deliberation, and affections are resolved by changing the sense of the terms: movement, appetite, choice, freedom, and passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The intellectual creature is defined by the non-identity of itself and infinite good, while God alone has identity of essence, intellect, and will; but the angel understands and chooses without discursive succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the principal conclusion, because the nexus of universal cognition, intellectual appetite, and will generates the whole first determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT2","text":"The distinction of will from essence and intellect is most firmly supported by the twofold opposition between infinite good outside the creature and the difference of cognition from inclination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT3","text":"The argument concerning free choice retains an internal tension: freedom is derived from universal judgment, but angelic choice lacking deliberation receives no further account of mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT4","text":"The composition of naturally determined intellect and free will is established through the distinction of the higher good, which admits no indetermination, from lower things, concerning which will is not determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT5","text":"The reinterpretation of passions and virtues coheres if analogical speech is maintained; it remains fragile where the same terms sometimes signify acts of will and sometimes sensitive passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: taxonomy of cognition and appetite → distinction of powers → intellectual freedom → exclusion of sensitive psychology.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_51:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_51@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_51:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 60","title":"First Part · Question 59","context":"Chapter 60","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 59"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 59","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 60","order":61,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_52"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_52@R001","sha256":"a9778681e1717e984aa4cf5e49ae63b740567e4caee13f838780b7e53d7d1fd6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat utrum dilectio angelica, ut radix actuum voluntatis, sit naturalis, electiva, reflexiva in se, extensa ad alium, et ordinata in Deum supra seipsum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS2","text":"Dilectio naturalis in voluntate angelica necessario manet, quia natura prior intellectu in natura intellectuali non destruitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS3","text":"Dilectio electiva non addit alterum principium naturae alienum, sed ex dilectione naturali finis procedit ad bona propter finem volita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS4","text":"Dilectio sui et alterius reducitur ad bonum proprium et ad unitatem: seipsum diligit ut bonum sibi perficiendum, alium ut naturae suae unitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS5","text":"Comparatio Dei ad creaturam mutat regulam dilectionis: Deus, ut bonum universale et ratio essendi creaturae, diligitur naturaliter principalius quam creatura seipsam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS6","text":"Textus ordinem naturalem, electionem liberam, gratiam caritatis et odium peccantis per diversos respectus obiecti distinguit, ne eorum coexistentia contradictionem inducat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A1","text":"Omnis actus appetitivae virtutis ex amore sive dilectione derivatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A2","text":"Natura est prior intellectu et in natura intellectuali servatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A3","text":"Omnis natura inclinationem propriam habet, quae appetitus naturalis vel amor naturalis dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A4","text":"In natura intellectuali inclinatio naturalis secundum voluntatem invenitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A5","text":"Dilectio naturalis, ut inclinatio auctore naturae indita, semper recta est; rectitudo tamen naturalis a rectitudine caritatis et virtutis distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A6","text":"Natura, quia est primum in unoquoque, principium est eorum quae ex ipsa procedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","text":"Voluntas naturaliter fertur in finem ultimum, et dilectio boni ut finis naturalis est; dilectio bonorum propter finem electiva est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A8","text":"Electio non exigit discursum rationis, quamvis amor rationalis stricte dictus cognitionem ratiocinativam consequatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A9","text":"Bonum subsistens amatur cui bonum volumus; bonum inhaerens amatur quod alteri haberi desideramus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A10","text":"Unumquodque naturaliter appetit bonum et perfectionem suam; haec inclinatio est dilectio sui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","text":"Unitas naturalis fundat dilectionem naturalem, ita ut communicatio in specie vel genere alterum efficiat naturaliter diligibilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A12","text":"Intensio dilectionis naturalis proportionatur gradui unitatis: quod est unum numero plus diligitur quam quod est unum specie vel genere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","text":"Pars quae secundum naturam alterius est principalius inclinatur ad illud cuius est quam ad seipsam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","text":"Deus est bonum universale simpliciter, a quo omnis creatura secundum id quod est dependet et cuius est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A15","text":"Deus ut bonum universale naturaliter diligitur; Deus ut bonum beatificans supernaturaliter diligitur caritate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A16","text":"Inclinatio naturalis manet manente natura, etiam ubi voluntas secundum aliquem respectum dissentit vel odit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX1","text":"Amor intellectualis non excludit amorem naturalem nisi “naturalis” restringatur ad naturam sensu et intellectu carentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX2","text":"Inclinatio naturae ab auctore indita libertatem angelicam non tollit, quia Angelus agitur et tamen agit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX3","text":"Dilectio naturalis non est amor moraliter indifferens inter caritatem et iniquitatem positus, sed recta inclinatio naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX4","text":"Dilectio electiva non est necessario amor discursivus aut proprie rationalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX5","text":"Amor sui non requirit dualitatem amantis et amati neque motum localem vel transitivum in aliud.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX6","text":"“Sicut seipsum” non significat aequalitatem intensitatis, identitatem cognitionis, vel identitatem voluntatis inter Angelum et alium Angelum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX7","text":"Dilectio Dei naturalis non fundatur in propinquitate naturarum nec in Deo tamquam fine ad bonum proprium reducto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX8","text":"Conservatio sui non est ultimus terminus inclinationis naturalis, quia natura etiam commune, totum et bonum universale conservare inclinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX9","text":"Dilectio naturalis Dei supra seipsum non est ipsa caritas, quia caritas Deum sub ratione beatificantis supernaturalis attingit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX10","text":"Odium Dei in peccante non demonstrat extinctionem dilectionis naturalis Dei ut boni communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D1","text":"In voluntate angelica necesse est esse dilectionem naturalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A2","CH_GGVC_P_52:A3","CH_GGVC_P_52:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D2","text":"In Angelis dilectio naturalis et dilectio electiva simul sunt, cum prima finem praebeat et secunda bona ad finem ordinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A6","CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_52:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D3","text":"Dilectio electiva constituit ordinem in quo actus angelici a mere naturalibus distinguuntur quoad meritum vel demeritum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_52:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D4","text":"Angelus seipsum naturaliter diligit dum sibi bonum et perfectionem appetit, atque elective diligit dum sibi per electionem aliquod bonum vult.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A9","CH_GGVC_P_52:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D5","text":"Angelus alium Angelum naturaliter diligit ut sibi similem secundum speciem, sed seipsum intensius diligit secundum unitatem numericam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","CH_GGVC_P_52:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D6","text":"Daemon naturalem dilectionem ad Angelos retinet secundum communionem naturae, dum eos odit secundum oppositionem iustitiae et iniustitiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","CH_GGVC_P_52:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D7","text":"Angelus Deum naturaliter plus et principalius diligit quam seipsum, quia creatura pars est boni universalis cuius Deus est principium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D8","text":"Caritas dilectionem naturalem Dei non destruit, sed eam perficit elevando Deum a ratione boni universalis ad rationem beatificantis supernaturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A5","CH_GGVC_P_52:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D9","text":"Deus naturaliter diligitur propter seipsum ut finis, quamvis dependentia creaturae a Deo rationem amoris ex parte amantis constituat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D10","text":"Visio essentiae divinae amorem Dei necessario inducit, sed cognitio Dei per effectus particulares voluntati contrarios odium secundum respectum particularem explicare potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A15","CH_GGVC_P_52:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD1","text":"Ordo dilectionis naturalis non a sola proximitate psychologica sui procedit, sed ab ordine ontologico unitatis, participationis et causalitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","CH_GGVC_P_52:A12","CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD2","text":"Natura, electio et gratia constituunt ordines subordinatos: natura finem et inclinationem praebet, electio media ordinat, caritas finem supernaturaliter perficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A6","CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_52:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD3","text":"Libertas angelica non definitur per inquisitionem discursivam, sed per actum voluntatis qui supra inclinationem naturalem ad particularia ordinanda procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A4","CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_52:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD4","text":"Eadem relatio potest simul amorem naturalem et odium electivum vel deformem continere, si obiectum sub diversis rationibus formalibus accipitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","CH_GGVC_P_52:A15","CH_GGVC_P_52:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD5","text":"Amor naturalis Dei supra seipsum efficit ut caritas non sit correctio inclinationis naturalis perversae, sed perfectio inclinationis naturaliter rectae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A5","CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","CH_GGVC_P_52:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX1","text":"Natura non est stratum irrationalitatis quod intellectui opponitur, sed principium quod etiam in voluntate intellectuali operatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX2","text":"Subjectum creatum non est terminus naturaliter absolutus, quia bonum proprium eius intra bonum universale includitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX3","text":"Iniquitas non potest a dilectione naturali ut tali procedere, quia inclinatio naturalis recta manet et perversio alio ordine ponenda est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX4","text":"Diversitas individuorum vel oppositio secundum iustitiam non delet communionem naturalem quae dilectionem naturalem fundat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX5","text":"Discursus cognoscitivus non est condicio universalis actionis electivae vel libertatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX1","text":"Nullum bonum creaturae est principium ultimum sui ipsius, quia omne bonum creatum a bono universali divino dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX2","text":"Nulla dilectio sui potest legitime totalizare seipsam contra totum cuius creatura est pars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX3","text":"Beatitudo supernaturalis non ex principiis naturae sufficienter derivatur, quamvis dilectio naturalis in Deum ut bonum universale feratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX4","text":"Visio essentiae divinae et odium Dei formaliter compositum esse non possunt, quia visio Deum ut bonum commune immediate manifestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS1","text":"Actus appetitivus → dilectio radicalis → natura in intellectu conservata → inclinatio naturalis in voluntate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS2","text":"Inclinatio naturalis finis → principium voluntatis → electio bonorum propter finem, sine necessitate discursus ratiocinativi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS3","text":"Bonum proprium → dilectio sui; unitas naturae → dilectio alterius; gradus unitatis → gradus dilectionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS4","text":"Pars creaturae → dependentia a bono universali → Deus ut ratio essendi et bonitatis → dilectio Dei supra dilectionem sui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS5","text":"Distinctio rationum obiecti — bonum universale/bonum beatificans; natura/iustitia; essentia/effectus particulares — → coexistentia amoris naturalis cum caritate vel odio secundum alium respectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AF1","text":"Dilectio ut radix appetitus → natura ut prius intellectu → dilectio naturalis in voluntate angelica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AF2","text":"Finis naturalis → dilectio electiva mediorum → dilectio sui → unitas specifica → dilectio alterius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AF3","text":"Unitas numerica sui → regula comparativa finita → ratio partis ad bonum universale → Deus naturaliter supra seipsum → distinctio naturae, gratiae et peccati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME1","text":"Natura reclassificatur non ut contraria intellectui, sed ut principium permanens cuius forma intellectualis est voluntaria inclinatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME2","text":"Electio separatur a discursu rationis et collocatur in ordine finis naturalis ad media volita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME3","text":"Dilectio alterius describitur per unitatem naturae et voluntatem boni alterius, non per aequalitatem intensitatis vel identitatem interioris accessus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME4","text":"Oppositio amoris sui et amoris Dei dissolvitur per transitum ab unitate individuali ad ordinem partis sub bono universali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME5","text":"Odium daemonis et peccatoris reclassificatur ut repugnantia ad rationes particulares, non ut negatio boni communis naturaliter dilecti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT1","text":"Surface — Angelus naturaliter et elective diligit, seipsum et alium diligit, atque Deum supra seipsum naturaliter diligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT2","text":"Structural — Natura praebet inclinationem finis, electio ordinat media, et unitas naturae distribuit relationes dilectionis inter subsistentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Apparentes contradictiones solvuntur per distinctionem rationum formalium: naturalis/electiva, finis/media, bonum commune/particulare, natura/gratia, amor/odium secundum diversos respectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creatura intelligitur ut pars a Deo dependens, cuius inclinatio naturalis ad bonum universale ordinem essendi antecedentem actus particulares exprimit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de prioritate naturae, inclinatione naturali, ordine finis et mediorum, unitate, parte et bono universali sufficiunt ad quinque conclusiones principales restituendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT2","text":"Systema firmissime cohaeret ubi dilectio naturalis exhibetur ut principium electionis et ubi amor Dei derivatur ex relatione partis ad bonum universale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT3","text":"Nondum plene determinatur quomodo inclinatio naturalis semper recta causaliter se habeat ad electionem quae secundum iustitiam vel iniustitiam dissentire potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter regulam qua seipsum propter maximam unitatem numeralem plus diligitur et regulam qua Deus propter causalitatem universalem supra seipsum diligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT5","text":"Distinctio boni universalis naturaliter dilecti et boni beatificantis caritate dilecti clausuram systematis praebet, sed modum internum elevationis naturae ad beatitudinem hic non explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia ab inesse dilectionis naturalis procedit ad electionem, ad unitatem inter creaturas, et demum ad primatum divini boni universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T163915880825Z_2582a570","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 60","source_sha256":"a9778681e1717e984aa4cf5e49ae63b740567e4caee13f838780b7e53d7d1fd6","sha256":"5d4dcbf94c0cb94436b88c4e5f386e4649929f67ccfbc4da8d5a98cb103aec04","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:39:15.881823+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS1","text":"The question examines whether angelic love, as the root of acts of the will, is natural, elective, reflexive upon itself, extended to another, and ordered to God above itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS2","text":"Natural love necessarily remains in the angelic will, because nature, prior to intellect in an intellectual nature, is not destroyed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS3","text":"Elective love does not add another principle alien to nature, but proceeds from natural love of the end to goods willed for the sake of the end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS4","text":"Love of self and of another is reduced to one's own good and to unity: one loves oneself as a good to be perfected for oneself, another as united to one's nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS5","text":"The comparison of God to the creature changes the rule of love: God, as universal good and the ground of the creature's being, is naturally loved more principally than the creature loves itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AS6","text":"The text distinguishes the natural order, free choice, the grace of charity, and the hatred of the sinner according to diverse respects of the object, lest their coexistence introduce contradiction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A1","text":"Every act of the appetitive power derives from love or dilection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A2","text":"Nature is prior to intellect and is preserved in an intellectual nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A3","text":"Every nature has its proper inclination, which is called natural appetite or natural love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A4","text":"In an intellectual nature, natural inclination is found in accordance with the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A5","text":"Natural love, as an inclination implanted by the author of nature, is always right; yet natural rectitude is distinguished from the rectitude of charity and virtue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A6","text":"Nature, because it is first in each thing, is the principle of those things that proceed from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","text":"The will is naturally borne toward the ultimate end, and love of the good as an end is natural; love of goods for the sake of the end is elective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A8","text":"Choice does not require discursive reasoning, although rational love strictly so called follows ratiocinative cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A9","text":"A subsisting good is loved to which we will good; an inhering good is loved which we desire another to possess.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A10","text":"Each thing naturally seeks its own good and perfection; this inclination is love of self.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","text":"Natural unity grounds natural love, such that communion in species or genus renders another naturally lovable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A12","text":"The intensity of natural love is proportioned to the degree of unity: what is one in number is loved more than what is one in species or genus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","text":"A part which according to its nature belongs to another is more principally inclined toward that of which it is than toward itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","text":"God is universal good simply, upon whom every creature depends according to that which it is and to whom it belongs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A15","text":"God as universal good is naturally loved; God as beatifying good is supernaturally loved by charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:A16","text":"Natural inclination remains so long as nature remains, even where the will dissents or hates according to some respect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX1","text":"Intellectual love does not exclude natural love unless “natural” is restricted to a nature lacking sense and intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX2","text":"An inclination implanted in nature by its author does not remove angelic freedom, because the Angel is acted upon and yet acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX3","text":"Natural love is not a morally indifferent love situated between charity and iniquity, but the right inclination of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX4","text":"Elective love is not necessarily discursive love or properly rational love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX5","text":"Self-love does not require a duality of lover and beloved, nor local or transitive movement into another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX6","text":"“As oneself” does not signify equality of intensity, identity of cognition, or identity of will between an Angel and another Angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX7","text":"Natural love of God is not grounded in the proximity of natures, nor in God as an end reduced to one's own good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX8","text":"Self-preservation is not the ultimate terminus of natural inclination, because nature also inclines to preserve the common good, the whole, and universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX9","text":"Natural love of God above oneself is not charity itself, because charity attains God under the aspect of supernatural beatification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:NX10","text":"Hatred of God in the sinner does not demonstrate the extinction of natural love of God as common good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D1","text":"There must be natural love in the angelic will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A2","CH_GGVC_P_52:A3","CH_GGVC_P_52:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D2","text":"In Angels natural love and elective love are present together, since the former supplies the end and the latter orders goods to the end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A6","CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_52:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D3","text":"Elective love constitutes the order in which angelic acts are distinguished from merely natural acts with respect to merit or demerit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_52:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D4","text":"An Angel naturally loves itself while it seeks good and perfection for itself, and electively loves itself while it wills some good for itself through choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A9","CH_GGVC_P_52:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D5","text":"An Angel naturally loves another Angel as similar to itself according to species, but loves itself more intensely according to numerical unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","CH_GGVC_P_52:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D6","text":"A demon retains natural love toward Angels according to communion of nature, while hating them according to the opposition of justice and injustice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","CH_GGVC_P_52:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D7","text":"An Angel naturally loves God more and more principally than itself, because the creature is a part of the universal good of which God is the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D8","text":"Charity does not destroy natural love of God, but perfects it by elevating God from the aspect of universal good to the aspect of supernatural beatification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A5","CH_GGVC_P_52:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D9","text":"God is naturally loved for His own sake as an end, although the creature's dependence on God constitutes the ground of love on the part of the lover.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:D10","text":"The vision of the divine essence necessarily induces love of God, but knowledge of God through particular effects contrary to the will can explain hatred according to a particular respect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A15","CH_GGVC_P_52:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD1","text":"The order of natural love does not proceed from psychological proximity to oneself alone, but from the ontological order of unity, participation, and causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","CH_GGVC_P_52:A12","CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD2","text":"Nature, choice, and grace constitute subordinate orders: nature provides the end and inclination, choice orders the means, charity supernaturally perfects the end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A6","CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_52:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD3","text":"Angelic freedom is not defined by discursive inquiry, but by an act of will that proceeds beyond natural inclination in ordering particulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A4","CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_52:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD4","text":"The same relation can simultaneously contain natural love and elective or deformed hatred, if the object is taken under diverse formal aspects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A11","CH_GGVC_P_52:A15","CH_GGVC_P_52:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SD5","text":"Natural love of God above oneself entails that charity is not a correction of a perverse natural inclination, but the perfection of a naturally right inclination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A5","CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","CH_GGVC_P_52:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX1","text":"Nature is not a stratum of irrationality opposed to intellect, but a principle that also operates in the intellectual will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX2","text":"The created subject is not a naturally absolute terminus, because its proper good is included within universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX3","text":"Iniquity cannot proceed from natural love as such, because natural inclination remains right and perversity must be posited in another order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX4","text":"Diversity of individuals or opposition according to justice does not destroy the natural communion that grounds natural love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX5","text":"Discursive cognition is not a universal condition of elective action or freedom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX1","text":"No good of a creature is the ultimate principle of itself, because every created good depends upon the divine universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX2","text":"No self-love can legitimately totalize itself against the whole of which the creature is a part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX3","text":"Supernatural beatitude is not sufficiently derived from the principles of nature, although natural love is borne toward God as universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX4","text":"The vision of the divine essence and formally composed hatred of God cannot coexist, because the vision immediately manifests God as the common good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS1","text":"Appetitive act → radical love → nature preserved in intellect → natural inclination in the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS2","text":"Natural inclination to the end → principle of the will → choice of goods for the sake of the end, without necessity of discursive reasoning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS3","text":"Proper good → love of self; unity of nature → love of another; degree of unity → degree of love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS4","text":"Part of the creature → dependence on universal good → God as ground of being and goodness → love of God above love of self.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:FGS5","text":"Distinction of aspects of the object — universal good/beatifying good; nature/justice; essence/particular effects — → coexistence of natural love with charity or hatred according to another respect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AF1","text":"Love as root of appetite → nature as prior to intellect → natural love in the angelic will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AF2","text":"Natural end → elective love of means → love of self → specific unity → love of another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:AF3","text":"Numerical unity of self → finite comparative rule → relation of part to universal good → God naturally above oneself → distinction of nature, grace, and sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME1","text":"Nature is reclassified not as contrary to intellect, but as a permanent principle whose intellectual form is voluntary inclination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME2","text":"Choice is separated from discursive reasoning and situated in the order from the natural end to the willed means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME3","text":"Love of another is described through unity of nature and the willing of another's good, not through equality of intensity or identity of interior access.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME4","text":"The opposition between self-love and love of God is dissolved through the transition from individual unity to the order of a part under universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ME5","text":"The hatred of the demon and the sinner is reclassified as repugnance toward particular aspects, not as denial of the naturally loved common good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT1","text":"Surface — An Angel loves naturally and electively, loves itself and another, and naturally loves God above itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT2","text":"Structural — Nature provides inclination to the end, choice orders the means, and unity of nature distributes relations of love among subsistents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Apparent contradictions are resolved through the distinction of formal aspects: natural/elective, end/means, common good/particular good, nature/grace, love/hatred according to diverse respects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The creature is understood as a part dependent upon God, whose natural inclination toward universal good expresses an order of being antecedent to particular acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning the priority of nature, natural inclination, the order of end and means, unity, part, and universal good suffice to restore the five principal conclusions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT2","text":"The system coheres most firmly where natural love is presented as the principle of choice and where love of God is derived from the relation of part to universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT3","text":"It is not yet fully determined how natural inclination, always right, is causally related to choice, which can dissent according to justice or injustice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains between the rule by which oneself is loved more on account of the greatest numerical unity and the rule by which God is loved above oneself on account of universal causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0090","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT5","text":"The distinction between the naturally loved universal good and the beatifying good loved by charity provides closure to the system, but does not here explain the internal mode of the elevation of nature to beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_52:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the inherence of natural love to choice, to unity among creatures, and finally to the primacy of the divine universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_52:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_52@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_52:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 61","title":"First Part · Question 60","context":"Chapter 61","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 60"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 60","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 61","order":62,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_53"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_53@R001","sha256":"a6bdb76523cf398d7d4dd1e459ac8c5e55861718f972049079800cad7d334761","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS1","text":"Quaestio originem angelorum determinat per quattuor nexus: causam essendi, initium temporale, ordinem ad creaturam corpoream et locum creationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS2","text":"Argumentatio ex distinctione Dei et creaturae procedit: Deus solus est esse per essentiam; angelus, quamvis immaterialis, ens participatum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS3","text":"Forma subsistens a causalitate materiali et transmutativa eximitur, non autem a causalitate producentis totam substantiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS4","text":"Creatio ex nihilo et libertas voluntatis divinae angelos ab aeternitate excludunt, etiam si natura eorum incorruptibilis est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS5","text":"Angelus pars universi est; propter bonum ordinis universalis simul cum creatura corporea creatus probabiliter dicitur, sed contraria sententia non damnatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS6","text":"Locus corporeus creationis non necessitatem ontologicam significat, sed ordinem spiritualis creaturae ad corpus eiusque praesidentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A1","text":"Deus solus est suum esse et ens per essentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A2","text":"In omni re praeter Deum essentia et esse distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","text":"Omne ens per participationem causatur ab eo quod est per essentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A4","text":"Substantia forma subsistens causam formalem sui esse non habet, sed causam habet producentem totam suam substantiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","text":"Creatura producitur ex nihilo, ita ut ante eius productionem nihil eius fuerit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A6","text":"Voluntas divina ad productionem creaturarum non ex necessitate determinatur, sed creat quae vult et quando vult.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A7","text":"Incorruptibilitas naturae intellectualis ex capacitate veritatis sequitur, sed non aeternitatem illius naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","text":"Angelus pars universi est, et bonitas universi consistit in ordine creaturarum ad invicem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A9","text":"Pars perfecta a suo toto separata esse non convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A10","text":"Creatura spiritualis et creatura corporea unum universum constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A11","text":"Angeli naturae corporali praesident, licet a corpore secundum esse et fieri non dependeant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX1","text":"Angelus non est ens a se, quamvis sit forma immaterialis et subsistens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX2","text":"Creatio angelica non est transmutatio materiae de potentia in actum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX3","text":"Absentia causae formalis non est absentia causae efficientis productivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX4","text":"Angelus non est aeternus, etiam si incorruptibilis et supra motum corporalem est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX5","text":"Esse supra tempus motus caelestis non est esse extra successionem essendi post non esse vel operationum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX6","text":"Angelus non est medium metaphysicum quod eandem rationem habeat ac Deus supra universum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX7","text":"Simultaneitas creationis angelicae et corporalis probabilior est, non tamen necessaria conclusio fidei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX8","text":"Creatio angelorum in loco corporeo non ponit dependentiam eorum a corpore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX9","text":"Ascensus angeli peccantis non est transitus ad altius caelum corporale, sed appetitus aequalitatis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D1","text":"Omnes angeli a Deo creati sunt, quia eorum esse participatum causam esse per essentiam requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A1","CH_GGVC_P_53:A2","CH_GGVC_P_53:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D2","text":"Immaterialitas angelica modum causalitatis creatricis mutat, non necessitatem causae creatricis tollit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","CH_GGVC_P_53:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D3","text":"Aeternitas Dei non communicatur creaturae ex sola divina causalitate, quia actus creandi liber voluntarius est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D4","text":"Incorruptibilitas angelorum conservat eorum naturam a corruptione, non removet initium donationis illius naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D5","text":"Creatio simultanea angelorum et corporum ex unitate universi probabiliter infertur, non ex impossibilitate absoluta creationis separatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_53:A9","CH_GGVC_P_53:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D6","text":"Caelum Empyreum, si sic nominetur, congruit ut locus creationis superiorum angelorum propter significationem praesidentiae universalis super corpora.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A10","CH_GGVC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D7","text":"Distinctio locorum angelicorum potest analogice respondere distinctioni virtutum universalium et particularium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SD1","text":"Tria praedicata—causa essendi, aeternitas et incorruptibilitas—radicaliter separantur: unum solum Deo competit, alterum creaturae initium negat, tertium creaturae corruptionem negat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A1","CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SD2","text":"Universum non constituitur mera aggregatione substantiarum, sed ordine partium cuius bonitas condicionem originis creaturarum interpretatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_53:A9","CH_GGVC_P_53:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SD3","text":"Locus angelicus fit index ordinis et potestatis, non principium essendi angelici.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A10","CH_GGVC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SD4","text":"Tempus non univoce definitur per motum corporeum, quia creatura spiritualis successionem essendi et operationis habere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet formam separatam per se sufficientem esse ad rationem sui esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet causam aeternam effectum creatum necessario et coaeternaliter producere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet incorruptibilitatem ad modum essendi divinum, id est aeternitatem sine initio, extendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet excellentiam ontologicam angelorum eos extra ordinem universi collocare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet relationem spiritus ad corpus intelligi posse solum ut dependentiam materialem aut collocationem localem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SNX1","text":"Nulla creatura, etiam intellectualis et incorruptibilis, participat modum divinum essendi a se et sine initio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SNX2","text":"Nullum ens creatum intelligitur plene extra ordinem causalitatis divinae et bonum totalitatis universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SNX3","text":"Sensus litteralis unicus de principio creationis non exigitur, ubi distinctae expositiones ordinem doctrinalem sine contradictione fidei servant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:FGS1","text":"Distinctio essentiae et esse → participatio essendi → dependentia causalis → creatio angelorum a Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:FGS2","text":"Creatio ex nihilo + voluntas divina libera → initium creaturae contingens → exclusio aeternitatis angelicae → compatibilitas cum incorruptibilitate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:FGS3","text":"Angelus ut pars universi + ordo ut bonum universi → simultaneitas creationis probabilior → permissio sententiae contrariae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:FGS4","text":"Unitas spiritualis et corporalis creaturae + praesidentia angelica → locus corporeus significativus → exclusio dependentiae corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AF1","text":"Immaterialitas angelica → quaestio de causa essendi → distinctio esse per essentiam et per participationem → creatio a Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AF2","text":"Causa divina aeterna → distinctio inter esse Dei et voluntatem liberam → creatio ex nihilo → initium angelorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AF3","text":"Excellentia angelica → reiectio status extracosmici → angelus ut pars universi → simultaneitas probabilior cum corpore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AF4","text":"Incorporalitas angelica → negatio dependentiae localis → locus supremus ut signum praesidentiae → ordinatio ad naturam corpoream.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter ens immateriale et ens creatum dissolvitur: immaterialitas non eximit a participatione essendi neque a creatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ME2","text":"Aeternitas, incorruptibilitas et supratemporalitas distinguuntur ut praedicata non convertibilia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ME3","text":"Angelus reclassificatur non ut tertium quid inter Deum et mundum, sed ut pars creata ordinis universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ME4","text":"Locus corporis supremi reclassificatur ex fundamento essendi in signum ordinis gubernativi inter spiritum et corpus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT1","text":"Surface — Quaestio explicite determinat utrum angeli causam, initium, prioritatem temporalem et locum creationis habeant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT2","text":"Structural — Distinctio essentiae et esse instituit asymmetriam causalitatis inter Deum, ens per essentiam, et creaturas, entia per participationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio singularia de angelis subordinat rationi totalitatis: ordo universi praevalet imagini angelorum ut substantiarum separatarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creatura spiritualis initium habet sine corruptione necessaria et successionem habet sine motu corporeo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de esse per essentiam, participatione et causalitate sufficienter restituunt conclusionem quod angeli a Deo creati sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de creatione ex nihilo et voluntate divina libera sufficienter restituunt negationem aeternitatis angelicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT3","text":"Simultaneitas angelorum cum creatura corporea non ex principiis necessitatem strictam obtinet, sed iudicium probabilitatis ex ratione boni universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter universalem rationem partis ad totum et permissam sententiam creationis angelorum ante mundum corporeum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT5","text":"Tensio manet inter negationem dependentiae angelorum a corpore et usum loci corporei ad exprimendum eorum ordinem ac potestatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, si distinctio causae essendi, initii temporalis, ordinis universalis et significationis localis non confunditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T163938736915Z_fda5b161","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 61","source_sha256":"a6bdb76523cf398d7d4dd1e459ac8c5e55861718f972049079800cad7d334761","sha256":"952ac68cbadd785dc56c6b2ea77dab4519f54f0ef90f78d0791bb1fea66a8ab3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:39:38.737846+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS1","text":"The question determines the origin of the angels through four connections: the cause of being, temporal beginning, order to corporeal creature, and the place of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS2","text":"The argument proceeds from the distinction between God and creature: God alone is being through essence; the angel, although immaterial, is a participated being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS3","text":"A subsistent form is exempt from material and transmutative causality, but not from the causality of one producing the whole substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS4","text":"Creation from nothing and the freedom of the divine will exclude angels from eternity, even if their nature is incorruptible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS5","text":"The angel is a part of the universe; for the sake of the good of universal order, it is probably said to have been created simultaneously with corporeal creature, but the contrary opinion is not condemned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AS6","text":"The corporeal place of creation does not signify ontological necessity, but the order of spiritual creature to body and its presidency over it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A1","text":"God alone is His own being and being through essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A2","text":"In every thing other than God, essence and being are distinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","text":"Every being through participation is caused by that which is through essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A4","text":"A substance that is a subsistent form does not have a formal cause of its being, but it has a cause producing its whole substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","text":"A creature is produced from nothing, such that before its production nothing of it existed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A6","text":"The divine will is not determined by necessity to the production of creatures, but creates what it wills and when it wills.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A7","text":"The incorruptibility of intellectual nature follows from its capacity for truth, but not the eternity of that nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","text":"The angel is a part of the universe, and the goodness of the universe consists in the order of creatures toward one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A9","text":"It is not fitting for a perfect part to be separated from its whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A10","text":"Spiritual creature and corporeal creature constitute one universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:A11","text":"Angels preside over corporeal nature, although they do not depend on body with respect to being and becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX1","text":"The angel is not a being from itself, although it is an immaterial and subsistent form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX2","text":"Angelic creation is not a transmutation of matter from potency into act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX3","text":"The absence of a formal cause is not the absence of an efficient productive cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX4","text":"The angel is not eternal, even if it is incorruptible and above corporeal motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX5","text":"To be above the time of celestial motion is not to be outside the succession of being after non-being or of operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX6","text":"The angel is not a metaphysical intermediary having the same account as God above the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX7","text":"The simultaneity of angelic and corporeal creation is more probable, yet not a necessary conclusion of faith.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX8","text":"The creation of angels in a corporeal place does not posit their dependence on body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:NX9","text":"The ascent of the sinning angel is not a passage to a higher corporeal heaven, but an appetite for divine equality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D1","text":"All angels were created by God, because their participated being requires a cause that is being through essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A1","CH_GGVC_P_53:A2","CH_GGVC_P_53:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D2","text":"Angelic immateriality changes the mode of creative causality, but does not remove the necessity of a creative cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","CH_GGVC_P_53:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D3","text":"God's eternity is not communicated to creature by divine causality alone, because the act of creating is freely voluntary.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D4","text":"The incorruptibility of angels preserves their nature from corruption; it does not remove the beginning of the bestowal of that nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D5","text":"The simultaneous creation of angels and bodies is probably inferred from the unity of the universe, not from the absolute impossibility of separate creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_53:A9","CH_GGVC_P_53:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D6","text":"The Empyrean Heaven, if it is so named, is fitting as the place of creation of the higher angels on account of the signification of universal presidency over bodies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A10","CH_GGVC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:D7","text":"The distinction of angelic places can correspond analogically to the distinction between universal and particular powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SD1","text":"Three predicates—cause of being, eternity, and incorruptibility—are radically separated: one belongs to God alone, another denies beginning to creature, and the third denies corruption to creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A1","CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SD2","text":"The universe is not constituted by a mere aggregation of substances, but by an order of parts whose goodness interprets the condition of the origin of creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_53:A9","CH_GGVC_P_53:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SD3","text":"Angelic place becomes an index of order and power, not a principle of angelic being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A10","CH_GGVC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SD4","text":"Time is not defined univocally through corporeal motion, because spiritual creature can have succession of being and operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX1","text":"It must be false that a separate form is sufficient through itself for the account of its own being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX2","text":"It must be false that an eternal cause necessarily and coeternally produces a created effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX3","text":"It must be false that incorruptibility is extended to the divine mode of being, that is, eternity without beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the ontological excellence of angels places them outside the order of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the relation of spirit to body can be understood only as material dependence or local placement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SNX1","text":"No creature, even intellectual and incorruptible, participates in the divine mode of being from itself and without beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SNX2","text":"No created being is understood as wholly outside the order of divine causality and the good of the totality of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:SNX3","text":"A single literal sense concerning the beginning of creation is not required where distinct expositions preserve doctrinal order without contradiction of faith.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:FGS1","text":"Distinction of essence and being → participation in being → causal dependence → creation of angels by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:FGS2","text":"Creation from nothing + free divine will → contingent beginning of creature → exclusion of angelic eternity → compatibility with incorruptibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:FGS3","text":"Angel as part of the universe + order as the good of the universe → more probable simultaneity of creation → permission of the contrary opinion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:FGS4","text":"Unity of spiritual and corporeal creature + angelic presidency → significant corporeal place → exclusion of corporeal dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AF1","text":"Angelic immateriality → question of the cause of being → distinction between being through essence and through participation → creation by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AF2","text":"Eternal divine cause → distinction between God's being and free will → creation from nothing → beginning of angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AF3","text":"Angelic excellence → rejection of extracosmic status → angel as part of the universe → more probable simultaneity with body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:AF4","text":"Angelic incorporeality → denial of local dependence → highest place as sign of presidency → ordination to corporeal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ME1","text":"The opposition between immaterial being and created being is dissolved: immateriality does not exempt from participation in being or from creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ME2","text":"Eternity, incorruptibility, and supratemporality are distinguished as non-convertible predicates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ME3","text":"The angel is reclassified not as a third thing between God and the world, but as a created part of universal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ME4","text":"The place of the highest body is reclassified from a foundation of being into a sign of governing order between spirit and body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT1","text":"Surface — The question explicitly determines whether angels have a cause, a beginning, temporal priority, and a place of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT2","text":"Structural — The distinction of essence and being establishes an asymmetry of causality between God, being through essence, and creatures, beings through participation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument subordinates particulars concerning angels to the account of totality: the order of the universe prevails over the image of angels as separate substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Spiritual creature has a beginning without necessary corruption and has succession without corporeal motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning being through essence, participation, and causality sufficiently reconstruct the conclusion that angels were created by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning creation from nothing and free divine will sufficiently reconstruct the denial of angelic eternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT3","text":"The simultaneity of angels with corporeal creature does not obtain strict necessity from the principles, but a judgment of probability from the account of the good of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains between the universal account of the part to the whole and the permitted opinion of the creation of angels before the corporeal world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT5","text":"A tension remains between the denial of the dependence of angels on body and the use of a corporeal place to express their order and power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_53:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if the distinction among the cause of being, temporal beginning, universal order, and local signification is not confused.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_53:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_53@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_53:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 62","title":"First Part · Question 61","context":"Chapter 62","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 61"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 61","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 62","order":63,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_54"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_54@R001","sha256":"4aa7860f51af9aed416f888149e4801c6cee02dcf8ccf23d1cbd8beb2d58125d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quo ordine natura angelica ab initiali conditione ad gratiam, meritum et gloriam perducatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS2","text":"Beatitudo naturalis, statim naturae angelicae conveniens, distinguitur ab ultima beatitudine visionis divinae, quae omnem facultatem creatam excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS3","text":"Transitus ad ultimum finem non a natura sola, sed a gratia movente et actum liberum meritorium informante generatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS4","text":"Ordo consummationis constituitur ut natura cum gratia initiali, conversio meritoria, deinde immediata fruitio in distincta successione actuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS5","text":"Diversitas graduum naturalium rationabiliter ordinatur ad diversos gradus conversionis, gratiae et gloriae, salva omnium dependentia a voluntate divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS6","text":"Gloria naturam et operationes naturales servat, voluntatem in bono confirmat et progressum essentialem claudit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS7","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica et reconstructiva procedit a distinctione naturae et finis ad medium gratiae, inde ad meritum, consummationem et proprietates status terminalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A1","text":"Beatitudo nominat ultimam perfectionem naturae rationalis vel intellectualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","text":"Alia perfectio ultima virtute naturae attingitur, alia in visione essentiae divinae consistit et omnem intellectum creatum excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","text":"Natura angelica perfectionem naturalem non discursu acquirit, sed statim secundum proprium modum possidet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","text":"Voluntas creata in finem supra naturam ferri non potest nisi motione agentis supernaturalis, quae auxilium gratiae dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A5","text":"Effectus posterius sub providentia divina per operationem creaturae producendi in prima conditione secundum principia seminalia praeordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","text":"Gratia est principium bene operandi et merendi gloriam, non finis operationis neque praemium consummatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A7","text":"Gratia naturam intellectualem secundum modum liberum inclinat, non per necessitatem antecedentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A8","text":"Soli Deo beatitudo perfecta est naturalis; creaturae beatitudo est finis naturae, non ipsa natura.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A9","text":"Operatio finem intra virtutem agentis efficit vel acquirit, sed finem supra virtutem meretur tamquam donum alterius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","text":"Meritum rationem viae ad finem nondum possessum habet, fruitio autem rationem termini iam adepti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","text":"Gratia naturam perficit secundum modum proprium naturae recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A12","text":"Instantia angelica distinguuntur secundum successionem actuum, non secundum tempus rerum corporalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","text":"Rationabiliter ponitur diversos gradus naturae angelicae a divina sapientia ad diversos gradus gratiae et gloriae ordinari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A14","text":"In Angelo nulla compositio naturarum motum intellectivum retardat, quare natura secundum totam suam virtutem movetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A15","text":"Principium prius salvatur in perfectione sibi addita; ideo natura eiusque actus in beatitudine servantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","text":"Visio essentiae divinae voluntati ipsam essentiam bonitatis praesentat et omnem actum eius sub ordine Dei constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A17","text":"Perfectio libertatis consistit in electione diversorum servato ordine finis, non in possibilitate ab ordine finis deficiendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A18","text":"Quia omnis visio creata finita est neque Deum comprehendit, praedestinatio divina unicuique creaturae determinatum visionis gradum praefigit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX1","text":"Angeli non sunt creati in ultima beatitudine, quamvis perfectionem naturalem ab initio possideant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX2","text":"Dilectio naturalis Dei ut principii naturae non sufficit ad conversionem in Deum ut obiectum visionis beatificae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX3","text":"Difficultas actus non reducitur ad contrarietatem vel impedimentum, sed etiam ex excessu finis supra potentiam oritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX4","text":"Praeparatio ad gratiam non postulat aliam gratiam habitualem in infinitum, sed operationem Dei voluntatem convertentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX5","text":"Gratia initialis aversionem Angeli non excludit per necessitatem, quia inclinatio gratiae modum liberum naturae servat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX6","text":"Meritum nec ex sola difficultate nec ex conversione naturali oritur, sed ex actu caritate per gratiam informato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX7","text":"Gloria neque post adeptionem meretur neque eodem actu quo fruitio exercetur acquiritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX8","text":"Beatitudo naturalem cognitionem et dilectionem non evacuat tamquam superfluas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX9","text":"Potentia rationalis non se habet ad opposita circa obiectum ad quod naturaliter et perfecte ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0144","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX10","text":"Possibilitas peccandi non constituit perfectionem liberi arbitrii, sed defectibilitatem eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX11","text":"Proportio graduum gratiae ad naturalia non facit gratiam debitam naturae aut ex operibus causatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX12","text":"Caritas perfecta comprehensoris non est principium novi meriti, sed actus fruitionis praemii iam possessi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX13","text":"Gradus essentialis beatitudinis post terminum praedestinatum non crescit, quamvis gaudium accidentale augeri possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0164","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D1","text":"Angelus ab initio beatus est secundum perfectionem naturalem, non secundum visionem essentiae divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A1","CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D2","text":"Conversio voluntatis angelicae ad beatitudinem ultimam necessario auxilio gratiae sustentatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","text":"Probabilius et dictis sanctorum consonantius est Angelos cum gratia gratum faciente creatos esse, quia principium operationis ad gloriam ante effectum terminalem dari convenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A5","CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","text":"Beatitudo angelica praeceditur actu libero caritate informato, qui finem supra naturam meretur ex gratia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8","CH_GGVC_P_54:A9","CH_GGVC_P_54:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D5","text":"Unicus actus meritorius sufficit, et gloria eum statim sequitur in alio instanti secundum successionem actuum angelicorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","CH_GGVC_P_54:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","text":"Rationabiliter maiores naturae angelicae gradus maiori conversionis intensitati atque amplioribus gratiae et gloriae gradibus respondent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D7","text":"Cognitio et dilectio naturales in gloria permanent, quia operationes naturales sub operationibus gloriae ordinantur neque eis opponuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D8","text":"Angelus beatus peccare non potest, quia voluntas videns ipsam bonitatem omnia eligit sub ordine Dei, quo libertas non minuitur sed perficitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","CH_GGVC_P_54:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","text":"Adepto gradu beatitudinis praedestinato, Angelus neque essentialiter proficit neque ulterius meretur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D10","text":"Ministeria beatorum sunt diffusio perfectionis iam possessae et pars praemii, non via ad novum meritum; ex eis tamen gaudium accidentale accrescere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A15","CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0162","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0164","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD1","text":"Natura, gratia et gloria constituunt ordinem elevationis non competitivum: natura recipitur, gratia operationem supernaturalem possibilitat, gloria utramque consummat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D1","CH_GGVC_P_54:D2","CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","CH_GGVC_P_54:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD2","text":"Transitus angelicus est irreversibilis: defectibilitas initialis admittit conversionem liberam, meritum terminatur in visione, visio voluntatem in bono confirmat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD3","text":"Status viae in Angelo realis sed minimus est, quia successio meriti et fruitionis requiritur sine discursu vel mora temporis corporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD4","text":"Hierarchia gloriae simul gratuita et naturae congruens manet, quia nec natura gratiam efficit nec voluntas divina ordinem naturalem a se institutum deserit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","CH_GGVC_P_54:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD5","text":"Adeptio finis mutat rationem operationis: actus ante terminum meretur, actus post terminum fruitur et perfectionem habitam diffundit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0162","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD6","text":"Capacitas naturalis determinat modum receptivum et intensitatem conversionis, sed neque obiectum beatificum neque possessionem eius producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D2","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX1","text":"Natura creata non potest ex se generare ordinem ad finem supernaturalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX2","text":"Perfectio creationis non implicat possessionem immediatam omnis finis ad quem creatura per operationem ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX3","text":"Gratia et libertas non sunt principia mutuo excludentia, quia elevatio recipitur secundum modum liberum recipientis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A7","CH_GGVC_P_54:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX4","text":"Operatio naturalis inferior non fit falsa aut inutilis per adventum cognitionis et dilectionis perfectioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0129","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX5","text":"Defectibilitas boni creati in se considerati non est invincibilis, quia perfecta coniunctio bono increato indefectibilitatem communicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX6","text":"Alternativa mali non est constitutiva rationalitatis aut libertatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX7","text":"Gratuitum non significat inordinatum vel sine congruentia ad capacitatem recipientis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX8","text":"Finis ultimus non potest manere terminus indefinite mobilis sine destructione rationis finis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX9","text":"Duratio corporalis non est mensura necessaria mutationis intellectualis angelicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX1","text":"Systema omnem creaturam sibi ipsi sufficientem ad beatificationem excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX2","text":"Creaturae praecluditur comprehensio Dei et summus modus visionis, etiam cum essentiam divinam vere videat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX3","text":"In termino beatifico nullum futurum essentiale superest quod eundem comprehensorem ad altiorem statum viae revocet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX4","text":"Ordo supernaturalis non admittitur ut substitutio naturae, sed tantum ut eius elevatio, conservatio et consummatio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","CH_GGVC_P_54:A15","CH_GGVC_P_54:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS1","text":"Distinctio fundamentalis operatur hoc modo: perfectio naturalis statim data ≠ gratia elevans ≠ gloria terminalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","CH_GGVC_P_54:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS2","text":"Finis supra naturam → motio gratiae → conversio libera caritatis → meritum finis donandi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A7","CH_GGVC_P_54:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS3","text":"Gratia initialis probabiliter naturae concreata → primus actus meritorius → distinctum instans actus → fruitio immediata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS4","text":"Ordo sapientiae divinae → gradus naturales diversi → intensitates conversionis diversae → gradus gratiae et gloriae proportionati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:A14","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS5","text":"Visio bonitatis per essentiam → ordinatio invariabilis voluntatis ad Deum → electio libera intra finem → impossibilitas peccati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","CH_GGVC_P_54:A17","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS6","text":"Gradus praedestinatus adeptus → clausura meriti essentialis → fruitio et diffusio perfectionis → augmentum accidentale sine progressu essentiali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A18","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0162","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0164","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AF1","text":"Ambiguitas beatitudinis initialis → distinctio perfectionis naturalis et visionis divinae → necessitas gratiae → probabilitas gratiae concreatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D1","CH_GGVC_P_54:D2","CH_GGVC_P_54:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AF2","text":"Gratia antecedens → actus caritatis meritorius → fruitio immediate subsequens → distributio graduum secundum ordinem naturae et providentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AF3","text":"Gloria naturam servans → voluntas in bono confirmata → peccatum impossibile → terminus essentialiter improgressibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D7","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME1","text":"Beatitudo ex notione univoca in duplicem perfectionem, naturalem et supernaturalem, reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A1","CH_GGVC_P_54:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME2","text":"Difficultas ab impedimento psychologico separatur et etiam ut excessus obiectivi finis supra potentiam describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME3","text":"Gratia non ut substitutum naturae, sed ut principium motus quem natura sola producere nequit, collocatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME4","text":"Libertas a potestate mali eligendi ad potestatem multipliciter agendi sub ordine finis transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A17","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME5","text":"Tempus angelicum non per durationem corporalem, sed per successionem actuum meriti et fruitionis describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A12","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME6","text":"Hierarchia naturalis et hierarchia gloriae non amplius habentur ut ordines extrinseci, sed ut ordines a providentia coordinati sine causalitate meritoria naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","CH_GGVC_P_54:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME7","text":"Operatio post beatitudinem a novo merito ad fruitionem et diffusionem perfectionis iam possessae reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0162","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei determinat statum Angelorum circa creationem, gratiam, meritum, gloriam, peccatum et profectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis ordinat naturam, gratiam et gloriam ut principium receptivum, medium elevans et terminum consummatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus dissolvit oppositiones inter gratiam et libertatem, stabilitatem et libertatem, gratuityatem et proportionem, perfectionem superiorem et permanentiam inferioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis praesupponit creaturam finite receptivam, finem causaliter priorem, motum supernaturalem et successionem actuum extra mensuram temporis corporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8","CH_GGVC_P_54:A12","CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam distinctionem naturae, gratiae et gloriae atque consequentias de merito, impeccabilitate et termino beatitudinis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT2","text":"Praemissae de supernaturalitate visionis divinae et de modo cognitionis angelicae ex tractatibus antecedentibus assumuntur neque intra hanc quaestionem integre demonstrantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT3","text":"Structura firmissima est in distinctionibus naturae et finis, viae et termini, gratiae imperfectae et consummatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT4","text":"Creatio Angelorum in gratia manet conclusio probabilior, non demonstratio necessaria; analogia rationum seminalium commissuram principalem praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT5","text":"Proportio naturalium ad gratiam et gloriam nititur congruentia providentiae et absentia impedimenti angelici, non causalitate naturae; ideo eius vis est rationalis, non absoluta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT6","text":"Tensio inter defectibilitatem creaturae et impeccabilitatem beati solvitur per coniunctionem perfectam bono increato, sed ipsa necessitas huius coniunctionis ex doctrina visionis assumitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0142","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT7","text":"Distinctio inter praemium essentiale immobile et gaudium accidentale crescibile impedit contradictionem, sed limes inter utrumque potius affirmatur quam plene derivatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0164","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT8","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: distinctio beatitudinum → necessitas gratiae → meritum et successio → mensura gloriae → conservatio naturae → impeccabilitas → clausura progressus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164008421353Z_bad35660","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 62","source_sha256":"4aa7860f51af9aed416f888149e4801c6cee02dcf8ccf23d1cbd8beb2d58125d","sha256":"807a84899841b47d74e161bbf23b1a19c8cb2fb3988fad642520793e9791f90f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:40:08.422305+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS1","text":"The question determines the order by which angelic nature is led from its initial condition to grace, merit, and glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS2","text":"Natural beatitude, immediately fitting angelic nature, is distinguished from the ultimate beatitude of the divine vision, which exceeds every created faculty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS3","text":"The transition to the ultimate end is brought about not by nature alone, but by grace moving and informing a free meritorious act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS4","text":"The order of consummation is constituted as nature with initial grace, meritorious conversion, and then immediate fruition, in a distinct succession of acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS5","text":"The diversity of natural grades is reasonably ordered to diverse grades of conversion, grace, and glory, while preserving the dependence of all upon the divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS6","text":"Glory preserves nature and natural operations, confirms the will in the good, and closes off essential progress.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AS7","text":"The metaphysical and reconstructive argument proceeds from the distinction of nature and end to the means of grace, thence to merit, consummation, and the properties of the terminal state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A1","text":"Beatitude names the ultimate perfection of rational or intellectual nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","text":"One ultimate perfection is attained by the power of nature; another consists in the vision of the divine essence and exceeds every created intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","text":"Angelic nature does not acquire natural perfection by discursive reasoning, but possesses it immediately according to its proper mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","text":"A created will cannot be borne toward an end above nature except by the motion of a supernatural agent, which is called the aid of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A5","text":"Effects to be produced later under divine providence through the operation of creatures are preordained in the first condition according to seminal principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","text":"Grace is the principle of acting well and meriting glory, not the end of operation or the consummated reward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A7","text":"Grace inclines intellectual nature according to a free mode, not through antecedent necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A8","text":"Perfect beatitude is natural to God alone; for a creature, beatitude is the end of nature, not nature itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A9","text":"An operation effects or acquires an end within the power of the agent, but merits an end above its power as the gift of another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","text":"Merit has the character of a way to an end not yet possessed, whereas fruition has the character of a term already attained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","text":"Grace perfects nature according to the proper mode of the receiving nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A12","text":"Angelic instants are distinguished according to the succession of acts, not according to the time of bodily things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","text":"It is reasonably held that diverse grades of angelic nature are ordered by divine wisdom to diverse grades of grace and glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A14","text":"In an angel, no composition of natures retards intellectual motion; hence nature is moved according to its whole power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A15","text":"The prior principle is preserved in the perfection added to it; therefore nature and its acts are preserved in beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","text":"The vision of the divine essence presents to the will the very essence of goodness and disposes every one of its acts under the order of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A17","text":"The perfection of freedom consists in the choice of diverse things while the order of the end is preserved, not in the possibility of failing from the order of the end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:A18","text":"Because every created vision is finite and does not comprehend God, divine predestination assigns to each creature a determinate grade of vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX1","text":"Angels are not created in ultimate beatitude, although they possess natural perfection from the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX2","text":"Natural love of God as the principle of nature does not suffice for conversion to God as the object of beatific vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX3","text":"The difficulty of an act is not reduced to contrariety or impediment, but also arises from the excess of the end over power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX4","text":"Preparation for grace does not require another habitual grace to infinity, but the operation of God converting the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX5","text":"Initial grace does not exclude the angel's turning away by necessity, because the inclination of grace preserves the free mode of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX6","text":"Merit arises neither from difficulty alone nor from natural conversion, but from an act informed by charity through grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX7","text":"Glory is neither merited after attainment nor acquired by the same act in which fruition is exercised.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX8","text":"Beatitude does not empty natural knowledge and love as superfluous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX9","text":"Rational power is not related to opposites concerning an object to which it is naturally and perfectly ordered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0144","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX10","text":"The possibility of sinning does not constitute the perfection of free choice, but its defectibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX11","text":"The proportion of grades of grace to natural things does not make grace owed to nature or caused by works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX12","text":"The perfect charity of the comprehensor is not the principle of new merit, but the act of fruition of the reward already possessed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:NX13","text":"The essential grade of beatitude does not increase after the predestined term, although accidental joy may increase.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0164","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D1","text":"From the beginning, an angel is blessed according to natural perfection, not according to the vision of the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A1","CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D2","text":"The conversion of the angelic will to ultimate beatitude is necessarily sustained by the aid of grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","text":"It is more probable and more consonant with the sayings of the saints that angels were created with sanctifying grace, because the principle of operation toward glory ought to be given before the terminal effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A5","CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","text":"Angelic beatitude is preceded by a free act informed by charity, which merits through grace an end above nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8","CH_GGVC_P_54:A9","CH_GGVC_P_54:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D5","text":"A single meritorious act suffices, and glory immediately follows it in another instant according to the succession of angelic acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","CH_GGVC_P_54:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","text":"It is reasonable that greater grades of angelic nature correspond to greater intensity of conversion and to more ample grades of grace and glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D7","text":"Natural knowledge and love remain in glory, because natural operations are ordered under the operations of glory and are not opposed to them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D8","text":"A blessed angel cannot sin, because the will seeing goodness itself chooses all things under the order of God, by which freedom is not diminished but perfected.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","CH_GGVC_P_54:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","text":"Having attained the predestined grade of beatitude, an angel neither progresses essentially nor merits further.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:D10","text":"The ministries of the blessed are the diffusion of perfection already possessed and part of the reward, not a way to new merit; from them, however, accidental joy can increase.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A15","CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0162","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0164","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD1","text":"Nature, grace, and glory constitute a non-competitive order of elevation: nature is received, grace makes supernatural operation possible, and glory consummates both.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D1","CH_GGVC_P_54:D2","CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","CH_GGVC_P_54:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD2","text":"The angelic transition is irreversible: initial defectibility admits free conversion, merit terminates in vision, and vision confirms the will in the good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD3","text":"The state of wayfarerhood in an angel is real but minimal, because the succession of merit and fruition is required without discursive reasoning or delay of bodily time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD4","text":"The hierarchy of glory remains at once gratuitous and congruous to nature, because neither does nature effect grace nor does the divine will abandon the natural order it has instituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","CH_GGVC_P_54:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD5","text":"The attainment of the end changes the character of operation: an act before the term merits, while an act after the term enjoys and diffuses possessed perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0162","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SD6","text":"Natural capacity determines the receptive mode and intensity of conversion, but produces neither the beatific object nor its possession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D2","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX1","text":"Created nature cannot of itself generate an order toward a supernatural end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX2","text":"The perfection of creation does not imply the immediate possession of every end to which a creature is ordered through operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX3","text":"Grace and freedom are not mutually exclusive principles, because elevation is received according to the free mode of the recipient.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A7","CH_GGVC_P_54:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX4","text":"An inferior natural operation does not become false or useless through the advent of more perfect knowledge and love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0129","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX5","text":"The defectibility of created good considered in itself is not invincible, because perfect union with uncreated good communicates indefectibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX6","text":"The alternative of evil is not constitutive of rationality or freedom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX7","text":"The gratuitous does not mean disordered or without congruence with the capacity of the recipient.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX8","text":"The ultimate end cannot remain an indefinitely movable term without destroying the character of an end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX9","text":"Bodily duration is not a necessary measure of angelic intellectual change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX1","text":"The system excludes every creature self-sufficient for beatification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX2","text":"Comprehension of God and the highest mode of vision are precluded to the creature, even when it truly sees the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX3","text":"At the beatific term, no essential future remains that would recall the same comprehensor to a higher state of wayfarerhood.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A10","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX4","text":"The supernatural order is not admitted as a substitution for nature, but only as its elevation, preservation, and consummation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A11","CH_GGVC_P_54:A15","CH_GGVC_P_54:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS1","text":"The fundamental distinction operates thus: natural perfection given immediately ≠ elevating grace ≠ terminal glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A3","CH_GGVC_P_54:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS2","text":"End above nature → motion of grace → free conversion of charity → merit of the end to be bestowed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A7","CH_GGVC_P_54:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS3","text":"Initial grace probably created together with nature → first meritorious act → distinct instant of act → immediate fruition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS4","text":"Order of divine wisdom → diverse natural grades → diverse intensities of conversion → proportionate grades of grace and glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:A14","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS5","text":"Vision of goodness through essence → invariable ordering of the will to God → free choice within the end → impossibility of sin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","CH_GGVC_P_54:A17","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS6","text":"Predestined grade attained → closure of essential merit → fruition and diffusion of perfection → accidental increase without essential progress.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A18","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0162","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0164","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AF1","text":"Ambiguity of initial beatitude → distinction of natural perfection and divine vision → necessity of grace → probability of connatural grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D1","CH_GGVC_P_54:D2","CH_GGVC_P_54:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AF2","text":"Antecedent grace → meritorious act of charity → immediately subsequent fruition → distribution of grades according to the order of nature and providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:AF3","text":"Glory preserving nature → will confirmed in the good → sin impossible → term incapable of essential progress.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D7","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME1","text":"Beatitude is reclassified from a univocal notion into a twofold perfection, natural and supernatural.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A1","CH_GGVC_P_54:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME2","text":"Difficulty is separated from psychological impediment and is also described as the objective excess of the end over power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME3","text":"Grace is situated not as a substitute for nature, but as the principle of a motion that nature alone cannot produce.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME4","text":"Freedom is transferred from the power of choosing evil to the power of acting in many ways under the order of the end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A17","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME5","text":"Angelic time is described not through bodily duration, but through the succession of acts of merit and fruition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A12","CH_GGVC_P_54:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME6","text":"Natural hierarchy and the hierarchy of glory are no longer regarded as extrinsic orders, but as orders coordinated by providence without the meritorious causality of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","CH_GGVC_P_54:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ME7","text":"Operation after beatitude is reclassified from new merit to fruition and the diffusion of perfection already possessed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0162","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT1","text":"The surface level determines the state of angels concerning creation, grace, merit, glory, sin, and progress.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT2","text":"The structural level orders nature, grace, and glory as receptive principle, elevating means, and consummated term.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level dissolves oppositions between grace and freedom, stability and freedom, gratuity and proportion, superior perfection and the permanence of the inferior.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level presupposes a finitely receptive creature, a causally prior end, supernatural motion, and a succession of acts outside the measure of bodily time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8","CH_GGVC_P_54:A12","CH_GGVC_P_54:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the distinction of nature, grace, and glory, together with the consequences concerning merit, impeccability, and the term of beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT2","text":"The premises concerning the supernatural character of the divine vision and the mode of angelic knowledge are assumed from preceding treatises and are not fully demonstrated within this question.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT3","text":"The firmest structure lies in the distinctions of nature and end, way and term, imperfect and consummated grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT4","text":"The creation of angels in grace remains a more probable conclusion, not a necessary demonstration; the analogy of seminal principles supplies the principal joint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT5","text":"The proportion of natural things to grace and glory rests on the congruence of providence and the absence of angelic impediment, not on the causality of nature; therefore its force is rational, not absolute.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT6","text":"The tension between the defectibility of the creature and the impeccability of the blessed is resolved through perfect union with uncreated good, but the necessity of this union itself is assumed from the doctrine of vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0142","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT7","text":"The distinction between the immovable essential reward and increaseable accidental joy prevents contradiction, but the boundary between the two is asserted rather than fully derived.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0164","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: distinction of beatitudes → necessity of grace → merit and succession → measure of glory → preservation of nature → impeccability → closure of progress.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_54:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_54@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_54:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 63","title":"First Part · Question 62","context":"Chapter 63","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 62"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 62","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 63","order":64,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_55"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_55@R001","sha256":"03301f20cd3c204b573b6d2e92316e09c34a0f464965727ce69b241187fbe360","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quomodo malum culpae in natura angelica bona, intellectuali et incorporea oriri possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS2","text":"Malitia angelica non est proprietas naturae, sed defectus liberi actus quo bonum proprium extra ordinem voluntatis divinae eligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS3","text":"Possibilitas culpae fundatur in distinctione inter voluntatem divinam, quae est regula sui actus, et voluntatem creatam, quae recta est tantum secundum regulam superiorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS4","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, reconstructiva et diagnostica: ex natura peccati deducit possibilitatem, speciem, obiectum, tempus et propagationem lapsus angelici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS5","text":"Motus procedit a possibilitate defectus ad formam superbiae, ab hac ad appetitum beatitudinis propria virtute, deinde ad successionem operationum et consensum socialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS6","text":"Clausura systematis statuit peccatum contra inclinationem naturalem esse, ideoque libertatem angelicam permittere lapsum sine eo quod natura mala aut lapsus maioritaria fiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0144","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","text":"Peccatum est declinatio actus a rectitudine quam habere debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A2","text":"Actus indefectibilis est tantum ubi virtus agentis ipsa est regula actus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","text":"Divina voluntas sola est regula sui actus; omnis voluntas creata rectitudinem accipit ex ordinatione ad voluntatem divinam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","text":"Omnis creatura rationalis secundum solam naturam peccare potest; impeccabilitas, si adest, ex dono gratiae est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A5","text":"Angelus, quamvis potentiam ad esse naturale non habeat, potentiam intellectivam habet qua per liberum arbitrium in diversa converti potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","text":"Appetitus semper fertur in bonum, sed electio boni fit culpabilis quando mensura vel regula debita non servatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A7","text":"Primum peccatum angelicum nec ex passione nec ex habitu peccaminoso praevio nec ex ignorantia rei intrinsece malae procedere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A8","text":"Natura spiritualis secundum affectum ferri potest tantum in bona spiritualia sibi convenientia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","text":"Superbia est recusatio subiectionis debitae regulae superiori, cuius motivum est excellentia propria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A10","text":"Invidia est renisus bono alterius quatenus illud aestimatur impedire excellentiam singularem appetitam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","text":"Omnis natura, quia a principio bono procedit, naturaliter tendit in bonum; natura intellectualis ordinatur ad bonum universale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A12","text":"Similitudo Dei recte appetitur per participationem et auxilium divinum, perverse autem cum beatitudo vel operatio divina propria virtute vindicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A13","text":"Operatio quae simul cum esse rei incipit ab agente producente causatur; Deus autem causa peccati esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","text":"Angeli in gratia creati uno actu meritorio ad beatitudinem ordinantur, quia quidquid est in merito a Deo est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","text":"Operationes intellectus et voluntatis angelicae instantaneae sunt, earumque successio non tempore continuo sed ordine operationum mensuratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A16","text":"Liberum arbitrium angelicum post electionem inflexibile manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A17","text":"Pronitas ad peccatum et motivum peccandi diversis rationibus aestimantur: maior inclinatio ad bonum pronitatem minuit, maior excellentia motivum superbiae auget.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A18","text":"Suggestio angelica non cogit; qui tamen ei in culpa consentit, ordine iustitiae potestati suggerentis in poena subditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A19","text":"Eventus contra inclinationem naturalem fiunt ut in paucioribus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX1","text":"Subsistentia formalis Angeli non excludit potentiam intellectivam ad actus oppositos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX2","text":"Incorruptibilitas corporum caelestium non probat impeccabilitatem angelicam, quia illa sola actione naturali, Angeli etiam libero arbitrio operantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX3","text":"Naturalis dilectio Dei ut principii essendi non est conversio necessaria ad Deum ut obiectum beatitudinis supernaturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX4","text":"Culpa non requirit electionem rei intrinsece malae neque errorem circa bonitatem rei electae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX5","text":"Peccata carnalia Daemonibus secundum affectum proprium non conveniunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX6","text":"Avaritia proprie temporalis, ira passionalis et acedia ex labore corporali in Daemonibus proprie non sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX7","text":"Appetitus similitudinis divinae non est appetitus aequalitatis naturae cum Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX8","text":"Nulla substantia intellectualis naturalem inclinationem ad malum habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX9","text":"Diabolus nec natura malus nec in primo instanti creationis culpabiliter malus fuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX10","text":"Distinctio instantium angelicorum moram temporis continui non requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX11","text":"Superior inclinatio ad Deum libertatem vel possibilitatem defectus non tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0144","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX12","text":"Peccatum primi Angeli alios nec coegit nec prioritate temporali continua praecessit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX13","text":"Frequentia mali inter homines ad naturam pure intellectualem Angelorum transferri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0174","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D1","text":"Angelus peccare potest quia voluntas eius regulam rectitudinis extra se habet et inter conversiones oppositas libere determinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D2","text":"Peccatum angelicum consistit in electione boni proprii absque ordine ad voluntatem divinam, non in appetitu mali ut mali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A7","CH_GGVC_P_55:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D3","text":"Primum peccatum Angeli necessario est superbia, quia primus defectus spiritualis est recusatio subiectionis debitae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A8","CH_GGVC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D4","text":"Daemonibus omnia peccata secundum reatum imputari possunt quia homines ad ea inducunt, sed secundum affectum proprie conveniunt sola peccata spiritualia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A8","CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D5","text":"Invidia consequitur superbiam quia excellentia singularis appetita bonum alterius tamquam impedimentum suum constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D6","text":"Appetere esse ut Deus significat appetere beatitudinem finalem propria virtute et ex hoc principatum super alia, non mutationem in naturam divinam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D7","text":"Daemones propria voluntate mali fiunt, quia ordinatio naturalis intellectus ad bonum universale naturalem malitiam excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D8","text":"Omnes Angeli in primo instanti boni fuerunt et mereri potuerunt, sed in eodem instanti culpabiliter deficere non potuerunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A13","CH_GGVC_P_55:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D9","text":"Praemissis creatione in gratia et actu meritorio primo, lapsus statim in operatione secunda poni debet, ne meritum statim beatitudine confirmetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D10","text":"Probabilius est supremum Angelum cecidisse, quia excellentia maius motivum superbiae praebet, quamvis opinio de principe ordinis inferioris non excludatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0138","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D11","text":"Primus Angelus alios in eodem instanti inducere potuit, quia expressio intelligibilis, perceptio et consensus discursum temporalem non requirunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D12","text":"Subiectio Daemonum primo peccatori in poena manifestat consensum eorum suggestioni eius in culpa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D13","text":"Plures Angeli permanserunt quam ceciderunt, quia peccatum contra inclinationem naturalem est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D14","text":"Distributio lapsus per ordines manet dependens ab incerta dignitate primi peccatoris: aut lapsus ad ordinem inferiorem restringitur, aut probabiliter singulos ordines attingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A17","CH_GGVC_P_55:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0178","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD1","text":"Malum angelicum nullam naturam positivam constituit, sed bonum naturale et bonum electum praesupponit quorum relatio ad regulam superiorem deficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD2","text":"Perfectio cognitionis non sufficit ad rectitudinem voluntatis, quia verum bonum cognitum potest sine ordine debito eligi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A7","CH_GGVC_P_55:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD3","text":"Gratia duplicem locum obtinet: actum meritorium efficit possibilem, sed sola gratia confirmans impeccabilitatem creaturae stabilit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","CH_GGVC_P_55:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0103","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD4","text":"Tempus lapsus angelici est ordo discretus conversionum intellectualium, non duratio physica inter creationem et culpam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:D8","CH_GGVC_P_55:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD5","text":"Excellentia angelica est moraliter ambivalens: minuit pronitatem naturalem ad defectum, sed auget materiam superbiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A17","CH_GGVC_P_55:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0136","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD6","text":"Malum angelicum propagatur socialiter per consensum non coactum et postea in dominium poenale hierarchicum convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A18","CH_GGVC_P_55:D11","CH_GGVC_P_55:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD7","text":"Libertas angelica per omnes gradus naturae possibilitatem lapsus servat, sed inclinatio ad bonum efficit ut actualis defectus minoritarius sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0144","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX1","text":"Systema falsum esse requirit quod cognitio veri boni voluntatem necessario rectam efficiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit sufficientiam naturae creatae ad beatitudinem supernaturalem finalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12","CH_GGVC_P_55:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit naturam malam ut principium substantiale vel intellectuale peccati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX4","text":"Systema negat omnem causalitatem inter actus simultaneos prioritatem temporis continui postulare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX5","text":"Systema negat libertatem deliberationem discursivam, passionem vel reversibilitatem post electionem necessario exigere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A7","CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX6","text":"Systema excludit necessitatem moralem ex gradu ontologico: superior natura maiorem bonitatem habet sine impeccabilitate naturali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0144","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX7","text":"Systema negat causalitatem universalem Dei defectum moralem creaturae causare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","CH_GGVC_P_55:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX8","text":"Systema excludit regulam statisticam humanam qua malum simpliciter ut in pluribus ponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0174","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX1","text":"Creatura intellectualis se ipsam ut principium ultimum sui finis constituere non potest; autonomia absoluta quam appetit structuram suae dependentiae destrueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12","CH_GGVC_P_55:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX2","text":"Malum purum, quod nullo bono naturali, obiectivo vel operativo nitatur, intra systema impossibile est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX3","text":"Nulla appropriatio moraliter neutra beatitudinis supernaturalis extra ordinem gratiae datur: modus adipiscendi ipsum obiectum rectum deformat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX4","text":"Praemissis actu primo meritorio et confirmatione post electionem, spatium temporale indifferens inter bonitatem initialem et decisionem ultimam praecluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX5","text":"Conversio post lapsum angelicum ex horizonte systematis removetur, quia electio spiritualis totalem virtutem agentis immobiliter determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS1","text":"Machina fundamentalis sic procedit: voluntas creata → regula divina exterior → possibilitas defectus ordinis → culpa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","CH_GGVC_P_55:A2","CH_GGVC_P_55:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS2","text":"Specificatio culpae sic generatur: bonum spirituale electum → mensura superior omissa → non-subiectio → superbia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A8","CH_GGVC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS3","text":"Obiectum lapsus sic constituitur: excellentia naturalis → beatitudo propria virtute appetita → assimilatio divina perversa → principatus → invidia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A10","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS4","text":"Genesis temporalis sic ordinatur: creatio bona in gratia → operatio prima meritoria → operatio secunda aversiva → electio inflexibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A13","CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS5","text":"Propagatio sic efficitur: affectio primi Angeli → expressio intelligibilis → consensus simultaneus aliorum → communio culpae → subiectio poenalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS6","text":"Distributio finalis sic sequitur: inclinatio naturalis ad bonum → peccatum ut eventus contra naturam → lapsus possibilis omnibus ordinibus → lapsus actualis pauciorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0178","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AF1","text":"Possibilitas culpae angelicae → distinctio affectus et reatus → superbia ut primum peccatum → beatitudo propria virtute ut obiectum → exclusio malitiae naturalis → distinctio primi et secundi instantis → quaestio dignitatis primi peccatoris → inductio aliorum → minoritas lapsorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AF2","text":"Analogiae naturales vel humanae propositae → distinctio naturae et liberi arbitrii → distinctio boni obiectivi et ordinis electionis → distinctio temporis continui et successionis intellectualis → restitutio causalitatis non coactivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME1","text":"Culpa ex classe rerum malarum in structuram relationis deficientis inter electionem boni et regulam superiorem transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME2","text":"Malitia daemonica ex natura substantiali in actum voluntarium contra inclinationem naturae reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME3","text":"Taxonomia peccatorum dividitur inter reatum ex inductione et affectum secundum capacitatem naturae spiritualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME4","text":"Similitudo Dei dividitur in participationem ordinatam et appropriationem autonomam beatitudinis vel potestatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME5","text":"Tempus angelicum ex continuo cosmologico in successionem formalem operationum intellectus et affectus redescribitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME6","text":"Excellentia hierarchica desinit esse simplex praesidium contra culpam et fit simul imminutio pronitatis atque augmentum motivi superbiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0136","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME7","text":"Causalitas primi peccatoris fit compatibilis cum simultaneitate, quia per suggestionem intelligibilem et consensum, non per coactionem, operatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME8","text":"Nomina hierarchica a scientia vel potentia sumpta bonis et malis communia manent, sed nomina a caritate vel inhabitatione divina sumpta peccatoribus excluduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0178","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME9","text":"Quaestio numeri lapsorum ex analogia cum multitudine humana ad rationem inclinationis naturalis transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0164","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0174","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei tractat possibilitatem, speciem, obiectum, originem temporalem, principatum, causalitatem et numerum peccatorum angelicorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis peccatum explicat per dependentiam voluntatis creatae a regula divina, electionem boni inordinatam et differentiam inter naturam intellectualem et sensitivam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus analogias corporales et humanas dissolvit atque quaestionem ex obiecto appetitus ad modum ordinationis, ex tempore physico ad successionem actuum et ex coactione ad consensum transfert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis praesupponit bonitatem omnis naturae creatae, malum ut privationem ordinis, causalitatem divinam non defectivam et tempus angelicum operationibus discretis constitutum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT1","text":"Axiomata proposita sufficiunt ad restituendas novem conclusiones principales et ordinem quo una ex altera generatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT2","text":"Firmissimum centrum est nexus inter regulam extrinsecam voluntatis creatae, electionem boni inordinatam et impossibilitatem malitiae naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT3","text":"Dignitas primi Angeli et distributio lapsus per ordines deliberate indeterminatae manent, quia criteria pronitatis et motivi conclusiones diversas sustinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0136","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0138","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0178","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT4","text":"Immediatus lapsus post primum instans dependet ab acceptis praemissis creationis in gratia, actus liberi primi et praemii post unum meritum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT5","text":"Commissura inter gratiam initialem et possibilitatem lapsus distinctionem implicitam postulat inter gratiam merendi et gratiam confirmantem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0103","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT6","text":"Causalitas simultanea primi peccatoris in alios possibilis redditur per locutionem intelligibilem instantaneam, sed prioritas causalis sine prioritate temporali manet locus fragilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0147","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT7","text":"Tensionem inter inclinationem universalem ad bonum et actualem electionem inordinatam systema distinguiendo obiectum bonum a modo electionis continet, non tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT8","text":"Contradictio stricta non emergit, sed cohaerentia pendet a successione discreta actuum, inflexibilitate post electionem et asymmetria causali inter meritum et culpam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT9","text":"Restitutio servat motum verum textus a metaphysica possibilitate defectus ad specificationem superbiae, temporalitatem lapsus, propagationem hierarchicam et proportionem finalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164043048565Z_358cff49","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 63","source_sha256":"03301f20cd3c204b573b6d2e92316e09c34a0f464965727ce69b241187fbe360","sha256":"41abd96beed5801c8c18b103add822db1c3c28f917370098867c41a2142d45df","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:40:43.050675+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS1","text":"The text asks how the evil of fault can arise in the good, intellectual, and incorporeal nature of angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS2","text":"Angelic malice is not a property of nature, but a defect of a free act by which one's own good is chosen outside the order of the divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS3","text":"The possibility of fault is grounded in the distinction between the divine will, which is the rule of its own act, and the created will, which is right only according to a higher rule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS4","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, reconstructive, and diagnostic: from the nature of sin it deduces the possibility, species, object, time, and propagation of the angelic fall.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS5","text":"The movement proceeds from the possibility of defect to the form of pride, from this to the appetite for beatitude by one's own power, then to the succession of operations and social consent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AS6","text":"The closure of the system establishes that sin is contrary to natural inclination, and therefore that angelic freedom permits a fall without nature being evil or the fall becoming predominant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0144","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","text":"Sin is a deviation of an act from the rectitude it ought to possess.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A2","text":"An indefectible act exists only where the power of the agent itself is the rule of the act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","text":"The divine will alone is the rule of its own act; every created will receives rectitude from its ordering to the divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","text":"Every rational creature can sin according to nature alone; impeccability, if present, is from the gift of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A5","text":"Although an angel does not have potency with respect to natural being, it has intellectual potency by which it can be turned toward diverse things through free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","text":"Appetite is always borne toward the good, but the choice of a good becomes culpable when the due measure or rule is not preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A7","text":"The first angelic sin cannot proceed either from passion, from a prior sinful habit, or from ignorance of something intrinsically evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A8","text":"A spiritual nature can be borne by affection only toward spiritual goods suitable to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","text":"Pride is the refusal of subjection to a due higher rule, the motive of which is one's own excellence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A10","text":"Envy is resistance to another's good insofar as it is judged to impede the singular excellence that is sought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","text":"Every nature, because it proceeds from a good principle, naturally tends toward the good; intellectual nature is ordered to the universal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A12","text":"Likeness to God is rightly sought through participation and divine help, but perversely when beatitude or divine operation is claimed by one's own power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A13","text":"An operation that begins together with a thing's being is caused by the producing agent; but God cannot be the cause of sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","text":"Angels created in grace are ordered to beatitude by one meritorious act, because whatever is in merit is from God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","text":"The operations of angelic intellect and will are instantaneous, and their succession is measured not by continuous time but by the order of operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A16","text":"Angelic free choice remains inflexible after choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A17","text":"Proneness to sin and the motive for sinning are assessed on different grounds: a greater inclination to good diminishes proneness, while greater excellence increases the motive for pride.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A18","text":"Angelic suggestion does not compel; yet one who consents to it in fault is, by the order of justice, subjected in punishment to the power of the suggester.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:A19","text":"Events contrary to natural inclination occur in the minority of cases.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX1","text":"The angel's formal subsistence does not exclude intellectual potency for opposite acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX2","text":"The incorruptibility of heavenly bodies does not prove angelic impeccability, because the former operate only by natural action, whereas angels also operate by free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX3","text":"Natural love of God as the principle of being is not a necessary turning toward God as the object of supernatural beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX4","text":"Fault does not require the choice of something intrinsically evil, nor error concerning the goodness of the thing chosen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX5","text":"Carnal sins are not suitable to demons according to their proper affection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX6","text":"Strictly temporal avarice, passionate anger, and acedia arising from bodily labor are not properly in demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX7","text":"The appetite for divine likeness is not an appetite for equality of nature with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX8","text":"No intellectual substance has a natural inclination toward evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX9","text":"The Devil was neither evil by nature nor culpably evil in the first instant of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX10","text":"The distinction of angelic instants does not require an interval of continuous time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX11","text":"A higher inclination toward God does not remove freedom or the possibility of defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0144","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX12","text":"The sin of the first angel neither compelled the others nor preceded them by continuous temporal priority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:NX13","text":"The frequency of evil among human beings cannot be transferred to the purely intellectual nature of angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0174","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D1","text":"An angel can sin because its will has the rule of rectitude outside itself and is freely determined between opposite turnings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D2","text":"Angelic sin consists in choosing one's own good without order to the divine will, not in desiring evil as evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A7","CH_GGVC_P_55:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D3","text":"The first sin of an angel is necessarily pride, because the first spiritual defect is refusal of due subjection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A8","CH_GGVC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D4","text":"All sins can be imputed to demons according to guilt because they induce human beings to them, but according to affection only spiritual sins are properly suitable to them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A8","CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D5","text":"Envy follows pride because the singular excellence sought makes another's good into its own impediment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D6","text":"To desire to be as God means to desire final beatitude by one's own power and, from this, dominion over other things, not transformation into the divine nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D7","text":"Demons become evil by their own will, because the natural ordering of intellect to the universal good excludes natural malice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D8","text":"All angels were good in the first instant and could merit, but they could not culpably defect in that same instant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A13","CH_GGVC_P_55:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D9","text":"Given creation in grace and a first meritorious act, the fall must be placed immediately in the second operation, lest merit be immediately confirmed by beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D10","text":"It is more probable that the highest angel fell, because excellence supplies a greater motive for pride, although the opinion concerning a prince of a lower order is not excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0138","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D11","text":"The first angel could induce others in the same instant, because intelligible expression, perception, and consent do not require temporal discursiveness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D12","text":"The subjection of demons to the first sinner in punishment manifests their consent to his suggestion in fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D13","text":"More angels remained than fell, because sin is contrary to natural inclination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:D14","text":"The distribution of the fall through the orders remains dependent on the uncertain rank of the first sinner: either the fall is restricted to a lower order, or it probably reaches every order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A17","CH_GGVC_P_55:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0178","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD1","text":"Angelic evil constitutes no positive nature, but presupposes natural good and chosen good whose relation to the higher rule is defective.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD2","text":"Perfection of knowledge does not suffice for rectitude of will, because a true known good can be chosen without due order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A7","CH_GGVC_P_55:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD3","text":"Grace occupies a twofold place: it makes a meritorious act possible, but only confirming grace establishes the creature's impeccability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","CH_GGVC_P_55:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0103","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD4","text":"The time of the angelic fall is a discrete order of intellectual turnings, not a physical duration between creation and fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:D8","CH_GGVC_P_55:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD5","text":"Angelic excellence is morally ambivalent: it diminishes natural proneness to defect, but increases the matter of pride.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A17","CH_GGVC_P_55:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0136","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD6","text":"Angelic evil is propagated socially through uncoerced consent and is later converted into hierarchical penal dominion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A18","CH_GGVC_P_55:D11","CH_GGVC_P_55:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SD7","text":"Angelic freedom preserves the possibility of falling through all grades of nature, but inclination to good makes actual defect a minority occurrence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0144","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX1","text":"The system requires it to be false that knowledge of the true good necessarily renders the will right.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the sufficiency of created nature for final supernatural beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12","CH_GGVC_P_55:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX3","text":"The system excludes an evil nature as the substantial or intellectual principle of sin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX4","text":"The system denies that all causality between simultaneous acts requires priority in continuous time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX5","text":"The system denies that freedom necessarily requires discursive deliberation, passion, or reversibility after choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A7","CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX6","text":"The system excludes moral necessity from ontological grade: a higher nature has greater goodness without natural impeccability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A4","CH_GGVC_P_55:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0144","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX7","text":"The system denies that God's universal causality causes the creature's moral defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","CH_GGVC_P_55:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:DNX8","text":"The system excludes a human statistical rule by which evil is posited simply as occurring in the majority of cases.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0174","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX1","text":"An intellectual creature cannot constitute itself as the ultimate principle of its own end; the absolute autonomy it seeks would destroy the structure of its dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A3","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12","CH_GGVC_P_55:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX2","text":"Pure evil, which rests on no natural, objective, or operative good, is impossible within the system.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX3","text":"No morally neutral appropriation of supernatural beatitude outside the order of grace is given: the manner of attaining the very right object deforms it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX4","text":"Given a first meritorious act and confirmation after choice, an indifferent temporal interval between initial goodness and ultimate decision is precluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:SNX5","text":"Conversion after the angelic fall is removed from the horizon of the system, because spiritual choice immovably determines the agent's total power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS1","text":"The fundamental mechanism proceeds thus: created will → external divine rule → possibility of defect of order → fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A1","CH_GGVC_P_55:A2","CH_GGVC_P_55:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS2","text":"The specification of fault is generated thus: chosen spiritual good → higher measure omitted → non-subjection → pride.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A6","CH_GGVC_P_55:A8","CH_GGVC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS3","text":"The object of the fall is constituted thus: natural excellence → beatitude sought by one's own power → perverse divine assimilation → dominion → envy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A9","CH_GGVC_P_55:A10","CH_GGVC_P_55:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS4","text":"The temporal genesis is ordered thus: good creation in grace → first meritorious operation → second aversive operation → inflexible choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A13","CH_GGVC_P_55:A14","CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS5","text":"Propagation is effected thus: affection of the first angel → intelligible expression → simultaneous consent of others → communion in fault → penal subjection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A15","CH_GGVC_P_55:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:FGS6","text":"The final distribution follows thus: natural inclination to good → sin as an event contrary to nature → fall possible to all orders → actual fall of the minority.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_55:A11","CH_GGVC_P_55:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0178","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AF1","text":"Possibility of angelic fault → distinction of affection and guilt → pride as the first sin → beatitude by one's own power as object → exclusion of natural malice → distinction of the first and second instant → question of the rank of the first sinner → induction of others → minority of the fallen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:AF2","text":"Proposed natural or human analogies → distinction of nature and free choice → distinction of objective good and order of choice → distinction of continuous time and intellectual succession → restoration of non-coercive causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME1","text":"Fault is transferred from the class of evil things into the structure of a defective relation between the choice of a good and the higher rule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME2","text":"Demonic malice is reclassified from substantial nature into a voluntary act contrary to the inclination of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME3","text":"The taxonomy of sins is divided between guilt from induction and affection according to the capacity of spiritual nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME4","text":"Likeness to God is divided into ordered participation and autonomous appropriation of beatitude or power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME5","text":"Angelic time is redescribed from cosmological continuity into the formal succession of operations of intellect and affection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME6","text":"Hierarchical excellence ceases to be a simple safeguard against fault and becomes at once a diminution of proneness and an increase of the motive for pride.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0136","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME7","text":"The causality of the first sinner becomes compatible with simultaneity, because it operates through intelligible suggestion and consent, not through coercion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME8","text":"Hierarchical names taken from knowledge or power remain common to the good and the evil, but names taken from charity or divine indwelling are excluded from sinners.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0178","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ME9","text":"The question of the number of the fallen is transferred from analogy with human multitude to the rationale of natural inclination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0164","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0174","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ALT1","text":"The surface level treats the possibility, species, object, temporal origin, primacy, causality, and number of angelic sins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ALT2","text":"The structural level explains sin through the dependence of created will on the divine rule, the disordered choice of a good, and the difference between intellectual and sensitive nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level dissolves bodily and human analogies and transfers the question from the object of appetite to the mode of ordering, from physical time to succession of acts, and from coercion to consent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level presupposes the goodness of every created nature, evil as a privation of order, non-defective divine causality, and angelic time constituted by discrete operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT1","text":"The proposed axioms suffice to reconstruct the nine principal conclusions and the order in which one is generated from another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT2","text":"The firmest center is the nexus between the extrinsic rule of created will, the disordered choice of a good, and the impossibility of natural malice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT3","text":"The rank of the first angel and the distribution of the fall through the orders remain deliberately indeterminate, because the criteria of proneness and motive support diverse conclusions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0136","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0138","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0178","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT4","text":"The immediate fall after the first instant depends on the accepted premises of creation in grace, the first free act, and reward after one merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT5","text":"The juncture between initial grace and the possibility of falling requires an implicit distinction between the grace of meriting and confirming grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0103","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT6","text":"The simultaneous causality of the first sinner upon others is made possible through instantaneous intelligible speech, but causal priority without temporal priority remains a fragile point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0147","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0157","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT7","text":"The system contains, rather than removes, the tension between universal inclination to good and actual disordered choice by distinguishing the good object from the mode of choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT8","text":"No strict contradiction emerges, but coherence depends on the discrete succession of acts, inflexibility after choice, and causal asymmetry between merit and fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_55:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text from the metaphysical possibility of defect to the specification of pride, the temporality of the fall, hierarchical propagation, and final proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_55:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_55@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_55:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 64","title":"First Part · Question 63","context":"Chapter 64","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 63"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 63","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 64","order":65,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_56"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_56@R001","sha256":"9e19634e8471b022106b4a0feaf14ec9d53fb61bfaf4c2ee223ec8eb54f5d0dd","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS1","text":"Quaestio poenam Daemonum explicat secundum quattuor effectus conexos: defectum cognitionis, immobilitatem voluntatis, dolorem et locum poenalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS2","text":"Poena daemonica naturam intellectualem non destruit, sed gratiam et ordinationem voluntatis privat, ita ut cognitionis integritas naturalis cum miseria morali simul maneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS3","text":"Fundamentum argumentationis est distinctio inter id quod naturae angelicae inseparabiliter competit et id quod per gratiam, caritatem vel visionem beatificam superadditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS4","text":"Immobilitas cognitionis angelicae post electionem causam praebet cur voluntas daemonica non mutetur, quamvis liberum arbitrium naturaliter maneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS5","text":"Dolor et locus poenalis reconfigurantur ut actus voluntatis et apprehensiones ordini voluntatis contrariae, non ut passiones corporales aut alterationes naturae spiritualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS6","text":"Argumentatio procedit a distinctione naturae et gratiae ad fixationem electionis, ab hac ad dolorem voluntarium, atque inde ad ordinem providentialem et eschatologicum locorum daemonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","text":"Simplicitas substantiae angelicae impedit ne dona naturalia per poenam subtrahantur; cognitio naturalis daemonum igitur integra manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A2","text":"Cognitio per gratiam distinguitur in cognitionem speculativam secretorum divinorum et cognitionem affectivam producentem amorem Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","text":"Daemonibus cognitio speculativa per gratiam non omnino tollitur, sed secundum necessitatem diminuitur; cognitio affectiva et caritas omnino absent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A4","text":"Substantia divina proportionem etiam intellectus angelici naturalis excedit, quamvis daemon naturaliter Deum imperfecte cognoscere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","text":"Intellectus angelicus immobiliter apprehendit, intellectus autem humanus discursu mobili procedit; appetitus modum apprehensionis sequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","text":"Angelus ante electionem ad opposita eligenda flexibilis est, sed post adhaesionem voluntas eius immobiliter ei quod elegit adhaeret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A7","text":"Stabilitas sempiterna ad rationem verae beatitudinis pertinet; propterea boni Angeli in bono confirmantur et Daemones in malo obstinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","text":"Actus daemonis ex voluntate deliberata procedens semper malus est, quamvis actus eius naturalis bonus esse possit et ad malum abuti possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A9","text":"Dolor, prout in natura incorporea reperitur, est renisus simplicis voluntatis ad id quod est vel non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A10","text":"Daemones dolore afficiuntur quia multa volunt non esse quae sunt, multa esse quae non sunt, beatitudine naturali privantur et voluntas eorum in multis cohibetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A11","text":"Dolor de culpa propter ipsam culpam bonitatem voluntatis ostendit; Daemon de culpa sua ut culpa non dolet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A12","text":"Locus Angelum aut animam non poenalit per alterationem naturae, sed per apprehensionem loci voluntati non convenientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A13","text":"Providentia bonum humanum directe per Angelos bonos et indirecte per impugnationem daemonum procurat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","text":"Infernum daemonibus ratione culpae debetur, aer caliginosus ratione exercitationis humanae usque ad diem iudicii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A15","text":"Post diem iudicii omnes mali, homines et Angeli, in Inferno erunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A16","text":"Daemones veritatem cognoscunt per subtilitatem naturae, revelationem ab Angelis sanctis et experientiam temporis in singularibus rebus completam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX1","text":"Obtenebratio daemonica non est privatio omnis veritatis, sed privatio luminis gratiae cum retentione luminis intellectualis naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX2","text":"Cognitio substantiarum separatarum non est beatitudo Angeli, quia ei connaturalis est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX3","text":"Cognitio naturalis Dei non est visio divinae substantiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX4","text":"Cognitio creaturae in propria natura daemonis non est cognitio vespertina, quia ad laudem Creatoris non refertur; cognitio eius nocturna dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX5","text":"Positio Origenis, qua omnis voluntas creata semper ad bonum et malum flectibilis ponitur, reicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX6","text":"Libertatis arbitrium daemonum non est potestas post electionem ad bonum redire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX7","text":"Veritatis confessio, si rerum evidentia extorquetur aut deceptioni servit, non est actus moraliter bonus daemonis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX8","text":"Gaudium, timor et dolor in Daemonibus non sunt passiones appetitus sensitivi neque affectiones organi corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX9","text":"Dolor daemonis non est paenitentia de malo culpae propter culpam ipsam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX10","text":"Aer caliginosus non excludit Infernum ut locum poenae daemonicae, quia loca diversa diversis rationibus poenalibus respondent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX11","text":"Poena sensibilis daemonum non differtur universaliter usque ad diem iudicii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D1","text":"Obtenebratio est poena graduata: natura cognoscitiva manet, revelatio speculativa restringitur, amor Dei penitus deficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A2","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D2","text":"Daemon potest verum de Deo cognoscere sine cognitione essentiae divinae et sine visione beatifica.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D3","text":"Cognitio daemonica rerum creatarum, quia caritate et relatione laudativa caret, veritatem retinet sine lumine sapientiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D4","text":"Obstinatio daemonica ex modo naturae et status electionis explicatur, non ex sola quantitate aut gravitate culpae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D5","text":"Misericordia liberat poenitentem, sed daemon immobiliter malo adhaerens capacitatem poenitentiae non habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D6","text":"Bonum materiale in actu daemonis apparere potest, sed bonitas moralis deficit si finis voluntatis perversus est aut actus coactus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D7","text":"Gaudium et dolor, atque dolor et timor, in Daemonibus simul esse possunt, quia ad obiecta diversa vel ad rationes diversas eiusdem rei referuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A9","CH_GGVC_P_56:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D8","text":"Dolor daemonis bonitatem naturae residualem testatur, non bonitatem voluntatis perversae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A10","CH_GGVC_P_56:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D9","text":"Daemon in aere caliginoso poenae gehennae non liberatur, quia debitam alligationem apprehendit etiam cum igne non actu alligatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A12","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D10","text":"Usus providentialis impugnationis daemonicae conservat munus indirectum ordinis naturalis sine conversione voluntatis daemonicae in bonum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD1","text":"Poena daemonica est ordinatio selectiva, non annihilatio: potentia naturalis manet, ordinatio affectiva ad Deum deficit, et electio perversa immobiliter perseverat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD2","text":"Irreversibilitas moralis daemonum nascitur ex ontologia cognitionis angelicae: apprehensio immobilis producit habitum voluntatis non discursivum sed definitivum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD3","text":"Providentia malitiam daemonum non approbat, sed eam intra ordinem indirectae exercitationis humanae includit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD4","text":"Locus poenalis spiritualium est relatio iuridico-voluntaria ad ordinem debitum, non circumscriptio physica naturam spiritualem transmutans.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A12","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","CH_GGVC_P_56:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD5","text":"Veritas cognita, veritas confessa et participatio salvifica veritatis separantur: prima manere potest ubi secunda perversa est et tertia omnino deficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet malitiam voluntatis ipsam naturam daemonis corruptam aut annihilatam facere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet libertatem intellectualem idem esse ac mutabilitatem temporaliter indefinitam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet cognitionem veri per se efficere caritatem, sapientiam affectivam aut conversionem moralem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet poenam spiritus reduci ad passionem corpoream, quia renisus voluntatis et apprehensio loci sufficiunt ad rationem doloris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A9","CH_GGVC_P_56:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet utilitatem indirectam daemonum in ordine humano culpam eorum dissolvere aut voluntatem eorum bonam efficere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet praesentem dispersionem daemonum in aere caliginoso statum finalem eorum constituere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","CH_GGVC_P_56:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SNX1","text":"Praecluditur spatium neutrum post ultimam electionem angelicam, in quo eadem voluntas fixa sine mutatione status ad contrarium redire possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SNX2","text":"Praecluditur ascensus ex perfectione naturali intellectus ad visionem Dei aut beatitudinem sine dono gratiae et caritatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SNX3","text":"Praecluditur principium mali naturae et providentiae independens, quia daemon etiam in perversitate bonum naturae retinet et intra ordinem divinum operatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SNX4","text":"Praecluditur perpetuitas ordinis poenalis provisoriae, quia ministerium daemonum temporale ad diem iudicii ordinatur et finali collocatione clauditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","CH_GGVC_P_56:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS1","text":"Simplicitas naturae angelicae → integritas donorum naturalium → imminutio cognitionis non potest significare ignorantiam universalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS2","text":"Distinctio naturae et gratiae → cognitio speculativa restricta + cognitio affectiva ablata → obtenebratio graduata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A2","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS3","text":"Intellectus angelicus immobilis → electio post adhaesionem fixa → voluntas daemonica obstinata → poenitentia impossibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS4","text":"Voluntas perversa + bonum naturale residuum + obiecta voluntati contraria → renisus voluntatis → dolor sine passione corporali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A9","CH_GGVC_P_56:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS5","text":"Providentia ordinis humani → impugnatio daemonica indirecte utilis → aer caliginosus temporalis; culpa daemonica → Infernus debitus → clausura universalis post iudicium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A12","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","CH_GGVC_P_56:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF1","text":"Privatio veritatis apparens → distinctio naturae et gratiae → cognitio naturalis servata, cognitio affectiva perdita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF2","text":"Libertas arbitrii apparens → distinctio electionis ante et post adhaesionem → obstinatio daemonica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF3","text":"Obiectio ex actibus bonis apparentibus → distinctio actus naturalis et actus deliberati → malitia voluntatis perseverans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF4","text":"Incompatibilitas doloris cum natura spirituali → dolor ut renisus voluntatis → miseria sine passione corporali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF5","text":"Inconvenientia loci poenalis spiritui → locus ut contrarietas voluntati et dispositio providentiae → aer temporalis, Infernus finalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME1","text":"Obtenebratio reclassificatur ab ignorantia simpliciter ad defectum hierarchicum luminis gratiae super naturam intellectualem integrum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME2","text":"Libertatis conceptus dividitur in potentiam electionis ante adhaesionem et immutabilitatem voluntatis post adhaesionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME3","text":"Actus veridici daemonum reclassificantur: veritas materialiter dicta non demonstrat rectitudinem voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME4","text":"Dolor reclassificatur a passione sensitiva ad actum voluntatis contra rem praesentem vel absentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME5","text":"Locus poenalis reclassificatur a situ physico exclusivo ad relationem voluntatis, culpae, ministerii temporalis et iudicii finalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus determinat quid Daemones cognoscant, utrum converti possint, quomodo doleant et ubi poenaliter consistant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ALT2","text":"Structural — Quattuor quaestiones reguntur distinctionibus naturae et gratiae, cognitionis et voluntatis, actus naturalis et deliberati, culpae et ministerii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio objectiones universalizantes dissolvit per divisiones modales, ut oppositio cognitionis et tenebrae, libertatis et obstinationis, aut aeris et Inferni falsa appareat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Natura angelica simplex et apprehensio immobilis constituunt temporalitatem decisionis definitivae, cui ministerium daemonicum temporale et iudicium eschatologicum subordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT1","text":"Systema extractum sufficit ad restituendas quattuor conclusiones principales: cognitionem naturalem retentam, voluntatem obstinatam, dolorem voluntarium et locum poenalem dupliciter ordinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT2","text":"Commissura firmissima est nexus inter modum apprehensionis angelicae immobilis et immobilitatem voluntatis post electionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT3","text":"Gradus concretus diminutionis cognitionis speculativae et criterium revelationis daemonibus concessae non plene determinantur, praeter regulam quod tantum revelatur quantum oportet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT4","text":"Tensio inter integritatem cognitionis naturalis et nomen obtenebrationis solvitur per distinctionem gratiae a natura, sed extensio practica utriusque cognitionis non ulterius mensuratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT5","text":"Nexus inter primam adhaesionem angelicam et perpetuam impossibilitatem reversionis affirmatur ex conditione naturae, sed processus internus illius transitionis non independenter evolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT6","text":"Ordinatio providentiae impugnationem daemonum ad bonum humanum refert, dum malitiam daemonum intactam retinet; compatibilitas ponitur per distinctionem directi et indirecti, non per ulteriorem causalitatis expositionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT7","text":"Relatio inter poenam ignis, aerem caliginosum et dolorem voluntatis componitur per apprehensionem alligationis debitae, sed mechanismus sensibilis illius poenae non amplius explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT8","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia a distinctione epistemica ad structuram electionis, inde ad phenomenologiam poenae, et tandem ad dispositionem providentialem atque finalem progreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164113717799Z_acb09f5e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 64","source_sha256":"9e19634e8471b022106b4a0feaf14ec9d53fb61bfaf4c2ee223ec8eb54f5d0dd","sha256":"087d3324cff7b7c4e75d3576006d31c6f84fdeeb584c4426da8306c9869b221e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:41:13.720345+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS1","text":"The question explains the punishment of the Demons according to four connected effects: defect of cognition, immobility of the will, pain, and penal place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS2","text":"Demonic punishment does not destroy intellectual nature, but deprives it of grace and the ordering of the will, so that the integrity of natural cognition remains together with moral misery.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS3","text":"The foundation of the argument is the distinction between what belongs inseparably to angelic nature and what is superadded through grace, charity, or the beatific vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS4","text":"The immobility of angelic cognition after choice provides the reason why the demonic will does not change, although free choice naturally remains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS5","text":"Pain and penal place are reconfigured as acts of the will and apprehensions contrary to the order of the will, not as bodily passions or alterations of spiritual nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AS6","text":"The argument proceeds from the distinction of nature and grace to the fixation of choice, from this to voluntary pain, and thence to the providential and eschatological ordering of the places of the Demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","text":"The simplicity of angelic substance prevents natural gifts from being taken away through punishment; therefore the natural cognition of the Demons remains intact.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A2","text":"Cognition through grace is distinguished into speculative cognition of divine secrets and affective cognition producing love of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","text":"Speculative cognition through grace is not wholly taken away from the Demons, but is diminished according to necessity; affective cognition and charity are wholly absent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A4","text":"The divine substance exceeds the proportion even of natural angelic intellect, although a Demon can naturally know God imperfectly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","text":"Angelic intellect apprehends immovably, whereas human intellect proceeds by mobile discourse; appetite follows the mode of apprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","text":"Before choice, an Angel is flexible for choosing opposites, but after adhesion its will adheres immovably to what it has chosen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A7","text":"Everlasting stability belongs to the notion of true beatitude; therefore good Angels are confirmed in good and Demons are hardened in evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","text":"An act of a Demon proceeding from deliberate will is always evil, although its natural act can be good and can be abused for evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A9","text":"Pain, insofar as it is found in incorporeal nature, is the resistance of simple will to that which is or is not.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A10","text":"Demons are affected by pain because they will many things that are not to be, and many things that are not to be; they are deprived of natural beatitude, and their will is restrained in many respects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A11","text":"Sorrow for guilt on account of guilt itself shows goodness of will; a Demon does not sorrow for its guilt as guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A12","text":"Place punishes an Angel or soul not by alteration of nature, but by the apprehension of a place unsuitable to the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A13","text":"Providence procures human good directly through good Angels and indirectly through the assault of Demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","text":"Hell is due to the Demons by reason of guilt, the darksome air by reason of human exercise until the day of judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A15","text":"After the day of judgment all the wicked, humans and Angels, will be in Hell.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:A16","text":"Demons know truth through subtlety of nature, revelation from holy Angels, and experience of time completed in singular things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX1","text":"Demonic darkening is not privation of all truth, but privation of the light of grace while retaining natural intellectual light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX2","text":"Knowledge of separate substances is not the beatitude of an Angel, because it is connatural to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX3","text":"Natural knowledge of God is not vision of the divine substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX4","text":"A Demon's knowledge of a creature in its own nature is not evening knowledge, because it is not referred to the praise of the Creator; it is called nocturnal knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX5","text":"Origen's position, according to which every created will is held always capable of bending toward good and evil, is rejected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX6","text":"The freedom of choice of Demons is not the power to return to good after choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX7","text":"Confession of truth, if extorted by the evidence of things or serving deception, is not a morally good act of a Demon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX8","text":"Joy, fear, and pain in Demons are not passions of the sensitive appetite or affections of a bodily organ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX9","text":"The pain of a Demon is not repentance for the evil of guilt on account of guilt itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX10","text":"The darksome air does not exclude Hell as a place of demonic punishment, because diverse places correspond to diverse penal reasons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:NX11","text":"The sensible punishment of Demons is not universally deferred until the day of judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D1","text":"Darkening is a graded punishment: cognitive nature remains, speculative revelation is restricted, love of God wholly fails.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A2","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D2","text":"A Demon can know truth about God without knowledge of the divine essence and without the beatific vision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D3","text":"Demonic cognition of created things, because it lacks charity and a laudatory relation, retains truth without the light of wisdom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D4","text":"Demonic obstinacy is explained from the mode of nature and the state of choice, not from the quantity or gravity of guilt alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D5","text":"Mercy frees the penitent, but a Demon adhering immovably to evil has no capacity for repentance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D6","text":"Material good can appear in an act of a Demon, but moral goodness fails if the end of the will is perverse or the act is compelled.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D7","text":"Joy and pain, and pain and fear, can coexist in Demons, because they are referred to different objects or to different aspects of the same thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A9","CH_GGVC_P_56:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D8","text":"The pain of a Demon testifies to residual goodness of nature, not to goodness of the perverse will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A10","CH_GGVC_P_56:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D9","text":"A Demon in the darksome air is not freed from the punishment of Gehenna, because it apprehends the due binding even when it is not actually bound by fire.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A12","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:D10","text":"The providential use of demonic assault preserves an indirect function of natural order without converting demonic will into good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD1","text":"Demonic punishment is selective ordering, not annihilation: natural power remains, affective ordering toward God fails, and perverse choice persists immovably.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD2","text":"The moral irreversibility of Demons arises from the ontology of angelic cognition: immobile apprehension produces a habit of will that is not discursive but definitive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD3","text":"Providence does not approve the malice of Demons, but includes it within the order of indirect human exercise.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD4","text":"The penal place of spiritual beings is a juridical-voluntary relation to due order, not a physical circumscription transforming spiritual nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A12","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","CH_GGVC_P_56:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SD5","text":"Known truth, confessed truth, and salvific participation in truth are separated: the first can remain where the second is perverse and the third wholly fails.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX1","text":"It must be false that the malice of the will itself makes the nature of a Demon corrupted or annihilated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX2","text":"It must be false that intellectual freedom is identical with temporally indefinite mutability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX3","text":"It must be false that knowledge of truth of itself produces charity, affective wisdom, or moral conversion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the punishment of a spirit is reduced to bodily passion, because resistance of the will and apprehension of place suffice for the notion of pain.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A9","CH_GGVC_P_56:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the indirect usefulness of Demons in the human order dissolves their guilt or makes their will good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:DNX6","text":"It must be false that the present dispersion of Demons in the darksome air constitutes their final state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","CH_GGVC_P_56:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SNX1","text":"A neutral space after the final angelic choice is precluded, in which the same fixed will could return to the contrary without a change of state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SNX2","text":"Ascent from the natural perfection of intellect to the vision of God or beatitude without the gift of grace and charity is precluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SNX3","text":"An independent principle of evil nature and providence is precluded, because a Demon even in perversity retains the good of nature and operates within the divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:SNX4","text":"The perpetuity of provisional penal order is precluded, because the temporal ministry of Demons is ordered to the day of judgment and is closed by final placement.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","CH_GGVC_P_56:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS1","text":"Simplicity of angelic nature → integrity of natural gifts → diminution of cognition cannot signify universal ignorance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A1","CH_GGVC_P_56:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS2","text":"Distinction of nature and grace → restricted speculative cognition + removed affective cognition → graded darkening.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A2","CH_GGVC_P_56:A3","CH_GGVC_P_56:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS3","text":"Immobile angelic intellect → choice fixed after adhesion → obstinate demonic will → repentance impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A5","CH_GGVC_P_56:A6","CH_GGVC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS4","text":"Perverse will + residual natural good + objects contrary to the will → resistance of the will → pain without bodily passion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A8","CH_GGVC_P_56:A9","CH_GGVC_P_56:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:FGS5","text":"Providence of human order → indirectly useful demonic assault → temporal darksome air; demonic guilt → due Hell → universal enclosure after judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_56:A12","CH_GGVC_P_56:A13","CH_GGVC_P_56:A14","CH_GGVC_P_56:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF1","text":"Apparent privation of truth → distinction of nature and grace → natural cognition preserved, affective cognition lost.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF2","text":"Apparent freedom of choice → distinction of choice before and after adhesion → demonic obstinacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF3","text":"Objection from apparently good acts → distinction of natural act and deliberate act → persisting malice of will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF4","text":"Incompatibility of pain with spiritual nature → pain as resistance of the will → misery without bodily passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:AF5","text":"Unsuitability of a penal place for a spirit → place as contrariety to the will and disposition of providence → temporal air, final Hell.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME1","text":"Darkening is reclassified from ignorance simply speaking to a hierarchical defect of the light of grace above intact intellectual nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME2","text":"The concept of freedom is divided into the power of choice before adhesion and immutability of the will after adhesion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME3","text":"Truthful acts of Demons are reclassified: materially stated truth does not demonstrate rectitude of will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME4","text":"Pain is reclassified from sensitive passion to an act of the will against a present or absent thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ME5","text":"Penal place is reclassified from exclusive physical situation to a relation of will, guilt, temporal ministry, and final judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines what Demons know, whether they can be converted, how they suffer pain, and where they remain punitively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ALT2","text":"Structural — The four questions are governed by distinctions of nature and grace, cognition and will, natural and deliberate act, guilt and ministry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument dissolves universalizing objections through modal divisions, so that the opposition of cognition and darkness, freedom and obstinacy, or air and Hell appears false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Simple angelic nature and immobile apprehension constitute the temporality of definitive decision, to which temporal demonic ministry and eschatological judgment are subordinated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT1","text":"The extracted system suffices to restore the four principal conclusions: retained natural cognition, obstinate will, voluntary pain, and penal place ordered in two ways.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT2","text":"The firmest joint is the connection between the mode of immobile angelic apprehension and the immobility of the will after choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT3","text":"The concrete degree of diminution of speculative cognition and the criterion of revelation granted to Demons are not fully determined, apart from the rule that only so much is revealed as is fitting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT4","text":"The tension between the integrity of natural cognition and the name of darkening is resolved through the distinction of grace from nature, but the practical extent of each cognition is not further measured.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT5","text":"The connection between the first angelic adhesion and the perpetual impossibility of reversal is affirmed from the condition of nature, but the internal process of that transition is not independently developed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT6","text":"The ordering of providence refers demonic assault to human good while retaining the malice of Demons intact; compatibility is posited through the distinction of direct and indirect, not through a further exposition of causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT7","text":"The relation between the punishment of fire, the darksome air, and pain of will is composed through apprehension of due binding, but the sensible mechanism of that punishment is not further explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_56:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the epistemic distinction to the structure of choice, thence to the phenomenology of punishment, and finally to providential and final disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_56:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_56@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_56:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 65","title":"First Part · Question 64","context":"Chapter 65","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 64"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 64","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 65","order":66,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_57"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_57@R001","sha256":"9c8325de15917500389b18a51bb5f12ebe5da801e338cfc59c5d2534b3ca2dfd","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS1","text":"Quaestio originem, finem, modum productionis et causalitatem formarum creaturae corporalis determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS2","text":"Corporum originem a Deo probat ex communitate essendi, quae diversa ad unum essendi principium refert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS3","text":"Bonitatem corporalium restituit distinguendo naturam particularem creaturae a nocumento relativo et ab usu culpabili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS4","text":"Finem corporalium ordinat per seriem finium proximorum, perfectionem universi et ultimam repraesentationem divinae bonitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS5","text":"Productionem primam Deo soli attribuit et generationem formarum naturalium a creatione distinguit, ut motus creaturarum secundarum sine potestate creandi intelligatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A1","text":"Diversa in aliquo uno convenientia causam unam illius unitatis requirunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A2","text":"Esse communiter invenitur in omnibus rebus, spiritualibus et corporalibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A3","text":"Quod in rebus communius et magis substratum est, directius ad causalitatem superioris causae pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","text":"Creatio est productio totius substantiae nullo subiecto praesupposito, et ideo soli Deo competit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A5","text":"Deus unus, per sapientiam diversa cognoscens, potest immediate diversorum effectuum causa esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A6","text":"Creatura corporalis secundum naturam suam est bona, licet sit bonum particulare et contractum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A7","text":"Contrarietas et nocumentum ex bonitate particulari non constituunt malitiam absolutam naturae corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A8","text":"Creatura corporalis avertit ab Deo non per se, sed per usum insipientem; ipsa allicit quia aliquod bonum divinum participat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A9","text":"Finis proximus creaturae non excludit finem ultimum divinae bonitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A10","text":"Quaelibet creatura ordinatur ad actum proprium, creatura inferior ad superiorem, partes ad perfectionem totius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A11","text":"Universum cum omnibus partibus ordinatur in Deum, quia divina bonitas in eo per imitationem repraesentatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A12","text":"Inaequalitas primae institutionis non est retributio meritorum, sed ordinatio sapientiae ad perfectionem universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A13","text":"Creaturae corruptibiles non in nihilum redeunt, sed secundum materiam permanent, dum secundum formas mutantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A14","text":"Formae corporales non proprie fiunt aut sunt per se, sed composita per formas esse et fieri habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A15","text":"Formae corporales in generatione causantur per reductionem materiae de potentia in actum ab agente composito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A16","text":"Substantiae spirituales creatae ad formas corporales movent, sed formas non per influxum formalem producunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX1","text":"Creatura corporalis non procedit a principio malo contra bonum Deum constituto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX2","text":"Diabolus non est deus saeculi per creationem, sed per servitutem eorum qui saeculariter vivunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX3","text":"Temporalitas rerum visibilium non infert eas a Deo non esse factas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX4","text":"Nocumentum alicuius rei non licet simpliciter cum malitia naturae eius identificare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX5","text":"Corporalia non per se retrahunt a Deo, quamvis per culpabilem usum in muscipulam fiant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX6","text":"Mundus corporalis non est poena primarie instituta pro lapsu creaturarum spiritualium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX7","text":"Inaequalitas creaturarum non praesupponit inaequalitatem moralem vel meritoriam ante institutionem mundi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX8","text":"Ordo productionis non significat quod una creatura aliam per creationem producat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX9","text":"Forma corporalis non derivatur ab idea separata subsistente eiusdem rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX10","text":"Effectus finitus non potest, eo ipso quod finitus est, a virtute creata produci modo creationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D1","text":"Unitas essendi in creaturis visibilibus et invisibilibus excludit pluralitatem principiorum creativorum independentium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A1","CH_GGVC_P_57:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D2","text":"Malum quod corporibus tribuitur est saepe relatio ad commodum particulare, non iudicium de natura corporali secundum se.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A6","CH_GGVC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D3","text":"Ipsa capacitas corporalium ad seducendum testatur bonum in eis participatum, quod ad Deum causaliter reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D4","text":"Utilitas creaturae corporalis ad creaturam spiritualem subordinata compatitur cum eius ordinatione immediata ad bonitatem Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A9","CH_GGVC_P_57:A10","CH_GGVC_P_57:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D5","text":"Diversitas et inaequalitas cosmicae sunt effectus ordinationis ad totum, non vestigia culpae praecosmicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A10","CH_GGVC_P_57:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D6","text":"Creatio immediata a Deo non destruit gradus creaturarum, quia diversitas effectuum ex una sapientia divina procedere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A3","CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","CH_GGVC_P_57:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D7","text":"Mensura virtutis causantis non pendet ex sola quantitate effectus, sed etiam ex modo quo effectus producitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D8","text":"Formae primae corporum immediate a Deo procedunt, formae autem posteriores per motum et generationem in materia educuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","CH_GGVC_P_57:A14","CH_GGVC_P_57:A15","CH_GGVC_P_57:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD1","text":"Dualismus non solum moraliter, sed ontologice dissolvitur: principium malum non potest habere causam essendi propriam extra primum essendi principium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A1","CH_GGVC_P_57:A2","CH_GGVC_P_57:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD2","text":"Causalitas dividitur in ordinem creativum, qui totam substantiam dat, et ordinem transmutativum, qui subiectum iam creatum ad actum determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","CH_GGVC_P_57:A14","CH_GGVC_P_57:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD3","text":"Theodicea corporalis dependet a conversione iudicii: bonum et malum rerum non ex usu privato, sed ex natura, ordine et perfectione totius aestimanda sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A6","CH_GGVC_P_57:A7","CH_GGVC_P_57:A10","CH_GGVC_P_57:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD4","text":"Causae secundae non sunt rivales Dei, quia operantur intra ordinem essendi et potentiae quem creatio divina iam praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A3","CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","CH_GGVC_P_57:A15","CH_GGVC_P_57:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD5","text":"Cosmologia non explicatur ex historia morali ante mundum, sed ex sapientia quae universum inaequale ad perfectionem totius instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A11","CH_GGVC_P_57:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod esse commune possit a principiis omnino disparatis et non ordinatis procedere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod materia vel corpus habeat malitiam originariam per se subsistentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod creatura, etiam spiritualis, possit ex nihilo totam substantiam producere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod forma sit res per se facta et per se corrupta, cuius causa quaerenda sit sicut causa compositi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet quod ordo mundi sit distributio poenarum respondens motibus liberorum arbitriorum praecedentibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SNX1","text":"Mundus corporalis non admittitur ut regio ontologice extra causalitatem primi principii posita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SNX2","text":"Perfectio universi non admittitur ut summa commodorum individuorum aut mera compensatio meritorum antecedentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SNX3","text":"Nulla creatura admittitur ut principium formale absolutum: forma, corpus et angelus causalitatem suam exercere possunt tantum intra ordinem divinitus institutum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS1","text":"Communicatio essendi in diversis → necessitas unius principii essendi → exclusio principii mali creatoris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS2","text":"Communius substratum → causalitas superior → creatio totius substantiae → immediatio divina in prima productione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS3","text":"Bonum corporale particulare → contrarietas et nocumentum relativum → culpa usus, non malitia naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS4","text":"Actus proprius → subordinatio partium → perfectio universi → repraesentatio divinae bonitatis → Deus ut finis ultimus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS5","text":"Compositum, non forma separata, proprie fit → materia movetur de potentia in actum → causae corporales et angelicae movent → Deus solus creat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF1","text":"Temporalitas, nocumentum et visibilium seductio → dubium de origine divina corporum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF2","text":"Communitas essendi → unum principium essendi → creatura corporalis a bono Deo procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF3","text":"Bonum particulare et usus culpabilis → dissolutio identificationis corporis cum malo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF4","text":"Fines proprii et subordinati → perfectio universi → bonitas divina ut finis ultimus corporalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF5","text":"Creatio sine praesupposito → exclusio creationis angelicae → generatio formarum per motum materiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME1","text":"Corpus reclassificatur a re putative mala vel anti-divina ad bonum particulare, contrarium et ordinabile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME2","text":"Distinctio fit inter corruptionem, temporalitatem, annihilationem et creationem; haec quattuor non amplius confunduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME3","text":"Causalitas reordinatur inter Deum creatorem, causas compositas generantes et angelos moventes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME4","text":"Finalitas describitur ut scala a perfectione propria creaturae ad bonitatem Dei per perfectionem universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME5","text":"Inaequalitas cosmica reclassificatur ab indice iniustitiae vel culpae ad conditionem perfectionis universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus quaerit utrum corpora a Deo sint, propter quid sint, et quomodo formae eorum causentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ALT2","text":"Structural — Structura causalis distinguit esse creatum, materiam subiectam, formam, compositum, motum et creationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Positiones dualisticae, origenianae, platonicae et emanationis angelicae solvuntur per mutationem generis causae quaesitae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Esse creatum manet sub Deo, dum corpora secundum formam et motum mutantur; mutatio temporalis non est defectio ab origine divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT1","text":"Systema sufficit ad restituendam conclusionem principalem: corporalia a Deo procedunt, in bonitatem eius ordinantur, et ab angelis non creantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT2","text":"Firmissimum cardo est distinctio inter causationem essendi sine praesupposito et motum rei iam existentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT3","text":"Demonstratio unitatis creatoris pendet ex principio quod unitas essendi in diversis necessario unam causam postulat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT4","text":"Concordia inter immediationem divinam et causalitatem secundam servatur solum si creatio, influxus formalis et motus transmutativus stricte distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT5","text":"Resolutio mali corporalis nititur transitu ab aestimatione utilitatis privatae ad aestimationem naturae et ordinis universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT6","text":"Commissura fragilis manet ubi perfectio totius universi ponitur ut ratio sufficiens diversitatis et nocumenti particularis; haec ratio ex axiomatica teleologia dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164136995232Z_a96b6d0d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 65","source_sha256":"9c8325de15917500389b18a51bb5f12ebe5da801e338cfc59c5d2534b3ca2dfd","sha256":"a5de98945d5254efe3554c85022eabe8f071b78888fca8e766abdbdde1e208dc","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:41:36.996149+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS1","text":"The question determines the origin, end, mode of production, and causality of the forms of corporeal creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS2","text":"It proves the origin of bodies from God on the basis of the community of being, which refers diverse things to one principle of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS3","text":"It restores the goodness of corporeal things by distinguishing the particular nature of the creature from relative harm and culpable use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS4","text":"It orders the end of corporeal things through a series of proximate ends, the perfection of the universe, and the ultimate representation of divine goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AS5","text":"It attributes first production to God alone and distinguishes the generation of natural forms from creation, so that the motion of secondary creatures may be understood without a power to create.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A1","text":"Diverse things agreeing in some one respect require one cause of that unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A2","text":"Being is found commonly in all things, spiritual and corporeal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A3","text":"What is more common and more underlying in things pertains more directly to the causality of a higher cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","text":"Creation is the production of the whole substance with no subject presupposed, and therefore belongs to God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A5","text":"The one God, knowing diverse things through wisdom, can be immediately the cause of diverse effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A6","text":"A corporeal creature is good according to its nature, although it is a particular and limited good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A7","text":"Contrariety and harm arising from particular goodness do not constitute an absolute evilness of corporeal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A8","text":"A corporeal creature turns away from God not through itself, but through an unwise use; it itself attracts because it participates in some divine good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A9","text":"The proximate end of a creature does not exclude the ultimate end of divine goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A10","text":"Every creature is ordered to its proper act, an inferior creature to a superior one, and parts to the perfection of the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A11","text":"The universe with all its parts is ordered to God, because divine goodness is represented in it by imitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A12","text":"The inequality of the first institution is not a recompense of merits, but an ordering of wisdom toward the perfection of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A13","text":"Corruptible creatures do not return into nothing, but remain according to matter while changing according to forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A14","text":"Corporeal forms do not properly come to be or exist through themselves, but composites have being and coming-to-be through forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A15","text":"Corporeal forms are caused in generation through the reduction of matter from potency to act by a composite agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:A16","text":"Created spiritual substances move toward corporeal forms, but do not produce forms through formal influx.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX1","text":"A corporeal creature does not proceed from an evil principle set against the good God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX2","text":"The devil is not the god of this age through creation, but through the servitude of those who live secularly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX3","text":"The temporality of visible things does not imply that they were not made by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX4","text":"The harmfulness of some thing may not simply be identified with the evilness of its nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX5","text":"Corporeal things do not in themselves draw one away from God, although through culpable use they become a snare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX6","text":"The corporeal world is not a punishment instituted primarily for the fall of spiritual creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX7","text":"The inequality of creatures does not presuppose moral or meritorious inequality before the institution of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX8","text":"The order of production does not signify that one creature produces another through creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX9","text":"A corporeal form is not derived from a subsisting separate idea of the same intelligible content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:NX10","text":"A finite effect cannot, precisely insofar as it is finite, be produced by created power in the mode of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D1","text":"The unity of being in visible and invisible creatures excludes a plurality of independent creative principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A1","CH_GGVC_P_57:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D2","text":"The evil attributed to bodies is often a relation to a particular advantage, not a judgment concerning corporeal nature in itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A6","CH_GGVC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D3","text":"The very capacity of corporeal things to seduce attests to the good participated in them, which is causally referred back to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D4","text":"The usefulness of a corporeal creature subordinated to a spiritual creature is compatible with its immediate ordering to the goodness of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A9","CH_GGVC_P_57:A10","CH_GGVC_P_57:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D5","text":"Cosmic diversity and inequality are effects of ordering to the whole, not traces of pre-cosmic fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A10","CH_GGVC_P_57:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D6","text":"Immediate creation by God does not destroy the grades of creatures, because diversity of effects can proceed from one divine wisdom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A3","CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","CH_GGVC_P_57:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D7","text":"The measure of causal power does not depend on the quantity of the effect alone, but also on the manner in which the effect is produced.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:D8","text":"The first forms of bodies proceed immediately from God, whereas subsequent forms are educed in matter through motion and generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","CH_GGVC_P_57:A14","CH_GGVC_P_57:A15","CH_GGVC_P_57:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD1","text":"Dualism is dissolved not only morally but ontologically: an evil principle cannot have a proper cause of being outside the first principle of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A1","CH_GGVC_P_57:A2","CH_GGVC_P_57:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD2","text":"Causality is divided into a creative order, which gives the whole substance, and a transmutative order, which determines an already-created subject to act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","CH_GGVC_P_57:A14","CH_GGVC_P_57:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD3","text":"Corporeal theodicy depends on a conversion of judgment: the good and evil of things must be assessed not from private use, but from nature, order, and the perfection of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A6","CH_GGVC_P_57:A7","CH_GGVC_P_57:A10","CH_GGVC_P_57:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD4","text":"Secondary causes are not rivals of God, because they operate within the order of being and potency that divine creation already presupposes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A3","CH_GGVC_P_57:A4","CH_GGVC_P_57:A15","CH_GGVC_P_57:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SD5","text":"Cosmology is explained not from a moral history before the world, but from wisdom that instituted an unequal universe for the perfection of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_57:A11","CH_GGVC_P_57:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX1","text":"It must be false that common being can proceed from principles wholly disparate and unordered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX2","text":"It must be false that matter or body has an original evilness subsisting through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX3","text":"It must be false that a creature, even a spiritual one, can produce the whole substance from nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX4","text":"It must be false that form is a thing made through itself and corrupted through itself, whose cause must be sought like the cause of a composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the order of the world is a distribution of punishments corresponding to preceding movements of free wills.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SNX1","text":"The corporeal world is not admitted as a region ontologically placed outside the causality of the first principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SNX2","text":"The perfection of the universe is not admitted as a sum of individual advantages or as a mere compensation for antecedent merits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:SNX3","text":"No creature is admitted as an absolute formal principle: form, body, and angel can exercise their causality only within the order divinely instituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS1","text":"Communication of being in diverse things → necessity of one principle of being → exclusion of an evil creative principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS2","text":"More common substrate → higher causality → creation of the whole substance → divine immediacy in first production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS3","text":"Particular corporeal good → contrariety and relative harm → fault of use, not evilness of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS4","text":"Proper act → subordination of parts → perfection of the universe → representation of divine goodness → God as ultimate end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:FGS5","text":"The composite, not the separate form, properly comes to be → matter is moved from potency to act → corporeal and angelic causes move → God alone creates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF1","text":"Temporality, harm, and the seduction of visible things → doubt concerning the divine origin of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF2","text":"Community of being → one principle of being → corporeal creature proceeds from the good God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF3","text":"Particular good and culpable use → dissolution of the identification of body with evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF4","text":"Proper and subordinate ends → perfection of the universe → divine goodness as the ultimate end of corporeal things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:AF5","text":"Creation without a presupposed subject → exclusion of angelic creation → generation of forms through the motion of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME1","text":"Body is reclassified from a putatively evil or anti-divine thing to a particular, contrary, and orderable good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME2","text":"A distinction is made among corruption, temporality, annihilation, and creation; these four are no longer confused.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME3","text":"Causality is reordered among God the creator, generative composite causes, and moving angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME4","text":"Finality is described as a scale from the creature's proper perfection to the goodness of God through the perfection of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ME5","text":"Cosmic inequality is reclassified from an index of injustice or fault to a condition of universal perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text asks whether bodies are from God, for what they are, and how their forms are caused.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ALT2","text":"Structural — The causal structure distinguishes created being, underlying matter, form, composite, motion, and creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Dualistic, Origenian, Platonic, and angelic-emanation positions are dissolved through a change in the kind of cause sought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Created being remains under God, while bodies change according to form and motion; temporal change is not a falling away from divine origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT1","text":"The system suffices to restore the principal conclusion: corporeal things proceed from God, are ordered to his goodness, and are not created by angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT2","text":"The firmest hinge is the distinction between causation of being without a presupposition and the motion of an already existing thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT3","text":"The demonstration of the unity of the creator depends on the principle that the unity of being in diverse things necessarily demands one cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT4","text":"The harmony between divine immediacy and secondary causality is preserved only if creation, formal influx, and transmutative motion are strictly distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT5","text":"The resolution of corporeal evil rests on the transition from an assessment of private utility to an assessment of universal nature and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_57:MRT6","text":"A fragile joint remains where the perfection of the whole universe is posited as the sufficient reason for diversity and particular harm; this account depends on axiomatic teleology.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_57:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_57@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_57:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 66","title":"First Part · Question 65","context":"Chapter 66","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 65"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 65","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 66","order":67,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_58"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_58@R001","sha256":"cc16718e34390aeeee408b95dd66da02fa000fe04fa6c5880581f541195cbb4a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS1","text":"Quaestio ordinem creationis ad distinctionem determinat per quattuor nodos: prioritatem informitatis, unitatem materiae corporalis, concreationem caeli Empyrei et concreationem temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS2","text":"Realitas corporalis creata numquam fuit actu ut materia pure informis vel ut subiectum homogenei corporis; informitas admittitur aut secundum originem aut secundum carentiam ulterioris decoris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS3","text":"Diversitas actuum et motuum diversitatem potentiarum materialium constituit, unde materia caelestium et elementorum una non est nisi analogice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS4","text":"Concreatio caeli Empyrei ratione auctoritatis et congruentiae gloriae, concreatio autem temporis secundum modum prioris informitatis conditionaliter statuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS5","text":"Argumentatio est dialectica, metaphysica, exegetica et reconstructiva: opiniones non simpliciter elidit, sed sensus terminorum, modos prioritatis et gradus probationis distinguit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS6","text":"Motus totius quaestionis procedit ab aequivocatione informitatis ad contradictionem actus sine forma, inde ad pluralitatem materiae, ordinem gloriae et mensuram successionis creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","text":"Terminus creationis est ens actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","text":"Materia secundum se est ens in potentia et actualitatem non habet nisi per formam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A3","text":"Duratio rei importat eam iam esse in actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","text":"Potentia specificatur ex actu ad quem ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A5","text":"Forma substantialis dat esse simpliciter; forma adveniens subiecto iam substantialiter actuali dat tantum esse determinatum secundum rationem accidentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A6","text":"Natura actum ex ente in potentia producit, Deus autem ens actu ex nihilo producere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","text":"Informitas aut omnem formam aut solum determinatam pulchritudinem et ordinationem excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","text":"Prioritas originis seu naturae prioritatem durationis non importat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","text":"Materia communis est in potentia ad omnes formas eorum quorum est materia et mutuam transmutationem eorum fundat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A10","text":"Diversi motus naturales diversas naturas indicant, et contrarietas principium generationis et corruptionis praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A11","text":"Materia caelestis ad solam formam propriam ordinatur et, ea recepta, ad esse non remanet in potentia sed tantum ad ubi; materia elementaris ad formas contrarias ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A12","text":"Unitas logica rationis corporeitatis unitatem materiae physicae vel unam formam corporeitatis non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","text":"Consummatio futura duplicem gloriam, spiritualem et corporalem, cum innovatione totius mundi complectitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A14","text":"Inchoatae gloriae spirituali in angelis congruit inchoatio gloriae corporalis in corpore incorruptibili, immutabili et lucido.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A15","text":"Corpus ad statum gloriae ordinatum non tenetur lege mobilitatis quae corporibus sensibilibus in praesenti statu mundi competit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A16","text":"Secundum rationem probabiliorem, causa superior immobilis potest corporibus mobilibus virtutem stabilem influere sine motu proprio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","text":"Tempus est numerus prioris et posterioris in motu atque mensura cuiuscumque primi motus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A18","text":"Tempus, ut mensura communis non permanens, inter primo creata secundum suum principium numeratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX1","text":"Materia omnino carens forma tempore formationem suam praecedere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX2","text":"Materia prima sub una forma communi corporeitatis ante formas distinctivas non fuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX3","text":"Ordo operationis divinae non reducitur ad temporalem ordinem quo natura potentiam in actum ducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX4","text":"Possibilitas accidentis sine subiecto possibilitatem materiae actu existentis sine forma non probat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX5","text":"Status primordialis non fuit chaos omnem distinctionem excludens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX6","text":"Nomina terrae et aquae non cogunt ut materia prima proprie terra vel aqua intelligatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX7","text":"Convenientia omnium corporum in uno genere logico unitatem materiae physicae non infert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX8","text":"Corporum corruptibilium et incorruptibilium per naturam eadem materia esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX9","text":"Corpus caeleste non est ipsum materiale subiectum cui substantia separata tamquam forma tantum extrinseca unitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX10","text":"Caelum Empyreum non demonstratur necessaria ratione naturali, sed auctoritatibus et congruentia sustinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX11","text":"Posterior creatio firmamenti et calumnia Manichaeorum rationes cogentes pro caelo Empyreo non sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX12","text":"Locus corporeus contemplationi non deputatur ex necessitate contemplationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX13","text":"Immobilitas caeli Empyrei influxum eius in corpora mobilia necessario non excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX14","text":"Tenebrae non sunt creatura positiva, nec imperfectio relativa initialis impotentiam agentis divini significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX15","text":"Divisio per diem et noctem non constituit tempus simpliciter, sed tempus iam positum distinguit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX16","text":"Tempus non est essentialiter numerus solius motus firmamenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX17","text":"Motus et locus non eodem modo ac tempus inter primo creata separatim computantur: motus subiecto mobili particulariter inhaeret, locus autem in caelo continente intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","text":"Materia totaliter informis quae duratione praeexisteret simul esset actu et careret omni principio actualitatis, quod contradictionem implicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","text":"Informitas materiae primae ut carentia omnis formae formationem tantum natura seu origine praecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D3","text":"Informitas ut carentia lucis, expositionis terrae vel ornatus potest formas substantiales iam praesupponere atque formationem ulteriorem tempore antecedere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A3","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D4","text":"Posita una forma substantiali communi, formae posteriores essent accidentales et generatio reduceretur ad alterationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D5","text":"Temporalis praecessio potentiae necessaria operationi naturali ad creationem ex nihilo transferri non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A6","CH_GGVC_P_58:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D6","text":"Si materia caelestis et elementaris esset communis, materia sub forma incorruptibili adhuc esset in potentia ad formas corruptibiles et simul sub forma atque privatione; corpus caeleste igitur corruptibilitatis dispositionem haberet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D7","text":"Unitas materiae corporalis servari potest tantum secundum analogiam potentiae, unitatem ordinis vel considerationem logicam, non secundum idem subiectum physicum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11","CH_GGVC_P_58:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","text":"Caelum Empyreum convenienter ponitur ut initium corporeae gloriae futurae, non ut conclusio naturali demonstratione necessaria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D9","text":"Immobilitas caeli Empyrei congruit statui consummatae gloriae anticipato ab initio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A14","CH_GGVC_P_58:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D10","text":"Caelum Empyreum potest aut ab influxu naturali eximi propter ordinem gloriae aut, probabilius, virtutem stabilem corporibus mobilibus communicare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A15","CH_GGVC_P_58:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","text":"In schemate Augustiniano materia et natura angelica formationem, motum et tempus natura tantum praecedunt; tempus igitur eis inter primo creata non connumeratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D12","text":"In schemate temporalis informitatis duratio ante ulteriorem formationem aliquod tempus necessario postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A3","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D13","text":"Si motus firmamenti nondum inceperat, tempus initiale mensurabat alium primum motum, minimum saltem successionem conceptionum et affectionum angelicarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D14","text":"Tempus non totum simul creatur, sed concreatur in principio a quo successiva eius actualitas fluit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1","text":"Concordia opinionum producitur non per identitatem sententiarum, sed per distinctionem sensuum informitatis, generum unitatis et modorum prioritatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3","CH_GGVC_P_58:D7","CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD2","text":"Relatio actus et potentiae simul regit possibilitatem status initialis et pluralitatem materiae corporalis: neque potentia pura durat neque potentiae ad actus incompatibiles idem subiectum naturale constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","CH_GGVC_P_58:D4","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD3","text":"Opus distinctionis non transit ab absoluta confusione ad primam actualitatem, sed ab actualitate iam multipliciter determinata ad ulteriorem ordinationem et decorem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4","text":"Duae constructiones cosmologicae conditionaliter manent: una formationem sine intervallo temporali ponit, altera statum initialem substantialiter formatum sed ornamentaliter imperfectum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3","CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD5","text":"Ordo creatus in ordinem naturalis decursus et ordinem gloriae distinguitur, quorum leges mobilitatis, causalitatis et perfectionis non sunt simpliciter eaedem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D9","CH_GGVC_P_58:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6","text":"Gradus certitudinis conclusionum inaequales sunt: impossibilitas materiae actu sine forma demonstratur, pluralitas materiae physice argumentatur, caelum Empyreum autem convenienter et probabiliter ponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6","CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD7","text":"Initium mundi structuram finis anticipat: gloria spiritualis iam adest, gloria corporalis exemplariter inchoatur, motus autem et tempus cursum ad consummationem mensurant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D9","CH_GGVC_P_58:D13","CH_GGVC_P_58:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX1","text":"Systema falsitatem requirit notionis qua potentia pura tamquam res actualis et temporaliter persistens concipitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit formas substantiales tamquam ornamenta extrinseca corpori iam substantialiter constituto superaddita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A5","CH_GGVC_P_58:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX3","text":"Termini materiae, informitatis, corporis et prioritatis univoce per omnes opiniones sumi non possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:A12","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX4","text":"Homogeneum subiectum corporeum omnibus motibus, formis et modis corruptibilitatis indifferenter commune structuraliter excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX5","text":"Mensura potentiae divinae ex tarditate et successione causalitatis naturalis sumi non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A6","CH_GGVC_P_58:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX6","text":"Tempus non est receptaculum absolutum motu independens in quo creatio postea collocetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12","CH_GGVC_P_58:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX7","text":"Omnis imperfectio initialis defectum agentis significare non potest; imperfectio relativa potest ordinem sapientiae exprimere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A6","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX8","text":"Gloria corporalis non est omnino extrinseca principio creationis neque tantum futurum sine praesentia exemplari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A14","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX1","text":"Nullum admittitur ante temporale in quo neque motus neque tempus sit; ubi prioritas non est successiva, ad originem vel naturam reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX2","text":"Absolutum chaos, omni forma, distinctione et ordine carens, non potest esse primus status actualis creationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX3","text":"Substratum corporeum neutrum, anterioribus determinationibus intactum et omnibus formis univoce commune, impossibile redditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D4","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6","CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX4","text":"Totus ordo corporalis ad praesentem cursum naturae, mobilitatis et corruptionis claudi non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A15","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX5","text":"Una chronologia litteralis quae Augustinianam prioritatem naturalem et temporalem informitatem aliorum sanctorum sine distinctione coniungat praecluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX6","text":"Certitudo demonstrativa caeli Empyrei tamquam obiecti naturaliter probati indisponibilis manet; systema eius positionem intra auctoritatem, congruentiam et probabilitatem continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_58:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS1","text":"Prima machina operatur hac serie: aequivocatio informitatis → divisio sensuum → probatio per actum et formam → informitas absoluta temporaliter exclusa → informitas relativa temporaliter admissa → opiniones conditionaliter conciliatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS2","text":"Secunda machina operatur hac serie: hypothesis materiae communis → potentia ad omnes formas → potentia caeli ad formas corruptibiles → privatio et corruptibilitas caeli → contradictio → unitas materiae ad analogiam reducta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6","CH_GGVC_P_58:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS3","text":"Tertia machina operatur hac serie: auctoritates de caelo Empyreo → rationes initiales non cogentes → duplex gloria futura → inchoatio spiritualis angelica → congrua inchoatio corporalis → corpus gloriosum immobile et probabiliter influens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A14","CH_GGVC_P_58:A15","CH_GGVC_P_58:A16","CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS4","text":"Quarta machina operatur hac serie: distinctio prioritatis naturalis et temporalis → absentia temporis in schemate Augustiniano vel necessitas temporis in schemate durationis → requisitus primus motus → successio angelica minima → concreatio temporis in principio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:A18","CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12","CH_GGVC_P_58:D13","CH_GGVC_P_58:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS5","text":"Machina communis est: terminum aequivocum distingue → modum prioritatis determina → potentiam per actum specifica → contradictionem consequentem proba → ordines naturae et gloriae separa → conclusionem secundum gradum certitudinis limita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF1","text":"Primus articulus movetur ab informitate primordiali ad distinctionem sensuum, ab hac distinctione ad contradictionem materiae actu sine forma, deinde ad duplicem modum prioritatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF2","text":"Secundus articulus movetur ab unitate generica corporis ad examen potentiae et motus, inde ad separationem materiae caelestis et elementaris atque ad unitatem mere analogicam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF3","text":"Tertius articulus movetur ab auctoritate de caelo Empyreo ad insufficientiam rationum initialium, inde ad congruentiam gloriae corporalis anticipatae et ad solutionem obiectionum de motu et influxu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF4","text":"Quartus articulus movetur a duplici schemate prioritatis ad condicionatam concreationem temporis, inde ad primum motum et ad rationem temporis ut mensurae communis successivae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF5","text":"Motus totius quaestionis est: creatio actualis → distinctio formarum et potentiarum → exclusio chaos homogenei → articulatio ordinis naturalis et gloriae → mensuratio temporalis secundum modum successionis admissum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_58:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_58:AF3","CH_GGVC_P_58:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME1","text":"Informitas ex statu simpliciter temporali in notionem duplicem reclassificatur: privatio omnis formae vel carentia ulterioris decoris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME2","text":"Unitas materiae dividitur in identitatem physicam, analogiam potentiae, unitatem ordinis et communitatem logicam corporis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D7","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME3","text":"Opus distinctionis non amplius legitur ut productio entis ex chaos actuali, sed ut ulterior ordinatio rerum iam formaliter distinctarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME4","text":"Caelum Empyreum ex corpore naturali superiori in exemplar corporeae gloriae reclassificatur, cui immobilitas non est defectus sed anticipatio finis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME5","text":"Tempus ex recipiente absoluto in mensuram successionis primi motus convertitur, quae non tota simul sed in principio concreatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:A18","CH_GGVC_P_58:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME6","text":"Catalogus rerum primo creatarum fit dependens a modo quo prioritas informitatis intelligitur, non absoluta enumeratio omnibus opinionibus communis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME7","text":"Cosmologia reordinatur inter initium iam formatum, cursum naturalem mobilem et consummationem gloriosam cuius forma initialiter anticipatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — Quattuor obiecta immediata examinantur: informitas initialis, communitas materiae, caelum Empyreum et tempus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — Relationes actus et potentiae, formae et materiae, motus et naturae, corruptionis et contrarietatis structuram cosmologicam determinant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A5","CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — Conflictus auctoritatum tractatur per distinctiones semanticorum, modorum prioritatis, ordinum causalium et graduum certitudinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Esse creatum concipitur ut actualitas formata, materia ut potentia relationalis, tempus ut numerus successionis, et initium mundi ut anticipatio ordinis finalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD7","CH_GGVC_P_58:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta quattuor articulos restituere sufficiunt, quia relationes formae ad actum, potentiae ad actum proprium, gloriae ad consummationem et temporis ad motum continent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT2","text":"Firmissima commissura est impossibilitas materiae duratione existentis sine forma, quae ex definitionibus actus, materiae et durationis directe sequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT3","text":"Argumentum de pluralitate materiae interne validissimum est concessis principiis Aristotelicis de motu naturali, contrarietate et corruptibilitate; ab his principiis tamen substantialiter dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A10","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT4","text":"Positio caeli Empyrei minus determinata manet, quia auctoritate et congruentia potius quam demonstratione naturali stabilitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT5","text":"Cohaerentia duorum schematum informitatis servatur tantum si carentia omnis formae a carentia decoris et prioritas naturalis a prioritate temporali constanter distinguuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT6","text":"Relatio inter angelicam carentiam temporum et successionem conceptionum angelicarum non plene conciliatur nisi prima ad schema Augustinianum, secunda ad schema temporalis durationis referatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT7","text":"Influxus caeli Empyrei immobilis commissura probabilis manet: analogia causalitatis angelicae et virtus stabilis possibilitatem praebent, necessitatem non demonstrant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A16","CH_GGVC_P_58:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT8","text":"Expositio scripturalis deliberatam indeterminationem inter significationem metaphysicam materiae et descriptionem elementorum incomplete ordinatorum retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT9","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: terminos distinguit, impossibilia per contradictionem removet, opiniones ad sensus proprios limitat et conclusiones secundum vim probationis gradatim constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS5","CH_GGVC_P_58:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164214576197Z_aa993b5d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 66","source_sha256":"cc16718e34390aeeee408b95dd66da02fa000fe04fa6c5880581f541195cbb4a","sha256":"d7f3bbb12fa526129d5189314f2f6342efd15b57563897f953de75642261eb11","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:42:14.577149+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS1","text":"The question determines the order of creation through four nodes: the priority of formlessness, the unity of corporeal matter, the concreation of the Empyrean heaven, and the concreation of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS2","text":"Created corporeal reality was never actually either matter purely formless or the subject of a homogeneous body; formlessness is admitted either according to origin or according to the lack of further adornment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS3","text":"The diversity of acts and motions establishes a diversity of material potentialities, whence the matter of the heavenly bodies and of the elements is one only analogically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS4","text":"The concreation of the Empyrean heaven is posited on grounds of authority and the fittingness of glory, whereas the concreation of time is posited conditionally according to the mode of prior formlessness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS5","text":"The argumentation is dialectical, metaphysical, exegetical, and reconstructive: it does not simply eliminate opinions, but distinguishes the senses of terms, modes of priority, and degrees of proof.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AS6","text":"The movement of the whole question proceeds from the equivocation of formlessness to the contradiction of act without form, thence to the plurality of matter, the order of glory, and the measure of created succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","text":"The terminus of creation is being in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","text":"Matter in itself is being in potency and has actuality only through form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A3","text":"The duration of a thing implies that it already exists in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","text":"Potency is specified by the act to which it is ordered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A5","text":"Substantial form gives being simply; a form supervening upon a subject already actual substantially gives only determinate being according to the nature of an accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A6","text":"Nature produces act from being in potency, but God can produce being in act from nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","text":"Formlessness excludes either every form or only determinate beauty and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","text":"Priority of origin or nature does not imply priority of duration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","text":"Common matter is in potency to all forms of those things of which it is the matter, and grounds their mutual transmutation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A10","text":"Different natural motions indicate different natures, and contrariety provides the principle of generation and corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A11","text":"Heavenly matter is ordered to its own form alone and, having received it, remains in potency not to being but only to where; elemental matter is ordered to contrary forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A12","text":"The logical unity of the notion of corporeity does not establish the unity of physical matter or one form of corporeity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","text":"Future consummation comprises a twofold glory, spiritual and corporeal, together with the renewal of the whole world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A14","text":"To the begun spiritual glory in the angels corresponds the beginning of corporeal glory in an incorruptible, immutable, and luminous body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A15","text":"A body ordered to the state of glory is not bound by the law of mobility that belongs to sensible bodies in the present state of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A16","text":"According to the more probable account, an immobile higher cause can infuse a stable power into mobile bodies without motion of its own.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","text":"Time is the number of prior and posterior in motion and the measure of any first motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:A18","text":"Time, as a non-permanent common measure, is counted among the things first created according to its principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX1","text":"Matter wholly lacking form cannot precede its formation in time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX2","text":"Prime matter did not exist under one common form of corporeity before distinctive forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX3","text":"The order of divine operation is not reducible to the temporal order by which nature leads potency into act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX4","text":"The possibility of an accident without a subject does not prove the possibility of matter actually existing without form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX5","text":"The primordial state was not a chaos excluding every distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX6","text":"The names earth and water do not compel one to understand prime matter properly as earth or water.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX7","text":"The agreement of all bodies in one logical genus does not entail the unity of physical matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX8","text":"Corruptible and incorruptible bodies cannot have the same matter by nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX9","text":"A heavenly body is not itself the material subject to which a separate substance is united as a merely extrinsic form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX10","text":"The Empyrean heaven is not demonstrated by necessary natural reasoning, but is supported by authorities and fittingness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX11","text":"The later creation of the firmament and the calumny of the Manichaeans are not compelling reasons for the Empyrean heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX12","text":"A corporeal place is not assigned to contemplation out of the necessity of contemplation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX13","text":"The immobility of the Empyrean heaven does not necessarily exclude its influence upon mobile bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX14","text":"Darkness is not a positive creature, nor does initial relative imperfection signify the impotence of the divine agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX15","text":"Division through day and night does not constitute time simply, but distinguishes time already posited.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX16","text":"Time is not essentially the number of the motion of the firmament alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:NX17","text":"Motion and place are not separately counted among the things first created in the same way as time: motion inheres particularly in a mobile subject, whereas place is understood in the containing heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","text":"Matter totally formless that preexisted in duration would simultaneously be in act and lack every principle of actuality, which entails a contradiction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","text":"The formlessness of prime matter, as the lack of every form, precedes formation only by nature or origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D3","text":"Formlessness as the lack of light, the exposure of earth, or adornment can already presuppose substantial forms and precede further formation in time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A3","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D4","text":"Given one common substantial form, subsequent forms would be accidental, and generation would be reduced to alteration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D5","text":"The temporal precedence of potency necessary for the operation of nature cannot be transferred to creation from nothing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A6","CH_GGVC_P_58:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D6","text":"If heavenly and elemental matter were common, matter under an incorruptible form would still be in potency to corruptible forms and simultaneously under form and privation; therefore the heavenly body would have a disposition toward corruptibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D7","text":"The unity of corporeal matter can be maintained only according to an analogy of potency, a unity of order, or logical consideration, not according to the same physical subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11","CH_GGVC_P_58:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","text":"The Empyrean heaven is fittingly posited as the beginning of future corporeal glory, not as a conclusion necessary by natural demonstration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D9","text":"The immobility of the Empyrean heaven befits the state of consummated glory anticipated from the beginning.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A14","CH_GGVC_P_58:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D10","text":"The Empyrean heaven can either be exempted from natural influence on account of the order of glory or, more probably, communicate a stable power to mobile bodies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A15","CH_GGVC_P_58:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","text":"In the Augustinian schema, matter and angelic nature precede formation, motion, and time only by nature; therefore time is not counted among the things first created with them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D12","text":"In the schema of temporal formlessness, duration before further formation necessarily requires some time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A3","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D13","text":"If the motion of the firmament had not yet begun, initial time measured another first motion, at least the succession of angelic conceptions and affections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:D14","text":"Time is not created all at once, but is concreated in the principle from which its successive actuality flows.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1","text":"The concord of opinions is produced not through identity of positions, but through distinction of the senses of formlessness, kinds of unity, and modes of priority.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3","CH_GGVC_P_58:D7","CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD2","text":"The relation of act and potency simultaneously governs the possibility of the initial state and the plurality of corporeal matter: neither does pure potency endure, nor do potentialities for incompatible acts constitute the same natural subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","CH_GGVC_P_58:D4","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD3","text":"The work of distinction does not pass from absolute confusion to first actuality, but from actuality already determined in many ways to further ordering and adornment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4","text":"Two cosmological constructions remain conditionally: one posits formation without a temporal interval, the other an initial state substantially formed but ornamentally imperfect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3","CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD5","text":"Created order is distinguished into the order of natural course and the order of glory, whose laws of mobility, causality, and perfection are not simply the same.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D9","CH_GGVC_P_58:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6","text":"The degrees of certainty of the conclusions are unequal: the impossibility of matter actually without form is demonstrated, the plurality of matter is argued physically, but the Empyrean heaven is posited fittingly and probably.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6","CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SD7","text":"The beginning of the world anticipates the structure of its end: spiritual glory is already present, corporeal glory is begun exemplarily, while motion and time measure the course toward consummation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D9","CH_GGVC_P_58:D13","CH_GGVC_P_58:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX1","text":"The system requires the falsity of the notion by which pure potency is conceived as an actual and temporally persisting thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX2","text":"The system excludes substantial forms as extrinsic ornaments superadded to a body already constituted substantially.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A5","CH_GGVC_P_58:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX3","text":"The terms matter, formlessness, body, and priority cannot be taken univocally across all opinions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:A12","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX4","text":"A homogeneous corporeal subject indifferently common to all motions, forms, and modes of corruptibility is structurally excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX5","text":"The measure of divine power cannot be taken from the slowness and succession of natural causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A6","CH_GGVC_P_58:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX6","text":"Time is not an absolute receptacle independent of motion in which creation is subsequently placed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12","CH_GGVC_P_58:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX7","text":"Not every initial imperfection can signify a defect in the agent; relative imperfection can express an order of wisdom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A6","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX8","text":"Corporeal glory is neither wholly extrinsic to the beginning of creation nor merely future without exemplary presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A14","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX1","text":"No temporal before is admitted in which there is neither motion nor time; where priority is not successive, it is reduced to origin or nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX2","text":"Absolute chaos, lacking every form, distinction, and order, cannot be the first actual state of creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX3","text":"A neutral corporeal substrate, untouched by prior determinations and univocally common to all forms, is rendered impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D4","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6","CH_GGVC_P_58:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX4","text":"The whole corporeal order cannot be confined to the present course of nature, mobility, and corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A15","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX5","text":"A single literal chronology that combines without distinction Augustinian natural priority and the temporal formlessness of other saints is precluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:SNX6","text":"Demonstrative certainty concerning the Empyrean heaven as an object naturally proved remains unavailable; the system confines its position to authority, fittingness, and probability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_58:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS1","text":"The first machine operates in this sequence: equivocation of formlessness → division of senses → proof through act and form → absolute formlessness temporally excluded → relative formlessness temporally admitted → opinions conditionally reconciled.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A2","CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:D1","CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS2","text":"The second machine operates in this sequence: hypothesis of common matter → potency to all forms → potency of heaven to corruptible forms → privation and corruptibility of heaven → contradiction → unity of matter reduced to analogy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6","CH_GGVC_P_58:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS3","text":"The third machine operates in this sequence: authorities concerning the Empyrean heaven → initial non-compelling reasons → twofold future glory → angelic spiritual beginning → fitting corporeal beginning → glorious body immobile and probably influential.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A14","CH_GGVC_P_58:A15","CH_GGVC_P_58:A16","CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS4","text":"The fourth machine operates in this sequence: distinction of natural and temporal priority → absence of time in the Augustinian schema or necessity of time in the schema of duration → required first motion → minimal angelic succession → concreation of time in the beginning.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:A18","CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12","CH_GGVC_P_58:D13","CH_GGVC_P_58:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS5","text":"The common machine is: distinguish the equivocal term → determine the mode of priority → specify potency through act → prove the consequent contradiction → separate the orders of nature and glory → limit the conclusion according to its degree of certainty.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF1","text":"The first article moves from primordial formlessness to a distinction of senses, from this distinction to the contradiction of matter actually without form, and then to the twofold mode of priority.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF2","text":"The second article moves from the generic unity of body to examination of potency and motion, thence to the separation of heavenly and elemental matter and to merely analogical unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF3","text":"The third article moves from authority concerning the Empyrean heaven to the insufficiency of the initial reasons, thence to the fittingness of anticipated corporeal glory and to the solution of objections concerning motion and influence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF4","text":"The fourth article moves from a twofold schema of priority to the conditional concreation of time, thence to first motion and to the account of time as a common successive measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:AF5","text":"The movement of the whole question is: actual creation → distinction of forms and potentialities → exclusion of homogeneous chaos → articulation of the order of nature and glory → temporal measurement according to the admitted mode of succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_58:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_58:AF3","CH_GGVC_P_58:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME1","text":"Formlessness is reclassified from a simply temporal state into a twofold notion: privation of every form or lack of further adornment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:D2","CH_GGVC_P_58:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME2","text":"The unity of matter is divided into physical identity, analogy of potency, unity of order, and logical commonality of body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D7","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME3","text":"The work of distinction is no longer read as the production of being from actual chaos, but as the further ordering of things already formally distinct.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME4","text":"The Empyrean heaven is reclassified from a higher natural body into an exemplar of corporeal glory, for which immobility is not a defect but an anticipation of the end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D8","CH_GGVC_P_58:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME5","text":"Time is transformed from an absolute receptacle into the measure of the succession of first motion, which is not concreated all at once but in the beginning.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A17","CH_GGVC_P_58:A18","CH_GGVC_P_58:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME6","text":"The catalogue of things first created becomes dependent on the way in which the priority of formlessness is understood, rather than an absolute enumeration common to all opinions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D12","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ME7","text":"Cosmology is reordered among an already formed beginning, the mobile natural course, and glorious consummation whose form is anticipated initially.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — Four immediate objects are examined: initial formlessness, the commonality of matter, the Empyrean heaven, and time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — The relations of act and potency, form and matter, motion and nature, corruption and contrariety determine the cosmological structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A5","CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — The conflict of authorities is treated through distinctions of semantic senses, modes of priority, causal orders, and degrees of certainty.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Created being is conceived as formed actuality, matter as relational potency, time as the number of succession, and the beginning of the world as an anticipation of the final order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD7","CH_GGVC_P_58:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the four articles because they contain the relations of form to act, potency to its proper act, glory to consummation, and time to motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A1","CH_GGVC_P_58:A4","CH_GGVC_P_58:A13","CH_GGVC_P_58:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT2","text":"The strongest joint is the impossibility of matter existing in duration without form, which follows directly from the definitions of act, matter, and duration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT3","text":"The argument concerning the plurality of matter is internally most valid given the Aristotelian principles concerning natural motion, contrariety, and corruptibility; nevertheless, it depends substantially upon those principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A9","CH_GGVC_P_58:A10","CH_GGVC_P_58:A11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT4","text":"The position of the Empyrean heaven remains less determinate because it is established by authority and fittingness rather than natural demonstration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT5","text":"The coherence of the two schemata of formlessness is preserved only if the lack of every form is constantly distinguished from the lack of adornment, and natural priority from temporal priority.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A7","CH_GGVC_P_58:A8","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT6","text":"The relation between angelic lack of times and the succession of angelic conceptions is not fully reconciled unless the former is referred to the Augustinian schema and the latter to the schema of temporal duration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:D11","CH_GGVC_P_58:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT7","text":"The influence of the immobile Empyrean heaven remains a probable joint: the analogy of angelic causality and stable power provide possibility, but do not demonstrate necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:A16","CH_GGVC_P_58:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT8","text":"Scriptural exposition retains a deliberate indeterminacy between the metaphysical signification of matter and the description of incompletely ordered elements.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_58:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: it distinguishes terms, removes impossibilities through contradiction, limits opinions to their proper senses, and establishes conclusions gradually according to the force of proof.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_58:FGS5","CH_GGVC_P_58:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_58:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_58@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_58:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 67","title":"First Part · Question 66","context":"Chapter 67","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 66"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 66","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 67","order":68,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_59"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_59@R001","sha256":"af34d9bab4cbe6d2cc1c85ab347a866b587796f2042aa7ef6d46e7f0e227298e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS1","text":"Quaestio de luce resolvitur distinguendo significationem primam nominis ab eius extensione usu loquentium recepta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS2","text":"Proprietas praedicationis spiritualis non ex obiecti dignitate sola, sed ex regula semantica qua nomen accipitur, determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS3","text":"Natura luminis corporalis per exclusionem corporis, formae substantialis et entis mere intentionalis constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS4","text":"Lumen ponitur qualitas activa corporis lucidi, ab agente dependens sed effectus naturales instrumentaliter producens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS5","text":"Productio lucis prima die explicatur ut prior formatio conditionis communissimae mundi, cum distinctione inter ordinem naturae, ordinem narrationis et ordinem motuum caelestium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS6","text":"Quaestio cosmologica in quaestionem de gradu formationis, communitate causali et aptitudine narrationis sacrae reconstituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A1","text":"Eiusdem nominis prima impositio et usus posterior ad diversa genera praedicationis pertinere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A2","text":"Nomen lucis primo significat id quod manifestationem sensui visus efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A3","text":"Nomen lucis usu extensum significare potest omne principium manifestationis cuiuscumque cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A4","text":"Duo corpora secundum naturam simul in eodem loco esse non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A5","text":"Illuminatio fit in instanti et ad diversas partes, ideo motus localis corporis esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A6","text":"Explicatio luminis ut corporis corruptionem, generationem vel congregationem corpoream sensui et rationi repugnantem postularet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A7","text":"Lumen aerem denominat et transmutationes naturales efficit; propterea esse mere intentionale non habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A8","text":"Forma substantialis per se sensibilis non est neque potest in uno subiecto substantialis et in alio accidentalis esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A9","text":"Lumen est qualitas activa consequens formam substantialem corporis a se lucentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A10","text":"Qualitas luminis non manet remoto luminari, quia illuminatio materiam ad formam substantialem suscipiendam non transmutat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A11","text":"Qualitas activa potest instrumentaliter operari in virtute formae substantialis sine eo quod ipsa sit forma substantialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A12","text":"In opere distinctionis prius formatur quod est primi corporis forma et quod communius communicatur quam quod est particulare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A13","text":"Narratio creationis potest vel formationem spiritualis naturae significare vel a sensibilibus rebus ex causa temporali et paedagogica initium capere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A14","text":"Lux primae diei intelligi potest ut virtus illuminativa solis communis et nondum ad effectus particulares determinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A15","text":"Distinctio diei et noctis communi motu caeli explicatur, dum diversitates dierum, mensium et annorum motibus propriis corporum caelestium attribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX1","text":"Lux spiritualis non est proprie dicta secundum primam nominis impositionem, quamvis proprie dici possit secundum usum extensum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX2","text":"Dignitas rei spiritualis non abrogat originem sensitivam significationis nominis lucis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX3","text":"Lumen non est corpus quod cum aere locum occupat aut per medium localiter fertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX4","text":"Lumen non est forma substantialis solis, aeris aut alterius corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX5","text":"Lumen non est similitudo mere intentionalis, qualis color in medio reputari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX6","text":"Tenebra non est contraria qualitas luci, sed privatio luminis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX7","text":"Productio lucis primae diei non postulat nubem lucidam transitoriam, materiam superfluam aut miraculosam contractionem luminis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX8","text":"Divisio spiritualis lucis a tenebris non requirit tenebras morales iam existentes in creatura spirituali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D1","text":"Praedicatio lucis de Deo vel de cognitione spirituali est metaphoricа ratione originis vocabuli, sed propria ratione usus vocabuli ad manifestationem universaliter extensi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A1","CH_GGVC_P_59:A2","CH_GGVC_P_59:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D2","text":"Lumen est accidens naturale actuale in medio illuminato, non ens materiale neque intentio sine efficacia naturali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A4","CH_GGVC_P_59:A5","CH_GGVC_P_59:A6","CH_GGVC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D3","text":"Dependentia luminis a luminari compatibilis est cum eius ratione qualitatis, quia non omnis qualitas eodem modo permanet post absentiam agentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A9","CH_GGVC_P_59:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D4","text":"Effectus luminis in formas inferiores et in visibilitatem colorum non elevant lumen ad statum formae substantialis, quia causalitas eius est instrumentalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A9","CH_GGVC_P_59:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D5","text":"Prioritas lucis in opere distinctionis est prioritas formationis communis et causaliter dispositivae, non prioritas absoluta omnis accidentis supra omnem substantiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A9","CH_GGVC_P_59:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D6","text":"Productio lucis primae diei et determinatio solis quarta die conciliantur per distinctionem virtutis illuminativae communis a virtute ad particulares effectus determinata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D7","text":"Narratio de luce potest simul admittere lectionem spiritualem Augustini et lectionem corporalem ordinatam ad sensibilia, sine necessitate unius causae narrationis omnibus interpretibus impositae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D8","text":"Dies et nox ante diversitates astronomicas particulares intelligi possunt, si motus communis caeli a motibus propriis siderum distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SD1","text":"Systema ordinem semanticum, ontologicum et cosmologicum subordinat: recta significatio vocabuli conditionem ponit ad rectam determinationem rei significatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:D1","CH_GGVC_P_59:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SD2","text":"Lumen fungitur ut medium inter formam substantialem et effectus sensibiles, quia ab illa derivatur et in virtute eius agit sine identitate cum illa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:D3","CH_GGVC_P_59:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SD3","text":"Ordo creationis describitur per transitum a conditionibus communibus ad determinationes particulares, ita ut prima lux sit principium distinctionis potius quam res cosmologica isolata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:D5","CH_GGVC_P_59:D6","CH_GGVC_P_59:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SD4","text":"Narratio sacra non simpliciter enumerat entia, sed ordinem formationis manifestat sub condicionibus capacitatis auditoris et ambitus narrationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:D7","CH_GGVC_P_59:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX1","text":"Non omne nomen quod de Deo aut de spiritualibus dicitur ibi secundum originariam impositionem proprie convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX2","text":"Efficacia causalis sensibilis non probat rem efficientem esse substantiam aut formam substantialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX3","text":"Instantaneitas apparentis effectus non licite reducitur ad motum localem corporis occulto tempore peractum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX4","text":"Absentia luminis non postulat positivum corpus tenebrarum neque corruptionem corporis luminosi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX5","text":"Ordo narrationis Geneseos non cogit ad lectionem in qua omne prius narratum temporaliter et complete ante omne posterius constitutum sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX6","text":"Institutio naturae primae non explicanda est per miraculum ad hoc fictum, ubi ratio ex naturis rerum sufficere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SNX1","text":"Prima principia distinctionis non sunt res maxime concretas et determinatas, sed conditiones communes per quas res particulares manifestari et distingui possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SNX2","text":"Tenebrae non constituunt principium positivum a luce coordinatum, sed defectum respectu principii manifestativi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SNX3","text":"Opus divinum non admittit entia cosmologica transitoria, superflua aut sine functione perseverante in institutione naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SNX4","text":"Creatura spiritualis non definiri debet per originariam privationem moralem, quia malitia daemonis futura praesciri potest sine eo quod creata sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:FGS1","text":"Impositio prima nominis → extensio per usum → duplex ratio proprietatis praedicationis spiritualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:FGS2","text":"Coexistentia luminis et aeris + instantaneitas illuminationis + imminutio absurditatum generationis → exclusio corporis → exclusio formae substantialis et intentionis merae → positio qualitatis activae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:FGS3","text":"Qualitas primi corporis + communitas luminis + prioritas communis ad particulare → prima formatio luminis → distinctio diei et noctis → determinatio ulterior effectuum sideralium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:FGS4","text":"Ambiguitas narrationis creationis → bifurcatio lectionis spiritualis et corporalis → conservatio ordinis formationis sine positura tenebrarum spiritualium originariarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AF1","text":"Ambiguitas vocabuli lucis → distinctio impositionis et usus → duplex proprietas praedicationis in spiritualibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AF2","text":"Apparentia physica luminis → probationes contra corpus → determinatio luminis ut qualitas activa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AF3","text":"Qualitas activa et communis → prioritas formativa → congruentia lucis primae diei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AF4","text":"Difficultas de sole, motu et tenebris → distinctio virtutis communis, motus communis et formationis spiritualis → conciliatio ordinis Geneseos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME1","text":"Proprietas nominum reclassificatur ex relatione univoca ad rem in relationem duplicem inter originem semanticam et usum linguarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME2","text":"Lumen reclassificatur ab obiecto mobili vel substantia ad qualitatem activam praesentiae-dependentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME3","text":"Tenebrae reclassificantur ab opposito positivo lucis ad privationem eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME4","text":"Prima dies reclassificatur ab initio accidentis isolati ad institutionem conditionis communis distinctionis cosmicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME5","text":"Ordo Geneseos reclassificatur ab mera successione rerum ad ordinem formationis, causalitatis et accommodationis narrationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ALT1","text":"Surface — Lux spiritualis proprie aut metaphorice dici potest; lumen corporale corpus, qualitas vel alia ratio entis esse quaeritur; primae diei congruentia examinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ALT2","text":"Structural — Relatio inter formam substantialem, qualitatem activam, subiectum recipiens, agens praesens et effectum instrumentalem lumen constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur per distinctiones semanticas, categorias ontologicas et ordines causales, non per repudiationem simplicem auctoritatis vel experientiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Tempus creationis distinguitur ab ordine formationis; prioritas communis, praesentia agentis et motus caeli condiciones rerum naturalium ordinant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT1","text":"Axiomata semantica, ontologica et cosmologica sufficiunt ad quattuor quaestiones restituendas, quia singulae conclusiones ex distinctione vocabuli, exclusionibus physicis et ordine formationis dependent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT2","text":"Firmitas maxima systematis est in convergentia trium probationum contra corporalitatem luminis: loci, motus et generationis vel corruptionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT3","text":"Classificatio luminis ut qualitatis activae cohaeret cum absentia permanentiae, quia dependentia ab agente per defectum transmutationis subiecti explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter lucem primae diei et solem quartae diei, quae distinctione virtutis communis et effectuum determinatorum conciliatur sed non ex principiis physicis independentibus demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT5","text":"Tensionem interpretativam servat duplex opinio de creatura spirituali: narratio potest vel eius formationem significare vel eam ex proposito narrationis praeterire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, si lux non tamquam unum obiectum simpliciter ponitur, sed tamquam nodus semanticus, physicus, causalis et exegeticus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164239902403Z_80af2ce9","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 67","source_sha256":"af34d9bab4cbe6d2cc1c85ab347a866b587796f2042aa7ef6d46e7f0e227298e","sha256":"47688c82a528823023a22db511c28e72dab2fd2906ee5c4a602a593b1d7cae77","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:42:39.903470+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS1","text":"The question concerning light is resolved by distinguishing the primary signification of the name from its extension accepted through the usage of speakers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS2","text":"The propriety of spiritual predication is determined not by the dignity of the object alone, but by the semantic rule according to which the name is taken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS3","text":"The nature of corporeal light is established through the exclusion of body, substantial form, and merely intentional being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS4","text":"Light is posited as an active quality of a luminous body, dependent on an agent yet instrumentally producing natural effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS5","text":"The production of light on the first day is explained as the prior formation of the most common condition of the world, with a distinction among the order of nature, the order of the narrative, and the order of celestial motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AS6","text":"The cosmological question is recast as a question concerning the grade of formation, causal commonality, and the suitability of sacred narrative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A1","text":"The first imposition of the same name and its later use can pertain to different kinds of predication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A2","text":"The name of light first signifies that which causes manifestation to the sense of sight.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A3","text":"By extended usage, the name of light can signify every principle of manifestation of any cognition whatsoever.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A4","text":"Two bodies cannot naturally be simultaneously in the same place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A5","text":"Illumination occurs in an instant and in different parts; therefore, it cannot be the local motion of a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A6","text":"An explanation of light as a body would require a corruption, generation, or corporeal aggregation contrary to sense and reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A7","text":"Light denominates the air and produces natural transformations; therefore, it does not have merely intentional being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A8","text":"A substantial form is not sensible through itself, nor can it be substantial in one subject and accidental in another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A9","text":"Light is an active quality consequent upon the substantial form of a body luminous through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A10","text":"The quality of light does not remain when the luminary is removed, because illumination does not transform matter so that it receives a substantial form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A11","text":"An active quality can operate instrumentally by the power of a substantial form without itself being a substantial form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A12","text":"In the work of distinction, that which is the form of the first body and that which is communicated more commonly is formed before what is particular.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A13","text":"The narrative of creation can either signify the formation of spiritual nature or begin from sensible things for a temporal and pedagogical reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A14","text":"The light of the first day can be understood as the illuminating power of the sun, common and not yet determined to particular effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:A15","text":"The distinction of day and night is explained by the common motion of the heaven, whereas the variations of days, months, and years are attributed to the proper motions of celestial bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX1","text":"Spiritual light is not properly so called according to the first imposition of the name, although it can properly be so called according to extended usage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX2","text":"The dignity of a spiritual thing does not abrogate the sensible origin of the signification of the name light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX3","text":"Light is not a body that occupies a place together with air or is locally conveyed through a medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX4","text":"Light is not the substantial form of the sun, air, or another body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX5","text":"Light is not a merely intentional likeness, such as color can be reckoned to be in a medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX6","text":"Darkness is not a quality contrary to light, but a privation of light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX7","text":"The production of light on the first day does not require a transient luminous cloud, superfluous matter, or a miraculous contraction of light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:NX8","text":"The division of spiritual light from darkness does not require moral darkness already existing in the spiritual creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D1","text":"The predication of light of God or of spiritual cognition is metaphorical by reason of the origin of the word, but proper by reason of the use of the word universally extended to manifestation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A1","CH_GGVC_P_59:A2","CH_GGVC_P_59:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D2","text":"Light is an actual natural accident in the illuminated medium, not a material being nor an intention without natural efficacy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A4","CH_GGVC_P_59:A5","CH_GGVC_P_59:A6","CH_GGVC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D3","text":"The dependence of light on the luminary is compatible with its character as a quality, because not every quality remains in the same way after the absence of the agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A9","CH_GGVC_P_59:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D4","text":"The effects of light upon lower forms and upon the visibility of colors do not elevate light to the status of a substantial form, because its causality is instrumental.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A9","CH_GGVC_P_59:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D5","text":"The priority of light in the work of distinction is the priority of common and causally dispositive formation, not the absolute priority of every accident over every substance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A9","CH_GGVC_P_59:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D6","text":"The production of light on the first day and the determination of the sun on the fourth day are reconciled through the distinction of common illuminating power from power determined to particular effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D7","text":"The narrative concerning light can simultaneously admit Augustine's spiritual reading and a corporeal reading ordered to sensible things, without the necessity of a single reason for the narrative imposed upon all interpreters.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:D8","text":"Day and night can be understood before particular astronomical variations, if the common motion of the heaven is distinguished from the proper motions of the stars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SD1","text":"The system subordinates semantic, ontological, and cosmological order: the correct signification of a word establishes the condition for the correct determination of the thing signified.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:D1","CH_GGVC_P_59:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SD2","text":"Light functions as a medium between substantial form and sensible effects, because it is derived from the former and acts by its power without being identical with it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:D3","CH_GGVC_P_59:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SD3","text":"The order of creation is described through a transition from common conditions to particular determinations, so that the first light is a principle of distinction rather than an isolated cosmological thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:D5","CH_GGVC_P_59:D6","CH_GGVC_P_59:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SD4","text":"Sacred narrative does not simply enumerate beings, but manifests the order of formation under the conditions of the hearer's capacity and the scope of the narrative.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_59:D7","CH_GGVC_P_59:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX1","text":"Not every name said of God or of spiritual things properly belongs there according to its original imposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX2","text":"Sensible causal efficacy does not prove that the efficient thing is a substance or a substantial form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX3","text":"The instantaneousness of an apparent effect may not lawfully be reduced to the local motion of a body accomplished in hidden time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX4","text":"The absence of light does not require a positive body of darkness or the corruption of a luminous body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX5","text":"The order of the narrative of Genesis does not compel a reading in which everything narrated earlier was temporally and completely established before everything later.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:DNX6","text":"The institution of first nature is not to be explained through a miracle invented for this purpose, where an account from the natures of things can suffice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SNX1","text":"The first principles of distinction are not the most concrete and determinate things, but common conditions through which particular things can be manifested and distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SNX2","text":"Darkness does not constitute a positive principle coordinated with light, but a defect in relation to the manifestative principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SNX3","text":"The divine work does not admit transient, superfluous, or functionless cosmological beings in the institution of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:SNX4","text":"The spiritual creature ought not to be defined by an original moral privation, because the future malice of the devil can be foreknown without its having been created.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:FGS1","text":"First imposition of the name → extension through use → twofold basis of the propriety of spiritual predication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:FGS2","text":"Coexistence of light and air + instantaneousness of illumination + avoidance of the absurdities of generation → exclusion of body → exclusion of substantial form and mere intention → positing of active quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:FGS3","text":"Quality of the first body + commonality of light + priority of the common over the particular → first formation of light → distinction of day and night → further determination of stellar effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:FGS4","text":"Ambiguity of the creation narrative → bifurcation into spiritual and corporeal readings → preservation of the order of formation without positing original spiritual darkness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AF1","text":"Ambiguity of the word light → distinction of imposition and use → twofold propriety of predication in spiritual things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AF2","text":"Physical appearance of light → proofs against body → determination of light as active quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AF3","text":"Active and common quality → formative priority → fittingness of the light of the first day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:AF4","text":"Difficulty concerning the sun, motion, and darkness → distinction of common power, common motion, and spiritual formation → reconciliation of the order of Genesis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME1","text":"The propriety of names is reclassified from a univocal relation to the thing into a twofold relation between semantic origin and linguistic usage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME2","text":"Light is reclassified from a mobile object or substance into an active quality dependent on presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME3","text":"Darkness is reclassified from a positive opposite of light into its privation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME4","text":"The first day is reclassified from the beginning of an isolated accident into the institution of a common condition of cosmic distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ME5","text":"The order of Genesis is reclassified from a mere succession of things into an order of formation, causality, and narrative accommodation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ALT1","text":"Surface — Spiritual light can be spoken of properly or metaphorically; corporeal light is investigated as to whether it is a body, a quality, or another mode of being; the fittingness of the first day is examined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ALT2","text":"Structural — The relation among substantial form, active quality, receiving subject, present agent, and instrumental effect constitutes light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved through semantic distinctions, ontological categories, and causal orders, not through a simple repudiation of authority or experience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The time of creation is distinguished from the order of formation; the priority of the common, the presence of the agent, and the motion of the heaven order the conditions of natural things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT1","text":"The semantic, ontological, and cosmological axioms suffice to reconstruct the four questions, because the individual conclusions depend upon the distinction of the word, physical exclusions, and the order of formation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT2","text":"The greatest strength of the system lies in the convergence of three proofs against the corporeality of light: place, motion, and generation or corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT3","text":"The classification of light as an active quality coheres with the absence of permanence, because dependence on the agent is explained through the lack of transformation of the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains between the light of the first day and the sun of the fourth day; it is reconciled through the distinction between common power and determinate effects, but is not demonstrated from independent physical principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT5","text":"The twofold opinion concerning the spiritual creature preserves an interpretive tension: the narrative can either signify its formation or pass it over on account of the purpose of the narrative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0068","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0079","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_59:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if light is posited not simply as a single object, but as a semantic, physical, causal, and exegetical node.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_59:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_59@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_59:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 68","title":"First Part · Question 67","context":"Chapter 68","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 67"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 67","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 68","order":69,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_60"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_60@R001","sha256":"dc869f5a95655804cf87f53bd8e44a134aae6439f37e97819e4826798771d630","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat quomodo firmamentum, aquae superiores, divisio aquarum et pluralitas caelorum intelligi possint salva veritate narrationis Genesis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS2","text":"Veritas Scripturae manet invariabilis, dum determinatio physica et semantica vocabulorum eius inter expositiones diversas variari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est exegetico-reconstructiva: enuntiatum revelatum cum cosmologiis et rationibus naturalibus compatibile efficitur per distinctionem sensuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS4","text":"Difficultas transit ab apparenti contradictione litterae ad quaestionem de referente terminorum firmamentum, aqua et caelum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS5","text":"Motus argumentationis procedit ab auctoritate textus ad exclusionem interpretationum naturaliter impossibilium, deinde ad ordinationem semanticam plurium sensuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A1","text":"Veritas Scripturae inconcusse tenenda est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A2","text":"Expositio particularis quae certa ratione falsa demonstratur non est pro sensu Scripturae retinenda.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","text":"Firmamentum secunda die factum potest significare vel caelum sidereum vel partem aeris nubibus condensandis aptam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A4","text":"Productio substantiae et formatio rei praeexistentis pertinent ad ordines operum diversos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A5","text":"Significatio dierum creationis ut successio temporis vel ut ordo naturae mutat iudicium de productione firmamenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A6","text":"Scriptura aquas supra firmamentum esse affirmat, et hae aquae corporaliter intelligendae sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A7","text":"Natura rerum secundum institutionem suam investiganda est, non per appellationem immediatam ad miraculum solvenda.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A8","text":"Nomen aquae potest elementum aquae, materiam informem vel corpora diaphana significare, pro ratione firmamenti accepti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A9","text":"Vapores supra caelum sidereum elevari non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A10","text":"Moyses rudibus loquens corpora sensibiliter manifesta exprimit et aerem invisibilem indirecte significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A11","text":"Caelum in Scripturis dicitur proprie, per participationem proprietatum caelestium et metaphorice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A12","text":"Unitas universi corporalis compatitur pluralitatem caelorum secundum regiones, sphaeras vel rationes denominationis distinctas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX1","text":"Expositio litteralis singularis non identificatur simpliciter cum veritate Scripturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX2","text":"Firmamentum non necessario est caelum sidereum in quo stellae fixae sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX3","text":"Aquae superiores non sunt substantiae spirituales rationales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX4","text":"Miraculum non est explanatio ordinaria inconvenientiae naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX5","text":"Aqua vaporabiliter resoluta supra caelum sidereum non collocatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX6","text":"Aqua Genesis non restringitur necessario ad elementum aquae eiusdem speciei et eiusdem loci naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D1","text":"Affirmatio aquarum superiorum statum existentiae conservat, dum natura, situs et modus earum sub interpretatione cosmologica relinquuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A1","CH_GGVC_P_60:A2","CH_GGVC_P_60:A6","CH_GGVC_P_60:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D2","text":"Formula firmamentum secunda die factum non per se significat primam productionem substantialem caeli siderei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A4","CH_GGVC_P_60:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D3","text":"Qualitas aquarum superiorum sequitur rationem firmamenti accepti, non intuitionem genericam de aqua gravi et fluida.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A6","CH_GGVC_P_60:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D4","text":"Divisio aquarum potest esse terminus locorum vel distinctio regionum generationis et quietis, non solum separatio efficiente causa facta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A8","CH_GGVC_P_60:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D5","text":"Silentium explicitum de aere non est negatio aeris, sed dispositio pedagogica qua corpus minus manifestum sub vocabulo aquae intelligi potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A8","CH_GGVC_P_60:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D6","text":"Numerus caelorum pendet a scala qua corpus caeleste sumitur, sive ut universitas corporalis sive ut regio vel sphaera distincta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A11","CH_GGVC_P_60:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SD1","text":"Systema distinguit inter enuntiatum revelatum immutabile et vehiculum cosmologicum mutabile quo enuntiatum explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A1","CH_GGVC_P_60:A2","CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SD2","text":"Contradictiones apparentes de tempore, situ et numero rerum caelestium convertuntur in electiones conditionales inter sensus, cosmologias et gradus denominationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A4","CH_GGVC_P_60:A5","CH_GGVC_P_60:A11","CH_GGVC_P_60:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SD3","text":"Ratio naturalis munus negativum et selectivum obtinet: falsas expositiones excludit, sed veritatem Scripturae ut talem non evacuat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A1","CH_GGVC_P_60:A2","CH_GGVC_P_60:A7","CH_GGVC_P_60:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod singulum vocabulum Scripturae unam et immobilem referentiam physicam sine interpretatione imponat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod perceptibilitas rudium sit mensura omnium corporum realium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod difficultas naturalis per miraculum invocatum sufficienter dissolvatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod unitas et pluralitas caelorum sint praedicata simpliciter quantitativa, nullo respectu ad rationem qua caelum dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SNX1","text":"Inadmissibilis est interpres qui expositionem suam particularem cum sensu revelato sine residuo identificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SNX2","text":"Inadmissibilis est conflictus stabilis inter verum sensum Scripturae et rationem certo demonstratam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS1","text":"Veritas revelata immota → separatio enuntiati Scripturae ab expositione particulari corrigibili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS2","text":"Ambiguitas firmamenti, aquae et caeli → pluralitas referentium cosmologicorum admissibilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS3","text":"Cosmologia firmamenti et ratio dierum → iudicium de creatione substantiali vel de formatione secundae diei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS4","text":"Impossibilitas naturalis demonstrata → exclusio ramorum interpretativorum et interdictio solutionis miraculosae ordinariae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS5","text":"Accommodatio ad sensum communem → extensio semantica aquae et caeli → explicatio divisionis aquarum et pluralitatis caelorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF1","text":"Enuntiata Genesis de firmamento, aquis et caelis movent difficultatem de ordine naturali et de proprietate vocabulorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF2","text":"Difficultas → distinctio inter veritatem Scripturae et expositionem determinatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF3","text":"Distinctio hermeneutica → distributio interpretationum secundum varias cosmologias firmamenti et dierum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF4","text":"Distributio cosmologica → exclusio impossibilium naturalium et reinterpretatio aquarum per materiam, diaphaneitatem vel vapores.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF5","text":"Reclassificatio aquae → explicatio divisionis et transitus ad caelum ut nomen analogum plurium ordinum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ME1","text":"Auctoritas Scripturae et determinatio cosmologica separantur in duas ordinationes: prima affirmat, secunda exponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ME2","text":"Firmamentum, aqua et caelum non amplius sunt obiecta univoca, sed termini quorum referens ex contextu cosmologico et semantico determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ME3","text":"Divisio aquarum reclassificatur ab imagine parietis inter duas massas liquidas ad relationem limitis, regionis et ordinis generationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ME4","text":"Oppositio unum caelum vel plures caeli dissolvitur per distinctionem inter universitatem corporalem, regiones naturales, sphaeras et usus metaphoricus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus directe quaerit de productione firmamenti, aquis superioribus, divisione aquarum et numero caelorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ALT2","text":"Structural — Argumentatio ordinatur per relationem inter semanticas Scripturae, cosmologias physicas, ordinem creationis et distinctiones locorum naturalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Textus fidem a ruina expositionis falsificatae defendit, dum rationi naturale munus exclusionis interpretationum tribuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creatio, formatio, incorruptibilitas caelestis, temporis successio et ordo naturae constituunt diversas condiciones entium cosmologicorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT1","text":"Systema extractum sufficit ad restituendam distinctionem principalem inter veritatem revelatam invariabilem et expositiones cosmologicas mutabiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT2","text":"Systema sufficit ad explicandam cur firmamentum, aqua et caelum plures referentias recipiant sine negatione enuntiatorum Scripturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT3","text":"Cohaerentia interna maxime nititur in regula qua ratio certa corrigit expositionem, non veritatem Scripturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet quia flexibilitas semantica vocabulorum aquae et caeli determinatum contentum physicum enuntiatorum late suspendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet quia rationes naturales interpretationes falsas removere possunt, sed regula interna non semper unice decernit quae cosmologia vera sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT6","text":"Reconstructio motum textus servat: auctoritas → distinctio expositionum → examen naturale → extensio semantica → reconciliatio cosmologica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164259129861Z_636bd76e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 68","source_sha256":"dc869f5a95655804cf87f53bd8e44a134aae6439f37e97819e4826798771d630","sha256":"07a511108d34a90377d9392a7252f5ff206c9fe56915ca6d54753df8cd5c8f52","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:42:59.130811+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS1","text":"The question investigates how the firmament, the upper waters, the division of the waters, and the plurality of heavens may be understood while preserving the truth of the Genesis narrative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS2","text":"The truth of Scripture remains invariable, while the physical and semantic determination of its terms may vary among different expositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS3","text":"The argumentation is exegetical-reconstructive: the revealed statement is made compatible with cosmologies and natural reasons through a distinction of senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS4","text":"The difficulty passes from the apparent contradiction of the letter to the question of the referent of the terms firmament, water, and heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from the authority of the text to the exclusion of naturally impossible interpretations, then to the semantic ordering of several senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A1","text":"The truth of Scripture must be held unwaveringly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A2","text":"A particular exposition that is demonstrated false by certain reasoning is not to be retained as the sense of Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","text":"The firmament made on the second day can signify either the starry heaven or a part of the air suited to the condensation of clouds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A4","text":"The production of substance and the formation of a pre-existing thing belong to different orders of works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A5","text":"The meaning of the days of creation as a succession of time or as an order of nature alters the judgment concerning the production of the firmament.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A6","text":"Scripture affirms that waters are above the firmament, and these waters must be understood corporeally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A7","text":"The nature of things must be investigated according to their institution, not resolved by immediate appeal to miracle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A8","text":"The name water can signify the element of water, formless matter, or diaphanous bodies, according to the account of the firmament adopted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A9","text":"Vapors cannot be raised above the starry heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A10","text":"Moses, speaking to the unlearned, expresses bodies manifest to the senses and signifies invisible air indirectly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A11","text":"Heaven is spoken of in the Scriptures properly, by participation in heavenly properties, and metaphorically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:A12","text":"The unity of the corporeal universe is compatible with a plurality of heavens according to distinct regions, spheres, or grounds of denomination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX1","text":"A single literal exposition is not simply identified with the truth of Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX2","text":"The firmament is not necessarily the starry heaven in which the fixed stars are located.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX3","text":"The upper waters are not rational spiritual substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX4","text":"Miracle is not the ordinary explanation of a natural incongruity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX5","text":"Water resolved into vapor is not placed above the starry heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:NX6","text":"The water of Genesis is not necessarily restricted to the element of water of the same species and the same natural place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D1","text":"The affirmation of the upper waters preserves their state of existence, while their nature, location, and mode are left under cosmological interpretation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A1","CH_GGVC_P_60:A2","CH_GGVC_P_60:A6","CH_GGVC_P_60:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D2","text":"The formula that the firmament was made on the second day does not in itself signify the first substantial production of the starry heaven.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A4","CH_GGVC_P_60:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D3","text":"The quality of the upper waters follows the account of the firmament adopted, not a generic intuition concerning water as heavy and fluid.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A6","CH_GGVC_P_60:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D4","text":"The division of the waters can be a boundary of places or a distinction of regions of generation and rest, not merely a separation effected by an efficient cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A8","CH_GGVC_P_60:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D5","text":"Explicit silence concerning air is not a negation of air, but a pedagogical arrangement by which a less manifest body may be understood under the term water.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A8","CH_GGVC_P_60:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:D6","text":"The number of heavens depends upon the scale at which a heavenly body is taken, whether as the corporeal universe or as a distinct region or sphere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A11","CH_GGVC_P_60:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SD1","text":"The system distinguishes between the immutable revealed statement and the mutable cosmological vehicle by which the statement is explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A1","CH_GGVC_P_60:A2","CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SD2","text":"Apparent contradictions concerning time, location, and the number of heavenly things are converted into conditional choices among senses, cosmologies, and levels of denomination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A3","CH_GGVC_P_60:A4","CH_GGVC_P_60:A5","CH_GGVC_P_60:A11","CH_GGVC_P_60:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SD3","text":"Natural reason has a negative and selective function: it excludes false expositions, but does not thereby evacuate the truth of Scripture as such.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_60:A1","CH_GGVC_P_60:A2","CH_GGVC_P_60:A7","CH_GGVC_P_60:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:DNX1","text":"It must be false that each term of Scripture imposes one fixed physical referent without interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the perceptibility of the unlearned is the measure of all real bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:DNX3","text":"It must be false that a natural difficulty is sufficiently dissolved by an invoked miracle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the unity and plurality of heavens are predicates simply quantitative, without regard to the account according to which heaven is spoken of.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SNX1","text":"An interpreter who identifies his particular exposition without remainder with the revealed sense is inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:SNX2","text":"A stable conflict between the true sense of Scripture and certainly demonstrated reason is inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS1","text":"Immovable revealed truth → separation of the statement of Scripture from corrigible particular exposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS2","text":"Ambiguity of firmament, water, and heaven → plurality of admissible cosmological referents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS3","text":"Cosmology of the firmament and account of the days → judgment concerning substantial creation or formation on the second day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS4","text":"Demonstrated natural impossibility → exclusion of interpretative branches and prohibition of ordinary miraculous solution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:FGS5","text":"Accommodation to common sense → semantic extension of water and heaven → explanation of the division of the waters and the plurality of heavens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF1","text":"The statements of Genesis concerning the firmament, waters, and heavens raise a difficulty concerning natural order and the propriety of terms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF2","text":"Difficulty → distinction between the truth of Scripture and determinate exposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF3","text":"Hermeneutical distinction → distribution of interpretations according to various cosmologies of the firmament and the days.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF4","text":"Cosmological distribution → exclusion of natural impossibilities and reinterpretation of waters through matter, diaphaneity, or vapors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:AF5","text":"Reclassification of water → explanation of division and transition to heaven as an analogous name of several orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ME1","text":"The authority of Scripture and cosmological determination are separated into two orders: the first affirms, the second explains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ME2","text":"Firmament, water, and heaven are no longer univocal objects, but terms whose referent is determined by cosmological and semantic context.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ME3","text":"The division of the waters is reclassified from the image of a wall between two liquid masses to a relation of boundary, region, and order of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ME4","text":"The opposition of one heaven or several heavens is dissolved through the distinction between the corporeal universe, natural regions, spheres, and metaphorical uses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text directly asks concerning the production of the firmament, the upper waters, the division of the waters, and the number of heavens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ALT2","text":"Structural — The argumentation is ordered through the relation among the semantics of Scripture, physical cosmologies, the order of creation, and distinctions of natural places.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text defends faith from the collapse of a falsified exposition, while assigning to natural reason the function of excluding interpretations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creation, formation, celestial incorruptibility, succession of time, and order of nature constitute diverse conditions of cosmological beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT1","text":"The extracted system suffices to restore the principal distinction between invariable revealed truth and mutable cosmological expositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT2","text":"The system suffices to explain why firmament, water, and heaven admit several referents without negation of the statements of Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence rests most of all on the rule by which certain reason corrects exposition, not the truth of Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains because the semantic flexibility of the terms water and heaven broadly suspends the determinate physical content of the statements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT5","text":"A fragile juncture remains because natural reasons can remove false interpretations, but the internal rule does not always determine uniquely which cosmology is true.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_60:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: authority → distinction of expositions → natural examination → semantic extension → cosmological reconciliation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_60:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_60@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_60:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 69","title":"First Part · Question 68","context":"Chapter 69","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 68"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 68","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 69","order":70,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_61"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_61@R001","sha256":"c403ecbc6daef20100c4fe18ff130789dbee622d38c86519d82a3d1d33af740a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat utrum congregatio aquarum et productio plantarum tertiae diei convenienter attribuantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS2","text":"Argumentatio difficultatem litterae resolvit distinguendo ordinem originis et naturae ab ordine durationis, quos expositiones Augustini et aliorum doctorum diverse constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS3","text":"Opus tertiae diei intelligitur ut remotio duplicis informitatis terrae: occultationis sub aquis et carentiae decoris convenientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS4","text":"Congregatio aquarum et apparentia aridae non solum motum localem, sed formationem elementarem, distinctionem loci et ordinationem ad finem viventium significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS5","text":"Productio plantarum ad formationem terrae refertur quia plantas, propter vitam occultam et immobilitatem, quasi ornamentum terrae Scriptura tractat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS6","text":"Argumentatio est reconstructiva et conciliativa: eadem littera sive causalem institutionem sive actualem primarum specierum productionem sustinere potest, dummodo creatio originalis a propagatione rerum distinguatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","text":"Ordo narrationis creationis potest ordinem originis et naturae significare sine ordine durationis temporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A2","text":"Expositio quae ordinem durationis admittit non materiam omnino informem, sed materiam carentem distinctione debita et pulchritudine consummata ponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A3","text":"In expositione Augustini, congregatio aquarum et apparentia aridae significant impressionem formarum substantialium aquae et terrae in materiam corporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A4","text":"In expositione aliorum doctorum, tertia dies format corpus inferius per discoopertionem terrae ab aquis et per distinctionem terrae a mari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A5","text":"Forma aquae ad fluxum mobilem, forma terrae ad stabilitatem visibilem ordinatur; ideo tertiae diei effectus per congregationem et apparentiam exprimitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A6","text":"Motus naturalis corporum a divina iussione principium naturae accipit et ad finem divinitus ordinatum subordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","text":"Terra tertia die dupliciter informis erat: aquis cooperta et decore plantarum carens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A8","text":"Vita plantarum est occulta, quia plantis desunt motus localis et sensus, quibus animatum maxime manifestatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A9","text":"Creatio originalis rerum et propagatio posterior rerum sunt operationes formaliter distinguendae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A10","text":"Secundum Augustinum, plantae tertia die causaliter in terra institutae sunt, non necessario actu in speciebus suis productae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A11","text":"Secundum alios expositores, species plantarum tertia die actu institui potuerunt, dum generatio similium ex similibus ad administrationem rerum pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A12","text":"Nominatio scripturalis potest materiam, elementum, proprietatem principalem vel denominationem relativam significare, non univoce idem obiectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A13","text":"Narratio Moysis ea praecipue proponit quae manifeste apparent et sensibiliter distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX1","text":"Materia prima non describitur necessario ut privatio absoluta omnis formae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX2","text":"Tertiae diei ordo non est necessario successio temporalis aquarum prius terram tegentium et postea recedentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX3","text":"Congregatio aquarum non postulat omnes aquas materialiter continuas in uno loco geometrico consistere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX4","text":"Motus naturalis aquae non excludit iussionem divinam, quia ipsa natura motus divinitus datur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX5","text":"Productio plantarum non propter vitam earum necessario ad opus ornatus animalium transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX6","text":"Spinae et tribuli non sunt per se effectus posterioris maledictionis, sed maledictio eorum relationem poenalem ad hominem constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX7","text":"Omissio metallorum et lapidum a narratione non eorum absentiam ex formatione terrae significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D1","text":"Congregatio aquarum, secundum expositionem Augustini, non requirit praevium statum terrae temporaliter aquis coopertae, quia cum ipsa congregatione formae aquae et terrae producuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","CH_GGVC_P_61:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D2","text":"Secundum expositionem temporalem, discoopertio terrae explicari potest per elevationem aquarum, densationem aquae prius rarae, vel receptacula concava terrae; prima via probabilior proponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A2","CH_GGVC_P_61:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D3","text":"Unitas congregationis aquarum est unitas termini maris vel separatio relativa a terra sicca, non unitas simplicis loci absoluti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A4","CH_GGVC_P_61:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D4","text":"Necessitas terrae discooperiendae non reducitur ad physicam aquae inclinationem, sed procedit ex fine secundum quem plantae et animalia super terram esse debent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A5","CH_GGVC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D5","text":"Productio plantarum est consummatio formationis terrae, quia plantas terrae quasi vestimentum et decor conveniens praebent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","CH_GGVC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D6","text":"Differentia inter productionem causalem et actualem plantarum pendet ex distinctione inter institutionem originalem naturarum et generationem propagativam earum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A9","CH_GGVC_P_61:A10","CH_GGVC_P_61:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D7","text":"Nomen terrae potest primo materiam vel naturam communem et postea aridam aquis discoopertam designare, sine contradictione denominationum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D8","text":"Scriptura visibilia et manifeste distincta narrando plantas commemorat, mineralia vero tacet quia eorum generatio occulta est et a terra sensibiliter parum separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SD1","text":"Ordo creationis describitur ut hierarchia perfectionis, a natura spirituali ad corpora superiora et inde ad elementa inferiora, etiam ubi ordo temporalis negatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","CH_GGVC_P_61:A3","CH_GGVC_P_61:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SD2","text":"Causalitas divina non naturam evacuans, sed naturas, motus proprios et fines eorum instituens intelligitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A5","CH_GGVC_P_61:A6","CH_GGVC_P_61:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SD3","text":"Tertia dies efficit transitum ab indistinctione terrestri ad terram habitabilem, visibilem et vegetabilem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A4","CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","CH_GGVC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SD4","text":"Narratio creationis est selective phenomenologica: ordinem naturalem manifestat secundum ea quae apparent, non secundum enumerationem exhaustivam omnium entium corporalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A12","CH_GGVC_P_61:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX1","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem assumptionis quod omnis distinctio narrationis cosmologicae sit successio temporalis homogena.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX2","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem oppositionis inter causalitatem divinam et motum naturalem corporum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX3","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem assumptionis quod creatio sit solum productio rerum iam actu completarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX4","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem univocitatis nominum cosmologicorum, praesertim terrae, caeli et diei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX5","text":"Systema requirit falsitatem principii quod sola vita manifesta per sensum et motum localem ad ordinem viventium pertineat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio circumagit impossibilitatem describendi creationem per solam temporalem antecessionem, quia origo formalis et ordo perfectionis temporalitatem excedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio excludit naturam ut sphaeram autonomam cuius motus et fines sine fundamento divino intelligi possint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SNX3","text":"Argumentatio excludit visibilitatem narrationis tamquam mensuram exhaustivam entis, quia invisibilia, occulta et causaliter instituta ad rerum ordinem pertinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS1","text":"Informitas nominata → distinctio interpretativa inter originem et durationem → determinatio modi formationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS2","text":"Materia corporalis indeterminata → impressio formarum aquae et terrae → fluxus aquae et stabilitas aridae → congregatio et apparentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS3","text":"Terra aquis cooperta et decore carens → separatio aquarum → arida visibilis → vegetatio ut decor terrae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS4","text":"Institutio originalis naturarum → virtus causalis vel prima institutio actualis specierum → propagatio similium ex similibus in administratione rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS5","text":"Nomen commune vel ambiguum → proprietas principalis vel relatio distinctiva → denominatio contextualiter determinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF1","text":"Inconvenientia apparens tertiae diei → distinctio ordinis originis ab ordine durationis → duplex expositio formationis elementorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF2","text":"Congregatio aquarum → formae aquae et terrae vel separatio temporalis aquarum → arida distincta a mari → terra ordinata ad vitam terrestrialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF3","text":"Duplex informitas terrae → remotio occultationis → remotio indecoris → productio plantarum ut consummatio terrae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF4","text":"Ambiguitas productionis plantarum → distinctio creationis originalis et propagationis → institutio causalis Augustini vel productio actualis aliorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF5","text":"Ambiguitas nominum et omissionum → denominatio relativa et selectio visibilium → cohaerentia litterae cosmologicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME1","text":"Dies creationis reclassificantur: non necessario partes chronologiae, sed gradus originis, perfectionis et formationis naturarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME2","text":"Congregatio aquarum reclassificatur: non mera translatio localis, sed signum formae elementaris, distinctionis terrestris et ordinationis teleologicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME3","text":"Plantae reclassificantur: non simpliciter animalia imperfecta nec mera res ornatus, sed principium quo terra suum decorem et aptitudinem manifestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME4","text":"Maledictio terrae reclassificatur: non nova institutio spinis et tribulis data, sed mutatio relationis eorum ad laborem hominis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME5","text":"Silentium narrationis reclassificatur: non negatio entium occultorum, sed modus repraesentationis secundum manifestam sensibilitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus defendit convenientiam congregationis aquarum, apparitionis aridae et productionis plantarum tertiae diei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ALT2","text":"Structural — Informitas, forma substantialis, distinctio elementorum, motus naturalis et decor terrae constituunt mechanismum formationis mundi inferioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Difficultates litterae solvuntur non per unam expositionem exclusivam, sed per distinctiones quae expositionem Augustini et expositiones temporales formaliter ordinant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Esse rerum distinguitur inter originem causalem, formationem naturalem, actualitatem specierum et propagationem temporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de duplici ordine, formatione elementorum, duplici informitate terrae et distinctione creationis a propagatione sufficiunt ad motum principalem argumentationis restituendum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","CH_GGVC_P_61:A3","CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","CH_GGVC_P_61:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT2","text":"Systema firmissime cohaeret ubi congregatio aquarum, apparentia aridae et vegetatio sub unica ratione formationis terrae colliguntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A4","CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","CH_GGVC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT3","text":"Commissura principalis manet inter expositionem Augustini, quae ordinem temporalem negat et productionem plantarum causaliter intelligit, et expositionem aliorum, quae successionem temporalem et productionem actualem admittit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","CH_GGVC_P_61:A2","CH_GGVC_P_61:A10","CH_GGVC_P_61:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT4","text":"Textus has expositiones iuxta se disponit potius quam unicum principium decisivum quo earum incompatibilitates omnino dissolvantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT5","text":"Relatio inter causam divinam, motum naturalem aquae et actiones secundarias, ut solis evaporatio, hierarchice asseritur, sed modus exactus cooperationis non ulterius determinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus, quia ab objectionibus de littera ad distinctiones ontologicas, temporales, teleologicas et semanticas procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164323265487Z_13a188a6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 69","source_sha256":"c403ecbc6daef20100c4fe18ff130789dbee622d38c86519d82a3d1d33af740a","sha256":"bfbc20eebdd69a2e1015300fb7cd23a1bf1940a8cd590cd4e4c248e34292f3b4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:43:23.267309+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS1","text":"The question examines whether the gathering of the waters and the production of plants are fittingly attributed to the third day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS2","text":"The argument resolves the difficulty of the letter by distinguishing the order of origin and nature from the order of duration, which Augustine's exposition and those of other doctors establish differently.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS3","text":"The work of the third day is understood as the removal of the earth's twofold formlessness: its concealment beneath the waters and its lack of fitting adornment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS4","text":"The gathering of the waters and the appearance of the dry land signify not only local motion, but elemental formation, distinction of place, and ordering to the end of living things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS5","text":"The production of plants is referred to the formation of the earth because Scripture treats plants, on account of their hidden life and immobility, as though they were an ornament of the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AS6","text":"The argument is reconstructive and conciliatory: the same letter can sustain either the causal institution or the actual production of the first species, provided that original creation is distinguished from the propagation of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","text":"The order of the creation narrative can signify the order of origin and nature without signifying an order of temporal duration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A2","text":"An exposition that admits an order of duration posits not matter altogether formless, but matter lacking due distinction and consummate beauty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A3","text":"In Augustine's exposition, the gathering of the waters and the appearance of the dry land signify the impressing of the substantial forms of water and earth upon corporeal matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A4","text":"In the exposition of other doctors, the third day forms the lower body through the uncovering of the earth from the waters and through the distinction of earth from sea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A5","text":"The form of water is ordered to mobile flow, and the form of earth to visible stability; therefore the effect of the third day is expressed through gathering and appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A6","text":"The natural motion of bodies receives from the divine command the principle of nature and is subordinated to the divinely ordered end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","text":"On the third day the earth was formless in two ways: covered by waters and lacking the adornment of plants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A8","text":"The life of plants is hidden, because plants lack local motion and sense, by which the animate is most manifested.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A9","text":"The original creation of things and the subsequent propagation of things are operations to be formally distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A10","text":"According to Augustine, plants were instituted causally in the earth on the third day, not necessarily actually produced in their species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A11","text":"According to other expositors, the species of plants could have been actually instituted on the third day, while the generation of like from like belongs to the governance of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A12","text":"Scriptural naming can signify matter, an element, a principal property, or a relative denomination, and not univocally the same object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:A13","text":"Moses's narrative chiefly sets forth those things that plainly appear and are sensibly distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX1","text":"Prime matter is not necessarily described as the absolute privation of every form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX2","text":"The order of the third day is not necessarily a temporal succession in which waters first cover the earth and afterward recede.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX3","text":"The gathering of the waters does not require all waters to remain materially continuous in one geometrical place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX4","text":"The natural motion of water does not exclude the divine command, because the very nature of motion is given divinely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX5","text":"The production of plants is not necessarily transferred to the work of the adornment of animals on account of their life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX6","text":"Thorns and thistles are not in themselves effects of the subsequent curse; rather, the curse establishes their penal relation to man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:NX7","text":"The omission of metals and stones from the narrative does not signify their absence from the formation of the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D1","text":"The gathering of the waters, according to Augustine's exposition, does not require a prior temporal state of the earth covered by waters, because with the gathering itself the forms of water and earth are produced.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","CH_GGVC_P_61:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D2","text":"According to the temporal exposition, the uncovering of the earth can be explained through the elevation of the waters, the condensation of water previously rarefied, or the concave receptacles of the earth; the first way is proposed as more probable.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A2","CH_GGVC_P_61:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D3","text":"The unity of the gathering of the waters is the unity of the boundary of the sea or relative separation from dry land, not the unity of a simple absolute place.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A4","CH_GGVC_P_61:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D4","text":"The necessity of uncovering the earth is not reduced to the physical inclination of water, but proceeds from the end according to which plants and animals ought to exist upon the earth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A5","CH_GGVC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D5","text":"The production of plants is the consummation of the formation of the earth, because plants furnish the earth with, as it were, clothing and fitting adornment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","CH_GGVC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D6","text":"The difference between the causal and actual production of plants depends upon the distinction between the original institution of natures and their propagative generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A9","CH_GGVC_P_61:A10","CH_GGVC_P_61:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D7","text":"The name earth can designate first matter or common nature, and afterward the dry land uncovered by waters, without contradiction of denominations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:D8","text":"By narrating visible and plainly distinct things, Scripture mentions plants, but is silent about minerals because their generation is hidden and they are sensibly little separated from the earth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SD1","text":"The order of creation is described as a hierarchy of perfection, from spiritual nature to higher bodies and thence to lower elements, even where temporal order is denied.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","CH_GGVC_P_61:A3","CH_GGVC_P_61:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SD2","text":"Divine causality is understood not as emptying nature, but as instituting natures, their proper motions, and their ends.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A5","CH_GGVC_P_61:A6","CH_GGVC_P_61:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SD3","text":"The third day effects a transition from terrestrial indistinction to inhabitable, visible, and vegetated earth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A4","CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","CH_GGVC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SD4","text":"The creation narrative is selectively phenomenological: it manifests the natural order according to what appears, not according to an exhaustive enumeration of all corporeal beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A12","CH_GGVC_P_61:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX1","text":"The system requires the falsity of the assumption that every distinction in cosmological narrative is homogeneous temporal succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX2","text":"The system requires the falsity of the opposition between divine causality and the natural motion of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX3","text":"The system requires the falsity of the assumption that creation is only the production of things already actually complete.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX4","text":"The system requires the falsity of the univocity of cosmological names, especially earth, heaven, and day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:DNX5","text":"The system requires the falsity of the principle that only life manifest through sense and local motion belongs to the order of living things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SNX1","text":"The argument revolves around the impossibility of describing creation through temporal precedence alone, because formal origin and the order of perfection exceed temporality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SNX2","text":"The argument excludes nature as an autonomous sphere whose motions and ends can be understood without a divine foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:SNX3","text":"The argument excludes the visibility of narrative as an exhaustive measure of being, because invisible, hidden, and causally instituted things belong to the order of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS1","text":"Named formlessness → interpretive distinction between origin and duration → determination of the mode of formation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS2","text":"Indeterminate corporeal matter → impressing of the forms of water and earth → flow of water and stability of dry land → gathering and appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS3","text":"Earth covered by waters and lacking adornment → separation of waters → visible dry land → vegetation as adornment of the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS4","text":"Original institution of natures → causal power or first actual institution of species → propagation of like from like in the governance of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:FGS5","text":"Common or ambiguous name → principal property or distinctive relation → contextually determined denomination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF1","text":"Apparent unfittingness of the third day → distinction of the order of origin from the order of duration → twofold exposition of the formation of the elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF2","text":"Gathering of the waters → forms of water and earth or temporal separation of waters → dry land distinct from sea → earth ordered to terrestrial life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF3","text":"Twofold formlessness of the earth → removal of concealment → removal of lack of adornment → production of plants as the consummation of the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF4","text":"Ambiguity of the production of plants → distinction between original creation and propagation → Augustine's causal institution or the actual production of others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:AF5","text":"Ambiguity of names and omissions → relative denomination and selection of visible things → coherence of the cosmological letter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME1","text":"The days of creation are reclassified: not necessarily parts of chronology, but degrees of origin, perfection, and formation of natures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME2","text":"The gathering of the waters is reclassified: not mere local translation, but a sign of elemental form, terrestrial distinction, and teleological ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME3","text":"Plants are reclassified: not simply imperfect animals nor mere things of adornment, but a principle by which the earth manifests its own beauty and fitness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME4","text":"The curse of the earth is reclassified: not a new institution given to thorns and thistles, but a change in their relation to human labor.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ME5","text":"The silence of the narrative is reclassified: not a denial of hidden beings, but a mode of representation according to manifest sensibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text defends the fittingness of the gathering of the waters, the appearance of dry land, and the production of plants on the third day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ALT2","text":"Structural — Formlessness, substantial form, distinction of the elements, natural motion, and the adornment of the earth constitute the mechanism of formation of the lower world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Difficulties of the letter are resolved not through one exclusive exposition, but through distinctions that formally order Augustine's exposition and temporal expositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The being of things is distinguished among causal origin, natural formation, the actuality of species, and temporal propagation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning the twofold order, the formation of the elements, the earth's twofold formlessness, and the distinction of creation from propagation suffice to restore the principal movement of the argument.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","CH_GGVC_P_61:A3","CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","CH_GGVC_P_61:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT2","text":"The system coheres most firmly where the gathering of the waters, the appearance of dry land, and vegetation are gathered under the single account of the formation of the earth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A4","CH_GGVC_P_61:A7","CH_GGVC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT3","text":"The principal joint remains between Augustine's exposition, which denies temporal order and understands the production of plants causally, and the exposition of others, which admits temporal succession and actual production.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A1","CH_GGVC_P_61:A2","CH_GGVC_P_61:A10","CH_GGVC_P_61:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT4","text":"The text sets these expositions alongside one another rather than providing a single decisive principle by which their incompatibilities are wholly dissolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT5","text":"The relation among divine cause, the natural motion of water, and secondary actions, such as the evaporation of the sun, is asserted hierarchically, but the exact mode of cooperation is not further determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_61:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text, because it proceeds from objections concerning the letter to ontological, temporal, teleological, and semantic distinctions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_61:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_61@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_61:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 70","title":"First Part · Question 69","context":"Chapter 70","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 69"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 69","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 70","order":71,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_62"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_62@R001","sha256":"8eab39c5b0f88bb0b8b8d793c8e614002f10878ddbb895db4840368ec2c76510","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS1","text":"Quaestio locum luminarium in opere ornatus, fines eorum et modum quo animata vel inanimata dicantur determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS2","text":"Argumentatio est exegetico-reconstructiva, cum ordinatio Geneseos per distinctiones metaphysicas creationis, distinctionis, ornatus, causalitatis et motus explicetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS3","text":"Quaestio de quarto die a mera prioritate materiali vel causali ad correspondentiam inter regiones mundi, res mobiles et opus ornatus transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS4","text":"Quaestio de fine luminarium ad ministerium humanum restringitur, ut significatio corporalis admittatur sine divinizatione siderum vel determinatione liberi arbitrii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS5","text":"Quaestio de animatione a dignitate apparenti vel motu visibili ad necessitatem operationum animae et ad relationem motoris spiritualis ad corpus mobile transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS6","text":"Motus conclusivus corpora caelestia constituit ut instrumenta ordinata, quae moventur et causant sub virtute motoris apprehendentis, non ut animalia per animam formaliter unitam viventia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","text":"Opera divina tripliciter distinguuntur in creationem, distinctionem et ornamentum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","text":"Creatio caelum et terram informia producit, dum distinctio ea vel per formas substantiales vel per convenientem decorem et ordinem perficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A3","text":"Perfectio ad ea pertinet quae caelo et terrae intrinseca sunt, ornamentum vero ad res ab eis distinctas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A4","text":"Distinctio rerum maxime per motum localem manifestatur; ideo res mobiles ad opus ornatus pertinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A5","text":"Ornatus respondet triplici regione caeli, medii elementi et terrae: luminaria caelum, aves et pisces aerem et aquam, animalia terrestria terram ornant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A6","text":"Luminaria producuntur in actu, non in sola potentia firmamenti, quia firmamentum virtutem productivam eorum non habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","text":"Moyses, ut populum ab idololatria revocaret, in descriptione luminarium causam utilitatis humanae specialiter profert, licet creaturae plures ordines finis habeant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A8","text":"Luminaria hominibus serviunt illuminando, tempora distinguendo et corporales mutationes utiles significando.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A9","text":"Luminaria sunt signa transmutationum corporalium, non eorum quae a libero arbitrio dependent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A10","text":"Causa sensibilis potest esse signum effectus occulti; appellatio signi potius quam causae occasionem idololatriae removet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A11","text":"Distinctio communis diei et noctis antecedit motus speciales stellarum, quibus differentiae temporum, dierum et annorum fiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A12","text":"Creatura dignior potest propter inferiorem ordinari non secundum se, sed secundum integritatem universi; anima humana corporibus luminarium praeeminet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","text":"Anima corpori ut forma unitur propter operationes quas per corpus exercet aut ad quas corpus necessarium ministerium praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","text":"Corpora caelestia operationes nutritivas et sensitivas non exercent, et operatio intellectualis per corpus non exercetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","text":"Motio corporis caelestis non exigit animam ei ut formam unitam, quia motor et mobile per contactum virtutis coniungi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A16","text":"Motus caelestis substantiam apprehendentem requirit, quia natura quae solum ad unum movet in termino quiesceret; corpus autem caeleste passive aptum est tali motui ab intellectu recipiendo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A17","text":"Corpus caeleste, ut instrumentum motum a vivente principali agente, ex virtute motoris causare vitam potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A18","text":"Moyses, populo rudi condescendens, ea sequitur quae sensibiliter apparent, non omnem differentiam naturae vel motus physice occultam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX1","text":"Ornamentum non est perfectio intrinseca caeli et terrae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX2","text":"Productio luminarium quarto die non exigit quod tota substantia eorum illo die ex nihilo vel per formam substantialem absolute incipiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX3","text":"Luminaria non sunt dii nec principia suprema et autonoma vitae terrestris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX4","text":"Signa caelestia non determinant actus qui libero arbitrio dependent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX5","text":"Causalitas et significatio sensibilis non se invicem excludunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX6","text":"Omnis distinctio temporis non a luminariis quarti diei dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX7","text":"Dignitas simpliciter superioris corporis non impedit quin ad inferius propter ordinem universi referatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX8","text":"Corpus caeleste non est animatum eo modo quo planta vel animal per animam formaliter corpori unitam animatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX9","text":"Motus caelestis naturalis non probat principium activum vitae corpori caelesti intrinsecum et autonomum esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D1","text":"Quarta dies luminariis assignatur quia ornatus caelestis per res mobiles completur, sicut ornatus medii elementi et terrae per mobilia propria completur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A3","CH_GGVC_P_62:A4","CH_GGVC_P_62:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D2","text":"Expositiones admissae formationem luminarium quarti diei intelligere possunt vel sine successione temporali, vel ut collationem virtutis determinatae, vel ut formationem ex materia praeiacente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D3","text":"Ministerium luminarium humanum tripliciter ordinatur ad cognitionem per visum, ad vicissitudines vitales temporum et ad opportunitatem operum ex significatione corporali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D4","text":"Vocabulum signi causalitatem luminarium non negat, sed causalitatem visibilem subordinatione epistemica et anti-idololatrica moderatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A9","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D5","text":"Ordo temporalis dividitur in distinctionem communem primi diei et determinationes speciales ex motibus stellarum quarto die incipientibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D6","text":"Illuminatio terrae non ponit luminaria simpliciter inferiora, sed eorum operationem ad hominem et ad integritatem universi ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D7","text":"Positio substantiae spiritualis moventis luminaria sufficit ad rationem motus sine anima caelesti ut forma corporis; differentia inter animatum et inanimatum hic ex parte magna terminologica fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D8","text":"Vita ab effectibus caelestibus producta ad virtutem motoris viventis refertur, non ad vitam formaliter inhaerentem corpori caelesti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SD1","text":"Series dierum non solum chronologiam rerum tradit, sed relationem structuralem inter regiones mundi distinctas et mobilia quae eas ornant constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A3","CH_GGVC_P_62:A4","CH_GGVC_P_62:A5","CH_GGVC_P_62:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SD2","text":"Polemica contra idololatriam vocabula causae, signi, utilitatis et ordinis diei ita disponit ut luminaria efficacia maneant, sed independentia sacra careant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A9","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SD3","text":"Causalitas caelestis stratificatur in corpus instrumentale, motorem apprehendentem et ordinem divinum, ita ut efficacia naturalis nec divinitatem nec animam corporis exigat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SD4","text":"Auctoritas scripturalis et accommodatio ad sensum simul operantur: ordo sacer normativus manet, dum descriptio sensibilis non in unicam physicam cosmologiam cogitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod visibilis efficacia luminarium sit explicatio ultima sui ipsius vel titulus divinitatis eorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod motus apparens, dignitas corporis vel effectus vitalis sufficienter demonstrent animam formaliter corpori caelesti inhaerere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod positio rei in narratione dierum identica sit cum prioritate materiali, causali vel temporali absoluta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A5","CH_GGVC_P_62:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod unio animae et corporis ex sola nobilitate corporis aut ex sola necessitate motus inferatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit cosmologiam planam, in qua corpora caelestia per se, sine ordine universali et sine motoribus superioribus, seipsa explicant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A12","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit sensum apparentem ut criterium ultimum naturae, situs vel status ontologici luminarium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit usum univocum vocabulorum naturae, vitae, motus naturalis et motus sui in corporibus, animalibus et motoribus spiritualibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:FGS1","text":"Creatio informis → distinctio regionum → ornamentum per res motu distinctas → correspondentia caeli, medii elementi et terrae → assignatio luminarium quartae diei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A3","CH_GGVC_P_62:A4","CH_GGVC_P_62:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:FGS2","text":"Productio actualis luminarium → ministerium humanum triplex → restrictio significationis ad mutationes corporales → imminutio causalitatis idololatricae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A6","CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A8","CH_GGVC_P_62:A9","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:FGS3","text":"Argumenta ex dignitate, causalitate vitae et motu → examen operationum animae → exclusio animae nutritivae et sensitivae → motio per contactum virtutis → corpus caeleste inanimatum formaliter, sed motum a vivente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:FGS4","text":"Descriptio sensibilis et pluralitas expositionum → suspensio reductionis ordinis scripturalis ad unam chronologiam vel physicam cosmologiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A11","CH_GGVC_P_62:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF1","text":"Caelum et terra informia → distinctio et perfectio → ornamentum extrinsecum per mobilia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF2","text":"Mobilitas localis → triplex regio mundi → luminaria ut ornatus caeli quarti diei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF3","text":"Utilitas humana → illuminatio, tempora et signa → restrictio significationis ad corporea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF4","text":"Causalitas caelestis apparens → recusatio divinitatis et fatalismi → luminaria ut signa causalia subordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF5","text":"Motus caelestis et effectus vitales → distinctio corporis et motoris → instrumentum inanimatum sub substantia apprehendente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME1","text":"Dies creationis reclassificantur secundum distinctionem regionum et mobilia ornantia, non secundum solam prioritatem causalem rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME2","text":"Tempus dividitur in ordinem communem cosmologicum et in differentias speciales stellarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME3","text":"Signum et causa componi possunt, dum significatio caelestis corporalis a dominio super liberum arbitrium separatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME4","text":"Motus, vita et animationis status separantur: corpus moveri, vitam causaliter efficere et tamen anima formaliter carere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME5","text":"Relatio superioris ad inferius ex sola scala dignitatis ad ordinem universi et ad praeeminentiam animae rationalis transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus quaerit cur luminaria quarto die producantur, cui fini serviant et utrum animata sint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ALT2","text":"Structural — Ordo creationis per triadem creationis, distinctionis et ornatus, cum regione, motu et fine correlatis, constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Interpretatio scripturalis contra idololatriam disponitur, ut sidera utilia et causalia maneant sine cultu, fato vel autonomia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Realitas caelestis per distinctiones inter formam et instrumentum, motorem et mobile, tempus commune et tempus speciale, apparentiam et naturam occultam ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficienter restituunt transitum a triplici opere mundi ad quartam diem, fines luminarium et negationem animationis formalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT2","text":"Centrum cohaerentiae est coniunctio inter ornamentum, motum localem et necessitatem operationum ad unionem animae cum corpore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT3","text":"Systema exacte non determinat unam physicam rationem productionis luminarium, situs siderum vel successionis temporalis, sed expositiones diversas conservat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter ordinem dierum, qui distinctiones narrativas distribuit, et expositionem Augustini, quae successionem temporalem in operibus non ponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter motum a motore per contactum virtutis et appellationem motus caelestis naturalis etiam ex parte principii activi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0087","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT6","text":"Conclusio quod differentia inter caelum animatum et inanimatum parva vel vocalis sit tensionem retinet cum distinctione initiali animae ut formae corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia quaestiones de die, fine et vita omnes ad eandem machinam ordinis, ministerii et motus subordinati reducuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164350840881Z_c1671dd9","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 70","source_sha256":"8eab39c5b0f88bb0b8b8d793c8e614002f10878ddbb895db4840368ec2c76510","sha256":"b6aeff2e44602395ed8712792788bf6f819dc718b47fdabcb7d36363da25da04","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:43:50.841863+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS1","text":"The question determines the place of the luminaries in the work of adornment, their ends, and the manner in which they are said to be animate or inanimate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS2","text":"The argumentation is exegetical-reconstructive, insofar as the ordering of Genesis is explained through the metaphysical distinctions of creation, distinction, adornment, causality, and motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS3","text":"The question of the fourth day is shifted from mere material or causal priority to the correspondence between the regions of the world, mobile things, and the work of adornment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS4","text":"The question of the end of the luminaries is restricted to human service, so that bodily signification is admitted without divinization of the stars or determination of free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS5","text":"The question of animation is shifted from apparent dignity or visible motion to the necessity of the operations of the soul and to the relation of a spiritual mover to a mobile body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AS6","text":"The concluding movement establishes heavenly bodies as ordered instruments, which are moved and cause under the power of an apprehending mover, not as animals living through a soul formally united to them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","text":"Divine works are distinguished threefold into creation, distinction, and adornment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","text":"Creation produces heaven and earth without form, whereas distinction perfects them either through substantial forms or through fitting beauty and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A3","text":"Perfection pertains to those things intrinsic to heaven and earth, whereas adornment pertains to things distinct from them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A4","text":"The distinction of things is manifested especially through local motion; therefore mobile things pertain to the work of adornment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A5","text":"Adornment corresponds to the threefold region of heaven, the middle element, and earth: luminaries adorn heaven, birds and fish air and water, terrestrial animals earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A6","text":"The luminaries are produced in act, not merely in the potency of the firmament, because the firmament does not have their productive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","text":"Moses, in order to turn the people away from idolatry, especially adduces in the description of the luminaries the cause of human usefulness, although creatures have multiple orders of end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A8","text":"The luminaries serve human beings by illuminating, distinguishing times, and signifying useful bodily changes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A9","text":"The luminaries are signs of bodily transmutations, not of those things that depend on free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A10","text":"A sensible cause can be a sign of a hidden effect; the designation of sign rather than cause removes an occasion for idolatry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A11","text":"The common distinction of day and night precedes the special motions of the stars, by which the differences of seasons, days, and years come about.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A12","text":"A more dignified creature can be ordered for the sake of an inferior one, not in itself, but according to the integrity of the universe; the human soul surpasses the bodies of the luminaries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","text":"The soul is united to the body as form on account of the operations that it exercises through the body or for which the body provides necessary service.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","text":"Heavenly bodies do not exercise nutritive and sensitive operations, and intellectual operation is not exercised through a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","text":"The motion of a heavenly body does not require a soul united to it as form, because mover and mobile can be joined through contact of power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A16","text":"Heavenly motion requires an apprehending substance, because a nature that moves only toward one thing would come to rest at its terminus; but a heavenly body is passively suited to receive such motion from an intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A17","text":"A heavenly body, as an instrument moved by a living principal agent, can by the power of its mover cause life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:A18","text":"Moses, condescending to a rude people, follows what appears sensibly, not every difference of nature or motion physically hidden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX1","text":"Adornment is not the intrinsic perfection of heaven and earth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX2","text":"The production of the luminaries on the fourth day does not require that their whole substance absolutely begin on that day from nothing or through a substantial form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX3","text":"The luminaries are not gods or supreme and autonomous principles of terrestrial life.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX4","text":"Celestial signs do not determine acts that depend on free choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX5","text":"Causality and sensible signification do not exclude one another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX6","text":"Not every distinction of time depends on the luminaries of the fourth day.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX7","text":"The simply superior dignity of a body does not prevent it from being referred to an inferior for the sake of the order of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX8","text":"A heavenly body is not animated in the manner in which a plant or animal is animated through a soul formally united to the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:NX9","text":"Natural heavenly motion does not prove that an active principle of life is intrinsic and autonomous to the heavenly body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D1","text":"The fourth day is assigned to the luminaries because celestial adornment is completed through mobile things, just as the adornment of the middle element and of earth is completed through their proper mobile things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A3","CH_GGVC_P_62:A4","CH_GGVC_P_62:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D2","text":"Admissible expositions can understand the formation of the luminaries on the fourth day either without temporal succession, or as the conferral of determinate power, or as formation from pre-existing matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D3","text":"The human service of the luminaries is ordered threefold: to knowledge through sight, to the vital vicissitudes of the seasons, and to the fittingness of works through bodily signification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D4","text":"The term sign does not deny the causality of the luminaries, but regulates visible causality by epistemic and anti-idolatrous subordination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A9","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D5","text":"The temporal order is divided into the common distinction of the first day and special determinations from the motions of the stars beginning on the fourth day.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D6","text":"The illumination of earth does not posit the luminaries as simply inferior, but orders their operation to human beings and to the integrity of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D7","text":"The positing of a spiritual substance moving the luminaries suffices for an account of motion without a celestial soul as form of the body; the difference between animate and inanimate here becomes largely terminological.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:D8","text":"Life produced by celestial effects is referred to the power of a living mover, not to life formally inhering in the heavenly body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SD1","text":"The series of days not only conveys a chronology of things, but establishes a structural relation between distinct regions of the world and the mobile things that adorn them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A3","CH_GGVC_P_62:A4","CH_GGVC_P_62:A5","CH_GGVC_P_62:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SD2","text":"The polemic against idolatry arranges the terms cause, sign, usefulness, and order of day in such a way that the luminaries remain efficacious but lack sacred independence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A9","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SD3","text":"Celestial causality is stratified into instrumental body, apprehending mover, and divine order, so that natural efficacy requires neither divinity nor a soul of the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SD4","text":"Scriptural authority and accommodation to sense operate together: the sacred order remains normative, while sensible description is not forced into a single physical cosmology.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:DNX1","text":"It must be false that the visible efficacy of the luminaries is the ultimate explanation of itself or a title of their divinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:DNX2","text":"It must be false that apparent motion, dignity of body, or vital effect sufficiently demonstrate that a soul formally inheres in a heavenly body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the position of a thing in the narrative of the days is identical with absolute material, causal, or temporal priority.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A5","CH_GGVC_P_62:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the union of soul and body is inferred from the nobility of the body alone or from the necessity of motion alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SNX1","text":"The system excludes a flat cosmology in which heavenly bodies explain themselves through themselves, without universal order and without higher movers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A12","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SNX2","text":"The system excludes apparent sense as the ultimate criterion of the nature, position, or ontological status of the luminaries.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:SNX3","text":"The system excludes the univocal use of the terms nature, life, natural motion, and self-motion in bodies, animals, and spiritual movers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:FGS1","text":"Formless creation → distinction of regions → adornment through things distinguished by motion → correspondence of heaven, the middle element, and earth → assignment of the luminaries to the fourth day.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A1","CH_GGVC_P_62:A3","CH_GGVC_P_62:A4","CH_GGVC_P_62:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:FGS2","text":"Actual production of the luminaries → threefold human service → restriction of signification to bodily changes → diminution of idolatrous causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A6","CH_GGVC_P_62:A7","CH_GGVC_P_62:A8","CH_GGVC_P_62:A9","CH_GGVC_P_62:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:FGS3","text":"Arguments from dignity, causality of life, and motion → examination of the operations of the soul → exclusion of nutritive and sensitive soul → motion through contact of power → heavenly body formally inanimate, yet moved by a living being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A13","CH_GGVC_P_62:A14","CH_GGVC_P_62:A15","CH_GGVC_P_62:A16","CH_GGVC_P_62:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:FGS4","text":"Sensible description and plurality of expositions → suspension of the reduction of scriptural order to a single chronology or physical cosmology.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_62:A2","CH_GGVC_P_62:A11","CH_GGVC_P_62:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF1","text":"Formless heaven and earth → distinction and perfection → extrinsic adornment through mobile things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF2","text":"Local mobility → threefold region of the world → luminaries as adornment of heaven on the fourth day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF3","text":"Human usefulness → illumination, times, and signs → restriction of signification to bodily things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF4","text":"Apparent celestial causality → rejection of divinity and fatalism → luminaries as subordinate causal signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:AF5","text":"Celestial motion and vital effects → distinction of body and mover → inanimate instrument under an apprehending substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME1","text":"The days of creation are reclassified according to the distinction of regions and adorning mobile things, not according to the causal priority of things alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME2","text":"Time is divided into a common cosmological order and the special differences of the stars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME3","text":"Sign and cause can be combined, while bodily celestial signification is separated from dominion over free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME4","text":"Motion, life, and the status of animation are separated: a body can be moved, causally produce life, and yet lack a soul formally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ME5","text":"The relation of superior to inferior is shifted from a scale of dignity alone to the order of the universe and the preeminence of the rational soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text asks why the luminaries are produced on the fourth day, to what end they serve, and whether they are animate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ALT2","text":"Structural — The order of creation is established through the triad of creation, distinction, and adornment, with region, motion, and end correlated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Scriptural interpretation is arranged against idolatry, so that the stars remain useful and causal without worship, fate, or autonomy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Celestial reality is ordered through distinctions between form and instrument, mover and mobile, common time and special time, appearance and hidden nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT1","text":"The axioms sufficiently reconstruct the transition from the threefold work of the world to the fourth day, the ends of the luminaries, and the denial of formal animation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT2","text":"The center of coherence is the conjunction between adornment, local motion, and the necessity of operations for the union of soul with body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT3","text":"The system does not exactly determine a single physical account of the production of the luminaries, the position of the stars, or temporal succession, but preserves diverse expositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains between the order of the days, which distributes narrative distinctions, and Augustine's exposition, which posits no temporal succession in the works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains between motion from a mover through contact of power and the designation of heavenly motion as natural also on the part of an active principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0085","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0087","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT6","text":"The conclusion that the difference between animate and inanimate heaven is slight or merely verbal retains a tension with the initial distinction of the soul as the form of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_62:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because the questions concerning day, end, and life are all reduced to the same framework of order, service, and subordinate motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_62:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_62@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_62:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 71","title":"First Part · Question 70","context":"Chapter 71","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 70"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 70","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 71","order":72,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_63"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_63@R001","sha256":"369333d4c1b6adfa58f1ce946fdcdc4e7f12d40664fa11071d776357e3c326e6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS1","text":"Quaestio est utrum opus quintae diei convenienter describatur, cum pisces et aves ex aquis produci dicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS2","text":"Descriptio quinta diei non significat aquam esse causam activam sufficientem omnium piscium et avium, sed opus ornatus respondet ordini distinctionis corporum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est dialectica et reconstructiva: obiectiones materialis causae, compositionis, motus, classificationis et perfectionis per distinctiones causales et ordinales resolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS4","text":"Motus procedit ab apparentia productionis materialis ad discrimen principii activi, materiae, affinitatis motus, mediorum et ordinum temporalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS5","text":"Conclusio coniungit ordinem scripturae cum pluralitate causarum naturalium, servata tamen distinctione inter productionem actualem et potentialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","text":"Opus ornatus respondet ordini distinctionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","text":"Dies quinta, cum sit medius inter tres dies ornatus, ad ornatum corporis medii, scilicet aquae, ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A3","text":"Mentio aquarum et firmamenti quinto die indicat eius responsionem ad secundum diem, sicut luminaria quarto die respondent luci primae diei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","text":"In generatione naturali principium activum animalium ex semine est virtus formativa seminis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","text":"In animalibus ex putrefactione generatis locum virtutis formativae tenet virtus caelestis corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","text":"Principium materiale generationis animalium est aliquod elementum vel elementatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","text":"In prima rerum institutione principium activum productionis animalium fuit verbum Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","text":"Virtus producendi animalia ex materia elementari procedit a virtute primitus elementis data, non ab aqua aut terra secundum se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","text":"Corpora piscium et avium secundum compositionem suam possunt habere maiorem proportionem elementi terrestris quam aquae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","text":"Eadem corpora secundum motus ad quos nata sunt habent quandam affinitatem cum corporibus in quibus moventur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","text":"Aer, quia insensibilis est, non per se connumeratur, sed inferior pars eius cum aqua et superior cum caelo ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A12","text":"Natura transit ab uno extremo ad aliud per media, quae secundum maiorem communicationem ad alterutrum extremum computantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","text":"Productio animalium in narratione ordinatur secundum corpora quae ornantur magis quam secundum propriam animalium dignitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A14","text":"In via generationis natura procedit ab imperfectioribus ad perfectiora.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A15","text":"Inter Augustinum et alios sanctos manet distinctio utrum pisces et aves quinto die actu an virtute producti sint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX1","text":"Aqua aut terra non habet in se virtutem producendi omnia animalia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX2","text":"Ea quae naturaliter ex semine generantur naturaliter sine semine generari non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX3","text":"Descriptio piscium et avium non fundatur in sola compositione corporum ex elemento dominante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX4","text":"Motus avium in aere non transfert productionem earum simpliciter ad aerem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX5","text":"Definitio piscium per reptationem aquatilium non sufficit ad omnia animalia inter aquatica et terrestria comprehensa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX6","text":"Ordo narrationis non sequitur simpliciter gradum propriae perfectionis animalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX7","text":"Contradictio inter productionem actu et productionem virtute non tollitur per unam interpretationem historicam coactam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D1","text":"Aquarum mentio quinto die designat relationem diei quintae ad secundum diem per ordinem ornatus corporis medii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D2","text":"Verbum “producant” non attribuit aquae principium activum universale, quia principium activum naturale vel est virtus seminis vel virtus caelestis corporis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D3","text":"In prima rerum institutione eadem productio referri potest ad productionem actualem secundum alios sanctos vel ad productionem potentialem secundum Augustinum, quia utrumque sub principio verbi Dei continetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D4","text":"Elementum terrestre in corporibus piscium et avium non impedit attributionem eorum aquae, quia attributio respicit affinitatem ad motum potius quam proportionem materialem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D5","text":"Aves aquae adscribuntur quia motum habent in inferiori parte aeris, quae cum aqua coniungitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D6","text":"Animalia media inter aquatica et terrestria secundum maiorem communicationem ad unum extremum computantur, dum mentio cetorum reliquas formas speciales includit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D7","text":"Piscium et avium praecessio animalium terrestrium non repugnat perfectioni terrestrium, quia series narrationis sequitur ornatum corporum et non ordinem dignitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD1","text":"Narratio creationis duas rationes ordinationis simul continet: ordinem ornatus corporum et ordinem generationis ab imperfectioribus ad perfectiora.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD2","text":"Apparens contradictio inter aquam, aerem, terram et productionem animalium solvitur per separationem principii activi, principii materialis et criterii classificationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD3","text":"Elementorum nomina in narratione creationis funguntur non tantum designatione materiae, sed etiam designatione corporum, motuum et mediorum quibus animalia ornantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD4","text":"Ordo causarum ab actu divino ad materiam elementarem, virtutem seminis vel virtutem caelestem, et inde ad animalia distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD5","text":"Taxonomia animalium fit gradatim et relationaliter, quia media inter extrema non constituunt tertium genus absolutum sed secundum maiorem affinitatem ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD6","text":"Interpretatio textus biblici servat pluralitatem lectionum de actu et potentia, dum unitatem causalitatis divinae retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit causam materialem unicam quae sola productionem animalium explicare possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit identitatem inter locum motus animalis et materiam vel causam activam eius generationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit classificationem animalium per proprietatem absolutam quae intermedia et gradus affinitatis ignoraret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit reductionem ordinis dierum ad unam tantum seriem perfectionis naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX5","text":"Systema excludit confusionem inter primam rerum institutionem et ordinariam generationem naturalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX6","text":"Systema excludit solutionem quae controversiam inter Augustinum et alios dissolveret negando alterutram rationem productionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio praecludit possibilitatem naturae materialis sibi sufficientis et a donatione primae virtutis independentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio praecludit lectionem literalem qua verba “ex aquis” designarent exhaustivam theoriam biologicam causarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SNX3","text":"Argumentatio praecludit ordinem temporis qui simul et simpliciter esset ordo perfectionis, generationis et ornatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SNX4","text":"Argumentatio praecludit ontologiam binariam in qua animalia aut aquatica aut terrestria essent sine mediis relationalibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS1","text":"Apparens insufficentia aquae, dominatio terrae, motus avium in aere, ambiguitas piscium et praecessio animalium terrestrium generant seriem obiectionum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_63:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_63:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_63:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_63:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS2","text":"Discretio principii activi a principio materiali destruit interpretationem aquae tamquam causae universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS3","text":"Discretio compositionis a motu transfert classificationem piscium et avium a elemento dominante ad affinitatem cum medio motus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS4","text":"Principium transitus per media permittit animalia mixta secundum maiorem communicationem ad unum extremum ordinare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS5","text":"Correspondentia inter distinctionem et ornatum constituit quintum diem ut ornatum corporis medii et ut responsionem ad secundum diem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS6","text":"Separatio ordinis ornatus ab ordine generationis explicat cur animalia minus perfecta prius narrentur quam animalia terrestria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS7","text":"Causalitas divina prima compatitur lectionem productionis actualis cum lectione productionis potentialis, sine reductione unius ad alteram.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF1","text":"Insufficientia aquae et anomaliae elementorum → distinctio principii activi et materialis → negatio causalitatis aquae secundum se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF2","text":"Oppositio aquae et aeris → distinctio motus, compositionis et mediorum → attributio avium aquae per inferiorem aeris partem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF3","text":"Inadaequatio definitionis per reptationem → principium transitus per media → classificatio secundum maiorem affinitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF4","text":"Praecessio animalium minus perfectorum → distinctio ordinis ornatus ab ordine generationis → coexistentia ordinum temporalium non identicorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF5","text":"Distinctiones causales et ordinales → quinta dies ut ornatus aquae et responsio ad secundum diem → concordia inter textum scripturae et doctrinam generationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME1","text":"“Aqua” reclassificatur ab hypothesi causae activae sufficientis ad signum corporis, medii et ordinis ornatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:D1","CH_GGVC_P_63:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME2","text":"Oppositio aqua–terra–aer dissolvitur in tabulam causarum et affinitatum, ubi idem animal diversis rationibus ad diversa elementa referri potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:D4","CH_GGVC_P_63:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME3","text":"Animalia inter aquatica et terrestria fiunt visibilia ut media classificatoria potius quam exceptiones ordinem perturbantes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME4","text":"Praecessio temporalis non amplius indicat inferiorem dignitatem, quia dies ordinantur secundum corpora ornata et non secundum perfectionem animalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME5","text":"Narratio creationis fit tabula stratificata in qua causalitas divina, causalitas naturalis, materia, motus et ordo scripturae simul sed non indistincte apparent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ALT1","text":"Surface — Assertio immediata est quod aquae pisces et aves producere dicantur quinto die.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ALT2","text":"Structural — Sub superficie agunt discrimina inter causam activam, causam materialem, compositionem corporis, motum et ordinem corporum ornatorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12","CH_GGVC_P_63:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones non solvuntur per unam causam contrariam, sed per mutationem criterii quo verba scripturae causalia, ordinalia et classificatoria distinguuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS5","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS6","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Realitas praesupponitur ut ordo causalitatum a verbo Dei ad materiam et virtutes naturales procedens, dum tempus continet ordinem ornatus distinctum ab ordine generationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam rationem principalem: aquae mentio ad ordinem ornatus pertinet et aquae non tribuitur causalitas activa universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A3","CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT2","text":"Distinctiones de compositione, motu, aere et mediis sufficiunt ad dissolvendas quattuor primas obiectiones.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT3","text":"Distinctio ordinis ornatus et ordinis generationis sufficit ad quintam obiectionem solvendas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT4","text":"Systema interne firmissimum est ubi separat causas, modos attributionis et ordines temporales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT5","text":"Nondum plene determinatur utrum productiones quinta die actu an virtute intellectae sint, quia textus duas expositiones servat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A15","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT6","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter sensum materialem locutionis “ex aquis” et eius functionem ordinativam, praesertim sub cosmologia distinctionis aeris, aquae et caeli.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus: obiectiones materiales mutantur in discrimina causalia, relationalia et ordinalia, quibus conclusio scripturalis denuo constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_63:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_63:AF3","CH_GGVC_P_63:AF4","CH_GGVC_P_63:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164417161658Z_b73d9073","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 71","source_sha256":"369333d4c1b6adfa58f1ce946fdcdc4e7f12d40664fa11071d776357e3c326e6","sha256":"2395621ee31e6bb4d69317d1e72504559a1986980103642ddde16fdb0931d362","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:44:17.163192+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS1","text":"The question is whether the work of the fifth day is fittingly described, when fish and birds are said to be produced from the waters.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS2","text":"The description of the fifth day does not signify that water is a sufficient active cause of all fish and birds, but the work of adornment corresponds to the order of the distinction of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS3","text":"The argumentation is dialectical and reconstructive: it resolves objections concerning material cause, composition, motion, classification, and perfection through causal and ordinal distinctions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS4","text":"The movement proceeds from the appearance of material production to the distinction of active principle, matter, affinity of motion, media, and temporal orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AS5","text":"The conclusion joins the order of Scripture with the plurality of natural causes, while preserving the distinction between actual and potential production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","text":"The work of adornment corresponds to the order of distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","text":"The fifth day, since it is intermediate among the three days of adornment, is ordered to the adornment of the intermediate body, namely water.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A3","text":"The mention of the waters and the firmament on the fifth day indicates its correspondence to the second day, just as the luminaries on the fourth day correspond to the light of the first day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","text":"In natural generation, the active principle of animals from seed is the formative power of the seed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","text":"In animals generated from putrefaction, the power of the heavenly body takes the place of formative power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","text":"The material principle of the generation of animals is some element or elemental composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","text":"In the first institution of things, the active principle of the production of animals was the word of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","text":"The power of producing animals from elemental matter proceeds from the power first given to the elements, not from water or earth considered in themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","text":"The bodies of fish and birds can, according to their composition, have a greater proportion of the terrestrial element than of water.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","text":"The same bodies, according to the motions for which they are naturally suited, have a certain affinity with the bodies in which they move.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","text":"Air, because it is imperceptible, is not counted by itself, but its lower part is ordered with water and its upper part with heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A12","text":"Nature passes from one extreme to another through intermediates, which are counted according to their greater communication with either extreme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","text":"The production of animals in the narrative is ordered according to the bodies that are adorned rather than according to the proper dignity of the animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A14","text":"In the way of generation, nature proceeds from the more imperfect to the more perfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:A15","text":"Between Augustine and the other saints there remains a distinction as to whether fish and birds were produced on the fifth day actually or virtually.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX1","text":"Water or earth does not have within itself the power to produce all animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX2","text":"Those things which are naturally generated from seed cannot naturally be generated without seed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX3","text":"The description of fish and birds is not founded on the composition of bodies from the dominant element alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX4","text":"The motion of birds in the air does not simply transfer their production to air.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX5","text":"The definition of fish through the creeping of aquatic creatures does not suffice for all animals included among aquatic and terrestrial beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX6","text":"The order of the narrative does not simply follow the degree of the animals' proper perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:NX7","text":"The contradiction between production in act and production in potency is not removed by a single forced historical interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D1","text":"The mention of the waters on the fifth day designates the relation of the fifth day to the second day through the order of adornment of the intermediate body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D2","text":"The word “producant” does not attribute to water a universal active principle, because the natural active principle is either the power of seed or the power of a heavenly body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D3","text":"In the first institution of things, the same production can be referred to actual production according to the other saints or to potential production according to Augustine, because both are contained under the principle of the word of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D4","text":"The terrestrial element in the bodies of fish and birds does not prevent their attribution to water, because the attribution concerns affinity to motion rather than material proportion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D5","text":"Birds are ascribed to water because they have motion in the lower part of the air, which is joined with water.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D6","text":"Animals intermediate between aquatic and terrestrial animals are counted according to their greater communication with one extreme, while the mention of whales includes the remaining special forms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:D7","text":"The precedence of fish and birds over terrestrial animals does not conflict with the perfection of terrestrial animals, because the series of the narrative follows the adornment of bodies and not the order of dignity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD1","text":"The creation narrative simultaneously contains two modes of ordering: the order of the adornment of bodies and the order of generation from the more imperfect to the more perfect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD2","text":"The apparent contradiction between water, air, earth, and the production of animals is resolved through the separation of active principle, material principle, and criterion of classification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD3","text":"The names of the elements in the creation narrative function not only as designations of matter, but also as designations of bodies, motions, and media by which animals are adorned.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD4","text":"The order of causes is distributed from the divine act to elemental matter, the power of seed or heavenly power, and thence to animals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD5","text":"The taxonomy of animals proceeds gradually and relationally, because intermediates between extremes do not constitute a third absolute genus but are ordered according to greater affinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SD6","text":"The interpretation of the biblical text preserves a plurality of readings concerning act and potency, while retaining the unity of divine causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX1","text":"The system excludes a single material cause that by itself could explain the production of animals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX2","text":"The system excludes identity between the place of an animal's motion and the matter or active cause of its generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX3","text":"The system excludes the classification of animals by an absolute property that would ignore intermediates and degrees of affinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the reduction of the order of days to only one series of natural perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX5","text":"The system excludes the confusion of the first institution of things with ordinary natural generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:DNX6","text":"The system excludes a solution that would dissolve the controversy between Augustine and the others by denying either mode of production.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SNX1","text":"The argumentation precludes the possibility of a material nature self-sufficient and independent from the bestowal of the first power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SNX2","text":"The argumentation precludes a literal reading by which the words “ex aquis” would designate an exhaustive biological theory of causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SNX3","text":"The argumentation precludes an order of time that would simultaneously and simply be an order of perfection, generation, and adornment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:SNX4","text":"The argumentation precludes a binary ontology in which animals would be either aquatic or terrestrial without relational intermediates.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS1","text":"The apparent insufficiency of water, the dominance of earth, the motion of birds in air, the ambiguity of fish, and the precedence of terrestrial animals generate a series of objections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_63:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_63:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_63:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_63:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS2","text":"The distinction of active principle from material principle destroys the interpretation of water as a universal cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS3","text":"The distinction of composition from motion shifts the classification of fish and birds from the dominant element to affinity with the medium of motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS4","text":"The principle of transition through intermediates permits mixed animals to be ordered according to their greater communication with one extreme.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS5","text":"The correspondence between distinction and adornment establishes the fifth day as the adornment of the intermediate body and as a response to the second day.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS6","text":"The separation of the order of adornment from the order of generation explains why less perfect animals are narrated before terrestrial animals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS7","text":"First divine causality is compatible with the reading of actual production and with the reading of potential production, without reducing one to the other.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF1","text":"Insufficiency of water and anomalies of the elements → distinction of active and material principle → denial of the causality of water considered in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF2","text":"Opposition of water and air → distinction of motion, composition, and media → attribution of birds to water through the lower part of air.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF3","text":"Inadequacy of the definition through creeping → principle of transition through intermediates → classification according to greater affinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF4","text":"Precedence of less perfect animals → distinction of the order of adornment from the order of generation → coexistence of non-identical temporal orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:AF5","text":"Causal and ordinal distinctions → fifth day as the adornment of water and response to the second day → concord between the text of Scripture and the doctrine of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME1","text":"“Water” is reclassified from the hypothesis of a sufficient active cause to a sign of body, medium, and order of adornment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:D1","CH_GGVC_P_63:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME2","text":"The opposition water–earth–air is dissolved into a map of causes and affinities, in which the same animal can be referred to different elements for different reasons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:D4","CH_GGVC_P_63:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME3","text":"Animals between aquatic and terrestrial beings become visible as classificatory intermediates rather than exceptions disrupting order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME4","text":"Temporal precedence no longer indicates inferior dignity, because the days are ordered according to adorned bodies and not according to the perfection of animals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ME5","text":"The creation narrative becomes a stratified map in which divine causality, natural causality, matter, motion, and the order of Scripture appear simultaneously but not indistinctly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ALT1","text":"Surface — The immediate assertion is that waters are said to produce fish and birds on the fifth day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ALT2","text":"Structural — Beneath the surface operate distinctions between active cause, material cause, bodily composition, motion, and the order of adorned bodies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8","CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12","CH_GGVC_P_63:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The objections are not resolved through one contrary cause, but through a change of the criterion by which the words of Scripture are distinguished as causal, ordinal, and classificatory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS5","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS6","CH_GGVC_P_63:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Reality is presupposed as an order of causalities proceeding from the word of God to matter and natural powers, while time contains an order of adornment distinct from the order of generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the principal account: the mention of water pertains to the order of adornment, and universal active causality is not attributed to water.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A1","CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A3","CH_GGVC_P_63:A4","CH_GGVC_P_63:A5","CH_GGVC_P_63:A6","CH_GGVC_P_63:A7","CH_GGVC_P_63:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT2","text":"The distinctions concerning composition, motion, air, and intermediates suffice to dissolve the first four objections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A9","CH_GGVC_P_63:A10","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT3","text":"The distinction of the order of adornment and the order of generation suffices to resolve the fifth objection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A13","CH_GGVC_P_63:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT4","text":"The system is internally strongest where it separates causes, modes of attribution, and temporal orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT5","text":"It is not yet fully determined whether the productions on the fifth day are understood actually or virtually, because the text preserves two expositions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A15","CH_GGVC_P_63:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT6","text":"A fragile juncture remains between the material sense of the expression “ex aquis” and its ordering function, especially under the cosmology of the distinction of air, water, and heaven.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:A2","CH_GGVC_P_63:A11","CH_GGVC_P_63:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_63:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: material objections are transformed into causal, relational, and ordinal distinctions, through which the scriptural conclusion is re-established.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_63:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_63:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_63:AF3","CH_GGVC_P_63:AF4","CH_GGVC_P_63:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_63:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_63@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_63:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 72","title":"First Part · Question 71","context":"Chapter 72","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 71"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 71","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 72","order":73,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_64"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_64@R001","sha256":"5bdb0a097e03961ed26c8f829f91c13ab8fcc44c397dfef4a5cf4a3392afbb22","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS1","text":"Quaestio est utrum descriptio Scripturae de productione animalium terrestrium sexto die convenienter ordinetur et enuntietur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS2","text":"Obiectiones spectant ad significationem animae viventis, distinctionem generum, omissionem benedictionis, generationem ex corruptione et nocivitatem animalium venenatorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS3","text":"Thesis est quod descriptio convenit, quia animalia terrestria ultimum corpus ornant et peculiarem gradum vitae inter non-humana habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS4","text":"Responsio apparentias contradictionis resolvit per ordinem dierum, gradus vitae, flexibilitatem generum, repetitionem implicatam et relationem inter corruptionem, utilitatem et totius universi integritatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS5","text":"Genus argumentationis est exegeticum, reconstructivum et ontologico-ordinativum, cum textus Scripturae per distinctiones philosophicas et theologicas restituatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","text":"Sextus dies ultimum corpus, terram, productione animalium terrestrium adornat et tertiae diei respondet, sicut quintus dies medium corpus adornat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","text":"Vocabulorum Scripturae diversitas gradus vitae in viventibus designat, non simpliciter varietatem nominum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A3","text":"Plantae vitam imperfectissimam et occultam habent; animalia terrestria, propter distinctionem membrorum et perfectionem generationis, communiter perfectiora sunt avibus et piscibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A4","text":"Perfectissimus gradus vitae est in homine, cuius vita non dicitur a terra vel aqua produci sicut vita ceterorum animalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","text":"Iumenta significant animalia domestica homini qualitercumque servientia, bestiae animalia saeva, reptilia animalia parum vel nullo modo a terra elevata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A6","text":"Quadrupedia potest poni quasi genus commune vel quasi terminus additus ad animalia quae sub iumentis, bestiis et reptilibus non continentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","text":"Mentio generis et speciei significat generationes similium ex similibus, sed eius repetitio in homine non est necessaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","text":"Benedictio dat virtutem multiplicandi per generationem, et eius repetitio in homine refertur ad specialem multiplicationis rationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","text":"Generatio unius est corruptio alterius, et generatio nobiliorum ex corruptione ignobiliorum primae rerum institutioni non repugnat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A10","text":"Animalia ex corruptione rerum inanimatarum vel plantarum tunc produci potuerunt, animalia autem ex corruptione animalium nonnisi potentialiter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","text":"Nocivitas animalium venenatorum non est absoluta proprietas creaturarum, quia ante peccatum homo rebus mundi ordinate usus fuisset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","text":"Quaedam res, etsi domui humanae non sunt necessariae, ad integritatem universitatis pertinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A13","text":"Animalia terrestria secundum Augustinum potentialiter, secundum alios sanctos in actu producuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A14","text":"Homo ad imaginem et similitudinem Dei formatus est, unde eius productio aliter quam productio plantarum et animalium describitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A15","text":"Auctoritas Scripturae sufficit ad confirmandam veritatem productionis animalium sexto die.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX1","text":"Descriptio terrae producentis animam viventem non ponit animalia terrestria simpliciter identica animae ut principio separato, sed eorum vitae perfectionem significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX2","text":"Quadrupedia non necessario constituitur species contra genus, quia potest esse genus commune vel categoria supplementaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX3","text":"Omissio generis et speciei in productione hominis non probat hominem extra omnem generationis ordinem poni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX4","text":"Non-repetitio benedictionis in animalibus terrestribus non significat eis virtutem generandi negari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX5","text":"Corruptio non universaliter excluditur a prima rerum institutione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX6","text":"Animalia venenosa non sunt propter suam naturam ante peccatum homini nociva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX7","text":"Valor creaturae non metiturur sola necessitate eius ad domum humanam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX8","text":"Homo non describitur eodem modo ac cetera animalia, quia eius vita et formatio ad similitudinem divinam referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D1","text":"Locutio «producat terra animam viventem» convenienter designat perfectionem vitae animalium terrestrium inter creaturas non humanas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D2","text":"Disparitas inter «quadrupedia», «iumenta», «bestias» et «reptilia» solvitur per categorias inter se inclusibiles et non per unam divisionem logicam simplicem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D3","text":"Mentio generis et speciei in animalibus significat ordinem generationis, non regulam quae eadem forma in omni narratione repeti debeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D4","text":"Non-repetitio benedictionis in animalibus terrestribus suppletur intellectu eius quod prius de avibus et piscibus dictum est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D5","text":"Repetitio benedictionis in homine indicat non simpliciter generationem biologicam, sed finem specialem multiplicationis humanae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D6","text":"Prima rerum institutio potest continere generationes ex corruptione inferiorum rerum, dummodo corruptio animalium non intelligatur tunc actualiter producere alia animalia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D7","text":"Nocivitas creaturae est relatio ad statum et usum hominis, non defectus absolutus in ipsa creatura.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D8","text":"Animalia quae homini directe non serviunt tamen rationem habent intra integritatem totius universi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D9","text":"Descriptio creationis admittit plures modos causalitatis temporalis, quia eadem productio potest dici potentialis vel actualis secundum expositionem receptam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A10","CH_GGVC_P_64:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD1","text":"Textus Scripturae simul ordinem cosmicum, gradus vitae et rationem nominum disponit, ita ut vocabula locum creaturarum in universitate significent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD2","text":"Apparentes defectus narrationis non solvuntur per correctionem litterae, sed per distinctionem inter ordinem ontologicum, usum linguisticum et modum causalitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:D1","CH_GGVC_P_64:D2","CH_GGVC_P_64:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD3","text":"Creaturarum perfectio est gradatim ordinata, sed non reducitur ad unam mensuram, quia perfectio vitae, generandi et sagacitatis non semper coincidit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A3","CH_GGVC_P_64:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4","text":"Utilitas humana subordinatur integritati universi, ita ut creatura superflua domui humanae nihilominus necessaria sit ordini totius.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD5","text":"Status ante peccatum reconfigurat oppositionem inter utile et nocivum, quia usus ordinatus hominis tollit nocivitatem quae postea apparere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD6","text":"Cognitio humana causarum creaturarum est limitata, unde iudicium de superfluitate vel noxietate sine comprehensione totius ordinis invalidum fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet creationem esse inventarium aequale rerum, in quo omnia vocabula eodem gradu ontologico operentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet divisionem taxonomicam unam et rigidam totam significationem terminorum Scripturae determinare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet corruptionem semper esse defectum incompatibilem cum prima institutione rerum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet nocivitatem esse proprietatem intrinsecam et invariabilem animalium venenatorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet creaturas secundum utilitatem immediatam homini aestimari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet hominem esse tantum unum ex animalibus in eodem ordine descriptionis, quia eius productio ad imaginem divinam refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A4","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SNX1","text":"Textus circumit possibilitatem totalis coincidentiae inter categorias taxonomicas, gradus vitae et modos causalitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SNX2","text":"Textus praecludit anthropocentricum iudicium quo id quod homini non prodest pro superfluo aut malo habetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SNX3","text":"Textus non admittit unicum modum temporis creationis, quia potentialis et actualis productio simul in expositione servantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A13","CH_GGVC_P_64:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SNX4","text":"Textus vetat iudicium humanum de ordine universi quod causam rei ignoratae pro superflua vel nociva pronuntiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS1","text":"Machina incipit ab apparentia incongruentiae inter verba Scripturae et categorias generis, speciei, vitae, benedictionis ac corruptionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS2","text":"Apparentia dissolvitur cum narrationis ordinem dierum coniungit cum gradu ontologico corporum et viventium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS3","text":"Distinctio inter genera taxonomica, significationes generationis et gradus vitae impedit ne diversa vocabula in unam divisionem reducantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6","CH_GGVC_P_64:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS4","text":"Quaestiones de omissione, repetitione, corruptione et nocivitate solvuntur per relationes implicitae continuationis, causalitatis potentialis, usus ordinati et integritatis universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:D4","CH_GGVC_P_64:D6","CH_GGVC_P_64:D7","CH_GGVC_P_64:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS5","text":"Conclusio finalis est convenientia descriptionis, non quia omnes distinctiones eliminentur, sed quia singulae in ordinem cosmicum, ontologicum et historicum referuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AF1","text":"Quaestio de inconvenientia descriptionis → divisio obiectionum semanticarum, taxonomicarum, genealogicarum et teleologicarum → ordo dierum et graduum vitae → flexibilitas generum et repetitio implicita → distinctio inter actuale et potentiale, utile et integrale, nocivum et ordinatum → convenientia finalis narrationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME1","text":"Lectio movetur a quaestione utrum verba recte classificentur ad quaestionem quomodo verba gradus vitae et ordinem corporum exprimant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter genus et speciem dissolvitur, quia categoriae Scripturae simul functiones classificatorias, supplementarias et ontologicas exercere possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6","CH_GGVC_P_64:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME3","text":"Silentium vel repetitio verborum fit elementum ordinativum: non-repetitio potest continuationem implicare, repetitio autem differentiam status indicare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","CH_GGVC_P_64:D4","CH_GGVC_P_64:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME4","text":"Corruptio et nocivitas denuo classificantur ut relationes temporales et ordinativae, non ut exclusionis absolutae signa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:D6","CH_GGVC_P_64:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME5","text":"Ager creaturarum describitur secundum integritatem totius universi, non secundum solam utilitatem immediatam hominis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ALT1","text":"Surface: Textus explicat productionem animalium terrestrium et vocabula quibus ea describuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ALT2","text":"Structural: Descriptio innititur hierarchiae corporum, graduum vitae, generum animalium et modorum generationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Obiectiones reorientantur ita ut apparentia contradictio fiat effectus distinctionum non agnitarum, non defectus simplicis in textu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Creaturae ordinantur per gradus vitae et per diversos modos productionis, dum status ante et post peccatum relationem inter hominem et mundum mutat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A4","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10","CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam quaestionem, responsionis principium, principales distinctiones et conclusiones de singulis obiectionibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3","CH_GGVC_P_64:A4","CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6","CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10","CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:A13","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14","CH_GGVC_P_64:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT2","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus, quia ab inconvenientia apparentis descriptionis ad ordinem ontologicum, semanticum et teleologicum progreditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT3","text":"Systema interne cohaeret quamdiu perfectio vitae, perfectio generationis et sagacitas non confunduntur in unam mensuram.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A3","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT4","text":"Firmissimum est nexus inter ordinem dierum, hierarchiam viventium et interpretationem vocabulorum Scripturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT5","text":"Distinctio inter expositionem Augustinianam potentialem et expositionem aliorum sanctorum actualem manet alternatio recepta, non plena resolutio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT6","text":"Tensio inter generationem ex corruptione et puritatem primae institutionis solvitur tantum per distinctionem inter res inanimatas, plantas et animalia, non per principium universale unum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT7","text":"Relatio inter humanam imaginem divinam et hominis inclusionem in ordine generationis partim componitur per repetitionem specialem benedictionis, sed non penitus formalizatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT8","text":"Conclusio de nocivitate animalium ante peccatum dependet ex suppositione usus ordinati et ex limitatione iudicii humani de causis universi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164444764910Z_12e82d21","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 72","source_sha256":"5bdb0a097e03961ed26c8f829f91c13ab8fcc44c397dfef4a5cf4a3392afbb22","sha256":"c5657facd776470a44c276a0bddd5468fdf922783dca514d42fa0b604c167306","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:44:44.766405+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS1","text":"The question is whether the Scriptural description of the production of terrestrial animals on the sixth day is fittingly ordered and stated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS2","text":"The objections concern the meaning of the living soul, the distinction of kinds, the omission of blessing, generation from corruption, and the harmfulness of venomous animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS3","text":"The thesis is that the description is fitting, because terrestrial animals adorn the last body and possess a distinctive grade of life among non-human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS4","text":"The response resolves appearances of contradiction through the order of the days, grades of life, flexibility of kinds, implicit repetition, and the relation among corruption, utility, and the integrity of the whole universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AS5","text":"The kind of argumentation is exegetical, reconstructive, and ontological-ordinative, as the text of Scripture is restored through philosophical and theological distinctions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","text":"The sixth day adorns the last body, the earth, by the production of terrestrial animals, and corresponds to the third day, just as the fifth day adorns the middle body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","text":"The diversity of Scriptural terms designates grades of life in living beings, not merely a variety of names.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A3","text":"Plants possess a most imperfect and hidden life; terrestrial animals, on account of the distinction of their members and the perfection of generation, are commonly more perfect than birds and fishes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A4","text":"The most perfect grade of life is in man, whose life is not said to be produced from the earth or water as is the life of other animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","text":"Beasts of burden signify domestic animals serving man in whatever way, wild beasts savage animals, and creeping things animals raised little or not at all from the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A6","text":"Quadrupeds may be posited either as a common genus or as a term added for animals not contained under beasts of burden, wild beasts, and creeping things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","text":"The mention of genus and species signifies generations of like from like, but its repetition in man is not necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","text":"Blessing gives the power of multiplying through generation, and its repetition in man is referred to a special mode of multiplication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","text":"The generation of one is the corruption of another, and the generation of nobler things from the corruption of baser things does not conflict with the first institution of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A10","text":"Animals could then have been produced from the corruption of inanimate things or plants, but animals from the corruption of animals only potentially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","text":"The harmfulness of venomous animals is not an absolute property of creatures, because before sin man would have used the things of the world in an ordered manner.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","text":"Certain things, although not necessary to the human household, pertain to the integrity of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A13","text":"According to Augustine, terrestrial animals are produced potentially; according to other saints, actually.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A14","text":"Man was formed in the image and likeness of God; hence his production is described otherwise than the production of plants and animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:A15","text":"The authority of Scripture suffices to confirm the truth of the production of animals on the sixth day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX1","text":"The description of the earth producing a living soul does not posit terrestrial animals as simply identical with the soul as a separate principle, but signifies the perfection of their life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX2","text":"Quadrupeds are not necessarily constituted as a species against a genus, because they may be a common genus or a supplementary category.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX3","text":"The omission of genus and species in the production of man does not prove that man is placed outside every order of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX4","text":"The non-repetition of the blessing in terrestrial animals does not signify that the power of generation is denied them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX5","text":"Corruption is not universally excluded from the first institution of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX6","text":"Venomous animals are not harmful to man before sin by reason of their nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX7","text":"The value of a creature is not measured by its necessity to the human household alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:NX8","text":"Man is not described in the same way as other animals, because his life and formation are referred to the divine likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D1","text":"The expression «let the earth bring forth a living soul» fittingly designates the perfection of the life of terrestrial animals among non-human creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D2","text":"The disparity among «quadrupeds», «beasts of burden», «wild beasts», and «creeping things» is resolved through mutually inclusive categories and not through one simple logical division.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D3","text":"The mention of genus and species in animals signifies the order of generation, not a rule that must be repeated in the same form in every narrative.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D4","text":"The non-repetition of the blessing in terrestrial animals is supplied by understanding what was previously said concerning birds and fishes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D5","text":"The repetition of the blessing in man indicates not merely biological generation, but the special end of human multiplication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D6","text":"The first institution of things can contain generations from the corruption of lower things, provided that the corruption of animals is not understood then actually to produce other animals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D7","text":"The harmfulness of a creature is a relation to the state and use of man, not an absolute defect in the creature itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D8","text":"Animals that do not directly serve man nevertheless have a rationale within the integrity of the whole universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:D9","text":"The description of creation admits multiple modes of temporal causality, because the same production can be called potential or actual according to the received exposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A10","CH_GGVC_P_64:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD1","text":"The text of Scripture simultaneously arranges cosmic order, grades of life, and the rationale of names, such that terms signify the place of creatures in the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD2","text":"Apparent defects of the narrative are not resolved by correcting the letter, but by distinguishing among ontological order, linguistic usage, and mode of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:D1","CH_GGVC_P_64:D2","CH_GGVC_P_64:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD3","text":"The perfection of creatures is arranged gradually, but is not reduced to one measure, because perfection of life, generation, and sagacity do not always coincide.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A3","CH_GGVC_P_64:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4","text":"Human utility is subordinated to the integrity of the universe, such that a creature superfluous to the human household is nevertheless necessary to the order of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD5","text":"The state before sin reconfigures the opposition between useful and harmful, because man's ordered use removes the harmfulness that can subsequently appear.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SD6","text":"Human knowledge of the causes of creatures is limited; hence judgment concerning superfluity or harmfulness without comprehension of the whole order becomes invalid.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX1","text":"It must be false that creation is an equal inventory of things, in which all terms operate at the same ontological grade.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX2","text":"It must be false that one rigid taxonomic division determines the whole meaning of Scriptural terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX3","text":"It must be false that corruption is always a defect incompatible with the first institution of things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX4","text":"It must be false that harmfulness is an intrinsic and invariable property of venomous animals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX5","text":"It must be false that creatures are to be assessed according to their immediate utility to man.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:DNX6","text":"It must be false that man is merely one among animals in the same order of description, because his production is referred to the divine image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A4","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SNX1","text":"The text avoids the possibility of a total coincidence among taxonomic categories, grades of life, and modes of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SNX2","text":"The text precludes the anthropocentric judgment by which what does not benefit man is held superfluous or evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SNX3","text":"The text does not admit a single mode of the time of creation, because potential and actual production are both retained in the exposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A13","CH_GGVC_P_64:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:SNX4","text":"The text forbids a human judgment concerning the order of the universe that declares a thing whose cause is unknown to be superfluous or harmful.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS1","text":"The framework begins from the appearance of an incongruity between the words of Scripture and the categories of genus, species, life, blessing, and corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS2","text":"The appearance is dissolved when it joins the narrative order of the days with the ontological grade of bodies and living beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS3","text":"The distinction among taxonomic genera, meanings of generation, and grades of life prevents diverse terms from being reduced to one division.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6","CH_GGVC_P_64:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS4","text":"Questions concerning omission, repetition, corruption, and harmfulness are resolved through relations of implicit continuation, potential causality, ordered use, and universal integrity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:D4","CH_GGVC_P_64:D6","CH_GGVC_P_64:D7","CH_GGVC_P_64:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS5","text":"The final conclusion is the fittingness of the description, not because all distinctions are eliminated, but because each is referred to a cosmic, ontological, and historical order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:AF1","text":"Question of the unfittingness of the description → division of semantic, taxonomic, genealogical, and teleological objections → order of days and grades of life → flexibility of genera and implicit repetition → distinction between actual and potential, useful and integral, harmful and ordered → final fittingness of the narrative.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME1","text":"The reading moves from the question whether words are correctly classified to the question how words express grades of life and the order of bodies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME2","text":"The opposition between genus and species is dissolved, because Scriptural categories can simultaneously perform classificatory, supplementary, and ontological functions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6","CH_GGVC_P_64:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME3","text":"The silence or repetition of words becomes an ordering element: non-repetition can imply continuation, while repetition can indicate a difference of state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","CH_GGVC_P_64:D4","CH_GGVC_P_64:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME4","text":"Corruption and harmfulness are reclassified as temporal and ordering relations, not as signs of absolute exclusion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:D6","CH_GGVC_P_64:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ME5","text":"The field of creatures is described according to the integrity of the whole universe, not according to man's immediate utility alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ALT1","text":"Surface: The text explains the production of terrestrial animals and the terms by which they are described.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ALT2","text":"Structural: The description rests on a hierarchy of bodies, grades of life, kinds of animals, and modes of generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: The objections are reoriented so that apparent contradiction becomes the effect of unrecognized distinctions, not a simple defect in the text.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Creatures are ordered through grades of life and diverse modes of production, while the state before and after sin changes the relation between man and the world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A4","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10","CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the question, the principle of the response, the principal distinctions, and the conclusions concerning the individual objections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3","CH_GGVC_P_64:A4","CH_GGVC_P_64:A5","CH_GGVC_P_64:A6","CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10","CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:A13","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14","CH_GGVC_P_64:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text, because it proceeds from the unfittingness of the apparent description to ontological, semantic, and teleological order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_64:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT3","text":"The system coheres internally so long as perfection of life, perfection of generation, and sagacity are not confused in one measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A3","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT4","text":"Strongest is the connection among the order of the days, the hierarchy of living beings, and the interpretation of Scriptural terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A1","CH_GGVC_P_64:A2","CH_GGVC_P_64:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT5","text":"The distinction between Augustine's potential exposition and the actual exposition of other saints remains a received alternative, not a full resolution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT6","text":"The tension between generation from corruption and the purity of the first institution is resolved only through the distinction among inanimate things, plants, and animals, not through one universal principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A9","CH_GGVC_P_64:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT7","text":"The relation between the human divine image and man's inclusion in the order of generation is partly reconciled through the special repetition of the blessing, but is not fully formalized.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A7","CH_GGVC_P_64:A8","CH_GGVC_P_64:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_64:MRT8","text":"The conclusion concerning the harmfulness of animals before sin depends on the supposition of ordered use and on the limitation of human judgment concerning the causes of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_64:A11","CH_GGVC_P_64:A12","CH_GGVC_P_64:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_64:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_64@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_64:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 73","title":"First Part · Question 72","context":"Chapter 73","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 72"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 72","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 73","order":74,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_65"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_65@R001","sha256":"5a0a39fdbe3245a0c187372283eaca2b3f8bc50c3de4384870f455d06236ba50","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat quomodo septimo die simul attribui possint completio operum, quies divina, benedictio et sanctificatio, cum creaturae et operationes postea appareant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS2","text":"Argumentatio est distinctiva et reconstructiva: apparentem contradictionem dissolvit distinguendo perfectionem, operationem, novitatem, quietem et effectum divinum in creaturas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS3","text":"Textus transit ab aequivocatione perfectionis ad ordinem triplicis consummationis: naturae in prima institutione, gratiae in incarnatione, gloriae in fine saeculi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS4","text":"Continuatio rerum post septimum diem reclassificatur non ut creatio absolute nova, sed ut explicatio materialis, causalis vel similitudinalis eorum quae in primis operibus praecontinentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS5","text":"Quies Dei non significat inertiam, sed cessationem a productione novarum creaturarum et fruitionem sui ipsius, manente conservatione et administratione creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS6","text":"Benedictio et sanctificatio septimi diei distribuuntur secundum duplicem quietem: multiplicatio creaturarum ad administrationem pertinet, sanctitas ad quietem creaturae in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","text":"Perfectio prima rei consistit in integritate substantiae suae, perfectio secunda consistit in fine vel operatione ad finem ordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","text":"Perfectio prima est causa perfectionis secundae, quia forma integra est principium operationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","text":"Perfectio ultima universi est beatitudo sanctorum, quae in ultima consummatione saeculi perficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","text":"Integritas universi in prima institutione rerum completa est, et haec perfectio primo septimo die attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A5","text":"Consummatio naturae pertinet ad primam institutionem rerum, consummatio gratiae ad incarnationem Christi, consummatio gloriae ad finem mundi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","text":"Cessatio a productione novarum creaturarum potest opus consummatum demonstrare, etiamsi Deus plures creaturas producere posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A7","text":"Post prima opera nihil a Deo fit totaliter novum, quia posteriora praeexistunt materialiter, causaliter vel secundum similitudinem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","text":"Administratio, conservatio et motio creaturae conditae distinguuntur a productione novae creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","text":"Quies dupliciter dicitur: cessatio ab operatione productiva et impletio desiderii in bono possesso.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A10","text":"Deus creaturis non indiget ad beatitudinem, sed in seipso sufficiens et beatus permanet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","text":"Benedictio ad multiplicationem pertinet, quae per administrationem creaturae et generationem similium ex similibus exercetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A12","text":"Sanctificatio maxime consistit in quiete in Deo, cuius fruitione res Deo dedicatae sanctae constituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX1","text":"Completio septimi diei non est ipsa ultima consummatio saeculi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX2","text":"Completio operum non exigit cessationem omnis divinae efficaciae in rebus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX3","text":"Eventus posteriores non sunt novitates simpliciter absolutae extra ordinem primae institutionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX4","text":"Quies Dei non est cessatio ex labore, motu corporali vel defectu virtutis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX5","text":"Deus non requiescit in creaturis quasi earum indigentia beatitudinem suam perficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX6","text":"Expositio qua Deus dicitur requiescere quia homines requiescere facit non est expositio primaria quietis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX7","text":"Benedictio et sanctificatio septimi diei non significant augmentum, diminutionem vel mutationem in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D1","text":"Una vox consummationis plures perfectiones temporaliter distinctas designat, quarum natura, gratia et gloria ordinem causaliter articulatum constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D2","text":"Septimus dies opus completum significat non quia omnis actio divina desinit, sed quia nova creaturarum institutio desinit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D3","text":"Creatio prima fungitur ut principium explicativum rerum posteriorum, sive per materiam, sive per virtutes causales, sive per similitudinem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D4","text":"Administratio creaturae conditae inaugurat perfectionem secundam, quia creaturas ad proprias operationes movet sine nova creatione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D5","text":"Benedictio septimi diei designat fecunditatem creaturae propagantis, sanctificatio vero finem eius in divina fruitione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D6","text":"Quies divina est simul negatio indigentiae divinae et fundamentum quietis beatificae creaturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SD1","text":"Prima institutio rerum constituit totalitatem causaliter apertam: futura intra ordinem creatum explicari possunt, quamvis temporaliter postea appareant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SD2","text":"Historia salutis non abolere perfectionem primam censetur, sed gradatim adducere naturam, gratiam et gloriam ad diversos modos consummationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SD3","text":"Oppositio inter creationem perfectam et mundum adhuc agentem solvitur per restrictionem completionis ad modum productionis, non ad omnem modum divinae praesentiae operativae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SD4","text":"Dies sanctus non ex proprietate temporis separata, sed ex ordine creaturae ad multiplicationem et quietem in Deo intelligitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit futurum creatum quod omni antecedenti fundamento materiali, causali vel similitudinali careat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit perfectionem divinam quae per acquisitionem creaturarum, usum creaturarum vel effectum creaturarum augeatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit notionem univocam perfectionis, secundum quam integritas naturae, gratia incarnationis et gloria finalis idem tempus vel idem actus essent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit quietem quae inertiam divinam significet, quia conservatio et administratio post cessationem creationis permanent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio praecidit possibilitatem ordinis creati absolute extrinseci primae institutioni, in quo posteriora nullo modo in initiis rerum praecesserint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio praecidit possibilitatem sanctitatis fundatae in mera cessatione temporali, separata a fruitione Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:FGS1","text":"Ambiguitas consummationis → distinctio perfectionis primae et secundae → distributio naturae, gratiae et gloriae in ordinem consummationum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:FGS2","text":"Apparens novitas posteriorum → classificatio praeexistentiae materialis, causalis vel similitudinalis → conservatio completionis primae institutionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:FGS3","text":"Apparens oppositio operis et quietis → distinctio creationis ab administratione et quietis ab inertia → quies Dei in seipso cum operatione conservativa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:FGS4","text":"Duplex quies divina → multiplicatio rerum per administrationem et quies creaturarum in Deo → benedictio et sanctificatio septimi diei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AF1","text":"Difficultas de completione operum → distinctio perfectionis substantialis et finalis → attributio primae perfectionis primae institutioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AF2","text":"Difficultas de posterioribus operibus → negatio novitatis absolutae → reductio posteriorum ad rationes in primis operibus contentas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AF3","text":"Difficultas de quiete Dei → distinctio cessationis et fruitionis → distributio multiplicationis ad benedictionem et divinae fruitionis ad sanctificationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ME1","text":"Notio completionis mutatur ab extremo chronologico simplici ad structuram graduatam integritatis, operationis et finis ultimi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ME2","text":"Notio novi mutatur ab eventu posteriore simpliciter ad eventum cuius principium materiale, causale vel similitudinale iam datum est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ME3","text":"Oppositio actio–quies dissolvitur, quia creatio nova, administratio conservativa et fruitio beatifica tres relationes diversas constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ME4","text":"Benedictio et sanctificatio desinunt esse praedicata redundanter adiuncta diei et fiunt duae functiones distinctae: propagatio creaturae et ordinatio ad Deum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ALT1","text":"Surface — Septimus dies dicitur completus, quietus, benedictus et sanctificatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ALT2","text":"Structural — Institutio prima continet integritatem universi et principia ex quibus administratio, multiplicatio et posteriora effecta procedunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Apparentes contradictiones scripturales et temporales solvuntur non per electionem unius sensus, sed per divisionem rationum secundum diversos respectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Deus immutabiliter sibi sufficit, dum creaturae temporaliter propagantur, conservantur et ad fruitionem divinam ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10","CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT1","text":"Distinctiones inter perfectionem primam et secundam, creationem et administrationem, cessationem et fruitionem sufficiunt ad restituendam machinam principalem quaestionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT2","text":"Systema maxime cohaeret ubi eadem distinctio modalis simultanee explicat completionem operum, operationem continuam et quietem divinam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT3","text":"Relatio inter perfectionem naturae, gratiae et gloriae determinatur ut ordo consummationum, sed modus precisus quo gratia et gloria ex institutione prima causaliter dependent non plene explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter potentiam Dei plures creaturas producendi et assertionem operis consummati, quia completio per cessationem voluntariam potius quam per exhaustionem potentiae definitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT5","text":"Classificatio posteriorum sub similitudine praecedente structuram completionis servat, sed amplitudinem rationis similitudinalis non ulterius delimitat, praesertim circa animas, incarnationem et gloriam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT6","text":"Attributio quietis post opera condita requirit ut relatio temporalis ad opera creaturarum distinguatur ab aeterna beatitudine Dei; distinctio asseritur, sed mechanice non amplius evolvitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia ex distinctione perfectionis procedit ad reordinationem novitatis, quietis, multiplicationis et sanctitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164505825707Z_4746f4cf","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 73","source_sha256":"5a0a39fdbe3245a0c187372283eaca2b3f8bc50c3de4384870f455d06236ba50","sha256":"29869330eeb9bf201463655504bff8c5d0d44304fae7402b36a1ce4ab57483eb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:45:05.826673+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS1","text":"The question investigates how, on the seventh day, the completion of works, divine rest, blessing, and sanctification can all be attributed together, although creatures and operations appear afterward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS2","text":"The argument is distinctive and reconstructive: it dissolves the apparent contradiction by distinguishing perfection, operation, novelty, rest, and divine effect upon creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS3","text":"The text moves from the equivocation of perfection to the order of a threefold consummation: of nature in the first institution, of grace in the Incarnation, and of glory at the end of the age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS4","text":"The continuation of things after the seventh day is reclassified not as absolutely new creation, but as material, causal, or similitudinal unfolding of those things that are precontained in the first works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS5","text":"The rest of God does not signify inactivity, but cessation from the production of new creatures and enjoyment of Himself, while the preservation and governance of the creature remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AS6","text":"The blessing and sanctification of the seventh day are distributed according to a twofold rest: the multiplication of creatures pertains to governance, holiness to the creature's rest in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","text":"The first perfection of a thing consists in the integrity of its substance; the second perfection consists in its end or in an operation ordered to the end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","text":"The first perfection is the cause of the second perfection, because an integral form is the principle of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","text":"The ultimate perfection of the universe is the beatitude of the saints, which is completed in the final consummation of the age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","text":"The integrity of the universe was complete in the first institution of things, and this perfection is attributed to the first seventh day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A5","text":"The consummation of nature pertains to the first institution of things, the consummation of grace to the Incarnation of Christ, and the consummation of glory to the end of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","text":"Cessation from the production of new creatures can demonstrate a completed work, even if God could produce more creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A7","text":"After the first works, nothing is made by God that is wholly new, because later things preexist materially, causally, or according to likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","text":"The governance, preservation, and motion of the created creature are distinguished from the production of a new creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","text":"Rest is spoken of in two ways: cessation from productive operation and fulfillment of desire in a possessed good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A10","text":"God does not need creatures for beatitude, but remains sufficient and blessed in Himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","text":"Blessing pertains to multiplication, which is exercised through the governance of the creature and the generation of like from like.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:A12","text":"Sanctification consists most especially in rest in God, by whose enjoyment things dedicated to God are constituted holy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX1","text":"The completion of the seventh day is not itself the final consummation of the age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX2","text":"The completion of works does not require the cessation of all divine efficacy in things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX3","text":"Later events are not simply absolute novelties outside the order of the first institution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX4","text":"The rest of God is not cessation due to labor, bodily motion, or deficiency of power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX5","text":"God does not rest in creatures as though need of them completed His beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX6","text":"The exposition according to which God is said to rest because He causes human beings to rest is not the primary exposition of divine rest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:NX7","text":"The blessing and sanctification of the seventh day do not signify increase, diminution, or change in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D1","text":"The one term consummation designates several temporally distinct perfections, of which nature, grace, and glory constitute a causally articulated order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D2","text":"The seventh day signifies a completed work not because all divine action ceases, but because the new institution of creatures ceases.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D3","text":"First creation functions as the explanatory principle of later things, whether through matter, causal powers, or likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D4","text":"The governance of the created creature inaugurates second perfection, because it moves creatures toward their proper operations without new creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D5","text":"The blessing of the seventh day designates the fecundity of the propagating creature, whereas sanctification designates its end in divine enjoyment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:D6","text":"Divine rest is at once the negation of divine need and the foundation of the creature's beatific rest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SD1","text":"The first institution of things constitutes a causally open totality: future things can unfold within the created order, although they appear later in time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SD2","text":"The history of salvation is considered not to abolish first perfection, but gradually to bring nature, grace, and glory to diverse modes of consummation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SD3","text":"The opposition between perfect creation and a world still acting is resolved by restricting completion to the mode of production, not to every mode of operative divine presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SD4","text":"The holy day is understood not from a separate property of time, but from the ordering of the creature to multiplication and rest in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:DNX1","text":"The system excludes a future created thing lacking every antecedent material, causal, or similitudinal foundation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a divine perfection increased through the acquisition of creatures, the use of creatures, or the effect of creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a univocal notion of perfection, according to which the integrity of nature, the grace of the Incarnation, and final glory would be the same time or the same act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:DNX4","text":"The system excludes rest signifying divine inactivity, because preservation and governance remain after the cessation of creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SNX1","text":"The argument precludes the possibility of a created order absolutely extrinsic to the first institution, in which later things did not in any way precede in the beginnings of things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:SNX2","text":"The argument precludes the possibility of holiness founded in mere temporal cessation, separated from the enjoyment of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:FGS1","text":"Ambiguity of consummation → distinction of first and second perfection → distribution of nature, grace, and glory into an order of consummations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:FGS2","text":"Apparent novelty of later things → classification of material, causal, or similitudinal preexistence → preservation of the completion of the first institution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:FGS3","text":"Apparent opposition of work and rest → distinction of creation from governance and of rest from inactivity → God's rest in Himself together with preservative operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:FGS4","text":"Twofold divine rest → multiplication of things through governance and rest of creatures in God → blessing and sanctification of the seventh day.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AF1","text":"Difficulty concerning the completion of works → distinction of substantial and final perfection → attribution of first perfection to the first institution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AF2","text":"Difficulty concerning later works → negation of absolute novelty → reduction of later things to principles contained in the first works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:AF3","text":"Difficulty concerning the rest of God → distinction of cessation and enjoyment → distribution of multiplication to blessing and divine enjoyment to sanctification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ME1","text":"The notion of completion is changed from a simple chronological endpoint into a graduated structure of integrity, operation, and ultimate end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A3","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ME2","text":"The notion of the new is changed from a later event simply speaking into an event whose material, causal, or similitudinal principle has already been given.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ME3","text":"The opposition action–rest is dissolved, because new creation, preservative governance, and beatific enjoyment constitute three distinct relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ME4","text":"Blessing and sanctification cease to be predicates redundantly joined to the day and become two distinct functions: propagation of the creature and ordering to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ALT1","text":"Surface — The seventh day is said to be complete, at rest, blessed, and sanctified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ALT2","text":"Structural — The first institution contains the integrity of the universe and the principles from which governance, multiplication, and later effects proceed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A4","CH_GGVC_P_65:A7","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Apparent scriptural and temporal contradictions are resolved not by choosing one meaning, but by dividing the reasons according to diverse respects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A1","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — God immutably suffices to Himself, while creatures are propagated, preserved, and ordered to divine enjoyment in time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10","CH_GGVC_P_65:A11","CH_GGVC_P_65:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT1","text":"The distinctions between first and second perfection, creation and governance, cessation and enjoyment suffice to restore the principal mechanism of the question.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT2","text":"The system is most coherent where the same modal distinction simultaneously explains the completion of works, continuous operation, and divine rest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A6","CH_GGVC_P_65:A8","CH_GGVC_P_65:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT3","text":"The relation among the perfection of nature, grace, and glory is determined as an order of consummations, but the precise mode by which grace and glory causally depend on the first institution is not fully explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A2","CH_GGVC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains between God's power to produce more creatures and the assertion of a completed work, because completion is defined by voluntary cessation rather than exhaustion of power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT5","text":"The classification of later things under antecedent likeness preserves the structure of completion, but does not further delimit the scope of similitudinal reason, especially concerning souls, the Incarnation, and glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT6","text":"The attribution of rest after created works requires that the temporal relation to the works of creatures be distinguished from God's eternal beatitude; the distinction is asserted, but not further developed mechanically.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_65:A9","CH_GGVC_P_65:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_65:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the distinction of perfection to the reordering of novelty, rest, multiplication, and holiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_65:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_65@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_65:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 74","title":"First Part · Question 73","context":"Chapter 74","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 73"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 73","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 74","order":75,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_66"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_66@R001","sha256":"ee497acb3defd9e1af85c3c1018df3629dac12a638acf5882b89e87e55c7cda7","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS1","text":"Quaestio numerum, unitatem vel pluralitatem, atque formulam linguisticam dierum examinat, ut narratio Genesis tamquam ordo institutionis mundi intelligatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS2","text":"Sufficientia dierum ex ordine distinguendi partes mundi et eas ornandi per propria complementa derivatur, non ex simplici rerum enumeratione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS3","text":"Controversia de uno die et septem diebus transfertur a sola successione temporali ad differentiam inter ordinem cognitionis angelicae et successionem statuum mundi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS4","text":"Formulae Scripturae de verbo, spiritu, bonitate, factione, vespere et mane exponuntur ut signa ordinum causalium, ontologicorum et cognoscitivorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS5","text":"Septimus dies claudit institutionem non nova productione, sed quiete a novis operibus et statu mundi cui nihil novum additur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","text":"Creatio, prout sola actio divina rerum substantiam producit, distinguitur a formatione per distinctionem et ornatum, quae mutationem creaturae vel ordinem cognitionis respicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","text":"Institutio mundi procedit a distinctione partium ad ornatum earum per habitatores vel perfectiones proprias.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","text":"Expositio communior sex dies disponit per tres partes mundi distinguendas et easdem tres partes ornandas: caelum, medium aquarum, terram.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A4","text":"Expositio Augustini senarium disponit per unam formationem spiritualem, duas formationes corporales et tres ornatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A5","text":"Productio animalium per ordinem ornatus partium mundi ordinatur, non per maiorem vel minorem differentiam naturalem inter species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","text":"In expositione dierum temporalium, quodlibet opus sequens novum perfectionis statum mundo addit; pluralitas dierum non ex impotentia divina procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A7","text":"“Omnia simul” ad creationem rerum quantum ad substantiam quodammodo informem refertur, non ad omnem distinctionem et ornatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","text":"“Dies” potest significare aut cognitionem angelicam operum naturaliter ordinatam aut successionem temporalem productionum et statuum mundi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A9","text":"Septimus dies significat cessationem a novis operibus condendis, non cessationem a propagatione rerum ex causis iam institutis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","text":"Formulae “in principio,” “dixit Deus,” “factum est” et “fecit Deus” diversos modos causalitatis et productionis designant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","text":"Expositio Augustini triplex esse rerum distinguit: esse in Verbo, esse in mente angelica, esse in natura propria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","text":"Superlatio Spiritus et divina complacentia bonitatis neque situm localem neque indigentiam, cognitionis acquisitionem aut affectionis mutationem in Deo significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A13","text":"Creatio et formatio diversis formulis Trinitatem insinuant: in creatione per creantem, principium et superlationem; in formatione per dicentem, Verbum et complacentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A14","text":"Diversae expositiones litterales admittuntur, dum fundamenta divinae causalitatis, ordinis rerum et distinctionis creationis a formatione servantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX1","text":"Creatio non est tertium genus operis quod, sicut distinctio et ornatus, die proprio mensurari debeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX2","text":"Ignis, aer et aqua non censentur omissa propterea quod Scriptura singulis proprium diem vel nomen separatum non attribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX3","text":"Dierum distributio animalium non sequitur taxonomiam specierum neque gradum differentiae naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX4","text":"Successio dierum non indicat moram, laborem otiosum aut indigentiam temporis in agere divino.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX5","text":"Vocabulum “dies” non univoce ad spatium temporale physicum restringitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX6","text":"Luminaria quarto die commemorata non requirunt novam productionem substantiae lucis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX7","text":"Quies septimae diei non est absoluta cessatio divinae efficaciae nec dies a Deo non factus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX8","text":"Spiritus super aquas ferri non significat corpus divinum loco motum aut amorem divinum rebus indigentem subiectum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX9","text":"“Vidit Deus quod esset bonum” non significat Deum post rem factam novam cognitionem vel novum gaudium recipere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX10","text":"Series “dixit,” “factum est,” “fecit” non est reiteratio inutilis eiusdem actus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D1","text":"Senarius sufficit quia opus institutionis per ordinem distinctionis et complementi distribuitur, sive triplici distinctione et triplici ornatu, sive formatione spirituali, corporali et ornativa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D2","text":"Volucres, pisces, terrestria et homo per respectum ad partes mundi ornandas aggregantur vel distinguuntur, etiam si naturae eorum diversitatem inaequalem habent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D3","text":"Creatio simul facta et formatio per dies distributa non contradicunt, quia “creatio” et “formatio” non eandem rationem productionis significant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D4","text":"Pluralitas dierum temporalium significat seriem perfectionum mundi, non seriem actuum divinorum tempore indigentium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D5","text":"Concordia inter Augustinum et alios maxime obtinet in causalitate divina et in ordine institutionis, dum differentiae de statu initiali materiae, temporalitate et actualitate productionum remanent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D6","text":"Omissio formulae bonitatis secunda die defectum ontologicum non demonstrat, quia approbatio ad opus posterius consummatum vel ad rationem manifesti et permanentis referri potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D7","text":"Locutio creatoria describit vel transitum ab exemplari Verbi ad cognitionem angelicam et naturam propriam, vel imperium, complementum et actionem immediatam Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D8","text":"Vespere, mane et “dies unus” possunt designare cognitiones angelicas, terminos temporis, mensuram diei naturalis vel reditum cyclicum, non unum sensum necessario exclusivum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SD1","text":"Mundus intelligitur ut systema partium functionali ordine dispositarum, in quo res per munus distinctionis, habitationis et perfectionis collocantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:D1","CH_GGVC_P_66:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SD2","text":"Tempus creationis non mensurat efficaciam Dei, sed ordinem perfectionum creaturae vel ordinem cognitionis creaturae spiritualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:D3","CH_GGVC_P_66:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SD3","text":"Narratio Genesis fit grammatica causalis stratificata, quae simul refert productionem rerum, rationem exemplarem Verbi, cognitionem angelicam et complacentiam divinam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:D6","CH_GGVC_P_66:D7","CH_GGVC_P_66:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SD4","text":"Pluralitas expositionum est circumscripta: licet littera de diebus varie explicetur, non licet removere creationem divinam, ordinem mundi aut dependentiam formationis a Deo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:D3","CH_GGVC_P_66:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX1","text":"Esse creatum non idem est ac esse plene distinctum, ornatum et in proprio statu perfectionis manifestatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX2","text":"Actio divina non subiicitur conditionibus successionis temporalis, situs localis, indigentiae amoris aut acquisitionis cognitionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A9","CH_GGVC_P_66:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX3","text":"Ordo creaturarum non ex discretis individuis aut nominibus Scripturae immediate colligitur, sed ex relatione earum ad structuram mundi perficiendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX4","text":"Interpretatio litteralis non postulat ut omnia vocabula temporalia, cosmologica et theologica in uno eodemque ordine semantico capiantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio excludit mundum in quo aeternum agere divinum per tempora creaturarum mensuratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio excludit identitatem inter primam positionem rei in esse et ultimam eius consummationem in ordine mundi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SNX3","text":"Argumentatio excludit chronologiam superficialem tamquam unicum principium intelligendi ordinem Genesis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS1","text":"Creatio prima, diebus non mensurata, ponit fundamentum rerum; distinctio format partes; ornatus eas per habitatores et perfectiones complet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS2","text":"Partes mundi distinguendae → partes ornandae → sex status perfectionis; vel formatio spiritualis → formatio corporalis superior et inferior → triplex ornatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS3","text":"Eadem series institutionis → dies temporales successive dispositi, vel cognitiones angelicae naturaliter ordinatae → pluralitas dierum sine necessaria pluralitate temporum divinorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS4","text":"Formulae Scripturae → distinctio modorum essendi et causalitatis → exclusio redundantiae verborum creatorialium → revelatio ordinis Trinitarii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS5","text":"Perfectio sexti status → cessatio a novis constitutionibus → propagatio ex causis institutis → septimus dies tamquam clausura ordinis creati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AF1","text":"Obiectiones de numero dierum → distinctio creationis ab institutione → distributio distinctionis et ornatus → sufficientia senarii et septenarii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AF2","text":"Obiectiones de “simul” et de pluralitate dierum → distinctio substantiae, formationis et cognitionis → coexistentia expositionis Augustini et expositionis temporalium dierum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A7","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AF3","text":"Obiectiones de locutionibus Scripturae → reclassificatio verborum ut signorum causalium et ontologicorum → cohaerentia formulae creatorialis et insinuatio Trinitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","CH_GGVC_P_66:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME1","text":"Dies reclassificatur ex mero intervallo chronologico in unitatem ordinis perfectionis, cognitionis vel institutionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME2","text":"Creaturae reclassificantur ex individuis separatim numerandis in complementa partium mundi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME3","text":"Oppositio “omnia simul” et “plures dies” solvitur per distinctionem inter productionem substantiae et formationem ordinatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME4","text":"Verba Scripturae reclassificantur ex narratione simpliciter descriptiva in indicia plurium modorum essendi, cognoscendi et causandi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME5","text":"Dissensio interpretum reclassificatur ex contradictione absoluta in diversitatem limitatam circa modum litterae et statum initialem rerum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A14","CH_GGVC_P_66:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus de numero dierum, de uno vel pluribus diebus, et de proprietate formularum Genesis directe disputat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ALT2","text":"Structural — Ratio dierum consistit in architectura mundi: partes distinguuntur, habitatoribus replentur et per status perfectionis ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones non per exclusionem unius expositionis solvuntur, sed per determinationem graduum quibus expositiones concordant vel dissentiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A14","CH_GGVC_P_66:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creatio divina, cognitio angelica, mutatio creaturae et tempus naturale ad diversos ordines pertinent nec mutuo confunduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT1","text":"Systema extractum sufficit ad restituendas tres quaestiones, quia continet rationem numeri, rationem dierum et rationem formularum Scripturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A4","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5","CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A9","CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","CH_GGVC_P_66:A13","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT2","text":"Firmissimum nodum systematis constituit distinctio inter creationem primam et formationem ordinatam, ex qua numerus dierum et sensus “simul” derivantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT3","text":"Minus determinata manet relatio exacta inter materiam informem Augustini et elementa sub propriis formis aliorum interpretum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis est imminutio differentiae inter expositionem dierum cognitionis angelicae et expositionem dierum temporalium, cum textus differentias reales de successione et productione retineat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT5","text":"Omissio bonitatis secunda diei non per unam rationem resolvitur, sed per plures explicationes alternativas iuxtapositas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT6","text":"Systema semanticum locutionum biblicarum cohaeret dum diversos ordines distinguit, sed pendet ab analogica translatione vocum temporalium, localium et affectivarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: difficultas enumerationis → separatio ordinum productionis → pluralitas moderata expositionum → grammatica causalis et Trinitaria narrationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_66:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_66:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_66:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164530684017Z_bd2b364f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 74","source_sha256":"ee497acb3defd9e1af85c3c1018df3629dac12a638acf5882b89e87e55c7cda7","sha256":"28e09960139e086f5df5e590eb5a0c05e78ee82db7aeb6453ae65ebc4d4a958c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:45:30.686488+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS1","text":"The question examines the number, unity or plurality, and linguistic formulation of the days, so that the Genesis narrative may be understood as an order of the institution of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS2","text":"The sufficiency of the days is derived from the order of distinguishing the parts of the world and adorning them through their proper complements, not from a simple enumeration of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS3","text":"The controversy concerning one day and seven days is transferred from temporal succession alone to the difference between the order of angelic cognition and the succession of states of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS4","text":"The Scriptural formulas concerning the word, spirit, goodness, making, evening, and morning are explained as signs of causal, ontological, and cognitive orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AS5","text":"The seventh day closes the institution not by a new production, but by rest from new works and by a state of the world to which nothing new is added.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","text":"Creation, insofar as it is the divine action alone that produces the substance of things, is distinguished from formation through distinction and adornment, which concerns the change of the creature or the order of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","text":"The institution of the world proceeds from the distinction of its parts to their adornment through inhabitants or proper perfections.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","text":"The more common exposition arranges the six days through the distinction of three parts of the world and the adornment of those same three parts: heaven, the middle region of the waters, and earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A4","text":"Augustine's exposition arranges the sixfold number through one spiritual formation, two corporeal formations, and three adornments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A5","text":"The production of animals is ordered according to the adornment of the parts of the world, not according to a greater or lesser natural difference among species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","text":"In the exposition of temporal days, each subsequent work adds a new state of perfection to the world; the plurality of days does not proceed from divine impotence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A7","text":"“All things at once” is referred to the creation of things as regards substance, in a certain manner formless, not to every distinction and adornment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","text":"“Day” can signify either angelic cognition of works naturally ordered, or the temporal succession of productions and states of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A9","text":"The seventh day signifies cessation from founding new works, not cessation from the propagation of things from causes already instituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","text":"The formulas “in the beginning,” “God said,” “it was made,” and “God made” designate diverse modes of causality and production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","text":"Augustine's exposition distinguishes a threefold being of things: being in the Word, being in the angelic mind, and being in their proper nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","text":"The hovering of the Spirit and the divine delight in goodness signify neither local position nor need, acquisition of cognition, or change of affection in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A13","text":"Creation and formation intimate the Trinity through different formulas: in creation through the creator, the principle, and hovering; in formation through the speaker, the Word, and delight.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:A14","text":"Diverse literal expositions are admitted, provided that the foundations of divine causality, the order of things, and the distinction of creation from formation are preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX1","text":"Creation is not a third kind of work that, like distinction and adornment, ought to be measured by its own day.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX2","text":"Fire, air, and water are not deemed omitted because Scripture does not assign to each a proper day or a separate name.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX3","text":"The distribution of animals among the days does not follow the taxonomy of species or the degree of natural difference.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX4","text":"The succession of days does not indicate delay, idle labor, or a need for time in divine action.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX5","text":"The term “day” is not univocally restricted to physical temporal duration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX6","text":"The luminaries mentioned on the fourth day do not require a new production of the substance of light.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX7","text":"The rest of the seventh day is not an absolute cessation of divine efficacy, nor is it a day not made by God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX8","text":"The Spirit's being borne over the waters does not signify a divine body moved in place or divine love subject to things in need.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX9","text":"“God saw that it was good” does not signify that God receives new knowledge or new joy after the thing has been made.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:NX10","text":"The sequence “said,” “it was made,” “made” is not a useless reiteration of the same act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D1","text":"The sixfold number suffices because the work of institution is distributed according to the order of distinction and completion, whether by threefold distinction and threefold adornment, or by spiritual, corporeal, and adornment-formations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D2","text":"Birds, fishes, terrestrial animals, and man are grouped or distinguished by reference to the parts of the world to be adorned, even if their natures possess unequal diversity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D3","text":"Creation made simultaneously and formation distributed through days do not contradict one another, because “creation” and “formation” do not signify the same account of production.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D4","text":"The plurality of temporal days signifies a series of perfections of the world, not a series of divine acts needing time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D5","text":"Harmony between Augustine and others obtains chiefly in divine causality and in the order of institution, while differences remain concerning the initial state of matter, temporality, and the actuality of productions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D6","text":"The omission of the formula of goodness on the second day does not demonstrate an ontological defect, because approval can be referred to a later consummated work or to the character of what is manifest and permanent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D7","text":"Creative speech describes either the transition from the exemplar of the Word to angelic cognition and proper nature, or God's command, completion, and immediate action.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:D8","text":"Evening, morning, and “one day” can designate angelic cognitions, temporal boundaries, the measure of a natural day, or cyclical return, not necessarily one exclusive sense.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SD1","text":"The world is understood as a system of parts arranged in a functional order, in which things are situated by the function of distinction, habitation, and perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:D1","CH_GGVC_P_66:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SD2","text":"The time of creation does not measure the efficacy of God, but the order of the creature's perfections or the order of cognition of the spiritual creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:D3","CH_GGVC_P_66:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SD3","text":"The Genesis narrative becomes a stratified causal grammar, which simultaneously relates the production of things, the exemplary account of the Word, angelic cognition, and divine delight.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:D6","CH_GGVC_P_66:D7","CH_GGVC_P_66:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SD4","text":"The plurality of expositions is circumscribed: although the letter concerning the days may be explained variously, it is not permissible to remove divine creation, the order of the world, or the dependence of formation upon God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:D3","CH_GGVC_P_66:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX1","text":"Created being is not the same as being fully distinguished, adorned, and manifested in its proper state of perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX2","text":"Divine action is not subject to the conditions of temporal succession, local position, need of love, or acquisition of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A9","CH_GGVC_P_66:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX3","text":"The order of creatures is not immediately inferred from discrete individuals or the names of Scripture, but from their relation to the completion of the structure of the world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX4","text":"Literal interpretation does not require that all temporal, cosmological, and theological terms be taken within one and the same semantic order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SNX1","text":"The argument excludes a world in which eternal divine action is measured by the times of creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SNX2","text":"The argument excludes identity between the first establishment of a thing in being and its ultimate consummation in the order of the world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:SNX3","text":"The argument excludes superficial chronology as the sole principle for understanding the order of Genesis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_66:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS1","text":"First creation, not measured by days, lays the foundation of things; distinction forms the parts; adornment completes them through inhabitants and perfections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS2","text":"Parts of the world to be distinguished → parts to be adorned → six states of perfection; or spiritual formation → higher and lower corporeal formation → threefold adornment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS3","text":"The same series of institution → temporal days successively arranged, or naturally ordered angelic cognitions → plurality of days without a necessary plurality of divine times.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS4","text":"Scriptural formulas → distinction of modes of being and causality → exclusion of redundancy in creative words → revelation of Trinitarian order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:FGS5","text":"Perfection of the sixth state → cessation from new establishments → propagation from instituted causes → seventh day as closure of the created order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AF1","text":"Objections concerning the number of days → distinction of creation from institution → distribution of distinction and adornment → sufficiency of the sixfold and sevenfold numbers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AF2","text":"Objections concerning “at once” and the plurality of days → distinction of substance, formation, and cognition → coexistence of Augustine's exposition and the exposition of temporal days.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A7","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:AF3","text":"Objections concerning Scriptural expressions → reclassification of words as causal and ontological signs → coherence of the creative formula and intimation of the Trinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","CH_GGVC_P_66:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME1","text":"Day is reclassified from a mere chronological interval into a unit of the order of perfection, cognition, or institution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME2","text":"Creatures are reclassified from individuals to be counted separately into complements of the parts of the world.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME3","text":"The opposition between “all things at once” and “many days” is resolved through the distinction between the production of substance and ordered formation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME4","text":"The words of Scripture are reclassified from simply descriptive narration into indications of multiple modes of being, knowing, and causing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ME5","text":"The disagreement of interpreters is reclassified from absolute contradiction into limited diversity concerning the mode of the letter and the initial state of things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A14","CH_GGVC_P_66:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text directly disputes concerning the number of days, one or several days, and the propriety of the formulas of Genesis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ALT2","text":"Structural — The rationale of the days consists in the architecture of the world: parts are distinguished, filled with inhabitants, and ordered through states of perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved not by excluding one exposition, but by determining the levels at which expositions agree or disagree.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A14","CH_GGVC_P_66:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Divine creation, angelic cognition, creaturely change, and natural time belong to diverse orders and are not mutually confused.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT1","text":"The extracted system suffices to reconstruct the three questions, because it contains the rationale of the number, the rationale of the days, and the rationale of the Scriptural formulas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A2","CH_GGVC_P_66:A3","CH_GGVC_P_66:A4","CH_GGVC_P_66:A5","CH_GGVC_P_66:A6","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7","CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A9","CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A11","CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","CH_GGVC_P_66:A13","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT2","text":"The firmest node of the system is constituted by the distinction between first creation and ordered formation, from which the number of days and the meaning of “at once” are derived.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT3","text":"The exact relation between Augustine's formless matter and the elements under their proper forms of other interpreters remains less determinate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A1","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture is the diminution of the difference between the exposition of the days of angelic cognition and the exposition of temporal days, since the text retains real differences concerning succession and production.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT5","text":"The omission of goodness on the second day is not resolved by one account, but by several juxtaposed alternative explanations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A12","CH_GGVC_P_66:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT6","text":"The semantic system of biblical expressions is coherent while distinguishing diverse orders, but depends upon an analogical translation of temporal, local, and affective terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:A8","CH_GGVC_P_66:A10","CH_GGVC_P_66:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_66:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: difficulty of enumeration → separation of orders of production → moderated plurality of expositions → causal and Trinitarian grammar of the narrative.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_66:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_66:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_66:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_66:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_66:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_66@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_66:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 75","title":"First Part · Question 74","context":"Chapter 75","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 74"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 74","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 75","order":76,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_67"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_67@R001","sha256":"5b7373298a07430b51b375f6dcac29c922a087696a496f016c11ece6bd875b40","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS1","text":"Natura humana theologice investigatur ex parte animae, corpore tantum secundum habitudinem ad animam considerato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS2","text":"Natura animae ex operationibus vitae inquiritur, quia modus operationis principium et modum essendi manifestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS3","text":"Anima humana est actus corporis et pars hominis, simul tamen principium incorporeum, per se subsistens atque incorruptibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS4","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica et reconstructiva errores corporeitatis, dualismi et spiritualis homogeneitatis per distinctiones actus et potentiae, operationis et organi, partis et totius dissolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS5","text":"Motus procedit ab effectibus vitalibus ad principium vitae, ab universalitate cognitionis ad subsistentiam, a diversitate operationum ad distinctionem formarum et specierum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS6","text":"Series concluditur anima humana media positione constituta: supra formas materiales propter intellectum subsistentem, infra angelum propter naturalem unibilitatem corpori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A1","text":"Anima est primum principium vitae in viventibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A2","text":"Vivere corpori non convenit ex eo quod corpus est, sed ex eo quod est corpus tali actu determinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A3","text":"Quod actu tale est, determinationem suam ab actu formali accipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","text":"Principium cognoscens naturas omnium corporum neque naturam corpoream determinatam neque organum corporeum determinatum habere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","text":"Modus operationis modum essendi sequitur: operatio propria per se subsistentiam manifestat, absentia vero operationis propriae per se non-subsistentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","text":"Sentire et operationes animae sensitivae cum immutatione corporis fiunt atque coniuncto attribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","text":"Definitio speciei naturalis formam et materiam communem comprehendit, non autem materiam signatam individuantem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A8","text":"Illud est res completa quod operationes illius rei exercet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A9","text":"Forma, inquantum forma, est actus; ens in potentia tantum non potest esse pars actus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A10","text":"Receptum recipitur secundum modum recipientis: intellectus formas absolute recipit, materia autem formas individuat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","text":"Forma creata subsistens esse participat atque finitur secundum capacitatem participantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","text":"Quod per se subsistit non corrumpitur per accidens ex corruptione alterius, sed tantum per corruptionem sui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A13","text":"Forma subsistens esse per se habet nec a se ipsa separari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","text":"Diversitas operationum naturalium diversitatem speciei et gradus naturalis manifestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A15","text":"Formae incorporeae a materia separatae non possunt solo numero distingui intra eandem speciem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","text":"Corpus non est de essentia animae, sed unibilitas corpori ad naturam animae pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","text":"Anima humana unita per phantasmata intelligit, angelus autem naturaliter sine corpore et sine collectione a visibilibus intelligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX1","text":"Anima non est corpus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX2","text":"Non quodlibet proximum principium operationis vitalis est anima; organum vitae non est primum principium vitae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX3","text":"Non omne movens movetur per se, neque motus animae per accidens corporeitatem eius probat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX4","text":"Contactus moventis et moti non restringitur ad contactum quantitatis, quia contactus virtutis rem incorpoream corpori coniungere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX5","text":"Cognitio rei corporeae non requirit similitudinem corpoream actu constitutam in natura cognoscentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX6","text":"Corpus non est organum quo intellectus intelligit, quamvis phantasma corporeum obiective requiratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX7","text":"Animae brutorum non sunt substantiae per se subsistentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX8","text":"Homo neque anima sola neque corpus solum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX9","text":"Anima humana non est composita ex materia corporali vel spirituali et forma.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX10","text":"Immaterialitas animae non facit eam actum purum aut infinitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX11","text":"Corruptio corporis non importat corruptionem animae humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX12","text":"Communis intellectualitas vel communis beatitudo aeterna non constituit animam et angelum in una specie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0133","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D1","text":"Anima, quia est primum principium vitae corporis, est actus corporis et non corpus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A1","CH_GGVC_P_67:A2","CH_GGVC_P_67:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","text":"Principium intellectivum est incorporeum et non exercet intelligere per organum corporeum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","text":"Anima humana per se subsistit, quia intellectus operationem propriam corpori non communicatam exercet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D4","text":"Anima sensitiva brutorum non subsistit, quia nullam operationem propriam praeter operationem coniuncti habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D5","text":"Animae brutorum cum corporibus corrumpuntur, anima autem humana ex sola corporis corruptione non corrumpitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D6","text":"Homo est compositum ex anima et corpore, quia materia communis ad speciem humanam pertinet et sentire est operatio coniuncti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D7","text":"Anima est hoc aliquid ut subsistens, non autem ut natura humana completa, hypostasis aut persona.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D8","text":"Anima intellectiva caret compositione materiae et formae, quia est forma et recipit formas rerum absolute.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A9","CH_GGVC_P_67:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D9","text":"Potentia intellectiva ad species intelligibiles non est materia prima neque eiusdem rationis cum potentia materiae ad formas individuales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A9","CH_GGVC_P_67:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D10","text":"Anima creata est finita et composita ex forma et esse participato, quamvis materia careat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","text":"Anima humana est incorruptibilis, quia subsistit et, ut forma subsistens, esse suum per corporis corruptionem aut separationem a se amittere non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:A13","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D12","text":"Creatio ex nihilo non constituit in anima potentiam passivam ad non esse; reductio in nihilum solam cessationem influxus creatoris significaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0114","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D13","text":"Necessitas phantasmatum dependentiam obiectivam et dispositivam a corpore constituit, non organicam executionem actus intellectivi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D14","text":"Anima separata, quia subsistere pergit, alium modum intelligendi quam cognitionem per phantasmata habere debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A13","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D15","text":"Anima et angelus non sunt eiusdem speciei, atque anima inferiorem intellectualitatis gradum tenet propter naturalem ordinationem ad corpus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","CH_GGVC_P_67:A15","CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD1","text":"Hylomorphismus humanus asymmetricus est: anima totum corpus actu informat, sed propter operationem intellectivam esse suum a corpore non accipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D1","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD2","text":"Eadem universalitas intellectus simul corporeitatem principii cognoscentis excludit et subsistentiam animae fundat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD3","text":"Gradus vitae secundum autonomiam operationis ordinantur: sensus ad coniunctum, intellectus ad principium subsistens pertinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD4","text":"Corporalitas neque accidens extrinsecum homini neque ratio totalis animae est; constituit materiam speciei humanae et condicionem naturalis operationis animae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD5","text":"Finitudo, immaterialitas et incorruptibilitas simul consistere possunt, quia finitude ex participatione essendi, materialitas ex modo receptionis, corruptibilitas ex modo subsistentiae discernuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A10","CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:D10","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD6","text":"Post mortem manet anima subsistens, non homo completus, atque permanentia subiecti mutationem modi cognoscendi requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D7","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX1","text":"Imaginabilitas corporea non est mensura entitatis; quod sub phantasmate corporis cogitari non potest non ideo nihil est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX2","text":"Determinatio corporea non potest esse fundamentum cognitionis universalis, quia eam potius contraheret et impediret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX3","text":"Dependentia ab aliquo corporeo non univoce organum, partem essentiae aut causam essendi significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX4","text":"Communitas generis animalis non tollit differentiam formae specificae inter hominem et bruta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX5","text":"Subsistentia non importat completionem specificam, personalitatem aut separationem naturalem a corpore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX6","text":"Potentia, receptio et transmutatio non sunt signa necessaria materiae, quia potentia intellectiva alterius rationis est quam potentia materiae primae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX7","text":"Immaterialitas creata non excludit compositionem metaphysicam nec finitudinem, sed solam compositionem materiae et formae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX8","text":"Communis finis supernaturalis non destruit distinctiones naturales specierum et graduum intellectualitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0133","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX1","text":"Materialismus ontologicus excluditur, quia neque vita neque intellectus ex corpore qua corpore explicari possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A2","CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:D1","CH_GGVC_P_67:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX2","text":"Dualismus hominem cum anima completa corpus extrinsecus utente identificans excluditur, quia sensus et species humana coniunctum requirunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX3","text":"Possibilitas hominis completi sine corpore praecluditur, etiam si anima sine corpore subsistere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D7","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX4","text":"Genus spirituale planum, in quo omnes substantiae intellectuales sola numero differant, excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","CH_GGVC_P_67:A15","CH_GGVC_P_67:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX5","text":"Continuatio cognitionis post separationem sub eodem modo phantasmatico inadmissibilis est; permanentia animae alium modum operationis postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS1","text":"Machina ab operationibus vitae manifestis ad primum earum principium progreditur: vita manifesta → primum principium → anima.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS2","text":"Corporeitas qua talis vitam non explicat; determinatio corporis vivi actum formalem requirit: corpus indeterminatum → corpus tale → actus corporis → anima non-corporea.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A2","CH_GGVC_P_67:A3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS3","text":"Universalitas obiecti intellectus determinationem corpoream excludit et operationem propriam ostendit: omnia corpora cognoscibilia → nulla natura corporea determinata → nullum organum → operatio per se → subsistentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS4","text":"Partitione operationum fit partitio modorum essendi: immutatio corporea → operatio coniuncti → anima sensitiva non subsistens; intelligere non organicum → anima humana subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS5","text":"Definitio speciei et distributio operationum integrant hominem: materia communis et forma → species naturalis → operationes sensitivae coniuncti → homo compositus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:A8","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS6","text":"Modus receptionis compositionem animae determinat: receptio absoluta formarum → exclusio materiae → forma subsistens → esse participatum → finita immaterialitas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A9","CH_GGVC_P_67:A10","CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D8","CH_GGVC_P_67:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS7","text":"Subsistentia et modus naturalis operationis ultimas conclusiones generant: forma subsistens → incorruptibilitas; unibilitas corpori → modus phantasmaticus → gradus inferior angelo → diversitas speciei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:A13","CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AF1","text":"Motus principalis est: operationes vitales → anima ut actus non-corporeus → intellectus ut principium subsistens → sensus ut operatio coniuncti → homo ut compositum → anima ut forma immaterialis → incorruptibilitas → distinctio ab angelo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AF2","text":"Forma dialectica recurrens est: obiectio ex praedicatione univoca → distinctio modorum → restitutio analogiae actus et potentiae vel operationis et esse → conclusio limitata → remotio consequentiae adversae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME1","text":"Relatio animae et corporis a relatione duorum corporum ad relationem actus et corporis actuati transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME2","text":"Subsistentia a completione specifica et personalitate separatur, unde anima simul subsistens et pars esse potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME3","text":"Dependentia intellectus a corpore in dependentiam ab organo et dependentiam ab obiecto phantasmatico dividitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","CH_GGVC_P_67:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME4","text":"Potentia materialis et potentia intellectiva distinguuntur, atque transmutabilitas non amplius materiam necessario indicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME5","text":"Compositio materiae et formae a compositione formae et esse participati separatur, quo substantia immaterialis finita cogitari potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D8","CH_GGVC_P_67:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME6","text":"Mors corporis a corruptione animae distinguitur, sicut corruptio per accidens a corruptione per se.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:D5","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME7","text":"Ager intellectualium substantiarum ex genere indifferenti in gradus et species secundum operationem naturalem et habitudinem ad corpus reordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","CH_GGVC_P_67:A15","CH_GGVC_P_67:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei septem determinationes quaerit: corporeitatem, subsistentiam, statum animae sensitivae, constitutionem hominis, compositionem animae, incorruptibilitatem et relationem ad angelum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis modum operationis ad modum essendi refert atque distinctionibus actus et potentiae, formae et materiae, partis et totius regitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A3","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus falsas univocationes dissolvit: moveri, tangere, subsistere, pati, componi et specie convenire secundum diversos modos distribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis animam ut formam creatam esse participantem constituit, cuius operatio corpori unita phantasmatis mediatur, post separationem autem alio modo continuatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad septem conclusiones principales restituendas, quia definitionem animae, regulam operationis et esse, hylomorphismum et participationem essendi continent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT2","text":"Firmissima commissura est transitus ab universalitate cognitionis ad exclusionem organi corporei et inde ad operationem propriam atque subsistentiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT3","text":"Cohaerentia systematis distinctione inter subsistentiam partis et completionem personae nititur; hac distinctione remota, anima aut accidens aut homo completus fieret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT4","text":"Distinctio inter corpus ut organum et corpus ut fons phantasmatum necessaria est, sed mechanismus dependentiae obiectivae tantum breviter determinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT5","text":"Modus cognitionis animae separatae affirmatur potius quam hic demonstratur atque ad ulteriorem tractationem differtur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT6","text":"Regula secundum quam formae incorporeae non multiplicantur numero intra unam speciem tensionem cum pluralitate animarum humanarum eiusdem speciei parit; solutio expresse in posterum differtur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT7","text":"Assertio animam non proprie in specie esse, sed compositum, commissuram terminologicam cum conclusione animam et angelum non esse eiusdem speciei relinquit; unibilitas corpori distinctionem sustinet, sed formulam non omnino dissolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT8","text":"Probatio ex desiderio naturali essendi semper principio non ulterius probato nititur, sed ad conclusionem incorruptibilitatis non est necessaria, quia argumentum ex forma subsistente iam sufficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT9","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: ab operationibus ad essentiam, ab essentia ad subsistentiam, a subsistentia ad incorruptibilitatem, atque a modo naturali operationis ad gradum specificum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164602497606Z_fbbc2430","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 75","source_sha256":"5b7373298a07430b51b375f6dcac29c922a087696a496f016c11ece6bd875b40","sha256":"a357c8ae174eeecf8509ae6d2fcf2b50960ac9298c4282ea7f1b5f617de62678","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:46:02.499751+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS1","text":"Human nature is investigated theologically on the side of the soul, the body being considered only according to its relation to the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS2","text":"The nature of the soul is investigated from the operations of life, because the mode of operation manifests the principle and mode of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS3","text":"The human soul is the act of the body and a part of the human being, yet at the same time an incorporeal principle, subsisting through itself and incorruptible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS4","text":"Metaphysical and reconstructive argumentation dissolves errors of corporeality, dualism, and spiritual homogeneity through distinctions of act and potency, operation and organ, part and whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS5","text":"The movement proceeds from vital effects to the principle of life, from the universality of cognition to subsistence, from the diversity of operations to the distinction of forms and species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AS6","text":"The series concludes with the human soul established in an intermediate position: above material forms on account of its subsistent intellect, below the angel on account of its natural unibility to the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A1","text":"The soul is the first principle of life in living things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A2","text":"Living belongs to a body not by reason of its being a body, but by reason of its being a body determined by such an act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A3","text":"What is actually such receives its determination from formal act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","text":"A principle cognizing the natures of all bodies can have neither a determinate corporeal nature nor a determinate corporeal organ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","text":"The mode of operation follows the mode of being: a proper operation manifests subsistence through itself, whereas the absence of a proper operation manifests non-subsistence through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","text":"Sensation and the operations of the sensitive soul occur with bodily alteration and are attributed to the composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","text":"The definition of a natural species includes form and common matter, but not individuating designated matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A8","text":"That is a complete thing which exercises the operations of that thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A9","text":"Form, insofar as it is form, is act; what is only in potency cannot be part of act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A10","text":"What is received is received according to the mode of the recipient: the intellect receives forms absolutely, whereas matter individuates forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","text":"A created subsistent form participates in being and is limited according to the capacity of the participant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","text":"What subsists through itself is not corrupted accidentally by the corruption of another, but only by its own corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A13","text":"A subsistent form has being through itself and cannot be separated from itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","text":"The diversity of natural operations manifests diversity of species and natural grade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A15","text":"Incorporeal forms separated from matter cannot be distinguished by number alone within the same species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","text":"The body is not of the essence of the soul, but unibility to the body belongs to the nature of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","text":"The human soul, when united, understands through phantasms, whereas the angel naturally understands without a body and without gathering from visible things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX1","text":"The soul is not a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX2","text":"Not every proximate principle of vital operation is a soul; the organ of life is not the first principle of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX3","text":"Not every mover is moved through itself, nor does the accidental motion of the soul prove its corporeality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX4","text":"The contact of mover and moved is not restricted to contact of quantity, because contact of power can unite an incorporeal thing to a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX5","text":"Cognition of a corporeal thing does not require a corporeal likeness actually constituted in the nature of the knower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX6","text":"The body is not the organ by which the intellect understands, although a corporeal phantasm is objectively required.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX7","text":"The souls of brute animals are not substances subsisting through themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX8","text":"The human being is neither the soul alone nor the body alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX9","text":"The human soul is not composed of corporeal or spiritual matter and form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX10","text":"The immateriality of the soul does not make it pure act or infinite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX11","text":"The corruption of the body does not entail the corruption of the human soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:NX12","text":"Common intellectuality or common eternal beatitude does not constitute the soul and the angel in one species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0133","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D1","text":"The soul, because it is the first principle of the life of the body, is the act of the body and not a body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A1","CH_GGVC_P_67:A2","CH_GGVC_P_67:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","text":"The intellective principle is incorporeal and does not exercise understanding through a corporeal organ.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","text":"The human soul subsists through itself, because the intellect exercises a proper operation not communicated to the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D4","text":"The sensitive soul of brute animals does not subsist, because it has no proper operation beyond the operation of the composite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D5","text":"The souls of brute animals are corrupted with their bodies, whereas the human soul is not corrupted by the corruption of the body alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D6","text":"The human being is composed of soul and body, because common matter belongs to the human species and sensation is an operation of the composite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D7","text":"The soul is a this something insofar as it subsists, but not insofar as it is a complete human nature, hypostasis, or person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D8","text":"The intellective soul lacks the composition of matter and form, because it is form and receives the forms of things absolutely.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A9","CH_GGVC_P_67:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D9","text":"The intellective potency with respect to intelligible species is not prime matter, nor is it of the same ratio as the potency of matter with respect to individual forms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A9","CH_GGVC_P_67:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D10","text":"The created soul is finite and composed of form and participated being, although it lacks matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","text":"The human soul is incorruptible, because it subsists and, as a subsistent form, cannot lose its own being through the corruption of the body or separation from itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:A13","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D12","text":"Creation from nothing does not constitute in the soul a passive potency toward non-being; reduction to nothing would signify only the cessation of the Creator's influx.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0114","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D13","text":"The necessity of phantasms establishes an objective and dispositive dependence on the body, not an organic execution of the intellective act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D14","text":"The separated soul, because it continues to subsist, must have a mode of understanding other than cognition through phantasms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A13","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:D15","text":"The soul and the angel are not of the same species, and the soul holds a lower grade of intellectuality on account of its natural ordination to the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","CH_GGVC_P_67:A15","CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD1","text":"Human hylomorphism is asymmetric: the soul actually informs the whole body, but on account of intellective operation it does not receive its being from the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D1","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD2","text":"The same universality of the intellect simultaneously excludes the corporeality of the cognizing principle and grounds the subsistence of the soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD3","text":"The grades of life are ordered according to the autonomy of operation: sense belongs to the composite, intellect to a subsistent principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD4","text":"Corporeality is neither an extrinsic accident to the human being nor the total account of the soul; it constitutes the matter of the human species and the condition of the soul's natural operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD5","text":"Finitude, immateriality, and incorruptibility can coexist, because finitude, materiality, and corruptibility are distinguished respectively from participation in being, the mode of reception, and the mode of subsistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A10","CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:D10","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SD6","text":"After death the subsistent soul remains, not the complete human being, and the permanence of the subject requires a change in the mode of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D7","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX1","text":"Corporeal imaginability is not the measure of entity; what cannot be thought under a bodily phantasm is not thereby nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX2","text":"Corporeal determination cannot be the foundation of universal cognition, because it would rather contract and impede it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX3","text":"Dependence on something corporeal does not univocally signify an organ, a part of essence, or a cause of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX4","text":"Community of animal genus does not remove the difference of specific form between the human being and brute animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX5","text":"Subsistence does not entail specific completeness, personality, or natural separation from the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX6","text":"Potency, reception, and transmutation are not necessary signs of matter, because intellective potency is of another ratio than the potency of prime matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX7","text":"Created immateriality does not exclude metaphysical composition or finitude, but only the composition of matter and form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:DNX8","text":"A common supernatural end does not destroy the natural distinctions of species and grades of intellectuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0133","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX1","text":"Ontological materialism is excluded, because neither life nor intellect can be explained from body precisely as body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A2","CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:D1","CH_GGVC_P_67:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX2","text":"Dualism identifying the human being with a complete soul using the body extrinsically is excluded, because sense and the human species require the composite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX3","text":"The possibility of a complete human being without a body is precluded, even if the soul can subsist without a body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D7","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX4","text":"A flat spiritual genus, in which all intellectual substances differ by number alone, is excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","CH_GGVC_P_67:A15","CH_GGVC_P_67:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:SNX5","text":"The continuation of cognition after separation under the same phantasmal mode is inadmissible; the permanence of the soul demands another mode of operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS1","text":"The mechanism progresses from manifest operations of life to their first principle: manifest life → first principle → soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS2","text":"Corporeality as such does not explain life; the determination of a living body requires formal act: indeterminate body → such a body → act of body → non-corporeal soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A2","CH_GGVC_P_67:A3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS3","text":"The universality of the object of the intellect excludes corporeal determination and shows a proper operation: all cognizable bodies → no determinate corporeal nature → no organ → operation through itself → subsistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS4","text":"The partition of operations yields a partition of modes of being: bodily alteration → operation of the composite → non-subsistent sensitive soul; non-organic understanding → subsistent human soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS5","text":"The definition of species and the distribution of operations integrate the human being: common matter and form → natural species → sensitive operations of the composite → composite human being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A6","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:A8","CH_GGVC_P_67:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS6","text":"The mode of reception determines the composition of the soul: absolute reception of forms → exclusion of matter → subsistent form → participated being → finite immateriality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A9","CH_GGVC_P_67:A10","CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D8","CH_GGVC_P_67:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:FGS7","text":"Subsistence and the natural mode of operation generate the final conclusions: subsistent form → incorruptibility; unibility to the body → phantasmal mode → lower grade than the angel → diversity of species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:A13","CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AF1","text":"The principal movement is: vital operations → soul as non-corporeal act → intellect as subsistent principle → sense as operation of the composite → human being as composite → soul as immaterial form → incorruptibility → distinction from the angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:AF2","text":"The recurrent dialectical form is: objection from univocal predication → distinction of modes → restoration of the analogy of act and potency or of operation and being → limited conclusion → removal of the adverse consequence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME1","text":"The relation of soul and body is transferred from the relation of two bodies to the relation of act and actualized body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME2","text":"Subsistence is separated from specific completeness and personality, whence the soul can be at once subsistent and a part.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D3","CH_GGVC_P_67:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME3","text":"The dependence of the intellect on the body is divided into dependence on an organ and dependence on the phantasmal object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","CH_GGVC_P_67:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME4","text":"Material potency and intellective potency are distinguished, and mutability no longer necessarily indicates matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME5","text":"The composition of matter and form is separated from the composition of form and participated being, whereby a finite immaterial substance can be conceived.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D8","CH_GGVC_P_67:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME6","text":"The death of the body is distinguished from the corruption of the soul, just as accidental corruption is distinguished from corruption through itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A12","CH_GGVC_P_67:D5","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ME7","text":"The field of intellectual substances is reordered from an indifferent genus into grades and species according to natural operation and relation to the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A14","CH_GGVC_P_67:A15","CH_GGVC_P_67:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ALT1","text":"The surface level seeks seven determinations: corporeality, subsistence, the state of the sensitive soul, the constitution of the human being, the composition of the soul, incorruptibility, and relation to the angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ALT2","text":"The structural level refers the mode of operation to the mode of being and is governed by distinctions of act and potency, form and matter, part and whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A3","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:A7","CH_GGVC_P_67:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level dissolves false univocities: being moved, touching, subsisting, being acted upon, being composed, and agreeing in species are distributed according to diverse modes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level establishes the soul as a created form participating in being, whose operation, when united to the body, is mediated by phantasms, but after separation continues in another mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A11","CH_GGVC_P_67:A16","CH_GGVC_P_67:A17","CH_GGVC_P_67:D11","CH_GGVC_P_67:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the seven principal conclusions, because they contain the definition of the soul, the rule of operation and being, hylomorphism, and participation in being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT2","text":"The strongest joint is the transition from the universality of cognition to the exclusion of a corporeal organ and thence to proper operation and subsistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:A4","CH_GGVC_P_67:A5","CH_GGVC_P_67:D2","CH_GGVC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT3","text":"The coherence of the system rests on the distinction between the subsistence of a part and the completeness of a person; once this distinction is removed, the soul would become either an accident or a complete human being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D6","CH_GGVC_P_67:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT4","text":"The distinction between the body as organ and the body as source of phantasms is necessary, but the mechanism of objective dependence is determined only briefly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_67:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT5","text":"The mode of cognition of the separated soul is affirmed rather than demonstrated here and is deferred to further treatment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT6","text":"The rule according to which incorporeal forms are not multiplied by number within one species creates a tension with the plurality of human souls of the same species; the solution is expressly deferred to a later time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0127","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT7","text":"The assertion that it is not properly the soul, but the composite, that is in a species leaves a terminological joint with the conclusion that the soul and the angel are not of the same species; unibility to the body sustains the distinction, but does not wholly dissolve the formulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0129","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT8","text":"The proof from the natural desire always to be rests on a principle not further proved, but it is not necessary for the conclusion of incorruptibility, because the argument from subsistent form already suffices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_67:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: from operations to essence, from essence to subsistence, from subsistence to incorruptibility, and from the natural mode of operation to the specific grade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0107","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_67:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_67@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_67:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 76","title":"First Part · Question 75","context":"Chapter 76","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 75"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 75","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 76","order":77,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_68"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_68@R001","sha256":"2878a6c8da84f3d2ca460da129d67936753f1bca11ee855d230dd25fa0c63865","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS1","text":"Quaestio est quomodo principium intellectivum, quamvis subsistens et operatione organum excedens, unum hominem corporeum constituat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS2","text":"Anima intellectiva est forma substantialis, unica, immediata et numero propria corporis humani.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica et reconstructiva, sed polemice procedit contra exemplaria animae ut motoris, intellectus communis, pluralitatis formarum et unionis mediatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS4","text":"Motus primarius ab attributione actus intelligendi ad principium formale subiecti intelligentis procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS5","text":"Ex unione formali deducuntur multiplicitas animarum, unitas graduum vitalium, exclusio aliarum formarum, dispositio corporis et immediatio unionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS6","text":"Distinctio inter essentiam animae, potentias eius et instrumenta operationum conciliat formalem corporeitatem cum operatione intellectiva incorporea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0212","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","text":"Id quo subiectum primo operatur est forma eius cui operatio per se attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A2","text":"Idem homo corporeus per se sentit et intelligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A3","text":"Intelligere est actio immanens agentis principalis, non actio transiens in motum instrumenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A4","text":"Natura et species rei ex propria operatione eiusque principio formali cognoscuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A5","text":"Operatio intellectiva nullo organo corporeo exercetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","text":"Forma substantialis dat composito esse simpliciter atque unitatem substantialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A7","text":"Anima intellectiva per se subsistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A8","text":"Anima intellectiva suum esse materiae communicat, ita ut idem esse sit animae et compositi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A9","text":"Homines numero diversi eandem numero formam substantialem habere non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A10","text":"Cognitio universalium ex immaterialitate speciei receptae provenit et ad obiecta indefinite multa patet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A11","text":"Forma perfectior virtute continet perfectiones et effectus formarum inferiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A12","text":"Materia propter formam ordinatur, ideoque ratio dispositionis corporis ex exigentiis operationum formae sumitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A13","text":"Anima humana veritatem naturaliter ex rebus sensibilibus per sensum colligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A14","text":"Sensus organum corporeum requirit, et organum tactus complexionem contrariorum mediam requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A15","text":"Accidentia et instrumenta motus esse substantiale materiae ordine naturae consequuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A16","text":"Forma substantialis materiae immediate per essentiam suam unitur ut actus eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A17","text":"Forma substantialis dat esse non solum toti sed etiam singulis partibus compositi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A18","text":"Totalitas essentiae, totalitas virtutis et totalitas quantitativa inter se distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0201","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0202","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX1","text":"Separatio intellectus non est separatio animae a corpore secundum essentiam, sed independentia potentiae intellectivae ab organo corporeo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX2","text":"Homo non est anima intellectiva sola, quia idem homo sentit corporaliter et intelligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX3","text":"Continuatio intellectus ad phantasmata per speciem intelligibilem, quam Commentator proponit, non sufficit ut intelligere huic homini attribuatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX4","text":"Unio animae ut motoris non constituit unum hominem simpliciter neque actionem intellectivam moto per se attribuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX5","text":"Unus intellectus numero omnibus hominibus communis excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX6","text":"Anima nutritiva, sensitiva et intellectiva in homine non sunt tres substantiae secundum essentiam distinctae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX7","text":"Praeter animam intellectivam nulla alia forma substantialis actu est in homine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX8","text":"Formae elementorum neque integrae actu in mixto manent, ut Avicenna posuit, neque gradum medium inter substantiam et accidens constituunt, ut Averroes posuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX9","text":"Nulla dispositio accidentalis inter animam et materiam formalem unionem mediat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX10","text":"Nullum corpus subtile, spiritus corporeus vel lux unionem substantialem animae et corporis mediat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0178","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0179","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX11","text":"Totam animam esse in qualibet parte non significat omnes potentias in qualibet parte adesse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX12","text":"Corruptibilitas corporis non facit corpus animae incorruptibili simpliciter improportionatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0141","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D1","text":"Principium quo hic homo intelligit est intrinsecum principium formale eius, non agens extrinsecum vel motor tantum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","CH_GGVC_P_68:A2","CH_GGVC_P_68:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D2","text":"Quia intelligere est propria operatio hominis, principium intellectivum est forma qua homo speciem humanam sortitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","CH_GGVC_P_68:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D3","text":"Independentia intellectus ab organo pertinet ad potentiam animae, non ad exclusionem animae ab officio formae corporis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","CH_GGVC_P_68:A2","CH_GGVC_P_68:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D4","text":"Anima post corporis corruptionem subsistit, sed aptitudinem et inclinationem naturalem ad unionem corporalem retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A7","CH_GGVC_P_68:A8","CH_GGVC_P_68:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D5","text":"Si unus intellectus esset omnium, Socrates et Plato respectu eiusdem intelligibilis unum agens principale et unum intelligere haberent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","CH_GGVC_P_68:A3","CH_GGVC_P_68:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D6","text":"Animae secundum multiplicationem corporum multiplicantur, sed earum multitudo post destructionem corporum manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A7","CH_GGVC_P_68:A8","CH_GGVC_P_68:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D7","text":"Plures intellectus individuati idem universale cognoscere possunt, quia individuatio cognoscentis speciem intelligibilem non materializat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A9","CH_GGVC_P_68:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D8","text":"Eadem numero anima in homine nutrit, sentit et intelligit, quia forma intellectiva virtute gradus inferiores continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","CH_GGVC_P_68:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D9","text":"Anima intellectiva sola dat homini esse, corporeitatem, vitam, sensum et intellectum; forma substantialis addita unitatem substantialem solveret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","CH_GGVC_P_68:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D10","text":"Formae elementares in corpore mixto non multiplicantur actu, sed virtute in qualitatibus remissis continentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","CH_GGVC_P_68:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D11","text":"Accidentia non possunt formalem unionem praecedere vel efficere, quia esse simpliciter ante modos accidentales constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","CH_GGVC_P_68:A15","CH_GGVC_P_68:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D12","text":"Corpus subtile vel spiritus potest motum administrare, sed non unionem substantialem efficere vel mediare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A15","CH_GGVC_P_68:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0181","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D13","text":"Anima intellectiva corpori organico mixto et ad aequalitatem complexionis reducto unitur, quia cognitio humana sensum et sensus tactum praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A12","CH_GGVC_P_68:A13","CH_GGVC_P_68:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D14","text":"Corruptibilitas corporis est consequentia materialis complexionis sensui necessariae, non finis per se intentus unionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A12","CH_GGVC_P_68:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D15","text":"Universalitas virtutis intellectivae requirit corpus organis diversis et instrumentis flexibilibus aptum potius quam auxiliis naturalibus ad unum effectum determinatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A10","CH_GGVC_P_68:A11","CH_GGVC_P_68:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D16","text":"Anima tota secundum essentiam est in qualibet parte corporis, sed potentiae eius secundum organa proportionata distribuuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A17","CH_GGVC_P_68:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD1","text":"Unitas hominis nec intellectum ad organum reducit nec animam extra essentiam hominis collocat; eadem anima corpus formaliter constituit et operatione intellectiva excedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D1","CH_GGVC_P_68:D3","CH_GGVC_P_68:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD2","text":"Individuatio intellectus et universalitas cognitionis ad axes diversos pertinent: prima ad formam huius compositi, secunda ad modum immaterialem speciei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D5","CH_GGVC_P_68:D6","CH_GGVC_P_68:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD3","text":"Hierarchia formarum est continens et perfectiva, non aggregativa: gradus superior inferiora assumit sine multiplicatione actuum substantialium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D8","CH_GGVC_P_68:D9","CH_GGVC_P_68:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD4","text":"Mediatio operativa admittitur ubi corpus movetur vel administratur, sed mediatio constitutiva excluditur ubi materia esse recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D11","CH_GGVC_P_68:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD5","text":"Modus cognitionis humanae structuram corporis determinat: dependentia epistemica a sensibilibus complexionem, organa diversa et flexibilitatem instrumentalem postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D13","CH_GGVC_P_68:D14","CH_GGVC_P_68:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD6","text":"Organismus est unum formaliter prius partibus, quamvis eadem anima essentialiter singulas partes actuet et potentias inaequaliter distribuat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D8","CH_GGVC_P_68:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet actionem immanentem subiecto attribui posse ex sola motione ab agente extrinseco.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet differentias rationis inter vegetativum, sensitivum et intellectivum necessario differentias substantiarum significare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0100","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet identitatem obiecti cogniti identitatem numeralem intellectus vel speciei receptae exigere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet genus et differentiam logicam ex formis naturalibus actu aggregatis constitui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0100","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet materiam ante formam substantialem iam corpus actu, quantam vel organicam esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet formam substantialem magis et minus recipere aut medium inter substantiam et accidens constituere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX7","text":"Falsum esse debet distantiam animae et corporis secundum proprietates separatim consideratas distantiam localem vel necessitatem pontis corporei inferre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0185","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX8","text":"Falsum esse debet animam separatam ad corpus naturaliter indifferentem esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit subiectum humanum completum sive in anima sola sive in corpore ante animationem constitutum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit hominem tamquam aggregationem plurium stratorum substantialiter iam actualium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit subiectum intellectivum transindividuale cui singuli homines tantum instrumentaliter conectantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX4","text":"Systema excludit tertium ens quod animam et corpus prius separatim constituta ontologice coniungat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX5","text":"Systema excludit praesentiam animae secundum extensionem, partitionem vel situm localem mensurandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0202","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX6","text":"Systema excludit oppositionem exhaustivam inter intellectum materialiter organicum et animam extrinsecam corpori adiectam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS1","text":"Attributio actus procedit hac serie: hic homo intelligit → intelligere est actio per se → primum principium actus est forma → anima intellectiva est forma huius hominis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS2","text":"Constitutio substantialis procedit hac serie: forma dat esse simpliciter → esse et unum convertuntur → unum compositum unam formam substantialem habet → pluralitas animarum et formarum in eodem homine excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS3","text":"Continuitas graduum procedit hac serie: forma superior continet inferiores virtute → una anima nutrit, sentit et intelligit → corporeitas et vita sunt effectus eiusdem formae → partes et potentiae ordinantur intra unum organismum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS4","text":"Individuatio procedit hac serie: forma est actus huius materiae → corpora numero distincta requirunt animas distinctas → subsistentia conservat distinctionem post corpus → immaterialitas speciei conservat cognitionem universalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS5","text":"Determinatio corporis procedit hac serie: intellectus humanus acquirit per sensum → sensus requirit organum → tactus requirit complexionem mediam → anima intellectiva requirit corpus mixtum, organicum et flexibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS6","text":"Immediatio procedit hac serie: esse substantiale est actus primus → accidentia et instrumenta sunt posteriora → nulla mediatio constitutiva admittitur → anima immediate totum et partes actuans potentias secundum organa distribuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AF1","text":"Hic homo intelligit → principium intellectivum est forma corporis → forma singulorum hominum numero multiplicatur → una anima omnes gradus vitae continet → nulla alia forma substantialis admittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AF2","text":"Unica forma perfectior exigentias materiae determinat → corpus ex ordine ad sensum configuratur → medium accidentale excluditur → medium corporeum excluditur → praesentia animae in toto et partibus secundum essentiam distinguitur a distributione potentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME1","text":"Separatio intellectus ex relatione animae ad corpus in relationem potentiae intellectivae ad organum transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME2","text":"Individuatio subiecti et universalitas obiecti a falsa oppositione liberantur et ut proprietates diversorum ordinum disponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME3","text":"Partes vegetativa, sensitiva et intellectiva ex substantiis aggregatis in gradus virtualiter contentos unius formae reclassificantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME4","text":"Corpus desinit esse subiectum iam actu constitutum cui anima additur, et fit materia cui anima esse, corporeitatem et organizationem confert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME5","text":"Mediatio dividitur in constitutivam, quae impossibilis est, et operativam, quae in motu et administratione corporis admittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0181","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME6","text":"Praesentia animae ex imagine locali in structuram formalem convertitur: essentia tota adest, potentiae autem secundum organa limitantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0202","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME7","text":"Corruptibilitas, nuditas auxiliis determinatis et diversitas organorum ex defectibus absolutis in consequentias complexionis sensitivae et aperturae rationalis reclassificantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ALT1","text":"**Altitude 1 — Surface** — Determinantur modus unionis animae et corporis, multiplicitas animarum, unitas graduum vitalium, numerus formarum, dispositio corporis, immediatio unionis et praesentia animae in partibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ALT2","text":"**Altitude 2 — Structural** — Omnes determinationes reguntur principio quod una forma substantialis unum esse compositi immediate constituit et inferiores perfectiones virtute continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ALT3","text":"**Altitude 3 — Metastrategic** — Quaestio animae a situ vel contactu ad attributionem actus, modum causalitatis et ordinem inter esse, potentias atque instrumenta transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0185","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ALT4","text":"**Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal** — Esse substantiale est prius accidentibus ordine naturae; anima multiplicata subsistit post corpus, dum in generatione embryonis forma sensitiva tantum formae perfectiori succedere dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad octo determinationes principales ex una doctrina formae substantialis restituendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT2","text":"Systema interne cohaeret, si conceduntur conversio entis et unius, causalitas formae respectu esse et continentia virtualis formarum inferiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT3","text":"Firmissima commissura est duplex demonstratio ex attributione actus intelligendi et ex unitate esse substantialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT4","text":"Status animae simul subsistentis et formae corporis hic affirmatur per communicationem unius esse, sed modus huius singularis subsistentiae ex quaestionibus prioribus supponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT5","text":"Multiplicatio animarum per corpora et permanentia distinctionis post corpora conciliantur per analogiam ad modum essendi, sed mechanismus individuationis persistentis breviter tantum explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT6","text":"Corpus dispositum animae requiritur, quamvis accidentia formam praeire nequeant; distinctio inter prioritatem formae et dispositiones quoad effectus posteriores contradictionem impedit, sed ordinem generationis comprimit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0162","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT7","text":"Convenientia corporis ex cognitione sensitiva deducitur, sed nexus teleologicus principio quod natura necessariis non deficit nititur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT8","text":"Successio animae sensitivae et intellectivae in embryone adhibetur ad objectionem solvendam, sed probatio eius in tractationem posteriorem differtur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT9","text":"Formulae reiectionis vehementes exemplaria adversa non sustinent; pondus argumenti in prioritate esse et immediatione formae manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0179","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT10","text":"Prooemium mediationem corpoream sexto et accidentalem septimo ponit, articuli autem ordinem invertunt; restitutio ordinem articulorum sequitur sine mutatione motus generativi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0167","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164636207094Z_db6b1fde","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 76","source_sha256":"2878a6c8da84f3d2ca460da129d67936753f1bca11ee855d230dd25fa0c63865","sha256":"9d3edc14e518a1232755745f5429a492767025b1325cb6a4d3db88d3d746beb6","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:46:36.208052+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS1","text":"The question is how the intellective principle, although subsistent and exceeding an organ in operation, constitutes one corporeal human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS2","text":"The intellective soul is the substantial form, unique, immediate, and numerically proper to the human body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS3","text":"The argument is metaphysical and reconstructive, but proceeds polemically against models of the soul as mover, common intellect, plurality of forms, and mediated union.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS4","text":"The primary movement proceeds from the attribution of the act of understanding to the formal principle of the understanding subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS5","text":"From formal union are deduced the multiplicity of souls, the unity of vital grades, the exclusion of other forms, the disposition of the body, and the immediacy of union.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AS6","text":"The distinction between the essence of the soul, its powers, and the instruments of its operations reconciles formal corporeity with incorporeal intellective operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0212","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","text":"That by which a subject first operates is the form of that to which the operation is attributed per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A2","text":"The same corporeal human being senses and understands per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A3","text":"Understanding is an immanent action of the principal agent, not an action passing into the motion of an instrument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A4","text":"The nature and species of a thing are known from its proper operation and its formal principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A5","text":"Intellective operation is exercised through no corporeal organ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","text":"A substantial form gives being simply and substantial unity to the composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A7","text":"The intellective soul subsists per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A8","text":"The intellective soul communicates its being to matter, so that the being of the soul and of the composite is the same.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A9","text":"Numerically diverse human beings cannot have the same numerically one substantial form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A10","text":"Knowledge of universals arises from the immateriality of the received species and extends to indefinitely many objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A11","text":"A more perfect form contains in power the perfections and effects of lower forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A12","text":"Matter is ordered for the sake of form, and therefore the account of the body's disposition is taken from the requirements of the form's operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A13","text":"The human soul naturally gathers truth from sensible things through sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A14","text":"Sense requires a corporeal organ, and the organ of touch requires a mean complexion of contraries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A15","text":"Accidents and instruments of motion follow upon the substantial being of matter in the order of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A16","text":"A substantial form is immediately united to matter through its essence as its act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A17","text":"A substantial form gives being not only to the whole but also to each part of the composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:A18","text":"Wholeness of essence, wholeness of power, and quantitative wholeness are distinguished from one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0201","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0202","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX1","text":"The separation of the intellect is not the separation of the soul from the body according to essence, but the independence of the intellective power from a corporeal organ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX2","text":"The human being is not the intellective soul alone, because the same human being senses corporeally and understands.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX3","text":"The connection of the intellect to phantasms through the intelligible species, which the Commentator proposes, is insufficient for understanding to be attributed to this human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX4","text":"The union of the soul as mover does not constitute one human being simply, nor does it attribute intellective action per se to the moved thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX5","text":"One numerically one intellect common to all human beings is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX6","text":"The nutritive, sensitive, and intellective souls in the human being are not three substances distinct according to essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX7","text":"Apart from the intellective soul, no other substantial form is actually present in the human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX8","text":"The forms of the elements neither remain actually entire in the mixed body, as Avicenna held, nor constitute an intermediate grade between substance and accident, as Averroes held.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX9","text":"No accidental disposition mediates the formal union between soul and matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX10","text":"No subtle body, corporeal spirit, or light mediates the substantial union of soul and body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0178","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0179","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX11","text":"The soul's being whole in every part does not signify that all powers are present in every part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:NX12","text":"The corruptibility of the body does not make the body simply disproportionate to the incorruptible soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0141","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D1","text":"The principle by which this human being understands is his intrinsic formal principle, not an extrinsic agent or merely a mover.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","CH_GGVC_P_68:A2","CH_GGVC_P_68:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D2","text":"Because understanding is the proper operation of the human being, the intellective principle is the form by which the human being obtains the human species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","CH_GGVC_P_68:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D3","text":"The independence of the intellect from an organ pertains to a power of the soul, not to the exclusion of the soul from the office of form of the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","CH_GGVC_P_68:A2","CH_GGVC_P_68:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D4","text":"The soul subsists after the corruption of the body, but retains aptitude and natural inclination for bodily union.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A7","CH_GGVC_P_68:A8","CH_GGVC_P_68:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D5","text":"If there were one intellect for all, Socrates and Plato, with respect to the same intelligible, would have one principal agent and one act of understanding.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A1","CH_GGVC_P_68:A3","CH_GGVC_P_68:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D6","text":"Souls are multiplied according to the multiplication of bodies, but their multitude remains after the destruction of bodies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A7","CH_GGVC_P_68:A8","CH_GGVC_P_68:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D7","text":"Several individuated intellects can know the same universal, because the individuation of the knower does not materialize the intelligible species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A9","CH_GGVC_P_68:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D8","text":"The numerically same soul in the human being nourishes, senses, and understands, because the intellective form contains the lower grades in power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","CH_GGVC_P_68:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D9","text":"The intellective soul alone gives the human being being, corporeity, life, sense, and intellect; an added substantial form would dissolve substantial unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","CH_GGVC_P_68:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D10","text":"Elementary forms in a mixed body are not actually multiplied, but are contained virtually in tempered qualities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","CH_GGVC_P_68:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D11","text":"Accidents cannot precede or effect formal union, because being simply is constituted before accidental modes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A6","CH_GGVC_P_68:A15","CH_GGVC_P_68:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D12","text":"A subtle body or spirit can administer motion, but cannot effect or mediate substantial union.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A15","CH_GGVC_P_68:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0181","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D13","text":"The intellective soul is united to an organic mixed body reduced to equality of complexion, because human knowledge presupposes sense and sense presupposes touch.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A12","CH_GGVC_P_68:A13","CH_GGVC_P_68:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D14","text":"The corruptibility of the body is a material consequence of the complexion necessary for sense, not an end intended per se by the union.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A12","CH_GGVC_P_68:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D15","text":"The universality of intellective power requires a body suited with diverse organs and flexible instruments rather than with natural aids determined to one effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A10","CH_GGVC_P_68:A11","CH_GGVC_P_68:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:D16","text":"The soul is whole according to essence in every part of the body, but its powers are distributed according to proportionate organs.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:A17","CH_GGVC_P_68:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD1","text":"The unity of the human being neither reduces intellect to an organ nor places the soul outside the essence of the human being; the same soul formally constitutes the body and exceeds it by intellective operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D1","CH_GGVC_P_68:D3","CH_GGVC_P_68:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD2","text":"The individuation of intellect and the universality of knowledge pertain to different axes: the former to the form of this composite, the latter to the immaterial mode of the species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D5","CH_GGVC_P_68:D6","CH_GGVC_P_68:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD3","text":"The hierarchy of forms is containing and perfective, not aggregative: the higher grade assumes the lower without multiplication of substantial acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D8","CH_GGVC_P_68:D9","CH_GGVC_P_68:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD4","text":"Operative mediation is admitted where the body is moved or administered, but constitutive mediation is excluded where matter receives being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D11","CH_GGVC_P_68:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD5","text":"The mode of human knowledge determines the structure of the body: epistemic dependence on sensibles demands complexion, diverse organs, and instrumental flexibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D13","CH_GGVC_P_68:D14","CH_GGVC_P_68:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SD6","text":"The organism is one formally prior to its parts, although the same soul essentially actualizes the individual parts and distributes powers unequally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_68:D8","CH_GGVC_P_68:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX1","text":"It must be false that an immanent action can be attributed to a subject from motion alone by an extrinsic agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX2","text":"It must be false that distinctions of reason between the vegetative, sensitive, and intellective necessarily signify distinctions of substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0100","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the identity of the known object requires numerical identity of intellect or of the received species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX4","text":"It must be false that genus and logical difference are constituted from naturally aggregated forms actually present.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0100","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX5","text":"It must be false that matter before substantial form is already an actually existing body, quantified, or organic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX6","text":"It must be false that substantial form receives more and less or constitutes an intermediate between substance and accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX7","text":"It must be false that the distance between soul and body according to separately considered properties entails local distance or the necessity of a corporeal bridge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0185","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:DNX8","text":"It must be false that the separated soul is naturally indifferent toward the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX1","text":"The system excludes a complete human subject constituted either in the soul alone or in the body before animation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX2","text":"The system excludes the human being as an aggregation of several strata already substantially actual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX3","text":"The system excludes a transindividual intellective subject to which individual human beings are connected only instrumentally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX4","text":"The system excludes a third being that ontologically joins soul and body previously constituted separately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX5","text":"The system excludes the presence of the soul as measurable according to extension, partition, or local position.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0202","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:SNX6","text":"The system excludes the exhaustive opposition between a materially organic intellect and a soul extrinsically added to the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS1","text":"Attribution of act proceeds in this sequence: this human being understands → understanding is an action per se → the first principle of act is form → the intellective soul is the form of this human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS2","text":"Substantial constitution proceeds in this sequence: form gives being simply → being and one are convertible → one composite has one substantial form → a plurality of souls and forms in the same human being is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS3","text":"Continuity of grades proceeds in this sequence: a higher form contains lower forms in power → one soul nourishes, senses, and understands → corporeity and life are effects of the same form → parts and powers are ordered within one organism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS4","text":"Individuation proceeds in this sequence: form is the act of this matter → numerically distinct bodies require distinct souls → subsistence preserves distinction after the body → the immateriality of species preserves universal knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS5","text":"Determination of the body proceeds in this sequence: the human intellect acquires through sense → sense requires an organ → touch requires a mean complexion → the intellective soul requires a mixed, organic, and flexible body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:FGS6","text":"Immediacy proceeds in this sequence: substantial being is first act → accidents and instruments are subsequent → no constitutive mediation is admitted → the soul immediately actualizing whole and parts distributes powers according to organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AF1","text":"This human being understands → the intellective principle is the form of the body → the form of individual human beings is numerically multiplied → one soul contains all grades of life → no other substantial form is admitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:AF2","text":"The unique more perfect form determines the requirements of matter → the body is configured in order to sense → an accidental medium is excluded → a corporeal medium is excluded → the presence of the soul in whole and parts according to essence is distinguished from the distribution of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME1","text":"The separation of intellect is transferred from the relation of the soul to the body to the relation of the intellective power to an organ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME2","text":"The individuation of the subject and the universality of the object are freed from a false opposition and arranged as properties of different orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME3","text":"Vegetative, sensitive, and intellective parts are reclassified from aggregated substances into grades virtually contained in one form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME4","text":"The body ceases to be an already actually constituted subject to which the soul is added, and becomes matter to which the soul confers being, corporeity, and organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME5","text":"Mediation is divided into constitutive, which is impossible, and operative, which is admitted in the motion and administration of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0181","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0183","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME6","text":"The presence of the soul is converted from a local image into a formal structure: the essence is wholly present, but the powers are limited according to organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0202","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0203","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0204","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ME7","text":"Corruptibility, nakedness with respect to determinate aids, and diversity of organs are reclassified from absolute defects into consequences of sensitive complexion and rational openness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ALT1","text":"**Altitude 1 — Surface** — The mode of union of soul and body, the multiplicity of souls, the unity of vital grades, the number of forms, the disposition of the body, the immediacy of union, and the presence of the soul in parts are determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ALT2","text":"**Altitude 2 — Structural** — All determinations are governed by the principle that one substantial form immediately constitutes one being of the composite and contains lower perfections in power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ALT3","text":"**Altitude 3 — Metastrategic** — The question of the soul is transferred from location or contact to the attribution of act, the mode of causality, and the order among being, powers, and instruments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0185","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:ALT4","text":"**Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal** — Substantial being is prior to accidents in the order of nature; the multiplied soul subsists after the body, while in the generation of the embryo the sensitive form is said only to succeed the more perfect form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct eight principal determinations from one doctrine of substantial form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0200","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT2","text":"The system coheres internally if the convertibility of being and one, the causality of form with respect to being, and the virtual containment of lower forms are granted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT3","text":"The strongest joint is the twofold demonstration from the attribution of the act of understanding and from the unity of substantial being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT4","text":"The status of the soul as simultaneously subsistent and form of the body is here affirmed through the communication of one being, but the mode of this singular subsistence is presupposed from prior questions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT5","text":"The multiplication of souls through bodies and the persistence of distinction after bodies are reconciled by analogy to the mode of being, but the mechanism of persistent individuation is explained only briefly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT6","text":"A body disposed for the soul is required, although accidents cannot precede form; the distinction between the priority of form and dispositions with respect to subsequent effects prevents contradiction, but compresses the order of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0162","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT7","text":"The suitability of the body is deduced from sensitive knowledge, but the teleological nexus rests on the principle that nature does not fail in necessities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT8","text":"The succession of the sensitive and intellective soul in the embryo is employed to resolve an objection, but its proof is deferred to a later treatment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT9","text":"Vehement formulas of rejection do not sustain contrary models; the weight of the argument remains in the priority of being and the immediacy of form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0177","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0179","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_68:MRT10","text":"The prologue places corporeal mediation sixth and accidental mediation seventh, but the articles invert the order; the reconstruction follows the order of the articles without altering the generative movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_68:P0167","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_68@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_68:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 77","title":"First Part · Question 76","context":"Chapter 77","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 76"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 76","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 77","order":78,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_69"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_69@R001","sha256":"9b3b2d687c945471711c29949dcbfe8797ae7cc75e9d82f414c8324f8e874a63","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quomodo essentia animae, pluralitas potentiarum, actus, obiecta, subiecta, origines et status post mortem inter se cohaereant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS2","text":"Una essentia animae multas potentias ordinatas naturaliter producit, quarum diversitas, subiectum et permanentia ex actibus atque obiectis propriis definiuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS3","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica et reconstructiva est, quia effectus operativos ad principia substantialia, causalia et ordinativa reducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS4","text":"Ex intermittentia operationum vitae proceditur ad distinctionem inter essentiam animae ut actum primum et potentias ut principia actuum secundorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS5","text":"Ex pluralitate operationum proceditur ad pluralitatem potentiarum, deinde ad earum specificationem per actus et rationes obiectorum per se.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS6","text":"Ex unitate originis et diversitate operationum proceditur ad triplicem ordinem potentiarum, distinctionem subiectorum et naturalem earum resultationem ab essentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS7","text":"Ex corruptione vel permanentia subiecti determinatur utrum potentia post mortem actu maneat an tantum virtute in anima tamquam principio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","text":"Potentia, quatenus potentia est, ad actum ordinatur et cum actu sibi proprio ad idem genus entis refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","text":"Operatio animae creatae non est substantia eius, sed essentia animae est actus primus ordinabilis per potentiam ad actum secundum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A3","text":"Proprietas ex principiis essentialibus speciei causata potest extra essentiam esse sine ratione accidentis mere extranei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","text":"Anima humana, in infimo gradu naturarum beatitudinis capacium et in confinio spiritualium corporaliumque constituta, bonitatem universalem per multas operationes attingit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A5","text":"Uni rei unum esse substantiale, plures autem operationes convenire possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","text":"Ratio potentiae sumitur ex actu ad quem ordinatur, iar ratio actus ex obiecto quod est principium vel finis eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A7","text":"Potentias distinguit differentia rationis obiecti per se, non quaelibet diversitas accidentalis neque sola identitas materialis obiecti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A8","text":"Potentia superior universaliorem rationem obiecti per se respicit quam potentia inferior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A9","text":"Pluralitas potentiarum ab una anima procedens ordinem requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","text":"Potentiae ordinantur secundum perfectionem naturae, secundum generationem et tempus ordine converso, atque secundum ordinem obiectorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","text":"Subiectum potentiae operativae est id cuius est operatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","text":"Intelligere et velle exercentur sine organo corporali, operationes autem sensitivae et nutritivae per organa corporalia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","text":"Anima est principium omnium potentiarum, sed sola anima vel coniunctum est earum subiectum secundum modum operationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A14","text":"Subiectum, inquantum actu est, proprium accidens producit; inquantum potentia est, illud recipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0128","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A15","text":"Omnes potentiae naturali resultatione, non transmutatione, ab essentia animae fluunt, diversificatae ordine potentiarum et organorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","text":"In processione ordinata potentia perfectior est principium activum et finale imperfectioris, imperfectior autem est principium susceptivum et prius generatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","text":"Accidens subiecto destructo actu manere non potest, quamvis eius principium virtute in radice remanere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX1","text":"Essentia animae non est eius potentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX2","text":"Unitas essentiae animae non importat unicam potentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX3","text":"Posterioritas actus in esse et exterioritas obiecti non impediunt prioritatem eorum secundum rationem et intentionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX4","text":"Non omnis diversitas obiectorum diversitatem potentiarum constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX5","text":"Contraria non exigunt potentias diversas, neque idem materialiter obiectum unam tantum potentiam exigit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX6","text":"Divisio potentiarum sub communi genere simultatem ordinis non excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX7","text":"Anima sola non est subiectum omnium potentiarum suarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX8","text":"Quod extra essentiam est non ideo est accidens extraneum vel a principiis speciei non causatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX9","text":"Emanatio potentiarum ab essentia non est motus neque transmutatio animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0135","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX10","text":"Simultas potentiarum cum anima non excludit originem ordinatam unius mediante alia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX11","text":"Potentiae sensitivae et nutritivae neque actu neque secundum proprios actus in anima separata permanent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX12","text":"Auctoritates recitatae, inquisitivae vel secundum aliud respectum prolatae non sunt assertiones univoce accipiendae contra distinctiones systematis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0182","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D1","text":"Essentia animae a potentia distinguitur, quia actus primus substantialis non potest esse immediatum et semper actu exercitum principium operationum intermittentium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","CH_GGVC_P_69:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D2","text":"Potentiae sunt accidentia in genere qualitatis, sed proprietates naturales mediae inter essentiam et accidens praedicabile extraneum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","text":"Una essentia animae plures potentias requirit, quia unum esse substantiale multas operationes ad finem universalem ordinatas sustentat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","CH_GGVC_P_69:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D4","text":"Species potentiae constituitur per actum et rationem formalem obiecti per se, non per circumstantias obiecti accidentales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D5","text":"Contraria sub una communi ratione obiecti cadere possunt, iar idem subiecto obiectum secundum diversas rationes ad diversas potentias pertinere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D6","text":"Diversa obiecta potentiarum inferiorum sub una ratione universaliori potentiae superioris continentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A7","CH_GGVC_P_69:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D7","text":"Ordo perfectionis a potentiis intellectivis ad sensitivas et nutritivas descendit, dum ordo generationis a nutritivis per sensitivas ad intellectivas ascendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A9","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","text":"Intellectus et voluntas sunt in anima sicut in subiecto, potentiae autem sensitivae et nutritivae sunt in coniuncto.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D9","text":"Diversitas subiectorum potentiarum non impedit quin omnes ab essentia animae procedant, quia anima actualitatem tam sibi quam coniuncto communicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A14","CH_GGVC_P_69:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D10","text":"Una potentia mediante alia ab essentia procedit secundum ordinem causae activae et finalis vel secundum ordinem principii susceptivi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A9","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D11","text":"Post mortem intellectus et voluntas actu permanent, potentiae autem organicae tantum virtute in anima tamquam principio vel radice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD1","text":"Anima constituit architecturam stratificatam: essentia dat esse, potentiae ordinant ad operandum, actus operationem perficiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:A5","CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","CH_GGVC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD2","text":"Prioritas causalis potentiarum non est absoluta, sed mutatur secundum perfectionem, finem, receptionem et generationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7","CH_GGVC_P_69:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD3","text":"Corpus non est mera occasio operationum sensitivarum, sed pars subiecti cui ipsae potentiae organicae inhaerent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD4","text":"Mors non uniformiter aufert vel conservat potentias, sed statum earum secundum permanentiam subiecti ab actu ad radicem virtualem contrahit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD5","text":"Identitas essentiae, potentiae et operationis est terminus divinae simplicitatis, non exemplar univoce transferendum ad animam creatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD6","text":"Accidentia operativa possunt substantiam manifestare et ad eius differentias cognoscendas adhiberi, quin propterea partes essentiae fiant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A3","CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX1","text":"Simplicitas animae creatae puritatem actus et absentiam omnis potentialitatis non importat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX2","text":"Naturaliter et necessario consequens essentiam non oportet esse de essentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX3","text":"Unitas ontologica subiecti homogenitatem operationum non requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX4","text":"Identitas vel diversitas materialis obiectorum non est principium ultimum classificationis potentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX5","text":"Exterioritas obiecti non reddit specificationem potentiae mere extrinsecam, quia principium et finis intrinsecam operationis proportionem determinant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX6","text":"Origo causalis non requirit successionem temporalem neque mutationem rei originantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX7","text":"Pluralitas coordinata et sine ordine non potest ex una essentia procedere secundum structuram huius systematis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX8","text":"Anima separata non est subiectum actuale totius apparatus sensitivi et nutritivi quem in coniuncto principiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX1","text":"Creatura cuius essentia sit immediate sua operatio intra systema excluditur; talis identitas soli Deo reservatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX2","text":"Accessus immediatus ad formas substantiales nobis indisponibilis est; earum cognitio per accidentia et operationes mediatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX3","text":"Sensorium actu integrum sine corpore et organis impossibile habetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX4","text":"Unicus ordo simpliciter linearis inter potentias inadmissibilis est, quia natura, generatio, obiectum et causalitas diversa principia prioritatis constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX5","text":"Separata anima non habetur ut subiectum completum omnium operationum humanae vitae, quamvis principium virtuale potentiarum organicarum maneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS1","text":"Operatio creata extra genus substantiae + anima ut actus primus + operatio intermittens ut actus secundus → distinctio essentiae et potentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS2","text":"Unum esse substantiale + finis universalis per multas operationes attingendus + confinium spirituale-corporale → pluralitas potentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","CH_GGVC_P_69:A5","CH_GGVC_P_69:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS3","text":"Ratio obiecti per se ut principium vel finis → species actus → species potentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:A7","CH_GGVC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS4","text":"Una essentia → pluralitas potentiarum → triplex ordo naturae, generationis et obiectorum → dependentiae non uniformes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A9","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS5","text":"Operatio sine organo vel per organum → determinatio operatoris → anima sola vel coniunctum ut subiectum potentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS6","text":"Actualitas subiecti + potentialitas receptiva → productio proprii accidentis → naturalis resultatio potentiarum ab essentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A14","CH_GGVC_P_69:A15","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS7","text":"Prioritas perfectionis → causalitas activa et finalis superioris; prioritas generationis → causalitas susceptiva imperfectioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","CH_GGVC_P_69:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS8","text":"Permanentia vel corruptio subiecti → permanentia vel corruptio actualis potentiae → remanentia virtualis in radice ubi subiectum organicum deficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AF1","text":"Intermittentia operum vitae → distinctio actus primi et secundi → distinctio essentiae et potentiae → potentia ut proprietas naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D1","CH_GGVC_P_69:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AF2","text":"Unitas esse substantialis → multiplicitas operationum requisitarum → pluralitas potentiarum → specificatio per actus et obiecta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","CH_GGVC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AF3","text":"Diversitas formalium obiectorum → gradus universalitatis → triplex ordo potentiarum → mediatio causalis unius per aliam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D5","CH_GGVC_P_69:D6","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7","CH_GGVC_P_69:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AF4","text":"Modus operationis → determinatio subiecti → resultatio ab essentia → probatio per corruptionem subiecti → permanentia actualis vel virtualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME1","text":"Anima non amplius ut principium operative simplex describitur, sed ut una essentia, plures potentiae et multiplices actus ordinatos continens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D1","CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME2","text":"Oppositio substantiae et accidentis ita reordinatur ut proprietates naturales extra essentiam, sed ex ea necessario causatae, classificari possint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D2","CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME3","text":"Obiecta ex rebus materialiter sumptis in rationes formales operationes specificantes transferuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D4","CH_GGVC_P_69:D5","CH_GGVC_P_69:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME4","text":"Unitas et multiplicitas non iam opponuntur, quia una essentia pluralitatem ordinatam potentiarum generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME5","text":"Corpus ex instrumento externo in partem subiecti potentiarum sensitivarum et nutritivarum reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME6","text":"Causalitas inter potentias in ordines activos, finales, susceptivos et generativos distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D10","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0133","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME7","text":"Permanentia post mortem ex simplici oppositione conservationis et corruptionis in distinctionem inter actum et radicem virtualem convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D11","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei quaerit utrum potentiae sint essentia, quot sint, quomodo distinguantur, ordinentur, subiciantur, oriantur et post mortem permaneant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis potentias per relationes actus, obiecti, subiecti, ordinis et causalitatis restituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D4","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus quaestiones apparentis identitatis per distinctiones inter essentiam et proprietatem, per se et per accidens, principium et subiectum, actum et virtutem dissolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D2","CH_GGVC_P_69:D4","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis creaturam inter actum et potentiam constituit atque ordinem perfectionis ab ordine generationis et statum coniuncti a statu animae separatae distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad octo quaestiones restituendas, quia essentiam, pluralitatem, specificationem, ordinem, subiectum, originem mediatam et permanentiam determinant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A15","CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT2","text":"Firmissima catena est ea quae ex modo operationis subiectum potentiae et ex permanentia subiecti statum post mortem infert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT3","text":"Systema contradictione formali caret, dummodo essentia, principium, subiectum, causa et ordo non univoce confundantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D2","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT4","text":"Demonstratio pluralitatis potentiarum minus stricte nititur analogia graduum perfectionis quam demonstratio distinctionis essentiae et potentiae distinctione actus primi et secundi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","CH_GGVC_P_69:D1","CH_GGVC_P_69:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT5","text":"Locutio qua una potentia ab alia oritur causalitatem analogicam variat inter principium activum, finem et dispositionem susceptivam, nec unicum genus causalitatis constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","CH_GGVC_P_69:D10","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT6","text":"Remanentia potentiarum organicarum virtute determinatur ut radix causalis, sed modus ontologicus huius virtualitatis non ulterius explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0176","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT7","text":"Commissura inter originem omnium potentiarum ab anima et subiectivitatem quarundam in coniuncto servatur distinctione principii et subiecti, sed ab ea distinctione omnino dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A15","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT8","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat ab distinctione ontologica per diversificationem et ordinationem causalium ad probationem finalem ex corruptione subiecti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_69:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_69:AF3","CH_GGVC_P_69:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164707071696Z_5745d727","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 77","source_sha256":"9b3b2d687c945471711c29949dcbfe8797ae7cc75e9d82f414c8324f8e874a63","sha256":"e88ed909cf29fc0a7187edd85367078fece152f5b0ed140378fae2886e124555","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:47:07.072643+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS1","text":"The question determines how the essence of the soul, the plurality of powers, acts, objects, subjects, origins, and states after death cohere with one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS2","text":"One essence of the soul naturally produces many ordered powers, whose diversity, subject, and persistence are defined from their proper acts and objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical and reconstructive, because it reduces operative effects to substantial, causal, and ordering principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS4","text":"From the intermittence of the operations of life, one proceeds to the distinction between the essence of the soul as first act and the powers as principles of second acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS5","text":"From the plurality of operations, one proceeds to the plurality of powers, and then to their specification through acts and the per se formal accounts of objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS6","text":"From unity of origin and diversity of operations, one proceeds to the threefold order of powers, the distinction of subjects, and their natural resultance from the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AS7","text":"From the corruption or persistence of the subject, it is determined whether a power remains actually after death or only virtually in the soul as a principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","text":"A power, insofar as it is a power, is ordered to act and is referred with its proper act to the same genus of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","text":"The operation of a created soul is not its substance, but the essence of the soul is a first act orderable through a power to a second act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A3","text":"A property caused from the essential principles of a species can be outside the essence without having the character of a merely extraneous accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","text":"The human soul, established in the lowest grade of natures capable of beatitude and on the boundary of spiritual and bodily things, attains universal goodness through many operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A5","text":"One substantial being can belong to one thing, while several operations can belong to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","text":"The account of a power is taken from the act to which it is ordered, and the account of the act from the object which is its principle or end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A7","text":"Powers are distinguished by a difference in the per se account of the object, not by any accidental diversity nor by the mere material identity of the object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A8","text":"A higher power regards a more universal per se account of the object than a lower power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A9","text":"A plurality of powers proceeding from one soul requires order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","text":"Powers are ordered according to the perfection of nature, according to generation and time in the reverse order, and according to the order of objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","text":"The subject of an operative power is that whose operation it is.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","text":"To understand and to will are exercised without a bodily organ, whereas sensitive and nutritive operations are exercised through bodily organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","text":"The soul is the principle of all powers, but either the soul alone or the composite is their subject according to the mode of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A14","text":"The subject, insofar as it is in act, produces its proper accident; insofar as it is in potency, it receives it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0128","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A15","text":"All powers flow from the essence of the soul by natural resultance, not by transmutation, diversified according to the order of powers and organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","text":"In an ordered procession, the more perfect power is the active and final principle of the less perfect, while the less perfect is the receptive principle and prior in generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","text":"An accident cannot remain actually when its subject has been destroyed, although its principle can remain virtually in the root.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX1","text":"The essence of the soul is not its power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX2","text":"The unity of the essence of the soul does not entail a single power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX3","text":"The posteriority of the act in being and the exteriority of the object do not impede their priority according to account and intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX4","text":"Not every diversity of objects constitutes a diversity of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX5","text":"Contraries do not require diverse powers, nor does the same object materially require only one power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX6","text":"The division of powers under a common genus does not exclude simultaneity of order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX7","text":"The soul alone is not the subject of all its powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX8","text":"What is outside the essence is not thereby an extraneous accident or not caused from the principles of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX9","text":"The emanation of powers from the essence is neither motion nor transmutation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0135","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX10","text":"The simultaneity of powers with the soul does not exclude the ordered origin of one through another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX11","text":"Sensitive and nutritive powers remain neither actually nor according to their proper acts in the separated soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:NX12","text":"Authorities cited inquisitively or uttered according to another respect are not assertions to be understood univocally against the distinctions of the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0182","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D1","text":"The essence of the soul is distinguished from its power because a substantial first act cannot be the immediate and always actually exercised principle of intermittent operations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","CH_GGVC_P_69:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D2","text":"Powers are accidents in the genus of quality, but natural properties intermediate between essence and an extraneous predicable accident.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","text":"One essence of the soul requires several powers, because one substantial being sustains many operations ordered to a universal end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","CH_GGVC_P_69:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D4","text":"The species of a power is constituted through the act and the formal account of the per se object, not through accidental circumstances of the object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D5","text":"Contraries can fall under one common account of the object, and the same object in subject can pertain, according to diverse accounts, to diverse powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D6","text":"Diverse objects of lower powers are contained under one more universal account of a higher power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A7","CH_GGVC_P_69:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D7","text":"The order of perfection descends from intellective powers to sensitive and nutritive powers, whereas the order of generation ascends from nutritive through sensitive to intellective powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A9","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","text":"Intellect and will are in the soul as in their subject, whereas sensitive and nutritive powers are in the composite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D9","text":"The diversity of the subjects of powers does not prevent all of them from proceeding from the essence of the soul, because the soul communicates actuality both to itself and to the composite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A14","CH_GGVC_P_69:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D10","text":"One power proceeds from the essence through another according to the order of active and final cause or according to the order of receptive principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A9","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:D11","text":"After death intellect and will remain actually, whereas organic powers remain only virtually in the soul as principle or root.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD1","text":"The soul constitutes a stratified architecture: essence gives being, powers order toward operating, acts complete operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:A5","CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","CH_GGVC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD2","text":"The causal priority of powers is not absolute, but varies according to perfection, end, reception, and generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7","CH_GGVC_P_69:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD3","text":"The body is not a mere occasion of sensitive operations, but a part of the subject in which the organic powers themselves inhere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD4","text":"Death does not uniformly remove or preserve powers, but contracts their state, according to the persistence of the subject, from act to a virtual root.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD5","text":"The identity of essence, power, and operation is the terminus of divine simplicity, not an exemplar to be transferred univocally to the created soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SD6","text":"Operative accidents can manifest substance and be employed for knowing its differences, without thereby becoming parts of the essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A3","CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX1","text":"The simplicity of a created soul does not entail purity of act and the absence of every potentiality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX2","text":"What naturally and necessarily follows the essence need not be of the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX3","text":"The ontological unity of a subject does not require homogeneity of operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX4","text":"The material identity or diversity of objects is not the ultimate principle of the classification of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX5","text":"The exteriority of the object does not render the specification of a power merely extrinsic, because principle and end determine the intrinsic proportion of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX6","text":"Causal origin does not require temporal succession or a change in the originating thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0149","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX7","text":"A coordinated plurality without order cannot proceed from one essence according to the structure of this system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX8","text":"The separated soul is not the actual subject of the whole sensitive and nutritive apparatus which it initiates in the composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX1","text":"A creature whose essence is immediately its operation is excluded within the system; such identity is reserved to God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX2","text":"Immediate access to substantial forms is unavailable to us; knowledge of them is mediated through accidents and operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX3","text":"An actually integral sensory apparatus without body and organs is held impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX4","text":"A single simply linear order among powers is inadmissible, because nature, generation, object, and causality constitute diverse principles of priority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:SNX5","text":"The separated soul is not held to be the complete subject of all operations of human life, although it remains the virtual principle of organic powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS1","text":"Created operation outside the genus of substance + soul as first act + intermittent operation as second act → distinction of essence and power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS2","text":"One substantial being + a universal end to be attained through many operations + spiritual-bodily boundary → plurality of powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","CH_GGVC_P_69:A5","CH_GGVC_P_69:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS3","text":"Per se account of the object as principle or end → species of act → species of power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:A7","CH_GGVC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS4","text":"One essence → plurality of powers → threefold order of nature, generation, and objects → non-uniform dependencies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A9","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS5","text":"Operation without an organ or through an organ → determination of the operator → soul alone or composite as subject of the power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS6","text":"Actuality of the subject + receptive potentiality → production of its proper accident → natural resultance of powers from the essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A14","CH_GGVC_P_69:A15","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS7","text":"Priority of perfection → active and final causality of the superior; priority of generation → receptive causality of the less perfect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","CH_GGVC_P_69:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:FGS8","text":"Persistence or corruption of the subject → persistence or actual corruption of the power → virtual remaining in the root where the organic subject fails.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AF1","text":"Intermittence of the works of life → distinction of first and second act → distinction of essence and power → power as natural property.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D1","CH_GGVC_P_69:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AF2","text":"Unity of substantial being → multiplicity of required operations → plurality of powers → specification through acts and objects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","CH_GGVC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AF3","text":"Diversity of formal objects → degrees of universality → threefold order of powers → causal mediation of one through another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D5","CH_GGVC_P_69:D6","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7","CH_GGVC_P_69:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:AF4","text":"Mode of operation → determination of the subject → resultance from essence → proof through corruption of the subject → actual or virtual persistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME1","text":"The soul is no longer described as an operatively simple principle, but as one essence containing several powers and multiple ordered acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D1","CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME2","text":"The opposition of substance and accident is so reordered that natural properties outside the essence, yet necessarily caused from it, can be classified.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D2","CH_GGVC_P_69:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME3","text":"Objects are transferred from things taken materially to formal accounts specifying operations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D4","CH_GGVC_P_69:D5","CH_GGVC_P_69:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME4","text":"Unity and multiplicity are no longer opposed, because one essence generates an ordered plurality of powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D3","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME5","text":"The body is reclassified from an external instrument into a part of the subject of sensitive and nutritive powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME6","text":"Causality among powers is distributed into active, final, receptive, and generative orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D10","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0133","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ME7","text":"Persistence after death is converted from a simple opposition between preservation and corruption into a distinction between act and virtual root.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D11","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ALT1","text":"The surface level asks whether powers are essence, how many they are, how they are distinguished, ordered, subjected, originate, and remain after death.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ALT2","text":"The structural level reconstructs powers through relations of act, object, subject, order, and causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D4","CH_GGVC_P_69:D7","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level dissolves questions of apparent identity through distinctions between essence and property, per se and per accidens, principle and subject, act and virtuality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D2","CH_GGVC_P_69:D4","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level establishes the creature between act and potency and distinguishes the order of perfection from the order of generation and the state of the composite from the state of the separated soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct eight questions, because they determine essence, plurality, specification, order, subject, mediated origin, and persistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A1","CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","CH_GGVC_P_69:A6","CH_GGVC_P_69:A10","CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A15","CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT2","text":"The strongest chain is that which infers the subject of a power from the mode of operation and the state after death from the persistence of the subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A11","CH_GGVC_P_69:A12","CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT3","text":"The system lacks formal contradiction, provided essence, principle, subject, cause, and order are not confused univocally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:D2","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT4","text":"The demonstration of the plurality of powers relies less strictly on the analogy of degrees of perfection than the demonstration of the distinction of essence and power relies on the distinction of first and second act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A2","CH_GGVC_P_69:A4","CH_GGVC_P_69:D1","CH_GGVC_P_69:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT5","text":"The expression by which one power arises from another varies analogical causality among active principle, end, and receptive disposition, and does not constitute a single genus of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A16","CH_GGVC_P_69:D10","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT6","text":"The virtual remaining of organic powers is determined as a causal root, but the ontological mode of this virtuality is not further explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A17","CH_GGVC_P_69:D11","CH_GGVC_P_69:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0176","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT7","text":"The juncture between the origin of all powers from the soul and the subjectivity of some in the composite is maintained by the distinction between principle and subject, but depends wholly upon that distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:A13","CH_GGVC_P_69:A15","CH_GGVC_P_69:D8","CH_GGVC_P_69:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_69:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text from ontological distinction through diversification and causal ordering to the final proof from the corruption of the subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_69:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_69:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_69:AF3","CH_GGVC_P_69:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_69:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_69@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_69:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 78","title":"First Part · Question 77","context":"Chapter 78","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 77"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 77","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 78","order":79,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_70"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_70@R001","sha256":"91a348757bb9a9bdacc79343efcd14c3180e7dffa824ab0dc739ebd700f24151","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS1","text":"Potentiae animae inferiores investigantur ut praeambula cognitionis potentiarum intellectivarum et appetitivarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS2","text":"Numerus potentiarum animae determinandus est ex ratione obiectorum et operationum, non ex numero partium animae, modorum vivendi vel organorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est taxonomica et reconstructiva: distinctiones numerales ad diversas rationes divisionis reducuntur, deinde potentiae ex actibus necessariis restituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS4","text":"Motus principalis procedit ab apparentibus contradictionibus numeralibus ad distinctionem criteriorum, atque inde ad ordinem quinque generum potentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS5","text":"Intra singula genera motus procedit ab obiecto vel operatione irreducibili ad potentiam propriam, et a potentia ad ordinem hierarchicum actuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS6","text":"Differentia hominis ab aliis animalibus constituitur per perfectionem rationaliter elevatam potentiarum sensitivarum, non per multiplicationem indefinitam earum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A1","text":"Potentia animae est proximum principium operationis animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","text":"Actiones quae ad unum proximum principium reduci non possunt diversas potentias requirunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A3","text":"Genera potentiarum formaliter distinguuntur secundum obiecta, et potentia altior universalius obiectum respicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A4","text":"Organa et media ordinantur ad potentias earumque actus, non potentiae ad diversitatem organorum aut mediorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A5","text":"Animae, modi vivendi et genera potentiarum secundum rationes diversas dividuntur: secundum excessum operationis supra naturam corpoream, secundum gradum viventis et secundum obiectum operationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A6","text":"Intellectiva operatio sine organo corporeo exercetur, sensitiva per organum sed non virtute qualitatis corporeae, vegetativa per organum et qualitatem corpoream instrumentalem, semper tamen ex principio intrinseco viventis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","text":"Potentia vegetativa pro obiecto habet corpus animae unitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","text":"Res extrinseca cognitioni coniungitur per similitudinem, sensibilis quidem ut corpus sensibile, intellectui autem sub ratione entis universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A9","text":"Appetitus animalis formam apprehensam consequitur, in omni sensitivo adest et in rem ipsam ut finem tendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A10","text":"Motus localis requirit potentiam exsecutivam qua corpus ad rem exteriorem tamquam ad terminum operationis dirigitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A11","text":"Corpus vivum indiget operationibus distinctis quibus esse alteri communicetur, quantitas debita acquiratur et substantia cum quantitate conservetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A12","text":"Generativa est principalior vegetativis potentiis, quia effectum in altero producit; augmentativa et nutritiva ei deserviunt, nutritiva etiam augmentativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","text":"Sensus est potentia passiva quae formam sensibilis secundum esse spirituale recipere debet; immutatio naturalis sola sensationem non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A14","text":"Sensibilia propria primo et per se sensum immutant, sensibilia autem communia per qualitates sensibiles proprias percipiuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A15","text":"Quinque sensus exteriores distinguuntur secundum modos immutationis: spiritualis sola in visu, naturalis ex parte obiecti in auditu et olfactu, naturalis ex parte organi in tactu et gustu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A16","text":"Vita animalis perfecta requirit apprehensionem rei absentis et intentionum utilitatis, nocivitatis vel convenientiae quae qualitatibus sensibilibus non reducuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A17","text":"Receptio et retentio sunt principia distincta, sicut forma sensibilis et intentio non sensibilis; ex his distinctionibus constituuntur sensus communis, imaginatio, aestimativa et memoria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A18","text":"In homine aestimativa et memorativa perficiuntur per affinitatem ad rationem universalem ut cogitativa et reminiscentiva, sine constitutione novarum potentiarum sensitivarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX1","text":"Quinque genera potentiarum non reducuntur ad tres animae partes, quia animae et potentiae diversis rationibus numerantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX2","text":"Quattuor modi vivendi non constituunt enumerationem completam generum potentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX3","text":"Appetitus animalis non est mera inclinatio naturalis qua unaquaeque potentia proprium actum appetit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX4","text":"Sensus et appetitus ut principia imperantia non sufficiunt ad motum localem sine virtute exsecutiva corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX5","text":"Operationes vegetativae non excluduntur a potentiis animae quia qualitatibus naturalibus instrumentaliter utuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX6","text":"Generatio viventis non reducitur ad generationem inanimati totaliter ab agente extrinseco productam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX7","text":"Numerus sensuum exteriorum non sumitur ex elementis organorum, mediis sensibilibus aut generibus materialibus qualitatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX8","text":"Non omne genus accidentis sensum proprium requirit, neque sensibilia communia sunt aut propria aut mere per accidens sensibilia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX9","text":"Immutatio naturalis corporis non sufficit ad sensationem; alioquin omne corpus alteratum sentiret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX10","text":"Sensus communis non est genus de sensibus propriis praedicatum, sed radix ad quam eorum apprehensiones referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX11","text":"Sensus proprii neque sensibilia diversorum sensuum inter se discernunt neque proprios actus immediate percipiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX12","text":"Intentiones convenientiae et nocivitatis non reducuntur ad formas sensibiles a sensibus exterioribus receptas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX13","text":"Quinta potentia interior ab Avicenna posita non est necessaria, neque cogitativa et reminiscentiva novas potentias supra aestimativam et memorativam constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D1","text":"Quinque genera potentiarum sunt vegetativum, sensitivum, intellectivum, appetitivum et motivum secundum locum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A3","CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A9","CH_GGVC_P_70:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D2","text":"Tres animae distinguuntur secundum tres gradus quibus operatio vitalis naturam corpoream excedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A5","CH_GGVC_P_70:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D3","text":"Quattuor modi vivendi constituuntur per additionem sensitivi, motus localis et intellectivi supra vegetativum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A5","CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D4","text":"Appetitivum gradum viventium distinctum non constituit, quia omni sensitivo inest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A5","CH_GGVC_P_70:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D5","text":"Potentia appetitiva requiritur quia res cognoscitur secundum similitudinem, sed appetitur secundum esse suum reale et propter usus cognitionem excedentes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D6","text":"Potentia motiva distinguitur ab apprehensione et appetitu, quia imperium motus sine dispositione exsecutiva membrorum effectum non producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D7","text":"Potentiae vegetativae sunt generativa, augmentativa et nutritiva, ordinatae respective ad communicationem esse, debitam quantitatem et conservationem viventis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","CH_GGVC_P_70:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D8","text":"Generativa est terminus principalis ordinis vegetativi, nutritiva autem fundamentum materiale augmentativae et generativae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A11","CH_GGVC_P_70:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D9","text":"Quinque sensus exteriores derivantur ex quinque rationibus quibus immutatio spiritualis cum immutatione naturali coniungitur vel ab ea separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","CH_GGVC_P_70:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D10","text":"Visus est sensuum maxime spiritualis; sequuntur auditus et olfactus, deinde tactus et gustus ut maxime materiales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A3","CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","CH_GGVC_P_70:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D11","text":"Magnitudo, figura, numerus, motus et quies potentiam propriam non constituunt, quia sensum mediante qualitate sensibili immutant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","CH_GGVC_P_70:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D12","text":"Tactus est unus genere et multiplex specie; gustus ab eo distinguitur vel ut tactus linguae a tactu per corpus diffuso, vel secundum diversam rationem immutationis organi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D13","text":"Quattuor vires sensitivae interiores sufficiunt: sensus communis ad receptionem et integrationem, imaginatio ad retentionem formarum, aestimativa ad apprehensionem intentionum et memoria ad earum conservationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A1","CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A16","CH_GGVC_P_70:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D14","text":"Sensus communis discernit sensibilia diversorum sensuum et percipit actus sensuum propriorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D15","text":"Cogitatio particularis et reminiscentia sunt modi perfectiores aestimativae et memoriae humanae, non facultates sensitivae specie additae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD1","text":"Diversitas numerorum non constituit contradictionem, quia tres animae, quattuor modi vivendi et quinque genera potentiarum sunt sectiones eiusdem realitatis secundum axes non convertibiles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:D1","CH_GGVC_P_70:D2","CH_GGVC_P_70:D3","CH_GGVC_P_70:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD2","text":"Hierarchia potentiarum exprimit incrementum universalitatis obiecti et decrementum dependentiae ab immutatione materiali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A3","CH_GGVC_P_70:A6","CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","CH_GGVC_P_70:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD3","text":"Multiplicatio potentiarum regitur principio sufficientiae oeconomicae: potentia nova ponitur solum ubi actus necessarius ad principium iam positum reduci nequit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A1","CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A4","CH_GGVC_P_70:A17","CH_GGVC_P_70:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD4","text":"Actio animalis perfecta constituit circuitum ab apprehensione praesentis vel absentis per aestimationem et appetitum ad exsecutionem corporalem motus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A9","CH_GGVC_P_70:A10","CH_GGVC_P_70:A16","CH_GGVC_P_70:A17","CH_GGVC_P_70:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD5","text":"Generatio est commissura inter vitam in proprio corpore inclusam et operationem ad alterum extensam, unde supremum vegetativi ad infimum sensitivi appropinquat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A6","CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","CH_GGVC_P_70:A11","CH_GGVC_P_70:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD6","text":"Differentia humana intra ordinem sensitivum est intensificatio rationalis potentiarum communium animalibus, non ruptura per novum genus sensus interioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A18","CH_GGVC_P_70:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX1","text":"Nulla partitio unica animae simul partes substantivas, gradus vitae et genera operationum adaequate repraesentat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX2","text":"Anatomia non est principium formale taxonomiae potentiarum, quamvis actuum sensibilium condicionem materialem praebeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX3","text":"Vita non potest ex motibus totaliter extrinsecis corporis constitui, quia operatio vitalis principium intrinsecum requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX4","text":"Repraesentatio rei non sufficit ad desiderium aut consecutionem rei; cognitio, appetitus et exsecutio formaliter non coincidunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX5","text":"Praesentia sensibilis non sufficit ad vitam animalis perfecti, quae absentiam, futurum utile et praeteritum retentum operative tractat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX6","text":"Qualitas sensibilis et intentio individualis utilitatis vel nocivitatis in unum obiectum apprehensivum conflari non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX7","text":"Distinctio actuum non legitimam multiplicationem potentiarum efficit nisi irreducibilitas principiorum etiam statuatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX8","text":"Differentia rationalis hominis non requirit duplicem seriem potentiarum interiorum, unam animalem et alteram proprie humanam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX1","text":"Numerus potentiarum absolute positus sine ratione divisionis est indisponibilis; omnis enumeratio valida criterio suo indexatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX2","text":"Cognitio sensibilis non potest totaliter explicari ut alteratio materialis, quia talem explicationem corpora non sentientia quoque implerent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX3","text":"Animalitas perfecta impossibilis esset si solum praesens agere posset; absentia debet intentionaliter praesens fieri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX4","text":"Similitudo cognitiva numquam est possessio realis obiecti; hoc intervallum appetitum et motum necessarios reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX5","text":"Natura animalis perfecta actum ad vitam necessarium sine principio proximo relinquere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX6","text":"Ordo potentiarum saltum absolutum inter gradus inferiores et superiores excludit; supremum inferioris ad infimum superioris accedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS1","text":"Complexum animatum → electio rationis divisionis → excessus supra corpus = tres animae / gradus viventis = quattuor modi / obiectum operationis = quinque genera potentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS2","text":"Corpus unitum → vegetativum; res exterior per similitudinem → sensitivum vel intellectivum secundum universalitatem; res exterior ut finis → appetitivum; res exterior ut terminus exsecutionis → motivum locale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS3","text":"Esse alteri communicandum → generativum; quantitas debita acquirenda → augmentativum; substantia restauranda et conservanda → nutritivum; nutritivum → augmentativum → generativum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS4","text":"Sensibile per se immutans → receptio spiritualis necessaria → variabilis adiunctio immutationis naturalis in obiecto vel organo → quinque sensus exteriores → hierarchia materialitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS5","text":"Forma sensibilis × receptio → sensus communis; forma sensibilis × retentio → imaginatio; intentio non sensibilis × apprehensio → aestimativa; intentio non sensibilis × retentio → memoria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS6","text":"Praesentia vel absentia rei → receptio formae → integratio et conservatio → apprehensio intentionis → memoria → appetitus finis → motus ad terminum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AF1","text":"Dependentia intellectivi et appetitivi ab inferioribus → inquisitio praeambulorum → genera potentiarum → vegetativum → sensus exteriores → sensus interiores.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AF2","text":"Enumerationes discrepantes → distinctio animarum, modorum vivendi et potentiarum → relatio ad obiectum → quinque genera → responsiones de appetitu et motu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_