]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ALT2","text":"Structural — Taxonomia regitur obiectis formalibus, irreducibilitate operationum, modis immutationis et distinctione receptionis a retentione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones numerales solvuntur per separationem axium divisionis, et multiplicatio facultatum continetur principio sufficientiae sine redundantia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Vita ponitur ut motus ab intrinseco, cognitio ut praesentia intentionalis, actio ut tendentia finalis, memoria ut retentio praeteriti et appetitus ut ordinatio ad rem nondum adeptam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituenda genera potentiarum et principales subdivisionum rationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT2","text":"Firmissima pars systematis est distinctio criteriorum qua tres animae, quattuor modi vivendi et quinque potentiae conciliantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT3","text":"Structura sensuum interiorum solide restituitur ex distinctionibus receptionis et retentionis, formarum et intentionum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT4","text":"Relatio inter regulam distinctionis per obiecta et regulam distinctionis per operationes irreducibiles non plene formalizatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT5","text":"Derivatio exacti numeri quinque sensuum exteriorum pendet a classificatione modorum immutationis cuius exhaustivitas non ulterius demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT6","text":"Unitas tactus, pluralitas specierum eius et separatio gustus manent commissura ambigua, duabus solutionibus alternativis sustentata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT7","text":"Transitus ab actu animali necessario ad potentiam realiter distinctam nititur principio quod natura in necessariis non deficit et irreducibilitate actuum, quorum nexus non amplius probatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT8","text":"Perfectio cogitativae et reminiscentivae per refluentiam rationis explicatur, sed mechanismus huius elevationis indeterminatus manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT9","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: discrepantia taxonomica → criterium formale → potentiae necessariae → hierarchia actuum → continuitas inter animal et hominem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164740612137Z_f50bfdf3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 78","source_sha256":"91a348757bb9a9bdacc79343efcd14c3180e7dffa824ab0dc739ebd700f24151","sha256":"fbb3c87b1c8c83a16cde5fe524f5ab7bff7e1c9bcb830bb6418f697f54fbf1a3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:47:40.613474+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS1","text":"The lower powers of the soul are investigated as preliminaries to the knowledge of the intellective and appetitive powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS2","text":"The number of the powers of the soul must be determined from the account of objects and operations, not from the number of parts of the soul, modes of living, or organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS3","text":"The argumentation is taxonomic and reconstructive: numerical distinctions are reduced to diverse grounds of division, then powers are restored from necessary acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS4","text":"The principal movement proceeds from apparent numerical contradictions to the distinction of criteria, and thence to the order of the five genera of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS5","text":"Within each genus, the movement proceeds from an irreducible object or operation to its proper power, and from power to the hierarchical order of acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AS6","text":"The difference of man from other animals is constituted by the rationally elevated perfection of sensitive powers, not by their indefinite multiplication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A1","text":"A power of the soul is the proximate principle of an operation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","text":"Actions that cannot be reduced to one proximate principle require diverse powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A3","text":"Genera of powers are formally distinguished according to objects, and the higher power regards a more universal object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A4","text":"Organs and media are ordered to powers and their acts, not powers to the diversity of organs or media.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A5","text":"Souls, modes of living, and genera of powers are divided according to diverse accounts: according to the excess of operation over corporeal nature, according to the grade of the living being, and according to the object of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A6","text":"The intellective operation is exercised without a bodily organ, the sensitive through an organ but not by the power of a corporeal quality, the vegetative through an organ and an instrumental corporeal quality, yet always from an intrinsic principle of the living being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","text":"The vegetative power has as its object the body united to the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","text":"An extrinsic thing is joined to cognition through a likeness, indeed to sense as a sensible body, but to intellect under the account of universal being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A9","text":"Animal appetite follows the apprehended form, is present in every sentient being, and tends toward the thing itself as an end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A10","text":"Local motion requires an executive power by which the body is directed toward an external thing as the terminus of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A11","text":"A living body requires distinct operations by which being is communicated to another, due quantity is acquired, and substance together with quantity is preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A12","text":"The generative power is more principal than the vegetative powers, because it produces an effect in another; the augmentative and nutritive powers serve it, and the nutritive also serves the augmentative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","text":"Sense is a passive power that must receive the form of the sensible according to spiritual being; natural alteration alone does not constitute sensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A14","text":"Proper sensibles first and per se alter sense, whereas common sensibles are perceived through proper sensible qualities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A15","text":"The five external senses are distinguished according to modes of alteration: spiritual alone in sight, natural on the part of the object in hearing and smell, natural on the part of the organ in touch and taste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A16","text":"Perfect animal life requires apprehension of an absent thing and of intentions of usefulness, harmfulness, or suitability that are not reducible to sensible qualities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A17","text":"Reception and retention are distinct principles, as are sensible form and non-sensible intention; from these distinctions common sense, imagination, the estimative power, and memory are constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:A18","text":"In man, the estimative and memorative powers are perfected through affinity with universal reason as the cogitative and reminiscitive powers, without the constitution of new sensitive powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX1","text":"The five genera of powers are not reduced to the three parts of the soul, because souls and powers are numbered according to diverse accounts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX2","text":"The four modes of living do not constitute a complete enumeration of the genera of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX3","text":"Animal appetite is not the mere natural inclination by which each power desires its proper act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX4","text":"Sense and appetite as commanding principles do not suffice for local motion without an executive power of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX5","text":"Vegetative operations are not excluded from the powers of the soul because they instrumentally use natural qualities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX6","text":"The generation of a living being is not reducible to the generation of an inanimate thing produced wholly by an extrinsic agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX7","text":"The number of external senses is not taken from the elements of organs, sensible media, or material genera of qualities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX8","text":"Not every genus of accident requires a proper sense, nor are common sensibles either proper sensibles or merely sensibles per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX9","text":"Natural alteration of the body does not suffice for sensation; otherwise every altered body would sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX10","text":"Common sense is not a genus predicated of the proper senses, but the root to which their apprehensions are referred.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0098","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX11","text":"The proper senses neither distinguish sensibles of diverse senses from one another nor immediately perceive their proper acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX12","text":"Intentions of suitability and harmfulness are not reducible to sensible forms received by the external senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:NX13","text":"The fifth interior power posited by Avicenna is not necessary, nor do the cogitative and reminiscitive powers constitute new powers above the estimative and memorative powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D1","text":"The five genera of powers are the vegetative, sensitive, intellective, appetitive, and locomotive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A3","CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A9","CH_GGVC_P_70:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D2","text":"The three souls are distinguished according to the three grades by which vital operation exceeds corporeal nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A5","CH_GGVC_P_70:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D3","text":"The four modes of living are constituted by the addition of the sensitive, local motion, and the intellective above the vegetative.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A5","CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D4","text":"The appetitive does not constitute a distinct grade of living beings, because it is present in every sentient being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A5","CH_GGVC_P_70:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D5","text":"An appetitive power is required because a thing is known according to a likeness, but desired according to its real being and on account of uses exceeding cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D6","text":"The motive power is distinguished from apprehension and appetite, because the command of motion produces no effect without the executive disposition of the members.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D7","text":"The vegetative powers are generative, augmentative, and nutritive, ordered respectively to the communication of being, due quantity, and the preservation of the living being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","CH_GGVC_P_70:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D8","text":"The generative power is the principal terminus of the vegetative order, while the nutritive power is the material foundation of the augmentative and generative powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A11","CH_GGVC_P_70:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D9","text":"The five external senses are derived from the five ways in which spiritual alteration is joined with or separated from natural alteration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","CH_GGVC_P_70:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D10","text":"Sight is the most spiritual of the senses; hearing and smell follow, then touch and taste as the most material.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A3","CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","CH_GGVC_P_70:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D11","text":"Magnitude, figure, number, motion, and rest do not constitute a proper power, because they alter sense by means of sensible quality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","CH_GGVC_P_70:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D12","text":"Touch is one in genus and multiple in species; taste is distinguished from it either as the touch of the tongue from touch diffused through the body, or according to a diverse account of alteration of the organ.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D13","text":"Four interior sensitive powers suffice: common sense for reception and integration, imagination for the retention of forms, the estimative power for the apprehension of intentions, and memory for their preservation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A1","CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A16","CH_GGVC_P_70:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D14","text":"Common sense distinguishes sensibles of diverse senses and perceives the acts of the proper senses.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:D15","text":"Particular cogitation and reminiscence are more perfect modes of the human estimative power and memory, not sensitive faculties added in species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD1","text":"Diversity of numbers does not constitute a contradiction, because the three souls, four modes of living, and five genera of powers are sections of the same reality according to non-convertible axes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:D1","CH_GGVC_P_70:D2","CH_GGVC_P_70:D3","CH_GGVC_P_70:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD2","text":"The hierarchy of powers expresses an increase in the universality of the object and a decrease in dependence upon material alteration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A3","CH_GGVC_P_70:A6","CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A13","CH_GGVC_P_70:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD3","text":"The multiplication of powers is governed by the principle of economic sufficiency: a new power is posited only where a necessary act cannot be reduced to an already posited principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A1","CH_GGVC_P_70:A2","CH_GGVC_P_70:A4","CH_GGVC_P_70:A17","CH_GGVC_P_70:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD4","text":"Perfect animal action constitutes a circuit from the apprehension of the present or absent through estimation and appetite to the bodily execution of motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A9","CH_GGVC_P_70:A10","CH_GGVC_P_70:A16","CH_GGVC_P_70:A17","CH_GGVC_P_70:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD5","text":"Generation is the joint between life enclosed in its own body and operation extended to another, whence the highest of the vegetative approaches the lowest of the sensitive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A6","CH_GGVC_P_70:A7","CH_GGVC_P_70:A11","CH_GGVC_P_70:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SD6","text":"The human difference within the sensitive order is the rational intensification of powers common to animals, not a rupture through a new genus of interior sense.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_70:A8","CH_GGVC_P_70:A18","CH_GGVC_P_70:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX1","text":"No single division of the soul adequately represents at once substantial parts, grades of life, and genera of operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX2","text":"Anatomy is not the formal principle of the taxonomy of powers, although it provides the material condition of sensible acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX3","text":"Life cannot be constituted from motions wholly extrinsic to the body, because vital operation requires an intrinsic principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX4","text":"The representation of a thing does not suffice for desire for or attainment of the thing; cognition, appetite, and execution do not formally coincide.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX5","text":"The presence of the sensible does not suffice for the life of a perfect animal, which operationally handles absence, useful future, and retained past.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX6","text":"Sensible quality and the individual intention of usefulness or harmfulness cannot be fused into one apprehensive object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX7","text":"The distinction of acts does not effect a legitimate multiplication of powers unless the irreducibility of principles is also established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:DNX8","text":"The rational difference of man does not require a double series of interior powers, one animal and the other properly human.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX1","text":"The number of powers posited absolutely without a ground of division is unusable; every valid enumeration is indexed to its criterion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX2","text":"Sensitive cognition cannot be wholly explained as material alteration, because non-sentient bodies would also fulfill such an explanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX3","text":"Perfect animality would be impossible if it could act only upon the present; absence must be made intentionally present.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX4","text":"Cognitive likeness is never real possession of the object; this interval renders appetite and motion necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX5","text":"The nature of a perfect animal cannot leave an act necessary for life without a proximate principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:SNX6","text":"The order of powers excludes an absolute leap between lower and higher grades; the highest of the lower approaches the lowest of the higher.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS1","text":"Animated composite → choice of ground of division → excess above body = three souls / grade of living being = four modes / object of operation = five genera of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS2","text":"United body → vegetative; external thing through likeness → sensitive or intellective according to universality; external thing as end → appetitive; external thing as terminus of execution → local motive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS3","text":"Being to be communicated to another → generative; due quantity to be acquired → augmentative; substance to be restored and preserved → nutritive; nutritive → augmentative → generative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS4","text":"Sensible that alters per se → spiritual reception necessary → variable conjunction of natural alteration in object or organ → five external senses → hierarchy of materiality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS5","text":"Sensible form × reception → common sense; sensible form × retention → imagination; non-sensible intention × apprehension → estimative power; non-sensible intention × retention → memory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:FGS6","text":"Presence or absence of the thing → reception of form → integration and preservation → apprehension of intention → memory → appetite for the end → motion toward the terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AF1","text":"Dependence of the intellective and appetitive upon the lower powers → investigation of preliminaries → genera of powers → vegetative → external senses → interior senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AF2","text":"Discrepant enumerations → distinction of souls, modes of living, and powers → relation to object → five genera → responses concerning appetite and motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AF3","text":"Necessities of the living body → acquisition of being, quantity, and preservation → three vegetative powers → order of service → primacy of the generative power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AF4","text":"Rejection of organic criteria → sense as spiritual reception → modes of alteration → five senses → grades of spirituality → the cases of touch and taste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:AF5","text":"Necessity of acting concerning the absent → distinction of reception and retention → distinction of forms and intentions → four interior senses → their rational perfection in man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ME1","text":"The conflict among the numbers of powers is converted into a question concerning the criterion of division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ME2","text":"Power is reclassified from an anatomical organ to the formal principle of an act concerning an object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ME3","text":"The opposition between soul and corporeal nature is replaced by a hierarchy of ways in which operation uses the body as an instrument or exceeds it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ME4","text":"Apprehension, appetite, and motion appear as distinct moments of one animal process, not as acts of one faculty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ME5","text":"The vegetative is ordered teleologically from the preservation of the individual to the production of another of the same species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ME6","text":"The external senses are ordered according to the proportion between intentional reception and natural alteration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ME7","text":"Interior sensibility is described through the double axis of forms and intentions, reception and retention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ME8","text":"The difference of man from animal is situated within the continuity of sensitive powers, with rationality elevating the mode of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ALT1","text":"Surface — Five genera of powers, three vegetative powers, five external senses, and four interior senses are enumerated and distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ALT2","text":"Structural — The taxonomy is governed by formal objects, the irreducibility of operations, modes of alteration, and the distinction of reception from retention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Numerical objections are resolved through the separation of axes of division, and the multiplication of faculties is restrained by the principle of sufficiency without redundancy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Life is posited as motion from within, cognition as intentional presence, action as final tendency, memory as retention of the past, and appetite as ordination toward a thing not yet attained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice for restoring the genera of powers and the principal grounds of subdivision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT2","text":"The firmest part of the system is the distinction of criteria by which the three souls, four modes of living, and five powers are reconciled.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT3","text":"The structure of the interior senses is solidly restored from the distinctions of reception and retention, forms and intentions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT4","text":"The relation between the rule of distinction through objects and the rule of distinction through irreducible operations is not fully formalized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT5","text":"The derivation of the exact number of five external senses depends on a classification of modes of alteration whose exhaustiveness is not further demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT6","text":"The unity of touch, the plurality of its species, and the separation of taste remain an ambiguous joint, supported by two alternative solutions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT7","text":"The transition from a necessary animal act to a really distinct power rests on the principle that nature does not fail in necessary things and on the irreducibility of acts, the connection of which is not further proved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT8","text":"The perfection of the cogitative and reminiscitive powers is explained through the overflow of reason, but the mechanism of this elevation remains indeterminate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_70:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: taxonomic discrepancy → formal criterion → necessary powers → hierarchy of acts → continuity between animal and man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_70:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_70@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_70:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 79","title":"First Part · Question 78","context":"Chapter 79","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 78"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 78","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 79","order":80,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_71"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_71@R001","sha256":"d803ebb2093d011af087ab1c33d276119b00398645b230c4f1fd37518dc52226","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quibus differentiis vita intellectiva humana in essentiam, potentias, habitus, actus et officia distribuenda sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS2","text":"Intellectus humanus est potentia animae duplicata secundum principium agens et possibile, dum pleraque alia nomina intellectiva modos, status, habitus, actus vel fines eiusdem potentiae significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, taxonomica, reconstructiva et polemica, quia doctrinas aemulas per criterium obiecti formalis et distinctionem potentiae, habitus atque actus diiudicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0184","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS4","text":"Motus ontologicus ab identitate operationis et esse in Deo ad intellectum creatum ut potentiam receptivam progreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS5","text":"Motus operationalis a formis materialibus tantum potentia intelligibilibus ad abstractionem per intellectum agentem, receptionem per possibilem et participationem luminis superioris procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS6","text":"Motus taxonomicus memoriam, rationem, rationem superiorem et inferiorem, intelligentiam atque intellectum speculativum et practicum ad unam structuram reducit, deinde synderesim ut habitum et conscientiam ut actum constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","text":"Identitas essentiae cum immediato principio operationis locum habet tantum ubi operatio est ipsum esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A2","text":"In solo Deo intelligere et esse idem sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","text":"Potentiae distinguuntur secundum rationes formales obiectorum, non secundum differentias accidentales obiecti vel modos actuum ad idem principium reducibiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0185","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","text":"Intellectus possibilis intelligibilia respicit sub communi ratione entis et veri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0184","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","text":"Intellectus humanus, quia creatus et finitus, non est actus omnium intelligibilium, sed ab intelligibili potentia in actum transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A6","text":"Passio tertio modo est receptio actus ab eo quod erat in potentia, sine abiectione et cum perfectione recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A7","text":"Formae rerum sensibilium in materia sunt intelligibiles potentia, quamvis sensibilia extra animam sint sensibilia actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A8","text":"Nihil de potentia reducitur in actum nisi per aliquod ens actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","text":"Actio rei non convenit nisi per principium formaliter ei inhaerens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A10","text":"Anima humana formas universales a condicionibus particularibus phantasmatum abstrahit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A11","text":"Virtus intelligendi animae humanae participatur ab intellectu superiori, quia participatum, mobile et imperfectum principium perfectum praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A12","text":"Respectu eiusdem obiecti principium activum quod obiectum actu facit et principium passivum quod ab obiecto actu movetur sunt diversae potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A13","text":"Animae humanae secundum homines numero multiplicantur, et una virtus numero diversis substantiis inesse nequit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A14","text":"Intellectus possibilis species receptas habitualiter conservat inter puram potentiam et actualem considerationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A15","text":"Ratiocinatio est motus ab intellectis simplicibus ad alia cognoscenda et reditus iudicialis ad principia, dum simplex intellectio est quies eiusdem processus cognoscitivi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A16","text":"Ordinatio veritatis apprehensae ad opus mutat finem cognitionis, non rationem formalem obiecti intellectivi; verum autem et bonum se mutuo includunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0221","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A17","text":"Prima principia speculabilium et operabilium naturaliter insunt ut habitus regentes ratiocinationem, non ut potentiae speciales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0234","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A18","text":"Applicatio scientiae ad ea quae aguntur est actus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX1","text":"Intellectus creatus non est essentia animae, etiamsi anima a principali sua virtute intellectus vel mens nominetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX2","text":"Passivitas intellectus possibilis non est passio materialis, corruptio vel amissio formae naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX3","text":"Immaterialitas intellectus possibilis sola non sufficit ad formas materiales actu intelligibiles efficiendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX4","text":"Systema formas naturales extra materiam subsistentes, quibus intellectus directe participet, non praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX5","text":"Intellectus agens non est tantum substantia separata species infundens, quia causa universalis propriam virtutem animae non tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX6","text":"Intellectus agens non est una numero virtus omnibus hominibus communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX7","text":"Sola praesentia intellectus agentis et possibilis actualem intellectionem non efficit sine phantasmatibus, dispositione virium sensitivarum et exercitio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX8","text":"Memoria intellectiva neque praeteritum ut praeteritum habet pro obiecto proprio neque potentiam ab intellectu distinctam constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX9","text":"Ratio non est potentia ab intellectu distincta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX10","text":"Intelligentia non est potentia supra intellectum, sed actus intellectus vel denominatio substantiae semper intelligentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX11","text":"Ratio superior et inferior non sunt diversae potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0177","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX12","text":"Intellectus speculativus et practicus non sunt diversae potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX13","text":"Synderesis non est potentia rationalis specialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0234","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX14","text":"Conscientia proprie neque potentia neque habitus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D1","text":"In omni creatura intellectuali intellectus est potentia intelligentis, non ipsa eius essentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","CH_GGVC_P_71:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D2","text":"Intelligere humanum est pati tertio modo, quo intellectus recipiendo actum perficitur neque corrumpitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D3","text":"Intellectus agens requiritur ut formas in phantasmatibus tantum potentia intelligibiles per abstractionem actu intelligibiles faciat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A7","CH_GGVC_P_71:A8","CH_GGVC_P_71:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","text":"Intellectus agens est virtus animae intrinseca et simul lumen ab intellectu superiori participatum; secundum fidei documenta intellectus separatus superior est Deus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A2","CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","CH_GGVC_P_71:A10","CH_GGVC_P_71:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D5","text":"Intellectus agens non movet possibilem ut obiectum iam actu intelligibile, sed obiecta actualia producit, quorum receptio condiciones phantasticas et sensitivas requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A7","CH_GGVC_P_71:A10","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D6","text":"Intellectus agens multiplicatur secundum animas, dum communitas primorum intelligibilium unitatem naturae humanae et fontis superioris, non identitatem numericam agentis, demonstrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A11","CH_GGVC_P_71:A13","CH_GGVC_P_71:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D7","text":"In ordine proprie intellectivo sola oppositio principii agentis et possibilis diversitatem potentiarum constituit; ceterae differentiae ad obiecta accidentalia, status, actus, officia vel fines pertinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","text":"Intellectus possibilis species in habitu conservat, unde memoria ut conservatio eadem potentia est; praeteritum autem ut praeteritum ad sensum pertinet, quamvis intellectus suum praeteritum intelligere possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D9","text":"Intellectus et ratio sunt una potentia secundum quietem simplicis apprehensionis et motum discursus, iar intelligentia actum eiusdem potentiae nominat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D10","text":"Ratio superior et inferior sunt officia eiusdem potentiae, quia temporalia ad aeterna inveniendum ducunt et aeterna ad temporalia iudicanda atque ordinanda redeunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0177","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D11","text":"Intellectus speculativus et practicus sunt una potentia, quae veritatem vel ad solam considerationem vel ad opus dirigendum ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0221","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","text":"Synderesis est habitus naturalis primorum principiorum operabilium, ex quibus ratio ad bonum instigat et de malo iudicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D13","text":"Conscientia est actualis applicatio cognitionis ad actionem, secundum quam actum testificatur, faciendum ligat vel instigat, factum autem excusat aut accusat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A18","CH_GGVC_P_71:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD1","text":"Intellectus humanus medius constituitur inter actum purum divinum et formas materiales: est receptivus sine materialitate et activus sine autosufficientia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D1","CH_GGVC_P_71:D2","CH_GGVC_P_71:D3","CH_GGVC_P_71:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD2","text":"Causalitas intelligendi duplicem ordinem habet: intellectus superior est causa universalis luminis, intellectus agens animae est causa propria abstractionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD3","text":"Universalitas cognitionis compatitur pluralitatem subiectorum, quia unitas obiecti et principiorum non requirit unitatem numericam potentiae cognoscentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D6","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD4","text":"Cognitio humana constituit processum temporalem phantasmatis, abstractionis, receptionis, retentionis habitualis, considerationis et iudicii discursivi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D3","CH_GGVC_P_71:D5","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD5","text":"Cognitio moralis non addit facultatem autonomam, sed ordinat eandem rationem per habitum principiorum et actum applicationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D11","CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX1","text":"Pluralitas nominum psychologicorum non implicat pluralitatem realem potentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX2","text":"Immaterialitas intellectus non importat possessionem actualem omnium intelligibilium neque cognitionem innatam completam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX3","text":"Passivitas non importat inferioritatem simplicem, quia potentia receptiva entis universalis potest esse nobilior activa potentia circa ens particulare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX4","text":"Communitas universalium et primorum principiorum non requirit subiectum intellectivum transpersonale.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D6","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX5","text":"Illuminatio superior neque occasionalismum cognitionis neque autonomiam animae a fonte superiori admittit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX6","text":"Species intelligibiles non debent ad singulos actus denuo ab intellectu separato effluere, quia intellectus eas habitualiter retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A14","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0119","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0121","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX7","text":"Vis normativa principiorum et conscientiae non requirit substantiam vel potentiam moralem specialem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX1","text":"Systema impossibile habet intellectum creatum qui sit actus purus, sui luminis causa prima et omnium intelligibilium actualis possessio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","CH_GGVC_P_71:A2","CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX2","text":"Cognitio humana ordinaria sine sensibilibus, phantasmatibus, abstractione et successione discursiva indisponibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D3","CH_GGVC_P_71:D5","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX3","text":"Unum intellectum humanum omnibus commune systema excludit, quia actus intelligendi principio proprio singulorum subiectorum formaliter inhaerere debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","CH_GGVC_P_71:A13","CH_GGVC_P_71:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX4","text":"Correspondentia biunivoca inter vocabula mentis et facultates reales excluditur; lexicon per potentiam, habitum, actum, statum, officium et finem resolvendum est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D7","CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX5","text":"Oppositio inter causalitatem divinam et agentiam personalem praecluditur, quia participatio causam universalem et virtutem intrinsecam simul requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS1","text":"Identitas operationis cum esse → exclusivitas divina → intellectus creatus ut potentia, non essentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","CH_GGVC_P_71:A2","CH_GGVC_P_71:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS2","text":"Finitas intellectus humani → potentia ad intelligibilia → receptio perfectiva → intellectus possibilis passivus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:A6","CH_GGVC_P_71:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS3","text":"Forma materialis potentia intelligibilis → necessitas entis actu → abstractio → species actu intelligibilis → receptio possibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A7","CH_GGVC_P_71:A8","CH_GGVC_P_71:A10","CH_GGVC_P_71:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS4","text":"Intellectus superior → lumen participatum → principium formale animae → intellectus agens intrinsecus → multiplicatio secundum animas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","CH_GGVC_P_71:A11","CH_GGVC_P_71:A13","CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS5","text":"Receptio speciei → conservatio habitualis → consideratio actualis → discursus → resolutio iudicialis ad principia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A14","CH_GGVC_P_71:A15","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS6","text":"Examen rationis formalis obiecti → distinctio agentis et possibilis → reductio memoriae, rationis, intelligentiae, officiorum et finium ad eandem structuram potentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS7","text":"Principia practica naturalia → habitus synderesis → applicatio ad agibilia → actus conscientiae → testimonium, obligatio vel iudicium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A17","CH_GGVC_P_71:A18","CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0234","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AF1","text":"Essentia vel potentia → potentia passiva → necessitas intellectus agentis → inhaerentia participata → pluralitas secundum animas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AF2","text":"Conservatio specierum → memoria intellectiva → unitas memoriae et intellectus → unitas rationis et intellectus → reductio rationis superioris et inferioris, intelligentiae atque intellectus practici et speculativi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9","CH_GGVC_P_71:D10","CH_GGVC_P_71:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AF3","text":"Potentia intellectiva una → principia operabilium ut habitus → synderesis → applicatio scientiae → conscientia ut actus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS6","CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME1","text":"Intellectus a nomine essentiae vel totius animae ad potentiam principalem creaturae intellectivae reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D1","CH_GGVC_P_71:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME2","text":"Passivitas a detrimento materiali ad receptionem perfectivam convertitur, dum activitas abstractionis ei correlata ponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D2","CH_GGVC_P_71:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME3","text":"Separatio intellectus agentis non substantiam extrinsecam significat, sed independentiam ab organo corporali intra virtutem animae participatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME4","text":"Universalitas obiecti ab unitate numerica subiecti separatur, unde veritas communis cum pluralitate intellectuum personalium componitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D6","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME5","text":"Memoria, ratio, intelligentia, ratio superior et inferior atque intellectus speculativus et practicus ex facultatibus aemulis in conservationem, actum, motum, officium vel finem eiusdem potentiae transferuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D7","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9","CH_GGVC_P_71:D10","CH_GGVC_P_71:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME6","text":"Ager cognitionis moralis in tria strata ordinatur: potentia rationalis communis, habitus principiorum et actus applicationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ALT1","text":"In gradu superficiei, textus tredecim appellationes vel distinctiones partis intellectivae secundum essentiam, potentiam, habitum et actum classificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_71:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ALT2","text":"In gradu structurali, tota classificatio regitur relationibus potentiae et actus, obiecti formalis, abstractionis, receptionis, retentionis et causalitatis intrinsecae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:A8","CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","CH_GGVC_P_71:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ALT3","text":"In gradu metastrategico, textus multiplicationem facultatum coercet et doctrinas Platonis, Avicennae atque intellectus communis per eadem criteria ontologica diiudicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_71:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ALT4","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali, intellectus humanus est virtus creata, participata, personaliter individuata et successive reducta de potentia per habitum ad actum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendam transitionem ab ontologia intellectus ad taxonomiam potentiarum, habituum et actuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12","CH_GGVC_P_71:A17","CH_GGVC_P_71:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT2","text":"Systema interne cohaeret, quia oppositionem actus et potentiae intra eandem animam secundum diversas rationes agentis et recipientis distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT3","text":"Firmissima commissura est criterium rationis formalis obiecti, quo multiplicatio potentiarum per differentias accidentales coercetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT4","text":"Transitus ab intellectu superiori philosophice requisito ad eius identificationem cum Deo expresse fidei documentis nititur, non sola deductione antecedenti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A11","CH_GGVC_P_71:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT5","text":"Participatio conciliat causam universalem et virtutem intrinsecam, sed modus quo virtus participata ab essentia animae procedit breviter tantum determinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT6","text":"Conservatio inamissibilis specierum stabilitur, sed nexus inter talem retentionem, condicionem phantasmatum et defectum actualis revocationis nondum explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A14","CH_GGVC_P_71:D5","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0086","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0120","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0121","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT7","text":"Reductio rationis, officiorum et finium ad unam potentiam pendet a latissima ratione entis et veri atque ab analogia motus et quietis; hae praemissae onus principale compressionis sustinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A15","CH_GGVC_P_71:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT8","text":"Synderesis ut habitus principiorum et conscientia ut applicatio distinguuntur, sed ratio erroris in applicatione conscientiae hic nondum formaliter explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT9","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus: essentia → potentia → actus abstractionis → participatio et individuatio → conservatio → reductio taxonomica → applicatio moralis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_71:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_71:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164811478082Z_d047cf1b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 79","source_sha256":"d803ebb2093d011af087ab1c33d276119b00398645b230c4f1fd37518dc52226","sha256":"6a412631602f578db8317ce78657cefbbefb949b7949017fd0f05224f6866cf0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:48:11.479091+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS1","text":"The text asks by what distinctions human intellectual life should be distributed into essence, powers, habits, acts, and offices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS2","text":"The human intellect is a power of the soul doubled according to the active and possible principle, whereas most other intellectual names signify modes, states, habits, acts, or ends of the same power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, taxonomic, reconstructive, and polemical, because it judges rival doctrines by the criterion of the formal object and the distinction of power, habit, and act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0184","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS4","text":"The ontological movement proceeds from the identity of operation and being in God to the created intellect as a receptive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS5","text":"The operational movement proceeds from material forms intelligible only potentially to abstraction through the active intellect, reception through the possible intellect, and participation in a higher light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AS6","text":"The taxonomic movement reduces memory, reason, higher and lower reason, intelligence, and speculative and practical intellect to one structure, then establishes synderesis as a habit and conscience as an act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","text":"The identity of essence with the immediate principle of operation obtains only where operation is being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A2","text":"In God alone, understanding and being are the same.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","text":"Powers are distinguished according to the formal accounts of their objects, not according to accidental differences of the object or modes of acts reducible to the same principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0185","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","text":"The possible intellect regards intelligibles under the common account of being and truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0184","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","text":"The human intellect, because it is created and finite, is not the actuality of all intelligibles, but passes from potential intelligibility to act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A6","text":"Passion in the third mode is the reception of act from that which was in potency, without casting off and with the perfection of the recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A7","text":"The forms of sensible things in matter are intelligible potentially, although sensibles outside the soul are sensible actually.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A8","text":"Nothing is reduced from potency to act except through some being in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","text":"The action of a thing belongs to it only through a principle formally inhering in it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A10","text":"The human soul abstracts universal forms from the particular conditions of phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A11","text":"The power of understanding of the human soul is participated from a higher intellect, because a participated, mobile, and imperfect principle presupposes a perfect one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A12","text":"With respect to the same object, the active principle that makes the object actual and the passive principle that is moved by the actual object are different powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A13","text":"Human souls are multiplied numerically according to human beings, and one power cannot inhere in numerically diverse substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A14","text":"The possible intellect habitually preserves received species between pure potency and actual consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A15","text":"Reasoning is motion from simply understood things to the cognition of other things and a judicial return to principles, whereas simple understanding is the rest of the same cognitive process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A16","text":"The ordering of apprehended truth to work changes the end of cognition, not the formal account of the intellectual object; moreover, the true and the good mutually include one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0221","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A17","text":"The first principles of speculative and practical matters naturally inhere as habits governing reasoning, not as special powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0234","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:A18","text":"The application of knowledge to things done is an act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX1","text":"The created intellect is not the essence of the soul, even though the soul is named intellect or mind from its principal power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX2","text":"The passivity of the possible intellect is not material passion, corruption, or the loss of a natural form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX3","text":"The immateriality of the possible intellect alone does not suffice to make material forms actually intelligible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX4","text":"The system does not presuppose natural forms subsisting outside matter in which the intellect directly participates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX5","text":"The active intellect is not merely a separate substance infusing species, because a universal cause does not remove the soul's proper power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX6","text":"The active intellect is not one power numerically common to all human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX7","text":"The mere presence of the active and possible intellect does not produce actual intellection without phantasms, the disposition of the sensitive powers, and exercise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX8","text":"Intellectual memory neither has the past as past for its proper object nor constitutes a power distinct from intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX9","text":"Reason is not a power distinct from intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX10","text":"Intelligence is not a power above intellect, but an act of intellect or a designation of a substance always understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX11","text":"Higher and lower reason are not different powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0177","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX12","text":"Speculative and practical intellect are not different powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX13","text":"Synderesis is not a special rational power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0234","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:NX14","text":"Conscience properly is neither a power nor a habit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D1","text":"In every intellectual creature, intellect is a power of the intelligent being, not its essence itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","CH_GGVC_P_71:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D2","text":"Human understanding is passion in the third mode, by which the intellect is perfected, and not corrupted, through receiving act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D3","text":"The active intellect is required in order to make, through abstraction, forms in phantasms that are intelligible only potentially actually intelligible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A7","CH_GGVC_P_71:A8","CH_GGVC_P_71:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","text":"The active intellect is an intrinsic power of the soul and at the same time a light participated from a higher intellect; according to the documents of faith, the higher separate intellect is God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A2","CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","CH_GGVC_P_71:A10","CH_GGVC_P_71:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D5","text":"The active intellect does not move the possible intellect as an already actually intelligible object, but produces actual objects, whose reception requires phantastic and sensitive conditions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A7","CH_GGVC_P_71:A10","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D6","text":"The active intellect is multiplied according to souls, whereas the commonality of first intelligibles demonstrates the unity of human nature and of the higher source, not the numerical identity of the agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A11","CH_GGVC_P_71:A13","CH_GGVC_P_71:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D7","text":"In the properly intellectual order, only the opposition of active and possible principle constitutes a diversity of powers; the remaining differences pertain to accidental objects, states, acts, offices, or ends.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","text":"The possible intellect preserves species in habit, whence memory as preservation is the same power; but the past as past pertains to sense, although intellect can understand its own past.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D9","text":"Intellect and reason are one power according to the rest of simple apprehension and the motion of discursive thought, and intelligence names the act of the same power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D10","text":"Higher and lower reason are offices of the same power, because temporal things lead to finding eternal things, and eternal things return to judging and ordering temporal things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0177","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D11","text":"Speculative and practical intellect are one power, which orders truth either to mere consideration or to directing work.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0221","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","text":"Synderesis is the natural habit of the first principles of things to be done, from which reason urges toward good and judges concerning evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:D13","text":"Conscience is the actual application of knowledge to action, according to which it bears witness to an act, binds or urges what is to be done, and excuses or accuses what has been done.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A18","CH_GGVC_P_71:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD1","text":"The human intellect is constituted midway between pure divine act and material forms: it is receptive without materiality and active without self-sufficiency.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D1","CH_GGVC_P_71:D2","CH_GGVC_P_71:D3","CH_GGVC_P_71:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD2","text":"The causality of understanding has a double order: the higher intellect is the universal cause of light, and the active intellect of the soul is the proper cause of abstraction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD3","text":"The universality of cognition is compatible with a plurality of subjects, because the unity of object and principles does not require the numerical unity of the cognizing power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D6","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD4","text":"Human cognition constitutes a temporal process of phantasm, abstraction, reception, habitual retention, consideration, and discursive judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D3","CH_GGVC_P_71:D5","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SD5","text":"Moral cognition does not add an autonomous faculty, but orders the same reason through the habit of principles and the act of application.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D11","CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX1","text":"A plurality of psychological names does not imply a real plurality of powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX2","text":"The immateriality of intellect does not entail actual possession of all intelligibles or complete innate cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX3","text":"Passivity does not entail simple inferiority, because a receptive power of universal being can be nobler than an active power concerning particular being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX4","text":"The commonality of universals and first principles does not require a transpersonal intellectual subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D6","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX5","text":"Higher illumination admits neither the occasionalism of cognition nor the autonomy of the soul from the higher source.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX6","text":"Intelligible species need not flow anew from the separate intellect for individual acts, because the intellect retains them habitually.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A14","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0119","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0121","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX7","text":"The normative force of principles and conscience does not require a special moral substance or power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX1","text":"The system holds impossible a created intellect that is pure act, the first cause of its own light, and the actual possession of all intelligibles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","CH_GGVC_P_71:A2","CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX2","text":"Ordinary human cognition is unavailable without sensibles, phantasms, abstraction, and discursive succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D3","CH_GGVC_P_71:D5","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX3","text":"The system excludes one human intellect common to all, because the act of understanding must formally inhere in the proper principle of individual subjects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","CH_GGVC_P_71:A13","CH_GGVC_P_71:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX4","text":"A one-to-one correspondence between terms of mind and real faculties is excluded; the lexicon must be resolved through power, habit, act, state, office, and end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D7","CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX5","text":"The opposition between divine causality and personal agency is precluded, because participation requires both a universal cause and an intrinsic power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS1","text":"Identity of operation with being → divine exclusivity → created intellect as power, not essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","CH_GGVC_P_71:A2","CH_GGVC_P_71:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS2","text":"Finitude of the human intellect → potency toward intelligibles → perfective reception → passive possible intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:A6","CH_GGVC_P_71:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS3","text":"Material form potentially intelligible → necessity of a being in act → abstraction → actually intelligible species → possible reception.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A7","CH_GGVC_P_71:A8","CH_GGVC_P_71:A10","CH_GGVC_P_71:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS4","text":"Higher intellect → participated light → formal principle of the soul → intrinsically active intellect → multiplication according to souls.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","CH_GGVC_P_71:A11","CH_GGVC_P_71:A13","CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS5","text":"Reception of species → habitual preservation → actual consideration → discursive thought → judicial resolution to principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A14","CH_GGVC_P_71:A15","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS6","text":"Examination of the formal account of the object → distinction of active and possible → reduction of memory, reason, intelligence, offices, and ends to the same structure of powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS7","text":"Natural practical principles → habit of synderesis → application to things to be done → act of conscience → testimony, obligation, or judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A17","CH_GGVC_P_71:A18","CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0234","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AF1","text":"Essence or power → passive power → necessity of the active intellect → participated inherence → plurality according to souls.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AF2","text":"Preservation of species → intellectual memory → unity of memory and intellect → unity of reason and intellect → reduction of higher and lower reason, intelligence, and practical and speculative intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9","CH_GGVC_P_71:D10","CH_GGVC_P_71:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:AF3","text":"One intellectual power → principles of things to be done as habits → synderesis → application of knowledge → conscience as act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS6","CH_GGVC_P_71:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME1","text":"Intellect is reclassified from the name of an essence or of the whole soul to the principal power of an intellectual creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D1","CH_GGVC_P_71:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME2","text":"Passivity is converted from material detriment to perfective reception, while the activity of abstraction is posited as correlated with it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D2","CH_GGVC_P_71:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME3","text":"The separation of the active intellect signifies not an extrinsic substance, but independence from a bodily organ within the participated power of the soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME4","text":"The universality of the object is separated from the numerical unity of the subject, whence common truth is composed with a plurality of personal intellects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D6","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME5","text":"Memory, reason, intelligence, higher and lower reason, and speculative and practical intellect are transferred from rival faculties into preservation, act, motion, office, or end of the same power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D7","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8","CH_GGVC_P_71:D9","CH_GGVC_P_71:D10","CH_GGVC_P_71:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0178","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ME6","text":"The field of moral cognition is ordered into three strata: common rational power, habit of principles, and act of application.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ALT1","text":"At the surface level, the text classifies thirteen appellations or distinctions of the intellectual part according to essence, power, habit, and act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_71:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0198","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ALT2","text":"At the structural level, the entire classification is governed by the relations of potency and act, formal object, abstraction, reception, retention, and intrinsic causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:A8","CH_GGVC_P_71:A9","CH_GGVC_P_71:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ALT3","text":"At the metastrategic level, the text restrains the multiplication of faculties and judges the doctrines of Plato, Avicenna, and the common intellect by the same ontological criteria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_71:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_71:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_71:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:ALT4","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, the human intellect is a created, participated, personally individuated power, successively reduced from potency through habit to act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore the transition from the ontology of intellect to the taxonomy of powers, habits, and acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A1","CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12","CH_GGVC_P_71:A17","CH_GGVC_P_71:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT2","text":"The system coheres internally, because it distinguishes the opposition of act and potency within the same soul according to the diverse accounts of agent and recipient.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A5","CH_GGVC_P_71:A12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT3","text":"The strongest joint is the criterion of the formal account of the object, by which the multiplication of powers through accidental differences is restrained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A3","CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT4","text":"The transition from the philosophically required higher intellect to its identification with God rests expressly on the documents of faith, not on antecedent deduction alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A11","CH_GGVC_P_71:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT5","text":"Participation reconciles the universal cause and intrinsic power, but the manner in which the participated power proceeds from the essence of the soul is only briefly determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D4","CH_GGVC_P_71:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT6","text":"The unfailing preservation of species is established, but the connection between such retention, the condition of phantasms, and the failure of actual recall is not yet explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A14","CH_GGVC_P_71:D5","CH_GGVC_P_71:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0086","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0120","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0121","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT7","text":"The reduction of reason, offices, and ends to one power depends on the broadest account of being and truth and on the analogy of motion and rest; these premises bear the principal burden of compression.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:A4","CH_GGVC_P_71:A15","CH_GGVC_P_71:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0158","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0216","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT8","text":"Synderesis as a habit of principles and conscience as application are distinguished, but the account of error in the application of conscience is not yet formally explained here.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:D12","CH_GGVC_P_71:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0253","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_71:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: essence → power → act of abstraction → participation and individuation → preservation → taxonomic reduction → moral application.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_71:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_71:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_71:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0235","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_71:P0252","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_71@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_71:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 80","title":"First Part · Question 79","context":"Chapter 80","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 79"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 79","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 80","order":81,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_72"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_72@R001","sha256":"68a2719f89ba629fe9c619e2b0887458565873ce7166425ce09191ce422fa899","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat utrum appetere in cognoscentibus exigat potentiam animae propriam ultra inclinationem naturalem omnibus rebus communem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS2","text":"Argumentatio distinguit inclinationem quae formam naturalem consequitur ab appetitu qui bonum apprehensum prosequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS3","text":"Eadem res potest esse obiectum cognitionis et appetitus secundum subiectum, sed diversae rationes obiectales exigunt potentias diversas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS4","text":"Divisio appetitus sequitur non rem singularem quae appetitur, sed genus apprehensionis a qua appetitus passive movetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS5","text":"Appetitus intellectivus attingit singularia sub ratione universali et bona immaterialia; tamen motus eius ad executionem mediante appetitu inferiori procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS6","text":"Motus argumentationis est: inclinatio communis → appetitus cognitivus proprius → distinctio formalis obiectorum → divisio sensitiva et intellectiva → subordinatio motus superioris et inferioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A1","text":"Omnem formam sequitur inclinatio ad id quod formae convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A2","text":"Forma rei cognitione carentis determinat rem ad unum esse proprium; inclinatio hanc formam consequens est appetitus naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A3","text":"Cognoscens, praeter formam propriam naturalem, species aliarum rerum recipere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A4","text":"Capacitas recipiendi formas aliarum rerum constituit modum formae altiorem quam forma naturalis ad unum esse propria determinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A5","text":"Inclinatio proportionata formae cognitivae excedit appetitum naturalem et est appetitus animalis seu appetitus consequens apprehensionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A6","text":"Appetibile apprehensum movet appetitum; appetitus est potentia passiva et mobilis respectu apprehensi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A7","text":"Potentiae distinguuntur per rationes formales obiectorum, non per materialem identitatem rei quae subiecto apprehenditur et appetitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A8","text":"Res apprehenditur ut ens sensibile vel intelligibile, sed appetitur ut conveniens vel bonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A9","text":"Differentia inter apprehensum sensu et apprehensum intellectu est differentia per se appetibilis moventis, quia appetibile non movet nisi ut apprehensum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A10","text":"Appetitus intellectivus fertur ad res singulares sub ratione universali et potest ferri in bona immaterialia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A11","text":"Universale intellectum non movet ad motum exteriorem nisi per particulare; appetitus superior movet inferiorem mediante inferiori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX1","text":"Appetitus animalis non reducitur ad inclinationem naturalem omnibus entibus, etiam inanimatis, communem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX2","text":"Identitas materialis rei cognitae et rei appetitae non tollit distinctionem potentiae cognitivae ab appetitiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX3","text":"Inclinatio naturalis cuiuslibet potentiae ad actum proprium non est idem ac appetitus animalis boni convenientis simpliciter animali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX4","text":"Appetitus sensitivus et intellectivus non differunt accidentaliter ex sola denominatione apprehensionis antecedentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX5","text":"Omnis appetitus non concluditur esse mere singularis ex eo quod res extra animam sunt singulares.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX6","text":"Appetitus intellectivus non instituit motum corporeum autonomum parallelum motui sensitivo, sed motum inferiorem instrumentaliter assumit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D1","text":"In cognoscente appetitus est necessarius, quia cognitio multiplicat formas receptas et postulatur inclinatio proportionata ad bona sub illis formis apprehensa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A3","CH_GGVC_P_72:A4","CH_GGVC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D2","text":"Appetitus animalis non appetit tantum id quod immediate convenit actui alicuius potentiae, sed id quod convenit animali simpliciter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A5","CH_GGVC_P_72:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D3","text":"Cognitio et appetitus sunt potentiae distinctae, quia eadem res sub diversa ratione formali est principium receptionis cognitivae et motus appetitivi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A7","CH_GGVC_P_72:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D4","text":"Appetitus sensitivus et intellectivus sunt potentiae diversae, quia mobilia passive proportionantur motivis activis, et apprehensa sensibilia atque intelligibilia sunt alterius generis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A6","CH_GGVC_P_72:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D5","text":"Universalitas intellectus non evacuat ordinem appetitus ad singularia, sed modum formalem quo singularia appetuntur determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D6","text":"Actio mota ab appetitu superiori requirit articulationem inter rationem universalem et apprehensionem seu appetitum particularem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A10","CH_GGVC_P_72:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SD1","text":"Systema constituit animam cognoscentem ut locum in quo pluralitas formarum alienarum recipitur sine amissione formae propriae, atque appetitus est principium ordinationis activa ad hanc pluralitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A2","CH_GGVC_P_72:A3","CH_GGVC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SD2","text":"Bonum non operatur hic ut res materialiter separata, sed ut ratio sub qua res apprehensa potest movere inclinationem appetitivam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A6","CH_GGVC_P_72:A7","CH_GGVC_P_72:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SD3","text":"Distinctio appetituum est architectura mediationis: diversitas cognitionum producit diversitatem desideriorum, sed desiderium intellectivum ad motum per desiderium sensitivum descendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A9","CH_GGVC_P_72:A10","CH_GGVC_P_72:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SD4","text":"Superioritas appetitus intellectivi non est imminutio ordinis sensibilis, sed subordinatio qua universale efficax fit solum in ordine particulari et mobili.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A10","CH_GGVC_P_72:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omnis inclinatio ad bonum univoce sit appetitus, alioquin differentia inter naturam inanimatam et animam cognoscentem evanesceret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod obiectum potentiae ex sola re extra animam definiatur, alioquin cognitio et appetitus, sensus et intellectus, non possent formaliter distingui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod universale, ut universale tantum manens, sit causa sufficiens motus exterioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit animam ut receptaculum mere speculativum formarum: cognitio, si formam alterius recipit, structuram inclinationis ultra naturam propriam requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit immediatam transitum ab intelligibili universali ad executionem corporalem; inter utrumque ordo particularis et inferioris appetitus indisponibilis manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS1","text":"Forma naturalis → inclinatio naturalis ad esse proprium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS2","text":"Cognitio formarum alienarum → excessus supra determinationem naturalem unius formae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS3","text":"Excessus formalis cognitionis → appetitus consequens apprehensionem → potentia appetitiva specialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS4","text":"Eadem res subiecto / diversa ratio obiectalis → distinctio cognitionis et appetitus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS5","text":"Apprehensum movens → appetitus mobilis → proportio motivi et mobilis → divisio sensitiva et intellectiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS6","text":"Ratio universalis boni → appetitus intellectivus singularium vel immaterialium → mediatio appetitus inferioris → motus exterior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AF1","text":"Appetere commune omnibus → distinctio inter appetitum naturalem et appetitum apprehensivum → necessitas potentiae appetitivae animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AF2","text":"Identitas rei cognitae et appetitae → distinctio rationum entis et boni convenientis → distinctio potentiarum cognitivae et appetitivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AF3","text":"Appetitus ut motus ab apprehenso → differentia sensibilis et intelligibilis → divisio appetitus sensitivi et intellectivi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AF4","text":"Intellectus universalis → appetitus sub ratione universali → mediatio particularis et inferioris → unitas motus animalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter appetitum naturale et appetitum animalem fit visibilis ut oppositio inter inclinationem ex forma propria et inclinationem ex bono apprehenso.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ME2","text":"Obiectum potentiae reclassificatur non secundum rem materialem, sed secundum rationem formalem qua res cognoscitur vel appetitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ME3","text":"Distinctio sensus et intellectus transit ex sola theoria cognitionis in principium divisionis motuum appetitivorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ME4","text":"Universale et singulare non disponuntur ut obiecta appetituum omnino separata, sed ut rationes et termini in uno ordine appetitus intellectivi mediati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ALT1","text":"Surface — Quaestio immediate examinat utrum appetitus sit potentia specialis et utrum in sensitivum atque intellectivum dividatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ALT2","text":"Structural — Potentiae distinguuntur ex habitudine passivi ad motivum et ex rationibus formalibus obiectorum apprehensorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Difficultas de unitate appetitus solvitur per translationem quaestionis a re appetita materialiter ad modum quo res apprehensa movet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Cognoscens excedit naturam ad unum determinatam per receptionem formarum plurium, sed motus eius in singulari ordine executionis mediate terminatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam necessitatem appetitus proprii, si principium generale quod formam sequitur inclinatio servatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter appetitum naturalem et animalem firmissime sustentatur per oppositionem inter formam propriam naturalem et bonum apprehensum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT3","text":"Divisio appetitus sensitivi et intellectivi cohaeret, quia ratio appetibilis dependet a genere apprehensi quod appetitum movet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter identitatem rei appetitae, quae extra animam singularis est, et universalitatem rationis sub qua intellectus eam appetit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT5","text":"Altera commissura est subordinatio appetitus superioris ad inferiorem: superior causam finalem et formalem praebet, inferior autem mediationem motus, sed modus exactus huius mediationis hic non ulterius determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia a communitate nominis appetitus ad differentias formales, deinde ad distinctionem potentiarum et ordinem motus procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164832579866Z_f6fc8860","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 80","source_sha256":"68a2719f89ba629fe9c619e2b0887458565873ce7166425ce09191ce422fa899","sha256":"5c0e6b5e7e739b9914887c5aa82daa0924b5e49aa9a6df38b27cb66b35659d2a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:48:32.582048+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS1","text":"The question determines whether appetition in cognizant beings requires a proper power of the soul beyond the natural inclination common to all things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS2","text":"The argument distinguishes the inclination consequent upon natural form from the appetite that pursues the apprehended good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS3","text":"The same thing can be the object of cognition and appetite with respect to the subject, but diverse objective formal accounts require diverse powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS4","text":"The division of appetite follows not the singular thing that is appetized, but the genus of apprehension by which appetite is passively moved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS5","text":"The intellective appetite attains singulars under a universal account and immaterial goods; nevertheless, its motion toward execution proceeds through the mediation of the lower appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AS6","text":"The movement of the argument is: common inclination → proper cognitive appetite → formal distinction of objects → sensitive and intellective division → subordination of higher and lower motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A1","text":"Every form is followed by an inclination toward that which befits the form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A2","text":"The form of a thing lacking cognition determines the thing to one proper being; the inclination consequent upon this form is natural appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A3","text":"A cognizant being, beyond its own natural form, can receive the species of other things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A4","text":"The capacity to receive the forms of other things constitutes a mode of form higher than natural form determined to one proper being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A5","text":"The inclination proportioned to cognitive form exceeds natural appetite and is animal appetite, or appetite consequent upon apprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A6","text":"The apprehended appetible moves appetite; appetite is a passive and movable power with respect to what is apprehended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A7","text":"Powers are distinguished by the formal accounts of their objects, not by the material identity of the thing that is apprehended and appetized by the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A8","text":"A thing is apprehended as sensible or intelligible being, but is appetized as suitable or good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A9","text":"The difference between what is apprehended by sense and what is apprehended by intellect is a difference in the essentially appetible mover, because the appetible moves only insofar as it is apprehended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A10","text":"The intellective appetite is borne toward singular things under a universal account and can be borne toward immaterial goods.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:A11","text":"The understood universal does not move to exterior motion except through the particular; the higher appetite moves the lower through the lower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX1","text":"Animal appetite is not reducible to the natural inclination common to all beings, including inanimate ones.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX2","text":"The material identity of the known thing and the appetized thing does not remove the distinction between cognitive and appetitive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX3","text":"The natural inclination of any power toward its proper act is not the same as the animal appetite for a good suitable simply to the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX4","text":"Sensitive and intellective appetite do not differ accidentally merely from the denomination of the antecedent apprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX5","text":"Not every appetite is concluded to be merely singular from the fact that things outside the soul are singular.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:NX6","text":"The intellective appetite does not establish an autonomous bodily motion parallel to sensitive motion, but instrumentally assumes the lower motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D1","text":"In a cognizant being, appetite is necessary, because cognition multiplies received forms and an inclination proportioned to the goods apprehended under those forms is required.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A3","CH_GGVC_P_72:A4","CH_GGVC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D2","text":"Animal appetite does not appetize only that which immediately befits the act of some power, but that which befits the animal simply.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A5","CH_GGVC_P_72:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D3","text":"Cognition and appetite are distinct powers, because the same thing under a diverse formal account is the principle of cognitive reception and appetitive motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A7","CH_GGVC_P_72:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D4","text":"Sensitive and intellective appetite are diverse powers, because things passively moved are proportioned to active movers, and sensible and intelligible apprehended objects are of another genus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A6","CH_GGVC_P_72:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D5","text":"The universality of the intellect does not evacuate the order of appetite toward singulars, but determines the formal mode in which singulars are appetized.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:D6","text":"Action moved by the higher appetite requires an articulation between the universal account and particular apprehension or appetite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A10","CH_GGVC_P_72:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SD1","text":"The system establishes the cognizant soul as the place in which a plurality of alien forms is received without loss of its proper form, and appetite is the principle of active ordering toward this plurality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A2","CH_GGVC_P_72:A3","CH_GGVC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SD2","text":"The good does not operate here as a materially separate thing, but as the account under which an apprehended thing can move appetitive inclination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A6","CH_GGVC_P_72:A7","CH_GGVC_P_72:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SD3","text":"The distinction of appetites is an architecture of mediation: diversity of cognitions produces diversity of desires, but intellective desire descends to motion through sensitive desire.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A9","CH_GGVC_P_72:A10","CH_GGVC_P_72:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SD4","text":"The superiority of intellective appetite is not a diminishment of the sensible order, but a subordination by which the universal becomes efficacious only in a particular and movable order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_72:A10","CH_GGVC_P_72:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:DNX1","text":"It must be false that every inclination toward the good is univocally appetite; otherwise, the difference between inanimate nature and the cognizant soul would vanish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the object of a power is defined from the thing outside the soul alone; otherwise, cognition and appetite, sense and intellect, could not be formally distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the universal, remaining only as universal, is a sufficient cause of exterior motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the soul as a merely speculative receptacle of forms: cognition, if it receives the form of another, requires a structure of inclination beyond its proper nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:SNX2","text":"The system excludes an immediate transition from the intelligible universal to bodily execution; between the two, the order of the particular and lower appetite remains indispensable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS1","text":"Natural form → natural inclination toward proper being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS2","text":"Cognition of alien forms → excess beyond the natural determination of one form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS3","text":"Formal excess of cognition → appetite consequent upon apprehension → special appetitive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS4","text":"The same thing in subject / diverse objective account → distinction of cognition and appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS5","text":"Apprehended mover → movable appetite → proportion of mover and movable → sensitive and intellective division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:FGS6","text":"Universal account of the good → intellective appetite for singulars or immaterial things → mediation of the lower appetite → exterior motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AF1","text":"Appetition common to all → distinction between natural appetite and apprehensive appetite → necessity of an appetitive power of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AF2","text":"Identity of the known and appetized thing → distinction between the accounts of being and suitable good → distinction between cognitive and appetitive powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AF3","text":"Appetite as motion from what is apprehended → difference between sensible and intelligible → division of sensitive and intellective appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:AF4","text":"Universal intellect → appetite under a universal account → mediation of the particular and lower → unity of animal motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ME1","text":"The opposition between natural appetite and animal appetite becomes visible as the opposition between inclination from one's proper form and inclination from the apprehended good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ME2","text":"The object of a power is reclassified not according to the material thing, but according to the formal account under which the thing is known or appetized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ME3","text":"The distinction between sense and intellect passes from mere theory of cognition into a principle for dividing appetitive motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ME4","text":"The universal and the singular are not arranged as altogether separate objects of appetites, but as accounts and termini within one order of mediated intellective appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ALT1","text":"Surface — The question immediately examines whether appetite is a special power and whether it is divided into sensitive and intellective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ALT2","text":"Structural — Powers are distinguished from the relation of what is passive to the mover and from the formal accounts of apprehended objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The difficulty concerning the unity of appetite is resolved by translating the question from the thing materially appetized to the mode in which the apprehended thing moves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The cognizant being exceeds nature determined to one thing through the reception of many forms, but its motion is mediately terminated in the singular order of execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the necessity of a proper appetite, provided that the general principle that inclination follows form is preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT2","text":"The distinction between natural and animal appetite is most firmly sustained by the opposition between one's proper natural form and the apprehended good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT3","text":"The division of sensitive and intellective appetite coheres, because the account of the appetible depends on the genus of apprehended object that moves appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains between the identity of the appetized thing, which is singular outside the soul, and the universality of the account under which the intellect appetizes it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT5","text":"Another juncture is the subordination of the higher appetite to the lower: the higher supplies final and formal causality, whereas the lower supplies mediation of motion, but the exact mode of this mediation is not further determined here.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_72:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the commonality of the name appetite to formal differences, then to the distinction of powers and the order of motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_72:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_72@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_72:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 81","title":"First Part · Question 80","context":"Chapter 81","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 80"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 80","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 81","order":82,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_73"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_73@R001","sha256":"dc3c4dfdd27dffc8abf17181f74a1aefc64ba15649a6f7739ee4786e1b9951ad","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat utrum sensualitas sit cognitio vel potius appetitus sensitivus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS2","text":"Nomen sensualitatis resolvitur per motum sensualem, qui non apprehensionem sed inclinationem appetitivam consequentem apprehensionem sensitivam significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS3","text":"Appetitus sensitivus, quamvis unus genere, per diversitatem relationis ad conveniens et ad impedimentum dividitur in concupiscibilem et irascibilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS4","text":"Irascibilis instituitur ut defensio concupiscibilis, quia tendit contra contraria quae bonum sensibile impediunt vel nocumentum inferunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS5","text":"In homine appetitus sensitivus subditur rationi per mediationem cogitativae particularis et voluntati per ordinem executionis motoriae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS6","text":"Obedientia sensibilis appetitus non tollit resistentiam eius, quia eodem appetitu sensus et imaginatio movere possunt contra imperium rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A1","text":"Potentia denominatur ab actu proprio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A2","text":"Operatio apprehensiva perficitur per praesentiam rei apprehensae in apprehendente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A3","text":"Operatio appetitiva perficitur per inclinationem appetentis in rem appetibilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A4","text":"Motus sensualis est appetitus apprehensionem sensitivam consequens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A5","text":"Sensualitas est nomen appetitus sensitivi, non potentiae cognitivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A6","text":"Appetitus sensitivus inclinat ad convenientia sensibilia prosequenda et nociva refugienda.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A7","text":"Conservatio animalis requirit inclinationem resistendi impedientibus et corrumpentibus, praeter inclinationem ad bonum conveniens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A8","text":"Concupiscibilis fertur simpliciter in conveniens sensibile et contra nocivum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A9","text":"Irascibilis fertur in arduum, id est in superationem contrariorum quae bonum concupiscibile impugnant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A10","text":"In homine vis cogitativa particulares intentiones confert et a ratione universali dirigi nata est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A11","text":"Motus executivus appetitus inferioris indiget consensu appetitus superioris, scilicet voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A12","text":"Appetitus sensitivus etiam a sensu et imaginatione moveri potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX1","text":"Sensualitas non comprehendit ipsos sensus corporis, qui sunt eius praeambuli apprehensivi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX2","text":"Sensualitas non est vis cognitiva, quamvis cum ratione in communitate motionis dividi possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX3","text":"Serpens sensualitatem non significat ratione nuntiationis peccati, sed ratione inclinationis in effectum peccati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX4","text":"Appetitus sensitivus non est una potentia indifferens respectu boni et impedimenti eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX5","text":"Irascibilis non versatur simpliciter circa nocivum, sed circa nocivum ut impugnans et resistendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX6","text":"Obedientia irascibilis et concupiscibilis rationi non est obedientia despotica nec exclusio omnis repugnantiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX7","text":"Imperium rationis non se extendit ad exteriores sensus eodem modo ac ad interiores vires, quia sensus exteriores pendent a sensibilibus praesentibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D1","text":"Sensualitas definitur per inclinationem consequenter ortam ex apprehensione sensitiva, non per actum quo obiectum cognoscitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A2","CH_GGVC_P_73:A3","CH_GGVC_P_73:A4","CH_GGVC_P_73:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D2","text":"Distinctio concupiscibilis et irascibilis sequitur diversitatem functionum appetitus, non diversitatem generis sensitivi appetitus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A6","CH_GGVC_P_73:A7","CH_GGVC_P_73:A8","CH_GGVC_P_73:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D3","text":"Irascibilis potest inclinare animam ad triste contra inclinationem concupiscibilis, quia bonum defensivum postulare potest certamen vel passionem praesentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A8","CH_GGVC_P_73:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D4","text":"Passiones irascibilis ab affectionibus concupiscibilis incipiunt et ad eas terminantur, quia defensio ordinatur ad bonum concupiscibile conservandum vel recuperandum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A8","CH_GGVC_P_73:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D5","text":"Ratio universalis movet appetitum sensitivum mediante ratione particulari, quae universalia in conclusiones singulares deducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D6","text":"Voluntas non producit appetitum sensitivum, sed impedit ne eius motus statim in executionem corporalem transeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D7","text":"Repugnantia passionum rationi compatitur cum eorum obedientia, quia idem appetitus diversis principiis movetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A10","CH_GGVC_P_73:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SD1","text":"Affectivitas humana constituitur ut ordo medius: sensibilis origine, rationaliter dirigibilis, sed non a ratione exhaustive determinatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A5","CH_GGVC_P_73:A10","CH_GGVC_P_73:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SD2","text":"Conflictus interior non est defectus extrinsecus accessorius, sed effectus structurae in qua appetitus sensitivus habet principium proprium motus sub regimine superiori.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A9","CH_GGVC_P_73:A11","CH_GGVC_P_73:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SD3","text":"Imperium rationis in appetitum est politicum et regale, quia gubernatio ordinat vim resistibilem potius quam instrumentum omnino iners administrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A11","CH_GGVC_P_73:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod apprehensio sensitiva ex se sit appetitus, quia cognitio et inclinatio per modos perfectionis diversos constituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omne bonum sensibile immediate et sine conflictu prosequendum sit, quia conservatio boni interdum postulat ingressum in triste et resistentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod ratio universalis sola immediate moveat passionem vel corpus, quia particulare cogitativum et consensus voluntatis sunt media necessaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod subiectio rationi aequivaleat immunitati a sensu et imaginatione, quia hae vires appetitum contra rationem movere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit imaginem rationis ut dominii absoluti, in quo imperium superius omnem causalitatem inferiorem absorbeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit imaginem sensibilitatis ut fata inexorabilia, in quo motus passionis necessario in actum corporalem perficiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS1","text":"Apprehensio sensitiva → inclinatio ad obiectum apprehensum → denominatio sensualitatis ut appetitus sensitivi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS2","text":"Bonum vel malum sensibile → concupiscibilis prosecutio vel fuga; impedimentum boni vel nocumentum impugnans → irascibilis resistentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS3","text":"Concupiscibile bonum → imminutio vel defensio eius → passio irascibilis → recuperatio vel vindicta → terminus concupiscibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS4","text":"Ratio universalis → cogitativa particularis → motus appetitus sensitivi; voluntas superior → consensus executivus → motus corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS5","text":"Sensus et imaginatio → motus autonomus appetitus sensitivi → possibilitas repugnantiae → regimen politicum rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF1","text":"Ambiguitas sensualitatis inter cognitionem et appetitum → distinctio quietis apprehensivae et motus appetitivi → sensualitas ut appetitus sensitivus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF2","text":"Unitas generica appetitus sensitivi → exigentia conservationis contra impedimenta → distinctio concupiscibilis et irascibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF3","text":"Irascibilis ut defensio concupiscibilis → conflictus passionum → subordinatio finalis irascibilis ad bonum concupiscibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF4","text":"Motus sensibilis animalis → cogitativa humana sub ratione universali → moderatio passionum per rationem → executio sub voluntate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF5","text":"Repugnantia passionis → pluralitas principiorum moventium → obedientia politica potius quam dominatio despotica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME1","text":"Cognitio et appetitus reclassificantur secundum modum perfectionis actus: praesentia obiecti in cognoscente opponitur inclinationi cognoscentis in obiectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME2","text":"Bonum sensibile non iam apparet ut solum obiectum delectationis, sed etiam ut bonum defendendum per motus ad arduum ordinatos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME3","text":"Irascibilis reclassificatur non ut appetitus parallelus concupiscibili, sed ut vis propugnatrix eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME4","text":"Ratio reclassificatur non ut causa unica passionum, sed ut principium dirigens quod per cogitativam particulares motus ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME5","text":"Libertas executiva reclassificatur ut interruptio catenae immediatae inter appetitum sensibilem et motum corporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT1","text":"Surface — Sensualitas est appetitus sensitivus divisus in concupiscibilem et irascibilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT2","text":"Structural — Appetitus sensitivus includit inclinationem ad bonum, fugam mali et resistentiam contra impedimenta boni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Ratio moderatur passiones per traductionem universalium in particularia, dum voluntas regit transitum ad executionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Motus animalis tendit ad effectum ex appetitu immediate; motus humanus inter appetitum et effectum ordinem superioris appetitus interponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT5","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Imperium rationis est temporale et contingens, quia passio a sensu vel imaginatione mota potest rationi reniti antequam voluntas executionem concedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam transitionem a nomine sensualitatis ad definitionem appetitus sensitivi et ad divisionem eius internam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter concupiscibilem et irascibilem maxime nititur in differentia inter bonum simpliciter appetitum et bonum contra impedimenta defendendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT3","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi duplex subordinatio explicatur: appetitus sensitivus dirigitur a ratione in actu et a voluntate in executione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT4","text":"Tensionem relinquit affirmatio quod irascibilis sit species propria et tamen omnes eius passiones a concupiscibili incipiant et in ipsum terminentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT5","text":"Tensionem relinquit usus vocabuli obedientiae, quia eadem vox simul significat naturalem aptitudinem ad regi et realem facultatem resistendi per sensum et imaginationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, si sensualitas, divisio passionum et regimen rationis non tamquam theses separatae sed tamquam gradus unius ordinis motus intelliguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164856353385Z_7d11bbe4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 81","source_sha256":"dc3c4dfdd27dffc8abf17181f74a1aefc64ba15649a6f7739ee4786e1b9951ad","sha256":"afe0df232167a3e919ecbd22e38c5552fa6a8d86de900c060e73fc9255072c6c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:48:56.354328+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS1","text":"The question determines whether sensuality is cognition or rather the sensitive appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS2","text":"The name of sensuality is resolved through sensual movement, which signifies not apprehension but an appetitive inclination consequent upon sensitive apprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS3","text":"The sensitive appetite, although one in genus, is divided into the concupiscible and the irascible through the diversity of its relation to the suitable and to an impediment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS4","text":"The irascible is established as the defense of the concupiscible, because it tends against contraries that impede sensible good or inflict harm.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS5","text":"In man, the sensitive appetite is subject to reason through the mediation of particular cogitative power and to the will through the order of motor execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AS6","text":"The obedience of the sensitive appetite does not remove its resistance, because sense and imagination can move it, by that same appetite, against the command of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A1","text":"A power is denominated from its proper act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A2","text":"An apprehensive operation is perfected through the presence of the apprehended thing in the apprehender.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A3","text":"An appetitive operation is perfected through the inclination of the appetitive subject toward the appetible thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A4","text":"Sensual movement is appetite consequent upon sensitive apprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A5","text":"Sensuality is the name of the sensitive appetite, not of a cognitive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A6","text":"The sensitive appetite inclines toward pursuing suitable sensibles and fleeing harmful things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A7","text":"The preservation of the animal requires an inclination to resist impediments and corrupting things, in addition to the inclination toward the suitable good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A8","text":"The concupiscible is borne simply toward the suitable sensible and against the harmful.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A9","text":"The irascible is borne toward the arduous, that is, toward overcoming contraries that assail the concupiscible good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A10","text":"In man, the cogitative power compares particular intentions and is naturally apt to be directed by universal reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A11","text":"The executive movement of the lower appetite requires the consent of the higher appetite, namely, the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:A12","text":"The sensitive appetite can also be moved by sense and imagination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX1","text":"Sensuality does not include the bodily senses themselves, which are its apprehensive preliminaries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX2","text":"Sensuality is not a cognitive power, although it may be divided with reason in a community of motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX3","text":"The serpent does not signify sensuality by reason of the announcement of sin, but by reason of inclination toward the effect of sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX4","text":"The sensitive appetite is not one indifferent power with respect to the good and its impediment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX5","text":"The irascible is not concerned simply with the harmful, but with the harmful as assailing and to be resisted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX6","text":"The obedience of the irascible and concupiscible to reason is neither despotic obedience nor the exclusion of all resistance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:NX7","text":"The command of reason does not extend to the external senses in the same manner as to the internal powers, because the external senses depend on present sensibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D1","text":"Sensuality is defined by the inclination consequently arising from sensitive apprehension, not by the act through which the object is known.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A2","CH_GGVC_P_73:A3","CH_GGVC_P_73:A4","CH_GGVC_P_73:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D2","text":"The distinction between the concupiscible and the irascible follows the diversity of the functions of appetite, not a diversity in the genus of sensitive appetite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A6","CH_GGVC_P_73:A7","CH_GGVC_P_73:A8","CH_GGVC_P_73:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D3","text":"The irascible can incline the soul toward the sorrowful against the inclination of the concupiscible, because a defensive good can require conflict or present suffering.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A8","CH_GGVC_P_73:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D4","text":"The passions of the irascible begin from and terminate in the affections of the concupiscible, because defense is ordered to preserving or recovering the concupiscible good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A8","CH_GGVC_P_73:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D5","text":"Universal reason moves the sensitive appetite by means of particular reason, which draws universals into singular conclusions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D6","text":"The will does not produce the sensitive appetite, but prevents its movement from passing immediately into bodily execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:D7","text":"The resistance of passions to reason is compatible with their obedience, because the same appetite is moved by diverse principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A10","CH_GGVC_P_73:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SD1","text":"Human affectivity is constituted as a middle order: sensible in origin, rationally governable, yet not exhaustively determined by reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A5","CH_GGVC_P_73:A10","CH_GGVC_P_73:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SD2","text":"Interior conflict is not an extrinsic and accessory defect, but an effect of a structure in which the sensitive appetite has its own principle of motion under a higher governance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A9","CH_GGVC_P_73:A11","CH_GGVC_P_73:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SD3","text":"The command of reason over appetite is political and royal, because governance orders a resistible power rather than administering an altogether inert instrument.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_73:A11","CH_GGVC_P_73:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:DNX1","text":"It must be false that sensitive apprehension is of itself appetite, because cognition and inclination are constituted through diverse modes of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:DNX2","text":"It must be false that every sensible good is to be pursued immediately and without conflict, because preservation of the good sometimes requires entering into the sorrowful and resistance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:DNX3","text":"It must be false that universal reason alone immediately moves passion or the body, because the particular cogitative power and the consent of the will are necessary intermediaries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:DNX4","text":"It must be false that subjection to reason is equivalent to immunity from sense and imagination, because these powers can move appetite against reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SNX1","text":"The system excludes an image of reason as absolute dominion, in which the higher command absorbs all lower causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:SNX2","text":"The system excludes an image of sensibility as inexorable fate, in which the movement of passion is necessarily brought to bodily act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS1","text":"Sensitive apprehension → inclination toward the apprehended object → denomination of sensuality as sensitive appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS2","text":"Sensible good or evil → concupiscible pursuit or flight; impediment of good or assailing harm → irascible resistance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS3","text":"Concupiscible good → its diminution or defense → irascible passion → recovery or vengeance → concupiscible terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS4","text":"Universal reason → particular cogitative power → movement of the sensitive appetite; higher will → executive consent → movement of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:FGS5","text":"Sense and imagination → autonomous movement of the sensitive appetite → possibility of resistance → political governance of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF1","text":"Ambiguity of sensuality between cognition and appetite → distinction of apprehensive rest and appetitive movement → sensuality as sensitive appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF2","text":"Generic unity of the sensitive appetite → requirement of preservation against impediments → distinction of the concupiscible and the irascible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF3","text":"The irascible as defense of the concupiscible → conflict of passions → final subordination of the irascible to the concupiscible good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF4","text":"Sensible animal movement → human cogitative power under universal reason → moderation of passions through reason → execution under the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:AF5","text":"Resistance of passion → plurality of moving principles → political obedience rather than despotic domination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME1","text":"Cognition and appetite are reclassified according to the mode of perfection of the act: the presence of the object in the knower is opposed to the inclination of the knower toward the object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME2","text":"The sensible good no longer appears as merely an object of delight, but also as a good to be defended through movements ordered toward the arduous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME3","text":"The irascible is reclassified not as an appetite parallel to the concupiscible, but as its defending power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME4","text":"Reason is reclassified not as the sole cause of passions, but as a directing principle that orders particular movements through the cogitative power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ME5","text":"Executive freedom is reclassified as the interruption of the immediate chain between sensible appetite and bodily movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT1","text":"Surface — Sensuality is the sensitive appetite divided into the concupiscible and the irascible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT2","text":"Structural — The sensitive appetite includes inclination toward the good, flight from evil, and resistance against impediments to the good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Reason moderates passions by translating universals into particulars, while the will governs the transition to execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Animal movement tends immediately from appetite to effect; human movement interposes between appetite and effect the order of the higher appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:ALT5","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The command of reason is temporal and contingent, because a passion moved by sense or imagination can resist reason before the will grants execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the transition from the name of sensuality to the definition of sensitive appetite and to its internal division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT2","text":"The distinction between the concupiscible and the irascible rests chiefly on the difference between the good simply desired and the good to be defended against impediments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT3","text":"The structure is strongest where the twofold subordination is explained: the sensitive appetite is directed by reason in act and by the will in execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT4","text":"The assertion leaves a tension that the irascible is a proper species and yet all its passions begin from the concupiscible and terminate in it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT5","text":"The use of the term obedience leaves a tension, because the same word simultaneously signifies a natural aptitude to be governed and a real capacity to resist through sense and imagination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_73:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if sensuality, the division of the passions, and the governance of reason are understood not as separate theses but as stages of a single order of motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_73:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_73@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_73:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 82","title":"First Part · Question 81","context":"Chapter 82","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 81"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 81","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 82","order":83,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_74"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_74@R001","sha256":"5cf2183d0d4178f343f499799697fbfb1b768d174be35dd446a1d27a7624f92f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat quomodo voluntas simul necessitate ultimi finis teneatur et libertatem electionis circa media conservet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS2","text":"Argumentatio est distinctiva et reconstructiva: necessitatem coactionis a necessitate naturali et necessitate finis separat, ut libertas non cum omni necessitate confundatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS3","text":"Motus procedit ab ultimo fine necessario ad bona particularia contingentia, quorum nexus cum beatitudine vel caret necessitate vel per visionem divinam necessarius demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS4","text":"Comparatio intellectus et voluntatis duplicem ordinem constituit: intellectus simpliciter eminet ratione obiecti, voluntas autem secundum quid eminet ratione rei superioris ad quam inclinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS5","text":"Systema completur per causalitatem reciprocum sed asymmetram et per reductionem appetitus intellectivi ad unam potentiam boni communis, contra partitionem irascibilis et concupiscibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A1","text":"Necessarium est id quod non potest non esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A2","text":"Necessitas naturalis ex principio intrinseco, necessitas finis ex conditione finis, et necessitas coactionis ex agente extrinseco oriuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A3","text":"Necessitas coactionis est contra inclinationem rei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","text":"Necessitas coactionis voluntati repugnat, quia motus voluntatis est inclinatio voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A5","text":"Necessitas naturalis et necessitas finis voluntati non repugnant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","text":"Voluntas ultimo fini, qui est beatitudo, naturaliter et necessario inhaeret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A7","text":"Electio est eorum quae sunt ad finem, non ipsius ultimi finis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","text":"Voluntas bonum universale et perfectum sub communi ratione boni respicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A9","text":"Ratio plura confert, sensus autem unum simpliciter apprehendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","text":"Bonum particulare quod ad beatitudinem necessario non connectitur voluntatem necessario non determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A11","text":"Certitudo visionis divinae nexus necessarii inter Deum et beatitudinem manifestat atque voluntatem videntis Deum necessario ad Deum inclinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","text":"Intellectus simpliciter voluntate nobilior est, quia obiectum eius est ratio boni appetibilis, simplicior et absolutior ipso bono appetibili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","text":"Voluntas secundum quid intellectum superat cum res in qua bonum invenitur anima superior est, quia voluntas ad rem prout in se est inclinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","text":"Intellectus voluntatem movet per modum finis, voluntas autem intellectum movet per modum agentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A15","text":"Voluntas, quia bonum et finem in communi respicit, omnes potentias animae ad suos actus movet praeter vires vegetativas arbitrio non subiectas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","text":"Potentia ordinata ad obiectum secundum rationem communem per differentias speciales sub illa ratione contentas non multiplicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A17","text":"Passiones cum concitatione animi ad appetitum sensitivum pertinent, affectus autem simplices absque passione sunt actus voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A18","text":"Omnem motum voluntatis apprehensio praecedit, sed principium primi intelligendi et consiliandi est principium intellectivum superius, Deus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX1","text":"Voluntarium non per omnem necessitatem destruitur; sola necessitas coactionis voluntario opponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX2","text":"Potentia rationalis ad opposita non excludit naturalem et necessariam voluntatis inclinationem in ultimum finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX3","text":"Dominium actuum non ad ipsum ultimum finem extenditur, sed ad electionem mediorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX4","text":"Bonum particulare sub ratione boni apprehensum non absorbet totam capacitatem voluntatis neque eam necessario movet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX5","text":"Eminentia intellectus et voluntatis per unum ordinem simplicem statui non potest, quia simpliciter et secundum quid diversa mensura comparationis sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX6","text":"Reciprocus motus intellectus et voluntatis nec idem causandi modus nec processus infinitus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX7","text":"Irascibilis et concupiscibilis non sunt duae potentiae voluntatis, et vires vegetativae voluntatis imperio non subduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D1","text":"Libertas voluntatis consistit in dominio electionis circa media, dum necessaria inclinatio ad beatitudinem manet extra electionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A3","CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","CH_GGVC_P_74:A5","CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D2","text":"Indeterminatio voluntatis ad bona particularia oritur ex amplitudine boni universalis et ex comparatione plurium bonorum, non ex absentia omnis ordinis ad bonum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A9","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D3","text":"Adhaesio Deo non est nunc voluntati necessaria ante certam visionem nexus eius cum beatitudine, sed videnti Deum per essentiam necessaria fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D4","text":"Intellectus simpliciter prior est voluntate, sed voluntas in ordine ad rem anima superiorem potest intellectum secundum quid superare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D5","text":"Reciprocitas intellectus et voluntatis est asymmetra: intellectus bonum ut finem proponit, voluntas actum intelligendi ut bonum speciale imperat, et series in apprehensione prima terminatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D6","text":"Voces amoris, concupiscentiae, irae et desiderii non semper diversitatem potentiarum significant, quia possunt vel passionem sensitivam vel affectum voluntatis denotare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D7","text":"Appetitus sensitivus ab apprehenso singulari determinatius movetur, appetitus intellectivus autem ex pluralitate rationum boni moveri potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A9","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SD1","text":"Libertas non definitur ut carentia necessitatis, sed ut ordo in quo necessitas naturalis ultimi finis cum contingentia electionis mediorum componitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","CH_GGVC_P_74:A5","CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SD2","text":"Necessitas voluntatis ad Deum habet condicionem epistemicam: non sola bonitas rei, sed certitudo nexus eius cum beatitudine voluntatem necessario determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SD3","text":"Ordo potentiarum non est scala unica, sed compositio ordinis formalis obiecti, ordinis realis rei appetitae et ordinis causalis motus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SD4","text":"Universalitas boni voluntatis simul unitatem appetitus intellectivi efficit et potestatem eius imperativam super actus potentiarum particularium fundat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15","CH_GGVC_P_74:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX1","text":"Libertas ut indifferentia absoluta ab omni fine naturali falsa esse debet, quia voluntas immobilem inclinationem ad beatitudinem requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A5","CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX2","text":"Determinismus ex quolibet bono particulari falso supponit bonum finitum capacitatem voluntatis universalis exhaurire posse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX3","text":"Hierarchia univoca, qua una potentia omni respectu altera superior ponitur, falsa esse debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX4","text":"Lexicon passionum non potest per se divisionem realem potentiarum animi demonstrare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX5","text":"Voluntas non potest sibi ipsi primam condicionem cognitionis fundare, quia omnis eius motus apprehensionem praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SNX1","text":"Subiectum voluntatis omnino sui principii exclusum est, quia finis ultimus non eligitur et principium primi intelligendi voluntatem antecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SNX2","text":"Omnis reductio motus animae ad unicum genus causalitatis exclusa est, quia finis intellectus et agens voluntatis diversos modos motus constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SNX3","text":"Bonum universale non est aggregatum bonorum particularium nec genus per species appetitivas in voluntate divisibile.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS1","text":"Necessitas multipliciter distincta → coactio ab inclinatione voluntatis separata → necessitas naturalis et finis voluntario compatibiles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A1","CH_GGVC_P_74:A2","CH_GGVC_P_74:A3","CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","CH_GGVC_P_74:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS2","text":"Finis ultimus necessario appetitus → electio ad media restricta → libertas intra ordinem teleologicum determinata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS3","text":"Bonum universale voluntatis + collatio rationis → particularia bona non necessitant → visio certi nexus cum beatitudine → adhaesio divina necessaria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A9","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS4","text":"Obiectum intellectus simplicius → eminentia simpliciter intellectus; res superior animae → eminentia relativa voluntatis; finis intellectus + agens voluntatis → reciprocitas causalis terminata in primo intelligibili.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS5","text":"Bonum commune voluntatis → una potentia intellectiva et imperium actuum; bona sensibilia particularia → divisio concupiscibilis et irascibilis; passio → appetitus sensitivus, affectus simplex → voluntas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A15","CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AF1","text":"Necessitas indifferenter posita → distinctio naturalis, finalis et coactae → coactio exclusa → beatitudo necessario volita → electio mediorum libera.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AF2","text":"Bonum universale → bona particularia insufficientia → cognitio certi nexus → necessitas ad Deum videnti → comparatio relativa intellectus et voluntatis → motus finalis et agens reciproce distincti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AF3","text":"Obiectum commune voluntatis → imminutio partitionis per species boni → irascibilis et concupiscibilis ad appetitum sensitivum restrictae → affectus rationales uni voluntati attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME1","text":"Necessitas reclassificatur: coactio libertatem tollit, necessitas naturalis et finalis ordinem internum voluntatis constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A2","CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","CH_GGVC_P_74:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME2","text":"Necessitas volendi non ex sola natura obiecti, sed ex relatione cognita inter bonum et beatitudinem intelligibilis fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME3","text":"Comparatio intellectus et voluntatis e scala fixa in tabulam plurium ordinum convertitur: formalis, realis et causalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME4","text":"Voluntas non tantum appetitus unus inter alios, sed principium imperativum actuum potentiarum particularium describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME5","text":"Distinctio psychologica passionis et affectus simplicis vocabula communia ab architectura reali potentiarum separat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ALT1","text":"Surface — Voluntas aliquid necessario vult, sed non omnia quae vult; intellectus et voluntas diversis respectibus comparantur; voluntas intellectum movet; in ipsa irascibilis et concupiscibilis non distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ALT2","text":"Structural — Obiectum formale, modus causalitatis et communitas vel particularitas boni distribuunt necessitatem, libertatem, eminentiam et divisionem potentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio voces univocas, sicut necessitas, superioritas, motus, ira et concupiscentia, per distinctiones respectuum dissolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A2","CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Natura immobilis ultimi finis fundamentum motuum voluntatis constituit, dum visio divina praesentem indeterminationem in necessariam adhaesionem convertit et Deus principium primi intelligendi manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de triplici necessitate, ultimo fine, obiecto universali et duplici motu sufficiunt ad responsiones quinque articulorum restituendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia systematis maxime pendet ex distinctione inter necessitatem coactionis et necessitatem naturalem vel finalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT3","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter necessitatem beatitudinis et non necessariam praesentem adhaesionem Deo, quia identitas beatitudinis verae cum Deo cognitione nexus medianda est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT4","text":"Reciproca causalitas intellectus et voluntatis interne distinguitur per finem et agens, sed transitus ab apprehensione prima ad motus voluntarios subsequentes breviter in principio divino sistitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT5","text":"Comparatio potentiarum stabilis manet tantum dum eminentia simpliciter ab eminentia secundum quid separatur; neglecta distinctione, conclusiones contrariae apparere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT6","text":"Distinctio passionis et affectus simplex partitionem voluntatis impedit, sed eadem vocabula analogice ad sensum et voluntatem translata ambiguitatem semanticam residuam servant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0096","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164920617384Z_f9c28eaa","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 82","source_sha256":"5cf2183d0d4178f343f499799697fbfb1b768d174be35dd446a1d27a7624f92f","sha256":"a834219aa2993d1981c2d6fe1c3a972071b145168ec8bbe9b00b7ca075a50a9a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:49:20.618305+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS1","text":"The question examines how the will is at once bound by the necessity of the ultimate end and preserves freedom of choice concerning the means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS2","text":"The argument is both distinctive and reconstructive: it separates the necessity of coercion from natural necessity and the necessity of the end, so that freedom is not conflated with every necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS3","text":"The movement proceeds from the necessarily willed ultimate end to contingent particular goods, whose connection with beatitude either lacks necessity or is shown necessary through divine vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS4","text":"The comparison of intellect and will establishes a twofold order: intellect simply excels by reason of its object, whereas will excels in a certain respect by reason of the higher thing toward which it inclines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AS5","text":"The system is completed through reciprocal but asymmetrical causality and through the reduction of intellectual appetite to one power of the common good, against the partition into irascible and concupiscible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A1","text":"That which cannot not be is necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A2","text":"Natural necessity arises from an intrinsic principle, necessity of the end from the condition of the end, and necessity of coercion from an extrinsic agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A3","text":"The necessity of coercion is contrary to the inclination of a thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","text":"The necessity of coercion is repugnant to the will, because the movement of the will is the inclination of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A5","text":"Natural necessity and necessity of the end are not repugnant to the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","text":"The will naturally and necessarily adheres to the ultimate end, which is beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A7","text":"Choice concerns those things that are for the end, not the ultimate end itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","text":"The will regards the universal and perfect good under the common aspect of the good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A9","text":"Reason compares several things, whereas sense apprehends one thing simply.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","text":"A particular good not necessarily connected to beatitude does not necessarily determine the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A11","text":"The certainty of divine vision manifests the necessary connection between God and beatitude and necessarily inclines the will of one seeing God toward God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","text":"Intellect is simply nobler than will, because its object is the intelligible aspect of the appetible good, simpler and more absolute than the appetible good itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","text":"Will surpasses intellect in a certain respect when the thing in which good is found is higher than the soul, because will inclines toward the thing as it is in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","text":"Intellect moves the will in the manner of an end, whereas will moves intellect in the manner of an agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A15","text":"Because it regards good and end in common, the will moves all powers of the soul to their acts, except vegetative powers not subject to command.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","text":"A power ordered to an object under a common aspect is not multiplied by specific differences contained under that aspect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A17","text":"Passions with agitation of the soul belong to the sensitive appetite, whereas simple affections without passion are acts of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:A18","text":"Every movement of the will is preceded by apprehension, but the principle of first understanding and deliberating is the higher intellectual principle, God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX1","text":"The voluntary is not destroyed by every necessity; only the necessity of coercion is opposed to the voluntary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX2","text":"A rational power toward opposites does not exclude the natural and necessary inclination of the will toward the ultimate end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX3","text":"Mastery over acts does not extend to the ultimate end itself, but to the choice of means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX4","text":"A particular good apprehended under the aspect of good does not absorb the whole capacity of the will or move it necessarily.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX5","text":"The eminence of intellect and will cannot be established by one simple order, because simply and in a certain respect are different measures of comparison.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX6","text":"The reciprocal movement of intellect and will is neither the same mode of causing nor an infinite process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:NX7","text":"The irascible and concupiscible are not two powers of the will, and vegetative powers are not subject to the command of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D1","text":"Freedom of the will consists in mastery of choice concerning means, while the necessary inclination toward beatitude remains outside choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A3","CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","CH_GGVC_P_74:A5","CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D2","text":"The indetermination of the will toward particular goods arises from the breadth of universal good and from the comparison of several goods, not from the absence of every order toward good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A9","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D3","text":"Adherence to God is not now necessary to the will before a certain vision of its connection with beatitude, but it becomes necessary to one seeing God through essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D4","text":"Intellect is simply prior to will, but will can surpass intellect in a certain respect in relation to a thing higher than the soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D5","text":"The reciprocity of intellect and will is asymmetrical: intellect proposes good as an end, will commands the act of understanding as a particular good, and the series terminates in first apprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D6","text":"The terms love, concupiscence, anger, and desire do not always signify a diversity of powers, because they can denote either sensitive passion or affection of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:D7","text":"The sensitive appetite is moved more determinately by an apprehended singular, whereas the intellectual appetite can be moved by a plurality of aspects of good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A9","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SD1","text":"Freedom is not defined as the absence of necessity, but as an order in which the natural necessity of the ultimate end is composed with the contingency of the choice of means.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","CH_GGVC_P_74:A5","CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SD2","text":"The necessity of the will toward God has an epistemic condition: not the goodness of the thing alone, but certainty of its connection with beatitude necessarily determines the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SD3","text":"The order of powers is not a single scale, but a composition of the formal order of the object, the real order of the desired thing, and the causal order of movement.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SD4","text":"The universality of the good of the will at once effects the unity of intellectual appetite and grounds its commanding power over the acts of particular powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15","CH_GGVC_P_74:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX1","text":"Freedom as absolute indifference from every natural end must be false, because the will requires an immovable inclination toward beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A5","CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX2","text":"Determinism from any particular good falsely supposes that a finite good can exhaust the capacity of the universal will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX3","text":"A univocal hierarchy, by which one power is posited as superior to another in every respect, must be false.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX4","text":"The lexicon of passions cannot by itself demonstrate a real division of the powers of the soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:DNX5","text":"The will cannot ground for itself the first condition of cognition, because all its movement presupposes apprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SNX1","text":"The subject of the will is wholly excluded from its own principle, because the ultimate end is not chosen and the principle of first understanding precedes the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SNX2","text":"Every reduction of the movement of the soul to a single kind of causality is excluded, because the end of intellect and the agent of will constitute diverse modes of movement.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:SNX3","text":"Universal good is neither an aggregate of particular goods nor a genus divisible in the will through appetitive species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS1","text":"Necessity distinctly differentiated in several ways → coercion separated from the inclination of the will → natural necessity and necessity of the end compatible with the voluntary.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A1","CH_GGVC_P_74:A2","CH_GGVC_P_74:A3","CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","CH_GGVC_P_74:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS2","text":"Ultimate end necessarily desired → choice restricted to means → freedom determined within teleological order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS3","text":"Universal good of the will + comparison by reason → particular goods do not necessitate → vision of a certain connection with beatitude → necessary divine adherence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A9","CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS4","text":"Object of intellect simpler → simple eminence of intellect; thing higher than the soul → relative eminence of will; end of intellect + agent of will → reciprocal causality terminated in the first intelligible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:FGS5","text":"Common good of the will → one intellectual power and command of acts; particular sensible goods → division of concupiscible and irascible; passion → sensitive appetite, simple affection → will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A15","CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AF1","text":"Necessity posited indiscriminately → distinction of natural, final, and coercive necessity → coercion excluded → beatitude necessarily willed → free choice of means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AF2","text":"Universal good → insufficiency of particular goods → cognition of a certain connection → necessity toward God for one seeing → relative comparison of intellect and will → final and agent movements reciprocally distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:AF3","text":"Common object of the will → diminution of partition by species of good → irascible and concupiscible restricted to sensitive appetite → rational affections attributed to the one will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME1","text":"Necessity is reclassified: coercion removes freedom, while natural and final necessity constitute the internal order of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A2","CH_GGVC_P_74:A4","CH_GGVC_P_74:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME2","text":"The necessity of willing becomes intelligible not from the nature of the object alone, but from the known relation between good and beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A10","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME3","text":"The comparison of intellect and will is transformed from a fixed scale into a map of several orders: formal, real, and causal.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME4","text":"The will is described not merely as one appetite among others, but as the commanding principle of the acts of particular powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ME5","text":"The psychological distinction between passion and simple affection separates common terms from the real architecture of powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A16","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ALT1","text":"Surface — The will wills something necessarily, but not everything that it wills; intellect and will are compared in different respects; the will moves intellect; the irascible and concupiscible are not distinguished within it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ALT2","text":"Structural — The formal object, mode of causality, and commonness or particularity of good distribute necessity, freedom, eminence, and division of powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A8","CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument dissolves univocal terms, such as necessity, superiority, movement, anger, and concupiscence, through distinctions of respects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A2","CH_GGVC_P_74:A12","CH_GGVC_P_74:A13","CH_GGVC_P_74:A14","CH_GGVC_P_74:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The immovable nature of the ultimate end constitutes the foundation of movements of the will, while divine vision transforms present indetermination into necessary adherence and God remains the principle of first understanding.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_74:A6","CH_GGVC_P_74:A11","CH_GGVC_P_74:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning threefold necessity, the ultimate end, the universal object, and twofold movement suffice to reconstruct the responses of the five articles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT2","text":"The coherence of the system depends chiefly on the distinction between the necessity of coercion and natural or final necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT3","text":"A fragile joint remains between the necessity of beatitude and the presently non-necessary adherence to God, because the identity of true beatitude with God must be mediated by cognition of the connection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT4","text":"The reciprocal causality of intellect and will is internally distinguished through end and agent, but the transition from first apprehension to subsequent voluntary movements is briefly halted in the divine principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT5","text":"The comparison of powers remains stable only so long as simple eminence is separated from eminence in a certain respect; if the distinction is neglected, contrary conclusions can appear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_74:MRT6","text":"The distinction between passion and simple affection prevents a partition of the will, but the same terms, analogically transferred to sense and will, retain residual semantic ambiguity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0092","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_74:P0096","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_74@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_74:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 83","title":"First Part · Question 82","context":"Chapter 83","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 82"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 82","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 83","order":84,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_75"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_75@R001","sha256":"07e6e5865d5675b24df362acba19e2444f11bb1e07a3db707509c58ec423f3fc","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS1","text":"Quaestio instituit utrum motus divinus, inclinatio naturalis, passiones et impedimenta executionis homini liberum arbitrium auferant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS2","text":"Libertatis principium non ponitur in absentia omnis causae, sed in iudicio rationali particularium contingentium, quod ad opposita se habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS3","text":"Electio resolvitur in consilium rationis et acceptationem appetitus; propter obiectum suum, bonum utile ad finem, principaliter est actus appetitivus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS4","text":"Liberum arbitrium, quamvis nomine actum iudicandi significet, est potentia electiva permanens, non habitus nec actus transitorius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS5","text":"Voluntas finis et electio eorum quae sunt ad finem sunt actus diversi eiusdem appetitus intellectivi; liberum arbitrium igitur non est potentia altera a voluntate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS6","text":"Causalitas divina et libertas humana componuntur per ordinem causarum: Deus movet voluntatem ut causam voluntariam, cuius motus proprius manet voluntarius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A1","text":"Agens absque iudicio non agit libere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A2","text":"Iudicium ex solo instinctu naturali determinato non est liberum iudicium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","text":"Ratio circa particularia operabilia contingentia ad opposita se habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A4","text":"Homo agit libere quia iudicium practicum format per collationem rationis, non per instinctum naturalem particularem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A5","text":"Liberum arbitrium est principium quo homo libere iudicat, et ideo est principium actus permanens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A6","text":"Potentia liberi arbitrii ad bene et male eligendum indifferenter se habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A7","text":"Habitus inclinat subiectum ad bene vel male se habendum circa actus aut passiones; talis inclinatio rationi liberi arbitrii non competit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A8","text":"Electio requirit consilium cognitivum de praeferendo et appetitivam acceptationem eius quod consilium diiudicavit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A9","text":"Obiectum proprium electionis est bonum utile, id est id quod appetitur propter finem; bonum autem est obiectum appetitus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A10","text":"Voluntas respicit finem simpliciter, electio autem media propter finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A11","text":"Diversitas actuum et obiectorum subordinata non requirit diversitatem potentiarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A12","text":"Liberum non requirit ut sit prima causa sui motus, sed ut per seipsum moveatur ad agendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A13","text":"Causa prima movendo causam voluntariam conservat et efficit proprietatem voluntariam motus eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A14","text":"Inclinationes naturales, corporales, habituales et passionales libertatem non destruunt, si subsunt iudicio rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A15","text":"Electio est in homine, quamvis executio electionis impediri possit et liberum arbitrium divino auxilio indigeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX1","text":"Liberum arbitrium non est potentia faciendi quidquid homo vult, quia appetitus sensitivus rationi repugnare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX2","text":"Libertatem non tollit motus ab alio, nisi motus proprius causae voluntariae destruatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX3","text":"Dominium electionis non est dominium infallibile executionis externae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX4","text":"Appetitus naturalis ultimi finis non subiacet libero arbitrio et non est obiectum electionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX5","text":"Liberum arbitrium non est habitus naturalis neque habitus acquisitus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX6","text":"Liberum arbitrium non est potentia pure cognitiva, quamvis consilium et iudicium rationis electionem praecedant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX7","text":"Liberum arbitrium non est potentia distincta a voluntate, sed vis electiva eiusdem potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX8","text":"Peccatum non destruit libertatem naturalem a coactione, sed libertatem a culpa et miseria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D1","text":"Homo est liberi arbitrii ex hoc quod rationalis est, quia rationalitas practico iudicio contingentium possibilitatem oppositorum aperit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A1","CH_GGVC_P_75:A2","CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","CH_GGVC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D2","text":"Consilia, exhortationes, praecepta, prohibitiones, praemia et poenae supponunt agentem cuius electiones non sunt naturaliter ad unum determinatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","CH_GGVC_P_75:A4","CH_GGVC_P_75:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D3","text":"Liberum arbitrium est potentia, quia nomen actus liberi iudicii transfertur ad principium stabile illius actus, quod neque habitus esse potest neque actus purus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A5","CH_GGVC_P_75:A6","CH_GGVC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D4","text":"Electio est principaliter appetitiva, quia deliberatio rationis sola non constituit electionem nisi appetitus id quod ratio praeferendum iudicat acceptet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A8","CH_GGVC_P_75:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D5","text":"Voluntas et liberum arbitrium sunt una potentia sub duplici actu: voluntas fertur in finem, vis electiva in media comparata ad finem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A10","CH_GGVC_P_75:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D6","text":"Motus divinus non evacuat libertatem, quia prima causa non concurrit voluntati ut causa rivalis, sed ut causa quae modum voluntarium operationis producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A12","CH_GGVC_P_75:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D7","text":"Dispositiones corporis, habitus et passiones inclinant electionem sine necessitatione, quatenus appetitus inferior et qualitates supervenientes rationi subiici possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","CH_GGVC_P_75:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SD1","text":"Libertas definitur ut causalitas rationaliter mediata intra ordinem causarum, non ut imminutio omnis dependentiae causalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","CH_GGVC_P_75:A4","CH_GGVC_P_75:A12","CH_GGVC_P_75:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SD2","text":"Structura electionis dividit agere humanum in ordinem finis non-electivi et ordinem mediorum electivorum; libertas igitur finita est per finem naturaliter appetitum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A9","CH_GGVC_P_75:A10","CH_GGVC_P_75:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SD3","text":"Responsabilitas moralis fundatur non in immunitate a passionibus, inclinationibus vel auxilio divino, sed in retentione iudicii rationalis et acceptationis electivae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A4","CH_GGVC_P_75:A8","CH_GGVC_P_75:A14","CH_GGVC_P_75:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SD4","text":"Unitas voluntatis et liberi arbitrii impedit ut electio tractetur velut facultas neutra extra ordinem boni et finis; ipsa est appetitus intellectualis mediorum propter finem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A9","CH_GGVC_P_75:A10","CH_GGVC_P_75:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX1","text":"Systema falsum esse requirit exemplar libertatis quod libertatem cum aseitate causali confundit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX2","text":"Systema falsum esse requirit exemplar in quo causalitas divina et causalitas creata necessario mutuo se excludunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX3","text":"Systema falsum esse requirit transitum ab inclinatione ad necessitatem, sive inclinatio sit naturalis, corporalis, habitualis sive passionalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX4","text":"Systema falsum esse requirit opinionem quod cognitio comparativa ipsa electionem absolvat sine actu appetitivo acceptante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX5","text":"Systema falsum esse requirit opinionem quod distinctio finis et mediorum multiplicet potentias, potius quam actus unius potentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio circumagit impossibilitatem libertatis absolute indeterminatae: liberum arbitrium semper exercetur sub ratione boni, finis, consilii et causalitatis primae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio excludit possibilitatem eligendi ultimum finem ut medium inter alternativa, quia beatitudo naturaliter appetitur et electionis obiectum sunt ea quae sunt ad finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SNX3","text":"Argumentatio non admittit libertatem ut plenam potestatem eventuum, quia electio manet hominis dum executio externa impediri potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS1","text":"Contingens particulare operabile → collatio rationis → iudicium non naturaliter determinatum → possibilitas ad opposita → liberum iudicium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS2","text":"Consilium de praeferendo → acceptatio appetitiva boni utilis → electio → actus liberi arbitrii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS3","text":"Actus nominatus “liberum iudicium” → inquisitio principii actus → exclusio habitus → positio potentiae electivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS4","text":"Finis simpliciter appetitus → media propter finem electa → distinctio actuum → analogia intelligere/ratiocinari → unitas voluntatis et liberi arbitrii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS5","text":"Motus primae causae → operatio secundum proprietatem causae voluntariae → motus proprius voluntarius → libertas salva sub auxilio divino.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AF1","text":"Obiectiones ex defectu dominationis, inclinatione et motu divino → distinctio inter electionem, executionem et passionem → libertas ut iudicium rationale contingentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AF2","text":"Nomen liberi iudicii → quaestio de principio actus → exclusio actus et habitus → liberum arbitrium ut potentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AF3","text":"Iudicium et comparatio → analysis electionis → consilium cognitivum subordinatum acceptationi appetitivae → liberum arbitrium ut potentia appetitiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AF4","text":"Voluntas finis / electio mediorum → analogia intellectus / ratio → diversitas actuum sine divisione potentiae → identitas voluntatis et liberi arbitrii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME1","text":"Libertas transfertur ab oppositione causatum-autonomum ad differentiam inter motum coactivum, motum instinctivum et motum rationaliter voluntarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME2","text":"Distinctio electionis ab executione separat dominium internum actus a potestate effectus exterioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME3","text":"Distinctio finis et mediorum reclassificat voluntatem et electionem ut modos unius appetitus, non ut facultates parallelas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME4","text":"Passiones, habitus et dispositiones corporales reclassificantur ut inclinationes rationaliter gubernabiles, non ut causae per se libertatem abolentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME5","text":"Peccatum reclassificatur ut imminutio libertatis moralis vel beatificae, non ut interitus potentiae naturalis electionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ALT1","text":"Surface — Homo dicitur liberi arbitrii; liberum arbitrium est potentia appetitiva eadem cum voluntate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ALT2","text":"Structural — Electio producitur ex ordine consilii rationalis, acceptationis appetitivae, inclinationum inferiorum et distinctionis finis a mediis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones deterministicas solvuntur non negando causas influentes, sed ordinando eas sub iudicio rationis et causalitate prima non-rivali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Agens liberum est causa secunda quae se movet, sed non prima causa sui; eius libertas est proprietas modi causalitatis, non exemptio ab ordine causali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de iudicio rationali contingentium, de structura electionis et de causalitate prima sufficiunt ad conclusionem quod homo libere eligit sub motu divino.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de indifferentia potentiae et de ratione habitus sufficiunt ad excludendum habitum atque ad ponendum liberum arbitrium ut potentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT3","text":"Unitas voluntatis et liberi arbitrii pendet a principio quod actus subordinati eiusdem ordinis obiectivi non dividunt potentiam; hoc principium est commissura principalis quarti articuli.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT4","text":"Compositio libertatis cum auxilio divino firmatur per distinctionem primae et secundae causae, sed modus quo auxilium determinans simul electionem in homine relinquit ulteriorius non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT5","text":"Systema tensionem continet inter indifferentiam liberi arbitrii ad bene et male et ordinationem naturalem voluntatis ad beatitudinem; resolutio fit per distinctionem inter finem necessarie appetitum et media eligibilia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT6","text":"Distinctio electionis ab executione servat dominium electionis, sed restringit libertatem effectivam ad principium internum potius quam ad successum actionis externae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus: a negationibus libertatis per distinctiones causales et psychologicas ad constitutionem metaphysicam potentiae electivae unius cum voluntate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T164943221604Z_8dda6839","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 83","source_sha256":"07e6e5865d5675b24df362acba19e2444f11bb1e07a3db707509c58ec423f3fc","sha256":"71ee52409352a105f455a789a0fd8bbd87b4875e503061ffa68869412ae81514","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:49:43.223636+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS1","text":"The question asks whether divine motion, natural inclination, passions, and impediments to execution deprive man of free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS2","text":"The principle of freedom is not placed in the absence of every cause, but in rational judgment concerning particular contingents, which stands toward opposites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS3","text":"Choice is resolved into the counsel of reason and the acceptance of appetite; by reason of its object, the useful good for an end, it is principally an appetitive act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS4","text":"Free choice, although by its name it signifies an act of judging, is an abiding elective power, not a habit nor a transitory act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS5","text":"The will of the end and the choice of those things that are for the end are diverse acts of the same intellectual appetite; therefore free choice is not a power other than the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AS6","text":"Divine causality and human freedom are reconciled through the order of causes: God moves the will as a voluntary cause, whose proper motion remains voluntary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A1","text":"An agent without judgment does not act freely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A2","text":"Judgment arising from a determined natural instinct alone is not free judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","text":"Reason concerning contingent particulars that are capable of being done stands toward opposites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A4","text":"Man acts freely because he forms practical judgment through the comparison of reason, not through a particular natural instinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A5","text":"Free choice is the principle by which man judges freely, and therefore it is an abiding principle of act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A6","text":"The power of free choice stands indifferently toward choosing well and badly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A7","text":"A habit inclines its subject to be disposed well or badly concerning acts or passions; such an inclination does not belong to the nature of free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A8","text":"Choice requires cognitive counsel concerning what is to be preferred and an appetitive acceptance of that which counsel has judged.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A9","text":"The proper object of choice is the useful good, that is, that which is desired for the sake of an end; but good is the object of appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A10","text":"The will regards the end simply, whereas choice regards the means for the sake of the end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A11","text":"The diversity of subordinated acts and objects does not require a diversity of powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A12","text":"Freedom does not require that it be the first cause of its own motion, but that it be moved to act through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A13","text":"The first cause, by moving a voluntary cause, preserves and brings about the voluntary character of its motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A14","text":"Natural, bodily, habitual, and passional inclinations do not destroy freedom if they are subject to the judgment of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:A15","text":"Choice is in man, although the execution of choice can be impeded and free choice needs divine help.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX1","text":"Free choice is not the power of doing whatever man wills, because sensitive appetite can resist reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX2","text":"Motion from another does not remove freedom unless the proper motion of the voluntary cause is destroyed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX3","text":"Mastery of choice is not infallible mastery of external execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX4","text":"The natural appetite for the ultimate end is not subject to free choice and is not an object of choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX5","text":"Free choice is neither a natural habit nor an acquired habit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX6","text":"Free choice is not a purely cognitive power, although the counsel and judgment of reason precede choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX7","text":"Free choice is not a power distinct from the will, but the elective force of the same power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:NX8","text":"Sin does not destroy natural freedom from coercion, but freedom from guilt and misery.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D1","text":"Man possesses free choice by virtue of being rational, because rationality opens the possibility of opposites through practical judgment of contingents.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A1","CH_GGVC_P_75:A2","CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","CH_GGVC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D2","text":"Counsels, exhortations, precepts, prohibitions, rewards, and punishments presuppose an agent whose choices are not naturally determined to one thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","CH_GGVC_P_75:A4","CH_GGVC_P_75:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D3","text":"Free choice is a power, because the name of the act of free judgment is transferred to the stable principle of that act, which can be neither a habit nor a pure act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A5","CH_GGVC_P_75:A6","CH_GGVC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D4","text":"Choice is principally appetitive, because deliberation of reason alone does not constitute choice unless appetite accepts what reason judges to be preferred.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A8","CH_GGVC_P_75:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D5","text":"Will and free choice are one power under a twofold act: the will tends toward the end, the elective force toward means compared to the end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A10","CH_GGVC_P_75:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D6","text":"Divine motion does not empty freedom, because the first cause does not concur with the will as a rival cause, but as a cause that produces the voluntary mode of operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A12","CH_GGVC_P_75:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:D7","text":"Dispositions of the body, habits, and passions incline choice without necessitating it, insofar as the lower appetite and supervening qualities can be subjected to reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","CH_GGVC_P_75:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SD1","text":"Freedom is defined as rationally mediated causality within the order of causes, not as the diminution of every causal dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A3","CH_GGVC_P_75:A4","CH_GGVC_P_75:A12","CH_GGVC_P_75:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SD2","text":"The structure of choice divides human action into a non-elective order of the end and an elective order of means; freedom is therefore bounded by the naturally desired end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A9","CH_GGVC_P_75:A10","CH_GGVC_P_75:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SD3","text":"Moral responsibility is founded not on immunity from passions, inclinations, or divine help, but on the retention of rational judgment and elective acceptance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A4","CH_GGVC_P_75:A8","CH_GGVC_P_75:A14","CH_GGVC_P_75:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SD4","text":"The unity of will and free choice prevents choice from being treated as a neutral faculty outside the order of good and end; it is itself the intellectual appetite for means for the sake of the end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_75:A9","CH_GGVC_P_75:A10","CH_GGVC_P_75:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX1","text":"For the system to be false requires a model of freedom that confuses freedom with causal aseity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX2","text":"For the system to be false requires a model in which divine causality and created causality necessarily exclude one another mutually.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX3","text":"For the system to be false requires an inference from inclination to necessity, whether the inclination is natural, bodily, habitual, or passional.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX4","text":"For the system to be false requires the view that comparative cognition itself completes choice without an accepting appetitive act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:DNX5","text":"For the system to be false requires the view that the distinction between end and means multiplies powers, rather than acts of one power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SNX1","text":"The argument concerns the impossibility of absolutely indeterminate freedom: free choice is always exercised under the aspect of good, end, counsel, and first causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SNX2","text":"The argument excludes the possibility of choosing the ultimate end as a means among alternatives, because happiness is naturally desired and the object of choice is those things that are for the end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:SNX3","text":"The argument does not admit freedom as complete power over outcomes, because choice remains man's while external execution can be impeded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS1","text":"Contingent particular capable of being done → comparison of reason → judgment not naturally determined → possibility toward opposites → free judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS2","text":"Counsel concerning what is to be preferred → appetitive acceptance of the useful good → choice → act of free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS3","text":"Act named “free judgment” → inquiry into the principle of the act → exclusion of habit → positing of elective power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS4","text":"End simply desired → means chosen for the sake of the end → distinction of acts → analogy of understanding/reasoning → unity of will and free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:FGS5","text":"Motion of the first cause → operation according to the property of the voluntary cause → proper voluntary motion → freedom preserved under divine help.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AF1","text":"Objections from lack of mastery, inclination, and divine motion → distinction among choice, execution, and passion → freedom as rational judgment of contingents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AF2","text":"Name of free judgment → question concerning the principle of the act → exclusion of act and habit → free choice as power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AF3","text":"Judgment and comparison → analysis of choice → cognitive counsel subordinated to appetitive acceptance → free choice as appetitive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:AF4","text":"Will of the end / choice of means → analogy of intellect / reason → diversity of acts without division of power → identity of will and free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME1","text":"Freedom is transferred from the opposition between caused and autonomous to the difference among coercive motion, instinctive motion, and rationally voluntary motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME2","text":"The distinction of choice from execution separates internal mastery of the act from power over the external effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME3","text":"The distinction between end and means reclassifies will and choice as modes of one appetite, not as parallel faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME4","text":"Passions, habits, and bodily dispositions are reclassified as rationally governable inclinations, not as causes that abolish freedom through themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ME5","text":"Sin is reclassified as a diminution of moral or beatific freedom, not as the destruction of the natural power of choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ALT1","text":"Surface — Man is said to possess free choice; free choice is an appetitive power identical with the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ALT2","text":"Structural — Choice is produced from the order of rational counsel, appetitive acceptance, lower inclinations, and the distinction of end from means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Deterministic objections are resolved not by denying influencing causes, but by ordering them under the judgment of reason and non-rival first causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — A free agent is a secondary cause that moves itself, but is not the first cause of itself; its freedom is a property of its mode of causality, not an exemption from causal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning rational judgment of contingents, the structure of choice, and first causality suffice for the conclusion that man chooses freely under divine motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning the indifference of power and the nature of habit suffice to exclude habit and to posit free choice as a power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT3","text":"The unity of will and free choice depends on the principle that subordinated acts of the same objective order do not divide the power; this principle is the principal joint of the fourth article.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT4","text":"The reconciliation of freedom with divine help is established through the distinction between first and second cause, but the manner in which determining help simultaneously leaves choice in man is not further explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT5","text":"The system contains a tension between the indifference of free choice toward good and evil and the natural ordering of the will toward happiness; the resolution is made through the distinction between the necessarily desired end and eligible means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT6","text":"The distinction of choice from execution preserves mastery of choice, but restricts effective freedom to the internal principle rather than the success of external action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_75:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: from negations of freedom through causal and psychological distinctions to the metaphysical constitution of an elective power one with the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_75:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_75@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_75:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 84","title":"First Part · Question 83","context":"Chapter 84","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 83"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 83","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 84","order":85,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_76"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_76@R001","sha256":"a5e41491ed20ba2b1bc4db0b977f0438acbc031a59ab7d8d3d4d4bed42ddea50","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS1","text":"Quaestio est quo principio, medio et ordine anima corpori coniuncta res corporales cognoscat et quatenus intellectio a potentiis sensitivis dependeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS2","text":"Anima corpora intellectu cognoscit immaterialiter, universaliter et necessario, species autem intelligibiles neque ex essentia sua neque innatas neque immediate a substantiis separatis accipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est reconstructiva et polemico-diagnostica: opiniones naturalistarum, Platonis et Avicennae ex communi confusione modi cogniti cum modo cognoscentis resolvuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS4","text":"Motus incipit a necessitate salvandi scientiam certam de corporibus mobilibus et transit ad distinctionem inter rem materialiter existentem et formam immaterialiter receptam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS5","text":"Exclusis cognitione per essentiam, speciebus innatis et influxu formarum separatarum, cognitio restituitur ut concursus sensus, phantasmatum, intellectus agentis et intellectus possibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS6","text":"Argumentum culminat in dependentia statui praesenti propria: species habitualiter retentae non sufficiunt sine conversione ad phantasmata, et ligamentum sensus perfectum iudicium impedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","text":"Forma recepta est in recipiente secundum modum recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A2","text":"Perfectio cognitionis gradum immaterialitatis receptionis formae cognitae sequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A3","text":"Scientia naturalis in intellectu est et corpus mobile pro obiecto habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A4","text":"Actus intellectus, formaliter ut intellectualis, organo corporeo non exercetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","text":"Obiectum proprium intellectus humani corpori coniuncti est quidditas sive natura in materia corporali existens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","text":"Natura materialis in individuo existit, quod sensu et imaginatione apprehenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","text":"Intellectus humanus initio est in potentia ad species intelligibiles, non naturaliter actu informatus omnibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","text":"Intellectus agens, ut virtus animae, phantasmata per abstractionem intelligibilia in actu facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","text":"Res sensibiles operationem sensitivam in coniuncto causant, ex qua phantasmata oriuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A10","text":"Phantasmata sunt materia causae intellectualis cognitionis, non tota eius causa perfecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A11","text":"Ad scientiam rerum materialium concurrunt lumen intellectuale et species intelligibiles a rebus acceptae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","text":"Rationes aeternae cognitionem humanam ordinariam fundant per lumen increatum participatum in intellectu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","text":"Species in intellectu possibili conservatae habitualiter manent, sed actualis earum usus conversionem ad phantasmata requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A14","text":"Sola essentia divina omnes effectus immaterialiter continet sicut causa universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A15","text":"Omnis motus aliquid immobile supponit, et rerum mutabilium habitudines immobiles esse possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A16","text":"Perfectum iudicium de re requirit cognitionem eorum quae ad rem pertinent, praesertim termini ad quem iudicium ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0154","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A17","text":"Omnia quae homo in statu praesentis vitae intelligit per comparationem ad res sensibiles naturales cognoscuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A18","text":"Ligamentum sensus accessum ad sensibilia et ordinatum usum phantasmatum gradatim impedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX1","text":"Intellectus non restringitur ad spiritualia, neque corpora ab eius obiectis excluduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX2","text":"Corpora non cognoscuntur per corpora aut per similitudines materiales et corporeas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX3","text":"Immaterialitas et immobilitas actus intellectualis non requirunt res intellectas extra intellectum immaterialiter et immobiliter subsistere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX4","text":"Scientiae et definitiones rerum naturalium non referuntur ad ideas separatas loco corporum sensibilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX5","text":"Anima humana corporalia non cognoscit per essentiam suam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX6","text":"Anima non est actu composita ex formis omnium rerum, sed ad sensibilia et intelligibilia est in potentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX7","text":"Species omnium intelligibilium animae non sunt naturaliter inditae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX8","text":"Species intelligibiles non effluunt in animam a formis separatis vel ab intellectu separato sicut a causa proxima.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX9","text":"Rationes aeternae in statu praesentis vitae non sunt communiter obiecta visa, neque sola earum participatio scientiam rerum materialium sufficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX10","text":"Sensus non est causa totalis et perfecta cognitionis intellectualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX11","text":"Conservatio speciei intelligibilis non sufficit ad intellectionem actualem sine phantasmatum usu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX12","text":"Superioritas intellectus super sensum non importat independentiam operationalem absolutam in statu praesentis vitae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","text":"Corpora materialia et mobilia ab intellectu cognoscuntur modo immateriali, universali et necessario.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A2","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D2","text":"Scientia stabilis rerum mobilium possibilis est, quia mutatio ipsa subiecta vel habitudines immobiles praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A3","CH_GGVC_P_76:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D3","text":"Anima est quodammodo omnia non per continentiam actualem essentiae, sed per potentiam sensitivam et intellectivam ad formas rerum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","text":"Unio animae intellectivae ad corpus munus epistemicum habet, quia corpus instrumenta praebet quibus materia cognitionis intellectualis acquiritur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10","CH_GGVC_P_76:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D5","text":"Defectus alicuius sensus scientiam propriorum sensibilium illius sensus excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D6","text":"Cognitio intellectualis ex sensu oritur quoad materiam, sed ab intellectu agente perficitur quoad actualem intelligibilitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D7","text":"Rationes aeternae causant cognitionem ut principium luminis, dum res sensibiles determinant quid materialiter cognoscatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A11","CH_GGVC_P_76:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D8","text":"Habitus scientiae est condicio necessaria sed non sufficiens intellectionis actualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D9","text":"Res incorporeae cognoscuntur in statu praesenti indirecte, per causam, excessum, remotionem vel comparationem ad corporalia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0145","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D10","text":"Ligamentum sensus perfectum iudicium intellectus impedit, quamvis processus intellectuales partiales secundum gradum solutionis sensuum remanere possint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A16","CH_GGVC_P_76:A17","CH_GGVC_P_76:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD1","text":"Systema cognitionem humanam inter reductionem ad solam immutationem sensibilem et reductionem ad solam illuminationem separatam constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D6","CH_GGVC_P_76:D7","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD2","text":"Corporalitas non est merum impedimentum intellectus humani, sed mediatio constitutiva operationis eius praesentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","CH_GGVC_P_76:D5","CH_GGVC_P_76:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD3","text":"Universalitas cognitionis non requirit universalia separatim subsistentia, quia ex modo immateriali receptionis oritur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD4","text":"Causalitas cognitionis ordinatur per strata: Deus est fons remotus luminis, intellectus agens actualizator proximus, sensibilia materia determinans, intellectus possibilis recipiens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10","CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5","text":"Intellectus sensum transcendit in modo cognoscendi, sed ab eo dependet in acquisitione, usu et iudicio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","CH_GGVC_P_76:D6","CH_GGVC_P_76:D8","CH_GGVC_P_76:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD6","text":"Modus cognitionis humanae est statui ontologico subiecti proportionatus; intellectus corpori coniunctus aliter operatur quam intellectus separatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD7","text":"Cognitio humana rerum incorporearum manet analogica et apophatica, quia obiectum proprium intellectus praesentis est natura materialis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0145","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX1","text":"Similitudo cognoscentis et cogniti identitatem modi essendi non requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A2","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX2","text":"Certitudo universalis non requirit obiectum universaliter et immobiliter extra intellectum subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","CH_GGVC_P_76:D2","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX3","text":"Superioritas facultatis non requirit separationem eius ab omni mediatione facultatis inferioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX4","text":"Essentia finita cognoscentis non potest ex sola sua determinatione omnes rerum formas actualiter repraesentare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A14","CH_GGVC_P_76:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX5","text":"Cognitio neque pura passio a sensibilibus neque pura productio sui ipsius ab anima est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX6","text":"Causa remota cognitionis causam proximam et mediationes naturales non substituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_76:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX7","text":"Illuminatio per rationes aeternas visionem immediatam rationum aeternarum non significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX8","text":"Possessio habitualis formae intelligibilis non est identica operationi actuali intelligendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX1","text":"Nulla cognitio humana ordinaria in statu praesenti est simul immediata, totaliter a sensu libera et perfecte determinata quoad res materiales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_76:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX2","text":"Subiectum humanum sui ipsius cognitioni sufficiens et a mundo sensibili clausum ex systemate excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX3","text":"Intellectus disembodiedus non potest normam immediatam operationis intellectus humani corpori coniuncti praebere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX4","text":"Causalitas cognitionis neque ab inferioribus sensibilibus neque a superioribus separatis totaliter clauditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX5","text":"Accessus positivus et quidditativus ad Deum vel substantias immateriales in statu praesenti indisponibilis manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D9","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0145","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX6","text":"Perfecta certitudo exercita non est a statu sensuum et imaginationis absolute immunis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D10","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS1","text":"Prima clausura est: scientia naturalis in intellectu est, corpus mobile eius obiectum est, motus autem immobile supponit; igitur scientia certa corporis mobilis non est contradictoria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A3","CH_GGVC_P_76:A15","CH_GGVC_P_76:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS2","text":"Error communis materialistarum et Platonicorum aequat modum formae in cognito cum modo eius in cognoscente; distinctio modi recipientis hanc bifurcationem dissolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A2","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS3","text":"Series exclusionis procedit a cognitione per essentiam ad species innatas, deinde ad influxum formarum separatarum et denique ad solam participationem idearum aeternarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS4","text":"Series positiva est: res sensibilis → immutatio coniuncti sensitivi → phantasma → abstractio intellectus agentis → species intelligibilis → actualizatio intellectus possibilis → cognitio universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS5","text":"Determinatio obiectiva a rebus sensibilibus et vis cognoscitiva a lumine intellectuali participato concurrunt sine substitutione alterius causae ab altera.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A11","CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS6","text":"Usus cognitionis sequitur circuitum: species habitualis → conversio ad phantasma → intellectio actualis → relatio ad particulare sensibile → iudicium; ligamentum sensus circuitum imperfectum reddit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:A16","CH_GGVC_P_76:A17","CH_GGVC_P_76:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS7","text":"Extensio ultra corporalia procedit non per mutationem obiecti proprii, sed per ascensum causalem, excessivum, comparativum et remotivum a corporalibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D9","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0145","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AF1","text":"Motus dialecticus est: mobilitas corporum → periculum incertitudinis → necessitas scientiae naturalis → distinctio rei materialis a receptione immateriali → cognitio intellectualis corporum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AF2","text":"Motus criticus est: identitas modi cogniti et cognoscentis → materialismus vel Platonismus → experimentum dependentiae sensitivae → exclusio essentiae, innatismi et influxus separati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AF3","text":"Motus reconstructivus est: potentia intellectiva → sensus → phantasma → abstractio activa → species intelligibilis → intellectio universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AF4","text":"Motus operationalis est: species acquisita → conversio ad phantasma → usus actualis → relatio ad sensibile → iudicium perfectum vel, sensu ligato, iudicium defectivum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter obiectum corporeum et cognitionem intellectualem solvitur per distinctionem obiecti cogniti a modo cognitionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME2","text":"Universalitas transfertur a regno formarum separatarum ad modum immaterialem receptionis in intellectu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME3","text":"Sensus reclassificatur ex causa tota cognitionis in mediationem materialem necessariam sed insufficientem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A10","CH_GGVC_P_76:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME4","text":"Intellectus agens reclassificatur ut causa proxima abstractionis intra animam, dum principia separata ad causalitatem remotam restringuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME5","text":"Corpus reclassificatur ex impedimento extrinseco in condicionem constitutivam cognitionis humanae praesentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME6","text":"Cognitio in rationibus aeternis dividitur in visionem earum ut obiecti et participationem earum ut principii luminis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME7","text":"Dependentia intellectus a sensu distinguitur a reductione intellectus ad sensum, ita ut transcendentia modalis et dependentia operationalis simul cogitari possint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei complectitur quaestiones de obiecto corporali, medio specierum, origine earum, rationibus aeternis, sensu, phantasmatibus et impedimento iudicii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis cognitionem ordinat ut cooperationem coniuncti sensitivi, imaginationis, intellectus agentis et intellectus possibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus falsas totalizationes naturalistarum, Platonis et Avicennae per distinctiones causae remotae et proximae, obiecti et modi, habitus et actus dissolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis praesupponit potentiam et actum, materiam individuantem, formas intentionaliter receptas, essentiam creatam finitam et modum cognitionis statui praesentis unionis animae et corporis proportionatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A14","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendas conclusiones octo articulorum, quia determinant obiectum, medium, originem, actualizationem et limites cognitionis corporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT2","text":"Modus internus quo intellectus agens abstractionem efficit manet minus determinatus quam necessitas eius causalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT3","text":"Structura interne cohaeret si distinctio inter independentiam formalem intellectus ab organo et dependentiam operationalem ab imaginatione servatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A4","CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT4","text":"Argumentatio firmissima est ubi defectus sensus, laesio imaginationis et gradus ligamenti sensitivi ad dependentiam actualis cognitionis adhibentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D5","CH_GGVC_P_76:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis est inter obiectum universale intellectus et necessitatem cognoscendi naturam ut in particulari existentem; distinctio abstractionis et conversionis hanc tensionem continet, non omnino explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT6","text":"Concursus luminis aeterni et specierum a rebus acceptarum Platonismum vitat, sed exacta coordinatio causalitatis formalis et determinationis obiectivae compressa manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A11","CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT7","text":"Argumentum ex utilitate corporis ad naturalitatem unionis animae et corporis quadam teleologia naturae nititur, quae hic potius adhibetur quam demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT8","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: scientia corporum vindicatur, falsa media excluduntur, mediatio sensitivo-intellectualis construitur, deinde limites usus et iudicii definiuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_76:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_76:AF3","CH_GGVC_P_76:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165013594592Z_f25281fe","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 84","source_sha256":"a5e41491ed20ba2b1bc4db0b977f0438acbc031a59ab7d8d3d4d4bed42ddea50","sha256":"8f216448bafdc2fcf59abd892c530808da6f3a2e357453f86292a65cb159b16a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:50:13.595568+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS1","text":"The question is by what principle, means, and order the soul united to the body knows corporeal things, and to what extent intellection depends upon the sensitive powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS2","text":"The soul knows bodies by intellect immaterially, universally, and necessarily; but it receives intelligible species neither from its own essence, nor as innate, nor immediately from separate substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS3","text":"The argumentation is reconstructive and polemical-diagnostic: the opinions of the naturalists, Plato, and Avicenna are resolved from a common confusion of the mode of the known with the mode of the knower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS4","text":"The movement begins from the necessity of safeguarding certain science of mobile bodies and proceeds to the distinction between a thing existing materially and a form received immaterially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS5","text":"Once cognition through essence, innate species, and the influx of separate forms have been excluded, cognition is restored as the concurrence of sense, phantasms, the agent intellect, and the possible intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AS6","text":"The argument culminates in the dependence proper to the present state: species retained habitually do not suffice without conversion to phantasms, and the binding of sense impedes perfect judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","text":"A form is received in the recipient according to the mode of the recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A2","text":"The perfection of cognition follows the degree of immateriality in the reception of the known form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A3","text":"Natural science is in the intellect and has a mobile body as its object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A4","text":"The act of intellect, formally as intellectual, is not exercised through a bodily organ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","text":"The proper object of the human intellect united to a body is the quiddity or nature existing in corporeal matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","text":"Material nature exists in the individual, which is apprehended by sense and imagination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","text":"The human intellect is initially in potency toward intelligible species, not naturally informed actually by all of them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","text":"The agent intellect, as a power of the soul, makes phantasms actually intelligible through abstraction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","text":"Sensible things cause sensitive operation in the composite, from which phantasms arise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A10","text":"Phantasms are the material of the cause of intellectual cognition, not its whole and perfect cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A11","text":"Intellectual light and intelligible species received from things concur for science of material things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","text":"Eternal reasons ground ordinary human cognition through uncreated light participated in the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","text":"Species preserved in the possible intellect remain habitually, but their actual use requires conversion to phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A14","text":"The divine essence alone contains all effects immaterially as a universal cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A15","text":"Every motion presupposes something immobile, and the relations of mutable things can be immobile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A16","text":"Perfect judgment concerning a thing requires cognition of those things that pertain to the thing, especially the term to which judgment is directed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0154","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A17","text":"All things that a human being understands in the state of the present life are known through comparison with natural sensible things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:A18","text":"The binding of sense progressively impedes access to sensibles and the ordered use of phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0159","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX1","text":"The intellect is not restricted to spiritual things, nor are bodies excluded from its objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX2","text":"Bodies are not known through bodies or through material and corporeal likenesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX3","text":"The immateriality and immobility of the intellectual act do not require the things understood to subsist outside the intellect immaterially and immovably.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX4","text":"The sciences and definitions of natural things are not referred to separate ideas in place of sensible bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX5","text":"The human soul does not know corporeal things through its own essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX6","text":"The soul is not actually composed of the forms of all things, but is in potency toward sensibles and intelligibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX7","text":"The species of all intelligibles are not naturally implanted in the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX8","text":"Intelligible species do not flow into the soul from separate forms or from the separate intellect as from a proximate cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX9","text":"Eternal reasons in the state of the present life are not commonly objects seen, nor does participation in them alone suffice for science of material things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX10","text":"Sense is not the total and perfect cause of intellectual cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX11","text":"The preservation of an intelligible species does not suffice for actual intellection without the use of phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:NX12","text":"The superiority of intellect over sense does not entail absolute operational independence in the state of the present life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","text":"Material and mobile bodies are known by the intellect in an immaterial, universal, and necessary mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A2","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D2","text":"Stable science of mobile things is possible because change itself presupposes an immobile subject or immobile relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A3","CH_GGVC_P_76:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D3","text":"The soul is in a certain way all things, not through actual containment in its essence, but through sensitive and intellective potency toward the forms of things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","text":"The union of the intellective soul with the body has an epistemic function, because the body provides the instruments by which the material of intellectual cognition is acquired.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10","CH_GGVC_P_76:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D5","text":"The defect of any sense excludes science of the proper sensibles of that sense.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D6","text":"Intellectual cognition arises from sense with respect to its matter, but is perfected by the agent intellect with respect to actual intelligibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D7","text":"Eternal reasons cause cognition as a principle of light, while sensible things determine what is known materially.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A11","CH_GGVC_P_76:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D8","text":"The habit of science is a necessary but insufficient condition of actual intellection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D9","text":"Incorporeal things are known in the present state indirectly, through cause, excess, removal, or comparison with corporeal things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0145","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:D10","text":"The binding of sense impedes perfect judgment of the intellect, although partial intellectual processes may remain according to the degree of release of the senses.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A16","CH_GGVC_P_76:A17","CH_GGVC_P_76:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD1","text":"The system establishes human cognition between reduction to sensible alteration alone and reduction to separate illumination alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D6","CH_GGVC_P_76:D7","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD2","text":"Corporeality is not a mere impediment to the human intellect, but a constitutive mediation of its present operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","CH_GGVC_P_76:D5","CH_GGVC_P_76:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD3","text":"The universality of cognition does not require universals subsisting separately, because it arises from the immaterial mode of reception.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD4","text":"The causality of cognition is ordered in levels: God is the remote source of light, the agent intellect the proximate actualizer, sensibles the determining matter, and the possible intellect the recipient.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10","CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5","text":"The intellect transcends sense in its mode of knowing, but depends on it in acquisition, use, and judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","CH_GGVC_P_76:D6","CH_GGVC_P_76:D8","CH_GGVC_P_76:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD6","text":"The mode of human cognition is proportioned to the ontological state of the subject; the intellect united to a body operates differently from the separate intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SD7","text":"Human cognition of incorporeal things remains analogical and apophatic, because the proper object of the present intellect is material nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0145","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX1","text":"The likeness of knower and known does not require identity of mode of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A2","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX2","text":"Universal certitude does not require an object subsisting universally and immovably outside the intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","CH_GGVC_P_76:D2","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX3","text":"The superiority of a faculty does not require its separation from every mediation of an inferior faculty.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX4","text":"The finite essence of a knower cannot, from its determination alone, actually represent all forms of things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A14","CH_GGVC_P_76:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX5","text":"Cognition is neither pure passion from sensibles nor pure self-production by the soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX6","text":"The remote cause of cognition does not replace the proximate cause and natural mediations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_76:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX7","text":"Illumination through eternal reasons does not signify immediate vision of eternal reasons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX8","text":"Habitual possession of an intelligible form is not identical with the actual operation of understanding.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX1","text":"No ordinary human cognition in the present state is at once immediate, wholly free from sense, and perfectly determined with respect to material things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_76:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX2","text":"A human subject sufficient for knowledge of itself and closed off from the sensible world is excluded by the system.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX3","text":"A disembodied intellect cannot provide the immediate norm of the operation of the human intellect united to a body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX4","text":"The causality of cognition is not totally enclosed either by lower sensibles or by higher separate things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX5","text":"Positive and quidditative access to God or immaterial substances remains unavailable in the present state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D9","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0145","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:SNX6","text":"Perfect certitude in exercise is not absolutely immune from the state of the senses and imagination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D10","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS1","text":"The first closure is: natural science is in the intellect, a mobile body is its object, and motion presupposes something immobile; therefore certain science of a mobile body is not contradictory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A3","CH_GGVC_P_76:A15","CH_GGVC_P_76:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS2","text":"The common error of materialists and Platonists equates the mode of the form in the known with its mode in the knower; the distinction of the mode of the recipient dissolves this bifurcation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A2","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS3","text":"The series of exclusions proceeds from cognition through essence to innate species, then to the influx of separate forms, and finally to participation in eternal ideas alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS4","text":"The positive series is: sensible thing → alteration of the sensitive composite → phantasm → abstraction by the agent intellect → intelligible species → actualization of the possible intellect → universal cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A9","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS5","text":"Objective determination from sensible things and cognitive power from participated intellectual light concur without one cause replacing the other.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A11","CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS6","text":"The use of cognition follows a circuit: habitual species → conversion to phantasm → actual intellection → relation to the particular sensible → judgment; the binding of sense renders the circuit imperfect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:A16","CH_GGVC_P_76:A17","CH_GGVC_P_76:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS7","text":"Extension beyond corporeal things proceeds not through a change of the proper object, but through causal, excessive, comparative, and negative ascent from corporeal things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D9","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0145","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AF1","text":"The dialectical movement is: mobility of bodies → danger of uncertainty → necessity of natural science → distinction of material thing from immaterial reception → intellectual cognition of bodies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AF2","text":"The critical movement is: identity of the mode of the known and the knower → materialism or Platonism → test of sensitive dependence → exclusion of essence, innatism, and separate influx.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AF3","text":"The reconstructive movement is: intellective potency → sense → phantasm → active abstraction → intelligible species → universal intellection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:AF4","text":"The operational movement is: acquired species → conversion to phantasm → actual use → relation to sensible thing → perfect judgment or, when sense is bound, defective judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0159","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME1","text":"The opposition between corporeal object and intellectual cognition is resolved through the distinction of the known object from the mode of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D1","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME2","text":"Universality is transferred from the realm of separate forms to the immaterial mode of reception in the intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME3","text":"Sense is reclassified from the whole cause of cognition into a necessary but insufficient material mediation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A10","CH_GGVC_P_76:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME4","text":"The agent intellect is reclassified as the proximate cause of abstraction within the soul, while separate principles are restricted to remote causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME5","text":"The body is reclassified from an extrinsic impediment into a constitutive condition of present human cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME6","text":"Cognition in eternal reasons is divided into vision of them as objects and participation in them as a principle of light.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ME7","text":"The dependence of intellect upon sense is distinguished from the reduction of intellect to sense, so that modal transcendence and operational dependence can be thought together.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ALT1","text":"The surface level includes questions concerning the corporeal object, the medium of species, their origin, eternal reasons, sense, phantasms, and the impediment to judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ALT2","text":"The structural level orders cognition as the cooperation of the sensitive composite, imagination, the agent intellect, and the possible intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_76:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level dissolves the false totalizations of the naturalists, Plato, and Avicenna through distinctions between remote and proximate cause, object and mode, habit and act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_76:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level presupposes potency and act, individuating matter, intentionally received forms, finite created essence, and a mode of cognition proportioned to the present state of the union of soul and body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A14","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the conclusions of the eight articles, because they determine the object, medium, origin, actualization, and limits of corporeal cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A1","CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A7","CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT2","text":"The internal mode by which the agent intellect effects abstraction remains less determined than its causal necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A8","CH_GGVC_P_76:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT3","text":"The structure coheres internally if the distinction is preserved between the formal independence of intellect from an organ and operational dependence upon imagination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A4","CH_GGVC_P_76:A13","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT4","text":"The argumentation is strongest where defects of sense, injury to imagination, and degrees of the binding of sense are employed to establish the dependence of actual cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D5","CH_GGVC_P_76:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint lies between the universal object of intellect and the necessity of knowing nature as existing in the particular; the distinction between abstraction and conversion contains this tension, but does not wholly explain it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A5","CH_GGVC_P_76:A6","CH_GGVC_P_76:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT6","text":"The concurrence of eternal light and species received from things avoids Platonism, but the exact coordination of formal causality and objective determination remains compressed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:A11","CH_GGVC_P_76:A12","CH_GGVC_P_76:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT7","text":"The argument from the usefulness of the body to the naturalness of the union of soul and body rests upon a certain teleology of nature, which is here employed rather than demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:D4","CH_GGVC_P_76:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_76:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: science of bodies is vindicated, false means are excluded, sensitive-intellectual mediation is constructed, and then the limits of use and judgment are defined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_76:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_76:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_76:AF3","CH_GGVC_P_76:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0117","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_76:P0155","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_76@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_76:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 85","title":"First Part · Question 84","context":"Chapter 85","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 84"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 84","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 85","order":86,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_77"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_77@R001","sha256":"f7508953c6d408a58b890bc8c475f3ce7b35d6e9899dd443464a18f1a47bb5c5","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS1","text":"Quaestio ordinatrix est quo modo et ordine intellectus humanus, in statu corpori coniuncto, res materiales cognoscat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS2","text":"Intellectus humanus materialia cognoscit abstrahendo naturam intelligibilem a condicionibus individualibus phantasmatum, non tamen sine conversione ad phantasmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS3","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica et reconstructiva falsas aequationes dissolvit distinguendo abstractionem a separatione, speciem qua intelligitur ab obiecto intellecto, atque apprehensionem simplicem a compositione et discursu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS4","text":"Motus argumentationis procedit a proportione obiecti ad potentiam cognoscitivam ad operationes abstractionis, ordinationis, compositionis, erroris et perfectionis intelligendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS5","text":"Medietas intellectus humani inter sensum corporalem et intellectum separatum fundamentum omnium limitationum atque facultatum examinatarum constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS6","text":"Successio, discursivitas et possibilitas erroris non sunt accidentia externa cognitionis humanae, sed effectus intellectus qui de potentia ad actum per species a phantasmatibus abstractas procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","text":"Obiectum cognoscibile proportionatur virtuti cognoscitivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","text":"Intellectus humanus non est actus organi corporalis, sed est potentia animae quae corporis forma est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","text":"Obiectum proprium intellectus humani in praesenti statu est quidditas rei materialis individualiter existentis, non tamen prout sub condicionibus individualibus existit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","text":"Cognitio intellectiva humana a cognitione sensitiva initium sumit, cuius phantasmata singularia repraesentant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","text":"Intellectus actualiter cognoscit abstrahendo a phantasmatibus et simul convertendo se ad phantasmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A6","text":"Intellectus agens phantasmata illuminat et naturam specificam abstrahibilem efficit; intellectus possibilis specie intelligibili informatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","text":"Abstractio per simplicem considerationem potest praetermittere quod ad rationem obiecti non pertinet sine affirmatione separationis realis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A8","text":"Terminus abstractionis determinatur eo materiae gradu qui rationem obiecti constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","text":"Species intelligibilis est forma qua intellectus rem cognoscit; res repraesentata est primum quod intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A10","text":"Natura intellecta existit in singularibus, sed abstractio et intentio universalitatis existunt in intellectu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","text":"Potentia cognoscitiva prius attingit actum incompletum et confusum quam actum completum et distinctum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","text":"Modus actionis intellectivae sequitur formam quae est principium actionis; ideo multa simul intelliguntur tantum sub una specie et per modum unius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","text":"Intellectus humanus primo quidditatem apprehendit, deinde proprietates et habitudines componit vel dividit, atque ex compositionibus ratiocinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A14","text":"Similitudo rei recipitur secundum modum intellectus; operationi intellectuali aliquid reale respondet, sed non eodem modo quo est in re.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A15","text":"Intellectus circa propriam quidditatem per se non fallitur, sed falli potest componendo, dividendo vel ratiocinando.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A16","text":"Gradus intelligendi variatur secundum perfectionem intellectus et dispositionem imaginationis, cogitationis et memoriae, non secundum mutationem veritatis obiecti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","text":"Indivisum totius et speciei cognoscitur ante distinctionem partium, sed indivisibile omnino cognoscitur post divisibile tamquam privatio eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A18","text":"Ordo acquisitionis cognitionis differt ab ordine perfectionis scientiae: principia possunt ex effectibus posterius inveniri, quamvis scientia completa effectus ad principia resolvat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX1","text":"Abstractio intellectualis non affirmat formam materialem extra materiam secundum rem existere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX2","text":"Intellectus humanus non cognoscit ideas separatas participando, sicut Plato posuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX3","text":"Species rei naturalis non abstrahitur a materia sensibili communi quae rationem eius ingreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX4","text":"Phantasmata propria virtute speciem in intellectum possibilem non imprimunt, neque eadem forma numero ex phantasmate in intellectum transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX5","text":"Species intelligibilis non est primum obiectum cognitionis, sed principium formale quo res cognoscitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX6","text":"Scientiae non sunt tantum de speciebus internis, neque omnis apparentia aut opinio eo ipso vera est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX7","text":"Intentio universalitatis non est substantia separata neque universale sic acceptum principium essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX8","text":"Intellectus non intelligit simul multa per diversas species et per modum multorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX9","text":"Intellectus humanus perfectam rei cognitionem non capit statim in simplici apprehensione quidditatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX10","text":"Elevatio intellectus supra tempus motus corporalis successionem operationum intelligibilium non tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0098","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX11","text":"Falsitas non inest simplici apprehensioni proprii obiecti eodem modo quo compositioni et divisioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0138","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX12","text":"Melior intellectio eiusdem rei non significat rem aliter esse neque diversitatem specificam inter intelligentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0153","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX13","text":"Indivisibile omnino non est primum cognitum propter similitudinem naturalem ad intellectus simplicitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0179","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D1","text":"Cognitio humana neque ad impressionem sensibilem reducitur neque per visionem formarum separatarum perficitur, sed per cooperationem phantasmatum, intellectus agentis et intellectus possibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D2","text":"Abstractio vera est quando modus intelligendi a modo existendi differt sine falsa affirmatione de statu reali rei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D3","text":"Res exterior manet obiectum primarium intellectus, quamvis forma cognoscendi intra intellectum recipiatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D4","text":"Universalitas non addit naturam separatam rebus, sed consequitur modum quo natura singulariter existens sine principiis individualibus apprehenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D5","text":"Scientiae naturales, mathematicae et considerationes maxime communes distinguuntur secundum diversos materiae gradus quos ratio obiecti retinet vel praetermittit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D6","text":"Singulare cognitione sensitiva prius est universali, sed intra cognitionem intellectivam magis commune cognitione confusa prius est minus communi cognitione distincta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D7","text":"Partes simul cognosci possunt confuse sub forma totius, sed distincta cuiusque cognitio successionem specierum requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D8","text":"Comparatio, differentia et compositio multa sub una ratione relationali uniunt, ideoque simultaneitatem secundum unam speciem servant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D9","text":"Successio intelligibilium operationum ex pluralitate specierum et conversione ad phantasmata oritur, etiamsi intellectus organo corporali non utatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D10","text":"Eadem discursivitas quae proprietates rei explicat etiam locum falsitatis aperit, quia utrumque per ordinationem unius apprehensi ad aliud fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D11","text":"Veritas obiectiva non recipit magis et minus, sed profunditas reductionis ad principia et capacitas intelligentis gradus recipiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A15","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0151","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D12","text":"Prioritas indivisibilis est aequivoca: integritas confusa et unitas specifica praecedunt analysim, punctum autem et unitas privativa post divisibile cognoscuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D13","text":"Principia possunt esse posteriora in inventione et tamen priora in resolutione demonstrativa atque perfectione scientiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D14","text":"Magis commune potest esse prius secundum generationem et apprehensionem confusam, dum minus commune est prius secundum perfectionem et intentionem naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD1","text":"Epistemologia quaestionis est hylomorphica: modus cognoscendi humanus ex coniunctione intellectus immaterialis cum anima corporis forma constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD2","text":"Mediatio speciei intelligibilis realismum non interrumpit, quia species non substituit rem sed intellectum ad rem formaliter determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A10","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD3","text":"Abstractio, dependentia a phantasmatibus et successio discursiva sunt effectus unius eiusdemque medietatis ontologicae intellectus humani.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD4","text":"Nulla series prioritatis absolute unica regit cognitionem, quia ordo variatur secundum sensum vel intellectum, confusionem vel distinctionem, generationem vel perfectionem, inventionem vel resolutionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD5","text":"Fallibilitas et scientia discursiva eodem mechanismo synthetico nituntur: ordinatio apprehensorum potest sive veram connexionem exprimere sive falsam imponere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD6","text":"Unitas speciei, non paucitas materialis contentorum, est principium simultaneitatis intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD7","text":"Universalitas epistemica compatitur singularitatem ontologicam, quia communitas est modus apprehensionis naturae quae in singularibus existit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD8","text":"Quo cognitio per formam unitiorem et perfectiorem procedit, eo minus compositione et successione indiget; inde intellectus humanus ab cognitione angelica et divina formaliter distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD9","text":"Intellectus humanus potest operatione non organica esse et tamen gradu perfectionis a dispositione corporis atque potentiarum sensitivarum dependere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX1","text":"Potentia cognoscitiva obiectum cuiuscumque modi indifferenter cognoscere non potest; forma obiecti semper capacitati potentiae commensuratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX2","text":"Corpori coniunctio non est impedimentum mere extrinsecum quod intra praesentem statum cognitionis humanae simpliciter removeri possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX3","text":"Cognitio humana intra proprias repraesentationes claudi non potest, quia talis clausura scientiam rerum et distinctionem veri a falso destrueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX4","text":"Ordo cognoscendi ordini essendi immediate aequari non potest; posterius cognitum potest ontologice prius esse et e converso.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A10","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX5","text":"Simplicitas potentiae intellectivae cognitionem immediatam omnium simplicium non inducit, quia prioritas obiecti ex proportione ad quidditatem materialem determinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX6","text":"Fallibilitas non penetrat ipsum primum contactum intellectus cum intelligibili, sed relationem apprehensorum constitutam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX7","text":"Unitas speciei humanae aequalitatem graduum intellectualium non requirit, quia forma secundum capacitatem materiae et potentiarum inferiorum individuatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX8","text":"Principium explanationis non oportet esse principium primae apprehensionis; scientia incipere potest ab effectibus quos postea ad causas resolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX1","text":"Cognitio humana immediata, tota et simul perfecta in praesenti statu indisponibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX2","text":"Prospectus humanus omnino separatus a corpore, sensu et imaginatione intra hanc machinam cognitionis inadmissibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX3","text":"Oppositio absoluta inter cognitionem internam et rem externam praecluditur, quia species immanens est ipsa determinatio formalis qua res extrinseca attingitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX4","text":"Coincidentia perfecta modi intelligendi cum modo materiali existendi impossibilis est; talis coincidentia intellectum ad singularitatem sensus reduceret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX5","text":"Una notio simpliciter absoluta prioritatis excluditur; omnis prioritas ad ordinem potentiae, temporis, perfectionis, cognitionis vel causalitatis refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX6","text":"Infallibilitas humana ex discursu ipso oriri non potest, sed tantum ex obiecto proprio, primis principiis et recta resolutione ad causas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A15","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS1","text":"Prima constitutio machinae est: proportio obiecti ad potentiam → medietas intellectus humani → quidditas rei materialis ut obiectum proprium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS2","text":"Series causalis cognitionis est: singulare sensibile → phantasma → illuminatio intellectus agentis → abstractio naturae specificae → receptio speciei in intellectu possibili → intellectio rei → reflexio supra speciem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A6","CH_GGVC_P_77:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS3","text":"Series ordinis cognitionis est: actus potentialis → cognitio confusa magis communis → distinctio differentiarum → cognitio minus communis → scientia completa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS4","text":"Regula simultaneitatis est: una species vel una ratio formalis → multa ut unum simul; plures species distinctae → plures actus successive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS5","text":"Series discursiva est: apprehensio quidditatis → apprehensio proprietatum → compositio vel divisio → ratiocinatio → veritas aut falsitas secundum convenientiam ordinationis cum re.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS6","text":"Regula prioritatis est: relatio ad obiectum proprium → distinctio generis indivisibilis → prioritas integritatis vel speciei, aut posterioritas privationis → resolutio scientiae ad principia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF1","text":"Proportio potentiae et obiecti → status medius intellectus humani → necessitas abstractionis a phantasmatibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF2","text":"Distinctio abstractionis a separatione → distinctio speciei ab obiecto → fundatio cognitionis rerum exteriorum et universalitatis intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF3","text":"Processus de potentia ad actum → prioritas cognitionis confusae → unitas formalis actus → successio cognitionum distinctarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF4","text":"Apprehensio imperfecta quidditatis → compositio et divisio → ratiocinatio → determinatio loci falsitatis → gradus perfectionis intelligentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0153","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF5","text":"Obiectum proprium materiale → triplex indivisibile → ordines diversi prioritatis → distinctio inventionis a perfectione scientiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME1","text":"Abstractio denuo describitur ut praetermissio condicionum non essentialium, non ut productio rei separatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME2","text":"Species intelligibilis ab obiecto terminali ad medium formale cognitionis reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME3","text":"Universale dividitur inter naturam in singularibus et intentionem universalitatis in intellectu, unde oppositio inter realismum et abstractionem dissolvitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A10","CH_GGVC_P_77:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME4","text":"Prioritas ex ordine unico in pluralitatem ordinum sensibilium, intellectualium, genetivorum, perfectivorum et demonstrativorum transformatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME5","text":"Simultaneitas non secundum numerum rerum sed secundum unitatem speciei vel rationis formalis mensuratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME6","text":"Falsitas ab intellectu simpliciter ad operationes compositionis, divisionis et consequentiae restringitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME7","text":"Corporalitas ex mero impedimento in condicionem structuralem modi humani intelligendi convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME8","text":"Indivisibile ex genere uno in integritatem potentialiter divisibilem, unitatem specificam et privationem divisionis distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei octo operationes examinat: abstractionem, functionem speciei, ordinem universalium, simultaneitatem, compositionem, errorem, gradus intelligentiae et prioritatem indivisibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis cognitionem per proportionem obiecti et potentiae, cooperationem intellectus agentis et possibilis, conversionem ad phantasmata atque transitum de potentia ad actum explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A6","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus oppositiones falsas dissolvit distinguendo abstractionem a separatione, medium ab obiecto, simultaneitatem ab indistinctione et apprehensionem ab iudicio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis hylomorphismum, individuationem per materiam, receptionem formae secundum capacitatem recipientis et successionem actuum spiritualium praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A8","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad octo articulos ex communi principio proportionis obiecti et potentiae restituendos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT2","text":"Firmissima pars systematis est nexus inter statum medium intellectus, abstractionem a phantasmatibus et distinctionem speciei qua intelligitur a re intellecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT3","text":"Cohaerentia interna maxime per distinctiones ordinum, modorum abstractionis et operationum intellectualium conservatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT4","text":"Modus causalis quo ex illuminatione phantasmatum species in intellectu possibili resultat affirmatur, sed non ulterius mechanice determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter intellectum organo non utentem et variationem virtutis intellectualis secundum dispositionem corporis atque potentiarum sensitivarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT6","text":"Distinctio speciei ut principii primarii et obiecti secundarii per reflexionem cohaeret, sed terminus huius reflexionis non plene explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT7","text":"Solutio simultaneitatis per unam rationem comparationis supponit, potius quam perfecte explicat, quomodo termini distincti in unam speciem relationalem colligantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0104","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT8","text":"Infallibilitas circa quidditatem limitatur errore per accidens in definitionibus compositis; criterium quo compositio intrusa discernitur structuram ulteriorem requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0136","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT9","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: a fundamento ontologico cognitionis ad abstractionem, ordinem operationum, limites erroris et pluralitatem prioritatis procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165050810737Z_65da82a0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 85","source_sha256":"f7508953c6d408a58b890bc8c475f3ce7b35d6e9899dd443464a18f1a47bb5c5","sha256":"d8b5ca44c2f992b56a585c599cb177d58b4e50554135e100f49ae2dddb41ff17","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:50:50.812060+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS1","text":"The governing question is in what manner and order the human intellect, in the state conjoined to the body, knows material things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS2","text":"The human intellect knows material things by abstracting intelligible nature from the individual conditions of phantasms, yet not without turning toward phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS3","text":"The metaphysical and reconstructive argument dissolves false equations by distinguishing abstraction from separation, the species by which a thing is understood from the object understood, and simple apprehension from composition and discursive reasoning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS4","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from the proportion of object to cognitive power to the operations of abstraction, ordering, composition, error, and perfection of understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS5","text":"The intermediate status of the human intellect between bodily sense and separate intellect constitutes the foundation of all the limitations and capacities examined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AS6","text":"Succession, discursiveness, and the possibility of error are not external accidents of human cognition, but effects of an intellect that proceeds from potency to act through species abstracted from phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","text":"The knowable object is proportioned to the cognitive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","text":"The human intellect is not the act of a bodily organ, but is a power of the soul, which is the form of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","text":"The proper object of the human intellect in the present state is the quiddity of a materially existing individual thing, yet not as existing under individual conditions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","text":"Human intellectual cognition takes its beginning from sensitive cognition, whose phantasms represent singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","text":"The intellect actually knows by abstracting from phantasms and at the same time turning itself toward phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A6","text":"The agent intellect illuminates phantasms and renders specific nature abstractible; the possible intellect is informed by the intelligible species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","text":"Abstraction through simple consideration can pass over what does not belong to the account of the object without affirming real separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A8","text":"The limit of abstraction is determined by that grade of matter which constitutes the account of the object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","text":"The intelligible species is the form by which the intellect knows the thing; the represented thing is that which is first understood.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A10","text":"The understood nature exists in singulars, but abstraction and the intention of universality exist in the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","text":"The cognitive power attains an incomplete and confused act before a complete and distinct act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","text":"The mode of intellectual action follows the form that is the principle of action; therefore many things are understood simultaneously only under one species and in the manner of one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","text":"The human intellect first apprehends the quiddity, then composes or divides properties and relations, and reasons from compositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A14","text":"The likeness of the thing is received according to the mode of the intellect; something real corresponds to intellectual operation, but not in the same manner as it is in the thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A15","text":"The intellect is not per se deceived concerning its proper quiddity, but it can be deceived in composing, dividing, or reasoning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A16","text":"The degree of understanding varies according to the perfection of the intellect and the disposition of imagination, cogitation, and memory, not according to a change in the truth of the object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","text":"The undividedness of the whole and of the species is known before the distinction of parts, but what is altogether indivisible is known after the divisible as its privation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:A18","text":"The order of acquiring cognition differs from the order of the perfection of science: principles can be discovered later from effects, although complete science resolves effects into principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX1","text":"Intellectual abstraction does not affirm that material form exists outside matter in reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX2","text":"The human intellect does not know separated ideas by participation, as Plato held.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX3","text":"The species of a natural thing is not abstracted from common sensible matter, which enters into its account.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX4","text":"Phantasms do not by their own power impress a species upon the possible intellect, nor is the same form numerically transferred from phantasm to intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX5","text":"The intelligible species is not the first object of cognition, but the formal principle by which the thing is known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX6","text":"The sciences are not only about internal species, nor is every appearance or opinion thereby true.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX7","text":"The intention of universality is not a separate substance, nor is the universal so understood a principle of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX8","text":"The intellect does not understand many things simultaneously through diverse species and in the manner of many.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX9","text":"The human intellect does not immediately grasp perfect cognition of a thing in simple apprehension of the quiddity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX10","text":"The elevation of the intellect above the time of bodily motion does not remove the succession of intelligible operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0098","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX11","text":"Falsity does not inhere in simple apprehension of the proper object in the same manner as in composition and division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0138","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX12","text":"A better understanding of the same thing does not mean that the thing is otherwise, nor a specific diversity among those understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0153","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:NX13","text":"What is altogether indivisible is not the first known on account of a natural likeness to the simplicity of the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0179","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D1","text":"Human cognition is neither reduced to sensible impression nor perfected through the vision of separated forms, but through the cooperation of phantasms, the agent intellect, and the possible intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D2","text":"Abstraction is true when the mode of understanding differs from the mode of existing without a false affirmation concerning the real state of the thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D3","text":"The external thing remains the primary object of the intellect, although the form of knowing is received within the intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D4","text":"Universality does not add a separate nature to things, but follows the manner in which a nature existing singularly is apprehended without individual principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D5","text":"Natural sciences, mathematics, and most common considerations are distinguished according to the diverse grades of matter which the account of the object retains or passes over.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D6","text":"The singular is prior to the universal in sensitive cognition, but within intellectual cognition the more common is prior in confused cognition to the less common in distinct cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D7","text":"Parts can be known simultaneously in a confused manner under the form of the whole, but distinct cognition of each requires succession of species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D8","text":"Comparison, difference, and composition unite many things under one relational account, and thus preserve simultaneity according to one species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D9","text":"The succession of intelligible operations arises from the plurality of species and the turning toward phantasms, even though the intellect does not use a bodily organ.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D10","text":"The same discursiveness that explicates the properties of a thing also opens the place of falsity, because both occur through the ordering of one apprehended thing to another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D11","text":"Objective truth does not admit of more and less, but the depth of reduction to principles and the capacity of the one understanding admit of degrees.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A15","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0151","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D12","text":"The priority of the indivisible is equivocal: confused integrity and specific unity precede analysis, but the point and privative unity are known after the divisible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D13","text":"Principles can be posterior in discovery and yet prior in demonstrative resolution and the perfection of science.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:D14","text":"The more common can be prior according to generation and confused apprehension, while the less common is prior according to perfection and the intention of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD1","text":"The epistemology of the question is hylomorphic: the human mode of knowing is constituted from the conjunction of an immaterial intellect with a soul that is the form of the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD2","text":"The mediation of the intelligible species does not interrupt realism, because the species does not substitute for the thing but formally determines the intellect toward the thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A10","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD3","text":"Abstraction, dependence on phantasms, and discursive succession are effects of one and the same ontological intermediacy of the human intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD4","text":"No single absolute series of priority governs cognition, because order varies according to sense or intellect, confusion or distinction, generation or perfection, discovery or resolution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD5","text":"Fallibility and discursive science rest on the same synthetic mechanism: the ordering of apprehended things can either express a true connection or impose a false one.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD6","text":"The unity of the species, not the scarcity of material contents, is the principle of intellectual simultaneity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD7","text":"Epistemic universality is compatible with ontological singularity, because commonness is a mode of apprehending the nature that exists in singulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD8","text":"The more cognition proceeds through a more unified and perfect form, the less it requires composition and succession; hence the human intellect is formally distinguished from angelic and divine cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SD9","text":"The human intellect can be non-organic in operation and yet depend, in degree of perfection, on the disposition of the body and of the sensitive powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX1","text":"A cognitive power cannot know an object of any mode indifferently; the form of the object is always commensurate with the capacity of the power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX2","text":"Conjunction with the body is not a merely extrinsic impediment that can simply be removed within the present state of human cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX3","text":"Human cognition cannot be enclosed within its own representations, because such enclosure would destroy science of things and the distinction of true from false.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX4","text":"The order of knowing cannot be immediately equated with the order of being; what is known later can be ontologically prior, and conversely.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A10","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX5","text":"The simplicity of the intellectual power does not entail immediate cognition of all simples, because the priority of the object is determined by proportion to material quiddity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0179","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX6","text":"Fallibility does not penetrate the very first contact of the intellect with the intelligible, but the constituted relation of apprehended things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX7","text":"The unity of the human species does not require equality of intellectual degrees, because form is individuated according to the capacity of matter and of the lower powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:DNX8","text":"The principle of explanation need not be the principle of first apprehension; science can begin from effects which it afterward resolves into causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX1","text":"Immediate, whole, and simultaneously perfect human cognition is unavailable in the present state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX2","text":"A human perspective wholly separated from body, sense, and imagination is inadmissible within this mechanism of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX3","text":"An absolute opposition between internal cognition and the external thing is precluded, because the immanent species is the very formal determination by which the extrinsic thing is attained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX4","text":"A perfect coincidence of the mode of understanding with the material mode of existing is impossible; such coincidence would reduce the intellect to the singularity of sense.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX5","text":"One simply absolute notion of priority is excluded; every priority is referred to an order of power, time, perfection, cognition, or causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:SNX6","text":"Human infallibility cannot arise from discourse itself, but only from the proper object, first principles, and correct resolution into causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A15","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS1","text":"The first constitution of the system is: proportion of object to power → intermediate status of the human intellect → quiddity of the material thing as proper object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS2","text":"The causal series of cognition is: sensible singular → phantasm → illumination by the agent intellect → abstraction of specific nature → reception of the species in the possible intellect → understanding of the thing → reflection upon the species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A6","CH_GGVC_P_77:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS3","text":"The series of the order of cognition is: potential act → more common confused cognition → distinction of differences → less common cognition → complete science.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS4","text":"The rule of simultaneity is: one species or one formal account → many as one simultaneously; several distinct species → several acts successively.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0096","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS5","text":"The discursive series is: apprehension of quiddity → apprehension of properties → composition or division → reasoning → truth or falsity according to the conformity of ordering with the thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A14","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:FGS6","text":"The rule of priority is: relation to the proper object → distinction of the genus of the indivisible → priority of integrity or species, or posteriority of privation → resolution of science into principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF1","text":"Proportion of power and object → intermediate status of the human intellect → necessity of abstraction from phantasms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF2","text":"Distinction of abstraction from separation → distinction of species from object → grounding of cognition of external things and intellectual universality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF3","text":"Process from potency to act → priority of confused cognition → formal unity of act → succession of distinct cognitions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF4","text":"Imperfect apprehension of quiddity → composition and division → reasoning → determination of the locus of falsity → degrees of perfection of the one understanding.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A13","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0153","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:AF5","text":"Material proper object → threefold indivisible → diverse orders of priority → distinction of discovery from the perfection of science.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A3","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME1","text":"Abstraction is described anew as passing over non-essential conditions, not as the production of a separate thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME2","text":"The intelligible species is reclassified from terminal object to formal medium of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME3","text":"The universal is divided between nature in singulars and the intention of universality in the intellect, whereby the opposition between realism and abstraction is dissolved.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A10","CH_GGVC_P_77:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME4","text":"Priority is transformed from a single order into a plurality of sensible, intellectual, generative, perfective, and demonstrative orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A11","CH_GGVC_P_77:A17","CH_GGVC_P_77:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME5","text":"Simultaneity is measured not according to the number of things but according to the unity of species or formal account.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME6","text":"Falsity is restricted from the intellect simply speaking to the operations of composition, division, and inference.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME7","text":"Corporeality is converted from a mere impediment into a structural condition of the human mode of understanding.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A4","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ME8","text":"The indivisible is distributed from one genus into potentially divisible integrity, specific unity, and the privation of division.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0171","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0172","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ALT1","text":"The surface level examines eight operations: abstraction, the function of the species, the order of universals, simultaneity, composition, error, degrees of intelligence, and the priority of the indivisible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ALT2","text":"The structural level explains cognition through the proportion of object and power, the cooperation of the agent and possible intellects, turning toward phantasms, and the transition from potency to act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A1","CH_GGVC_P_77:A5","CH_GGVC_P_77:A6","CH_GGVC_P_77:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level dissolves false oppositions by distinguishing abstraction from separation, medium from object, simultaneity from indistinction, and apprehension from judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A7","CH_GGVC_P_77:A9","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level presupposes hylomorphism, individuation through matter, reception of form according to the capacity of the recipient, and succession of spiritual acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_77:A2","CH_GGVC_P_77:A8","CH_GGVC_P_77:A12","CH_GGVC_P_77:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore eight articles from the common principle of the proportion of object and power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT2","text":"The firmest part of the system is the nexus between the intermediate status of the intellect, abstraction from phantasms, and the distinction of the species by which a thing is understood from the thing understood.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence is preserved chiefly through distinctions of orders, modes of abstraction, and intellectual operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT4","text":"The causal mode by which a species results in the possible intellect from the illumination of phantasms is affirmed, but is not further mechanically determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT5","text":"A fragile juncture remains between an intellect not using an organ and the variation of intellectual power according to the disposition of the body and the sensitive powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0154","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT6","text":"The distinction of the species as primary principle and the object as secondary through reflection coheres, but the terminus of this reflection is not fully explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT7","text":"The solution of simultaneity through one account of comparison presupposes, rather than perfectly explains, how distinct terms are gathered into one relational species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0104","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT8","text":"Infallibility concerning quiddity is limited by error per accidens in composite definitions; the criterion by which an imposed composition is discerned requires a further structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0135","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0136","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_77:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: it proceeds from the ontological foundation of cognition to abstraction, the order of operations, the limits of error, and the plurality of priority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_77:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_77@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_77:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 86","title":"First Part · Question 85","context":"Chapter 86","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 85"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 85","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 86","order":87,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_78"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_78@R001","sha256":"24ba9074f82e680588ecf82817983a1426f6447409315e78ab9a120249926a4a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quid intellectus humanus de rebus materialibus cognoscere possit, distinguendo singulare, infinitum, contingens et futurum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS2","text":"Objectum proprium intellectus humani directe est universale abstractum a materia individuali; propterea singulare materiale non cognoscitur primo et directe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS3","text":"Cognitio singularis, contingentis et futuri admittitur tantum secundum modos mediatos: per conversionem ad phantasmata, per rationes universales, vel per cognitionem causarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS4","text":"Infinitum materiale non datur intellectui ut totum actu comprehensibile, sed solum ut processus potentiae in quo semper plura accipi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS5","text":"Contingentia et futura non simpliciter excluduntur ab intellectu, sed resolvuntur in distinctionem inter rem singularem temporalem et rationem necessariam vel ordinem causalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS6","text":"Argumentatio progreditur a limitibus abstractionis ad doctrinam graduatam cognitionis: universale directe, singulare reflexe, infinitum successive, contingens formaliter, futurum causaliter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A1","text":"Materia individualis est principium singularitatis in rebus materialibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A2","text":"Intellectus humanus intelligit abstrahendo speciem intelligibilem a materia individuali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","text":"Quod abstrahitur a materia individuali habet rationem universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A4","text":"Intellectus humanus, etiam post abstractionem, intelligit actu convertendo se ad phantasmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A5","text":"Singulare immateriale non repugnat intelligibilitati, quia materialitas, non singularitas simpliciter, cognitionem intellectualem impedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A6","text":"Potentia cognoscitiva proportionatur suo obiecto proprio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A7","text":"Infinitum materiale est in rebus solum potentia, secundum successionem unius post alterum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A8","text":"Intellectus humanus non intelligit simul actu nisi quod per unam speciem intelligibilem cognoscit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A9","text":"Cognitio habitualis distincta causatur ex consideratione actuali praecedenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A10","text":"Contingentia ex parte materiae possibilitatem essendi et non essendi habent; necessitas vero rationem formae consequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A11","text":"Intellectus directe cognoscit rationes universales et necessarias; sensus directe cognoscit singularia contingentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A12","text":"Futura in seipsis soli Deo sunt cognoscibilia, quia aeternus intuitus divinus totum temporis cursum simul complectitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A13","text":"Futura in causis cognosci possunt certitudinaliter si causae ad effectum necessario ordinantur, vel coniecturaliter si ad effectum ut in pluribus inclinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A14","text":"Cognitio humana connaturalis a sensibus procedit, non ex participatione immediata idearum universalium causarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX1","text":"Intellectus humanus non est cognoscitivus directus et primus singularium materialium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX2","text":"Cognitio intellectualis non est separatio absoluta ab omni singulari, quia actus intelligendi humanus phantasmata requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX3","text":"Universale non est singulare materialiter apprehensum subtiliori gradu, sed forma a materia individuali abstracta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX4","text":"Infinitum materiale non est unum totum perfectum nec una specie intelligibili comprehensibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX5","text":"Infinitum non cognoscitur ab intellectu humano neque actu simul neque habitu distincto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX6","text":"Contingens non est omnino extra scientiam, sed non cognoscitur intellectualiter sub ipsa ratione suae contingentiae singularis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX7","text":"Futurum non cognoscitur a homine ut praesens in seipso.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX8","text":"Alienatio a sensibus non constituit per se modum naturalem cognitionis futurorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D1","text":"Intellectus universale directe cognoscit, sed singulare cuius phantasma adest indirecte et reflexe attingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A1","CH_GGVC_P_78:A2","CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","CH_GGVC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D2","text":"Propositio de Socrate componitur non ex cognitione intellectuali directa Socratis ut singularis, sed ex universali intellecto et phantasmate singulari reflexe adhibito.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A2","CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","CH_GGVC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D3","text":"Electio practica non procedit immediate ex universali, sed indiget apprehensione particulari partis sensitivae ut conclusio singularis efficiatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A4","CH_GGVC_P_78:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D4","text":"Infinitum cognoscitur a potentia intellectus ut indefinita capacitas ulterioris apprehensionis, non ut multitudo actu completa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A6","CH_GGVC_P_78:A7","CH_GGVC_P_78:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D5","text":"Habitualis scientia infinitorum distincta impossibilis est, quia posceret considerationem actualem et enumerationem omnium partium infinitarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A7","CH_GGVC_P_78:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D6","text":"Scientiae contingentium sunt necessariae secundum rationes formales universales, et contingentes secundum res singulares quas considerant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A10","CH_GGVC_P_78:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D7","text":"Praecognitio humana futurorum est scientia ubi ordo causae ad effectum necessarius est, coniectura ubi causae effectum solum frequenter inducunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D8","text":"Praevisiones quae in somno vel alienatione sensuum contingunt non probant autonomam praescientiam animae, sed ad impressiones causarum spiritualium vel corporalium referuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SD1","text":"Cognitio humana non dividitur in ignorantiam et possessionem simplicem, sed in ordines accessus distinctos: directum universalis, reflexum singularis, successivum infiniti et causale futuri.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","CH_GGVC_P_78:A4","CH_GGVC_P_78:A7","CH_GGVC_P_78:A11","CH_GGVC_P_78:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SD2","text":"Abstrahere a materia individuali non destruit dependentiam cognitionis humanae a sensibilibus, sed constituit duplicem ordinem in quo universale est forma cognitionis et phantasma condicio exercitii eius.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A2","CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","CH_GGVC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SD3","text":"Necessitas scientifica non transfertur simpliciter ad res contingentes, sed residet in rationibus formalibus quibus intellectus res contingentes intelligibiles reddit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A10","CH_GGVC_P_78:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SD4","text":"Praescientia absoluta reservatur intuitui aeterno divino, dum cognitio humana futurorum intra ordinem causalitatis temporalis continetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A12","CH_GGVC_P_78:A13","CH_GGVC_P_78:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet intellectum humanum esse intuitum immediatum rerum singularium, quia eius obiectum proprium per abstractionem constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet potentiam infinitam intellectus significare possessionem actualem infinitorum cognitorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet contingentiam rerum impedire omnem scientiam, quia formae et rationes universales contingentium necessitatem intelligibilem continent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet abstractionem a tempore conferre intellectui humano praesentiam immediatam futurorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet recessum a sensibus naturaliter animam ad cognitionem futurorum reducere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit modelum cognitionis in quo intelligere significat rem totam, singularem et temporaliter praesentem sine mediatione possidere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit aequivocationem inter infinitatem formalem, quae divinam intelligibilitatem non tollit, et infinitatem materialem, quae privationem termini importat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit assimilationem intellectus humani ad scientiam divinam, quia humanus intellectus per sensus, phantasmata et causas operatur, Deus vero per aeternam simultatem temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS1","text":"Materia individualis → principium singularitatis → abstractio speciei → universale ut obiectum directum intellectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS2","text":"Species abstracta + conversio ad phantasma → reflexio intellectus → cognitio indirecta singularis → iudicium practicum vel propositio singularis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS3","text":"Infinitum materiale potentia → apprehensio per successionem → impossibilitas totalitatis simul → cognitio infinita solum potentialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS4","text":"Contingentia ex materia + necessitas ex forma → sensus singularis contingentis / intellectus ratio universalis necessaria → scientia contingentium secundum rationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS5","text":"Futurum ut singulare temporale → incognoscibile in se humano intellectui → relatio ad causam → scientia necessarii aut coniectura frequentialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS6","text":"Alienatio sensuum + impressio causae superioris → phantasmata ordinata vel commota → signa futurorum sine praescientia naturali absoluta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AF1","text":"Singularitas materialis → abstractio intellectualis → universalitas directa → reflexio ad phantasmata → singularitas indirecte cognita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AF2","text":"Infinitum ut potentia successiva → absentia speciei totalis → impossibilitas comprehensionis actualis et habitualis → potentia ad plura intelligenda.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AF3","text":"Contingentia materialis → separatio formae et materiae → ratio universalis necessaria → scientia de contingentibus sub ratione necessitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AF4","text":"Futurum singulare → incognoscibilitas in se → inspectio causarum → certitudo necessarii vel coniectura effectus frequentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME1","text":"Oppositio simplicis generis inter cognitionem universalis et cognitionem singularis dissolvitur in distinctionem inter cognitionem directam et cognitionem reflexam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME2","text":"Infinitum reclassificatur non ut obiectum immensae multitudinis iam possessae, sed ut regula inexhaustae successionis cognoscitivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME3","text":"Scientia contingentium reclassificatur ut cognitio rationum universalium necessariarum in rebus quae secundum materiam contingentes sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME4","text":"Futurum reclassificatur secundum tres status: futurum in se, futurum in causis necessariis et futurum in causis ut in pluribus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME5","text":"Praevisio extraordinaria reclassificatur a facultate naturali animae ad significationem causaliter impressam in phantasia vel intellectu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ALT1","text":"Surface — Intellectus humanus quaeritur utrum singularia, infinita, contingentia et futura cognoscat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ALT2","text":"Structural — Abstractio a materia, conversio ad phantasmata, successio actuum et proportio potentiae ad obiectum ordinant limites cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Quaestio non solvitur per responsum nudum affirmativum vel negativum, sed per multiplicationem modorum cognitionis et distinctionem obiecti, medii et causalitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Materia fundat singularitatem et contingentiam, forma necessitatem intelligibilem, et aeternitas divina praesentiam totius temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de materia individuali, abstractione, phantasmatibus et universalitate sufficiunt ad conclusionem de cognitione indirecta singularium restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de potentia, specie unica et successione sufficiunt ad negationem cognitionis actualis vel habitualis infinitorum restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT3","text":"Distinctio materiae et formae sustinet concordiam inter contingentiam rerum et necessitatem rationum scientificarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT4","text":"Distinctio futuri in se et futuri in causis sustinet limitem cognitionis humanae futurorum sine exclusione omnis praecognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter universalitatem intellectus et dependentiam eius actualem a phantasmatibus singularibus, quia reflexio ad singulare mediari dicitur potius quam ulterius resolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT6","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in explicatione praenuntiationum extraordinariarum, quia causae spirituales et corporales admittuntur, sed criterium internum quo earum impressiones discernantur non determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, quia una regula abstractionis progressive limites singularis, infiniti, contingentis et futuri distribuit secundum diversos modos cognoscibilitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165112735925Z_6f159728","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 86","source_sha256":"24ba9074f82e680588ecf82817983a1426f6447409315e78ab9a120249926a4a","sha256":"045c45364d074b9361229d26de1efa2c963c15d0598fc2047bea2c5aaf7fc7e8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:51:12.736885+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS1","text":"The question determines what the human intellect can know about material things, distinguishing the singular, the infinite, the contingent, and the future.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS2","text":"The proper object of the human intellect directly is the universal abstracted from individual matter; therefore the material singular is not known primarily and directly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS3","text":"Knowledge of the singular, the contingent, and the future is admitted only according to mediated modes: through turning to phantasms, through universal notions, or through knowledge of causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS4","text":"The material infinite is not given to the intellect as a whole actually comprehensible, but only as a process of potency in which more can always be apprehended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS5","text":"Contingency and future things are not simply excluded from the intellect, but are resolved into a distinction between the temporal singular thing and a necessary notion or causal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AS6","text":"The argument proceeds from the limits of abstraction to a graduated doctrine of knowledge: the universal directly, the singular reflexively, the infinite successively, the contingent formally, the future causally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A1","text":"Individual matter is the principle of singularity in material things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A2","text":"The human intellect understands by abstracting the intelligible species from individual matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","text":"What is abstracted from individual matter has the character of the universal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A4","text":"The human intellect, even after abstraction, understands actually by turning itself to phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A5","text":"The immaterial singular is not incompatible with intelligibility, because materiality, not singularity simply, impedes intellectual knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A6","text":"A cognitive power is proportioned to its proper object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A7","text":"The material infinite exists in things only potentially, according to the succession of one after another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A8","text":"The human intellect does not understand simultaneously in act except what it knows through one intelligible species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A9","text":"Distinct habitual knowledge is caused by preceding actual consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A10","text":"Contingent things, on the part of matter, have the possibility of being and not being; necessity, however, follows the nature of form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A11","text":"The intellect directly knows universal and necessary notions; sense directly knows contingent singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A12","text":"Future things in themselves are knowable to God alone, because the eternal divine intuition simultaneously embraces the whole course of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A13","text":"Future things can be known in their causes with certainty if the causes are necessarily ordered to the effect, or conjecturally if they are inclined toward the effect in most cases.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:A14","text":"Connatural human knowledge proceeds from the senses, not from immediate participation in the ideas of universal causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX1","text":"The human intellect is not the direct and primary knower of material singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX2","text":"Intellectual knowledge is not an absolute separation from every singular, because the human act of understanding requires phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX3","text":"The universal is not the singular materially apprehended at a subtler level, but a form abstracted from individual matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX4","text":"The material infinite is neither one perfect whole nor comprehensible by one intelligible species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX5","text":"The infinite is not known by the human intellect either actually and simultaneously or by distinct habitual knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX6","text":"The contingent is not wholly outside science, but it is not known intellectually under the very nature of its singular contingency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX7","text":"The future is not known by man as present in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:NX8","text":"Withdrawal from the senses does not of itself constitute the natural mode of knowing future things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D1","text":"The intellect directly knows the universal, but indirectly and reflexively attains the singular whose phantasm is present.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A1","CH_GGVC_P_78:A2","CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","CH_GGVC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D2","text":"A proposition about Socrates is composed not from direct intellectual knowledge of Socrates as singular, but from the understood universal and a singular phantasm reflexively employed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A2","CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","CH_GGVC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D3","text":"Practical choice does not proceed immediately from the universal, but requires a particular apprehension of the sensitive part for a singular conclusion to be effected.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A4","CH_GGVC_P_78:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D4","text":"The infinite is known by the power of the intellect as an indefinite capacity for further apprehension, not as a multitude actually completed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A6","CH_GGVC_P_78:A7","CH_GGVC_P_78:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D5","text":"Distinct habitual knowledge of infinite things is impossible, because it would require actual consideration and enumeration of all infinite parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A7","CH_GGVC_P_78:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D6","text":"The sciences of contingent things are necessary according to universal formal notions, and contingent according to the singular things they consider.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A10","CH_GGVC_P_78:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D7","text":"Human foreknowledge of future things is science where the order of cause to effect is necessary, and conjecture where causes induce the effect only frequently.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:D8","text":"Predictions occurring in sleep or withdrawal of the senses do not prove autonomous foreknowledge of the soul, but are referred to impressions of spiritual or bodily causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SD1","text":"Human knowledge is divided not into ignorance and simple possession, but into distinct orders of access: the direct universal, the reflexive singular, the successive infinite, and the causal future.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","CH_GGVC_P_78:A4","CH_GGVC_P_78:A7","CH_GGVC_P_78:A11","CH_GGVC_P_78:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SD2","text":"Abstraction from individual matter does not destroy the dependence of human knowledge upon sensibles, but establishes a twofold order in which the universal is the form of knowledge and the phantasm the condition of its exercise.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A2","CH_GGVC_P_78:A3","CH_GGVC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SD3","text":"Scientific necessity is not simply transferred to contingent things, but resides in the formal notions by which the intellect renders contingent things intelligible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A10","CH_GGVC_P_78:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SD4","text":"Absolute foreknowledge is reserved to eternal divine intuition, while human knowledge of future things is contained within the order of temporal causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_78:A12","CH_GGVC_P_78:A13","CH_GGVC_P_78:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX1","text":"It must be false that the human intellect is the immediate intuition of singular things, because its proper object is constituted through abstraction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the infinite power of the intellect signifies actual possession of infinitely many things known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the contingency of things impedes all science, because the forms and universal notions of contingent things contain intelligible necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX4","text":"It must be false that abstraction from time confers upon the human intellect the immediate presence of future things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:DNX5","text":"It must be false that withdrawal from the senses naturally leads the soul to knowledge of future things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SNX1","text":"The system excludes a model of knowledge in which understanding means possessing a whole thing, singular and temporally present, without mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SNX2","text":"The system excludes the equivocation between formal infinity, which does not remove divine intelligibility, and material infinity, which entails privation of a limit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:SNX3","text":"The system excludes assimilation of the human intellect to divine knowledge, because the human intellect operates through senses, phantasms, and causes, whereas God operates through the eternal simultaneity of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS1","text":"Individual matter → principle of singularity → abstraction of species → universal as the direct object of the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS2","text":"Abstracted species + turning to the phantasm → reflection of the intellect → indirect knowledge of the singular → practical judgment or singular proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS3","text":"Material infinite in potency → apprehension through succession → impossibility of totality simultaneously → infinite knowledge only potential.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS4","text":"Contingency from matter + necessity from form → sense of the contingent singular / intellect's necessary universal notion → science of contingent things according to notion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS5","text":"Future as temporal singular → unknowable in itself to the human intellect → relation to cause → science of the necessary or frequentist conjecture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:FGS6","text":"Withdrawal of the senses + impression of a higher cause → ordered or stirred phantasms → signs of future things without absolute natural foreknowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AF1","text":"Material singularity → intellectual abstraction → direct universality → reflection upon phantasms → singularity indirectly known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AF2","text":"Infinite as successive potency → absence of a total species → impossibility of actual and habitual comprehension → potency for understanding more.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AF3","text":"Material contingency → separation of form and matter → necessary universal notion → science concerning contingent things under the aspect of necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:AF4","text":"Future singular → unknowability in itself → examination of causes → certainty of the necessary or conjecture of the frequent effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME1","text":"The simple generic opposition between knowledge of the universal and knowledge of the singular is dissolved into the distinction between direct knowledge and reflexive knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME2","text":"The infinite is reclassified not as an object of an immense multitude already possessed, but as the rule of inexhaustible cognitive succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME3","text":"The science of contingent things is reclassified as knowledge of necessary universal notions in things that are contingent according to matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME4","text":"The future is reclassified according to three states: the future in itself, the future in necessary causes, and the future in causes as in most cases.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ME5","text":"Extraordinary prediction is reclassified from a natural faculty of the soul to a causally impressed signification in the phantasy or intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ALT1","text":"Surface — It is asked whether the human intellect knows singulars, infinites, contingents, and future things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ALT2","text":"Structural — Abstraction from matter, turning to phantasms, succession of acts, and the proportion of power to object order the limits of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The question is not resolved by a bare affirmative or negative answer, but by multiplying the modes of knowledge and distinguishing object, medium, and causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Matter grounds singularity and contingency, form intelligible necessity, and divine eternity the presence of all time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning individual matter, abstraction, phantasms, and universality suffice to reconstruct the conclusion concerning indirect knowledge of singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning potency, the single species, and succession suffice to reconstruct the negation of actual or habitual knowledge of infinite things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT3","text":"The distinction between matter and form sustains the concord between the contingency of things and the necessity of scientific notions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT4","text":"The distinction between the future in itself and the future in causes sustains the limit of human knowledge of future things without excluding all foreknowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains between the universality of the intellect and its actual dependence on singular phantasms, because reflection upon the singular is said to be mediated rather than further resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT6","text":"A fragile joint remains in the explanation of extraordinary predictions, because spiritual and bodily causes are admitted, but the internal criterion by which their impressions are distinguished is not determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_78:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because one rule of abstraction progressively distributes the limits of the singular, the infinite, the contingent, and the future according to diverse modes of knowability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_78:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_78@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_78:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 87","title":"First Part · Question 86","context":"Chapter 87","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 86"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 86","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 87","order":88,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_79"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_79@R001","sha256":"beb33de5984f2812b71ef8e7d1e9f941bcc481b1173c3469ef1891d87727da06","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quo ordine anima intellectiva seipsam, habitus suos, actum intelligendi et actum voluntatis cognoscat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS2","text":"Cognoscibilitas proportionaliter sequitur actualitatem rei, ita ut quod est tantum in potentia non sit per essentiam obiectum cognitionis actualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS3","text":"Intellectus humanus, quia in genere intelligibilium est potentia et naturaliter ad materialia convertitur, se cognoscit per actus suos ab obiectis materialibus informatos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS4","text":"Ordo reflexivus cognitionis humanae procedit ab obiecto materiali ad actum intelligendi, ab actu ad intellectum, et ab actibus propriis ad habitus ac potentias.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS5","text":"Actus voluntatis intelligibilis est quia voluntas et intellectus in una anima radicantur, et bonum voluntatis ac verum intellectus mutuo includuntur secundum diversas rationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS6","text":"Motus argumentationis est: actualitas cognoscibilis → distinctio graduum intellectus → mediatio per actum → cognitio reflexiva animae, habituum et voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A1","text":"Omne cognoscibile cognoscitur secundum quod est actu, non secundum quod est solum in potentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A2","text":"Modus cognoscibilitatis essentiae sequitur gradum quo essentia est actus in ordine intelligibilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A3","text":"Essentia divina est actus purus et ideo per seipsam perfecte intelligibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A4","text":"Essentia angelica est actus intelligibilis non purus; angelus igitur se per essentiam cognoscit, sed alia per similitudines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A5","text":"Intellectus humanus est potentia respectu intelligibilium et non est per essentiam suam actu intelligibilis sibi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A6","text":"Intellectus humanus in statu praesentis vitae intelligibilis fit per species a sensibilibus abstractas lumine intellectus agentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","text":"Actus intelligendi est perfectio immanens intellectus et est prius cognoscibilis quam ipsa potentia intellectiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A8","text":"Habitus medius est inter potentiam puram et actum perfectum; ideo non est per seipsum plene cognoscibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A9","text":"Habitus cognoscitur quia praesens actum proprium causat, et natura habitus ex consideratione actus investigatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A10","text":"Praesentia animae sufficit ad perceptionem existentiae suae per actum, sed non sufficit ad cognitionem quidditativam naturae suae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A11","text":"Obiectum primum intellectus humani est natura rei materialis; actus intelligendi et intellectus cognoscuntur reflexive et secundario.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A12","text":"Actus voluntatis est inclinatio intelligibilis consequens formam intellectam et in intellectu cognoscibilis ut principiatum in suo principio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A13","text":"Intellectus et voluntas sunt potentiae distinctae, sed in una substantia animae radicatae et mutuo principium quodammodo habentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A14","text":"Bonum et verum ratione differunt, sed se invicem comprehendunt; propter hanc inclusionem actus voluntatis sub cognitionem intellectus cadit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX1","text":"Cognitio sui humana non est intuitio immediata essentiae animae per essentiam suam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX2","text":"Incorporeitas animae non sufficit ut intellectus humanus sit idem cum suo intelligibili modo quo substantia separata est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX3","text":"Praesentia interior animae non est idem ac manifestatio quidditativa naturae animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX4","text":"Habitus praesens in anima non est obiectum intellectus per hoc solum quod in anima subiective existit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX5","text":"Habitus non cognoscitur immediate sicut res exterior per speciem obiecti neque sicut obiectum per se notum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX6","text":"Cognitio actus intelligendi non exigit infinitum processum actu completum, quamvis intellectus in potentia ad infinitum reflecti possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX7","text":"Analogiam inter sensum et intellectum impedit conditio materialis organi sensus, quae intellectui non convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX8","text":"Distinctio potentiarum voluntatis et intellectus non constituit separationem subiecti quae actum voluntatis intellectui absentem reddat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D1","text":"Intellectus humanus se cognoscit ex hoc quod se intelligere percipit, non quia essentia sua primum obiectum cognitionis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A5","CH_GGVC_P_79:A6","CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","CH_GGVC_P_79:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D2","text":"Cognitio particularis sui, qua aliquis percipit se animam intellectivam habere, distinguitur a cognitione universali naturae mentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","CH_GGVC_P_79:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D3","text":"Cognitio existentiae mentis est immediatior quam cognitio differentiae specificae mentis ab aliis rebus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D4","text":"Cognitio habitus bifariam fit: perceptive per productionem actus proprii, inquisitive per analysim rationis actus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A8","CH_GGVC_P_79:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D5","text":"Fides vel alius habitus non cognoscitur per motus corporis exteriores, sed per perceptionem actus interioris quem habitus producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D6","text":"Ordo cognoscendi in intellectu humano est obiectum → actus → potentia, non potentia → actus → obiectum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","CH_GGVC_P_79:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D7","text":"Actus voluntatis cognoscitur tum existientialiter, dum aliquis percipit se velle, tum quidditative, dum ratio actus et principii eius investigatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A12","CH_GGVC_P_79:A13","CH_GGVC_P_79:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SD1","text":"Interioritas psychica non constituit immediatam obiectivitatem: quod maxime intrinsecum est cognoscitur humaniter secundum operationem qua in actum emergit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A1","CH_GGVC_P_79:A5","CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","CH_GGVC_P_79:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SD2","text":"Reflexio humana est structuraliter mediata ab exterioritate materiali, quia obiectum materiale non est simplex occasio sed initium actualizationis intellectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A5","CH_GGVC_P_79:A6","CH_GGVC_P_79:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SD3","text":"Scientia animae dividitur in perceptionem praesentiae operantis et definitionem naturae, quarum prima est quasi connaturalis, secunda laboriosa et errori exposita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A9","CH_GGVC_P_79:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SD4","text":"Distinctio intellectus et voluntatis servatur sine dualismo subiectorum, quia communicatio cognitionis fundatur in unitate animae et conversione veri ac boni.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A13","CH_GGVC_P_79:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omne incorporeum sit ex hoc ipso sibi plene praesens ut obiectum intellectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod identitas subiecti cognoscentis cum re in anima existente sufficiat ad cognitionem illius rei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod reflexio sit actus primarius aequalis cognitioni obiecti exterioris in intellectu humano.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod distinctio functionalis potentiarum animae inferat mutuam eorum cognitionis incommunicabilitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet quod cognitio quidditativa sui ex sola conscientia actuali deduci possit sine inquisitione et iudicio normato veritate divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SNX1","text":"Excluditur subiectum humanum absolute sui transparens, cui esse, essentia, actus et scientia sui uno eodemque ordine coinciderent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SNX2","text":"Excluditur cognitio interioritatis prorsus libera a conversione intellectus ad naturas materiales in statu praesentis vitae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SNX3","text":"Excluditur reductio animae ad obiectum staticum, quia anima, habitus et voluntas cognoscuntur proprie ut principia et perfectiones in actu operantes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:FGS1","text":"Actualitas cognoscibilis → gradus actus in ordine intelligibilium → distinctio Dei, angeli et intellectus humani → determinatio modi proprii cognitionis sui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:FGS2","text":"Obiectum materiale intelligitur → intellectus per speciem fit actu intelligens → actus intelligendi cognoscitur → intellectus ut principium actus cognoscitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:FGS3","text":"Principium imperfecte actuosum → actus proprius productus → praesentia principii percepta → natura principii per inquisitionem discernitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:FGS4","text":"Forma intellecta → inclinatio voluntatis → actus voluntatis in eadem anima radicatus → perceptio volendi et cognitio rationis voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AF1","text":"Apparens cognitio animae per essentiam → principium actualitatis → imminutio status intelligibilis intellectus humani → cognitio sui per actum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AF2","text":"Praesentia habituum → distinctio praesentiae subiectivae ab obiecto cognito → actus habitus → perceptio et inquisitio habitus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AF3","text":"Obiectum primum materiale → actus intelligendi secundarius → intellectus reflexive cognitus → infinitas reflexionis tantum potentialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AF4","text":"Distinctio voluntatis ab intellectu → unitas substantialis animae et conversio boni veri → actus voluntatis intelligibiliter praesens → cognitio velle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter cognitionem externorum et cognitionem interiorum dissolvitur: utrumque cognoscitur secundum modum actualitatis, non secundum solam localem praesentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME2","text":"Distinctio inter praesentiam existentialem et cognitionem quidditativam fit necessaria ad intelligendam scientiam animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME3","text":"Habitus reclassificatur non ut obiectum intellectus primarium, sed ut dispositio qua intellectus operatur et quae ex actu manifestatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME4","text":"Reflexio reclassificatur non ut fundamentum cognitionis humanae, sed ut operatio secunda ab obiecto materiali et actu intellectus derivata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME5","text":"Voluntas reclassificatur non ut regio intellectui extranea, sed ut inclinatio intelligibilis intra unitatem animae et ordinem veri-boni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ALT1","text":"Surface — Anima intellectiva cognoscit seipsam, habitus, actum intelligendi et actum voluntatis non uno modo, sed secundum ordines diversos mediationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ALT2","text":"Structural — Actualitas, species intelligibilis, obiectum primum, actus et potentia constituunt ordinem per quem cognitio reflexiva generatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Quaestio de conscientia sui transfertur ab immediata possessione interioris ad investigationem principiorum ex actibus manifestatorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Status praesentis vitae intellectum humanum ad materialia ordinat; ideo modus cognitionis sui humanus a modo divino et angelico ontologice distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT1","text":"Axiomata actualitatis, gradus intelligibilitatis et ordinis obiectum–actus–potentia sufficiunt ad restituendam negationem cognitionis animae humanae per essentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter praesentiam et quidditatem est necessaria ne cognitio particularis sui cum scientia naturae animae confundatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT3","text":"Axiomata de habitu ut medio inter potentiam et actum explanant cur habitus per actus cognoscatur, sed non plene determinant quomodo actus singuli ad habitus distinctos referantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT4","text":"Systema firmissime cohaeret ubi ex actualitate cognoscibilis derivat ordinem cognitionis reflexivae humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter immediatam perceptionem sui per actum et necessitatem inquisitionis subtilis, quia utriusque cognitionis discrimen dependet ab ambigua latitudine notionis praesentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT6","text":"Tensionem continet affirmatio reflexionis potentialiter infinitae cum requisitione cognitionis actualis, quam textus tolerat distinguendo infinitum in potentia ab infinito actu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, si cognitio voluntatis non additur ut thema separatum, sed tamquam extensio principii quod actus intra unam animam intelligibiliter praesentes cognosci possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165138526348Z_2068a8ea","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 87","source_sha256":"beb33de5984f2812b71ef8e7d1e9f941bcc481b1173c3469ef1891d87727da06","sha256":"4a1240025a9a5ebc3610d6c29046662f90588fcbcf512abc4638b57d570bd0ee","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:51:38.527338+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS1","text":"The question determines in what order the intellectual soul knows itself, its habits, the act of understanding, and the act of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS2","text":"Knowability follows proportionally upon the actuality of a thing, such that what exists only in potency is not, through its essence, an object of actual cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS3","text":"The human intellect, because it is potency in the genus of intelligibles and naturally turns toward material things, knows itself through its acts informed by material objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS4","text":"The reflexive order of human cognition proceeds from the material object to the act of understanding, from the act to the intellect, and from proper acts to habits and powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS5","text":"The act of the will is intelligible because will and intellect are rooted in one soul, and the good of the will and the true of the intellect mutually include one another according to different notions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AS6","text":"The movement of the argument is: knowable actuality → distinction of grades of intellect → mediation through act → reflexive cognition of the soul, habits, and will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A1","text":"Everything knowable is known insofar as it is in act, not insofar as it is only in potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A2","text":"The mode of knowability of an essence follows the degree to which the essence is act in the order of intelligibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A3","text":"The divine essence is pure act and therefore perfectly intelligible through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A4","text":"The angelic essence is intelligible act, but not pure act; therefore, an angel knows itself through its essence, but knows other things through likenesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A5","text":"The human intellect is potency with respect to intelligibles and is not actually intelligible to itself through its essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A6","text":"In the state of the present life, the human intellect becomes intelligible through species abstracted from sensibles by the light of the agent intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","text":"The act of understanding is an immanent perfection of the intellect and is knowable prior to the intellectual power itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A8","text":"A habit is intermediate between pure potency and perfect act; therefore, it is not fully knowable through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A9","text":"A habit is known because, being present, it causes its proper act, and the nature of the habit is investigated from consideration of the act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A10","text":"The presence of the soul suffices for the perception of its existence through an act, but does not suffice for quidditative cognition of its nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A11","text":"The primary object of the human intellect is the nature of a material thing; the act of understanding and the intellect are known reflexively and secondarily.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A12","text":"The act of the will is an intelligible inclination consequent upon an understood form and is knowable in the intellect as what is originated in its principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A13","text":"Intellect and will are distinct powers, but are rooted in the one substance of the soul and mutually possess the character of principle in some respect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:A14","text":"The good and the true differ in notion, but comprehend one another; because of this inclusion, the act of the will falls under the cognition of the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX1","text":"Human self-knowledge is not an immediate intuition of the essence of the soul through its essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX2","text":"The incorporeality of the soul does not suffice for the human intellect to be identical with its intelligible in the manner in which a separate substance is.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX3","text":"The interior presence of the soul is not the same as a quidditative manifestation of the nature of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX4","text":"A habit present in the soul is not an object of the intellect merely because it exists subjectively in the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX5","text":"A habit is not known immediately as an external thing through a species of the object, nor as an object known through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX6","text":"Cognition of the act of understanding does not require an actually completed infinite process, although the intellect can be reflected upon to infinity in potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX7","text":"The material condition of the organ of sense, which does not belong to the intellect, prevents an analogy between sense and intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:NX8","text":"The distinction between the powers of will and intellect does not constitute a separation of subjects that would render the act of the will absent from the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D1","text":"The human intellect knows itself from the fact that it perceives itself to understand, not because its essence is the primary object of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A5","CH_GGVC_P_79:A6","CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","CH_GGVC_P_79:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D2","text":"Particular self-knowledge, by which someone perceives that he has an intellectual soul, is distinguished from universal knowledge of the nature of mind.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","CH_GGVC_P_79:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D3","text":"Cognition of the existence of the mind is more immediate than cognition of the specific difference of the mind from other things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D4","text":"Cognition of a habit occurs in two ways: perceptively through the production of its proper act, and investigatively through analysis of the notion of the act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A8","CH_GGVC_P_79:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D5","text":"Faith or another habit is not known through external movements of the body, but through perception of the interior act that the habit produces.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D6","text":"The order of knowing in the human intellect is object → act → power, not power → act → object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","CH_GGVC_P_79:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:D7","text":"The act of the will is known both existentially, when someone perceives himself to will, and quidditatively, when the notion of the act and its principle is investigated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A12","CH_GGVC_P_79:A13","CH_GGVC_P_79:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SD1","text":"Psychic interiority does not constitute immediate objectivity: what is most intrinsic is humanly known according to the operation by which it emerges into act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A1","CH_GGVC_P_79:A5","CH_GGVC_P_79:A7","CH_GGVC_P_79:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SD2","text":"Human reflection is structurally mediated by material exteriority, because the material object is not a mere occasion but the beginning of the actualization of the intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A5","CH_GGVC_P_79:A6","CH_GGVC_P_79:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SD3","text":"Knowledge of the soul is divided into perception of operative presence and definition of nature, of which the former is quasi-connatural, the latter laborious and prone to error.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A9","CH_GGVC_P_79:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SD4","text":"The distinction of intellect and will is preserved without a dualism of subjects, because the communication of cognition is founded upon the unity of the soul and the convertibility of the true and the good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_79:A13","CH_GGVC_P_79:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX1","text":"It must be false that every incorporeal thing is, by that very fact, fully present to itself as an understood object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the identity of the knowing subject with a thing existing in the soul suffices for cognition of that thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX3","text":"It must be false that reflection is a primary act equal to cognition of an external object in the human intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the functional distinction of the powers of the soul entails their mutual incommunicability of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:DNX5","text":"It must be false that quidditative self-knowledge can be deduced from actual consciousness alone without investigation and judgment regulated by divine truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SNX1","text":"An absolutely self-transparent human subject is excluded, for which being, essence, act, and self-knowledge would coincide in one and the same order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SNX2","text":"Cognition of interiority wholly free from the turning of the intellect toward material natures in the state of the present life is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:SNX3","text":"The reduction of the soul to a static object is excluded, because the soul, habits, and will are properly known as principles and perfections operating in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:FGS1","text":"Knowable actuality → grades of act in the order of intelligibles → distinction of God, angel, and human intellect → determination of the proper mode of self-knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:FGS2","text":"A material object is understood → the intellect becomes actually understanding through the species → the act of understanding is known → the intellect is known as the principle of the act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:FGS3","text":"A principle imperfectly in act → a proper act produced → the presence of the principle perceived → the nature of the principle discerned through investigation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:FGS4","text":"An understood form → inclination of the will → an act of the will rooted in the same soul → perception of willing and cognition of the notion of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AF1","text":"Apparent cognition of the soul through essence → principle of actuality → diminution of the intelligible status of the human intellect → self-knowledge through act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AF2","text":"Presence of habits → distinction of subjective presence from known object → act of the habit → perception and investigation of the habit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AF3","text":"Primary material object → secondary act of understanding → reflexively known intellect → infinity of reflection only in potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:AF4","text":"Distinction of will from intellect → substantial unity of the soul and convertibility of the good and the true → intelligibly present act of the will → cognition of willing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME1","text":"The opposition between cognition of external things and cognition of interior things is dissolved: both are known according to the mode of actuality, not according to mere local presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME2","text":"The distinction between existential presence and quidditative cognition becomes necessary for understanding knowledge of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME3","text":"A habit is reclassified not as a primary object of the intellect, but as a disposition by which the intellect operates and which is manifested from its act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME4","text":"Reflection is reclassified not as the foundation of human cognition, but as a secondary operation derived from the material object and the act of the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ME5","text":"The will is reclassified not as a region alien to the intellect, but as an intelligible inclination within the unity of the soul and the order of true and good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ALT1","text":"Surface — The intellectual soul knows itself, habits, the act of understanding, and the act of the will not in one way, but according to diverse orders of mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ALT2","text":"Structural — Actuality, intelligible species, primary object, act, and potency constitute the order through which reflexive cognition is generated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The question of self-consciousness is transferred from immediate possession of the interior to investigation of principles from manifested acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The state of the present life orders the human intellect toward material things; therefore, the human mode of self-knowledge is ontologically distinguished from the divine and angelic mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT1","text":"The axioms of actuality, grades of intelligibility, and the order object–act–power suffice to restore the negation of cognition of the human soul through essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT2","text":"The distinction between presence and quiddity is necessary lest particular self-knowledge be confused with knowledge of the nature of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT3","text":"The axioms concerning habit as intermediate between potency and act explain why a habit is known through acts, but do not fully determine how individual acts are referred to distinct habits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT4","text":"The system coheres most firmly where it derives the order of human reflexive cognition from knowable actuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains between immediate self-perception through act and the necessity of subtle investigation, because the distinction between the two cognitions depends on the ambiguous breadth of the notion of presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT6","text":"The affirmation of potentially infinite reflection contains a tension with the requirement of actual cognition, which the text tolerates by distinguishing the infinite in potency from the infinite in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_79:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if cognition of the will is not added as a separate theme, but as an extension of the principle that acts intelligibly present within one soul can be known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_79:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_79@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_79:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 88","title":"First Part · Question 87","context":"Chapter 88","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 87"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 87","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 88","order":89,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_80"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_80@R001","sha256":"dcf644157daf1ec51887e7c4b49cb649a61b9f1a3d2a14c6f5a17150d0a41c9d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS1","text":"Quaestio constituitur utrum intellectus humanus, in statu vitae praesentis, substantias immateriales per se, per materialia, vel Deum ut primum cognitum attingere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS2","text":"Thesis regens statuit obiectum proportionatum intellectui humano esse quidditatem rei materialis, quia intelligit per conversionem ad phantasmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS3","text":"Ex disproportione inter intellectum phantasmatibus indigentem et substantias immateriales concluditur eas nec primo nec per se perfecte intelligi posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS4","text":"Via abstractionis a materialibus non transit in quidditatem immaterialem, quia substantiae immateriales non sunt formae materialium sed alterius rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS5","text":"Cognitio immaterialium, quatenus conceditur, est partialis et indirecta: per remotionem, effectus non adaequantes, habitudinem ad materialia, vel rationem communem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS6","text":"Deus, quamvis sit causa luminis cognoscentis, non est primum cognitum; cognitio eius a creaturis incipit, dum ipsum lumen est quo intellectus cognoscit, non quod primo cognoscit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A1","text":"Intellectus humanus in statu vitae praesentis naturaliter ordinatur ad naturas rerum materialium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A2","text":"Intellectus humanus nihil intelligit in statu praesentis vitae nisi convertendo se ad phantasmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A3","text":"Cognitio requirit proportionem inter obiectum cognitum et potentiam cognoscitivam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A4","text":"Substantiae immateriales sub sensum et imaginationem non cadunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A5","text":"Similitudo naturae cognoscentis et cogniti sola non sufficit ad cognitionem; requiritur similitudo rei in cognoscente ut forma.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A6","text":"Abstrahere quidditatem materialem a materia non producit quidditatem omnino immaterialem, si utraque est alterius rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A7","text":"Effectus vel similitudines materiales virtutem et naturam substantiarum immaterialium non adaequant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A8","text":"Anima humana seipsam cognoscit per actum suum proprium, qui virtutem et naturam eius perfecte demonstrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A9","text":"Intellectus agens est virtus animae, non substantia separata, et active se extendit ad eadem materialia ad quae intellectus possibilis receptive se extendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A10","text":"Substantiae immateriales creatae cum materialibus conveniunt solum in genere logico substantiae, non in genere naturali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A11","text":"Deus nec in genere naturali nec in genere logico cum rebus materialibus convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A12","text":"Causa prima cognitionis non propterea est primum cognitum, nisi causa et cognitum ad eundem ordinem pertineant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX1","text":"Non-Platonismus: formae immateriales subsistentes non sunt obiecta prima et per se intellectus humani praesentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX2","text":"Non-similitudo simplex: immaterialitas mentis non infert cognitionem immediatam omnium immaterialium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX3","text":"Non-convertibilitas intelligibilitatis: quod est maxime intelligibile secundum se non est propterea maxime intelligibile nobis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX4","text":"Non-continuatio abstractionis: iterata remotio materiae a quidditatibus materialibus non pertingit ad substantiam immaterialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX5","text":"Non-unio Averroistica: participatio luminis intellectus agentis neque unionem substantiae separatae neque cognitionem substantiarum separatarum efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX6","text":"Non-comprehensio quidditativa: doctrina de substantiis immaterialibus non est apprehensio perfecta earum quidditatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX7","text":"Non-primum-Deus: Deus non est primum obiectum intellectus humani, licet sit prima causa virtutis cognoscitivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D1","text":"Substantiae immateriales, quia phantasmata non habent et intellectui humano improportionatae sunt, per se et primo intelligi non possunt in vita praesenti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A1","CH_GGVC_P_80:A2","CH_GGVC_P_80:A3","CH_GGVC_P_80:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D2","text":"Scientia de substantiis immaterialibus procedit per remotionem et relationem, non per definitionem quidditativam propriam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A6","CH_GGVC_P_80:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D3","text":"Cognitio animae ex proprio actu praebet analogiam limitatam ad incorporea, non cognitionem simpliciter perfectam substantiarum separatarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A7","CH_GGVC_P_80:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D4","text":"De angelis aliquid affirmative cognosci potest secundum rationem communem substantiae, non secundum rationem speciei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A7","CH_GGVC_P_80:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D5","text":"De Deo per similitudines materiales nihil affirmative cognoscitur eodem modo quo de angelis, quia Deus nulli generi communi subiacet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A7","CH_GGVC_P_80:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D6","text":"Intellectus agens non aperit accessum praesentem ad substantias separatas, quia eius operatio propria materialia facit intelligibilia actu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A1","CH_GGVC_P_80:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D7","text":"Deus cognoscitur ex creaturis ut causa, non intuetur ut primum obiectum, quia causalitas luminis non convertitur in praesentiam obiectivam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A1","CH_GGVC_P_80:A2","CH_GGVC_P_80:A11","CH_GGVC_P_80:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SD1","text":"Ordo cognitionis humanae subordinat metaphysicam immaterialium condicionibus cognitionis materialis: ascensus est realis sed non transitum ad aequationem quidditativam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:D1","CH_GGVC_P_80:D2","CH_GGVC_P_80:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SD2","text":"Transcendentia obiecti non mensuratur sola dignitate ontologica, sed proportione ad modum receptivum intellectus humani.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A3","CH_GGVC_P_80:A4","CH_GGVC_P_80:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SD3","text":"Causalitas divina bifurcatur in causam facultatis cognoscitivae et obiectum cognitionis: primum non infert secundum ut primitatem epistemicam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SD4","text":"Differentia angelorum et Dei non est tantum gradus distantiae, sed mutatio generis cognoscibilitatis: angeli ratione communi continguntur, Deus nulli generi communi comparatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:D4","CH_GGVC_P_80:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:DNX1","text":"Falsa esse debet identitas inter modum essendi immaterialem et modum cognosci ab intellectu humano.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:DNX2","text":"Falsa esse debet suppositio quod omne ens naturaliter intelligibile sit propter intellectum humanum ordinatum vel ab eo actu comprehendendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:DNX3","text":"Falsa esse debet suppositio quod remotio limitationum materialium producat positive formam cognitionis immaterialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:DNX4","text":"Falsa esse debet aequatio inter fundamentum transcendens cognitionis et obiectum quod intellectus primo apprehendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit cognitionem humanam ut accessum universalem ad omne intelligibile; obiectum est cognoscibile nobis solum intra condicionem proportionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit transitum continuum a sensibilibus ad increatum: inter creaturas et Deum non datur genus, species, vel similitudo materialis affirmative mediatrix.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit felicitatem intellectualem praesentem fundatam in unione substantialis intellectus humani cum intellectu separato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:FGS1","text":"Status praesens → conversio ad phantasmata → obiectum proportionatum: quidditas materialis → exclusio cognitionis per se immaterialium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:FGS2","text":"Materiale cognitum → abstractio → imminutio conditionum materialium → differentia rationis persistens → negatio transitus in quidditatem immaterialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:FGS3","text":"Effectus, remotiones, et rationes communes → cognitio aliqualis → negatio aequationis quidditativae → doctrina limitata de angelis et Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:FGS4","text":"Deus ut causa luminis intellectivi → lumen ut quo cognoscitur → distinctio causae et obiecti → cognitio Dei ex creaturis, non ut primi cogniti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AF1","text":"Praetensio cognitionis immediatae → determinatio obiecti humani per phantasmata → disproportio immaterialium → rejectio Platonismi et unionis Averroisticae → cognitio remotionis et effectuum → distinctio angelorum a Deo → Deus ex creaturis cognoscitur, non primo apprehenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME1","text":"Distinctio inter intelligibile secundum se et intelligibile quoad nos fit principium ordinans cognitionem metaphysicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME2","text":"Oppositio materiale/immateriale desinit esse scala simplex dignitatis cognoscitivae et fit differentia proportionis obiecti ad facultatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME3","text":"Abstractionis operatio reclassificatur ut cognitio formarum materialium, non ut machina generans essentias separatas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME4","text":"Cognitio indirecta distinguitur a comprehensione: remotionis, effectuum et generis logici viae aliquid ostendunt sine quidditate propria exhibenda.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME5","text":"Causa cognitionis et obiectum primum cognitionis separantur, ita ut Deus fundamentum luminis sit sine primitate obiectiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ALT1","text":"Surface — Anima humana non intelligit substantias immateriales per se in statu praesentis vitae; Deus non est primum cognitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ALT2","text":"Structural — Cognitio humana dependet a phantasmatibus, abstractione formarum materialium, et proportione potentiae ad obiectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio convertit quaestionem ab excellentia obiecti ad condiciones cognitionis humanae, atque excludit inferentias a causalitate, similitudine, vel abstractione simplici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Status vitae praesentis limitat extensionem intellectus; Deus et substantiae separatae non solum sunt absentes a sensu, sed diverso modo excedunt ordinem genericum et phantasmaticum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam conclusionem principalem, quia dependentiam intellectus a phantasmatibus cum regula proportionis et immaterialitate obiecti coniungunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT2","text":"Systema firmissimum est ubi negat transitum ab abstractione materialium ad quidditatem immaterialem, quia hic nexus directe ex differentia rationis substantiarum deducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT3","text":"Cognitio “aliqualis” immaterialium manet minus determinata: conceditur per remotionem, effectus, et rationem communem, sed mensura interna sufficientiae eius non plene explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter cognitionem animae ex actu proprio et negationem cognitionis substantiarum separatarum ex effectibus, quia decisiva differentia est adaequatio effectus, non sola indirectio viae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT5","text":"Distinctio angelorum et Dei interne cohaeret dum genus logicum angelis conceditur et Deo negatur; tamen cognitio affirmativa angelorum restringitur ad rationem communem, non ad naturam specificam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat si status praesentis vitae retinetur ut conditio limitans; remoto hoc termino, conclusiones de impossibilitate simpliciter ultra intentionem explicitam extenderentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165202453990Z_c39630d8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 88","source_sha256":"dcf644157daf1ec51887e7c4b49cb649a61b9f1a3d2a14c6f5a17150d0a41c9d","sha256":"a56154fb939a076233772fb790e16d11feaed220886a375e827802a5c00e8cfa","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:52:02.455205+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS1","text":"The question is posed whether the human intellect, in the state of the present life, can attain immaterial substances through themselves, through material things, or God as the first known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS2","text":"The governing thesis establishes that the proportionate object of the human intellect is the quiddity of a material thing, because it understands by turning to phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS3","text":"From the disproportion between the intellect requiring phantasms and immaterial substances, it is concluded that these can be understood neither first nor through themselves perfectly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS4","text":"The way of abstraction from material things does not pass into an immaterial quiddity, because immaterial substances are not forms of material things but are of another intelligible character (ratio).","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS5","text":"Knowledge of immaterial things, insofar as it is conceded, is partial and indirect: through removal, non-adequate effects, relation to material things, or a common intelligible character (ratio).","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AS6","text":"God, although He is the cause of the light of knowing, is not the first known; knowledge of Him begins from creatures, while the light itself is that by which the intellect knows, not that which it knows first.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A1","text":"The human intellect in the state of the present life is naturally ordered to the natures of material things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A2","text":"The human intellect understands nothing in the state of the present life except by turning itself to phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A3","text":"Knowledge requires proportion between the known object and the cognitive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A4","text":"Immaterial substances do not fall under sense and imagination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A5","text":"The likeness of the knowing nature and the known alone does not suffice for knowledge; the likeness of the thing in the knower as a form is required.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A6","text":"To abstract a material quiddity from matter does not produce a wholly immaterial quiddity, if each is of another intelligible character (ratio).","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A7","text":"Material effects or likenesses do not adequately represent the power and nature of immaterial substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A8","text":"The human soul knows itself through its own act, which perfectly manifests its power and nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A9","text":"The agent intellect is a power of the soul, not a separate substance, and it actively extends itself to the same material things to which the possible intellect receptively extends itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A10","text":"Created immaterial substances agree with material things only in the logical genus of substance, not in a natural genus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A11","text":"God agrees with material things neither in a natural genus nor in a logical genus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:A12","text":"The first cause of knowledge is not thereby the first known, unless the cause and the known belong to the same order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX1","text":"Non-Platonism: subsisting immaterial forms are not the first and per se objects of the present human intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX2","text":"Non-simple likeness: the immateriality of the mind does not entail immediate knowledge of all immaterial things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX3","text":"Non-convertibility of intelligibility: what is most intelligible in itself is not therefore most intelligible to us.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX4","text":"Non-continuation of abstraction: the repeated removal of matter from material quiddities does not reach an immaterial substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX5","text":"Non-Averroistic union: participation in the light of the agent intellect effects neither union with a separate substance nor knowledge of separate substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX6","text":"Non-quiddity-based comprehension: doctrine concerning immaterial substances is not a perfect apprehension of their quiddity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:NX7","text":"Non-first-God: God is not the first object of the human intellect, although He is the first cause of cognitive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D1","text":"Immaterial substances, because they do not have phantasms and are disproportionate to the human intellect, cannot be understood through themselves and first in the present life.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A1","CH_GGVC_P_80:A2","CH_GGVC_P_80:A3","CH_GGVC_P_80:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D2","text":"Knowledge concerning immaterial substances proceeds through removal and relation, not through a proper quidditative definition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A6","CH_GGVC_P_80:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D3","text":"Knowledge of the soul from its proper act provides a limited analogy to incorporeal things, not simply perfect knowledge of separate substances.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A7","CH_GGVC_P_80:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D4","text":"Something affirmative can be known about angels according to the common intelligible character (ratio) of substance, not according to the intelligible character (ratio) of species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A7","CH_GGVC_P_80:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D5","text":"Nothing affirmative is known of God through material likenesses in the same way as of angels, because God falls under no common genus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A7","CH_GGVC_P_80:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D6","text":"The agent intellect does not open present access to separate substances, because its proper operation makes material things actually intelligible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A1","CH_GGVC_P_80:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:D7","text":"God is known from creatures as cause, not intuited as the first object, because the causality of light is not converted into objective presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A1","CH_GGVC_P_80:A2","CH_GGVC_P_80:A11","CH_GGVC_P_80:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SD1","text":"The order of human knowledge subordinates the metaphysics of immaterial things to the conditions of material knowledge: the ascent is real but does not pass into quidditative adequation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:D1","CH_GGVC_P_80:D2","CH_GGVC_P_80:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SD2","text":"The transcendence of the object is measured not by ontological dignity alone, but by proportion to the receptive mode of the human intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:A3","CH_GGVC_P_80:A4","CH_GGVC_P_80:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SD3","text":"Divine causality bifurcates into the cause of the cognitive faculty and the object of knowledge: the former does not entail the latter as epistemic firstness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SD4","text":"The difference between angels and God is not merely a degree of distance, but a change in the kind of knowability: angels are attained by a common intelligible character (ratio), God is compared with no common genus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_80:D4","CH_GGVC_P_80:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:DNX1","text":"The identity between the immaterial mode of being and the mode of being known by the human intellect must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:DNX2","text":"The supposition that every being naturally intelligible is ordered to the human intellect or is to be actually comprehended by it must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:DNX3","text":"The supposition that the removal of material limitations positively produces a form of immaterial knowledge must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:DNX4","text":"The equation between the transcendent foundation of knowledge and the object that the intellect first apprehends must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SNX1","text":"The system excludes human knowledge as universal access to everything intelligible; an object is knowable by us only within the condition of proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SNX2","text":"The system excludes a continuous passage from sensibles to the uncreated: between creatures and God there is no genus, species, or materially mediating affirmative likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:SNX3","text":"The system excludes present intellectual happiness founded upon the substantial union of the human intellect with a separate intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:FGS1","text":"Present state → turning to phantasms → proportionate object: material quiddity → exclusion of per se knowledge of immaterial things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:FGS2","text":"Known material thing → abstraction → diminution of material conditions → persistent difference of intelligible character (ratio) → denial of passage into an immaterial quiddity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:FGS3","text":"Effects, removals, and common intelligible characters (rationes) → some knowledge → denial of quidditative adequation → limited doctrine concerning angels and God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:FGS4","text":"God as cause of intellectual light → light as that by which one knows → distinction of cause and object → knowledge of God from creatures, not as the first known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:AF1","text":"Claim of immediate knowledge → determination of the human object through phantasms → disproportion of immaterial things → rejection of Platonism and Averroistic union → knowledge through removal and effects → distinction of angels from God → God is known from creatures, not first apprehended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME1","text":"The distinction between what is intelligible in itself and what is intelligible with respect to us becomes the ordering principle of metaphysical knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME2","text":"The opposition material/immaterial ceases to be a simple scale of cognitive dignity and becomes a difference in the proportion of object to faculty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME3","text":"The operation of abstraction is reclassified as knowledge of material forms, not as a machine generating separate essences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME4","text":"Indirect knowledge is distinguished from comprehension: the ways of removal, effects, and logical genus show something without presenting a proper quiddity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ME5","text":"The cause of knowledge and the first object of knowledge are separated, such that God is the foundation of light without objective firstness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ALT1","text":"Surface — The human soul does not understand immaterial substances through themselves in the state of the present life; God is not the first known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ALT2","text":"Structural — Human knowledge depends on phantasms, abstraction of material forms, and proportion of power to object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument shifts the question from the excellence of the object to the conditions of human knowledge, and excludes inferences from causality, likeness, or simple abstraction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The state of the present life limits the extension of the intellect; God and separate substances are not only absent from sense, but in different ways exceed the generic and phantasmatic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal conclusion, because they join the dependence of the intellect on phantasms with the rule of proportion and the immateriality of the object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT2","text":"The system is strongest where it denies passage from the abstraction of material things to an immaterial quiddity, because this nexus is directly deduced from the difference of intelligible character (ratio) of the substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT3","text":"Some knowledge of immaterial things remains less determinate: it is conceded through removal, effects, and a common intelligible character (ratio), but the internal measure of its sufficiency is not fully explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains between knowledge of the soul from its proper act and the denial of knowledge of separate substances from effects, because the decisive difference is the adequation of the effect, not the mere indirectness of the way.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT5","text":"The distinction between angels and God coheres internally so long as logical genus is granted to angels and denied to God; nevertheless, affirmative knowledge of angels is restricted to a common intelligible character (ratio), not to specific nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_80:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if the state of the present life is retained as a limiting condition; once this term is removed, the conclusions concerning impossibility simply speaking would be extended beyond the explicit intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_80:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_80@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_80:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 89","title":"First Part · Question 88","context":"Chapter 89","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 88"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 88","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 89","order":90,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_81"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_81@R001","sha256":"2caa8498eb1b6f747abac858d218eba5119fad4b0fc488d18ba1566d7b57f61e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS1","text":"Investigatur quomodo anima humana, amisso corpore et potentiis sensitivis, naturaliter cognoscere possit atque quid eius cognitio attingat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS2","text":"Anima separata intelligere potest, quia eadem natura sub diverso modo essendi diversum modum operandi suscipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysico-reconstructiva et dialectica, quoniam difficultates ex corruptione organorum per distinctiones naturae, status, speciei et modi operationis dissolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS4","text":"Motus initialis procedit ab absentia phantasmatum ad principium quo modus operationis ex modo essendi determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS5","text":"Modus cognitionis separatae deinde per hierarchiam luminis intellectualis, capacitatem recipientis et proportionem obiecti limitatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS6","text":"Permanentia scientiae explicatur divisione habitus inter intellectum incorruptibilem et vires sensitivas corruptibiles, atque distinctione speciei actus a modo agendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS7","text":"Quaestio cognitionis distantium tandem a loco ad actualitatem obiecti, habitudinem cognoscentis et ordinationem divinam transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A1","text":"Nihil operatur nisi inquantum est actu; modus operandi rei sequitur modum essendi eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","text":"Natura animae post mortem manet eadem, sed modus essendi eius ex unione corporali in separationem mutatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","text":"Unio corporis est animae naturalis, separatio autem a corpore est praeter rationem naturae eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A4","text":"Anima corpori unita naturaliter intelligit per conversionem ad phantasmata in organis corporeis existentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","text":"Anima separata intelligit per conversionem ad intelligibilia simpliciter et per species ex influentia divini luminis participatas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","text":"In hierarchia participationis divini luminis efficacia intellectiva decrescit a primo principio, et anima humana infimum gradum substantiarum intellectualium tenet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","text":"Omne receptum determinatur secundum modum recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A8","text":"Cognitio propria et perfecta rerum animae humanae proportionata requirit acquisitionem ex sensibilibus mediante corpore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","text":"Perfectio cognitionis substantiae separatae mensuratur conformitate obiecti ad modum substantiae cognoscentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A10","text":"Species a divino lumine participatae repraesentare possunt universalia et singularia, quia participant similitudinem causalitatis divinae utrorumque principiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","text":"Cognitio singularis animae separatae determinatur per cognitionem praecedentem, affectionem, habitudinem naturalem vel ordinationem divinam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","text":"Habitus scientiae acquisitae formaliter est in intellectu, materialiter autem et dispositive in viribus sensitivis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","text":"Pars intellectualis habitus morte non corrumpitur, quia intellectus est incorruptibilis et intentioni intelligibili simplici nihil est contrarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A14","text":"Species actus cognoscitivi ab obiecto determinatur, modus autem actus a virtute et statu cognoscentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A15","text":"Distantia localis separat entia actu existentia, distantia autem temporalis futurorum implicat defectum actualis entitatis et cognoscibilitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A16","text":"Ordo naturalis animae separatae eam a conversatione viventium segregat et conversationi substantiarum spiritualium coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A17","text":"Influentia luminis naturalis, cuius Deus est auctor, a lumine gratuito, revelatione et cognitione gloriae distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A18","text":"Secundum sententiam Gregorii textui praeponderantem, visio claritatis divinae praesentia viventium animabus beatis manifestat, earum interventu iustitiae divinae subiecto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0151","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX1","text":"Unio corporis non est impedimentum animae mere accidentale, cuius remotione cognitio angelica naturaliter redeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX2","text":"Separatio animae non constituit eam substantiam angelicam neque cognitionem angelis connaturalem ei confert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX3","text":"Corruptio sensus et imaginationis non infert corruptionem omnis intellectionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX4","text":"Anima separata non intelligit per species innatas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX5","text":"Anima separata non abstrahit novas species a sensibilibus, quia organa sensitiva non manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX6","text":"Cognitio separata non reducitur ad species ante mortem conservatas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX7","text":"Origo divina specierum non facit cognitionem eo ipso gratuitam vel supernaturalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX8","text":"Cognitio substantiarum separatarum superiorum non est perfecta nec beatifica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX9","text":"Cognitio omnium naturalium non est propria, determinata vel aequalis scientiae studio acquisitae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX10","text":"Anima separata neque omnia singularia cognoscit neque ab omni cognitione singularium excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX11","text":"Habitus scientiae non est totus in viribus sensitivis neque totus per earum corruptionem destruitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX12","text":"Usus scientiae conservatae non retinet modum conversionis ad phantasmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX13","text":"Distantia localis non est causa naturalis ignorantiae animae separatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX14","text":"Distantia temporalis futurorum non est eiusdem rationis ac distantia localis rerum praesentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX15","text":"Cura mortuorum de viventibus et apparitiones mortuorum non probant cognitionem directam et naturalem rerum praesentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX16","text":"Separatio sola non confert ultimam felicitatem neque visionem Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D1","text":"Anima separata intelligere potest, quamvis modus intellectionis phantasmatibus innixus cum corpore cesset.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A1","CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","CH_GGVC_P_81:A4","CH_GGVC_P_81:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D2","text":"Unio corporis ordinatur ad bonum animae, quia intellectui humano infimo cognitionem propriam rerum sensibilium praebet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D3","text":"Modus intelligendi per intelligibilia simpliciter est nobilior absolute, sed in anima humana separata imperfectior propter debilitatem recipientis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D4","text":"Anima separata seipsam per seipsam intelligit, quia iam non indiget actu ex phantasmatibus abstracto ut sibi fiat intelligibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D5","text":"Anima separata alias animas separatas perfecte, Angelos autem imperfecte cognoscit, quia primis conformis est et secundis inferior.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D6","text":"Anima separata omnia naturalia aliquo modo cognoscit, sed communiter et confuse potius quam proprie et perfecte.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D7","text":"Studium praesentis vitae non fit supervacuum, quia cognitionem propriam et determinatam producit quam status separationis naturaliter non praebet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A8","CH_GGVC_P_81:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D8","text":"Anima separata cognoscit tantum singularia ad quae aliqua determinata habitudo eam ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A10","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D9","text":"Habitus scientiae acquisitae manet secundum partem intellectualem, sed perit secundum dispositiones virium sensitivarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D10","text":"Scientia acquisita et cognitio ex speciebus infusis in eadem anima coexistere possunt, quia non sunt unius rationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D11","text":"Anima separata potest per species ante mortem acquisitas eadem obiecta intelligere, sed modo statui separationis conveniente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","CH_GGVC_P_81:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D12","text":"Propinquitas vel remotio loci cognitionem animae separatae non mensurat, quia species divinitus participatae ad utrumque aequaliter se habent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D13","text":"Futura non cognoscuntur naturaliter in seipsis, quia nondum sunt entia actu, sed tantum in causis vel per revelationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A15","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D14","text":"Animae mortuorum secundum cognitionem naturalem nesciunt quae inter vivos aguntur, non propter locum, sed propter segregationem ordinis et conversationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","CH_GGVC_P_81:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D15","text":"Notitia rerum viventium mortuis contingere potest per animas supervenientes, Angelos, Daemones, revelationem vel dispensationem miracularem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A16","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D16","text":"Textus sententiam Gregorii praeponit, qua animae beatae praesentia viventium cognoscunt, sed sententiam Augustini dubitative contrariam non omnino demonstrative excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A17","CH_GGVC_P_81:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0151","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D17","text":"Cognitio naturalis substantiarum separatarum magnam quidem perfectionem affert, sed ultima felicitas in sola visione Dei per gratiam consistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD1","text":"Corporalitas non est carcer intellectus, sed instrumentum epistemicum quo intellectus infimus cognitionem determinatam sibi proportionatam acquirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","CH_GGVC_P_81:A8","CH_GGVC_P_81:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD2","text":"Separatio simul defectum ontologicum et libertatem operationalem inducit: anima extra statum naturalem est, sed a conversione ad organa solvitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD3","text":"Topologia cognitionis separatae fundatur in modo essendi, proportione et habitudine, non in mensura spatii physici.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","CH_GGVC_P_81:A15","CH_GGVC_P_81:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD4","text":"Continuitas intellectualis post mortem est asymmetrica: contentum formale persistit, apparatus sensitivus perit, modus actualizationis mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","CH_GGVC_P_81:A14","CH_GGVC_P_81:D9","CH_GGVC_P_81:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD5","text":"Causalitas divina cognitionem naturalem constituit potius quam tollit; distinctio naturae et gratiae pendet ex modo participationis, non ex sola origine divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD6","text":"Universalitas medii cognoscitivi non producit aequalitatem accessus, quia capacitas recipientis cognitionem confundit et habitudo particularis singularia selectat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A10","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","CH_GGVC_P_81:D6","CH_GGVC_P_81:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD7","text":"Mors neque omniscientiam neque vacuitatem cognitivam efficit, sed cognitionem generaliter diffusam, imperfectam et circa singularia selectivam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:D6","CH_GGVC_P_81:D8","CH_GGVC_P_81:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD8","text":"Differentiae scientiae acquisitae post mortem manere possunt sine conversione ordinis moralis in ordinem intellectualem, quia hae differentiae minoris momenti sunt quam praerogativae gloriae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD9","text":"Communicatio beatorum cum rebus viventium non est regressus ad conversationem corporalem, sed cognitio et interventus iustitiae divinae subordinati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A16","CH_GGVC_P_81:A18","CH_GGVC_P_81:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet operationem animae ab eius natura ita fixe determinari ut mutatio status nullam mutationem modi cognoscendi admittat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet corpus esse malum extrinsecum cuius remotio plenitudinem intellectualem animae statim restituat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet maiorem intelligibilitatem obiecti perfectiorem cognitionem in quolibet intellectu necessario producere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet incorporeitatem cognoscentis omnem limitationem, confusionem vel selectivitatem cognitionis auferre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet causalitatem divinam et naturalitatem cognitionis inter se excludi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse oportet scientiam acquisitam aut omnino corporalem aut ab omni formatione sensitiva independentem esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX7","text":"Falsum esse oportet identitatem speciei intelligibilis identitatem modi intelligendi secum ferre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0122","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX8","text":"Falsum esse oportet praesentiam affectivam, curam vel apparitionem cognitionem directam rei praesentis demonstrare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX9","text":"Falsum esse oportet cognitionem incorpoream secundum leges transmissionis localis constitui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX10","text":"Falsum esse oportet ordinem moralem omnes differentias naturales vel acquisitas inter animas absorbere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX1","text":"Excluditur possibilitas animae humanae naturaliter completae ut substantiae disembodiatae, quia talis positio unionem corporis bono animae contrariam redderet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX2","text":"Excluditur beatitudo naturaliter consequens ex sola morte, quoniam separatio nec intellectum angelicum nec visionem Dei constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX3","text":"Excluditur mors tamquam consummatio epistemica absoluta vel deletio absoluta; utrumque extremum distinctionem status, speciei et modi destrueret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX4","text":"Indisponibilis est communis praesentia naturalis viventium et mortuorum; communicatio eorum indiget mediatione vel ordinatione speciali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX5","text":"Excluditur mensura univoca cognitionis divinae, angelicae et humanae, quia eadem participatio secundum diversos modos recipientium diversificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX6","text":"Excluditur transparentia universalis singularium, quamvis medium cognoscitivum a causa universali procedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX7","text":"Impossibile habetur ut anima beata rebus viventium se ingerat praeter exigentiam dispositionis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS1","text":"Series fundamentalis est: actualitas rei → modus essendi → modus operandi → modus cognoscendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A1","CH_GGVC_P_81:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS2","text":"Bifurcatio status est: unio naturalis → phantasmata → cognitio propria; separatio praeter naturam → intelligibilia simpliciter → species participatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","CH_GGVC_P_81:A4","CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS3","text":"Calibratio cognitionis est: lumen participatum → efficacia recipientis → conformitas obiecti → cognitio perfecta, imperfecta, communis vel selectiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS4","text":"Distributio obiectorum est: proprium esse → cognitio sui; modus conformis → aliae animae; modus superior → Angeli imperfecte; naturalia → communiter; singularia → secundum determinationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","CH_GGVC_P_81:A10","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","CH_GGVC_P_81:D4","CH_GGVC_P_81:D5","CH_GGVC_P_81:D6","CH_GGVC_P_81:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS5","text":"Continuitas scientiae est: actus cum phantasmatibus → dispositio sensitiva et species intellectualis → mors → amissio dispositionis et permanentia speciei → novus modus usus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","CH_GGVC_P_81:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS6","text":"Discretio distantiae est: obiectum actu existens et localiter remotum → cognoscibile; obiectum futurum nondum actu existens → non cognoscibile in se naturaliter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A15","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS7","text":"Regimen cognitionis viventium est: segregatio naturalis → ignorantia praesentium; mediatio vel revelatio → notitia particularis; visio gloriae → cognitio secundum dispositionem divinae iustitiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A16","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17","CH_GGVC_P_81:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF1","text":"Dependentia apparens a phantasmatibus → distinctio naturae et status → principium modi essendi → possibilitas intellectionis separatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF2","text":"Possibilitas intellectionis separatae → hierarchia recipientium → cognitio sui et substantiarum separatarum → cognitio confusa naturalium → cognitio selectiva singularium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF3","text":"Scientia acquisita → divisio habitus inter intellectum et sensum → permanentia partis intellectualis → mutatio modi usus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF4","text":"Cognitio singularium → negatio impedimenti localis → distinctio loci a tempore → segregatio conversationis mortuorum → exceptiones revelationis et gloriae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF5","text":"Privatio organorum → reconstitutio modi cognoscendi → limitatio per recipiens → continuitas intellectualis → clausura per ordinem divinum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME1","text":"Corpus ex impedimento extrinseco in condicionem cognitionis determinatae intellectui humano proportionatae reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter cognitionem divinitus infusam et cognitionem naturalem corruit; discrimen in genere luminis et modo participationis ponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME3","text":"Perfectio cognitionis dividitur inter nobilitatem simpliciter et perfectionem relative ad capacitatem cognoscentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME4","text":"Cognitio post mortem ex oppositione scientiae et ignorantiae in gradus cognitionis perfectae, imperfectae, communis, confusae et selectivae resolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME5","text":"Cognitio singularium ex monopolio sensus transfertur ad repraesentationem intelligibilem, sed sub condicione habitudinis determinatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME6","text":"Identitas scientiae trans statum non amplius ex identitate modi operationis, sed ex permanentia specierum sub mutatione modi usus intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME7","text":"Distantia cognitiva ex mensura locali in differentiam actualitatis, proportionis et ordinationis convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME8","text":"Relatio viventium et mortuorum ex observatione spatiali in distinctionem conversationum ontologicarum et mediationum divinarum redescribitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME9","text":"Mors ex simplici corruptione potentiarum in transitum inter regimina cognitionis conceptualiter mutatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ALT1","text":"In gradu superficiei examinantur possibilitas intellectionis separatae, obiecta eius, permanentia scientiae, distantia et cognitio rerum viventium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ALT2","text":"In gradu structurali cognitionem regunt status animae, hierarchia luminis intellectualis, modus recipientis, distributio habitus et ordinatio conversationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ALT3","text":"In gradu metastrategico quaestiones ex disiunctionibus absolutis ad distinctiones inter naturam et statum, speciem et modum, locum et actualitatem, naturam et gratiam transferuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ALT4","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali operatio fundatur in actu et modo essendi, futura autem propter defectum actualis entitatis a rebus localiter remotis distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT1","text":"Corpus axiomatum sufficit ad restituendam possibilitatem, ambitum, limites et continuitatem cognitionis animae separatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT2","text":"Firmissima commissura est nexus inter modum essendi, modum operandi et determinationem recepti secundum recipiens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT3","text":"Mechanismus exactus impressionis specierum divinarum et gradus cognitionis communis atque confusae non ulterius determinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT4","text":"Tensionem inter modum intelligendi simpliciter nobiliorem et unionem corporalem bono animae ordinatam solvit relativitas perfectionis ad capacitatem recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT5","text":"Tensionem inter affectionem praecedentem tamquam determinationem singularis et ignorantiam rerum viventium ordinatio segregationis ponitur componere, sed modus huius praelationis non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT6","text":"Permanentia usus scientiae nititur distinctione valida sed compressa inter speciem actus et modum agendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT7","text":"Concordia de cognitione animarum beatarum non plene clauditur, quia sententia Gregorii praeponderat sine plena eliminatione dubitationis Augustini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0151","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT8","text":"Contradictio directa vitatur distinctionibus status naturalis, cognitionis naturalis et cognitionis gloriae, sed earum fines auctoritate metaphysica potius quam analysi mechanismi stabiliuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT9","text":"Restitutio servat motum verum argumentationis ab apparentia impossibilitatis ad cognitionem graduatam, selective determinatam et ordinatione divina conclusam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165240135800Z_6366c4fa","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 89","source_sha256":"2caa8498eb1b6f747abac858d218eba5119fad4b0fc488d18ba1566d7b57f61e","sha256":"146745bcd638d6dd9216fa165532b9c5a732125fbe16b67c5d97a95badf72813","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:52:40.136897+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS1","text":"It is investigated how the human soul, having lost the body and sensitive powers, can naturally know and what its cognition attains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS2","text":"The separated soul can understand, because the same nature under a different mode of being receives a different mode of operating.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical-reconstructive and dialectical, because it resolves difficulties arising from the corruption of organs through distinctions of nature, state, species, and mode of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS4","text":"The initial movement proceeds from the absence of phantasms to the principle by which the mode of operation is determined by the mode of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS5","text":"The mode of separated cognition is then limited through the hierarchy of intellectual light, the capacity of the recipient, and the proportion of the object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS6","text":"The persistence of knowledge is explained by the division of habit between the incorruptible intellect and corruptible sensitive powers, and by the distinction of the species of act from the mode of acting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AS7","text":"Finally, the question of knowledge of distant things is transferred from place to the actuality of the object, the relation of the knower, and divine ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A1","text":"Nothing operates except insofar as it is actual; the mode of a thing's operation follows its mode of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","text":"The nature of the soul remains the same after death, but its mode of being changes from bodily union to separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","text":"Union with the body is natural to the soul, whereas separation from the body is beyond the order of its nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A4","text":"The soul united to the body naturally understands through turning toward phantasms existing in bodily organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","text":"The separated soul understands through turning toward intelligibles simply and through species participated from the influence of divine light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","text":"In the hierarchy of participation in divine light, intellectual efficacy decreases from the first principle, and the human soul holds the lowest grade among intellectual substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","text":"Everything received is determined according to the mode of the recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A8","text":"Proper and perfect knowledge of things proportionate to the human soul requires acquisition from sensibles through the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","text":"The perfection of a separated substance's knowledge is measured by the conformity of the object to the mode of the knowing substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A10","text":"Species participated from divine light can represent universals and singulars, because they participate in the likeness of divine causality of both principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","text":"The separated soul's knowledge of singulars is determined by preceding knowledge, affection, natural relation, or divine ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","text":"The habit of acquired knowledge is formally in the intellect, but materially and dispositively in the sensitive powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","text":"The intellectual part of the habit is not corrupted by death, because the intellect is incorruptible and nothing is contrary to the simple intelligible intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0096","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A14","text":"The species of the cognitive act is determined by the object, whereas the mode of the act is determined by the power and state of the knower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A15","text":"Local distance separates beings actually existing, whereas the temporal distance of future things entails a lack of actual being and knowability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A16","text":"The natural order of the separated soul segregates it from intercourse with the living and joins it to intercourse with spiritual substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A17","text":"The influence of natural light, of which God is the author, is distinguished from gratuitous light, revelation, and knowledge of glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:A18","text":"According to Gregory's opinion, predominant in the text, the vision of divine brightness manifests the presence of the living to blessed souls, subject to divine justice's intervention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0151","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX1","text":"Union with the body is not a merely accidental impediment to the soul, upon whose removal angelic cognition naturally returns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX2","text":"The separation of the soul does not make it an angelic substance, nor does it confer upon it cognition connatural to angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX3","text":"The corruption of sense and imagination does not entail the corruption of all understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX4","text":"The separated soul does not understand through innate species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX5","text":"The separated soul does not abstract new species from sensibles, because the sensitive organs do not remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX6","text":"Separated knowledge is not reduced to species preserved before death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX7","text":"The divine origin of species does not thereby make cognition gratuitous or supernatural.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX8","text":"Knowledge of higher separated substances is neither perfect nor beatific.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX9","text":"Knowledge of all natural things is not proper, determinate, or equal to knowledge acquired by study.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX10","text":"The separated soul neither knows all singulars nor is excluded from every knowledge of singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX11","text":"The habit of knowledge is not wholly in the sensitive powers, nor is it wholly destroyed through their corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX12","text":"The use of preserved knowledge does not retain the mode of turning toward phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX13","text":"Local distance is not a natural cause of the separated soul's ignorance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX14","text":"The temporal distance of future things is not of the same account as the local distance of present things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX15","text":"The care of the dead for the living and apparitions of the dead do not prove direct and natural knowledge of present things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:NX16","text":"Separation alone confers neither ultimate happiness nor the vision of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D1","text":"The separated soul can understand, although the mode of understanding based on phantasms ceases with the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A1","CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","CH_GGVC_P_81:A4","CH_GGVC_P_81:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D2","text":"Union with the body is ordered to the good of the soul, because it affords proper knowledge of sensible things to the lowest human intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D3","text":"The mode of understanding through intelligibles simply is nobler absolutely, but more imperfect in the separated human soul because of the weakness of the recipient.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D4","text":"The separated soul understands itself through itself, because it no longer needs an act abstracted from phantasms in order to become intelligible to itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D5","text":"The separated soul knows other separated souls perfectly, but Angels imperfectly, because it is conformed to the former and inferior to the latter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D6","text":"The separated soul knows all natural things in some way, but commonly and confusedly rather than properly and perfectly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D7","text":"Study in the present life does not become superfluous, because it produces proper and determinate knowledge that the state of separation does not naturally provide.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A8","CH_GGVC_P_81:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D8","text":"The separated soul knows only those singulars to which some determinate relation orders it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A10","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D9","text":"The habit of acquired knowledge remains according to its intellectual part, but perishes according to the dispositions of the sensitive powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D10","text":"Acquired knowledge and cognition from infused species can coexist in the same soul, because they are not of one account.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D11","text":"The separated soul can understand the same objects through species acquired before death, but in a mode befitting the state of separation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","CH_GGVC_P_81:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D12","text":"Nearness or remoteness of place does not measure the separated soul's knowledge, because divinely participated species stand equally toward both.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D13","text":"Future things are not naturally known in themselves, because they are not yet beings in act, but only in their causes or through revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A15","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D14","text":"According to natural knowledge, the souls of the dead do not know what occurs among the living, not because of place, but because of segregation of order and intercourse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","CH_GGVC_P_81:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D15","text":"Knowledge of the affairs of the living can come to the dead through incoming souls, Angels, Demons, revelation, or miraculous dispensation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A16","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D16","text":"The text prefers Gregory's opinion, according to which blessed souls know the presence of the living, but does not entirely demonstratively exclude Augustine's doubtfully contrary opinion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A17","CH_GGVC_P_81:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0151","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:D17","text":"Natural knowledge of separated substances indeed brings great perfection, but ultimate happiness consists solely in the vision of God through grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD1","text":"Corporeality is not a prison of the intellect, but an epistemic instrument by which the lowest intellect acquires determinate knowledge proportionate to itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","CH_GGVC_P_81:A8","CH_GGVC_P_81:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD2","text":"Separation simultaneously introduces ontological defect and operational freedom: the soul is outside its natural state, but is freed from turning toward organs.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A2","CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD3","text":"The topology of separated cognition is grounded in mode of being, proportion, and relation, not in the measure of physical space.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","CH_GGVC_P_81:A15","CH_GGVC_P_81:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD4","text":"Intellectual continuity after death is asymmetrical: formal content persists, the sensitive apparatus perishes, and the mode of actualization changes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","CH_GGVC_P_81:A14","CH_GGVC_P_81:D9","CH_GGVC_P_81:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD5","text":"Divine causality constitutes rather than removes natural cognition; the distinction between nature and grace depends on the mode of participation, not on divine origin alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD6","text":"The universality of the cognitive medium does not produce equality of access, because the recipient's capacity renders cognition confused and particular relation selects singulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A10","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","CH_GGVC_P_81:D6","CH_GGVC_P_81:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD7","text":"Death produces neither omniscience nor cognitive emptiness, but knowledge generally diffuse, imperfect, and selective concerning singulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:D6","CH_GGVC_P_81:D8","CH_GGVC_P_81:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD8","text":"Differences of acquired knowledge can remain after death without the conversion of moral order into intellectual order, because these differences are of lesser importance than the prerogatives of glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SD9","text":"The communication of the blessed with the affairs of the living is not a return to bodily intercourse, but knowledge and intervention subordinate to divine justice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A16","CH_GGVC_P_81:A18","CH_GGVC_P_81:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX1","text":"It must be false that the soul's operation is so fixedly determined by its nature that a change of state admits no change in its mode of knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the body is an extrinsic evil whose removal immediately restores the soul's intellectual fullness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the greater intelligibility of an object necessarily produces more perfect knowledge in every intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the incorporeality of the knower removes every limitation, confusion, or selectivity of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX5","text":"It must be false that divine causality and the naturalness of cognition exclude one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX6","text":"It must be false that acquired knowledge is either wholly corporeal or independent of every sensitive formation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX7","text":"It must be false that identity of intelligible species entails identity of mode of understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0122","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX8","text":"It must be false that affective presence, care, or apparition demonstrates direct knowledge of a present thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX9","text":"It must be false that incorporeal cognition is constituted according to the laws of local transmission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:DNX10","text":"It must be false that moral order absorbs all natural or acquired differences among souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX1","text":"The possibility of a human soul naturally complete as a disembodied substance is excluded, because such a position would make union with the body contrary to the soul's good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX2","text":"Beatitude naturally consequent upon death alone is excluded, since separation constitutes neither angelic intellect nor the vision of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX3","text":"Death is excluded as either absolute epistemic consummation or absolute deletion; either extreme would destroy the distinction of state, species, and mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX4","text":"A common natural presence of the living and the dead is unavailable; their communication requires mediation or special ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX5","text":"A univocal measure of divine, angelic, and human cognition is excluded, because the same participation is diversified according to the different modes of recipients.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX6","text":"Universal transparency of singulars is excluded, although the cognitive medium proceeds from a universal cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:SNX7","text":"It is held impossible for a blessed soul to intervene in the affairs of the living apart from the requirement of divine disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS1","text":"The fundamental sequence is: actuality of the thing → mode of being → mode of operating → mode of knowing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A1","CH_GGVC_P_81:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS2","text":"The bifurcation of state is: natural union → phantasms → proper knowledge; separation beyond nature → intelligibles simply → participated species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A3","CH_GGVC_P_81:A4","CH_GGVC_P_81:A5","CH_GGVC_P_81:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS3","text":"The calibration of knowledge is: participated light → efficacy of the recipient → conformity of the object → perfect, imperfect, common, or selective knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A6","CH_GGVC_P_81:A7","CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS4","text":"The distribution of objects is: one's own being → self-knowledge; conforming mode → other souls; higher mode → Angels imperfectly; natural things → commonly; singulars → according to determination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A9","CH_GGVC_P_81:A10","CH_GGVC_P_81:A11","CH_GGVC_P_81:D4","CH_GGVC_P_81:D5","CH_GGVC_P_81:D6","CH_GGVC_P_81:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS5","text":"The continuity of knowledge is: act with phantasms → sensitive disposition and intellectual species → death → loss of disposition and persistence of species → new mode of use.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A12","CH_GGVC_P_81:A13","CH_GGVC_P_81:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS6","text":"The distinction of distance is: actually existing and locally remote object → knowable; future object not yet actually existing → not naturally knowable in itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A15","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:FGS7","text":"The regime of knowledge of the living is: natural segregation → ignorance of present things; mediation or revelation → particular knowledge; vision of glory → knowledge according to the disposition of divine justice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_81:A16","CH_GGVC_P_81:A17","CH_GGVC_P_81:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF1","text":"Apparent dependence on phantasms → distinction of nature and state → principle of mode of being → possibility of separated understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF2","text":"Possibility of separated understanding → hierarchy of recipients → knowledge of self and separated substances → confused knowledge of natural things → selective knowledge of singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF3","text":"Acquired knowledge → division of habit between intellect and sense → persistence of the intellectual part → change in the mode of use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF4","text":"Knowledge of singulars → denial of local impediment → distinction of place from time → segregation of the intercourse of the dead → exceptions of revelation and glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:AF5","text":"Privation of organs → reconstitution of the mode of knowing → limitation by the recipient → intellectual continuity → closure through divine order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME1","text":"The body is reclassified from an extrinsic impediment into a condition of determinate knowledge proportionate to the human intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME2","text":"The opposition between divinely infused cognition and natural cognition collapses; the difference is located in the kind of light and the mode of participation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME3","text":"The perfection of cognition is divided between nobility simply and perfection relative to the capacity of the knower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME4","text":"Knowledge after death is resolved from the opposition of knowledge and ignorance into degrees of perfect, imperfect, common, confused, and selective knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME5","text":"Knowledge of singulars is transferred from the monopoly of sense to intelligible representation, but under the condition of determinate relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME6","text":"The identity of knowledge across states is understood no longer from identity of the mode of operation, but from the persistence of species under a change in the mode of use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME7","text":"Cognitive distance is converted from local measure into a difference of actuality, proportion, and ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME8","text":"The relation of the living and the dead is redescribed from spatial observation into a distinction of ontological interchanges and divine mediations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0154","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0156","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ME9","text":"Death is conceptually transformed from simple corruption of powers into a transition between regimes of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ALT1","text":"At the surface level are examined the possibility of separated understanding, its objects, the persistence of knowledge, distance, and knowledge of the affairs of the living.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ALT2","text":"At the structural level, cognition is governed by the state of the soul, the hierarchy of intellectual light, the mode of the recipient, the distribution of habit, and the ordering of intercourse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ALT3","text":"At the metastrategic level, questions are transferred from absolute disjunctions to distinctions between nature and state, species and mode, place and actuality, nature and grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:ALT4","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, operation is grounded in act and mode of being, whereas future things are distinguished from locally remote things because of their lack of actual being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT1","text":"The body of axioms suffices to restore the possibility, scope, limits, and continuity of the separated soul's knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0133","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT2","text":"The strongest joint is the nexus between mode of being, mode of operating, and the determination of what is received according to the recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT3","text":"The exact mechanism of the impression of divine species and the degrees of common and confused knowledge are not further determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT4","text":"The relativity of perfection to the capacity of the recipient resolves the tension between the mode of understanding simply nobler and bodily union ordered to the soul's good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT5","text":"The ordering of segregation is posited to reconcile the tension between preceding affection as a determination of a singular and ignorance of the affairs of the living, but the manner of this priority is not explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT6","text":"The persistence of the use of knowledge rests on a valid but compressed distinction between the species of act and the mode of acting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT7","text":"Agreement concerning the knowledge of blessed souls is not fully closed, because Gregory's opinion predominates without the full elimination of Augustine's doubt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0151","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT8","text":"Direct contradiction is avoided by distinctions of natural state, natural knowledge, and knowledge of glory, but their boundaries are established by metaphysical authority rather than by analysis of mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_81:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the argument from the appearance of impossibility to graduated knowledge, selectively determined and concluded by divine ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_81:P0152","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_81@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_81:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 90","title":"First Part · Question 89","context":"Chapter 90","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 89"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 89","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 90","order":91,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_82"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_82@R001","sha256":"2879f0eeb2a2f629025d8a2869e2225f62696650adf163b2f09108a17c6952b0","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat utrum anima rationalis originem, causam efficientem et ordinem temporalem habeat qui eius subsistentiae spirituali et muneri formae corporis simul respondeant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS2","text":"Argumentatio a negatione consubstantialitatis divinae incipit: proprietates animae creatae non sunt proprietates Dei actus puri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS3","text":"Ex subsistentia animae rationalis infertur ipsi proprie competere esse et fieri, ideoque eius productio a productione formarum non subsistentium separatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS4","text":"Quia anima neque ex materia corporali neque ex substantia spirituali praeiacente fieri potest, eius productio creatio esse debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS5","text":"Quia creatio est actio sine praesupposito et talis actio soli primo agenti competit, anima rationalis immediate a Deo producitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS6","text":"Quia anima est forma corporis et pars naturae humanae, eius perfectio naturalis non consistit in separatione, sed in unione corporali; ideo non est ante corpus seorsum creata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A1","text":"Deus est actus purus, nihil ab alio accipiens et nullam diversitatem in se habens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A2","text":"Anima humana quandoque intelligit in potentia, scientiam a rebus acquirit et diversas potentias habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A3","text":"Simplicitas essentiae animae non significat quod anima sit suum esse; anima est ens per participationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A4","text":"Simplicia possunt esse diversa seipsis, quamvis non differant differentiis ex quibus componantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A5","text":"Id cui proprie competit esse subsistens, ipsi etiam proprie competit fieri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A6","text":"Formae non subsistentes non proprie fiunt, sed dicuntur fieri per fieri compositorum subsistentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A7","text":"Anima rationalis est forma subsistens cui proprie competit esse et fieri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A8","text":"Anima rationalis non dependet in suo esse a materia corporali et capacitatem materiae corporalis excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A9","text":"Anima rationalis ex materia corporali vel spirituali praeiacente fieri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A10","text":"Creatio est productio sine aliquo praesupposito, et soli primo agenti competit agere nullo praesupposito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A11","text":"Anima est naturaliter forma corporis et pars naturae humanae, cuius perfectio naturalis in unione cum corpore consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A12","text":"Deus res primas instituit in perfecto statu naturae quem species earum exigit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A13","text":"Separatio animae a corpore post mortem provenit ex defectu corporis et non constituit exemplar originarium productionis animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX1","text":"Inspiratio divina non est emissio corporalis alicuius partis substantiae Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX2","text":"Anima non est de substantia Dei, quia potentia cognoscitiva, receptio scientiae et pluralitas potentiarum naturae divinae repugnant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX3","text":"Forma simplex non est propterea actus purus neque Deus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX4","text":"Diversitas inter Deum et mentem humanam non requirit differentias compositivas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX5","text":"Anima rationalis non educitur de potentia materiae, licet sit actus corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX6","text":"Creatio animae rationalis non implicat creationem omnium formarum, quia ceterae formae non sunt subsistentes eodem modo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX7","text":"Angelus non potest animam rationalem producere, etiam si in virtute Dei operari dicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX8","text":"Anima humana non est substantia completa corpori extrinsece adiuncta ad solam administrationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX9","text":"Prioritas animae ad corpus non sequitur ex eius permanentia post mortem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D1","text":"Anima a Deo essentialiter distinguitur, quamvis sit simplex et intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A1","CH_GGVC_P_82:A2","CH_GGVC_P_82:A3","CH_GGVC_P_82:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D2","text":"Anima rationalis proprie fieri dicitur, quia subsistit et proprium esse participatum habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A3","CH_GGVC_P_82:A5","CH_GGVC_P_82:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D3","text":"Productio animae rationalis est creatio, quia nullum subiectum materiale aut spirituale praesupponibile eius productioni sufficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A7","CH_GGVC_P_82:A8","CH_GGVC_P_82:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D4","text":"Creatio animae rationalis non est regula generalis productionis formarum, sed sequitur statum formae subsistentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A5","CH_GGVC_P_82:A6","CH_GGVC_P_82:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D5","text":"Anima rationalis immediate a Deo producitur, quia creatio non est transmutatio et solus Deus agit absque praesupposito.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A9","CH_GGVC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D6","text":"Ordo angelicus potest ad motum, reductionem vel transmutationem pertinere, sed originem creativam animae non mediat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A9","CH_GGVC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D7","text":"Anima non seorsum ante corpus instituitur, quia talis separatio perfectioni naturae humanae originariae non conveniret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A11","CH_GGVC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D8","text":"Supervivere animam corpore destructo non probat eam prius sine corpore exstitisse, quia mors est defectus posterior et non ratio primae institutionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A11","CH_GGVC_P_82:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SD1","text":"Anima rationalis locum duplex obtinet: secundum esse subsistit ultra materiam, secundum naturam autem humanam non est completa sine corpore.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A7","CH_GGVC_P_82:A8","CH_GGVC_P_82:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SD2","text":"Hierarchia causarum secundarum non est scala universalis originum: ubi productio exigit creationem, omnis mediatio creaturalis sistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A9","CH_GGVC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SD3","text":"Dignitas spiritualis animae non decernit ordinem eius temporalem, quia principium temporale determinatur a perfectione propriae naturae compositae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A11","CH_GGVC_P_82:A12","CH_GGVC_P_82:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SD4","text":"Creatio hic definitur non ut productio omnium formarum, sed ut ratio originis entis subsistentis quod ex nullo subiecto praeexistente procedere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A5","CH_GGVC_P_82:A6","CH_GGVC_P_82:A7","CH_GGVC_P_82:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet continuum ontologicum quo anima, propter spiritualitatem vel simplicitatem, pars ipsius divinitatis aestimetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omnis forma eadem ratione ex materia educatur; alioquin subsistentia animae et creatio eius evanescerent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omnes substantiae spirituales unam naturam completam aequaliter participent et solis meritis corporibus aut puritati distribuantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod causalitas superioris ad inferius semper productionem specificam efficiat; transmutatio creaturam causaliter finitam definit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet quod separatio sit status perfectior animae humanae quam unio corporalis; separatio post mortem ex defectu corporis accidit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SNX1","text":"Non admittitur anima humana tamquam natura humana per se completa, cui corpus solum instrumentum vel provincia exterior adiungatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SNX2","text":"Non admittitur catena causalis universa in qua omne novum ens ex aliquo subiecto priore per mutationem explicetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SNX3","text":"Non admittitur prioritas temporalis ut signum necessarium dignitatis metaphysicae; anima Angelis assimilatur intellectualitate, non ordine suae productionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SNX4","text":"Non admittitur mors ut principium interpretativum primae conditionis humanae; status originarius per exigentiam naturae integrae, non per defectum posteriorem, mensuratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:FGS1","text":"Potentia cognoscitiva + esse participatum + pluralitas potentiarum → distinctio animae a Deo → exclusio consubstantialitatis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:FGS2","text":"Forma subsistens + esse a materia independens + impossibilitas materiae praeiacentes → creatio necessaria → actio primi agentis → productio divina immediata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:FGS3","text":"Anima ut forma corporis + anima ut pars naturae humanae + institutio prima in perfectione naturali → exclusio animae praeexistentis → creatio simul cum corpore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:FGS4","text":"Subsistentia animae post mortem + mors ut defectus corporis → permanentia posterior non convertitur in prioritatem originariam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AF1","text":"Inspiratio divina figurata et simplicitas animae → distinctio inter participationem creatam et actum purum → anima non est de substantia Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AF2","text":"Subsistentia animae → proprietas essendi et fiendi → exclusio eductionis ex materia → creatio animae rationalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AF3","text":"Creatio sine praesupposito → exclusio transmutationis et mediationis angelicae → Deus solus immediate causat animam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AF4","text":"Anima forma corporis et pars humanae naturae → perfectio originaria naturae compositae → anima non praeexistit corpori → creatur cum corpore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME1","text":"Distinctio Deus–anima non per compositionem differentiarum, sed per oppositionem inter actum purum et ens participatum, fit cogitabilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME2","text":"Creatio reclassificatur ut productio propria subsistentis, non ut explicatio indiscriminata omnis formae naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME3","text":"Anima rationalis inter formas materiales et substantias spirituales completas collocatur: subsistit sicut ens spirituale, sed naturaliter corpori unitur sicut forma humana.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME4","text":"Ordo causalis dividitur inter transmutationem, quae causis creatis convenit, et creationem, quae soli Deo reservatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME5","text":"Ordo temporalis primae productionis non ex analogia cum Angelis neque ex statu animae separatae, sed ex perfectione naturae humanae compositae determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ALT1","text":"Surface — Anima humana non est divina, creatur, immediate a Deo producitur et non ante corpus seorsum instituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ALT2","text":"Structural — Ratio productionis sequitur modum essendi: forma subsistens creatur; forma non subsistens in fieri compositi includitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones ex imagine respirationis, simplicitate, ordine hierarchico, perfectione spirituali et permanentia post mortem solvuntur per distinctiones inter participationem et identitatem, creationem et transmutationem, naturam et defectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Esse subsistens animae fundat originem creatam, sed forma corporalis animae ordinat originem temporalem ad corpus; subsistentia separata posterior non instituit naturam humanam primam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de actu puro, esse participato et potentia cognoscitiva sufficienter sustinent exclusionem animae ex substantia Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de subsistentia, independentia a materia et creatione sine praesupposito sufficienter restituunt transitum a natura animae ad immediatam causalitatem divinam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT3","text":"Structura firmissime consistit in nexus: modus essendi → modus fiendi → genus causalitatis competentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT4","text":"Commissura principalis est duplex positio animae: anima subsistit per se, sed non habet perfectionem naturalem humanam nisi ut forma corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT5","text":"Ambiguitas residua spectat expositionem Augustini de operibus sex dierum, quam textus tolerabilem conditionaliter iudicat, sed non assertive recipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0063","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT6","text":"Motus argumentationis servatur, si prima separatio Dei ab anima, deinde creatio animae, postea causalitas divina immediata, ultimo simultas animae et corporis retinentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165306359464Z_4cd6e249","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 90","source_sha256":"2879f0eeb2a2f629025d8a2869e2225f62696650adf163b2f09108a17c6952b0","sha256":"466b26be4ad1148fcef692b7d49113fa854d3c2501a824f5b2a4a7c0be068b0b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:53:06.360514+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS1","text":"The question determines whether the rational soul has an origin, an efficient cause, and a temporal order that correspond simultaneously to its spiritual subsistence and its office as the form of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS2","text":"The argument begins from the denial of divine consubstantiality: the properties of the created soul are not the properties of God, pure act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS3","text":"From the subsistence of the rational soul it is inferred that being and coming-to-be properly belong to it; therefore, its production is distinguished from the production of non-subsistent forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS4","text":"Because the soul can come to be neither from bodily matter nor from pre-existing spiritual substance, its production must be creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS5","text":"Because creation is action without a presupposed subject, and such action belongs to the first agent alone, the rational soul is produced immediately by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AS6","text":"Because the soul is the form of the body and a part of human nature, its natural perfection does not consist in separation but in bodily union; therefore, it was not created separately before the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A1","text":"God is pure act, receiving nothing from another and having no diversity within Himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A2","text":"The human soul sometimes understands potentially, acquires knowledge from things, and has diverse powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A3","text":"The simplicity of the soul's essence does not signify that the soul is its own being; the soul is a being by participation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A4","text":"Simple things can differ through themselves, although they do not differ by differences from which they are composed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A5","text":"That to which subsistent being properly belongs, to it coming-to-be also properly belongs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A6","text":"Non-subsistent forms do not properly come to be, but are said to come to be through the coming-to-be of subsistent composites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A7","text":"The rational soul is a subsistent form to which being and coming-to-be properly belong.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A8","text":"The rational soul does not depend in its being on bodily matter and exceeds the capacity of bodily matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A9","text":"The rational soul cannot come to be from pre-existing bodily or spiritual matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A10","text":"Creation is production without any presupposed subject, and acting without a presupposed subject belongs to the first agent alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A11","text":"The soul is naturally the form of the body and a part of human nature, whose natural perfection consists in union with the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A12","text":"God established first things in the perfect state of nature required by their species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:A13","text":"The separation of the soul from the body after death proceeds from a defect of the body and does not constitute the original model of the soul's production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX1","text":"Divine inspiration is not a bodily emission of some part of God's substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX2","text":"The soul is not of God's substance, because cognitive potentiality, the reception of knowledge, and a plurality of powers are incompatible with the divine nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX3","text":"A simple form is not thereby pure act or God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX4","text":"The diversity between God and the human mind does not require compositional differences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX5","text":"The rational soul is not educed from the potentiality of matter, although it is the act of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX6","text":"The creation of the rational soul does not entail the creation of all forms, because other forms are not subsistent in the same way.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX7","text":"An angel cannot produce a rational soul, even if he is said to act by the power of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX8","text":"The human soul is not a complete substance extrinsically joined to the body for administration alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:NX9","text":"The priority of the soul to the body does not follow from its permanence after death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D1","text":"The soul is essentially distinct from God, although it is simple and intellectual.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A1","CH_GGVC_P_82:A2","CH_GGVC_P_82:A3","CH_GGVC_P_82:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D2","text":"The rational soul is properly said to come to be because it subsists and has its own participated being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A3","CH_GGVC_P_82:A5","CH_GGVC_P_82:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D3","text":"The production of the rational soul is creation, because no presupposable material or spiritual subject suffices for its production.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A7","CH_GGVC_P_82:A8","CH_GGVC_P_82:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D4","text":"The creation of the rational soul is not the general rule for the production of forms, but follows from the status of a subsistent form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A5","CH_GGVC_P_82:A6","CH_GGVC_P_82:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D5","text":"The rational soul is produced immediately by God, because creation is not transmutation and God alone acts without a presupposed subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A9","CH_GGVC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D6","text":"The angelic order can pertain to motion, reduction, or transmutation, but does not mediate the creative origin of the soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A9","CH_GGVC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D7","text":"The soul is not established separately before the body, because such separation would not accord with the perfection of original human nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A11","CH_GGVC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:D8","text":"The soul's survival after the body is destroyed does not prove that it previously existed without a body, because death is a subsequent defect and not the principle of its first establishment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A11","CH_GGVC_P_82:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SD1","text":"The rational soul occupies a twofold position: according to being, it subsists beyond matter; according to human nature, however, it is not complete without the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A7","CH_GGVC_P_82:A8","CH_GGVC_P_82:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SD2","text":"The hierarchy of secondary causes is not a universal ladder of origins: where production requires creation, every creaturely mediation ceases.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A9","CH_GGVC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SD3","text":"The spiritual dignity of the soul does not determine its temporal order, because the temporal principle is determined by the perfection of its own composite nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A11","CH_GGVC_P_82:A12","CH_GGVC_P_82:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SD4","text":"Creation is here defined not as the production of all forms, but as the account of the origin of a subsistent being that can proceed from no pre-existing subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_82:A5","CH_GGVC_P_82:A6","CH_GGVC_P_82:A7","CH_GGVC_P_82:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX1","text":"An ontological continuum by which the soul, on account of spirituality or simplicity, is judged to be a part of divinity itself must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX2","text":"It must be false that every form is educed from matter in the same manner; otherwise the subsistence of the soul and its creation would vanish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX3","text":"It must be false that all spiritual substances equally participate in one complete nature and are assigned to bodies or to purity solely according to merits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the causality of a superior over an inferior always effects specific production; transmutation defines the causally finite creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:DNX5","text":"It must be false that separation is a more perfect state of the human soul than bodily union; separation after death occurs through a defect of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SNX1","text":"The human soul is not admitted as a human nature complete in itself, to which the body is joined merely as an instrument or external province.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SNX2","text":"A universal causal chain is not admitted in which every new being is explained from some prior subject through change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SNX3","text":"Temporal priority is not admitted as a necessary sign of metaphysical dignity; the soul is assimilated to angels in intellectuality, not in the order of its production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:SNX4","text":"Death is not admitted as the interpretive principle of the first human condition; the original state is measured by the requirement of integral nature, not by a subsequent defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:FGS1","text":"Cognitive potentiality + participated being + plurality of powers → distinction of the soul from God → exclusion of divine consubstantiality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:FGS2","text":"Subsistent form + being independent of matter + impossibility of pre-existing matter → necessary creation → action of the first agent → immediate divine production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:FGS3","text":"Soul as form of the body + soul as part of human nature + first establishment in natural perfection → exclusion of the pre-existent soul → creation together with the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:FGS4","text":"Subsistence of the soul after death + death as a defect of the body → subsequent permanence is not converted into original priority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AF1","text":"Figurative divine inspiration and the soul's simplicity → distinction between created participation and pure act → the soul is not of God's substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AF2","text":"Subsistence of the soul → propriety of being and coming-to-be → exclusion of eduction from matter → creation of the rational soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AF3","text":"Creation without a presupposed subject → exclusion of transmutation and angelic mediation → God alone immediately causes the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:AF4","text":"Soul as form of the body and part of human nature → original perfection of composite nature → the soul does not pre-exist the body → it is created with the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME1","text":"The distinction between God and soul becomes thinkable not through a composition of differences, but through the opposition between pure act and participated being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME2","text":"Creation is reclassified as the proper production of a subsistent being, not as an indiscriminate explanation of every natural form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME3","text":"The rational soul is placed between material forms and complete spiritual substances: it subsists as a spiritual being, but is naturally united to the body as a human form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME4","text":"The causal order is divided between transmutation, which belongs to created causes, and creation, which is reserved to God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ME5","text":"The temporal order of first production is determined not from analogy with angels nor from the state of the separated soul, but from the perfection of composite human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ALT1","text":"Surface — The human soul is not divine, is created, is produced immediately by God, and is not established separately before the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ALT2","text":"Structural — The mode of production follows the mode of being: a subsistent form is created; a non-subsistent form is included in the coming-to-be of the composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections from the image of breathing, simplicity, hierarchical order, spiritual perfection, and permanence after death are resolved through distinctions between participation and identity, creation and transmutation, nature and defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The soul's subsistent being grounds its created origin, but the soul's bodily form orders its temporal origin to the body; subsequent separated subsistence does not establish original human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning pure act, participated being, and cognitive potentiality sufficiently sustain the exclusion of the soul from God's substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning subsistence, independence from matter, and creation without a presupposed subject sufficiently reconstruct the transition from the nature of the soul to immediate divine causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT3","text":"The structure rests most firmly on the nexus: mode of being → mode of coming-to-be → kind of appropriate causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT4","text":"The principal juncture is the soul's twofold position: the soul subsists through itself, yet does not possess natural human perfection except as the form of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT5","text":"The residual ambiguity concerns Augustine's exposition on the works of the six days, which the text judges conditionally tolerable but does not affirmatively accept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0063","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_82:MRT6","text":"The movement of the argument is preserved if first the separation of God from the soul, then the creation of the soul, afterward immediate divine causality, and finally the simultaneity of soul and body are retained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_82:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_82@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_82:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 91","title":"First Part · Question 90","context":"Chapter 91","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 90"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 90","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 91","order":92,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_83"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_83@R001","sha256":"72379ec9ad417f597cc74b66bb5acdbefa88fa001738ece84879e36aca1cdbc2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS1","text":"Quaestio productionem corporis primi hominis per quattuor nexus constituit: materiam, causam efficientem, dispositionem finalem, modumque et ordinem a Scriptura significatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS2","text":"Dignitas corporis humani non ex nobilitate absoluta materiae neque ex maxima distantia a materia pendet, sed ex proportione ad animam rationalem eiusque operationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS3","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica et reconstructiva apparentem inferioritatem materialem in aptitudinem teleologicam convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS4","text":"Corpus primi hominis ex limo terrae formatur quia corpus elementare et aequabiliter mixtum requiritur ad medium inter substantias spirituales et corporales constituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS5","text":"Prima formatio corporis humani non ad causam creatam reducitur, quia nulla forma materialis humana praeexsistens erat ex qua compositum eiusdem speciei generari posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS6","text":"Comparatio hominis cum animalibus specialiter instructis ostendit corpus humanum ordinari ad cognitionem, rationem, manus et locutionem potius quam ad maximam potentiam sensitivam, velocitatem aut defensionem naturalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS7","text":"Locutiones Scripturae de formatione, inspiratione et pluralitate divina per distinctiones teleologicas, trinitarias et hylomorphicas explicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A1","text":"Deus rebus naturalibus perfectionem dat secundum modum et finem proprium, non secundum perfectionem simpliciter consideratam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A2","text":"Materia est propter formam, et instrumenta corporis sunt propter operationes formae agentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","text":"Anima rationalis est forma corporis humani et finis proximus dispositionis eius corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A4","text":"Homo secundum animam ad substantias spirituales pertinet, secundum corpus elementa materialia continet, atque ideo minor mundus dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","text":"Mixtio corporis humani aequalitatem requirit: inferiora elementa abundant secundum substantiam, superiora secundum virtutem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A6","text":"Cognitio rationalis a sensibus incipit, et organa sensuum ex corpore passibili ac proportionato formari debent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A7","text":"Organum sensus aut contrariis caret aut medium inter contraria constituitur, ut ea quae percipit in potentia recipere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A8","text":"Forma in materia per causam creatam non producitur nisi per generationem compositi ex composito et per formam materialem praeexistentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A9","text":"Solus Deus materiam creando producere potest atque formam in materia inducere sine adminiculo formae materialis praeexistentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A10","text":"Corpus primi hominis nullum corpus eiusdem speciei praeexigens habuit, ex cuius virtute per generationem formari posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A11","text":"Motus caelestis transmutationes naturales causat, non autem effectus qui praeter ordinem naturae sola virtute divina fiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A12","text":"Rationes causales in creaturis vel potentiam activam simul et passivam vel potentiam passivam tantum significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A13","text":"Ratio et manus homini vicem armorum, tegumentorum et instrumentorum determinatorum supplent, quia natura rationalis infinita instrumenta sibi parare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A14","text":"Prima institutio humana non ponenda est ut productio temporalis corporis sine anima vel animae sine corpore, quia utrumque est pars naturae humanae et corpus ab anima dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A15","text":"Pluralitas in locutione «faciamus hominem» pluralitatem personarum divinarum significat, non consortium angelorum in causalitate productionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A16","text":"Locutio de inspiratione in faciem situm animae non determinat, sed operationes vitae in facie per sensus manifestas designat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A17","text":"Distinctio imaginis divinae et sexus corporalis temporalem prioritatem animae ante sextum diem non imponit, quia anima et corpus diversimode intra rationes causales intelligi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX1","text":"Dignitas hominis non exigit ut corpus eius absque materia praeiacente formetur, quamvis materia ipsa per creationem a Deo sit producta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX2","text":"«Limus terrae» non significat corpus humanum sola terra constare neque alia elementa ex eius compositione excludi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX3","text":"Corpus caeleste, quamvis simpliciter nobilius corpore terrestri, non est propter impassibilitatem suam materia conveniens organis cognitionis sensitivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX4","text":"Quinta essentia et lux corporea neque materialiter corpori humano admittuntur neque animae rationali ut medium unionis necessarium ponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX5","text":"Angelus formam materialem novam sine seminibus vel forma materiali praeexistente inducere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX6","text":"Causalitas caelestis non sufficit ad generationem animalium perfectorum ex sola materia disposita, nec ad formationem primi hominis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX7","text":"Optima dispositio corporis humani non coincidit cum excellentia absoluta in odoratu, visu, auditu, velocitate aut defensione naturali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX8","text":"Defectus apparens corporis non est defectus simpliciter, si ex necessitate materiae sequitur dispositionem ad finem rationalem requisitam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX9","text":"Statura recta non assimilatur staturae plantarum, quia homo per caput ad superius mundi et per pedes ad inferius mundi ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX10","text":"«Faciamus hominem» non est colloquium Dei cum angelis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX11","text":"«Inspiravit spiraculum vitae» non designat infusionem temporaliter posteriorem Spiritus Sancti nec corpus prius sine anima completum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX12","text":"«In faciem eius» non localizat animam in facie nec removet animam a toto corpore et a corde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D1","text":"Corpus humanum terrestre est non quia forma eius sit inferior, sed quia mixtio elementaris temperata aptissima est animae rationali per sensus operanti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A2","CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D2","text":"Passibilitas corporis subcaelestis condicionem epistemicam cognitionis humanae constituit, dum impassibilitas corporis caelestis hanc condicionem impedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6","CH_GGVC_P_83:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D3","text":"Nomen «limus» terram et aquam secundum abundantiam corporalem significat, non totam physicam corporis humani compositionem exhaustive determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A4","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D4","text":"Homo medium inter spiritualia et corporalia constituit quia anima rationalis spiritualis corpori elementari et sensitivo unitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A4","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D5","text":"Formatio primi corporis humani immediate divina est, dum generatio humana posterior causis creatis et caelesti cooperationi secundum ordinem naturalem attribui potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A8","CH_GGVC_P_83:A9","CH_GGVC_P_83:A10","CH_GGVC_P_83:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D6","text":"Ministerium angelicum circa corpora possibile est, sed non constituit causalitatem principalem quae materiam creat aut primam formam humanam producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A8","CH_GGVC_P_83:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D7","text":"Praeexistentia rei in rationibus causalibus secundum potentiam passivam tantum non transfert ad creaturas potestatem illam rem producendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A9","CH_GGVC_P_83:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D8","text":"Inaequalitas hominis cum animalibus in sensibus exterioribus et velocitate compensatur per aequalitatem complexionis, sensus interiores, rationem et manus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A1","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","CH_GGVC_P_83:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D9","text":"Statura recta cognitionem sensibilem universalem, libertatem manuum, dispositionem cerebri et locutionem simul possibilitates corporales facit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A2","CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D10","text":"Specialis modus Scripturae in productione hominis intentionem finalem, imaginem divinam et pluralitatem personarum significat sine multiplicatione causarum efficientium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A1","CH_GGVC_P_83:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D11","text":"Inspiratio spiraculi vitae explicat formationem hominis ut unitatem corporis et animae, non ut successionem duarum productionum separatarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A14","CH_GGVC_P_83:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D12","text":"Differentia inter animam actu productam et corpus secundum rationes causales intellectum imaginis et sexus componere potest sine animae creatione ante sextum diem posita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A12","CH_GGVC_P_83:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD1","text":"Anthropologia constituitur ut mediata cosmologia: homo non est materiae terrestris exceptio, sed locus in quo spirituale, caeleste, elementare et sensitivum ordinate conveniunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A4","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD2","text":"Limitatio materialis corporis humani non est exterior animae rationali, sed condicio positiva qua cognitio intellectualis a sensibilibus incipiens fieri potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6","CH_GGVC_P_83:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD3","text":"Causalitas mundi dividitur inter ordinem naturalem reproductivum et actionem divinam quae materiam, formas primas et effectus supra naturam sine causis creatis sufficientibus producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A8","CH_GGVC_P_83:A9","CH_GGVC_P_83:A10","CH_GGVC_P_83:A11","CH_GGVC_P_83:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD4","text":"Perfectio organica non est cumulatio omnium excellentiarum animalium, sed ordinatio finita in qua quaedam potentiae imminutæ sunt ut operationes superiores possibilitentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A1","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","CH_GGVC_P_83:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD5","text":"Universalitas rationis in corpore humano per universalitatem instrumentalem exprimitur: manus non sunt unum instrumentum determinatum, sed potentia instrumenta infinita efficiendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A2","CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD6","text":"Exegesis Scripturae hic functionem metaphysicam habet: locutiones de Deo distinguunt finem humanum, originem divinam, unitatem compositi et pluralitatem personarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A14","CH_GGVC_P_83:A15","CH_GGVC_P_83:A16","CH_GGVC_P_83:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar quod dignitatem formae ex nobilitate physica materiae vel ex maiori distantia a potentia materiali deducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar rationalitatis separatae a conditionibus sensitivis, passibilibus et instrumentalibus corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod potentia passiva materiae vel ratio causalis in creatura posita ad potentiam activam creaturae producendi sufficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar causalitatis creaturae clausae, in quo omnis forma materialis ex causis naturalibus vel angelicis sine origine divina immediata derivari possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar organismi perfecti quod perfectionem ex armis innatis, tegumentis, velocitate et sensibus exterioribus acutissimis unice aestimat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar hominis ut aggregati temporalis, in quo corpus prius completum animam postea recipiat vel anima ante corpus humanum perfecte subsistat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX7","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar litterae Scripturae quod pluralitatem divinam in pluralitatem agentium creatorum, aut inspirationem in motum corporalem localem resolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit perfectionem creatam ut possessionem simultaneam omnium bonorum sine detrimento, limitatione materiae aut ordine ad finem determinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit continuum naturalisticum in quo prima institutio speciei humanae eadem causalitate explicatur qua generatio posterior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit dualismum in quo anima rationalis et corpus eius duas res complete constitutas, solum posterius coniungendas, efficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SNX4","text":"Systema excludit mensuram naturalem quae hominem solum per comparationem competitivam cum animalibus particulariter specializatis iudicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS1","text":"Perfectio divina operum → perfectio relativa ad finem proprium → recusatio perfectionis corporalis simpliciter mensuratae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS2","text":"Anima rationalis ut forma et finis corporis → operationes intellectui sensibus innixae → necessitas corporis passibilis, temperati et organice dispositi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS3","text":"Necessitas aequalitatis mixtionis → abundantia elementorum inferiorum secundum substantiam et superiorum secundum virtutem → corpus ex limo terrae nominatum et minor mundus constitutus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS4","text":"Regula formae materialis ex forma materiali → absentia corporis humani praeexistentis → impossibilitas productionis primae per virtutem creatam → formatio immediata a Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS5","text":"Comparatio cum animalibus specializatis → distinctio finis rationalis et finis particularis → imminutio sensus exterioris, armorum aut velocitatis reclassificata ut condicio operationum superiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS6","text":"Ambiguitas locutionum Scripturae → distinctio causae efficientis, personarum divinarum, formae animae et manifestationis vitalis → unitas formationis humanae doctrinaliter servata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS7","text":"Corpus elementare et sensibile + anima rationalis + causalitas divina immediata + dispositio teleologica → homo ut compositum rationi, cognitioni et dominio instrumentalium operationum aptum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AF1","text":"Nobilitas materiae postulata → distinctio nobilitatis simplicis et convenientiae finalis → limus elementaris et aequabilis → corpus humanum ut minor mundus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AF2","text":"Causae creatae et caelestes postulatae → regula generationis formae materialis → absentia antecedentis corporis humani → productio primi corporis immediate divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AF3","text":"Defectus sensuum, armorum et staturae obiecti → perfectio relativa ad animam rationalem → ratio, manus, sensus interiores et statura recta → dispositio humana optima secundum finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AF4","text":"Inconvenientia sermonis Scripturae obiecta → distinctio intentionis, Trinitatis, formae animae et manifestationis vitalis → narratio productionis humanae metaphysice cohaerens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter corpus nobile et corpus terrestre dissolvitur, quia nobilitas corporis ad formam et finem, non ad materiam simpliciter nobiliorem, refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME2","text":"Corpus humanum reclassificatur ut nexus cosmicus inter spirituale, caeleste, elementare et sensitivum, non ut pars isolata unius ordinis corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME3","text":"Causae distinguuntur secundum capacitatem producendi: Deus creat materiam et primam formam in materia; causae naturales generant ex praeexistenti; angeli ministeria limitata exhibere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME4","text":"Oppositio inter corporis defectum et corporis perfectionem dissolvitur, quia imminutio specializata in conditionem instrumentalis universalitatis convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME5","text":"Distinctio inter potentiam activam et passivam novum campum causalitatis aperit, in quo praeexistentia possibilitatis non importat praeexistentiam causae creatae sufficientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME6","text":"Termini Scripturae «faciamus», «inspiravit» et «in faciem» reordinantur ut signa intentionis, pluralitatis personalis, formae animae et manifestationis vitae, non ut narrationes causales univoce materiales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus materiam, auctorem, dispositionem et ordinem productionis corporis primi hominis determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ALT2","text":"Structural — Corpus explicatur per relationem formae et materiae, aequalitatem mixtionis, ordinem causarum et finalitatem instrumentorum corporalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones ex nobilitate, efficientia causali et defectu comparativo non directe negantur, sed mensurae iudicii ad finem animae rationalis transferuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Prima formatio distinguitur a generatione naturali, et unitas animae et corporis opponitur successioni temporali duarum substantiarum complete constitutarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de finalitate relativa, anima ut forma, mixtione elementari et causalitate formarum materialium sufficiunt ad responsa de materia, causa efficiente et dispositione corporis regeneranda.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT2","text":"Firmissimus nexus systematis est relatio inter animam rationalem et corpus instrumentale, quae materiam, aequalitatem complexionis, manus, staturam rectam et defectus apparentes in uno principio colligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT3","text":"Systema pendet a physica elementorum, a doctrina complexionis et a principio quod cognitio rationalis per sensus corporales incipit; haec principia interne assumuntur potius quam ulterius demonstrantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT4","text":"Commissura inter actionem immediatam Dei et ministerium angelorum servatur per distinctionem causae principalis et ministerii, sed extensio positiva huius ministerii non plene determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT5","text":"Commissura delicata manet inter negationem productionis animae sine corpore et expositionem Augustini quae animam in actu, corpus autem secundum rationes causales distinguit; solutio pendet ab aequivocatione inter ordinem causalitatis et ordinem temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT6","text":"Exegesis quarti articuli cohaeret si locutiones Scripturae doctrinaliter distinctivas habentur, sed non ex sola grammatica demonstratur cur unaquaeque locutio ad significationem metaphysicam determinatam referenda sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat motum verum textus: apparentia inferioritatis materialis vel corporalis → distinctio causalis et finalis → ordinatio corporis ad animam rationalem → affirmatio formationis divinae immediatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165338849750Z_ee2803a6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 91","source_sha256":"72379ec9ad417f597cc74b66bb5acdbefa88fa001738ece84879e36aca1cdbc2","sha256":"a0398d22cca037ab54a69ae3f9056da4e0c3f27f89bf7fc1f1b7b4728d784ac8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:53:38.850923+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS1","text":"The question establishes the production of the first human being's body through four connections: matter, efficient cause, final disposition, and the mode and order signified by Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS2","text":"The dignity of the human body depends neither on the absolute nobility of matter nor on the greatest distance from matter, but on its proportion to the rational soul and its operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS3","text":"Metaphysical and reconstructive argumentation converts apparent material inferiority into teleological aptitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS4","text":"The body of the first human being is formed from the slime of the earth because an elemental and evenly mixed body is required in order to constitute a mean between spiritual and corporeal substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS5","text":"The first formation of the human body is not reducible to a created cause, because no pre-existing material human form existed from which a composite of the same species could be generated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS6","text":"Comparison of man with specially equipped animals shows that the human body is ordered to knowledge, reason, hands, and speech rather than to the greatest sensory power, speed, or natural defense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AS7","text":"Scriptural expressions concerning formation, inspiration, and divine plurality are explained through teleological, Trinitarian, and hylomorphic distinctions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A1","text":"God gives natural things perfection according to their proper mode and end, not according to perfection considered simply.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A2","text":"Matter is for the sake of form, and the instruments of the body are for the sake of the operations of the acting form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","text":"The rational soul is the form of the human body and the proximate end of its bodily disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A4","text":"Man belongs to spiritual substances according to the soul, contains material elements according to the body, and is therefore called a lesser world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","text":"The mixture of the human body requires equality: the lower elements abound according to substance, the higher according to power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A6","text":"Rational knowledge begins from the senses, and the organs of sense must be formed from a passible and proportioned body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A7","text":"An organ of sense either lacks contraries or is constituted as a mean between contraries, so that it can receive in potency what it perceives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A8","text":"Form in matter is not produced through a created cause except through the generation of a composite from a composite and through a pre-existing material form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A9","text":"God alone can produce matter by creating and induce form in matter without the aid of a pre-existing material form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A10","text":"The body of the first human being had no pre-existing body of the same species from whose power it could be formed through generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A11","text":"Celestial motion causes natural transmutations, but not effects that occur beyond the order of nature through divine power alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A12","text":"Causal reasons in creatures signify either both active and passive potency or passive potency alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A13","text":"Reason and hands supply man with the place of arms, coverings, and determinate instruments, because rational nature can prepare infinite instruments for itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A14","text":"The first human institution must not be posited as the temporal production of a body without a soul or of a soul without a body, because each is a part of human nature and the body depends on the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A15","text":"The plurality in the expression «faciamus hominem» signifies the plurality of divine persons, not the partnership of angels in the causality of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A16","text":"The expression concerning inspiration does not determine the location of the soul, but designates the operations of life manifest in the face through the senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:A17","text":"The distinction between the divine image and bodily sex does not impose the temporal priority of the soul before the sixth day, because soul and body can be understood differently within causal reasons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX1","text":"The dignity of man does not require that his body be formed without pre-existing matter, although matter itself was produced by God through creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX2","text":"«Limus terrae» does not signify that the human body consists of earth alone, nor does it exclude the other elements from its composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX3","text":"The celestial body, although simply nobler than the terrestrial body, is not, on account of its impassibility, matter suitable for the organs of sensory knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX4","text":"The fifth essence and corporeal light are admitted neither materially into the human body nor posited as a necessary medium of union for the rational soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX5","text":"An angel cannot induce a new material form without seeds or a pre-existing material form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX6","text":"Celestial causality does not suffice for the generation of perfect animals from matter alone disposed, nor for the formation of the first human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX7","text":"The optimal disposition of the human body does not coincide with absolute excellence in smell, sight, hearing, speed, or natural defense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX8","text":"An apparent bodily defect is not a defect simply, if it follows from the necessity of matter for the disposition required for the rational end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX9","text":"An upright stature is not assimilated to the stature of plants, because man is ordered through his head to the higher part of the world and through his feet to the lower part of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX10","text":"«Faciamus hominem» is not a conversation of God with angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX11","text":"«Inspiravit spiraculum vitae» does not designate a temporally later infusion of the Holy Spirit, nor a body previously complete without a soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:NX12","text":"«In faciem eius» neither locates the soul in the face nor removes the soul from the whole body and from the heart.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D1","text":"The human body is terrestrial not because its form is inferior, but because a tempered elemental mixture is most suitable to the rational soul operating through the senses.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A2","CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D2","text":"The passibility of the subcelestial body constitutes the epistemic condition of human knowledge, whereas the impassibility of the celestial body impedes this condition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6","CH_GGVC_P_83:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D3","text":"The name «limus» signifies earth and water according to bodily abundance; it does not exhaustively determine the entire physical composition of the human body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A4","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D4","text":"Man constitutes a mean between spiritual and corporeal things because the spiritual rational soul is united to an elemental and sentient body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A4","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D5","text":"The formation of the first human body is immediately divine, whereas subsequent human generation can be attributed to created causes and celestial cooperation according to the natural order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A8","CH_GGVC_P_83:A9","CH_GGVC_P_83:A10","CH_GGVC_P_83:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D6","text":"Angelic ministry concerning bodies is possible, but does not constitute the principal causality that creates matter or produces the first human form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A8","CH_GGVC_P_83:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D7","text":"The pre-existence of a thing in causal reasons according to passive potency alone does not transfer to creatures the power to produce that thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A9","CH_GGVC_P_83:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D8","text":"Man's inequality with animals in the external senses and speed is compensated by equality of complexion, the internal senses, reason, and hands.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A1","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","CH_GGVC_P_83:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D9","text":"Upright stature simultaneously makes possible universal sensible knowledge, freedom of the hands, the disposition of the brain, and speech.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A2","CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D10","text":"The special mode of Scripture in the production of man signifies final intention, the divine image, and plurality of persons without multiplication of efficient causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A1","CH_GGVC_P_83:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D11","text":"The inspiration of the breath of life explains the formation of man as a unity of body and soul, not as a succession of two separate productions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A14","CH_GGVC_P_83:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:D12","text":"The difference between the soul actually produced and the body according to causal reasons can reconcile the understanding of image and sex without positing the creation of the soul before the sixth day.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A12","CH_GGVC_P_83:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD1","text":"Anthropology is constituted as mediated cosmology: man is not an exception to terrestrial matter, but the place in which the spiritual, celestial, elemental, and sentient meet in an ordered way.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A4","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD2","text":"The material limitation of the human body is not external to the rational soul, but the positive condition through which intellectual knowledge beginning from sensible things can occur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A6","CH_GGVC_P_83:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD3","text":"The causality of the world is divided between the reproductive natural order and divine action, which produces matter, first forms, and effects above nature without sufficient created causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A8","CH_GGVC_P_83:A9","CH_GGVC_P_83:A10","CH_GGVC_P_83:A11","CH_GGVC_P_83:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD4","text":"Organic perfection is not the accumulation of all animal excellences, but a finite ordering in which certain powers are diminished so that higher operations may be made possible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A1","CH_GGVC_P_83:A5","CH_GGVC_P_83:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD5","text":"The universality of reason is expressed in the human body through instrumental universality: hands are not one determinate instrument, but a power of making infinite instruments.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A2","CH_GGVC_P_83:A3","CH_GGVC_P_83:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SD6","text":"The exegesis of Scripture here has a metaphysical function: expressions concerning God distinguish the human end, divine origin, unity of the composite, and plurality of persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_83:A14","CH_GGVC_P_83:A15","CH_GGVC_P_83:A16","CH_GGVC_P_83:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX1","text":"The model that deduces the dignity of form from the physical nobility of matter or from greater distance from material potency must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX2","text":"A model of rationality separated from the sensory, passible, and instrumental conditions of the body must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the passive potency of matter or a causal reason posited in a creature suffices for the active potency of a creature to produce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX4","text":"The model of a closed creaturely causality, in which every material form can be derived from natural or angelic causes without immediate divine origin, must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX5","text":"The model of the perfect organism that assesses perfection solely from innate arms, coverings, speed, and most acute external senses must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX6","text":"The model of man as a temporal aggregate, in which a previously complete body receives the soul later or the soul subsists perfectly before the human body, must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:DNX7","text":"The model of the letter of Scripture that resolves divine plurality into a plurality of created agents, or inspiration into local bodily motion, must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SNX1","text":"The system excludes created perfection as the simultaneous possession of all goods without loss, material limitation, or order to a determinate end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SNX2","text":"The system excludes a naturalistic continuum in which the first institution of the human species is explained by the same causality as subsequent generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SNX3","text":"The system excludes a dualism in which the rational soul and its body make two completely constituted things, to be joined only subsequently.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:SNX4","text":"The system excludes a natural measure that judges man only through competitive comparison with particularly specialized animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS1","text":"Divine perfection of works → perfection relative to the proper end → rejection of bodily perfection measured simply.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS2","text":"Rational soul as form and end of the body → operations of the intellect relying on the senses → necessity of a passible, tempered, and organically disposed body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS3","text":"Necessity of equality of mixture → abundance of lower elements according to substance and of higher according to power → body called from the slime of the earth and constituted as a lesser world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS4","text":"Rule of material form from material form → absence of a pre-existing human body → impossibility of first production through created power → immediate formation by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS5","text":"Comparison with specialized animals → distinction of rational end and particular end → diminution of external sense, arms, or speed reclassified as a condition of higher operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS6","text":"Ambiguity of Scriptural expressions → distinction of efficient cause, divine persons, form of the soul, and vital manifestation → unity of human formation doctrinally preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:FGS7","text":"Elemental and sentient body + rational soul + immediate divine causality + teleological disposition → man as a composite suited to reason, knowledge, and mastery of instrumental operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AF1","text":"Nobility of matter postulated → distinction between simple nobility and final suitability → elemental and equal slime → human body as lesser world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AF2","text":"Created and celestial causes postulated → rule of generation of material form → absence of an antecedent human body → production of the first body immediately divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AF3","text":"Defects of senses, arms, and stature objected → perfection relative to the rational soul → reason, hands, internal senses, and upright stature → optimal human disposition according to the end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:AF4","text":"Incongruity of Scriptural discourse objected → distinction of intention, Trinity, form of the soul, and vital manifestation → metaphysically coherent account of human production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME1","text":"The opposition between noble body and terrestrial body is dissolved, because the nobility of the body is referred to form and end, not to matter that is simply nobler.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME2","text":"The human body is reclassified as a cosmic nexus between the spiritual, celestial, elemental, and sentient, not as an isolated part of one corporeal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME3","text":"Causes are distinguished according to their capacity for producing: God creates matter and the first form in matter; natural causes generate from what pre-exists; angels can render limited ministries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME4","text":"The opposition between bodily defect and bodily perfection is dissolved, because specialized diminution is converted into a condition of instrumental universality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME5","text":"The distinction between active and passive potency opens a new field of causality, in which the pre-existence of possibility does not entail the pre-existence of a sufficient created cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ME6","text":"The Scriptural terms «faciamus», «inspiravit», and «in faciem» are reordered as signs of intention, personal plurality, form of the soul, and manifestation of life, not as univocally material causal accounts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines the matter, author, disposition, and order of the production of the body of the first human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ALT2","text":"Structural — The body is explained through the relation of form and matter, equality of mixture, order of causes, and finality of bodily instruments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections from nobility, causal efficiency, and comparative defect are not directly denied, but the measures of judgment are transferred to the end of the rational soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — First formation is distinguished from natural generation, and the unity of soul and body is opposed to the temporal succession of two completely constituted substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning relative finality, the soul as form, elemental mixture, and the causality of material forms suffice to regenerate the responses concerning matter, efficient cause, and bodily disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT2","text":"The firmest connection of the system is the relation between the rational soul and the instrumental body, which gathers matter, equality of complexion, hands, upright stature, and apparent defects into one principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT3","text":"The system depends on the physics of the elements, the doctrine of complexion, and the principle that rational knowledge begins through bodily senses; these principles are assumed internally rather than further demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT4","text":"The juncture between the immediate action of God and angelic ministry is preserved through the distinction between principal cause and ministry, but the positive extent of this ministry is not fully determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT5","text":"A delicate juncture remains between the denial of the production of the soul without a body and Augustine's exposition, which distinguishes the soul in act but the body according to causal reasons; the solution depends on equivocation between the order of causality and the order of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT6","text":"The exegesis of the fourth article coheres if Scriptural expressions are held to be doctrinally distinctive, but it is not demonstrated from grammar alone why each expression should be referred to a determinate metaphysical meaning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0086","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0091","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0093","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_83:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: appearance of material or bodily inferiority → causal and final distinction → ordering of the body to the rational soul → affirmation of immediate divine formation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_83:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_83@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_83:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 92","title":"First Part · Question 91","context":"Chapter 92","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 91"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 91","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 92","order":93,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_84"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_84@R001","sha256":"bdf103d6a845ff06b19c2bf664c92d5d25fc550c2d566ce0816ec43f690e7bfd","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat utrum productio mulieris, eius materia, modus formationis et causa immediata cum perfectione primae institutionis rerum conveniant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS2","text":"Argumentatio difficultates ex defectu, subiectione, peccato, communitate speciei, quantitate materiae et ordine causae naturalis ortas resolvit distinguendo ordinem naturae particularis ab ordine naturae universalis et divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS3","text":"Productio feminae ponitur necessaria propter generationem, sed species humana ab aliis viventibus distinguitur quia generatio subordinationem habet ad vitam intellectualem et domesticam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS4","text":"Formatio mulieris ex viro et ex costa simul causas sociales, coniugales, hierarchicas et sacramentales significat, nec ad solam efficientiam corporalem reducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS5","text":"Conclusio finalis ordinem naturalem limitatum cum potentia creatoris coniungit: quod natura ex materia determinata efficere non potest, Deus immediate efficere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A1","text":"Femina in prima rerum institutione necessaria est ut adiutorium viri in opere generationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A2","text":"In animalibus perfectis virtus activa generationis principaliter masculini sexus est, virtus passiva feminini sexus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A3","text":"Quanto vita ad opus nobilius ordinatur, tanto distinctio virtutum generationis magis separari potest sine destructione unitatis generationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A4","text":"Femina respectu naturae particularis dici potest deficiens vel occasionata, sed respectu naturae universalis ordinatur et intenditur ad generationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A5","text":"Intentio naturae universalis a Deo, universali auctore naturae, dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A6","text":"Subiectio servilis, quae ad utilitatem praesidentis ordinatur, a subiectione oeconomica vel civili, quae ad bonum subiectorum ordinatur, distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A7","text":"Ordo humanae multitudinis etiam ante peccatum gubernationem per sapientiores requirit, et in hoc ordine femina viro subiecta ponitur propter maiorem discretionem rationis in viro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A8","text":"Bonum commune universi non tollendum est propter malum particulare quod ex aliquo bono contingenter oriri potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A9","text":"Deus potest quodlibet malum ordinare in bonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A10","text":"Formatio mulieris ex viro competit ut vir sit principium suae speciei, ut coniugalis adhaesio firmetur, et ut vita domestica humana constituatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A11","text":"Virtus naturae creatae ex materia determinata procedit, sed virtus divina infinita idem secundum speciem ex quacumque materia producere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A12","text":"Origo ex viro quae non est generatio naturalis propinquitatem matrimonialiter impedientem non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A13","text":"Formatio mulieris ex costa significat coniunctionem socialem quae nec dominationem mulieris in virum nec servilem eius depressionem admittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A14","text":"Materia eadem sine additione non multiplicatur nisi per rarefactionem, quia augmentum dimensionum est conditio multiplicationis materialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A15","text":"Costa ad perfectionem Adae pertinebat ut principii speciei, non ut individui per se completissimi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A16","text":"Ratio causalis praeexistens corporis mulieris in primis operibus est potentia passiva ordinata ad potentiam activam creatoris, non potentia activa creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX1","text":"Femina non instituitur ut adiutorium viri in quolibet opere externo, quia vir ad alia opera convenientius ab alio viro adiuvatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX2","text":"Defectus feminae secundum intentionem particularis virtutis generativae non est defectus simpliciter in ordine naturae universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX3","text":"Status innocentiae non excludit omnem inaequalitatem neque omnem subiectionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX4","text":"Praescientia occasionis peccati non imponit abolitionem boni ex quo illa occasio contingenter sumi potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX5","text":"Formatio mulieris ex viro non est generatio naturalis nec relationem patris et filiae constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX6","text":"Costa non significat nec principatum mulieris, qui per caput significaretur, nec servilem subiectionem, quae per pedes significaretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX7","text":"Multiplicatio corporis mulieris ex costa non intelligitur ut materia eadem augeatur sine additione vel rarefactione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX8","text":"Rationes causales primae conditionis non sufficiunt ut creatura active corpus mulieris ex costa producat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX9","text":"Ministerium angelicum in formatione mulieris nec affirmatur nec ad formationem corporis eius causaliter necessarium statuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D1","text":"Unitas coniugalis carnalis non confunditur cum indistinctione sexualium virtutum, quia distinctio servit ipsi operi generationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A1","CH_GGVC_P_84:A2","CH_GGVC_P_84:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D2","text":"Iudicium de femina mutatur secundum ordinem comparationis: quod est defectivum respectu causae particularis potest esse intentum respectu causae universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A4","CH_GGVC_P_84:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D3","text":"Hierarchia praelapsaria in textu non ex poena peccati deducitur, sed ex ordine gubernationis ad bonum subiectorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A6","CH_GGVC_P_84:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D4","text":"Integritas universi praevalet eliminationi praeventivae omnis condicionis ex qua peccatum occasionari potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A8","CH_GGVC_P_84:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D5","text":"Origo mulieris ex viro facit coniugalem unionem simul naturaliter aptam ad vitam domesticam et symbolicam respectu originis Ecclesiae a Christo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A10","CH_GGVC_P_84:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D6","text":"Identitas specifica maris et feminae non exigit identitatem materiae originariae, si causa efficiens divina supra determinationem naturae operatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D7","text":"Exemptio Evae ab impedimento propinquitatis fundatur in distinctione inter originem materialem et generationem naturalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D8","text":"Integritas corporis Adae post subtractionem costae servatur, quia imminutio individualis non sequitur ex eo quod pars ad perfectionem principii speciei pertineat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A15","CH_GGVC_P_84:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D9","text":"Productio corporis mulieris requirit additionem materiae, creationem vel conversionem, non mera multiplicatione materiae praeexistentis explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D10","text":"Praeexistentia causalis mulieris in prima conditione significat possibilitatem divinitus producibilem, non operationem naturalem iam sufficientem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A11","CH_GGVC_P_84:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD1","text":"Ordo creatus intelligitur ut duplex: natura particularis secundum vias determinatas operatur, dum natura universalis sub auctoritate divina fines quos causae particulares non explicant continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A4","CH_GGVC_P_84:A5","CH_GGVC_P_84:A11","CH_GGVC_P_84:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD2","text":"Ordo sexualis non solum biologice, sed simul teleologice, domestice, politice et sacramentaliter constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A1","CH_GGVC_P_84:A7","CH_GGVC_P_84:A10","CH_GGVC_P_84:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD3","text":"Malum contingens non fungitur criterio supremo ordinationis creaturae, quia perfectio communis et ordinatio divina mali ad bonum normam decisionis constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A8","CH_GGVC_P_84:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD4","text":"Narratio originis corporeae recipit munus normativum: situs materialis originis distribuit limites dominationis, subiectionis et coniunctionis socialis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A13","CH_GGVC_P_84:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD5","text":"Causalitas divina non est causa naturalis amplificata, sed causa quae materiam, modum productionis et ipsam possibilitatem effectus supra ordinem naturalem disponere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A11","CH_GGVC_P_84:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX1","text":"Perfectionem primae institutionis rerum falsum est definire ut absentiam omnis asymmetriae, subiectionis vel distinctionis functionalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX2","text":"Bonitatem creaturae falsum est aestimare ex immunitate ab omni usu peccaminoso futuro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX3","text":"Ordo naturae falsum est habere pro systemate causaliter clauso, cuius materiae et processus divinam actionem exceptionalem excludant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX4","text":"Relatio sexualis humana falsum est reducere ad generationem animalem, quia vita communis stabilis et distributio operum domesticorum ad eius rationem pertinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX5","text":"Significatio corporis falsum est habere ut physicae originis accidens extrinsecum, quia ipsa origo ex latere normam socialem et figuram sacramentalem vehit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit possibilitatem quod natura particularis sit ultima mensura intentionis creatricis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit mundum in quo imminutio possibilitatis peccati praevaleat perfectioni boni communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit originem humanam cuius veritas exhausta sit per causationem materialem et naturalem sine ordine symbolico ad Christum et Ecclesiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SNX4","text":"Systema excludit aequationem societatis rectae cum dominatione absoluta vel cum servitute absoluta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS1","text":"Obiectio ex defectu particulari → distinctio naturae particularis et universalis → femina restituitur ut effectus intentus ad generationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS2","text":"Obiectio ex subiectione vel peccato → distinctio servilis et civilis subiectionis → ordo hierarchicus praelapsarius ad bonum commune affirmatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS3","text":"Obiectio ex occasione mali → praevalentia perfectionis universi → conservatio boni cui malum contingenter adiungi potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS4","text":"Obiectio ex materia vel consanguinitate → distinctio generationis naturalis et formationis divinae → origo ex viro sine filiatione naturali declaratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS5","text":"Obiectio ex quantitate costae → negatio multiplicationis sine mutatione vel additione → interventus divinus materiam addit vel convertit, retenta costa ut materia praesupposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS6","text":"Obiectio ex causalitate creaturali → limitatio naturae ad materiam determinatam → sola immediata virtus Dei format corpus humanum ex materia extraordinaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF1","text":"Defectus apparens feminae → distinctio intentionis particularis et universalis → necessitas feminae ad generationem → affirmatio productionis primae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF2","text":"Subiectio et occasio peccati → distinctio ordinis civilis a servili et boni communis a malo particulari → compatibilitas feminae cum statu innocentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF3","text":"Origo ex viro → principium speciei, adhaesio coniugalis et domus → origo non-generativa sine impedimento propinquitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF4","text":"Costa ut materia → significatio socialis et sacramentalis → resolutio difficultatis quantitatis per additionem vel conversionem divinam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF5","text":"Praeexistentia possibilitatis causalis → negatio virtutis activae creaturalis → productio immediata a Deo supra ordinem naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME1","text":"Distinctio naturae particularis et universalis permittit idem effectum ut localiter defectivum et universaliter intentum classificari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter innocentiam et omnem inaequalitatem dissolvitur per distinctionem inter servitutem poenalem et gubernationem ad bonum subiectorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter bonum creatum et occasionem peccati dissolvitur, quia eadem res bonum commune constituere et malum particulare contingenter occasionare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME4","text":"Origo ex viro reclassificatur non ut processus biologicus ordinarius, sed ut nexus principialis, coniugalis, domesticus et sacramentalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME5","text":"Rationes causales reclassificantur ex causis efficientibus creaturalibus in potentiam passivam quae operationem creatoris expectat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME6","text":"Corpus et situs corporis reclassificantur ut portatores ordinis socialis et typologiae ecclesialis, non tantum ut materiae quantitativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus affirmat feminam in prima institutione productam, ex viro et ex costa formatam, immediate a Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT2","text":"Structural — Ordo generationis, vitae domesticae, gubernationis et causalitatis naturalis distribuit sexuum munera, subiectionem et limites causae creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones non directe negantur, sed per distinctiones ordinum convertuntur: particulare/universale, servile/civile, naturale/divinum, activum/passivum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creaturae causalitas determinata est et temporalis, sed potentia creatoris eam fundat, excedit et possibilitates passivas ad actum producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT5","text":"Sacramental — Origo mulieris ex viro et ex latere ordinem originarium ad relationem Christi et Ecclesiae typologice refert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de fine generationis, duplici ordine naturae et excessu causalitatis divinae sufficiunt ad conclusionem quod femina necessario producitur et immediate a Deo formatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT2","text":"Distinctio subiectionis servilis et civilis est commissura necessaria, quia sine ea affirmatio naturalis subiectionis feminae cum statu innocentiae non componitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT3","text":"Distinctio naturae particularis et universalis sustinet conciliationem inter feminam ut occasionatam et feminam ut intentam, sed statum exactum illius defectus intra ordinem universalem non ulterius determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT4","text":"Ratio originis ex viro interne cohaeret si formatio divina a generatione naturali separatur; haec separatio simul fundamentum est responsionis ad impedimentum propinquitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT5","text":"Explicatio materialis formationis ex costa firmiter negat multiplicationem sine additione vel rarefactione, sed electionem inter creationem et conversionem non absolute concludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT6","text":"Argumentatio maximam firmitatem habet ubi limites causalitatis naturalis exponit; fragilitas residet in transitu a differentiis generationis ad ordinem socialem hierarchicum, qui in praemissa de maiori discretione rationis viri consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165410101848Z_e1a8705a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 92","source_sha256":"bdf103d6a845ff06b19c2bf664c92d5d25fc550c2d566ce0816ec43f690e7bfd","sha256":"35ed40f64a1a633da8b5c60deaf5bb8cbedeca22ebfd4f4fb8f5ae720efeca07","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:54:10.102806+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS1","text":"The question investigates whether the production of woman, her matter, mode of formation, and immediate cause accord with the perfection of the first institution of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS2","text":"The argument resolves difficulties arising from defect, subjection, sin, community of species, quantity of matter, and the order of natural causation by distinguishing the order of particular nature from that of universal and divine nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS3","text":"The production of woman is posited as necessary for generation, but the human species is distinguished from other living beings because generation is subordinated to intellectual and domestic life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS4","text":"The formation of woman from man and from a rib simultaneously signifies social, conjugal, hierarchical, and sacramental causes, and is not reduced to bodily efficiency alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AS5","text":"The final conclusion joins the limited natural order with the power of the creator: what nature cannot effect from determinate matter, God can effect immediately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A1","text":"Woman is necessary in the first institution of things as a help to man in the work of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A2","text":"In perfect animals, the active power of generation belongs principally to the male sex, and the passive power to the female sex.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A3","text":"The more life is ordered to a nobler work, the more the distinction of generative powers can be separated without the destruction of the unity of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A4","text":"Woman can be called defective or occasioned with respect to particular nature, but with respect to universal nature she is ordered and intended for generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A5","text":"The intention of universal nature depends on God, the universal author of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A6","text":"Servile subjection, which is ordered to the benefit of the ruler, is distinguished from economic or civil subjection, which is ordered to the good of those subjected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A7","text":"The order of human multitude requires governance by the wiser even before sin, and in this order woman is posited as subject to man on account of the greater discretion of reason in man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A8","text":"The common good of the universe is not to be removed on account of a particular evil that can contingently arise from some good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A9","text":"God can order any evil toward good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A10","text":"The formation of woman from man is fitting so that man may be the principle of his species, conjugal attachment may be strengthened, and human domestic life may be constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A11","text":"The power of created nature proceeds from determinate matter, but infinite divine power can produce the same thing in species from any matter whatsoever.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A12","text":"An origin from man that is not natural generation does not establish kinship that impedes marriage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A13","text":"The formation of woman from a rib signifies a social conjunction that admits neither the domination of woman over man nor her servile depression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A14","text":"The same matter without addition is not multiplied except through rarefaction, because increase of dimensions is the condition of material multiplication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A15","text":"The rib belonged to the perfection of Adam as principle of the species, not as an individual complete in himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:A16","text":"The pre-existing causal account of the woman's body in the first works is passive potency ordered to the active power of the creator, not an active potency of the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX1","text":"Woman is not instituted as man's helper in any external work, because man is more fittingly helped by another man in other works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX2","text":"The defect of woman according to the intention of particular generative power is not a defect simply speaking in the order of universal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX3","text":"The state of innocence does not exclude every inequality or every subjection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX4","text":"Foreknowledge of an occasion of sin does not entail the abolition of the good from which that occasion can contingently be taken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX5","text":"The formation of woman from man is not natural generation and does not establish the relation of father and daughter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX6","text":"The rib signifies neither woman's primacy, which would be signified by the head, nor servile subjection, which would be signified by the feet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX7","text":"The multiplication of the woman's body from a rib is not understood as the increase of the same matter without addition or rarefaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX8","text":"The causal accounts of the first condition do not suffice for a creature actively to produce the woman's body from a rib.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:NX9","text":"Angelic ministry in the formation of woman is neither affirmed nor posited as causally necessary for the formation of her body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D1","text":"Carnal conjugal unity is not confused with the indistinction of sexual powers, because the distinction serves the very work of generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A1","CH_GGVC_P_84:A2","CH_GGVC_P_84:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D2","text":"Judgment concerning woman changes according to the order of comparison: what is defective with respect to a particular cause can be intended with respect to a universal cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A4","CH_GGVC_P_84:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D3","text":"In the text, prelapsarian hierarchy is not derived from the punishment of sin, but from the order of governance toward the good of those subjected.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A6","CH_GGVC_P_84:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D4","text":"The integrity of the universe prevails over the preventive elimination of every condition from which sin can be occasioned.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A8","CH_GGVC_P_84:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D5","text":"The origin of woman from man makes conjugal union both naturally suited to domestic life and symbolic with respect to the origin of the Church from Christ.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A10","CH_GGVC_P_84:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D6","text":"The specific identity of male and female does not require identity of originating matter, if the divine efficient cause operates above the determination of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D7","text":"Eve's exemption from the impediment of kinship is founded on the distinction between material origin and natural generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D8","text":"The integrity of Adam's body after the removal of the rib is preserved, because individual diminution does not follow from the fact that a part belonged to the perfection of the principle of the species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A15","CH_GGVC_P_84:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D9","text":"The production of the woman's body requires an addition of matter, creation, or conversion; it is not explained by the mere multiplication of pre-existing matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:D10","text":"The causal pre-existence of woman in the first condition signifies a possibility producible by God, not a natural operation already sufficient.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A11","CH_GGVC_P_84:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD1","text":"Created order is understood as twofold: particular nature operates according to determinate ways, while universal nature under divine authority contains ends that particular causes do not explain.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A4","CH_GGVC_P_84:A5","CH_GGVC_P_84:A11","CH_GGVC_P_84:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD2","text":"The sexual order is constituted not only biologically, but also teleologically, domestically, politically, and sacramentally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A1","CH_GGVC_P_84:A7","CH_GGVC_P_84:A10","CH_GGVC_P_84:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD3","text":"Contingent evil does not function as the supreme criterion for the ordering of the creature, because common perfection and divine ordering of evil toward good constitute the norm of decision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A8","CH_GGVC_P_84:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD4","text":"The narrative of bodily origin assumes a normative function: the material location of origin distributes the limits of domination, subjection, and social conjunction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A13","CH_GGVC_P_84:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SD5","text":"Divine causality is not an amplified natural cause, but a cause that can dispose matter, the mode of production, and the very possibility of the effect above the natural order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_84:A11","CH_GGVC_P_84:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX1","text":"It is false to define the perfection of the first institution of things as the absence of every asymmetry, subjection, or functional distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX2","text":"It is false to judge the goodness of a creature from immunity to every future sinful use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX3","text":"It is false to take the order of nature as a causally closed system whose matter and processes exclude exceptional divine action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX4","text":"It is false to reduce human sexual relation to animal generation, because stable common life and the distribution of domestic tasks pertain to its account.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:DNX5","text":"It is false to regard bodily signification as an extrinsic accident of physical origin, because origin itself from the side bears a social norm and a sacramental figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that particular nature is the ultimate measure of creative intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SNX2","text":"The system excludes a world in which the reduction of the possibility of sin prevails over the perfection of the common good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SNX3","text":"The system excludes a human origin whose truth is exhausted by material and natural causation without a symbolic order toward Christ and the Church.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:SNX4","text":"The system excludes the equation of a right society with absolute domination or with absolute servitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS1","text":"Objection from particular defect → distinction between particular and universal nature → woman is restored as an effect intended for generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS2","text":"Objection from subjection or sin → distinction between servile and civil subjection → prelapsarian hierarchical order for the common good is affirmed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS3","text":"Objection from the occasion of evil → preeminence of the perfection of the universe → preservation of the good to which evil can contingently be joined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS4","text":"Objection from matter or consanguinity → distinction between natural generation and divine formation → origin from man without natural filiation is declared.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS5","text":"Objection from the quantity of the rib → denial of multiplication without change or addition → divine intervention adds or converts matter, with the rib retained as presupposed matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:FGS6","text":"Objection from creaturely causality → limitation of nature to determinate matter → the immediate power of God alone forms a human body from extraordinary matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF1","text":"Apparent defect of woman → distinction between particular and universal intention → necessity of woman for generation → affirmation of first production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF2","text":"Subjection and occasion of sin → distinction of civil from servile order and of common good from particular evil → compatibility of woman with the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF3","text":"Origin from man → principle of the species, conjugal attachment, and household → non-generative origin without impediment of kinship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF4","text":"Rib as matter → social and sacramental signification → resolution of the difficulty of quantity through divine addition or conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:AF5","text":"Pre-existence of causal possibility → denial of creaturely active power → immediate production by God above the order of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME1","text":"The distinction between particular and universal nature permits the same effect to be classified as locally defective and universally intended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME2","text":"The opposition between innocence and every inequality is dissolved through the distinction between penal servitude and governance toward the good of those subjected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME3","text":"The opposition between created good and an occasion of sin is dissolved, because the same thing can constitute a common good and contingently occasion a particular evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME4","text":"Origin from man is reclassified not as an ordinary biological process, but as a principial, conjugal, domestic, and sacramental nexus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME5","text":"Causal accounts are reclassified from creaturely efficient causes into passive potency awaiting the operation of the creator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ME6","text":"The body and the location of the body are reclassified as bearers of social order and ecclesial typology, not merely as quantitative matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text affirms that woman was produced in the first institution, formed from man and from a rib, immediately by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT2","text":"Structural — The order of generation, domestic life, governance, and natural causality distributes the roles of the sexes, subjection, and the limits of created causation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are not directly denied, but transformed through distinctions of orders: particular/universal, servile/civil, natural/divine, active/passive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creaturely causality is determinate and temporal, but the power of the creator founds and exceeds it, and brings passive possibilities into act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:ALT5","text":"Sacramental — The origin of woman from man and from the side refers the original order typologically to the relation of Christ and the Church.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning the end of generation, the twofold order of nature, and the excess of divine causality suffice for the conclusion that woman is necessarily produced and immediately formed by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT2","text":"The distinction between servile and civil subjection is a necessary joint, because without it the affirmation of woman's natural subjection cannot be reconciled with the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT3","text":"The distinction between particular and universal nature supports the reconciliation between woman as occasioned and woman as intended, but does not further determine the exact status of that defect within the universal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT4","text":"The account of origin from man is internally coherent if divine formation is separated from natural generation; this separation is at the same time the basis of the response to the impediment of kinship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT5","text":"The material explanation of formation from a rib firmly denies multiplication without addition or rarefaction, but does not absolutely conclude the choice between creation and conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_84:MRT6","text":"The argument has greatest strength where it expounds the limits of natural causality; its fragility lies in the transition from differences of generation to hierarchical social order, which consists in the premise concerning man's greater discretion of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_84:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_84@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_84:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 93","title":"First Part · Question 92","context":"Chapter 93","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 92"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 92","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 93","order":94,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_85"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_85@R001","sha256":"717162915cbba8733fb0bb59a6a051769de3a5c60503b5814dafea477e06bda6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS1","text":"Textus determinat quibus condicionibus homo ad imaginem Dei dicatur, ubi haec imago resideat, quibus modis perficiatur et quomodo a similitudine distinguatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS2","text":"Imago Dei proprie convenit creaturae intellectuali secundum mentem, quatenus processiones cognitionis et amoris ad Deum ordinatae Trinitatem imperfecte repraesentant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est definitoria, distinctiva, hierarchica et reconstructiva: ambiguitates nominum per criterios principales et secundarios ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS4","text":"Motus initialis transit a distinctione similitudinis, imaginis et imaginis perfectae ad restrictionem imaginis proprie dictae ad naturam intellectualem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS5","text":"Motus medius comparat gradus imaginis, universalitatem eius in hominibus et locum formalem eius in mente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS6","text":"Motus trinitarius transfert distinctionem processionum divinarum ad processiones interiores verbi et amoris, salva imperfectione repraesentationis creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS7","text":"Motus finalis restringit imaginem ad operationem mentis in Deum directam vel mediatam et reordinat similitudinem ut condicionem imaginis aut perfectionem eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0184","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","text":"Imago est similitudo ab exemplari expressa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","text":"Aequalitas non pertinet ad rationem imaginis simpliciter, sed ad perfectionem imaginis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","text":"Imago requirit similitudinem secundum speciem vel secundum proprietatem ultimam speciei, non secundum genus aut accidens commune tantum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","text":"Convenientia imaginis ad exemplar potest constitui secundum analogiam vel proportionem, etiam sine identitate numerica, specifica aut generica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","text":"Creaturae Deo assimilantur gradatim secundum esse, vivere et intelligere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","text":"Sola natura intellectualis ad repraesentationem specificam Dei sufficienter accedit ut proprie imago dicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","text":"Gradus imaginis principaliter sequitur gradum perfectionis naturae intellectualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","text":"In creatura rationali imago Dei formaliter residet in mente; partes non intellectuales Deum tantum per modum vestigii repraesentant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","text":"Personae divinae distinguuntur secundum relationes originis: Verbum procedit a dicente, amor ab utroque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","text":"Mens Trinitatem imitatur formando verbum ex cognitione et amorem notitiam atque verbum connectentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A11","text":"Una natura divina in tribus personis secundum relationes originis existit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","text":"Aptitudo naturalis ad Deum cognoscendum et amandum in natura mentis consistit et omnibus hominibus communis est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","text":"Eadem imago secundum gratiam imperfecte actualizatur, secundum gloriam perfecte consummatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","text":"Imago Trinitatis principaliter attenditur secundum actus mentis, secundario secundum habitus et potentias in quibus actus virtualiter continentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","text":"Obiectum determinat speciem verbi et amoris; imago divina proprie constituitur cum mens in Deum directe vel mediate fertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A16","text":"Similitudo potest imaginem praecedere ut ratio communior vel sequi ut perfectio expressionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A17","text":"Deus ut exemplar humanum exemplatum in infinitum excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX1","text":"Interdictum imaginum corporalium ab homine fabricatarum non excludit imaginem spiritualem a Deo menti impressam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX2","text":"Imago creata non requirit aequalitatem naturae cum Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX3","text":"Non omnis similitudo causalis aut expressa rationem imaginis proprie dictae constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX4","text":"Creaturae irrationales et universum secundum totalitatem non sunt proprie imago Dei, quamvis similitudinem vel imaginem improprie dictam participent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX5","text":"Invariabilitas speciei substantialis non excludit quin una species intellectualis alia perfectior sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX6","text":"Peccatum imaginem naturalem non delet, sed eius claritatem et conformitatem minuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0167","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX7","text":"Imago Dei principaliter neque in corpore neque in figura neque in distinctione sexuum constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX8","text":"Imago in homine neque ad essentiam divinam sine personis neque ad solum Filium restringitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX9","text":"Imago Trinitatis in mente non praebet cognitionem naturalem perfectam Trinitatis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX10","text":"Imago non constituitur principaliter per facultates statice possessas neque requirit actum actualem sine intermissione permanentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX11","text":"Quaelibet processio verbi et amoris circa quodlibet obiectum non sufficit ad imaginem Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0163","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX12","text":"Similitudo non opponitur imagini quasi genus extrinsecum, sed aut infra rationem imaginis deficit aut eius perfectionem significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0186","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D1","text":"Homo est imago Dei imperfecta et dicitur ad imaginem, quia ab exemplari divino derivatur sine aequalitate et ad exemplar infinite superius accedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D2","text":"In creaturis non intellectualibus substantia finita, species et ordo indicant principium, verbum et amorem producentis solum per modum vestigii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D3","text":"Angelus est simpliciter magis ad imaginem Dei quam homo propter perfectiorem intellectualitatem; homo praevalet tantum secundum analogias secundarias.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D4","text":"Omnes homines possident imaginem creationis, iusti imaginem conformitatis gratiae, beati imaginem consummatae gloriae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D5","text":"Deformitas peccati mutat qualitatem actualis conformitatis, non fundamentum naturale imaginis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D6","text":"Totus homo denominative imago Dei dicitur, quamvis imago formaliter tantum in mente insit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0115","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D7","text":"Mas et femina aequaliter imaginem secundum naturam intellectualem participant, quamvis textus ordinem originis et finis viro secundariam analogiam divinam attribuat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D8","text":"Repraesentatio naturae divinae et repraesentatio trium personarum non sunt imagines concurrentes, quia distinctio originum intra unam naturam subsistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D9","text":"Imago permanet cum actus cessant, quia actus manent virtualiter in aptitudine, potentia et habitu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D10","text":"Cognitio sui vel temporalium imaginem Dei constituit tantum quatenus mentem mediate ad Deum refert vel obiecta in Deo cognoscuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D11","text":"Similitudo inferior imagine communior est, similitudo posterior imagine perfectior est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD1","text":"Perfectio imaginis mensuratur intensive et collective per capacitatem summi boni, non extensive per multitudinem perfectionum distributarum in universo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD2","text":"Ontologia imaginis est participativa et scalaris: maior vel minor propinquitas ad exemplar statui potest sine identitate naturae et sine variatione speciei intra idem individuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD3","text":"Imago humana est structura directionalis: aptitudo naturalis ad Deum per gratiam conformatur et per gloriam consummatur, sed distantia exemplaris non tollitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD4","text":"Similitudo trinitaria mentis habet vim repraesentativam sine vi demonstrativa sufficienti ad mysterium divinum naturaliter probandum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD5","text":"Praedicatio imaginis de homine integro dependet ab interioritate intellectuali, dum corporeitas et ceterae partes eandem causalitatem divinam gradu vestigiali tantum manifestant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD6","text":"Gratia et gloria non aliam imaginem extrinsecam introducunt, sed potentiam naturalem eiusdem imaginis ad actum conformem et consummatum promovent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX1","text":"Systema falsum esse requirit quod relatio creaturae ad Deum aut univoca identitas aut pura aequivocitas esse debeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit causalitatem efficientem universalem tamquam condicionem sufficientem imaginis proprie dictae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit exemplar formalisticum quo sola structura processionis, obiecto neglecto, imaginem Dei constituat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0163","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit perfectionem extensivam totius universi tamquam superiorem perfectione intensiva mentis intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX5","text":"Systema excludit aequalitatem omnium creaturarum intellectualium ex sola communione naturae intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX6","text":"Systema excludit permanentiam imaginis a continuitate actus conscientis dependere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX7","text":"Systema excludit corpus, sexum aut relationes generationis humanae tamquam principium formale imaginis trinitariae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX8","text":"Systema excludit mentem humanam ut potentiam obiective neutralem cuius finis intrinsecus a Deo separari possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX9","text":"Systema excludit cognitionem reflexivam mentis tamquam probationem naturalem exhaustivam Trinitatis increatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX10","text":"Systema excludit gratiam tamquam primam productionem imaginis, quia gratia imaginem naturaliter iam praesentem reformat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0167","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX1","text":"Identitas naturae et aequalitas cum exemplari divino creaturae rationali praeclusae sunt; earum absentia constituit rationem imaginis imperfectae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17","CH_GGVC_P_85:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX2","text":"Comprehensio naturalis Trinitatis indisponibilis manet, quamvis mens vestigium processionum personalium intra se experiatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX3","text":"Finis autonomus mentis, in se ipsa vel in temporalibus clausus, inadmissibilis est; mens imaginem suam tantum ex orientatione ad Deum obtinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0165","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX4","text":"Nulla totalitas creata, corporeitas vel ordinatio socialis interioritatem intellectualem ut locum principalem imaginis substituere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX5","text":"Obiectum temporale et mutabile non potest esse terminus ultimus imaginis; recipitur in ea tantum si ad Deum refertur vel in Deo videtur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0165","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0169","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS1","text":"Similitudo ab exemplari expressa generat imaginem; plenitudo sine defectu generat imaginem perfectam; distantia infinita relinquit imaginem imperfectam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS2","text":"Esse → vivere → intelligere constituit seriem crescentis assimilationis; solus gradus intellectivus limen imaginis proprie dictae attingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS3","text":"Natura intellectualis → mens → cognitio actualis → verbum interius → amor procedens constituit machinam repraesentationis trinitariae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS4","text":"Aptitudo naturalis → conformitas gratiae → consummatio gloriae constituit seriem modalem eiusdem imaginis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS5","text":"Processio mentalis circa obiectum quodlibet generat structuram triadicam; sola directio ad Deum directam vel mediatam eam in imaginem Dei determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS6","text":"Criterium principale intellectualitatis regit comparationes simpliciter; analogiae corporis, generationis et ordinis admittuntur tantum secundum quid.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS7","text":"Similitudo communior → imago → similitudo perfectiva constituit ordinem quo idem nomen antecedenter et consequenter ad imaginem refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A16","CH_GGVC_P_85:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AF1","text":"Praedicatio scripturaria imaginis → definitio similitudinis expressae → exclusio aequalitatis necessariae → constitutio imaginis imperfectae humanae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17","CH_GGVC_P_85:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AF2","text":"Ratio imaginis → restrictio ad intellectualia → comparatio angeli et hominis → universalitas naturalis → relatio ad Trinitatem → localizatio in mente → primatus actuum → restrictio obiectiva ad Deum → distinctio similitudinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A11","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AF3","text":"Apparens contradictio → distinctio principalis et secundaria → distributio inter proprie et improprie, simpliciter et secundum quid, actum et principium → restitutio praedicationis limitatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_85:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_85:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_85:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0186","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME1","text":"Ager similitudinis dividitur in vestigium causale, imaginem specificam imperfectam et imaginem perfectam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME2","text":"Hierarchia creaturarum non iam per solam causalitatem vel bonitatem extensivam, sed per capacitatem intellectualem repraesentandi Deum describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME3","text":"Praedicatio imaginis de homine integro in distinctionem inter denominationem totius et inhaerentiam formalem in mente convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME4","text":"Facultates mentis reclassificantur ut principia virtualia imaginis, dum actus cognitionis et amoris locum principalem obtinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME5","text":"Oppositio inter imaginem naturalem et imaginem gratiae solvitur in gradus unius structurae: capacitas, reformatio et consummatio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME6","text":"Oppositio inter imaginem essentiae divinae et imaginem personarum corruit, quia unitas naturae et relationes originis mutuo implicantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A11","CH_GGVC_P_85:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME7","text":"Psychologia verbi et amoris ab exemplari obiective neutro in structuram theologicam obiecto divino determinatam mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0163","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME8","text":"Distinctio inter perfectionem extensivam universi et perfectionem intensivam mentis impedit ne maior totalitas materialis eo ipso maior imago habeatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface: Textus definit utrum, ubi, in quibus subiectis, secundum quos actus et respectu cuius obiecti imago Dei inveniatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_85:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural: Mechanismus imaginis consistit in intellectu qui verbum format et voluntate quae amorem producit, sub determinatione obiecti divini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic: Distinctiones inter principaliter et secundario, simpliciter et secundum quid, proprie et improprie ordinant auctoritates apparenter contrarias.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS6","CH_GGVC_P_85:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0186","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal: Participatio analogica coniungit distantiam creaturae, processiones trinitarias et progressionem ab aptitudine naturali per gratiam ad gloriam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad definitionem imaginis, restrictionem subiecti, structuram trinitariam, gradus perfectionis et distinctionem similitudinis restituenda.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A11","CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:A16","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT2","text":"Minus determinatus manet transitus a similitudine secundum speciem ad convenientiam analogicam inter intellectum creatum et naturam divinam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT3","text":"Cohaerentia interna principaliter servatur per subordinations criteriorum secundariorum criterio intellectualitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT4","text":"Structura firmissima est coniunctio inter mentem, processiones verbi et amoris, atque determinationem earum per obiectum divinum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter primatum actuum et permanentiam universalem imaginis, quam textus per continentiam virtualem in potentiis et habitibus componit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0146","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT6","text":"Tensio epistemica manet inter repraesentationem naturalem processionum trinitariarum et impossibilitatem cognitionis naturalis perfectae Trinitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT7","text":"Universalitas principalis imaginis in utroque sexu cohaeret formaliter, sed analogia secundaria principii et finis asymmetriam sexualem denuo introducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT8","text":"Quaedam transitus, praesertim inter analogiam, repraesentationem specificam et mysterium trinitarium, auctoritatibus et distinctionibus magis quam demonstratione completa sustinentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT9","text":"Restitutio servat motum verum textus a definitione imaginis per localizationem et operationem mentis ad orientationem in Deum et clausuram terminologicam similitudinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_85:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_85:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_85:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165444087194Z_2058c21b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 93","source_sha256":"717162915cbba8733fb0bb59a6a051769de3a5c60503b5814dafea477e06bda6","sha256":"7013de7250747f5886aba5b3fed2286ec97b62629c958acde6c0908d5e7110b1","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:54:44.088540+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS1","text":"The text determines under what conditions man is said to be in the image of God, where this image resides, in what ways it is perfected, and how it is distinguished from likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS2","text":"The image of God properly belongs to the intellectual creature according to the mind, insofar as the processions of knowledge and love ordered to God imperfectly represent the Trinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS3","text":"The argumentation is definitional, distinctive, hierarchical, and reconstructive: ambiguities of terms are ordered through primary and secondary criteria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS4","text":"The initial movement proceeds from the distinction of likeness, image, and perfect image to the restriction of image properly so called to intellectual nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS5","text":"The middle movement compares the degrees of image, its universality in human beings, and its formal location in the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS6","text":"The trinitarian movement transfers the distinction of divine processions to the interior processions of word and love, while preserving the imperfection of created representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AS7","text":"The final movement restricts the image to an operation of the mind directed to God directly or mediately and reorders likeness as a condition of the image or its perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0184","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","text":"An image is a likeness expressed from an exemplar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","text":"Equality does not belong to the notion of image simply, but to the perfection of image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","text":"An image requires likeness according to species or according to the ultimate property of the species, not according to genus or merely a common accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","text":"The correspondence of an image to its exemplar can be constituted according to analogy or proportion, even without numerical, specific, or generic identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","text":"Creatures are assimilated to God in degrees according to being, living, and understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","text":"Only intellectual nature sufficiently approaches the specific representation of God so as properly to be called an image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","text":"The degree of image principally follows the degree of perfection of intellectual nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","text":"In a rational creature the image of God formally resides in the mind; non-intellectual parts represent God only in the mode of a trace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","text":"The divine persons are distinguished according to relations of origin: the Word proceeds from the speaker, love from both.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","text":"The mind imitates the Trinity by forming a word from knowledge and love connecting knowledge and word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A11","text":"One divine nature exists in three persons according to relations of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","text":"The natural aptitude for knowing and loving God consists in the nature of the mind and is common to all human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","text":"The same image is imperfectly actualized according to grace and perfectly consummated according to glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","text":"The image of the Trinity is principally considered according to acts of the mind, secondarily according to habits and powers in which the acts are virtually contained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","text":"The object determines the species of word and love; the divine image is properly constituted when the mind is borne toward God directly or mediately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A16","text":"Likeness can precede image as a more common notion or follow it as the perfection of expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:A17","text":"God, as exemplar, infinitely exceeds the human thing exemplified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX1","text":"The prohibition of corporeal images fabricated by man does not exclude the spiritual image impressed by God upon the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX2","text":"A created image does not require equality of nature with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX3","text":"Not every causal or expressed likeness constitutes the notion of image properly so called.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX4","text":"Irrational creatures and the universe according to its totality are not properly the image of God, although they participate in likeness or in image improperly so called.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX5","text":"The invariability of substantial species does not exclude one intellectual species being more perfect than another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX6","text":"Sin does not destroy the natural image, but diminishes its clarity and conformity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0167","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX7","text":"The image of God is constituted principally neither in the body nor in shape nor in the distinction of sexes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0120","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX8","text":"The image in man is restricted neither to the divine essence without the persons nor to the Son alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0096","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX9","text":"The image of the Trinity in the mind does not provide perfect natural knowledge of the divine Trinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX10","text":"The image is constituted neither principally through statically possessed faculties nor does it require an actual act enduring without interruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX11","text":"Every procession of word and love concerning any object whatsoever does not suffice for the image of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0163","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:NX12","text":"Likeness is not opposed to image as an extrinsic genus, but either falls short of the notion of image or signifies its perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0186","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D1","text":"Man is an imperfect image of God and is said to be to the image, because he is derived from the divine exemplar without equality and approaches an infinitely superior exemplar.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D2","text":"In non-intellectual creatures, finite substance, species, and order indicate the principle, word, and love of the producer only in the mode of a trace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D3","text":"An angel is simply more in the image of God than man on account of more perfect intellectuality; man prevails only according to secondary analogies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D4","text":"All human beings possess the image of creation, the just the image of conformity of grace, the blessed the image of consummated glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D5","text":"The deformity of sin changes the quality of actual conformity, not the natural foundation of the image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D6","text":"The whole human being is denominatively called the image of God, although the image formally inheres only in the mind.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0115","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D7","text":"Male and female equally participate in the image according to intellectual nature, although the text attributes to man a secondary divine analogy according to the order of origin and end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D8","text":"The representation of the divine nature and the representation of the three persons are not competing images, because the distinction of origins subsists within one nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D9","text":"The image remains when acts cease, because acts remain virtually in aptitude, power, and habit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0146","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D10","text":"Knowledge of oneself or of temporal things constitutes the image of God only insofar as it refers the mind mediately to God or the objects are known in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:D11","text":"Likeness inferior to image is more common; likeness subsequent to image is more perfect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD1","text":"The perfection of image is measured intensively and collectively by the capacity for the highest good, not extensively by the multitude of perfections distributed in the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD2","text":"The ontology of image is participatory and scalar: greater or lesser proximity to the exemplar can be posited without identity of nature and without variation of species within the same individual.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD3","text":"The human image is a directional structure: natural aptitude for God is conformed through grace and consummated through glory, but the distance of the exemplar is not removed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD4","text":"The trinitarian likeness of the mind has representative force without demonstrative force sufficient naturally to prove the divine mystery.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD5","text":"The predication of image of the whole human being depends on intellectual interiority, while corporeality and the other parts manifest the same divine causality only at the level of a trace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SD6","text":"Grace and glory do not introduce another extrinsic image, but advance the natural power of the same image to a conforming and consummated act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX1","text":"The system requires it to be false that the relation of creature to God must be either univocal identity or pure equivocity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX2","text":"The system excludes universal efficient causality as a sufficient condition of image properly so called.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a formalistic model whereby the structure of procession alone, with the object neglected, constitutes the image of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0163","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the extensive perfection of the whole universe as superior to the intensive perfection of the intellectual mind.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX5","text":"The system excludes the equality of all intellectual creatures solely from their common possession of intellectual nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX6","text":"The system excludes the dependence of the permanence of the image upon the continuity of conscious act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX7","text":"The system excludes the body, sex, or relations of human generation as the formal principle of the trinitarian image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX8","text":"The system excludes the human mind as an objectively neutral power whose end could intrinsically be separated from God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX9","text":"The system excludes reflexive knowledge of the mind as an exhaustive natural proof of the uncreated Trinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX10","text":"The system excludes grace as the first production of the image, because grace reforms the image already naturally present.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0167","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX1","text":"Identity of nature and equality with the divine exemplar are precluded to the rational creature; their absence constitutes the notion of imperfect image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17","CH_GGVC_P_85:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX2","text":"Natural comprehension of the Trinity remains unavailable, although the mind experiences within itself a trace of personal processions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX3","text":"An autonomous end of the mind, enclosed within itself or temporal things, is inadmissible; the mind obtains its image only from orientation toward God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0165","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX4","text":"No created totality, corporeality, or social ordering can substitute for intellectual interiority as the principal location of the image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0117","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX5","text":"A temporal and mutable object cannot be the ultimate terminus of the image; it is received into it only if referred to God or seen in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0165","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0169","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS1","text":"Likeness expressed from an exemplar generates image; fullness without defect generates perfect image; infinite distance leaves imperfect image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS2","text":"Being → living → understanding constitutes a series of increasing assimilation; the intellectual grade alone reaches the threshold of image properly so called.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS3","text":"Intellectual nature → mind → actual knowledge → interior word → proceeding love constitutes the mechanism of trinitarian representation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS4","text":"Natural aptitude → conformity of grace → consummation of glory constitutes the modal series of the same image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS5","text":"A mental procession concerning any object generates a triadic structure; only a direct or mediate direction to God determines it as the image of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS6","text":"The primary criterion of intellectuality governs comparisons simply; analogies of body, generation, and order are admitted only in a qualified respect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS7","text":"More common likeness → image → perfective likeness constitutes the order by which the same name is referred antecedently and consequently to image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A16","CH_GGVC_P_85:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AF1","text":"Scriptural predication of image → definition of expressed likeness → exclusion of necessary equality → constitution of the imperfect human image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17","CH_GGVC_P_85:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AF2","text":"Notion of image → restriction to intellectual beings → comparison of angel and man → natural universality → relation to the Trinity → localization in the mind → primacy of acts → objective restriction to God → distinction of likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A11","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:AF3","text":"Apparent contradiction → primary and secondary distinction → distribution between properly and improperly, simply and in a qualified respect, act and principle → restoration of limited predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_85:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_85:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_85:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0186","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME1","text":"The field of likeness is divided into causal trace, imperfect specific image, and perfect image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME2","text":"The hierarchy of creatures is described no longer through causality alone or extensive goodness, but through the intellectual capacity to represent God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME3","text":"The predication of image of the whole human being is converted into a distinction between denomination of the whole and formal inherence in the mind.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME4","text":"The faculties of the mind are reclassified as virtual principles of the image, while acts of knowledge and love obtain the principal place.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME5","text":"The opposition between natural image and image of grace is resolved into stages of one structure: capacity, reformation, and consummation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME6","text":"The opposition between the image of divine essence and the image of the persons collapses, because unity of nature and relations of origin mutually imply one another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A11","CH_GGVC_P_85:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME7","text":"The psychology of word and love is transformed from an objectively neutral model into a theological structure determined by the divine object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0161","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0163","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ME8","text":"The distinction between the extensive perfection of the universe and the intensive perfection of the mind prevents a greater material totality from thereby being held to possess a greater image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface: The text defines whether, where, in what subjects, according to which acts, and in relation to which object the image of God is found.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_85:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural: The mechanism of image consists in the intellect that forms a word and the will that produces love, under determination by the divine object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic: Distinctions between principally and secondarily, simply and in a qualified respect, properly and improperly order apparently contrary authorities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS6","CH_GGVC_P_85:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0186","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal: Analogical participation joins the distance of the creature, trinitarian processions, and progression from natural aptitude through grace to glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore the definition of image, the restriction of its subject, its trinitarian structure, the degrees of perfection, and the distinction of likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A1","CH_GGVC_P_85:A2","CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A5","CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A11","CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A13","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15","CH_GGVC_P_85:A16","CH_GGVC_P_85:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT2","text":"The transition from likeness according to species to analogical correspondence between created intellect and divine nature remains less determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence is principally preserved through the subordination of secondary criteria to the criterion of intellectuality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A6","CH_GGVC_P_85:A7","CH_GGVC_P_85:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT4","text":"The firmest structure is the conjunction between mind, the processions of word and love, and their determination by the divine object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A8","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10","CH_GGVC_P_85:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT5","text":"A fragile juncture remains between the primacy of acts and the universal permanence of the image, which the text reconciles through virtual containment in powers and habits.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A12","CH_GGVC_P_85:A14","CH_GGVC_P_85:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0146","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT6","text":"An epistemic tension remains between the natural representation of trinitarian processions and the impossibility of perfect natural knowledge of the Trinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_85:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_85:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0112","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT7","text":"The principal universality of the image in both sexes coheres formally, but the secondary analogy of principle and end reintroduces sexual asymmetry.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT8","text":"Certain transitions, especially between analogy, specific representation, and the trinitarian mystery, are supported more by authorities and distinctions than by complete demonstration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:A3","CH_GGVC_P_85:A4","CH_GGVC_P_85:A9","CH_GGVC_P_85:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_85:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text from the definition of image through the localization and operation of the mind to orientation toward God and the terminological closure of likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_85:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_85:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_85:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_85:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_85:P0183","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_85@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_85:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 94","title":"First Part · Question 93","context":"Chapter 94","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 93"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 93","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 94","order":95,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_86"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_86@R001","sha256":"8df023b8238cd72e3caf92904e91aac7db4dd551f4bc50c28891ddfaeea92bc5","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS1","text":"Textus investigat quatenus status primi hominis cognitionem Dei, Angelorum, rerum omnium et veritatis a deceptione immunem determinaverit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS2","text":"Status innocentiae integritatem naturae et cognitionem excellentiorem confert, sed non beatitudinem consummatam neque modum cognitionis substantiarum separatarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS3","text":"Visio divinae essentiae negatur ex nexu inter visionem beatificam, immobilitatem voluntatis in Deo et peccatum Adae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS4","text":"Cognitio primi hominis definiri debet per distinctionem inter modum naturalem animae corpori coniunctae et integritatem eiusdem animae a corpore non impeditam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS5","text":"Scientia universalis primi hominis derivatur ex munere originario instructionis et gubernationis, non ex omniscientia absoluta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS6","text":"Deceptio excluditur, quia rectitudo innocentiae ignorantiam pati potest, assensum autem falsi tamquam veri non potest pati; seductio mulieris ad peccatum interius iam praecedens refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS7","text":"Argumentatio metaphysico-reconstructiva procedit a distinctione statuum animae ad determinationem graduum cognitionis, limitum scientiae et condicionum possibilitatis erroris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","text":"Divina essentia est ipsa beatitudo hominis perfecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","text":"Qui Deum per essentiam videt voluntate a Deo averti et peccare non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A3","text":"Adam peccavit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","text":"Anima humana corpori coniuncta secundum vitam animalem intelligit per conversionem ad phantasmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","text":"Integritas innocentiae modum naturalem animae corpori coniunctae non tollit, sed inferiora superioribus subdit et impedimentum eorum removet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A6","text":"Deus per creaturam cognoscitur, et per effectus intelligibiles clarius quam per effectus sensibiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A7","text":"Cognitio Angeli excedit modum cognitionis humanae per phantasmata, ita quod cognitio humana sui ipsius ad cognitionem essentiae angelicae non sufficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A8","text":"Res a Deo primo institutae producuntur in perfectione sufficienti ad hoc quod sint principia aliorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A9","text":"Primus homo instituitur ut principium aliorum per instructionem et gubernationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","text":"Instructio et gubernatio requirunt cognitionem eorum quae homines naturaliter cognoscere possunt et eorum supernaturalium quae ad vitam humanam illius status ordinandam necessaria sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A11","text":"Adam scientiam per species a Deo infusas accepit, quae tamen eiusdem rationis manet cum scientia humana a rebus acquisita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","text":"Cognitio primi hominis non comprehendit cogitationes humanas, futura contingentia neque singularia ad gubernationem vitae humanae non necessaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","text":"Falsum est malum intellectus, sicut verum est bonum eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","text":"Innocentia admittere potest carentiam notitiae, sed non assensum falsi quasi veri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A15","text":"Deceptio intellectus accidit ex inferioribus, cum phantasia vel simile naturale iudicatorium ligat; ratio non ligata veritatem diiudicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A16","text":"Seductio mulieris peccatum operis praecedens iam peccatum internae elationis et superbam de se praesumptionem subsequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A17","text":"Adam in naturalibus proficere potuisset modo sciendi per experientiam, et in supernaturalibus etiam numero cognitorum per novas revelationes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX1","text":"Beatitudo paradisiaca non est perfecta beatitudo quae in visione divinae essentiae consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX2","text":"Cognitio Dei sine medio demonstrationis non est cognitio Dei sine medio creato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX3","text":"Carentia obscuritatis ex peccato non excludit omnem obscuritatem creaturae respectu immensitatis divinae claritatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX4","text":"Corpus incorruptibile non mutat animam primi hominis in animam separatam neque cognitionem eius in cognitionem angelicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX5","text":"Scientia omnium non est scientia omnium simpliciter, sed scientia omnium ad naturam humanam et regimen vitae humanae pertinentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX6","text":"Species infusae non efficiunt scientiam primi hominis alterius generis quam scientia humana naturaliter acquisita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX7","text":"Ignorantia non idem est ac deceptio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX8","text":"Apparentia sensibilis vel phantastica falsum repraesentans non necessario producit assensum falsum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX9","text":"Seductio ante peccatum operis non probat deceptionem in integritate originaria, quia praesupponit peccatum interius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D1","text":"Adam, secundum communem statum illius vitae, Deum per essentiam non vidit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","CH_GGVC_P_86:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D2","text":"Adam Deum per effectus intelligibiles clarius et firmius quam homo post peccatum cognoscebat, manente tamen mediatione creaturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D3","text":"Adam Angelos per essentiam videre non poterat, quamvis de eis cognitionem certiorem quam homines post lapsum haberet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D4","text":"Scientia primi hominis comprehendebat universum naturale humaniter scibile et supernaturalia ad statum illum gubernandum necessaria, non autem objecta contingentia vel inutilia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A8","CH_GGVC_P_86:A9","CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D5","text":"Infusio divina scientiam Adae accelerat et complet, non autem eius rationem cognoscitivam in speciem alienam convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D6","text":"Progressus cognitivus Adae naturaliter esset mutatio a cognitione intellectuali ad cognitionem etiam experimentalem, supernaturaliter autem accessio novarum revelationum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D7","text":"Carentia scientiae de aliquo non facit intellectum innocentis falsitati consentientem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D8","text":"Sensuum et phantasiae repraesentationes aberrantes deceptionem non efficiunt, si ratio recta et non ligata superius iudicium exercet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D9","text":"Deceptio mulieris non describit statum innocentiae integrum, sed effectum interioris elationis iam admissae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D10","text":"In rebus ignotis, textus vel suspensionem assensus vel speciale divinum auxilium admittit ut deceptio vitetur, sine electione definitiva inter has duas explicationes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD1","text":"Status innocentiae constituitur ut regimen epistemicum medium inter cognitionem postlapsariam impeditam et beatitudinem visionis immediatae divinae essentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD2","text":"Perfectio cognitiva primi hominis mensuratur munere causaliter originario instructionis et gubernationis, non amplitudine cognitionis sine fine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A8","CH_GGVC_P_86:A9","CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD3","text":"Integritas intellectualis definitur positive per ordinem hierarchicum et negative per impossibilitatem assensus falsi, non per absentiam omnis ignorantiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD4","text":"Peccatum Adae fungitur indicio modali quod distinguit statum meriti a statu consummatae beatitudinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","CH_GGVC_P_86:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD5","text":"Cognitio originaria est simul plena secundum ambitum suum ordinatum et progressiva secundum modum experientiae atque novas illuminationes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet perfectionem naturalem innocentiae idem esse ac perfectionem eschatologicam beatitudinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","CH_GGVC_P_86:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet incorruptibilitatem corporis per se sufficere ad cognitionem substantiarum separatarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","CH_GGVC_P_86:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet omnem defectum cognitionis esse malum intellectus eiusdem rationis ac falsitas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet identitatem naturae humanae exigere eundem modum initialis acquisitionis scientiae in primo homine et in posteris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A8","CH_GGVC_P_86:A9","CH_GGVC_P_86:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet phantasma vel sensibile apparens intellectum necessitate cogere ad falsum assensum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SNX1","text":"Textus excludit continuum in quo maior claritas cognitionis per creaturas tandem sine ruptione in visionem divinae essentiae transeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","CH_GGVC_P_86:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SNX2","text":"Textus excludit cognitionem humanam sibi sufficientem et a subiectione animae Deo atque superiorum inferioribus independentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SNX3","text":"Textus excludit innocentiam tamquam transparentiam cognitivam universalem, quia ignorantia manet possibilis etiam ubi deceptio impossibilis ponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SNX4","text":"Textus excludit errorem tamquam proprietatem neutram naturae integrae, quia falsitas ad malum intellectus et ad dissolutionem ordinis refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS1","text":"Modus naturalis animae corpori coniunctae + integritas innocentiae → cognitio per phantasmata manens, sed ab impedimento inferiorum liberata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS2","text":"Visio divinae essentiae → immobilitas voluntatis in Deo → impossibilitas peccati; peccatum Adae → negatio visionis essentiae in statu communi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS3","text":"Effectus creati → distinctio sensibilium et intelligibilium → cognitio Dei per effectus intelligibiles clara, firma, sed mediata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS4","text":"Cognitio humana per phantasmata + excessus modi angelici → negatio visionis Angelorum per essentiam → cognitio Angelorum elevata sed imperfecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS5","text":"Prima institutio perfecta + munus instructionis et gubernationis → species infusae → scientia naturalium universaliter requisitorum et supernaturalium necessariorum → exclusio contingentium et inutilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS6","text":"Rectitudo animae Deo subiectae → inferiora superioribus subiecta → ratio non ligata → ignorantia sine falso assensu; elatio interior → ruptura rectitudinis → seductio possibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF1","text":"Conditio primi hominis → distinctio animae et corporis → determinatio cognitionis, voluntatis et integritatis originariae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF2","text":"Beatitudo paradisiaca apparens → distinctio beatitudinis imperfectae et perfectae → negatio visionis divinae essentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF3","text":"Natura animae corpori coniunctae → conversio ad phantasmata → negatio cognitionis angelicae per essentiam → affirmatio cognitionis angelicae excellentioris quam nostrae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF4","text":"Institutio primi hominis ut principii aliorum → necessitas instructionis et gubernationis → scientia infusa sufficienter universalis → delimitatio eius obiecti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF5","text":"Ignorantia rerum non necessariarum → distinctio privationis et falsitatis → negatio deceptionis in statu innocentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF6","text":"Seductio relata → reclassificatio eius ut effectus elationis interioris praecedentis → conservatio immunitatis originalis a deceptione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME1","text":"Paradisus reclassificatur non ut patria beatifica, sed ut status integritatis naturalis ordinatae ad praemium ulterius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME2","text":"Oppositio simplex inter cognitionem mediatam et immediatam dissolvitur per distinctionem medii demonstrationis a medio creato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME3","text":"Scientia omnium reclassificatur ab omniscientia quantitativa ad sufficientiam teleologicam pro munere originario hominis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME4","text":"Ignorantia, falsitas, deceptio et peccatum internum separantur ut quattuor conditiones non convertibiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME5","text":"Impedimentum cognitionis substantiarum separatarum transfertur a sola corruptibilitate corporis ad disproportionem inter obiectum connaturale intellectus humani et excellentiam obiecti angelici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus negat Adam Deum et Angelos per essentiam vidisse, affirmat scientiam sufficienter universalem, et negat deceptionem in innocentia permanente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ALT2","text":"Structural — Status innocentiae componitur ex modo naturali animae corpori coniunctae et ordine rectitudinis quo inferiora superioribus subduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio objectiones resolvit per distinctiones operativas: beatitudo imperfecta et perfecta, duplex medium, ignorantia et deceptio, natura et integritas, ambitus scientiae et omniscientia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Ordo creationis procedit ab actu perfecto principio aliorum ad propagationem, instructionem, experientiam, meritum et revelationes ulteriores; lapsus hunc ordinem per elationem interiorem frangit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de beatitudine, peccato, modo cognitionis per phantasmata, integritate, institutione originaria et falsitate sufficiunt ad quattuor responsiones principales restituendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT2","text":"Articulus primus maxime pendet a nexu necessario inter visionem divinae essentiae et impossibilitatem peccandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT3","text":"Articulus secundus maxime cohaeret ex distinctione inter modum essendi naturalem animae corpori coniunctae et gradum integritatis eiusdem animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter scientiam infusam omnium naturaliter scibilium et progressum experimentalem, qui mutationem modi sciendi concedit sine incremento numeri naturalium cognitorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT5","text":"Exceptio possibilis raptus Adae ad visionem divinae essentiae enuntiatur, sed condiciones et functionem eius intra systema non explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT6","text":"De rebus ignotis textus duas vias non plene conciliatas relinquit, scilicet abstinentiam ab assensu falso et divinum auxilium speciale contra deceptionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT7","text":"Seductio mulieris cum immunitate originaria a deceptione conciliatur per prioritatem peccati interioris, sed haec conciliatio ex chronologia elationis mentalis pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT8","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, quia a statu animae distinguit cognitionis gradus, ab his scientiae ambitum, atque ab ordine rectitudinis impossibilitatem deceptionis deducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165515849945Z_ca01aa15","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 94","source_sha256":"8df023b8238cd72e3caf92904e91aac7db4dd551f4bc50c28891ddfaeea92bc5","sha256":"6185a2a079515727dd5296b04eaa1d91e66a838c42e451ba58b99557d682507d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:55:15.851746+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS1","text":"The text investigates to what extent the state of the first man determined a knowledge of God, the Angels, all things, and truth immune from deception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS2","text":"The state of innocence confers integrity of nature and more excellent knowledge, but not consummate beatitude nor the mode of knowledge of separate substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS3","text":"The vision of the divine essence is denied on the basis of the connection between beatific vision, the immovability of the will in God, and Adam's sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS4","text":"The knowledge of the first man must be defined by the distinction between the natural mode of the soul conjoined to the body and the integrity of that same soul not impeded by the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS5","text":"The universal knowledge of the first man derives from his original office of instruction and governance, not from absolute omniscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS6","text":"Deception is excluded because the rectitude of innocence can suffer ignorance but cannot suffer assent to the false as true; the woman's seduction into sin is referred to an already preceding interior sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AS7","text":"The metaphysical-reconstructive argument proceeds from the distinction of the states of the soul to the determination of degrees of knowledge, limits of knowledge, and conditions of the possibility of error.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","text":"The divine essence is itself the perfect beatitude of man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","text":"He who sees God through His essence cannot turn away from God in will and sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A3","text":"Adam sinned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","text":"The human soul conjoined to the body, according to animal life, understands by turning to phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","text":"The integrity of innocence does not remove the natural mode of the soul conjoined to the body, but subjects lower things to higher and removes their impediment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A6","text":"God is known through creatures, and more clearly through intelligible effects than through sensible effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A7","text":"The knowledge of an Angel exceeds the human mode of knowledge through phantasms, such that human knowledge of itself does not suffice for knowledge of the angelic essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A8","text":"Things first instituted by God are produced in perfection sufficient for them to be principles of others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A9","text":"The first man is instituted as a principle of others through instruction and governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","text":"Instruction and governance require knowledge of those things that men can naturally know and of those supernatural things necessary for ordering the human life of that state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A11","text":"Adam received knowledge through species infused by God, which nevertheless remains of the same character as human knowledge acquired from things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","text":"The knowledge of the first man does not encompass human thoughts, future contingents, or singulars not necessary for the governance of human life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","text":"The false is the evil of the intellect, just as the true is its good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","text":"Innocence can admit lack of knowledge, but not assent to the false as though true.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A15","text":"Deception of the intellect occurs from the lower powers, when phantasy or a similar natural faculty of judgment binds it; reason unbound judges truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A16","text":"The woman's seduction, preceding the sin of deed, follows upon the sin of interior exaltation and proud presumption concerning herself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:A17","text":"Adam could have advanced in natural matters in the mode of knowing through experience, and in supernatural matters also in the number of things known through new revelations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX1","text":"Paradisal beatitude is not the perfect beatitude that consists in the vision of the divine essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX2","text":"Knowledge of God without the medium of demonstration is not knowledge of God without a created medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX3","text":"The absence of obscurity from sin does not exclude every obscurity of the creature in relation to the immensity of divine clarity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX4","text":"An incorruptible body does not change the soul of the first man into a separate soul nor his knowledge into angelic knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX5","text":"Knowledge of all things is not knowledge of all things simply, but knowledge of all things pertaining to human nature and the governance of human life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX6","text":"Infused species do not make the knowledge of the first man of a different genus from naturally acquired human knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX7","text":"Ignorance is not the same as deception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX8","text":"A sensible or phantastic appearance representing the false does not necessarily produce false assent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:NX9","text":"Seduction before the sin of deed does not prove deception in original integrity, because it presupposes interior sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D1","text":"Adam, according to the common state of that life, did not see God through His essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","CH_GGVC_P_86:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D2","text":"Adam knew God through intelligible effects more clearly and firmly than man after sin, while the mediation of the creature nevertheless remained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D3","text":"Adam could not see the Angels through their essence, although he had more certain knowledge of them than men after the Fall.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D4","text":"The knowledge of the first man encompassed the natural universe knowable in a human manner and the supernatural things necessary for governing that state, but not contingent or useless objects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A8","CH_GGVC_P_86:A9","CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D5","text":"Divine infusion accelerates and completes Adam's knowledge, but does not convert his cognitive character into an alien species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D6","text":"Adam's cognitive progress would naturally have been a change from intellectual knowledge to knowledge also through experience, but supernaturally an addition of new revelations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D7","text":"The lack of knowledge about something does not make the intellect of the innocent consent to falsehood.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D8","text":"Aberrant representations of the senses and phantasy do not produce deception if right and unbound reason exercises higher judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D9","text":"The woman's deception does not describe the integral state of innocence, but the effect of an interior exaltation already admitted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:D10","text":"Regarding unknown things, the text admits either suspension of assent or special divine assistance in order to avoid deception, without definitively choosing between these two explanations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD1","text":"The state of innocence is constituted as an intermediate epistemic regime between impeded postlapsarian knowledge and the beatitude of immediate vision of the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD2","text":"The cognitive perfection of the first man is measured by the causally original office of instruction and governance, not by an unlimited scope of knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A8","CH_GGVC_P_86:A9","CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD3","text":"Intellectual integrity is defined positively through hierarchical order and negatively through the impossibility of false assent, not through the absence of all ignorance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD4","text":"Adam's sin serves as a modal indication distinguishing the state of merit from the state of consummate beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","CH_GGVC_P_86:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SD5","text":"Original knowledge is at once complete according to its ordered scope and progressive according to the mode of experience and new illuminations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A10","CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX1","text":"It must be false that the natural perfection of innocence is identical with the eschatological perfection of beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","CH_GGVC_P_86:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the incorruptibility of the body is sufficient in itself for knowledge of separate substances.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A4","CH_GGVC_P_86:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX3","text":"It must be false that every defect of knowledge is an evil of the intellect of the same character as falsehood.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the identity of human nature requires the same mode of initial acquisition of knowledge in the first man and in his descendants.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A8","CH_GGVC_P_86:A9","CH_GGVC_P_86:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:DNX5","text":"It must be false that a phantasm or an appearing sensible object compels the intellect by necessity to false assent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SNX1","text":"The text excludes a continuum in which greater clarity of knowledge through creatures eventually passes without rupture into the vision of the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A1","CH_GGVC_P_86:A2","CH_GGVC_P_86:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SNX2","text":"The text excludes human knowledge that is self-sufficient and independent from the soul's subjection to God and from the subjection of lower things to higher.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A5","CH_GGVC_P_86:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SNX3","text":"The text excludes innocence as universal cognitive transparency, because ignorance remains possible even where deception is held impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A12","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:SNX4","text":"The text excludes error as a neutral property of integral nature, because falsehood is referred to the evil of the intellect and to the dissolution of order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_86:A13","CH_GGVC_P_86:A14","CH_GGVC_P_86:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS1","text":"Natural mode of the soul conjoined to the body + integrity of innocence → knowledge through phantasms remaining, but freed from the impediment of the lower powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS2","text":"Vision of the divine essence → immovability of the will in God → impossibility of sin; Adam's sin → denial of the vision of the essence in the common state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS3","text":"Created effects → distinction of sensibles and intelligibles → knowledge of God through intelligible effects clear, firm, but mediated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS4","text":"Human knowledge through phantasms + excess of the angelic mode → denial of vision of Angels through their essence → elevated but imperfect knowledge of Angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS5","text":"Perfect first institution + office of instruction and governance → infused species → knowledge of universally required natural things and necessary supernatural things → exclusion of contingents and useless things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:FGS6","text":"Rectitude of the soul subjected to God → lower things subjected to higher → reason unbound → ignorance without false assent; interior exaltation → rupture of rectitude → seduction possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF1","text":"Condition of the first man → distinction of soul and body → determination of original knowledge, will, and integrity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF2","text":"Apparent paradisal beatitude → distinction of imperfect and perfect beatitude → denial of the vision of the divine essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF3","text":"Nature of the soul conjoined to the body → turning to phantasms → denial of angelic knowledge through essence → affirmation of angelic knowledge more excellent than ours.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF4","text":"Institution of the first man as a principle of others → necessity of instruction and governance → sufficiently universal infused knowledge → delimitation of its object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF5","text":"Ignorance of non-necessary things → distinction of privation and falsehood → denial of deception in the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:AF6","text":"Reported seduction → reclassification of it as the effect of preceding interior exaltation → preservation of original immunity from deception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME1","text":"Paradise is reclassified not as the beatific homeland, but as a state of natural integrity ordered to a further reward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME2","text":"The simple opposition between mediated and immediate knowledge is dissolved through the distinction between the medium of demonstration and the created medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME3","text":"Knowledge of all things is reclassified from quantitative omniscience to teleological sufficiency for man's original office.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME4","text":"Ignorance, falsehood, deception, and interior sin are separated as four non-convertible conditions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ME5","text":"The impediment to knowledge of separate substances is transferred from the corruptibility of the body alone to the disproportion between the connatural object of the human intellect and the excellence of the angelic object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text denies that Adam saw God and the Angels through their essence, affirms sufficiently universal knowledge, and denies deception in enduring innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ALT2","text":"Structural — The state of innocence is composed of the natural mode of the soul conjoined to the body and the order of rectitude by which lower things are subjected to higher.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument resolves objections through operative distinctions: imperfect and perfect beatitude, a twofold medium, ignorance and deception, nature and integrity, scope of knowledge and omniscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The order of creation proceeds from a perfect act, a principle of others, to propagation, instruction, experience, merit, and further revelations; the Fall breaks this order through interior exaltation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning beatitude, sin, the mode of knowledge through phantasms, integrity, original institution, and falsehood suffice to reconstruct the four principal responses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT2","text":"The first article depends most of all on the necessary connection between the vision of the divine essence and the impossibility of sinning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT3","text":"The second article coheres most of all from the distinction between the natural mode of being of the soul conjoined to the body and the degree of integrity of that same soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains between infused knowledge of all things naturally knowable and experimental progress, which allows a change in the mode of knowing without an increase in the number of natural things known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT5","text":"A possible exception of Adam's rapture to the vision of the divine essence is stated, but its conditions and function within the system are not explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT6","text":"Concerning unknown things, the text leaves two not fully reconciled paths, namely abstention from false assent and special divine assistance against deception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT7","text":"The woman's seduction is reconciled with original immunity from deception through the priority of interior sin, but this reconciliation depends on the chronology of mental exaltation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_86:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it distinguishes degrees of knowledge from the state of the soul, the scope of knowledge from these, and derives from the order of rectitude the impossibility of deception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_86:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_86@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_86:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 95","title":"First Part · Question 94","context":"Chapter 95","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 94"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 94","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 95","order":96,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_87"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_87@R001","sha256":"92e5dcb59ff8a6b3166d16edeabb584af83dfca3991006b53bd277694eed7183","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS1","text":"Quaestio voluntatem primi hominis per quattuor effectus connexos examinat: gratiam originariam, passiones, virtutes et efficaciam meriti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS2","text":"Argumentatio rectitudinem primi status constituit ut ordinem causaliter hierarchicum: Deus rationem, ratio vires inferiores, anima corpus ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS3","text":"Solutio inferit gratiam originariam ex eo quod obedientia inferiorum post peccatum solvitur, naturalibus tamen perman entibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS4","text":"Passiones et virtutes non simpliciter adsunt aut absunt, sed secundum obiectum, imperium rationis, habitum et actum distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS5","text":"Comparatio meriti ante et post lapsum multiplicat mensuras: radix gratiae et caritatis, quantitas absoluta operis, quantitas proportionalis facultati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS6","text":"Motus concludit statum innocentiae superiorem fuisse secundum gratiam et magnitudinem absolutam operum, statum autem post lapsum maiorem proportionem meriti ex infirmitate habere posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","text":"Rectitudo primi status consistit in subiectione rationis Deo, virium inferiorum rationi et corporis animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","text":"Subiectio virium inferiorum rationi et corporis animae non est naturalis, quia post peccatum solvitur, cum naturalia permaneant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","text":"Prima subiectio rationis Deo, ut causa subiectionum inferiorum, est donum supernaturale gratiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A4","text":"Gratia in primo instanti creationis adesse potest, quia voluntas consensum in eodem instanti elicere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","text":"Passiones animae sunt motus appetitus sensitivi circa bonum vel malum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","text":"Status innocentiae nullum malum praesens vel imminens habet, nullum bonum tunc necessarium absens, et appetitum sensitivum rationi totaliter subicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","text":"Virtutes sunt perfectiones quibus ratio in Deum ordinatur et vires inferiores regulae rationis disponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","text":"Ubi materia vel actus virtutis imperfectionem perfectioni primi status repugnantem importat, virtus adest secundum habitum, non secundum actum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","text":"Perfectio primi status visionem Dei per essentiam et fruitionem beatitudinis finalis nondum continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A10","text":"Virtus moralis passiones per se ordinat, non universaliter tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","text":"Quantitas meriti ex radice gratiae et caritatis praemium essentiale respicit, ex quantitate operis praemium accidentale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","text":"Quantitas operis meritorii absoluta a magnitudine operis, proportionalis ab excessu operis supra facultatem agentis mensuratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","text":"Absentia impedimenti in natura humana gratiam copiosiorem et maiora opera absolute possibilia reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","text":"Infirmitas post lapsum efficit ut opus minus absolute maiorem facultatem agentis proportionaliter excedere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A15","text":"Homo post lapsum gratia ad plura indiget, non tamen magis ad finem principalem, qui est vita aeterna.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A16","text":"Difficultas actualis mensuram proportionalem meriti respicit et promptitudinem voluntatis a caritate causatam significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A17","text":"Resistentia tentationi sine gratia non est meritoria, et absentia interioris impulsus ad malum resistentiam in primo statu faciliorem facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A18","text":"Perseverantia ut habitus eligendi bonum distinguitur a perseverantia ut continuatio actus sine interruption e.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX1","text":"Adam non excluditur a spiritualitate animae; negatur tantum spiritualitas corporis quae in Christo incohatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX2","text":"Spiritus Sanctus in Adam non abest simpliciter, sed non eodem modo quo in fidelibus ad hereditatem aeternam statim admittendis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX3","text":"Gratia originaria non requirit tempus naturae ante gratiam nec actum naturae quo gratia mereatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX4","text":"Innocentia non est carentia omnis passionis, sed carentia passionum mali et passionum rationi repugnantium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX5","text":"Impassibilitas animae non est privatio amoris, gaudii, spei vel desiderii ordinati, sed exclusio passionum rationem impedientium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX6","text":"Habere omnes virtutes non significat omnem virtutem in omni materia actu exerceri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX7","text":"Perfectio originaria non est beatitudo consummata, quia fides et spes ibi manere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX8","text":"Maior difficultas post lapsum non constituit conditionem simpliciter meliorem nec efficaciam meriti univoce maiorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D1","text":"Primus homo creatus est in gratia, quia rectitudo quae inferiores subiectiones causat naturam excedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D2","text":"In innocentia amor, gaudium, spes et desiderium ordinatum esse possunt; timor, dolor et cupiditas boni tunc abs entis excluduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D3","text":"Passiones licitae in primo statu iudicium rationis consequuntur neque illud praeveniunt aut impediunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D4","text":"Rectitudo primi status exigit omnes virtutes aliquo modo adesse, quia ipsa est ordinatio rationis in Deum et inferiorum secundum rationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D5","text":"Caritas et iustitia in primo homine secundum habitum et actum adfuerunt; fides et spes similiter adfuerunt, quia beatitudo finalis nondum possidebatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D6","text":"Poenitentia et misericordia adesse poterant habitualiter sine actu, dum temperantia et fortitudo actum habere poterant circa delectationem, spem et audaciam ordinandas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D7","text":"Meritum in innocentia maius fuisset secundum radicem gratiae et secundum quantitatem absolutam operis; post lapsum maius esse potest secundum quantitatem proportionalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D8","text":"Difficultas post lapsum non probat gratiam simpliciter copiosiorem, sed potest opus facultatem infirmiorem proportionate excedere atque, ut poenalis, satisfactoria esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","CH_GGVC_P_87:A15","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D9","text":"Resistentia tentationi, si gratia desit, meritoria non est; in primo autem statu resistentia minus impedita fuisset, quia interior concupiscentia ad malum non urgebat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D10","text":"Adam perseverantiam ut habitum habere potuit, quamvis perseverantiam ut continuationem nunquam interruptam non habuerit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SD1","text":"Iustitia originalis non est aggregatum perfectionum naturalium, sed architectura supernaturalis in qua gratia per rationem corpus et appetitus ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SD2","text":"Status innocentiae est integritas non consummata: gratiam et virtutes continet, sed visionem beatam, fruitionem finalem et perseverantiam inintermissam non includit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SD3","text":"Lapsus non tantum culpam adiungit, sed ordinem affectivum et corporalem dissolvit atque mensuram proportionalem meriti mutat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SD4","text":"Comparatio statuum ante et post lapsum univoca esse non potest, quia gratia, magnitudo operis, infirmitas et proportio diversa praemiorum et meritorum ratio nes constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX1","text":"Natura humana sola non sufficit ad stabilendum ordinem integrum inter Deum, rationem, appetitum et corpus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX2","text":"Perfectio affectiva non postul at abolitionem passionis, sed abolitionem motus affectivi qui rationi antecedit vel repugnat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX3","text":"Virtus non est tantum remedium peccati, miseriae vel passionis immoderatae, quia virtutes ordinantes etiam sine his malis manent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX4","text":"Integritas originaria non aequatur gloriae nec confirmationi ultimae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX5","text":"Meritum non habet unam mensuram in qua difficultas, caritas, gratia et magnitudo operis in eandem quantitatem redigantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SNX1","text":"Creatura neque gratiam ex sola natura producit neque rectitudinem originariam ex se ips a causaliter fundat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SNX2","text":"Possibilitas lapsus manere debet ut status primus sit vere rectus sed non finaliter consummatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SNX3","text":"Adversitas post lapsum nec beneficium purum nec malum simpliciter mensurabile est, quia proportionalem meritum augere potest dum gratiam, integritatem et magnitudinem absolutam operis minuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","CH_GGVC_P_87:A15","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS1","text":"Rectitudo hierarchica → probatio per amissionem post peccatum et permanentiam naturalium → subiectio non naturalis → gratia originaria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS2","text":"Carentia mali et boni tunc necessarii absentis + appetitus totaliter rationi subiectus → passiones ordinatae admittuntur, passiones inordinatae excluduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS3","text":"Virtus ut perfectio ordinis + distinctio habitus et actus + imperfectio materiae → distributio virtutum secundum actum, habitum vel conditionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS4","text":"Meritum ex gratia et caritate → praemium essentiale; meritum ex opere absoluto vel proportionali → praemium accidentale.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS5","text":"Integritas originaria → gratia copiosior et opera maiora absolute; infirmitas postlapsaria → excessus proportionatus maior; comparatio univoca inter status impeditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","CH_GGVC_P_87:A15","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AF1","text":"Creatio primi hominis → rectitudo hierarchica → exclusio causalitatis mere naturalis → gratia in ipsa origine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AF2","text":"Innocentia → determinatio boni et mali obiecti → subiectio appetitus → passiones ordinatae sine perturbatione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AF3","text":"Rectitudo → virtutes omnes aliquo modo → distinctio habitus et actus → imperfectio compatibilis vel incompatibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AF4","text":"Gratia et caritas + opus absolutum/proportionale → comparatio innocentiae et lapsus → superioritas diversa secundum mensuram assumptam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME1","text":"Iustitia originalis reclassificatur a perfectione morali generica ad structuram causalem supernaturalis subiectionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter passionem et innocentiam dissolvitur, quia oppositio vera est inter passionem ordinatam et passionem rationi repugnantem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME3","text":"Virtus reclassificatur per tres modos: praesentia habitualis, exercitium actuale et aptitudo conditionalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME4","text":"Fides et spes non iam signa solius imperfectionis sunt, sed virtutes compatibiles cum integritate non consummata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME5","text":"Comparatio meriti reclassificatur ab una scala difficultatis ad pluralitatem radicis gratiae, magnitudinis operis et proportionis ad facultatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus statuit utrum primus homo gratiam, passiones, virtutes et meritum habuerit vel exercuerit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ALT2","text":"Structural — Omnia responsa dependent ab ordine Deus → ratio → vires inferiores → corpus et ab eius conservatione vel dissolutione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio quaestiones binarias in distinctiones modales convertit: naturale et supernaturale, habitus et actus, absolutum et proportionale, integritas et gloria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Status primus ponitur inter naturam nudam et gloriam consummatam, dum lapsus ordinem praesentem, affectivum et meritorium temporaliter reconfigurat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT1","text":"Systema extractum sufficit ad conclusionem de gratia originaria et ad partitiones de passionibus, virtutibus et merito restituendas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT2","text":"Firmitas maxima systematis est nexus causaliter ordinatus inter gratiam, subiectionem rationis Deo et obedientiam inferiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT3","text":"Commissura principalis est transitus ab amissione post peccatum ad conclusionem quod obedientia originaria supernaturalis fuerit; transitus permanentiam naturae post lapsum praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT4","text":"Compatibilitas gratiae in primo instanti et consensus voluntatis resolvitur per distinctionem instantis et motus non continui, sed ordinem exactum istius concomitantiae ulterius non explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT5","text":"Distinctio habitus et actus virtutes incompatibili materiae servat, sed relatio inter gratiam originariam et defectibilitatem perseverantiae non plene determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT6","text":"Comparatio meriti interne cohaeret solum si praemium essentiale et accidentale, quantitas absoluta et proportionalis stricte distinguuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: rectitudo originaria → gratia → ordinatio passionum et virtutum → comparatio meriti post lapsum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165542395791Z_eab7df74","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 95","source_sha256":"92e5dcb59ff8a6b3166d16edeabb584af83dfca3991006b53bd277694eed7183","sha256":"cea46974c9f73677e5a45926c2c2b1f0fadd5cef7d79fd4fa7f78a75d0605123","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:55:42.396787+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS1","text":"The question examines the will of the first human being through four connected effects: original grace, passions, virtues, and the efficacy of merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS2","text":"The argument establishes the rectitude of the first state as a causally hierarchical order: God orders reason, reason the lower powers, and the soul the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS3","text":"The solution infers original grace from the fact that the obedience of the lower powers is dissolved after sin, while natural things nevertheless remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS4","text":"Passions and virtues are not simply present or absent, but are distinguished according to object, the command of reason, habit, and act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS5","text":"The comparison of merit before and after the fall multiplies the measures: the root of grace and charity, the absolute quantity of the work, and the quantity proportional to capacity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AS6","text":"The argument concludes that the state of innocence was superior according to grace and the absolute magnitude of works, whereas the state after the fall can have a greater proportion of merit by reason of weakness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","text":"The rectitude of the first state consists in the subjection of reason to God, of the lower powers to reason, and of the body to the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","text":"The subjection of the lower powers to reason and of the body to the soul is not natural, because it is dissolved after sin, although natural things remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","text":"The first subjection of reason to God, as the cause of the lower subjections, is the supernatural gift of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A4","text":"Grace can be present in the first instant of creation, because the will can elicit consent in the same instant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","text":"The passions of the soul are motions of the sensitive appetite concerning good or evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","text":"The state of innocence has no present or imminent evil, no absent good then necessary, and subjects the sensitive appetite wholly to reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","text":"Virtues are perfections by which reason is ordered to God and the lower powers are disposed according to the rule of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","text":"Where the matter or act of a virtue entails an imperfection opposed to the perfection of the first state, the virtue is present according to habit, not according to act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","text":"The perfection of the first state does not yet include the vision of God through essence and the enjoyment of final beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A10","text":"Moral virtue of itself orders passions; it does not universally remove them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","text":"The quantity of merit, from the root of grace and charity, concerns the essential reward; from the quantity of the work, the accidental reward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","text":"The absolute quantity of a meritorious work is measured by the magnitude of the work; its proportional quantity, by the excess of the work over the capacity of the agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","text":"The absence of impediment in human nature renders more abundant grace and greater works absolutely possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","text":"Weakness after the fall makes it possible for a work lesser in absolute terms to exceed proportionally more greatly the capacity of the agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A15","text":"The human being after the fall needs grace for more things, though not more for the principal end, which is eternal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A16","text":"Actual difficulty concerns the proportional measure of merit and signifies the promptness of the will caused by charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A17","text":"Resistance to temptation without grace is not meritorious, and the absence of an interior impulse toward evil makes resistance easier in the first state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:A18","text":"Perseverance as a habit of choosing good is distinguished from perseverance as the continuation of an act without interruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX1","text":"Adam is not excluded from the spirituality of the soul; only the spirituality of the body that is begun in Christ is denied.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX2","text":"The Holy Spirit is not simply absent in Adam, but is not present in the same way as in the faithful who are immediately to be admitted to the eternal inheritance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX3","text":"Original grace requires neither a time of nature before grace nor an act of nature by which grace is merited.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX4","text":"Innocence is not the absence of every passion, but the absence of passions of evil and of passions opposed to reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX5","text":"Impassibility of the soul is not the privation of ordered love, joy, hope, or desire, but the exclusion of passions that impede reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX6","text":"To have all virtues does not mean that every virtue is actually exercised in every matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX7","text":"Original perfection is not consummated beatitude, because faith and hope can remain there.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:NX8","text":"Greater difficulty after the fall does not constitute a condition simply better, nor an efficacy of merit univocally greater.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D1","text":"The first human being was created in grace, because the rectitude that causes the lower subjections exceeds nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D2","text":"In innocence, love, joy, hope, and ordered desire can be present; fear, pain, and desire for a good then absent are excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D3","text":"Permissible passions in the first state follow the judgment of reason and neither precede nor impede it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D4","text":"The rectitude of the first state requires all virtues to be present in some manner, because it itself is the ordering of reason to God and of lower things according to reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D5","text":"Charity and justice were present in the first human being according to habit and act; faith and hope were likewise present, because final beatitude was not yet possessed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D6","text":"Repentance and mercy could be present habitually without act, while temperance and fortitude could have act concerning the ordering of delight, hope, and daring.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D7","text":"Merit in innocence would have been greater according to the root of grace and according to the absolute quantity of the work; after the fall it can be greater according to proportional quantity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D8","text":"Difficulty after the fall does not prove grace simply more abundant, but a work can proportionately exceed a weaker capacity and, as penal, be satisfactory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","CH_GGVC_P_87:A15","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D9","text":"Resistance to temptation, if grace is lacking, is not meritorious; in the first state, however, resistance would have been less impeded, because interior concupiscence did not press toward evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:D10","text":"Adam could have perseverance as a habit, although he did not have perseverance as uninterrupted continuation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SD1","text":"Original justice is not an aggregate of natural perfections, but a supernatural architecture in which grace orders body and appetites through reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SD2","text":"The state of innocence is unconsummated integrity: it contains grace and virtues, but does not include the beatific vision, final enjoyment, and uninterrupted perseverance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SD3","text":"The fall not only adds guilt, but dissolves affective and bodily order and changes the proportional measure of merit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SD4","text":"The comparison of the states before and after the fall cannot be univocal, because grace, magnitude of work, weakness, and proportion constitute diverse accounts of rewards and merits.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX1","text":"Human nature alone does not suffice to establish an integral order among God, reason, appetite, and body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX2","text":"Affective perfection does not demand the abolition of passion, but the abolition of affective motion that precedes or opposes reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX3","text":"Virtue is not merely a remedy for sin, misery, or immoderate passion, because ordering virtues remain even without these evils.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX4","text":"Original integrity is not equivalent to glory or to final confirmation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:DNX5","text":"Merit does not have a single measure in which difficulty, charity, grace, and magnitude of work are reduced to the same quantity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SNX1","text":"The creature neither produces grace from nature alone nor causally grounds original rectitude from itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SNX2","text":"The possibility of falling must remain in order that the first state may be truly rectified but not finally consummated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:SNX3","text":"Adversity after the fall is neither a pure benefit nor an evil simply measurable, because it can increase proportional merit while diminishing grace, integrity, and the absolute magnitude of work.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","CH_GGVC_P_87:A15","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS1","text":"Hierarchical rectitude → proof through loss after sin and the permanence of natural things → non-natural subjection → original grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS2","text":"Absence of evil and of a good then necessary but absent + appetite wholly subjected to reason → ordered passions are admitted; disordered passions are excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS3","text":"Virtue as perfection of order + distinction of habit and act + imperfection of matter → distribution of virtues according to act, habit, or condition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS4","text":"Merit from grace and charity → essential reward; merit from absolute or proportional work → accidental reward.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:FGS5","text":"Original integrity → more abundant grace and absolutely greater works; postlapsarian weakness → greater proportional excess; univocal comparison between states is impeded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14","CH_GGVC_P_87:A15","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AF1","text":"Creation of the first human being → hierarchical rectitude → exclusion of merely natural causality → grace in the very origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AF2","text":"Innocence → determination of the object of good and evil → subjection of appetite → ordered passions without disturbance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AF3","text":"Rectitude → all virtues in some manner → distinction of habit and act → compatible or incompatible imperfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:AF4","text":"Grace and charity + absolute/proportional work → comparison of innocence and fall → diverse superiority according to the measure assumed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A13","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME1","text":"Original justice is reclassified from generic moral perfection to the causal structure of supernatural subjection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME2","text":"The opposition between passion and innocence is dissolved, because the true opposition is between ordered passion and passion opposed to reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A5","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME3","text":"Virtue is reclassified through three modes: habitual presence, actual exercise, and conditional aptitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A7","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME4","text":"Faith and hope are no longer signs of imperfection alone, but virtues compatible with unconsummated integrity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ME5","text":"The comparison of merit is reclassified from a single scale of difficulty to a plurality of the root of grace, magnitude of work, and proportion to capacity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A11","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12","CH_GGVC_P_87:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text establishes whether the first human being had or exercised grace, passions, virtues, and merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ALT2","text":"Structural — All answers depend on the order God → reason → lower powers → body and on its preservation or dissolution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A1","CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument converts binary questions into modal distinctions: natural and supernatural, habit and act, absolute and proportional, integrity and glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A2","CH_GGVC_P_87:A8","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The first state is placed between bare nature and consummated glory, while the fall temporally reconfigures the present, affective, and meritorious order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_87:A3","CH_GGVC_P_87:A6","CH_GGVC_P_87:A9","CH_GGVC_P_87:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT1","text":"The extracted system suffices to restore the conclusion concerning original grace and the divisions concerning passions, virtues, and merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT2","text":"The system's greatest strength is the causally ordered nexus among grace, the subjection of reason to God, and the obedience of the lower powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT3","text":"The principal joint is the transition from loss after sin to the conclusion that original obedience was supernatural; the transition presupposes the permanence of nature after the fall.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT4","text":"The compatibility of grace in the first instant and consent of the will is resolved through the distinction between instant and non-continuous motion, but it does not further explain the exact order of this concomitance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT5","text":"The distinction between habit and act preserves virtues from incompatible matter, but the relation between original grace and the defectibility of perseverance is not fully determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT6","text":"The comparison of merit is internally coherent only if essential and accidental reward, and absolute and proportional quantity, are strictly distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_87:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: original rectitude → grace → ordering of passions and virtues → comparison of merit after the fall.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_87:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_87@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_87:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 96","title":"First Part · Question 95","context":"Chapter 96","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 95"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 95","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 96","order":97,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_88"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_88@R001","sha256":"5bfb2a8948dfcde38bfd8920050e597150d61af05aecc2bf7cc83cfd6f7d1a99","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS1","text":"Quaestio dominii in innocentia resolvitur distinguendo subiectionem naturalem, poenalem et gubernativam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS2","text":"Dominium non est potestas univoca, sed relatio quae variatur secundum naturam subiecti, modum usus et finem directionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS3","text":"Animalia homini subiiciuntur quia ordo naturae, providentiae et prudentiae universalis imperfectiora perfectiori ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS4","text":"Universitas creaturarum homini subiectarum restringitur: Angelis non imperat; animalibus imperat; plantis et rebus inanimatis utitur sine immutatione imperata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS5","text":"Integritas innocentiae non tollit disparitatem, sed tollit defectum et poenalem subiectionem ex disparitate nascentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS6","text":"Dominium hominis super hominem admittitur tantum ut directio liberorum ad bonum proprium vel commune, non ut servilis ordinatio alterius ad utilitatem dominantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A1","text":"Inobedientia inferiorum ad hominem sequitur in poenam inobedientiae hominis ad Deum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A2","text":"Quod naturaliter homini subiectum est, in statu innocentiae ei non repugnasset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A3","text":"In usu naturali imperfectiora ordinantur ad usum perfectorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A4","text":"Providentia divina inferiora per superiora gubernat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A5","text":"Prudentia universalis hominis superat participationem particularem prudentiae quae in animalibus invenitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A6","text":"Modus dominii respondet modo quo ratio potest subiectum ordinare: per imperium ubi subiectum rationi aliquatenus obedit, per usum ubi non obedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A7","text":"Homo cum Angelis convenit secundum rationem; ideo Angelos dominio humano non subicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A8","text":"Integritas primi status excludit peccatum et defectum, non omnem distinctionem sexus, aetatis, scientiae, iustitiae aut corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A9","text":"Liberum arbitrium permittit in hominibus diversos gradus applicationis ad volendum, agendum et cognoscendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A10","text":"Servus ad bonum alterius ordinatur, liber autem est causa sui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A11","text":"Dominium servile necessario subiecto poenale est, quia bonum eius in utilitatem alterius transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A12","text":"Gubernatio libera dirigitur ad bonum ipsius directi vel ad bonum commune.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A13","text":"Vita socialis plurium principium dirigens requirit, quia multi diversa intendunt et unus ad unum ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A14","text":"Excellentia scientiae vel iustitiae debet in utilitatem aliorum administrari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX1","text":"Dominium hominis in animalia non est imminutio dominii divini nec imminutio superioritatis angelicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX2","text":"Discordia naturalis inter animalia non evacuat eorum subiectionem ad hominem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX3","text":"Innocentia non mutat naturas animalium ferocium nec universalem eorum victum in herbas convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX4","text":"Dominium in plantas et res inanimatas non est imperium voluntatis humanae super earum naturas aut motus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX5","text":"Usus animalium in innocentia non fundatur in indigentia tegumenti, cibi, vehiculi vel subsidii corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX6","text":"Aequalitas sine peccato non est exclusio omnis disparitatis naturalis, voluntariae vel ordinativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX7","text":"Subiectio hominis homini non est necessario servitus nec libertatis privatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX8","text":"Praesidentia iusta non procedit ex cupiditate dominandi, sed ex officio consulendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D1","text":"Animalia in innocentia homini obedissent, quia subiectio eorum naturalis ab inobedientia poenali non impediretur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A1","CH_GGVC_P_88:A2","CH_GGVC_P_88:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D2","text":"Homo animalibus praeesset sine abolitione praedationis et discordiae naturalis inter animalia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A3","CH_GGVC_P_88:A4","CH_GGVC_P_88:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D3","text":"Homo in ordine creaturarum minister providentiae fieret, non dominus naturarum per mutationem absolutam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A4","CH_GGVC_P_88:A6","CH_GGVC_P_88:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D4","text":"Cognitio experimentalis naturarum animalium constituit usum eorum proprium statui innocentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A5","CH_GGVC_P_88:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D5","text":"Disparitas in iustitia et scientia oriri potest sine culpa, quia libertas diversos progressus admittit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A8","CH_GGVC_P_88:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D6","text":"Disparitas corporalis potest esse sine defectu, quia corpus integrum adhuc sub legibus naturae et exterioribus condicionibus manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D7","text":"Gubernatio hominis super hominem in innocentia licita esset tantum si libertatem subiecti per bonum proprium vel commune conservaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A10","CH_GGVC_P_88:A11","CH_GGVC_P_88:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D8","text":"Praelatio socialis exigit conversionem superioritatis personalis in ministerium ordinativum aliorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A13","CH_GGVC_P_88:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SD1","text":"Dominium per totam quaestionem reclassificatur ut functio proportionalis: imperium, usus vel gubernatio variantur secundum capacitatem subiecti et finem relationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A5","CH_GGVC_P_88:A6","CH_GGVC_P_88:A10","CH_GGVC_P_88:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SD2","text":"Ordo innocentiae non est natura abolita, sed natura sine repugnantia poenali et sine defectu culpabili.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A1","CH_GGVC_P_88:A2","CH_GGVC_P_88:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SD3","text":"Hierarchia fit legitima non ex sola superioritate, sed ex subordinatione superioritatis ad bonum commune et ad perfectionem inferioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A12","CH_GGVC_P_88:A13","CH_GGVC_P_88:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SD4","text":"Universalitas dominii humani est analogica, quia eadem vox diversas relationes ad animalia, plantas, res inanimatas et homines significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A6","CH_GGVC_P_88:A7","CH_GGVC_P_88:A10","CH_GGVC_P_88:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod homo sit dominus autonomus naturae, quia humanum dominium intra ordinem providentiae et superioritatem angelicam continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod pax perfecta aequalitatem materialem aut suppressionem differentiarum naturalium requirat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod persona libera possit legitime fieri instrumentum privatae utilitatis alterius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod integritas creaturae finitae exigat exemptionem ab omni causalitate naturali, corporeali vel cosmica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit possibilitatem dominii unius modi, quo imperium politicum, possessio, usus rerum et gubernatio naturae indistincte explicarentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit societatem humanam sine principio unificante, quia multitudo sine directione ad bonum commune non constituit ordinem socialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit libertatem definitam ut mera absentia subiectionis, quia directio ad bonum subiecti cum libertate conciliatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:FGS1","text":"Disobedientia humana → poenalis repugnantia inferiorum → per oppositionem, innocentia restituit obedientiam eorum quae naturaliter homini subiciuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:FGS2","text":"Gradus naturae et participationis rationis → determinatio capacitatis obedientiæ → distinctio imperii, usus et exclusionis superiorum spiritualium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:FGS3","text":"Integritas sine culpa → disparitas sine defectu → excellentia diversa → obligatio gubernandi ad bonum commune, exclusa servitute.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AF1","text":"Repugnantia creaturarum post lapsum → identificatio poenae → restitutio subiectionis naturalis animalium in innocentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AF2","text":"Vocabulum universae creaturae → divisio creaturarum secundum rationem, sensum, naturam et corpus → distributio modorum dominii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AF3","text":"Obiectio ex aequalitate innocentiae → distinctio disparitatis a defectu → admissio ordinis inaequalis sine culpa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AF4","text":"Obiectio ex libertate → distinctio servitutis et gubernationis → praelatio ordinata ad bonum proprium et commune.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME1","text":"Dominium fit categoria relationum diversarum, non nomen simplex potestatis unius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter naturam et innocentiam dissolvitur: natura animalium et causae corporales permanent, sed poenalis inordinatio removetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME3","text":"Aequalitas et dilectio separantur ab uniformitate, ita ut dilectio maior inter inaequales possibilis permaneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME4","text":"Subiectio humana bifurcatur in servilem appropriationem et liberam directionem, quarum sola posterior cum innocentia componitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME5","text":"Superioritas scientiae et iustitiae reclassificatur ab excellentia privata ad munus ministeriale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ALT1","text":"Surface — Quaestio immediate determinat utrum Adam animalibus, homo creaturis, homines inter se et unus homo alteri dominarentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ALT2","text":"Structural — Ordo creaturarum disponitur secundum gradus rationis, participationis prudentiae, naturae corporalis et finis proprii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur per translationem quaestionis a possessione potestatis ad modum relationis et ad finem gubernationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Status innocentiae intelligitur ut conditio naturae integrae ante poenalem inobedientiam, non ut abolita finitudine vel causalitate creaturali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendum argumentum, si dominium semper legitur secundum subiectum, modum subiectionis et finem ordinationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT2","text":"Centrum cohaerentiae est distinctio inter imperium, usum et gubernationem, quae contradictionem apparentem inter universalem praesidentiam et limites humanae potestatis dissolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT3","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in transitu a superioritate naturali ad ius gubernandi, quia excellentia non ipsa per se servilem dominationem excludit nisi finis communis addatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT4","text":"Determinatio practica hominis ut executoris providentiae super animalia manet incompleta, quia textus affirmat ordinem sine plene describendo mechanismum singularium actuum gubernativorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT5","text":"Disparitas sine defectu stabilitur, sed proportio inter liberum arbitrium, elevationem divinam et diversitatem corporalem non ulterius formalizatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: a repugnantia et apparentibus oppositionibus ad analogicam doctrinam dominii ordinati, finiti et finaliter communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165604473743Z_95bcb63c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 96","source_sha256":"5bfb2a8948dfcde38bfd8920050e597150d61af05aecc2bf7cc83cfd6f7d1a99","sha256":"7d5b3164df91f0eab506ad5d0feb87793549714696155c7f3a7f618b8feb628c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:56:04.476252+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS1","text":"The question of dominion in innocence is resolved by distinguishing natural, penal, and governing subjection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS2","text":"Dominion is not a univocal power, but a relation that varies according to the nature of the subject, the mode of use, and the end of direction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS3","text":"Animals are subjected to man because the order of nature, providence, and universal prudence orders the more imperfect to the more perfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS4","text":"The universality of creatures subjected to man is restricted: he does not command Angels; he commands animals; he uses plants and inanimate things without commanding their alteration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS5","text":"The integrity of innocence does not remove disparity, but removes defect and the penal subjection arising from disparity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AS6","text":"Man's dominion over man is admitted only as the direction of free persons toward their own or the common good, not as the servile ordering of another to the utility of the dominator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A1","text":"The disobedience of lower beings toward man follows as a punishment for man's disobedience toward God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A2","text":"That which is naturally subject to man would not have resisted him in the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A3","text":"In natural use, the more imperfect are ordered to the use of the more perfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A4","text":"Divine providence governs lower things through higher things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A5","text":"Man's universal prudence surpasses the particular participation in prudence found in animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A6","text":"The mode of dominion corresponds to the way in which reason can order the subject: through command where the subject in some measure obeys reason, through use where it does not obey.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A7","text":"Man agrees with Angels according to reason; therefore he does not subject Angels to human dominion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A8","text":"The integrity of the first state excludes sin and defect, not every distinction of sex, age, knowledge, justice, or body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A9","text":"Free choice permits in human beings diverse degrees of application to willing, acting, and knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A10","text":"A slave is ordered to the good of another, whereas a free person is the cause of himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A11","text":"Servile dominion is necessarily penal to the subject, because his good is transferred to the utility of another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A12","text":"The governance of free persons is directed to the good of the person directed himself or to the common good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A13","text":"The social life of many requires a directing principle, because many intend diverse things and one orders toward one thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:A14","text":"Excellence in knowledge or justice ought to be administered for the utility of others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX1","text":"Man's dominion over animals is neither a diminution of divine dominion nor a diminution of angelic superiority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX2","text":"Natural discord among animals does not void their subjection to man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX3","text":"Innocence does not change the natures of ferocious animals nor convert their universal diet into herbs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX4","text":"Dominion over plants and inanimate things is not a command of the human will over their natures or motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX5","text":"The use of animals in innocence is not founded on a need for clothing, food, transport, or bodily assistance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX6","text":"Equality without sin is not the exclusion of every natural, voluntary, or ordering disparity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX7","text":"The subjection of man to man is not necessarily slavery nor a deprivation of liberty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:NX8","text":"Just presidency does not proceed from a desire to dominate, but from the office of providing counsel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D1","text":"Animals would have obeyed man in innocence, because their natural subjection would not have been impeded by penal disobedience.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A1","CH_GGVC_P_88:A2","CH_GGVC_P_88:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D2","text":"Man would have presided over animals without the abolition of predation and natural discord among animals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A3","CH_GGVC_P_88:A4","CH_GGVC_P_88:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D3","text":"In the order of creatures, man would become a minister of providence, not a lord of natures through absolute alteration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A4","CH_GGVC_P_88:A6","CH_GGVC_P_88:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D4","text":"Experimental knowledge of the natures of animals constitutes a use of them proper to the state of innocence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A5","CH_GGVC_P_88:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D5","text":"Disparity in justice and knowledge can arise without fault, because freedom admits diverse progresses.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A8","CH_GGVC_P_88:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D6","text":"Bodily disparity can exist without defect, because the integral body still remains under the laws of nature and external conditions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D7","text":"The governance of man over man in innocence would be licit only if it preserved the liberty of the subject through his own good or the common good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A10","CH_GGVC_P_88:A11","CH_GGVC_P_88:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:D8","text":"Social prelation requires the conversion of personal superiority into an ordering service of others.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A13","CH_GGVC_P_88:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SD1","text":"Dominion is reclassified throughout the question as a proportional function: command, use, or governance vary according to the capacity of the subject and the end of the relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A5","CH_GGVC_P_88:A6","CH_GGVC_P_88:A10","CH_GGVC_P_88:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SD2","text":"The order of innocence is not nature abolished, but nature without penal resistance and without culpable defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A1","CH_GGVC_P_88:A2","CH_GGVC_P_88:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SD3","text":"Hierarchy becomes legitimate not from superiority alone, but from the subordination of superiority to the common good and to the perfection of the inferior.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A12","CH_GGVC_P_88:A13","CH_GGVC_P_88:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SD4","text":"The universality of human dominion is analogical, because the same word signifies diverse relations to animals, plants, inanimate things, and human beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_88:A6","CH_GGVC_P_88:A7","CH_GGVC_P_88:A10","CH_GGVC_P_88:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:DNX1","text":"It must be false that man is the autonomous lord of nature, because human dominion is contained within the order of providence and angelic superiority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:DNX2","text":"It must be false that perfect peace requires material equality or the suppression of natural differences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:DNX3","text":"It must be false that a free person can legitimately become an instrument of another's private utility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the integrity of a finite creature requires exemption from every natural, bodily, or cosmic causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility of dominion of a single mode, by which political command, possession, use of things, and governance of nature would be explained indiscriminately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SNX2","text":"The system excludes human society without a unifying principle, because a multitude without direction to the common good does not constitute a social order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:SNX3","text":"The system excludes liberty defined as the mere absence of subjection, because direction toward the good of the subject is reconciled with liberty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:FGS1","text":"Human disobedience → penal resistance of lower beings → by opposition, innocence restores the obedience of those things that are naturally subjected to man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:FGS2","text":"Degrees of nature and participation in reason → determination of the capacity for obedience → distinction of command, use, and the exclusion of spiritual superiors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:FGS3","text":"Integrity without fault → disparity without defect → diverse excellence → obligation to govern toward the common good, slavery excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AF1","text":"Resistance of creatures after the fall → identification of punishment → restoration of the natural subjection of animals in innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AF2","text":"The term universal creature → division of creatures according to reason, sense, nature, and body → distribution of modes of dominion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AF3","text":"Objection from the equality of innocence → distinction of disparity from defect → admission of unequal order without fault.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:AF4","text":"Objection from liberty → distinction between slavery and governance → prelation ordered to one's own and the common good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME1","text":"Dominion becomes a category of diverse relations, not a simple name for a single power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME2","text":"The opposition between nature and innocence is dissolved: the nature of animals and bodily causes remain, but penal disorder is removed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME3","text":"Equality and love are separated from uniformity, so that greater love among unequals remains possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME4","text":"Human subjection bifurcates into servile appropriation and free direction, of which only the latter accords with innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ME5","text":"Superiority in knowledge and justice is reclassified from private excellence to ministerial office.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ALT1","text":"Surface — The question immediately determines whether Adam would have had dominion over animals, man over creatures, human beings over one another, and one man over another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ALT2","text":"Structural — The order of creatures is arranged according to degrees of reason, participation in prudence, bodily nature, and proper end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved by shifting the question from the possession of power to the mode of relation and the end of governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The state of innocence is understood as the condition of integral nature before penal disobedience, not as finitude or creaturely causality abolished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the argument if dominion is always read according to the subject, the mode of subjection, and the end of ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT2","text":"The center of coherence is the distinction between command, use, and governance, which dissolves the apparent contradiction between universal presidency and the limits of human power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT3","text":"A fragile joint remains in the transition from natural superiority to the right to govern, because excellence does not itself exclude servile domination unless the common end is added.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT4","text":"The practical determination of man as executor of providence over animals remains incomplete, because the text affirms order without fully describing the mechanism of individual governing acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT5","text":"Disparity without defect is established, but the proportion between free choice, divine elevation, and bodily diversity is not further formalized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_88:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: from resistance and apparent oppositions to an analogical doctrine of ordered, finite, and ultimately common dominion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_88:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_88@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_88:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 97","title":"First Part · Question 96","context":"Chapter 97","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 96"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 96","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 97","order":98,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_89"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_89@R001","sha256":"1d5027745b19cc9a4ce610b23b67dfe857dffe80876220f5d43000b9b166a187","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quomodo corpus primi hominis simul naturale et a morte, laesione atque dissolutione conservatum esse potuerit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS2","text":"Argumentatio statum innocentiae distinguit tam ab incorruptibilitate naturali quam ab immortalitate gloriosa praemiali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS3","text":"Conservatio corporis primi hominis fundatur in virtute supernaturali animae, manente eius subiectione ad Deum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS4","text":"Impassibilitas, nutritio et usus ligni vitae explicantur per distinctionem inter mutationes naturae perfectivas et mutationes dispositionem naturalem destruentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS5","text":"Motus argumentationis procedit ab aequivocatione immortalitatis ad systema conservationis temporalis, quod alimento, providentia et ligno vitae sustentatur sed finitam efficaciam retinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A1","text":"Incorruptibilitas dicitur vel ex natura materiae, vel ex gloria formae redundantis, vel ex efficienti causa corruptionem prohibente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A2","text":"Immortalitas primi hominis non erat dispositio corpori naturaliter inhaerens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","text":"Anima primi hominis habebat virtutem supernaturaliter datam corpus a corruptione praeservandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A4","text":"Virtus animae corpus conservans durabat tantum quamdiu anima Deo subiecta manebat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A5","text":"Immortalitas innocentiae differt ab immortalitate gloriae, quae in praemium promittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A6","text":"Passio proprie dicta removet patiens a dispositione naturali; passio communiter dicta omnem mutationem, etiam perfectivam, significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A7","text":"Homo innocens erat impassibilis a passionibus destructive dispositivis, sed patiebatur mutationes ad bonum naturae ordinatas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A8","text":"Corpus primi hominis animalem vitam habebat, quia anima ei communicabat vitam secundum rationem animae, non secundum plenam rationem spiritus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A9","text":"Vita animalis alimento indiget, quia calor naturalis humidum corporis consumere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A10","text":"Alteratio nutritiva primo in alimento accidit, quod in substantiam nutriti convertitur; ideo nutritio impassibilitati proprie dictae non repugnat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A11","text":"Cibus ordinarius restaurat humidum deperditum, sed non per se impedit debilitationem virtutis speciei ex admixtione materiae extraneae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A12","text":"Lignum vitae virtutem activam speciei contra senectutem et corruptionem fortificabat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A13","text":"Virtus ligni vitae finita erat; ideo corruptionem ad tempus inhibebat, non immortalitatem simpliciter neque aeternam corporis indispositionem ad dissolutionem causabat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX1","text":"Immortalitas primi hominis non est incorruptibilitas naturalis corporis neque exemptio ab omni potentia materiali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX2","text":"Status innocentiae non est status gloriae nec possessio praemii ultimi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX3","text":"Impassibilitas non est absentia omnis sensationis, somni, mutationis vel operationis vegetativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX4","text":"Necessitas cibi non est signum corruptibilitatis simpliciter, sed signum vitae animalis materiali restaurationi obnoxiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX5","text":"Alteratio alimenti non est passio destructiva corporis nutriti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX6","text":"Lignum vitae non est causa absoluta immortalitatis nec principium infinitam durationem conferens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX7","text":"Receptio gratiae post peccatum non secum fert restitutionem omnium effectuum corporalium primi status.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D1","text":"Homo innocens erat mortalitate naturae exposita, sed morte eventuali preservatus per causam supernaturalem corporis conservantem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A2","CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","CH_GGVC_P_89:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D2","text":"Peccatum mortem introducit non quia naturam humanam in aliam speciem mutat, sed quia conditionem supernaturalem qua corpus custodiebatur destruit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","CH_GGVC_P_89:A4","CH_GGVC_P_89:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D3","text":"Sensatio, somnus et nutritio in statu innocentiae admittuntur, quia perfectionem vitae animalis servant potius quam dispositionem naturalem evertunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A6","CH_GGVC_P_89:A7","CH_GGVC_P_89:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D4","text":"Homo innocens cibo indigebat, quamvis non esset naturaliter dissolubilis, quia corpus eius humidum per calorem naturalem deperdere poterat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A2","CH_GGVC_P_89:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D5","text":"Excretio superfluitatum non repugnat perfectioni primi status, si providentia divina indecentiam effectus removet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A8","CH_GGVC_P_89:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D6","text":"Lignum vitae erat medicina conservationis contra senectutem, non fons illius virtutis supernaturalis qua anima corpus universaliter custodiebat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","CH_GGVC_P_89:A11","CH_GGVC_P_89:A12","CH_GGVC_P_89:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D7","text":"Etiam si homo in innocentia non peccasset, conservatio per lignum vitae repetitam eius assumptionem vel ulteriorem translationem ad vitam spiritualem postulasset.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A12","CH_GGVC_P_89:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SD1","text":"Status innocentiae constituit ordinem hybridum: corpus manet animale et materialiter operans, sed eius defectus sub regimine supernaturali suspenduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","CH_GGVC_P_89:A8","CH_GGVC_P_89:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SD2","text":"Immortalitas innocentiae est regimen conservationis conditionale et temporale, non mutatio ontologica qua corpus fiat intrinsece incorruptibile.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A2","CH_GGVC_P_89:A4","CH_GGVC_P_89:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SD3","text":"Historia corporis humani dividitur in tres ordines non convertibiles: naturam praesentem corruptibilem, innocentiam supernaturaliter custoditam, et gloriam spiritualiter consummatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A1","CH_GGVC_P_89:A5","CH_GGVC_P_89:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SD4","text":"Conservatio vitae requirit duplex remedium, quia imminutio materiae et imminutio virtutis speciei sunt defectus causales distincti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A9","CH_GGVC_P_89:A11","CH_GGVC_P_89:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:DNX1","text":"Definitio hominis per mortalitatem non potest statum hominis exhauste determinare, quia mortalitas naturalis per donum supernaturale impediri potest sine mutatione speciei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:DNX2","text":"Integritas corporalis non requirit abolitionem materiae, nutritionis, alterationis aut superfluitatum, sed ordinationem eorum ne in dissolutionem vergant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:DNX3","text":"Gratia recuperata non est reditus simpliciter ad conditionem originariam, quia remissio culpae et reparatio corporalis eiusdem ordinis non coincidunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:DNX4","text":"Nulla virtus corporalis finita potest corpus per se in durationem infinitam stabilire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SNX1","text":"Vita ultima corporis non potest fundari in sola perfectione naturae animalis neque in medicamento naturali, sed requirit ordinem ultra conservationem temporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SNX2","text":"Status innocentiae non est terminus eschatologicus, quia eius immortalitas a conditione morali, providentia exteriori et remediis temporalibus pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SNX3","text":"Corpus gloriosum non est corpus innocens indefinite prolongatum, sed corpus cui anima communicat aliud principium vitae, scilicet id quod sibi competit ut spiritui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:FGS1","text":"Aequivocatio incorruptibilitatis → distinctio naturae, gloriae et causae efficientis → attribuitur primo homini immortalitas conditionalis, non naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:FGS2","text":"Distinctio passionis destructive et mutationis perfectivae → sensatio, somnus, nutritio et separatio generativa admittuntur → impassibilitas proprie dicta servatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:FGS3","text":"Persistens vita animalis → duplex defectus corporis identificatur → cibus restaurat humidum, lignum vitae fortificat speciem → conservatio finita et repetenda concluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AF1","text":"Mortalitas in definitione hominis posita → distinctio mortalitatis naturalis ab eventu mortis → immortalitas innocentiae conditionalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AF2","text":"Impassibilitas apparenter negans sensationem et nutritionem → distinctio passionis → permissio mutationum perfectivarum sine corruptione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AF3","text":"Immortalitas apparenter negans necessitatem cibi → vita animalis et deperditio humidi → necessitas alimenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AF4","text":"Lignum vitae apparenter causa absoluta immortalitatis → duplex defectus corporalis → medicina temporalis contra senectutinem, non incorruptibilitas simpliciter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ME1","text":"Immortalitas redistribuitur inter tria genera: naturalem incorruptibilitatem, conservationem supernaturalem innocentiae et incorruptionem gloriosam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter impassibilitatem et vitam organicam dissolvitur, quia mutationes perfectivae a passionibus corruptivis separantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ME3","text":"Alimentum et lignum vitae recollocantur ut remedia diversorum defectuum, non ut causae eiusdem generis conservationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ME4","text":"Peccatum describitur ut ruptio ordinis gubernativi corporis ad animam et animae ad Deum, non tantum ut transgressio extrinseca.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ALT1","text":"Surface — Quaestio examinat utrum homo innocens esset immortalis, impassibilis, cibo indigens et per lignum vitae conservandus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ALT2","text":"Structural — Corpus animale permanet sub legibus caloris, nutritionis, admixtionis et senectutis, sed virtute animae et providentia divinitus ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio difficultates non removet negando processūs corporales, sed reclassificando eos secundum utrum naturam perficiant an destruant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Tempus innocentiae est duratio conservata et condicionalis; gloria autem designat alium modum communicationis vitae animae ad corpus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam conclusionem principalem: immortalitas primi hominis erat supernaturalis, conditionalis et a gloria distincta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT2","text":"Distinctio triplex incorruptibilitatis et distinctio duplex passionis sunt cardines sine quibus responsiones ad objectiones cohaerere non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT3","text":"Systema maxime firmum est ubi eadem distinctio naturae, doni et gloriae simul mortalitatem naturalem et conservationem praeternaturalem ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in ratione causali qua virtus animae supernaturalis corpus materiale a corruptione universaliter praeservat, cum modus huius influxus non ulterius determinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT5","text":"Tensio permanet inter restitutionem gratiae post peccatum et non-restitutionem immortalitatis, quae per reservationem reparationis ad Christum affirmatur potius quam intra praesentem mechanismum explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, quia ab objectionibus essentialibus procedit ad distinctiones causales et inde ad regimen temporale corporis innocens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165628226976Z_2f7988ec","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 97","source_sha256":"1d5027745b19cc9a4ce610b23b67dfe857dffe80876220f5d43000b9b166a187","sha256":"04bab41d4c127897320c13bf94b51ad2b38c62dfe0119be6f6760f3821bf7c2b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:56:28.229561+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS1","text":"The question determines how the body of the first man could be at once natural and preserved from death, injury, and dissolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS2","text":"The argument distinguishes the state of innocence both from natural incorruptibility and from the reward-bearing glorious immortality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS3","text":"The preservation of the body of the first man is founded upon the supernatural power of the soul, so long as its subjection to God remained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS4","text":"Impassibility, nourishment, and the use of the tree of life are explained through the distinction between changes that perfect nature and changes that destroy the natural disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from the equivocation of immortality to a system of temporal preservation, sustained by nourishment, providence, and the tree of life, yet retaining finite efficacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A1","text":"Incorruptibility is spoken of either from the nature of matter, or from the glory overflowing from form, or from an efficient cause preventing corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A2","text":"The immortality of the first man was not a disposition naturally inhering in the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","text":"The soul of the first man possessed a supernaturally given power to preserve the body from corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A4","text":"The power of the soul preserving the body endured only so long as the soul remained subject to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A5","text":"The immortality of innocence differs from the immortality of glory, which is promised as a reward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A6","text":"Passion properly so called removes the patient from its natural disposition; passion commonly so called signifies every change, even a perfective one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A7","text":"The innocent man was impassible with respect to passions destructively affecting the disposition, but underwent changes ordered to the good of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A8","text":"The body of the first man had animal life, because the soul communicated life to it according to the nature of soul, not according to the full nature of spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A9","text":"Animal life requires nourishment, because natural heat can consume the moisture of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A10","text":"Nutritive alteration occurs first in the food, which is converted into the substance of the nourished; therefore nourishment does not conflict with impassibility properly so called.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A11","text":"Ordinary food restores lost moisture, but does not of itself prevent the weakening of the power of the species through the admixture of extraneous matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A12","text":"The tree of life strengthened the active power of the species against old age and corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:A13","text":"The power of the tree of life was finite; therefore it restrained corruption for a time, but did not cause immortality simply speaking or an eternal indisposition of the body to dissolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX1","text":"The immortality of the first man is neither the natural incorruptibility of the body nor exemption from every material potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX2","text":"The state of innocence is neither the state of glory nor the possession of the ultimate reward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX3","text":"Impassibility is not the absence of every sensation, sleep, change, or vegetative operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX4","text":"The necessity of food is not a sign of corruptibility simply speaking, but a sign of animal life subject to material restoration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX5","text":"The alteration of food is not a destructive passion of the nourished body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX6","text":"The tree of life is not an absolute cause of immortality nor a principle conferring infinite duration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:NX7","text":"The reception of grace after sin does not entail the restoration of all the bodily effects of the first state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D1","text":"The innocent man was exposed to mortality of nature, but preserved from eventual death through a supernatural cause preserving the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A2","CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","CH_GGVC_P_89:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D2","text":"Sin introduces death not because it changes human nature into another species, but because it destroys the supernatural condition by which the body was guarded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","CH_GGVC_P_89:A4","CH_GGVC_P_89:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D3","text":"Sensation, sleep, and nourishment are admitted in the state of innocence, because they preserve the perfection of animal life rather than overturn the natural disposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A6","CH_GGVC_P_89:A7","CH_GGVC_P_89:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D4","text":"The innocent man required food, although he was not naturally dissoluble, because his body could lose moisture through natural heat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A2","CH_GGVC_P_89:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D5","text":"The excretion of superfluities does not conflict with the perfection of the first state, if divine providence removes the indecency of the effect therefrom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A8","CH_GGVC_P_89:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D6","text":"The tree of life was a medicine of preservation against old age, not the source of that supernatural power by which the soul universally guarded the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","CH_GGVC_P_89:A11","CH_GGVC_P_89:A12","CH_GGVC_P_89:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:D7","text":"Even if man had not sinned in innocence, preservation through the tree of life would have required its repeated reception or a further translation to spiritual life.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A12","CH_GGVC_P_89:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SD1","text":"The state of innocence constitutes a hybrid order: the body remains animal and operates materially, but its defects are suspended under supernatural governance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A3","CH_GGVC_P_89:A8","CH_GGVC_P_89:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SD2","text":"The immortality of innocence is a conditional and temporal regime of preservation, not an ontological change whereby the body becomes intrinsically incorruptible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A2","CH_GGVC_P_89:A4","CH_GGVC_P_89:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SD3","text":"The history of the human body is divided into three non-convertible orders: present corruptible nature, supernaturally guarded innocence, and spiritually consummated glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A1","CH_GGVC_P_89:A5","CH_GGVC_P_89:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SD4","text":"The preservation of life requires a twofold remedy, because diminution of matter and diminution of the power of the species are distinct causal defects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_89:A9","CH_GGVC_P_89:A11","CH_GGVC_P_89:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:DNX1","text":"The definition of man through mortality cannot exhaustively determine the state of man, because natural mortality can be impeded by a supernatural gift without a change of species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:DNX2","text":"Bodily integrity does not require the abolition of matter, nourishment, alteration, or superfluities, but their ordering so that they do not tend toward dissolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:DNX3","text":"Recovered grace is not simply a return to the original condition, because the remission of guilt and bodily restoration do not coincide in the same order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:DNX4","text":"No finite bodily power can of itself establish the body in infinite duration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SNX1","text":"The ultimate life of the body cannot be founded on the perfection of animal nature alone or on a natural medicine, but requires an order beyond temporal preservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SNX2","text":"The state of innocence is not an eschatological terminus, because its immortality depends on moral condition, external providence, and temporal remedies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:SNX3","text":"The glorious body is not an innocent body indefinitely prolonged, but a body to which the soul communicates another principle of life, namely that which belongs to it as spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:FGS1","text":"Equivocation of incorruptibility → distinction of nature, glory, and efficient cause → conditional, not natural, immortality is attributed to the first man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:FGS2","text":"Distinction of destructive passion and perfective change → sensation, sleep, nourishment, and generative separation are admitted → impassibility properly so called is preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:FGS3","text":"Persistent animal life → a twofold bodily defect is identified → food restores moisture, the tree of life strengthens the species → finite and repeatable preservation is concluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AF1","text":"Mortality posited in the definition of man → distinction of natural mortality from the occurrence of death → conditional immortality of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AF2","text":"Impassibility apparently denying sensation and nourishment → distinction of passion → permission of perfective changes without corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AF3","text":"Immortality apparently denying the necessity of food → animal life and loss of moisture → necessity of nourishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:AF4","text":"The tree of life apparently the absolute cause of immortality → twofold bodily defect → temporal medicine against old age, not incorruptibility simply speaking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ME1","text":"Immortality is redistributed among three kinds: natural incorruptibility, the supernatural preservation of innocence, and glorious incorruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ME2","text":"The opposition between impassibility and organic life is dissolved, because perfective changes are separated from corruptive passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ME3","text":"Food and the tree of life are relocated as remedies for different defects, not as causes of the same kind of preservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ME4","text":"Sin is described as a rupture of the governing order of the body to the soul and of the soul to God, not merely as an extrinsic transgression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ALT1","text":"Surface — The question examines whether the innocent man was immortal, impassible, in need of food, and to be preserved through the tree of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ALT2","text":"Structural — The animal body remains under the laws of heat, nourishment, admixture, and old age, but is divinely ordered by the power of the soul and by providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument does not remove difficulties by denying bodily processes, but by reclassifying them according to whether they perfect or destroy nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The time of innocence is a preserved and conditional duration; glory, however, designates another mode of the soul's communication of life to the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal conclusion: the immortality of the first man was supernatural, conditional, and distinct from glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT2","text":"The threefold distinction of incorruptibility and the twofold distinction of passion are hinges without which the responses to objections cannot cohere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT3","text":"The system is strongest where the same distinction of nature, gift, and glory orders together natural mortality and preternatural preservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains in the causal account by which the supernatural power of the soul universally preserves the material body from corruption, since the mode of this influence is not further determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT5","text":"A tension remains between the restoration of grace after sin and the non-restoration of immortality, which is affirmed through the reservation of repair to Christ rather than explained within the present mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_89:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from essential objections to causal distinctions and thence to the temporal regime of the innocent body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_89:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_89@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_89:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 98","title":"First Part · Question 97","context":"Chapter 98","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 97"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 97","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 98","order":99,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_90"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_90@R001","sha256":"dc8ec8c4e477133b7f573acab835defcecb3f405ec57531c50941d01515ccc92","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat utrum conservatio et multiplicatio generis humani in statu innocentiae generationem, atque generationem per coitum, postulassent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS2","text":"Thesis affirmat generationem in innocentia futuram fuisse ad multiplicationem individuorum, et coitum futurum fuisse ut usum naturalem sexuum sine libidine inordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysico-teleologica et reconstructiva: ex natura composita hominis, fine naturae et ordine virium animae modum vitae innocuae restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS4","text":"Obiectio ex immortalitate solvitur distinguendo incorruptionem hominis per gratiam conservatam a corruptibilitate naturali corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS5","text":"Obiectio ex similitudine angelica solvitur distinguendo statum innocentiae, in quo homo animalis secundum corpus manet, a statu resurrectionis, in quo etiam corpus spirituale erit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS6","text":"Conclusio procedit per divisionem coitus in actum naturalem generationis et deformitatem concupiscentiae: primum innocentiae convenit, secunda ab ea excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A1","text":"Intentio naturae principaliter fertur in id quod semper et perpetuo manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A2","text":"In rebus corruptibilibus species, non individuum, est id quod permanenter manet; ideo generatio ad conservationem speciei ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A3","text":"Substantiae incorruptibiles permanent secundum individua sicut secundum speciem; ideo individua earum per se intenduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A4","text":"Homo componitur ex corpore naturaliter corruptibili et anima naturaliter incorruptibili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A5","text":"Praeservatio corporis humani a corruptione non destruit eius naturalem corruptibilitatem neque usum generationis ei debitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A6","text":"Multiplicitas individuorum humanorum est per se intenta a naturae auctore, qui solus animas humanas creat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A7","text":"Ea quae homini naturalia sunt neque per peccatum dantur neque per peccatum subtrahuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","text":"Vita animalis, distinctio sexuum et membra generationi deputata sunt naturali constitutioni hominis propria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A9","text":"Ubi sexuum distinctio viget, generatio naturaliter requirit virtutem activam maris et passivam feminae in coitu coniunctas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","text":"In innocentia inferiores vires animae rationi omnino subderentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A11","text":"Libido non est ipsa delectatio sensibilis, sed effusio concupiscibilis immoderata et praeter mensuram rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A12","text":"Coitus per se nec bestialitatem nec corruptionem integritatis virginalis necessario infert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A13","text":"Communis usus possessionum discordiam non parit ubi voluntates recte ordinatae unicuique secundum debitam competentiam res subiectas communicant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX1","text":"Generatio non definitur per corruptionem actualem individui, quia corpori naturaliter corruptibili competit etiam si a corruptione conservetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX2","text":"Generatio humana in innocentia non ordinatur necessario ad reparationem speciei mortibus imminutæ, sed ad multiplicationem individuorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX3","text":"Immortalitas paradisiaca non est identica conditioni resurrectionis nec exclusionem vitae animalis efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX4","text":"Coitus non identificatur cum libidine, concupiscentia inordinata, bestialitate aut defectu dominii rationalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX5","text":"Continentia non est bonum absolute laudabile, sed remedium contra libidinem inordinatam praesentis status.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX6","text":"Sexus et organa generationis non sunt instituta solum propter statum post peccatum praevisum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX7","text":"Communitas rerum non postulat divisionem dominii nisi voluntates sint tales ut communitas sit occasio discordiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D1","text":"Generatio in statu innocentiae necessaria est ad multiplicationem generis humani, quamvis non ad conservationem speciei contra mortalitatem individuorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A2","CH_GGVC_P_90:A4","CH_GGVC_P_90:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D2","text":"Status innocentiae includit fecunditatem humanam, quia immunitas a morte naturalem condicionem corporis et ordinationem generationis non abolit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A4","CH_GGVC_P_90:A5","CH_GGVC_P_90:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D3","text":"Coitus in innocentia futurus est, quia usus naturalium membrorum et distinctio sexuum ad generationem ordinantur, nec peccatum illa instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A7","CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","CH_GGVC_P_90:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D4","text":"Delectatio coitus potest esse maior secundum sensum et tamen carere libidine, quia ratio moderatur adhaesionem appetitus, non necessario quantitatem delectationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","CH_GGVC_P_90:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D5","text":"Integritas corporalis et actus generativus componi possunt, si coniunctio sexualis per voluntarium usum naturae, non per impetum libidinis, regitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","CH_GGVC_P_90:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D6","text":"Multiplicatio hominum non cogit ad proprietatum divisionem, quia necessitas divisionis oritur ex discordia, non ex multitudine secundum se.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D7","text":"Quod primi parentes in Paradiso non coierunt non probat coitum ibi impossibilem, quia expulsio propter peccatum vel expectatio mandati divini actum suspendere potuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A7","CH_GGVC_P_90:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD1","text":"Peccatum non creat sexualitatem humanam, sed naturalem ordinem generationis subicit deformitati libidinis et inquietudini appetitivae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A7","CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","CH_GGVC_P_90:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD2","text":"Innocentia non est imminutio naturae animalis, sed perfecta subordinatio eius rationi, qua actus corporales fines suos servant sine rebellionis forma.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","CH_GGVC_P_90:A9","CH_GGVC_P_90:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD3","text":"Status innocentiae medius constituitur inter naturam corporaliter corruptibilem et gloriam resurrectionis: corpus manet animale et generativum, sed a corruptione et libidine conservatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A4","CH_GGVC_P_90:A5","CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","CH_GGVC_P_90:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD4","text":"Ordo socialis innocens non requirit coactionem proprietariam, quia rectitudo voluntatum removet causam propter quam communitas rerum fit occasio contentionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD5","text":"Puritas moralis non consistit in absentia delectationis, sed in mensura rationali qua appetitus delectationi non inordinate inhaeret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","CH_GGVC_P_90:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX1","text":"Systema negat exemplar quo innocentia significaret corporeitatem, sexualitatem et vitam animalem quasi spiritualitati adversas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX2","text":"Systema negat exemplar quo generatio sit solum compensatio mortis et non via positiva multiplicationis individuorum per se intentorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX3","text":"Systema negat inseparabilitatem inter sensibilem delectationem et culpabilem libidinem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX4","text":"Systema negat quod ordo naturae per gratiam conservationis evacuetur; gratia hic naturam praeservat et ordinat, non eius fines naturales destruit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX5","text":"Systema negat quod multitudo humana per se divisionem, proprietatem exclusivam aut conflictum socialem producat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio ordinatur circa impossibilitatem ut innocentia sit iam plena conditio eschatologica, quia homo innocens adhuc corpus animale, sexuatum et generativum habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio excludit quod peccatum sit principium ontologicum sexus, generationis aut delectationis; peccatum solum modum inordinatum eorum explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SNX3","text":"Argumentatio excludit puritatem tamquam fugam a corpore, eamque reconstituit ut imperium rationis super corpus sine diminutione boni sensibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SNX4","text":"Argumentatio excludit necessitatem conflictus tam in appetitu corporali quam in communitate possessionum, ubi ordo rationalis perfecte viget.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS1","text":"Corpus naturaliter corruptibile + anima naturaliter incorruptibilis → duplex relatio ad perpetuitatem → generatio corpori conveniens + multiplicatio individuorum humanorum per se intenta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS2","text":"Praeservatio a morte → non abolitio naturae corporis → non abolitio generationis → generatio innocens ad multiplicationem, non ad reparationem mortalitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS3","text":"Vita animalis + sexuum distinctio + organa naturalia + activum/passivum generationis → coitus naturaliter requisitus ad generationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS4","text":"Distinctio actus naturalis et libidinis inordinatae + plena subiectio inferiorum rationi → coitus voluntarius, delectabilis et fecundus sine inquietudine animi vel corruptione integritatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS5","text":"Voluntates ordinate dispositae → communis usus rerum sine discordia → multiplicatio hominum sine necessaria divisione dominii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AF1","text":"Immortalitas sine corruptione et multiplicatio sine divisione → distinctio inter naturam corporis, conservationem divinam et ordinem voluntatum → generatio ad multiplicationem individuorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AF2","text":"Similitudo angelica et foeditas coitus → distinctio inter Paradisum et resurrectionem, naturam et libidinem, delectationem et inordinationem → coitus innocens et rationaliter moderatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AF3","text":"Sexualitas naturalis + ratio dominans + absentia libidinis → fecunditas absque libidine → innocentia ut natura integra, non natura suppressa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME1","text":"Generatio reclassificatur a remedio contra interitum individuorum ad instrumentum multiplicationis eorum quorum multitudo per se intenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME2","text":"Coitus reclassificatur in actum naturalem generativum et accidentem postlapsarium libidinis, ita ut actus sine accidente cogitari possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME3","text":"Innocentia reclassificatur non ut status angelicus aut eschatologicus, sed ut vita animalis perfecta sub regimine rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME4","text":"Delectatio sensibilis reclassificatur non ut indicium bestialitatis, sed ut bonum sensibile cuius moralitas ex modo appetitus dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME5","text":"Communitas rerum reclassificatur ab occasione necessariae confusionis ad formam usus pacifici condicionatam rectitudine voluntatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus affirmat generationem et coitum in statu innocentiae futuros fuisse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ALT2","text":"Structural — Conclusio pendet ex compositione hominis ex corpore corruptibili et anima incorruptibili, ex teleologia perpetuitatis, et ex distinctione naturae ab accidentibus postlapsariis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones non negantur simpliciter, sed restringuntur per distinctiones status: corruptibilitas naturalis/conservatio, Paradisus/resurrectio, coitus/libido, communitas/discordia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Tempus innocentiae describitur ut conditio historica integra sed nondum glorificata, in qua natura manet eadem dum eius defectus et inordinationes non dominantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de perpetuitate, compositione hominis, multiplicatione individuorum et naturalitate sexuum sufficiunt ad restituendam conclusionem de generatione innocenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter actum coitus et libidinem inordinatam est commissura principalis sine qua conclusio de coitu innocenti sustineri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT3","text":"Systema interne cohaeret dum immobilitas mortis intelligitur ut praeservatio superaddita corpori naturaliter corruptibili, non ut mutatio naturae corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet transitus a corruptibilitate naturali corporis ad necessitatem generationis, cum in statu innocentiae generatio explicite non ad conservationem speciei sed ad multiplicationem individuorum ordinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT5","text":"Assertio de integritate virginali salva in coitu requirit possibilitatem physiologicam positam ut compatibilitas inter coitum et incorruptionem servetur, non ex antecedentibus teleologicis sola deductam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT6","text":"Responsio de communitate possessionum dependet a rectitudine voluntatum et non exhibet mechanismum distributionis rerum praeter competentiam cuique debitam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia ab objectionibus quae naturam cum defectu confundunt procedit ad naturam integram, corporalem, fecundam et rationi subiectam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165653881745Z_83132d16","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 98","source_sha256":"dc8ec8c4e477133b7f573acab835defcecb3f405ec57531c50941d01515ccc92","sha256":"8f1ce45ae128d51227e10ccc2f1d3c8185d036d3a44c9e26a5d8ea5597c80278","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:56:53.882654+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS1","text":"The question investigates whether the preservation and multiplication of the human race in the state of innocence would have required generation, and generation through intercourse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS2","text":"The thesis affirms that generation would have occurred in innocence for the multiplication of individuals, and intercourse would have occurred as the natural use of the sexes without disordered lust.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical-teleological and reconstructive: from the composite nature of man, the end of nature, and the order of the powers of the soul, it reconstructs the mode of innocent life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS4","text":"The objection from immortality is resolved by distinguishing the incorruption of man preserved through grace from the natural corruptibility of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS5","text":"The objection from angelic likeness is resolved by distinguishing the state of innocence, in which man remains animal according to the body, from the state of resurrection, in which the body too will be spiritual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AS6","text":"The conclusion proceeds through a division of intercourse into the natural act of generation and the deformity of concupiscence: the former befits innocence; the latter is excluded from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A1","text":"The intention of nature is directed principally toward that which remains always and perpetually.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A2","text":"In corruptible things, the species, not the individual, is that which remains permanently; therefore generation is ordered to the preservation of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A3","text":"Incorruptible substances endure according to individuals as according to species; therefore their individuals are intended in themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A4","text":"Man is composed of a naturally corruptible body and a naturally incorruptible soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A5","text":"The preservation of the human body from corruption does not destroy its natural corruptibility or the use of generation due to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A6","text":"A multiplicity of human individuals is intended in itself by the author of nature, who alone creates human souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A7","text":"Those things natural to man are neither given through sin nor taken away through sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","text":"Animal life, the distinction of sexes, and members assigned to generation belong properly to man's natural constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A9","text":"Where the distinction of sexes obtains, generation naturally requires the active power of the male and the passive power of the female joined in intercourse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","text":"In innocence, the lower powers of the soul would be wholly subject to reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A11","text":"Lust is not sensory pleasure itself, but an immoderate effusion of the concupiscible power beyond the measure of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A12","text":"Intercourse in itself does not necessarily entail either bestiality or the corruption of virginal integrity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:A13","text":"The common use of possessions does not produce discord where rightly ordered wills communicate things subject to them to each according to due competence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX1","text":"Generation is not defined by the actual corruption of the individual, because it befits a naturally corruptible body even if it is preserved from corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX2","text":"Human generation in innocence is not necessarily ordered to the restoration of a species diminished by deaths, but to the multiplication of individuals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX3","text":"Paradisal immortality is not identical with the condition of resurrection, nor does it bring about the exclusion of animal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX4","text":"Intercourse is not identified with lust, disordered concupiscence, bestiality, or a defect of rational dominion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX5","text":"Continence is not an absolutely praiseworthy good, but a remedy against the disordered lust of the present state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX6","text":"Sex and the organs of generation were not instituted solely on account of the foreseen state after sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:NX7","text":"Community of goods does not require a division of ownership unless wills are such that community becomes an occasion of discord.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D1","text":"Generation in the state of innocence is necessary for the multiplication of the human race, although not for the preservation of the species against the mortality of individuals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A2","CH_GGVC_P_90:A4","CH_GGVC_P_90:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D2","text":"The state of innocence includes human fecundity, because immunity from death did not abolish the natural condition of the body and the ordering of generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A4","CH_GGVC_P_90:A5","CH_GGVC_P_90:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D3","text":"Intercourse would have occurred in innocence, because the use of natural members and the distinction of sexes are ordered to generation, and sin did not institute them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A7","CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","CH_GGVC_P_90:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D4","text":"The pleasure of intercourse can be greater according to sense and yet lack lust, because reason moderates the attachment of appetite, not necessarily the quantity of pleasure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","CH_GGVC_P_90:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D5","text":"Bodily integrity and the generative act can be compatible if sexual union is governed by the voluntary use of nature, not by the impulse of lust.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","CH_GGVC_P_90:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D6","text":"The multiplication of human beings does not compel a division of property, because the necessity of division arises from discord, not from multitude in itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:D7","text":"That the first parents did not have intercourse in Paradise does not prove intercourse there impossible, because expulsion on account of sin or expectation of the divine command could have suspended the act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A7","CH_GGVC_P_90:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD1","text":"Sin does not create human sexuality, but subjects the natural order of generation to the deformity of lust and the unrest of appetite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A7","CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","CH_GGVC_P_90:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD2","text":"Innocence is not a diminution of animal nature, but its perfect subordination to reason, whereby bodily acts preserve their ends without a form of rebellion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","CH_GGVC_P_90:A9","CH_GGVC_P_90:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD3","text":"The state of innocence is constituted as intermediate between a bodily corruptible nature and the glory of resurrection: the body remains animal and generative, but is preserved from corruption and lust.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A4","CH_GGVC_P_90:A5","CH_GGVC_P_90:A8","CH_GGVC_P_90:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD4","text":"The innocent social order does not require proprietary coercion, because the rectitude of wills removes the cause on account of which community of goods becomes an occasion of contention.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SD5","text":"Moral purity does not consist in the absence of pleasure, but in the rational measure by which appetite does not adhere to pleasure inordinately.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_90:A10","CH_GGVC_P_90:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX1","text":"The system denies the model according to which innocence would signify corporeality, sexuality, and animal life as though opposed to spirituality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX2","text":"The system denies the model according to which generation is merely compensation for death and not a positive way of multiplying individuals intended in themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX3","text":"The system denies the inseparability of sensory pleasure and culpable lust.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX4","text":"The system denies that the order of nature is emptied by the grace of preservation; grace here preserves and orders nature, rather than destroying its natural ends.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:DNX5","text":"The system denies that human multitude in itself produces division, exclusive property, or social conflict.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SNX1","text":"The argumentation is ordered around the impossibility that innocence should already be the full eschatological condition, because innocent man still has an animal, sexed, and generative body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SNX2","text":"The argumentation excludes sin as the ontological principle of sex, generation, or pleasure; sin explains only their disordered mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SNX3","text":"The argumentation excludes purity as flight from the body, and reconstitutes it as the rule of reason over the body without diminution of sensible good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:SNX4","text":"The argumentation excludes the necessity of conflict both in bodily appetite and in the community of possessions, where rational order perfectly prevails.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS1","text":"Naturally corruptible body + naturally incorruptible soul → twofold relation to perpetuity → generation befitting the body + multiplication of human individuals intended in themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS2","text":"Preservation from death → not abolition of the nature of the body → not abolition of generation → innocent generation for multiplication, not for the restoration of mortality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS3","text":"Animal life + distinction of sexes + natural organs + active/passive elements of generation → intercourse naturally required for generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS4","text":"Distinction between natural act and disordered lust + full subjection of lower powers to reason → voluntary, pleasurable, and fecund intercourse without unrest of soul or corruption of integrity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:FGS5","text":"Rightly disposed wills → common use of things without discord → multiplication of human beings without a necessary division of ownership.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AF1","text":"Immortality without corruption and multiplication without division → distinction between the nature of the body, divine preservation, and the order of wills → generation for the multiplication of individuals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AF2","text":"Angelic likeness and the foulness of intercourse → distinction between Paradise and resurrection, nature and lust, pleasure and disorder → innocent and rationally moderated intercourse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:AF3","text":"Natural sexuality + ruling reason + absence of lust → fecundity without lust → innocence as integral nature, not suppressed nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME1","text":"Generation is reclassified from a remedy against the perishing of individuals to an instrument for multiplying those whose multitude is intended in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME2","text":"Intercourse is reclassified into the natural generative act and the postlapsarian accident of lust, so that the act can be conceived without the accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME3","text":"Innocence is reclassified not as an angelic or eschatological state, but as perfect animal life under the rule of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME4","text":"Sensible pleasure is reclassified not as an indication of bestiality, but as a sensible good whose morality depends on the mode of appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ME5","text":"Community of goods is reclassified from an occasion of necessary confusion to a form of peaceful use conditioned by the rectitude of wills.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text affirms that generation and intercourse would have occurred in the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ALT2","text":"Structural — The conclusion depends on the composition of man from a corruptible body and an incorruptible soul, on the teleology of perpetuity, and on the distinction of nature from postlapsarian accidents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The objections are not simply denied, but restricted through distinctions of states: natural corruptibility/preservation, Paradise/resurrection, intercourse/lust, community/discord.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The time of innocence is described as a historical condition that is integral but not yet glorified, in which nature remains the same while its defects and disorders do not prevail.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning perpetuity, the composition of man, the multiplication of individuals, and the naturalness of the sexes suffice to reconstruct the conclusion concerning innocent generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT2","text":"The distinction between the act of intercourse and disordered lust is the principal joint without which the conclusion concerning innocent intercourse cannot be sustained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT3","text":"The system coheres internally so long as immunity from death is understood as a preservation added to a naturally corruptible body, not as a change in the nature of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains in the transition from the natural corruptibility of the body to the necessity of generation, since in the state of innocence generation is explicitly ordered not to the preservation of the species but to the multiplication of individuals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT5","text":"The assertion that virginal integrity is preserved in intercourse requires a posited physiological possibility in order to maintain compatibility between intercourse and incorruption, rather than one deduced from teleological antecedents alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT6","text":"The response concerning the community of possessions depends on the rectitude of wills and does not present a mechanism for distributing goods beyond the competence due to each.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_90:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from objections that confuse nature with defect to an integral, bodily, fecund nature subject to reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_90:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_90@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_90:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 99","title":"First Part · Question 98","context":"Chapter 99","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 98"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 98","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 99","order":100,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_91"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_91@R001","sha256":"5fce250e9f3c670f03d482ed9ceb73d5d3976780159eb41c9a1ec11c7548f0e7","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS1","text":"Quaestio conditionem prolis in statu innocentiae constituit per distinctionem inter imperfectum generationis, rectitudinem originalem, et complementum naturae humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS2","text":"Argumentatio recusat inferre ex absentia peccati abolitionem omnium limitum nativitatis, quia generatum secundum naturam initio imperfectum manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS3","text":"Rectitudo innocentiae corporis animae subiecti non infantibus motum universalem tribuit, sed impedit ne membra voluntati ordinatae in actibus aetati convenientibus resistant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS4","text":"Argumentatio corporales defectus distinguit secundum originem: defectus generationem sequentes cum innocentia compatibiles sunt; defectus ad corruptionem ordinati excluduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS5","text":"Diversitas sexualis non ut aberratio naturae particularis sed ut pars complementi naturae humanae et intentionis naturae universalis reconstituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS6","text":"Generatio in innocentia non ad multiplicationem extrinsecam tantum reducitur, sed ad vitam animalem, cui nutritio et generatio essentialiter conveniunt, refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A1","text":"In rebus non auctoritate divina supra naturam traditis, natura rerum sequenda est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A2","text":"Omne per generationem productum prius imperfectum est quam perficiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A3","text":"Infantes humanae naturae secundum conditionem naturalem propter humiditatem cerebri nervos ad motum membrorum universalem nondum idoneos habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","text":"Rectitudo primi status consistit in perfecta subiectione corporis ad animam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A5","text":"Voluntas ordinata tendit solum in actus subiecto secundum aetatem convenientes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A6","text":"Defectus pueriles generationem consequentes specie differunt a defectibus senilibus ad corruptionem ordinatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A7","text":"Nihil quod ad complementum naturae humanae pertinet in statu innocentiae deesse potuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A8","text":"Diversitas sexus ad perfectionem naturae humanae pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A9","text":"Femina praeter intentionem naturae particularis dici potest, non tamen praeter intentionem naturae universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A10","text":"In statu innocentiae corpus animae magis subiectum esse potuit, ita ut sexus prolis secundum voluntatem generantis distingueretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A11","text":"Vita animalis usum alimenti et generationem complectitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX1","text":"Status innocentiae non est exemptio a lege secundum quam generatum ab imperfectione initiali ad perfectionem procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX2","text":"Subiectio corporis animae non est potentia infantis ad omnes actus quos adultus exercere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX3","text":"Carentia virtutis ad actus aetati non convenientes non est repugnantia corporis voluntati ordinatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX4","text":"Omnis imminutio corporalis non est poena peccati neque necessario afflictio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX5","text":"Immortalitas innocentiae non excludit defectus generationis, sed excludit defectus corruptionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX6","text":"Femina non est universaliter eventus innaturalis aut defectus ordinis humani.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX7","text":"Regula qua agens sibi simile generat non sufficit ad omnem sexus differentiam causaliter explicandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX8","text":"Generatio non est functio supervacua post sufficientem multiplicationem a primis parentibus possibilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D1","text":"Infans in innocentia virtutem motus sufficientem ad sugendum et ad alios actus pueritiae convenientes habuisset, non autem ad quoslibet actus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A2","CH_GGVC_P_91:A3","CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D2","text":"Impotentia puerilis fit defectus incompatibilis cum innocentia tantum si etiam actus pueritiae convenientes impedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D3","text":"Afflictio ex proposito delectabili frustrato in innocentia non sequeretur, quia appetitus infantis non tenderet nisi ad id quod suo statui conveniret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D4","text":"Pueritia imperfecta cum innocentia componitur, dum senectus corruptiva ab ea removetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A2","CH_GGVC_P_91:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D5","text":"Uterque sexus per generationem in statu innocentiae productus fuisset.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A7","CH_GGVC_P_91:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D6","text":"Sexus femineus ad ordinem naturae universalis pertinet etiam si in ordine causae particularis ut non directe intentus describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A8","CH_GGVC_P_91:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D7","text":"In statu innocentiae distinctio sexus prolis voluntati generantis specialiter subici potuisset, propter altiorem subiectionem corporis animae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D8","text":"Generatio ad omnes homines pertinuisset, quia est actus vitae animalis et non munus primorum parentum tantum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D9","text":"Ex generatione universali masculorum et feminarum numero aequalium productio ut consequens probabilis, non ut demonstratio absoluta, proponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:D5","CH_GGVC_P_91:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD1","text":"Innocentia naturam generationis non destruit, sed eius defectus sub ordine voluntatis, aetatis, et incorruptibilitatis selective disponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A2","CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A5","CH_GGVC_P_91:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD2","text":"Defectus corporalis non per solam carentiam potentiae definitur, sed per relationem ad actum debitum et ad resistentiam vel non-resistentiam corporis voluntati ordinatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A3","CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD3","text":"Perfectionis humanae forma non est maturitas uniformis individui, sed ordinata diversitas aetatum, actuum, et sexuum intra naturam completam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A5","CH_GGVC_P_91:A7","CH_GGVC_P_91:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD4","text":"Generatio in innocentia duplicem rationem habet: naturae humanae perfectionem per sexuum diversitatem servat et vitam animalem per universalem generationis usum exercet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A8","CH_GGVC_P_91:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD5","text":"Causalitas sexus a defectu particularis causae ad ordinem universalis naturae et ad regimen animae in corpore elevatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A9","CH_GGVC_P_91:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX1","text":"Textus tacite excludit notionem perfectionis quae omnem differentiam inter infantem et adultum statim abolere deberet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX2","text":"Textus tacite excludit aequationem inter naturam creatam et naturam lapsam, quia naturalis imperfectio generationis a poenali corporis inordinatione separatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX3","text":"Textus tacite excludit conceptionem voluntatis rectae ut desiderii sine termino, quia ipsa ordinatio voluntatis per aetatem et actus convenientes limitatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX4","text":"Textus tacite excludit opinionem quod intentio causae particularis ultimam naturae rationem constituat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX5","text":"Textus tacite excludit masculinitatem ut normam sufficientem complementi humani, quia perfectio naturae humanae diversitatem sexus requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX6","text":"Textus tacite excludit immortalitatem ut cessationem vitae generativae, quia incorruptibilitas generationem non reddit inutilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio circa impossibilitatem paradisi ut status naturae statice iam consummatae ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio circa impossibilitatem rectitudinis quae ordinem aetatis et proprios actus creaturae dissolvat ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SNX3","text":"Argumentatio circa impossibilitatem naturae humanae plenae sine diversitate sexuali ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SNX4","text":"Argumentatio circa impossibilitatem explicandi sexum per defectum materialem vel virtutis activae solum ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS1","text":"Natura generationis → imperfectio initialis corporis → imminutio potentiae non universalis in infante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS2","text":"Rectitudo originalis → subiectio corporis animae → absentia repugnantiae ad voluntatem ordinatam → sufficientia ad actus aetati proprios.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS3","text":"Distinctio generationis et corruptionis → admissio defectuum puerilium → exclusio defectuum senilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS4","text":"Complementum naturae humanae → necessitas diversitatis sexualis → generatio utriusque sexus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS5","text":"Vita animalis → nutritio et generatio → generatio communis omnibus → proportio sexualis ut consequentia proposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AF1","text":"Apparens oppositio inter innocentiam et infantilem impotentiam → distinctio inter naturam generationis et inordinationem peccati → potentia sufficienter puerilis, non adulta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AF2","text":"Apparens oppositio inter immortalitatem et defectum pueritiae → distinctio inter defectum generationis et defectum corruptionis → pueritia admittitur, senectus removetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AF3","text":"Apparens imminutio feminae ad eventum praeter naturam → transitus ab intentione particulari ad intentionem universalem → diversitas sexus ut complementum naturae humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AF4","text":"Multiplicatio sufficienter a primis parentibus possibilis → generatio ut actus vitae animalis → generatio omnibus conveniens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME1","text":"Corpus infantis reclassificatur non ut corpus simpliciter infirmum, sed ut corpus cuius potentia mensuranda est per actus propriae aetatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter naturam et gratiam sive rectitudinem dissolvitur in structuram graduatam, ubi rectitudo naturam ordinat sine lege generationis simpliciter abolenda.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter defectum et poenam dissolvitur per distinctionem causalium ordinum generationis et corruptionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME4","text":"Sexus femineus reclassificatur ab eventu defectivo causae particularis ad elementum positivum perfectionis naturae universalis et humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME5","text":"Generatio reclassificatur ab instrumento multiplicationis contingenter necessario ad actum proprium vitae animalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ALT1","text":"Surface — Quaestio immediate examinat utrum infantes in innocentia motum membrorum perfectum et utrum proles utriusque sexus habuissent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ALT2","text":"Structural — Solutio ordinem naturae per generationem, ordinem corporis ad animam, et differentiam inter generationem ac corruptionem constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio objectiones ex infirmitate, nobilitate, afflictione, similitudine agentis, et sufficientia multiplicationis in distinctiones causarum, finium, et graduum ordinis convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Natura humana perfecta tempus generationis, aetatum successionem, sexualem diversitatem, et vitam animalem retinet, sed corruptionem et rebellionem corporis excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad conclusionem de motu infantili restituendam, si imperfectio generationis, rectitudo corporis, et actus aetati convenientes simul servantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT2","text":"Structura firmissime nititur distinctione inter defectum qui voluntati ordinatae repugnat et limitationem quae actui aetati incongruo tantum opponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT3","text":"Distinctio inter generationem et corruptionem satis sustinet admissionem pueritiae et exclusionem senectutis, sed amplitudo singulorum defectuum puerilium non ulterius determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT4","text":"Conclusio de utriusque sexus generatione directe ex complemento naturae humanae sequitur et interne cohaeret cum distinctione naturae particularis atque universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter causas extrinsecas sexus, dispositionem conceptionis, et electionem voluntatis generantis, quae enumerantur sed in unam causalitatis rationem non rediguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT6","text":"Numerica sexuum aequalitas non eadem firmitate ac generatio utriusque sexus stabilitur, quia ut consequens apparens, non ut necessitas demonstrata, enuntiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165716474099Z_4f85f7ea","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 99","source_sha256":"5fce250e9f3c670f03d482ed9ceb73d5d3976780159eb41c9a1ec11c7548f0e7","sha256":"1e02279756df67c3c7744b595f3fb15fc1c6e9b483c5cc36bff85b482134b47a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:57:16.476021+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS1","text":"The question establishes the condition of offspring in the state of innocence through the distinction between the imperfection of generation, original rectitude, and the completion of human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS2","text":"The argument refuses to infer from the absence of sin the abolition of all limits of birth, because what is generated according to nature initially remains imperfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS3","text":"The rectitude of innocence, by which the body is subject to the soul, does not attribute universal movement to infants, but prevents the members from resisting the ordered will in acts appropriate to their age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS4","text":"The argument distinguishes bodily defects according to their origin: defects consequent upon generation are compatible with innocence; defects ordered toward corruption are excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS5","text":"Sexual diversity is reconstituted not as an aberration of particular nature but as part of the completion of human nature and of the intention of universal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AS6","text":"Generation in innocence is not reduced merely to extrinsic multiplication, but is referred to animal life, to which nutrition and generation essentially belong.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A1","text":"In matters not transmitted by divine authority as being above nature, the nature of things must be followed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A2","text":"Everything produced through generation is imperfect before it is perfected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A3","text":"Infants of human nature, according to their natural condition, because of the moisture of the brain, do not yet have nerves suitable for the universal movement of the limbs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","text":"The rectitude of the first state consists in the perfect subjection of the body to the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A5","text":"The ordered will tends only toward acts appropriate to the subject according to age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A6","text":"Childish defects consequent upon generation differ in species from senile defects ordered toward corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A7","text":"Nothing belonging to the completion of human nature could be lacking in the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A8","text":"Diversity of sex belongs to the perfection of human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A9","text":"Woman may be said to be apart from the intention of particular nature, but not apart from the intention of universal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A10","text":"In the state of innocence the body could have been more subject to the soul, such that the sex of offspring would be distinguished according to the will of the generator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:A11","text":"Animal life encompasses the use of food and generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX1","text":"The state of innocence is not an exemption from the law according to which what is generated proceeds from initial imperfection to perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX2","text":"The subjection of the body to the soul is not the infant's power for all acts that an adult can perform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX3","text":"Lack of power for acts inappropriate to age is not resistance of the body to the ordered will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX4","text":"Not every bodily diminution is a punishment of sin or necessarily an affliction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX5","text":"The immortality of innocence does not exclude defects of generation, but excludes defects of corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX6","text":"Woman is not universally an unnatural outcome or a defect of human order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX7","text":"The rule by which an agent generates what is like itself does not suffice to explain causally every difference of sex.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:NX8","text":"Generation is not a superfluous function after sufficient multiplication could have been possible through the first parents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D1","text":"An infant in innocence would have had sufficient power of movement for sucking and for other acts appropriate to childhood, but not for every act whatsoever.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A2","CH_GGVC_P_91:A3","CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D2","text":"Childish impotence becomes a defect incompatible with innocence only if it also impedes acts appropriate to childhood.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D3","text":"Affliction from a frustrated pleasurable intention would not follow in innocence, because the infant's appetite would tend only toward that which was appropriate to its state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D4","text":"Imperfect childhood is compatible with innocence, while corruptive old age is removed from it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A2","CH_GGVC_P_91:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D5","text":"Both sexes would have been produced through generation in the state of innocence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A7","CH_GGVC_P_91:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D6","text":"The female sex belongs to the order of universal nature even if, in the order of particular cause, it is described as not directly intended.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A8","CH_GGVC_P_91:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D7","text":"In the state of innocence, the distinction of the sex of offspring could have been specially subject to the will of the generator, on account of the higher subjection of the body to the soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D8","text":"Generation would have belonged to all human beings, because it is an act of animal life and not a function of the first parents alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:D9","text":"From universal generation, the production of males and females equal in number is proposed as a probable consequence, not as an absolute demonstration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:D5","CH_GGVC_P_91:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD1","text":"Innocence does not destroy the nature of generation, but selectively disposes its defects under the order of will, age, and incorruptibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A2","CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A5","CH_GGVC_P_91:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD2","text":"A bodily defect is not defined by mere lack of power, but by its relation to the due act and to the resistance or non-resistance of the body to the ordered will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A3","CH_GGVC_P_91:A4","CH_GGVC_P_91:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD3","text":"The form of human perfection is not the uniform maturity of the individual, but the ordered diversity of ages, acts, and sexes within complete nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A5","CH_GGVC_P_91:A7","CH_GGVC_P_91:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD4","text":"Generation in innocence has a twofold account: it preserves the perfection of human nature through diversity of sexes and exercises animal life through the universal use of generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A8","CH_GGVC_P_91:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SD5","text":"The causality of sex is elevated from the defect of a particular cause to the order of universal nature and to the governance of the soul in the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_91:A9","CH_GGVC_P_91:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX1","text":"The text tacitly excludes a notion of perfection that would have to abolish at once every difference between infant and adult.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX2","text":"The text tacitly excludes the equation of created nature with fallen nature, because the natural imperfection of generation is separated from the penal disorder of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX3","text":"The text tacitly excludes a conception of right will as desire without limit, because the ordering of the will itself is limited by age and appropriate acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX4","text":"The text tacitly excludes the opinion that the intention of a particular cause constitutes the ultimate account of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX5","text":"The text tacitly excludes masculinity as a sufficient norm of human completion, because the perfection of human nature requires diversity of sex.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:DNX6","text":"The text tacitly excludes immortality as the cessation of generative life, because incorruptibility does not render generation useless.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SNX1","text":"The argument is ordered around the impossibility of paradise as a state of nature statically already consummated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SNX2","text":"The argument is ordered around the impossibility of a rectitude that dissolves the order of age and the proper acts of the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SNX3","text":"The argument is ordered around the impossibility of a complete human nature without sexual diversity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:SNX4","text":"The argument is ordered around the impossibility of explaining sex by material defect or active power alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS1","text":"Nature of generation → initial imperfection of the body → diminution of non-universal power in the infant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS2","text":"Original rectitude → subjection of the body to the soul → absence of resistance to the ordered will → sufficiency for acts proper to age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS3","text":"Distinction of generation and corruption → admission of childish defects → exclusion of senile defects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS4","text":"Completion of human nature → necessity of sexual diversity → generation of both sexes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:FGS5","text":"Animal life → nutrition and generation → generation common to all → sexual proportion as a proposed consequence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AF1","text":"Apparent opposition between innocence and infantile impotence → distinction between the nature of generation and the disorder of sin → power sufficiently infantile, not adult.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AF2","text":"Apparent opposition between immortality and the defect of childhood → distinction between the defect of generation and the defect of corruption → childhood is admitted, old age is removed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AF3","text":"Apparent reduction of woman to an outcome apart from nature → transition from particular intention to universal intention → diversity of sex as completion of human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:AF4","text":"Multiplication sufficiently possible through the first parents → generation as an act of animal life → generation appropriate to all.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME1","text":"The infant's body is reclassified not as a simply weak body, but as a body whose power must be measured by the acts of its proper age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME2","text":"The opposition between nature and grace or rectitude is dissolved into a graduated structure, in which rectitude orders nature without simply abolishing the law of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME3","text":"The opposition between defect and punishment is dissolved through the distinction of the causal orders of generation and corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME4","text":"The female sex is reclassified from the defective outcome of a particular cause to a positive element of the perfection of universal and human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ME5","text":"Generation is reclassified from an instrument of contingently necessary multiplication to a proper act of animal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ALT1","text":"Surface — The question immediately examines whether infants in innocence would have had perfect movement of the limbs and whether offspring of both sexes would have existed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ALT2","text":"Structural — The solution establishes the order of nature through generation, the order of body to soul, and the difference between generation and corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument converts objections from weakness, nobility, affliction, the likeness of the agent, and the sufficiency of multiplication into distinctions of causes, ends, and degrees of order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Perfect human nature retains the time of generation, the succession of ages, sexual diversity, and animal life, but excludes corruption and the rebellion of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the conclusion concerning infantile movement, if the imperfection of generation, the rectitude of the body, and acts appropriate to age are preserved together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT2","text":"The structure relies most firmly on the distinction between a defect that resists the ordered will and a limitation that opposes only an act unsuitable to age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT3","text":"The distinction between generation and corruption sufficiently supports the admission of childhood and the exclusion of old age, but the extent of individual childish defects is not further determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT4","text":"The conclusion concerning the generation of both sexes follows directly from the completion of human nature and coheres internally with the distinction between particular and universal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT5","text":"A fragile juncture remains between the extrinsic causes of sex, the disposition of conception, and the choice of the generative will, which are enumerated but not reduced to one account of causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_91:MRT6","text":"Numerical equality of the sexes is not established with the same firmness as the generation of both sexes, because it is enunciated as an apparent consequence, not as a demonstrated necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_91:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_91@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_91:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 100","title":"First Part · Question 99","context":"Chapter 100","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 99"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 99","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 100","order":101,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_92"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_92@R001","sha256":"717d14ab7350e447488641711ecb0f715acd2891f251da5857823d5745fb6442","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS1","text":"Quaestio distinguit utrum proles in innocentia iustitiam originalem haberet et utrum eadem proles in tali iustitia immutabiliter confirmata nasceretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS2","text":"Prima pars quaestionis statum prolis ex similitudine generationis specificae et ex natura iustitiae originalis determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS3","text":"Iustitia originalis, licet donum divinum sit neque ex principiis naturae specie causetur, toti naturae data sicut accidens naturae speciei constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS4","text":"Gratia, quae radix iustitiae originalis est, non per semen traducitur, sed a Deo simul cum anima rationali confertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS5","text":"Secunda pars quaestionis confirmationem non ex originaria rectitudine, sed ex visione aperta Dei definit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS6","text":"Quia visio Dei beatifica vitam animalem et usum generationis tolleret, parentes generantes confirmati non essent nec proles ipsis perfectior nasceretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A1","text":"Homo naturaliter generat sibi simile secundum speciem, nisi operatio naturae errore impediatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A2","text":"Accidentia naturae speciei in prole parentibus assimilantur; accidentia individualia tali necessitate non communicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A3","text":"Iustitia originalis est accidens toti naturae humanae divinitus datum, non accidens mere individuale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A4","text":"Peccatum originale, oppositum iustitiae originali, est peccatum naturae et a parente ad posteros derivatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A5","text":"Radix iustitiae originalis est subiectio supernaturalis rationis ad Deum per gratiam gratum facientem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A6","text":"Anima rationalis non traducitur, sed a Deo infunditur statim cum corpus ad eam recipiendam dispositum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A7","text":"Gratia in statu innocentiae cum anima rationali confertur, non virtute seminis transfunditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","text":"Creatura rationalis in iustitia confirmatur per beatitudinem visionis apertae Dei, cui viso averti non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A9","text":"Visio Dei per essentiam hominem spiritualem mente et corpore efficit atque vitam animalem, cui soli usus generationis competit, terminat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A10","text":"Proles in nativitate perfectionem parentum generantium non excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A11","text":"Liberum arbitrium hominis vertibile manet ante electionem et post electionem, dissimiliter a libero arbitrio angelico.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A12","text":"Necessitas peccandi absolute irreversibilis damnatis tantum convenit, sicut necessitas non peccandi beatis tantum convenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX1","text":"Iustitia originalis non est proprietas ex principiis naturae specificae naturaliter causata, quamvis ad naturam speciei referatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX2","text":"Gratia non fit naturalis per propagationem neque per virtutem seminis a parentibus in prolem transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX3","text":"Anima rationalis non est effectus traductivus generationis corporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX4","text":"Hereditas iustitiae non importat necessitatem exercendi omnes actus iustitiae; habitus iustitiae ab executione actus distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX5","text":"Iustitia originalis non idem est quod iustitia confirmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX6","text":"Carentia peccati originalis non excludit possibilitatem peccati personalis per liberum arbitrium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX7","text":"Ex maiori boni virtute non sequitur transmissio hereditarii status impeccabilitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX8","text":"Analogiam inter hominem et angelum confirmationis diversitas liberi arbitrii impedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D1","text":"Proles innocentium in iustitia originali nasceretur, quia donum naturae speciei in generatione specifica assimilative communicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A1","CH_GGVC_P_92:A2","CH_GGVC_P_92:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D2","text":"Proles in iustitia originali nata etiam cum gratia nasceretur, quia gratia est radix rectitudinis quae iustitiam originalem constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A5","CH_GGVC_P_92:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D3","text":"Concessio gratiae prolis non destruit eius gratuitatem, quia divinum collatum cum anima distinguitur a physica transfusione per semen.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A6","CH_GGVC_P_92:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D4","text":"Proles in innocentia iustitia confirmata non nasceretur, quia parentes dum generant beatifica visione confirmati esse non possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","CH_GGVC_P_92:A9","CH_GGVC_P_92:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D5","text":"Proles a peccato originali immunis adhuc per proprium liberum arbitrium peccare posset.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A11","CH_GGVC_P_92:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D6","text":"Status originarius sine culpa hereditaria non producit statum beatum sine possibilitate aversionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","CH_GGVC_P_92:A11","CH_GGVC_P_92:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SD1","text":"Systema duplicem originis rationem instituit: natura speciei statum iustitiae originalis fundat, Deus autem animam et gratiam immediate confert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A1","CH_GGVC_P_92:A3","CH_GGVC_P_92:A5","CH_GGVC_P_92:A6","CH_GGVC_P_92:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SD2","text":"Ordo generationis et ordo beatitudinis sunt temporaliter et functionaliter incompatibiles: generatio pertinet ad vitam animalem, confirmatio ad eius consummationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","CH_GGVC_P_92:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SD3","text":"Integritas originis hereditario communicari potest sine clausura futurae historiae moralis singularium personarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A3","CH_GGVC_P_92:A11","CH_GGVC_P_92:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SD4","text":"Peccatum originale et beatifica impeccabilitas non sunt termini simmetrici transmissionis, quia alterum naturam vulnerat, alterum visionem Dei consummantem requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A4","CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","CH_GGVC_P_92:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX1","text":"Falsa est aequatio similitudinis specificae cum una et eadem causalitate physica: idem status naturae potest in prole esse per donationem divinam, non per semen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX2","text":"Falsa est aequatio immunitatis a peccato originali cum impossibilitate peccati personalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX3","text":"Falsa est opinio quod rectitudo initialis sit forma imperfecta eiusdem confirmationis quae beatitudinem constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX4","text":"Falsa est regula quod maior bonitas causae sufficiat ad inferendam necessitatem boni in omnibus effectibus genealogicis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX5","text":"Falsa est translatio directa condicionis angelicae ad hominem, quia libertas humana post electionem vertibilis manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit anthropologiam pure naturalem, in qua status primus et consummatio ultima sola generationis vi explicari possent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit genealogiam moralem totalem, in qua linea parentum libertatem personalem prolis vel irrevocabiliter corrumpat vel irrevocabiliter perficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit coexistentiam stabilem generationis animalis et visionis beatificae consummatae sub lege communi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:FGS1","text":"Similitudo specifica → distinctio accidentis specifici ab individuali → iustitia originalis ut donum totius naturae → proles iusta originaliter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:FGS2","text":"Iustitia originalis → subiectio rationis per gratiam → anima rationalis immediate a Deo infusa → gratia simul collata et tamen non naturaliter traducta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:FGS3","text":"Confirmatio → visio Dei aperta → impossibilitas aversionis et cessatio vitae animalis → cessatio generationis → parentes generantes non confirmati → proles non confirmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:FGS4","text":"Immunitas a culpa hereditaria → liberum arbitrium humanum vertibile → possibilitas peccati personalis → negatio impeccabilitatis hereditariae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AF1","text":"Generatio humana → assimilatio secundum naturam speciei → iustitia originalis ut donum naturae → gratia divinitus cum anima collata → nativitas in iustitia originali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AF2","text":"Distinctio iustitiae originalis et confirmationis → confirmatio per visionem Dei → terminatio vitae generativae → parentes generantes non confirmati → nativitas sine confirmatione → persistentia possibilitatis peccati personalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ME1","text":"Iustitia originalis reclassificatur ut donum divinum naturae speciei, non ut qualitas privata primi parentis neque ut effectus mere naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ME2","text":"Propagatio reordinatur in duplex planum: assimilatio naturalis ad statum speciei et collatio divina immediata eorum quae corpus generans efficere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter innocentiam et peccatum substituitur distinctione triplici inter iustitiam originalem, culpam originalem et confirmationem beatificam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ME4","text":"Generatio non iam signum perfectionis consummatae, sed index status animalis nondum per visionem Dei terminati, intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus decernit prolem innocentium cum iustitia originali et gratia nasci, sed non cum iustitia confirmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ALT2","text":"Structural — Argumentatio distinguit accidentia naturae speciei ab accidentibus individualibus et causalitatem generationis a collatione divina animae ac gratiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumenta contraria solvuntur per separationem habituum ab actibus, originis a causalitate physica, et rectitudinis initialis a confirmatione finali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Homo describitur ut creatura cuius generatio animalis ad tempus pertinet, beatitudo autem per visionem Dei libertatem ab aversione consummat et illum ordinem generationis finit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad conclusionem primam, si iustitia originalis simul donum divinum et accidens naturae speciei intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT2","text":"Nodus firmissimus est distinctio inter similitudinem specificam, quae prolem parentibus assimilare facit, et infusionem divinam, quae animam ac gratiam non per semen confert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT3","text":"Commissura systematis manet quod donum non ex principiis speciei causatum tamen ut accidens naturae speciei propagabile describitur; cohaerentia pendet ex distinctione status assimilati et causae efficientis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT4","text":"Negatio confirmationis sufficienter procedit ex connexione visionis beatificae cum cessatione vitae generativae et ex minoris perfectionis regula prolis respectu parentum generantium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT5","text":"Exceptio privilegii specialis et immunitas per providentiam divinam admittuntur, sed non per regulam communem ulterius determinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: hereditas iustitiae affirmatur, causalitas naturalistica gratiae negatur, et impeccabilitas hereditaria per ordinem beatitudinis atque libertatis excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165740294472Z_de7d8884","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 100","source_sha256":"717d14ab7350e447488641711ecb0f715acd2891f251da5857823d5745fb6442","sha256":"d215589e1d3945d6c677aaa823b3478fc853571fbd37e6247c907c219e613f3b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:57:40.295433+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS1","text":"The question distinguishes whether offspring in innocence would have original justice and whether the same offspring would be born immutably confirmed in such justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS2","text":"The first part of the question determines the state of offspring from the likeness of specific generation and from the nature of original justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS3","text":"Original justice, although it is a divine gift and is not caused from the principles of nature specific to the species, is constituted as given to the whole nature, like an accident of the nature of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS4","text":"Grace, which is the root of original justice, is not transmitted through seed, but is conferred by God together with the rational soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS5","text":"The second part of the question defines confirmation not from original rectitude, but from the open vision of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AS6","text":"Because the beatific vision of God would remove animal life and the use of generation, generating parents would not be confirmed, nor would offspring be born more perfect than they.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A1","text":"Man naturally generates one like himself according to species, unless the operation of nature is hindered by error.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A2","text":"Accidents of the nature of the species are assimilated in offspring to those of the parents; individual accidents are not shared by such necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A3","text":"Original justice is an accident divinely given to the whole human nature, not a merely individual accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A4","text":"Original sin, the opposite of original justice, is a sin of nature and is derived from parent to descendants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A5","text":"The root of original justice is the supernatural subjection of reason to God through sanctifying grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A6","text":"The rational soul is not transmitted, but is infused by God as soon as the body is disposed to receive it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A7","text":"Grace in the state of innocence is conferred with the rational soul, not transfused by the power of seed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","text":"A rational creature is confirmed in justice through the blessedness of the open vision of God, from whom, once seen, it cannot turn away.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A9","text":"The vision of God through essence makes man spiritual in mind and body and brings to an end animal life, to which alone the use of generation belongs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A10","text":"Offspring at birth do not surpass the perfection of their generating parents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A11","text":"Human free choice remains mutable before choice and after choice, unlike angelic free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:A12","text":"An absolutely irreversible necessity of sinning belongs only to the damned, just as the necessity of not sinning belongs only to the blessed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX1","text":"Original justice is not a property naturally caused from the principles of specific nature, although it is referred to the nature of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX2","text":"Grace does not become natural through propagation, nor does it pass from parents to offspring through the power of seed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX3","text":"The rational soul is not a transmissive effect of bodily generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX4","text":"The inheritance of justice does not entail the necessity of exercising all acts of justice; the habit of justice is distinguished from the execution of an act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX5","text":"Original justice is not the same as confirmed justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX6","text":"The absence of original sin does not exclude the possibility of personal sin through free choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX7","text":"The transmission of a hereditary state of impeccability does not follow from a greater power of good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:NX8","text":"The diversity of free choice impedes an analogy of confirmation between man and angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D1","text":"The offspring of the innocent would be born in original justice, because a gift of the nature of the species is communicated assimilatively in specific generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A1","CH_GGVC_P_92:A2","CH_GGVC_P_92:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D2","text":"Offspring born in original justice would also be born with grace, because grace is the root of the rectitude that constitutes original justice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A5","CH_GGVC_P_92:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D3","text":"The conferral of grace upon offspring does not destroy its gratuity, because what is divinely bestowed with the soul is distinguished from physical transfusion through seed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A6","CH_GGVC_P_92:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D4","text":"Offspring in innocence would not be born in confirmed justice, because parents, while generating, cannot be confirmed by the beatific vision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","CH_GGVC_P_92:A9","CH_GGVC_P_92:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D5","text":"Offspring immune from original sin could nevertheless sin through their own free choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A11","CH_GGVC_P_92:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:D6","text":"The original state without hereditary guilt does not produce a blessed state without the possibility of turning away.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","CH_GGVC_P_92:A11","CH_GGVC_P_92:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SD1","text":"The system establishes a twofold account of origin: the nature of the species grounds the state of original justice, but God immediately confers the soul and grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A1","CH_GGVC_P_92:A3","CH_GGVC_P_92:A5","CH_GGVC_P_92:A6","CH_GGVC_P_92:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SD2","text":"The order of generation and the order of blessedness are temporally and functionally incompatible: generation belongs to animal life, confirmation to its consummation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","CH_GGVC_P_92:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SD3","text":"Integrity of origin can be communicated hereditarily without closing off the future moral history of individual persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A3","CH_GGVC_P_92:A11","CH_GGVC_P_92:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SD4","text":"Original sin and beatific impeccability are not symmetrical terms of transmission, because the former wounds nature, whereas the latter requires the consummating vision of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_92:A4","CH_GGVC_P_92:A8","CH_GGVC_P_92:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX1","text":"The equation of specific likeness with one and the same physical causality is false: the same state of nature can be in offspring through divine bestowal, not through seed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX2","text":"The equation of immunity from original sin with the impossibility of personal sin is false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX3","text":"The opinion that initial rectitude is an imperfect form of the same confirmation that constitutes blessedness is false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX4","text":"The rule that the greater goodness of a cause suffices to infer the necessity of good in all genealogical effects is false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:DNX5","text":"The direct transfer of the angelic condition to man is false, because human freedom remains mutable after choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SNX1","text":"The system excludes a purely natural anthropology in which the first state and final consummation could be explained by the power of generation alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SNX2","text":"The system excludes a total moral genealogy in which the line of parents either irrevocably corrupts or irrevocably perfects the personal freedom of offspring.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:SNX3","text":"The system excludes the stable coexistence, under a common law, of animal generation and consummated beatific vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:FGS1","text":"Specific likeness → distinction of specific accident from individual accident → original justice as a gift of the whole nature → offspring originally just.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:FGS2","text":"Original justice → subjection of reason through grace → rational soul immediately infused by God → grace conferred together with it and yet not naturally transmitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:FGS3","text":"Confirmation → open vision of God → impossibility of turning away and cessation of animal life → cessation of generation → generating parents not confirmed → offspring not confirmed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:FGS4","text":"Immunity from hereditary guilt → mutable human free choice → possibility of personal sin → negation of hereditary impeccability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AF1","text":"Human generation → assimilation according to the nature of the species → original justice as a gift of nature → grace divinely conferred with the soul → birth in original justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:AF2","text":"Distinction between original justice and confirmation → confirmation through the vision of God → termination of generative life → generating parents not confirmed → birth without confirmation → persistence of the possibility of personal sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ME1","text":"Original justice is reclassified as a divine gift of the nature of the species, not as a private quality of the first parent nor as a merely natural effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ME2","text":"Propagation is reordered onto a twofold plane: natural assimilation to the state of the species and immediate divine conferral of those things which the generating body cannot effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ME3","text":"The opposition between innocence and sin is replaced by a threefold distinction among original justice, original guilt, and beatific confirmation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ME4","text":"Generation is understood no longer as a sign of consummate perfection, but as an indication of an animal state not yet terminated by the vision of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines that the offspring of the innocent are born with original justice and grace, but not with confirmed justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ALT2","text":"Structural — The argument distinguishes accidents of the nature of the species from individual accidents and the causality of generation from the divine conferral of soul and grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Contrary arguments are resolved by separating habits from acts, origin from physical causality, and initial rectitude from final confirmation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Man is described as a creature whose animal generation belongs to time, whereas blessedness through the vision of God consummates freedom from turning away and brings that order of generation to an end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice for the first conclusion, if original justice is understood simultaneously as a divine gift and an accident of the nature of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT2","text":"The strongest node is the distinction between specific likeness, which makes offspring assimilate to their parents, and divine infusion, which confers soul and grace not through seed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT3","text":"The system's joint remains that a gift not caused from the principles of the species is nevertheless described as propagable as an accident of the nature of the species; coherence depends on the distinction between the assimilated state and the divine efficient cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT4","text":"The negation of confirmation proceeds sufficiently from the connection of beatific vision with the cessation of generative life and from the rule of the lesser perfection of offspring in relation to generating parents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT5","text":"The exception of special privilege and immunity through divine providence are admitted, but are not further determined by a common rule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_92:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: the inheritance of justice is affirmed, the naturalistic causality of grace is denied, and hereditary impeccability is excluded through the order of blessedness and freedom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_92:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_92@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_92:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 101","title":"First Part · Question 100","context":"Chapter 101","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 100"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 100","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 101","order":102,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_93"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_93@R001","sha256":"6c4cd9fbb2202aefc7367498c69cd60b23990a59024aa4b920b6e1cb9b9ea124","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit utrum pueri in statu innocentiae perfectam scientiam et perfectum usum rationis statim a nativitate habuissent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS2","text":"Quaestio dividitur inter perfectionem scientiae et perfectionem usus rationis, quia hae per diversas causas determinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS3","text":"Assertio principalis est pueros non perfectos in scientia nec perfecto rationis usu nasci, quamvis in statu innocentiae citius et melius ad perfectionem procederent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS4","text":"Argumentatio ex distinctione inter corruptionis impedimentum et naturalem corporis sensuumque progressionem constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS5","text":"Genus argumentationis est reconstructivum et naturae-ordinatum: objectiones de Adam, peccato, iustitia et animalibus per causas naturales secundum statum innocentiae restringuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS6","text":"Motus generativus procedit ab apparentia immediatae perfectionis ad distinctionem inter perfectionem absolutam, perfectionem status et perfectionem temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A1","text":"In rebus supra naturam auctoritas praevalet; ubi autem auctoritas deficit, condicio naturae sequenda est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","text":"Homo naturaliter scientiam per sensus acquirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","text":"Anima corpori unitur quia corpore indiget ad propriam operationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","text":"Perfecta scientia Adae fuit accidens individuale ad munus patris et instructoris totius humani generis pertinens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A5","text":"Generatio transmittit accidentia naturalia vel gratuita totius naturae, non omne accidens individuale parentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","text":"Ignorantia est privatio scientiae quae pro determinato tempore haberi debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A7","text":"Nescientia rerum quae tempore dato sciendae non sunt ignorantia proprie dicta non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A8","text":"Ad iustitiam sufficit scientia quae per universalia principia iuris actiones dirigit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","text":"Usus rationis quodammodo dependet ab usu virium sensitivarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","text":"Vires sensitivae sunt virtutes organorum corporalium, ita ut impedimentum organorum earumque actus rationis usum impediat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","text":"In pueris vires sensitivae impediuntur propter nimiam humiditatem cerebri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","text":"Natura in omnibus generatis ab imperfecto ad perfectum procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","text":"Corruptio corporis addit impedimentum quod rationis usum etiam secundum ea quae ad omnem aetatem pertinent perturbat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A14","text":"In statu innocentiae pueri impedimentum corruptionis non habuissent, sed impedimentum naturale aetatis retinuissent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX1","text":"Pueri in statu innocentiae non nascerentur perfecti in scientia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX2","text":"Pueri in statu innocentiae non haberent statim a nativitate perfectum usum rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX3","text":"Perfecta scientia Adae per generationem ad filios non transferretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX4","text":"Innocentia naturalem necessitatem sensuum et corporis ad scientiam acquirendam non tolleret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX5","text":"Nescientia puerorum de rebus nondum suo tempore cognoscendis ignorantia culpabilis aut privatio debitae scientiae non esset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX6","text":"Absentia corruptionis non sufficeret ad perfectum rationis usum, quia impedimentum aetatis et organorum maneret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX7","text":"Scientia sufficiens ad iustitiam non aequivaleret scientiae universali et consummatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX8","text":"Apparens industria animalium statim post nativitatem non probaret in homine perfectum usum rationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D1","text":"Pueri in statu innocentiae scientiam tempore procedente sine difficultate acquisivissent, inveniendo vel addiscendo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D2","text":"Filii Adae ad perfectionem scientiae patris non assimilarentur, quia generatio eius perfectionem individualem non transmitteret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D3","text":"Pueri non carerent omni cognitione, sed tantum cognitione rerum quae ad ulteriorem tempus pertinerent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D4","text":"Pueri haberent scientiam sufficientem ad opera iustitiae, praesertim per universalium principiorum cognitionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A8","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D5","text":"Pueri in statu innocentiae rationis usum perfectum non haberent, sed eum secundum statum illum perfectiorem quam nunc haberent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D6","text":"Natura animalium non praebet instantaneam perfectionem industriae, ita ut comparatio cum animalibus objectionem non sustineat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD1","text":"Status innocentiae naturam humanam non aboleret, sed eam a superaddito corruptionis impedimento liberam relinqueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD2","text":"Perfectionis notio in systemate non est univoca, sed secundum aetatem, statum et officium distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A8","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD3","text":"Peccatum originale explicat aggravationem generalem corporis, non autem omnem puerilem imperfectionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD4","text":"Generatio naturam communem transmittere potest, sed perfectionem quae ad singulare munus vel statum pertinet non necessario producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD5","text":"Humana cognitio etiam in statu incorrupto temporalem mediationem corporis, sensuum et organorum retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD6","text":"Apparens conflictus inter nescientiam puerorum et iustitiae sufficientiam solvitur per distinctionem inter cognitionem universalium principiorum et scientiam rerum ulterius cognoscendarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A7","CH_GGVC_P_93:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX1","text":"Systema falsum habet exemplar secundum quod innocentia hominem statim in adultam perfectionem intellectualem restitueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D1","CH_GGVC_P_93:D5","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX2","text":"Systema negat generationem esse replicationem totius perfectionis parentis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX3","text":"Systema negat intellectum humanum posse ad propriam operationem sine mediatione corporis et sensuum plene exerceri.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX4","text":"Systema negat omnem imperfectionem puerilem ad peccatum vel corruptionem reduci posse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX5","text":"Systema negat cognitionem universalium principiorum et scientiam omnium particularium unam eandemque perfectionem constituere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D3","CH_GGVC_P_93:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX6","text":"Systema negat instinctum aut industriam naturalem animalium cum perfecto rationis usu hominis identificari posse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio circumit notionem innocentiae tamquam abolitionem temporis evolutionis, quam tamen explicite non nominat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SNX2","text":"Inadmissibile fit exemplar in quo perfectio humana ab initio tota praesens est et progressus posterius nihil essentiale addit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","CH_GGVC_P_93:D1","CH_GGVC_P_93:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SNX3","text":"Inadmissibile fit exemplar in quo corpus incorruptum ad operationem animae nihil pertinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SNX4","text":"Argumentatio excludit explicationem quae totam limitationem humanam uni causae peccati attribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS1","text":"Quaestio de rebus supra naturam → applicatio regulae auctoritatis et naturae → examinatio condicionis humanae naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS2","text":"Acquisitio scientiae per sensus + dependentia animae a corpore → scientia perfecta non adest statim a principio → scientia postea sine difficultate acquiritur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS3","text":"Perfectio Adae individualis + limitatio transmissionis generativae → filii scientia patri non assimilantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS4","text":"Distinctio scientiae debitae et nondum debitae → absentia scientiae non est ignorantia → nescientia remanet sine privatione culpabili.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS5","text":"Sufficientia universalium principiorum ad iustitiam → directio rectae actionis sine scientia perfecta omnium rerum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS6","text":"Dependentia rationis a viribus sensitivis + impedimentum organorum puerilium → usus rationis imperfectus; absentia corruptionis → usus relativius perfectior, non perfectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS7","text":"Comparatio cum animalibus → demonstratio imperfectae industriae etiam in animalibus → dissolutio argumenti ab instinctu ad rationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AF1","text":"Apparens consequentia perfectionis Adae, absentiae ignorantiae et iustitiae → quaestio utrum filii scientiam perfectam nascerentur → distinctio inter perfectionem individualem et naturae conditionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AF2","text":"Apparens consequentia absentiae corruptionis et animalium industriae → quaestio utrum pueri perfectum rationis usum haberent → distinctio inter corruptionis impedimentum et impedimentum organorum puerilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AF3","text":"Distinctio inter scientiam perfectam, scientiam sufficientem et nescientiam → distinctio inter usum rationis perfectum et usum rationis status-relative meliorem → conclusio de progressu sine difficultate in statu innocentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME1","text":"Status innocentiae denuo describitur non ut abolitio naturae, sed ut natura sine impedimento corruptionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter scientiam et ignorantiam in tria genera reordinatur: scientia perfecta, scientia tempore debita et nescientia rerum nondum debitarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D3","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME3","text":"Similitudo filialis dividitur inter transmissionem proprietatum naturae et non-transmissionem perfectionis individualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D2","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME4","text":"Perfectio denuo classificatur secundum munus, aetatem et statum, non secundum praesentiam aut absentiam unius simplicis qualitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME5","text":"Impedimentum corporis dividitur inter corruptionem superadditam et maturitatem organicam naturalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME6","text":"Comparatio hominis cum animalibus amittit vim probativam, quia industria naturalis ipsa gradibus temporalibus subiecta ostenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ALT1","text":"Surface: Immediateum obiectum est scientia et usus rationis puerorum in statu innocentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ALT2","text":"Structural: Mechanismus explicans est relatio inter animam, corpus, sensus, organa et temporalem maturationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Argumentatio oppositiones simplices inter innocentiam et imperfectionem, vel inter nescientiam et ignorantiam, in distinctiones causales et temporales convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_93:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Humanum subiectum constituitur ut ens corporeum cuius perfectio per progressionem ab imperfecto ad perfectum ordinatur, etiam sine corruptione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam conclusionem duplicem: scientia perfecta et perfectus rationis usus a nativitate absunt, sed progressus ad utrumque facilior et status-relative melior est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia interna firmissima est in distinctione inter corruptionis impedimentum et naturalem maturationem organorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT3","text":"Argumentatio etiam distinctione inter perfectionem individualem et proprietates generabiles nititur ad objectionem de similitudine Adae et filiorum dissolvendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter tabulam rasam et scientiam universalium principiorum iustitiae, quia origo et modus huius scientiae sufficientis non plene explicantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A7","CH_GGVC_P_93:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT5","text":"Relatio inter absentiam corruptionis et persistentiam nimiae humiditatis cerebri assumitur, sed nexus eius intra systema tantum causaliter indicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT6","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: objectiones de perfectione statim praesenti → divisio causarum → distinctio graduum perfectionis → conclusio de progressu naturali sine corruptione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_93:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_93:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165805029083Z_763083e4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 101","source_sha256":"6c4cd9fbb2202aefc7367498c69cd60b23990a59024aa4b920b6e1cb9b9ea124","sha256":"1d692e68683b5417f7629dc255c3d4531d3dc4d502f546e34dd93d0f481d063f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:58:05.031282+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS1","text":"The text asks whether children in the state of innocence would have had perfect knowledge and perfect use of reason immediately from birth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS2","text":"The question is divided between perfection of knowledge and perfection of the use of reason, because these are determined by different causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS3","text":"The principal assertion is that children would be born neither perfect in knowledge nor with perfect use of reason, although in the state of innocence they would advance more swiftly and better toward perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS4","text":"The argument is constituted from the distinction between the impediment of corruption and the natural development of the body and senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS5","text":"The kind of argumentation is reconstructive and nature-ordered: objections concerning Adam, sin, justice, and animals are constrained by natural causes according to the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AS6","text":"The generative movement proceeds from the appearance of immediate perfection to the distinction between absolute perfection, perfection of state, and perfection of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A1","text":"In matters above nature, authority prevails; but where authority is lacking, the condition of nature must be followed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","text":"Man naturally acquires knowledge through the senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","text":"The soul is united to the body because it needs the body for its proper operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","text":"Adam's perfect knowledge was an individual accident pertaining to the office of father and instructor of the whole human race.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A5","text":"Generation transmits natural or gratuitous accidents of the whole nature, not every individual accident of the parent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","text":"Ignorance is the privation of knowledge which ought to be possessed at a determinate time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A7","text":"Nescience of things that are not to be known at a given time is not ignorance properly so called.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A8","text":"For justice, knowledge that directs actions through universal principles of law suffices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","text":"The use of reason depends in some manner on the use of the sensitive powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","text":"The sensitive powers are powers of bodily organs, such that an impediment of the organs and of their acts impedes the use of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","text":"In children the sensitive powers are impeded on account of the excessive moisture of the brain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","text":"In all generated things, nature proceeds from the imperfect to the perfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","text":"Corruption of the body adds an impediment that disturbs the use of reason even with respect to those things that pertain to every age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:A14","text":"In the state of innocence, children would not have had the impediment of corruption, but would have retained the natural impediment of age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX1","text":"Children in the state of innocence would not be born perfect in knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX2","text":"Children in the state of innocence would not have perfect use of reason immediately from birth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX3","text":"Adam's perfect knowledge would not be transferred to his children through generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX4","text":"Innocence would not remove the natural necessity of the senses and body for acquiring knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX5","text":"Children's nescience of things not yet to be known in their own time would not be culpable ignorance or the privation of due knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX6","text":"The absence of corruption would not suffice for perfect use of reason, because the impediment of age and organs would remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX7","text":"Knowledge sufficient for justice would not be equivalent to universal and consummate knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:NX8","text":"The apparent industry of animals immediately after birth would not prove perfect use of reason in man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D1","text":"Children in the state of innocence would have acquired knowledge over time without difficulty, by discovering or learning.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D2","text":"Adam's children would not be assimilated to the perfection of their father's knowledge, because generation would not transmit his individual perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D3","text":"Children would not lack all cognition, but only cognition of things pertaining to a later time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D4","text":"Children would have knowledge sufficient for works of justice, especially through cognition of universal principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A8","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D5","text":"Children in the state of innocence would not have perfect use of reason, but would have it more perfect than they do now according to that state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:D6","text":"The nature of animals does not provide instantaneous perfection of industry, such that comparison with animals does not sustain the objection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD1","text":"The state of innocence would not abolish human nature, but would leave it free from the superadded impediment of corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD2","text":"The notion of perfection in the system is not univocal, but is distributed according to age, state, and office.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A8","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD3","text":"Original sin explains the general aggravation of the body, but not every childish imperfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD4","text":"Generation can transmit common nature, but does not necessarily produce perfection pertaining to a singular office or state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD5","text":"Human cognition, even in an incorrupt state, retains the temporal mediation of body, senses, and organs.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SD6","text":"The apparent conflict between children's nescience and sufficiency for justice is resolved through the distinction between cognition of universal principles and knowledge of things to be known later.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A7","CH_GGVC_P_93:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX1","text":"The system holds false the model according to which innocence would immediately restore man to adult intellectual perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D1","CH_GGVC_P_93:D5","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX2","text":"The system denies that generation is a replication of the whole perfection of the parent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX3","text":"The system denies that the human intellect can be fully exercised in its proper operation without the mediation of body and senses.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX4","text":"The system denies that every childish imperfection can be reduced to sin or corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX5","text":"The system denies that cognition of universal principles and knowledge of all particulars constitute one and the same perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D3","CH_GGVC_P_93:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX6","text":"The system denies that the instinct or natural industry of animals can be identified with man's perfect use of reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SNX1","text":"The argumentation circumvents the notion of innocence as the abolition of developmental time, though it does not explicitly name it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SNX2","text":"The model in which the whole of human perfection is present from the beginning and subsequent progress adds nothing essential becomes inadmissible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","CH_GGVC_P_93:D1","CH_GGVC_P_93:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SNX3","text":"The model in which an incorrupt body has no bearing on the operation of the soul becomes inadmissible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:SNX4","text":"The argumentation excludes an explanation that attributes the whole of human limitation to the single cause of sin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_93:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS1","text":"Question concerning matters above nature → application of the rule of authority and nature → examination of the natural human condition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS2","text":"Acquisition of knowledge through the senses + dependence of the soul on the body → perfect knowledge is not present immediately from the beginning → knowledge is later acquired without difficulty.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS3","text":"Adam's individual perfection + limitation of generative transmission → children are not assimilated to their father in knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS4","text":"Distinction between due and not-yet-due knowledge → absence of knowledge is not ignorance → nescience remains without culpable privation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A6","CH_GGVC_P_93:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS5","text":"Sufficiency of universal principles for justice → direction of right action without perfect knowledge of all things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS6","text":"Dependence of reason on the sensitive powers + impediment of childish organs → imperfect use of reason; absence of corruption → relatively more perfect use, not perfect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:FGS7","text":"Comparison with animals → demonstration of imperfect industry even in animals → dissolution of the argument from instinct to reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AF1","text":"Apparent consequence of Adam's perfection, absence of ignorance, and justice → question whether children would be born with perfect knowledge → distinction between individual perfection and the condition of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AF2","text":"Apparent consequence of the absence of corruption and the industry of animals → question whether children would have perfect use of reason → distinction between the impediment of corruption and the impediment of childish organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:AF3","text":"Distinction between perfect knowledge, sufficient knowledge, and nescience → distinction between perfect use of reason and use of reason better relative to the state → conclusion concerning progress without difficulty in the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME1","text":"The state of innocence is redescribed not as abolition of nature, but as nature without the impediment of corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME2","text":"The opposition between knowledge and ignorance is reordered into three kinds: perfect knowledge, knowledge due in time, and nescience of things not yet due.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D3","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME3","text":"Filial similarity is divided between the transmission of properties of nature and the non-transmission of individual perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D2","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME4","text":"Perfection is redescribed according to office, age, and state, not according to the presence or absence of one simple quality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME5","text":"The impediment of the body is divided between superadded corruption and natural organic maturity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ME6","text":"The comparison of man with animals loses probative force, because natural industry itself is shown to be subject to temporal stages.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ALT1","text":"Surface: The immediate object is the knowledge and use of reason of children in the state of innocence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ALT2","text":"Structural: The explanatory mechanism is the relation among soul, body, senses, organs, and temporal maturation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A10","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: The argumentation converts simple oppositions between innocence and imperfection, or between nescience and ignorance, into causal and temporal distinctions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_93:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_93:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: The human subject is constituted as a corporeal being whose perfection is ordered through progression from the imperfect to the perfect, even without corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A3","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the twofold conclusion: perfect knowledge and perfect use of reason are absent from birth, but progress toward both is easier and relatively better in that state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A9","CH_GGVC_P_93:A12","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT2","text":"The strongest internal coherence lies in the distinction between the impediment of corruption and the natural maturation of the organs.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT3","text":"The argumentation also relies on the distinction between individual perfection and generable properties in order to dissolve the objection concerning the similarity of Adam and his children.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A4","CH_GGVC_P_93:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains between the tabula rasa and knowledge of the universal principles of justice, because the origin and mode of this sufficient knowledge are not fully explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A2","CH_GGVC_P_93:A7","CH_GGVC_P_93:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT5","text":"The relation between the absence of corruption and the persistence of the excessive moisture of the brain is assumed, but its connection within the system is only causally indicated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:A11","CH_GGVC_P_93:A13","CH_GGVC_P_93:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_93:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: objections concerning immediately present perfection → division of causes → distinction of degrees of perfection → conclusion concerning natural progress without corruption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_93:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_93:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_93:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_93:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_93@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_93:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 102","title":"First Part · Question 101","context":"Chapter 102","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 101"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 101","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 102","order":103,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_94"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_94@R001","sha256":"8e8ae6d576cd5ac983a9bd635928b77a453eb50c4bd73348b3d8aaad83c37780","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS1","text":"Quaestio locum Paradisi determinat per quattuor nexus: corporalitatem, congruentiam habitationis, finem positionis humanae et ordinem creationis hominis ad illum locum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS2","text":"Narratio Scripturae historica veritatem rei corporalis constituit, cuius sensus spiritualis superstrui potest sed fundamentum historicum tollere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS3","text":"Difficultates cosmographicae, hydrographicae et empiricae non corporalitatem Paradisi destruunt, sed eius remotionem, similitudinem caelestem et occultationem loci exigunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS4","text":"Congruentia Paradisi ex statu primi hominis derivatur: corpus, natura sua corruptibile, per donum animae et per conditiones corporales aptas conservabatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS5","text":"Paradisus nec principium naturale nec finis ultimus hominis est, sed habitatio temporalis gratiae, ad bonum hominis ordinata et ad translationem finalem in caelum disposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A1","text":"Narratio Scripturae historica fundamentum veritatis rei gestae constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A2","text":"Paradisus est locus corporeus terrestris in parte orientali et nobiliori terrae constitutus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A3","text":"Remotio et impedimenta loci corporalis absentiam Paradisi ab investigatione humana explicare possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","text":"Incorruptibilitas primi hominis non ex natura corporis, sed ex virtute animae dono Dei concessa procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A5","text":"Temperies aeris est conditio externa corporis humani contra corruptionem tuendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A6","text":"Paradisus alimenta contra corruptionem internam et aerem temperatum contra corruptionem externam continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A7","text":"Locus rationali creaturae congruit secundum distinctionem naturae, status et finis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A8","text":"Caelum Empyreum Angelo secundum naturam competit, homini autem solum secundum beatitudinem finalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A9","text":"Operatio hominis in innocentia iucunda est, non labor poenalis; custodia eius est retentio Paradisi per obedientiam, non defensio contra invasores.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A10","text":"Paradisus ad bonum hominis ordinatur, non homo ad utilitatem Paradisi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A11","text":"Homo extra Paradisum creatus et postea in Paradisum translatus est, ut incorruptibilitas eius gratiae Dei, non naturae humanae, attribuatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A12","text":"Res materiales Paradisi spiritualiter significare possunt sine amissione suae corporalitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX1","text":"Interpretatio spiritualis Paradisi veritatem historicam et corporalem narrationis non evacuat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX2","text":"Similitudo Paradisi ad globum lunarem non elevationem localem supra regionem humanam significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX3","text":"Fontes fluminum alibi manifesti corporalem originem fluminum in Paradiso non excludunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX4","text":"Inquisitio geographica humana non est mensura exhaustiva omnium locorum corporalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX5","text":"Lignum vitae et lignum scientiae non sunt symbola mere spiritualia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX6","text":"Animae vel substantiae spirituali non competit locus naturalis proprie dictus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX7","text":"Habitatio Paradisi non est habitatio naturalis, perpetua aut finaliter beata hominis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX8","text":"Operari et custodire Paradisum non significat hominem propter Paradisum institutum esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D1","text":"Sensum spiritualem rerum Paradisi admittit tantum interpretatio quae rem materialem et historice gestam conservat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A1","CH_GGVC_P_94:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D2","text":"Inaccessibilitas Paradisi non est imminutio corporalitatis eius, sed conditio quae discordantiam inter narrationem et cognitionem geographicam componit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A2","CH_GGVC_P_94:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D3","text":"Paradisus congruus est homini non quia corpus eius naturaliter incorruptibile est, sed quia donum conservans et media corporalia simul ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","CH_GGVC_P_94:A5","CH_GGVC_P_94:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D4","text":"Diversitas loci Angeli et hominis non inferioritatem simplicem, sed diversitatem naturae, gubernationis creaturae corporalis et status beatitudinis exprimit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A7","CH_GGVC_P_94:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D5","text":"Actio hominis in Paradiso est exercitium naturae integrae et custodia obedientiae, non productio necessaria ad sustentandum locum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A9","CH_GGVC_P_94:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D6","text":"Translatio hominis in Paradisum designat statum gratiae inter originem terrenam et beatitudinem caelestem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A8","CH_GGVC_P_94:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SD1","text":"Paradisus tribus stratis simul constat: res corporalis historice data, signum spiritualiter intelligibile et instrumentum gratiae ad statum humanum conservandum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A1","CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","CH_GGVC_P_94:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SD2","text":"Distributio locorum cosmica fit index ordinis metaphysici: natura angelica caelum tenet, natura humana terram inhabitat, gratia humanam habitationem elevat, beatitudo hominem transferendae conditioni destinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A2","CH_GGVC_P_94:A7","CH_GGVC_P_94:A8","CH_GGVC_P_94:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SD3","text":"Amissio habitationis Paradisi post peccatum non efficit locum inanem, sed manifestat bonum gratuito concessum et damnum per culpam contractum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","CH_GGVC_P_94:A10","CH_GGVC_P_94:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX1","text":"Falsa est oppositio qua veritas litteralis et significatio spiritualis alterutrum se excludere putantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX2","text":"Falsa est imminutio qua incorruptibilitas primi hominis proprietas intrinseca naturae corporeae habetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX3","text":"Falsa est regula qua idem locus originis, habitationis et finis omnibus creaturis secundum univocam naturae rationem convenire debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX4","text":"Falsa est opinio qua utilitas loci ex sola continua occupatione actuali iudicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX5","text":"Falsa est identificatio omnis operis humani cum poena, labore et necessitate postlapsaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SNX1","text":"Excluditur humana conditio quae ex natura sua stabilitatem incorruptibilem et habitationem definitivam sibi vindicare possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SNX2","text":"Excluditur continuus nexus inter originem humanam, statum innocentiae et finem beatum: homo nec in Paradiso incipit nec ibi consummatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SNX3","text":"Excluditur cognitio humana quae visibilitatem, accessibilitatem et mensurabilitatem geographici loci pro condicione omnis realitatis corporalis postulat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS1","text":"Narratio historica → positio fundamenti corporalis → admissio sensus spiritualis ut superstructura significans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS2","text":"Obiectiones de elevatione, fluminibus et absentia geographica → distinctio inter situm, similitudinem et remotionem → conservatio corporalitatis Paradisi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS3","text":"Corpus naturaliter corruptibile + virtus animae divinitus data → necessitas alimenti et aeris temperati → congruentia habitationis Paradisi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS4","text":"Distinctio naturae angelicae, naturae humanae et beatitudinis finalis → separatio caeli Empyrei, Paradisi terrestris et translationis caelestis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS5","text":"Positio hominis in Paradiso → actio iucunda et custodia obedientiae → ordinatio Paradisi ad bonum hominis → amissibilitas loci per peccatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AF1","text":"Narratio Scripturae → veritas historica → Paradisus corporeus et terrestris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AF2","text":"Difficultas empirica → remotionis et occultationis ratio → corporalitas sine geographicā exhibitione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AF3","text":"Corruptibilitas corporis → donum conservans animae + media corporalia → Paradisus temperatus ut habitatio primi status.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AF4","text":"Habitatio temporalis → actio et custodia ordinatae ad hominem → creatio extra Paradisum → manifestatio gratiae → translatio finalis in caelum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter locum corporalem et sensum spiritualem solvitur per ordinem fundamenti et significationis, non per reductionem alterius ad alterum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ME2","text":"Locus non iam tantum spatium geometricum apparet, sed medium proportionatum naturae, statui, gratiae et fini creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ME3","text":"Immortalitas prima reclassificatur ex proprietate naturali in donum supernaturale corpori per animam applicatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ME4","text":"Labor, custodia et habitatio reclassificantur ex necessitatibus defensivis vel poenalibus in formas boni, obedientiae et conservationis condicionatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ALT1","text":"Surface — Paradisus statuitur locus corporeus, orientalis, temperatus, plantis et alimentis instructus, homini ante peccatum conveniens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ALT2","text":"Structural — Congruentia loci producitur ex commercio corporis corruptibilis, animae conservantis, condicionum environmentalium et obedientiae humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones empiricae et allegoricae non directe negantur, sed in distinctiones de genere narrationis, ordine significationis et limitibus cognitionis convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Vita humana ordinatur ut processus ab origine naturali extra Paradisum, per statum gratiae in Paradiso, ad beatitudinem spiritualem in caelo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de narratione historica, corporalitate, gratia conservante et distinctione status sufficiunt ad seriem principalem quaestionum restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT2","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi corporalitas Paradisi, significatio spiritualis et donum supernaturale non competunt, sed per ordinem fundationis componuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT3","text":"Determinatio physica loci manet incompleta, quia eius situs orientalis, remotus et temperatissimus affirmatur, dum quaestio de regione aequinoctiali aperta relinquitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter virtutem animae corpus conservantis et gratuitam incorruptibilitatem: textus utramque asserit, sed modum exactum causalitatis inter donum et virtutem non explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT5","text":"Duplex interpretatio operationis et custodiae — Deus hominem servans vel homo Paradisum colens — retinetur sine plena reductione ad unam rationem univocam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, si Paradisus intelligitur non ut res geographica solitaria, sed ut nodus in quo historia, symbolum, gratia, obedientia et destinatio humana coartantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A1","CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","CH_GGVC_P_94:A9","CH_GGVC_P_94:A11","CH_GGVC_P_94:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165828986230Z_db86d190","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 102","source_sha256":"8e8ae6d576cd5ac983a9bd635928b77a453eb50c4bd73348b3d8aaad83c37780","sha256":"ac6604dc9769d3eb91c9992d7b293b5dd263e073293e699157bba37145d4fc48","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:58:28.988280+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS1","text":"The question determines the place of Paradise through four connections: corporeality, suitability of habitation, the end of human placement, and the ordering of human creation to that place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS2","text":"The historical narrative of Scripture establishes the truth of the corporeal reality, upon which a spiritual sense can be superimposed but cannot remove the historical foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS3","text":"Cosmographical, hydrographical, and empirical difficulties do not destroy the corporeality of Paradise, but require its remoteness, heavenly likeness, and concealment of location.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS4","text":"The suitability of Paradise is derived from the state of the first human: the body, corruptible by its nature, was preserved through the gift of the soul and through suitable bodily conditions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AS5","text":"Paradise is neither the human being's natural beginning nor ultimate end, but a temporal habitation of grace, ordered to the human good and disposed for final translation into heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A1","text":"The historical narrative of Scripture establishes the foundation of the truth of the event.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A2","text":"Paradise is a corporeal terrestrial place established in the eastern and nobler part of the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A3","text":"The remoteness and impediments of the corporeal place can explain the absence of Paradise from human investigation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","text":"The incorruptibility of the first human proceeds not from the nature of the body, but from the power of the soul granted by God's gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A5","text":"The temperateness of the air is an external condition for preserving the human body against corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A6","text":"Paradise contains food against internal corruption and temperate air against external corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A7","text":"A place is suitable to a rational creature according to the distinction of nature, state, and end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A8","text":"The Empyrean Heaven befits the angel according to nature, but the human being only according to final beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A9","text":"The activity of the human being in innocence is pleasant, not penal labor; and its keeping is the retention of Paradise through obedience, not defense against invaders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A10","text":"Paradise is ordered to the good of the human being, not the human being to the utility of Paradise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A11","text":"The human being was created outside Paradise and afterward translated into Paradise, so that his incorruptibility may be attributed to the grace of God, not to human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:A12","text":"The material things of Paradise can signify spiritually without loss of their corporeality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX1","text":"The spiritual interpretation of Paradise does not evacuate the historical and corporeal truth of the narrative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX2","text":"The likeness of Paradise to the lunar sphere does not signify local elevation above the human region.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX3","text":"Sources of rivers manifest elsewhere do not exclude the corporeal origin of rivers in Paradise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX4","text":"Human geographical inquiry is not an exhaustive measure of all corporeal places.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX5","text":"The tree of life and the tree of knowledge are not merely spiritual symbols.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX6","text":"A natural place properly so called does not belong to the soul or spiritual substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX7","text":"The habitation of Paradise is not the human being's natural, perpetual, or finally beatific habitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:NX8","text":"To work and keep Paradise does not signify that the human being was instituted for the sake of Paradise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D1","text":"Only an interpretation that preserves the material reality and historical event admits the spiritual sense of the things of Paradise.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A1","CH_GGVC_P_94:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D2","text":"The inaccessibility of Paradise is not a diminution of its corporeality, but a condition that reconciles the discordance between narrative and geographical knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A2","CH_GGVC_P_94:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D3","text":"Paradise is suitable to the human being not because his body is naturally incorruptible, but because the preserving gift and corporeal means are jointly ordered.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","CH_GGVC_P_94:A5","CH_GGVC_P_94:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D4","text":"The diversity of the place of angel and human being expresses not simple inferiority, but a diversity of nature, governance of the corporeal creature, and state of beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A7","CH_GGVC_P_94:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D5","text":"The human being's action in Paradise is an exercise of integral nature and a keeping of obedience, not production necessary to sustain the place.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A9","CH_GGVC_P_94:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:D6","text":"The translation of the human being into Paradise designates a state of grace between earthly origin and heavenly beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A8","CH_GGVC_P_94:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SD1","text":"Paradise consists simultaneously of three layers: a corporeal reality historically given, a spiritually intelligible sign, and an instrument of grace for preserving the human state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A1","CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","CH_GGVC_P_94:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SD2","text":"The distribution of cosmic places becomes an index of metaphysical order: angelic nature holds heaven, human nature inhabits earth, grace elevates human habitation, and beatitude destines the human being for a condition of translation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A2","CH_GGVC_P_94:A7","CH_GGVC_P_94:A8","CH_GGVC_P_94:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SD3","text":"The loss of Paradise's habitation after sin does not render the place empty, but manifests a good freely granted and a loss incurred through fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","CH_GGVC_P_94:A10","CH_GGVC_P_94:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX1","text":"False is the opposition by which literal truth and spiritual signification are thought mutually to exclude one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX2","text":"False is the diminution by which the incorruptibility of the first human is held to be an intrinsic property of corporeal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX3","text":"False is the rule by which the same place of origin, habitation, and end must suit all creatures according to a univocal account of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX4","text":"False is the opinion by which the usefulness of a place is judged solely from continuous actual occupation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:DNX5","text":"False is the identification of every human work with punishment, labor, and postlapsarian necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SNX1","text":"Excluded is a human condition which, by its own nature, could claim for itself incorruptible stability and definitive habitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SNX2","text":"Excluded is a continuous connection between human origin, the state of innocence, and the blessed end: the human being neither begins in Paradise nor is consummated there.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:SNX3","text":"Excluded is a human knowledge that demands visibility, accessibility, and geographical measurability as the condition of all corporeal reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS1","text":"Historical narrative → positing of a corporeal foundation → admission of spiritual sense as a signifying superstructure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS2","text":"Objections concerning elevation, rivers, and geographical absence → distinction between situation, likeness, and remoteness → preservation of the corporeality of Paradise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS3","text":"Naturally corruptible body + divinely given power of the soul → necessity of food and temperate air → suitability of Paradise as a habitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS4","text":"Distinction of angelic nature, human nature, and final beatitude → separation of the Empyrean Heaven, terrestrial Paradise, and heavenly translation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:FGS5","text":"Placement of the human being in Paradise → pleasant action and keeping of obedience → ordering of Paradise to the human good → loss of the place through sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AF1","text":"Narrative of Scripture → historical truth → corporeal and terrestrial Paradise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AF2","text":"Empirical difficulty → account of remoteness and concealment → corporeality without geographical manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AF3","text":"Corruptibility of the body → preserving gift of the soul + corporeal means → temperate Paradise as habitation of the first state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:AF4","text":"Temporal habitation → action and keeping ordered to the human being → creation outside Paradise → manifestation of grace → final translation into heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ME1","text":"The opposition between corporeal place and spiritual sense is resolved through the order of foundation and signification, not through the reduction of one to the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ME2","text":"Place no longer appears merely as geometric space, but as a medium proportioned to the nature, state, grace, and end of the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ME3","text":"Original immortality is reclassified from a natural property into a supernatural gift applied to the body through the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ME4","text":"Labor, keeping, and habitation are reclassified from defensive or penal necessities into forms of good, obedience, and conditioned preservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ALT1","text":"Surface — Paradise is established as a corporeal, eastern, temperate place, furnished with plants and food, suitable to the human being before sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ALT2","text":"Structural — The suitability of the place is produced by the interplay of the corruptible body, the preserving soul, environmental conditions, and human obedience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Empirical and allegorical objections are not directly denied, but transformed into distinctions concerning the genre of narrative, the order of signification, and the limits of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Human life is ordered as a process from natural origin outside Paradise, through a state of grace in Paradise, to spiritual beatitude in heaven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT1","text":"Axioms concerning historical narrative, corporeality, preserving grace, and the distinction of states suffice for reconstructing the principal series of questions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT2","text":"The structure is strongest where the corporeality of Paradise, spiritual signification, and the supernatural gift do not compete, but are coordinated through an order of foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT3","text":"The physical determination of the place remains incomplete, because its eastern, remote, and most temperate situation is affirmed, while the question of the equinoctial region is left open.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains between the power of the soul preserving the body and gratuitous incorruptibility: the text asserts both, but does not explain the exact mode of causality between gift and power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT5","text":"The twofold interpretation of working and keeping — God preserving the human being or the human being cultivating Paradise — is retained without full reduction to one univocal account.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_94:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if Paradise is understood not as an isolated geographical thing, but as a nexus in which history, symbol, grace, obedience, and human destiny are bound together.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_94:A1","CH_GGVC_P_94:A4","CH_GGVC_P_94:A9","CH_GGVC_P_94:A11","CH_GGVC_P_94:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_94:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_94@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_94:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 103","title":"First Part · Question 102","context":"Chapter 103","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 102"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 102","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 103","order":104,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_95"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_95@R001","sha256":"149b39f3cd902f6ab5fde0e17e73e46014f5831c953340ac90849d3a0d07f999","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS1","text":"Quaestio est qua ratione mundus gubernetur, quem finem gubernatio habeat, quomodo unitas eius cum diversitate, contingentia, malo et resistentia componatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS2","text":"Deus, quia est causa universalis et bonum per essentiam, omnia ad se tamquam ad ultimum finem gubernat, nulla re vel eventu extra ordinem universalem relicto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, teleologica, reconstructiva et polemica, quoniam ex ordine effectuum ad causam gubernantem ascendit et exemplaria fortuitus, pluralitatis principiorum atque derelictionis mundi excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS4","text":"Motus procedit ab ordine naturali et bonitate creante ad gubernationem, ab extrinseco principio ad extrinsecum finem, ab unitate boni ad unum gubernatorem, deinde ad modos executionis et inclusionem apparentium exceptionum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS5","text":"Malum, casus, contingentia et resistentia non tolluntur in ordine particulari, sed per distinctionem ordinis particularis et universalis intra gubernationem divinam reponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","text":"Gubernatio est directio gubernatorum ad finem qui rationem boni habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A2","text":"Cursus certus rerum cognitione carentium ad id quod melius est providentiam cognoscentem requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A3","text":"Summa bonitas quae res producit easdem ad perfectionem perducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","text":"Ultima perfectio uniuscuiusque rei in consecutione finis consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","text":"Finis universalis respondet principio universali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","text":"Deus est causa universalis totius entis et principium extrinsecum universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","text":"Deus est bonus per essentiam, omnis autem creatura tantum per participationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A8","text":"Esse creatum ex nihilo conservatione gubernantis indiget ne in nihilum decidat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","text":"Unum per se est causa unitatis, quae ad rationem bonitatis et esse pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A10","text":"Perfectio universi diversitatem rerum, motuum et operationum requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","text":"Creatura Deo assimilatur et propria bonitate et causalitate bonitatis in aliis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A12","text":"Extensio gubernationis determinatur extensione finis et causalitatis gubernantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","text":"Ratio gubernationis, quae est providentia, distinguitur ab executione gubernationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A14","text":"Perfectius est aliquid et bonum esse et aliis causam bonitatis fieri quam solum in se bonum esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","text":"Quod ab ordine causae particularis deficit ex alia causa procedit, quae ad causam primam universalem reducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","text":"Malum in bono fundatur et est defectus alicuius ordinis particularis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A17","text":"Casus et contingentia denominantur per comparationem ad causas particulares vel proximas deficientes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A18","text":"Omnis inclinatio naturalis vel voluntaria a primo movente ad aliquod bonum imprimitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX1","text":"Ordo mundi non ex fortuito universali provenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX2","text":"Carentia cognitionis finis non excludit motionem ad finem ab alio cognitum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX3","text":"Stabilitas mundi et necessitas naturalis non faciunt gubernationem superfluam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX4","text":"Ordo intrinsecus universi non est ultimus finis gubernationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX5","text":"Diversitas motuum et conflictus rerum non probant pluralitatem gubernantium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX6","text":"Unitas gubernatoris non cogit effectus gubernationis ad unum tantum modum vel numerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX7","text":"Inferiora, corruptibilia, singularia et humana a gubernatione divina non excluduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX8","text":"Gubernatio sui a creatura rationali exercita non aufert necessitatem gubernationis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX9","text":"Omnia non immediate a Deo gubernantur quantum ad executionem, neque providentia ipsa inter causas secundas dividitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX10","text":"Malum, casus et contingentia non sunt eventus extra ordinem gubernationis universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX11","text":"Repugnantia bono particulari non constituit resistentiam totalem ordini divino.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D1","text":"Ordo regularis naturalium cognitione carentium demonstrat mundum ratione gubernari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D2","text":"Productio rerum a summa bonitate necessario continuatur earum directione ad perfectionem finalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A3","CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D3","text":"Deus est finis extrinsecus et ultimus universi, dum ordo intrinsecus universi est finis proximus ad Deum ordinatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D4","text":"Gubernatio mundi ab uno procedit, quia directio ad optimum unitatem intendit et unum est causa unitatis per se.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D5","text":"Diversitas rerum et motuum est modus unius ordinis perfecti, non indicium plurium principiorum gubernantium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","CH_GGVC_P_95:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D6","text":"Effectus gubernationis est unus ratione assimilationis ad summum bonum, duo ratione conservationis et motionis, innumerabiles ratione particularium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8","CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D7","text":"Nihil ens divinae gubernationi subtrahitur, quia nihil est extra causalitatem Dei vel ordinationem ad eius bonitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D8","text":"Una ars divina res secundum diversas naturas gubernat, rationales per propriam actionem et normas, irrationales secundum motionem eis proportionatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A10","CH_GGVC_P_95:A12","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D9","text":"Deus immediate omnium providentiam habet, sed executionem gubernationis causis secundis communicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D10","text":"Casus et contingentia manent reales respectu causarum proximarum, quamvis nihil sit casuale respectu providentiae universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D11","text":"Malum relinquit ordinem boni particularis, sed quia in bono fundatur non potest extra ordinem universalem subsistere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D12","text":"Peccans potest bono sibi debito repugnare, sed appetendo aliquod bonum adhuc intra inclinationem et ordinem universalem operatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD1","text":"Creatio, conservatio et gubernatio constituunt unum continuum causalitatis divinae: res producitur, in esse sustinetur et ad perfectionem dirigitur ab eodem principio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A3","CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8","CH_GGVC_P_95:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD2","text":"Participatio est simul ontologia et ratio executionis: creatura Deo assimilatur recipiendo bonum et communicando bonum aliis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD3","text":"Distinctio causarum universalium et particularium sinit ordinem universalem infallibilem affirmari sine suppressione contingentiae localis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A10","CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD4","text":"Malum et resistentia habent realitatem privativam ac particularem, non potestatem constituendi alterum ordinem ontologicum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD5","text":"Unitas gubernationis non homogenizat mundum, sed diversitatem et causalitatem secundam tamquam modos perfectioris unitatis instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","CH_GGVC_P_95:A10","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX1","text":"Nulla natura creata est sibi sufficiens quoad esse, conservationem vel finem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX2","text":"Nullum bonum intramundanum est bonum per essentiam aut finis ultimus totius.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX3","text":"Causa secunda non est principium independens, quamvis veram causalitatem exerceat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14","CH_GGVC_P_95:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX4","text":"Pluralitas rerum et causarum non requirit pluralitatem principiorum ultimorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","CH_GGVC_P_95:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX5","text":"Malum purum, bono omnino carens, esse non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX6","text":"Motio divina et actio propria creaturae non habentur ut causalitates eiusdem ordinis sibi mutuo exclusae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX1","text":"Locus ontologicus extra ordinem causae universalis non datur; totaliter ab eo exire idem esset ac non esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX2","text":"Eventus sine reductione ad aliquam causam universaliter impossibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX3","text":"Voluntas potest bonum debitum recusare, sed non potest bonum qua tale neque omnem ordinem causalem recusare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX4","text":"Deus non potest intra seriem bonorum participantium tamquam unus finis inter alios collocari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX5","text":"Universum in quo solus Deus causaliter ageret, creaturis omni causalitate privata, perfectam gubernationem non repraesentaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS1","text":"Causa universalis extrinseca → productio ex nihilo → dependentia conservativa → perfectio per finem → gubernatio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A3","CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS2","text":"Principium extrinsecum + bonum per essentiam → finis ultimus extrinsecus → participatio creaturarum → ordo intrinsecus subordinatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS3","text":"Bonum → unitas → causa per se una → unus gubernator → diversitas ordinata sub uno fine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","CH_GGVC_P_95:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS4","text":"Providentia immediata → executio mediata → causalitas secundaria → conservatio in bono et motio ad bonum → assimilatio Dei communicata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS5","text":"Defectus ab ordine proximo → interventus alterius causae → reductio ad causam primam → reinclusio in ordine universali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS6","text":"Appetitus boni particularis → recusatio boni debiti → malum et poena in ordine particulari → permanentia intra ordinem universalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AF1","text":"Ordo naturalis et bonitas creans → necessitas gubernationis → Deus ut finis ultimus → unus gubernator → assimilatio per conservationem et motionem → universalitas subiectionis → providentia immediata et executio mediata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D1","CH_GGVC_P_95:D2","CH_GGVC_P_95:D3","CH_GGVC_P_95:D4","CH_GGVC_P_95:D6","CH_GGVC_P_95:D7","CH_GGVC_P_95:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AF2","text":"Diversitas, casus, contingentia, malum et resistentia → distinctio causarum particularium et universalis → relativizatio defectus → clausura omnis exterioritatis respectu ordinis divini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D5","CH_GGVC_P_95:D10","CH_GGVC_P_95:D11","CH_GGVC_P_95:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME1","text":"Res cognitione carentes ex rebus sine fine apparentibus in effectus directionis intellectualis reclasificantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME2","text":"Ordo intrinsecus mundi ex ultimo fine in bonum proximum ad finem extrinsecum subordinatum transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME3","text":"Diversitas et conflictus ex indiciis pluralitatis gubernantium in modos perfectae unitatis universi convertuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D4","CH_GGVC_P_95:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME4","text":"Mediatio causarum secundarum ex signo defectus gubernatoris in effectum perfectionis communicatae mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D9","CH_GGVC_P_95:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0098","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME5","text":"Casus et contingentia non amplius regiones extra providentiam, sed relationes effectuum ad causas proximas designant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0114","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME6","text":"Malum et resistentia ex principiis aemulis in defectus particulares intra ordinem universalem rediguntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D11","CH_GGVC_P_95:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0112","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0130","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME7","text":"Gubernatio sui creaturae rationalis intra gubernationem divinam includitur potius quam ei opponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D7","CH_GGVC_P_95:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0079","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0091","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ALT1","text":"Surface — Examinantur existentia, finis, unitas, effectus, extensio, mediatio, infallibilitas et irresistibilitas gubernationis mundi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ALT2","text":"Structural — Systema ordinatur per distinctiones principii et finis, boni essentialis et participati, causae universalis et particularis, providentiae et executionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones ex malo, casu, diversitate et libertate solvuntur ostendendo eas ordinem particularem pro ordine universali accipere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D5","CH_GGVC_P_95:D8","CH_GGVC_P_95:D10","CH_GGVC_P_95:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Esse creatum est participatum et continue dependens, dum ordo aeternus et immutabilis per causas proximas contingentes temporaliter exsequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad octo articulorum motum restituendum: gubernationem, finem, unitatem, effectus, extensionem, mediationem, indefectibilitatem et irresistibilitatem universalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT2","text":"Restitutio doctrinis anterioribus de creatione ex nihilo, bonitate divina, providentia, participatione et malo ut privatione necessario innititur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT3","text":"Cohaerentia interna maxime pendet a distinctione ordinis universalis et particularis atque a distinctione providentiae et executionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT4","text":"Firmissima commissura est coextensio causalitatis universalis, finis universalis et gubernationis universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT5","text":"Relatio inter immutabilem ordinem providentiae et veram contingentiam effectuum per relativitatem ad causas proximas statuitur, sed nexus modalis ulterius non demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0116","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT6","text":"Imputabilitas voluntatis manet commissura fragilis, quia inclinatio voluntaria a primo movente impressa dicitur simulque repugnantia particularis iuste punitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT7","text":"Argumenta ex sagitta, domo, exercitu et ministris structuram causalitatis illustrant, sed non supplent praemissas metaphysicas ex tractatibus prioribus assumptas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT8","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat, quia apparentia contra gubernationem non delet, sed secundum gradus causalitatis et finalitatis reclasificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165857733302Z_d2c9f86b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 103","source_sha256":"149b39f3cd902f6ab5fde0e17e73e46014f5831c953340ac90849d3a0d07f999","sha256":"8edc4d158ae5f9b28ea55123c233832bc6631b05d03d2b6cf97ea3fd5e2bc34b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:58:57.734961+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS1","text":"The question is by what principle the world is governed, what end governance has, how its unity is reconciled with diversity, contingency, evil, and resistance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS2","text":"God, because He is the universal cause and good through essence, governs all things toward Himself as toward their ultimate end, leaving no thing or event outside the universal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, teleological, reconstructive, and polemical, since it ascends from the order of effects to the governing cause and excludes models of chance, plurality of principles, and abandonment of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS4","text":"The movement proceeds from natural order and creative goodness to governance, from an extrinsic principle to an extrinsic end, from the unity of goodness to one governor, then to modes of execution and the inclusion of apparent exceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AS5","text":"Evil, chance, contingency, and resistance are not removed at the particular level, but are situated within divine governance by the distinction between particular and universal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","text":"Governance is the direction of the governed toward an end that has the character of good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A2","text":"The determinate course of things lacking knowledge toward that which is better requires a knowing providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A3","text":"The highest goodness that produces things brings those same things to perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","text":"The ultimate perfection of each thing consists in the attainment of its end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","text":"A universal end corresponds to a universal principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","text":"God is the universal cause of all being and the extrinsic principle of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","text":"God is good through essence, whereas every creature is so only through participation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A8","text":"Created being from nothing requires the preservation of the governor lest it fall into nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","text":"That which is one through itself is the cause of unity, which pertains to the notion of goodness and being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A10","text":"The perfection of the universe requires diversity of things, motions, and operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","text":"A creature is assimilated to God both by its own goodness and by causing goodness in others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A12","text":"The scope of governance is determined by the scope of the governor's end and causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","text":"The plan of governance, which is providence, is distinguished from the execution of governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A14","text":"It is more perfect both to be good and to become a cause of goodness for others than merely to be good in oneself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","text":"What falls away from the order of a particular cause proceeds from another cause, which is reduced to the universal first cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","text":"Evil is grounded in good and is a defect of some particular order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A17","text":"Chance and contingency are denominated by comparison with deficient particular or proximate causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:A18","text":"Every natural or voluntary inclination is impressed by the first mover toward some good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX1","text":"The order of the world does not arise from universal chance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX2","text":"Lack of knowledge of the end does not exclude motion toward an end known by another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX3","text":"The stability of the world and natural necessity do not render governance superfluous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX4","text":"The intrinsic order of the universe is not the ultimate end of governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX5","text":"The diversity of motions and conflict of things do not prove a plurality of governors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX6","text":"The unity of the governor does not compel the effects of governance into only one mode or number.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX7","text":"Lower things, corruptible things, singular things, and human things are not excluded from divine governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX8","text":"Self-governance exercised by a rational creature does not remove the necessity of divine governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX9","text":"Not all things are governed immediately by God with respect to execution, nor is providence itself divided among secondary causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX10","text":"Evil, chance, and contingency are not events outside the order of universal governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:NX11","text":"Opposition to a particular good does not constitute total resistance to the divine order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D1","text":"The regular order of natural things lacking knowledge demonstrates that the world is governed by reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D2","text":"The production of things by the highest goodness is necessarily continued by their direction toward final perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A3","CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D3","text":"God is the extrinsic and ultimate end of the universe, while the intrinsic order of the universe is the proximate end ordered to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D4","text":"The governance of the world proceeds from one, because direction toward the best intends unity and one is through itself the cause of unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D5","text":"The diversity of things and motions is a mode of one perfect order, not an indication of multiple governing principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","CH_GGVC_P_95:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D6","text":"The effect of governance is one by reason of assimilation to the highest good, two by reason of preservation and motion, innumerable by reason of particulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8","CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D7","text":"No being is withdrawn from divine governance, because nothing is outside God's causality or ordination to His goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D8","text":"One divine art governs things according to diverse natures: rational things through their own action and rules, irrational things according to motion proportioned to them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A10","CH_GGVC_P_95:A12","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D9","text":"God has immediate providence over all things, but communicates the execution of governance to secondary causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D10","text":"Chance and contingency remain real with respect to proximate causes, although nothing is casual with respect to universal providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D11","text":"Evil departs from the order of a particular good, but because it is grounded in good it cannot subsist outside the universal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:D12","text":"One who sins can oppose the good due to him, but by desiring some good he still acts within the universal inclination and order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD1","text":"Creation, preservation, and governance constitute one continuum of divine causality: a thing is produced, sustained in being, and directed to perfection by the same principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A3","CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8","CH_GGVC_P_95:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD2","text":"Participation is at once ontology and the principle of execution: a creature is assimilated to God by receiving good and communicating good to others.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD3","text":"The distinction between universal and particular causes allows the universal infallible order to be affirmed without suppressing local contingency.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A10","CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD4","text":"Evil and resistance have privative and particular reality, not the power to establish another ontological order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SD5","text":"The unity of governance does not homogenize the world, but establishes diversity and secondary causality as modes of more perfect unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","CH_GGVC_P_95:A10","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX1","text":"No created nature is sufficient to itself with respect to being, preservation, or end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX2","text":"No intramundane good is good through essence or the ultimate end of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX3","text":"A secondary cause is not an independent principle, although it exercises true causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14","CH_GGVC_P_95:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX4","text":"The plurality of things and causes does not require a plurality of ultimate principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","CH_GGVC_P_95:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX5","text":"Pure evil, wholly devoid of good, cannot exist.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:DNX6","text":"Divine motion and the creature's proper action are not regarded as mutually exclusive causalities of the same order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX1","text":"No ontological place outside the order of the universal cause is given; to depart from it entirely would be the same as not to be.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX2","text":"An event without reduction to some cause is universally impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX3","text":"The will can refuse a due good, but it cannot refuse good as such nor every causal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX4","text":"God cannot be placed within the series of participating goods as one end among others.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:SNX5","text":"A universe in which God alone acted causally, with creatures deprived of all causality, would not represent perfect governance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0107","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS1","text":"Extrinsic universal cause → production from nothing → preservative dependence → perfection through an end → governance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A3","CH_GGVC_P_95:A4","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS2","text":"Extrinsic principle + good through essence → extrinsic ultimate end → participation of creatures → subordinate intrinsic order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A6","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS3","text":"Good → unity → one cause through itself → one governor → diversity ordered under one end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A9","CH_GGVC_P_95:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS4","text":"Immediate providence → mediate execution → secondary causality → preservation in good and motion toward good → communicated assimilation to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A11","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS5","text":"Defect from proximate order → intervention of another cause → reduction to the first cause → reinclusion in universal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A15","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:FGS6","text":"Appetite for a particular good → refusal of a due good → evil and punishment in particular order → remaining within universal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A16","CH_GGVC_P_95:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AF1","text":"Natural order and creative goodness → necessity of governance → God as ultimate end → one governor → assimilation through preservation and motion → universality of subjection → immediate providence and mediate execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D1","CH_GGVC_P_95:D2","CH_GGVC_P_95:D3","CH_GGVC_P_95:D4","CH_GGVC_P_95:D6","CH_GGVC_P_95:D7","CH_GGVC_P_95:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:AF2","text":"Diversity, chance, contingency, evil, and resistance → distinction between particular and universal causes → relativization of defect → closure of every exteriority with respect to divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D5","CH_GGVC_P_95:D10","CH_GGVC_P_95:D11","CH_GGVC_P_95:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME1","text":"Things lacking knowledge are reclassified from things appearing to be without an end into effects of intellectual direction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A1","CH_GGVC_P_95:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME2","text":"The intrinsic order of the world is transferred from being the ultimate end into a proximate good subordinated to the extrinsic end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME3","text":"Diversity and conflict are converted from signs of a plurality of governors into modes of the perfect unity of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D4","CH_GGVC_P_95:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0054","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME4","text":"The mediation of secondary causes is changed from a sign of the governor's defect into an effect of communicated perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D9","CH_GGVC_P_95:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0098","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0103","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME5","text":"Chance and contingency no longer designate regions outside providence, but relations of effects to proximate causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0114","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME6","text":"Evil and resistance are reduced from rival principles to particular defects within the universal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D11","CH_GGVC_P_95:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0112","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0130","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ME7","text":"The self-governance of the rational creature is included within divine governance rather than opposed to it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D7","CH_GGVC_P_95:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0079","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0091","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ALT1","text":"Surface — The existence, end, unity, effects, scope, mediation, infallibility, and irresistibility of the governance of the world are examined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ALT2","text":"Structural — The system is ordered through the distinctions of principle and end, essential and participated good, universal and particular cause, providence and execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A5","CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections from evil, chance, diversity, and freedom are resolved by showing that they take particular order for universal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:D5","CH_GGVC_P_95:D8","CH_GGVC_P_95:D10","CH_GGVC_P_95:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Created being is participated and continuously dependent, while the eternal and immutable order is executed temporally through contingent proximate causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_95:A7","CH_GGVC_P_95:A8","CH_GGVC_P_95:A13","CH_GGVC_P_95:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the movement of eight articles: governance, end, unity, effects, scope, mediation, indefectibility, and universal irresistibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction necessarily relies upon prior doctrines concerning creation from nothing, divine goodness, providence, participation, and evil as privation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence depends most of all on the distinction between universal and particular order and on the distinction between providence and execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT4","text":"The strongest joint is the coextension of universal causality, universal end, and universal governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT5","text":"The relation between the immutable order of providence and the true contingency of effects is established through relativity to proximate causes, but the modal nexus is not further demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0116","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0127","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT6","text":"The imputability of the will remains a fragile joint, because voluntary inclination is said to be impressed by the first mover, while particular opposition is at the same time justly punished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0138","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT7","text":"Arguments from the arrow, house, army, and ministers illustrate the structure of causality, but do not supply the metaphysical premises assumed from prior treatises.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_95:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement, because it does not eliminate appearances against governance, but reclassifies them according to degrees of causality and finality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0121","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_95:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_95@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_95:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 104","title":"First Part · Question 103","context":"Chapter 104","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 103"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 103","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 104","order":105,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_96"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_96@R001","sha256":"2b75a6fa5f52e8fcb013dcd2933750f496855fd0a6adc94c04c8a26dab46d5d9","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS1","text":"Quaestio constituitur utrum esse creatum post productionem per se permaneat an influxu divino continuo pendeat, atque utrum ex hoc sequatur possibilitas vel eventus reductionis in nihilum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS2","text":"Argumentatio metaphysico-causalis distinguit causam fiendi a causa essendi, ut dependentia creaturae non ex mutatione initiali, sed ex communicatione essendi intelligatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS3","text":"Omnis creatura directe a Deo conservatur, quia esse eius non est idem quod essentia eius, sed esse participatum ab ente per essentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS4","text":"Conservatio divina, quamvis principalis et immediata, ordinem causarum mediarum non excludit, quia causae creatae effectus suos secundario conservare possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS5","text":"Cum communicatio essendi a libera voluntate divina dependeat, Deus influxum essendi subtrahere potest; reductio in nihilum igitur possibilis est per cessationem influendi, non per actionem positivam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS6","text":"Quod tamen Deus potest facere non describitur ut eventus ordinis dati: naturae creaturarum et ratio manifestationis divinae bonitatis fundant conclusionem quod nihil omnino in nihilum redigetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A1","text":"Deus est ens per essentiam, quia essentia eius est ipsum esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","text":"Omnis creatura est ens participative, quia essentia eius non est ipsum esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A3","text":"Effectus dependet a causa secundum rationem qua causa est eius causa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A4","text":"Causa quae causat effectum solum secundum fieri non est per se causa permanentiae esse eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","text":"Conservatio per se est dependentia conservati a conservante, ita quod sine conservante esse non possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A6","text":"Conservatio indirecta consistit in remotione vel impedimento corrumpentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A7","text":"In ordine causarum, effectus dependet principaliter a causa prima et secundario a causis mediis ordinatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A8","text":"Deus, creando omnia immediate, ordinem rerum instituit in quo quaedam ab aliis dependent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","text":"Conservatio divina est continuatio actionis qua Deus dat esse, et haec actio est sine motu et tempore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A10","text":"Communicatio essendi creaturae dependet a libera voluntate divina et non ex necessitate naturae divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A11","text":"Non esse nullam causam per se habet, quia omne causans causat inquantum est ens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A12","text":"Creaturae immateriales non habent potentiam ad non esse in seipsis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A13","text":"In creaturis materialibus materia incorruptibilis manet ut subiectum generationis et corruptionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A14","text":"Miracula ordinantur ad manifestationem gratiae, dum conservatio rerum manifestat divinam potentiam et bonitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX1","text":"Conservatio per se non est mera defensio contra corrumpens, sed continuata dependentia essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX2","text":"Nulla creatura potest esse causa conservationis sui ipsius, quia nullus effectus potest sibi conferre rationem causae propriae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX3","text":"Deus non potest creaturae communicare ut conservetur in esse, divina operatione cessante, quia hoc esset communicare independentiam a causa essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX4","text":"Conservatio divina non est actio nova quae aliquid creaturae superaddat nec processus temporalis qui continue accumulat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX5","text":"Bonitas divina non imponit Deo necessitatem producendi vel conservandi res.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX6","text":"Reductio in nihilum non est actio positiva ad non esse terminata nec causalitas per se non essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX7","text":"Ex eo quod creaturae a nihilo inceperunt non sequitur quod ad solum Deum redeant per universalem annihilationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX8","text":"Desitio formarum et accidentium non est reductio entis completi in nihilum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D1","text":"Nulla creatura ne per momentum quidem subsistit nisi influxus divinus esse eius continuet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A1","CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","CH_GGVC_P_96:A3","CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D2","text":"Necessitas quae ex forma creaturae vel ex absentia contrarii nascitur non efficit creaturam simpliciter independentem, quia potentia ad non esse potest fundari in substractione influxus divini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A1","CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","CH_GGVC_P_96:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D3","text":"Conservatio immediata a Deo et conservatio mediata per causas creatas non sunt causae aemulae, sed causalitates principali et secundariae diversorum ordinum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A7","CH_GGVC_P_96:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D4","text":"Causa creata potest, forma vel dispositione iam inducta, effectum conservare sine nova immutatione effectus, quamvis introductio illius formae mutationem requirat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A4","CH_GGVC_P_96:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D5","text":"Deus potest creaturam in nihilum redigere subtrahendo influxum essendi, quia libere esse communicat et conservatio est continuatio illius communicationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","CH_GGVC_P_96:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D6","text":"Deus non est causa per se tendendi in non esse, sed potest esse causa per accidens desitionis creaturae per subtractionem suae actionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A10","CH_GGVC_P_96:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D7","text":"Nihil omnino in nihilum redigitur secundum ordinem rerum, quia immaterialia carent potentia intrinseca ad non esse et materialia non perdunt materiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A12","CH_GGVC_P_96:A13","CH_GGVC_P_96:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D8","text":"Duratio creaturae non mensuratur sola finitate virtutis receptivae creaturae, sed influxu activo divinae virtutis infinitae; contraria tamen durationem quorumdam finire possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A1","CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0082","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D9","text":"Formae et accidentia desinentia non pereunt simpliciter, sed manent in potentia materiae vel subiecti secundum modum essendi sibi proprium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SD1","text":"Ordo creatus fit structura dependentiae stratificatae: omnis esse creatum directe a Deo pendet, sed effectus intra creaturam a causis mediis secundario dependent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A7","CH_GGVC_P_96:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SD2","text":"Contingentia radicalis creaturae et stabilitas actualis ordinis creati non sunt contrariae, quia prima significat revocabilitatem influxus divini, altera perseverantiam sub ordine divinitus instituto.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","CH_GGVC_P_96:A10","CH_GGVC_P_96:A12","CH_GGVC_P_96:A13","CH_GGVC_P_96:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SD3","text":"Non esse habet structuram privativam asymmetricam: esse requirit causalitatem positivam, imminutio esse per subtractionem intelligitur, sed non esse neque causam per se neque processum naturalem proprium constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","CH_GGVC_P_96:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SD4","text":"Argumentatio transit a cosmologia originis ad cosmologiam conservationis: initium ex nihilo non definit finem rerum, quia duratio earum a causa essendi praesentiter influente pendet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A3","CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","CH_GGVC_P_96:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod connexio esse cum forma creata creaturam simpliciter necessariam vel a Deo independentem efficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omnis causalitas sit actio ad terminum positivum productum, quia subtractio influxus explicare debet desitionem essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod causalitas divina immediata causalitatem creatam mediatam eliminet, quia ordo causarum secundariarum est ipse effectus creationis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod corruptio naturalis sit annihilatio, quia corruptio materialis subiectum retinet et desitio formarum in potentia residet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet quod creaturae finitas vel principium post nihil imponat universo terminum in quo solus Deus remaneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SNX1","text":"Excluditur possibilitas esse creati omnino sui fundati, quia creatura neque est esse per essentiam neque sibi conservatio esse conferre potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SNX2","text":"Excluditur nihilum tamquam terminus positivus, causa per se, vel inclinatio naturalis rerum, quia non esse non causat et creatura naturaliter esse appetit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SNX3","text":"Excluditur consummatio cosmica naturaliter definita per evanitionem omnium creaturarum, quia ordo naturarum et manifestatio bonitatis in conservatione, non in annihilatione, ponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SNX4","text":"Excluditur Deus necessitate naturae ad productionem vel conservationem adstrictus, quia voluntas divina est principium communicationis essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS1","text":"Ens per essentiam Dei + esse participatum creaturae → dependentia per se creaturae ab influxu essendi → conservatio continua.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS2","text":"Distinctio causae fiendi et causae essendi → exclusio analogiae agentis mere factivi → necessitas causae essendi ad permanentiam esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS3","text":"Causa prima principalis + causae mediae ordinatae → conservatio divina immediata simul cum conservatione creata secundaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS4","text":"Voluntas divina libera + conservatio ut influxus continuatus → possibilitas substractionis influxus → possibilitas reductionis in nihilum sine actione positiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS5","text":"Naturae immateriales et materia permanens + conservatio ut manifestatio bonitatis → exclusio annihilationis actualis secundum ordinem rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AF1","text":"Apparens autarkia creaturarum et perseverantia formarum → distinctio conservationis indirectae et per se → dependentia esse creati a Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AF2","text":"Dependentia immediata a causa prima → quaestio de causis mediis → ordinatio conservationis principalis divinae et secundariae creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AF3","text":"Influxus essendi voluntarius → potestas subtrahendi influxum → possibilitas annihilationis per cessationem agendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AF4","text":"Possibilitas substractionis divinae → examen naturarum creatarum et finis miraculorum → negatio annihilationis actualis omnium rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME1","text":"Conservatio reclassificatur ex custodia negativa contra corruptionem in causationem ontologicam permanentiae essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME2","text":"Causalitas dividitur inter productionem fieri et sustentationem esse, ita ut permanentia effectus non ex omni agente eodem modo explicetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter conservationem divinam immediatam et mediationem creatam dissolvitur per distinctionem causalitatis principalis et secundariae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME4","text":"Annihilatio reclassificatur ex mutatione vel corruptione in privationem influxus essendi, dum corruptio ordinaria ad mutationem formarum et subiecti reducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME5","text":"Finitas creaturae non iam directe indicat finem durationis, quia potentia receptiva creaturae a virtute activa divina, quae esse influit, distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0082","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus examinat utrum creaturae in esse serventur, utrum per media serventur, utrum Deus annihilare possit, et utrum aliquid annihiletur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ALT2","text":"Structural — Esse creatum constituitur ut effectus participationis cuius permanentia dependet a causalitate essendi principali et ordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio separat possibilitatem quae ex libertate divina sequitur ab eventu qui ex ordine naturarum et ratione manifestationis divinae iudicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Tempus creaturae non est solum extensio virtutis finitae, sed duratio recepta ab influxu essendi qui sine motu et tempore datur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de esse per essentiam, participatione creaturae, causalitate essendi et influxu continuo sufficiunt ad conclusionem universalem de conservatione divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT2","text":"Firmissimus nexus systematis est transitus ab identitate divinae essentiae et esse ad dependentiam creaturae cuius essentia ab esse distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT3","text":"Tensione moderata manet nomen conservationis divinae immediatae cum conservatione per causas medias; textus eam resolvit per ordinem principalis et secundariae causalitatis, non per negationem mediorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT4","text":"Transitus a possibilitate annihilationis ad negationem annihilationis actualis non ex sola dependentia metaphysica sequitur, sed praemissas ulteriores de naturis creaturis, gratia et manifestatione bonitatis requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT5","text":"Distinctio inter nihilum simpliciter et desitionem formarum vel accidentium sustinet conclusionem finalem, sed onus systematis transfert ad differentiam inter ens completum, formam et potentiam subiecti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus: dependentia essendi → ordinatio causalitatis → potestas substractionis → exclusio annihilationis ut eventus ordinarii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165924414316Z_63b47120","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 104","source_sha256":"2b75a6fa5f52e8fcb013dcd2933750f496855fd0a6adc94c04c8a26dab46d5d9","sha256":"f84ff1bacb9155890d3fd276b9990aa2ec525e9fe72118b9d5c1626e5164e5bf","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:59:24.415282+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS1","text":"The question is posed whether created being, after production, remains through itself or depends upon a continuous divine influx, and whether from this there follows the possibility or occurrence of reduction to nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS2","text":"The metaphysical-causal argument distinguishes the cause of becoming from the cause of being, so that the creature's dependence may be understood not from initial change, but from the communication of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS3","text":"Every creature is directly conserved by God, because its being is not identical with its essence, but is being participated from being through essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS4","text":"Divine conservation, although principal and immediate, does not exclude the order of intermediate causes, because created causes can secondarily conserve their effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS5","text":"Since the communication of being depends on the free divine will, God can withdraw the influx of being; reduction to nothing is therefore possible through cessation of inflowing, not through a positive action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AS6","text":"Yet what God can do is not described as an event of the given order: the natures of creatures and the rationale of the manifestation of divine goodness ground the conclusion that nothing whatsoever will be reduced to nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A1","text":"God is being through essence, because His essence is being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","text":"Every creature is being by participation, because its essence is not being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A3","text":"An effect depends on a cause according to the respect in which the cause is its cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A4","text":"A cause that causes an effect only according to becoming is not through itself the cause of the permanence of its being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","text":"Conservation through itself is the dependence of the conserved upon the conserver, such that it cannot be without the conserver.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A6","text":"Indirect conservation consists in the removal or prevention of what corrupts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A7","text":"In the order of causes, an effect depends principally on the first cause and secondarily on ordered intermediate causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A8","text":"God, by creating all things immediately, established an order of things in which some depend on others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","text":"Divine conservation is the continuation of the action by which God gives being, and this action is without motion and time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A10","text":"The communication of a creature's being depends on the free divine will and not on a necessity of the divine nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A11","text":"Non-being has no cause through itself, because everything causing causes insofar as it is a being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A12","text":"Immaterial creatures do not have potency toward non-being within themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A13","text":"In material creatures, incorruptible matter remains as the subject of generation and corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:A14","text":"Miracles are ordered to the manifestation of grace, whereas the conservation of things manifests divine power and goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX1","text":"Conservation through itself is not mere defense against what corrupts, but a continued dependence of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX2","text":"No creature can be the cause of its own conservation, because no effect can confer upon itself the rationale of its own cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX3","text":"God cannot communicate to a creature that it be conserved in being while divine operation ceases, because this would be to communicate independence from the cause of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX4","text":"Divine conservation is not a new action that adds something to the creature, nor a temporal process that continuously accumulates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX5","text":"Divine goodness does not impose upon God a necessity to produce or conserve things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX6","text":"Reduction to nothing is not a positive action terminated in non-being, nor causality through itself of non-being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX7","text":"From the fact that creatures began from nothing it does not follow that they return to God alone through universal annihilation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:NX8","text":"The cessation of forms and accidents is not the reduction of a complete being to nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D1","text":"No creature subsists even for a moment unless the divine influx continues its being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A1","CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","CH_GGVC_P_96:A3","CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D2","text":"The necessity arising from a creature's form or from the absence of a contrary does not render the creature simply independent, because potency toward non-being can be grounded in the withdrawal of the divine influx.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A1","CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","CH_GGVC_P_96:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D3","text":"Immediate conservation by God and mediate conservation through created causes are not rival causes, but principal and secondary causalities of different orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A7","CH_GGVC_P_96:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D4","text":"A created cause can, once a form or disposition has been induced, conserve an effect without a new alteration of the effect, although the introduction of that form requires alteration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A4","CH_GGVC_P_96:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D5","text":"God can reduce a creature to nothing by withdrawing the influx of being, because He freely communicates being and conservation is the continuation of that communication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","CH_GGVC_P_96:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D6","text":"God is not a cause through itself tending toward non-being, but can be an accidental cause of a creature's cessation through withdrawal of His action.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A10","CH_GGVC_P_96:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D7","text":"Nothing whatsoever is reduced to nothing according to the order of things, because immaterial beings lack an intrinsic potency toward non-being and material beings do not lose matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A12","CH_GGVC_P_96:A13","CH_GGVC_P_96:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D8","text":"The duration of a creature is not measured by the finitude of the creature's receptive power alone, but by the active influx of infinite divine power; contraries can nevertheless bring the duration of some things to an end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A1","CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0082","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:D9","text":"Ceasing forms and accidents do not perish simply, but remain in the potency of matter or of the subject according to their proper mode of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SD1","text":"The created order becomes a structure of stratified dependence: all created being depends directly on God, but effects within creation depend secondarily on intermediate causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A2","CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A7","CH_GGVC_P_96:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SD2","text":"The radical contingency of the creature and the actual stability of the created order are not contraries, because the former signifies the revocability of divine influx, the latter perseverance under the divinely instituted order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","CH_GGVC_P_96:A10","CH_GGVC_P_96:A12","CH_GGVC_P_96:A13","CH_GGVC_P_96:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SD3","text":"Non-being has an asymmetric privative structure: being requires positive causality, diminution of being is understood through withdrawal, but non-being constitutes neither a cause through itself nor a proper natural process.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","CH_GGVC_P_96:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SD4","text":"The argument passes from a cosmology of origin to a cosmology of conservation: beginning from nothing does not determine the end of things, because their duration depends on the cause of being presently inflowing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_96:A3","CH_GGVC_P_96:A5","CH_GGVC_P_96:A9","CH_GGVC_P_96:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX1","text":"It must be false that the connection of being with created form renders a creature simply necessary or independent of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX2","text":"It must be false that all causality is action toward a produced positive terminus, because the withdrawal of influx must explain cessation of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX3","text":"It must be false that immediate divine causality eliminates mediate created causality, because the order of secondary causes is itself an effect of divine creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX4","text":"It must be false that natural corruption is annihilation, because material corruption retains a subject and the cessation of forms remains in potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the finitude of creatures or their principle after nothing imposes upon the universe a terminus in which God alone remains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SNX1","text":"The possibility of created being wholly founded upon itself is excluded, because a creature is neither being through essence nor able to confer upon itself conservation of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SNX2","text":"Nothing is excluded as a positive terminus, a cause through itself, or a natural inclination of things, because non-being does not cause and a creature naturally desires being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SNX3","text":"A cosmic consummation naturally defined by the vanishing of all creatures is excluded, because the order of natures and the manifestation of goodness are posited in conservation, not in annihilation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:SNX4","text":"God, bound by necessity of nature to production or conservation, is excluded, because the divine will is the principle of the communication of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS1","text":"Being through God's essence + participated being of the creature → dependence through itself of the creature on the influx of being → continuous conservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS2","text":"Distinction between cause of becoming and cause of being → exclusion of the analogy of the merely productive agent → necessity of the cause of being for the permanence of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS3","text":"Principal first cause + ordered intermediate causes → immediate divine conservation together with secondary created conservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS4","text":"Free divine will + conservation as continued influx → possibility of withdrawal of influx → possibility of reduction to nothing without positive action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:FGS5","text":"Immaterial natures and permanent matter + conservation as manifestation of goodness → exclusion of actual annihilation according to the order of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AF1","text":"Apparent autarky of creatures and perseverance of forms → distinction between indirect conservation and conservation through itself → dependence of created being on God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AF2","text":"Immediate dependence on the first cause → question concerning intermediate causes → ordering of principal divine and secondary created conservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AF3","text":"Voluntary influx of being → power to withdraw influx → possibility of annihilation through cessation of acting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:AF4","text":"Possibility of divine withdrawal → examination of created natures and the end of miracles → negation of the actual annihilation of all things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME1","text":"Conservation is reclassified from negative guardianship against corruption into ontological causation of the permanence of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME2","text":"Causality is divided between the production of becoming and the sustaining of being, so that the permanence of an effect is not explained in the same way by every agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME3","text":"The opposition between immediate divine conservation and created mediation is dissolved through the distinction between principal and secondary causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME4","text":"Annihilation is reclassified from change or corruption into privation of the influx of being, while ordinary corruption is reduced to change of forms and subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ME5","text":"The finitude of a creature no longer directly indicates an end of duration, because the creature's receptive power is distinguished from the active divine power that infuses being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0082","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text examines whether creatures are conserved in being, whether they are conserved through intermediaries, whether God can annihilate, and whether anything is annihilated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ALT2","text":"Structural — Created being is constituted as an effect of participation whose permanence depends on principal and ordered causality of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument separates the possibility that follows from divine freedom from the event judged from the order of natures and the rationale of the manifestation of divine goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — A creature's time is not merely the extension of finite power, but duration received from the influx of being that is given without motion and time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning being through essence, creaturely participation, causality of being, and continuous influx suffice for the universal conclusion concerning divine conservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT2","text":"The firmest nexus of the system is the transition from the identity of divine essence and being to the dependence of the creature whose essence is distinguished from being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT3","text":"A moderate tension remains in the designation of immediate divine conservation together with conservation through intermediate causes; the text resolves it through the order of principal and secondary causality, not through denial of intermediaries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT4","text":"The transition from the possibility of annihilation to the denial of actual annihilation does not follow from metaphysical dependence alone, but requires further premises concerning created natures, grace, and the manifestation of goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT5","text":"The distinction between nothing simply and the cessation of forms or accidents supports the final conclusion, but transfers the burden of the system to the difference between complete being, form, and the potency of the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_96:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: dependence of being → ordering of causality → power of withdrawal → exclusion of annihilation as an ordinary event.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_96:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_96@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_96:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 105","title":"First Part · Question 104","context":"Chapter 105","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 104"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 104","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 105","order":106,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_97"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_97@R001","sha256":"37d2c196571b5e6dea6306a4f6fcd809ccdd0173a464d79e12878318a0712add","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quousque gubernatio divina mutationem creaturarum immediate causare possit et quomodo causalitati creatae concurrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS2","text":"Deus materiam, corpora, intellectum et voluntatem immediate movere potest atque in omni agente operatur, causalitate propria creaturae servata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS3","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica et reconstructiva est, sed etiam polemica adversus occasionalismum, causalitatem creatam independentem et ordinem naturae Deo superiorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS4","text":"Probationes a dependentia potentiae, formae, virtutis et esse creati ad ordinationem causarum et actionum sub causa prima procedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS5","text":"Motus argumenti est: potentia et forma → motus corporis → operatio intellectus et voluntatis → concursus causalis → ordines causarum → actio praeter ordinem secundarium → definitio et gradatio miraculi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A1","text":"Potentia passiva reduci potest in actum ab ea potentia activa sub cuius potestate continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","text":"Materia, quia a Deo producta est, sub potestate divina continetur, et forma est actus materiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A3","text":"Virtus divina universalis ad effectum particularem determinatur per intellectum et voluntatem divinam, quae rationes proprias omnium formarum cognoscunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A4","text":"Omnis motus corporis vel formam consequitur vel ad formam tamquam via ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","text":"Operatio intellectualis proxime dependet a virtute intelligendi et similitudine rei intellectae, quas Deus causat, imprimit et conservat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","text":"Voluntas ad bonum universale patet, sed solus Deus, qui est bonum universale et causa virtutis volendi, eam sufficienter et efficaciter movere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","text":"Motus a principio intrinseco manet voluntarius, etiamsi ipsum principium intrinsecum ab alio causetur; coactio tantum ex motu contra inclinationem propriam oritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","text":"Virtutes creatae veras operationes proprias producunt, quia operatio est perfectio et finis rei creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","text":"In agentibus ordinatis secundum agens operatur in virtute primi, atque eadem actio a primo et secundo agente diversorum ordinum procedere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A10","text":"Omnis operatio propter bonum verum vel apparens fit, quod similitudinem summi boni participat; ideo Deus est finis cuiuslibet operationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","text":"Deus formas, virtutes et esse creaturarum dat et conservat atque agentia ad operationem applicat; ideo in rebus intime operatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","text":"Quaelibet causa ordinem in effectibus suis constituit, et ordines causarum inferiorum sub ordinibus causarum superiorum continentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","text":"Ordo causarum secundarum ex arbitrio voluntatis divinae procedit, non ex necessitate naturae; Deus igitur praeter illum ordinem, sed numquam contra ordinem causae primae, agere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","text":"Miraculum est effectus manifestus cuius causa simpliciter omnibus occulta est, scilicet Deus, et qui praeter causas nobis notas producitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A15","text":"Actus a solo Deo productus non est proprie miraculum, si res producta non est nata per alias causas ad ordinem naturae pertinere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0128","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A16","text":"Magnitudo miraculi mensuratur secundum excessum supra facultatem naturae, sive in substantia facti, sive in subiecto, sive in modo et ordine productionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX1","text":"Causalitas formae non requirit semper similitudinem specificam inter agens et effectum, quia sufficit continentia virtualis effectus in causa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX2","text":"Universalitas virtutis divinae non importat indeterminationem neque necessitatem agentis particularis intermedii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX3","text":"Substantiae separatae creatae formas materiae immediate non imprimunt, quia materia sub earum virtute non continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX4","text":"Motio divina corporis contactum corporalem non requirit; contactus virtualis sine mutua passione sufficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX5","text":"Infinitas potentiae divinae non cogit corpus moveri in instanti, quia Deus non agit ut virtus infinita in magnitudine ex necessitate naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX6","text":"Motio intellectus a Deo non requirit ut essentia divina intellectui creato comprehensibilis fiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX7","text":"Motio divina voluntatis nec coactionem, nec contradictionem inter motionem intrinsecam et extrinsecam, nec abolitionem meriti infert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX8","text":"Operatio Dei in omni agente non significat quod solus Deus immediate omnia efficiat aut quod virtutes creatae otiosae sint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX9","text":"Actio praeter ordinem secundarum causarum non est actio contra naturam, iustitiam, voluntatem divinam aut immutabilitatem Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX10","text":"Creatio, productio animae et iustificatio impii non sunt proprie miracula, quamvis a solo Deo fiant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX11","text":"Miraculi magnitudo neque ex infinitate potentiae divinae, neque ex dignitate rei, raritate eventus aut absentia spei gratiae sumitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0130","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D1","text":"Deus materiam immediate ad quamlibet formam determinatam movere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A1","CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","CH_GGVC_P_97:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D2","text":"Deus quodlibet corpus secundum quemcumque motum immediate movere potest, quia potest formam et dispositionem ad formam immediate causare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","CH_GGVC_P_97:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D3","text":"Deus intellectum creatum immediate movet et per concessionem virtutis intelligendi et per impressionem specierum intelligibilium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D4","text":"Deus voluntatem immediate movet tamquam bonum universale obiectivum et tamquam causa interioris inclinationis ad bonum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","CH_GGVC_P_97:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D5","text":"Motio divina voluntatis rationem actus voluntarii et imputabilitatem ad meritum vel demeritum non tollit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","text":"Una operatio creata simul vere est a creatura ut causa secunda et a Deo ut causa prima, fine ultimo et causa conservante.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A10","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D7","text":"Deus effectus causarum secundarum sine eis producere potest vel effectus producere ad quos earum virtus non se extendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D8","text":"Miraculum non est omne opus soli Deo proprium, sed opus quod ordinem naturalem rei aptae tali ordini excedit et ad causam divinam occultam refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D9","text":"Miracula supremi, medii et infimi gradus distinguuntur secundum excessum in substantia effectus, in subiecto effectus aut in modo productionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1","text":"Immediatio causalitatis divinae et mediatio causalitatis creatae non sunt oppositae, quia ad diversos ordines causalitatis pertinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:D1","CH_GGVC_P_97:D2","CH_GGVC_P_97:D3","CH_GGVC_P_97:D4","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD2","text":"Totalis dependentia creaturae a Deo causalitatem creatam non minuit, sed eius virtutem, conservationem et applicationem constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD3","text":"Ordo naturae stabilis est intra causalitatem secundam, sed contingens et non exhaustivus respectu voluntatis causae primae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD4","text":"Miraculum ordinem naturae non destruit, sed eius limites manifestat, quoniam excessus tantum ex comparatione ad facultatem naturalem mensuratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A15","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD5","text":"Gubernatio divina unam structuram continuam constituit, quae operationes ordinarias per causas secundas et operationes extraordinarias praeter earum ordinem complectitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:D7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet causas divinam et creatam tamquam agentia univoca eiusdem ordinis inter se concurrere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet virtutem creatam semel datam posse sine conservatione et applicatione causae primae operari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet ordinem causarum naturalium totum campum causalitatis possibilis exhaurire.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet libertatem voluntatis in absentia omnis causae extrinsecae consistere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnipotentiam divinam per contradictionem, arbitrium sine ordine aut productionem effectui incongruam manifestari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A3","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse oportet miraculum esse meram admirationem subiectivam sine fundamento in excessu obiectivo supra facultatem naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0130","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SNX1","text":"Systema nullum ambitum esse, potentiae aut operationis admittit qui causalitati divinae conservanti et ordinanti sit extraneus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SNX2","text":"Excluditur disiunctio ultima secundum quam aut Deus vere agit aut creatura vere agit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SNX3","text":"Possibilitas ut Deus contra ordinem suae praescientiae, voluntatis, bonitatis vel iustitiae agat absolute praecluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SNX4","text":"Excluditur tam natura causaliter clausa quam exceptio miraculosa sine ordine; extraordinarium supra ordinem secundarium manet intra ordinem causae primae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS1","text":"Schema fundamentale est: productio creaturae → continentia sub potestate divina → reductio potentiae in actum → possibilitas motionis immediatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A1","CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","CH_GGVC_P_97:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS2","text":"Extensio ad corpora procedit: causalitas formae → forma ut principium vel terminus motus → potestas immediata super omnem motum corporalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A4","CH_GGVC_P_97:D1","CH_GGVC_P_97:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS3","text":"Extensio ad operationes interiores procedit: causalitas virtutis et obiecti → principium intrinsecum creatum → actus proprius intellectus vel voluntatis → dependentia a causa prima sine coactione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D3","CH_GGVC_P_97:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS4","text":"Schema concursus est: finis divinus + virtus primi agentis + forma conservata et applicata → actio causae secundae → unus effectus causaliter plurium ordinum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A10","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS5","text":"Schema extraordinarii est: ordo secundarum causarum sub ordine primo → suspensio vel excessus mediationis secundae → effectus divinus praeter ordinem naturalem → miraculum, si effectus naturaliter ad talem ordinem pertinet → gradus secundum modum excessus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A15","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AF1","text":"Primus motus est: gubernatio ut mutatio creaturarum → potestas super materiam et formam → potestas super motum corporis → causalitas principiorum intellectus → causalitas obiecti et inclinationis voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AF2","text":"Secundus motus est: motio singularium potentiarum → operatio Dei in omni agente → distinctio ordinis primi et ordinum secundorum → actio praeter ordinem naturalem → definitio miraculi → hierarchia excessuum miraculorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME1","text":"Causalitas a campo competitivo agentium horizontalium in hierarchiam causarum diversorum ordinum transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter actionem immediatam Dei et mediationem creaturae dissolvitur, quia immediatio causae primae mediationem secundae sustentare potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:D1","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME3","text":"Natura non amplius ut ordo absolutus, sed ut ordo causarum secundarum intra ordinem ampliorem causae primae describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME4","text":"Libertas et imputabilitas non per independentiam causalitatis, sed per conservationem principii intrinseci et inclinationis propriae definiuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D4","CH_GGVC_P_97:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME5","text":"Miraculum ab eventu tantum insolito in relationem mensurabilem inter effectum et facultatem naturae reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16","CH_GGVC_P_97:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME6","text":"Transcendentia divina non ut distantia causalis, sed ut universalitas quae intimius esse et operationem creaturae attingit, describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei examinat an Deus immediate materiam, corpus, intellectum et voluntatem moveat, in agentibus operetur atque miracula efficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis causalitatem disponit per potentiam et actum, formam et operationem, causas primas et secundas atque ordines inclusos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus oppositiones inter Deum et creaturam, motionem et libertatem, naturam et miraculum in distinctiones ordinum causalium convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis ponit esse et operationem creaturae continuo a Deo conservari, dum exceptiones ordinis naturalis in voluntate divina immutabili iam continentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad omnes octo conclusiones principales restituendas, quia continent principia motionis immediatae, concursus causalis, ordinum et miraculi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A1","CH_GGVC_P_97:A4","CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT2","text":"Structura firmissima est distinctio causarum primi et secundi ordinis, quia simul immediationem divinam et operationem propriam creaturae sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT3","text":"Restitutio intra quaestionem non est omnino sui iuris, quia productionem materiae, cognitionem rationum formarum, infinitatem potentiae et causalitatem ipsius esse ex disputationibus prioribus assumit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT4","text":"Commissura libertatis manet compressa, quia conservatio principii intrinseci ad imputabilitatem affirmandam sufficit, sed relatio inter determinationem divinam et contingentiam actus ulterius non explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT5","text":"Commissura inter ordinem contingenter institutum et immutabilitatem Dei per reservationem exceptionum in voluntate divina solvitur, sed haec praehabitio potius asseritur quam intra quaestionem demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT6","text":"Definitio miraculi tensionem retinet inter causam omnibus occultam et causam tamen ut Deum nominatam, atque inter excessum obiectivum naturae et relationem ad causas nobis notas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0130","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT7","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat, quia a dominio ontologico Dei ad concursus modum, deinde ad limites ordinis naturalis et classificationem miraculorum procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_97:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T165954075134Z_ff1ba63f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 105","source_sha256":"37d2c196571b5e6dea6306a4f6fcd809ccdd0173a464d79e12878318a0712add","sha256":"6dec627e30a3b92b06507bc6d037f2a0ba2eac6cc3fe97d125603aa3d27a13bb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T16:59:54.076050+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS1","text":"The question determines how far divine governance can immediately cause the change of creatures and how it concurs with created causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS2","text":"God can immediately move matter, bodies, intellect, and will, and operates in every agent, while the creature's proper causality is preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical and reconstructive, but also polemical against occasionalism, independent created causality, and an order of nature superior to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS4","text":"The proofs proceed from the dependence of power, form, virtue, and created being to the ordering of causes and actions under the first cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument is: potency and form → motion of body → operation of intellect and will → causal concurrence → orders of causes → action beyond the secondary order → definition and gradation of miracle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A1","text":"Passive potency can be reduced to act by that active potency under whose power it is contained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","text":"Matter, because it has been produced by God, is contained under divine power, and form is the act of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A3","text":"The universal divine power is determined to a particular effect through divine intellect and will, which know the proper intelligible accounts of all forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A4","text":"Every motion of a body either follows upon form or is ordered to form as its way.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","text":"Intellectual operation depends proximately on the power of understanding and the likeness of the understood thing, which God causes, impresses, and preserves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","text":"The will is open to the universal good, but God alone, who is the universal good and the cause of the power of willing, can move it sufficiently and effectively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","text":"Motion from an intrinsic principle remains voluntary, even if that intrinsic principle itself is caused by another; coercion arises only from motion contrary to one's proper inclination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","text":"Created powers produce true proper operations, because operation is the perfection and end of a created thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","text":"In ordered agents, the second operates by the power of the first, and the same action can proceed from the first and second agent of diverse orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A10","text":"Every operation occurs for a true or apparent good, which participates in a likeness of the highest good; therefore God is the end of every operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","text":"God gives and preserves the forms, powers, and being of creatures and applies agents to operation; therefore He operates intimately in things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","text":"Every cause establishes an order in its effects, and the orders of lower causes are contained under the orders of higher causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","text":"The order of secondary causes proceeds from the choice of the divine will, not from the necessity of nature; therefore God can act beyond that order, but never against the order of the first cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","text":"A miracle is a manifest effect whose cause is simply hidden from all, namely God, and which is produced beyond causes known to us.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A15","text":"An act produced by God alone is not properly a miracle if the thing produced is not naturally apt to pertain to the order of nature through other causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0128","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:A16","text":"The magnitude of a miracle is measured according to its excess over the capacity of nature, whether in the substance of what is done, in the subject, or in the manner and order of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX1","text":"The causality of form does not always require specific likeness between agent and effect, because virtual containment of the effect in the cause suffices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX2","text":"The universality of divine power does not imply indetermination or the necessity of an intervening particular agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX3","text":"Created separate substances do not immediately impress forms into matter, because matter is not contained under their power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX4","text":"Divine motion of a body does not require bodily contact; virtual contact without reciprocal passion suffices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX5","text":"The infinity of divine power does not compel a body to be moved in an instant, because God does not act as an infinite power in magnitude by necessity of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX6","text":"The motion of the intellect by God does not require that the divine essence become comprehensible to the created intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX7","text":"Divine motion of the will entails neither coercion, nor contradiction between intrinsic and extrinsic motion, nor abolition of merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX8","text":"God's operation in every agent does not mean that God alone immediately effects all things or that created powers are idle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX9","text":"Action beyond the order of secondary causes is not action against nature, justice, the divine will, or the immutability of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX10","text":"Creation, the production of the soul, and the justification of the ungodly are not properly miracles, although they are done by God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:NX11","text":"The magnitude of a miracle is not taken from the infinity of divine power, nor from the dignity of the thing, the rarity of the event, or the absence of hope of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0130","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D1","text":"God can immediately move matter to any determinate form whatsoever.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A1","CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","CH_GGVC_P_97:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D2","text":"God can immediately move any body according to any motion whatsoever, because He can immediately cause form and disposition toward form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","CH_GGVC_P_97:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D3","text":"God immediately moves the created intellect both by granting the power of understanding and by impressing intelligible species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D4","text":"God immediately moves the will as universal objective good and as the cause of the interior inclination toward good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","CH_GGVC_P_97:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D5","text":"Divine motion of the will does not remove the character of voluntary act or imputability to merit or demerit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","text":"One created operation is at once truly from the creature as secondary cause and from God as first cause, ultimate end, and conserving cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A10","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D7","text":"God can produce the effects of secondary causes without them, or produce effects to which their power does not extend.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D8","text":"A miracle is not every work proper to God alone, but a work that exceeds the natural order of a thing apt for such an order and is referred to a hidden divine cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:D9","text":"Miracles of the highest, middle, and lowest grade are distinguished according to excess in the substance of the effect, in the subject of the effect, or in the manner of production.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1","text":"The immediacy of divine causality and the mediation of created causality are not opposed, because they pertain to diverse orders of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:D1","CH_GGVC_P_97:D2","CH_GGVC_P_97:D3","CH_GGVC_P_97:D4","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD2","text":"The creature's total dependence on God does not diminish created causality, but constitutes its power, preservation, and application.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD3","text":"The order of nature is stable within secondary causality, but contingent and non-exhaustive with respect to the will of the first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD4","text":"A miracle does not destroy the order of nature, but manifests its limits, since excess is measured only by comparison with natural capacity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A15","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SD5","text":"Divine governance constitutes one continuous structure, which encompasses ordinary operations through secondary causes and extraordinary operations beyond their order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:D7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX1","text":"It must be false that divine and created causes concur with one another as univocal agents of the same order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX2","text":"It must be false that a created power, once given, can operate without the preservation and application of the first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the order of natural causes exhausts the whole field of possible causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX4","text":"It must be false that freedom of the will consists in the absence of every extrinsic cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX5","text":"It must be false that divine omnipotence is manifested through contradiction, choice without order, or production incongruous to the effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A3","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX6","text":"It must be false that a miracle is mere subjective wonder without a foundation in objective excess over the capacity of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0130","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SNX1","text":"The system admits no domain of being, power, or operation extraneous to divine conserving and ordering causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SNX2","text":"The ultimate disjunction according to which either God truly acts or the creature truly acts is excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SNX3","text":"The possibility that God act against the order of His foreknowledge, will, goodness, or justice is absolutely precluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:SNX4","text":"Both causally closed nature and miraculous exception without order are excluded; the extraordinary beyond the secondary order remains within the order of the first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS1","text":"The fundamental schema is: production of creature → containment under divine power → reduction of potency to act → possibility of immediate motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A1","CH_GGVC_P_97:A2","CH_GGVC_P_97:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS2","text":"The extension to bodies proceeds: causality of form → form as principle or terminus of motion → immediate power over every bodily motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A4","CH_GGVC_P_97:D1","CH_GGVC_P_97:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS3","text":"The extension to interior operations proceeds: causality of power and object → created intrinsic principle → proper act of intellect or will → dependence on the first cause without coercion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D3","CH_GGVC_P_97:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS4","text":"The schema of concurrence is: divine end + power of the first agent + form preserved and applied → action of the secondary cause → one effect causally of multiple orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A10","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS5","text":"The schema of the extraordinary is: order of secondary causes under the first order → suspension or excess of secondary mediation → divine effect beyond the natural order → miracle, if the effect naturally pertains to such an order → grades according to the mode of excess.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A15","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AF1","text":"The first movement is: governance as change of creatures → power over matter and form → power over the motion of body → causality of the principles of intellect → causality of the object and inclination of will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:AF2","text":"The second movement is: motion of particular powers → God's operation in every agent → distinction of the first order and secondary orders → action beyond the natural order → definition of miracle → hierarchy of miraculous excesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME1","text":"Causality is transferred from a competitive field of horizontal agents to a hierarchy of causes of diverse orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME2","text":"The opposition between God's immediate action and creaturely mediation is dissolved, because the immediacy of the first cause can sustain the mediation of the second.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:D1","CH_GGVC_P_97:D6","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME3","text":"Nature is no longer described as an absolute order, but as an order of secondary causes within the broader order of the first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A12","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME4","text":"Freedom and imputability are defined not through independence of causality, but through preservation of the intrinsic principle and proper inclination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D4","CH_GGVC_P_97:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME5","text":"Miracle is reclassified from a merely unusual event into a measurable relation between effect and the capacity of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16","CH_GGVC_P_97:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ME6","text":"Divine transcendence is described not as causal distance, but as a universality that reaches more intimately the being and operation of the creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ALT1","text":"The surface level examines whether God immediately moves matter, body, intellect, and will, operates in agents, and performs miracles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ALT2","text":"The structural level arranges causality through potency and act, form and operation, first and secondary causes, and contained orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level converts oppositions between God and creature, motion and freedom, nature and miracle into distinctions of causal orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level posits that the being and operation of the creature are continuously preserved by God, while exceptions to the natural order are already contained in the immutable divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0115","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct all eight principal conclusions, because they contain the principles of immediate motion, causal concurrence, orders, and miracle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A1","CH_GGVC_P_97:A4","CH_GGVC_P_97:A5","CH_GGVC_P_97:A6","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT2","text":"The firmest structure is the distinction between causes of the first and second order, because it simultaneously sustains divine immediacy and the creature's proper operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A8","CH_GGVC_P_97:A9","CH_GGVC_P_97:A11","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT3","text":"The reconstruction within the question is not wholly self-sufficient, because it assumes from prior disputations the production of matter, knowledge of the intelligible accounts of forms, the infinity of power, and the causality of being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT4","text":"The juncture concerning freedom remains compressed, because preservation of the intrinsic principle suffices to affirm imputability, but the relation between divine determination and the contingency of the act is not further explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A7","CH_GGVC_P_97:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT5","text":"The juncture between contingently instituted order and the immutability of God is resolved by reserving exceptions in the divine will, but this precontainment is asserted rather than demonstrated within the question.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A13","CH_GGVC_P_97:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0115","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT6","text":"The definition of miracle retains a tension between a cause hidden from all and a cause nevertheless named as God, and between the objective excess over nature and the relation to causes known to us.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:A14","CH_GGVC_P_97:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0130","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_97:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement, because it proceeds from God's ontological dominion to the mode of concurrence, then to the limits of the natural order and the classification of miracles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_97:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_97:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_97:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0141","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_97:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_97@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_97:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 106","title":"First Part · Question 105","context":"Chapter 106","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 105"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 105","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 106","order":107,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_98"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_98@R001","sha256":"76da3f5c635bd42e60defca7e52b70d1583b52ccf8b61c18ed9a9b825b05ec73","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat utrum et quomodo creatura spiritualis aliam creaturam spiritualem moveat, distinguendo illuminationem intellectualem a motu voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS2","text":"Argumentatio metaphysico-hierarchica illuminationem definit ut communicationem veritatis cognitae, non ut productionem luminis vel perfectionis essentialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS3","text":"Differentia graduum angelicorum causat communicationem asymmetricam: superior veritatem universalius captam inferiori secundum capacitatem eius distinguit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS4","text":"Motus voluntatis a creatura spirituali excluditur, quia solus Deus et bonum universale voluntatem sufficienter movent aut ipsam potentiam volendi immutant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS5","text":"Hierarchia caelestis instituit legem stabilem qua inferiores per superiores reducuntur, ita ut illuminatio ascensum inversum non admittat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS6","text":"Communicatio superioris non tollit excellentiam superioris, quia idem verum ab inferiori minus eminenter recipitur et nova revelatio ordinem illuminationis temporaliter continuat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A1","text":"Lumen intellectui pertinens est manifestatio veritatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A2","text":"Illuminare est alteri manifestationem veritatis cognitae tradere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A3","text":"Intelligere requirit virtutem intellectivam et similitudinem rei intellectae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","text":"Superior Angelus virtutem intellectivam inferioris confortare potest per conversionem ad ipsum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A5","text":"Veritas universaliter cognita ab superiore distingui debet ut intellectus inferior eam recipere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","text":"Omnes Angeli immediate Dei essentiam vident, sed superiores plures rationes divinorum operum cognoscunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A7","text":"Lumen naturae, gratiae et gloriae a solo Deo confertur; Angelus creatus solum lumen iam datum confortat et veritatem manifestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A8","text":"Solus Deus mentem creatam immediate format et potentiam volendi creaturae tribuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A9","text":"Nihil voluntatem sufficienter movet nisi bonum universale, quod est Deus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A10","text":"Angelus potest bona creata ordinata ad Deum manifestare et sic voluntatem per modum suadentis inclinare, non efficaciter immutare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A11","text":"Lex divinitatis statuit ut inferiora in Deum per superiora reducantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A12","text":"Bonum participatum se communicat, sed receptio inferioris perfectionem superioris non aequat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A13","text":"Usque ad diem iudicii superioribus Angelis nova revelantur de dispositione mundi et salute electorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX1","text":"Illuminatio angelica non est communicatio visionis essentiae divinae, quia omnes Angeli hanc visionem immediate habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX2","text":"Illuminatio angelica non est collatio luminis naturae, gratiae aut gloriae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX3","text":"Creatura spiritualis non format immediate mentem alterius neque ei ultimam formam intellectualem imprimit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX4","text":"Purgatio et perfectio ab Angelo causatae non sunt remissio culpae aut consecutio finis voluntatis, sed remotio ignorantiae et consummatio cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX5","text":"Persuasio angelica non est motus sufficienter causans actum voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX6","text":"Inferior Angelus superiorem illuminare non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX7","text":"Ordo spiritualium substantiarum non recipit praetermissionem divinam analogam miraculo praeter ordinem corporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX8","text":"Communicatio omnium quae superior recipit non significat identitatem modi cognitionis inter superiorem et inferiorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D1","text":"Illuminatio angelica duas operationes simul continet: robur intellectuale inferioris auget et veritatem ad mensuram capacitatis inferioris explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A2","CH_GGVC_P_98:A3","CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","CH_GGVC_P_98:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D2","text":"Beatitudo communis Angelorum compatitur inaequalitatem cognitionis rationum divinorum operum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","CH_GGVC_P_98:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D3","text":"Angelus inferior per illuminationem non novum principium luminis accipit, sed lumen suum naturale ad cognitionem determinatam efficacius exercet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","CH_GGVC_P_98:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D4","text":"Angelus amorem Dei in alio promovere potest proponendo bona creata ad bonitatem divinam ordinata, sed amor sic elicitus non sub creaturae dominio causali ponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A9","CH_GGVC_P_98:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D5","text":"Distinctio inter illuminationem et motum voluntatis conservat divinum monopolium iustificationis, etiam dum Angelis munus purgandi et perficiendi tribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A7","CH_GGVC_P_98:A8","CH_GGVC_P_98:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D6","text":"Hierarchia caelestis est unidirectionalis ordo cognitionis: superior inferiori communicat, inferior vero superiorem non instruit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","CH_GGVC_P_98:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D7","text":"Ecclesiastica hierarchia non potest regulam reciprocae doctrinae angelis imponere, quia gradus humanus, sanctitas et scientia in hominibus non necessario coincidunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D8","text":"Communicatio universalis boni cohaeret cum permanentia graduum, quia inferior idem contentum recipit minus eminenter quam superior intelligit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A5","CH_GGVC_P_98:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D9","text":"Illuminatio non exhauritur, quia nova revelatio superioribus data materiam novae communicationis inferioribus conservat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A12","CH_GGVC_P_98:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SD1","text":"Systema simultanee ponit communionem beatificam et inaequalitatem epistemicam: omnes eundem Deum vident, sed ordo proximioritatis determinat quot rationes operum divinorum quisque percipiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","CH_GGVC_P_98:A11","CH_GGVC_P_98:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SD2","text":"Causalitas angelica in cognitione ministerialis est et accommodativa, dum causalitas divina originaria manet tam in esse potentiarum quam in actu ultimo voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","CH_GGVC_P_98:A5","CH_GGVC_P_98:A8","CH_GGVC_P_98:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SD3","text":"Diffusio perfectionis non est imminutio ordinis, sed ipsum medium quo superioritas suam bonitatem participat et inferioritas ad Deum reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A11","CH_GGVC_P_98:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SD4","text":"Historia salutis in caelesti cognitione progressum materialem inducit sine mutatione formae hierarchicae: revelata crescunt, sed directio mediationis non mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A11","CH_GGVC_P_98:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit cognitionem creatam quae sine mediis graduum et sine mensura recipientis eodem modo omnibus communicetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit aequationem inter doctrinam et creationem: manifestare verum non est causare ipsum lumen, mentem aut voluntatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit libertatem angelicam ut principium autonomum ordinis, quia conversio voluntaria ad alium Angelum lege divina regulatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit ordinem spiritualem contingenter dispensabilem, etiam cum ordo corporalis ad finem humanum miraculo praeteriri possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SNX1","text":"Impossibilis ponitur creatura quae alterius intellectum vel voluntatem ita possideat ut auctor creatus perfectionis interioris fiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SNX2","text":"Impossibilis ponitur aequalitas angelica quae omnem differentiam inter propinquitatem ad Deum, modum cognitionis et munus mediationis deleat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SNX3","text":"Impossibilis ponitur accessus immediatus inferiorum ad omnes rationes divinae dispositionis extra ordinem superiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS1","text":"Veritas cognita + necessitas manifestationis alteri → illuminatio definitur ut traditio manifestativa, non ut infusio luminis essentialis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A1","CH_GGVC_P_98:A2","CH_GGVC_P_98:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS2","text":"Superior cognoscens universaliter + inferior recipiens secundum modum suum → confortatio virtutis + distinctio veritatis → illuminatio inferioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A3","CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","CH_GGVC_P_98:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS3","text":"Creatura manifestans bonum + Deus solus movens voluntatem sufficienter → persuasio possibilis + immutatio voluntatis angelica impossibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A8","CH_GGVC_P_98:A9","CH_GGVC_P_98:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS4","text":"Proximitas ad Deum + plenior cognitio + lex reductionis per superiores → hierarchia cognitiva unidirectionalis → illuminatio inferioris a superiore tantum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","CH_GGVC_P_98:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS5","text":"Bonum communicativum + receptio graduata + revelatio continua → communicatio non aequans + permanentia superioritatis + continuatio illuminationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A12","CH_GGVC_P_98:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AF1","text":"Motus creaturae spiritualis → distinctio intellectus et voluntatis → illuminatio recodificatur ut manifestatio veritatis, non translatio luminis creati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AF2","text":"Manifestatio veritatis → accommodatio universalis ad particulare → subordinatio intellectualis → communicatio superioris ad inferiorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AF3","text":"Persuasio sine dominio voluntatis → exclusio motus ascendentis → diffusio boni sine aequatione → hierarchia perpetuo activa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME1","text":"Illuminatio reclassificatur ab infusione ontologica ad operationem epistemicam ministerialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME2","text":"Purgatio et perfectio reclassificantur, in actione angelica, ab effectibus moralibus in effectus cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME3","text":"Libertatis et causalitatis distinctio efficitur: Angelus suadet et proponit, Deus autem voluntatem intrinsece movet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME4","text":"Hierarchia reclassificatur non ut sola praelatio honoris, sed ut distributio proximioritatis divinae, cognitionis et mediationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME5","text":"Communicatio boni reclassificatur ut ratio conservationis ordinis: communicare non evacuare superioritatem significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus determinat quid unus Angelus alteri facere possit: illuminare potest, voluntatem immutare non potest, superiorem illuminare non potest, et inferiori communicat quidquid recipit secundum modum recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ALT2","text":"Structural — Ordo angelicus cognitionem distribuit per differentiam universalitatis, capacitatis receptivae et propinquitatis ad Deum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones ex beatitudine communi, libertate, analogia ecclesiastica et communicatione universali solvuntur per distinctionem inter principium divinum, ministerium creatum et modum recipiendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Deus est causa immediata formae intellectualis et inclinationis voluntatis; creaturae autem perfectiones communicant ordinate, dum nova revelatio historiam mundi et salutis electorum in ordinem permanentem inducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad quattuor conclusiones restituendas, si definitio illuminationis, monopolium divinum circa voluntatem, lex hierarchica et communicabilitas boni simul retinentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT2","text":"Firmissimum systematis nexum constituit distinctio inter manifestare veritatem et causare lumen, mentem vel voluntatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT3","text":"Tensionem continet doctrina qua omnes Angeli Dei essentiam immediate vident, sed superiores tamen plures rationes in Deo cognoscunt; resolutio pendet ex distinctione inter essentiam visam et rationes operum divinorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT4","text":"Tensionem continet assertio quod Angelus voluntatem inclinat per persuasionem, non tamen movet; limes inter inclinationem obiecti propositi et motum potentiae voluntatis praecise servandus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis apparet ubi invariabilitas ordinis spiritualis distinguitur a possibilitate miraculi in ordine corporali: ratio data ex ordinatione hominum et invisibilitate operationum angelicarum necessitatem universalem ordinis spiritualis sustinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT6","text":"Communicatio omnium quae superior recipit cum permanentia ignorantiae inferioris cohaeret solum si “omnia” ad communicationem graduatam et ad revelationes tunc receptas refertur, non ad identitatem cognitionis aut ad plenitudinem divinam exhaustam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170017567206Z_4ab04061","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 106","source_sha256":"76da3f5c635bd42e60defca7e52b70d1583b52ccf8b61c18ed9a9b825b05ec73","sha256":"5827f6851ba1b8e2d0096240319081a00048e7b6cb323e22b5db64bc1199f360","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:00:17.568295+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS1","text":"The question investigates whether and how a spiritual creature moves another spiritual creature, distinguishing intellectual illumination from the movement of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS2","text":"The metaphysical-hierarchical argument defines illumination as the communication of known truth, not as the production of light or essential perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS3","text":"The difference among angelic grades causes asymmetric communication: the superior distinguishes for the inferior, according to the latter's capacity, truth grasped more universally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS4","text":"Movement of the will by a spiritual creature is excluded, because God alone and the universal good sufficiently move the will or alter the very power of willing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS5","text":"The celestial hierarchy establishes a stable law by which lower beings are led back to God through higher beings, such that illumination does not admit an inverse ascent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AS6","text":"The superior's communication does not remove the superiority of the superior, because the same truth is received less eminently by the inferior, and new revelation temporally continues the order of illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A1","text":"Light pertaining to the intellect is the manifestation of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A2","text":"To illuminate is to convey to another the manifestation of known truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A3","text":"Understanding requires an intellective power and a likeness of the thing understood.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","text":"A superior Angel can strengthen the intellective power of an inferior through the latter's turning toward him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A5","text":"Truth known universally by the superior must be distinguished so that the inferior intellect can receive it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","text":"All Angels immediately see the essence of God, but the superiors know more intelligible accounts of the divine works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A7","text":"The light of nature, grace, and glory is conferred by God alone; a created Angel only strengthens light already given and manifests truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A8","text":"God alone immediately forms the created mind and bestows upon the creature the power of willing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A9","text":"Nothing sufficiently moves the will except the universal good, which is God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A10","text":"An Angel can manifest created goods ordered to God and thus incline the will in the manner of one persuading, not effectively alter it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A11","text":"The law of divinity establishes that lower things are led back to God through higher things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A12","text":"Participated good communicates itself, but the reception of the inferior does not equal the perfection of the superior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:A13","text":"Until the day of judgment, new things are revealed to the superior Angels concerning the disposition of the world and the salvation of the elect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX1","text":"Angelic illumination is not the communication of the vision of the divine essence, because all Angels immediately possess this vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX2","text":"Angelic illumination is not the bestowal of the light of nature, grace, or glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX3","text":"A spiritual creature does not immediately form another's mind or imprint upon it the ultimate intellectual form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX4","text":"Purification and perfection caused by an Angel are not the remission of guilt or the attainment of the end of the will, but the removal of ignorance and the consummation of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX5","text":"Angelic persuasion is not a movement sufficiently causing an act of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX6","text":"An inferior Angel cannot illuminate a superior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX7","text":"The order of spiritual substances does not admit a divine bypass analogous to a miracle outside the corporeal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:NX8","text":"The communication of all that the superior receives does not signify identity of the mode of cognition between superior and inferior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D1","text":"Angelic illumination simultaneously contains two operations: it increases the intellectual strength of the inferior and explicates truth according to the measure of the inferior's capacity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A2","CH_GGVC_P_98:A3","CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","CH_GGVC_P_98:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D2","text":"The common beatitude of the Angels is compatible with inequality in the cognition of the intelligible accounts of the divine works.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","CH_GGVC_P_98:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D3","text":"Through illumination, an inferior Angel receives not a new principle of light, but exercises its natural light more effectively toward determinate cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","CH_GGVC_P_98:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D4","text":"An Angel can promote love of God in another by proposing created goods ordered to divine goodness, but love thus elicited is not placed under the causal dominion of a creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A9","CH_GGVC_P_98:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D5","text":"The distinction between illumination and movement of the will preserves the divine monopoly of justification, even while the office of purifying and perfecting is attributed to Angels.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A7","CH_GGVC_P_98:A8","CH_GGVC_P_98:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D6","text":"The celestial hierarchy is a unidirectional order of cognition: the superior communicates to the inferior, whereas the inferior does not instruct the superior.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","CH_GGVC_P_98:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D7","text":"The ecclesiastical hierarchy cannot impose upon Angels a rule of reciprocal teaching, because human rank, holiness, and knowledge do not necessarily coincide in human beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D8","text":"The universal communication of good coheres with the permanence of grades, because the inferior receives the same content less eminently than the superior understands it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A5","CH_GGVC_P_98:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:D9","text":"Illumination is not exhausted, because new revelation given to superiors preserves material for new communication to inferiors.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A12","CH_GGVC_P_98:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SD1","text":"The system simultaneously posits beatific communion and epistemic inequality: all see the same God, but the order of proximity determines how many intelligible accounts of the divine works each perceives.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","CH_GGVC_P_98:A11","CH_GGVC_P_98:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SD2","text":"Angelic causality in cognition is ministerial and accommodative, while divine causality remains original both in the being of powers and in the ultimate act of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","CH_GGVC_P_98:A5","CH_GGVC_P_98:A8","CH_GGVC_P_98:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SD3","text":"The diffusion of perfection is not a diminution of order, but the very means by which superiority shares its goodness and inferiority is led back to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A11","CH_GGVC_P_98:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SD4","text":"The history of salvation introduces material progress into celestial cognition without changing the hierarchical form: revealed things increase, but the direction of mediation does not change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A11","CH_GGVC_P_98:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:DNX1","text":"The system excludes created cognition communicated in the same way to all without the mediation of grades and without the measure of the recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the equation of teaching with creation: to manifest truth is not to cause light itself, mind, or will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:DNX3","text":"The system excludes angelic freedom as an autonomous principle of order, because voluntary turning toward another Angel is regulated by divine law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a spiritual order contingently dispensable, even though the corporeal order can be bypassed by miracle for a human end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SNX1","text":"Impossible is posited a creature that so possesses another's intellect or will as to become the created author of interior perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SNX2","text":"Impossible is posited an angelic equality that would erase every difference among proximity to God, mode of cognition, and office of mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:SNX3","text":"Impossible is posited an immediate access of inferiors to all intelligible accounts of the divine disposition outside the order of superiors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS1","text":"Known truth + necessity of manifestation to another → illumination is defined as manifestative transmission, not as infusion of essential light.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A1","CH_GGVC_P_98:A2","CH_GGVC_P_98:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS2","text":"Superior knowing universally + inferior receiving according to its own mode → strengthening of power + distinction of truth → illumination of the inferior.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A3","CH_GGVC_P_98:A4","CH_GGVC_P_98:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS3","text":"Creature manifesting good + God alone sufficiently moving the will → persuasion possible + angelic alteration of the will impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A8","CH_GGVC_P_98:A9","CH_GGVC_P_98:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS4","text":"Proximity to God + fuller cognition + law of reduction through superiors → unidirectional cognitive hierarchy → illumination of the inferior by the superior alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A6","CH_GGVC_P_98:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:FGS5","text":"Communicative good + graded reception + continuous revelation → non-equalizing communication + permanence of superiority + continuation of illumination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_98:A12","CH_GGVC_P_98:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AF1","text":"Movement of a spiritual creature → distinction of intellect and will → illumination is recodified as manifestation of truth, not transfer of created light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AF2","text":"Manifestation of truth → accommodation of the universal to the particular → intellectual subordination → communication from superior to inferior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:AF3","text":"Persuasion without dominion over the will → exclusion of ascending movement → diffusion of good without equalization → perpetually active hierarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME1","text":"Illumination is reclassified from ontological infusion to a ministerial epistemic operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME2","text":"Purification and perfection are reclassified, in angelic action, from moral effects into effects of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME3","text":"The distinction of freedom and causality is effected: the Angel persuades and proposes, whereas God intrinsically moves the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME4","text":"Hierarchy is reclassified not as mere precedence of honor, but as a distribution of divine proximity, cognition, and mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ME5","text":"The communication of good is reclassified as a principle of preserving order: to communicate does not mean to empty out superiority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines what one Angel can do to another: it can illuminate, cannot alter the will, cannot illuminate a superior, and communicates to the inferior whatever it receives according to the mode of the recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ALT2","text":"Structural — The angelic order distributes cognition through difference of universality, receptive capacity, and proximity to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections from common beatitude, freedom, ecclesiastical analogy, and universal communication are resolved through the distinction among divine principle, created ministry, and mode of receiving.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — God is the immediate cause of intellectual form and inclination of the will; creatures, however, communicate perfections in an ordered way, while new revelation introduces the history of the world and the salvation of the elect into a permanent order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct four conclusions, if the definition of illumination, the divine monopoly concerning the will, the hierarchical law, and the communicability of good are retained together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT2","text":"The strongest nexus of the system consists in the distinction between manifesting truth and causing light, mind, or will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT3","text":"The doctrine contains a tension whereby all Angels immediately see the essence of God, yet superiors nevertheless know more intelligible accounts in God; the resolution depends on the distinction between the essence seen and the intelligible accounts of divine works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT4","text":"The assertion contains a tension that an Angel inclines the will through persuasion yet does not move it; the boundary between the inclination of the proposed object and the movement of the power of the will must be precisely preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint appears where the invariability of the spiritual order is distinguished from the possibility of miracle in the corporeal order: the reason given from the ordering of human beings and the invisibility of angelic operations supports the universal necessity of the spiritual order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_98:MRT6","text":"The communication of all that the superior receives coheres with the persistence of the inferior's ignorance only if “all” is referred to graded communication and to revelations then received, not to identity of cognition or to exhausted divine fullness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_98:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_98@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_98:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 107","title":"First Part · Question 106","context":"Chapter 107","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 106"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 106","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 107","order":108,"parents":["RAW_GGVC_P_99"],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_99@R001","sha256":"0d840ae7b23b49c4ab5cec307083ddc18ffb3386cd9d6bcae6fa95440c6c6d37","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quid sit locutio angelica et quibus condicionibus eius directio, ordinatio hierarchica, relatio ad Deum, independentia localis et communicabilitas limitentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS2","text":"Locutio reconstituitur non ut emissio signi sensibilis, sed ut ordinatio voluntaria conceptus intellecti ad manifestationem apud alterum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS3","text":"Distinctio inter locutionem et illuminationem solvitur per duplex principium conceptus manifestati: prima veritas generat illuminationem, voluntas creata locutionem tantum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS4","text":"Relatio angelica ad Deum non potest esse manifestatio Deo facta, sed fit motus receptivus quo angelus divinam voluntatem consulit vel excellentiam admiratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS5","text":"Quia operatio intellectualis angelica abstrahitur a loco et tempore, distantia localis neque transmissionem neque perceptionem locutionis impedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS6","text":"Quia voluntas loquentis conceptum ad determinatum auditorem ordinare potest, accessus ad locutionem non ex communitate naturae nec ex absentia distantiae, sed ex destinatione voluntaria procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A1","text":"Voluntas movet intellectum ab intelligibili habitualiter retento ad intelligibile actu consideratum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A2","text":"Voluntas conceptum actu intellectum ad alterum ordinare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","text":"Loqui ad alterum est conceptum mentis voluntarie ad ipsius alterius manifestationem ordinare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A4","text":"Conceptus mentis creaturae manet absconditus nisi voluntas eius ad manifestationem ipsum ordinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A5","text":"Angelus corporeum obstaculum non habet quo conceptus manifestandus signo sensibili mediari debeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","text":"Manifestatio rei secundum dependentiam a prima veritate est simul locutio et illuminatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","text":"Manifestatio eorum quae ex voluntate creata dependent est locutio, non illuminatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A8","text":"Deus est regula omnis veritatis, voluntas autem creata non est regula veritatis sed lumen participans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A9","text":"Operatio intellectualis angelica, cum sit a loco et tempore abstracta, distantia locali non impeditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A10","text":"Voluntas loquentis determinat ad quem conceptus manifestandus ordinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX1","text":"Locutio angelica non est vox, nutus, membrum corporale neque signum sensibile externum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX2","text":"Cognitio angelica alterius mentis non est transparentia spontanea quae voluntariam conceptus retentionem aboleat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX3","text":"Locutio non aequatur illuminationi, quamvis omnis illuminatio intra genus locutionis contineatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX4","text":"Angelus inferior superiorem illuminare non potest, quia illuminatio a principio divino per superiores ad inferiores derivatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX5","text":"Angelus Deo non loquitur ut Deo veritatem vel voluntatem ignotam manifestet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX6","text":"Distantia localis non est causa silentii, imminutæ perceptionis vel restrictionis extensionis locutionis angelicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX7","text":"Locutio unius angeli ad alium non fit omnibus angelis necessario communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D1","text":"Angelus alteri statim manifestat conceptum cum voluntas conceptum ad illum ordinat, quia corporalis mediatio signorum abest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A2","CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D2","text":"Angelus sibi ipsi loquitur cum voluntas conceptum habitualiter retentum ad actualem considerationem convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A1","CH_GGVC_P_99:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D3","text":"Angelus inferior superiori loqui potest de eo quod ad voluntatem suam pertinet, quamvis superiorem illuminare non possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D4","text":"Superior angelus inferiori loquitur dupliciter: illuminando cum manifestat veritatem sub regula divina, et simpliciter loquendo cum manifestat propriam voluntatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D5","text":"Locutio angeli ad Deum est receptiva, quia ordinatur ad accipiendum cognitionem vel ad admirandum excellentiam incomprehensam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D6","text":"Consultatio divina intermittit secundum novitatem eorum quae agenda occurrunt, laudatio et admiratio divina permanent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D7","text":"Accessus selectivus ad locutionem compatitur cum absentia impedimenti localis, quia limitatio non est physica sed voluntaria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A9","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D8","text":"Illuminationes omnibus communes sunt inquantum a prima regula veritatis procedunt, locutiones voluntatis creatae privatae manere possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD1","text":"Systema communicationis angelicae duplicem ordinem constituit: ordinem veritatis, qui hierarchice descendit, et ordinem voluntatis, qui a quolibet volente ad quemlibet destinatarium procedere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD2","text":"Hierarchia angelica non est imminutio absolutae facultatis loquendi, sed restrictio unius specialis modi locutionis, scilicet illuminationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD3","text":"Secretum mentale in angelis non procedit ex opacitate materiali, sed ex dominio voluntatis super destinationem conceptus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A2","CH_GGVC_P_99:A4","CH_GGVC_P_99:A5","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD4","text":"Distinctio inter locutionem ad creaturam et locutionem ad Deum fundatur in asymmetria cognitionis: creatura potest manifestare creaturae, Deo autem nihil conferre potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD5","text":"Communicatio angelica est non-spatialis sed non-publica: infinitas extensionis localis non producit universalitatem receptionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A9","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:DNX1","text":"Communitas naturae intellectualis non sufficit ut omnes conceptus omnibus intellectibus pateant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:DNX2","text":"Omnis relatio superioris et inferioris non est relatio unidirectionalis, quia ordo veritatis distinguitur ab ordine voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:DNX3","text":"Absentia corporis non destruit distinctionem inter interiorem conceptum et conceptum alteri communicatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:DNX4","text":"Cognoscere quid alter velit non constituit per se perfectionem intellectus cognoscentis, nisi voluntas cognita sit divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit campum intelligibilem simpliciter publicum, in quo omne intellectum ab uno angelo ipso facto omnibus angelis communicetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit voluntatem creatam ut fontem normativum veritatis et illuminationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit reciprocitatem cognitivam inter Deum et angelum, quia omnis motus locutionis angelicae ad Deum est petitio, consultatio vel admiratio, non informatio Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS1","text":"Intelligibile habituale → motus voluntatis → conceptus actu consideratus → ordinatio ad alterum → manifestatio conceptus → locutio angelica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS2","text":"Conceptus manifestatus sub prima veritate → regula divina → perfectio intellectus recipientis → illuminatio hierarchice descendens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS3","text":"Conceptus dependens a voluntate creata → destinatio propria volentis → locutio sine illuminatione → communicatio ascensiva, descensiva vel selectiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS4","text":"Conceptus ordinatus ad Deum → impossibilitas informationis divinae → consultatio vel admiratio → locutio receptiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS5","text":"Abstractio intellectualis a loco → imminutio causalitatis localis → absentia impedimenti distantiae → selectio auditoris per voluntatem, non per situm.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AF1","text":"Apparitio impossibilitatis locutionis sine corpore → redefinitio locutionis ut manifestatio voluntarie destinata → distinctio locutionis et illuminationis → distributio hierarchiae secundum principium divinum → conversio locutionis ad Deum in receptionem → exclusio causalitatis localis → determinatio audientis per voluntariam destinationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME1","text":"Locutio transfertur e campo phonico et corporeo ad campum voluntariae ordinationis intellectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME2","text":"Oppositio simplex superioris loquentis et inferioris audientis dissolvitur in distinctionem inter fluxum illuminationis et circulationem locutionis voluntariae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME3","text":"Secretum non amplius explicatur per clausuram corporis, sed per non-destinationem voluntariam conceptus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME4","text":"Spatium reclassificatur ut conditio accidentalis operationis angeli, non ut mensura efficaciae vel extensionis communicationis intellectualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME5","text":"Communitas angelica dividitur inter veritates communes, quae illuminationem recipiunt, et motus voluntatis proprios, qui destinatarios particulares habere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus definit an angeli loquantur, quo ordine loquantur, num Deo loquantur, utrum distantia obstet, et utrum omnes locutionem percipiant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ALT2","text":"Structural — Locutio producitur per compositionem intellectus, voluntatis, manifestationis et destinationis, non per instrumentum corporale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Hierarchia cognitiva restringitur ad veritatem divinam communicandam, dum voluntas creata efficit canales communicationis non-hierarchicos et selectivos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Intellectus angelicus abstrahitur a loco et tempore, sed consultatio divina describitur secundum novitatem agendorum, unde ordo actionis novitatem sine locali mediatione retinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam definitionem locutionis, quia nexus voluntatis, conceptus et manifestationis omnes conclusiones principales generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter primam veritatem et voluntatem creatam sufficit ad restituendum discrimen illuminationis, locutionis ascensivae et locutionis descensivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT3","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi secretum, selectio auditoris et absentia distantiae ex eodem principio voluntariae destinationis connectuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT4","text":"Tensionem relinquit quod boni angeli se invicem in Verbo vident, dum tamen locutio particularis ab aliis voluntarie excludi potest; textus differentiam inter visionem et conceptum ad se ordinatum supponit potius quam plene formalizat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT5","text":"Tensionem relinquit quod locutio ad Deum sub eadem definitione ponitur cum locutione ad creaturam, quamvis prima manifestatio alteri sit et secunda ordinatio ad accipiendum ab altero.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, si locutio non tamquam genus univocum transmissionis, sed tamquam ordinatio conceptus diversimode determinata per veritatem, voluntatem, recipientem et finem accipitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170038821918Z_83b79b27","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 107","source_sha256":"0d840ae7b23b49c4ab5cec307083ddc18ffb3386cd9d6bcae6fa95440c6c6d37","sha256":"5b1b51165b0e76c5d65ed0b878bdbb3249ee19ec6917ab7e13f387a6fb88dc1f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:00:38.824085+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS1","text":"The question determines what angelic speech is and under what conditions its direction, hierarchical ordering, relation to God, local independence, and communicability are limited.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS2","text":"Speech is reconstructed not as the emission of a sensible sign, but as the voluntary ordering of an understood concept toward manifestation to another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS3","text":"The distinction between speech and illumination is resolved through the twofold principle of the manifested concept: first truth generates illumination, created will speech alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS4","text":"The angelic relation to God cannot be a manifestation made to God, but becomes a receptive motion by which the angel consults the divine will or admires excellence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS5","text":"Because angelic intellectual operation is abstracted from place and time, local distance impedes neither the transmission nor the perception of speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AS6","text":"Because the speaker's will can order a concept to a determinate hearer, access to speech proceeds not from community of nature nor from the absence of distance, but from voluntary designation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A1","text":"Will moves the intellect from an intelligible habitually retained to an intelligible actually considered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A2","text":"Will can order an actually understood concept toward another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","text":"To speak to another is voluntarily to order a concept of the mind to its manifestation to that very other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A4","text":"A concept of a creature's mind remains hidden unless its will orders it toward manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A5","text":"An angel has no corporeal obstacle by which a concept to be manifested must be mediated through a sensible sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","text":"The manifestation of a thing according to dependence upon first truth is at once speech and illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","text":"The manifestation of those things which depend on created will is speech, not illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A8","text":"God is the rule of all truth, whereas created will is not a rule of truth but a participating light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A9","text":"Angelic intellectual operation, being abstracted from place and time, is not impeded by local distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:A10","text":"The speaker's will determines to whom the concept to be manifested is ordered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX1","text":"Angelic speech is not voice, gesture, bodily member, or external sensible sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX2","text":"Angelic cognition of another's mind is not a spontaneous transparency that abolishes the voluntary retention of a concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX3","text":"Speech is not equated with illumination, although every illumination is contained within the genus of speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX4","text":"An inferior angel cannot illuminate a superior, because illumination is derived from the divine principle through superiors to inferiors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX5","text":"An angel does not speak to God so as to manifest to God a truth or will unknown to Him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX6","text":"Local distance is not a cause of silence, diminished perception, or restriction of the extension of angelic speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:NX7","text":"The speech of one angel to another does not become necessarily common to all angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D1","text":"An angel immediately manifests a concept to another when the will orders the concept toward that one, because corporeal mediation by signs is absent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A2","CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D2","text":"An angel speaks to itself when the will turns a habitually retained concept toward actual consideration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A1","CH_GGVC_P_99:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D3","text":"An inferior angel can speak to a superior concerning what pertains to its will, although it cannot illuminate the superior.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D4","text":"A superior angel speaks to an inferior in two ways: by illuminating when it manifests truth under the divine rule, and by simply speaking when it manifests its own will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D5","text":"An angel's speech to God is receptive, because it is ordered toward receiving cognition or toward admiring incomprehensible excellence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D6","text":"Divine consultation is intermittent according to the novelty of things to be done that arise, while divine praise and admiration endure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D7","text":"Selective access to speech is compatible with the absence of local impediment, because the limitation is not physical but voluntary.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A9","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:D8","text":"Illuminations are common to all insofar as they proceed from the first rule of truth; utterances of created will can remain private.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD1","text":"The system of angelic communication establishes a twofold order: an order of truth, which descends hierarchically, and an order of will, which can proceed from any willing being to any recipient.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD2","text":"Angelic hierarchy is not a diminishment of the absolute capacity to speak, but a restriction of one special mode of speech, namely illumination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A6","CH_GGVC_P_99:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD3","text":"Mental secrecy in angels does not proceed from material opacity, but from the dominion of will over the destination of the concept.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A2","CH_GGVC_P_99:A4","CH_GGVC_P_99:A5","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD4","text":"The distinction between speech to a creature and speech to God is founded upon an asymmetry of cognition: a creature can manifest to a creature, but can contribute nothing to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A3","CH_GGVC_P_99:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SD5","text":"Angelic communication is non-spatial but not public: infinity of local extension does not produce universality of reception.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_99:A9","CH_GGVC_P_99:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:DNX1","text":"Community of intellectual nature does not suffice for all concepts to be open to all intellects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:DNX2","text":"Not every relation of superior and inferior is a unidirectional relation, because the order of truth is distinguished from the order of will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:DNX3","text":"The absence of a body does not destroy the distinction between an interior concept and a concept communicated to another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:DNX4","text":"Knowing what another wills does not in itself constitute the perfection of the knowing intellect, unless the known will is divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SNX1","text":"The system excludes an intelligible field that is simply public, in which everything understood by one angel is thereby communicated to all angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SNX2","text":"The system excludes created will as a normative source of truth and illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:SNX3","text":"The system excludes cognitive reciprocity between God and angel, because every motion of angelic speech toward God is petition, consultation, or admiration, not information given to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS1","text":"Habitual intelligible → motion of will → actually considered concept → ordering toward another → manifestation of the concept → angelic speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS2","text":"Concept manifested under first truth → divine rule → perfection of the recipient intellect → hierarchically descending illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS3","text":"Concept dependent on created will → the willing one's own designation → speech without illumination → ascending, descending, or selective communication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS4","text":"Concept ordered toward God → impossibility of divine information → consultation or admiration → receptive speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:FGS5","text":"Intellectual abstraction from place → diminution of local causality → absence of impediment from distance → selection of the hearer through will, not position.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:AF1","text":"Appearance of the impossibility of speech without a body → redefinition of speech as voluntarily designated manifestation → distinction between speech and illumination → distribution of hierarchy according to the divine principle → conversion of speech to God into reception → exclusion of local causality → determination of the hearer through voluntary designation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME1","text":"Speech is transferred from the phonic and corporeal field to the field of voluntary ordering of the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME2","text":"The simple opposition of superior speaker and inferior hearer is dissolved into the distinction between the flow of illumination and the circulation of voluntary speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME3","text":"Secrecy is no longer explained through bodily enclosure, but through the voluntary non-designation of the concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME4","text":"Space is reclassified as an accidental condition of angelic operation, not as a measure of the efficacy or extension of intellectual communication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ME5","text":"The angelic community is divided between common truths, which receive illumination, and proper motions of will, which can have particular recipients.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines whether angels speak, in what order they speak, whether they speak to God, whether distance obstructs, and whether all perceive speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ALT2","text":"Structural — Speech is produced through the composition of intellect, will, manifestation, and designation, not through a corporeal instrument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Cognitive hierarchy is restricted to communicating divine truth, while created will produces non-hierarchical and selective channels of communication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The angelic intellect is abstracted from place and time, but divine consultation is described according to the novelty of things to be done, whence the order of action retains novelty without local mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the definition of speech, because the nexus of will, concept, and manifestation generates all the principal conclusions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT2","text":"The distinction between first truth and created will suffices to restore the difference between illumination, ascending speech, and descending speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT3","text":"The structure is strongest where secrecy, selection of the hearer, and absence of distance are connected from the same principle of voluntary designation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT4","text":"It leaves a tension in that good angels see one another in the Word, while particular speech can nevertheless be voluntarily excluded from others; the text presupposes rather than fully formalizes the difference between vision and a concept ordered to oneself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0077","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT5","text":"It leaves a tension in that speech to God is placed under the same definition as speech to a creature, although the former is manifestation to another and the latter ordering to receive from another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC_P_99:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if speech is understood not as a univocal genus of transmission, but as an ordering of a concept variously determined by truth, will, recipient, and end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC_P_99:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC_P_99@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC_P_99:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 108","title":"First Part · Question 107","context":"Chapter 108","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 107"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 107","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 108","order":109,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__100"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__100@R001","sha256":"33e5c4fdc63837380034abc4f95a242df9a1b3801c4466d68bd8512a143fc950","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quibus principiis multitudo angelica in hierarchias et ordines distinguatur, quomodo hi gradus nominentur et ordinentur, utrum permaneant, et quomodo homines ad eos referantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS2","text":"Unitas hierarchiae sumitur ex uno principe, pluralitas autem ex diversis modis quibus multitudo gubernationem et illuminationem recipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, reconstructiva et distinctiva: apparentia repugnantia solvuntur per distinctiones respectus, finis, causalitatis et attributionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS4","text":"Motus procedit a definitione hierarchiae ad eius divisionem, ab hierarchiis ad ordines, ab ordinibus communibus ad officia singularia, deinde ad fundamentum naturale et gratuitum distinctionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS5","text":"Nomina et gradus ordinum ex modo participationis perfectionum, ex relatione ad Deum et ex functione in gubernatione derivantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS6","text":"Distinctio graduum ab executione officiorum separatur, ut permanentia ordinum cum cessatione quarundam operationum post iudicium componatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS7","text":"Conclusio includit homines in ordines angelicos secundum gloriam gratiae, exclusa translatione naturae et servata una societate beatorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A1","text":"Hierarchia est sacer principatus constans ex principe et multitudine sub eo ordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A2","text":"Unus Deus princeps constituit unam hierarchiam omnis creaturae rationalis sacrorum capacis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A3","text":"Diversi modi recipiendi gubernationem et illuminationem constituunt diversas hierarchias; homines sub similitudinibus sensibilibus, angeli in puritate intelligibili recipiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A4","text":"Rationes rerum ab angelis cognoscuntur vel in primo principio universali, vel in causis creatis universalibus, vel secundum applicationem ad res et causas proprias.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A5","text":"Hierarchiae angelicae non distinguuntur ex modo videndi essentiam Dei, sed ex modo cognoscendi rationes rerum creatarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A6","text":"Multitudo hierarchica requirit diversos ordines secundum diversos actus et officia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A7","text":"Quaelibet multitudo perfecta in summum, medium et infimum reducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A8","text":"Perfectiones spirituales omnibus angelis communes sunt, sed excellentius possidentur ab eis qui eas perfectius aliis communicare possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A9","text":"Cognitio humana angelos in ordinibus communibus comprehendit, quamvis secundum perfectam rerum distinctionem quilibet angelus proprium officium et proprium ordinem habeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A10","text":"Ordo gubernationis distinguitur secundum relationem ad finem naturalem vel ad finem supernaturalem visionis et fruitionis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A11","text":"In angelis dona gratuita capacitati naturali proportionantur; in hominibus eadem proportio necessaria non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A12","text":"Nomen proprium ordinis sumitur ex perfectione naturae eius proportionata, non ex perfectione deficienter participata neque ex perfectione excedenter habita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A13","text":"Excellentia inferioris ordinis continetur in superiori, sed excellentia superioris non continetur in inferiori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A14","text":"Processus hierarchicus distinguit considerationem finis, dispositionem universalem agendorum et applicationem dispositionis ad effectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A15","text":"In angelis conversio et subiectio ad Deum dignior est quam praelatio super inferiores, ex qua illa praelatio derivatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0131","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A16","text":"Distinctio graduum ex natura et gloria permanet, quamvis executio officiorum secundum statum finis mutetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A17","text":"Cognitio inferiorum angelorum a lumine superiorum dependet non solum in acquisitione, sed etiam in conservatione scientiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A18","text":"Homines, manente distinctione naturae, per gratiam ad aequalitatem singulorum graduum angelicorum elevari possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX1","text":"Omnes angeli non sunt una hierarchia ex parte unius modi recipiendi gubernationem, quamvis una sint ex parte unius principis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX2","text":"Unitas speciei et modi intelligendi propria hominibus ad angelos transferri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX3","text":"Ordo qui hierarchiam significat non est idem ac unus gradus intra hierarchiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX4","text":"Communitas donorum spiritualium diversitatem ordinum non excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX5","text":"Ordines caelestes non distinguuntur simpliciter per purgare, illuminare et perficere, quia quilibet angelus haec altiori modo exercere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX6","text":"Angeli eiusdem ordinis non sunt simpliciter aequales, sed tantum secundum similitudinem communem officii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX7","text":"Distinctio hierarchiarum et ordinum neque ex sola natura neque ex sola gratia constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX8","text":"Communitas nominis non impedit eius appropriationem ordini cui propria excellentia vel immediata functio respondet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX9","text":"Participata dominatio angelica singularitatem dominii divini non tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX10","text":"Ordines a praelatione nominati non sunt propter hoc supremi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0131","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX11","text":"Evacuatio ministeriorum post iudicium non est annihilatio ordinum neque abolitio graduum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX12","text":"Assumptio hominum ad ordines angelicos non est conversio naturae humanae in naturam angelicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX13","text":"Daemones non sunt animae defunctorum, quamvis homines mali ad poenam daemonum transferri possint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0173","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX14","text":"Hierarchia divinis personis attribui non potest, quia in eis non sunt purgatio, illuminatio et perfectio unius ab alia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D1","text":"Eadem rationalis societas est una hierarchia secundum principem, sed in hierarchiam humanam et angelicam atque in tres hierarchias angelicas dividitur secundum modos receptionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A2","CH_GGVC__100:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D2","text":"Tres hierarchiae angelicae respondent cognitioni rationum in Deo, in causis creatis universalibus et in causis propriis singulorum effectuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A3","CH_GGVC__100:A4","CH_GGVC__100:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D3","text":"Quaelibet hierarchia tres ordines continet, quia diversitas actuum eius ad summum, medium et infimum reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A6","CH_GGVC__100:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D4","text":"Plures angeli sub uno ordine communi continentur propter similitudinem officii et imperfectionem cognitionis humanae, quamvis inter se inaequales et singulariter ordinati maneant.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A8","CH_GGVC__100:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D5","text":"Perfectio omnibus communis fit nomen proprium ordinis in quo secundum proportionem propriam vel eminentiam determinatam invenitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A8","CH_GGVC__100:A12","CH_GGVC__100:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D6","text":"Prima hierarchia ad finem divinum, secunda ad universalem dispositionem ministeriorum, tertia ad executionem effectuum ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A4","CH_GGVC__100:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D7","text":"Ordinatio Dionysiana ponit Seraphim, Cherubim et Thronos secundum unionem, cognitionem et receptionem divinorum; Dominationes, Virtutes et Potestates secundum definitionem, facultatem et ordinationem agendorum; Principatus, Archangelos et Angelos secundum ductum, mediationem et simplicem executionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A12","CH_GGVC__100:A13","CH_GGVC__100:A14","CH_GGVC__100:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D8","text":"Ordinatio Gregorii, quae Principatus inter Dominationes et Potestates atque Virtutes inter Potestates et Archangelos collocat, a Dionysiana principaliter secundum distributionem nominum ministerialium differt.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A6","CH_GGVC__100:A12","CH_GGVC__100:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D9","text":"Post iudicium cessant officia ordinata ad conducendum creaturas in finem, sed permanent officia pertinentia ad consecutionem finis et ad conservationem illuminationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A16","CH_GGVC__100:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D10","text":"Homines ad ordines angelicos assumuntur secundum gloriam gratuitam, non secundum gradum naturalem, atque cum angelis unam societatem beatam constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A2","CH_GGVC__100:A10","CH_GGVC__100:A11","CH_GGVC__100:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D11","text":"Aequalitas gloriae cum angelis non confert sanctis ordinariam administrationem rerum humanarum, quia munus medium angelorum ex ordine naturae manet, salva dispensatione speciali.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A3","CH_GGVC__100:A10","CH_GGVC__100:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD1","text":"Unitas et pluralitas hierarchiae non sunt praedicata absoluta, sed effectus diversorum respectuum ad principem et ad modum receptionis multitudinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A1","CH_GGVC__100:A2","CH_GGVC__100:A3","CH_GGVC__100:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD2","text":"Ordo angelicus est simul ordo cognitionis, causalitatis et operationis: maior universalitas cognoscendi generat superiorem modum disponendi et communicandi.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A4","CH_GGVC__100:A6","CH_GGVC__100:A8","CH_GGVC__100:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD3","text":"Novem ordines sunt descriptio communis et epistemice contracta realitatis cuius differentiae individuales humana cognitio non perfecte attingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A9","CH_GGVC__100:D3","CH_GGVC__100:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD4","text":"Gradus perfectionis non mensuratur sola possessione boni, sed potestate illud ordinate in inferiores effundendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A8","CH_GGVC__100:A13","CH_GGVC__100:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD5","text":"Consummatio eschatologica mutat modum operationis hierarchicae, non ipsam structuram dependentiae, distinctionis et communicationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A16","CH_GGVC__100:A17","CH_GGVC__100:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD6","text":"Gratia ordinem naturalem in angelis complet secundum capacitatem, in hominibus autem fines eius transcendit sine naturarum confusione.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A10","CH_GGVC__100:A11","CH_GGVC__100:A18","CH_GGVC__100:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX1","text":"Multitudo omnino indifferens hierarchiam constituere non potest, quia unitas sine gradibus confusionem, non ordinem, produceret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX2","text":"Aequalis et immediata receptio illuminationis ab omnibus intellectibus creatis excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX3","text":"Perfectio quae communicari non potest titulum superioris gradus praebere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX4","text":"Nomina communium ordinum non exhauriunt distinctiones reales officiorum angelicorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX5","text":"Gratia nec naturam delet nec ad naturalem capacitatem hominum necessario clauditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX6","text":"Consecutio finis dependentiam cognitionis inferioris a superiori non dissolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX7","text":"Unitas societatis beatae identitatem naturae vel speciei non requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX8","text":"Auctoritatum discrepantia nominalis non cogit ad pluralitatem incompatibilium rerum, si functiones diversis terminis distribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SNX1","text":"Systema possibilitatem universi creati sine mediatione graduum tacite praecludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SNX2","text":"Aequalitas absoluta creaturarum rationalium inadmissibilis est, quia receptionem, cognitionem et communicationem graduum privaret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SNX3","text":"Finis ultimus ut cessatio omnis relationis causalis et illuminationis concipi non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id