t":"Officium proprium uniuscuiusque angeli manet expresse indeterminatum, quia textus ipsum ultra cognitionem humanam ponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT4","text":"Reductio cuiuslibet multitudinis perfectae ad summum, medium et infimum vim generativam magnam habet, sed analogia potius quam demonstratione interna sustentatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT5","text":"Concordia ordinationum Dionysii et Gregorii per aequivalentiam functionum probabiliter construitur, sed differentiam terminologicam non omnino formaliter solvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT6","text":"Disparitas qua gratia angelis secundum naturalia, hominibus autem non eodem modo datur, ex prioribus quaestionibus dependet et hic non ulterius demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT7","text":"Tensionem inter novem ordines communes et proprium ordinem cuiusque angeli solvit distinctio cognitionis communis et perfectae, sed analogia vocabuli ordinis manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT8","text":"Relatio inter assumptionem hominum ad ordines et absentiam ordinariae administrationis angelicae distinguit gloriam ab officio, non tamen omnem correspondentiam inter gradum et ministerium explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0171","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT9","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: ab unitate principii per gradatam mediationem ad permanentiam ordinis et communionem finalem sine confusione naturarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170114364969Z_20ac22db","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 108","source_sha256":"33e5c4fdc63837380034abc4f95a242df9a1b3801c4466d68bd8512a143fc950","sha256":"77123471cfc5f9edc6812e8c5abc2a32345623a02395d0860a7ca6020299bb26","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:01:14.365937+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS1","text":"The question determines by which principles the angelic multitude is distinguished into hierarchies and orders, how these grades are named and ordered, whether they endure, and how human beings are related to them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS2","text":"The unity of hierarchy is taken from one ruler, whereas plurality is taken from the diverse ways in which the multitude receives governance and illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, reconstructive, and distinctive: apparent contradictions are resolved through distinctions of relation, end, causality, and attribution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS4","text":"The movement proceeds from the definition of hierarchy to its division, from hierarchies to orders, from common orders to singular offices, then to the natural and gratuitous foundation of distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS5","text":"The names and grades of the orders are derived from the mode of participation in perfections, from relation to God, and from function in governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS6","text":"The distinction of grades is separated from the execution of offices, so that the permanence of orders may be reconciled with the cessation of certain operations after judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AS7","text":"The conclusion includes human beings in the angelic orders according to the glory of grace, excluding a transmutation of nature and preserving one society of the blessed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A1","text":"A hierarchy is a sacred principate consisting of a ruler and a multitude ordered under him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A2","text":"One God as ruler constitutes one hierarchy of every rational creature capable of sacred things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A3","text":"Diverse modes of receiving governance and illumination constitute diverse hierarchies; human beings receive under sensible likenesses, angels in intelligible purity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A4","text":"The intelligible principles of things are known by angels either in the first universal principle, or in universal created causes, or according to their application to things and proper causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A5","text":"Angelic hierarchies are not distinguished by the mode of seeing the essence of God, but by the mode of knowing the intelligible principles of created things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A6","text":"A hierarchical multitude requires diverse orders according to diverse acts and offices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A7","text":"Every perfect multitude is reduced to highest, middle, and lowest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A8","text":"Spiritual perfections are common to all angels, but are possessed more excellently by those who can communicate them to others more perfectly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A9","text":"Human knowledge comprehends angels in common orders, although according to the perfect distinction of things each angel has a proper office and a proper order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A10","text":"The order of governance is distinguished according to relation to the natural end or to the supernatural end of divine vision and fruition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A11","text":"In angels, gratuitous gifts are proportioned to natural capacity; in human beings, the same proportion is not necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A12","text":"The proper name of an order is taken from the perfection proportioned to its nature, not from a perfection participated deficiently nor from a perfection possessed excessively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A13","text":"The excellence of the lower order is contained in the higher, but the excellence of the higher is not contained in the lower.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A14","text":"Hierarchical process distinguishes consideration of the end, universal disposition of things to be done, and application of the disposition to the effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A15","text":"In angels, conversion and subjection to God is more worthy than prelation over inferiors, from which that prelation is derived.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0131","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A16","text":"The distinction of grades from nature and glory remains, although the execution of offices changes according to the state of the end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A17","text":"The knowledge of lower angels depends on the light of higher angels not only in the acquisition, but also in the preservation, of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:A18","text":"Human beings, while the distinction of nature remains, can be raised by grace to equality with individual angelic grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX1","text":"All angels are not one hierarchy with respect to one mode of receiving governance, although they are one with respect to one ruler.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX2","text":"The unity of species and mode of understanding proper to human beings cannot be transferred to angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX3","text":"An order that signifies a hierarchy is not the same as one grade within a hierarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX4","text":"Community of spiritual gifts does not exclude diversity of orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX5","text":"The heavenly orders are not distinguished simply by purifying, illuminating, and perfecting, because every angel can exercise these in a higher mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX6","text":"Angels of the same order are not simply equal, but only according to the common likeness of office.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX7","text":"The distinction of hierarchies and orders is constituted neither by nature alone nor by grace alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX8","text":"Community of name does not prevent its appropriation to the order to which proper excellence or immediate function corresponds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX9","text":"Participated angelic dominion does not remove the singularity of divine dominion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0097","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX10","text":"Orders named from prelation are not thereby supreme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0131","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX11","text":"The emptying of ministries after judgment is not the annihilation of orders nor the abolition of grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX12","text":"The assumption of human beings into angelic orders is not the conversion of human nature into angelic nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX13","text":"Demons are not the souls of the dead, although evil human beings can be transferred to the punishment of demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0173","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:NX14","text":"Hierarchy cannot be attributed to the divine persons, because in them there is not purification, illumination, and perfection of one by another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D1","text":"The same rational society is one hierarchy according to its ruler, but is divided into a human and an angelic hierarchy and into three angelic hierarchies according to modes of reception.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A2","CH_GGVC__100:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D2","text":"The three angelic hierarchies correspond to knowledge of intelligible principles in God, in universal created causes, and in the proper causes of individual effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A3","CH_GGVC__100:A4","CH_GGVC__100:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D3","text":"Each hierarchy contains three orders, because the diversity of its acts is reduced to highest, middle, and lowest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A6","CH_GGVC__100:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D4","text":"Several angels are contained under one common order on account of likeness of office and the imperfection of human knowledge, although they remain unequal among themselves and singularly ordered.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A8","CH_GGVC__100:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D5","text":"A perfection common to all becomes the proper name of the order in which it is found according to proper proportion or determined eminence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A8","CH_GGVC__100:A12","CH_GGVC__100:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D6","text":"The first hierarchy is ordered to the divine end, the second to the universal disposition of ministries, the third to the execution of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A4","CH_GGVC__100:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D7","text":"The Dionysian ordering places Seraphim, Cherubim, and Thrones according to union, knowledge, and reception of divine things; Dominations, Virtues, and Powers according to the defining, capacity, and ordering of things to be done; Principalities, Archangels, and Angels according to guidance, mediation, and simple execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A12","CH_GGVC__100:A13","CH_GGVC__100:A14","CH_GGVC__100:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D8","text":"The ordering of Gregory, which places Principalities between Dominations and Powers and Virtues between Powers and Archangels, differs from the Dionysian principally according to the distribution of ministerial names.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A6","CH_GGVC__100:A12","CH_GGVC__100:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0137","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D9","text":"After judgment, offices ordered to leading creatures to the end cease, but offices pertaining to the attainment of the end and to the preservation of illumination remain.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A16","CH_GGVC__100:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D10","text":"Human beings are assumed into angelic orders according to gratuitous glory, not according to natural grade, and with angels constitute one blessed society.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A2","CH_GGVC__100:A10","CH_GGVC__100:A11","CH_GGVC__100:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:D11","text":"Equality of glory with angels does not confer upon the saints the ordinary administration of human affairs, because the mediating office of angels remains from the order of nature, without prejudice to special dispensation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A3","CH_GGVC__100:A10","CH_GGVC__100:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD1","text":"The unity and plurality of hierarchy are not absolute predicates, but effects of diverse relations to the ruler and to the mode of reception of the multitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A1","CH_GGVC__100:A2","CH_GGVC__100:A3","CH_GGVC__100:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD2","text":"Angelic order is at once an order of knowledge, causality, and operation: greater universality of knowing generates a higher mode of disposing and communicating.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A4","CH_GGVC__100:A6","CH_GGVC__100:A8","CH_GGVC__100:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD3","text":"The nine orders are a common and epistemically contracted description of a reality whose individual differences human knowledge does not perfectly attain.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A9","CH_GGVC__100:D3","CH_GGVC__100:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD4","text":"A degree of perfection is not measured by possession of a good alone, but by the power to pour it forth in an ordered manner upon inferiors.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A8","CH_GGVC__100:A13","CH_GGVC__100:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD5","text":"Eschatological consummation changes the mode of hierarchical operation, not the very structure of dependence, distinction, and communication.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A16","CH_GGVC__100:A17","CH_GGVC__100:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SD6","text":"Grace completes the natural order in angels according to capacity, but in human beings transcends its limits without confusion of natures.","refs":["CH_GGVC__100:A10","CH_GGVC__100:A11","CH_GGVC__100:A18","CH_GGVC__100:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX1","text":"A multitude wholly undifferentiated cannot constitute a hierarchy, because unity without grades would produce confusion, not order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX2","text":"Equal and immediate reception of illumination by all created intellects is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX3","text":"A perfection that cannot be communicated cannot furnish the title of a higher grade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX4","text":"The names of common orders do not exhaust the real distinctions of angelic offices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX5","text":"Grace neither destroys nature nor is necessarily confined to the natural capacity of human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX6","text":"Attainment of the end does not dissolve the dependence of lower knowledge on higher knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX7","text":"The unity of the blessed society does not require identity of nature or species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:DNX8","text":"Nominal discrepancy among authorities does not compel a plurality of incompatible things, if functions are distributed by diverse terms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SNX1","text":"The system tacitly precludes the possibility of a created universe without mediation of grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SNX2","text":"The absolute equality of rational creatures is inadmissible, because it would deprive reception, knowledge, and communication of grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SNX3","text":"The ultimate end cannot be conceived as the cessation of every causal relation and illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0155","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SNX4","text":"Exhaustive human knowledge of the angelic order remains unavailable; the schema of nine orders is the limit of common knowledge, not the full measure of the thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:SNX5","text":"The communion of human beings and angels through confusion of natures is impossible; only unity of end and glory permits passage between grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS1","text":"Consideration of the ruler leads from one God to one rational hierarchy: one ruler → one sacred society.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS2","text":"Consideration of the multitude introduces division: diverse modes of reception → human and angelic hierarchy → three angelic hierarchies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS3","text":"The necessity of order generates an internal tripartition: a non-confused multitude → diverse acts and offices → highest, middle, and lowest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS4","text":"Grades and names are produced from the communication of perfection: common perfection → unequal possession → communicative excess → appropriation of a name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS5","text":"The structure of the nine orders follows from the causality of operation: end → universal disposition → execution; in each stratum again highest → middle → lowest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS6","text":"The limits of taxonomy arise from the limit of knowledge: common human knowledge → common orders → concealment of the proper office of each angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS7","text":"The structure of orders is constituted from a twofold end: nature disposes → grace completes → glory consummates the grade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS8","text":"Consummation distinguishes the substance of order from wayfaring operation: end attained → cessation of leading → permanence of grades and preservative illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:FGS9","text":"The inclusion of human beings proceeds without transmutation: distinct nature → grace not proportioned to nature → equality of glory → one blessed society.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AF1","text":"Definition of hierarchy → distinction of ruler and multitude → three modes of angelic knowledge → three hierarchies → three orders in each → natural and gratuitous foundation → appropriation of names → ordering of nine grades → eschatological permanence → assumption of human beings according to glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:AF2","text":"Objection from the appearance of unity or contradiction → distinction of relations and modes of attribution → limited concession → restoration of multiform order under one principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME1","text":"The unity and plurality of hierarchy are transferred from contradictory opposition into a distinction according to relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME2","text":"Hierarchy is reclassified from a mere scale of dignities into a structure of reception, communication, and causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME3","text":"The exclusive opposition of nature and grace collapses; nature disposes, grace completes, and in human beings transcends natural proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME4","text":"The names of orders no longer signify exclusive possession of perfections, but their proper, excessive, or participated mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME5","text":"The three hierarchies become a chart of descent from intelligible principles in God to universal causes and thence to singular effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME6","text":"The nine orders become a functional series from conversion to God through universal disposition to particular execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME7","text":"The state after judgment is no longer described as an abolition of order, but as a transformation of office from leading to consummation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME8","text":"The assumption of human beings is transferred from a change of species to equality of glory within one blessed society.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ME9","text":"Angelic taxonomy is rendered visible as common and non-exhaustive knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ALT1","text":"The surface level contains the distinction of three hierarchies, nine orders, names, grades, duration, and the inclusion of human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ALT2","text":"The structural level orders modes of illumination, offices, communication of perfections, and mediation from universal causes to particular effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0153","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level resolves contradictions through variation of relation, analogy of names, distinction of grades from offices, and reconciliation of functions in Dionysius and Gregory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0122","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0137","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level presupposes the distinction of nature and grace, final causality, the permanence of grades, and the change of operations between the state of the way and consummation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the division of hierarchies, orders, names, grades, duration, and the assumption of human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT2","text":"The structure is firmest in the distinctions of ruler and multitude, nature and grace, grade and execution of office.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT3","text":"The proper office of each angel remains expressly indeterminate, because the text places it beyond human knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT4","text":"The reduction of every perfect multitude to highest, middle, and lowest has great generative force, but is supported by analogy rather than internal demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT5","text":"The concord of the orderings of Dionysius and Gregory is probably constructed through equivalence of functions, but does not altogether formally resolve terminological difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0122","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0137","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT6","text":"The disparity whereby grace is given to angels according to natural things, but not in the same manner to human beings, depends on prior questions and is not further demonstrated here.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0169","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT7","text":"The tension between nine common orders and the proper order of each angel is resolved by the distinction of common and perfect knowledge, but the analogy of the term order remains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0053","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT8","text":"The relation between the assumption of human beings into orders and the absence of ordinary angelic administration distinguishes glory from office, but does not explain every correspondence between grade and ministry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0171","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__100:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: from the unity of the principle through graded mediation to the permanence of order and final communion without confusion of natures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0148","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__100:P0167","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__100@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__100:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 109","title":"First Part · Question 108","context":"Chapter 109","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 108"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 108","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 109","order":110,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__101"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__101@R001","sha256":"77c63b150212cae397ded3ac58deb8278334e150066ac2a1a9f0419619b08906","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat utrum malitia daemonum ordinem, praelationem, illuminationem et subiectionem ad Angelos bonos destruat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS2","text":"Argumentatio ordinem angelicum dividit secundum naturam, gratiam imperfectam et gloriam consummatam, ut damnum morale a permanenti dispositione naturali separet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS3","text":"Ex permanenti gradu naturae sequitur subordinatio actionum daemonicarum et igitur praelatio interna, quamvis voluntates daemonum sint perversae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS4","text":"Manifestatio conceptus inter daemones possibilis manet, sed illuminatio proprie dicta negatur, quia illuminationem constituit ordinatio veritatis ad Deum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS5","text":"Praelatio bonorum Angelorum super malos non ex gradu naturae, sed ex propinquitate ad Deum et participatione divinae iustitiae derivatur; inde malum permittitur, non tamen extra regimen relinquitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A1","text":"Ordo angelicus secundum naturam, gratiam imperfectam et gloriam consummatam formaliter distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A2","text":"Malum sine aliquo bono esse non potest; natura bona daemonum post lapsum manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A3","text":"Gradus naturae inter daemones inaequales permanent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A4","text":"Cum actio naturam sequatur, ordinatio naturarum ordinat actiones earum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A5","text":"Praelatio consistit in subordinatione actionis subditi actioni praelati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A6","text":"Ordo daemonum a divina iustitia ordinante fundatur, non a iustitia vel amicitia daemonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A7","text":"Obedientia daemonica ex communi nequitia et recognitione maioris virtutis procedere potest sine concordia caritatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A8","text":"Illuminatio proprie est manifestatio veritatis quae intellectum ad Deum ordinat et purgationem ac perfectionem importat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A9","text":"Manifestatio conceptus sine ordinatione ad Deum locutio est, non illuminatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A10","text":"Cognitio naturalis Angelorum et daemonum ab initio conditionis completa est quantum ad sua naturalia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A11","text":"Omnis praelatio originaliter in Deo consistit et creaturis secundum perfectionem atque propinquitatem ad Deum participatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A12","text":"Fruitio Dei est maxima perfectio creaturae rationalis, qua boni Angeli pollent et daemones privantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A13","text":"Virtus divinae iustitiae, cui boni Angeli inhaerent, virtutem naturalem daemonum excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A14","text":"Regimen divinum mala permittere potest propter bona ex eis elicienda, sine eo quod malum a regimine subtrahatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX1","text":"Daemones non sunt in ordinibus angelicis secundum gloriam consummatam, nec umquam in eis fuerunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX2","text":"Ordinatio daemonum ex parte voluntatis eorum sacra non est, quia naturam suam ad malum abutuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX3","text":"Nomina Seraphim, Thronorum et Dominationum daemonibus non competunt, quia caritatem, inhabitationem divinam et libertatem a peccato significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX4","text":"Praelatio daemonica non est iusta secundum propriam voluntatem nec fundatur in mutua amicitia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX5","text":"Subiectio daemonum non identica est servituti humanae post peccatum, quia daemonum inaequalitas naturalis praecedit eius operationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX6","text":"Quaelibet manifestatio veritatis vel superioritas luminis naturalis illuminationem non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX7","text":"Praelatio bonorum Angelorum non significat quod daemones a malefaciendo omnino cohibeantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D1","text":"Daemones simul extra ordinem gloriae et intra ordinem naturae collocantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A1","CH_GGVC__101:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D2","text":"Ordo daemonicus realis est, sed eius realitas naturalis non transfertur in dignitatem sacram vel gloriosam.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A1","CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D3","text":"Praelatio inter daemones necessario sequitur gradus naturales et subordinationem actionum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A3","CH_GGVC__101:A4","CH_GGVC__101:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D4","text":"Unitas operationis daemonicae est cooperatio instrumentalis ad malum, non communio finis boni.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A6","CH_GGVC__101:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D5","text":"Maior scientia naturalis daemonis superioris communicationem efficere potest, sed non actum illuminativum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9","CH_GGVC__101:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D6","text":"Revelatio divinorum mysteriorum daemonibus facta potest esse illuminatio ex parte Angeli revelantis, non ex parte daemonis recipientis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D7","text":"Angelus bonus naturaliter inferior daemonem naturaliter superiorem regere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A12","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D8","text":"Permissio actionis daemonicae intra regimen bonorum Angelorum negligentiam eorum non inducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SD1","text":"Malum daemonicum non constituit ordinem autonomum: naturam bonam retinet, ordinationem externam patitur, et fines perversos intra regimen divinum exsequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A6","CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SD2","text":"Duplex hierarchia distinguitur: gradus naturae explicat praelationem daemonum inter se, gradus propinquitatis ad Deum explicat praelationem bonorum Angelorum super daemones.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A3","CH_GGVC__101:A5","CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SD3","text":"Cognitio non efficit perfectionem spiritualem per se, quia eius species formalis a fine ad quem communicatur pendet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9","CH_GGVC__101:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SD4","text":"Regimen bonum non per abolitionem omnium malorum, sed per subiectionem et ordinationem malorum ad fines superiores definitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A13","CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX1","text":"Malum non potest esse principium subsistens et omnino inordinatum, quia daemonum malitia naturam bonam atque ordinem divinum praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX2","text":"Potestas naturalis non est ultima regula praelationis, quia perfectio in Deo fundata naturalem excellentiam superare potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A12","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX3","text":"Transmissio veri non est neutra secundum rationem spiritualem, quia veritas sine conversione ad Deum illuminationis nomen non recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX4","text":"Ordo socialis sine caritate vel iustitia propria potest operari, sed tantum ut ordinatio coacta vel instrumentalis ad finem perversum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A5","CH_GGVC__101:A6","CH_GGVC__101:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX5","text":"Providentia non identificatur cum immediata immunitate bonorum a malo, quia permissio mali ad bonum eliciendum eius operationem includit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SNX1","text":"Casus voluntatis creaturam a gloria et illuminatione excludere potest, sed naturam, cognitionem naturalem et ordinabilitatem eius non annihilat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A1","CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SNX2","text":"Nulla creatura vel potestas naturalis extra ordinem originarium Dei constitui potest, etiam cum voluntarie ordini divino repugnat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A6","CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SNX3","text":"Vera superioritas non per dominationem effectivam aut scientiam maiorem, sed per participationem finis divini mensuratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS1","text":"Distinctio naturae / gratiae imperfectae / gloriae → separatio eorum quae lapsus tollit ab iis quae relinquit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS2","text":"Natura bona retenta + inaequalitas naturalis → ordinatio actionum → praelatio daemonum interna.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A3","CH_GGVC__101:A4","CH_GGVC__101:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS3","text":"Voluntas a Deo aversa + definitio finalis illuminationis → communicatio conceptus sine illuminatione.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS4","text":"Praelatio a Deo originaliter procedens + maior propinquitas bonorum Angelorum ad Deum → regimen bonorum Angelorum super daemones.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A12","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS5","text":"Regimen divinum + permissio mali propter bona elicita → actio daemonica manet nociva, sed non extra ordinationem providentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AF1","text":"Malitia daemonum → distinctio naturae et gloriae → ordo naturalis residuus → praelatio daemonica interna.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AF2","text":"Manifestatio veri → examen finis manifestationis → locutio daemonica sine illuminatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AF3","text":"Inaequalitas naturalis → insufficiens ratio supremae praelationis → propinquitas ad Deum → regimen bonorum Angelorum → permissio ordinata mali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME1","text":"Ordo dividitur in ordinem naturalem, ordinem gratiae et ordinem gloriae, ita ut lapsus non aequaliter omnia genera ordinis deleat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME2","text":"Praelatio reclassificatur ut subordinatio actionum, quae potest subsistere sine iustitia voluntatis, caritate vel concordia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter scientiam et ignorantiam substituitur distinctione inter cognitionem communicabilem et veritatem illuminativam ad Deum ordinatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME4","text":"Excellentia naturalis et auctoritas spiritualis separantur, ut inferior natura bonus Angelus superiori natura daemoni praeesse possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME5","text":"Regimen mali non per simplicem prohibitionem, sed per permissionem, subiectionem et conversionem effectuum ad fines superiores intellegitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ALT1","text":"Surface — Daemones ordines et praelationem internam habent, non illuminant proprie, et bonis Angelis subiiciuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ALT2","text":"Structural — Naturae inaequalitas actiones hierarchizat, dum iustitia divina ordinem daemonum continet sine consensu morali daemonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Termini ordinis, praelationis et illuminationis a nudis proprietatibus descriptivis ad relationem finis, Dei et providentiae transferuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Lapsus gratiam imperfectam et gloriam excludit, sed data naturalia remanere facit; creatura igitur simul corrupta secundum voluntatem et ordinabilis secundum naturam manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad quattuor conclusiones si distinctio naturae, gratiae et gloriae tamquam cardo totius systematis retinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT2","text":"Firmitas maxima systematis in transitu ab inaequalitate naturali ad subordinationem actionum consistit, quo praelatio daemonica sine iustitia daemonum explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT3","text":"Definitio illuminationis per ordinationem ad Deum efficaciter separat locutionem a perfectione spirituali, sed statum revelationis receptae a fine voluntatis recipientis dependere facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT4","text":"Tensio ordinata manet inter praelationem daemonum ex natura et praelationem bonorum Angelorum ex iustitia divina; textus eam per duos ordines normativos distinguit, sed mensuram concretam inter eos non explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT5","text":"Concordia daemonum negatur, sed obedientia operationalis affirmatur; communis nequitia et maior virtus mechanismum proximum praebent, quamvis stabilitas huius coordinationis ulterius non determinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT6","text":"Permissio mali necessitatem exclusionis negligentiae solvit, sed ratio cur haec vel illa actio daemonica permittatur ad generale principium boni eliciendi reducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: malum non simpliciter inordinationem producit, sed distinctionem graduum ordinis exigit, ex qua subiectio finalis daemonum derivatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170139523859Z_a63138ce","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 109","source_sha256":"77c63b150212cae397ded3ac58deb8278334e150066ac2a1a9f0419619b08906","sha256":"42c95b42fb4c59c54c079e37d72a6363f828f20fc737d4c7b2ce5ead092f9cf8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:01:39.524887+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS1","text":"The question examines whether the malice of the demons destroys order, prelation, illumination, and subjection to the good Angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS2","text":"The argument divides angelic order according to nature, imperfect grace, and consummated glory, so as to separate moral damage from enduring natural disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS3","text":"From the enduring grade of nature follows the subordination of demonic actions and thus internal prelation, although the wills of the demons are perverse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS4","text":"The manifestation of a concept among demons remains possible, but illumination properly so called is denied, because illumination is constituted by the ordering of truth to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AS5","text":"The prelation of good Angels over the wicked derives not from a grade of nature, but from proximity to God and participation in divine justice; hence evil is permitted, yet not left outside governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A1","text":"Angelic order is formally distinguished according to nature, imperfect grace, and consummated glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A2","text":"Evil cannot exist without some good; the good nature of the demons remains after the fall.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A3","text":"The grades of nature among demons remain unequal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A4","text":"Since action follows nature, the ordering of natures orders their actions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A5","text":"Prelation consists in the subordination of the action of the subject to the action of the superior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A6","text":"The order of demons is founded on divine justice as ordering, not on the justice or friendship of the demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A7","text":"Demonic obedience can proceed from common wickedness and recognition of greater power without concord of charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A8","text":"Illumination properly is the manifestation of truth that orders the intellect to God and entails purification and perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A9","text":"The manifestation of a concept without ordering to God is speech, not illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A10","text":"The natural knowledge of Angels and demons was complete from the beginning of their condition as regards their natural endowments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A11","text":"All prelation originally consists in God and is participated by creatures according to perfection and proximity to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A12","text":"The enjoyment of God is the greatest perfection of the rational creature, possessed by the good Angels and lacking to the demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A13","text":"The power of divine justice, to which the good Angels adhere, exceeds the natural power of the demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:A14","text":"Divine governance can permit evils for the sake of goods to be drawn from them, without evil thereby being withdrawn from governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX1","text":"Demons are not in the angelic orders according to consummated glory, nor were they ever in them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX2","text":"The ordering of demons on the part of their will is not sacred, because they abuse their nature for evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX3","text":"The names Seraphim, Thrones, and Dominations do not belong to demons, because they signify charity, divine indwelling, and freedom from sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX4","text":"Demonic prelation is not just according to its own will, nor is it founded in mutual friendship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX5","text":"The subjection of demons is not identical with human servitude after sin, because the natural inequality of demons precedes its operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX6","text":"Not every manifestation of truth or superiority of natural light constitutes illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:NX7","text":"The prelation of good Angels does not signify that demons are altogether restrained from doing evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D1","text":"Demons are situated at once outside the order of glory and within the order of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A1","CH_GGVC__101:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D2","text":"Demonic order is real, but its natural reality is not transferred into sacred or glorious dignity.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A1","CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D3","text":"Prelation among demons necessarily follows natural grades and the subordination of actions.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A3","CH_GGVC__101:A4","CH_GGVC__101:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D4","text":"The unity of demonic operation is instrumental cooperation toward evil, not communion in a good end.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A6","CH_GGVC__101:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D5","text":"The greater natural knowledge of a superior demon can effect communication, but not an illuminative act.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9","CH_GGVC__101:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D6","text":"The revelation of divine mysteries made to demons can be illumination on the part of the revealing Angel, not on the part of the receiving demon.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D7","text":"A good Angel naturally inferior can govern a demon naturally superior.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A12","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:D8","text":"Permission of demonic action within the governance of good Angels does not entail their negligence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SD1","text":"Demonic evil does not constitute an autonomous order: it retains good nature, undergoes external ordering, and carries out perverse ends within divine governance.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A6","CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SD2","text":"A twofold hierarchy is distinguished: the grade of nature explains the prelation of demons among themselves, while the grade of proximity to God explains the prelation of good Angels over demons.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A3","CH_GGVC__101:A5","CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SD3","text":"Knowledge does not of itself effect spiritual perfection, because its formal species depends on the end for which it is communicated.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9","CH_GGVC__101:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SD4","text":"Good governance is defined not by the abolition of all evils, but by the subjection and ordering of evils to higher ends.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A13","CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX1","text":"Evil cannot be a subsisting and utterly disordered principle, because the malice of demons presupposes good nature and divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX2","text":"Natural power is not the ultimate rule of prelation, because perfection founded in God can surpass natural excellence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A12","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX3","text":"The transmission of truth is not neutral in spiritual respect, because truth without conversion to God does not receive the name of illumination.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX4","text":"A social order without charity or proper justice can operate, but only as a compelled or instrumental ordering toward a perverse end.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A5","CH_GGVC__101:A6","CH_GGVC__101:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:DNX5","text":"Providence is not identified with the immediate immunity of the good from evil, because its operation includes the permission of evil in order that good may be drawn from it.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SNX1","text":"The fall of the will can exclude a creature from glory and illumination, but does not annihilate its nature, natural knowledge, and capacity for ordering.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A1","CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SNX2","text":"No creature or natural power can be constituted outside the original order of God, even when it voluntarily resists divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A6","CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:SNX3","text":"True superiority is measured not by effective domination or greater knowledge, but by participation in the divine end.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS1","text":"Distinction of nature / imperfect grace / glory → separation of what the fall removes from what it leaves behind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS2","text":"Retained good nature + natural inequality → ordering of actions → internal prelation of demons.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A2","CH_GGVC__101:A3","CH_GGVC__101:A4","CH_GGVC__101:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS3","text":"Will turned away from God + final definition of illumination → communication of a concept without illumination.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A8","CH_GGVC__101:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS4","text":"Prelation originally proceeding from God + greater proximity of good Angels to God → governance of good Angels over demons.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A11","CH_GGVC__101:A12","CH_GGVC__101:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:FGS5","text":"Divine governance + permission of evil for the sake of goods drawn forth → demonic action remains harmful, but not outside the ordering of providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__101:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AF1","text":"Malice of demons → distinction of nature and glory → residual natural order → internal demonic prelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AF2","text":"Manifestation of truth → examination of the end of manifestation → demonic speech without illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:AF3","text":"Natural inequality → insufficient ground of supreme prelation → proximity to God → governance of good Angels → ordered permission of evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME1","text":"Order is divided into natural order, order of grace, and order of glory, so that the fall does not equally destroy every kind of order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME2","text":"Prelation is reclassified as the subordination of actions, which can subsist without justice of will, charity, or concord.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME3","text":"The opposition between knowledge and ignorance is replaced by the distinction between communicable knowledge and illuminative truth ordered to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME4","text":"Natural excellence and spiritual authority are separated, so that a good Angel inferior in nature can preside over a demon superior in nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ME5","text":"The governance of evil is understood not through simple prohibition, but through permission, subjection, and the conversion of effects to higher ends.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ALT1","text":"Surface — Demons have orders and internal prelation, do not properly illuminate, and are subjected to good Angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ALT2","text":"Structural — The inequality of natures hierarchizes actions, while divine justice contains the order of demons without the moral consent of demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The terms order, prelation, and illumination are transferred from bare descriptive properties to the relation of end, God, and providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The fall excludes imperfect grace and glory, but leaves natural endowments remaining; therefore the creature remains at once corrupted according to the will and orderable according to nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice for the four conclusions if the distinction of nature, grace, and glory is retained as the hinge of the whole system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT2","text":"The system's greatest strength consists in the transition from natural inequality to the subordination of actions, by which demonic prelation is explained without the justice of demons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT3","text":"The definition of illumination through ordering to God effectively separates speech from spiritual perfection, but makes the status of received revelation depend on the end of the recipient's will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT4","text":"An ordered tension remains between the prelation of demons from nature and the prelation of good Angels from divine justice; the text distinguishes it through two normative orders, but does not explain the concrete measure between them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT5","text":"Concord among demons is denied, but operational obedience is affirmed; common wickedness and greater power provide the proximate mechanism, although the stability of this coordination is not further determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT6","text":"The permission of evil resolves the need to exclude negligence, but the reason why this or that demonic action is permitted is reduced to the general principle of drawing forth good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__101:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: evil does not simply produce disorder, but requires a distinction of grades of order, from which the final subjection of demons is derived.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__101:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__101@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__101:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 110","title":"First Part · Question 109","context":"Chapter 110","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 109"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 109","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 110","order":111,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__102"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__102@R001","sha256":"e52dfd949e1b70d49974dd2bd0e638baa9c37e14ea5ab43e57b498083063daa5","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat utrum gubernatio angelica creaturas corporales regat, et quos limites habeat in informatione materiae, motu locali et productione miraculorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS2","text":"Textus affirmat corporalia spiritualibus substantiis gubernari, quia virtus corporalis particularis est et ad hic et nunc contracta, spiritualis autem universalior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS3","text":"Gubernatio angelica non transfert Angelis potestatem immediate formandi materiam, quia forma non est res per se facta, sed principium quo compositum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS4","text":"Potestas angelica immediate ad motum localem extenditur et mediate effectus corporales ordinare potest per agentes corporales et semina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS5","text":"Miraculum redefinitur ut effectus praeter ordinem totius naturae creatae; hac definitione sola causalitas divina miraculi proprie capax manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS6","text":"Motus argumenti procedit a superioritate spiritualis naturae ad partitionem causarum: gubernatio universalis → exclusio informationis immediatae → admissio motus localis → clausura divina miraculi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A1","text":"Potestas particularis a potestate universaliori gubernatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A2","text":"Virtus formae corporalis est individuata per materiam et determinata ad hic et nunc.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A3","text":"Virtus substantiae spiritualis est universalior quam virtus corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A4","text":"Corpus non agit nisi motum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A5","text":"Forma non est ens subsistens quod proprie fiat, sed id quo compositum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A6","text":"Proprie fit compositum, cuius fieri est via in esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A7","text":"Agens naturale producit effectum sibi similem, sive ut compositum sive ut virtute continens compositum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A8","text":"Deus solus virtute sua materiam et formam compositi universaliter comprehendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A9","text":"Informatio materiae procedit immediate aut a Deo aut ab agente corporali, non ab Angelo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A10","text":"Motus localis est perfectior motus corporeus, quia mobile secundum locum solum ad extrinsecum ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A11","text":"Natura corporalis immediate a natura spirituali secundum locum moveri potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A12","text":"Quidquid creatura propria virtute facit, intra ordinem totius naturae creatae fit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A13","text":"Miraculum proprie est effectus praeter ordinem totius naturae creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX1","text":"Actiones corporales determinatae non constituunt autonomiam corporalem a motu spirituali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX2","text":"Praesidentia angelica non est immediata productio formarum substantialium in materia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX3","text":"Superioritas virtutis non importat facultatem efficiendi eodem modo quod inferior virtus efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX4","text":"Corpus administratum non est instrumentum quod ad nutum Angeli substantialiter informatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX5","text":"Motus localis non requirit causalitatem formae substantialis neque unionem vitalem moventis cum moto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX6","text":"Effectus praeter ordinem naturae particularis non est propter hoc miraculum simpliciter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX7","text":"Opera Angelorum et Daemonum, etiam insolita, non excedunt ordinem totius creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX8","text":"Diversitas rectorum corporalium non multiplicat ordines angelicos secundum numerum specierum corporalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D1","text":"Administratio angelica corporum sequitur ex disproportionibus universalitatis inter virtutem spiritualem et corporalem, non ex indigentia corporis ad novas naturas accipiendas.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A1","CH_GGVC__102:A2","CH_GGVC__102:A3","CH_GGVC__102:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D2","text":"Angelus effectus corporales extraordinarios disponere potest movendo agentes corporales, quamvis materiam ad formam substantialem immediate non reducat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A7","CH_GGVC__102:A9","CH_GGVC__102:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D3","text":"Motus localis est locus immediatus causalitatis angelicae, quia non exigit transformationem intrinsecam materiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A10","CH_GGVC__102:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D4","text":"Semina corporalia a potestatibus spiritualibus localiter applicata effectus visibiles producere possunt sine creatione novae causalitatis naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A7","CH_GGVC__102:A11","CH_GGVC__102:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D5","text":"Prodigia daemonica miracula dicuntur quoad nos, cum causae creatae ignotae effectum praeter ordinem naturae nobis notae producunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A12","CH_GGVC__102:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D6","text":"Angeli miracula facere dicuntur improprie, vel quia Deus ad eorum desiderium operatur vel quia ministerium in opere divino exhibent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A12","CH_GGVC__102:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D7","text":"Praesidentia particularis super res corporales distribuitur ex ordine sapientiae divinae, dum ordines angelici secundum officia generalia manent distincti.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A1","CH_GGVC__102:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SD1","text":"Systema causale dividitur inter gubernationem angelicam, quae motus et dispositiones ordinat, et causalitatem divinam, quae fundamentum compositi et exceptionem ab ordine creato servat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:D1","CH_GGVC__102:D2","CH_GGVC__102:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SD2","text":"Miraculum non per raritatem, admirationem vel interruptionem causalitatis particularis, sed per relationem ad totalitatem naturae creatae classificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:D5","CH_GGVC__102:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SD3","text":"Superioritas angelica non destruit causalitatem corporalem, sed eam subordinat et instrumentaliter componit ad effectus quos corpus solum non attingeret.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:D2","CH_GGVC__102:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SD4","text":"Ordo universi simul admittit multitudinem rectorum particularium et recusat fragmentationem hierarchiae angelicae in tot ordines quot sunt res corporales.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:D7","CH_GGVC__102:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX1","text":"Causalitas non ordinatur per scalam simplicem qua omnis virtus superior omnia inferioris opera eodem modo efficere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX2","text":"Natura corporalis non est machinamentum sibi sufficiens, quod ex formis propriis sine motu superiori integritatem operationis consequatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX3","text":"Spiritus creatus non est demiurgus qui materiam ex seipso immediate informat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX4","text":"Anomalia sensibilis non est signum sufficiens transcendentiae causalitatis creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX5","text":"Potestas spiritualis creata nullam positionem extra totalem ordinem creaturae occupare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SNX1","text":"Nulla creatura sibi vindicare potest actum qui ordinem totius creaturae suspendat, quia talis exceptio causalitatem creatam ut totalitatem transcenderet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SNX2","text":"Invisibilitas causae non transfert effectum ex ordine naturae in ordinem miraculi simpliciter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SNX3","text":"Gubernatio universi non admittit oppositionem inter naturam et spiritum tamquam duas causalitates coordinate et independenter agentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SNX4","text":"Ordo divinus non reducitur ad seriem contractuum privatorum inter creaturas, sed universum sicut lex publica ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS1","text":"Universalitas spiritualis + particularitas corporalis → necessitas gubernationis spiritualis corporum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS2","text":"Distinctio compositi a forma + similitudo agentis et facti → exclusio informationis immediatae materiae ab Angelo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS3","text":"Exterioritas motus localis + superioritas naturae spiritualis → admissio motus localis angelici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS4","text":"Motus localis angelicus + applicatio seminum et agentium corporalium → effectus naturales insoliti sine transgressione ordinis creati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS5","text":"Definitio miraculi per ordinem totius naturae creatae + inclusio omnis virtutis creaturae in illo ordine → exclusivitas divina miraculi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS6","text":"Ignorantia ordinis causalis creati → miraculum quoad nos, non miraculum simpliciter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF1","text":"Determinatio actionum corporalium → dependentia corporis a motu → praesidentia angelica universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF2","text":"Praesidentia angelica → distinctio gubernationis ab informatione → negatio potestatis angelicae formalis immediatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF3","text":"Negatio informationis → identificatio motus localis ut motus extrinsecus perfectior → potestas angelica localiter movendi corpora.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF4","text":"Effectus insoliti per causas creatas → distinctio ordinis ignoti ab ordine universali → reclassificatio prodigiorum daemonum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF5","text":"Miraculum praeter ordinem totius creaturae → impossibilitas exceptionis creatae → Deus solus facit miracula proprie dicta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME1","text":"Gubernatio corporum distinguitur a productione formarum: administrare non idem est substantialiter informare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME2","text":"Causalitas angelica relocatur ab origine formarum ad motum localem, dispositionem agentium et applicationem seminum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME3","text":"Miraculum transfertur ex categoria effectus insoliti in categoria exceptionis ab ordine universali naturae creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME4","text":"Prodigium daemonicum classificatur ut effectus causae creatae ignotae, non ut rivalis causalitas divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME5","text":"Relatio inter Angelos et corpora describitur ut subordinatio hierarchica universalis, non ut correspondentia naturalis fixa unius spiritus ad unam speciem corporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus determinat utrum Angeli corpora administrent, materiam transmutent, localiter moveant et miracula faciant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT2","text":"Structural — Systema distribuit causalitatem inter Deum, Angelos, agentes corporales, semina et ordinem universi creati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio dissolvit transitum illicitum a superioritate angelica ad omnipotentiam angelicam per distinctiones modi causalitatis et amplitudinis ordinis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Compositum, non forma separata, est subiectum generationis; motus localis, quia ad extrinsecum ordinatur, constituit punctum contactus immediati inter spirituale et corporale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT5","text":"Epistemic — Quod praeter naturam nobis notam accidit potest videri miraculosum, quamvis intra causas creatas et ordinem universi maneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam conclusionem principalem: corpora ab Angelis gubernantur, sed non immediate ad formas substantialiter informandas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter informationem materiae et motum localem est commissura decisiva quae simul negat potentiam formalem et concedit efficaciam angelicam corporalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT3","text":"Systema interne cohaeret si gubernatio intelligitur ut subordinatio motiva et dispositiva, non ut causalitas creatrix aut formalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT4","text":"Firmissimum nexus est definitio miraculi per ordinem totius naturae creatae, quia ex ea immediate sequitur exclusivitas divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet transitus ab universalitate virtutis spiritualis ad necessitatem praesidentiae angelicae immediatae super corpora inferiora, qui plus hierarchiam metaphysicam quam mechanismum determinatum explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT6","text":"Tensio residua inter pluralitatem rectorum particularium et paucitatem ordinum generalium solvitur per distinctionem inter distributionem sapientiae divinae et differentiam officiorum genericorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus, quia ab affirmatione gubernationis per restrictionem causalitatis angelicae ad clausuram miraculi in sola causalitate divina progreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170203825223Z_c42d230c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 110","source_sha256":"e52dfd949e1b70d49974dd2bd0e638baa9c37e14ea5ab43e57b498083063daa5","sha256":"0206623b0b1a0b1d0f306c6d2c82004c6cb17fa6c4d82256a6549805c48e3e79","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:02:03.826236+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS1","text":"The question examines whether angelic governance rules corporeal creatures, and what limits it has regarding the informing of matter, local motion, and the production of miracles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS2","text":"The text affirms that corporeal things are governed by spiritual substances, because corporeal power is particular and contracted to the here and now, whereas spiritual power is more universal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS3","text":"Angelic governance does not confer upon Angels the power immediately to form matter, because form is not a thing made per se, but the principle by which the composite exists.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS4","text":"Angelic power extends immediately to local motion and can mediately order corporeal effects through corporeal agents and seeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS5","text":"A miracle is redefined as an effect beyond the order of the whole of created nature; under this definition, divine causality alone remains properly capable of miracle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AS6","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from the superiority of spiritual nature to a partition of causes: universal governance → exclusion of immediate informing → admission of local motion → divine closure of miracle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A1","text":"Particular power is governed by more universal power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A2","text":"The power of corporeal form is individuated by matter and determined to the here and now.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A3","text":"The power of spiritual substance is more universal than the power of a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A4","text":"A body acts only when moved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A5","text":"Form is not a subsisting being that is properly made, but that by which the composite exists.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A6","text":"Properly speaking, it is the composite that is made, whose coming-to-be is a way into being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A7","text":"A natural agent produces an effect like itself, either as a composite or as containing the composite virtually.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A8","text":"God alone, by His power, universally comprehends the matter and form of the composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A9","text":"The informing of matter proceeds immediately either from God or from a corporeal agent, not from an Angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A10","text":"Local motion is the more perfect corporeal motion, because what is movable according to place is ordered only to an extrinsic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A11","text":"Corporeal nature can be moved locally immediately by spiritual nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A12","text":"Whatever a creature does by its own power occurs within the order of the whole of created nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:A13","text":"A miracle properly is an effect beyond the order of the whole of created nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX1","text":"Determinate corporeal actions do not constitute corporeal autonomy from spiritual motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX2","text":"Angelic presidency is not the immediate production of substantial forms in matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX3","text":"Superiority of power does not entail the capacity to effect in the same manner what an inferior power effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX4","text":"A governed body is not an instrument that is substantially informed at the Angel's command.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX5","text":"Local motion does not require the causality of substantial form or a vital union of mover with moved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX6","text":"An effect beyond the order of particular nature is not thereby a miracle simply speaking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX7","text":"The works of Angels and Demons, even unusual ones, do not exceed the order of the whole of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:NX8","text":"The diversity of corporeal rulers does not multiply angelic orders according to the number of corporeal species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D1","text":"Angelic administration of bodies follows from disparities of universality between spiritual and corporeal power, not from a body's need to receive new natures.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A1","CH_GGVC__102:A2","CH_GGVC__102:A3","CH_GGVC__102:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D2","text":"An Angel can dispose extraordinary corporeal effects by moving corporeal agents, although it does not immediately reduce matter to substantial form.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A7","CH_GGVC__102:A9","CH_GGVC__102:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D3","text":"Local motion is the immediate domain of angelic causality, because it does not require the intrinsic transformation of matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A10","CH_GGVC__102:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D4","text":"Corporeal seeds locally applied by spiritual powers can produce visible effects without the creation of a new natural causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A7","CH_GGVC__102:A11","CH_GGVC__102:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D5","text":"Demonic prodigies are called miracles with respect to us, when unknown created causes produce an effect beyond the order of nature known to us.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A12","CH_GGVC__102:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D6","text":"Angels are said to perform miracles improperly, either because God works at their desire or because they render ministry in the divine work.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A12","CH_GGVC__102:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:D7","text":"Particular presidency over corporeal things is distributed according to the order of divine wisdom, while angelic orders remain distinct according to general offices.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:A1","CH_GGVC__102:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SD1","text":"The causal system is divided between angelic governance, which orders motions and dispositions, and divine causality, which preserves the foundation of the composite and the exception from created order.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:D1","CH_GGVC__102:D2","CH_GGVC__102:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SD2","text":"A miracle is classified not by rarity, wonder, or interruption of particular causality, but by its relation to the totality of created nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:D5","CH_GGVC__102:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SD3","text":"Angelic superiority does not destroy corporeal causality, but subordinates and instrumentally arranges it for effects that a body alone would not attain.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:D2","CH_GGVC__102:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SD4","text":"The order of the universe simultaneously admits a multitude of particular rulers and rejects fragmentation of the angelic hierarchy into as many orders as there are corporeal things.","refs":["CH_GGVC__102:D7","CH_GGVC__102:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX1","text":"Causality is not ordered by a simple scale whereby every higher power can effect all the works of an inferior power in the same manner.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX2","text":"Corporeal nature is not a self-sufficient mechanism that, from its own forms without higher motion, attains integrity of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX3","text":"A created spirit is not a demiurge that immediately informs matter from itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX4","text":"A sensible anomaly is not a sufficient sign of the transcendence of created causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:DNX5","text":"Created spiritual power can occupy no position outside the total order of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SNX1","text":"No creature can claim for itself an act that suspends the order of the whole of creation, because such an exception would transcend created causality as a totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SNX2","text":"The invisibility of a cause does not transfer an effect from the order of nature into the order of miracle simply speaking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SNX3","text":"Governance of the universe does not admit an opposition between nature and spirit as two coordinated and independently acting causalities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:SNX4","text":"The divine order is not reduced to a series of private contracts among creatures, but orders the universe as a public law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS1","text":"Spiritual universality + corporeal particularity → necessity of spiritual governance of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS2","text":"Distinction of the composite from form + likeness of agent and thing made → exclusion of the immediate informing of matter by an Angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS3","text":"Exteriority of local motion + superiority of spiritual nature → admission of angelic local motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS4","text":"Angelic local motion + application of corporeal seeds and agents → unusual natural effects without transgression of created order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS5","text":"Definition of miracle through the order of the whole of created nature + inclusion of every creaturely power within that order → divine exclusivity of miracle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:FGS6","text":"Ignorance of the created causal order → miracle with respect to us, not miracle simply speaking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF1","text":"Determination of corporeal actions → dependence of body on motion → universal angelic presidency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF2","text":"Angelic presidency → distinction of governance from informing → denial of immediate formal angelic power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF3","text":"Denial of informing → identification of local motion as the more perfect extrinsic motion → angelic power locally to move bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF4","text":"Unusual effects through created causes → distinction of unknown order from universal order → reclassification of demonic prodigies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:AF5","text":"Miracle beyond the order of the whole of creation → impossibility of a created exception → God alone performs miracles properly so called.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME1","text":"Governance of bodies is distinguished from production of forms: to administer is not the same as to inform substantially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME2","text":"Angelic causality is relocated from the origin of forms to local motion, the disposition of agents, and the application of seeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME3","text":"Miracle is transferred from the category of unusual effect to the category of exception from the universal order of created nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME4","text":"A demonic prodigy is classified as the effect of an unknown created cause, not as a rival to divine causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ME5","text":"The relation between Angels and bodies is described as universal hierarchical subordination, not as a fixed natural correspondence of one spirit to one corporeal species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines whether Angels administer bodies, transmute matter, move locally, and perform miracles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT2","text":"Structural — The system distributes causality among God, Angels, corporeal agents, seeds, and the order of the created universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument dissolves the illicit transition from angelic superiority to angelic omnipotence through distinctions of the mode of causality and the scope of order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The composite, not separate form, is the subject of generation; local motion, because it is ordered to the extrinsic, constitutes the point of immediate contact between spiritual and corporeal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:ALT5","text":"Epistemic — What occurs beyond nature known to us can appear miraculous, although it remains within created causes and the order of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the principal conclusion: bodies are governed by Angels, but not immediately informed as to substantial forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT2","text":"The distinction between the informing of matter and local motion is the decisive joint that simultaneously denies formal power and grants corporeal angelic efficacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT3","text":"The system coheres internally if governance is understood as motive and dispositive subordination, not as creative or formal causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT4","text":"The strongest nexus is the definition of miracle through the order of the whole of created nature, because divine exclusivity immediately follows from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT5","text":"The fragile joint remains the transition from the universality of spiritual power to the necessity of immediate angelic presidency over lower bodies, which explains more a metaphysical hierarchy than a determinate mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT6","text":"The residual tension between the plurality of particular rulers and the small number of general orders is resolved through the distinction between the distribution of divine wisdom and the difference of generic offices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__102:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from the affirmation of governance through the restriction of angelic causality to the closure of miracle in divine causality alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__102:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__102@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__102:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 111","title":"First Part · Question 110","context":"Chapter 111","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 110"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 110","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 111","order":112,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__103"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__103@R001","sha256":"2c71dbaa8411656c60d36f0e98b5f1298ae0dfd1721645539b9af7befa47b956","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quos effectus Angelus, virtute naturali, in humanas potentias cognoscitivas, appetitivas et sensitivas producere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS2","text":"Argumentatio ordinem providentiae assumit, quo inferiora per superiora reguntur, sed causalitatem angelicam ab immediata causalitate Dei distinguit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS3","text":"Illuminatio humana per Angelos explicatur ut robur intellectus et propositio veri sub sensibilibus similitudinibus, non ut infusio nudae veritatis intelligibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS4","text":"Motus voluntatis dividitur in inclinationem intrinsecam, Deo propriam, et motum extrinsecum per apprehensionem boni vel passionem, cui Angelus concurrere potest sine necessitatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS5","text":"Imaginatio et sensus Angelis subiiciuntur mediantibus mutationibus corporalibus, praecipue motu spirituum, humorum et sensibilium exteriorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS6","text":"Progressus argumenti transit ab illuminatione intellectus ad limites libertatis voluntatis, deinde ad mediations corporeas imaginationis et sensus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A1","text":"Ordo divinae providentiae subicit actiones inferiorum actionibus superiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A2","text":"Illuminatio consistit in confortatione intellectus inferioris et manifestatione veri proportionata capacitati eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A3","text":"Intellectus humanus, in statu praesenti, intelligit convertendo se ad phantasmata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A4","text":"Fides, secundum habitum quo intellectus voluntati divinam veritatem appetenti obedit, est a solo Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A5","text":"Credibilia possunt homini proponi mediantibus Angelis, qui divina revelata administrant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A6","text":"Motus voluntatis ab interiori est inclinatio voluntatis in volitum et a solo Deo causatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A7","text":"Voluntas ab exteriori movetur per bonum apprehensum et per passiones appetitus sensitivi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A8","text":"Angelus voluntatem movet persuasive vel passionem concitando, sed non efficaciter eam necessitat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A9","text":"Potentiae organo corporali utentes pati possunt mutationem ex locali motu spirituum et humorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A10","text":"Angelus potest corpus movere localiter et, per hanc causalitatem, dispositiones corporales quibus imaginatio et sensus operantur immutare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A11","text":"Imaginatio non recipit ab Angelo formam omnino a sensu non acceptam, sed ex impressionibus interioriter conservatis informatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A12","text":"Angelus praeter ordinem universae creaturae agere non potest, sed praeter ordinem communem alicuius naturae particularis operari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX1","text":"Illuminatio angelica non est immediata collatio fidei neque productio habitus fidei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX2","text":"Angelus homini veritatem intelligibilem nudam non proponit, quia modus cognitionis humanae phantasmatibus indiget.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX3","text":"Cognitio illuminationis non infert cognitionem principii quo illuminatio causatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX4","text":"Angelus voluntatem ab interiori non transformat nec actum voluntatis efficaciter determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX5","text":"Daemon cogitationes non interius causat, quia usus virtutis cogitativae voluntati subiectus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX6","text":"Angelus imaginationi non imprimit formas imaginarias quae nullo modo per sensum prius acceptae fuerint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX7","text":"Commixtio Angeli cum imaginatione humana non est per essentiam, sed per effectum causatum in imaginatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX8","text":"Visio imaginaria ab Angelo causata non est per se deceptio; deceptio ex defectu intellectus recipientis oritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX9","text":"Angelus non mutat ordinem universalem naturae, etiam cum sensum praeter modum communem immutat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D1","text":"Angelus hominem ad cognitionem divinam adiuvat, non novam naturam intellectualem conferendo, sed intellectum roborando et sensibilia ad veritatem altiorem ordinando.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A2","CH_GGVC__103:A3","CH_GGVC__103:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D2","text":"Illuminatio fidei duplicem structuram habet: Deus producit principium assensus, Angelus vel homo materiam credibilem proponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A4","CH_GGVC__103:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D3","text":"Persuasio angelica voluntatem inclinat tantum sub conditione consensus liberi, quia passio non tollit potentiam resistendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A7","CH_GGVC__103:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D4","text":"Bonae et malae suggestiones differunt causaliter: daemonicus influxus movet persuasive vel passionaliter, bona autem cogitatio principaliter Deo attribuitur, licet ministerio angelico procuretur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A5","CH_GGVC__103:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D5","text":"Apparitiones imaginariae angelicae ex materia sensibili antea recepta elaborantur per dispositionem corporalem, non per productionem imaginum ex nihilo sensibili.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A9","CH_GGVC__103:A10","CH_GGVC__103:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D6","text":"Eadem mutatio corporalis potest imaginationem perturbare vel sensum immutare, quia utraque potentia organica dispositionibus spirituum et humorum afficitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A9","CH_GGVC__103:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D7","text":"Angelus sensum mutat sive obiectum sensibile exterius opponendo sive organum sensus interius disponendo.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A9","CH_GGVC__103:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D8","text":"Singularis mutatio sensus non destruit ordinem creatum, si intra potentiam angelicam et sub ordine universali providentiae continetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A1","CH_GGVC__103:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD1","text":"Textus constituit hierarchiam causarum in qua Deus est causa intrinseca principiorum intellectualium et voluntariorum, Angelus causa ministerialis et dispositiva, corpus autem medium operationum imaginativarum et sensitivarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A1","CH_GGVC__103:A4","CH_GGVC__103:A6","CH_GGVC__103:A9","CH_GGVC__103:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD2","text":"Libertas voluntatis servatur non per absentiam omnium influxuum exteriorum, sed per distinctionem inter inclinationem passionalem et determinationem intrinsecam.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A6","CH_GGVC__103:A7","CH_GGVC__103:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD3","text":"Revelatio ad hominem perveniens necessario sub forma accommodata descendit, quia veritas superior in signa sensibilia convertenda est ut intellectus humanus eam recipiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A2","CH_GGVC__103:A3","CH_GGVC__103:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD4","text":"Distinctio inter veritatem manifestatam et causam manifestationis permittit actionem angelicam realem manere, etiamsi recipiens eius auctorem non percipiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A2","CH_GGVC__103:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD5","text":"Ordo naturae non identificatur cum ordine communi particularium causarum, quia providentia universalis admittit mutationes singulares per causas superiores.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A1","CH_GGVC__103:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod omnis causalitas in homine sit aut immediate divina aut mere humana; alioquin ministerium angelicum cognitionis et passionis nullam functionem haberet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod libertas voluntatis immunitas sit ab omni dispositione corporali; alioquin motus passionum ad voluntatem inclinans explicari non posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod cognitio humana ad veritatem intelligibilem sine conversione ad sensibilia ascendat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod imago interior sit forma autonomice et sine corpore operans; textus eam effectibus motuum corporalium alligat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod apparitio imaginaria ipsa deceptionem constituat; deceptio requirit defectum iudicii interpretantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod lex particularis naturae sit terminus supremus causalitatis; superius agens eam singulariter disponere potest sine dissolutione ordinis universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit possibilitatem creaturae quae principium internum assensus fidei aut inclinationis voluntariae per se producat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit cognitionem humanam perfecte immediatam, quia omnis illuminatio humana quae ab Angelo administratur sensibilibus velaminibus mediatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit causalitatem angelicam omnipotentem: Angelus disponit, proponit, movet et perturbat, sed nec formas naturales ex nihilo producit nec ordinem universum transgreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SNX4","text":"Systema excludit reductionem interioritatis humanae ad animam separatam, quia imaginatio, passio et sensus in dispositionibus corporalibus causaliter radicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:FGS1","text":"Ordo providentiae → superioritas angelica → proportio inferioris recipientis → illuminatio mediata per phantasmata → cognitio divina humanitus recepta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:FGS2","text":"Distinctio interioris et exterioris motus voluntatis → causalitas divina principii inclinantis → persuasio angelica et excitatio passionis → inclinatio non necessitans → libertas consensus vel resistentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:FGS3","text":"Potentia angelica ad motum localem → mutatio spirituum, humorum vel obiecti sensibilis → immutatio imaginationis aut sensus → apparitio, perturbatio vel perceptio singulariter alterata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:FGS4","text":"Limites formae naturalis et ordinis universalis → exclusio productionis absolutae → admissio dispositionis particularis → causalitas angelica ministerialis intra creationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF1","text":"Actio angelica in hominem → divisio potentiarum humanarum → determinatio intellectus per illuminationem accommodatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF2","text":"Illuminatio intellectus → distinctio fidei ut habitus divinitus infusi et credibilium angelice propositorum → conservatio causalitatis divinae immediatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF3","text":"Quaestio de motu voluntatis → distinctio motus interioris et exterioris → negatio dominationis angelicae intrinsecae → permissio persuasionis et passionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF4","text":"Quaestio de imaginatione → reductio apparitionis ad motus corporales interiores → admissio visionis imaginariae sine infusione formarum novas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF5","text":"Quaestio de sensu → duplex via exterioris obiecti et interioris dispositionis → mutatio singularis sensus intra ordinem creaturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME1","text":"Illuminatio reclassificatur ab actu simpliciter immediato ad structuram hierarchicam, in qua Deus est fons et Angelus minister revelationis accommodatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME2","text":"Voluntas reclassificatur ut libera non quia nullo modo movetur, sed quia nullus influxus creatus eius actum intrinsecum necessario efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME3","text":"Cogitatio, imaginatio et passio distinguuntur: cogitatio non interius a daemone causatur, imaginatio corporali dispositione movetur, passio voluntatem inclinare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME4","text":"Visio imaginaria reclassificatur ab indice necessario deceptionis ad signum ambiguum, cuius veritas vel deceptio ex illuminatione et iudicio intellectus pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME5","text":"Ordo naturae distinguitur in ordinem universalem inviolabilem et modum communem particularium effectuum singulariter mutabilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ALT1","text":"Surface — Angelus potest intellectum illuminare, voluntatem persuasive inclinare, imaginationem movere et sensum immutare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ALT2","text":"Structural — Effectus angelici in homine dividuntur inter causalitatem immediatam Dei, mediationem angelicam, libertatem voluntatis et condiciones corporales potentiarum organicarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones solvuntur per distinctiones causales: principium et ministerium, interior et exterior motus, forma et dispositio, ordo universalis et ordo particularis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Humanus modus cognoscendi est incorporatus et praesens: intellectus ad phantasmata convertitur, dum imaginatio et sensus mutationibus corporalibus temporaliter variantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendum nucleum argumenti, quia ordinem hierarchicum, modum cognitionis humanae, libertatem voluntatis et mediationem corporalem simul continent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT2","text":"Systema maxime cohaeret ubi causalitas divina principialis a causalitate angelica ministeriali distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT3","text":"Structura firmissima est in distinctione inter motum voluntatis intrinsecum et influxum externum, qua persuasio angelica cum libertate voluntatis componitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT4","text":"Punctum minus determinatum manet proportio inter motum corporalem ab Angelo causatum et qualemcumque actum concretum imaginationis vel sensus inde sequendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT5","text":"Commissura systematis in hoc consistit quod Angelus dicitur imaginationem et sensum movere per corpus, dum formae imaginariae et actus vitales a principiis interioribus dependere servantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, si illuminatio, libertas et corporalis mutatio non ut quaestiones separatae, sed ut gradus limitandae causalitatis angelicae leguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170230373899Z_222a2c86","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 111","source_sha256":"2c71dbaa8411656c60d36f0e98b5f1298ae0dfd1721645539b9af7befa47b956","sha256":"d1ce7d81abe5cbea692219ac80302968c32415076a75f51d6fb2fc68f5de9166","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:02:30.374873+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS1","text":"The question determines what effects an Angel, by natural power, can produce in human cognitive, appetitive, and sensitive powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS2","text":"The argument assumes the order of providence, by which lower things are governed through higher things, but distinguishes angelic causality from the immediate causality of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS3","text":"Human illumination through Angels is explained as the strengthening of the intellect and the presentation of truth under sensible likenesses, not as the bare infusion of intelligible truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS4","text":"The movement of the will is divided into intrinsic inclination, proper to God, and extrinsic movement through apprehension of the good or passion, in which an Angel can concur without necessitating.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS5","text":"Imagination and sense are subject to Angels through bodily changes, especially the movement of spirits, humors, and external sensibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AS6","text":"The progress of the argument passes from the illumination of the intellect to the limits of the freedom of the will, then to the bodily mediations of imagination and sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A1","text":"The order of divine providence subjects the actions of lower things to the actions of higher things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A2","text":"Illumination consists in the strengthening of the lower intellect and the manifestation of truth proportioned to its capacity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A3","text":"The human intellect, in its present state, understands by turning itself toward phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A4","text":"Faith, according to the habit by which the intellect obeys the will desiring divine truth, is from God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A5","text":"Objects of belief can be proposed to man through Angels, who administer divine revelations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A6","text":"The movement of the will from within is the inclination of the will toward the willed object and is caused by God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A7","text":"The will is moved from without through the apprehended good and through passions of the sensitive appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A8","text":"An Angel moves the will persuasively or by arousing passion, but does not efficaciously necessitate it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A9","text":"Powers using a bodily organ can undergo change from the local motion of spirits and humors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A10","text":"An Angel can move a body locally and, through this causality, alter the bodily dispositions by which imagination and sense operate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A11","text":"Imagination does not receive from an Angel a form not received at all from sense, but is informed from impressions preserved inwardly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:A12","text":"An Angel cannot act outside the order of the whole creation, but can operate outside the common order of a particular nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX1","text":"Angelic illumination is not the immediate bestowal of faith nor the production of the habit of faith.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX2","text":"An Angel does not present bare intelligible truth to man, because the mode of human cognition requires phantasms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX3","text":"Knowledge of illumination does not entail knowledge of the principle by which illumination is caused.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX4","text":"An Angel neither transforms the will from within nor efficaciously determines the act of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX5","text":"A demon does not cause thoughts inwardly, because the use of the cogitative power is subject to the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX6","text":"An Angel does not imprint upon imagination imaginary forms that have not previously been received in any way through sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX7","text":"The conjunction of an Angel with human imagination is not through essence, but through an effect caused in the imagination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX8","text":"An imaginary vision caused by an Angel is not in itself deception; deception arises from a defect of the receiving intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:NX9","text":"An Angel does not change the universal order of nature, even when it alters sense beyond the common mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D1","text":"An Angel assists man toward divine knowledge, not by conferring a new intellectual nature, but by strengthening the intellect and ordering sensibles toward higher truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A2","CH_GGVC__103:A3","CH_GGVC__103:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D2","text":"The illumination of faith has a twofold structure: God produces the principle of assent; an Angel or man proposes the matter to be believed.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A4","CH_GGVC__103:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D3","text":"Angelic persuasion inclines the will only under the condition of free consent, because passion does not remove the power of resistance.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A7","CH_GGVC__103:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D4","text":"Good and evil suggestions differ causally: demonic influence moves persuasively or through passion, whereas a good thought is principally attributed to God, although it is procured through angelic ministry.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A5","CH_GGVC__103:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D5","text":"Angelic imaginary apparitions are elaborated from sensible matter previously received through bodily disposition, not through the production of images from sensible nothingness.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A9","CH_GGVC__103:A10","CH_GGVC__103:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D6","text":"The same bodily change can disturb imagination or alter sense, because each organic power is affected by the dispositions of spirits and humors.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A9","CH_GGVC__103:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D7","text":"An Angel alters sense either by placing an external sensible object before it or by inwardly disposing the organ of sense.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A9","CH_GGVC__103:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:D8","text":"A singular alteration of sense does not destroy the created order if it is contained within angelic power and under the universal order of providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A1","CH_GGVC__103:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD1","text":"The text establishes a hierarchy of causes in which God is the intrinsic cause of intellectual and voluntary principles, the Angel a ministerial and dispositive cause, and the body the medium of imaginative and sensitive operations.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A1","CH_GGVC__103:A4","CH_GGVC__103:A6","CH_GGVC__103:A9","CH_GGVC__103:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD2","text":"The freedom of the will is preserved not through the absence of all external influences, but through the distinction between passional inclination and intrinsic determination.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A6","CH_GGVC__103:A7","CH_GGVC__103:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD3","text":"Revelation reaching man necessarily descends under an accommodated form, because higher truth must be converted into sensible signs so that the human intellect may receive it.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A2","CH_GGVC__103:A3","CH_GGVC__103:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD4","text":"The distinction between manifested truth and the cause of manifestation permits angelic action to remain real, even if its recipient does not perceive its author.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A2","CH_GGVC__103:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SD5","text":"The order of nature is not identified with the common order of particular causes, because universal providence admits singular changes through higher causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__103:A1","CH_GGVC__103:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX1","text":"It must be false that every causality in man is either immediately divine or merely human; otherwise the angelic ministry of cognition and passion would have no function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX2","text":"It must be false that freedom of the will is immunity from every bodily disposition; otherwise the movement of passions inclining the will could not be explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX3","text":"It must be false that human cognition ascends to intelligible truth without turning toward sensibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX4","text":"It must be false that an interior image is a form operating autonomously and without a body; the text binds it to the effects of bodily motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX5","text":"It must be false that an imaginary apparition itself constitutes deception; deception requires a defect in the interpreting judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:DNX6","text":"It must be false that a particular law of nature is the supreme limit of causality; a higher agent can singularly dispose it without dissolving the order of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility of a creature that of itself produces the internal principle of the assent of faith or of voluntary inclination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SNX2","text":"The system excludes perfectly immediate human cognition, because every human illumination administered by an Angel is mediated by sensible veils.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SNX3","text":"The system excludes omnipotent angelic causality: an Angel disposes, proposes, moves, and disturbs, but neither produces natural forms from nothing nor transcends the universal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:SNX4","text":"The system excludes the reduction of human interiority to a separate soul, because imagination, passion, and sense are causally rooted in bodily dispositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:FGS1","text":"Order of providence → angelic superiority → proportion of the lower recipient → illumination mediated through phantasms → divine knowledge received humanly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:FGS2","text":"Distinction of interior and exterior movement of the will → divine causality of the inclining principle → angelic persuasion and arousal of passion → non-necessitating inclination → freedom of consent or resistance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:FGS3","text":"Angelic power for local motion → change of spirits, humors, or sensible object → alteration of imagination or sense → apparition, disturbance, or singularly altered perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:FGS4","text":"Limits of natural form and universal order → exclusion of absolute production → admission of particular disposition → ministerial angelic causality within creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF1","text":"Angelic action upon man → division of human powers → determination of the intellect through accommodated illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF2","text":"Illumination of the intellect → distinction of faith as a habit divinely infused and of objects of belief angelically proposed → preservation of the immediate divine causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF3","text":"Question concerning the movement of the will → distinction of interior and exterior movement → denial of intrinsic angelic dominion → allowance of persuasion and passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF4","text":"Question concerning imagination → reduction of apparition to interior bodily motions → admission of imaginary vision without infusion of new forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:AF5","text":"Question concerning sense → twofold way of external object and internal disposition → singular alteration of sense within the order of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME1","text":"Illumination is reclassified from a simply immediate act to a hierarchical structure, in which God is the source and the Angel the minister of accommodated revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME2","text":"The will is reclassified as free not because it is moved in no way, but because no created influence necessarily produces its intrinsic act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME3","text":"Thought, imagination, and passion are distinguished: thought is not caused inwardly by a demon, imagination is moved by bodily disposition, and passion can incline the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME4","text":"Imaginary vision is reclassified from a necessary sign of deception to an ambiguous sign, whose truth or deception depends on the illumination and judgment of the intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ME5","text":"The order of nature is distinguished into an inviolable universal order and a common mode of particular effects that can be singularly changed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ALT1","text":"Surface — An Angel can illuminate the intellect, incline the will persuasively, move imagination, and alter sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ALT2","text":"Structural — Angelic effects in man are divided among the immediate causality of God, angelic mediation, the freedom of the will, and the bodily conditions of organic powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections are resolved through causal distinctions: principle and ministry, interior and exterior movement, form and disposition, universal order and particular order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The human mode of cognition is embodied and present: the intellect turns toward phantasms, while imagination and sense vary temporally through bodily changes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the core of the argument, because they contain together the hierarchical order, the mode of human cognition, the freedom of the will, and bodily mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT2","text":"The system is most coherent where principal divine causality is distinguished from ministerial angelic causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT3","text":"The firmest structure lies in the distinction between the intrinsic movement of the will and external influence, by which angelic persuasion is reconciled with the freedom of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT4","text":"The less determined point remains the proportion between bodily motion caused by an Angel and whatever concrete act of imagination or sense is to follow from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT5","text":"The joint of the system consists in this: that an Angel is said to move imagination and sense through the body, while imaginary forms and vital acts are preserved as dependent on interior principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__103:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if illumination, freedom, and bodily change are read not as separate questions, but as stages in limiting angelic causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__103:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__103@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__103:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 112","title":"First Part · Question 111","context":"Chapter 112","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 111"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 111","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 112","order":113,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__104"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__104@R001","sha256":"932a8deeb0ab49990445ada7625de41592d7da246d9c9e647b217fa7a861f67a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quomodo missio angelica possibilis sit, cum operatio intellectualis locum per se non exigat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS2","text":"Missio exterior non est translatio localis nuda, sed nova applicatio virtutis angelicae ad creaturam corporalem ex imperio divino.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS3","text":"Ministerium angelicum definitur per dependentiam causal-em a Deo principio et ordinationem in Deum finem, non per inferioritatem simplicem ad homines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS4","text":"Textus distinguit missionem exteriorem, quae executionem circa corporalia requirit, ab illuminatione interiori, quae intra ordinem angelicum universaliter diffunditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS5","text":"Ordinatio hierarchica dividit angelos inter visionem immediatam mysteriorum, dispositionem mandatorum et executionem ministeriorum exteriorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS6","text":"Quaestio progreditur a possibilitate missionis ad restrictionem eius per ordines, deinde ad distinctionem ambiguae assistentiae et ad distributionem munerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A1","text":"Deus, ut agens universale, omnibus entibus adest; Angelus, ut agens particulare, virtute sua hic est ita quod non alibi est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A2","text":"Angelus mittitur cum ex imperio divino virtus eius de novo applicatur ad corpus vel creaturam corporalem circa quam operatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A3","text":"Actio angelica a Deo procedit ut a primo principio et in Deum reducitur ut in ultimum finem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A4","text":"Minister est instrumentum intelligens ab alio motum et ad finem alterius ordinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A5","text":"Operatio intellectualis contemplativa locum non determinat, sed operatio ab intellectu regulata et imperata locum determinare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A6","text":"Actio exterior angelica contemplationem non impedit, quia ab eadem operatione intellectuali regulatur quae contemplationem sustinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A7","text":"Dignitas angeli non a loco corporeo, ne caelesti quidem, formaliter dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A8","text":"Ordo providentiae administrat inferiora per superiora.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A9","text":"Ordo angelicus secundum dona gratiae constituitur, non secundum ordinem naturalem qui propter altiorem gratiam intermitti possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A10","text":"Nullum ministerium divinum est tam magnum quin per inferiores ordines exerceri possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A11","text":"Assistendi nomen dupliciter dicitur: secundum visionem divinae essentiae et secundum perceptionem immediatam secretorum divinorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A12","text":"Omnes angeli beati divinam essentiam immediate vident, sed soli superiores mysteria divina in claritate essentiae immediate percipiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A13","text":"Missio exterior proprie executionem divini ministerii circa creaturam corporalem significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A14","text":"Nomen ordinis angelici proprium modum causalitatis eius manifestat: quaedam nomina imperium vel dispositionem, alia executionem significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A15","text":"Quinque ordines inferiores ad ministerium exterius mittuntur; quattuor superiores ad illud non mittuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX1","text":"Missio angelica non est motus localis corporalis neque mera mutatio situs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX2","text":"Intellectualitas non excludit operationem ad locum determinatam, nisi intellectualitas in sola contemplatione consistat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX3","text":"Ministerium angelicum non significat hominem esse simpliciter superiorem Angelo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX4","text":"Missio exterior non minuit dignitatem angelicam neque beatitudinem contemplativam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX5","text":"Non omnes angeli ad exterius ministerium mittuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX6","text":"Personarum divinarum missio non est ministerium angelico sensu; nomen missionis ibi aequivoce adhibetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX7","text":"Assistens et ministrans non sunt oppositiones absolutae, quia eadem angelica natura secundum diversos respectus utrumque nomen recipere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX8","text":"Illuminatio per superiorem non aufert omnem immediationem ad Deum, sed solam immediatam cognitionem secretorum divinorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX9","text":"Dominationes ministrant non exsequendo exteriora, sed disponendo et imperando executionem aliorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D1","text":"Missio angelica fit sine transitu substantiali, quia sola applicatio novae virtutis particularis ad determinatum effectum sufficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A1","CH_GGVC__104:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D2","text":"Locus ministerii sequitur ordinationem actionis imperatae, non naturam intellectualem agentis simpliciter.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A2","CH_GGVC__104:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D3","text":"Exterioritas operationis angelicae non introducit divisionem inter contemplationem et actionem, quia actio exterior est ratio-nata a contemplatione.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A5","CH_GGVC__104:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D4","text":"Angelus ministrans Deo et hominibus servit per ordinem causalem divinum, non per subiectionem ontologicam ad eos quibus auxiliatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A3","CH_GGVC__104:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D5","text":"Superioritas ordinis angelici non exigit ut superiores in exteriora mittantur, quia inferiores possunt ministeria etiam maxima efficaciter exequi.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A8","CH_GGVC__104:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D6","text":"Missio exterior et illuminatio interior sunt modi causalitatis diversi; universalis illuminatio angelica non probat universalem missionem exterior-em.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A11","CH_GGVC__104:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D7","text":"Omnes beati angeli assistunt secundum fruitionem visionis, sed sola prima hierarchia assistit secundum accessum immediatum ad secreta divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A11","CH_GGVC__104:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D8","text":"Executio exterior distribuitur secundum nomina ordinum quae actum indicant, dum dispositio et imperium sine executione exteriori manere possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A13","CH_GGVC__104:A14","CH_GGVC__104:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SD1","text":"Hierarchia angelica non est scala dignitatis immobilis, sed catena cognitionis, imperii et executionis per quam causalitas divina gradatim communicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A3","CH_GGVC__104:A8","CH_GGVC__104:A12","CH_GGVC__104:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SD2","text":"Eadem actio exterior potest simul exprimere maximam dependentiam a Deo et veram causalitatem intelligentis creaturae, quia angelus instrumentum intelligens est.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A2","CH_GGVC__104:A3","CH_GGVC__104:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SD3","text":"Distinctio inter visionem essentiae et cognitionem mysteriorum impedit ut beatitudo, immediatio et auctoritas hierarchica in unum idemque reducantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A11","CH_GGVC__104:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SD4","text":"Ordo ministerialis constituitur non ex sola propinquitate ad Deum, sed ex specie muneris: videre, disponere, illuminare, mandare et exsequi.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A8","CH_GGVC__104:A13","CH_GGVC__104:A14","CH_GGVC__104:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod omnis praesentia agentis intellectualis sit ubique indifferens; aliter missio angelica determinata concipi non posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod contemplatio perfecta ab omni causalitate exteriori separatur; aliter angelica beatitudo cum ministerio componi non posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod superioritas semper immediate agit in inferius; aliter mediatio hierarchica et missio inferiorum evacuantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod visio Dei aequalem omnibus cognitionem secretorum divinorum producit; aliter assistentia hierarchica distingui non posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet quod ministerium sit unum munus indifferens; aliter dispositio, mandatum et executio per ordines separari non possent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit imaginationem causalitatis divinae quae creaturas aut superfluas aut autonomas facit; divina operatio per creatas intelligentias ordinate transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit aequationem immediationis cum absentia mediationis: idem angelus potest immediate Deum videre et mediate divina mysteria recipere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit aequationem dignitatis cum immobilitate vel non-operatione; summa dignitas potest consistere in visione, imperio vel dispositione sine exteriori executione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS1","text":"Universalitas divinae praesentiae + particularitas virtutis angelicae → possibilitas applicationis novae ad determinatum corpus → missio angelica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS2","text":"Imperium divinum + actio angelica ordinata a Deo et in Deum → instrumentum intelligens → ministerium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS3","text":"Ordo providentiae per superiora + sufficientia inferiorum ad ministeria divina → exclusio missionis exterioris superiorum ordinum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS4","text":"Visio essentiae omnibus + cognitio immediata mysteriorum solis superioribus → duplex assistentia → conciliatio ministerii exterioris cum assistentia visionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS5","text":"Nomen ordinis → species causalitatis implicata → dispositio vel executio → distributio missionis exterioris ad quinque ordines inferiores.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF1","text":"Intellectualitas angelica et difficultas loci → distinctio contemplationis ab actione imperata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF2","text":"Virtus particularis applicata ex imperio divino → missio → ministerium instrumentale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF3","text":"Missio admissa → distinctio exterioris ministerii ab illuminatione interiori → negatio missionis universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF4","text":"Ambiguitas assistentiae → distinctio visionis beatificae a cognitione secretorum → duplex usus nominis assistendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF5","text":"Duplex assistentia + nomina ordinum → separatio dispositionis ab executione → quinque ordines mittuntur, quattuor superiores non mittuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME1","text":"Missio reclassificatur a motu locali ad relationem operativam inter virtutem creatam, corpus determinatum et imperium divinum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME2","text":"Oppositio contemplationis et actionis exterioris corruit in ordine angelico, ubi actio exterior ex intellectu contemplativo regulatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME3","text":"Ministerium reclassificatur ab indice inferioritatis socialis ad modum causalitatis subordinatae fini divino.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME4","text":"Assistendi nomen dividitur inter fruitionem universalem divinae essentiae et accessum hierarchice distinctum ad mysteria divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME5","text":"Hierarchia angelica describitur per functiones causales, non per solam distantiam graduum: superiores illuminant et disponunt, inferiores exsequuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus decernit utrum angeli mittantur, qui mittantur, utrum missi assistant, et ex quibus ordinibus missio procedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ALT2","text":"Structural — Missio exterior explicatur per applicationem virtutis particularis, imperium divinum, mediationem hierarchicam et executionem circa corporalia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Ambiguitates terminorum “missio,” “ministerium” et “assistens” solvuntur per distinctionem respectuum, ne contraria testimonia eundem sensum imponere videantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Deus est universaliter praesens sine mutatione locali; angelus autem per novam applicationem virtutis incipit esse ubi prius non erat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de universalitate divina, particularitate angelica et applicatione virtutis sufficiunt ad rationem missionis sine motu locali restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de causalitate instrumentali et de contemplatione regulante actionem sufficiunt ad concilianda ministerium, dignitatem et beatitudinem angelicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT3","text":"Distinctio missionis exterioris ab illuminatione interiori est commissura necessaria qua universalitas ministerii spiritualis cum restrictione missionis exterioris componitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT4","text":"Duplex sensus assistentiae interne cohaeret, sed tensionem semanticam servat, quia angeli missi et assistunt et non assistunt secundum respectus diversos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT5","text":"Distributio missionis per nomina ordinum firmiter pendet ab assumptione quod nomina angelica proprietates functionales manifestent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT6","text":"Quaestio numerum assistentium et ministrantium non definitive stabilit, sed duas rationes interpretativas relinquit, quarum una alteri oppositam proportionem producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0082","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0083","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170255124016Z_b60d4c4b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 112","source_sha256":"932a8deeb0ab49990445ada7625de41592d7da246d9c9e647b217fa7a861f67a","sha256":"184eb70724e87730e1e26d878b989c4842010da0732bab2b94cdb8d0b5a07dfc","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:02:55.125200+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS1","text":"The question determines how angelic mission is possible, since intellectual operation does not of itself require place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS2","text":"Exterior mission is not bare local translation, but a new application of angelic power to a corporeal creature by divine command.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS3","text":"Angelic ministry is defined by causal dependence on God as principle and ordination to God as end, not by simple inferiority to human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS4","text":"The text distinguishes exterior mission, which requires execution concerning corporeal things, from interior illumination, which is universally diffused within the angelic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS5","text":"Hierarchical ordination divides the angels among immediate vision of mysteries, disposition of commands, and execution of exterior ministries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AS6","text":"The question proceeds from the possibility of mission to its restriction by orders, then to the distinction of ambiguous assistance and to the distribution of offices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A1","text":"God, as universal agent, is present to all beings; an Angel, as particular agent, is here by his power in such a way that he is not elsewhere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A2","text":"An Angel is sent when, by divine command, his power is newly applied to a body or corporeal creature concerning which he operates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A3","text":"Angelic action proceeds from God as first principle and is referred back to God as ultimate end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A4","text":"A minister is an intelligent instrument moved by another and ordered to another's end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A5","text":"Contemplative intellectual operation does not determine place, but operation regulated and commanded by intellect can determine place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A6","text":"Exterior angelic action does not impede contemplation, because it is regulated by the same intellectual operation that sustains contemplation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A7","text":"The dignity of an angel does not formally depend on a corporeal place, not even a heavenly one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A8","text":"The order of providence administers lower things through higher things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A9","text":"The angelic order is constituted according to gifts of grace, not according to a natural order that can be interrupted on account of higher grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A10","text":"No divine ministry is so great that it cannot be exercised through lower orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A11","text":"The term of assisting is used in two ways: according to vision of the divine essence and according to immediate perception of divine secrets.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A12","text":"All blessed angels immediately see the divine essence, but only the higher ones immediately perceive divine mysteries in the clarity of the essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A13","text":"Exterior mission properly signifies the execution of divine ministry concerning a corporeal creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A14","text":"The proper name of an angelic order manifests its mode of causality: some names signify command or disposition, others execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:A15","text":"The five lower orders are sent to exterior ministry; the four higher orders are not sent to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX1","text":"Angelic mission is neither corporeal local motion nor a mere change of position.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX2","text":"Intellectuality does not exclude operation determined to a place, unless intellectuality consists in contemplation alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX3","text":"Angelic ministry does not signify that a human being is simply superior to an Angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX4","text":"Exterior mission does not diminish angelic dignity or contemplative beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX5","text":"Not all angels are sent to exterior ministry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX6","text":"The mission of divine persons is not ministry in the angelic sense; the term mission is used equivocally there.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX7","text":"Assisting and ministering are not absolute oppositions, because the same angelic nature can receive both names according to different respects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX8","text":"Illumination through a superior does not remove all immediacy to God, but only immediate knowledge of divine secrets.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:NX9","text":"Dominations minister not by executing exterior things, but by disposing and commanding the execution of others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D1","text":"Angelic mission occurs without substantial transit, because the application alone of a new particular power to a determinate effect suffices.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A1","CH_GGVC__104:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D2","text":"The place of ministry follows the ordination of commanded action, not simply the intellectual nature of the agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A2","CH_GGVC__104:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D3","text":"The exteriority of angelic operation does not introduce a division between contemplation and action, because exterior action is regulated by contemplation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A5","CH_GGVC__104:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D4","text":"An angel ministering to God and human beings serves through the divine causal order, not through ontological subjection to those whom he aids.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A3","CH_GGVC__104:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D5","text":"The superiority of the angelic order does not require that higher ones be sent into exterior matters, because lower ones can effectively execute even the greatest ministries.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A8","CH_GGVC__104:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D6","text":"Exterior mission and interior illumination are different modes of causality; universal angelic illumination does not prove universal exterior mission.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A11","CH_GGVC__104:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D7","text":"All blessed angels assist according to the enjoyment of vision, but only the first hierarchy assists according to immediate access to divine secrets.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A11","CH_GGVC__104:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:D8","text":"Exterior execution is distributed according to the names of orders that indicate action, while disposition and command can remain without exterior execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A13","CH_GGVC__104:A14","CH_GGVC__104:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SD1","text":"The angelic hierarchy is not a fixed ladder of dignity, but a chain of knowledge, command, and execution through which divine causality is communicated gradually.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A3","CH_GGVC__104:A8","CH_GGVC__104:A12","CH_GGVC__104:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SD2","text":"The same exterior action can simultaneously express the greatest dependence on God and the true causality of an intelligent creature, because an angel is an intelligent instrument.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A2","CH_GGVC__104:A3","CH_GGVC__104:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SD3","text":"The distinction between vision of the essence and knowledge of mysteries prevents beatitude, immediacy, and hierarchical authority from being reduced to one and the same thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A11","CH_GGVC__104:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SD4","text":"The ministerial order is constituted not by proximity to God alone, but by the kind of office: to see, dispose, illuminate, command, and execute.","refs":["CH_GGVC__104:A8","CH_GGVC__104:A13","CH_GGVC__104:A14","CH_GGVC__104:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX1","text":"It must be false that every presence of an intellectual agent is everywhere indifferent; otherwise determinate angelic mission could not be conceived.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX2","text":"It must be false that perfect contemplation is separated from every exterior causality; otherwise angelic beatitude could not be combined with ministry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX3","text":"It must be false that superiority always acts immediately upon what is lower; otherwise hierarchical mediation and the mission of lower beings are voided.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the vision of God produces equal knowledge of divine secrets in all; otherwise hierarchical assistance could not be distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:DNX5","text":"It must be false that ministry is one indifferent office; otherwise disposition, command, and execution could not be separated among the orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SNX1","text":"The system excludes an imagining of divine causality that makes creatures either superfluous or autonomous; divine operation passes in an ordered way through created intelligences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SNX2","text":"The system excludes the equation of immediacy with the absence of mediation: the same angel can immediately see God and mediately receive divine mysteries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:SNX3","text":"The system excludes the equation of dignity with immobility or non-operation; the highest dignity can consist in vision, command, or disposition without exterior execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS1","text":"Universality of divine presence + particularity of angelic power → possibility of new application to a determinate body → angelic mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS2","text":"Divine command + angelic action ordered from God and to God → intelligent instrument → ministry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS3","text":"Order of providence through higher beings + sufficiency of lower beings for divine ministries → exclusion of exterior mission of the higher orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS4","text":"Vision of the essence for all + immediate knowledge of mysteries for higher beings alone → twofold assistance → reconciliation of exterior ministry with assistance of vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:FGS5","text":"Name of order → implied kind of causality → disposition or execution → distribution of exterior mission to the five lower orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF1","text":"Angelic intellectuality and the difficulty of place → distinction of contemplation from commanded action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF2","text":"Particular power applied by divine command → mission → instrumental ministry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF3","text":"Mission admitted → distinction of exterior ministry from interior illumination → denial of universal mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF4","text":"Ambiguity of assistance → distinction of beatific vision from knowledge of secrets → twofold use of the term of assisting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:AF5","text":"Twofold assistance + names of orders → separation of disposition from execution → five orders are sent, four higher orders are not sent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME1","text":"Mission is reclassified from local motion to an operative relation among created power, a determinate body, and divine command.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME2","text":"The opposition between contemplation and exterior action collapses in the angelic order, where exterior action is regulated by contemplative intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME3","text":"Ministry is reclassified from an index of social inferiority to a mode of causality subordinated to the divine end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME4","text":"The term of assisting is divided between universal enjoyment of the divine essence and hierarchically distinct access to divine mysteries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ME5","text":"The angelic hierarchy is described through causal functions, not through distance of ranks alone: higher beings illuminate and dispose, lower beings execute.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text decides whether angels are sent, which are sent, whether those sent assist, and from which orders mission proceeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ALT2","text":"Structural — Exterior mission is explained through the application of particular power, divine command, hierarchical mediation, and execution concerning corporeal things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Ambiguities of the terms “mission,” “ministry,” and “assisting” are resolved through distinction of respects, lest contrary testimonies appear to impose the same sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — God is universally present without local change; an angel, however, through a new application of power begins to be where he was not before.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning divine universality, angelic particularity, and the application of power suffice to reconstruct an account of mission without local motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning instrumental causality and contemplation regulating action suffice to reconcile angelic ministry, dignity, and beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT3","text":"The distinction of exterior mission from interior illumination is the necessary joint by which the universality of spiritual ministry is combined with the restriction of exterior mission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT4","text":"The twofold sense of assistance coheres internally, yet retains semantic tension, because sent angels both assist and do not assist according to different respects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT5","text":"The distribution of mission through the names of the orders firmly depends upon the assumption that angelic names manifest functional properties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__104:MRT6","text":"The question does not definitively establish the number of those assisting and ministering, but leaves two interpretive accounts, one of which produces a proportion opposed to the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0082","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__104:P0083","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__104@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__104:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 113","title":"First Part · Question 112","context":"Chapter 113","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 112"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 112","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 113","order":114,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__105"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__105@R001","sha256":"9142e34dab24610f3bac3e8e5871466d7d3bd47f9e0dd40f6ca2a01a9e840728","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat quibus fundamentis custodia angelica necessaria, singularis, universalis et continua sit, quamvis homo peccare, damnari et tribulationibus subici possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS2","text":"Custodia angelica constituitur ut executio mediata providentiae divinae circa hominem rationalem, defectibilem et viatorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est metaphysica, reconstructiva et disputativa: obiectiones solvuntur distinctionibus causalitatis, universalitatis, temporis, voluntatis et cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS4","text":"Fundamentum procedit ab ordine quo variabilia per invariabilia regulantur et quo providentia singularia incorruptibilia principaliter respicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS5","text":"Motus transit a necessitate custodiae ad eius individuationem et distributionem hierarchicam, deinde ad universalitatem, initium, permanentiam et effectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS6","text":"Clausura reinterpretatur derelictio ut permissio particularis, dolor ut impossibilis in voluntate beata, et pugna ut oppositio rerum consultarum sine discordia voluntatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A1","text":"In ordine providentiae mobilia et variabilia per immobilia et invariabilia moventur et regulantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A2","text":"Cognitio practica et affectus hominis multipliciter a bono deficere possunt, neque liberum arbitrium aut cognitio naturalis legis per se sufficienter dirigunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A3","text":"Deus affectum ad bonum immediate per gratiam et virtutes inclinat, sed instructionem rationis de viis congruis mediantibus Angelis transmittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A4","text":"Custodia Angelorum est executio divinae providentiae circa homines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A5","text":"Providentia principaliter ordinatur ad ea quae perpetuo manent, res autem transeuntes respicit secundum ordinem earum ad permanentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A6","text":"Anima rationalis est forma propria et incorruptibilis singularis hominis, unde homo non tantum secundum speciem sed etiam secundum individuum permanet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A7","text":"Custodia angelica attingit invisibilia et occulta quae ad salutem singularis hominis secundum se pertinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A8","text":"Gradus agentis custodientis augetur secundum universalitatem obiecti custodiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A9","text":"Angeli inferiores virtutes officiorum superiorum participant atque ut executores earum operantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A10","text":"Status viatoris hominem periculis interioribus et exterioribus exponit atque rationem officii custodialis constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A11","text":"Custodia angelica est beneficium homini concessum ratione naturae rationalis, non ratione solius status Christiani.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A12","text":"Custodia ultimo ordinatur ad illuminationem et salutem, sed etiam effectus inferiores habet, praesertim prohibitionem nocumentorum et cohibitionem malorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A13","text":"Assignatio proprii custodis incipit a nativitate; ante separationem a matre proles probabiliter custodia Angeli matris continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A14","text":"Angelica illuminatio et instigatio voluntatem humanam non necessitant, quia homo ab eis per passionem et malitiam recedere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A15","text":"Nulla res participans esse totaliter providentiae divinae subtrahitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A16","text":"Voluntas Angelorum beatorum totaliter ordini divinae iustitiae adhaeret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A17","text":"Voluntas universalis de salute et voluntas particularis de ordine iustitiae secundum circumstantias distingui possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A18","text":"Angeli divinam sententiam sequuntur, sed ordinem sapientiae circa merita contraria non cognoscunt nisi Deo revelante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX1","text":"Liberum arbitrium et lex naturalis custodiam angelicam non excludunt, quia utrumque circa particularia opera defectibile manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX2","text":"Custodia immediata Dei custodiam angelicam non reddit superfluam, quia providentia divina per causas secundas instruit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX3","text":"Peccatum vel perditio custoditi negligentiam Angeli non probat; apparitio visibilis et miraculum ad gratiam specialem, non ad legem communem custodiae, pertinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX4","text":"Potentia unius Angeli ad multos custodiendos non excludit distributionem singularem, quia assignatio mensuratur providentia circa individuum, non sola capacitate agentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX5","text":"Missio angelica non identificatur tota cum custodia particulari; ordines superiores custodiae universaliores habent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX6","text":"Custodia neque Baptismo neque praedestinatione neque fide circumscribitur, quia etiam non salvandi a multis malis retrahuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX7","text":"Christus Angelum custodem tamquam superiorem non habuit, quia secundum humanitatem immediate a Verbo regulabatur; Angelos tamen tamquam ministros inferiores habuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX8","text":"Absentia localis Angeli non est absentia effectus custodiae, neque permissio tribulationis est derelictio totalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX9","text":"Angeli beati de peccatis aut poenis hominum non dolent, quia nihil contra voluntatem eorum iustitiae divinae adhaerentem simpliciter accidit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX10","text":"Pugna inter bonos Angelos non est discordia voluntatum neque favor iniustitiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D1","text":"Defectibilitas practica hominis intra ordinem providentiae facit necessariam regulationem angelicam ad bonum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A1","CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:A3","CH_GGVC__105:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D2","text":"Actio Dei et actio Angeli non concurrunt ut causae rivales: Deus immediate dat inclinationem bonam, Angelus mediate dirigit executionem prudentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A3","CH_GGVC__105:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D3","text":"Singulus homo providentiae comparatur sicut species vel genus rerum corruptibilium, quia eius forma rationalis singulariter permanet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A5","CH_GGVC__105:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D4","text":"Ex singulari permanentia personae et occultis eius salutis rationibus rationabiliter sequitur singularem hominem singulari Angelo committi.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D5","text":"Custodia particularis ad infimum ordinem pertinet, custodiae autem universaliores superioribus ordinibus distribuuntur, salvis potentiis superiorum per inferiores executis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A8","CH_GGVC__105:A9","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D6","text":"Custodia omnibus hominibus ratione naturae et viae competit, etiamsi in quibusdam non ad salutem sed tantum ad restrictionem mali efficax sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:A11","CH_GGVC__105:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D7","text":"Assignatio custodis a nativitate, non a Baptismo, incipit; tutela fetus ante nativitatem per custodiam matris tantum probabiliter explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A11","CH_GGVC__105:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D8","text":"Angelus hominem numquam totaliter deserit, sed secundum iudicium divinum potest non impedire culpam, poenam aut tribulationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D9","text":"Officium custodis terminatur cum statu viatoris: post terminum Angelus non iam custodit, sed in regno conregnat, dum in Inferno daemon punit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D10","text":"Angeli peccatum et poenam absolute non volunt, sed particulariter volunt ordinem iustitiae quo peccatum permittitur aut poena infligitur; ideo non dolent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D11","text":"Hieronymus resistentiam Danielis principi daemonum tribuit; Gregorius eam inter bonos Angelos ad consultationem de meritis oppositis refert, concordia voluntatum integra manente.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD1","text":"Custodia angelica est forma providentiae simul mediata, individuata, hierarchica et non coactiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D1","CH_GGVC__105:D2","CH_GGVC__105:D4","CH_GGVC__105:D5","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD2","text":"Eadem proprietas rationalis hominem singulariter dignum providentia et propter defectibilitatem indigentem custodia constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD3","text":"Universalitas custodiae non requirit uniformitatem effectus: eadem tutela in uno ad salutem, in alio tantum ad limitationem mali pervenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D6","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD4","text":"Peccatum, poena et tribulatio non sunt effectus positivi custodiae, sed eventus permissive intra ordinem providentiae comprehensi.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D8","CH_GGVC__105:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD5","text":"Concordia angelica est teleologica potius quam epistemice completa: Angeli idem iudicium divinum volunt, quamvis eius dispositionem nondum omnes cognoscant.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD6","text":"Relatio custodialis est officium temporale status viae, non relatio immutabilis inter eundem Angelum et hominem post terminum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D7","CH_GGVC__105:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX1","text":"Causalitas divina et causalitas angelica tacite excluduntur ne in eodem plano rivalitatis ponantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX2","text":"Autonomia practica hominis, qua ratio et voluntas sibi ad bonum sufficerent, structuraliter excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX3","text":"Persona humana non reducitur ad individuum transiens cuius sola species providentiae principaliter subsistat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A5","CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX4","text":"Custodia non definitur ut cautio eventus boni neque ut impedimentum necessarium omnis culpae et poenae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX5","text":"Dignitas ecclesialis, fides praesens et exitus salutis non constituunt condiciones necessarias assignationis custodis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A11","CH_GGVC__105:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX6","text":"Malum permissum non constituit regionem a providentia vacantem.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A15","CH_GGVC__105:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX7","text":"Voluntas beata non retinet preferenceiam privatam quae ordini iustitiae divinae finaliter adversetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX8","text":"Oppositio meritorum vel rerum consultarum non infert oppositionem voluntatum angelicarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A18","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX1","text":"Regio entis omnino extra providentiam intra systema impossibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX2","text":"Ordo providentiae neque solum immediatus neque in causas secundas independentes divisus esse potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D2","CH_GGVC__105:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX3","text":"Defectus qui neque iustitia divina fiat neque ab ea permittatur structuram totam dissolveret atque ideo praecluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A15","CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX4","text":"Plena cognitio ordinis divini circa merita repugnantia Angelis ante revelationem indisponibilis manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A18","CH_GGVC__105:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX5","text":"Custodia quae voluntatem necessitat aut bonum exitum infallibiliter efficiat inadmissibilis est, quia libertatem, permissionem et diversitatem effectuum tolleret.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:SD3","CH_GGVC__105:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS1","text":"Schema necessitatis ordinatur sic: variabilitas humana → insufficientia directionis propriae → regulatio per invariabile → mediatio angelica → motus ad bonum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A1","CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS2","text":"Schema individuationis ordinatur sic: anima rationalis incorruptibilis → permanentia singularis → providentia circa individuum → custos singularis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A5","CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:D3","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS3","text":"Schema hierarchicum ordinatur sic: amplitudo obiecti → universalitas agentis → gradus ordinis → custodia particularis inferior vel universalis superior.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A8","CH_GGVC__105:A9","CH_GGVC__105:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS4","text":"Schema temporale ordinatur sic: natura rationalis separata in nativitate → assignatio custodis → status viae → terminus → mutatio relationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A11","CH_GGVC__105:A13","CH_GGVC__105:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS5","text":"Schema efficaciae ordinatur sic: illuminatio vel cohibitio → responsio libera → profectus aut defectus permissus → permanentia providentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A12","CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS6","text":"Schema affectivum ordinatur sic: adhaesio voluntatis divinae iustitiae → distinctio voluntatis absolutae et particularis → permissio ordinata → absentia doloris.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:A17","CH_GGVC__105:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS7","text":"Schema resistentiae ordinatur sic: merita contraria → sententia divina nondum revelata → consultatio angelica → resistentia secundum obiecta → concordia in exsecutione sententiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A18","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AF1","text":"Primus motus procedit per hanc catenam: defectibilitas humana → necessitas custodiae → causalitas divina mediata → individuatio custodis → distributio hierarchica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AF2","text":"Secundus motus procedit per hanc catenam: status viatoris → universalitas custodiae → fundamentum in natura rationali → initium a nativitate → permanentia sub permissione defectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AF3","text":"Motus finalis procedit per hanc catenam: apparentia defectus custodialis → subiectio iustitiae divinae → exclusio doloris → reinterpretatio pugnae → concordia angelica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME1","text":"Custodia a mera defensione externa in regimen practicum convertitur quod illuminationem, instructionem et cohibitionem complectitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A3","CH_GGVC__105:A7","CH_GGVC__105:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME2","text":"Singularis persona humana fit obiectum directum providentiae propter permanentiam animae propriae, non tantum ut pars speciei.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D3","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME3","text":"Hierarchia angelica secundum universalitatem rei administratae, non secundum solam potentiam nudam, describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A8","CH_GGVC__105:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME4","text":"Libertas humana inter sufficientiam autonomam et necessitatem coactivam collocatur: indiget illuminatione, sed ab ea recedere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME5","text":"Successus salutis desinit esse criterium praesentiae custodiae; efficacia distinguitur secundum illuminationem, restrictionem mali et ultimum exitum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A12","CH_GGVC__105:D6","CH_GGVC__105:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME6","text":"Dolor et pugna angelica ex affectibus contrariis in modos loquendi de iustitia, cognitione incompleta et obiectis contrariis transferuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME7","text":"Vita praesens constituitur ut intervallum viatorium quod initium, durationem et terminum officii custodialis mensurat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:D7","CH_GGVC__105:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface: homines custodiuntur, singulis singuli Angeli assignantur, custodia particularis infimo ordini competit, omnibus viatoribus a nativitate adest, numquam totaliter cessat, dolorem non parit et concordiam angelicam non tollit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D1","CH_GGVC__105:D4","CH_GGVC__105:D5","CH_GGVC__105:D6","CH_GGVC__105:D7","CH_GGVC__105:D8","CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural: custodia est distributio hierarchica providentiae per causas secundas secundum permanentiam personae, universalitatem obiecti et pluralitatem effectuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:SD1","CH_GGVC__105:SD2","CH_GGVC__105:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic: contradictiones apparentes dissolvuntur distinguendo immediatum a mediato, particulare ab universali, totalem derelictionem a permissione particulari, voluntatem absolutam a circumstantiata et obiecta contraria a voluntatibus contrariis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D2","CH_GGVC__105:D5","CH_GGVC__105:D8","CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal: participatio essendi fundat universalitatem providentiae, incorruptibilitas animae individuationem curae, status viatoris durationem officii, et cognitio angelica limitata necessitatem revelationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:A15","CH_GGVC__105:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT1","text":"Axiomata proposita sufficiunt ad restituendas omnes octo determinationes principales quaestionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A1","CH_GGVC__105:A4","CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:A8","CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:A13","CH_GGVC__105:A15","CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT2","text":"Structura firmissima est identificatio custodiae cum executione providentiae, quia eadem ratio necessitatem, universalitatem et permanentiam sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A4","CH_GGVC__105:D1","CH_GGVC__105:D6","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT3","text":"Transitus ab incorruptibilitate singularis hominis ad unum Angelum pro uno homine rationabilis et probabilis exhibetur, non demonstrative necessarius.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D3","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT4","text":"Terminus nativitatis minus firmus manet, quia anima rationalis ante partum admittitur, tutela autem per Angelum matris tantum probabiliter ponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A13","CH_GGVC__105:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0080","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0090","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT5","text":"Universalitas formulae de omni viatore per casum Christi qualificatur, cui status viatoris aderat sed custos superior propter immediatam regulationem Verbi non debebatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT6","text":"Exclusio doloris et discordiae cohaeret, sed distinctionibus voluntatis universalis et particularis atque rerum contrariarum a voluntatibus contrariis nititur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A17","CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT7","text":"Permissio divina defectum cum custodia componit, sed textus signum internum non dat quo custodia deficiens a defectu iuste permisso separetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D8","CH_GGVC__105:SD4","CH_GGVC__105:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT8","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: a metaphysica mediationis ad individuationem, hierarchiam, temporalitatem et reconciliationem defectus cum ordine providentiae procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:AF1","CH_GGVC__105:AF2","CH_GGVC__105:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170328437402Z_b7760de0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 113","source_sha256":"9142e34dab24610f3bac3e8e5871466d7d3bd47f9e0dd40f6ca2a01a9e840728","sha256":"c5fd40285a4907bc9698a954f1975516bf4f87c5bf3b9bc17a709841d975be41","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:03:28.439462+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS1","text":"The question determines on what grounds angelic guardianship is necessary, individual, universal, and continuous, although a human being may sin, be damned, and be subjected to tribulations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS2","text":"Angelic guardianship is constituted as the mediated execution of divine providence concerning the rational, fallible, wayfaring human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS3","text":"The argumentation is metaphysical, reconstructive, and disputative: objections are resolved by distinctions of causality, universality, time, will, and knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS4","text":"The foundation proceeds from the order by which variable things are regulated by invariable things and by which providence principally regards incorruptible singulars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS5","text":"The movement proceeds from the necessity of guardianship to its individuation and hierarchical distribution, then to universality, beginning, continuance, and effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AS6","text":"The conclusion reinterprets abandonment as particular permission, sorrow as impossible in the blessed will, and conflict as opposition of matters under deliberation without discord of wills.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A1","text":"In the order of providence, mobile and variable things are moved and regulated by immobile and invariable things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A2","text":"Practical knowledge and human affection can fail from the good in many ways, and neither free choice nor natural knowledge of the law sufficiently directs by itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A3","text":"God immediately inclines affection toward the good through grace and virtues, but transmits instruction of reason concerning suitable ways through Angels as mediators.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A4","text":"The guardianship of Angels is the execution of divine providence concerning human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A5","text":"Providence is principally ordered to those things that remain perpetually, but regards transitory things according to their order toward permanent things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A6","text":"The rational soul is the proper and incorruptible form of the individual human being; hence the human being remains not only according to species but also according to the individual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A7","text":"Angelic guardianship reaches invisible and hidden things that pertain in themselves to the salvation of the individual human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A8","text":"The rank of the guarding agent increases according to the universality of the object of guardianship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A9","text":"Lower Angels participate in the powers of the offices of higher Angels and act as their executors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A10","text":"The state of the wayfarer exposes the human being to interior and exterior dangers and constitutes the rationale of the guarding office.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A11","text":"Angelic guardianship is a benefit granted to the human being by reason of rational nature, not by reason of Christian status alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A12","text":"Guardianship is ultimately ordered to illumination and salvation, but it also has lower effects, especially the prevention of harms and the restraint of evils.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A13","text":"The assignment of a proper guardian begins at birth; before separation from the mother, offspring are probably contained within the guardianship of the mother's Angel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A14","text":"Angelic illumination and instigation do not necessitate the human will, because a human being can depart from them through passion and malice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A15","text":"No thing participating in being is totally withdrawn from divine providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A16","text":"The will of the blessed Angels wholly adheres to the order of divine justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A17","text":"A universal will concerning salvation and a particular will concerning the order of justice according to circumstances can be distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:A18","text":"Angels follow the divine judgment, but do not know the order of wisdom concerning contrary merits unless God reveals it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX1","text":"Free choice and natural law do not exclude angelic guardianship, because each remains fallible with respect to particular acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX2","text":"God's immediate guardianship does not render angelic guardianship superfluous, because divine providence instructs through secondary causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX3","text":"The sin or perdition of the guarded person does not prove the Angel's negligence; visible appearance and miracle pertain to special grace, not to the common law of guardianship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX4","text":"The power of one Angel to guard many does not exclude individual distribution, because assignment is measured by providence concerning the individual, not by the agent's capacity alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX5","text":"Angelic mission is not wholly identified with particular guardianship; higher orders have more universal guardianships.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX6","text":"Guardianship is confined neither to Baptism nor predestination nor faith, because even those who will not be saved are restrained from many evils.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX7","text":"Christ did not have a guardian Angel as a superior, because according to his humanity he was immediately regulated by the Word; nevertheless, he had Angels as inferior ministers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX8","text":"The Angel's local absence is not absence of the effect of guardianship, nor is the permission of tribulation total abandonment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX9","text":"Blessed Angels do not grieve over the sins or punishments of human beings, because nothing simply happens against their will adhering to divine justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:NX10","text":"Conflict among good Angels is neither discord of wills nor favoring injustice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D1","text":"The practical fallibility of the human being within the order of providence makes angelic regulation toward the good necessary.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A1","CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:A3","CH_GGVC__105:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D2","text":"God's action and the Angel's action do not concur as rival causes: God immediately gives good inclination; the Angel mediately directs prudent execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A3","CH_GGVC__105:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D3","text":"The individual human being is related to providence as the species or genus of corruptible things, because his rational form remains individually.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A5","CH_GGVC__105:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D4","text":"From the individual permanence of the person and the hidden grounds of his salvation, it reasonably follows that an individual human being is entrusted to an individual Angel.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D5","text":"Particular guardianship belongs to the lowest order, while more universal guardianships are distributed among higher orders, with the powers of the higher executed through the lower.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A8","CH_GGVC__105:A9","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D6","text":"Guardianship belongs to all human beings by reason of nature and the way, even if in some it is efficacious not for salvation but only for the restriction of evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:A11","CH_GGVC__105:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D7","text":"The assignment of a guardian begins at birth, not at Baptism; the protection of the fetus before birth is explained only probably through the guardianship of the mother.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A11","CH_GGVC__105:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D8","text":"The Angel never totally abandons the human being, but according to divine judgment may not prevent fault, punishment, or tribulation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D9","text":"The guardian's office ends with the state of the wayfarer: after the end, the Angel no longer guards, but reigns together in the kingdom, while in Hell the demon punishes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D10","text":"Angels do not will sin and punishment absolutely, but particularly will the order of justice by which sin is permitted or punishment inflicted; therefore they do not grieve.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:D11","text":"Hieronymus attributes Daniel's resistance to the prince of demons; Gregorius refers it among good Angels to deliberation concerning opposed merits, with concord of wills remaining intact.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD1","text":"Angelic guardianship is a form of providence at once mediated, individuated, hierarchical, and non-coercive.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D1","CH_GGVC__105:D2","CH_GGVC__105:D4","CH_GGVC__105:D5","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD2","text":"The same rational property constitutes the human being both singularly worthy of providence and, because of fallibility, in need of guardianship.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD3","text":"The universality of guardianship does not require uniformity of effect: the same protection reaches salvation in one person, but in another only the limitation of evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D6","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD4","text":"Sin, punishment, and tribulation are not positive effects of guardianship, but events permissively contained within the order of providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D8","CH_GGVC__105:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD5","text":"Angelic concord is teleological rather than epistemically complete: Angels will the same divine judgment, although not all yet know its disposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SD6","text":"The guardianship relation is a temporal office of the state of the way, not an immutable relation between the same Angel and the human being after the end.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D7","CH_GGVC__105:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX1","text":"Divine causality and angelic causality are tacitly excluded from being placed on the same plane of rivalry.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX2","text":"Human practical autonomy, by which reason and will would suffice to themselves for the good, is structurally excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX3","text":"The human person is not reduced to a transitory individual whose species alone principally subsists for providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A5","CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX4","text":"Guardianship is not defined as a guarantee of a good outcome nor as the necessary prevention of every fault and punishment.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX5","text":"Ecclesial dignity, present faith, and the outcome of salvation do not constitute necessary conditions for the assignment of a guardian.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A11","CH_GGVC__105:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX6","text":"Permitted evil does not constitute a region empty of providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A15","CH_GGVC__105:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX7","text":"The blessed will retains no private preference that would ultimately oppose the order of divine justice.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:DNX8","text":"Opposition of merits or of matters under deliberation does not entail opposition of angelic wills.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A18","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX1","text":"A region of being wholly outside providence is impossible within the system.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX2","text":"The order of providence can be neither solely immediate nor divided into independent secondary causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D2","CH_GGVC__105:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX3","text":"A defect that neither comes about through divine justice nor is permitted by it would dissolve the entire structure and is therefore precluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A15","CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX4","text":"Full knowledge of the divine order concerning conflicting merits remains unavailable to Angels before revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A18","CH_GGVC__105:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:SNX5","text":"A guardianship that necessitates the will or infallibly produces a good outcome is inadmissible, because it would remove freedom, permission, and diversity of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:SD3","CH_GGVC__105:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS1","text":"The schema of necessity is ordered thus: human variability → insufficiency of self-direction → regulation by the invariable → angelic mediation → movement toward the good.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A1","CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS2","text":"The schema of individuation is ordered thus: incorruptible rational soul → individual permanence → providence concerning the individual → individual guardian.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A5","CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:D3","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS3","text":"The hierarchical schema is ordered thus: scope of object → universality of agent → rank of order → lower particular or higher universal guardianship.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A8","CH_GGVC__105:A9","CH_GGVC__105:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS4","text":"The temporal schema is ordered thus: rational nature separated at birth → assignment of guardian → state of the way → end → change of relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A11","CH_GGVC__105:A13","CH_GGVC__105:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS5","text":"The schema of efficacy is ordered thus: illumination or restraint → free response → permitted progress or failure → continuance of providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A12","CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS6","text":"The affective schema is ordered thus: adherence of the will to divine justice → distinction of absolute and particular will → ordered permission → absence of sorrow.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:A17","CH_GGVC__105:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:FGS7","text":"The schema of resistance is ordered thus: contrary merits → divine judgment not yet revealed → angelic deliberation → resistance according to objects → concord in the execution of judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A18","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AF1","text":"The first movement proceeds through this chain: human fallibility → necessity of guardianship → mediated divine causality → individuation of the guardian → hierarchical distribution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AF2","text":"The second movement proceeds through this chain: state of the wayfarer → universality of guardianship → foundation in rational nature → beginning from birth → continuance under permission of failure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:AF3","text":"The final movement proceeds through this chain: appearance of failure in guardianship → subjection to divine justice → exclusion of sorrow → reinterpretation of conflict → angelic concord.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME1","text":"Guardianship is transformed from mere external defense into practical governance that includes illumination, instruction, and restraint.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A3","CH_GGVC__105:A7","CH_GGVC__105:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME2","text":"The individual human person becomes a direct object of providence because of the permanence of its proper soul, not merely as a part of the species.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D3","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME3","text":"The angelic hierarchy is described according to the universality of the thing administered, not according to bare power alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A8","CH_GGVC__105:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME4","text":"Human freedom is situated between autonomous sufficiency and coercive necessity: it needs illumination, yet can depart from it.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A2","CH_GGVC__105:A14","CH_GGVC__105:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME5","text":"The success of salvation ceases to be a criterion of the presence of guardianship; efficacy is distinguished according to illumination, restraint of evil, and final outcome.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A12","CH_GGVC__105:D6","CH_GGVC__105:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME6","text":"Angelic sorrow and conflict are transferred from contrary affections into modes of speaking about justice, incomplete knowledge, and contrary objects.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ME7","text":"Present life is constituted as a wayfaring interval that measures the beginning, duration, and end of the guarding office.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:D7","CH_GGVC__105:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface: human beings are guarded, individual Angels are assigned to individuals, particular guardianship belongs to the lowest order, is present for all wayfarers from birth, never wholly ceases, produces no sorrow, and does not remove angelic concord.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D1","CH_GGVC__105:D4","CH_GGVC__105:D5","CH_GGVC__105:D6","CH_GGVC__105:D7","CH_GGVC__105:D8","CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural: guardianship is the hierarchical distribution of providence through secondary causes according to the permanence of the person, universality of the object, and plurality of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:SD1","CH_GGVC__105:SD2","CH_GGVC__105:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic: apparent contradictions are resolved by distinguishing immediate from mediated, particular from universal, total abandonment from particular permission, absolute will from circumstanced will, and contrary objects from contrary wills.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D2","CH_GGVC__105:D5","CH_GGVC__105:D8","CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal: participation in being grounds the universality of providence, incorruptibility of the soul the individuation of care, the state of the wayfarer the duration of the office, and limited angelic knowledge the necessity of revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:A15","CH_GGVC__105:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT1","text":"The proposed axioms suffice to restore all eight principal determinations of the question.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A1","CH_GGVC__105:A4","CH_GGVC__105:A6","CH_GGVC__105:A8","CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:A13","CH_GGVC__105:A15","CH_GGVC__105:A16","CH_GGVC__105:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT2","text":"The firmest structure is the identification of guardianship with the execution of providence, because the same rationale supports necessity, universality, and continuance.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A4","CH_GGVC__105:D1","CH_GGVC__105:D6","CH_GGVC__105:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT3","text":"The transition from the incorruptibility of the individual human being to one Angel for one human being is presented as reasonable and probable, not demonstratively necessary.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D3","CH_GGVC__105:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT4","text":"The boundary of birth remains less firm, because the rational soul is admitted before birth, whereas protection through the mother's Angel is only posited probably.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A13","CH_GGVC__105:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0080","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0090","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT5","text":"The universality of the formula concerning every wayfarer is qualified by the case of Christ, to whom the state of the wayfarer belonged but who was not owed a superior guardian because of the immediate regulation of the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A10","CH_GGVC__105:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT6","text":"The exclusion of sorrow and discord coheres, but rests upon the distinctions of universal and particular will and of contrary things from contrary wills.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:A17","CH_GGVC__105:D10","CH_GGVC__105:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT7","text":"Divine permission reconciles failure with guardianship, but the text gives no internal sign by which deficient guardianship may be separated from justly permitted failure.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:D8","CH_GGVC__105:SD4","CH_GGVC__105:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__105:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: it proceeds from the metaphysics of mediation to individuation, hierarchy, temporality, and reconciliation of failure with the order of providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__105:AF1","CH_GGVC__105:AF2","CH_GGVC__105:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__105:P0139","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__105@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__105:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 114","title":"First Part · Question 113","context":"Chapter 114","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 113"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 113","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 114","order":115,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__106"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__106@R001","sha256":"5d5b75c600f56a82bf5c5ac09ae41b0ca403aa998ce05ee4b9064771910d696c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS1","text":"Quaestio determinat utrum et quo ordine impugnatio daemonum homines attingat, quin divina gubernatio vel humana responsabilitas dissolvatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS2","text":"Textus impugnationem dividit inter malitiam daemonis ut principium proximum et ordinationem Dei ut principium ordinans quod malum ad bonum refert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS3","text":"Tentatio reconstituitur non ex solo experimento, sed ex fine tentantis: Diabolus explorat ut ad peccatum praecipitet, Deus manifestat, homo vel iuvat vel nocet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS4","text":"Causalitas daemonica limitatur per distinctiones directi et indirecti, voluntarii et inclinantis, miraculi proprii et operis naturaliter vel phantastice extraordinarii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS5","text":"Victoria hominis daemonem non annihilat nec perpetuo excludit, sed impugnationem eius temporaliter restringit sub permissione divina et prudentia hostili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A1","text":"Impugnatio daemonum ex invidia profectus humani impediendi et ex superbia ministerium divinum imitandi procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A2","text":"Deus malis ordinate utitur et impugnationem daemonum ad bona, praecipue ad gloriam electorum, ordinare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A3","text":"Daemones ad peccatum instigantes a Deo non mittuntur, sed iusto iudicio permittuntur; ad poenam inferendam mitti possunt sub fine divinae iustitiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A4","text":"Inaequalitas naturalis inter hominem et daemonem compensatur principaliter gratia divina et secundario custodia angelica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A5","text":"Tentare proprie est experimentum sumere ut aliquid de aliquo sciatur, sed species tentationis ex fine ulteriori determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A6","text":"Tentare ad nocendum et ad peccatum praecipitandum est proprium officium Diaboli, quamvis alii analogice vel instrumentaliter tentare dicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A7","text":"Daemon interioris conditionis hominis cognitionem directam non habet, sed ex exterioribus explorat ad quod vitium homo pronior sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A8","text":"Daemon voluntatem humanam immutare non potest, sed inferiores vires mutando voluntatem inclinare potest sine necessitatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A9","text":"Diabolus est causa indirecta omnium peccatorum ratione primi peccati et pronitatis inde derivatae, non autem causa directa cuiuslibet peccati singularis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A10","text":"Homo per liberum arbitrium et corruptionem carnis per se in peccatum ruere potest, sed ad meritum proficere non potest sine auxilio divino per Angelos ministrato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A11","text":"Miraculum proprie dictum ordinem totius naturae creatae excedit et soli Deo competit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A12","text":"Daemones effectus naturales extraordinarios per semina et virtutes naturales disponere, vel apparentias sensuum immutare, possunt; effectus naturam creatam transcendentes efficere non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A13","text":"Opera specie similia discernuntur per finem et ius operationis: sancti sub publica administratione et iussu Dei, magi ad propriam gloriam per privata commercia agunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A14","text":"Restrictio daemonis victi ex clementia divina et ex formidine daemonis ne iterata congressione vincatur procedit, sed reditus eius manet possibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX1","text":"Impugnatio daemonica non est ministerium salutis daemonibus a Deo commissum, etiamsi eius eventus divina providentia ordinari possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX2","text":"Certamen hominis cum daemonibus non est pugna naturaliter aequalium, nec tamen ob inaequalitatem gratia et custodia divina destituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX3","text":"Tentatio non univoce Diabolo attribuitur, quia Deus, homo, caro et mundus diversis rationibus tentare dicuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX4","text":"Daemon nec voluntatem cogit nec interiorem hominis habitum immediate intuetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX5","text":"Peccatum non est necessario effectus suggestionis daemonicae, quamvis nullum genus peccati sit quod interdum tali suggestione non contingat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX6","text":"Signum hominibus admirabile non est propter hoc miraculum proprie dictum nec testimonium veritatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX7","text":"Victoria contra daemonem non constituit immunitatem perpetuam ab omni futura temptatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D1","text":"Eadem actio daemonica formaliter sub malitia daemonis cadit et materialiter intra providentiam divinam ordinari potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A1","CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D2","text":"Tentatio daemonica est exploratio indirecta dispositionum humanarum ordinata ad electionem vitii opportunioris, non cognitio immediata voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A5","CH_GGVC__106:A6","CH_GGVC__106:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D3","text":"Suggestio daemonica causalitatem moralem habet per inclinationem et persuasionem, non per determinationem voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A8","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D4","text":"Universalis narratio de origine peccati servatur per causalitatem indirectam primi peccati, dum imputatio peccati singularis libero arbitrio reservatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A9","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D5","text":"Veritas rei effectae et veritas miraculi separandae sunt, quia daemon potest veros effectus naturales producere sine transgressione ordinis creati.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D6","text":"Discernimentum signorum non ex sola spectacularitate effectus, sed ex ordine causali, fine et auctoritate operationis procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D7","text":"Repulsio temptationis non destruit hostem, sed spatium resistendi instituit intra recurrentem conflictus possibilitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SD1","text":"Ordo moralium malorum fit asymmetricus: malum daemonicum agit ut parasiticum principium impugnans, dum bonum meritorium auxilium supernaturale requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A9","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SD2","text":"Providentia non tollit malitiam agentis secundarii, sed eam includit in ordine cuius finis bonus extrinsecus daemonis intentioni manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A1","CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SD3","text":"Epistemologia deceptionis constituitur ex discrimine inter apparentiam, effectum realem naturalem et miraculum proprie divinum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A7","CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SD4","text":"Conflictus spiritualis describitur ut regimen permissionum et auxilii, non ut autonomia absoluta daemonum neque ut securitas stabilis hominum post singulas victorias.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A4","CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet peccatum humanum mere extrinsecus daemonice productum; aliter libertas arbitrii et ratio propriae culpae evacuantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A8","CH_GGVC__106:A9","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet creaturam posse suam virtutem supra ordinem universae naturae extendere; aliter differentia Dei et daemonis causaliter collaberetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet admirationem sensibilem per se fidem vel veritatem confirmare; aliter signum diabolicum et miraculum divinum indiscreta fierent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet victoriam moralem semel factam in condicionem irrevocabilem converti; conflictus manet temporalis et reiterabilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SNX1","text":"Textus excludit dualismum in quo daemon et Deus essent principia causaliter commensurabilia, quia daemonis malitia, potestas et occasio intra ordinem divinum continentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A3","CH_GGVC__106:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SNX2","text":"Textus excludit libertatem humanam sibi sufficientem, quia homo potest cadere ex se, sed non potest ad meritum proficere sine gratia et ministerio angelico.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A4","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SNX3","text":"Textus excludit praesentiam divinam immediate legibilem ex eventu mirabili, quia idem campus sensibilis veros effectus naturales, phantasmata et miracula proprie dicta continere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:FGS1","text":"Malitia daemonica → suggestio et exploratio dispositionum → inclinatio virium inferiorum → possibilitas consensus liberi ad peccatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A1","CH_GGVC__106:A6","CH_GGVC__106:A7","CH_GGVC__106:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:FGS2","text":"Impugnatio mala → permissio et ordinatio divina → gratia et custodia angelica → exercitium, resistentia vel gloria electorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A3","CH_GGVC__106:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:FGS3","text":"Effectus extraordinarius → examen ordinis naturae → distinctio rei verae, apparentiae et miraculi → iudicium ex fine et iure operationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:FGS4","text":"Victoria contra tentationem → imminutio temporalis impugnationis → possibilitas reditus daemonis → perseverantia sub auxilio divino necessaria.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A4","CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF1","text":"Impugnatio daemonica apparenter iniusta → distinctio malitiae daemonicae et ordinis divini → compensatio per gratiam et Angelos → impugnatio permissa et ad bonum ordinabilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF2","text":"Ambiguitas vocabuli tentationis → distinctio finis experimentalis → proprium officium Diaboli ut nocentis → limitatio eius per ignorantiam interioris et impotentiam super voluntatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF3","text":"Apparens universalitas causae diabolicae → distinctio causalitatis indirectae et directae → reservatio peccati singularis libero arbitrio et carni corruptae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF4","text":"Apparens miraculum daemonis → distinctio miraculi proprii, effectus naturalis et phantasmatis → discernimentum per ordinem naturae, finem et ius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF5","text":"Victoria super tentatorem → recessus limitatus → reditus possibilis → conflictus temporalis sub divina permissione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ME1","text":"Causalitas mali redistribuitur inter originem indirectam diabolicam, suggestionem proximam possibilem, corruptionem carnis et consensum liberi arbitrii.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A8","CH_GGVC__106:A9","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ME2","text":"Oppositio simplex inter verum miraculum et mendacium dissolvitur in triplicem campum: miraculum divinum, effectus naturalis realis supra facultatem humanam, et apparentia phantastica.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ME3","text":"Impugnatio daemonica non tamquam potestas autonoma, sed tamquam actio hostilis intra regimen permissionis, auxilii et ordinationis divinae intelligibilis fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A1","CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ME4","text":"Victoria spiritualis reclassificatur ex eventu definitivo in actum resistentiae cui perseverantia et custodia ulterior requiruntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A4","CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ALT1","text":"Surface — Daemones homines impugnant, tentant, interdum effectus admirabiles producunt, et post victoriam aliquando recedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ALT2","text":"Structural — Impugnatio operatur per suggestionem, explorationem, immutationem virium inferiorum, causas naturales et deceptionem sensuum, non per dominationem voluntatis aut naturae universalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Textus certamen transfert ab oppositione simplici hominis et daemonis ad ordinem triadicum in quo gratia, ministerium angelicum, permissio divina et libertas humana constituunt campum pugnae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Deus solus ordinem totius naturae transcendit; creatura daemonica intra causationem creatam manet, et eius impugnatio temporaliter permittitur, restringitur atque reiterari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam seriem principalem: malitia daemonica movet impugnationem, providentia eam ordinat, libertas consensum retinet, gratia resistentiam et meritum sustentat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT2","text":"Systema cohaeret quia una distinctio graduum causalium—divinus, daemonicus, naturalis, voluntarius—simul solvendas quaestiones de tentatione, peccato, signis et victoria sustinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT3","text":"Firmissimum nodum constituit distinctio inter ordinem universalem naturae, potestatem creaturae et effectum sensibus admirabilem, quae daemonis potentiam simul concedit et limitat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter inclinationem inferiorum virium et libertatem voluntatis, quia modus quo inclinatio concreta ad consensum se habeat formaliter non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter recessum daemonis victi et possibilitatem reditus eius, quia restrictio temporalis affirmatur sine determinato criterio quo idem daemon, idem homo et idem genus temptationis discernantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia ab apparentibus exceptionibus ad distinctiones causales, limites negativos et ordinationem providentialem procedit, non quia omnes difficultates mechanicas exhaurit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170355677723Z_f1d63ac2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 114","source_sha256":"5d5b75c600f56a82bf5c5ac09ae41b0ca403aa998ce05ee4b9064771910d696c","sha256":"b9db5957357006add5a373765f420230122a3ce2ae6506a788ba152586a39ed5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:03:55.678660+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS1","text":"The question determines whether and in what order the assault of demons reaches human beings, without dissolving either divine governance or human responsibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS2","text":"The text divides the assault between the malice of the demon as proximate principle and the ordination of God as the ordering principle that refers evil to good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS3","text":"Temptation is reconstituted not from mere testing, but from the end of the tempter: the Devil tests in order to precipitate into sin, God manifests, and man either helps or harms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS4","text":"Demonic causality is limited by the distinctions of direct and indirect, voluntary and inclining, proper miracle and a work extraordinary naturally or phantasmatically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AS5","text":"The victory of a human being neither annihilates the demon nor excludes it perpetually, but temporarily restricts its assault under divine permission and hostile prudence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A1","text":"The assault of demons proceeds from envy of obstructing human advancement and from pride in imitating divine ministry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A2","text":"God uses evils in an ordered manner and can order the assault of demons to goods, especially to the glory of the elect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A3","text":"Demons inciting to sin are not sent by God, but are permitted by just judgment; they can be sent to inflict punishment under the end of divine justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A4","text":"The natural inequality between human being and demon is compensated principally by divine grace and secondarily by angelic guardianship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A5","text":"To tempt properly is to undertake a test so that something may be known about someone, but the species of temptation is determined by its further end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A6","text":"To tempt for harming and precipitating into sin is the proper office of the Devil, although others are said to tempt analogically or instrumentally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A7","text":"A demon does not have direct knowledge of a human being's interior condition, but investigates from externals to which vice the human being is more prone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A8","text":"A demon cannot change the human will, but by changing the lower powers it can incline the will without necessitating it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A9","text":"The Devil is an indirect cause of all sins by reason of the first sin and the proneness derived from it, but not the direct cause of each individual sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A10","text":"A human being can fall into sin of itself through free choice and the corruption of the flesh, but cannot advance to merit without divine aid administered through Angels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A11","text":"A miracle properly so called exceeds the order of the whole of created nature and belongs to God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A12","text":"Demons can dispose extraordinary natural effects through seeds and natural powers, or alter sensory appearances; they cannot produce effects transcending created nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A13","text":"Works similar in appearance are distinguished by their end and the right of operation: saints act under the public administration and command of God, magicians for their own glory through private dealings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:A14","text":"The restriction of a defeated demon proceeds from divine clemency and from the demon's fear lest it be defeated in repeated encounter, but its return remains possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX1","text":"Demonic assault is not a ministry of salvation entrusted to demons by God, even if its outcome can be ordered by divine providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX2","text":"The contest of a human being with demons is not a struggle of natural equals, yet neither is the human being, on account of inequality, deprived of grace and divine guardianship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX3","text":"Temptation is not attributed univocally to the Devil, because God, human being, flesh, and world are said to tempt for different reasons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX4","text":"A demon neither compels the will nor immediately beholds the human being's interior disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX5","text":"Sin is not necessarily the effect of demonic suggestion, although there is no kind of sin that is not at times affected by such suggestion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX6","text":"A sign marvelous to human beings is not, on that account, a miracle properly so called or a testimony of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:NX7","text":"Victory against a demon does not establish perpetual immunity from every future temptation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D1","text":"The same demonic action formally falls under the demon's malice and can materially be ordered within divine providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A1","CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D2","text":"Demonic temptation is an indirect investigation of human dispositions ordered toward the selection of the more opportune vice, not immediate knowledge of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A5","CH_GGVC__106:A6","CH_GGVC__106:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D3","text":"Demonic suggestion has moral causality through inclination and persuasion, not through determination of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A8","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D4","text":"The universal account of the origin of sin is preserved through the indirect causality of the first sin, while the imputation of individual sin is reserved to free choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A9","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D5","text":"The truth of the effect produced and the truth of miracle must be separated, because a demon can produce true natural effects without transgressing the created order.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D6","text":"Discernment of signs proceeds not from the effect's spectacularity alone, but from the causal order, the end, and the authority of the operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:D7","text":"The repulsion of temptation does not destroy the enemy, but establishes a space for resistance within the possibility of recurrent conflict.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SD1","text":"The order of moral evils becomes asymmetric: demonic evil acts as a parasitic assailing principle, while meritorious good requires supernatural aid.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A9","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SD2","text":"Providence does not remove the malice of the secondary agent, but includes it within an order whose good end remains extrinsic to the demon's intention.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A1","CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SD3","text":"An epistemology of deception is constituted by the distinction between appearance, real natural effect, and properly divine miracle.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A7","CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SD4","text":"Spiritual conflict is described as a regime of permissions and aid, not as the absolute autonomy of demons nor as the stable security of human beings after individual victories.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A4","CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:DNX1","text":"It must be false that human sin is produced merely extrinsically by demons; otherwise freedom of choice and the rationale of personal guilt are emptied.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A8","CH_GGVC__106:A9","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:DNX2","text":"It must be false that a creature can extend its power above the order of universal nature; otherwise the distinction between God and demon would collapse causally.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:DNX3","text":"It must be false that sensible wonder in itself confirms faith or truth; otherwise a demonic sign and a divine miracle would become indistinguishable.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:DNX4","text":"It must be false that a moral victory once achieved is converted into an irrevocable condition; conflict remains temporal and reiterable.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SNX1","text":"The text excludes a dualism in which demon and God would be causally commensurable principles, because the demon's malice, power, and opportunity are contained within the divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A3","CH_GGVC__106:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SNX2","text":"The text excludes human freedom sufficient unto itself, because a human being can fall of itself but cannot advance to merit without grace and angelic ministry.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A4","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:SNX3","text":"The text excludes a divine presence immediately legible from a marvelous event, because the same sensible field can contain true natural effects, phantasms, and miracles properly so called.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:FGS1","text":"Demonic malice → suggestion and investigation of dispositions → inclination of lower powers → possibility of free consent to sin.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A1","CH_GGVC__106:A6","CH_GGVC__106:A7","CH_GGVC__106:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:FGS2","text":"Evil assault → divine permission and ordination → grace and angelic guardianship → exercise, resistance, or glory of the elect.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A3","CH_GGVC__106:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:FGS3","text":"Extraordinary effect → examination of the order of nature → distinction of true thing, appearance, and miracle → judgment from the end and right of operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12","CH_GGVC__106:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:FGS4","text":"Victory against temptation → temporary diminution of assault → possibility of the demon's return → perseverance under divine aid necessary.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A4","CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF1","text":"Demonic assault apparently unjust → distinction of demonic malice and divine order → compensation through grace and Angels → assault permitted and capable of being ordered to good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF2","text":"Ambiguity of the term temptation → distinction of the experimental end → the proper office of the Devil as one harming → its limitation through ignorance of the interior and impotence over the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF3","text":"Apparent universality of the diabolical cause → distinction of indirect and direct causality → reservation of individual sin to free choice and corrupted flesh.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF4","text":"Apparent miracle of a demon → distinction of proper miracle, natural effect, and phantasm → discernment through the order of nature, end, and right.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:AF5","text":"Victory over the tempter → limited withdrawal → possible return → temporal conflict under divine permission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ME1","text":"The causality of evil is redistributed among indirect diabolical origin, possible proximate suggestion, corruption of the flesh, and consent of free choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A8","CH_GGVC__106:A9","CH_GGVC__106:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ME2","text":"The simple opposition between true miracle and falsehood is dissolved into a threefold field: divine miracle, real natural effect beyond human capacity, and phantasmal appearance.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A11","CH_GGVC__106:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ME3","text":"Demonic assault becomes intelligible not as autonomous power, but as hostile action within the regime of divine permission, aid, and ordination.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A1","CH_GGVC__106:A2","CH_GGVC__106:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ME4","text":"Spiritual victory is reclassified from a definitive event into an act of resistance requiring perseverance and further guardianship.","refs":["CH_GGVC__106:A4","CH_GGVC__106:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ALT1","text":"Surface — Demons assault and tempt human beings, sometimes produce marvelous effects, and after defeat occasionally withdraw.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ALT2","text":"Structural — Assault operates through suggestion, investigation, alteration of lower powers, natural causes, and sensory deception, not through domination of the will or of universal nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text transfers the contest from a simple opposition of human being and demon to a triadic order in which grace, angelic ministry, divine permission, and human freedom constitute the field of battle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — God alone transcends the order of the whole of nature; the demonic creature remains within created causation, and its assault is permitted, restricted, and can be reiterated temporally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the principal sequence: demonic malice moves assault, providence orders it, freedom retains consent, and grace sustains resistance and merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT2","text":"The system coheres because one distinction of causal levels—divine, demonic, natural, voluntary—supports at once the questions to be resolved concerning temptation, sin, signs, and victory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT3","text":"The firmest knot consists in the distinction between the universal order of nature, the power of a creature, and an effect marvelous to the senses, which simultaneously grants and limits the demon's power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains between the inclination of lower powers and the freedom of the will, because the manner in which concrete inclination relates to consent is not formally explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains between the withdrawal of a defeated demon and the possibility of its return, because temporary restriction is affirmed without a determined criterion by which the same demon, the same human being, and the same kind of temptation are distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0086","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__106:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because it proceeds from apparent exceptions to causal distinctions, negative limits, and providential ordination, not because it exhausts all mechanical difficulties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__106:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__106@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__106:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 115","title":"First Part · Question 114","context":"Chapter 115","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 114"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 114","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 115","order":116,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__107"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__107@R001","sha256":"e8221771024f31696465a4fbc4419eefcbfd233fbf9444869c6eb3badc48f684","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS1","text":"Quaestio est quo pacto creatura corporalis vere agat, quousque causalitas caelestis extendatur et utrum ex ea necessitas effectuum sequatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS2","text":"Corpus agit secundum actum in corpus secundum potentiam, sed eius causalitas materialiter contracta, mediata et impedibilis est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS3","text":"Argumentatio diagnostica et reconstructiva falsas explicationes actionis corporalis removet, deinde causalitatem per gradus ontologicos distribuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS4","text":"Motus initialis procedit ab apparentia actionis corporalis ad principium actus et potentiae, atque inde ad definitionem rationum seminalium ut virtutum naturalium activarum et passivarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS5","text":"Motus medius causalitatem caelestem inferioribus corporibus tribuit, sed intellectum, voluntatem et substantias daemonicas ab eius dominio eximit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS6","text":"Motus finalis transit a causalitate caelesti ad eius limites: libertatem voluntatis, defectibilitatem causarum particularium et irreducibilitatem concursus per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A1","text":"Agere est aliquid facere actu et actui, inquantum actus est, per se competit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A2","text":"Corpus, quia ex actu et potentia componitur, agit secundum quod est actu et patitur secundum quod est in potentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A3","text":"Determinatio formae per materiam quantitati subiectam actionem non tollit, sed eam ad causalitatem particularem contrahit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A4","text":"Qualitas activa propria virtute causat formam accidentalem et, ut instrumentum formae substantialis, ad formam substantialem agit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A5","text":"Rationes seminales sunt virtutes activae et passivae quae generationum et motuum naturalium principia constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A6","text":"Virtutes naturales sunt idealiter in Verbo, universaliter in elementis, particulariter in rebus successive productis et ulterius causaliter in seminibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A7","text":"Miracula non fiunt praeter rationes ideales aut omnem potentiam passivam creaturae, sed praeter virtutes naturales activas et potentias passivas eis ordinatas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A8","text":"Omnis motus ab immobili procedit, et ea quae sunt immobiliora causaliter ordinantur ad ea quae sunt mobiliora.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A9","text":"Qualitates activae inferiorum corporum sunt dispositiones materiales ad formas substantiales neque ad earum diversitatem producendam per se sufficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A10","text":"Variatio generationis et corruptionis requirit principium activum mobile cuius praesentia et absentia variantur; hoc munus corporibus caelestibus attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A11","text":"Virtus caelestis effectus inferiores virtualiter continet, sed secundum diversas dispositiones materiae diversimode recipitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A12","text":"Corpora caelestia in corpora directe et per se imprimunt, in vires autem animae organis alligatas directe sed per accidens ratione organorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A13","text":"Intellectus et voluntas non sunt actus organorum corporeorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A14","text":"Intellectus necessario accipit ab inferioribus viribus apprehensivis, voluntas autem inclinationem appetitus sensitivi sequi vel refutare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A15","text":"Daemones sunt substantiae intellectuales corporibus non unitae atque ideo actioni caelestium corporum nullo modo subduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A16","text":"Daemones dispositionibus naturalibus ut mediis utuntur easque intentionaliter eligunt, non quasi ab eis passive determinati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A17","text":"Virtus caelestis, quia finita, effectus producit mediantibus causis particularibus et materia determinate disposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A18","text":"Quod est per se causam habet; concursus autem per accidens, quia non est vere unum ens, causam ut talis non habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX1","text":"Actiones corporales non sunt omnes actiones virtutis spiritualis corpora penetrantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX2","text":"Forma corporalis quantitate individuata non est agens universale, sed ex hoc non sequitur eam omnino non agere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX3","text":"Actio corporalis non consistit in motu locali aut effluxione partium agentis in patiens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX4","text":"Accidens non causat formam substantialem ut causa principalis, sed potest eam causare ut instrumentum formae substantialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX5","text":"Rationes seminales non sunt entia spiritualiter exsistentia in materia, sed virtutes materiales sic nominatae ex origine ideali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX6","text":"Semen non significat tantum principium activum, quia sub eo etiam principium passivum generationis comprehenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX7","text":"Rationes ideales sunt causales, sed non proprie seminales, quia semen principium separatum non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX8","text":"Corpora caelestia non sunt prima causa generationis et corruptionis neque numina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX9","text":"Qualitates elementares inferiores neque species separatae immobiles sufficiunt ad variationem temporalem generationis et corruptionis explicandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX10","text":"Corpora caelestia non causant electiones et actus humanos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX11","text":"Intellectus non reducitur ad sensum, nec homo instinctu naturali ad actiones suas necessario determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX12","text":"Praedictiones astrologicae non sunt infallibiles in singularibus neque libertatem voluntatis destruunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX13","text":"Daemones neque effectus ficti virtutis caelestis neque animalia corpore aerea et passiva sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0105","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX14","text":"Posita quacumque causa, effectus non semper ex necessitate ponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D1","text":"Actio corporis individuati est particularis transitus ab actu huius corporis ad potentiam alterius corporis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D2","text":"Corpus potest efficere mutationes tam accidentales quam substantiales, quia eius qualitas activa duplicem causalitatem, propriam et instrumentalem, exercet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D3","text":"Nomen rationis seminalis materiae convenit analogice ex ordine virtutis materialis ad rationem idealem originariam.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D4","text":"Eadem causalitas naturalis secundum gradus diversos universaliter vel particulariter existit, non ut idem principium numero, sed ut ordo virtutum correspondentium.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D5","text":"Agens inferius movet materiam ad speciem ut instrumentum corporis caelestis, dum corpus caeleste variationem generationis ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A8","CH_GGVC__107:A9","CH_GGVC__107:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D6","text":"Unitas influxus caelestis non inducit uniformitatem effectuum, quia receptio variatur secundum dispositionem materiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D7","text":"Impressio caelestis imaginationem et passiones per organa attingit, intellectum indirecte perturbare potest, voluntatem autem necessario non determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D8","text":"Astrologia eventus humanos in communi et ut in pluribus praedicere potest quatenus plures homines passiones sequuntur, non quatenus voluntas necessario astris subiacet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D9","text":"Concordantia operationum daemonum cum luna aut constellationibus significat electionem materiae aptae vel intentionem deceptionis, non passionem daemonis ab astro.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D10","text":"Res corporales et ritus daemones alliciunt ut signa honoris ab eis intellecta, non ut causae physice cogentes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D11","text":"Actio voluntaria potest effectum caelestem impedire tam in homine quam in rebus exterioribus operationi humanae subiectis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D12","text":"Effectus naturales possunt deficere sine causa necessitante defectum, quia causae particulares sunt impedibiles et earum concursus potest esse per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD1","text":"Causalitas systematis est stratificata et non competitiva: causa superior inferioribus agentibus causalitatem non aufert, sed per ea operatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A6","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD2","text":"Universalitas causae caelestis est relativa et virtualis: latius quam agens inferius operatur, sed neque causalitatem divinam neque actionem universalem simpliciter possidet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD3","text":"Immaterialitas potentiae constituit terminum causalitatis corporalis, quamvis non omnem dependentiam indirectam a corpore removeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD4","text":"Fatum caeleste, si admittitur, restringitur ad ordinem corporeum, ut in pluribus operantem, nec voluntatem aut substantias intellectuales claudit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD5","text":"Contingentia naturalis non est sola ignorantia causae, sed consequitur defectibilitatem causarum particularium et non-unitatem concursus per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD6","text":"Miraculum ordinem activum naturae excedit sine abolitione originis idealis aut receptivitatis creatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6","CH_GGVC__107:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX1","text":"Systema tacite excludit notionem univocam actionis secundum quam omnis causa eodem modo et eodem gradu operetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX2","text":"Causa superior causam inferiorem non reddit inanem; exclusa est causalitas summa tamquam monopolium quod operationes proximas absorbeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX3","text":"Dependentia causalis non importat per se necessitatem effectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX4","text":"Regularis concordantia temporis, corporis et eventus non sufficit ad probandam subiectionem causalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX5","text":"Non omnis aggregatio factorum est unum ens cui causa propria assignari debeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX6","text":"Immaterialitas intellectus non requirit independentiam operationalem absolutam ab imaginatione, memoria et aliis viribus organicis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX7","text":"Libertas non definitur absentia passionum vel inclinationum, sed potestas voluntatis eas sequendi aut refutandi.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX8","text":"Usus instrumentalis dispositionum corporalium non aequatur passioni aut subiectioni agentis intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX1","text":"Impossibilis habetur clausura astralis in qua omnes motus, electiones et operationes spirituales in unam necessitatem cosmicam reducuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX2","text":"Systema nullum planum causale homogeneum admittit in quo materia, corpus, anima organica, intellectus et spiritus eodem modo patiantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX3","text":"Excluditur alternativa absoluta inter solam causalitatem spiritualem et solam mechanicam corporalem; ordo requirit causalitates formales, instrumentales, materiales et intellectuales simul distinctas.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A6","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX4","text":"Praecluditur totalizatio retrospectiva qua omnis concursus fortuitus in causam praeexistentem et necessitantem resolvatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0131","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX5","text":"Nulla causa creata possidet iurisdictionem simul universalem, immediatam et infallibilem super omnes ordines effectuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS1","text":"Prima generatio sequitur seriem: compositio actus et potentiae → corpus simul agens et patiens → realitas actionis corporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS2","text":"Determinatio causalis sequitur seriem: forma in materia quantificata → individuatio → actio particularis, non abolitio actionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS3","text":"Generatio naturalis sequitur seriem: ratio idealis → virtus universalis elementaris → causa particularis → semen → effectus naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS4","text":"Causalitas inferiorum sequitur seriem: principium caeleste mobile → causa particularis instrumentalis → dispositio materiae → effectus variabilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A9","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS5","text":"Terminus anthropologicus sequitur seriem: impressio caelestis in corpus → affectio virium organicarum → inclinatio vel perturbatio → iudicium intellectus indirecte affectum → voluntas non necessitata.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS6","text":"Terminus daemonicus sequitur seriem: substantia intellectualis incorporea → electio dispositionis naturalis vel signi → operatio mediata → nulla passio a corpore caelesti.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS7","text":"Contingentia sequitur seriem: causa ut in pluribus → causa particularis defectibilis → concursus per accidens → effectus non necessarius → impossibilitas reductionis ad causam praeexistentem unam.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF1","text":"Primus articulus procedit ab apparentia actionis corporalis → errores negantes vel mechanice transferentes actionem → distinctio actus et potentiae → affirmatio corporis ut agentis particularis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF2","text":"Secundus articulus procedit a difficultate rationis in materia → derivatio vocabuli a generatione viventium → definitio virtutum activarum et passivarum → ordinatio quadripartita rationum seminalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF3","text":"Tertius articulus procedit ab insufficientia qualitatum inferiorum et specierum immobilium → necessitas principii activi mobilis → causalitas caelestis → diversificatio per materiam recipientem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF4","text":"Quartus articulus procedit ab impressione caelesti in corpus → discrimen potentiarum organicarum et immaterialium → distinctio intellectus et voluntatis → negatio necessitatis actuum humanorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF5","text":"Quintus articulus procedit a correlationibus daemonum cum corporibus → reiectio daemonum fictorum vel corporeorum → natura intellectualis incorporea → interpretatio correlationum ut usus mediorum et signorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF6","text":"Sextus articulus procedit a specie necessitatis universalis → causae operantes ut in pluribus → impedimenta particularia → distinctio per se et per accidens → contingentia effectuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME1","text":"Corpus ex ultimo patiente in compositum agens et patiens reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME2","text":"Rationes seminales ex quasi entitatibus spiritualibus in materia in ordinem virtutum naturalium activarum et passivarum transferuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME3","text":"Corpora caelestia inter causas reales sed secundarias, mediatas, finitas et materialiter impedibiles collocantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME4","text":"Oppositio inter influxum corporalem et libertatem dissolvitur distinguendo inclinationem organicam a determinatione voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME5","text":"Concordantiae astrologicae et rituales ex probationibus subiectionis in indices dispositionis materialis, consuetudinis passionum vel intentionis spiritualis mutantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME6","text":"Casus ex effectu causae occultae necessariae in effectum concursus qui ut concursus causam non habet reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ALT1","text":"Surface — In superficie examinantur actio corporum, rationes seminales, causalitas caelestis, actus humani, daemones et necessitas effectuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ALT2","text":"Structural — Structura operatur per compositionem actus et potentiae, instrumentalitatem causarum inferiorum, mediationem caelestem et diversitatem recipientium.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Certamen conceptuale a dilemmate inter inertiam corporis et necessitatem cosmicam ad quaestionem graduum, mediorum et limitum causalitatis transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Realitas distribuitur inter potentiam puram, corpora actu et potentia composita, potentias immateriales et ordinem idealem; temporalitas generationis oritur ex praesentia, absentia, successione et concursu causarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A6","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad sex articulos restituendos, quia actionem corporalem, ordinem seminalem, causalitatem caelestem eiusque limites continent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT2","text":"Nondum hic demonstrantur fundamenta recepta de immaterialitate intellectus, natura daemonum et ordine motus caelestis; quaestio ea partim ex tractationibus prioribus assumit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT3","text":"Structura interne cohaeret per distinctiones actus et potentiae, causae principalis et instrumentalis, actionis directae et indirectae, atque causalitatis per se et per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT4","text":"Firmissima commissura est distinctio inter inclinationem organicam et determinationem voluntatis, quia simul influxum corporalem et libertatem servat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter contractionem particularem formae corporalis et universalem virtutem corporis caelestis; cohaerentia pendet ex universalitate relativa et virtuali, non simpliciter formali.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT6","text":"Tensio inter reductionem motuum inferiorum ad caelestia et irreducibilitatem concursus per accidens solvitur distinguendo causas factorum concurrentium a causa ipsius concursus.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A8","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0131","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT7","text":"Dependentia operationis daemonicae a mediis naturalibus sine subiectione daemonis constat tantum si usus intentionalis instrumenti a passione agentis stricte distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT8","text":"Distinctio inter potentiam passivam creaturae universaliter receptivam et potentias passivas ordinatas agentibus naturalibus necessaria est ad doctrinam miraculi, sed hic breviter tantum formalizatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT9","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: affirmatio agentiae corporalis → ordinatio virtutum naturalium → extensio causalitatis caelestis → exclusio intellectuum et voluntatis → negatio necessitatis universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:AF1","CH_GGVC__107:AF2","CH_GGVC__107:AF3","CH_GGVC__107:AF4","CH_GGVC__107:AF5","CH_GGVC__107:AF6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170428631764Z_9b540a41","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 115","source_sha256":"e8221771024f31696465a4fbc4419eefcbfd233fbf9444869c6eb3badc48f684","sha256":"c4e7c302a46e8f35f4956d3001c36354a72ba551055fca2e4a1f7aa0799cdbae","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:04:28.634072+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS1","text":"The question is how a bodily creature truly acts, how far celestial causality extends, and whether the necessity of effects follows from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS2","text":"A body acts according to act upon a body according to potency, but its causality is materially contracted, mediated, and impedible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS3","text":"The diagnostic and reconstructive argument removes false explanations of bodily action, then distributes causality through ontological grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS4","text":"The initial movement proceeds from the appearance of bodily action to the principle of act and potency, and thence to the definition of seminal reasons as active and passive natural powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS5","text":"The middle movement attributes celestial causality to lower bodies, but exempts intellect, will, and demonic substances from its dominion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AS6","text":"The final movement passes from celestial causality to its limits: freedom of the will, the defectibility of particular causes, and the irreducibility of concurrence per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A1","text":"To act is to make something actual, and it belongs per se to act, insofar as it is act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A2","text":"A body, because it is composed of act and potency, acts insofar as it is in act and is acted upon insofar as it is in potency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A3","text":"The determination of form through matter subject to quantity does not remove action, but contracts it to particular causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A4","text":"An active quality causes an accidental form by its own power and, as an instrument of substantial form, acts toward substantial form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A5","text":"Seminal reasons are active and passive powers that constitute the principles of natural generations and motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A6","text":"Natural powers are ideally in the Word, universally in the elements, particularly in successively produced things, and further causally in seeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A7","text":"Miracles occur neither beyond ideal reasons nor beyond every passive potency of the creature, but beyond active natural powers and the passive potencies ordered to them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A8","text":"Every motion proceeds from an immobile source, and those things that are more immobile are causally ordered to those that are more mobile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A9","text":"The active qualities of lower bodies are material dispositions toward substantial forms and do not suffice per se to produce their diversity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A10","text":"The variation of generation and corruption requires a mobile active principle whose presence and absence vary; this role is attributed to celestial bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A11","text":"Celestial power virtually contains lower effects, but is received differently according to different dispositions of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A12","text":"Celestial bodies impress directly and per se upon bodies, but upon powers of the soul bound to organs directly yet per accidens by reason of the organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A13","text":"Intellect and will are not acts of bodily organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A14","text":"The intellect necessarily receives from lower apprehensive powers, whereas the will can follow or reject the inclination of the sensitive appetite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A15","text":"Demons are intellectual substances not united to bodies and therefore are in no way subject to the action of celestial bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A16","text":"Demons use natural dispositions as means and intentionally choose them, not as though passively determined by them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A17","text":"Celestial power, because it is finite, produces effects through particular causes and matter determinately disposed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:A18","text":"That which is per se has a cause; but concurrence per accidens, because it is not truly one being, has no cause as such.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX1","text":"Bodily actions are not all actions of a spiritual power penetrating bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX2","text":"A bodily form individuated by quantity is not a universal agent, but it does not follow from this that it does not act at all.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX3","text":"Bodily action does not consist in local motion or in an efflux of the agent's parts into the patient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX4","text":"An accident does not cause substantial form as a principal cause, but can cause it as an instrument of substantial form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX5","text":"Seminal reasons are not beings existing spiritually in matter, but material powers so named from their ideal origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX6","text":"Seed does not signify only an active principle, because under it the passive principle of generation is also comprehended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX7","text":"Ideal reasons are causal, but not properly seminal, because seed is not a separate principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX8","text":"Celestial bodies are neither the first cause of generation and corruption nor deities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX9","text":"Neither the elementary qualities of lower bodies nor immobile separate species suffice to explain the temporal variation of generation and corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX10","text":"Celestial bodies do not cause human choices and acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX11","text":"The intellect is not reduced to sense, nor is man necessarily determined by natural instinct to his actions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX12","text":"Astrological predictions are not infallible in singulars and do not destroy freedom of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX13","text":"Demons are neither fictitious effects of celestial power nor animals with aerial and passive bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0105","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:NX14","text":"Given any cause, its effect is not always posited of necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D1","text":"The action of an individuated body is a particular transition from the act of this body to the potency of another body.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D2","text":"A body can bring about both accidental and substantial changes, because its active quality exercises a twofold causality, proper and instrumental.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D3","text":"The name of seminal reason belongs to matter analogically from the ordering of material power to the original ideal reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D4","text":"The same natural causality exists universally or particularly according to different grades, not as the same principle numerically, but as an order of corresponding powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D5","text":"A lower agent moves matter toward species as an instrument of a celestial body, while the celestial body orders the variation of generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A8","CH_GGVC__107:A9","CH_GGVC__107:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D6","text":"The unity of celestial influx does not induce uniformity of effects, because reception varies according to the disposition of matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D7","text":"Celestial impression reaches imagination and passions through organs, can indirectly disturb the intellect, but does not necessarily determine the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D8","text":"Astrology can predict human events in general and for the most part insofar as most human beings follow passions, not insofar as the will is necessarily subject to the stars.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0094","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D9","text":"The agreement of the operations of demons with the moon or constellations signifies the choice of suitable matter or an intention of deception, not the passion of a demon from a star.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D10","text":"Bodily things and rites attract demons as signs of honor understood by them, not as physically compelling causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D11","text":"Voluntary action can impede a celestial effect both in man and in external things subject to human operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0123","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:D12","text":"Natural effects can fail without a cause necessitating the failure, because particular causes are impedible and their concurrence can be per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD1","text":"The causality of the system is stratified and non-competitive: a higher cause does not remove causality from lower agents, but operates through them.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A6","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD2","text":"The universality of celestial cause is relative and virtual: it operates more broadly than a lower agent, but possesses neither divine causality nor universal action simply speaking.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD3","text":"The immateriality of a power constitutes the limit of bodily causality, although it does not remove every indirect dependence on the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD4","text":"Celestial fate, if admitted, is restricted to the corporeal order, operating for the most part, and does not enclose the will or intellectual substances.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD5","text":"Natural contingency is not mere ignorance of a cause, but follows from the defectibility of particular causes and the non-unity of concurrence per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SD6","text":"A miracle exceeds the active order of nature without abolishing ideal origin or created receptivity.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6","CH_GGVC__107:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX1","text":"The system tacitly excludes a univocal notion of action according to which every cause operates in the same way and at the same grade.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX2","text":"A higher cause does not render a lower cause empty; supreme causality is excluded as a monopoly that absorbs proximate operations.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX3","text":"Causal dependence does not per se entail necessity of effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX4","text":"Regular agreement of time, body, and event does not suffice to prove causal subjection.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX5","text":"Not every aggregation of factors is one being to which a proper cause ought to be assigned.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX6","text":"The immateriality of the intellect does not require absolute operational independence from imagination, memory, and other organic powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX7","text":"Freedom is not defined by the absence of passions or inclinations, but by the power of the will to follow or reject them.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:DNX8","text":"The instrumental use of bodily dispositions is not equivalent to the passion or subjection of an intellectual agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX1","text":"An astral closure is held impossible in which all motions, choices, and spiritual operations are reduced to a single cosmic necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX2","text":"The system admits no homogeneous causal plane in which matter, body, organic soul, intellect, and spirit undergo affection in the same way.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX3","text":"The absolute alternative between solely spiritual causality and solely mechanical bodily causality is excluded; order requires formal, instrumental, material, and intellectual causalities, distinct at once.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A6","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX4","text":"The retrospective totalization whereby every fortuitous concurrence is resolved into a pre-existing and necessitating cause is foreclosed.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0131","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:SNX5","text":"No created cause possesses simultaneously universal, immediate, and infallible jurisdiction over all orders of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS1","text":"The first generation follows the series: composition of act and potency → body at once acting and acted upon → reality of bodily action.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS2","text":"Causal determination follows the series: form in quantified matter → individuation → particular action, not abolition of action.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS3","text":"Natural generation follows the series: ideal reason → universal elementary power → particular cause → seed → natural effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS4","text":"The causality of lower things follows the series: mobile celestial principle → particular instrumental cause → disposition of matter → variable effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A9","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS5","text":"The anthropological limit follows the series: celestial impression upon the body → affection of organic powers → inclination or disturbance → judgment of intellect indirectly affected → will not necessitated.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS6","text":"The demonic limit follows the series: incorporeal intellectual substance → choice of natural disposition or sign → mediated operation → no passion from a celestial body.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:FGS7","text":"Contingency follows the series: cause as in the majority of cases → defectible particular cause → concurrence per accidens → non-necessary effect → impossibility of reduction to one pre-existing cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF1","text":"The first article proceeds from the appearance of bodily action → errors denying or mechanically transferring action → distinction of act and potency → affirmation of the body as a particular agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF2","text":"The second article proceeds from the difficulty of reason in matter → derivation of the term from the generation of living things → definition of active and passive powers → fourfold ordering of seminal reasons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF3","text":"The third article proceeds from the insufficiency of lower qualities and immobile species → necessity of a mobile active principle → celestial causality → diversification through receiving matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF4","text":"The fourth article proceeds from celestial impression upon the body → distinction of organic and immaterial powers → distinction of intellect and will → denial of the necessity of human acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF5","text":"The fifth article proceeds from correlations of demons with bodies → rejection of fictitious or bodily demons → incorporeal intellectual nature → interpretation of correlations as use of means and signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:AF6","text":"The sixth article proceeds from the appearance of universal necessity → causes operating for the most part → particular impediments → distinction of per se and per accidens → contingency of effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME1","text":"The body is reclassified from a merely ultimate patient into a composite acting and acted upon.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME2","text":"Seminal reasons are transferred from quasi-spiritual entities in matter into an order of active and passive natural powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME3","text":"Celestial bodies are placed among real but secondary, mediated, finite, and materially impedible causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME4","text":"The opposition between bodily influx and freedom is dissolved by distinguishing organic inclination from determination of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME5","text":"Astrological and ritual agreements are transformed from proofs of subjection into indices of material disposition, habitual passions, or spiritual intention.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A11","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ME6","text":"Chance is reclassified from an effect of a necessary hidden cause into an effect of concurrence which, as concurrence, has no cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ALT1","text":"Surface — At the surface are examined the action of bodies, seminal reasons, celestial causality, human acts, demons, and the necessity of effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ALT2","text":"Structural — The structure operates through the composition of act and potency, the instrumentality of lower causes, celestial mediation, and diversity of recipients.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The conceptual contest is transferred from the dilemma between the inertia of body and cosmic necessity to the question of grades, means, and limits of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A14","CH_GGVC__107:A17","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Reality is distributed among pure potency, bodies composed of act and potency, immaterial powers, and the ideal order; the temporality of generation arises from the presence, absence, succession, and concurrence of causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A2","CH_GGVC__107:A6","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the six articles, because they contain bodily action, the seminal order, celestial causality, and its limits.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A5","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT2","text":"The received foundations concerning the immateriality of the intellect, the nature of demons, and the order of celestial motion are not yet demonstrated here; the question partly assumes them from earlier treatments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT3","text":"The structure coheres internally through the distinctions of act and potency, principal and instrumental cause, direct and indirect action, and causality per se and per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A1","CH_GGVC__107:A4","CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT4","text":"The strongest joint is the distinction between organic inclination and determination of the will, because it preserves bodily influx and freedom simultaneously.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A12","CH_GGVC__107:A13","CH_GGVC__107:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT5","text":"A fragile joint remains between the particular contraction of bodily form and the universal power of the celestial body; coherence depends upon relative and virtual universality, not simply formal universality.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A3","CH_GGVC__107:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT6","text":"The tension between the reduction of lower motions to celestial ones and the irreducibility of concurrence per accidens is resolved by distinguishing the causes of the concurrent factors from the cause of the concurrence itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A8","CH_GGVC__107:A10","CH_GGVC__107:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0125","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0131","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT7","text":"The dependence of demonic operation on natural means without subjection of the demon holds only if the intentional use of an instrument is strictly distinguished from the passion of the agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A15","CH_GGVC__107:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT8","text":"The distinction between the universally receptive passive potency of the creature and the passive potencies ordered to natural agents is necessary for the doctrine of miracle, but is only briefly formalized here.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__107:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: affirmation of bodily agency → ordering of natural powers → extension of celestial causality → exclusion of intellects and will → denial of universal necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC__107:AF1","CH_GGVC__107:AF2","CH_GGVC__107:AF3","CH_GGVC__107:AF4","CH_GGVC__107:AF5","CH_GGVC__107:AF6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__107:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__107@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__107:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 116","title":"First Part · Question 115","context":"Chapter 116","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 115"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 115","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 116","order":117,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__108"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__108@R001","sha256":"abbbe254e5b0b00e757c939e23f7ce0b496941bec8ec151ac5904b5242c06cde","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS1","text":"Quaestio fatum non ut causam autonomam, sed ut modum ordinandi inter providentiam divinam, causas secundas, contingentiam et eventus humanos constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS2","text":"Eventus fortuitus respectu causarum proximarum potest esse intentus respectu causae superioris intellectivae, ita ut casus localis providentiam universalem non destruat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS3","text":"Fatum astrale repudiatur, quia corpora caelestia neque actus voluntarios per se neque eventus per accidens efficere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS4","text":"Fatum definitur ut ordo causarum secundarum ad effectus a providentia divina praeordinatos, non ut ipsa providentia neque ut substantia una intra creaturas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS5","text":"Ordo fatalis mobilis est secundum mutationem causarum creatarum, sed immutabilis conditionaliter secundum dependentiam ab immobili providentia; ad ea tantum patet quae per causas secundas procedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A1","text":"Id quod est fortuitum vel casuale respectu causae inferioris potest esse per se intentum respectu causae superioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A2","text":"Eventus per accidens non est effectus per se alicuius principii naturalis agentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A3","text":"Intellectus potest id quod per accidens accidit sub una ratione apprehendere et ordinare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A4","text":"Providentia divina est causa ordinans eventus qui respectu causarum creatarum casuales apparent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A5","text":"Solus Deus voluntatem immutare potest; ideo ordinatio actuum humanorum ultimo Deo attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A6","text":"Corpora caelestia agunt ut principia naturalia et non sunt causae directae actuum humanorum voluntariorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A7","text":"Providentia divina effectus suos per causas medias seu secundas exsequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A8","text":"Fatum essentialiter est dispositio vel ordo causarum secundarum dependentium a Deo ad effectus producendos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A9","text":"Ordo fatalis, ut relatio, unus est respectu principii divini et multiplicatur respectu causarum mediarum vel effectuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A10","text":"Causae secundae sunt mutabiles; quare fatum, secundum ipsas causas consideratum, mobile est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A11","text":"Dependentia fati ab immobili providentia necessitatem conditionalem constituit, non necessitatem absolutam omnium eventuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A12","text":"Quae immediate a Deo fiunt nec causis secundis subduntur, fato non subduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A13","text":"Quanto aliquid magis causis secundis subicitur et a prima mente distat, tanto magis nexibus fati implicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX1","text":"Fatum non est dispositio siderum tempore conceptionis vel nativitatis constituta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX2","text":"Fatum non est causa naturalis per se eventuum accidentalium, fortuitorum vel casualium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX3","text":"Fatum non tollit casum et fortunam secundum comparationem ad causas proximas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX4","text":"Fatum non est ipsa providentia divina essentialiter, sed eius ordinatio in causis secundis recepta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX5","text":"Fatum non est substantia neque qualitas multiplicata secundum multitudinem creaturarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX6","text":"Immutabilitas fati non importat necessitatem absolutam neque exclusionem contingentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX7","text":"Non omnia quae divinae voluntati et potestati subduntur eo ipso subduntur fato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX8","text":"Nomen “fatum” non recipitur sine cautela, quia facile ad necessitatem stellarum et determinismum astralem transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D1","text":"Contingentia eventus non consistit in carentia omnis ordinis, sed in eius relatione ad causas proximas deficientes vel ignorantes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A1","CH_GGVC__108:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D2","text":"Eventus accidentaliter unus in ordine naturali potest esse intentionaliter unus in ordine intellectus divini.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A2","CH_GGVC__108:A3","CH_GGVC__108:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D3","text":"Astrorum causalitas, etiamsi naturales effectus producat, explicare non potest seriem eventuum humanorum contingentium vel voluntariorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A2","CH_GGVC__108:A5","CH_GGVC__108:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D4","text":"Fatum est media ratio causalitatis: a Deo ut primo principio dependet, in creaturis ut ordo causarum operatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D5","text":"Unitas fati non est unitas rei singularis, sed unitas relationis ordinis ad unum principium.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A8","CH_GGVC__108:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D6","text":"Mobilitas causarum secundarum et immutabilitas providentiae non opponuntur, quia ad diversos respectus eiusdem ordinis referuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A10","CH_GGVC__108:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D7","text":"Creatio, glorificatio et effectus immediate divini providentiae subsunt sine mediatione fatali.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SD1","text":"Providentia universalis et contingentia creata compatibiles fiunt per stratificationem causalitatis: idem effectus contingens est infra, ordinatus est supra.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A1","CH_GGVC__108:A4","CH_GGVC__108:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SD2","text":"Fatum causalitatem creatam non absorbet, sed eam definit ut executionem ordinatam effectuum quos providentia praeordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8","CH_GGVC__108:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SD3","text":"Necessitas in systemate non est proprietas universalis eventuum, sed proprietas conditionalis consequentiae ex praescientia et ordinatione divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A10","CH_GGVC__108:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SD4","text":"Gradus subiectionis fato mensurat non mutabilitatem simpliciter, sed gradum mediationis per causas secundas.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A12","CH_GGVC__108:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX1","text":"Systema negat eventum omnino incausatum: quod casuale est in ordine proximo non manet extra ordinem causae superioris.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A1","CH_GGVC__108:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX2","text":"Systema negat naturam creatam posse per se totalitatem eventuum explicare, quia accidentale naturalem causalitatem per se excedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A2","CH_GGVC__108:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX3","text":"Systema negat causalitatem univocam, in qua causa divina et causae secundae eodem modo ad effectum referantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A4","CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX4","text":"Systema negat ordinem causarum creatarum esse ultimum principium explicationis, quia ipse ordo a Deo dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX5","text":"Systema negat omne divinum agere in seriem causarum secundarum resolvi, quia effectus immediati Dei extra fatum manent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SNX1","text":"Fatum nequit esse nomen supremi principii realitatis, quia principium supremum est providentia divina, dum fatum est tantum ordo causalis derivatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SNX2","text":"Contingentia nequit intelligi ut regio realitatis providentiae divinae subtracta, sed tantum ut modus relationis ad causas creatas.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A1","CH_GGVC__108:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SNX3","text":"Necessitas absoluta nequit ex ordine divino inferri, quia providentia immutabilis operatur etiam per causas contingentes et mobiles.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A10","CH_GGVC__108:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS1","text":"Eventus apparenter fortuitus → relatio ad causam proximam → accidentalitas et contingentia localis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS2","text":"Eventus fortuitus → relatio ad intellectum superiorem → unitas intentionalis → providentia ordinans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS3","text":"Providentia ordinans → executio per causas secundas → ordo relativus causarum mediarum → fatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS4","text":"Ordo causarum secundarum → mobilitas secundum causata → dependentia ab immobili providentia → immutabilitas conditionalis sine necessitate absoluta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS5","text":"Effectus per causas secundas → subiectio fato; effectus immediate divini → subiectio providentiae sine fato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AF1","text":"Casus apparens → distinctio causarum proximarum et superiorum → recusatio astrologiae et naturalismi causaliter clausi → providentia intellectiva → fatum ut series causarum secundarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AF2","text":"Definitio relationalis fati → duplex respectus mobilitatis et immutabilitatis → necessitas conditionalis → delimitatio eorum quae fato subsunt et quae immediate a Deo procedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME1","text":"Casus reclassificatur non ut defectus omnis ordinis, sed ut discrepantia inter ordinem causae proximae et ordinem causae superioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME2","text":"Oppositio “providentia aut fortuna” dissolvitur, quia fortuna locum habet in ordine causarum secundarum sub providentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME3","text":"Oppositio “fatum aut libertas humana” removetur, quia voluntas non corporibus caelestibus sed soli Deo ultimo subicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME4","text":"Fatum transfertur ex imagine necessitatis impersonalis ad structuram relationalem causationis creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME5","text":"Creaturae non una classe sub fato ordinantur, sed distinguuntur secundum utrum effectus per causas secundas an immediate a Deo procedant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ALT1","text":"Surface — Fatum quaeritur an sit, ubi sit, utrum immobile sit, et utrum omnia ei subsint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ALT2","text":"Structural — Fatum est ordo causarum secundarum quo providentia divina effectus in creaturis exsequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Quaestio de necessitate convertitur in distinctionem respectuum causalium, qua contingentia inferior et ordinatio superior simul affirmantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Mobilitas pertinet ad seriem creatam temporaliter mutantem; immobilitas pertinet ad ordinem eius ab aeterna providentia dependentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de relativitate casus, causalitate intellectiva divina et mediatione causarum secundarum sufficiunt ad definitionem fati restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter providentiam et fatum servatur solum si fatum stricte ad ordinem causarum secundarum restringitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT3","text":"Nodus firmissimus est duplex relatio eiusdem eventus ad causam proximam et ad causam superiorem, qua casus sine inordinatione universali intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter fatum mobile secundum causas creatas et fatum immutabile secundum providentiam, quae per distinctionem respectuum solvitur potius quam per unam proprietatem simplicem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT5","text":"Tensio terminologica manet, quia nomen “fatum” retinetur ad ordinem causarum exprimendum et simul recusatur propter implicationem determinismi astralis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT6","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, si a casu apparente ad providentiam, ab providentia ad causas secundas, et ab eis ad limites fati procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170450781851Z_829973cb","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 116","source_sha256":"abbbe254e5b0b00e757c939e23f7ce0b496941bec8ec151ac5904b5242c06cde","sha256":"46856825aa866fc0ac6f5c9c0f405c4102a6ad4e6860aca92ae676d67b0baaaa","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:04:50.784205+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS1","text":"The question establishes fate not as an autonomous cause, but as a mode of ordering among divine providence, secondary causes, contingency, and human events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS2","text":"An event fortuitous with respect to proximate causes can be intended with respect to a higher intellectual cause, so that local chance does not destroy universal providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS3","text":"Astral fate is rejected, because celestial bodies can bring about neither voluntary acts per se nor events per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS4","text":"Fate is defined as the order of secondary causes toward effects preordained by divine providence, not as providence itself nor as one substance within creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AS5","text":"The fatal order is mobile according to the change of created causes, but conditionally immutable according to its dependence on immutable providence; it extends only to those things that proceed through secondary causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A1","text":"That which is fortuitous or casual with respect to an inferior cause can be intended per se with respect to a higher cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A2","text":"An event per accidens is not the effect per se of any natural agent-principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A3","text":"The intellect can apprehend and order under one aspect that which happens per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A4","text":"Divine providence is the cause ordering events that appear casual with respect to created causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A5","text":"God alone can change the will; therefore, the ordering of human acts is ultimately attributed to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A6","text":"Celestial bodies act as natural principles and are not direct causes of voluntary human acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A7","text":"Divine providence executes its effects through intermediate or secondary causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A8","text":"Fate is essentially a disposition or order of secondary causes dependent on God for the production of effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A9","text":"The fatal order, as a relation, is one with respect to the divine principle and is multiplied with respect to intermediate causes or effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A10","text":"Secondary causes are mutable; therefore fate, considered according to those causes themselves, is mobile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A11","text":"The dependence of fate on immutable providence establishes conditional necessity, not the absolute necessity of all events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A12","text":"Things done immediately by God and not subject to secondary causes are not subject to fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:A13","text":"The more something is subject to secondary causes and distant from the first mind, the more it is entangled in the bonds of fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX1","text":"Fate is not a disposition of the stars established at the time of conception or birth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX2","text":"Fate is not a natural cause per se of accidental, fortuitous, or casual events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX3","text":"Fate does not remove chance and fortune according to their relation to proximate causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX4","text":"Fate is not essentially divine providence itself, but its ordering received in secondary causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX5","text":"Fate is neither a substance nor a quality multiplied according to the multitude of creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX6","text":"The immutability of fate does not entail absolute necessity or the exclusion of contingency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX7","text":"Not all things subject to divine will and power are thereby subject to fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:NX8","text":"The name “fate” is not accepted without caution, because it is easily transferred to the necessity of the stars and astral determinism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D1","text":"The contingency of an event does not consist in the lack of all order, but in its relation to deficient or ignorant proximate causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A1","CH_GGVC__108:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D2","text":"An event accidentally one in the natural order can be intentionally one in the order of the divine intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A2","CH_GGVC__108:A3","CH_GGVC__108:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D3","text":"The causality of the stars, even if it produces natural effects, cannot explain the series of contingent or voluntary human events.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A2","CH_GGVC__108:A5","CH_GGVC__108:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D4","text":"Fate is an intermediate account of causality: it depends on God as first principle and operates in creatures as an order of causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D5","text":"The unity of fate is not the unity of a singular thing, but the unity of the relation of order to one principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A8","CH_GGVC__108:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D6","text":"The mobility of secondary causes and the immutability of providence are not opposed, because they refer to different respects of the same order.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A10","CH_GGVC__108:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:D7","text":"Creation, glorification, and immediately divine effects are subject to providence without fatal mediation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SD1","text":"Universal providence and created contingency are made compatible through a stratification of causality: the same effect is contingent below and ordered above.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A1","CH_GGVC__108:A4","CH_GGVC__108:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SD2","text":"Fate does not absorb created causality, but defines it as the ordered execution of effects that providence preordains.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8","CH_GGVC__108:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SD3","text":"Necessity in the system is not a universal property of events, but a conditional property of consequence from divine foreknowledge and ordering.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A10","CH_GGVC__108:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SD4","text":"The degree of subjection to fate measures not mutability simply, but the degree of mediation through secondary causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A12","CH_GGVC__108:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX1","text":"The system denies an event wholly uncaused: what is casual in the proximate order does not remain outside the order of a higher cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A1","CH_GGVC__108:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX2","text":"The system denies that created nature can by itself explain the totality of events, because the accidental exceeds natural causality per se.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A2","CH_GGVC__108:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX3","text":"The system denies univocal causality, in which the divine cause and secondary causes are related to the effect in the same way.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A4","CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX4","text":"The system denies that the order of created causes is the ultimate principle of explanation, because that order itself depends on God.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:DNX5","text":"The system denies that every divine action is reducible to the series of secondary causes, because God's immediate effects remain outside fate.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SNX1","text":"Fate cannot be the name of the supreme principle of reality, because the supreme principle is divine providence, whereas fate is only a derived causal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SNX2","text":"Contingency cannot be understood as a region of reality withdrawn from divine providence, but only as a mode of relation to created causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A1","CH_GGVC__108:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:SNX3","text":"Absolute necessity cannot be inferred from the divine order, because immutable providence operates also through contingent and mobile causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC__108:A7","CH_GGVC__108:A10","CH_GGVC__108:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS1","text":"Apparently fortuitous event → relation to a proximate cause → accidentality and local contingency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS2","text":"Fortuitous event → relation to a higher intellect → intentional unity → ordering providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS3","text":"Ordering providence → execution through secondary causes → relative order of intermediate causes → fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS4","text":"Order of secondary causes → mobility according to caused things → dependence on immutable providence → conditional immutability without absolute necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:FGS5","text":"Effects through secondary causes → subjection to fate; immediately divine effects → subjection to providence without fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AF1","text":"Apparent chance → distinction between proximate and higher causes → rejection of astrology and causally closed naturalism → intellectual providence → fate as a series of secondary causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:AF2","text":"Relational definition of fate → twofold respect of mobility and immutability → conditional necessity → delimitation of what is subject to fate and what proceeds immediately from God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME1","text":"Chance is reclassified not as the defect of all order, but as a discrepancy between the order of a proximate cause and the order of a higher cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME2","text":"The opposition “providence or fortune” is dissolved, because fortune has a place in the order of secondary causes under providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME3","text":"The opposition “fate or human freedom” is removed, because the will is subject not to celestial bodies but ultimately to God alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME4","text":"Fate is transferred from the image of impersonal necessity to the relational structure of created causation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ME5","text":"Creatures are not ordered under fate in one class, but are distinguished according to whether effects proceed through secondary causes or immediately from God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ALT1","text":"Surface — It is asked concerning fate whether it exists, where it is, whether it is immobile, and whether all things are subject to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ALT2","text":"Structural — Fate is the order of secondary causes by which divine providence executes effects in creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The question of necessity is transformed into a distinction of causal respects, through which lower contingency and higher ordering are affirmed simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Mobility pertains to the created series changing temporally; immobility pertains to its order dependent on eternal providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning the relativity of chance, divine intellectual causality, and the mediation of secondary causes suffice to restore the definition of fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT2","text":"The distinction between providence and fate is preserved only if fate is strictly restricted to the order of secondary causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT3","text":"The firmest node is the twofold relation of the same event to a proximate cause and to a higher cause, by which chance is understood without universal disorder.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT4","text":"A fragile juncture remains between fate mobile according to created causes and fate immutable according to providence, which is resolved through a distinction of respects rather than through one simple property.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT5","text":"A terminological tension remains, because the name “fate” is retained to express the order of causes and at the same time rejected because of its implication of astral determinism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__108:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if it proceeds from apparent chance to providence, from providence to secondary causes, and from these to the limits of fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__108:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__108@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__108:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 117","title":"First Part · Question 116","context":"Chapter 117","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 116"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 116","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 117","order":118,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__109"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__109@R001","sha256":"61ac876b3dade8feed472ede2d5db6b4eb711fbdd8fe716ef712fd6b2af393be","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quatenus homo, creatura simul spiritualis et corporalis, effectus cognitivos vel corporales per propriam virtutem producere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS2","text":"Thesis est hominem scientiam in alio vere causare posse, sed ministerialiter; illum autem nec Angelos de divinis illuminare, nec materiam corporalem immediate immutare, nec anima separata corpora naturaliter movere posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est reconstructiva et diagnostica: apparentiae efficaciae humanae per distinctionem causarum principalium, ministerialium, naturalium et supernaturalium resolvuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS4","text":"Doctrina explicatur ut reductio intellectus discipuli de potentia in actum per signa, exempla et ordinem demonstrativum ab extrinseco propositum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS5","text":"Potestas spiritualis non ex sola spiritualitate deducitur, sed ex ordine naturali virtutis ad proprium subiectum, obiectum et medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS6","text":"Motus textus procedit ab efficacia cognitivi ministerii humano concessa ad negationem dominationis humanae immediatae super Angelos, materiam et corpora externa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A1","text":"In attributione cuiuslibet effectus distinguenda sunt virtus naturalis, gratia vel virtus divina, et causalitas principalis vel ministerialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A2","text":"Virtus naturalis cuiuslibet creaturae ad proprium obiectum et ordinem determinatur; ex sola spiritualitate dominium indeterminatum non sequitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A3","text":"Materia corporalis recipit formam ab agente ex materia et forma composito vel a Deo, qui materiam et formam virtualiter continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A4","text":"Intellectus possibilis est proprius cuiusque animae humanae, nec unus numero omnibus hominibus communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A5","text":"Intellectus possibilis humanus est in potentia ad intelligibilia et scientiam completam a principio non possidet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A6","text":"Lumen intellectus agentis et principia universalia naturaliter cognita sunt principium interius acquisitionis scientiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A7","text":"Scientia acquiritur procedendo ex notis ad ignota, per applicationem principiorum universalium ad particularia sensu, memoria et experimento accepta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A8","text":"Magister lumen intelligibile nec species intelligibiles directe in discipulo causat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A9","text":"Magister discipulo exteriora instrumenta praebet, cum proponit signa, exempla, propositiones et ordinem principiorum ad conclusiones.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A10","text":"Lumen intellectus discipuli est causa principalis scientiae acquisitae; magister est causa coadiuvans et ministerialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A11","text":"De rebus divinis homo Angelum non illuminat, quia homo etiam supremus in statu viae Angelis secundum actum subditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A12","text":"Maioritas hominis respectu Angeli secundum virtutem caritatis vel beatitudinem merendam non constituit maiorem actualem virtutem illuminandi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A13","text":"Anima humana virtutem motivam naturalem habet respectu corporis cuius est forma et quod vivificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A14","text":"Immutatio animae humanae in corpora exteriora naturaliter procedit, si procedit, per immutationem proprii corporis et per media corporalia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A15","text":"Miracula sanctorum ex potestate gratiae proveniunt, non ex virtute naturali animae humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX1","text":"Doctrina humana non est illuminatio divina principalis neque infusio immediata scientiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX2","text":"Scientia non est qualitas activa quae, sicut calor, per se scientiam similem in altero producat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX3","text":"Unitas Averroistica intellectus possibilis et specierum intelligibilium omnibus communium repudiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX4","text":"Reminiscentia Platonica scientiae animae ab origine completae repudiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX5","text":"Signa doctrinalia neque omnino nota neque omnino ignota sunt: nota sunt universaliter et confuse, ignota particulariter et distincte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX6","text":"Illuminatio de divinis non ascendit ab hominibus ad Angelos, et locutio cogitationum illuminationem non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX7","text":"Materia corporalis non obedit ad nutum substantiae spiritualis creatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX8","text":"Sanctitas, imaginatio vehemens vel fama miraculorum non demonstrant naturalem potestatem animae super materiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX9","text":"Anima separata non est motor naturalis corporum exteriorum, quia nullum corpus vivificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D1","text":"Doctrina humana est vera causalitas scientiae, sed causalitas quae operationem propriam intellectus discipuli ordinat potius quam scientiam in eum transfert.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A5","CH_GGVC__109:A6","CH_GGVC__109:A7","CH_GGVC__109:A8","CH_GGVC__109:A9","CH_GGVC__109:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D2","text":"Demonstratio scientiam facit quia discipulo seriem inferentialem exhibet qua ex principiis iam notis conclusio ignota deduci potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A6","CH_GGVC__109:A7","CH_GGVC__109:A9","CH_GGVC__109:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D3","text":"Magister et discipulus eandem scientiam habere possunt secundum identitatem rei scitae, sine identitate intellectus aut speciei numero communis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A4","CH_GGVC__109:A5","CH_GGVC__109:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D4","text":"Maioritas hominis futura vel virtualis non evertit ordinem actualem quo Angelus hominem in divinis praecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A11","CH_GGVC__109:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D5","text":"Homo Angelis cogitationes suas manifestare potest per locutionem, sed secretum cordis non manifestatum solius Dei cognitioni immediate patet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D6","text":"Mysteria per praedicationem apostolicam in rebus impleta Angelis apparere possunt, quin praedicatores Angelos formaliter illuminent.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D7","text":"Apprehensiones animae corpus proprium afficere possunt, sed effectus exteriores requirunt catenam corporalem mediorum, non imperium immediatum animae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A2","CH_GGVC__109:A3","CH_GGVC__109:A13","CH_GGVC__109:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D8","text":"Miracula, fascinationis effectus et narrationes magicae non probant per se virtutem naturalem animae, quia ad gratiam, media corporalia vel daemonum simulationem referri possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A3","CH_GGVC__109:A14","CH_GGVC__109:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D9","text":"Anima separata, corpore vivificante carens, nullum corpus sua naturali virtute localiter movere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A2","CH_GGVC__109:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SD1","text":"Systema causale triplicem ordinem instituit: Deus ut causa transcendens, principium intrinsecum ut causa principalis creata, et agens externum ut causa ministerialis vel dispositiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A3","CH_GGVC__109:A10","CH_GGVC__109:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SD2","text":"Efficacia humana non est possessio absoluta subiecti spiritualis, sed relatio determinata inter virtutem, recipiens, corpus proprium et media proportionata.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A2","CH_GGVC__109:A11","CH_GGVC__109:A13","CH_GGVC__109:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SD3","text":"Effectus extraordinarius non identificat causam suam: prius examinanda est competentia causalis agentis quam effectus ad eius naturam referatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A2","CH_GGVC__109:A3","CH_GGVC__109:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SD4","text":"Ordo actualis naturae et ordo beatitudinis futurae distinguuntur, ita ut potentia ad maiorem perfectionem non sit praesens potestas causaliter superior.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A11","CH_GGVC__109:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet quod spiritualitas creata sit genus univocum dominationis super cognitionem, corpora et motum localem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet quod discens sit receptaculum passivum cui scientia quasi res translata imponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet quod eventus visibilis vel narratio mirabilis originem naturalem effectus sufficienter demonstret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet quod meritum futurum vel dignitas virtualis praesentem ordinem causalitatis statim mutet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SNX1","text":"Negatur possibilitas causae creatae quae lumen intelligibile, formam corporalem vel obedientiam materiae immediate ex se constituat; haec positio causae primae reservatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SNX2","text":"Negatur possibilitas efficaciae spiritualis humanae vagae, quae a proprio subiecto separata in quodlibet obiectum sine medio et sine ordine naturali transeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS1","text":"Praetensio virtutis humanae → distinctio naturae, gratiae, causalitatis principalis et ministerialis → examen proportionis inter agentem, effectum et recipiens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS2","text":"Potentia intellectus discipuli + lumen interius + principia praecognita → signa et ordo a magistro proposita → demonstratio → scientia actualis in discipulo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS3","text":"Comparatio hominis et Angeli → distinctio locutionis a divina illuminatione → subordinatio actualis hominis → negatio doctrinae angelicae ab homine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS4","text":"Petitio immutationis materiae → requisitum agentis materialis vel divini → reductio actionis animae ad corpus proprium et media corporalia → negatio imperii immediati super materiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS5","text":"Separatio animae a corpore → imminutio relationis formalis ad corpus vivificatum → absentia corporis obedientis → negatio motus localis naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS6","text":"Apparens exceptio miraculosa vel magica → reattributio ad gratiam, Deum, medium corporale aut daemonis simulationem → conservatio limitis naturae humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AF1","text":"Efficacia hominis compositi dubia → doctrina humana qualificata → prohibitio illuminationis angelicae ascendentis → restrictio immutationis materiae → negatio motus animae separatae → clausura ambitus naturalis humanae virtutis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AF2","text":"Potentia intellectus → principia universalia praecognita → ministerium signorum et demonstrationis → actus scientiae in discipulo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AF3","text":"Maioritas spiritualis apparens → distinctio actus et virtutis futurae → subordinatio actualis hominis ad Angelum → impossibilitas illuminationis angelicae humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AF4","text":"Anima ut forma corporis vivi → motus et immutatio per corpus proprium → separatio animae → defectus corporis naturaliter obedientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME1","text":"Doctrina reclassificatur ab infusione scientiae ad cooperationem externam cum causalitate interiori discipuli.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME2","text":"Signum doctrinale inter ignorantiam absolutam et scientiam completam collocatur, ut medium transitus a cognitione confusa ad cognitionem distinctam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME3","text":"Comparatio hominis et Angeli describitur per ordinem actualem illuminationis, non per dignitatem moralem, caritatem vel beatitudinem possibilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME4","text":"Effectus corporalis reclassificatur per catenam causalem materialem, gratiam vel operationem occultam, non per attributionem immediatam ad voluntatem animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME5","text":"Narrationes de miraculis, fascinatione et animabus mortuorum fiunt materia discernendi causas, non probationes simplices potestatis naturalis humanae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus directe examinat doctrinam inter homines, doctrinam Angelorum, immutationem materiae et motum corporum ab anima separata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ALT2","text":"Structural — Mechanismus pendet ex intellectu agente, intellectu possibili, hierarchia illuminationis, unione formae ad corpus et mediatione agentium corporalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Argumentatio apparentias potestatis resolvit exigendo ut omnis effectus ad causam proportionatam, ordinem actualem et medium proprium reducatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Systema supponit transitum de potentia in actum, distinctionem naturae et gratiae, atque divisionem inter statum praesentem et perfectionem futuram.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituenda quattuor responsa principales: doctrina ministerialis affirmatur, illuminatio angelica humana negatur, immutatio immediata materiae negatur, motus naturalis animae separatae negatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia systematis maxime pendet ex principio quod omnis virtus creata ad proprium subiectum, obiectum et ordinem determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT3","text":"Pars firmissima est analogia inter medicum et magistrum, qua agens externum veram efficaciam habet sine usurpatione causalitatis principalis interioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT4","text":"Commissura fragilis manet in formula qua magister dicitur scientiam causare, cum tamen lumen, species et operatio intellectualis principalis discipuli maneant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT5","text":"Distinctio inter mysterium Angelis in rebus manifestatum et illuminationem Angelis ab homine datam necessaria est, sed terminus causalis inter manifestationem et doctrinam stricte non elaboratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT6","text":"Explicationes effectuum fascinationis per spiritus corporales, aerem continuum vel daemonum cooperationem limites metaphysicos servant, sed nexus empiricos non ex principiis generalibus derivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0079","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT7","text":"Distinctio naturae et gratiae exceptiones miraculorum continet, sed criterium internum quo casus singularis ad gratiam potius quam ad causam naturalem referatur non completur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT8","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, quia affirmatio doctrinae qualificatae fit norma ex qua ceteri casus potentiae spiritualis humanae per limitationem causalitatis ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170516956061Z_63b80485","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 117","source_sha256":"61ac876b3dade8feed472ede2d5db6b4eb711fbdd8fe716ef712fd6b2af393be","sha256":"7d509e957f0b730694c3f94d7b3772c6dc7129f3c35dd131c365bfe13a68a3fe","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:05:16.959002+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS1","text":"The text asks to what extent man, a creature at once spiritual and corporeal, can produce cognitive or corporeal effects through his own power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS2","text":"The thesis is that man can truly cause knowledge in another, but ministerially; whereas he can neither illuminate Angels concerning divine things, nor immediately alter corporeal matter, nor can the separated soul naturally move bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS3","text":"The argumentation is reconstructive and diagnostic: appearances of human efficacy are resolved by the distinction of principal, ministerial, natural, and supernatural causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS4","text":"Teaching is explained as the reduction of the disciple's intellect from potency to act through signs, examples, and a demonstrative order proposed from without.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS5","text":"Spiritual power is not inferred from spirituality alone, but from the natural ordering of a power to its proper subject, object, and medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AS6","text":"The movement of the text proceeds from the efficacy of cognitive ministry granted to man to the denial of man's immediate dominion over Angels, matter, and external bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A1","text":"In attributing any effect, natural power, grace or divine power, and principal or ministerial causality must be distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A2","text":"The natural power of every creature is determined to its proper object and order; indeterminate dominion does not follow from spirituality alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A3","text":"Corporeal matter receives form from an agent composed of matter and form, or from God, who virtually contains matter and form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A4","text":"The possible intellect belongs properly to each human soul, and is not one in number common to all men.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A5","text":"The human possible intellect is in potency toward intelligibles and does not possess complete knowledge from the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A6","text":"The light of the agent intellect and naturally known universal principles are the interior principle of the acquisition of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A7","text":"Knowledge is acquired by proceeding from the known to the unknown, through the application of universal principles to particulars received by sense, memory, and experience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A8","text":"The teacher does not directly cause intelligible light or intelligible species in the disciple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A9","text":"The teacher provides the disciple with external instruments when he sets forth signs, examples, propositions, and an order from principles to conclusions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A10","text":"The light of the disciple's intellect is the principal cause of acquired knowledge; the teacher is a cooperating and ministerial cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A11","text":"Concerning divine things, man does not illuminate an Angel, because even the highest man in the state of wayfarerhood is subject to Angels in act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A12","text":"The superiority of man over an Angel with respect to the power of charity or beatitude to be merited does not establish a greater actual power of illuminating.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A13","text":"The human soul has a natural motive power with respect to the body of which it is the form and which it vivifies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A14","text":"The alteration caused by the human soul in external bodies proceeds naturally, if it proceeds at all, through the alteration of its own body and through corporeal media.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:A15","text":"The miracles of saints proceed from the power of grace, not from the natural power of the human soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX1","text":"Human teaching is not principal divine illumination nor immediate infusion of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX2","text":"Knowledge is not an active quality which, like heat, produces similar knowledge in another through itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX3","text":"The Averroistic unity of the possible intellect and of intelligible species common to all is repudiated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX4","text":"The Platonic recollection of knowledge complete in the soul from its origin is repudiated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX5","text":"Doctrinal signs are neither altogether known nor altogether unknown: they are known universally and confusedly, unknown particularly and distinctly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX6","text":"Illumination concerning divine things does not ascend from men to Angels, and the communication of thoughts does not constitute illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX7","text":"Corporeal matter does not obey at the command of a created spiritual substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX8","text":"Sanctity, vehement imagination, or reports of miracles do not demonstrate the natural power of the soul over matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:NX9","text":"The separated soul is not a natural mover of external bodies, because it vivifies no body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D1","text":"Human teaching is a true causality of knowledge, but a causality that orders the proper operation of the disciple's intellect rather than transfers knowledge into it.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A5","CH_GGVC__109:A6","CH_GGVC__109:A7","CH_GGVC__109:A8","CH_GGVC__109:A9","CH_GGVC__109:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D2","text":"Demonstration produces knowledge because it presents to the disciple an inferential series by which an unknown conclusion can be deduced from principles already known.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A6","CH_GGVC__109:A7","CH_GGVC__109:A9","CH_GGVC__109:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D3","text":"Teacher and disciple can possess the same knowledge according to the identity of the thing known, without identity of intellect or of a species common in number.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A4","CH_GGVC__109:A5","CH_GGVC__109:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D4","text":"The future or virtual superiority of man does not overturn the actual order by which an Angel precedes man in divine things.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A11","CH_GGVC__109:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D5","text":"Man can manifest his thoughts to Angels through speech, but the unmanifested secret of the heart lies immediately open to the knowledge of God alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D6","text":"Mysteries fulfilled in things through apostolic preaching can appear to Angels, without preachers formally illuminating Angels.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D7","text":"The apprehensions of the soul can affect its own body, but external effects require a corporeal chain of media, not the immediate command of the soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A2","CH_GGVC__109:A3","CH_GGVC__109:A13","CH_GGVC__109:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D8","text":"Miracles, effects of fascination, and magical accounts do not of themselves prove the natural power of the soul, since they can be referred to grace, corporeal media, or demonic simulation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A3","CH_GGVC__109:A14","CH_GGVC__109:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:D9","text":"The separated soul, lacking a vivifying body, cannot locally move any body by its natural power.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A2","CH_GGVC__109:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SD1","text":"The causal system establishes a threefold order: God as transcendent cause, an intrinsic principle as created principal cause, and an external agent as ministerial or dispositive cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A3","CH_GGVC__109:A10","CH_GGVC__109:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SD2","text":"Human efficacy is not the absolute possession of a spiritual subject, but a determinate relation among power, recipient, one's own body, and proportionate media.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A2","CH_GGVC__109:A11","CH_GGVC__109:A13","CH_GGVC__109:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SD3","text":"An extraordinary effect does not identify its cause: the causal competence of the agent must first be examined before the effect is referred to its nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A1","CH_GGVC__109:A2","CH_GGVC__109:A3","CH_GGVC__109:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SD4","text":"The actual order of nature and the order of future beatitude are distinguished, such that potency for greater perfection is not a present causally superior power.","refs":["CH_GGVC__109:A11","CH_GGVC__109:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:DNX1","text":"It must be false that created spirituality is a univocal genus of dominion over cognition, bodies, and local motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the learner is a passive receptacle upon which knowledge is imposed as though it were a transferred thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:DNX3","text":"It must be false that a visible event or marvelous account sufficiently demonstrates the natural origin of an effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:DNX4","text":"It must be false that future merit or virtual dignity immediately changes the present order of causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SNX1","text":"The possibility of a created cause that immediately establishes from itself intelligible light, corporeal form, or the obedience of matter is denied; this position is reserved to the first cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a vague human spiritual efficacy is denied, one which, separated from its proper subject, passes into any object without a medium and without natural order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS1","text":"Claim of human power → distinction of nature, grace, principal and ministerial causality → examination of the proportion between agent, effect, and recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS2","text":"Potency of the disciple's intellect + interior light + previously known principles → signs and order proposed by the teacher → demonstration → actual knowledge in the disciple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS3","text":"Comparison of man and Angel → distinction of speech from divine illumination → actual subordination of man → denial of angelic teaching by man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS4","text":"Request for alteration of matter → requirement of a material or divine agent → reduction of the soul's action to its own body and corporeal media → denial of immediate command over matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS5","text":"Separation of the soul from the body → diminution of the formal relation to the vivified body → absence of an obedient body → denial of natural local motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:FGS6","text":"Apparent miraculous or magical exception → reattribution to grace, God, a corporeal medium, or demonic simulation → preservation of the limit of human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AF1","text":"Doubtful efficacy of composite man → qualified human teaching → prohibition of ascending angelic illumination → restriction of the alteration of matter → denial of motion by the separated soul → closure of the sphere of natural human power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AF2","text":"Potency of intellect → previously known universal principles → ministry of signs and demonstration → act of knowledge in the disciple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AF3","text":"Apparent spiritual superiority → distinction of act and future power → actual subordination of man to Angel → impossibility of human angelic illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:AF4","text":"Soul as form of a living body → motion and alteration through one's own body → separation of the soul → lack of a naturally obedient body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME1","text":"Teaching is reclassified from the infusion of knowledge to external cooperation with the disciple's interior causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME2","text":"The doctrinal sign is situated between absolute ignorance and complete knowledge, as a medium of passage from confused to distinct cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME3","text":"The comparison of man and Angel is described by the actual order of illumination, not by moral dignity, charity, or possible beatitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME4","text":"A corporeal effect is reclassified through a material causal chain, grace, or hidden operation, not through immediate attribution to the will of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ME5","text":"Accounts of miracles, fascination, and the souls of the dead become material for discerning causes, not simple proofs of natural human power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text directly examines teaching among men, the teaching of Angels, the alteration of matter, and the motion of bodies by the separated soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ALT2","text":"Structural — The mechanism depends on the agent intellect, possible intellect, hierarchy of illumination, union of form to body, and mediation of corporeal agents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argumentation resolves appearances of power by requiring that every effect be reduced to a proportionate cause, actual order, and proper medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The system presupposes the transition from potency to act, the distinction of nature and grace, and the division between the present state and future perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the four principal answers: ministerial teaching is affirmed, human angelic illumination is denied, the immediate alteration of matter is denied, and the natural motion of the separated soul is denied.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT2","text":"The coherence of the system depends chiefly on the principle that every created power is determined to its proper subject, object, and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT3","text":"The strongest part is the analogy between physician and teacher, by which an external agent has true efficacy without usurping interior principal causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT4","text":"A fragile joint remains in the formula by which the teacher is said to cause knowledge, while the disciple's light, species, and principal intellectual operation nevertheless remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT5","text":"The distinction between a mystery manifested to Angels in things and illumination given to Angels by man is necessary, but the causal boundary between manifestation and teaching is not strictly elaborated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT6","text":"Explanations of effects of fascination through corporeal spirits, continuous air, or demonic cooperation preserve metaphysical limits, but do not derive empirical connections from general principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0063","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0079","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT7","text":"The distinction of nature and grace contains miraculous exceptions, but the internal criterion by which a singular case is referred to grace rather than to a natural cause is not completed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__109:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text, because the affirmation of qualified teaching becomes the norm by which the remaining cases of human spiritual power are ordered through limitation of causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__109:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__109@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__109:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 118","title":"First Part · Question 117","context":"Chapter 118","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 117"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 117","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 118","order":119,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__110"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__110@R001","sha256":"dec8c48cd7fc89b0917455052ff99cc4c9d15f358fcb782a9ef4cba8aa6b0f48","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS1","text":"Quaestio examinat utrum animae per generationem seminalem traduci possint et utrum animae humanae corporibus praeexstiterint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS2","text":"Argumentatio originem cuiusque formae ad modum eius essendi et operandi reducit: forma corpore dependens generationi naturali, forma corpus transcendens creationi divinae attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS3","text":"Virtus seminis causam instrumentalem animae sensitivae exercet, sed principium intellectivum, cum immateriale sit, efficere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS4","text":"Unitas formae substantialis successionem embryonis per corruptionem formarum priorum explicat, donec anima intellectiva creetur et corpori infundatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS5","text":"Naturalis ordinatio animae humanae ad corpus praeexistentiam animae et unionem accidentalem excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS6","text":"Creatio animarum continua multiplicat individua intra species iam institutas, nec cooperatio divina bono naturae cum approbatione vitii confunditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A1","text":"Esse formarum corporalium per se non ipsis, sed compositis subsistentibus per eas competit; propterea fieri compositis competit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A2","text":"Generatio naturalis est transmutatio materiae de potentia in actum per agens corporeum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A3","text":"Anima sensitiva per se non subsistit neque per se operatur, sed cum corpore corrumpitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A4","text":"Generans naturaliter simile sibi producit, et vivens hoc immediate vel per semen efficere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A5","text":"Virtus generativa in semine derivatur ab anima generantis in virtute totius animae et motionem instrumentalem constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A6","text":"Virtus seminalis non est anima, nec pars animae, nec forma prolis; effectu posito, cessare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A7","text":"In uno animali vel homine unum tantum principium formale substantiale est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A8","text":"Forma substantialis perfectior non est eadem numero forma minus perfecta gradatim aucta, sed adveniens formam priorem corrumpit et perfectiones eius continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A9","text":"Virtus activa materiae inhaerens vel corpore utens effectum immaterialem producere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A10","text":"Principium intellectivum operatione a corpore non communicata materiam transcendit et subsistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A11","text":"Substantia immaterialis subsistens per generationem non fit, sed a Deo per creationem causatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A12","text":"Virtutes corporales materiam disponunt; in ordine agentium causa superior ad ultimam formam pertingere potest ubi inferiores ad dispositionem sistunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A13","text":"Anima humana corpori naturaliter unitur, quia intelligit a sensibus et phantasmatibus accipiendo; homo est compositum per se, non anima sola.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A14","text":"Anima intellectiva in fine generationis humanae a Deo creatur et corpori infunditur, unice perfectiones nutritivas et sensitivas continens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A15","text":"Operatio divina post initium mundi novas species non condit, sed individua multiplicat secundum similitudines specierum ab initio positas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A16","text":"Separatio animae a corpore corruptionem corporis ex peccato consequentem exprimit, non principium originarium operum divinorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A17","text":"In actu adulterorum Deus bono naturae cooperatur, non inordinatae voluptati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX1","text":"Anima sensitiva non est substantia perfecta per se subsistens; creatio immediata eius non est principium explicans generationem animalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX2","text":"Virtus generativa non agit sola virtute sua inferiori, sed virtute animae integrae cuius potentia est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX3","text":"In semine non inest anima sensitiva actualis neque pars eius, sed virtus motiva instrumentalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX4","text":"Virtus seminalis non manet ut anima prolis, nec eius cessatio corruptionem agentis principalis constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX5","text":"Opera vitae embryonis non procedunt a sola anima matris neque a principio vitali extrinseco.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX6","text":"Homo non ex tribus animabus simul positis constituitur, nec eadem anima numero per gradus vegetativa, sensitiva et intellectiva fit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX7","text":"Intellectus unus omnibus hominibus communis non admittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX8","text":"Unio animae ad corpus non est accidens ex quo homo ens per accidens constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX9","text":"Animae humanae non ante corpora creantur neque corporibus voluntate contingenti aut vi poenali adiunguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX10","text":"Creatio animarum praesentium neque requiem divinam tollit neque novas species in universo introducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX11","text":"Cooperatio divina cum generatione naturali non est cooperatio cum deformitate morali actus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D1","text":"Anima sensitiva animalis ex transmutatione materiae per virtutem seminalem naturaliter producitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A1","CH_GGVC__110:A2","CH_GGVC__110:A3","CH_GGVC__110:A4","CH_GGVC__110:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D2","text":"Virtus generativa animalis effectum sensitivum producere potest, quia non agit ut potentia vegetativa isolata, sed ut instrumentum animae animalis integrae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A4","CH_GGVC__110:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D3","text":"Cessatio virtutis seminalis post productionem formae non destruit animam prolis, quia instrumentum causale non est forma effecta.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A5","CH_GGVC__110:A6","CH_GGVC__110:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D4","text":"Generatio humana causalitatem dividit: semen corpus et materiam disponit, Deus animam intellectivam creat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A9","CH_GGVC__110:A10","CH_GGVC__110:A11","CH_GGVC__110:A12","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D5","text":"Progressio embryonis non est alteratio continua unius formae permanentis, sed series generationum et corruptionum usque ad ultimam formam substantialem.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A7","CH_GGVC__110:A8","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D6","text":"Homo generat hominem non producens immediate animam rationalem, sed materiam disponens ad receptionem formae humanae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A4","CH_GGVC__110:A9","CH_GGVC__110:A12","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D7","text":"Animae humanae non praeexistunt, quia perfectio earum naturalis unionem ad corpus requirit et creatio earum termino generationis corporalis respondet.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A13","CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D8","text":"Creatio continua animarum non imperfectum universum initio factum demonstrat, quia numerus individuorum augeri potest sine multiplicatione specierum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D9","text":"Conceptio ex adulterio creationem animae non impedit, quia creatio respicit bonum naturale generationis, non inordinationem voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD1","text":"Modus essendi constituit taxonomiam causalitatis: formae corporeae per causalitatem immanentem generantur, principium intellectivum per causalitatem creatricem incipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A1","CH_GGVC__110:A2","CH_GGVC__110:A3","CH_GGVC__110:A9","CH_GGVC__110:A10","CH_GGVC__110:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD2","text":"Reproductio humana est cooperatio inaequalis causarum ordinatarum, in qua natura condiciones corporales efficit et Deus formam subsistentem ponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A4","CH_GGVC__110:A5","CH_GGVC__110:A11","CH_GGVC__110:A12","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD3","text":"Tempus embryonis per saltus ontologicos, non per perfectionem gradatim cumulativam subiecti eiusdem, ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A7","CH_GGVC__110:A8","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD4","text":"Individuum humanum originem suam corporaliter conditionatam habet, sed principium eius intellectivum ad corruptionem corporis non reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A10","CH_GGVC__110:A13","CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD5","text":"Perfectio universi completudinem specierum requirit, non numerum individuorum omnino clausum.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD6","text":"Vitium morale ordinem voluntatis depravat, sed bonum naturale et causalitas creatrix quae illud sustinet non annihilantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet omne exemplar quo generans parentale omnes principia prolis univoce et sufficienter transmittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet naturam corpoream esse systema causaliter clausum et originem hominis totaliter explicare posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet hominem ante corpus vel sine corpore perfectionem naturalem plenam habere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet omnem progressionem viventis esse accessionem continuam sine corruptione reali formarum priorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet perfectionem initialem universi omnem actionem creatricem temporalem excludere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet separationem animae a corpore statum originarium et normam positivae naturae constituere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SNX1","text":"Praecluditur possibilitas ut natura corporalis sit causa totalis hominis, cum ad dispositionem materiae tantum pertingat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SNX2","text":"Praecluditur possibilitas ut anima humana sit substantia spiritualis completa cui corpus extrinsecum et contingens accedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SNX3","text":"Praecluditur possibilitas ut creatio divina uno initio temporali exhausta sit, quamvis constitutio specierum initio completa maneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS1","text":"Operatio corpore dependens → esse formae in composito → generatio materialis; operatio corpore non participata → subsistentia immaterialis → creatio divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS2","text":"Anima generantis → virtus seminalis derivata → transmutatio materiae → anima sensitiva; virtus instrumentalis → cessatio post effectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS3","text":"Vita embryonis intrinseca → formae successivae → corruptio formarum priorum → materia ad ultimam formam disposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS4","text":"Dispositio corporalis per naturam → creatio animae intellectivae a Deo → informatio corporis → una anima intellectiva, sensitiva et nutritiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS5","text":"Ordinatio naturalis animae ad corpus → exclusio praeexistentiae → creatio individuorum temporalium intra species ab initio institutas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AF1","text":"Quaestio de anima sensitiva ex semine → criterium essendi et operandi non subsistentis → generatio per virtutem seminalem instrumentalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AF2","text":"Quaestio de anima intellectiva ex semine → operatio a corpore independens → impossibilitas causalitatis seminalis → creatio divina post dispositionem corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AF3","text":"Quaestio de animabus ante corpus → necessitas naturalis unionis animae et corporis → creatio et infusio in termino generationis → multiplicatio individuorum sine novis speciebus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME1","text":"Nomen animae in duas classes causaliter diversas dividitur: animam sensitivam corpore dependentem et animam intellectivam subsistentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME2","text":"Generatio reclassificatur ut ordo causarum inaequalium, non ut transmissio integrae animae parentis ad prolem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME3","text":"Vita embryonalis reclassificatur ut successio formarum substantialium, non ut una anima paulatim aucta neque ut pluralitas animarum coexistentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME4","text":"Corpus humanum reclassificatur ut conditio naturalis perfectionis animae humanae, non ut carcer, poena originaria aut accidens extrinsecum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME5","text":"Historia creationis distinguit completionem specierum ab aperta multiplicatione individuorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei — Textus decernit utrum anima sensitiva et anima intellectiva ex semine causentur atque utrum animae humanae ante corpora creatae sint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis — Ratio causalis distinguit virtutem seminalem instrumentalem, dispositionem materiae, successionem formarum et creationem animae intellectivae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus — Obiectiones solvuntur non negando generationem, sed distribuendo causalitatem inter ordines corporeos, instrumentales et divinos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus-temporalis — Modus operationis determinat modum essendi et originis, dum initium individui corpori coniungitur, separatio autem animae a corpore statui corruptionis assignatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT1","text":"Systema conclusiones de anima sensitiva, anima intellectiva et creatione temporali animarum restituere sufficit, quia distinctionem inter generationem et creationem ex modo essendi deducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT2","text":"Firmissimum nodum constituit connexio inter operationem a corpore independentem, subsistentiam et necessitatem creationis divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT3","text":"Ratio animae sensitivae nititur principio quod forma non subsistens per transmutationem corporalem produci potest; hic transitus metaphysice positus, non ulterius resolutus, manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT4","text":"Exactus nexus inter ultimam dispositionem materiae et actum creationis animae intellectivae affirmatur, sed mechanismus termini non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT5","text":"Unitas animae contra pluralitatem animarum servatur per corruptionem formarum priorum, sed requirit distinctionem strictam inter retentionem perfectionum et identitatem numericam formae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT6","text":"Formula creationis simul cum corpore infusae temporalius determinanda manet, quia creatio in fine generationis humanae, non in primo initio materiae embryonalis, collocatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT7","text":"Concordia inter naturalem necessitatem corporis et subsistentiam animae separatae servatur tantum si separatio ut status corruptioni consecutus, non ut perfectio originaria, intelligatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT8","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat: divisio animae sensitivae et intellectivae → ordinatio generationis → exclusio praeexistentiae → doctrina creationis individuorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170544797411Z_9fa187c8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 118","source_sha256":"dec8c48cd7fc89b0917455052ff99cc4c9d15f358fcb782a9ef4cba8aa6b0f48","sha256":"36de2943c211cafdaa84f52c0f47da5906303b1941137a6f787d8da07113db3a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:05:44.798358+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS1","text":"The question examines whether souls can be transmitted through seminal generation and whether human souls preexisted bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS2","text":"The argument reduces the origin of each form to its mode of being and operating: a form dependent on the body is attributed to natural generation, while a form transcending the body is attributed to divine creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS3","text":"The power of the semen exercises the instrumental causality of the sensitive soul, but it cannot produce the intellective principle, since this is immaterial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS4","text":"The unity of substantial form explains the succession of the embryo through the corruption of prior forms, until the intellective soul is created and infused into the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS5","text":"The natural ordering of the human soul to the body excludes the soul's preexistence and accidental union.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AS6","text":"The continuous creation of souls multiplies individuals within species already established, nor is divine cooperation with the good of nature confused with approval of vice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A1","text":"The being of bodily forms belongs per se not to themselves, but to the subsisting composites through them; therefore coming-to-be belongs to the composites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A2","text":"Natural generation is the transmutation of matter from potency into act through a bodily agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A3","text":"The sensitive soul neither subsists per se nor operates per se, but is corrupted together with the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A4","text":"A natural generator produces what is like itself, and a living being can effect this immediately or through semen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A5","text":"The generative power in semen is derived from the soul of the generator in the power of the whole soul and constitutes an instrumental motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A6","text":"The seminal power is neither a soul, nor a part of a soul, nor the form of the offspring; once its effect has been produced, it can cease.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A7","text":"In one animal or human being there is only one substantial formal principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A8","text":"A more perfect substantial form is not numerically the same less perfect form gradually increased, but, upon arriving, corrupts the prior form and contains its perfections.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A9","text":"An active power inhering in matter or using a body cannot produce an immaterial effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A10","text":"The intellective principle transcends matter and subsists through an operation not shared with the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A11","text":"A subsisting immaterial substance does not come to be through generation, but is caused by God through creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A12","text":"Bodily powers dispose matter; in the order of agents, a higher cause can reach the ultimate form where lower causes stop at disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A13","text":"The human soul is naturally united to the body because it understands by receiving from the senses and phantasms; the human being is a composite per se, not the soul alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A14","text":"At the end of human generation, the intellective soul is created by God and infused into the body, uniquely containing the nutritive and sensitive perfections.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A15","text":"Divine operation after the beginning of the world does not establish new species, but multiplies individuals according to the likenesses of species established from the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A16","text":"The separation of the soul from the body expresses the corruption of the body consequent upon sin, not the original principle of divine works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:A17","text":"In the act of adulterers, God cooperates with the good of nature, not with disordered pleasure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX1","text":"The sensitive soul is not a perfect substance subsisting per se; its immediate creation is not a principle explaining animal generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX2","text":"The generative power does not act by its own inferior power alone, but by the power of the whole soul whose potency it is.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX3","text":"In semen there is neither an actual sensitive soul nor a part of it, but an instrumental motive power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX4","text":"The seminal power does not remain as the soul of the offspring, nor does its cessation constitute the corruption of the principal agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX5","text":"The operations of embryonic life do not proceed from the mother's soul alone nor from an extrinsic vital principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX6","text":"A human being is not constituted from three souls posited simultaneously, nor does the same soul numerically become vegetative, sensitive, and intellective through stages.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX7","text":"One intellect common to all human beings is not admitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX8","text":"The union of the soul to the body is not an accident from which a human being is constituted as a being per accidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX9","text":"Human souls are neither created before bodies nor joined to bodies by contingent will or penal force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX10","text":"The creation of present souls neither removes divine rest nor introduces new species into the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:NX11","text":"Divine cooperation with natural generation is not cooperation with the moral deformity of the act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D1","text":"The sensitive soul of an animal is naturally produced from the transmutation of matter through seminal power.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A1","CH_GGVC__110:A2","CH_GGVC__110:A3","CH_GGVC__110:A4","CH_GGVC__110:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D2","text":"The generative power of an animal can produce a sensitive effect because it does not act as an isolated vegetative potency, but as an instrument of the whole animal soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A4","CH_GGVC__110:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D3","text":"The cessation of seminal power after the production of the form does not destroy the soul of the offspring, because the causal instrument is not the produced form.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A5","CH_GGVC__110:A6","CH_GGVC__110:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D4","text":"Human generation divides causality: semen disposes the body and matter; God creates the intellective soul.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A9","CH_GGVC__110:A10","CH_GGVC__110:A11","CH_GGVC__110:A12","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D5","text":"The progression of the embryo is not a continuous alteration of one enduring form, but a series of generations and corruptions up to the ultimate substantial form.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A7","CH_GGVC__110:A8","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D6","text":"A human being generates a human being not by immediately producing the rational soul, but by disposing matter for the reception of the human form.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A4","CH_GGVC__110:A9","CH_GGVC__110:A12","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D7","text":"Human souls do not preexist, because their natural perfection requires union with the body and their creation corresponds to the terminus of bodily generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A13","CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D8","text":"The continuous creation of souls does not demonstrate that the universe was made imperfect at the beginning, because the number of individuals can increase without multiplication of species.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:D9","text":"Conception from adultery does not impede the creation of the soul, because creation regards the natural good of generation, not the disorder of the will.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD1","text":"The mode of being establishes a taxonomy of causality: bodily forms are generated through immanent causality; the intellective principle begins through creative causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A1","CH_GGVC__110:A2","CH_GGVC__110:A3","CH_GGVC__110:A9","CH_GGVC__110:A10","CH_GGVC__110:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD2","text":"Human reproduction is an unequal cooperation of ordered causes, in which nature effects bodily conditions and God posits the subsisting form.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A4","CH_GGVC__110:A5","CH_GGVC__110:A11","CH_GGVC__110:A12","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD3","text":"The time of the embryo is ordered through ontological leaps, not through the gradually cumulative perfection of the same subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A7","CH_GGVC__110:A8","CH_GGVC__110:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD4","text":"The human individual has an origin bodily conditioned, but its intellective principle is not reduced to the corruption of the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A10","CH_GGVC__110:A13","CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD5","text":"The perfection of the universe requires completeness of species, not an absolutely closed number of individuals.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SD6","text":"Moral vice depraves the order of the will, but the natural good and the creative causality sustaining it are not annihilated.","refs":["CH_GGVC__110:A14","CH_GGVC__110:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX1","text":"Every model according to which the parental generator transmits all the principles of the offspring univocally and sufficiently must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX2","text":"It must be false that bodily nature is a causally closed system and can totally explain the origin of the human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX3","text":"It must be false that a human being has full natural perfection before the body or without the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX4","text":"It must be false that every progression of a living being is continuous accretion without real corruption of prior forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the initial perfection of the universe excludes every temporal creative action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:DNX6","text":"It must be false that the separation of the soul from the body constitutes the original state and the norm of positive nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SNX1","text":"The possibility that bodily nature is the total cause of the human being is precluded, since it reaches only to the disposition of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SNX2","text":"The possibility that the human soul is a complete spiritual substance to which the body is added as extrinsic and contingent is precluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:SNX3","text":"The possibility that divine creation was exhausted in one temporal beginning is precluded, although the constitution of species remains complete from the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS1","text":"Operation dependent on the body → being of the form in the composite → material generation; operation not participated in by the body → immaterial subsistence → divine creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS2","text":"Soul of the generator → derived seminal power → transmutation of matter → sensitive soul; instrumental power → cessation after effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS3","text":"Intrinsic life of the embryo → successive forms → corruption of prior forms → matter disposed for the ultimate form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS4","text":"Bodily disposition through nature → creation of the intellective soul by God → informing of the body → one intellective, sensitive, and nutritive soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:FGS5","text":"Natural ordering of the soul to the body → exclusion of preexistence → creation of temporal individuals within species established from the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AF1","text":"Question concerning the sensitive soul from semen → criterion of non-subsisting being and operation → generation through instrumental seminal power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AF2","text":"Question concerning the intellective soul from semen → operation independent of the body → impossibility of seminal causality → divine creation after bodily disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:AF3","text":"Question concerning souls before the body → natural necessity of the union of soul and body → creation and infusion at the terminus of generation → multiplication of individuals without new species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME1","text":"The name soul is divided into two causally distinct classes: the body-dependent sensitive soul and the subsisting intellective soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME2","text":"Generation is reclassified as an order of unequal causes, not as the transmission of the whole soul of the parent to the offspring.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME3","text":"Embryonic life is reclassified as a succession of substantial forms, not as one gradually increased soul nor as a plurality of coexisting souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME4","text":"The human body is reclassified as a natural condition of the perfection of the human soul, not as a prison, original punishment, or extrinsic accident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ME5","text":"The history of creation distinguishes the completion of species from the open multiplication of individuals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ALT1","text":"Surface level — The text decides whether the sensitive soul and the intellective soul are caused from semen and whether human souls were created before bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ALT2","text":"Structural level — The causal account distinguishes instrumental seminal power, the disposition of matter, the succession of forms, and the creation of the intellective soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic level — Objections are resolved not by denying generation, but by distributing causality among bodily, instrumental, and divine orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:ALT4","text":"Ontological-temporal level — The mode of operation determines the mode of being and origin, while the beginning of the individual is joined to the body, whereas the separation of soul from body is assigned to the state of corruption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT1","text":"The system suffices to restore conclusions concerning the sensitive soul, the intellective soul, and the temporal creation of souls, because it deduces the distinction between generation and creation from the mode of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT2","text":"The firmest nexus consists in the connection between operation independent of the body, subsistence, and the necessity of divine creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT3","text":"The account of the sensitive soul rests upon the principle that a non-subsisting form can be produced through bodily transmutation; this transition is metaphysically posited, not further resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT4","text":"The exact nexus between the ultimate disposition of matter and the act of creation of the intellective soul is affirmed, but the mechanism of the terminus is not explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT5","text":"The unity of the soul against a plurality of souls is maintained through the corruption of prior forms, but requires a strict distinction between the retention of perfections and the numerical identity of form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT6","text":"The formula of creation simultaneously infused with the body remains to be determined more temporally, because creation is situated at the end of human generation, not at the first beginning of embryonic matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT7","text":"The harmony between the natural necessity of the body and the subsistence of the separated soul is maintained only if separation is understood as a state consequent upon corruption, not as original perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__110:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: division of the sensitive and intellective soul → ordering of generation → exclusion of preexistence → doctrine of the creation of individuals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__110:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__110@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__110:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 119","title":"First Part · Question 118","context":"Chapter 119","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 118"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 118","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111","layer":"CH","title":"First Part · Question 119","order":120,"parents":["RAW_GGVC__111"],"revision":"CH_GGVC__111@R001","sha256":"2ba66d1764e2c20e6912acb2e30546511746de91e9ff8e659b3aed0d6a5dae53","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS1","text":"Quaestio investigat utrum alimentum vere ingrediatur constitutionem corporis humani et utrum semen ex alimento superfluo oriatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS2","text":"Argumentatio ab aequivocatione “veritatis naturae” procedit ad distinctionem naturae specificae, naturae individualis et materiae in utramque ordinatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS3","text":"Positio materiae humanae primigeniae, numero fixae et per successionem propagatae, destruitur quia multiplicationem corporum, nutritionem et generationem naturalem explicare nequit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS4","text":"Alimentum, formam priorem amittens et formam corporis viventis accipiens, vere in carnem, os et partes corporis convertitur, salva identitate individui per successionem continuam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS5","text":"Semen definitur ut alimentum iam sub virtute generantis ordinatum, sed nondum in substantiam membrorum determinatorum conversum; sic virtus nutritiva generativae ministrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS6","text":"Similitudo genealogica et affinitas non a permanenti identitate materiae, sed a derivatione virtutis formalis per generationem explicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A1","text":"Id ad veritatem naturae pertinet quod ad esse et constitutionem eius concurrit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A2","text":"Natura eadem aliter consideratur secundum speciem communem et secundum individuum materia signata determinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A3","text":"Forma humana non est inseparabiliter alligata unicae materiae primigeniae, quia a materia corporis corruptibilis separari potest et alteri materiae advenire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A4","text":"Multiplicatio naturalis materiae corporalis fit per conversionem alterius in corpus, non per nudam numeralem repetitionem eiusdem materiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A5","text":"Virtus nutritiva corporis viventis potest materiam dissimilem assumere et sub forma viventis assimilare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A6","text":"Quod ex alimento succedit loco eius quod per calorem naturalem deperditur, ad veritatem corporis nutriti pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A7","text":"Identitas numerica viventis non requirit permanentiam omnium partium materialium, sed continuationem formae in materia paulatim substituta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A8","text":"Forma specifica corporis manere potest dum materia eius paulatim consumitur et restauratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A9","text":"Alimentum gradatim a potentia communi ad virtutem corporis et deinde ad determinationem partium reducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A10","text":"Semen oportet esse potentia totum corpus et virtutem producendi totum habere ab anima generantis derivatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A11","text":"Similitudo generantis et geniti formaliter, non materialiter, fundatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A12","text":"Virtus conversiva corporis passibilis continua operatione debilitatur, unde augmentum, restauratio, imminutio et mors successive oriuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX1","text":"Alimentum non est mera exterior natura sustentans humidum radicale sine vera conversione in corpus humanum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX2","text":"Materia quae a primo homine derivatur non est unica materia substantialis sufficiens ad omnium corporum humanorum multiplicationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX3","text":"Caro secundum speciem et caro secundum materiam non sunt duae carnes diversae, quarum altera sola naturam humanam retineat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX4","text":"Humidum radicale non significat omne nutrimentum vel omnem materiam corporis, sed id in quo virtus speciei fundatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX5","text":"Mors non est mera defectio materiae reparabilis, sed defectio virtutis conversivae quae restaurationem efficere desinit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX6","text":"Semen non est pars actu resoluta ex membris nec animal parvum actu completum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX7","text":"Generatio non est transmissio identicae materiae corporalis per seriem genealogicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D1","text":"Si alimentum formam corporis viventis recipit, conversio eius non est mera adiunctio quantitativa, sed ingressus in veritatem corporis humani.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A1","CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D2","text":"Multiplicatio corporum humanorum requirit materiam noviter assimilabilem; aliter una species humana ad unum individuum reduceretur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A3","CH_GGVC__111:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D3","text":"Restauratio nutritiva et augmentum sunt operationes eiusdem virtutis assimilativae, sed diversum effectum habent secundum quantitatem materiae conversae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A6","CH_GGVC__111:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D4","text":"Corpus idem numero manet cum substitutio materiae est continua et materia ad corpus iam praeexistens convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A7","CH_GGVC__111:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D5","text":"Alimentum nondum in membrum determinatum conversum potest, sub virtute animae generantis, materiam seminalem praebere.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A9","CH_GGVC__111:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D6","text":"Genitum patri, avo et consanguineis assimilatur per continuationem virtutis formalis, quamvis materia seminis immediate ex alimento proveniat.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A10","CH_GGVC__111:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D7","text":"Opus generativum naturaliter supponit opus nutritivum, quia generativa assumit quod nutritiva ad potentiam corporis iam disposuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A9","CH_GGVC__111:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SD1","text":"Corpus vivens constituitur ut identitas processualis: materia eius fluit, forma et ordinatio corporis per successionem conservantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A7","CH_GGVC__111:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SD2","text":"Generatio et nutritio sunt duo gradus unius causalitatis formalis: nutritio materiam intra individuum assimilat, generatio eandem potentiam ad novum individuum extendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A9","CH_GGVC__111:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SD3","text":"Genealogia corporalis non est conservatio particulae materialis originariae, sed transmissio ordinata formae et virtutis per materias semper mutabiles.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A3","CH_GGVC__111:A4","CH_GGVC__111:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SD4","text":"Mortalitas explicatur intra structuram nutritionis: defectus mortis est defectus operationis assimilativae, non absoluta absentia materiae alimentariae.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A6","CH_GGVC__111:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:DNX1","text":"Falsa esse debet opinio quod identitas individui ex immobilitate eiusdem materiae numericae constituatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:DNX2","text":"Falsa esse debet opinio quod forma humana materiam extrinsecam assimilare nequeat sine imminutioe veritatis naturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:DNX3","text":"Falsa esse debet opinio quod similitudo consanguinea ex communione materiae, potius quam ex virtute formae, oriatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:DNX4","text":"Falsa esse debet opinio quod generatio animalis sit divisio corporis iam actu perfecti in corpus minus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit corpus vivens ut rem materialiter clausam, cuius veritas ab omni materia posteriore immunis permaneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SNX2","text":"Systema excludit originem genealogicam ut praesentiam actualem omnium futurorum corporum in corpore primi parentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SNX3","text":"Systema excludit immortalitatem naturalem quae ex continua copia alimenti simpliciter sequeretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:FGS1","text":"Distinctio esse/veritatis naturae → distinctio speciei et individui → determinatio materiae ad formam humanam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:FGS2","text":"Reiectio materiae primigeniae fixae → necessitas multiplicationis materialis naturalis → conversio alimenti in corpus humanum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:FGS3","text":"Alimentum dissimile → assimilatio nutritiva communis → determinatio ad corpus vel potentiam corporis → semen potentia totum → generatio similis per virtutem formalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:FGS4","text":"Consumptio continua → imminutio virtutis conversivae → cessatio augmenti → defectus restaurationis → imminutio et mors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AF1","text":"Dubium de alimento → definitio veritatis naturae → imminutio positionis materiae primigeniae → conversio alimenti in veritatem corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AF2","text":"Obiectio de fluxu materiae → distinctio formae et materiae → substitutio continua → conservatio identitatis numericae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AF3","text":"Dubium de semine → exclusio membri resoluti → semen ut potentia totum → subordinatio nutritivae generativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AF4","text":"Obiectio de consanguinitate → separatio materiae et formae → derivatio virtutis generativae → assimilatio genealogica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME1","text":"Corpus humanum reclassificatur ab aggregato materiae originariae ad unitatem formalem quae materiam externam continue assimilat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter “materiam nativam” et “materiam nutritivam” desinit esse oppositio inter veram et extrinsecam humanitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME3","text":"Identitas individui transfertur a permanentia partium materialium ad ordinem continuatum conversionis sub eadem forma.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME4","text":"Genealogia reordinatur ut transmissio virtutis formalis per materiam contingenter assumptam, non ut transmissio eiusdem materiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME5","text":"Semen collocatur inter alimentum et membrum: non est alimentum crude externum, nec pars membri actu distincta, sed materia virtualiter totalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ALT1","text":"Surface — Utrum alimentum in corpus humanum convertatur et utrum semen sit superfluum alimenti determinatur affirmative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ALT2","text":"Structural — Nutritio operatur per conversionem materiae dissimilis in partes corporis, generatio per virtutem seminalem ad totum corpus ordinatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Obiectiones materialem permanentiam praesupponentes solvuntur per transpositionem quaestionis ad causalitatem formalem et ordinem potentiae ad actum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Ens vivens idem manet per tempus non quia materia immutata perseverat, sed quia forma materiam successive assumptam in unum corpus ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de veritate naturae, assimilabilitate materiae, identitate formali et semine potentia totum sufficiunt ad utrumque articulum restituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT2","text":"Structura maxime cohaeret ubi nutritionem, augmentationem, restaurationem et generationem sub graduum conversione materiae coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT3","text":"Commissura fragilis manet inter exigentiam identitatis materiae, in objectione positam, et responsionem quae identitatem per continuitatem formae et successionis materialis conservat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT4","text":"Indeterminatum manet criterium precisum quo materia nutritiva iam “veram naturam speciei” perfecte accepisse dicatur, praesertim inter sanguinem, semen et membrum formatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT5","text":"Argumentatio servat motum proprium: ex impossibilitate materiae clausae infert conversionem nutritivam, deinde ex conversione nutritiva derivat structuram seminis et genealogiae formalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170608981869Z_75b4778f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Part · Question 119","source_sha256":"2ba66d1764e2c20e6912acb2e30546511746de91e9ff8e659b3aed0d6a5dae53","sha256":"abb53c0196ef39d964c59cb95272fc07235164d4374a3d8bdb048ab8d7cd475f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:06:08.982805+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS1","text":"The question investigates whether nourishment truly enters into the constitution of the human body and whether semen arises from superfluous nourishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS2","text":"The argument proceeds from the equivocation of “truth of nature” to the distinction between specific nature, individual nature, and matter ordered to each.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS3","text":"The position of primordial human matter, fixed in number and propagated through succession, is destroyed because it cannot explain the multiplication of bodies, nutrition, and natural generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS4","text":"Nourishment, losing its prior form and receiving the form of the living body, is truly converted into flesh, bone, and parts of the body, while the identity of the individual is preserved through continuous succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS5","text":"Semen is defined as nourishment already ordered under the power of the generator, but not yet converted into the substance of determinate members; thus the nutritive power serves the generative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AS6","text":"Genealogical likeness and kinship are explained not by the permanent identity of matter, but by the derivation of formal power through generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A1","text":"That which concurs in its being and constitution pertains to the truth of a nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A2","text":"The same nature is considered differently according to the common species and according to the individual determined by designated matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A3","text":"The human form is not inseparably bound to a single primordial matter, because it can be separated from the matter of a corruptible body and come to another matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A4","text":"The natural multiplication of corporeal matter occurs through the conversion of something else into a body, not through the bare numerical repetition of the same matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A5","text":"The nutritive power of a living body can take up dissimilar matter and assimilate it under the form of the living being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A6","text":"What succeeds through nourishment in the place of what is lost through natural heat pertains to the truth of the nourished body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A7","text":"The numerical identity of a living being does not require the permanence of all material parts, but the continuation of the form in gradually substituted matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A8","text":"The specific form of the body can remain while its matter is gradually consumed and restored.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A9","text":"Nourishment is gradually reduced from common potentiality to the power of the body and then to the determination of the parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A10","text":"Semen must be potentially the whole body and possess, derived from the soul of the generator, the power of producing the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A11","text":"The likeness of generator and generated is founded formally, not materially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:A12","text":"The transformative power of a passible body is weakened by continuous operation, whence growth, restoration, diminution, and death arise successively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX1","text":"Nourishment is not a merely external nature sustaining radical moisture without true conversion into the human body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX2","text":"Matter derived from the first man is not a single substantial matter sufficient for the multiplication of all human bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX3","text":"Flesh according to species and flesh according to matter are not two different fleshes, one of which alone retains human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX4","text":"Radical moisture does not signify all nourishment or all the matter of the body, but that in which the power of the species is founded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX5","text":"Death is not a mere deficiency of reparable matter, but a deficiency of transformative power that ceases to effect restoration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX6","text":"Semen is not a part actually resolved from the members, nor a small animal actually complete.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:NX7","text":"Generation is not the transmission of identical corporeal matter through a genealogical series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D1","text":"If nourishment receives the form of the living body, its conversion is not mere quantitative addition, but entry into the truth of the human body.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A1","CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D2","text":"The multiplication of human bodies requires newly assimilable matter; otherwise the one human species would be reduced to one individual.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A3","CH_GGVC__111:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D3","text":"Nutritive restoration and growth are operations of the same assimilative power, but have a different effect according to the quantity of matter converted.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A6","CH_GGVC__111:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D4","text":"The body remains numerically the same when the substitution of matter is continuous and matter is converted into an already pre-existing body.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A7","CH_GGVC__111:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D5","text":"Nourishment not yet converted into a determinate member can, under the power of the generative soul, provide seminal matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A9","CH_GGVC__111:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D6","text":"The generated being is likened to its father, grandfather, and blood relatives through the continuation of formal power, although the matter of semen immediately proceeds from nourishment.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A10","CH_GGVC__111:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:D7","text":"The generative work naturally presupposes the nutritive work, because the generative takes up what the nutritive has already disposed toward the potentiality of the body.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A9","CH_GGVC__111:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SD1","text":"The living body is constituted as a processual identity: its matter flows, while the form and ordering of the body are preserved through succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A7","CH_GGVC__111:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SD2","text":"Generation and nutrition are two stages of one formal causality: nutrition assimilates matter within the individual, while generation extends the same potentiality to a new individual.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A5","CH_GGVC__111:A9","CH_GGVC__111:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SD3","text":"Corporeal genealogy is not the preservation of an original material particle, but the ordered transmission of form and power through ever mutable matters.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A3","CH_GGVC__111:A4","CH_GGVC__111:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SD4","text":"Mortality is explained within the structure of nutrition: the defect of death is a defect of assimilative operation, not the absolute absence of alimentary matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC__111:A6","CH_GGVC__111:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:DNX1","text":"The opinion that the identity of the individual is constituted by the immobility of the same numerical matter must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:DNX2","text":"The opinion that the human form cannot assimilate extrinsic matter without diminution of the truth of nature must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:DNX3","text":"The opinion that consanguineous likeness arises from community of matter rather than from the power of form must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:DNX4","text":"The opinion that animal generation is the division of a body already actually perfected into a lesser body must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the living body as a materially closed thing whose truth remains immune from all subsequent matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SNX2","text":"The system excludes genealogical origin as the actual presence of all future bodies in the body of the first parent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:SNX3","text":"The system excludes natural immortality that would simply follow from a continuous supply of nourishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:FGS1","text":"Distinction of being/truth of nature → distinction of species and individual → determination of matter to human form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:FGS2","text":"Rejection of fixed primordial matter → necessity of natural material multiplication → conversion of nourishment into the human body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:FGS3","text":"Dissimilar nourishment → common nutritive assimilation → determination to body or potentiality of body → semen potentially whole → generation of like through formal power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:FGS4","text":"Continuous consumption → diminution of transformative power → cessation of growth → defect of restoration → diminution and death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AF1","text":"Doubt concerning nourishment → definition of the truth of nature → diminution of the position of primordial matter → conversion of nourishment into the truth of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AF2","text":"Objection concerning the flux of matter → distinction of form and matter → continuous substitution → preservation of numerical identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AF3","text":"Doubt concerning semen → exclusion of a resolved member → semen as potentially whole → subordination of the nutritive to the generative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:AF4","text":"Objection concerning consanguinity → separation of matter and form → derivation of generative power → genealogical likeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME1","text":"The human body is reclassified from an aggregate of original matter to a formal unity that continuously assimilates external matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME2","text":"The opposition between “native matter” and “nutritive matter” ceases to be an opposition between true and extrinsic humanity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME3","text":"The identity of the individual is transferred from the permanence of material parts to the continued order of conversion under the same form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME4","text":"Genealogy is reordered as the transmission of formal power through contingently assumed matter, not as the transmission of the same matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ME5","text":"Semen is placed between nourishment and member: it is neither crude external nourishment nor a part of a member actually distinct, but virtually total matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ALT1","text":"Surface — Whether nourishment is converted into the human body and whether semen is a superfluity of nourishment is determined affirmatively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ALT2","text":"Structural — Nutrition operates through the conversion of dissimilar matter into parts of the body, generation through seminal power ordered to the whole body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Objections presupposing material permanence are resolved by transposing the question to formal causality and the order of potentiality to act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — A living being remains the same through time not because unchanged matter persists, but because form orders successively assumed matter into one body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning the truth of nature, the assimilability of matter, formal identity, and semen as potentially whole suffice to restore both articles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT2","text":"The structure is most coherent where it joins nutrition, growth, restoration, and generation under the conversion of matter by degrees.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT3","text":"A fragile joint remains between the requirement of the identity of matter, posited in the objection, and the response that preserves identity through the continuity of form and material succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT4","text":"The precise criterion by which nutritive matter is said already perfectly to have received the “true nature of the species” remains indeterminate, especially between blood, semen, and a formed member.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GGVC__111:MRT5","text":"The argument preserves its proper movement: from the impossibility of closed matter it infers nutritive conversion, then from nutritive conversion it derives the structure of semen and formal genealogy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GGVC__111:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GGVC__111@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GGVC__111:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 120","title":"First Part · Question 119","context":"Chapter 120","original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 119"},"original_title":"Prima pars · Quaestio 119","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 01–03","order":1,"parents":["CH_GGVC_PPP0","CH_GGVC_PPQ1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_01@R001","sha256":"7de0084eb994311d1c4a4fd61d70158e07220a2fdfc98076f4ab53c87797d1d2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-01","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo doctrina, cuius finis et obiectum rationem humanam excedunt, incipienti finite cognoscenti communicetur sine veritatis reductione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-02","text":"Responsio globalis doctrinam sacram constituit ut ordinem mediationum: revelatio principia praebet, disciplina receptionem ordinat, effectus autem ascensum demonstrativum ad Deum aperiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A6","CH_GGVC_PPP0:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-03","text":"Argumentatio fit architectonica et reconstructiva, quia ex defectibus recipientis atque insufficientia cognitionis naturalis structuram scientiae et viam legitimam ad eius subiectum construit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-04","text":"Motus transit ab impedimentis transmissionis ad unitatem formalem doctrinae, deinde ab illa unitate ad mundum tamquam ordinem effectuum per quos primum principium cognoscitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-05","text":"Progressio est spiralis: Deus, ut principium et finis doctrinae, creaturas ordinat; creaturae vicissim ut signa et effectus cognitionem ad idem principium reducunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-06","text":"Totum systema asymmetria inter immediationem ontologicam Dei et mediationem epistemicam hominis regitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-07","text":"Clausura non est comprehensio quidditativa, sed cognitio realis existentiae, causalitatis et ordinis, intra limites litterae, effectuum et negationis disciplinatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-08","text":"Haec clausura condiciones scientiae stabilit, sed materialem ordinem totius doctrinae et cognitionem exhaustivam Dei aperte relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Finis supernaturalis et finita receptivitas humana simul revelationem atque accommodationem doctrinae requirunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A1","CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] Deus est centrum formale sacrae doctrinae, quia omnia ut subiectum, principium et finis ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Certitudo fontis et claritas recipientis distinguuntur, ita ut veritas maxime certa homini mediate et imperfecte pateat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Mediatio naturalis, sensibilis vel rationalis veritatem revelatam non destruit, sed receptionem eius secundum naturam humanam efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A15","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Unitas scientiae ex ratione formali cognitionis, non ex homogeneitate materiali rerum tractatarum, constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Ratio dupliciter ministrat: ex principiis fidei conclusiones elicit et ex effectibus creatis causam esse demonstrat, principia tamen revelata non constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A12","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D11","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Ordo tradendi est condicio cognitionis, non dispositio externa post veritatem iam constitutam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPP0:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Res inferiores cognoscuntur intra relationem ad Deum et funguntur effectibus, signis vel mediis, non terminis autonomis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Cognitio Dei terminatur ad affirmationem realem per effectus et remotionem, non ad comprehensionem quidditatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A17","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Pluralitas materiarum, sensuum et viarum stabilis manet quoad modos, sed ad unum primum principium formaliter convergit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-01","text":"Accommodatio redit cum mutatione: initio statum incipientium respicit, deinde figuram sensibilem amplectitur, tandem ascensum ab effectibus notioribus quoad nos ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-02","text":"Ordo a dispositione pedagogica contra occasionem migrat ad rationem formalem scientiae et deinde ad reductionem ontologicam plurium dependentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-03","text":"Incipiens ex categoria locali auditoris in figuram universalem cognoscentis humani mutatur, qui a sensu incipit et quidditatem divinam ignorat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-04","text":"Revelatio ex remedio insufficientiae naturalis in principium scientiae subalternatae mutatur, dum demonstrabilitas naturalis existentiae divinae intra eius ambitum subordinatum persistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-05","text":"Negatio ab eliminatione impedimentorum pedagogicorum ad remotionem praedicatorum inadmissibilium et exclusionem principiorum ultimorum plurium amplificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A17","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-06","text":"Repetitio inutilis localiter excluditur, sed multiplicitas functionaliter redit in viis convergentibus, ubi variatio dependentiarum non redundantiam sed confirmationem structuralem efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-01","text":"Multiplicatio quaestionum, inordinatio et repetitio manent vitia pedagogica localia; hoc gradu autem in legem generalem mutantur qua forma transmissionis scientialitatem receptam condicionat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-02","text":"Distinctio sensuum Scripturae manet machina hermeneutica inferioris gradus; sursum persistit solum principium quod multiplicitas semantica fundamento litterali contineri debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D16","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-03","text":"Gradatio auctoritatum est localis disputationi theologicae, sed amplificatur in regulam qua vis externa argumenti a principiis communiter admissis distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:NX12","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-04","text":"Quinque viae non singillatim globalizantur; hoc gradu fiunt variationes unius reductionis a diversis ordinibus dependentiae ad principium non dependens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-05","text":"Malum, natura et voluntas humana manent obiecta objectionum localium, sed eorum subordinatio regulam globalem instituit qua nulla realitas defectibilis vim principii ultimi obtinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-06","text":"Auxilium divinum manet condicio theologica exsecutionis, non substitutum ordinis disciplinaris neque ratio formalis scientiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-01","text":"Systema cognitionem Dei naturaliter immediatam, quidditativam et communem homini excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-02","text":"Neque ratio naturalis sibi sufficiens neque fides naturam auferens admittitur; earum relatio est asymmetrica perfectio et ministerium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-03","text":"Doctrina non constituitur accumulatione materiae aut ordine ab accidentalitate disputationis accepto.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-04","text":"Pluralitas sensuum, creaturarum et viarum non potest in autonomias aequivocas aut principia ultima plurima dissolvi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX10","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX11","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-05","text":"Neque conceptus existentiam rei producit neque effectus finitus causam infinitam perfecte comprehendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod accessibilitas intellectui humano sit mensura veritatis; aliter distinctio rei in se et cognitionis quoad nos corrueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod modus transmissionis veritati extrinsecus sit, quia ordo tradendi ipsam possibilitatem cognitionis constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:SNX5","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod mediatio recipientis certitudinem fontis contaminet; defectus claritatis subiectivae ad intellectum, non ad veritatem divinam, refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod scientia una materiam unius generis requirat; unitas hic ex lumine et ratione formali provenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod ens mobile, contingens aut causaliter medium ultimam sui explicationem praebeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSA-01","text":"Absentia circa quam systema ordinatur est visio directa quidditatis divinae: indisponibilitas eius revelationem, figuram, effectum et remotionem necessaria facit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSA-02","text":"Tribunal epistemicum neutrum supra revelationem et rationem excluditur, sicut demonstratio vera contra fidem impossibilis ponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSA-03","text":"Communicatio divina omni medio sensibili carens humanae cognitioni indisponibilis est, quia cognitio humana a sensu incipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX5","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSA-04","text":"Mundus ontologice clausus et finis creatus ad Deum non ordinatus possibilitates inadmissibiles sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-01","text":"Defectus recipientis scientiam non minuit, sed formam qua certitudo eius ordinanda et tradenda est determinat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-03","CL_GGVC_01:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-02","text":"Pluralitas argumentorum et materiarum legitimatur, dummodo diversitas modorum sub una ratione formali ad idem principium convergat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-05","CL_GGVC_01:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-03","text":"Necessitas revelationis et demonstrabilitas naturalis divini esse efficiunt oeconomiam epistemicam inclusivam sed inaequalem, non partitionem simplicem fidei et rationis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-01","CL_GGVC_01:GA-06","CL_GGVC_01:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-04","text":"Sensibile duplicem mediationem exercet: in Scriptura figuram ad intelligibile remittit, in mundo effectum ad causam; neutrobique terminus cognitionis fit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-04","CL_GGVC_01:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D14","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-05","text":"Cum Deus rationem formalem totius materiae praebeat, rectus ordo disciplinae teleologicus est, non mere didacticus aut editorialis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-02","CL_GGVC_01:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-06","text":"Res creatae simul ontologice dependent et semantice operantur: dependentia earum cognitionem primi principii efficit sine conversione earum in principia autonoma.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-08","CL_GGVC_01:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-01","text":"Sacra doctrina fit machina quae excessum obiecti supra recipientem in cognitionem ordinatam convertit, revelationem et structuram transmissionis coniungendo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-02","text":"Subiectum cognoscens non est possessor immediatus principiorum, sed recipiens disciplinandus qui ab ignorantia quidditatis per media ascendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:DNX6","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-03","text":"Realitas reconfiguratur ut ordo hierarchicus effectuum et signorum, in quo causalitas ontologica et significatio theologica sibi respondent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-04","text":"Tempus cognitionis est processus a sensu et disciplina initiali ad cognitionem perfectiorem Dei atque finem beatitudinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-05","text":"Vis strategica argumentationis variatur secundum principia cum interlocutore communia, dum certitudo interna doctrinae ex fonte divino invariata manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D12","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus principalis est Deus ut principium → revelatio → doctrina → interpretatio creaturarum et historiae → reditus cognitivus ad Deum ut finem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-02","text":"Cognitio a sensibili ascendit, proprietatem sensibilem removet et affirmationem de Deo renovat; terminus prior sic medium ulterioris ascensus fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-03","text":"Materiae et viae multiplicantur, formaliter uniuntur et iterum ut modi distincti deployantur; convergentia igitur diversitatem ordinat, non delet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-04","text":"Necessitas accommodationis ordinem materiae restringit, sed proprietas materiae vicissim limites accommodationis imponit, unde reordinatio fit recursiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPP0:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-05","text":"Attractor systematis est primum principium universale, ad quod omnis autonomia regionalis effectuum, finium et perfectionum reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B01","text":"Finis supra rationem + recipiens finitus + necessitas praecognitionis finis → exigentia doctrinae accommodatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B02","text":"Insufficientia cognitionis naturalis + principia a Deo data → revelatio salutaris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B03","text":"Revelatio + scientia superior + ratio formalis una → scientia subalternata cuius subiectum est Deus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B04","text":"Receptio sensibilis + figura + ratio ministerialis + fundamentum litterale → communicatio ordinata sine mutatione principiorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D14","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B05","text":"Effectus manifesti + ordines multiplices dependentiae → demonstratio causaliter convergens in principium primum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B06","text":"Affirmatio causae + remotio comprehensionis quidditativae → cognitio realis sed non exhaustiva Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A17","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AFM-B01","text":"Impedimenta receptionis → distinctio necessarii a superfluo → nova constitutio ordinis doctrinae → accommodatio disciplinata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPP0:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AFM-B02","text":"Finis supernaturalis → insufficientia rationis → revelatio → principia scientiae subalternatae → unitas formalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AFM-B03","text":"Ignorantia quidditatis → non-evidentia quoad nos → demonstratio ex effectibus → convergentia causalium → positio primi principii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AFM-B04","text":"Pluralitas materiarum et viarum → reductio formalis ad Deum → cognitio existentiae → clausura apophatica circa essentiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-01","text":"Pedagogia reclassificatur ut epistemologia operativa: brevitas, claritas et ordo fiunt condiciones cognitionis potius quam ornamenta expositionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:D6","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-02","text":"Scientia reclassificatur relatione ad lumen et rationem formalem, non possessione immediata principiorum aut catalogo materiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-03","text":"Certitudo et evidentia separantur: veritas potest secundum naturam certissima esse dum accessus humanus mediatus manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-04","text":"Oppositio fidei et rationis corruit; substituitur ordo praeambuli, complementi, subalternationis et ministerii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX6","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-05","text":"Mundus ex rerum collectione in campum effectuum, signorum et dependentiarum convertitur, cuius pluralitas ad causam et finem communem reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei proprietates sacrae doctrinae et quaestionem de existentia Dei explicite tractat, sub proposito institutionis incipientium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis revelationem, rationem formalem, ordinem disciplinae et dependentiam effectuum in unam mediationis architecturam componit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus lectionem et disputationem secundum principia concessa, gradus auctoritatis et limites demonstrationis denuo constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis realitatem ut dependentiam a principio immobili et historiam cognitionis ut ascensum ad finem futurum ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus doctrinam per objectiones, distinctiones et reductiones ordinat, ita ut forma argumentandi ipsam accommodationem quam statuit exsequatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-01","text":"Brevitas incipientibus requisita cum amplitudine et dignitate materiae tensionem servat; plenitudo indiscriminata excluditur, sed mensura compressionis non formaliter definitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPP0:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-02","text":"Distinctio certitudinis divinae et evidentiae humanae cohaerentiam servat, sed modum participationis certitudinis superioris non explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-03","text":"Philosophia ministerium exercet sine constitutione principiorum, sed limes inter manifestationem instrumentalem et dependentiam conceptualem instabilis manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-04","text":"Transitus a regressu causalium ad primum terminum et a gradibus perfectionis ad maximum causale nititur nexibus generativis non ulterius demonstratis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-05","text":"Auctoritas divina res ipsas significare facit, sed dependentia omnis sensus spiritualis a littera tensionem inter excessum semanticum et stabilitatem argumenti continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD7","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MP-01","text":"Notio incipientis mutatur ex statu pedagogico particulari in condicionem universalem intellectus humani qui a sensu procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MP-02","text":"Ordo mutatur ex criterio dispositionis doctrinae in structuram ontologicam qua diversa dependentiae genera ad principium reducuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MP-03","text":"Accommodatio mutatur ex brevitate et claritate in metaphoram sensibilem atque demonstrationem ab effectibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:D6","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D14","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MP-04","text":"Deus mutatur ex subiecto formali scientiae in terminum causalem viarum, dum prohibitio cognitionis quidditativae utrumque statum continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:HSI-01","text":"Imago occulta est machina descensus et reditus: lumen a scientia divina ad doctrinam descendit, doctrina autem creaturas ordinat ut ascensus ad principium fiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:FGS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum intra hanc machinam est discipulus et viator, non spectator absolutus: recipit principia, sensum ordinat et per effectus progreditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est ascensus disciplinaris a sensu praesenti per historiam signorum ad cognitionem et beatitudinem futuram.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio possibilis impedimenta accumulationis removet, mediis concessis utitur et inter demonstrationem, dissolutionem obiectionum atque remotionem apophaticam transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata praesentia sufficiunt ad restituendam accommodationem doctrinae, constitutionem scientiae revelatae et ascensum demonstrativum ab effectibus ad Deum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi una ratio formalis materiam multiplicem ordinat et ignorantiam quidditatis in methodum demonstrationis quia convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B03","text":"Minus determinata manent materialis ordo doctrinae, analogia subalternationis theologicae et nexus quibus quaedam viae primum terminum inferunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B04","text":"Systema hoc gradu cohaeret non identitate simplici, sed reditu variato eiusdem legis mediationis per pedagogiam, scientiam, hermeneuticam et causalitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B05","text":"Reductioni axiomaticae adhuc resistunt auxilium divinum ut condicio exsecutionis, participatio humana certitudinis divinae et pluralitas intentionum quae littera continet sine regula exhaustiva determinationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170643189594Z_e8016faa","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 01–03","source_sha256":"7de0084eb994311d1c4a4fd61d70158e07220a2fdfc98076f4ab53c87797d1d2","sha256":"a1097bace3b08bad643c32a6bac58a0a4d978f2252e839db09f1a197136a66b7","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:06:43.190535+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-01","text":"The central question is how a doctrine whose end and object exceed human reason is communicated to a finite knower who is beginning, without reduction of truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-02","text":"The global response establishes sacred doctrine as an order of mediations: revelation provides principles, discipline orders reception, while effects open a demonstrative ascent to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A6","CH_GGVC_PPP0:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-03","text":"The argumentation is architectonic and reconstructive, because from the defects of the recipient and the insufficiency of natural knowledge it constructs the structure of science and the legitimate path to its subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-04","text":"The movement passes from impediments to transmission to the formal unity of doctrine, then from that unity to the world as an order of effects through which the first principle is known.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-05","text":"The progression is spiral: God, as the principle and end of doctrine, orders creatures; creatures in turn, as signs and effects, lead knowledge back to the same principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-06","text":"The entire system is governed by the asymmetry between God's ontological immediacy and human epistemic mediation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-07","text":"The closure is not quidditative comprehension, but real knowledge of existence, causality, and order, within the limits of letter, effects, and disciplined negation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AS-08","text":"This closure establishes the conditions of science, but expressly leaves open the material order of the whole doctrine and exhaustive knowledge of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The supernatural end and finite human receptivity together require both revelation and the accommodation of doctrine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A1","CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] God is the formal center of sacred doctrine, because He orders all things as subject, principle, and end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The certainty of the source and the clarity of the recipient are distinguished, so that truth most certain becomes manifest to man mediately and imperfectly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Natural, sensible, or rational mediation does not destroy revealed truth, but renders its reception possible according to human nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A15","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The unity of science is constituted by the formal ratio of knowledge, not by the material homogeneity of the things treated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Reason ministers in two ways: it draws conclusions from the principles of faith and demonstrates from created effects that a cause exists; yet it does not constitute the revealed principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A12","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D11","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The order of teaching is a condition of knowledge, not an external arrangement after truth has already been constituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPP0:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Lower things are known within their relation to God and function as effects, signs, or means, not as autonomous termini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Knowledge of God terminates in real affirmation through effects and removal, not in comprehension of quiddity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A17","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The plurality of matters, senses, and ways remains stable as to modes, but formally converges upon one first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-01","text":"Accommodation returns with mutation: at first it concerns the condition of beginners, then embraces sensible figure, and finally orders ascent from effects better known to us.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-02","text":"Order migrates from pedagogical arrangement against occasion to the formal ratio of science and then to the ontological reduction of multiple dependencies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-03","text":"The beginner is transformed from a local category of the hearer into a universal figure of the human knower, who begins from sense and is ignorant of divine quiddity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-04","text":"Revelation is transformed from a remedy for natural insufficiency into a principle of subalternate science, while the natural demonstrability of divine existence persists within its subordinate scope.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-05","text":"Negation is expanded from the elimination of pedagogical impediments to the removal of inadmissible predicates and the exclusion of multiple ultimate principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A17","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RMD-06","text":"Useless repetition is locally excluded, but multiplicity returns functionally in convergent ways, where variation of dependencies produces not redundancy but structural confirmation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-01","text":"Multiplication of questions, disorder, and repetition remain local pedagogical defects; at this level, however, they are transformed into a general law by which the form of transmission conditions received scientificity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-02","text":"The distinction of the senses of Scripture remains a lower-level hermeneutical mechanism; above, only the principle persists that semantic multiplicity must be contained by a literal foundation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D16","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-03","text":"The gradation of authorities is local to theological disputation, but is expanded into a rule whereby the external force of an argument is distinguished from principles commonly admitted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:NX12","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-04","text":"The five ways are not individually globalized; at this level they become variations of one reduction from diverse orders of dependence to a non-dependent principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-05","text":"Evil, nature, and human will remain objects of local objections, but their subordination establishes the global rule by which no defectible reality possesses the force of an ultimate principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:CGD-06","text":"Divine assistance remains a theological condition of execution, not a substitute for disciplinary order or the formal ratio of science.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes naturally immediate, quidditative, and common knowledge of God for man.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-02","text":"Neither natural reason sufficient to itself nor faith removing nature is admitted; their relation is asymmetric perfection and ministry.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-03","text":"Doctrine is not constituted by an accumulation of material or by an order taken from the accidentality of disputation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-04","text":"The plurality of senses, creatures, and ways cannot be dissolved into equivocal autonomies or multiple ultimate principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX10","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX11","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:GNX-05","text":"Neither does a concept produce the existence of a thing nor does a finite effect perfectly comprehend an infinite cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that accessibility to the human intellect is the measure of truth; otherwise the distinction between the thing in itself and knowledge as to us would collapse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that the mode of transmission is extrinsic to truth, because the order of teaching constitutes the very possibility of knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:SNX5","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that mediation by the recipient contaminates the certainty of the source; the defect of subjective clarity pertains to the intellect, not to divine truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that one science requires material of one genus; unity here proceeds from light and formal ratio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that a mobile, contingent, or causally intermediate being provides the ultimate explanation of itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSA-01","text":"The absence around which the system is ordered is the direct vision of divine quiddity: its unavailability makes revelation, figure, effect, and removal necessary.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSA-02","text":"A neutral epistemic tribunal above revelation and reason is excluded, just as a true demonstration against faith is held impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSA-03","text":"Divine communication lacking every sensible medium is unavailable to human knowledge, because human knowledge begins from sense.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX5","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSA-04","text":"An ontologically closed world and a created end not ordered to God are inadmissible possibilities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-01","text":"The defect of the recipient does not diminish science, but determines the form in which its certainty must be ordered and handed on.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-03","CL_GGVC_01:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-02","text":"The plurality of arguments and matters is legitimized, provided that diversity of modes converges under one formal ratio upon the same principle.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-05","CL_GGVC_01:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-03","text":"The necessity of revelation and the natural demonstrability of divine being yield an inclusive but unequal epistemic economy, not a simple partition of faith and reason.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-01","CL_GGVC_01:GA-06","CL_GGVC_01:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-04","text":"The sensible exercises a double mediation: in Scripture it refers figure to the intelligible, in the world effect to cause; in neither case does it become the terminus of knowledge.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-04","CL_GGVC_01:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D14","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-05","text":"Since God provides the formal ratio of all matter, the right order of discipline is teleological, not merely didactic or editorial.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-02","CL_GGVC_01:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:XD-06","text":"Created things are at once ontologically dependent and semantically operative: their dependence makes knowledge of the first principle possible without converting them into autonomous principles.","refs":["CL_GGVC_01:GA-08","CL_GGVC_01:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-01","text":"Sacred doctrine becomes a machine that converts the excess of the object over the recipient into ordered knowledge, by joining revelation and the structure of transmission.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-02","text":"The knowing subject is not the immediate possessor of principles, but a recipient to be disciplined, who ascends from ignorance of quiddity through means.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:DNX6","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-03","text":"Reality is reconfigured as a hierarchical order of effects and signs, in which ontological causality and theological signification correspond to one another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-04","text":"The time of knowledge is a process from sense and initial discipline to more perfect knowledge of God and the end of beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:BSD-05","text":"The strategic force of argumentation varies according to principles shared with the interlocutor, while the internal certainty of doctrine remains invariant from the divine source.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D12","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-01","text":"The principal circuit is God as principle → revelation → doctrine → interpretation of creatures and history → cognitive return to God as end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-02","text":"Knowledge ascends from the sensible, removes sensible property, and renews affirmation concerning God; the prior terminus thus becomes the means of a further ascent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-03","text":"Matters and ways are multiplied, formally unified, and again deployed as distinct modes; convergence therefore orders diversity rather than abolishing it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-04","text":"The necessity of accommodation restricts the order of matter, but the property of matter in turn imposes limits on accommodation, whence reordering becomes recursive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPP0:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:RLE-05","text":"The attractor of the system is the universal first principle, to which every regional autonomy of effects, ends, and perfections is reduced.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B01","text":"End above reason + finite recipient + necessity of foreknowledge of the end → requirement of accommodated doctrine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B02","text":"Insufficiency of natural knowledge + principles given by God → salvific revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B03","text":"Revelation + higher science + one formal ratio → subalternate science whose subject is God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B04","text":"Sensible reception + figure + ministerial reason + literal foundation → ordered communication without change of principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D14","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B05","text":"Manifest effects + multiple orders of dependence → causally convergent demonstration in the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FGS-B06","text":"Affirmation of cause + removal of quidditative comprehension → real but non-exhaustive knowledge of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A17","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AFM-B01","text":"Impediments to reception → distinction of necessary from superfluous → new constitution of the order of doctrine → disciplined accommodation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPP0:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AFM-B02","text":"Supernatural end → insufficiency of reason → revelation → principles of subalternate science → formal unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AFM-B03","text":"Ignorance of quiddity → non-evidence as to us → demonstration from effects → convergence of causalities → positing of the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:AFM-B04","text":"Plurality of matters and ways → formal reduction to God → knowledge of existence → apophatic closure concerning essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-01","text":"Pedagogy is reclassified as operative epistemology: brevity, clarity, and order become conditions of knowledge rather than ornaments of exposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:D6","CH_GGVC_PPP0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-02","text":"Science is reclassified in relation to light and formal ratio, not to immediate possession of principles or a catalogue of matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-03","text":"Certainty and evidence are separated: truth can be most certain according to its nature while human access remains mediated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-04","text":"The opposition of faith and reason collapses; it is replaced by an order of preamble, complement, subalternation, and ministry.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:DNX6","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MME-05","text":"The world is converted from a collection of things into a field of effects, signs, and dependencies, whose plurality is reduced to a common cause and end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level explicitly treats the properties of sacred doctrine and the question of God's existence, under the purpose of instructing beginners.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level composes revelation, formal ratio, disciplinary order, and the dependence of effects into one architecture of mediation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level reconstitutes reading and disputation according to conceded principles, degrees of authority, and the limits of demonstration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level orders reality as dependence on an immobile principle and the history of knowledge as ascent to a future end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level orders doctrine through objections, distinctions, and reductions, so that the form of arguing itself executes the accommodation it establishes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPP0:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-01","text":"The brevity required for beginners maintains tension with the breadth and dignity of the matter; indiscriminate fullness is excluded, but the measure of compression is not formally defined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPP0:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-02","text":"The distinction between divine certainty and human evidence preserves coherence, but does not explain the mode of participation in higher certainty.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-03","text":"Philosophy exercises ministry without constituting principles, but the boundary between instrumental manifestation and conceptual dependence remains unstable.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-04","text":"The transition from the regress of causes to the first terminus and from degrees of perfection to the causal maximum rests on generative links not further demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:FL-05","text":"Divine authority makes things themselves signify, but the dependence of every spiritual sense on the letter contains a tension between semantic excess and argumentative stability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:SD7","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MP-01","text":"The notion of the beginner changes from a particular pedagogical state into the universal condition of the human intellect that proceeds from sense.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MP-02","text":"Order changes from a criterion for the arrangement of doctrine into an ontological structure by which diverse kinds of dependence are reduced to a principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MP-03","text":"Accommodation changes from brevity and clarity into sensible metaphor and demonstration from effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:D6","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D14","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MP-04","text":"God changes from the formal subject of science into the causal terminus of the ways, while the prohibition of quidditative knowledge contains both states.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:HSI-01","text":"The hidden image is a machine of descent and return: light descends from divine science to doctrine, while doctrine orders creatures so that ascent to the principle may occur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:FGS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:HSI-02","text":"The subject within this machine is a disciple and wayfarer, not an absolute spectator: he receives principles, orders sense, and progresses through effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:HSI-03","text":"Time is a disciplinary ascent from present sense through the history of signs to future knowledge and beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:A16","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:HSI-04","text":"Possible navigation removes the impediments of accumulation, uses granted means, and passes between demonstration, dissolution of objections, and apophatic removal.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B01","text":"The present axioms suffice to reconstruct the accommodation of doctrine, the constitution of revealed science, and the demonstrative ascent from effects to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B02","text":"The structure is strongest where one formal ratio orders multiple matter and converts ignorance of quiddity into a method of demonstration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B03","text":"The material order of doctrine, the analogy of theological subalternation, and the links through which certain ways infer the first terminus remain less determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ2:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B04","text":"At this level the system coheres not by simple identity, but by the varied return of the same law of mediation through pedagogy, science, hermeneutics, and causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_01:MRT-B05","text":"Divine assistance as a condition of execution, human participation in divine certainty, and the plurality of intentions that the letter contains without an exhaustive rule of determination still resist axiomatic reduction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPP0:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ1:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_01:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 01–03","context":"Prima pars · Prooemium · Prima pars · Quaestio 1 · Prima pars · Quaestio 2"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 04–06","order":2,"parents":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_02@R001","sha256":"51d04fffece8212a0c1adaafb4da43e8edca70d319b51ee08903f2df27cd4cef","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-01","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo primum principium, cuius quidditas directe non comprehenditur, simul omnino simplex, universaliter perfectum et radix bonitatis omnis esse possit sine compositione aut communitate generica cum effectibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis statuit Deum esse ipsum esse simplex, quod omnes perfectiones effectuum eminenter continet, dum ens creatum eandem actualitatem limitate recipit atque ideo bonum est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-03","text":"Actualitas est fundamentum commune: in principio excludit potentiam, ut plenitudo essendi perfectionem causaliter colligit, et in effectibus entitatem, perfectionem atque appetibilitatem constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-04","text":"Argumentatio fit apophatica in remotione compositionis, reconstructiva in restitutione perfectionis simplicis, et teleologica in conversione actualitatis participatae ad bonum et finem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-05","text":"Motus progreditur a remotione modorum creatorum ad concentrationem perfectionum in causa simplici, inde ad diffusionem participatam essendi et tandem ad ordinationem appetitivam omnis actualitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-06","text":"Motus verus est cumulativus et spiralis: obiectio identitatem apparentem frangit, distinctio ordines separat, et notio prior eadem manens novam functionem in gradu sequenti acquirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-07","text":"Causalitas transit ab efficientia et exemplari praesentia sine commixtione ad participationem analogicam, deinde ad prioritatem finis, qua bonum actualizationem dirigit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est causalis, analogica et teleologica, non quidditative definitiva: effectus cognitionem affirmativam praebent, remotiones transcendens principium custodiunt, analogia participationem ordinat, et bonum ordinem effectuum claudit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-01","text":"[Attractor] Actualitas est cardo generativus quo esse, perfectio, intelligibilitas et appetibilitas secundum rationes distinctas connectuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A12","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Primum principium est actus purus, ipsum suum esse et omnino simplex; nulla distinctio constituens ipsum antecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Compositio importat posterioritatem, dependentiam a componentibus et necessitatem causae adunantis; ideo primo principio convenire non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A15","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Simplicitas non est imminutio perfectionis, sed modus quo plenitudo absque aggregatione vel distinctione partium subsistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Omnis perfectio effectuum in causa universali praeexistit eminentiori et uniformi modo, non sicut forma recepta vel pars composita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Deus est ens et perfectus per essentiam; creaturae sunt entia et perfectae per participationem limitatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Causalitas primi principii est efficiens et exemplaris sine ingressu mereologico; in ordine boni dependentia effectuum etiam fine movente ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Ens et bonum sunt idem secundum rem actualem, sed differunt ratione, quia bonum eandem actualitatem ut perfectam et appetibilem significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Similitudo creaturae ad Deum est causaliter ordinata, analogica et non reciproca, quia relatio non coordinat duo membra eiusdem generis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Malum non est principium positivum, sed privatio actus debiti in subiecto bono, cuius entitatem omnino consumere non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A11","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Prioritas distribuitur inter ordinem essendi, intelligendi, causandi et perficiendi; hi ordines in unicam successionem reduci non possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Principium simplex perfectiones sine compositione concentrat, eas causaliter sine commixtione distribuit, et in effectibus ut actualitatem, perfectionem atque bonitatem participatam restituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-01","text":"Actus identitatem structuralem retinet, sed functionem amplificat: primo potentiam ex Deo removet, deinde perfectionem divinam mensurat, postremo entitatem, intelligibilitatem et bonitatem creatam generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-02","text":"Simplicitas transit ab exclusione compositionum ad principium positivum unitatis eminentis, quo diversae perfectiones in causa non dividuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-03","text":"Ipsum esse primo distinguitur ab esse communi, deinde plenitudinem omnis perfectionis continet, tandem ut actualitas fontalis relationem entis ad bonum aperit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D11","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-04","text":"Perfectio mutatur ab eo quod Deo non advenit in plenitudinem actualitatis causalis, atque inde in rationem qua actualitas effectus appetibilis fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-05","text":"Participatio progreditur a distributione defectiva eius quod in Deo est unum ad similitudinem analogicam, deinde ad bonitatem cuiuslibet actualitatis finitae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-06","text":"Causalitas mutat campum sine identitate amittenda: prima efficientia excludit dependentiam principii, causalitas exemplaris servat similitudinem, et causalitas finalis movet actualizationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-07","text":"Materia et potentia invertunt functionem: a constitutione primi principii excluduntur, sed in creaturis intra ordinem boni manent quatenus ad actum ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-08","text":"Negatio, opere apophatico peracto, non evanescit sed in structuram positivam absorbetur: remotio compositionis simplicem plenitudinem facit cogitabilem, quae actualitatem bonam diffundit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-09","text":"Multiplicitas nominum, perfectionum et rationum boni non constituit pluralitatem intrinsecam principii, sed modos conceptionis, effectus participatos et positiones functionales intra ordinem appetitus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-01","text":"Imagines membrorum, situs, motus et passionum manent solutiones locales praedicationis corporeae; ad gradum praesentem ascendit sola regula qua modus significandi creatus a constitutione divina separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX11","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-02","text":"Enumeratio inferior octo modorum compositionis non globalizatur ut index, sed amplificatur in legem unam: omne quod potentiam, partes vel causam unionis postulat a primo actu removetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-03","text":"Examen locale perfectionis, continentiae perfectionum et similitudinis fit commissura praesentis gradus, quia simplicitatem apophaticam in causalitatem participativam convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-04","text":"Modus, species et ordo manent architectura proxima perfectionis creatae; non transferuntur in Deum ut principia constituentia, sed indicant quomodo bonitas participata in effectibus integratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-05","text":"Honestum, delectabile et utile manent divisio localis motus appetitivi, sed praesentem structuram confirmant quatenus medium et quies a bono per se desiderato dependent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D12","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-06","text":"Obiectio de principio materiali imperfecto non simpliciter aboletur: ad primum principium est impossibilis, sed materia creata intra bonum per potentiam et ordinem recuperatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-07","text":"Distinctiones inter rem et rationem, causam et partem, conceptionem et causalitatem e solutionibus localibus in methodum globalem ascendunt, qua contradictiones apparentes per ordinum distributionem solvuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D10","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-01","text":"Systema excludit omnem potentiam, receptivitatem et compositionem intrinsecam a primo principio, quia haec actualizationem vel causam priorem exigerent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX9","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-02","text":"Deus non includitur in ente communi, genere, specie aut plano ontologico univoco quod ipsum cum effectibus coordinaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-03","text":"Causalitas universalis non permittit ut Deus materialiter vel formaliter effectus ingrediatur; praesentia causalis a compositione mereologica separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-04","text":"Plenitudo divina non est aggregatum perfectionum creatarum neque simultas oppositionum realium, sed earum praeexistentia simplex et eminens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-05","text":"Similitudo non est reciproca, quia effectus causam imitatur, causa autem ad effectum tamquam ad exemplar sui non ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A14","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-06","text":"Bonitas non est natura addita enti neque valor extrinsecus impositus, sed ratio perfectionis appetibilis quae actualitatem ipsam consequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-07","text":"Malum non potest esse substantia positiva, principium contrarium enti aut purum nihilum per se appetibile.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet primum principium esse receptorem essendi vel actualitatis, quia quod esse ab alio accipit iam intra ordinem causatorum cadit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A11","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet simplicitatem significare vacuitatem vel carentiam, alioquin principium simplex universalem perfectionum causalitatem sustinere non posset.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet esse minimum commune vel actualitatem axiologice neutram, quia omnis perfectio et appetibilitas ab actu essendi dependent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet finem rei extrinsecus et arbitrarie imponi, quia forma actualis inclinationem ad operationem et complementum infert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnes prioritates in unam successionem contrahi; talis contractio prioritatem entis in intellectu cum prioritate boni in causando confundit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet perfectiones creatas autonomum ordinem constituere, quia earum modus est participatio limitata causae quam perfecte imitari non possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-01","text":"Absentia fundamentalis est totalitas ontologica Deo prior: nullum planum univocum potest Deum, creaturas et perfectiones eorum tamquam membra homogena continere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-02","text":"Comprehensio positiva quidditatis manet indisponibilis, sed haec absentia sermonem non destruit; effectus, remotiones et analogia spatium cognitionis non comprehensivae constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-03","text":"Possibilitas indisponibilis est malum absolutum aut nihilum finale, quia privatio sine bono subiecto nec subsistere nec appetitum terminare potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-04","text":"Relatio causae primae et creaturae reciprocam clausuram non admittit: creatura causam imitatur, sed causa neque ab effectu mensuratur neque eiusdem ordinis similitudi subicitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-05","text":"Nullum actuale extra ambitum boni collocari potest; quod extra bonum absolute poneretur simul extra actualitatem et ens caderet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-01","text":"Simplicitas est condicio continentiae eminentis: nisi compositiones removerentur, pluralitas perfectionum causae universalis in partes receptas resolveretur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-04","CL_GGVC_02:GA-05","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-02","text":"Cum Deus sit ipsum esse, plenitudinem perfectionis contineat, et bonum cum ente secundum rem convertatur, bonitas divina non accidit essentiae sed cum esse divino identificatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-02","CL_GGVC_02:GA-05","CL_GGVC_02:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-03","text":"Perfectio creaturae, quia est participatio essendi, simul est vestigium analogicum causae et bonitas limitata eius actualitatis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-06","CL_GGVC_02:GA-08","CL_GGVC_02:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-04","text":"Causalitas divina potest esse universaliter productiva et finaliter ordinans sine compositione cum effectibus, quia efficientia, exemplaritas et finalitas dependentiam exprimunt, non ingressum partis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-07","CL_GGVC_02:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-05","text":"Transcendentia generis similitudinem non tollit sed eius modum constituit: quanto causa minus coordinatur effectui, tanto similitudo magis participatione quam identitate mensuratur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-06","CL_GGVC_02:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-06","text":"Materia a ratione primi principii excluditur, sed ab ordine boni non excluditur; eadem potentia quae perfectionem principii destrueret in effectu capacitatem ordinatam ad perfectionem significat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-01","CL_GGVC_02:GA-06","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-07","text":"Malum causae primae non opponitur ut principium aequale, quia tantum in bono causato subsistit et, si omne bonum auferret, proprium quoque subiectum destrueret.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-10","CL_GGVC_02:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-08","text":"Multiplicitas praedicatorum, perfectionum et rationum appetibilitatis non reintroducit compositionem in principium, quia dividitur inter conceptionem intellectus, pluralitatem effectuum et ordinem functionum creatarum.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-04","CL_GGVC_02:GA-05","CL_GGVC_02:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-09","text":"Actus est simpliciter prior potentia, ens prius bono in intelligendo, et bonum prius ente in causando; prioritas igitur relatio ordinata est, non proprietas univoca.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-01","CL_GGVC_02:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-01","text":"Simplicitas divina fit maxima densitas causalis: principium eo plura eminenter continet quo minus ex perfectionibus distinctis componitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-02","text":"Ontologia et axiologia realiter coextensivae sunt, sed formaliter non confunduntur: actualitas constituit ens, eadem vero sub ratione perfectionis appetibilis bonum constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-03","text":"Transcendentia non significat absentiam causalitatis, sed modum praesentiae sine commixtione: causa extra genus effectuum manet, dum ipsi eius esse et perfectionem participant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-04","text":"Creatura simul ontologice, axiologice et teleologice dependet: esse recipit, perfectionem limitatam possidet, et per formam ad complementum suum inclinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-05","text":"Malum acquirit statum ontologice parasiticum et causaliter subordinatum: non diffunditur ex principio contrario, sed oritur ubi participatio actus debiti deficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-06","text":"Intellectus et appetitus non aperiunt duas realitates, sed duos accessus ad eandem actualitatem: intellectus eam primo ut ens, appetitus ut perfectam et finaliter appetibilem attingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-07","text":"Causalitas non est series temporalis simplex: finis efficientem movet, efficiens formam inducit, et forma in effectu virtutem ac bonitatem completam antecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-08","text":"Cognitio principii est constitutive asymmetrica: existentia et causalitas ex effectibus tenentur, sed modus intrinsecus quo simplicitas omnes perfectiones unit non comprehenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus epistemicus procedit ab effectibus ad existentiam causae, ab existentia ad remotiones, et a causa sic purificata ad novam interpretationem effectuum tamquam participationum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AF1","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-02","text":"Via amplificationis actus est: immobilitas primi entis → plenitudo perfectionis primi agentis → actualitas communis ex qua entitas, cognitio et appetibilitas effectuum oriuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-03","text":"Via amplificationis negationis est: remotio compositionis → simplicitas positiva → continentia perfectionum → bonitas actualitatis participatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-04","text":"Circuitus causalitatis est: bonum ut finis movet efficientem → efficiens inducit formam → forma constituit actum → actus perfectus fit bonum appetibile; idem bonum antecedit causaliter et consequitur perfective.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-05","text":"Attractor participationis colligit transcendens principium, similitudinem analogicam et bonitatem finitam, ita ut distantia ontologica ipsa modum communicationis definiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-06","text":"Circuitus dialecticus recurrit: contradictio apparens → distinctio rationum vel ordinum → restrictio illationis → conservatio thesis in forma ampliore.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-07","text":"Privatio clausuram negativam efficit: malum bonum praesupponit, ipsum minuit, sed totaliter abolere nequit quin se ipsum cum subiecto destruat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B01","text":"Effectus finiti → cognitio existentiae primi principii → impossibilitas comprehensionis quidditativae → inquisitio per remotiones.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B02","text":"Remotio potentiae, receptivitatis et compositionis → exclusio dependentiae intrinsecae → simplicitas primi actus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B03","text":"Simplicitas primi actus + independentia essendi → identitas essentiae et esse → ipsum esse subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B04","text":"Ipsum esse simplex + causalitas universalis → continentia eminens perfectionum → plenitudo sine aggregatione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B05","text":"Plenitudo causalis sine commixtione → effectus limitati → participatio essendi → similitudo analogica et non reciproca.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B06","text":"Actualitas participata → entitas → perfectio → appetibilitas → bonitas secundum modum effectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B07","text":"Bonum ut finis → motio causae efficientis → forma et actus in effectu → bonum perfectum; defectus actus debiti → privatio localis, non principium contrarium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:AFM-B01","text":"Effectus cogniti → remotio compositionis → actus purus et ipsum esse → simplicitas absoluta → plenitudo eminens → participatio analogica → actualitas creata ut bonum → ordinatio finalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:AFM-B02","text":"Prioritas actus → exclusio principii materialis → perfectio primi agentis → continentia effectuum → distinctio realis causae ab effectibus → identitas realis entis et boni in effectibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AF1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AF1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:AFM-B03","text":"Praedicatio creata → distinctio rei a modo significandi → causalitas eminens → analogia participationis → distributio apparentium contradictionum inter ordines rei, rationis et causae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AF2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-01","text":"Simplicitas reclassificatur a minima complexitate in maximam intensitatem actus, quae multitudinem perfectionum sine partibus sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-02","text":"Esse reclassificatur ab indeterminato communi in actualitatem fontalem, ex qua forma, perfectio, intelligibilitas et bonitas derivantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-03","text":"Transcendentia reclassificatur a separatione sterili in causalitatem universalem sine commixtione, qua principium extra genera effectuum manet sed totum ordinem essendi fundat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-04","text":"Analogia reclassificatur a similitudine debili in structuram ontologicam participationis, quae communicationem perfectionis et inaequalitatem modorum simul servat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-05","text":"Oppositio ontologiae et bonitatis corruit: bonitas fit dimensio finalis actualitatis, quamvis distinctio rationum entis et appetibilis permaneat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-06","text":"Malum reclassificatur ab ente positivo vel principio cosmico in defectum localem actus debiti intra bonum subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-07","text":"Prioritas reclassificatur ex serie unica in tabulam ordinum distinctam, qua actus, ens et bonum singula sub diversa ratione prima esse possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-08","text":"Lectio apta systemati non potest imaginibus materialibus aut oppositionibus immediatis acquiescere; debet rationes, ordines causales et modos praedicationis distribuere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei examinantur remotiones compositionis, perfectio et similitudo divina, deinde relatio entis ad bonum, causalitatem finalem et divisiones appetibilitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali actus et potentia, essentia et esse, causalitas et participatio, forma et finis constituunt mechanismum recurrentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico systema interpretationem regit per remotiones, distinctiones ordinum et analogiam, ne modi cognitionis creatae in principium transferantur univoce.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas est dependentia potentiae ab actu et processus causaliter multiplex, in quo finis antecedit efficientiam, forma autem bonitatem completam in causato.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo forma disputativa ipsam structuram asseritam efficit: apparentias recipit, earum illationes distinguit, et contradictionem in ordinum pluralitatem convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-01","text":"Cognitio quidditativa negatur, sed identitas essentiae et esse demonstratur; cohaerentia pendet a distinctione inter comprehensionem modi divini et veritatem propositionis metaphysicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-02","text":"Simplicitas et continentia omnium perfectionum conciliantur per eminentiam uniformem, sed modus positivus huius unitatis manet non determinatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-03","text":"Analogia prohibet identitatem genericam et reciprocitatem, sed plena ratio eius nondum formaliter explicatur; structuram tamen causalitatis participativae sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-04","text":"Causalitas efficiens et exemplaris sine commixtione cum causalitate finali coniungitur, sed nexus formalis inter causalitatem primi principii et fines proximos effectuum compresse relinquitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-05","text":"Universalitas boni pendet a notione actus debiti; norma qua perfectio debita et ultimus actus determinantur praesupponitur potius quam plene deducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-06","text":"Res per primum actum est ens simpliciter sed bonum tantum secundum quid, per ultimum autem actum bonum simpliciter; bonitas igitur simul omnem actualitatem comitatur et complementum ulterius requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MP-01","text":"Actus mutatur ab instrumento exclusionis potentiae divinae in mensuram perfectionis et tandem in fontem communem entitatis, cognitionis atque appetibilitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MP-02","text":"Simplicitas mutatur a conclusione negativa ad principium unitivum, quo pluralitas perfectionum causaliter continetur sine pluralitate constituentium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MP-03","text":"Materia mutatur ab indice potentialitatis principianti Deo repugnantis in subiectum creatum quod ad bonum per aptitudinem et ordinem pertinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MP-04","text":"Similitudo mutatur a convenientia formae in relationem causaliter asymmetricam, cuius veritas ex participatione potius quam ex coordinatione nascitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A12","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite est quasi fons intensive simplex cuius plenitudo non dividitur, sed in effectibus tamquam modi limitati actualitatis, perfectionis et bonitatis distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum cognoscens fit duplex receptor eiusdem actus: intellectus actualitatem ut ens apprehendit, appetitus eam ut perfectionem quaerendam vel possidendam sequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-03","text":"Tempus causale non est linea unica, sed implicatio ordinum: finis movet ante productionem, efficiens producit, forma constituit, et quies appetitus completionem signat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-04","text":"Primum principium imaginatur ut centrum extra tabulam categorialem, non spatiale nec mereologicum, quod tamen totam tabulam causaliter et exemplariter sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-05","text":"Malum est cavitas localis intra fluxum boni, non rivus contrarius: defectus actus debiti manet dependens ab actualitate quam minuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de actu, simplicitate, esse subsistente, causalitate eminenti, participatione, conversione entis et boni atque privatione mali sufficiunt ad structuram praesentis gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B02","text":"Firmissimum centrum est concursus actus puri, simplicitatis et perfectionis: inde derivantur independentia principii, continentia causalium perfectionum et bonitas actualitatis participatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum satis determinantur modus positivus continentiae eminentis, plena ratio analogiae et norma qua actus debitus vel ultima perfectio effectus mensuratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B04","text":"Systema cohaeret non per seriem univocam, sed per reditum ordinatum actualitatis et per distinctionem ordinum essendi, intelligendi, causandi et perficiendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B05","text":"Commissurae minus explicatae nituntur principiis causalibus assumptis, transitu analogico a forma ad inclinationem et solutionibus dialecticis quae apparentias potius distribuunt quam positive exhauriunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B06","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat, sed reductio axiomatica non potest supplere id quod systema constitutive negat: comprehensionem quidditativam modi quo simplicitas, plenitudo et bonitas in primo principio unum sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170728114517Z_7ca59e46","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 04–06","source_sha256":"51d04fffece8212a0c1adaafb4da43e8edca70d319b51ee08903f2df27cd4cef","sha256":"d53f075c907ebb61729bed77ce0c6571f4ab3d714e10f6ee2b9e967b9c3ce7f0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:07:28.115589+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-01","text":"The central question is how the first principle, whose quiddity is not directly comprehended, can at once be wholly simple, universally perfect, and the root of all goodness without composition or generic community with effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis holds that God is subsistent simple being itself, which eminently contains all the perfections of effects, while created being receives the same actuality in a limited way and is therefore good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-03","text":"Actuality is the common foundation: in the principle it excludes potency, so that fullness of being entails perfection causally, and in effects it constitutes entity, perfection, and appetibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-04","text":"The argument proceeds apophatically in the removal of composition, reconstructively in the restoration of simple perfection, and teleologically in the conversion of participated actuality toward good and end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-05","text":"The movement advances from the removal of created modes to the concentration of perfections in the simple cause, thence to the participated diffusion of being, and finally to the appetitive ordering of all actuality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-06","text":"The true movement is cumulative and spiral: objection breaks apparent identity, distinction separates orders, and a prior notion, remaining the same, acquires a new function at the subsequent level.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-07","text":"Causality passes from efficient causality and exemplary presence without commingling to analogical participation, then to the priority of the end, by which the good directs actualization.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BAS-08","text":"The closure is causal, analogical, and teleological, not quidditatively definitive: effects furnish affirmative knowledge, removals preserve the transcendent principle, analogy orders participation, and the good closes the order of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-01","text":"[Attractor] Actuality is the generative hinge by which being, perfection, intelligibility, and appetibility are connected according to distinct formal accounts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A12","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The first principle is pure act, its own being itself, and wholly simple; no distinction constituting it precedes it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Composition entails posteriority, dependence on components, and the need for a uniting cause; therefore it cannot belong to the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A15","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Simplicity is not a diminution of perfection, but the mode by which fullness subsists without aggregation or distinction of parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Every perfection of effects pre-exists in the universal cause in a more eminent and uniform mode, not as a received form or a composite part.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] God is being and perfect through essence; creatures are beings and perfect through limited participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] The causality of the first principle is efficient and exemplary without mereological ingress; in the order of the good, the dependence of effects is also ordered by a moving end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Being and good are the same in respect of actual reality, but differ in formal account, because good signifies the same actuality as perfect and appetible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] The likeness of creature to God is causally ordered, analogical, and non-reciprocal, because the relation does not coordinate two members of the same genus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Evil is not a positive principle, but the privation of due act in a good subject, whose entity it cannot wholly consume.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A11","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Priority is distributed among the orders of being, understanding, causing, and perfecting; these orders cannot be reduced to a single succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] The simple principle concentrates perfections without composition, distributes them causally without commingling, and restores them in effects as participated actuality, perfection, and goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-01","text":"Act retains structural identity but expands its function: first it removes potency from God, then measures divine perfection, and finally generates created entity, intelligibility, and goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-02","text":"Simplicity passes from the exclusion of compositions to the positive principle of eminent unity, by which diverse perfections are not divided in the cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-03","text":"Being itself is first distinguished from common being, then contains the fullness of every perfection, and finally, as fontal actuality, opens the relation of being to good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D11","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-04","text":"Perfection changes from that which does not accrue to God into the fullness of causal actuality, and thence into the formal account by which the actuality of an effect becomes appetible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-05","text":"Participation progresses from the defective distribution of what is one in God to analogical likeness, then to the goodness of every finite actuality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-06","text":"Causality changes its field without losing identity: primary efficiency excludes the dependence of the principle, exemplary causality preserves likeness, and final causality moves actualization.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-07","text":"Matter and potency invert their function: they are excluded from the constitution of the first principle, but remain in creatures within the order of good insofar as they are ordered to act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-08","text":"Negation, once its apophatic work is done, does not vanish but is absorbed into a positive structure: the removal of composition makes simple fullness thinkable, and this diffuses good actuality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RMD-09","text":"The multiplicity of names, perfections, and formal accounts of good does not constitute intrinsic plurality in the principle, but modes of conception, participated effects, and functional positions within the order of appetite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-01","text":"Images of limbs, position, motion, and passions remain local solutions to corporeal predication; only the rule by which a created mode of signifying is separated from divine constitution rises to the present level.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX11","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-02","text":"The lower enumeration of eight modes of composition is not globalized as an index, but expanded into one law: whatever requires potency, parts, or a cause of union is removed from the first act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-03","text":"The local examination of perfection, the containment of perfections, and likeness becomes the joint of the present level, because it converts apophatic simplicity into participative causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-04","text":"Mode, species, and order remain the proximate architecture of created perfection; they are not transferred to God as constitutive principles, but indicate how participated goodness is integrated in effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-05","text":"The honorable, the pleasurable, and the useful remain a local division of appetitive motion, but confirm the present structure insofar as means and rest depend on the good desired for its own sake.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D12","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-06","text":"The objection concerning an imperfect material principle is not simply abolished: it is impossible with respect to the first principle, but created matter is recovered within the good through potency and order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:CGD-07","text":"Distinctions between thing and formal account, cause and part, conception and causality rise from local solutions into a global method, by which apparent contradictions are resolved through the distribution of orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D10","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes every potency, receptivity, and intrinsic composition from the first principle, because these would require actualization or a prior cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX9","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-02","text":"God is not included within common being, genus, species, or a univocal ontological plane that would coordinate him with effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-03","text":"Universal causality does not permit God to enter effects materially or formally; causal presence is separated from mereological composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-04","text":"Divine fullness is not an aggregate of created perfections nor a simultaneity of real oppositions, but their simple and eminent pre-existence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-05","text":"Likeness is not reciprocal, because the effect imitates the cause, whereas the cause is not ordered to the effect as to an exemplar of itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A14","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-06","text":"Goodness is not a nature added to being nor a value imposed extrinsically, but the formal account of appetible perfection consequent upon actuality itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:GNX-07","text":"Evil cannot be a positive substance, a principle contrary to being, or pure nothingness appetible through itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that the first principle is a receiver of being or actuality, because what receives being from another already falls within the order of caused things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A11","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that simplicity signifies emptiness or lack, otherwise the simple principle could not sustain universal causality of perfections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that being is the least common element or axiologically neutral actuality, because every perfection and appetibility depend upon the act of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that the end of a thing is imposed extrinsically and arbitrarily, because actual form entails an inclination toward operation and completion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that all priorities are contracted into one succession; such contraction confuses the priority of being in understanding with the priority of good in causing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that created perfections constitute an autonomous order, because their mode is limited participation in a cause which they cannot perfectly imitate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-01","text":"The fundamental absence is an ontological totality prior to God: no univocal plane can contain God, creatures, and their perfections as homogeneous members.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-02","text":"Positive comprehension of quiddity remains unavailable, but this absence does not destroy discourse; effects, removals, and analogy constitute the space of non-comprehensive knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-03","text":"The unavailable possibility is absolute evil or final nothingness, because privation without a good subject can neither subsist nor terminate appetite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-04","text":"The relation of first cause and creature admits no reciprocal closure: the creature imitates the cause, but the cause is neither measured by the effect nor subjected to likeness of the same order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSA-05","text":"No actual being can be placed outside the scope of good; what were posited absolutely outside good would simultaneously fall outside actuality and being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-01","text":"Simplicity is the condition of eminent containment: unless compositions were removed, the plurality of perfections of the universal cause would be resolved into received parts.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-04","CL_GGVC_02:GA-05","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-02","text":"Since God is being itself, contains the fullness of perfection, and good is convertible with being in reality, divine goodness does not accrue to essence but is identified with divine being.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-02","CL_GGVC_02:GA-05","CL_GGVC_02:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-03","text":"The perfection of a creature, because it is a participation of being, is at once an analogical trace of the cause and the limited goodness of its actuality.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-06","CL_GGVC_02:GA-08","CL_GGVC_02:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-04","text":"Divine causality can be universally productive and finally ordering without composition with effects, because efficiency, exemplarity, and finality express dependence, not the ingress of a part.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-07","CL_GGVC_02:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-05","text":"Transcendence of genus does not remove likeness but constitutes its mode: the less the cause is coordinated with the effect, the more likeness is measured by participation rather than identity.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-06","CL_GGVC_02:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-06","text":"Matter is excluded from the formal account of the first principle, but not from the order of good; the same potency that would destroy the perfection of the principle signifies in the effect a capacity ordered to perfection.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-01","CL_GGVC_02:GA-06","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-07","text":"Evil is not opposed to the first cause as an equal principle, because it subsists only in caused good and, if it removed every good, would also destroy its own subject.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-10","CL_GGVC_02:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-08","text":"The multiplicity of predicates, perfections, and formal accounts of appetibility does not reintroduce composition into the principle, because it is divided among the conception of the intellect, the plurality of effects, and the order of created functions.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-04","CL_GGVC_02:GA-05","CL_GGVC_02:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:XD-09","text":"Act is simply prior to potency, being prior to good in understanding, and good prior to being in causing; priority, therefore, is an ordered relation, not a univocal property.","refs":["CL_GGVC_02:GA-01","CL_GGVC_02:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-01","text":"Divine simplicity becomes maximal causal density: the principle contains more eminently insofar as it is composed less of distinct perfections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-02","text":"Ontology and axiology are really coextensive, but are not formally confused: actuality constitutes being, while that same actuality under the formal account of appetible perfection constitutes good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-03","text":"Transcendence does not signify the absence of causality, but a mode of presence without commingling: the cause remains outside the genus of effects, while they participate in its being and perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-04","text":"The creature depends simultaneously ontologically, axiologically, and teleologically: it receives being, possesses limited perfection, and through form inclines toward its completion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-05","text":"Evil acquires an ontologically parasitic and causally subordinate status: it does not diffuse from a contrary principle, but arises where participation in due act fails.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-06","text":"Intellect and appetite do not open two realities, but two accesses to the same actuality: intellect first attains it as being, appetite as perfect and finally appetible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-07","text":"Causality is not a simple temporal series: the end moves the efficient cause, the efficient cause induces form, and form precedes complete power and goodness in the effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:BSD-08","text":"Knowledge of the principle is constitutively asymmetrical: existence and causality are grasped from effects, but the intrinsic mode by which simplicity unites all perfections is not comprehended.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-01","text":"The epistemic circuit proceeds from effects to the existence of the cause, from existence to removals, and from the cause thus purified to a new interpretation of effects as participations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AF1","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-02","text":"The path of amplification of act is: immobility of the first being → fullness of perfection of the first agent → common actuality from which entity, knowledge, and appetibility of effects arise.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-03","text":"The path of amplification of negation is: removal of composition → positive simplicity → containment of perfections → goodness of participated actuality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-04","text":"The circuit of causality is: good as end moves the efficient cause → the efficient cause induces form → form constitutes act → perfect act becomes appetible good; the same good precedes causally and follows perfectively.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-05","text":"The attractor of participation gathers the transcendent principle, analogical likeness, and finite goodness, such that ontological distance itself defines the mode of communication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-06","text":"The dialectical circuit recurs: apparent contradiction → distinction of formal accounts or orders → restriction of inference → preservation of the thesis in a broader form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:RLE-07","text":"Privation effects a negative closure: evil presupposes good, diminishes it, but cannot wholly abolish it without destroying itself together with its subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B01","text":"Finite effects → knowledge of the existence of the first principle → impossibility of quidditative comprehension → inquiry through removals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B02","text":"Removal of potency, receptivity, and composition → exclusion of intrinsic dependence → simplicity of the first act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B03","text":"Simplicity of the first act + independence of being → identity of essence and being → subsistent being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B04","text":"Simple being itself + universal causality → eminent containment of perfections → fullness without aggregation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B05","text":"Causal fullness without commingling → limited effects → participation in being → analogical and non-reciprocal likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B06","text":"Participated actuality → entity → perfection → appetibility → goodness according to the mode of the effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FGS-B07","text":"Good as end → motion of the efficient cause → form and act in the effect → perfect good; lack of due act → local privation, not a contrary principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:AFM-B01","text":"Known effects → removal of composition → pure act and being itself → absolute simplicity → eminent fullness → analogical participation → created actuality as good → final ordering.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:AFM-B02","text":"Priority of act → exclusion of a material principle → perfection of the first agent → containment of effects → real distinction of cause from effects → real identity of being and good in effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AF1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AF1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:AFM-B03","text":"Created predication → distinction of thing from mode of signifying → eminent causality → analogy of participation → distribution of apparent contradictions among the orders of thing, formal account, and cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AF2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-01","text":"Simplicity is reclassified from minimal complexity into maximal intensity of act, which sustains a multitude of perfections without parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-02","text":"Being is reclassified from an indeterminate common element into fontal actuality, from which form, perfection, intelligibility, and goodness are derived.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-03","text":"Transcendence is reclassified from sterile separation into universal causality without commingling, by which the principle remains outside the genera of effects yet founds the whole order of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-04","text":"Analogy is reclassified from weak likeness into the ontological structure of participation, which simultaneously preserves the communication of perfection and inequality of modes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-05","text":"The opposition of ontology and goodness collapses: goodness becomes the final dimension of actuality, although the distinction of the formal accounts of being and appetibility remains.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-06","text":"Evil is reclassified from a positive being or cosmic principle into a local defect of due act subsisting within good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-07","text":"Priority is reclassified from a single series into a chart of distinct orders, by which act, being, and good can each be first under a different formal account.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MME-08","text":"A reading suited to the system cannot rest content with material images or immediate oppositions; it must distribute formal accounts, causal orders, and modes of predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, removals of composition, divine perfection and likeness, then the relation of being to good, final causality, and divisions of appetibility are examined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, act and potency, essence and being, causality and participation, form and end constitute the recurrent mechanism.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the system governs interpretation through removals, distinctions of orders, and analogy, lest modes of created knowledge be transferred univocally to the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, reality is the dependence of potency on act and a causally multiple process, in which the end precedes efficiency, while form precedes complete goodness in the caused thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the disputative form effects the asserted structure itself: it receives appearances, distinguishes their inferences, and converts contradiction into a plurality of orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS6","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-01","text":"Quidditative knowledge is denied, but the identity of essence and being is demonstrated; coherence depends on the distinction between comprehension of the divine mode and the truth of the metaphysical proposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-02","text":"Simplicity and the containment of all perfections are reconciled through uniform eminence, but the positive mode of this unity remains undetermined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-03","text":"Analogy prohibits generic identity and reciprocity, but its full account is not yet formally explained; it nevertheless sustains the structure of participative causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-04","text":"Efficient and exemplary causality without commingling is joined with final causality, but the formal nexus between the causality of the first principle and the proximate ends of effects is left compressed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-05","text":"The universality of good depends on the notion of due act; the norm by which due perfection and the ultimate act are determined is presupposed rather than fully deduced.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:FL-06","text":"A thing is being simply through the first act but good only in a certain respect, whereas through the ultimate act it is good simply; goodness therefore both accompanies every actuality and requires further completion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MP-01","text":"Act changes from an instrument for excluding divine potency into a measure of perfection and finally into the common source of entity, knowledge, and appetibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MP-02","text":"Simplicity changes from a negative conclusion into a unitive principle, by which a plurality of perfections is causally contained without a plurality of constituents.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MP-03","text":"Matter changes from an index of potentiality incompatible with an originating God into a created subject that pertains to good through aptitude and order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MP-04","text":"Likeness changes from agreement of form into a causally asymmetric relation, whose truth arises from participation rather than coordination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A12","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly like an intensively simple source whose fullness is not divided, but is distributed in effects as limited modes of actuality, perfection, and goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-02","text":"The knowing subject becomes a twofold receiver of the same act: intellect apprehends actuality as being, appetite pursues it as a perfection to be sought or possessed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-03","text":"Causal time is not a single line, but an implication of orders: the end moves before production, the efficient cause produces, form constitutes, and the rest of appetite marks completion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-04","text":"The first principle is imagined as a center outside the categorical chart, neither spatial nor mereological, which nevertheless causally and exemplarily sustains the entire chart.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:HSI-05","text":"Evil is a local hollow within the flow of good, not a contrary stream: the lack of due act remains dependent on the actuality it diminishes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:SD4","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms concerning act, simplicity, subsistent being, eminent causality, participation, the convertibility of being and good, and the privation of evil suffice to restore the structure of the present group.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B02","text":"The strongest center is the concurrence of pure act, simplicity, and perfection: from this are derived the independence of the principle, the containment of causal perfections, and the goodness of participated actuality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B03","text":"The positive mode of eminent containment, the full account of analogy, and the norm by which due act or the ultimate perfection of an effect is measured are not yet sufficiently determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B04","text":"The system coheres not through a univocal series, but through the ordered return of actuality and through the distinction of the orders of being, understanding, causing, and perfecting.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B05","text":"The less explicated joints rely on assumed causal principles, the analogical transition from form to inclination, and dialectical solutions that distribute appearances rather than positively exhaust them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ5:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ3:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_02:MRT-B06","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement, but axiomatic reduction cannot supply what the system constitutively denies: quidditative comprehension of the mode in which simplicity, fullness, and goodness are one in the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ3:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ4:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_02:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 04–06","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 3 · Prima pars · Quaestio 4 · Prima pars · Quaestio 5"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 07–09","order":3,"parents":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_03@R001","sha256":"22101a65747618b0c1ec7bc1e57349e5aa344e1fbe3a4e1e58db8fc9822f61d6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo bonitas, infinitas et praesentia divina de eodem principio praedicentur sine reductione ad bonum causatum, magnitudinem interminatam vel inclusionem localem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis est quod Deus, quia ipsum esse subsistens est, essentialiter bonus, simpliciter infinitus et omnibus intime praesens est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-03","text":"Creatura eandem perfectionem non possidet eodem modo: bonitatem formalem propriam habet, sed esse receptum, contractum et continue dependens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-04","text":"Argumentatio procedit per distinctiones modorum praedicationis et relationis, ne genus commune, quantitas aut localitas structuram causalitatis essendi usurpent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-05","text":"Motus progreditur a perfectione appetibili ad causam efficientem et finalem, deinde a modo essendi causae ad non-receptionem atque ab effectu essendi ad praesentiam conservantem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-06","text":"Progressio est recursiva: ipsum esse primo ut fons perfectionis, deinde ut actus non contractus, postremo ut effectus proprius continue causatus redit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-07","text":"Praedicata divina non adduntur lineariter, sed se mutuo interpretantur: eminentia modi essendi fundat simul excessum bonitatis, infinitatem et intimam causalitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est modalis: quidquid actu vel possibiliter esse potest divinam praesentiam requirit, quamvis praesentia specialis gratiae a causalitate communi distincta maneat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-01","text":"[Attractor] Deus est ipsum esse subsistens, cui esse non recipitur in alio nec ab essentia distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Omne esse creatum recipitur, ad naturam determinatam contrahitur et a Deo ut effectu proprio dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A11","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Causalitas divina est principium efficiens, exemplare et finale perfectionum atque causa conservans ipsius esse creati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Perfectio transit ab obiecto appetitus ad amplitudinem formae non contractae et tandem ad actum essendi rebus intimum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Participatio divina creaturae propriam bonitatem formalem constituit nec eam cum bonitate divina identificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Receptio creaturae simul determinat propriam actualitatem et excludit identitatem essentiae, infinitatem simpliciter atque subsistentiam independentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Transcendentia divina non distantiam producit, sed, cum causalitate immediata coniuncta, intimam praesentiam ad omne esse causatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:FGS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Praedicatio de Deo et creaturis nec univocatione generica nec aequivocatione inordinata regitur, sed causalitate et similitudine deficienti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Conservatio continua non est effectus posterior causalitati, sed ipsa forma ontologica praesentiae divinae in creatura persistente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Deus totus adest omni enti et omni loco possibili sine divisione, distributione partium aut commensuratione spatiali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] Infinitas simpliciter soli esse non recepto convenit; processus creatus infinitus tantum potentialiter vel successive procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-01","text":"Ipsum esse identitatem retinet, sed functionem mutat: fundamentum bonitatis essentialis fit ratio infinitatis et deinde principium praesentiae conservantis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-02","text":"Perfectio redit functionaliter: primo appetitum terminat, deinde carentiam contractionis significat, postremo ut esse intimum immediate causatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-03","text":"Participatio migrat a similitudine quae bonitatem formalem constituit ad receptionem quae finitatem inducit atque ad dependentiam quae praesentiam causae exigit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-04","text":"Infinitum vim invertit: privatio formae est imperfectio materialis, absentia autem receptionis est plenitudo actus formalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-05","text":"Causalitas exemplaris, effectiva et finalis extenditur in conservationem continuam, ita ut causalitas originis causalitas praesentiae fiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-06","text":"Relatio significata per “in” a continentia locali ad praesentiam causalem, manifestationem cognitivam et relationem obiecti operationis transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-07","text":"“Summum,” “infinitum” et “ubique” a maximis intra mensuram communem discedunt et modos excessus extragenerici, non-receptionis atque necessariae praesentiae designant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-08","text":"Analyses locales divisionis, numeri et successionis, opere negativo peracto, in regulam generalem absorbentur qua processus indefinitus a totalitate infinita actuali separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-01","text":"Appetitus naturalis et similitudo agentis manent machinae locales bonitatis, sed hoc gradu amplificantur in circuitum quo principium efficiens idem est ac finis perfectionis participatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-02","text":"Terminatio materiae per formam, figura quantitatis et mensura numeri manent probationes locales contra infinitum actuale; currenti gradu communem grammaticam receptionis et totalitatis praebent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-03","text":"Praesentia per gratiam est ramus specialis relationis rationalis, non principium ex quo bonitas, infinitas aut praesentia communis deducuntur; eius explicatio ulterius differtur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-04","text":"Distinctio inter essentiam et esse creatum sursum amplificatur: eadem receptio explicat bonitatem non essentialem, finitatem simpliciter et dependentiam conservativam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-05","text":"Eminentia quae localiter bonitates creatas non destruit fit hoc gradu nexus inter transcendentiam et intimitatem: causa excedens effectum ipsum esse eius immediate attingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-06","text":"Comparatio quantitativa, extensiva vel generica obsolescit ut schema globalis praedicationis; “summum,” “infinitum” et “ubique” per modum essendi recodificantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-01","text":"Deus et creaturae non participant genus commune bonitatis vel infinitatis cuius Deus summus gradus tantum esset.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:NX5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-02","text":"Deus non est forma intrinseca, pars essentiae aut accidens creaturae, quamvis eam causaliter intime constituat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:NX7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-03","text":"Creatura neque perfectionem ex se possidet neque esse simpliciter infinitum aut per se conservatum habere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-04","text":"Nulla magnitudo, multitudo aut successio creata constituit totalitatem infinitam actu completam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX7","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-05","text":"Praesentia divina non est extensio, receptio in loco aut occupatio competitiva eiusdem spatii cum corporibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-06","text":"Causalitas divina non absolvitur productione initiali neque sufficienter mediatur per causas creatas; praesentia specialis tamen ex qualibet perfectione superaddita non sequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet esse constituere rationem genericam neutralem quam Deus et creaturae uniformiter possideant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem carentiam termini univoce perfectionem aut imperfectionem significare; receptionis absentia et formae absentia contrarias rationes producunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet causam primam unam causam extrinsecam inter alias esse, quia eius causalitas ipsum esse immediate attingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet creaturae realitatem aut independentiam absolutam aut absorptionem formalem in bonitatem divinam exigere; participatio utramque possibilitatem excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet spatium receptaculum ontologice prius causalitate esse, cui divina praesentia postea applicetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet originem, conservationem et finem creaturae relationes separabiles esse: eadem causalitas perfectionem producit, esse sustinet et appetitum ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSA-01","text":"Nulla regio actualis vel possibilis entis extra causalitatem divinam cogitari potest; possibilitas ipsa essendi praesentiam causae postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSA-02","text":"Inadmissibilis est tertius modus quo aliquid simul creatum, ipsum esse subsistens et simpliciter infinitum exsisteret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSA-03","text":"Indisponibilis est creatura quae bonitatem propriam retineat sed actualem influxum primi boni et causae essendi non requirat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSA-04","text":"Systema circa duplicem impossibilitatem ordinatur: creatura nec extra Deum causaliter stare nec cum essentia divina formaliter identificari potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:NX7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-01","text":"Bonitas essentialis, infinitas simpliciter et praesentia intima sunt tres consequentiae eiusdem identitatis divinae cum esse subsistente: plenitudo perfectionis, immunitas a receptione et causalitas ipsius esse.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-01","CL_GGVC_03:GA-03","CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-02","text":"Eadem receptio qua creatura propriam bonitatem formalem acquirit eius esse contrahit atque continuam dependentiam constituit; proprietas creaturae igitur et dependentia non sunt oppositae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-02","CL_GGVC_03:GA-05","CL_GGVC_03:GA-06","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-03","text":"Transcendentia non-receptionis, causalitate immediata coniuncta, in intimitatem convertitur: Deus rebus non miscetur quia eas non recipit, sed eis intime adest quia esse earum causat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-01","CL_GGVC_03:GA-07","CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:FGS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-04","text":"Causalitas perfectionis circuitum efficientem et finalem format: quod a Deo ut similitudo procedit ad Deum ut bonum appetibile ordinatur, dum actus essendi eius praesentia conservatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-03","CL_GGVC_03:GA-04","CL_GGVC_03:GA-05","CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-05","text":"Quodlibet ens aut locus possibilis, si ponatur, esse receptum requirit; ideo ubiquitas divina non a magnitudine mundi sed ab universalitate causalitatis essendi sequitur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-02","CL_GGVC_03:GA-10","CL_GGVC_03:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-06","text":"Gratia causalitatem communem non auget, sed in creatura rationali novam rationem relationis instituit qua Deus obiectum cognitionis et amoris fit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-03","CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","CL_GGVC_03:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-07","text":"Infinitum potentiale creatum non est exceptio a finitudine, sed temporalizatio eius: post quodlibet finitum aliud sumi potest, nulla tamen totalitate infinita simul data.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-02","CL_GGVC_03:GA-06","CL_GGVC_03:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-01","text":"Ontologia emergens est participatio asymmetrica: creatura habet actualitatem formalem propriam, sed originem, mensuram et permanentiam eius a causa non recepta accipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-02","text":"Causalitas divina est non competitiva: quo immediatius Deus esse rei causat, eo firmius creatura propriam formam retinet et Deus intimior fit sine compositione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-03","text":"Tempus creatum bifariam ordinatur: permanentia est dependentia causalis continua, successio autem indefinita procedere potest sine constitutione totalitatis infinitae actualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-04","text":"Cognitio praedicatorum divinorum requirit analogiam modorum potius quam translationem directam: bonitas, infinitas et praesentia per causam, receptionem et relationem disambiguantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-05","text":"Subiectum creatum fit ens finite perfectibile quod propria forma bonum est, sed appetitu et conservatione ad principium suae perfectionis refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-06","text":"Spatium et possibilitas non constituunt exteriora Deo data; sunt ordines effectuum quorum quaelibet positio causalitatem divinam praesupponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus teleologicus est: appetitus quaerit perfectionem, perfectio similitudinem agentis participat, et similitudo effectum ad causam primam appetibilem reducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-02","text":"Circuitus ontologicus est: receptio essendi producit finitatem, finitas dependentiam, dependentia praesentiam conservantem, et conservatio permanentiam recepti esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-03","text":"Via amplificationis procedit a bonitate divina ut causalitate ad esse non receptum ut infinitatem, inde ad praesentiam intimam ut conservationem universalis effectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-04","text":"Attractor totius structurae est ipsum esse: sub eo appetibilitas, formalitas, infinitas, causalitas et praesentia in unum principium ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-05","text":"Negationes stratificantur: bonitas divina non est causata, infinitas non est materialis, praesentia non est localis; cumulatae positive definiunt actum non receptum et causaliter intimissimum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-06","text":"Distinctio actus et potentiae claudit reditum ab indefinita operatione ad infinitam rem actualem: quod semper continuari potest numquam propterea totum simul datur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-07","text":"Praesentia specialis a circuitu communi ramificatur: dependentiam ontologicam non substituit, sed relationem rationalem cognitionis et amoris super eam instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B01","text":"Ipsum esse subsistens → esse in nullo receptum → identitas essentiae et actus essendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B02","text":"Identitas essendi → plenitudo essentialis perfectionis + absentia contractionis → bonitas per essentiam + infinitas simpliciter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B03","text":"Prima causalitas → perfectiones et esse ut effectus proprii → principium exemplare, efficiens et finale creaturarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B04","text":"Participatio receptiva → similitudo divina formaliter inhaerens + contractio ad naturam determinatam → bonitas propria finita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B05","text":"Totalitas creata actu determinata → figura, numerus et terminus; successio potentiae admixta → processus indefinitus sine infinito actuali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B06","text":"Causatio continua ipsius esse → coniunctio immediata causae et effectus → praesentia divina intima sine compositione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B07","text":"Omne esse actuale vel possibile → necessitas causalitatis divinae → ubiquitas primi et per se; cognitio et amor per gratiam → praesentia specialis subordinata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:AFM-B01","text":"Bonum appetibile → perfectio participata → causa prima → bonitas essentialis → ipsum esse subsistens → non-receptio → infinitas → esse creatum receptum → conservatio continua → praesentia intima → ubiquitas modalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AF1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:AFM-B02","text":"Univocatio generica → distinctio causalitatis; infinitum quantitativum → distinctio actus et potentiae; inclusio localis → distinctio praesentiae causalis: errores de mensura communi successive dissolvuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:AFM-B03","text":"Praesentia communis per esse → creatura rationalis capax cognitionis et amoris → gratia → modus specialis relationis ad Deum ut obiectum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-01","text":"Bonitas, infinitas et praesentia desinunt esse regiones attributivas separatae et fiunt aspectus coordinati metaphysicae perfectionis, non-receptionis et causalitatis essendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-02","text":"Oppositio inter transcendentiam et immanentiam causalem corruit: Deus eo intimior effectui est quo minus eius esse modo receptivo participat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:FGS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-03","text":"Oppositio inter dependentiam et proprietatem creaturae corruit: bonitas formalis propria non minuitur sed constituitur causalitate participata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-04","text":"Infinitas reclassificatur secundum modum essendi: divina est actualis plenitudo non recepta, creata autem indefinita potentia divisionis, additionis vel successionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-05","text":"Spatium et tempus a mensuris divini actus in modos creaturae convertuntur: locus causalitatem non circumscribit, successio totalitatem infinitam non constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-06","text":"Lectio valida obiectiones ut errores translationis inter modos tractare debet: a genere ad causam, a potentia ad actum et a situ ad praesentiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei affirmantur bonitas summa et essentialis Dei, infinitas eius, praesentia in omnibus et proprietas ubiquitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali operantur causalitas, participatio, receptio, contractio et conservatio, quae perfectionem creatam simul constituunt et finiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico certamen movetur contra translationes illegitimas inter praedicationem genericam, totalitatem actualem, processum potentialem et praesentiam localem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali Deus est actus essendi non receptus, creatura autem ens perfectibile cuius permanentia influxum praesentem requirit et cuius successio numquam tota simul datur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo textus terminos recurrentes in campos novos transfert, ita ut ipsa successio distinctionum univocationem, quantificationem et localizationem dissolvat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-01","text":"Transitus a similitudine causae ad appetitum Dei pendet ab ordine teleologico causaliter instituto; hic ordo supponitur potius quam intra cluster integre demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-02","text":"Transitus a causalitate immediata ad praesentiam nititur principio quod agens effectui suo coniungi debet, principio ex metaphysica vel physica antecedenti recepto.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-03","text":"Bonitas propria creaturae et totalis dependentia eius cohaerent per participationem, sed modus precisus quo causalitas divina formam creatam constituit ulterius non explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-04","text":"Exclusio infiniti actualis creati pendet a nexu inter actualitatem totalem, figuram, numerum et terminationem; si hic nexus solvatur, clausura quantitativa vacillat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-05","text":"Ubiquitas ad loca possibilia extenditur contrafactualiter; vis conclusionis pendet ab universalitate principii quod nihil possibile esse potest sine causalitate divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-06","text":"Modus specialis praesentiae per gratiam classificatur, sed ratio singularis unionis deliberate incompleta manet et a clausura communis causalitatis non derivatur exhaustive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MP-01","text":"Bonum mutatur ab eo quod appetitur in structuram metaphysicam perfectionis causatae, similitudinis participatae et finis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MP-02","text":"Infinitum mutatur a privatione materiali imperfecta in eminentiam positivam ipsius esse non recepti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MP-03","text":"“Esse in” mutatur ab inclusione contenti in continente in coniunctionem causae agentis cum effectu essendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MP-04","text":"Totalitas mutatur a toto quantitativo simul terminato ad praesentiam totius essentiae divinae sine commensuratione partium et loci.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-01","text":"Imago occulta realitatis est actus fontalis non receptus qui actus finitos receptos producit et sine interpolatione continue conservat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-02","text":"Creatura intra hanc machinam est centrum finitum formae propriae, bonum participatione et ad fontem perfectionis appetitive atque causaliter relatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est duplex: persistentia rei est causalitas praesens, successio autem via semper continuabilis quae numquam in infinitum totum simul clauditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-04","text":"Spatium non est vas externum, sed ordo locorum et corporum quos causalitas incorporalis per contactum virtutis contingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-05","text":"Navigatio possibilis fit per distinctionem relationum: creatura a causalitate communi numquam exit, sed per cognitionem et amorem in relationem specialem transire potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de ipso esse subsistente, esse creato recepto et causalitate conservante sufficiunt ad nucleum bonitatis, infinitatis et praesentiae restituendum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est oppositio asymmetrica inter identitatem Dei cum esse et receptionem creaturae, quia ex ea essentialitas, finitas et dependentia directe ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B03","text":"Modus participationis nondum satis determinatus manet: distinctio causae divinae et formae creatae contradictionem impedit, sed constitutionem formalem creaturae non exhaustive explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B04","text":"Clausura contra infinitum actuale cohaeret tantum retentis principiis de actu, figura, numero et simultanea totalitate; haec sunt condiciones reconstructionis, non merae illustrationes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B05","text":"Restitutio praesentiae requirit principium coniunctionis immediati agentis cum effectu et metaphysicam contactus incorporalis, quae hic assumuntur sed non iterum demonstrantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B06","text":"Cluster cohaeret ut progressio ab bonitate causali per infinitatem non receptam ad praesentiam conservantem; praesentia specialis gratiae tamen reductioni completae resistit et aperta manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170809813619Z_8bf4dccd","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 07–09","source_sha256":"22101a65747618b0c1ec7bc1e57349e5aa344e1fbe3a4e1e58db8fc9822f61d6","sha256":"6e0244f56f4f0ec78316a0e43bf4e19267c31d46648ba94b21aafc5ec51008a4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:08:09.815043+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how goodness, infinity, and divine presence are predicated of the same principle without reduction to caused good, unbounded magnitude, or local inclusion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis is that God, because He is subsistent being itself, is essentially good, simply infinite, and intimately present to all things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-03","text":"A creature does not possess the same perfection in the same way: it has its own formal goodness, but received, contracted, and continuously dependent being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-04","text":"The argument proceeds through distinctions of modes of predication and relation, lest a common genus, quantity, or locality usurp the structure of the causality of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-05","text":"The movement advances from desirable perfection to efficient and final cause, then from the mode of being of the cause to non-reception, and from the effect of being to conserving presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-06","text":"The progression is recursive: being itself returns first as the source of perfection, then as uncontracted act, and finally as a proper effect continuously caused.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-07","text":"Divine predicates are not added linearly, but mutually interpret one another: the eminence of the mode of being grounds at once the excess of goodness, infinity, and intimate causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BAS-08","text":"The closure is modal: whatever can be actually or possibly requires divine presence, although the special presence of grace remains distinct from common causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-01","text":"[Attractor] God is subsistent being itself, whose being is neither received in another nor distinguished from essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Every created being is received, contracted to a determinate nature, and depends on God as upon its proper effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A11","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Divine causality is the efficient, exemplary, and final principle of perfections and the conserving cause of created being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Perfection passes from the object of appetite to the amplitude of uncontracted form and finally to the act of being most intimate to things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Divine participation constitutes the creature's own formal goodness and does not identify it with divine goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Creaturely reception simultaneously determines its own actuality and excludes identity of essence, infinity simply speaking, and independent subsistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Divine transcendence does not produce distance but, joined to immediate causality, intimate presence to every caused being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:FGS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Predication concerning God and creatures is governed neither by generic univocity nor by disordered equivocity, but by causality and deficient likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Continuous conservation is not an effect subsequent to causality, but the very ontological form of divine presence in the persisting creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] God is wholly present to every being and every possible place without division, distribution of parts, or spatial commensuration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] Infinity simply speaking belongs to unreceived being alone; an infinite created process proceeds only potentially or successively.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-01","text":"Being itself retains its identity but changes function: the foundation of essential goodness becomes the ground of infinity and then the principle of conserving presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-02","text":"Perfection returns functionally: first it terminates appetite, then signifies the lack of contraction, and finally is immediately caused as intimate being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-03","text":"Participation migrates from likeness constituting formal goodness to reception inducing finitude, and to dependence requiring the presence of the cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-04","text":"The infinite reverses its force: privation of form is material imperfection, whereas absence of reception is fullness of formal act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-05","text":"Exemplary, efficient, and final causality extends into continuous conservation, so that causality of origin becomes causality of presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-06","text":"The relation signified by “in” is transferred from local containment to causal presence, cognitive manifestation, and the relation of the object of operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-07","text":"“Highest,” “infinite,” and “everywhere” depart from maxima within a common measure and designate modes of extra-generic excess, non-reception, and necessary presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RMD-08","text":"Local analyses of division, number, and succession, once their negative work is completed, are absorbed into the general rule by which an indefinite process is separated from an actually infinite totality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-01","text":"Natural appetite and likeness to the agent remain local engines of goodness, but at this level they are amplified into a circuit in which the efficient principle is the same as the end of participated perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A5","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-02","text":"The termination of matter by form, the figure of quantity, and the measure of number remain local proofs against the actual infinite; at the current level they provide a common grammar of reception and totality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-03","text":"Presence through grace is a special branch of rational relation, not a principle from which goodness, infinity, or common presence are deduced; its explanation is deferred further.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-04","text":"The distinction between essence and created being is amplified upward: the same reception explains non-essential goodness, finitude simply speaking, and conserving dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-05","text":"The eminence that locally does not destroy created goodnesses becomes at this level the nexus between transcendence and intimacy: the cause exceeding the effect immediately reaches its very being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:CGD-06","text":"Quantitative, extensive, or generic comparison becomes obsolete as a schema of global predication; “highest,” “infinite,” and “everywhere” are recodified through the mode of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-01","text":"God and creatures do not share a common genus of goodness or infinity of which God would be merely the highest degree.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:NX5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-02","text":"God is not an intrinsic form, a part of essence, or an accident of the creature, although He causally constitutes it intimately.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:NX7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-03","text":"The creature neither possesses perfection from itself nor can have being simply infinite or conserved through itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-04","text":"No created magnitude, multitude, or succession constitutes an actually complete infinite totality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX7","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-05","text":"Divine presence is not extension, reception in a place, or competitive occupation of the same space with bodies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:GNX-06","text":"Divine causality is not completed by initial production nor sufficiently mediated through created causes; nevertheless, special presence does not follow from every superadded perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that being constitutes a neutral generic account uniformly possessed by God and creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that every lack of a limit univocally signifies perfection or imperfection; absence of reception and absence of form produce contrary accounts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that the first cause is one extrinsic cause among others, because its causality immediately reaches being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that the reality of the creature requires either absolute independence or formal absorption into divine goodness; participation excludes both possibilities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that space is a receptacle ontologically prior to causality, to which divine presence is subsequently applied.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that the origin, conservation, and end of the creature are separable relations: the same causality produces perfection, sustains being, and orders appetite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSA-01","text":"No actual or possible region of being can be conceived outside divine causality; the very possibility of being demands the presence of the cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSA-02","text":"A third mode is inadmissible in which something would exist simultaneously as created, subsistent being itself, and simply infinite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSA-03","text":"A creature is unavailable that retains its own goodness but does not require the actual influx of the first good and cause of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSA-04","text":"The system is ordered around a double impossibility: the creature can neither stand causally outside God nor be formally identified with the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:NX7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-01","text":"Essential goodness, infinity simply speaking, and intimate presence are three consequences of the same divine identity with subsistent being: fullness of perfection, immunity from reception, and causality of being itself.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-01","CL_GGVC_03:GA-03","CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-02","text":"The same reception by which the creature acquires its own formal goodness contracts its being and constitutes continuous dependence; therefore, creaturely propriety and dependence are not opposites.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-02","CL_GGVC_03:GA-05","CL_GGVC_03:GA-06","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-03","text":"The transcendence of non-reception, joined to immediate causality, is converted into intimacy: God is not mixed with things because He does not receive them, but is intimately present to them because He causes their being.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-01","CL_GGVC_03:GA-07","CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:FGS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-04","text":"The causality of perfection forms an efficient and final circuit: what proceeds from God as likeness is ordered to God as desirable good, while its act of being is conserved by His presence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-03","CL_GGVC_03:GA-04","CL_GGVC_03:GA-05","CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-05","text":"Any possible being or place, if posited, requires received being; therefore divine ubiquity follows not from the magnitude of the world but from the universality of the causality of being.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-02","CL_GGVC_03:GA-10","CL_GGVC_03:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-06","text":"Grace does not augment common causality, but establishes in the rational creature a new account of relation by which God becomes the object of knowledge and love.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-03","CL_GGVC_03:GA-09","CL_GGVC_03:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:XD-07","text":"The potential infinite in creatures is not an exception to finitude, but its temporalization: after any finite thing another can be taken, yet no infinite totality is given all at once.","refs":["CL_GGVC_03:GA-02","CL_GGVC_03:GA-06","CL_GGVC_03:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-01","text":"The emergent ontology is asymmetric participation: the creature has its own formal actuality, but receives its origin, measure, and permanence from the unreceived cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-02","text":"Divine causality is non-competitive: the more immediately God causes the being of a thing, the more firmly the creature retains its own form and the more intimate God becomes without composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-03","text":"Created time is ordered in two ways: permanence is continuous causal dependence, while succession can proceed indefinitely without constituting an actually infinite totality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-04","text":"Knowledge of divine predicates requires an analogy of modes rather than direct translation: goodness, infinity, and presence are disambiguated through cause, reception, and relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-05","text":"The created subject becomes a finitely perfectible being that is good through its own form, but is referred by appetite and conservation to the principle of its perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:BSD-06","text":"Space and possibility do not constitute external things given to God; they are orders of effects, each positing of which presupposes divine causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD6","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-01","text":"The teleological circuit is this: appetite seeks perfection, perfection participates in the likeness of the agent, and likeness leads the effect back to the desirable first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-02","text":"The ontological circuit is this: reception of being produces finitude, finitude dependence, dependence conserving presence, and conservation the permanence of received being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-03","text":"The path of amplification proceeds from divine goodness as causality to unreceived being as infinity, thence to intimate presence as conservation of a universal effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-04","text":"The attractor of the whole structure is being itself: under it desirability, formality, infinity, causality, and presence are ordered into one principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A6","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-05","text":"Negations are stratified: divine goodness is not caused, infinity is not material, presence is not local; cumulatively they positively define an unreceived act causally most intimate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-06","text":"The distinction of act and potency closes the return from indefinite operation to an infinite actual thing: what can always be continued is never thereby given wholly at once.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:RLE-07","text":"Special presence branches off from the common circuit: it does not replace ontological dependence, but establishes upon it the rational relation of knowledge and love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B01","text":"Subsistent being itself → being received in nothing → identity of essence and act of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B02","text":"Identity of being → essential fullness of perfection + absence of contraction → goodness through essence + infinity simply speaking.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B03","text":"First causality → perfections and being as proper effects → exemplary, efficient, and final principle of creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B04","text":"Receptive participation → formally inhering divine likeness + contraction to a determinate nature → finite proper goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B05","text":"Actually determined created totality → figure, number, and limit; succession mixed with potency → indefinite process without an actual infinite.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B06","text":"Continuous causation of being itself → immediate conjunction of cause and effect → intimate divine presence without composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FGS-B07","text":"Every actual or possible being → necessity of divine causality → ubiquity of the first and through itself; knowledge and love through grace → subordinated special presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A13","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:AFM-B01","text":"Desirable good → participated perfection → first cause → essential goodness → subsistent being itself → non-reception → infinity → received created being → continuous conservation → intimate presence → modal ubiquity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AF1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:AFM-B02","text":"Generic univocity → distinction of causality; quantitative infinite → distinction of act and potency; local inclusion → distinction of causal presence: errors concerning common measure are successively dissolved.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:AFM-B03","text":"Common presence through being → rational creature capable of knowledge and love → grace → special mode of relation to God as object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-01","text":"Goodness, infinity, and presence cease to be separate attributive regions and become coordinated aspects of a metaphysics of perfection, non-reception, and the causality of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-02","text":"The opposition between transcendence and causal immanence collapses: God is more intimate to the effect insofar as its being participates less in a receptive mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:FGS5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-03","text":"The opposition between dependence and creaturely propriety collapses: proper formal goodness is not diminished but constituted by participated causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME2","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-04","text":"Infinity is reclassified according to the mode of being: divine infinity is unreceived actual fullness, whereas created infinity is the indefinite potency of division, addition, or succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-05","text":"Space and time are converted from measures of divine act into modes of the creature: place does not circumscribe causality, and succession does not constitute an infinite totality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MME-06","text":"A valid reading must treat objections as errors of translation between modes: from genus to cause, from potency to act, and from position to presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the supreme and essential goodness of God, His infinity, presence in all things, and the property of ubiquity are affirmed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, causality, participation, reception, contraction, and conservation operate, simultaneously constituting and limiting created perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the contest is directed against illegitimate translations between generic predication, actual totality, potential process, and local presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, God is unreceived act of being, whereas the creature is a perfectible being whose permanence requires present influx and whose succession is never given wholly at once.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the text transfers recurrent terms into new fields, so that the very succession of distinctions dissolves univocation, quantification, and localization.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:AS6","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-01","text":"The transition from likeness of the cause to appetite for God depends on a teleological order causally instituted; this order is presupposed rather than fully demonstrated within the cluster.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-02","text":"The transition from immediate causality to presence rests on the principle that an agent must be conjoined to its effect, a principle received from prior metaphysics or physics.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-03","text":"The creature's own goodness and its total dependence cohere through participation, but the precise manner in which divine causality constitutes created form is not further explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-04","text":"The exclusion of a created actual infinite depends on the nexus between total actuality, figure, number, and termination; if this nexus is dissolved, the quantitative closure wavers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-05","text":"Ubiquity is extended counterfactually to possible places; the force of the conclusion depends on the universality of the principle that nothing possible can be without divine causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:FL-06","text":"The special mode of presence through grace is classified, but the singular account of union deliberately remains incomplete and is not exhaustively derived from the closure of common causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MP-01","text":"Good is transformed from that which is desired into the metaphysical structure of caused perfection, participated likeness, and end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MP-02","text":"The infinite is transformed from imperfect material privation into the positive eminence of unreceived being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MP-03","text":"“To be in” is transformed from the inclusion of content in container into the conjunction of the agent cause with the effect of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MP-04","text":"Totality is transformed from a quantitative whole simultaneously terminated into the presence of the whole divine essence without commensuration of parts and place.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:A9","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-01","text":"The hidden image of reality is an unreceived fontal act that produces received finite acts and continuously conserves them without interpolation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-02","text":"Within this mechanism, the creature is a finite center of its own form, good by participation and referred appetitively and causally to the source of perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-03","text":"Time is twofold: the persistence of a thing is present causality, whereas succession is an ever-continuable path that is never closed into an infinite whole simultaneously.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD1","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-04","text":"Space is not an external vessel, but an order of places and bodies which incorporeal causality touches through contact of power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:HSI-05","text":"Navigation becomes possible through the distinction of relations: the creature never exits common causality, but through knowledge and love can pass into a special relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:SD5","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B01","text":"Axioms concerning subsistent being itself, received created being, and conserving causality suffice to restore the core of goodness, infinity, and presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the asymmetric opposition between God's identity with being and creaturely reception, because essentiality, finitude, and dependence are directly ordered from it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:FGS4","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B03","text":"The mode of participation remains insufficiently determined: the distinction between divine cause and created form prevents contradiction, but does not exhaustively explain the creature's formal constitution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B04","text":"The closure against the actual infinite coheres only if the principles concerning act, figure, number, and simultaneous totality are retained; these are conditions of reconstruction, not mere illustrations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ7:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B05","text":"The restoration of presence requires the principle of the conjunction of an immediate agent with its effect and a metaphysics of incorporeal contact, which are assumed here but not demonstrated again.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_03:MRT-B06","text":"The cluster coheres as a progression from causal goodness through unreceived infinity to conserving presence; the special presence of grace nevertheless resists complete reduction and remains open.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ6:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PPQ8:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_03@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_03:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 07–09","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 6 · Prima pars · Quaestio 7 · Prima pars · Quaestio 8"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 10–12","order":4,"parents":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9","CH_GGVC_PP_2","CH_GGVC_PP_3"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_04@R001","sha256":"815add04bb4de77553cf533b2979c103dc9712a2a7e95c9399b5fc6363f14d4b","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo idem primum ens absolute immutabile, aeternum et unum sit, dum creaturae mutationi, successioni et multitudini diversimode subiacent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-02","text":"Thesis globalis Deum ut ipsum esse, actum purum, simplicem et infinitum constituit, cui immutabilitas, aeternitas et unitas non accidunt sed secundum diversas rationes idem esse exprimunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-03","text":"Argumentatio condiciones motus, successionis et divisionis detegit, eas a primo ente removet, deinde remotionem in structuram positivam durationis et unitatis convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-04","text":"Motus cognitionis a sensibilibus compositis et successivis ad ens indivisum procedit, non per extensionem notionum creatarum sed per distinctionem et remotionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-05","text":"Immutabilitas, prius conclusio de actu puro, fit principium aeternitatis; simplicitas et infinitas, prius exclusiones motus, redeunt ut principia maximae unitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-06","text":"Motus systematis est cumulativus et spiralis: eadem fundamenta ad gradus modalem, temporalem et transcendentalem redeunt, sed in quolibet gradu novam functionem generant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-07","text":"Creaturae non per oppositionem aequalem Deo constituuntur, sed ut entia recepta, participantia et divisa, quorum stabilitas semper dependentiam atque aliquem modum unitatis retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-08","text":"Clausura est ontologica: Deus neque intra durationem communem neque intra numerum principiorum collocatur, sed est fons immutabilis mensurae, permanentiae et ordinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Mutatio potentiam, permanentiam alicuius cum transitu alterius atque acquisitionem termini nondum possessi requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Deus est primum ens, actus purus, omnino simplex, infinitam perfectionem essendi comprehendens et ipsum esse subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Quia nulla potentia, compositio aut perfectio acquirenda in Deo est, omnis mutatio ab eo excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Immutabilitas absoluta est ratio generativa aeternitatis divinae, non proprietas ab aeternitate seiuncta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Aeternitas est permanentia interminabilis tota simul, cui successio intrinseca, principium et finis desunt; ideo tempus infinitum non est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Mensura durationis modum vel respectum essendi sequitur, non subiectum ut indivisum totum neque vas extrinsecum omnibus commune.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Unum transcendens nihil reale enti addit, sed indivisionem illius esse significat; quare unitas ad omne ens pertinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Unitas divina non est singularitas numerica, sed incommunicabilitas naturae subsistentis, plenitudo infinita et immunitas ab omni divisione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Creatura esse recipit et conservatur, ideo permanentiam atque stabilitatem non ex se possidet, sed participat sub potentia causae creantis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A8","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Eadem creatura secundum diversos respectus immobilis et mutabilis, temporalis et aeviterna, una et multa esse potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Multiplicitas mensuratorum vel ordinatorum ad primum simplicissimum reducitur, a quo unitatem ordinis accipit sine abolitione differentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A17","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Solus Deus coniungit absentiam omnis potentiae, identitatem cum propria aeternitate et maximam unitatem essendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-01","text":"Actus purus, simplicitas et infinitas identitatem retinent, sed functionem mutant: motum primo excludunt, aeternitatem deinde fundant, tandem pluralitatem divinorum principiorum impossibilem faciunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-02","text":"Immutabilitas a conclusione negativa de motu ad principium positivum durationis divinae transit, donec Deus non modo aeternus sed sua aeternitas constituatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-03","text":"Motus a translatione physica ad omnem ordinem potentiae et actus amplificatur, atque in campo durationis ut successio numerabilis reapparet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-04","text":"Simplicitas primo compositionem mobilis excludit, deinde identitatem esse et durationis sustinet, postremo omnem divisionem actualem vel potentialem removet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-05","text":"Infinitas ab exclusione perfectionis acquirendae ad exclusionem differentiae inter plura absoluta transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-06","text":"Participatio a diffusione causali similitudinis ad permanentiam creatam et tandem ad multitudinem quae unitatem retinet migrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-07","text":"Negatio non terminatur in absentia: remotionem compositionis, successionis et divisionis in modum cognoscendi perfectionem simplicem transformat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-08","text":"Unum numericum a praedicatione divina removetur; unum transcendens eius locum capit, dum multitudo in entitate unitatum et ordine superiori absorbetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:NX2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-01","text":"Taxonomiae corporum, substantiarum incorporearum et beatorum manent determinationes locales; hic gradu persistit regula communis quod omnis stabilitas creata dependentiam aut potentiam aliquam retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-02","text":"Singulae locutiones scripturales de motu, tempore vel pluralitate ad inferiorem tractationem pertinent; hic ampliantur in regulam praedicationis non univocae de Deo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-03","text":"Conclusio localis de absoluta immutabilitate Dei sursum transit et fit praemissa necessaria attributionis aeternitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-04","text":"Simplicitas et infinitas inferiores quaestionem motus cum quaestione unitatis conectunt, atque hoc gradu unam structuram indivisi actus efficiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-05","text":"Unitas aevi manet conclusio localis et conditionalis, quia ab ordine nondum demonstrato aeviternorum dependet; ideo axioma globale huius synthesis non fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-06","text":"Connexio durationis et unitatis per modum essendi tantum hoc gradu emergit: duratio stabilitatem vel successionem, unitas indivisionem eiusdem esse exprimit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-01","text":"Deus non est quies potentiae latentis, compositum partim manens partim transiens, neque ens quod perfectionem nondum habitam acquirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-02","text":"Deus neque successionem admittit neque aeternitate quasi mensura extrinseca continetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A16","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-03","text":"Unitas divina non est unitas numerica, nec Deus individuum numerabile inter alia eiusdem ordinis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:NX2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-04","text":"Nulla creatura permanentiam autonomam obtinet, quia productio et conservatio eius semper a primo ente dependent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-05","text":"Verba motus et formae grammaticae temporales mutationem realem in Deo per se non probant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-06","text":"Immobilitas secundum unum respectum, interminabilitas vel diuturnitas creaturae numquam immutabilitatem aut aeternitatem absolutam constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet Deum et creaturas sub genere neutro durationis vel entitatis aequaliter commensurari posse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet durationem vas autonomum esse, in quo res iam constitutae extrinsecus collocentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet unitatem principio extrinseco enti addi, quia ipsum principium uniens iam unitatem praesupponeret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet aeternitatem ex tempore sine termino produci posse, quia extensio successionis successionem non tollit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet immaterialitatem aut adeptionem finis sufficere ad omnem potentiam et dependentiam creatam removendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet plura principia aequaliter prima aut plura absoluta infinite perfecta coexistere posse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX5","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-07","text":"Falsum esse oportet intellectum humanum perfectiones simplices et divinas sine mediatione compositorum, distinctionum et remotionum comprehendere posse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSA-01","text":"Systema circa absentiam triplicis dispersionis ordinatur: nulla dispersio actus in potentiam, durationis in successionem, esse in divisionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A16","CH_GGVC_PP_3:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSA-02","text":"Possibilitas maxime inadmissibilis est creatura quae permanentiam increatam et a conservante independentem possideat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSA-03","text":"Inadmissibilis est operatio divina quae, ut causalis fiat, Deum temporaliter fieri, accedere vel migrare requirat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSA-04","text":"Inadmissibilis est multitudo absoluta quae nullam unitatem participet vel plura principia ultima aequaliter perfecta constituat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-01","text":"Eadem actualitas quae omnem mutationem excludit aeternitatem generat; aeternitas igitur non additur Deo, sed immutabilitatem actus puri sub ratione durationis exprimit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-02","CL_GGVC_04:GA-03","CL_GGVC_04:GA-04","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-02","text":"Simplicitas est operator communis immutabilitatis et unitatis: compositionem requisitam motui excludit atque divisionem requisitam pluralitati divinae impedit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-01","CL_GGVC_04:GA-02","CL_GGVC_04:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-03","text":"Infinitas duplicem clausuram efficit: nihil Deo acquirendum relinquit et nullam differentiam admittit qua plures dii distinguerentur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-02","CL_GGVC_04:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-04","text":"Conservatio continua, participatio permanentiae et unitas retenta in multitudine unam ontologiam creaturae efficiunt: creatura stabilis est tantum ut recepta, ordinata et dependens.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-09","CL_GGVC_04:GA-10","CL_GGVC_04:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-05","text":"Distinctio respectuum permittit ut idem ens partialiter immobile, operatione temporale, esse aeviternum, essentialiter unum et accidentaliter multiplex sit sine contradictione.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-06","CL_GGVC_04:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-06","text":"Unitas mensurae et unitas ordinis eadem forma reductionis utuntur: multiplicitas non per aggregationem, sed per relationem ad primum simplicissimum cohaeret.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-07","text":"Cumulatio exclusionum potentiae, successionis et pluralitatis absolutorum propositionem positivam format: primum esse est actus indivisus, totus simul et incomparable.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-03","CL_GGVC_04:GA-05","CL_GGVC_04:GA-08","CL_GGVC_04:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-08","text":"Motus, temporalitas et unitas de Deo non possunt ex usu creato univoce transferri; unumquodque praedicatum per causalitatem, identitatem vel remotionem ontologice reclassificatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-03","CL_GGVC_04:GA-05","CL_GGVC_04:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-09","text":"Potentia creatoris ad non esse creaturae extrinsecam mutabilitatem constituit, sed successionem intrinsecam non necessario infert; dependentia creata cum duratione aeviterna compatibilis manet si hi axes distinguuntur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-06","CL_GGVC_04:GA-09","CL_GGVC_04:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-01","text":"Immutabilitas, aeternitas et maxima unitas sunt tres conversiones eiusdem identitatis divinae cum esse: modaliter, temporaliter et transcendentaliter consideratae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-02","text":"Tempus non est ambitus antecedens realitatem, sed effectus intelligibilis essendi transmutabilis; aeternitas similiter non ambit Deum, sed ipsum esse immobile exprimit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-03","text":"Causalitas primi principii efficax manet sine mutatione agentis, quia processus et accessus in effectu recepto, non in transitu divino, locantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-04","text":"Creatura non est subiectum unius mensurae vel unius indivisionis simpliciter, sed nodus respectuum cui permanentia, successio, unitas et multiplicitas diversimode conveniunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:D10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-05","text":"Cognitio primi entis progreditur per remotionem condicionum compositorum; forma negativa cognitionis non vacuitatem, sed accessum ad perfectionem simplicem constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-06","text":"Primum principium non est summum membrum intra seriem communiter mensuratam, sed causa ipsius ordinis, mensurae et unitatis seriei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-01","text":"Potentia mutationem possibilitat, mutatio successionem manifestat, successio tempus generat, et tempus vicissim modum potentiae entis mensurati indicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-02","text":"Simplicitas immutabilitatem generat, immutabilitas aeternitatem, identitas esse et aeternitatis simplicitatem confirmat, atque eadem simplicitas in maxima unitate redit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-03","text":"Esse indivisionem requirit, indivisio unitatem constituit, unitates multitudinem efficiunt, multitudo ordinem postulat, et ordo ad unum principium redit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-04","text":"Cognitio a composito incipit, compositionem removet, distinctionibus objectiones dissolvit et per negationem ad simplicem perfectionem recurrit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-05","text":"Perfectio divina similitudinem diffundit, creatura stabilitatem participat, participatio dependentiam conservat, et dependentia ad causam immutabilem refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-06","text":"Attractor totius structurae est primum simplicissimum in quo maxima entitas, plena indivisio et immutabilitas coincidunt, dum cetera per ordinem ad illud mensurantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A17","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A14","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B01","text":"Entia mutabilia, successiva et divisa praebent campum initialem ex quo condiciones mutationis, temporis et multitudinis extrahuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B02","text":"Mutatio → potentia + compositio + acquisitio; harum condicionum analysis structuram mobilis in elementa ontologica resolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B03","text":"Actus purus + simplicitas + plenitudo infinita → remotio condicionum mutationis → immutabilitas absoluta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B04","text":"Mutabilitas successiva → tempus; stabilitas cum mutatione adiuncta → aevum; immutabilitas absoluta → aeternitas tota simul.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B05","text":"Ens → indivisio → unum transcendens; ipsum esse simplex et infinitum → impossibilitas divisionis divinae → Deus maxime unus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B06","text":"Creaturae recipiunt esse, permanentiam et unitatem secundum respectus diversos; multiplicitas earum ad mensuram et causam primam ordinatur sine conversione in identitatem divinam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A17","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AFM-B01","text":"Motus creatus → analysis potentiae, compositionis et acquisitionis → actus purus immutabilis → aeternitas tota simul → ens omnino indivisum → Deus maxime unus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AFM-B02","text":"Principium unum et immobile → diffusio causalis sine transitu → permanentiae creatae participatae → multiplicitas dependens et ordinata → reductio ad primum sine abolitione differentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-01","text":"Mutatio reclassificatur ab alteratione corporali in omnem transitum potentiae ad actum, unde etiam dependentia, finis et electio ad campum mutabilitatis pertinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-02","text":"Duratio ex quantitate continua in modum essendi mutatur; aeternitas, aevum et tempus gradus longitudinis esse desinunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-03","text":"Unitas ex accidente numerico in proprietatem transcendentalem entis transfertur, et unitas divina ex singularitate numerabili in incommunicabilem plenitudinem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-04","text":"Subiectum creatum aspectualiter describitur: eadem res secundum esse, operationem, finem, substantiam vel accidens diversis mensuris et unitatibus subiacet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-05","text":"Multitudo non iam alterum principium unitati oppositum est, sed distributio entium quae unitatem propriam et ordinem communem retinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-06","text":"Lectio valida praedicatorum divinorum requirit mutationem principii classificationis et distinctionem inter proprietatem, participationem, metaphoram, negationem et causalitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei quaerit immutabilitatem Dei, rationes aeternitatis et aevi, atque naturam unius et maximae unitatis divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis potentiam, compositionem, successionem et divisionem ut mechanismos distribuit ex quibus mutabilitas, tempus et multitudo oriuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus objectiones non simpliciter negat, sed eas per distinctiones respectuum et translationem a numero vel longitudine ad modum essendi reconstituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis realitatem a puro esse immobili ad esse participatum, stabile vel successivum ordinat, distinguens ordinem rei ab ordine apprehensionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus assertiones suas efficit removendo compositionem, successionem et divisionem per eandem seriem distinctionum quam doctrina postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FL-01","text":"Mutabilitas extrinseca creaturae sub potentia annihilantis latius patet quam mutatio in subiecto; nisi haec amplitudo servetur, transitus a dependentia ad mutabilitatem vacillat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FL-02","text":"Aeternitas dicitur mensura esse divini, quamvis Deus nullo alio mensuretur; identitas Dei cum sua aeternitate hanc tensionem claudit, sed notionem mensurae analogicam reddit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FL-03","text":"Aevum stabilitatem intrinsecam cum mutatione adiuncta coniungit; distinctio deficit si mutatio adiuncta in successionem ipsius esse aeviterni convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FL-04","text":"Unitas aevi ex uno primo aeviterno pendet, sed haec hierarchia conditionalis firmitatem unitatis divinae non participat nec ex ea sola demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MP-01","text":"Notio motus mutatur cum a translatione corporali ad omnem potentiam ordinatam ad actum, deinde ad successionem numerabilem extenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MP-02","text":"Immutabilitas mutatur a termino exclusionis in principium generativum aeternitatis propriae Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MP-03","text":"Mensura mutatur ab instrumento extrinseco in rationem consequentem modum essendi mensurati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MP-04","text":"Unum mutatur ab unitate quantitativa, quae numerum fundat, in indivisionem transcendentalem convertibilem cum ente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite apparet ut ordo a fonte simplici et indiviso descendens ad entia stabilitatem, successionem et unitatem secundum gradus diversos participantia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-02","text":"Fons immobilis non est centrum iners, sed actus causaliter diffusivus cuius operatio effectus mutat sine transitu in agente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A10","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-03","text":"Creatura est nodus respectuum potius quam massa ontologica simplex: esse stabile, operationes successivae, unitas essentialis et multiplicitas accidentalis in ea distribuuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:D10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-04","text":"Tempus est imago essendi cuius partes recedunt et adveniunt; aeternitas est permanentia cui nihil praeterit nec supervenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-05","text":"Subiectum cognoscens navigat a compositis per remotionem et distinctionem, cavens ne imagines motus, temporis et numeri in Deum univoce transferat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de actu puro, simplicitate, plenitudine, indivisione entis et participatione creata sufficiunt ad structuram principalem immutabilitatis, aeternitatis et unitatis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B02","text":"Commissura firmissima est transitus ab immutabilitate absoluta ad aeternitatem tota simul, quia successio immediate ex motu et potentia derivatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B03","text":"Integratio unitatis divinae firma est quatenus simplicitatem, infinitatem et ipsum esse cum argumentis antecedentibus communicat, quamvis ex aeternitate sola non deducatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B04","text":"Determinatio unius aevi insufficienter stabilita manet, quia hierarchiam aeviternorum assumit quam hic ordo argumentorum nondum probat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B05","text":"Restitutio motum recursivum systematis servat, sed doctrina praedicationis analogicae, amplitudo mutabilitatis extrinsecae et transitus a negatione cognitiva ad perfectionem realem manent commissurae irreducibiles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170850618237Z_f974237a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 10–12","source_sha256":"815add04bb4de77553cf533b2979c103dc9712a2a7e95c9399b5fc6363f14d4b","sha256":"266b40ee1bf8768aab558d7ff0ca050aea298e6974cd89f7cc59a88712316be7","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:08:50.620466+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-01","text":"The system asks how the same first being is absolutely immutable, eternal, and one, while creatures are variously subject to change, succession, and multitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-02","text":"The global thesis establishes God as subsistent being itself, pure act, simple and infinite, to whom immutability, eternity, and unity do not accrue but express the same being according to diverse respects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-03","text":"The argument uncovers the conditions of motion, succession, and division, removes them from the first being, then converts that removal into a positive structure of duration and unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-04","text":"The movement of cognition proceeds from sensible, composite, and successive things to undivided being, not by extending created notions but through distinction and removal.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-05","text":"Immutability, previously a conclusion concerning pure act, becomes the principle of eternity; simplicity and infinity, previously exclusions of motion, return as principles of the highest unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-06","text":"The system's movement is cumulative and spiral: the same foundations return at the modal, temporal, and transcendental levels, but at each level generate a new function.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-07","text":"Creatures are constituted not through an opposition equal to God, but as received, participating, and divided beings, whose stability always retains dependence and some mode of unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AS-08","text":"The closure is ontological: God is situated neither within common duration nor within a number of principles, but is the immutable source of measure, permanence, and order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Change requires potency, the persistence of one thing together with the transition of another, and the acquisition of a term not yet possessed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A2","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] God is the first being, pure act, altogether simple, comprehending infinite perfection of being, and subsistent being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Because there is in God no potency, composition, or perfection to be acquired, every change is excluded from him.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Absolute immutability is the generative principle of divine eternity, not a property separated from eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Eternity is interminable permanence, whole simultaneously, lacking intrinsic succession, beginning, and end; therefore it is not infinite time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] The measure of duration follows the mode or respect of being, not the subject as an undivided whole nor an extrinsic vessel common to all.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Transcendental one adds nothing real to being, but signifies the indivision of its being; therefore unity belongs to every being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Divine unity is not numerical singularity, but the incommunicability of subsisting nature, infinite fullness, and immunity from every division.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] The creature receives and is preserved in being; therefore it possesses neither permanence nor stability from itself, but participates in them under the power of the creating cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A7","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A8","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] The same creature can be, according to diverse respects, immobile and mutable, temporal and aeviternal, one and many.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] A multiplicity of things measured or ordered is reduced to the first and most simple, from which it receives unity of order without abolition of differences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A17","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] God alone conjoins the absence of every potency, identity with his own eternity, and the highest unity of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-01","text":"Pure act, simplicity, and infinity retain their identity but change function: they first exclude motion, then ground eternity, and finally make a plurality of divine principles impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-02","text":"Immutability passes from a negative conclusion concerning motion to a positive principle of divine duration, until God is constituted not merely eternal but his own eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-03","text":"Motion is enlarged from physical locomotion to every order of potency and act, and reappears in the field of duration as numerable succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-04","text":"Simplicity first excludes the composition of the mobile, then sustains the identity of being and duration, and finally removes every actual or potential division.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-05","text":"Infinity is transferred from the exclusion of perfection to be acquired to the exclusion of difference among several absolutes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-06","text":"Participation migrates from the causal diffusion of likeness to created permanence and finally to multitude retaining unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-07","text":"Negation does not terminate in absence: it transforms the removal of composition, succession, and division into a mode of knowing simple perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RMD-08","text":"Numerical one is removed from divine predication; transcendental one takes its place, while multitude is absorbed into the being of unities and into higher order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:NX2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-01","text":"Taxonomies of bodies, incorporeal substances, and the blessed remain local determinations; at this level the common rule persists that all created stability retains some dependence or potency.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD3","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-02","text":"Individual scriptural expressions concerning motion, time, or plurality belong to lower treatment; here they are enlarged into a rule of non-univocal predication concerning God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-03","text":"The local conclusion concerning God's absolute immutability moves upward and becomes a necessary premise for the attribution of eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-04","text":"The lower simplicity and infinity connect the question of motion with the question of unity, and at this level produce one structure of undivided act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-05","text":"The unity of aevum remains a local and conditional conclusion, because it depends upon an order of aeviternal things not yet demonstrated; therefore it does not become a global axiom of this synthesis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:CGD-06","text":"The connection of duration and unity through mode of being emerges only at this level: duration expresses stability or succession, unity the indivision of that same being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-01","text":"God is not the rest of latent potency, a composite partly remaining and partly passing, nor a being that acquires a perfection not yet possessed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX2","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-02","text":"God neither admits succession nor is contained by eternity as though by an extrinsic measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A16","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-03","text":"Divine unity is not numerical unity, nor is God a numerable individual among others of the same order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:NX2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-04","text":"No creature obtains autonomous permanence, because its production and preservation always depend on the first being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-05","text":"Words of motion and temporal grammatical forms do not, in themselves, prove real change in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:GNX-06","text":"Immobility according to one respect, interminability, or creaturely long duration never constitute absolute immutability or eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that God and creatures can be equally measured under a neutral genus of duration or being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that duration is an autonomous vessel in which already constituted things are extrinsically placed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that unity is added to being by an extrinsic principle, because the unifying principle itself would already presuppose unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that eternity can be produced from time without limit, because the extension of succession does not remove succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that immateriality or attainment of an end suffices to remove every created potency and dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that several equally first principles or several infinitely perfect absolutes can coexist.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX5","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:DBN-07","text":"It must be false that the human intellect can comprehend simple and divine perfections without the mediation of composites, distinctions, and removals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSA-01","text":"The system is ordered around the absence of threefold dispersion: no dispersion of act into potency, of duration into succession, or of being into division.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A16","CH_GGVC_PP_3:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSA-02","text":"The most inadmissible possibility is a creature possessing uncreated permanence independent of its conserver.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSA-03","text":"Inadmissible is a divine operation which, in order to be causal, requires God to become, advance, or migrate temporally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSA-04","text":"Inadmissible is an absolute multitude participating in no unity or constituting several equally perfect ultimate principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-01","text":"The same actuality that excludes every change generates eternity; eternity therefore is not added to God, but expresses the immutability of pure act under the aspect of duration.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-02","CL_GGVC_04:GA-03","CL_GGVC_04:GA-04","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-02","text":"Simplicity is the common operator of immutability and unity: it excludes the composition required for motion and prevents the division required for divine plurality.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-01","CL_GGVC_04:GA-02","CL_GGVC_04:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-03","text":"Infinity effects a double closure: it leaves nothing for God to acquire and admits no difference by which several gods might be distinguished.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-02","CL_GGVC_04:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-04","text":"Continuous preservation, participation in permanence, and unity retained in multitude produce one ontology of the creature: a creature is stable only as received, ordered, and dependent.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-09","CL_GGVC_04:GA-10","CL_GGVC_04:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-05","text":"The distinction of respects permits the same being to be partially immobile, temporal in operation, aeviternal in being, essentially one, and accidentally multiple without contradiction.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-06","CL_GGVC_04:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-06","text":"Unity of measure and unity of order employ the same form of reduction: multiplicity coheres not through aggregation but through relation to the first and most simple.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-07","text":"The accumulation of exclusions of potency, succession, and plurality of absolutes forms a positive proposition: the first being is undivided act, whole simultaneously and incomparable.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-03","CL_GGVC_04:GA-05","CL_GGVC_04:GA-08","CL_GGVC_04:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-08","text":"Motion, temporality, and unity cannot be transferred univocally to God from created use; each predicate is ontologically reclassified through causality, identity, or removal.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-03","CL_GGVC_04:GA-05","CL_GGVC_04:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:XD-09","text":"The creator's power over the creature's non-being constitutes extrinsic mutability, but does not necessarily entail intrinsic succession; created dependence remains compatible with aeviternal duration if these axes are distinguished.","refs":["CL_GGVC_04:GA-06","CL_GGVC_04:GA-09","CL_GGVC_04:GA-10","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-01","text":"Immutability, eternity, and highest unity are three conversions of the same divine identity with being, considered modally, temporally, and transcendentally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-02","text":"Time is not an ambit preceding reality, but an intelligible effect of mutable being; similarly, eternity does not encompass God, but expresses immobile being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-03","text":"The causality of the first principle remains efficacious without change in the agent, because process and advance are located in the received effect, not in divine transition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-04","text":"The creature is not simply the subject of one measure or one indivision, but a nexus of respects to which permanence, succession, unity, and multiplicity belong in diverse ways.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:D10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-05","text":"Knowledge of the first being progresses through the removal of composite conditions; the negative form of knowledge constitutes not emptiness but access to simple perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:BSD-06","text":"The first principle is not the highest member within a commonly measured series, but the cause of the series' very order, measure, and unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-01","text":"Potency makes change possible, change manifests succession, succession generates time, and time in turn indicates the mode of potency of the measured being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-02","text":"Simplicity generates immutability, immutability eternity, identity of being and eternity confirms simplicity, and that same simplicity returns in highest unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-03","text":"Being requires indivision, indivision constitutes unity, unities produce multitude, multitude demands order, and order returns to one principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-04","text":"Knowledge begins from the composite, removes composition, dissolves objections by distinctions, and returns through negation to simple perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-05","text":"Divine perfection diffuses likeness, the creature participates in stability, participation preserves dependence, and dependence is referred to the immutable cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:RLE-06","text":"The attractor of the entire structure is the first and most simple, in which highest being, complete indivision, and immutability coincide, while all else is measured through order toward it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A17","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A14","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B01","text":"Mutable, successive, and divided beings provide the initial field from which the conditions of change, time, and multitude are extracted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B02","text":"Change → potency + composition + acquisition; analysis of these conditions resolves the structure of the mobile into ontological elements.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS2","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A3","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B03","text":"Pure act + simplicity + infinite fullness → removal of the conditions of change → absolute immutability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A4","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B04","text":"Successive mutability → time; stability joined with change → aevum; absolute immutability → eternity whole simultaneously.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B05","text":"Being → indivision → transcendental one; simple and infinite being itself → impossibility of divine division → God is maximally one.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FGS-B06","text":"Creatures receive being, permanence, and unity according to diverse respects; their multiplicity is ordered to the first measure and cause without conversion into divine identity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A17","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AFM-B01","text":"Created motion → analysis of potency, composition, and acquisition → immutable pure act → eternity whole simultaneously → being altogether undivided → God is maximally one.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:AFM-B02","text":"One and immobile principle → causal diffusion without transition → participated created permanences → dependent and ordered multiplicity → reduction to the first without abolition of differences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-01","text":"Change is reclassified from bodily alteration into every transition from potency to act, whence dependence, end, and choice also belong to the field of mutability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ME1","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-02","text":"Duration changes from continuous quantity into a mode of being; eternity, aevum, and time cease to be degrees of length.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-03","text":"Unity is transferred from a numerical accident into a transcendental property of being, and divine unity from numerable singularity into incommunicable fullness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-04","text":"The created subject is described aspectually: the same thing is subject to diverse measures and unities according to being, operation, end, substance, or accident.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME6","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-05","text":"Multitude is no longer another principle opposed to unity, but a distribution of beings retaining their proper unity and common order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MME-06","text":"A valid reading of divine predicates requires a change in the principle of classification and a distinction among property, participation, metaphor, negation, and causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level asks about God's immutability, the accounts of eternity and aevum, and the nature of one and of the highest divine unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level distributes potency, composition, succession, and division as mechanisms from which mutability, time, and multitude arise.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level does not merely negate objections, but reconstitutes them through distinctions of respects and translation from number or length to mode of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level orders reality from pure immobile being to participated, stable, or successive being, distinguishing the order of the thing from the order of apprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level effects its assertions by removing composition, succession, and division through the same series of distinctions demanded by the doctrine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FL-01","text":"The creature's extrinsic mutability under the power of annihilation extends more broadly than change in a subject; unless this breadth is maintained, the passage from dependence to mutability falters.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FL-02","text":"Eternity is called the measure of divine being, although God is measured by nothing else; God's identity with his own eternity closes this tension, but renders the notion of measure analogical.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FL-03","text":"Aevum joins intrinsic stability with accompanying change; the distinction fails if accompanying change is converted into succession of aeviternal being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:FL-04","text":"The unity of aevum depends on one first aeviternal being, but this conditional hierarchy does not share the firmness of divine unity nor is it demonstrated from that alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PP_2:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MP-01","text":"The notion of motion changes when it is extended from bodily locomotion to every potency ordered to act, and then to numerable succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MP-02","text":"Immutability changes from a term of exclusion into the generative principle of God's proper eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MP-03","text":"Measure changes from an extrinsic instrument into a notion consequent upon the mode of being of what is measured.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MP-04","text":"One changes from quantitative unity, which grounds number, into transcendental indivision convertible with being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as an order descending from a simple and undivided source to beings participating, according to diverse degrees, in stability, succession, and unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-02","text":"The immobile source is not an inert center, but causally diffusive act whose operation changes effects without transition in the agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:A10","CH_GGVC_PPQ9:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-03","text":"The creature is a nexus of respects rather than a simple ontological mass: stable being, successive operations, essential unity, and accidental multiplicity are distributed in it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:D10","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-04","text":"Time is an image of being whose parts recede and arrive; eternity is permanence to which nothing passes away or supervenes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:HSI-05","text":"The knowing subject navigates from composites through removal and distinction, taking care not to transfer images of motion, time, and number univocally to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_2:FGS8","CH_GGVC_PP_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B01","text":"Axioms concerning pure act, simplicity, fullness, the indivision of being, and created participation suffice to reconstruct the principal structure of immutability, eternity, and unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_3:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest joint is the transition from absolute immutability to eternity whole simultaneously, because succession is immediately derived from motion and potency.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PP_2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B03","text":"The integration of divine unity is firm insofar as it shares simplicity, infinity, and being itself with preceding arguments, although it is not deduced from eternity alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_3:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_3:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B04","text":"The determination of one aevum remains insufficiently established, because it assumes a hierarchy of aeviternal beings that this order of arguments has not yet proven.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_04:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction preserves the system's recursive movement, but the doctrine of analogical predication, the breadth of extrinsic mutability, and the transition from cognitive negation to real perfection remain irreducible joints.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PPQ9:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_2:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_04@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_04:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 10–12","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 9 · Prima pars · Quaestio 10 · Prima pars · Quaestio 11"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 13–15","order":5,"parents":["CH_GGVC_PP_4","CH_GGVC_PP_5","CH_GGVC_PP_6"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_05@R001","sha256":"952192a16c133525e020d2a00ead5598cfeba4f066d2e10d8b7f8e6df150a43a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo Deus, in se maxime intelligibilis et perfecte sciens, intellectui creato vere cognoscibilis et nominabilis sit sine dependentia, comprehensione vel reductione ad modum creatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B02","text":"Eadem essentia divina triplicem functionem suscipit: est species cognitionis divinae, obiectum immediate visibile intellectui glorificato et causa per effectus analogice cognita intellectui viatoris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B03","text":"Argumentatio perfectiones cognitionis et sermonis retinet, modos autem potentiales, compositos, materiales et comprehensivos recursiva correctione apophatica removet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B04","text":"Motus duplex fit: intellectus creatus ab effectibus ad cognitionem, nominationem et visionem elevatam ascendit, dum cognitio divina a perfecta sui cognitione ad propriam cognitionem omnium descendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:FGS6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B05","text":"Simplicitas divina ex apparenti impedimento pluralitatis in principium multiplicium nominum, cognitorum et participationum sine compositione interna convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B06","text":"Systema spiraliter inter ascensum creaturae ad Deum et diffusionem perfectionis divinae ad creaturas movetur, causalitate utramque directionem asymmetrice ordinante.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B07","text":"Successio, novitas denominationis et contingentia ad ordinem creatum relegantur, dum aeternitas et invariabilitas cognitionis divinae mutationem rerum sine mutatione Dei continent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B08","text":"Clausura est asymmetrica: creatura veritatem et beatitudinem sine comprehensione recipit, Deus autem se et alia comprehendit sine receptione; nexus scientiae ad effectum tamen voluntatem adhuc postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Cognitio secundum modum cognoscentis determinatur; identitas obiecti diversitatem receptionis, conceptionis et visionis non tollit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Purus actus est maxime intelligibilis et summe cognoscitivus, sed haec intelligibilitas obiectiva accessibilitatem naturalem intellectus finiti non secum fert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] In Deo essentia, esse, intellectus, species intelligibilis et actus intelligendi realiter unum sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Cognitio naturalis Dei est vera, causalis et analogica, sed eius veritas ad cognitionem quidditativam essentiae divinae non pervenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Visio beatifica obiectum immediate attingit, quia gratia potentiam creatam transformat, non quia finitudinem eius abolet aut obiectum dividit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Perfectiones creaturae in Deo unite et eminenter praeexistunt; attributio divina perfectionem servat, modum creatum removet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Simplicitas divina multiplicitatem rationum, nominum et cognitorum non excludit, sed eam extra compositionem rei divinae ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Causalitas coniungit cognitionem creatam, analogiam semanticam et scientiam divinam: effectus causam manifestant, nomina ad causam ordinantur, causa autem effectus in propria virtute cognoscit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Omnis novitas temporalis in relatione creaturae, effectu vel causa proxima collocatur, non in essentia aut scientia divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Tres ordines cognitionis complent structuram: cognitio divina comprehensiva, cognitio viatoris analogica et mediata, atque visio gloriosa immediata sed non comprehensiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D13","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-01","text":"Lex modi cognoscentis identitatem functionis servat in visione creata et scientia divina, sed in nominatione mutatur in legem qua vox mensuram conceptionis intellectualis sequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-02","text":"Species intelligibilis functionem mutat: species creata ut repraesentatio essentiae excluditur, essentia divina intellectui glorificato immediate unitur, et in cognitione divina ipsa essentia est species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-03","text":"Simplicitas a limite semantico ad principium generativum transit: una essentia pluralitatem contentorum visionis, nominum non synonymorum et cognitorum sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D9","CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-04","text":"Causalitas migrat a via cognitionis naturalis ad structuram analogiae et tandem ad rationem qua Deus alia in propria virtute cognoscit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-05","text":"Mediatio non semper eandem functionem retinet: in visione perficit potentiam sine interpositione obiectiva, in sermone format conceptionem, in Deo vero omnis exterioritas epistemica evanescit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-06","text":"Negatio ex limite locali in operationem universalem mutatur: perfectionem non delet, sed modum creatum removet ut attributio eminens, sermo verus et scientia simplex constitui possint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-01","text":"Gradus luminis, exceptio raptus, ordines proprietatis nominum et divisiones scientiae speculativae ac practicae manent determinationes locales, non axiomata totius gregis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-02","text":"Distinctiones locales inter obiectum et capacitatem, significatum et modum significandi, cognitum et modum cognoscentis amplificantur in unam legem receptionis proportionatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-03","text":"Causalitas, eminentia perfectionum et perfecta cognitio virtutis propriae unitates coniungunt atque transitum a cognitione creaturae ad scientiam creatoris efficiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-04","text":"Scala analysis mutatur ab obiecto, potentia et medio visionis ad originem et terminum significationis, deinde ad identitatem intellectus, speciei et actus divini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ME7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-05","text":"Oppositiones simplicis cognitionis et ignorantiae, univocationis et aequivocationis, simplicitatis et pluralitatis superantur atque aliter codificantur per gradus cognitionis, analogiam et continentiam eminentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ME4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-01","text":"Systema nec transcendentiam cum absoluta incognoscibilitate nec eminentiam Dei cum innominalitate absoluta identificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-02","text":"Nulla species creata, nomen univocum aut planum semanticum commune essentiam divinam ad mensuram creaturae redigere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-03","text":"Pluralitas propositionum, nominum, relationum et cognitorum compositionem, mutationem aut variationem scientiae divinae non inducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:NX17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-04","text":"Ascensus autonomus, omniscientia creaturae et identitas ontologica per participationem excluduntur; communicatio divina manet donum finito modo receptum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-05","text":"Infallibilitas scientiae divinae nec necessitatem absolutam contingentium nec actualizationem omnium possibilium constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:NX15","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod veritas cognitionis vel nominis comprehensionem essentiae aut exhaustionem cognoscibilitatis requirat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod distinctio rationum vel pluralitas cognitorum pluralitatem partium, specierum aut actuum in Deo inferat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod denominatio realis relationem intrinsecam symmetricam aut mutationem in utroque termino postulet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:DNX6","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod omnis cognitio per formam extrinsecam receptam constituatur; aliter nec visio immediata nec scientia divina consisteret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSA-01","text":"Systema circa absentiam mensurae communis creatoris et creaturae ordinatur; nulla commensuratio finiti et infiniti cognitionem vel praedicationem fundat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSA-02","text":"Inadmissibilis est exterioritas epistemica ex qua Deus formam, perfectionem, mensuram aut determinationem cognitionis accipiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSA-03","text":"Viatori indisponibilis manet positio quidditativa ex qua essentia divina secundum se cognoscatur; haec absentia totam doctrinam visionis et nominum circumterminat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSA-04","text":"Participatio non potest in identitatem creatoris et creaturae aut multiplicationem naturae divinae converti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX5","CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-01","text":"Eadem lex receptionis cognitionem, nominationem et visionem ordinat: veritas ab identitate obiecti provenit, diversitas autem a modo cognoscentis et concipientis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-01","CL_GGVC_05:GA-04","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-02","text":"Essentia divina sine multiplicatione est principium formale scientiae divinae, obiectum visionis gloriosae et terminus remotus cognitionis analogicae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-03","CL_GGVC_05:GA-05","CL_GGVC_05:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-03","text":"Ordo causalitatis directionem epistemicam invertit: creatura ex effectibus ad Deum ascendit, Deus autem ex cognitione propriae virtutis effectus cognoscit et, voluntate adiuncta, causat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-04","CL_GGVC_05:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-04","text":"Multiplicitas contentorum visionis, rationum nominum et rerum cognitarum extra essentiam divinam distribuitur, dum ipsa essentia manet unica ratio intelligendi.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D9","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-05","text":"Successio cognitionis creatae, temporalitas denominationum et contingentia eventuum sunt tres formae eiusdem relocationis temporis ex Deo in ordinem creatum.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-06","text":"Apophasis et gratia operationes analogas sed inaequales efficiunt: prima modum conceptus purificat, altera potentiam cognoscentis elevat, utraque sine mutatione essentiae divinae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-05","CL_GGVC_05:GA-06","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-07","text":"Quia scientia sola effectum non determinat, denominationes temporales creatoris vel domini actualizationem voluntariam in creatura significant, non novam cognitionem aut relationem realem in Deo.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-08","CL_GGVC_05:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-01","text":"Una essentia divina tres asymmetrismos epistemicos generat: Deus comprehendit per identitatem, viator vere cognoscit per effectus et nomina, beatus immediate videt sine comprehensione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D13","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-02","text":"Simplicitas non est vacuitas differentiarum, sed concentratio principii ex quo differentiae cognoscibiles, rationes praedicabiles et participationes finitae sine divisione oriuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-03","text":"Ontologia participationis et epistemologia causalitatis se mutuo exigunt: creatura Deum indicat quia perfectionem eius participat, Deus creaturam proprie cognoscit quia eius principia causaliter continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-04","text":"Tempus fit proprietas ordinis creati cogniti, denominati et causati; aeternitas vero non tempus delet, sed omnes eius differentias sine successione continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-05","text":"Potentia agendi distribuitur asymmetrice: creatura perfectionem recipit et elevatur, Deus autem effectum per scientiam et voluntatem producit; voluntas igitur commissura ulterior necessaria manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-01","text":"Effectus creatus cognitionem causae parit; cognitio nomen format; nomen apophatice corrigitur; correctio ad causam eminentiorem remittit, quae rursus effectuum intelligibilitatem fundat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A17","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-02","text":"Cognitio divina sui ad virtutem, possibilia et effectus extenditur; effectus voluntarie actualizati relationes temporales constituunt, quae sine mutatione Dei ad causam referuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-03","text":"Desiderium primi principii ad gratiam et visionem amplificatur; visio incomprehensibilitatem non aufert, sed beatitudinem per praesentiam finis sine exhaustione claudit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-04","text":"Simplicitas est attractor recursivus: omnis pluralitas primo compositionem minari videtur, deinde ad unitatem causalem vel intentionalem reducitur et ex ea distinctior restituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-05","text":"Ipsum esse subsistens est attractor terminalis: rationem visionis sine specie creata, proprietatem nominis qui est et identitatem essentiae cum actu intelligendi simul ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B01","text":"Actus purus → maxima intelligibilitas et immaterialitas → identitas essentiae, esse et intelligere → cognitio divina perfecta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B02","text":"Identitas obiecti → receptio secundum modum cognoscentis → diversitas cognitionis divinae, naturalis et gloriosae sine mutatione obiecti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B03","text":"Sensus et phantasmata → effectus causales → cognitio naturalis imperfecta → conceptio intellectualis → nomen verum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A16","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B04","text":"Perfectio significata → remotio modi creati → analogia → pluralitas rationum sub unitate rei → affirmatio vera sine comprehensione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B05","text":"Insufficientia naturalis → lumen gloriae → perfectio potentiae → unio immediata obiecti → visio finita totius essentiae sine comprehensione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B06","text":"Cognitio perfecta virtutis divinae → cognitio omnium possibilium → determinatio voluntaria effectuum → praesentia aeterna temporalium → contingentia servata in causis proximis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AFM-B01","text":"Actus purus → intelligibilitas maxima → excessus super capacitatem creatam → distinctio cognitionis divinae et creatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AFM-B02","text":"Effectus sensibiles → cognitio causalis → nominatio analogica → correctio apophatica → affirmatio vera de Deo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:FGS6","CH_GGVC_PP_5:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AFM-B03","text":"Cognitio divina sui → cognitio virtutis → cognitio possibilium et effectuum → voluntas determinans → causalitas temporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AFM-B04","text":"Elevatio intellectus → visio totius essentiae → incomprehensibilitas servata → beatitudo finita → contingentia et temporalitas extra Deum repositae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-01","text":"Cognoscibilitas Dei desinit esse oppositio binaria et in obiectum, potentiam, medium, modum atque statum cognoscentis distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-02","text":"Communitas sermonis de Deo et creatura extra dilemma univocationis et aequivocationis reordinatur per analogiam causalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-03","text":"Simplicitas ex impedimento pluralitatis in principium cognitionis universalis, multiplicitatis semanticae et participationis distinctae convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-04","text":"Tempus non amplius mensura communis Dei et creaturae est, sed ordo variabilis aeternitati totus praesens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-05","text":"Apophasis a silentio terminali in methodum constitutivam mutatur, quae perfectionem retinet dum modum creatum excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei aguntur possibilitas et modus visionis, proprietas nominum atque amplitudo scientiae divinae circa se, alia, possibilia et contingentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali systema per modum essendi, potentiam cognoscitivam, conceptionem, speciem intelligibilem, causalitatem et actum cognitionis ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico quaestiones extra oppositiones cognoscibilis et incognoscibilis, silentii et praedicationis, simplicitatis et differentiae constituuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali Deus est ipsum esse et causa eminens, creatura participatio asymmetrice relata, aeternitas autem praesentia non successiva temporis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo ipsa forma argumenti perfectiones successive retinet, modos creatos removet et differentias sub unitate simplici restituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FL-01","text":"Desiderium naturale primi principii ad finem ordinatur quem nulla facultas naturalis assequi potest; nexus inter ordinationem naturalem et donum supernaturale manet tensus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FL-02","text":"Nomina perfectionum aliquid positive in substantia divina significant, quamvis essentia in statu viae quidditative ignoretur; significationis substantialis modus ab hac absentia pendet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FL-03","text":"Essentia divina ut forma intelligibilis intellectui creato unitur, sed unio nec informationem substantialem nec identitatem ontologicam efficere potest; mechanismus huius immediationis compresse manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FL-04","text":"Scientia divina effectus non causat sine voluntate, et contingentia causae proximae servatur; modus concursus scientiae, voluntatis et causalitatis contingentis nondum explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MP-01","text":"Species mutatur a repraesentatione creata exclusa ad praesentiam essentiae obiective unitae et tandem ad identitatem essentiae cum specie cognitionis divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MP-02","text":"Simplicitas mutatur ab apparenti restrictione pluralitatis in rationem qua multiplicitas sine multiplicatione cognoscentis continetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MP-03","text":"Comprehensio sensum scalariter mutat: creatura totam essentiam videt sine adaequatione infinita, Deus autem se comprehendit quia modus cognoscentis cognoscibilitati obiecti perfecte respondet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:NX11","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:HSI-01","text":"Systema realitatem velut circuitum causal-intelligibilem imaginatur: perfectiones a centro simplici ad effectus exeunt, effectus autem cognitionem et nomina ad centrum reducunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum creatum est receptaculum proportionatum et elevabile, cuius capacitas transformari potest sine conversione in fontem aut mensuram obiecti divini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:HSI-03","text":"Subiectum divinum non est receptaculum, sed actus in quo intellectus, species, cognitum et intelligere unum sunt atque res creatae mensurantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:HSI-04","text":"Tempus est circumferentia variabilis circa centrum aeternum: omnia tempora praesentialiter cognoscuntur, dum contingentia ramificationum in causis proximis permanet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:A16","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendam structuram a cognoscibilitate Dei per nominationem analogicam usque ad scientiam divinam et visionem beatificam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est nexus inter distinctionem obiecti et capacitatis, analogiam ut mediam communitatem atque identitatem actus intelligendi cum essentia divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum satis determinantur modus unionis essentiae cum intellectu creato, relatio significationis substantialis ad ignorantiam quidditativam, concursus causae primae et contingentis atque functio voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MRT-B04","text":"Restitutio motum recursivum servat, quia non confundit pluralitatem cum compositione; forma exacta analogiae et commissura causalitatis voluntariae tamen reductioni plenae resistunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T170927956380Z_d4665c23","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 13–15","source_sha256":"952192a16c133525e020d2a00ead5598cfeba4f066d2e10d8b7f8e6df150a43a","sha256":"77516d33dffcb53481051c2606bd44f287099398edcf09225eaafaf684abf512","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:09:27.958533+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B01","text":"The system asks how God, maximally intelligible and perfectly knowing in himself, is truly knowable and nameable to created intellect without dependence, comprehension, or reduction to a created mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B02","text":"The same divine essence assumes a threefold function: it is the species of divine knowledge, the object immediately visible to the glorified intellect, and the cause known analogically through effects by the wayfarer's intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B03","text":"The argument retains the perfections of knowledge and discourse, but removes potential, composite, material, and comprehensive modes by recursive apophatic correction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B04","text":"A twofold movement occurs: created intellect ascends from effects to elevated knowledge, naming, and vision, while divine knowledge descends from perfect self-knowledge to proper knowledge of all things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:FGS6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B05","text":"Divine simplicity is transformed from an apparent impediment of plurality into the principle of multiple names, known things, and participations without internal composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B06","text":"The system moves spirally between the creature's ascent to God and the diffusion of divine perfection to creatures, with causality asymmetrically ordering both directions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B07","text":"Succession, novelty of denomination, and contingency are relegated to the created order, while the eternity and invariability of divine knowledge encompass changes in things without change in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AS-B08","text":"The closure is asymmetrical: the creature receives truth and beatitude without comprehension, whereas God comprehends himself and others without reception; the connection of knowledge to effect nevertheless still requires will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Knowledge is determined according to the mode of the knower; identity of object does not eliminate diversity of reception, conception, and vision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Pure act is maximally intelligible and supremely knowing, but this objective intelligibility does not entail the natural accessibility of finite intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] In God, essence, being, intellect, intelligible species, and the act of understanding are really one.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Natural knowledge of God is true, causal, and analogical, but its truth does not attain quidditative knowledge of the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Beatific vision immediately attains the object, because grace transforms created power, not because it abolishes its finitude or divides the object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Creaturely perfections pre-exist in God unitedly and eminently; divine attribution preserves the perfection and removes the created mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Divine simplicity does not exclude a multiplicity of intelligible accounts, names, and known things, but orders it outside composition in the divine reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Causality joins created knowledge, semantic analogy, and divine knowledge: effects manifest the cause, names are ordered to the cause, while the cause knows effects in its own power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Every temporal novelty is located in the creature's relation, effect, or proximate cause, not in divine essence or knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Three orders of knowledge complete the structure: comprehensive divine knowledge, analogical and mediated knowledge of the wayfarer, and immediate but non-comprehensive glorious vision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D13","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-01","text":"The law of the knower's mode preserves identity of function in created vision and divine knowledge, but in naming it changes into the law by which utterance follows the measure of intellectual conception.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-02","text":"The intelligible species changes function: a created species as representation of essence is excluded, divine essence is immediately united to the glorified intellect, and in divine knowledge essence itself is the species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-03","text":"Simplicity passes from a semantic limit to a generative principle: one essence sustains the plurality of contents of vision, non-synonymous names, and known things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D9","CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-04","text":"Causality migrates from the way of natural knowledge to the structure of analogy and finally to the account by which God knows other things in his own power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-05","text":"Mediation does not always retain the same function: in vision it perfects power without objective interposition, in discourse it forms conception, but in God every epistemic exteriority vanishes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RMD-06","text":"Negation changes from a local limit into a universal operation: it does not destroy perfection, but removes the created mode so that eminent attribution, true discourse, and simple knowledge may be constituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-01","text":"Degrees of light, the exception of rapture, orders of the propriety of names, and divisions of speculative and practical knowledge remain local determinations, not axioms of the whole group.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-02","text":"Local distinctions between object and capacity, what is signified and mode of signifying, known thing and mode of the knower are amplified into one law of proportionate reception.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-03","text":"Causality, eminence of perfections, and perfect knowledge of one's own power join the units and effect the transition from knowledge of the creature to knowledge of the creator.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-04","text":"The scale of analysis changes from the object, power, and medium of vision to the origin and terminus of signification, then to the identity of divine intellect, species, and act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ME7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:CGD-05","text":"The oppositions of simple knowledge and ignorance, univocity and equivocity, simplicity and plurality are overcome and otherwise codified through degrees of knowledge, analogy, and eminent containment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ME4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-01","text":"The system identifies neither transcendence with absolute unknowability nor God's eminence with absolute unnameability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-02","text":"No created species, univocal name, or common semantic plane can reduce the divine essence to the measure of the creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-03","text":"A plurality of propositions, names, relations, and known things does not introduce composition, change, or variation into divine knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:NX17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-04","text":"Autonomous ascent, creaturely omniscience, and ontological identity through participation are excluded; divine communication remains a gift received in a finite mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:GNX-05","text":"The infallibility of divine knowledge establishes neither the absolute necessity of contingents nor the actualization of all possibles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:NX15","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that the truth of knowledge or of a name requires comprehension of essence or exhaustion of knowability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:DNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that a distinction of intelligible accounts or a plurality of known things entails a plurality of parts, species, or acts in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:DNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that real denomination requires an intrinsic symmetrical relation or change in both terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:DNX6","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that every knowledge is constituted through a received extrinsic form; otherwise neither immediate vision nor divine knowledge could stand.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSA-01","text":"The system is ordered around the absence of a common measure of creator and creature; no commensuration of finite and infinite grounds knowledge or predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSA-02","text":"Epistemic exteriority from which God might receive the form, perfection, measure, or determination of knowledge is inadmissible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSA-03","text":"The wayfarer remains without a quidditative position from which the divine essence may be known according to itself; this absence bounds the entire doctrine of vision and names.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSA-04","text":"Participation cannot be converted into identity of creator and creature or multiplication of the divine nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX5","CH_GGVC_PP_5:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-01","text":"The same law of reception orders knowledge, naming, and vision: truth proceeds from identity of object, while diversity proceeds from the mode of knower and conceiver.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-01","CL_GGVC_05:GA-04","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-02","text":"Without multiplication, divine essence is the formal principle of divine knowledge, the object of glorious vision, and the remote terminus of analogical knowledge.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-03","CL_GGVC_05:GA-05","CL_GGVC_05:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-03","text":"The order of causality reverses epistemic direction: the creature ascends from effects to God, whereas God knows effects from knowledge of his own power and, with will conjoined, causes them.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-04","CL_GGVC_05:GA-08","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-04","text":"The multiplicity of contents of vision, accounts of names, and things known is distributed outside divine essence, while essence itself remains the single intelligible account.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D9","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-05","text":"The succession of created knowledge, temporality of denominations, and contingency of events are three forms of the same relocation of time from God into the created order.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-06","text":"Apophasis and grace effect analogous but unequal operations: the former purifies the mode of conception, the latter elevates the power of the knower, both without change in divine essence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-05","CL_GGVC_05:GA-06","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:XD-07","text":"Because knowledge alone does not determine an effect, temporal denominations of creator or lord signify voluntary actualization in the creature, not new knowledge or a real relation in God.","refs":["CL_GGVC_05:GA-08","CL_GGVC_05:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-01","text":"One divine essence generates three epistemic asymmetries: God comprehends through identity, the wayfarer truly knows through effects and names, and the blessed immediately see without comprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D13","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-02","text":"Simplicity is not emptiness of differences, but concentration of the principle from which knowable differences, predicable accounts, and finite participations arise without division.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-03","text":"The ontology of participation and the epistemology of causality mutually require one another: the creature indicates God because it participates in his perfection, and God properly knows the creature because he causally contains its principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-04","text":"Time becomes a property of the created order that is known, denominated, and caused; eternity, however, does not destroy time, but contains all its differences without succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:BSD-05","text":"The power of acting is distributed asymmetrically: the creature receives perfection and is elevated, while God produces the effect through knowledge and will; will therefore remains a necessary further joint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-01","text":"The created effect gives rise to knowledge of the cause; knowledge forms a name; the name is apophatically corrected; the correction refers back to the more eminent cause, which in turn grounds the intelligibility of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A17","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-02","text":"Divine self-knowledge extends to power, possibles, and effects; voluntarily actualized effects constitute temporal relations, which are referred to the cause without change in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-03","text":"Desire for the first principle is amplified toward grace and vision; vision does not remove incomprehensibility, but consummates beatitude through presence of the end without exhaustion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-04","text":"Simplicity is a recursive attractor: every plurality first seems to threaten composition, then is reduced to causal or intentional unity and is restored from it more distinctly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:RLE-05","text":"Subsistent being itself is the terminal attractor: it simultaneously orders the account of vision without a created species, the propriety of the name qui est, and the identity of essence with the act of understanding.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:D13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B01","text":"Pure act → maximal intelligibility and immateriality → identity of essence, being, and understanding → perfect divine knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B02","text":"Identity of object → reception according to the mode of the knower → diversity of divine, natural, and glorious knowledge without change of object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B03","text":"Sense and phantasms → causal effects → imperfect natural knowledge → intellectual conception → true name.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A16","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B04","text":"Signified perfection → removal of created mode → analogy → plurality of accounts under unity of thing → true affirmation without comprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B05","text":"Natural insufficiency → light of glory → perfection of power → immediate union of object → finite vision of the whole essence without comprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FGS-B06","text":"Perfect knowledge of divine power → knowledge of all possibles → voluntary determination of effects → eternal presence of temporal things → contingency preserved in proximate causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AFM-B01","text":"Pure act → maximal intelligibility → excess over created capacity → distinction of divine and created knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AFM-B02","text":"Sensible effects → causal knowledge → analogical naming → apophatic correction → true affirmation about God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:FGS6","CH_GGVC_PP_5:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AFM-B03","text":"Divine self-knowledge → knowledge of power → knowledge of possibles and effects → determining will → temporal causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:AFM-B04","text":"Elevation of intellect → vision of the whole essence → incomprehensibility preserved → finite beatitude → contingency and temporality placed outside God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-01","text":"God's knowability ceases to be a binary opposition and is distributed among the object, power, medium, mode, and state of the knower.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-02","text":"The community of discourse concerning God and creature is reordered beyond the dilemma of univocity and equivocity through causal analogy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-03","text":"Simplicity is transformed from an impediment of plurality into a principle of universal knowledge, semantic multiplicity, and distinct participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-04","text":"Time is no longer a common measure of God and creature, but a variable order wholly present to eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MME-05","text":"Apophasis changes from terminal silence into a constitutive method that retains perfection while excluding the created mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B01","text":"At the level of surface are treated the possibility and mode of vision, the propriety of names, and the scope of divine knowledge concerning itself, other things, possibles, and contingents.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ALT1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, the system is ordered through mode of being, cognitive power, conception, intelligible species, causality, and act of knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, questions are constituted beyond the oppositions of knowable and unknowable, silence and predication, simplicity and difference.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, God is being itself and eminent cause, the creature is asymmetrically related participation, while eternity is the non-successive presence of time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_5:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the very form of the argument successively retains perfections, removes created modes, and restores differences under simple unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FL-01","text":"Natural desire is ordered to the first principle as an end that no natural faculty can attain; the connection between natural ordination and supernatural gift remains tense.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_4:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FL-02","text":"Names of perfections signify something positively in the divine substance, although essence is quidditatively unknown in the state of wayfaring; the mode of substantial signification depends on this absence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_5:A2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FL-03","text":"Divine essence as intelligible form is united to created intellect, but the union can effect neither substantial informing nor ontological identity; the mechanism of this immediacy remains compressed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_4:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:FL-04","text":"Divine knowledge does not cause effects without will, and the contingency of the proximate cause is preserved; the mode of concurrence of knowledge, will, and contingent causality is not yet explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MP-01","text":"Species changes from an excluded created representation to the presence of objectively united essence, and finally to identity of essence with the species of divine knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MP-02","text":"Simplicity changes from an apparent restriction of plurality into the account by which multiplicity is contained without multiplication of the knower.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MP-03","text":"Comprehension changes its sense scalarly: the creature sees the whole essence without infinite adequation, whereas God comprehends himself because the mode of the knower perfectly corresponds to the knowability of the object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:NX11","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:HSI-01","text":"The system imagines reality as a causal-intelligible circuit: perfections proceed from the simple center to effects, while effects lead knowledge and names back to the center.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_5:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:HSI-02","text":"The created subject is a proportionate and elevable receptacle, whose capacity can be transformed without conversion into a source or measure of the divine object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_4:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:HSI-03","text":"The divine subject is not a receptacle, but an act in which intellect, species, known thing, and understanding are one and by which created things are measured.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:HSI-04","text":"Time is a variable circumference around the eternal center: all times are known as present, while the contingency of ramifications remains in proximate causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_6:A16","CH_GGVC_PP_6:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the structure from God's knowability through analogical naming to divine knowledge and beatific vision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the connection between the distinction of object and capacity, analogy as a middle commonality, and the identity of the act of understanding with divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MRT-B03","text":"The mode of the union of essence with created intellect, the relation of substantial signification to quidditative ignorance, the concurrence of first and contingent cause, and the function of will are not yet sufficiently determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_05:MRT-B04","text":"The reconstruction preserves recursive movement because it does not confuse plurality with composition; the exact form of analogy and the joint of voluntary causality nevertheless resist full reduction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_4:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PP_6:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PP_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_05@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_05:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 13–15","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 12 · Prima pars · Quaestio 13 · Prima pars · Quaestio 14"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 16–18","order":6,"parents":["CH_GGVC_PP_7","CH_GGVC_PP_8","CH_GGVC_PP_9"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_06@R001","sha256":"dcf23ac26458813c286c5af9640fb3d67a95cc9895f02e82935574d3b6d92892","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-01","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo unus intellectus divinus simplicissimus rationes rerum contineat, veritatem fundet atque falsitatem sine sui defectu circumscribat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis constituit intellectum divinum principium originans in quo pluralitas rationum, unitas primae veritatis et exclusio erroris eiusdem architecturae momenta sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio metaphysica fit per distinctiones directionis causalis, modi attributionis et operationis cognoscitivae, non per additionem entium inter Deum, res et intellectum creatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_7:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-04","text":"Motus descendit ab intellectu exemplari ad ordinem rerum, transit per res ut mensuras cognitionis creatae, atque terminatur in iudicio adaequato vel inadaequato.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-05","text":"Motus est recursivus sed asymmetricus: relatio intellectus et rei redit, dum causalitas ab intellectu divino ad rem descendit et mensuratio cognitionis humanae a re ad intellectum ascendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-06","text":"Multiplicitas idearum et veritatum non opponitur unitati primae mensurae, quia pluralitas distribuitur inter rationes intellectas, res mensuratas et actus creatos.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-07","text":"Malum, privatio, non ens et falsum recipiuntur tantum per dependentiam a positivo intelligibili, quo cognosci possunt sine ratione exemplari aut causalitate defectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D8","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-08","text":"Clausura reducitur ad primam veritatem, quae omnem conformitatem mensurat et errorem divinum excludit, dum intellectum finitum compositioni mutabili atque falsitati apertum relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Ordo idearum, veri et falsi constituitur per relationem intellectus ad rem, non per formas aut veritates separatim subsistentes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] Intellectus divinus est principium originans, mensura universalis et causa intelligibilis omnis rei creatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Una essentia divina plures rationes proprias rerum continet sine multiplicatione formarum quibus Deus intelligit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A8","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Similitudo transit ab exemplari productionis ad conformitatem cognitionis, deinde ad repraesentationem deficientem quae falsam acceptionem occasionare potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Mensuratio constituit triadem asymmetricam: intellectus divinus mensurat rem, res mensurat intellectum creatum, intellectus creatus conformitatem iudicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Ens est fundamentum cognoscibilitatis et veri; non ens ingreditur cognitionem tantum ut ens rationis in positivo fundatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Veritas formaliter est in intellectu, secundario autem rebus attribuitur secundum ordinem ad intellectum originantem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] In intellectu creato verum et falsum proprie manifestantur in iudicio componente vel dividente, quamvis intellectus divinus sine compositione verissimus sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Ordo universi est finis intellectus divini et postulat proprias rationes partium, quarum conformitas falsitatem simplicem a rebus naturalibus excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] In Deo esse, intelligere, mensura et veritas identificantur; ideo prima veritas sola est aeterna, immutabilis et erroris incapax.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A11","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Falsitas est inadaequatio determinata cognitionis, sed subsistere non potest nisi in ente vel vero quod defectum sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","text":"[Persistent] Malum et privatio cognoscuntur per bonum et ens, non per rationem propriam positivam neque ut defectus a Deo causati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-13","text":"[Mutating] Pluralitas primo apparet ut multitudo rationum idealium, deinde ut multitudo veritatum creatarum, sed utroque gradu ad unam mensuram divinam reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D8","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Defectibilitas cognitionis incipit ubi potentia ab obiecto proprio ad relationem, accidens, absentiam aut compositionem progreditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-01","text":"Forma intellecta redit primo ut exemplar rei, deinde ut mensura veritatis eius, postremo ut norma cui acceptio falsa non adaequatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-02","text":"Similitudo identitatem functionalem non servat: in intellectu divino productionem dirigit, in cognitione creata rem recipit, in apparentia deficiente errorem occasionatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-03","text":"Respectus intellectus ad rem migrat a ratione exemplari ad conformitatem veram et inde ad inadaequationem falsam, manente relatione sed mutata directione et valore.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A11","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-04","text":"Multiplicitas rationum divinarum transfertur in pluralitatem rerum et veritatum creatarum, dum varietas errorum ex diversis operationibus finitis, non ex prima mensura, nascitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D8","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-05","text":"Compositio et divisio, absentes a constitutione idearum divinarum, emergunt ut locus cognitionis explicitae veri atque ut punctum proprium falsitatis intellectualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-06","text":"Malum et non ens, exclusa ratione exemplari propria, redeunt ut entia rationis vel privationes cognoscibiles atque tandem ut fundamenta dependentia enuntiationum verarum aut falsarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-07","text":"Simplicitas divina primo pluralitatem idearum moderatur, deinde aeternitatem veritatis fundat, postremo possibilitatem erroris divini terminaliter excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-08","text":"Ordo universi ab obiecto intentionis creatricis in fundamentum obiectivitatis transit atque tandem efficit ut res naturalis simpliciter falsa esse nequeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-01","text":"Distributio idearum inter materiam, genera, accidentia et individua localis manet; ad gradum praesentem persistit sola regula qua intelligibilitas secundum modum dependentiae ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-02","text":"Taxonomia errorum sensus et phantasiae localis est, sed sursum amplificatur in distinctionem globalem inter obiectum proprium et operationem derivatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-03","text":"Ordo particularis entis, veri et boni non totam synthesim regit; sursum servatur principium quo ens cognoscibilitatem et veritatem fundat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-04","text":"Distinctio localis inter exemplar et rationem ampliatur in discrimen globale inter productionem rei, cognitionem eius et causalitatem veritatis de defectu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-05","text":"Idea ut essentia relative intellecta et Deus ut prima veritas non confunduntur, sed coniunguntur per intellectum divinum ut fontem rationis et mensurae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-06","text":"Transitus maior fit ab intellectu divino qui rem causat et mensurat ad rem creatam quae veritatem intellectus humani causat sine se ipsam ultimate mensurare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-07","text":"Quaestiones locales de loco ideae, veri et falsi superantur per structuram directionalem: formalitas, causalitas et denominatio diversis terminis distribuuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-08","text":"Falsitas artificialis et deviatio voluntaria manent casus inferiores, sed altius significant facultatem agentis mediati ordinem intellectus originantis imperfecte exsequendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-01","text":"Systema negat formas ideales aut veritates aeternas extra intellectum et essentiam divinam subsistentes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-02","text":"Multiplicitas rationum et veritatum compositionem realem aut operationem discursivam in Deo non introducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-03","text":"Apparentia humana nec esse rei nec veritatem absolutam constituit atque contradictiones perspectivarum mensura ultima fieri non possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-04","text":"Purum non ens, malum propriam ideam habens et falsum sine fundamento positivo excluduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX6","CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-05","text":"Res naturalis secundum ordinem ad intellectum divinum simpliciter falsa vel ontologice mendax esse non potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-06","text":"Veritas de Deo, intellectu creato, rebus et signis univoce non praedicatur neque omnes actus creatos in unam veritatem numero contrahit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-07","text":"Error omnibus gradibus cognitionis aequaliter non inest, quia obiectum proprium sensus et simplex quidditatis apprehensio per se falsitatem excludunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:NX3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-08","text":"Abstractio ab hic et nunc aut sola forma semantica enuntiabilis aeternitatem et immutabilitatem veritatis creatae non efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX12","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod causalitas intellectualis sine forma intellecta operari possit, quia tum ideae, ordo et mensuratio rei communi principio carerent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod mensuratio inter Deum, rem et intellectum humanum sit causaliter symmetrica.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod omnis distinctio rationis distinctionem realem vel compositionem in primo intellectu importet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod omne cognitum eodem modo producatur quo cognoscitur, quia scientia privationis causalitatem defectus non inducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod falsitas pura et sine subiecto exsistat, cum omnis inadaequatio ente vel vero sustentetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet quod res creata aut intellectus humanus sui ipsius et totius veri mensura ultima sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-01","text":"Regio intelligibilium supra vel extra Deum indisponibilis est, quia formae et veritates aeternales intra intellectum divinum reducuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-02","text":"Radicaliter contingens chaos quod nullam rationem divinam neque ordinem intelligibilem habeat ontologice inadmissibile est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-03","text":"Possibilitas erroris in primo intellectu excluditur, quia simul causalitatem rerum, primam veritatem et normam omnis adaequationis destrueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-04","text":"Possibilitas rei omnino extra rationem divinam et omnem comparationem ad intellectum manet indisponibilis, quia neque intelligibilitatem neque statum veri aut falsi obtineret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-05","text":"Defectus absolutus, positivus et primae causae aemulus excluditur; malum et falsum tantum dependentia privativa operantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-01","text":"Res creata denominative vera est quia exemplar intellectum in esse participat; conformitas ad cognitionem humanam hanc veritatem non constituit sed cognoscit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-02","CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","CL_GGVC_06:GA-07","CL_GGVC_06:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-02","text":"Amplitudo cognitionis divinae excedit amplitudinem productionis exemplaris, unde malum vere cognosci potest sine idea propria et sine causalitate divina defectus.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-04","CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-03","text":"Eadem solutio structuram plurium idearum et plurium veritatum regit: multiplicitas intentionalis vel analogica ad unam essentiam et mensuram reducitur sine reali compositione primi principii.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-03","CL_GGVC_06:GA-10","CL_GGVC_06:GA-13","CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-04","text":"Intentio divina ordinis efficit ut res naturalis ontologice vera sit secundum propriam rationem, quamvis intellectui finito occasionem falsae opinionis praebere possit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-02","CL_GGVC_06:GA-07","CL_GGVC_06:GA-09","CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-05","text":"Intellectus finitus non deficit primo in receptione quidditatis, sed cum receptionem in compositionem, attributionem vel consequentiam non necessariam extendit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-08","CL_GGVC_06:GA-14","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-06","text":"Negativum tribus gradibus integratur: caret ratione exemplari propria, cognoscitur ut ens rationis, atque falsitatem vel veritatem enuntiabilem tantum super fundamento positivo sustinet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-06","CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-07","text":"Rationes rerum et prima veritas aeternaliter in Deo manent, dum conformitates creatae mutantur; tamen habitudo huius aeternitatis ad contingentiam futurorum nondum plene determinatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-10","CL_GGVC_06:GA-13","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D9","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-08","text":"Falsitas artificialis et deviatio voluntaria ostendunt effectum mediatum a ratione exemplari deficere posse, quamvis prima causa cognitionem defectus habeat nec defectum qua defectum producat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-01","text":"Realitas constituitur ut ordo intelligibiliter mensuratus in quo idea productionem, veritas conformitatem et falsitas defectum relationis designant.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-01","CL_GGVC_06:GA-02","CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-02","text":"Obiectivitas neque ex mente humana neque ex re solitaria oritur, sed ex duplici dependentia qua res a divino intellectu mensuratur et intellectum humanum mensurat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","CL_GGVC_06:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-03","text":"Cognitio divina defectuum cum bonitate causae primae componitur, quia causatur quidquid positivum est in apprehensione vel actu, non autem defectus ordinis ut talis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-04","text":"Tempus dividit statum mensurae a statu conformitatis: rationes et prima veritas sunt aeternae, res et iudicia creata successione mutantur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-10","CL_GGVC_06:GA-13","CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-05","text":"Subiectum creatum fit mensuratum capax veritatis, sed defectibile quando ab obiecto proprio ad iudicium derivatum transit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","CL_GGVC_06:GA-08","CL_GGVC_06:GA-14","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-06","text":"Methodus contradictiones non delet sed earum terminos secundum subiectum, rationem, causalitatem et gradum operationis redistribuit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-01","CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-07","text":"Falsum acquirit statum formaliter positivum ut acceptio determinata, sed ontologice dependentem ut defectus in subiecto vero.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-01","text":"Cognitio divina propriae imitabilitatis rationes determinat, rationes res ordinatas producunt, res cognitionem creatam mensurant, et veritas creata ad primam mensuram reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_7:A11","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-02","text":"Via amplificationis procedit a similitudine exemplari ad conformitatem cognoscitivam atque inde ad similitudinem deficientem quae iudicium inadaequatum provocare potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-03","text":"Attractor unitatis in multiplicitate iterationes regit: plures rationes et plures veritates manent distinctae, sed ad unum actum et unam primam mensuram reducuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-04","text":"Circuitus negativus bonum vel ens praesupponit, privationem per illud cognoscit, veritatem cognitionis servat atque autonomiam ontologicam mali vel falsi iterum excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-05","text":"Via erroris incipit a receptione per se recta, progreditur ad attributionem vel compositionem derivatam et terminatur in acceptione determinata quae rei non adaequatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-06","text":"Mutatio rei tollit veritatem determinatam et aliam substituit, dum communis possibilitas conformitatis persistit; repetitio veri igitur mutationem status, non immobilitatem enuntiabilis, significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-07","text":"Ordo universi est attractor ontologicus qui proprias rationes partium colligit et falsitatem simplicem a rebus naturalibus arcet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-08","text":"Relatio mensurationis redit sine circulo causali: intellectus divinus causat rem, res causat veritatem humanam, sed intellectus humanus esse rei non causat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B01","text":"Una essentia intelligens se perfecte cognoscit secundum omnes modos quibus a creaturis imitari potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B02","text":"Modi imitabilitatis intellecti → rationes propriae rerum → pluralitas intentionalis sine pluralitate reali in Deo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A11","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B03","text":"Rationes propriae ut exemplaria → productio intellectualis partium → ordo universi ut effectus principaliter intentus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B04","text":"Productio secundum exemplar → conformitas rei ad intellectum originantem → veritas rei denominative constituta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B05","text":"Res conformis primae mensurae → species recepta in intellectu creato → mensuratio cognitionis humanae a re.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B06","text":"Receptio rei → iudicium componens vel dividens → adaequatio ut veritas aut inadaequatio ut falsitas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B07","text":"Cognitio privationis vel falsi → restitutio fundamenti positivi → separatio veritatis cognitionis a causalitate defectus → clausura in prima veritate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D8","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:AFM-B01","text":"Una essentia intelligens → multiplices rationes intellectae → productio exemplaris ordinis → entia mensurata et vera → receptio in intellectu finito → iudicium adaequatum vel inadaequatum → pluralitas veritatum et errorum → reductio ad primam veritatem atque exclusio falsi autonomi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-01","text":"Idea, veritas et falsitas reclassificantur ut modi directionales unius relationis inter intellectum, rationem et rem, non ut regiones ontologicae separatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-02","text":"Oppositio inter unitatem divinam et multiplicitatem intelligibilem solvitur distinguendo rem intelligentem unam, rationes multas et veritates creatas analogice derivatas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-03","text":"Oppositio subiecti et obiecti in structuram trium graduum convertitur: intellectus divinus mensurans, res mensurata simulque mensurans, intellectus humanus mensuratus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-04","text":"Negativum non amplius ut nihil simpliciter tractatur, sed ut ens rationis, privatio vel inadaequatio cuius intelligibilitas a positivo dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-05","text":"Ager erroris describitur per operationes et transitus cognitionis, non per obiecta falsa simpliciter: defectus oritur inter receptionem, repraesentationem et iudicium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-06","text":"Aeternitas et immutabilitas transferuntur ab enuntiabili abstracto ad modum intellectus in quo veritas formaliter existit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-07","text":"Distinctio formalitatis a causalitate fit instrumentum necessarium: locus formalis veri, causa cognitionis et causa rei non sunt idem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei ideas divinas, sedem et proprietates veritatis atque distributionem falsitatis inter res et potentias cognoscitivas examinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis ideas, verum et falsum per rationes exemplares, relationes mensurantis et mensurati atque gradus operationis cognoscitivae distribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus aporias solvit mutando subiectum attributionis, directionem causalitatis et modum quo idem terminus per se vel secundum quid dicitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis realitatem ut ordinem intelligibiliter causatum ponit, cui prima mensura aeterna respondet, conformitates autem creatae multiplicabiles et mutabiles sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus eandem operationem repetit: entitatem separatam negat, relationem distinguit, eam in intellectu divino fundat atque defectus locales secundum gradus redistribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-01","text":"Pluralitas rationum propriarum requirit distinctionem intelligibilem robustam, dum omnis pluralitas realis in Deo negatur; modus subsistentiae huius distinctionis manet compressus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-02","text":"Veritas intellectus creati proprie compositioni et divisioni adscribitur, sed prima veritas intellectui divino simplici; analogia operationis iudicativae transitum sustinet sine plena explicatione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-03","text":"Falsum ut contrarium veri aliquid determinatum ponit, simul tamen ut privatio in subiecto vero fundatur; eius positivitas formalis et dependentia ontologica separandae sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-04","text":"Veritas formaliter in intellectu est, quamvis res veritatem intellectus humani causet; cohaerentia pendet ex rigida distinctione loci formalis a causalitate obiectiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-05","text":"Cognitio divina universaliter se extendit, sed malum propria idea caret et non ens tantum ut ens rationis cognoscitur; universalitas cognitionis igitur universalitatem rationum positivarum non importat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_7:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-06","text":"Aeternitas rationum et veritatis futurorum in causa divina affirmatur, sed modus quo haec aeternitas contingentiam eventuum servet nondum definitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-01","text":"Idea mutatur ab apparente forma separata in essentiam divinam relative intellectam, deinde in rationem mensurantem rem determinatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-02","text":"Veritas mutatur a conformitate intellectus creati in identitatem primae mensurae divinae, deinde iterum distribuitur in multiplices actus analogice dependentes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-03","text":"Similitudo mutat functionem ab exemplari efficiente ad medium receptivum et tandem ad occasionem fallaciae quando ultra proprium repraesentationis ambitum transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-04","text":"Falsitas ab attributione relativa rei transfertur ad actum cognoscitivum determinatum, unde res falsa, apparentia fallax et iudicium falsum diversis gradibus collocantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-05","text":"Immunitas obiecti proprii mutatur in defectibilitatem ubi cognitio ad compositionem vel relationem accidentalem progreditur; transitus operationis est verum punctum mutationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-01","text":"Imago occulta est machina mensurationis asymmetricae: intellectus divinus dat rationem, res eam participat, intellectus creatus participationem recipit atque iudicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum creatum est mensuratum capax reflexionis, cui certitudo ad obiectum proprium alligatur et periculum in transitu ad compositionem crescit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est distributio mutabilium conformitatum circa mensuram aeternam: veritates determinatae succedunt, prima veritas non transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D9","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio cognoscitiva tuta manet intra informationem obiecti proprii, sed fit instabilis ubi absentia, imago, accidens aut praedicatio pro re ipsa accipitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-05","text":"Totum campum prima veritas illuminat, dum falsitas umbra dependens est quae nullam materiam propriam habet sed super ente vero cadit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de intellectu divino originante, rationibus pluribus, mensuratione asymmetrica, iudicio creato et defectu dependenti ad structuram praesentis gradus restituendam sufficiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est nexus inter unam essentiam intelligibilem, proprias rationes rerum, intellectum divinum mensurantem et gradus finitos conformitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum satis determinatur quomodo rationes plures sine pluralitate reali in Deo distinguantur neque quomodo veritas iudicativa intellectui simplici attribuatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B04","text":"Contingentia futurorum sub veritate aeterna et causalitas occasionalis apparentiae fallacis manent regiones minus conclusae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B05","text":"Conformitas et analogia sunt commissurae irreducibiles: systema eis utitur ad causalitatem, attributionem et multiplicitatem connectendas, sed earum naturam ultimam non resolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B06","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat, quia progressionem ab exemplari divino per veritatem mensuratam ad falsitatem derivativam retinet et repetitiones ut mutationes functionis, non redundantias, ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171014733681Z_d0133cb5","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 16–18","source_sha256":"dcf23ac26458813c286c5af9640fb3d67a95cc9895f02e82935574d3b6d92892","sha256":"1de51b37d8c9ba21106ab786924b3014334d17f0d16cc6ac07697c0c23035e65","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:10:14.734612+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-01","text":"The central question is how one utterly simple divine intellect contains the accounts of things, grounds truth, and circumscribes falsity without defect in itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis establishes the divine intellect as the originating principle in which the plurality of accounts, the unity of first truth, and the exclusion of error are moments of the same architecture.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-03","text":"The metaphysical argument proceeds through distinctions of causal direction, mode of attribution, and cognitive operation, not through the addition of entities between God, things, and created intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_7:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-04","text":"The movement descends from the exemplary intellect to the order of things, passes through things as measures of created cognition, and terminates in an adequate or inadequate judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-05","text":"The movement is recursive but asymmetric: the relation of intellect and thing returns, while causality descends from the divine intellect to the thing and the measurement of human cognition ascends from the thing to the intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-06","text":"The multiplicity of ideas and truths does not oppose the unity of the first measure, because plurality is distributed among understood accounts, measured things, and created acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-07","text":"Evil, privation, non-being, and the false are admitted only through dependence on the positive intelligible, whereby they can be known without an exemplary account or a causality of defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D8","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BAS-08","text":"The closure is reduced to first truth, which measures every conformity and excludes divine error, while leaving finite intellect open to mutable composition and falsity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The order of ideas, the true, and the false is constituted through the relation of intellect to thing, not through forms or truths subsisting separately.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] The divine intellect is the originating principle, universal measure, and intelligible cause of every created thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] One divine essence contains several proper accounts of things without multiplication of the forms by which God understands.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A8","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Likeness passes from the exemplar of production to conformity of cognition, then to a deficient representation that can occasion a false apprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Measurement constitutes an asymmetric triad: divine intellect measures the thing, the thing measures created intellect, created intellect judges conformity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Being is the foundation of cognoscibility and of the true; non-being enters cognition only as a being of reason grounded in the positive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Truth is formally in the intellect, but is secondarily attributed to things according to their order to the originating intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] In created intellect, the true and the false are properly manifested in a judgment composing or dividing, although divine intellect is most true without composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] The order of the universe is the end of divine intellect and requires proper accounts of the parts, whose conformity excludes simple falsity from natural things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] In God, being, understanding, measure, and truth are identified; therefore first truth alone is eternal, immutable, and incapable of error.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A11","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Falsity is a determinate inadequacy of cognition, but cannot subsist except in a being or truth that sustains the defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:A10","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","text":"[Persistent] Evil and privation are known through the good and being, not through a proper positive account nor as defects caused by God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-13","text":"[Mutating] Plurality first appears as a multitude of ideal accounts, then as a multitude of created truths, but at both levels is reduced to one divine measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D8","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] The defectibility of cognition begins where a power proceeds from its proper object to relation, accident, absence, or composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-01","text":"The understood form returns first as exemplar of the thing, then as measure of its truth, and finally as the norm to which false apprehension is not adequate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-02","text":"Likeness does not preserve functional identity: in divine intellect it directs production, in created cognition it receives the thing, in deficient appearance it occasions error.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-03","text":"The respect of intellect to thing migrates from exemplary account to true conformity and thence to false inadequacy, while the relation remains but its direction and value change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A11","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-04","text":"The multiplicity of divine accounts is transferred into the plurality of created things and truths, while the variety of errors arises from diverse finite operations, not from the first measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D8","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-05","text":"Composition and division, absent from the constitution of divine ideas, emerge as the locus of explicit cognition of the true and as the proper point of intellectual falsity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-06","text":"Evil and non-being, excluded from having a proper exemplary account, return as beings of reason or cognoscible privations and finally as dependent foundations of true or false propositions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-07","text":"Divine simplicity first regulates the plurality of ideas, then grounds the eternity of truth, and finally excludes the possibility of divine error conclusively.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RMD-08","text":"The order of the universe passes from the object of creative intention into the foundation of objectivity and finally brings it about that a natural thing cannot be simply false.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-01","text":"The distribution of ideas among matter, genera, accidents, and individuals remains local; at the present level only the rule persists by which intelligibility is ordered according to the mode of dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-02","text":"The taxonomy of errors of sense and imagination is local, but is amplified upward into the global distinction between a proper object and a derived operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-03","text":"The particular order of being, truth, and good does not govern the whole synthesis; upward, the principle is retained whereby being grounds cognoscibility and truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-04","text":"The local distinction between exemplar and account is expanded into the global difference between production of the thing, cognition of it, and the causality of truth concerning defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-05","text":"Idea as essence understood relatively and God as first truth are not confused, but are joined through divine intellect as the source of account and measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-06","text":"The major transition occurs from divine intellect, which causes and measures the thing, to the created thing, which causes the truth of human intellect without ultimately measuring itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A12","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-07","text":"Local questions concerning the location of idea, truth, and falsity are surpassed through a directional structure: formality, causality, and denomination are distributed among diverse terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:CGD-08","text":"Artificial falsity and voluntary deviation remain lower cases, but at a higher level signify the capacity of a mediated agent to execute imperfectly the order of originating intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-01","text":"The system denies ideal forms or eternal truths subsisting above or outside divine intellect and essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-02","text":"The multiplicity of accounts and truths does not introduce real composition or discursive operation into God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-03","text":"Human appearance constitutes neither the being of the thing nor absolute truth, and contradictions of perspectives cannot become the ultimate measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-04","text":"Pure non-being, evil having its own idea, and falsity without a positive foundation are excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX6","CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-05","text":"A natural thing, according to its order to divine intellect, cannot be simply false or ontologically mendacious.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:NX1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-06","text":"Truth is not predicated univocally of God, created intellect, things, and signs, nor does it contract all created acts into one truth in number.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-07","text":"Error does not inhere equally at all levels of cognition, because the proper object of sense and simple apprehension of quiddity exclude falsity through themselves.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:NX3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:GNX-08","text":"Abstraction from hic et nunc or the semantic form of the enunciable alone does not effect the eternity and immutability of created truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX12","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that intellectual causality can operate without an understood form, because then ideas, order, and the measurement of the thing would lack a common principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that measurement between God, thing, and human intellect is causally symmetrical.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that every distinction of reason entails a real distinction or composition in the first intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that everything known is produced in the same manner in which it is known, because knowledge of privation does not introduce a causality of defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that pure and subjectless falsity exists, since every inadequacy is sustained by being or truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that a created thing or human intellect is the ultimate measure of itself and of the whole true.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-01","text":"A region of intelligibles above or outside God is unavailable, because eternal forms and truths are reduced within divine intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-02","text":"A radically contingent chaos having no divine account or intelligible order is ontologically inadmissible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-03","text":"The possibility of error in the first intellect is excluded, because it would simultaneously destroy the causality of things, first truth, and the norm of every adequation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-04","text":"The possibility of a thing entirely outside divine account and every comparison to intellect remains unavailable, because it would possess neither intelligibility nor the status of true or false.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX1","CH_GGVC_PP_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSA-05","text":"An absolute, positive defect rivaling the first cause is excluded; evil and falsity operate only dependently and privatively.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SNX3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-01","text":"A created thing is denominatively true because it participates in being in the understood exemplar; conformity to human cognition does not constitute this truth but knows it.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-02","CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","CL_GGVC_06:GA-07","CL_GGVC_06:GA-09","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-02","text":"The scope of divine cognition exceeds the scope of exemplary production; hence evil can truly be known without a proper idea and without divine causality of defect.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-04","CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-03","text":"The same solution governs the structure of several ideas and several truths: intentional or analogical multiplicity is reduced to one essence and measure without real composition of the first principle.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-03","CL_GGVC_06:GA-10","CL_GGVC_06:GA-13","CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-04","text":"The divine intention of order brings it about that a natural thing is ontologically true according to its proper account, although it can offer finite intellect an occasion for false opinion.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-02","CL_GGVC_06:GA-07","CL_GGVC_06:GA-09","CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-05","text":"Finite intellect does not first fail in reception of quiddity, but when it extends reception into composition, attribution, or a non-necessary consequence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-08","CL_GGVC_06:GA-14","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-06","text":"The negative is integrated at three levels: it lacks a proper exemplary account, is known as a being of reason, and sustains enunciable falsity or truth only upon a positive foundation.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-06","CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PP_7:NX5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-07","text":"The accounts of things and first truth remain eternally in God, while created conformities change; yet the relation of this eternity to the contingency of future things is not yet fully determined.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-10","CL_GGVC_06:GA-13","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D9","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:XD-08","text":"Artificial falsity and voluntary deviation show that an effect mediated by an exemplary account can fail, although the first cause has knowledge of the defect and does not produce the defect as defect.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-01","text":"Reality is constituted as an intelligibly measured order in which idea designates production, truth conformity, and falsity a defect of relation.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-01","CL_GGVC_06:GA-02","CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-02","text":"Objectivity arises neither from human mind nor from an isolated thing, but from the double dependence whereby the thing is measured by divine intellect and measures human intellect.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","CL_GGVC_06:GA-07","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-03","text":"Divine cognition of defects is compatible with the goodness of the first cause, because whatever is positive in apprehension or act is caused, but not the defect of order as such.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CL_GGVC_06:GA-12","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-04","text":"Time divides the state of measure from the state of conformity: accounts and first truth are eternal, while created things and judgments change in succession.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-10","CL_GGVC_06:GA-13","CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-05","text":"The created subject becomes something measured and capable of truth, but defectible when it passes from its proper object to derived judgment.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","CL_GGVC_06:GA-08","CL_GGVC_06:GA-14","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-06","text":"The method does not erase contradictions, but redistributes their terms according to subject, account, causality, and degree of operation.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-01","CL_GGVC_06:GA-05","CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:BSD-07","text":"The false acquires a formally positive status as determinate apprehension, but an ontologically dependent status as defect in a true subject.","refs":["CL_GGVC_06:GA-11","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-01","text":"Divine cognition determines the accounts of its own imitability, the accounts produce ordered things, things measure created cognition, and created truth is reduced to the first measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_7:A11","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-02","text":"The path of amplification proceeds from exemplary likeness to cognitive conformity and thence to deficient likeness, which can provoke an inadequate judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-03","text":"The attractor of unity in multiplicity governs iterations: several accounts and several truths remain distinct, but are reduced to one act and one first measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-04","text":"The negative circuit presupposes good or being, knows privation through it, preserves the truth of cognition, and again excludes the ontological autonomy of evil or falsity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-05","text":"The path of error begins from reception correct through itself, proceeds to derived attribution or composition, and terminates in a determinate apprehension inadequate to the thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-06","text":"A change of the thing removes one determinate truth and substitutes another, while the common possibility of conformity persists; repetition of the true therefore signifies change of state, not immobility of the enunciable.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D12","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-07","text":"The order of the universe is an ontological attractor that gathers together the proper accounts of parts and wards off simple falsity from natural things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:RLE-08","text":"The relation of measurement returns without a causal circle: divine intellect causes the thing, the thing causes human truth, but human intellect does not cause the being of the thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B01","text":"One essence, understanding itself, knows itself perfectly according to all the modes in which it can be imitated by creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B02","text":"Understood modes of imitability → proper accounts of things → intentional plurality without real plurality in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A11","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B03","text":"Proper accounts as exemplars → intellectual production of parts → order of the universe as principally intended effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B04","text":"Production according to exemplar → conformity of the thing to originating intellect → truth of the thing constituted denominatively.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B05","text":"Thing conformed to the first measure → species received in created intellect → measurement of human cognition by the thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B06","text":"Reception of the thing → judgment composing or dividing → adequation as truth or inadequation as falsity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FGS-B07","text":"Cognition of privation or the false → restoration of the positive foundation → separation of the truth of cognition from the causality of defect → closure in first truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D14","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D8","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:AFM-B01","text":"One understanding essence → multiple understood accounts → exemplary production of order → measured and true beings → reception in finite intellect → adequate or inadequate judgment → plurality of truths and errors → reduction to first truth and exclusion of autonomous falsity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A9","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-01","text":"Idea, truth, and falsity are reclassified as directional modes of one relation among intellect, account, and thing, not as separate ontological regions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-02","text":"The opposition between divine unity and intelligible multiplicity is resolved by distinguishing one understanding thing, many accounts, and created truths analogically derived.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-03","text":"The opposition of subject and object is converted into a structure of three degrees: measuring divine intellect, the thing measured and at the same time measuring, measured human intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-04","text":"The negative is no longer treated as nothing simply, but as a being of reason, privation, or inadequacy whose intelligibility depends on the positive.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-05","text":"The field of error is described through operations and transitions of cognition, not through simply false objects: defect arises between reception, representation, and judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-06","text":"Eternity and immutability are transferred from the abstract enunciable to the mode of intellect in which truth formally exists.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MME-07","text":"The distinction of formality from causality becomes a necessary instrument: the formal locus of the true, the cause of cognition, and the cause of the thing are not the same.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level examines divine ideas, the seat and properties of truth, and the distribution of falsity among things and cognitive powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:AS1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level distributes ideas, the true, and the false through exemplary accounts, relations of measurer and measured, and degrees of cognitive operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level resolves aporias by changing the subject of attribution, the direction of causality, and the mode in which the same term is said per se or secundum quid.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level posits reality as an intelligibly caused order, to which an eternal first measure corresponds, while created conformities are multipliable and mutable.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:ALT4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level repeats the same operation: it denies a separate entity, distinguishes the relation, grounds it in divine intellect, and redistributes local defects according to degrees.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-01","text":"The plurality of proper accounts requires a robust intelligible distinction, while every real plurality in God is denied; the mode of subsistence of this distinction remains compressed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_7:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-02","text":"The truth of created intellect is properly ascribed to composition and division, but first truth to simple divine intellect; an analogy of judicative operation sustains the transition without full explanation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-03","text":"The false, as contrary to the true, posits something determinate, yet is at the same time grounded as privation in a true subject; its formal positivity and ontological dependence must be separated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-04","text":"Truth is formally in the intellect, although the thing causes the truth of human intellect; coherence depends upon a rigid distinction between formal locus and objective causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-05","text":"Divine cognition extends itself universally, but evil lacks a proper idea and non-being is known only as a being of reason; universality of cognition therefore does not entail universality of positive accounts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT5","CH_GGVC_PP_7:A13","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:FL-06","text":"The eternity of accounts and of the truth of future things in the divine cause is affirmed, but the mode by which this eternity preserves the contingency of events is not yet defined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-01","text":"Idea changes from an apparently separate form into divine essence understood relatively, then into an account measuring a determinate thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:ME1","CH_GGVC_PP_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-02","text":"Truth changes from conformity of created intellect into identity of the first divine measure, then is again distributed into multiple analogically dependent acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-03","text":"Likeness changes function from efficient exemplar to receptive medium and finally to an occasion of deception when transferred beyond its proper sphere of representation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:A3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D4","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-04","text":"Falsity is transferred from a relative attribution of the thing to a determinate cognitive act, whence a false thing, deceptive appearance, and false judgment are located at diverse levels.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MP-05","text":"The immunity of the proper object changes into defectibility where cognition proceeds to composition or accidental relation; the transition of operation is the true point of change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:AS3","CH_GGVC_PP_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-01","text":"The hidden image is a machine of asymmetric measurement: divine intellect gives the account, the thing participates in it, created intellect receives and judges the participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:ME2","CH_GGVC_PP_8:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-02","text":"The created subject is something measured and capable of reflection, whose certainty is bound to the proper object and whose danger increases in the transition to composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:SD3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-03","text":"Time is the distribution of mutable conformities around an eternal measure: determinate truths succeed one another; first truth does not pass away.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D9","CH_GGVC_PP_8:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-04","text":"Cognitive navigation remains safe within the information of the proper object, but becomes unstable where absence, image, accident, or predication is taken for the thing itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_9:A7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:D6","CH_GGVC_PP_9:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:HSI-05","text":"First truth illuminates the whole field, while falsity is a dependent shadow that has no proper matter but falls upon true being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:D7","CH_GGVC_PP_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B01","text":"Axioms concerning originating divine intellect, several accounts, asymmetric measurement, created judgment, and dependent defect suffice to restore the structure of the present level.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT1","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the nexus between one intelligible essence, the proper accounts of things, measuring divine intellect, and finite degrees of conformity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT2","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B03","text":"It is not yet sufficiently determined how several accounts are distinguished without real plurality in God, nor how judicative truth is attributed to simple intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT4","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B04","text":"The contingency of future things under eternal truth and the occasional causality of deceptive appearance remain less concluded regions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT8","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B05","text":"Conformity and analogy are irreducible joints: the system employs them to connect causality, attribution, and multiplicity, but does not resolve their ultimate nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT3","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_06:MRT-B06","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement, because it retains the progression from divine exemplar through measured truth to derivative falsity and orders repetitions as changes of function, not redundancies.","refs":["CH_GGVC_PP_7:MRT6","CH_GGVC_PP_8:MRT9","CH_GGVC_PP_9:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_06@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_06:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 16–18","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 15 · Prima pars · Quaestio 16 · Prima pars · Quaestio 17"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 19–21","order":7,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_10","CH_GGVC_P_11","CH_GGVC_P_12"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_07@R001","sha256":"41a7fd5ab7d1f0727978e7ee0bd95ebdff4d20092a0efd6aa473877f71e18e64","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo vita, voluntas et amor Deo proprie attribuantur sine motu passivo, indigentia, compositione aut mutabilitate, simulque causalitatem creaturarum explicent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-02","text":"Thesis globalis unum actum simplicem constituit ut vitam intellectualem, voluntatem boni et amorem causaliter bonum communicantem, rationibus distinctis sed re identicis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-03","text":"Argumentatio a manifestationibus creatis ad rationes formales regreditur, imperfectiones removet, rationes purificatas Deo attribuit, deinde eas per effectus causales comprobatas restituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-04","text":"Motus procedit ab interioritate operationis ad determinationem voluntariam effectuum atque inde ad productionem et distributionem bonitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:A10","CH_GGVC_P_12:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-05","text":"Progressio est cumulativa et spiralis: unumquodque attributum priorem structuram retinet, sed eam in maiorem causalitatis, modalitatis et bonitatis amplitudinem transfert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-06","text":"Differentiatio crescit ab executione, forma et fine operationis ad modos necessarios vel contingentes effectuum, ac tandem ad inaequalem bonorum collationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A6","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-07","text":"Malum limitem distributum constituit: cognoscitur sine vita exemplari propria, permittitur sine volitione per se et repudiatur ut defectus sine destructione naturae amatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-08","text":"Clausura causaliter asymmetrica est: unus actus invariabilis multiplicitatem rerum, modorum et bonorum producit, sed nulla multiplicitas creata ad compositionem vel mutationem fontis regreditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A11","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Praedicatum perfectionis Deo secundum rationem formalem purificatam attribuitur, non secundum modum corporeum, passivum aut defectivum quo in creaturis manifestatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A4","CH_GGVC_P_12:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Esse, vivere, intelligere et velle in Deo unum actum realem constituunt, cui amor ut prima inclinatio voluntatis ad bonum inseparabiliter convenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A11","CH_GGVC_P_11:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Perfectio primo ut interioritas principiorum operationis mensuratur, deinde ut potestas efficiendi ipsum modum quo effectus agit vel evenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A6","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Bonitas divina est obiectum necessarium voluntatis divinae, dum creaturae non necessariae voluntur ut participationes eius sine incremento perfectionis divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_11:A5","CH_GGVC_P_11:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Unitas actus divini multiplicibus terminis intentionalibus, effectibus et gradibus boni compatitur, quia pluralitas obiectiva actum non multiplicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Causalitas divina non solum esse effectus, sed etiam ordinem causarum secundarum atque modum necessarium vel contingentem eventus instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A13","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_11:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Relatio causalis inter Deum et creaturam asymmetrica est: creatura a Deo esse et bonum recipit, Deus autem ab obiecto exteriori neque movetur neque perficitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Necessitas et immutabilitas actus primi necessitatem absolutam effectuum non inferunt, sed contingentiam ut modum positive intentum includere possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Amor divinus universalis est secundum collationem esse, sed inaequalis secundum magnitudinem boni unicuique rei voliti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:A7","CH_GGVC_P_12:D3","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Malum non est ratio positiva vitae, voluntatis aut amoris divini, sed privatio cognita, culpa permissa vel defectus a natura amata distinctus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Distinctiones inter modos essendi, necessitates, causalitates, obiecta et signa custodiunt unitatem divinam ne in uniformitatem semanticam vel modalem contrahatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:D9","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Maxima immanentia actus divini non sterilitatem sed maximam fecunditatem causaliter ordinatam constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_11:A4","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Rationes rerum ut intellectae ad vitam divinam pertinent, ut volitae in esse determinantur, et ut amata bonitatem recipiunt, sine divisione huius processus in tres actus reales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:D8","CH_GGVC_P_11:D5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-01","text":"Motus non identice redit: a mutatione imperfecti in actum immanentem perfectum transfertur, deinde ab amore expellitur quatenus passionem receptivam significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-02","text":"Autodeterminatio ab interioritate executionis, formae et finis ad causalitatem producendam ipsum modum effectus amplificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A6","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-03","text":"Intellectus identitatem structuralem retinet, sed functionem mutat: primo gradum vitae definit, postea voluntatem et ordinem causalium determinationum fundat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A8","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-04","text":"Bonum migrat a fine operationis ad obiectum principale voluntatis, ac tandem in effectum quem amor divinus rebus confert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-05","text":"Simplicitas stabiliter redit, sed crescentem pluralitatem ordinat: prius identitatem attributorum, deinde pluralitatem volitorum, postremo inaequalitatem bonorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-06","text":"Necessitas vim apparentem invertit: quod primo libertati et contingentiae obstare videtur, fit fundamentum infallibilis productionis modorum contingentium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-07","text":"Participatio a conformitate exemplati ad ordinem voliti et inde ad bonum causaliter collatum transfertur, manente dependentia creaturae a fonte divino.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A16","CH_GGVC_P_11:A5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-08","text":"Malum per negationem cumulativam mutatur: caret ratione exemplari propria, excluditur ab obiecto voluntatis per se, et separatur ut defectus a natura amata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-01","text":"Gradatio plantarum, animalium et intellectuum manet apparatus localis; hoc gradu absorbetur in regulam generalem qua perfectio crescit secundum interioritatem principiorum actionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A7","CH_GGVC_P_10:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-02","text":"Divisio operationis, permissionis, praecepti, prohibitionis et consilii localiter semanticam voluntatis ordinat, sed globaliter subordinatur distinctioni inter actum divinum et signa temporalia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:D13","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-03","text":"Comparationes particulares inter Christum, angelos, homines et praedestinatos non ascendunt ut axiomata; permanent probationes locales regulae boni voliti secundum ordinem et tempus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:D9","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-04","text":"Definitio vitae per actum immanentem sursum amplificatur, quia eadem interioritas identitatem realem intellectus et voluntatis atque impassibilitatem amoris sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A9","CH_GGVC_P_11:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-05","text":"Connexio praesentis gradus non est mera successio trium attributorum: intellectus voluntatem fundat, voluntas amorem fert, amor causalitatem voluntatis ut productionem boni explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1","CH_GGVC_P_12:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-06","text":"Maior transitus fit cum interioritas divina ex statu perfectionis intrinsecae in principium ordinis extrinseci effectuum convertitur, nulla mutatione intrinseca interposita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:A10","CH_GGVC_P_12:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-07","text":"Imagines locales motus, appetitus et affectus obsolescunt quatenus univoce accipiuntur, sed formaliter recodificatae instrumenta attributionis analogicae fiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-01","text":"Deus non vivit, vult aut amat per mutationem corporalem, passionem sensitivam vel transitum de potentia ad actum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-02","text":"Nullum bonum externum Deum determinat, perficit aut ad agendum allicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-03","text":"Praedicata creaturarum non transferuntur univoce ad Deum secundum modum materialem, temporalem aut receptivum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-04","text":"Pluralitas attributorum, volitorum et bonorum non constituit pluralitatem actuum vel compositionem in Deo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-05","text":"Efficacia causae primae non absorbet differentiam inter necessarium et contingens neque veritatem causarum secundarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-06","text":"Malum non admittitur ut ens positivum, exemplar proprium aut obiectum aequale divinae cognitionis, voluntatis et amoris.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_12:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-07","text":"Signa normativa, historica vel affectiva non sunt transcriptio perspicua beneplaciti aeterni aut mensura exhaustiva dilectionis divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX7","CH_GGVC_P_12:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet proprietatem visibilem rem sufficienter definire; aliter transitus a motu, appetitu et affectu creato ad rationem formalem divinam impossibilis esset.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet causalitatem secundam veram solum si a causa prima independens sit; dependentia hic ipsum modum propriae actionis instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet simplicitatem causae uniformitatem terminorum, effectuum vel bonorum postulare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet libertatem potentiam passivam, mutationem consilii aut facultatem peccandi necessario continere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet bonitatem creaturae amorem divinum antecedere tamquam causam determinantem; bonitas creata est potius effectus boni voliti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet cognosci, voleri et amari eundem statum formalem rei constituere, quia scientia, voluntas et amor diversas habitudines intentionales exprimunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_11:D15","CH_GGVC_P_12:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSA-01","text":"Systema nullam mensuram superiorem admittit qua actus divinus secundum modos creatos motus, necessitatis vel amoris iudicetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_12:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSA-02","text":"Possibilitas relationis symmetricae inter Deum et creaturam inadmissibilis est, quia creatura fontem neque complet neque reconfigurat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSA-03","text":"Intelligibilitas, bonitas et agentia creata non possunt ultimum principium sui iuris constituere; earum propria operatio intra dependentiam causaliter datam subsistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSA-04","text":"Actus aeternus non est plene perspicuus in successione effectuum, praeceptorum, permissionum aut signorum dilectionis temporalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-01","text":"Vita intellectualis, voluntas et amor seriem formalem constituunt: actus intelligibilis bonum apprehendit, voluntas in illud inclinat, amor bonum alteri volitum in ratione sua includit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A12","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1","CL_GGVC_07:GA-02","CL_GGVC_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-02","text":"Eadem creatura triplici habitudine ordinatur: ut intellecta ad vitam divinam pertinet, ut volita causaliter producitur, et ut amata esse ac bonitatem recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:D8","CH_GGVC_P_11:D5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D2","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","CL_GGVC_07:GA-09","CL_GGVC_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-03","text":"Creatio non est exitus Dei a propria immanentia, sed effectus exterior actus qui intrinsece perfectus, immobilis et invariabilis manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:D6","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_12:D4","CL_GGVC_07:GA-02","CL_GGVC_07:GA-07","CL_GGVC_07:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-04","text":"Agentia creata est realis quatenus creatura se ad operationem agit, sed ipsa autonomia operativa est modus sub ordine causae universalis institutus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A1","CH_GGVC_P_11:D7","CL_GGVC_07:GA-03","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-05","text":"Contingentia non est residuum impotentiae divinae, sed forma effectus quam causa immutabilis efficaciter producit sine conversione in necessitatem absolutam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","CL_GGVC_07:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-06","text":"Negatio mali per tres unitates systema positivum finit: esse malum non potest vita exemplaris, obiectum volitum per se aut bonum amore productum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD3","CL_GGVC_07:GA-10","CL_GGVC_07:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-07","text":"Libertas divina consistit in non necessaria habitudine ad creaturas sub necessaria adhaesione bonitati, non in mutabilitate aut possibilitate mali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX14","CL_GGVC_07:GA-04","CL_GGVC_07:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-01","text":"Ontologia emergens est ontologia participationis modaliter ordinatae: esse, operari et bonum creaturae sunt propria, sed non sui ipsorum ultima principia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A16","CH_GGVC_P_11:A5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D3","CL_GGVC_07:GA-03","CL_GGVC_07:GA-07","CL_GGVC_07:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-02","text":"Causalitas prima est prior non tantum effectui, sed ipsi distinctioni modali inter eventum necessarium et contingentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A13","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","CL_GGVC_07:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-03","text":"Tempus pertinet ad ordinem effectuum et bonorum collatorum, non ad successionem intellectionis, volitionis aut amoris in causa divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13","CL_GGVC_07:GA-02","CL_GGVC_07:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-04","text":"Subiectum creatum fit agens dependens: vere ex se operatur secundum principia propria, quamvis illa principia, fines et modi a causa prima ordinentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A5","CH_GGVC_P_11:A12","CL_GGVC_07:GA-03","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-05","text":"Cognitio humana ex effectibus temporalibus non potest decretum aeternum vel gradum dilectionis simpliciter reconstruere, quia signum et beneplacitum, status praesens et bonum futurum non coincidunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX7","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13","CL_GGVC_07:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-06","text":"Ordo moralis non requirit malum ut principium positivum: natura et agentia subsistunt ex bono, dum defectus moraliter imputabilis intra operationem dependentem emergit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD3","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","CL_GGVC_07:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-07","text":"Methodus globalis attributionem analogicam et inversionem causalem coniungit: ratio formalis ab imperfectione separatur, deinde in Deo non ut effectus sed ut principium perfectionis creatae ponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1","CL_GGVC_07:GA-01","CL_GGVC_07:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus attributionis est: manifestatio creata → extractio rationis formalis → remotio imperfectionis → attributio divina → reinterpretatio manifestationis ut effectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-02","text":"Interioritas actus divini communicabilitatem auget; communicatio effectus producit; effectus autem ad fontem reducuntur sine regressu mutationis in fontem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:A4","CH_GGVC_P_12:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-03","text":"Intelligere → bonum apprehensum → velle → amare → bonum creatum constituit viam amplificationis qua actus immanens in ordinem causaliter fecundum explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A1","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1","CH_GGVC_P_12:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-04","text":"Simplicitas → pluralitas terminorum → diversitas modorum → inaequalitas bonorum → regressus ad unum actum constituit principalem circuitum ordinis creati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_11:D9","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-05","text":"Immutabilitas, quae primo contingentiam excludere videtur, eam causaliter instituit; contingentia sic ad efficaciam causae potius quam ad defectum eius regreditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-06","text":"Malum circuitum positivum non complet, sed ut limes recursivus cognitionem a constitutione, permissionem a volitione et naturam a defectu distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-07","text":"Attractor totius structurae est actus simplex, immanens et invariabilis qui, eo ipso quod a nullo exteriori determinatur, ordinem multiplicem efficaciter determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:A11","CH_GGVC_P_12:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B01","text":"Manifestationes creatae motus, appetitus et amoris materiam initialem praebent, sed nondum rationem divinam constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B02","text":"Ex manifestatione extrahitur ratio formalis: operatio a se, inclinatio intellectiva ad bonum et velle bonum alteri.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A1","CH_GGVC_P_11:A1","CH_GGVC_P_12:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B03","text":"Ratio formalis purgatur subtractione mutationis imperfectae, appetitus carentis et passionis corporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B04","text":"Ratio purificata cum essentia divina identificatur, ita ut vivere, intelligere et velle non sint accidentia recepta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A11","CH_GGVC_P_11:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B05","text":"Bonitas divina necessario amata creaturas non necessarias ordinat ut participationes, nullo complemento divino ex eis requisito.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_11:A5","CH_GGVC_P_11:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B06","text":"Unus actus effectus producit una cum causis, modis et gradibus boni quibus effectus inter se distinguuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_12:A8","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B07","text":"Filtrum terminale distinguit cognitum a constituto, permissum a volito per se, naturam amatam a defectu repudiato, atque signum temporale a beneplacito aeterno.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AFM-B01","text":"Manifestatio motus et affectus → extractio rationis formalis → remotio imperfectionis → identitas actus divini → bonitas necessario amata → creaturae libere volitae → modi effectuum instituti → bona inaequaliter collata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AFM-B02","text":"Malum cognitum → exclusio rationis exemplaris propriae → negatio volitionis per se → permissio culpae → distinctio naturae et defectus → conservatio amoris entis sine amore peccati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-01","text":"Ager praedicationis divinae reordinatur: proprietas creata non negatur simpliciter nec transfertur univoce, sed ad rationem formalem analogice reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A4","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-02","text":"Motus reclassificatur ab alteratione physica ad interioritatem operationis, ita ut immobilitas cum vita perfectissima componatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A2","CH_GGVC_P_10:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-03","text":"Simplicitas reclassificatur ab uniformitate sterili ad invariantiam productivam quae multiplices relationes et effectus continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-04","text":"Causalitas reclassificatur ut productio effectus cum modo suo, non ut impulsus qui solum existentiam indeterminatam confert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_11:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-05","text":"Bonitas creata ab antecedente motivo amoris divini in effectum amoris causaliter constitutivum convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-06","text":"Malum reclassificatur ut privatio quae distinctiones causales et morales exigit, non ut alterum principium positivo bono oppositum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-07","text":"Signa voluntatis et dilectionis reclassificantur ut mediationes analogicae fallibiles, non ut superficies ex qua decretum aeternum directe legatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX7","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei examinantur vita, voluntas et amor divinus, eorum obiecta, modi, effectus atque relationes ad contingentiam et malum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali unus actus immanens per intellectum, voluntatem et amorem ordinem rerum, causarum, modorum et bonorum constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A11","CH_GGVC_P_11:A11","CH_GGVC_P_12:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico distinctiones formales, modales et causales falsas oppositiones inter immobilitatem et vitam, efficaciam et contingentiam, universalitatem et inaequalitatem dissolvunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas est ordo participationum temporalium ab actu aeterno causatus, in quo esse, modus et bonum simul dependent sed formaliter distinguuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo textus suas theses efficit per reditum distinctionum: obiectio anthropomorphica inducitur, ratio dividitur, imperfectio excluditur et praedicatum restituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FL-01","text":"Transitus ab exteriori signo motus ad praedicationem substantialem vitae theoriam nominationis et essentiae praesupponit quam ipsa series non plene demonstrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FL-02","text":"Libera determinatio unius ordinis creati ab actu simplici et immutabili affirmatur, sed ratio selectionis huius ordinis potius quam alterius non ulterius explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FL-03","text":"Causalitas universalis et defectus moralis cohaerent per distinctionem per se et per accidens, sed commissura inter dependentiam totalem et imputabilitatem creatam manet aperta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FL-04","text":"Regula qua maior dilectio maius bonum efficit potest circularis videri, quia melioritas rei vicissim ex maiori bono divinitus volito mensuratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MP-01","text":"Motus sensum mutat cum ab actu imperfecti ad operationem perfectam immanentem transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A2","CH_GGVC_P_10:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MP-02","text":"Autodeterminatio sensum amplificat cum a dominio executionis, formae et finis ad productionem modorum causalium transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A6","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MP-03","text":"Bonum functionem mutat cum ex fine apprehenso in obiectum necessarium divinae voluntatis atque effectum amoris constitutivi transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_12:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MP-04","text":"Amor invertitur ab affectione provocata a bonitate iam inventa in causalitatem quae bonitatem rei amata producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite apparet ut ordo concentricus cuius centrum est actus simplex et immanens, circum quem rationes intellectae, volita ordinata et bona participata disponuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A12","CH_GGVC_P_11:A11","CH_GGVC_P_12:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum creatum est centrum operativum derivatum: intra se principium proximum actionis habet, sed principia, fines et ipsum modum agendi a causa prima recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A5","CH_GGVC_P_11:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est dispositio effectuum circa fontem aeternum: mutationes, futura bona et eventus contingentes succedunt sine successione actus divini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio rationalis fit per distinctiones inter rationem et modum, causam primam et secundam, actum et signum, naturam et defectum; confusio horum graduum principale periculum est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B01","text":"Identitas actus divini, interioritas vitae, causalitas voluntatis, productio bonitatis per amorem et distinctio mali sufficiunt ad structuram huius gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est nexus inter actum simplicem et productionem diversorum modorum atque bonorum, quia unitatem fontis cum pluralitate ordinata effectuum componit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B03","text":"Minus determinata manent electio ordinis creati non necessarii, commissura inter causalitatem totalem et culpam, atque mensura comparationum particularium dilectionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B04","text":"Systema cohaeret si identitas realis a distinctione rationum, necessitas causae a modo effectus, et amor naturae a repudiatione defectus constanter separantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B05","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat quatenus vitam, voluntatem et amorem non ut tractatus parallelos, sed ut amplificationes unius actus ab immanentia ad causalitatem et bonitatem legit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT9","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171054847305Z_2f5c9f97","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 19–21","source_sha256":"41a7fd5ab7d1f0727978e7ee0bd95ebdff4d20092a0efd6aa473877f71e18e64","sha256":"968125e121e9995a3edaaec9e40fa08f9d761475d4c67b3432c99d33e54787ab","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:10:54.848312+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-01","text":"The system asks how life, will, and love are properly attributed to God without passive motion, need, composition, or mutability, while also explaining the causality of creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-02","text":"The global thesis establishes one simple act as intellectual life, will of the good, and love causally communicating good, distinct in account but identical in reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-03","text":"The argument proceeds from created manifestations to formal accounts, removes imperfections, attributes the purified accounts to God, then restores them as confirmed through causal effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-04","text":"The movement proceeds from the interiority of operation to the voluntary determination of effects, and thence to the production and distribution of goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:A10","CH_GGVC_P_12:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-05","text":"The progression is cumulative and spiral: each attribute retains the prior structure, but transfers it into a greater scope of causality, modality, and goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-06","text":"Differentiation increases from the execution, form, and end of operation to the necessary or contingent modes of effects, and finally to the unequal bestowal of goods.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A6","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-07","text":"Evil constitutes a distributed limit: it is known without a proper exemplary life, permitted without volition per se, and repudiated as a defect without the destruction of the loved nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AS-08","text":"The closure is causally asymmetrical: one invariable act produces a multiplicity of things, modes, and goods, but no created multiplicity returns to composition or change in the source.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A11","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A predicate of perfection is attributed to God according to a purified formal account, not according to the bodily, passive, or defective mode in which it is manifested in creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A4","CH_GGVC_P_12:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] To be, to live, to understand, and to will constitute in God one real act, to which love, as the first inclination of the will toward the good, belongs inseparably.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A11","CH_GGVC_P_11:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Perfection is first measured as the interiority of the principles of operation, then as the power of effecting the very mode in which an effect acts or occurs.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A6","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Divine goodness is the necessary object of the divine will, while non-necessary creatures are willed as participations in it without any increase of divine perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_11:A5","CH_GGVC_P_11:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] The unity of the divine act is compatible with multiple intentional termini, effects, and degrees of good, because objective plurality does not multiply the act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Divine causality establishes not only the being of effects, but also the order of secondary causes and the necessary or contingent mode of events.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A13","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_11:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] The causal relation between God and creature is asymmetrical: the creature receives being and good from God, whereas God is neither moved nor perfected by an external object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] The necessity and immutability of the first act do not entail the absolute necessity of effects, but can include contingency as a positively intended mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Divine love is universal according to the bestowal of being, but unequal according to the magnitude of the good willed for each thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:A7","CH_GGVC_P_12:D3","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Evil is not a positive account of divine life, will, or love, but a known privation, permitted fault, or defect distinct from the loved nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Distinctions among modes of being, necessities, causalities, objects, and signs preserve divine unity from being contracted into semantic or modal uniformity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:D9","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] The supreme immanence of the divine act constitutes not sterility but maximal causally ordered fecundity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_11:A4","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] The accounts of things, as understood, pertain to divine life; as willed, they are determined in being; and as loved, they receive goodness, without dividing this process into three real acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:D8","CH_GGVC_P_11:D5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-01","text":"Motion does not return identically: it is transferred from the change of the imperfect to perfect immanent act, then excluded from love insofar as it signifies receptive passion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-02","text":"Self-determination is amplified from the interiority of execution, form, and end to causality producing the very mode of the effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A6","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-03","text":"Intellect retains structural identity but changes function: it first defines the degree of life, and later grounds will and the order of causal determinations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A8","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-04","text":"The good migrates from the end of operation to the principal object of will, and finally to the effect that divine love confers upon things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-05","text":"Simplicity returns steadily, but orders increasing plurality: first the identity of attributes, then the plurality of things willed, and finally the inequality of goods.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-06","text":"Necessity reverses its apparent force: what first seems to oppose freedom and contingency becomes the foundation of the infallible production of contingent modes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-07","text":"Participation is transferred from conformity to the exemplar to the order of what is willed, and thence to the causally bestowed good, while the creature's dependence on the divine source remains.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A16","CH_GGVC_P_11:A5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RMD-08","text":"Evil is transformed through cumulative negation: it lacks a proper exemplary account, is excluded from the object of will per se, and is separated as a defect from the loved nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-01","text":"The gradation of plants, animals, and intellects remains a local apparatus; at this level it is absorbed into the general rule by which perfection increases according to the interiority of the principles of action.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A7","CH_GGVC_P_10:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-02","text":"The division of operation, permission, command, prohibition, and counsel locally orders the semantics of will, but globally is subordinated to the distinction between divine act and temporal signs.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:D13","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-03","text":"Particular comparisons among Christ, angels, human beings, and the predestined do not rise as axioms; they remain local proofs of the rule of the good willed according to order and time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:D9","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-04","text":"The definition of life through immanent act is amplified upward, because the same interiority supports the real identity of intellect and will and the impassibility of love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A9","CH_GGVC_P_11:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-05","text":"The connection at the present level is not a mere succession of three attributes: intellect grounds will, will bears love, and love explains the causality of will as the production of good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1","CH_GGVC_P_12:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-06","text":"The greater transition occurs when divine interiority is converted from a state of intrinsic perfection into a principle of the extrinsic order of effects, with no intrinsic change intervening.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:A10","CH_GGVC_P_12:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:CGD-07","text":"Local images of motion, appetite, and affection become obsolete insofar as they are taken univocally, but, formally recodified, they become instruments of analogical attribution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-01","text":"God does not live, will, or love through bodily change, sensitive passion, or transition from potency to act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-02","text":"No external good determines, perfects, or attracts God to act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-03","text":"Predicates of creatures are not transferred univocally to God according to a material, temporal, or receptive mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-04","text":"The plurality of attributes, things willed, and goods does not constitute a plurality of acts or composition in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-05","text":"The efficacy of the first cause does not absorb the difference between the necessary and the contingent, nor the reality of secondary causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-06","text":"Evil is not admitted as a positive being, a proper exemplar, or an object equal to divine knowledge, will, and love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_12:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:GNX-07","text":"Normative, historical, or affective signs are not a transparent transcription of eternal good pleasure or an exhaustive measure of divine love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX7","CH_GGVC_P_12:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that a visible property sufficiently defines a thing; otherwise the transition from created motion, appetite, and affection to the divine formal account would be impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that secondary causality is true only if it is independent of the first cause; dependence here establishes the very mode of its proper action.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that the simplicity of the cause requires uniformity of termini, effects, or goods.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that freedom necessarily includes passive potency, change of counsel, or the capacity to sin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that the goodness of the creature precedes divine love as a determining cause; created goodness is rather the effect of the good willed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that to be known, willed, and loved constitutes the same formal state of a thing, because knowledge, will, and love express diverse intentional relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_11:D15","CH_GGVC_P_12:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSA-01","text":"The system admits no higher measure by which the divine act may be judged according to created modes of motion, necessity, or love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_12:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSA-02","text":"The possibility of a symmetrical relation between God and creature is inadmissible, because the creature neither completes nor reconfigures the source.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSA-03","text":"Created intelligibility, goodness, and agency cannot constitute an ultimate principle independent in its own right; their proper operation subsists within causally given dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSA-04","text":"The eternal act is not fully transparent in the succession of effects, commands, permissions, or temporal signs of love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-01","text":"Intellectual life, will, and love constitute a formal series: intelligible act apprehends the good, will inclines toward it, and love includes in its account the good willed for another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A12","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1","CL_GGVC_07:GA-02","CL_GGVC_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-02","text":"The same creature is ordered by a threefold relation: as understood, it pertains to divine life; as willed, it is causally produced; and as loved, it receives being and goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:D8","CH_GGVC_P_11:D5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D2","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","CL_GGVC_07:GA-09","CL_GGVC_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-03","text":"Creation is not God's exit from his own immanence, but the external effect of an act that remains intrinsically perfect, immobile, and invariable.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:D6","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_12:D4","CL_GGVC_07:GA-02","CL_GGVC_07:GA-07","CL_GGVC_07:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-04","text":"Created agency is real insofar as the creature moves itself to operation, but that very operative autonomy is a mode established under the order of universal causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A1","CH_GGVC_P_11:D7","CL_GGVC_07:GA-03","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-05","text":"Contingency is not a residue of divine impotence, but a form of effect that the immutable cause efficaciously produces without conversion into absolute necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","CL_GGVC_07:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-06","text":"The negation of evil delimits the positive system through three units: evil cannot be exemplary life, an object willed per se, or a good produced by love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD3","CL_GGVC_07:GA-10","CL_GGVC_07:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:XD-07","text":"Divine freedom consists in a non-necessary relation to creatures under necessary adherence to goodness, not in mutability or the possibility of evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX14","CL_GGVC_07:GA-04","CL_GGVC_07:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-01","text":"The emerging ontology is an ontology of modally ordered participation: the being, operation, and good of the creature are proper to it, but are not their own ultimate principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A16","CH_GGVC_P_11:A5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D3","CL_GGVC_07:GA-03","CL_GGVC_07:GA-07","CL_GGVC_07:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-02","text":"First causality is prior not only to the effect, but to the very modal distinction between necessary and contingent event.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A13","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","CL_GGVC_07:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-03","text":"Time belongs to the order of effects and bestowed goods, not to a succession of understanding, willing, or loving in the divine cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13","CL_GGVC_07:GA-02","CL_GGVC_07:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-04","text":"The created subject becomes a dependent agent: it truly operates from itself according to its proper principles, although those principles, ends, and modes are ordered by the first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A5","CH_GGVC_P_11:A12","CL_GGVC_07:GA-03","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-05","text":"Human knowledge from temporal effects cannot simply reconstruct the eternal decree or the degree of love, because sign and good pleasure, present state and future good, do not coincide.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX7","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13","CL_GGVC_07:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-06","text":"The moral order does not require evil as a positive principle: nature and agency subsist from the good, while a morally imputable defect emerges within dependent operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD3","CL_GGVC_07:GA-06","CL_GGVC_07:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:BSD-07","text":"The global method joins analogical attribution and causal inversion: the formal account is separated from imperfection, then posited in God not as an effect but as the principle of created perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1","CL_GGVC_07:GA-01","CL_GGVC_07:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-01","text":"The circuit of attribution is: created manifestation → extraction of formal account → removal of imperfection → divine attribution → reinterpretation of manifestation as effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-02","text":"The interiority of the divine act increases communicability; communication produces effects; effects, however, are led back to the source without a regress of change into the source.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:A4","CH_GGVC_P_12:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-03","text":"Understanding → apprehended good → willing → loving → created good constitutes the path of amplification by which immanent act is unfolded into a causally fruitful order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A1","CH_GGVC_P_12:A1","CH_GGVC_P_12:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-04","text":"Simplicity → plurality of termini → diversity of modes → inequality of goods → return to one act constitutes the principal circuit of the created order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_11:D9","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-05","text":"Immutability, which first seems to exclude contingency, causally establishes it; contingency thus returns to the efficacy of the cause rather than to its defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-06","text":"Evil does not complete the positive circuit, but as a recursive limit distinguishes knowledge from constitution, permission from volition, and nature from defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:RLE-07","text":"The attractor of the whole structure is a simple, immanent, and invariable act which, precisely because it is determined by nothing external, efficaciously determines a multiple order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:A11","CH_GGVC_P_12:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B01","text":"Created manifestations of motion, appetite, and love provide the initial material, but do not yet constitute the divine account.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B02","text":"From manifestation a formal account is extracted: operation from itself, intellectual inclination toward the good, and willing good for another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A1","CH_GGVC_P_11:A1","CH_GGVC_P_12:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B03","text":"The formal account is purified by the subtraction of imperfect change, deficient appetite, and bodily passion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B04","text":"The purified account is identified with the divine essence, so that living, understanding, and willing are not received accidents.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A11","CH_GGVC_P_11:A2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B05","text":"Divine goodness, necessarily loved, orders non-necessary creatures as participations, with no divine completion from them required.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_11:A5","CH_GGVC_P_11:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B06","text":"One act produces effects together with the causes, modes, and degrees of good by which effects are distinguished from one another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_12:A8","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FGS-B07","text":"The terminal filter distinguishes what is known from what is constituted, what is permitted from what is willed per se, the loved nature from the repudiated defect, and the temporal sign from eternal good pleasure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AFM-B01","text":"Manifestation of motion and affection → extraction of formal account → removal of imperfection → identity of divine act → necessarily loved goodness → freely willed creatures → instituted modes of effects → unequally bestowed goods.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:AFM-B02","text":"Known evil → exclusion of a proper exemplary account → negation of volition per se → permission of fault → distinction of nature and defect → preservation of love for being without love of sin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A17","CH_GGVC_P_11:NX13","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-01","text":"The field of divine predication is reordered: a created property is neither simply denied nor transferred univocally, but is analogically reduced to a formal account.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A4","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-02","text":"Motion is reclassified from physical alteration to the interiority of operation, so that immobility is combined with most perfect life.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A2","CH_GGVC_P_10:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-03","text":"Simplicity is reclassified from sterile uniformity to productive invariance containing multiple relations and effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-04","text":"Causality is reclassified as the production of an effect together with its mode, not as an impulse conferring only indeterminate existence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A14","CH_GGVC_P_11:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-05","text":"Created goodness is converted from an antecedent motive of divine love into a causally constitutive effect of love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-06","text":"Evil is reclassified as a privation requiring causal and moral distinctions, not as another principle opposed to positive good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MME-07","text":"Signs of will and love are reclassified as fallible analogical mediations, not as a surface from which the eternal decree is directly read.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX7","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B01","text":"At the level of the surface, divine life, will, and love are examined, together with their objects, modes, effects, and relations to contingency and evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_11:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, one immanent act through intellect, will, and love constitutes the order of things, causes, modes, and goods.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A11","CH_GGVC_P_11:A11","CH_GGVC_P_12:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, formal, modal, and causal distinctions dissolve false oppositions between immobility and life, efficacy and contingency, universality and inequality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, reality is an order of temporal participations caused by the eternal act, in which being, mode, and good depend together but are formally distinct.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A10","CH_GGVC_P_11:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the text effects its theses through the return of distinctions: an anthropomorphic objection is introduced, the account is divided, imperfection is excluded, and the predicate is restored.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FL-01","text":"The transition from the external sign of motion to the substantial predication of life presupposes a theory of naming and essence that the series itself does not fully demonstrate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_10:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FL-02","text":"The free determination of one created order by a simple and immutable act is affirmed, but the reason for the selection of this order rather than another is not further explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FL-03","text":"Universal causality and moral defect cohere through the distinction of per se and per accidens, but the joint between total dependence and created imputability remains open.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_11:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:FL-04","text":"The rule that greater love effects a greater good can appear circular, because the superiority of a thing is in turn measured by the greater good divinely willed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_12:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MP-01","text":"Motion changes meaning when it is transferred from the act of the imperfect to perfect immanent operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A2","CH_GGVC_P_10:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MP-02","text":"Self-determination expands in meaning when it passes from mastery of execution, form, and end to the production of causal modes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A6","CH_GGVC_P_11:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MP-03","text":"The good changes function when it passes from the apprehended end into the necessary object of the divine will and the effect of constitutive love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:A3","CH_GGVC_P_12:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MP-04","text":"Love is inverted from an affection provoked by goodness already found into a causality that produces the goodness of the loved thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_12:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as a concentric order whose center is a simple and immanent act, around which understood accounts, ordered things willed, and participated goods are arranged.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A12","CH_GGVC_P_11:A11","CH_GGVC_P_12:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:HSI-02","text":"The created subject is a derived operative center: it has within itself the proximate principle of action, but receives its principles, ends, and the very mode of acting from the first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:A5","CH_GGVC_P_11:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:HSI-03","text":"Time is the disposition of effects around the eternal source: changes, future goods, and contingent events succeed one another without succession in the divine act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_12:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:HSI-04","text":"Rational navigation occurs through distinctions between account and mode, first and secondary cause, act and sign, nature and defect; confusion of these levels is the principal danger.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_12:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B01","text":"The identity of divine act, the interiority of life, the causality of will, the production of goodness through love, and the distinction of evil suffice to restore the structure of this cluster.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the nexus between simple act and the production of diverse modes and goods, because it combines the unity of the source with the ordered plurality of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B03","text":"Less determined remain the selection of the non-necessary created order, the joint between total causality and fault, and the measure of particular comparisons of love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B04","text":"The system coheres if real identity is constantly separated from distinction of accounts, the necessity of the cause from the mode of the effect, and love of nature from repudiation of defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_07:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement insofar as it reads life, will, and love not as parallel treatises, but as amplifications of one act from immanence to causality and goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_10:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_11:MRT9","CH_GGVC_P_12:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_07@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_07:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 19–21","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 18 · Prima pars · Quaestio 19 · Prima pars · Quaestio 20"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 22–24","order":8,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_13","CH_GGVC_P_14","CH_GGVC_P_15"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_08@R001","sha256":"2a9c42afa6f44df79bb57b2d3633f692ab565124e6cc22a66152611cc7550c02","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo attributa divina ordinem moralem, cosmicum et salutarem constituant, salva simul transcendentia Dei, contingentia creaturarum, libertate rationali et iustitia distributionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis statuit unicam causalitatem divinam sapientem et bonam omnia ordinare, sed modos effectuum, causalitatem secundam atque asymmetriam inter bonum causatum et culpam permissam conservare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_14:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio reconstructiva et metaphysica praedicata primo a modis creaturalibus purgat, deinde rationes eorum causales ad structuram ordinis divini transfert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-04","text":"Motus incipit ab attributionibus moralibus, transit ad providentiam ut rationem universalem ordinis, atque terminatur in praedestinatione ut applicatione speciali ad finem supernaturalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_14:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-05","text":"Directio systematis progreditur a misericordia fundante debitum ad creationem ordinis, ab ordine ad providentiam universalem, et a providentia ad transmissionem rationalium ultra proportionem naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_14:A2","CH_GGVC_P_15:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-06","text":"Motus verus est recursivus et cumulativus: ratio aeterna redit in exsecutionem temporalem, causalitas prima in causalitates secundas, certitudo finis in modos contingentes quibus finis efficitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-07","text":"Amplificatio fit spiraliter, quia misericordia primo omnem iustitiam ontologice praesupponit, providentia deinde totum ens complectitur, praedestinatio denique eandem structuram circa salutem contrahit et intendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A10","CH_GGVC_P_15:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est duplex: genera ordinis, causalitatis et modalitatis per bonitatem explicantur, sed distributio singularis electionis regressum terminat in voluntate divina sine ratione ulteriori expressa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A16","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Sapientia, bonitas et voluntas divina constituunt principium immanens quo actio Dei ordinatur, nullo iure, lege vel fine extrinseco mensurata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A2","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Deus producit non solum entia, sed etiam ordinem, fines, proportiones et modos causalitatis quibus entia suam perfectionem participant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A2","CH_GGVC_P_14:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Ratio ordinis aeternaliter in Deo manet, dum eius exsecutio temporaliter in creaturis et per creaturas procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Iustitia divina non aequalitatem reciprocationis constituit, sed proportionem qua unicuique conveniunt natura, dignitas, ordo et finis a Deo instituti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A3","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] Misericordia est causaliter prior debito creato, quia donum primum constituit ipsum campum in quo iustitia, meritum et retributio postea intelliguntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A10","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Extensio providentiae aequatur extensioni causalitatis primae; ideo nullum ens, singulare vel actus liber ab ordine divino simpliciter excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A3","CH_GGVC_P_14:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Causalitas prima causalitatem secundam non evacuat, sed eam communicat et ordinat tamquam dignitatem creaturae atque medium exsecutionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Necessitas, contingentia et libertas sunt modi effectuum a providentia dispositi, non limites exteriores qui certitudinem ordinis infringant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A11","CH_GGVC_P_15:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Defectus non est principium positivum autonomum: vel per communicationem perfectionis removetur, vel propter bonum universalius permittitur, vel ut culpa causae secundae imputatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Praedestinatio est contractio specialis providentiae circa creaturam rationalem ad finem supernaturalem sola natura inattingibilem ordinandam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Totus ordo salutis a dilectione divina procedit, sed gratiam, usum liberi arbitrii, meritum et gloriam ut effectus internos causaliter ordinatos continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] Reprobatio est providentia defectum a fine permittens et poenam ordinans, non causa culpae eodem modo quo praedestinatio est causa gratiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A11","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","text":"[Persistent] Infallibilitas divina comprehendit simul eventum et modum eveniendi; necessitas finis est conditionata ex ordine posito, non absoluta ex natura causarum proximarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A12","CH_GGVC_P_15:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Inaequalitas gratuitorum non est iniusta ubi debitum antecedens non violatur, quamvis assignatio singularis bonorum regressum explicativum in simplici voluntate terminet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A17","CH_GGVC_P_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-15","text":"[Emergent] Preces, opera et merita valent ut causae secundae exsecutionis, non ut principia quae decretum aeternum constituant, mutent vel corrigant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A18","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-01","text":"Ordo redit functionaliter: primo est proportio sapientiae in rebus, deinde ratio providentiae omnium, denique ordinatio selectorum ad salutem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A5","CH_GGVC_P_14:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-02","text":"Iustitia identitatem ordinativam retinet, sed a distributione perfectionum naturalium ad ordinem poenae et differentiam salutarem sub misericordia transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-03","text":"Misericordia mutatur ab universali communicatione perfectionis in formam specialem qua gratia et gloria aliquibus causaliter conferuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-04","text":"Defectus migrat per tres campos: privatio misericorditer removenda, imperfectio cosmologica propter totum permittenda, casus voluntarius sub reprobatione imputandus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-05","text":"Conformitas effectus ad intellectum divinum, primo veritas causalis appellata, in providentia absorbetur ut relatio inter rationem aeternam et exsecutionem ordinatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A6","CH_GGVC_P_14:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-06","text":"Libertas ex obiecto apparentis exclusionis mutatur in proprium modum causae secundae, cuius actus simul causatur, contingenter procedit et imputabilis manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A9","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-07","text":"Certitudo amplificatur: ab ordine voluntatis secundum sapientiam transit ad infallibilitatem providentiae atque ad necessitatem conditionatam salutis electorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-08","text":"Debitum naturale, quod ex ordine creato sequitur, cedit coram fine supernaturali ubi nulla exigentia naturae donationem gratiae antecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-09","text":"Distinctio aeterni et temporalis persistit, sed a providentia generali ad totam seriem vocationis, gratiae, liberi actus, meriti et gloriae extenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-10","text":"Veritas ut nomen explicitum iustitiae post primam unitatem evanescit, opere tamen suo functa manet in exigentia ut effectus rationi divinae et modo proviso respondeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:D3","CH_GGVC_P_14:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-01","text":"Veritas ut denominatio propria iustitiae divinae manet mechanismus localis; ad gradum praesentem eius functio sub conformitate effectus ad ordinem providentialem absorbetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:D3","CH_GGVC_P_13:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-02","text":"Casus et fortuna manent vocabula localia cosmologiae providentiae; sursum persistit sola regula generalis quod exterioritas ad causam particularem non sit exterioritas ad causam universalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_14:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-03","text":"Numerus materialiter definitus electorum et occultatio propriae praedestinationis sunt determinationes locales doctrinae salutis, non axiomata totius ordinis creati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A14","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-04","text":"Dependentia debiti ab ordine divino sursum amplificatur in principium quo absentia debiti supernaturalis gratuitatem et inaequalitatem gratiae tuetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-05","text":"Providentia universalis fungitur commissura inter architecturam iustitiae et ordinem praedestinationis, quia speciale salutis decretum intra rationem omnium finium constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-06","text":"Distinctio causae primae et causarum secundarum unitates coniungit, quia eodem schemate explicantur gubernatio, libertas, meritum, preces et exsecutio salutis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-07","text":"Remotio defectus fit misericordiae mechanismus inferior; permissio defectus et imputatio culpae efficiunt transitionem ad structuram superiorem in qua bonitas, iustitia et libertas simul ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-08","text":"Oppositiones inter iustitiam et misericordiam, providentiam et contingentiam, gratiam et libertatem obsolescunt ut oppositiones unius plani atque recodificantur ut relationes ordinum causalium distinctorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_15:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-01","text":"Systema excludit legem, debitum vel ius creatum quod voluntatem divinam antecedat et Deum quasi agentem sub superiore mensura obliget.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_13:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-02","text":"Attributa divina excludunt passionem, indigentiam et virtutem civilem univoce translatam; retinentur tantum rationes perfectivae, causales et ordinativae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_13:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-03","text":"Nullus casus absolutus neque exterioritas ontologica ad providentiam admittitur, quia omnis particularitas intra causalitatem universalem continetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-04","text":"Causalitas divina et creata non sunt causae rivales quarum incrementum alterius actionem minuat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_15:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-05","text":"Infallibilitas non imponit necessitatem uniformem neque libertas requirit exclusionem a certitudine ordinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-06","text":"Malum non est principium positivum autonomum, nec Deus eodem modo causa culpae ponitur quo causa boni salutaris est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-07","text":"Misericordia et iustitia non sunt potestates rivales: donum supra debitum non destruit ordinem, sed eius radicem gratuitam manifestat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_13:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-08","text":"Meritum, oratio et opus temporale neque electionem antecedenter causant neque decretum aeternum retroactive mutant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:D4","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet ordinem creatum posse se ipsum fundare, quia ens, finis, debitum et modus causalitatis ad bonitatem et sapientiam primam resolvuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_14:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet libertatem consistere in independentia a causa prima; aliter tota conservatio causalitatis secundae sub providentia corrueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_15:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet mensuram meriti, aequalitatis vel iuris distributionem gratuitorum antecedere; talis mensura simplicem prioritatem donationis everteret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet mundum defectu omnino carentem unicam normam bonitatis divinae constituere, quia bonum universi permissionem aliquorum defectuum complectitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet salutem et perditionem symmetricam causalitatem habere: bonum salutare ad causam primam totaliter reducitur, culpa autem defectui voluntatis creatae imputatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet causam temporalem actum aeternum constituere vel mutare; efficientia temporalis valet solum intra ordinem exsecutionis iam positum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_15:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-07","text":"Falsum esse oportet voluntatem antecedentem salutis universalis idem esse ac decretum consequens salutis omnium, quia reprobatio ut permissio defectus manere debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-08","text":"Falsum esse oportet naturam rationalem ex se ius vel sufficientiam ad visionem divinam habere; aliter praedestinatio ut transmissio gratuita supervacua fieret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-01","text":"Possibilitas altissima exclusa est locus ontologicus extra ordinem divinum, ex quo causalitas, iustitia vel eventus sine relatione ad primum principium aestimari possent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_14:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-02","text":"Nulla causalitas secunda neutralis relinquitur quae ordinem causae primae impedire, corrigere aut simpliciter effugere possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_14:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-03","text":"Abest mensura ulterior per quam identitas singularis electi vel reprobati demonstrari possit; systema hanc quaestionem ad simplicem voluntatem terminat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A16","CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-04","text":"Creaturae indisponibilis est prospectus certus sui status aeterni, quamvis ordo singularis apud Deum materialiter definitus ponatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-05","text":"Ontologice inadmissibilis est symmetria qua bonitas et culpa ex Deo eodem genere causalitatis procederent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-01","text":"Providentia est exsecutio universalis architecturae iustitiae cuius ipsum debitum misericordia gratuita antecedenter constituit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-04","CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_14:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-02","text":"Causalitas creata est simul effectus causalitatis primae et dignitas participata; ideo actio creaturae auget manifestationem providentiae potius quam eius ambitum minuit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-06","CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_14:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_14:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-03","text":"Cum certitudo providentialis modum effectus includat, praedestinatio potest infallibiliter salutem producere per actus qui secundum causas proximas liberi et contingentes manent.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","CL_GGVC_08:GA-11","CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","CH_GGVC_P_14:A12","CH_GGVC_P_15:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-04","text":"Misericordia quae defectum removet et providentia quae defectum permittit non simpliciter contradicunt, sed diversas relationes boni particularis ad ordinem universaliorem exprimunt.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CL_GGVC_08:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-05","text":"Poena intra opus divinum iustum et misericordia fundatum ordinari potest, quamvis culpa quae poenam exigit non divinae causalitati symmetrice attribuatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CL_GGVC_08:GA-09","CL_GGVC_08:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_13:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-06","text":"Quia finis supernaturalis facultatem naturae excedit et Deus creaturae debitor non est, collatio gratiae inaequalis iniustitiam ex debito violato constituere nequit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CL_GGVC_08:GA-10","CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","CH_GGVC_P_13:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-07","text":"Distinctio rationis aeternae ab exsecutione temporali efficit ut preces et opera sint causaliter efficacia sine mutatione decreti.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CL_GGVC_08:GA-15","CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-08","text":"Veritas causalis effectus ampliatur in veritatem historicam ordinis: eventus rationi divinae respondet non solum quia fit, sed quia modo proviso fit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","CH_GGVC_P_13:A6","CH_GGVC_P_14:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-09","text":"Praedestinatio providentiam non suspendit, sed eius universalitatem circa obiectum capax finis supernaturalis specialiter contrahit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-06","CL_GGVC_08:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_15:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-10","text":"Sapientia actionem divinam globaliter ordinat, sed non praebet rationem discursivam identitatis singulorum electorum; intelligibilitas structurae igitur cum clausura voluntatis singularis coexsistit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-01","CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","CH_GGVC_P_13:A2","CH_GGVC_P_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-01","text":"Realitas emergit ut ordo causalitatum inclusarum, in quo universale particulare continet sine proprietatibus et modis particularium abolendis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-02","CL_GGVC_08:GA-06","CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_14:A4","CH_GGVC_P_14:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-02","text":"Tempus non constituit novitatem in Deo, sed est extensio exsecutiva rationis aeternae per series creatas, contingentes et causaliter ordinatas.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-03","text":"Subiectum rationale fit causa secunda causata, vere agens et imputabilis, sed cognitione directa sui loci in ordine aeterno carens.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","CL_GGVC_08:GA-15","CH_GGVC_P_14:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-04","text":"Iustitia distributiva reordinatur: proportio naturae regit debita constituta, sed aequalitas antecedens non regit dona quae naturam excedunt.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-04","CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","CH_GGVC_P_13:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-05","text":"Malum fit defectus localis intra ordinem boni, sed transitus a permissione cosmologica ad derelictionem salvificam auget difficultatem causalitatis et imputabilitatis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-09","CL_GGVC_08:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_14:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-06","text":"Methodus systematis oppositiones non componit per medium indistinctum, sed terminos in diversos gradus causalitatis, modalitatis et exsecutionis relocat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_14:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_15:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-07","text":"Certitudo finis actionem temporalem non evacuat, sed necessitatem agendi per media ordinata auget, quia ipsa media ad certum effectum pertinent.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-11","CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","CL_GGVC_08:GA-15","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-08","text":"Systema genera diversitatis per bonitatem explicat, sed singularia electionis non ulterius deducit; plenitudo architectonica igitur cum indigentia rationis distributivae singularis cohaeret.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-01","CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus gratuitatis est: donum primum constituit naturam et finem, natura et finis constituunt debitum, debitum iustitiam, iustitia autem ad donum prius resolvitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A10","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-02","text":"Circuitus manifestationis est: sapientia ordinat effectus, effectus ordinem servant, ordo iustitiam gubernantis manifestat atque ad sapientiam ut regulam redit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A2","CH_GGVC_P_13:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-03","text":"Circuitus modalitatis est: providentia causas diversorum modorum praeparat, causae effectus secundum proprios modos producunt, effectus ita certitudinem providentiae complent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A11","CH_GGVC_P_14:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-04","text":"Via defectus procedit a permissione particularis mali ad conservationem boni universalioris, quod vicissim permissionem intra ordinem providentialem reponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_14:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-05","text":"Circuitus praedestinationis procedit a dilectione ad gratiam, a gratia ad actum liberum et meritum, a merito ad gloriam, quae ordinem aeternum explet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-06","text":"Oratio efficaciam recipit ab ordine quem implere dicitur: decretum media praeordinat, media effectum producunt, effectus certitudinem decreti manifestat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A18","CH_GGVC_P_15:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-07","text":"Bonitas divina est attractor qui misericordiam, iustitiam, diversitatem effectuum et unitatem principii in unam causalitatem formaliter multiplicem contrahit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-08","text":"Via amplificationis transit ab ordine cuiuslibet operis ad providentiam cuiuslibet entis, deinde ad ordinationem specialem rationalium ad salutem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-09","text":"Reprobatio est attractor instabilis: permissio defectus, causalitas derelictionis, libertas culpae et iustitia poenae in eo conveniunt sine plena reductione ad unum genus causalitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A11","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B01","text":"Praedicatum creaturale → remotio passionis et limitationis → retentio perfectionis causalis et ordinativae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_13:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B02","text":"Sapientia et bonitas immanentes → voluntas sibi non extrinsece regulata → actio divina ordinata potius quam arbitraria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A2","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B03","text":"Productio entium → constitutio naturarum, finium et proportionum → ortus debiti creati → iustitia distributiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_13:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B04","text":"Universalitas causalitatis primae → universalitas ordinationis ad finem → providentia omnium entium et eventuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A3","CH_GGVC_P_14:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B05","text":"Communicatio causalitatis → exsecutio per causas secundas → diversitas modorum necessarii, contingentis et liberi sub certitudine una.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B06","text":"Finis naturam excedens → insufficientia facultatis creatae → ordinatio divina specialis → praedestinatio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B07","text":"Permissio casus a fine → derelictio et ordinatio poenae → reprobatio sine causatione symmetrica culpae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A11","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B08","text":"Decretum aeternum → ordinatio precum, operum et meritorum → exsecutio temporalis → effectus certus per media contingentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A18","CH_GGVC_P_15:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B09","text":"Diversitas effectuum → manifestatio misericordiae et iustitiae → ratio communis in bonitate → terminus singularis in voluntate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A15","CH_GGVC_P_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:AFM-B01","text":"Depuratio praedicatorum → principium immanens sapientiae et bonitatis → constitutio ordinis et debiti → providentia universalis → exsecutio per causas secundas → ordinatio supernaturalis → praedestinatio et reprobatio asymmetrica → clausura in bonitate et voluntate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:AFM-B02","text":"Certitudo ordinis → praeparatio diversarum causarum → effectus secundum modos necessarios, contingentes et liberos → necessitas conditionata finis sine necessitatione absoluta actuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:AFM-B03","text":"Defectus ut privatio → misericordia removens vel providentia permittens → culpa causae secundae → poena ordinata → asymmetria terminalis inter salutem causatam et perditionem permissam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-01","text":"Praedicata moralia reclassificantur ex habitibus vel passionibus subiecti in rationes causales quibus Deus perfectionem communicat et ordinem instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_13:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-02","text":"Debitum desinit esse mensura Deo antecedens et fit relatio interna naturae, finis et ordinis a voluntate divina constitutorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:D2","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-03","text":"Casus reclassificatur ex eventu simpliciter inordinato in defectum coordinationis respectu causae particularis intra ordinem universalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_14:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-04","text":"Oppositio inter causalitatem divinam et creatam corruit, quia immediatio rationis et mediatio exsecutionis ad diversos ordines pertinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_15:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-05","text":"Necessitas et contingentia non amplius describunt praesentiam vel absentiam providentiae, sed diversos modos eiusdem ordinis efficiendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_15:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-06","text":"Malum dividitur in defectum permissum, culpam imputabilem, derelictionem et poenam, ita ut nulla unica causalitas positiva omnibus membris attribuatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_15:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-07","text":"Iustitia gratuitorum separatur ab aequalitate distributiva antecedente: ratio communis diversitatis ex bonitate sumitur, sed collatio singularis debitum non sequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A17","CH_GGVC_P_15:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-08","text":"Preces et opera transferuntur ex alternativa inter mutare decretum et esse superflua in media interna quibus decretum temporaliter impletur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:ME8","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei tractantur iustitia, misericordia, providentia, contingentia, libertas, praedestinatio, reprobatio et media salutis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_14:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali agunt causalitas universalis, rationes finium, proportiones debiti, causae secundae, permissio defectus atque distributio modorum effectuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_15:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico oppositiones solvuntur non per abolitionem alterius termini, sed per distinctionem ordinum in quibus uterque diversam functionem recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_15:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas est exsecutio temporalis rationis aeternae, cuius effectus modos necessarios, contingentes et liberos vere servant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_15:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo textus ipsas oppositiones quas tractat recursiva distinctione redistribuit, ita ut forma argumentationis ordinem hierarchicum quem affirmat efficiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_13:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-01","text":"Sapientia voluntatem divinam globaliter ordinat, sed electio singularis nullam rationem ulteriorem praeter voluntatem recipit; nexus inter rationalitatem universalem et assignationem individualem incompletus manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-02","text":"Misericordia defectum removet, providentia defectum propter totum permittit, reprobatio casum a fine permittit; criteria transitus inter remotionem et permissionem non plene explicantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-03","text":"Compatibilitas infallibilitatis et libertatis per distinctionem modorum causalium stabilitur, sed mechanismus interior quo certitudo causae primae actum contingentem non necessitet ulterius non demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-04","text":"Reprobatio causaliter derelictionem et poenam ordinat, dum culpa soli arbitrio creato imputatur; haec commissura asymmetriam requirit sed eius medium causale fragile relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-05","text":"Permissio mali ex praelatione boni universi pendet, sed analogia inter diversitatem cosmicam et distributionem salutis identitates singulares non demonstrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-06","text":"Iustitia primo proportionem unicuique convenientem significat, postea vero inaequalitatem gratuitorum tuetur per absentiam debiti; continuitas pendet ex distinctione inter naturam debitam et donum supernaturale.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-01","text":"Iustitia mutatur ab aequalitate inter agentes in architecturam teleologicam secundum quam effectus esse, proportionem et finem recipiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-02","text":"Misericordia mutatur ab efficacia ontologica universali removendi defectum in rationem specialem gratiae qua diversitas salutaris bonitatem manifestat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-03","text":"Providentia mutatur ab universali ratione ordinis in praedestinationem cum idem schema ad finem supernaturalem et ad aliquos rationales contrahitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-04","text":"Defectus mutatur a privatione simpliciter removenda in eventum permissum atque, in campo morali, in culpam causae secundae imputabilem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-05","text":"Libertas mutatur ab apparentia exterioritatis ad providentiam in modum contingentem causalitatis secundae intra providentiam constitutae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:D4","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-06","text":"Certitudo mutatur ab immobilitate rationis divinae in necessitatem conditionatam quae eventum et modum eventus simul complectitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A12","CH_GGVC_P_15:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite est architectura causalitatum inclusarum, cuius ratio aeternaliter immobilis per ramos temporales et transeuntes se exsequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum est causa secunda causata: recipit virtutem agendi, proprium modum contingentem servat et propter actum suum imputabilitatem suscipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est campus exsecutionis, non locus in quo decretum divinum deliberando formatur aut mutationem recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio possibilis non est fuga extra ordinem, sed actio intra eum per preces, opera, libertatem et meritum tamquam media vere causalia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_15:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-05","text":"Machina duplicem tractum defectus gerit: perfectionem misericorditer communicat, defectus particulares propter totum permittit, et casum moralem per reprobationem sine culpae causatione ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de sapientia immanente, dono fundante debitum, providentia universali, causis secundis, modalitate effectuum et speciali ordine salutis sufficiunt ad structuram principalem huius gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est distinctio inter rationem ordinis immediate in Deo existentem et exsecutionem temporalem per causas secundas, quia plures oppositiones eodem actu componit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum satis determinantur mechanismus interior libertatis sub causalitate prima, ratio singularis electionis et commissura inter derelictionem divinam atque culpam creatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B04","text":"Systema hac magnitudine cohaeret si causalitas prima et secunda non competitive accipiuntur, iustitia non ut limitatio Dei intelligitur, et contingentia ut modus provisus retinetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_13:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B05","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat reducendo distinctiones ad providentiam et inclusionem causarum secundarum; reductioni tamen resistit terminus voluntatis simplicis ubi explicatio identitatum singularium cessat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT9","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171147907287Z_48307b80","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 22–24","source_sha256":"2a9c42afa6f44df79bb57b2d3633f692ab565124e6cc22a66152611cc7550c02","sha256":"74a259d0a73810de12ac2edf6e210827e2ac6e98879a42edbb23161e43472fa1","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:11:47.908277+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how divine attributes constitute moral, cosmic, and salvific order while preserving at once the transcendence of God, the contingency of creatures, rational freedom, and distributive justice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis posits a single wise and good divine causality ordering all things, while preserving modes of effects, secondary causality, and the asymmetry between caused good and permitted fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_14:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-03","text":"The reconstructive and metaphysical argument first purges predicates of creaturely modes, then transfers their causal accounts to the structure of divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-04","text":"The movement begins from moral attributions, passes to providence as the universal account of order, and ends in predestination as a special application to the supernatural end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_14:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-05","text":"The direction of the system proceeds from mercy grounding what is due to the creation of order, from order to universal providence, and from providence to the conveyance of rational beings beyond the proportion of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_14:A2","CH_GGVC_P_15:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-06","text":"The true movement is recursive and cumulative: eternal reason returns in temporal execution, primary causality in secondary causalities, and certainty of the end in the contingent modes through which the end is effected.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-07","text":"The amplification proceeds spirally, because mercy first ontologically presupposes all justice, providence then encompasses the whole of being, and predestination finally contracts and intensifies the same structure around salvation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A10","CH_GGVC_P_15:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BAS-08","text":"The closure is twofold: kinds of order, causality, and modality are explained through goodness, but the singular distribution of election terminates the regress in divine will without a further expressed reason.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A16","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Divine wisdom, goodness, and will constitute the immanent principle by which God's action is ordered, measured by no extrinsic right, law, or end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A2","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] God produces not only beings, but also the order, ends, proportions, and modes of causality by which beings participate in their perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A2","CH_GGVC_P_14:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] The account of order remains eternally in God, while its execution proceeds temporally in creatures and through creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Divine justice does not constitute equality of reciprocation, but the proportion by which the nature, dignity, order, and end established by God are fitting to each.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A3","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] Mercy is causally prior to created obligation, because the first gift constitutes the very field within which justice, merit, and recompense are subsequently understood.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A10","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The scope of providence is equal to the scope of primary causality; therefore no being, individual, or free act is simply excluded from divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A3","CH_GGVC_P_14:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Primary causality does not evacuate secondary causality, but communicates and orders it as the dignity of the creature and the means of execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Necessity, contingency, and freedom are modes of effects disposed by providence, not external limits that disrupt the certainty of order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A11","CH_GGVC_P_15:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Defect is not an autonomous positive principle: it is either removed through the communication of perfection, or permitted for the sake of a more universal good, or imputed as the fault of a secondary cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Predestination is a special contraction of providence for ordering a rational creature to a supernatural end unattainable by nature alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] The whole order of salvation proceeds from divine love, but contains grace, the use of free will, merit, and glory as internally causally ordered effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] Reprobation is providence permitting failure from the end and ordering punishment, not a cause of fault in the same way that predestination is a cause of grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A11","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","text":"[Persistent] Divine infallibility comprehends both the event and the mode of its occurrence; the necessity of the end is conditioned by the order posited, not absolute from the nature of proximate causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A12","CH_GGVC_P_15:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Inequality of gratuitous gifts is not unjust where no antecedent obligation is violated, although the singular assignment of goods terminates explanatory regress in simple will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A17","CH_GGVC_P_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GA-15","text":"[Emergent] Prayers, works, and merits are efficacious as secondary causes of execution, not as principles that constitute, alter, or correct the eternal decree.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A18","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-01","text":"Order returns functionally: first as the proportion of wisdom in things, then as the providential account of all things, finally as the ordering of the elect to salvation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A5","CH_GGVC_P_14:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-02","text":"Justice retains its ordering identity, but passes from the distribution of natural perfections to the order of punishment and salvific differentiation under mercy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-03","text":"Mercy changes from the universal communication of perfection into a special form by which grace and glory are causally conferred on some.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-04","text":"Defect migrates through three fields: privation to be mercifully removed, cosmological imperfection to be permitted for the sake of the whole, voluntary falling to be imputed under reprobation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-05","text":"The conformity of the effect to the divine intellect, first called causal truth, is absorbed into providence as the relation between eternal reason and ordered execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A6","CH_GGVC_P_14:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-06","text":"Freedom changes from an object of apparent exclusion into the proper mode of a secondary cause, whose act is at once caused, proceeds contingently, and remains imputable.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A9","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-07","text":"Certainty is amplified: from the order of will according to wisdom it passes to the infallibility of providence and to the conditioned necessity of the salvation of the elect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-08","text":"Natural obligation, which follows from created order, yields before the supernatural end, where no claim of nature precedes the gift of grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-09","text":"The distinction between the eternal and the temporal persists, but is extended from general providence to the whole series of calling, grace, free act, merit, and glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RMD-10","text":"Truth as the explicit name of justice disappears after the first unity, yet remains operative in the requirement that the effect correspond to divine reason and to the mode provided.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:D3","CH_GGVC_P_14:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-01","text":"Truth as the proper designation of divine justice remains a local mechanism; at the present level its function is absorbed under the conformity of the effect to providential order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:D3","CH_GGVC_P_13:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-02","text":"Chance and fortune remain local terms of the cosmology of providence; at the higher level only the general rule persists that externality to a particular cause is not externality to a universal cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_14:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-03","text":"The materially determined number of the elect and the concealment of one's own predestination are local determinations of the doctrine of salvation, not axioms of the whole created order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A14","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-04","text":"The dependence of obligation on divine order is amplified upward into the principle by which the absence of supernatural obligation safeguards the gratuity and inequality of grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-05","text":"Universal providence functions as the joint between the architecture of justice and the order of predestination, because the special decree of salvation is constituted within the account of all ends.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-06","text":"The distinction between primary cause and secondary causes joins the unities, because governance, freedom, merit, prayers, and the execution of salvation are explained by the same schema.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-07","text":"The removal of defect is an inferior mechanism of mercy; permission of defect and imputation of fault effect the transition to a higher structure in which goodness, justice, and freedom are ordered together.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:CGD-08","text":"Oppositions between justice and mercy, providence and contingency, grace and freedom become obsolete as oppositions on a single plane and are recoded as relations of distinct causal orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_15:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes any created law, obligation, or right that precedes divine will and binds God as though acting under a higher measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_13:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-02","text":"Divine attributes exclude passion, need, and civic virtue transferred univocally; only perfective, causal, and ordering accounts are retained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_13:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-03","text":"No absolute chance or ontological externality to providence is admitted, because every particularity is contained within universal causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-04","text":"Divine and created causality are not rival causes whose increase diminishes the action of the other.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_15:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-05","text":"Infallibility does not impose uniform necessity, nor does freedom require exclusion from the certainty of order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-06","text":"Evil is not an autonomous positive principle, nor is God posited as cause of fault in the same way as he is cause of salvific good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-07","text":"Mercy and justice are not rival powers: the gift above obligation does not destroy order, but manifests its gratuitous root.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_13:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:GNX-08","text":"Merit, prayer, and temporal work neither antecedently cause election nor retroactively alter the eternal decree.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:D4","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that created order can ground itself, because being, end, obligation, and mode of causality are resolved into first goodness and wisdom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_14:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that freedom consists in independence from the primary cause; otherwise the entire preservation of secondary causality under providence would collapse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_15:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that a measure of merit, equality, or right precedes the distribution of gratuitous gifts; such a measure would overthrow the simple priority of gift-giving.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that a world wholly lacking defect constitutes the sole norm of divine goodness, because the good of the universe includes the permission of certain defects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that salvation and perdition have symmetrical causality: salvific good is wholly reduced to the primary cause, while fault is imputed to the defect of created will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that a temporal cause constitutes or changes an eternal act; temporal efficacy is valid only within the already established order of execution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_15:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-07","text":"It must be false that the antecedent will of universal salvation is the same as the consequent decree of the salvation of all, because reprobation as permission of defect must remain.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:DBN-08","text":"It must be false that rational nature has of itself a right or sufficiency for the divine vision; otherwise predestination as gratuitous conveyance would become superfluous.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-01","text":"The highest excluded possibility is an ontological place outside divine order, from which causality, justice, or events could be assessed without relation to the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_14:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-02","text":"No neutral secondary causality remains that could impede, correct, or simply escape the order of the primary cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_14:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-03","text":"There is no further measure by which the singular identity of the elect or reprobate could be demonstrated; the system terminates this question in simple will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A16","CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-04","text":"A certain prospect of its own eternal state is unavailable to the creature, although a singular order materially determined is posited in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSA-05","text":"Ontologically inadmissible is a symmetry by which goodness and fault would proceed from God through the same kind of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-01","text":"Providence is the universal execution of the architecture of justice, whose very obligation gratuitous mercy antecedently constitutes.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-04","CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_14:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-02","text":"Created causality is at once an effect of primary causality and a participated dignity; therefore the action of the creature increases the manifestation of providence rather than diminishing its scope.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-06","CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_14:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_14:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-03","text":"Since providential certainty includes the mode of the effect, predestination can infallibly produce salvation through acts which remain free and contingent according to proximate causes.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","CL_GGVC_08:GA-11","CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","CH_GGVC_P_14:A12","CH_GGVC_P_15:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-04","text":"Mercy that removes defect and providence that permits defect do not simply contradict one another, but express diverse relations of particular good to more universal order.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CL_GGVC_08:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-05","text":"Punishment can be ordered within a divine work grounded in justice and mercy, although the fault requiring punishment is not symmetrically attributed to divine causality.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CL_GGVC_08:GA-09","CL_GGVC_08:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_13:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-06","text":"Because the supernatural end exceeds the capacity of nature and God is not indebted to the creature, the unequal conferral of grace cannot constitute injustice through violated obligation.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CL_GGVC_08:GA-10","CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","CH_GGVC_P_13:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-07","text":"The distinction of eternal reason from temporal execution makes prayers and works causally efficacious without a change of decree.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CL_GGVC_08:GA-15","CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-08","text":"The causal truth of the effect is amplified into the historical truth of order: the event corresponds to divine reason not only because it occurs, but because it occurs in the mode provided.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","CH_GGVC_P_13:A6","CH_GGVC_P_14:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-09","text":"Predestination does not suspend providence, but specially contracts its universality around an object capable of a supernatural end.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-06","CL_GGVC_08:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_15:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:XD-10","text":"Wisdom orders divine action globally, but does not provide a discursive account of the identity of individual elect; thus the intelligibility of structure coexists with the closure of singular will.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-01","CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","CH_GGVC_P_13:A2","CH_GGVC_P_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-01","text":"Reality emerges as an order of included causalities, in which the universal contains the particular without abolishing the properties and modes of particulars.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-02","CL_GGVC_08:GA-06","CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_14:A4","CH_GGVC_P_14:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-02","text":"Time does not constitute novelty in God, but is the executory extension of eternal reason through created, contingent, and causally ordered series.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-03","text":"The rational subject becomes a caused secondary cause, truly acting and imputable, yet lacking direct knowledge of its place in the eternal order.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","CL_GGVC_08:GA-15","CH_GGVC_P_14:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-04","text":"Distributive justice is reordered: the proportion of nature governs established obligations, but antecedent equality does not govern gifts exceeding nature.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-04","CL_GGVC_08:GA-05","CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","CH_GGVC_P_13:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-05","text":"Evil becomes a local defect within the order of good, but the transition from cosmological permission to salvific abandonment increases the difficulty of causality and imputability.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-09","CL_GGVC_08:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_14:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-06","text":"The method of the system does not compose oppositions through an indistinct middle, but relocates the terms into different levels of causality, modality, and execution.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-03","CL_GGVC_08:GA-07","CL_GGVC_08:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_14:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_15:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-07","text":"Certainty of the end does not evacuate temporal action, but increases the necessity of acting through ordered means, because the means themselves belong to the certain effect.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-11","CL_GGVC_08:GA-13","CL_GGVC_08:GA-15","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:BSD-08","text":"The system explains kinds of diversity through goodness, but does not further deduce the particulars of election; architectural fullness thus coheres with the lack of a singular distributive account.","refs":["CL_GGVC_08:GA-01","CL_GGVC_08:GA-14","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-01","text":"The circuit of gratuity is this: the first gift constitutes nature and end, nature and end constitute obligation, obligation constitutes justice, but justice is resolved into the prior gift.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A10","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-02","text":"The circuit of manifestation is this: wisdom orders effects, effects preserve order, order manifests the justice of the governor, and returns to wisdom as rule.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A2","CH_GGVC_P_13:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-03","text":"The circuit of modality is this: providence prepares causes of diverse modes, causes produce effects according to their proper modes, and effects thus fulfill the certainty of providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A11","CH_GGVC_P_14:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-04","text":"The path of defect proceeds from the permission of particular evil to the preservation of more universal good, which in turn situates permission within providential order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_14:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-05","text":"The circuit of predestination proceeds from love to grace, from grace to free act and merit, from merit to glory, which fulfills the eternal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-06","text":"Prayer receives efficacy from the order it is said to fulfill: the decree preordains the means, the means produce the effect, and the effect manifests the certainty of the decree.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A18","CH_GGVC_P_15:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-07","text":"Divine goodness is the attractor that contracts mercy, justice, diversity of effects, and unity of principle into one formally multiple causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-08","text":"The path of amplification passes from the order of every work to the providence of every being, then to the special ordering of rational beings to salvation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:RLE-09","text":"Reprobation is an unstable attractor: permission of defect, causality of abandonment, freedom of fault, and justice of punishment converge in it without full reduction to one kind of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A11","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B01","text":"Creaturely predicate → removal of passion and limitation → retention of causal and ordering perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_13:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B02","text":"Immanent wisdom and goodness → will regulated not extrinsically to itself → divine action ordered rather than arbitrary.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A2","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B03","text":"Production of beings → constitution of natures, ends, and proportions → emergence of created obligation → distributive justice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_13:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B04","text":"Universality of primary causality → universality of ordering to the end → providence of all beings and events.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A3","CH_GGVC_P_14:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B05","text":"Communication of causality → execution through secondary causes → diversity of necessary, contingent, and free modes under one certainty.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B06","text":"End exceeding nature → insufficiency of created capacity → special divine ordering → predestination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B07","text":"Permission of falling away from the end → abandonment and ordering of punishment → reprobation without symmetrical causation of fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A11","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B08","text":"Eternal decree → ordering of prayers, works, and merits → temporal execution → certain effect through contingent means.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A18","CH_GGVC_P_15:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FGS-B09","text":"Diversity of effects → manifestation of mercy and justice → common account in goodness → singular terminus in will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A15","CH_GGVC_P_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:AFM-B01","text":"Purification of predicates → immanent principle of wisdom and goodness → constitution of order and obligation → universal providence → execution through secondary causes → supernatural ordering → asymmetrical predestination and reprobation → closure in goodness and will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:AFM-B02","text":"Certainty of order → preparation of diverse causes → effects according to necessary, contingent, and free modes → conditioned necessity of the end without absolute necessitation of acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:AFM-B03","text":"Defect as privation → mercy removing or providence permitting → fault of the secondary cause → ordered punishment → terminal asymmetry between caused salvation and permitted perdition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-01","text":"Moral predicates are reclassified from habits or passions of a subject into causal accounts by which God communicates perfection and establishes order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_13:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-02","text":"Obligation ceases to be a measure antecedent to God and becomes an internal relation of nature, end, and order constituted by divine will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:D2","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-03","text":"Chance is reclassified from a simply disordered event into a defect of coordination with respect to a particular cause within universal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_14:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-04","text":"The opposition between divine and created causality collapses, because immediacy of reason and mediation of execution belong to different orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_15:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-05","text":"Necessity and contingency no longer describe the presence or absence of providence, but different modes of effecting the same order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_15:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-06","text":"Evil is divided into permitted defect, imputable fault, abandonment, and punishment, so that no single positive causality is attributed to all members.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_15:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-07","text":"The justice of gratuitous gifts is separated from antecedent distributive equality: the common account of diversity is taken from goodness, but singular conferral does not follow obligation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:A17","CH_GGVC_P_15:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MME-08","text":"Prayers and works are transferred from the alternative between altering the decree and being superfluous into internal means by which the decree is temporally fulfilled.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:ME8","CH_GGVC_P_15:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, justice, mercy, providence, contingency, freedom, predestination, reprobation, and the means of salvation are treated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_14:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_15:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level operate universal causality, accounts of ends, proportions of obligation, secondary causes, permission of defect, and distribution of modes of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_15:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, oppositions are resolved not by the abolition of either term, but by distinguishing the orders in which each receives a different function.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_15:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, reality is the temporal execution of eternal reason, whose effects truly preserve necessary, contingent, and free modes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_15:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the text redistributes through recursive distinction the very oppositions it treats, so that the form of argumentation effects the hierarchical order it affirms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_13:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-01","text":"Wisdom globally orders divine will, but singular election receives no further account beyond will; the nexus between universal rationality and individual assignment remains incomplete.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-02","text":"Mercy removes defect, providence permits defect for the sake of the whole, and reprobation permits falling away from the end; the criteria of transition between removal and permission are not fully explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-03","text":"The compatibility of infallibility and freedom is secured through the distinction of causal modes, but the inner mechanism by which the certainty of the primary cause does not necessitate the contingent act is not further demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-04","text":"Reprobation causally orders abandonment and punishment, while fault is imputed to created free choice alone; this joint requires asymmetry but leaves its causal mediation fragile.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_15:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-05","text":"Permission of evil depends on the preference of the good of the universe, but the analogy between cosmic diversity and the distribution of salvation does not demonstrate singular identities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:FL-06","text":"Justice first signifies the proportion fitting to each, but later safeguards the inequality of gratuitous gifts through the absence of obligation; continuity depends on the distinction between due nature and supernatural gift.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A3","CH_GGVC_P_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-01","text":"Justice changes from equality among agents into a teleological architecture according to which effects receive being, proportion, and end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-02","text":"Mercy changes from the universal ontological efficacy of removing defect into the special account of grace by which salvific diversity manifests goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_15:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-03","text":"Providence changes from the universal account of order into predestination when the same schema is contracted to the supernatural end and to certain rational beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A1","CH_GGVC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-04","text":"Defect changes from privation simply to be removed into a permitted event and, in the moral field, into fault imputable to a secondary cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-05","text":"Freedom changes from the appearance of externality to providence into the contingent mode of secondary causality constituted within providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:D4","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MP-06","text":"Certainty changes from the immobility of divine reason into conditioned necessity that comprehends at once the event and the mode of the event.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A12","CH_GGVC_P_15:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly an architecture of included causalities, whose eternally immobile account executes itself through temporal and transient branches.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a caused secondary cause: it receives the power of acting, preserves its own contingent mode, and incurs imputability on account of its act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A7","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-03","text":"Time is the field of execution, not the place in which the divine decree is formed by deliberation or undergoes change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:A5","CH_GGVC_P_15:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-04","text":"Possible navigation is not flight outside the order, but action within it through prayers, works, freedom, and merit as truly causal means.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_15:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:HSI-05","text":"The machine bears a double track of defect: it mercifully communicates perfection, permits particular defects for the sake of the whole, and orders moral falling through reprobation without causing fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:A7","CH_GGVC_P_14:A8","CH_GGVC_P_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B01","text":"Axioms concerning immanent wisdom, the gift grounding obligation, universal providence, secondary causes, the modality of effects, and the special order of salvation suffice to reconstruct the principal structure of this cluster.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_13:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the distinction between the account of order existing immediately in God and temporal execution through secondary causes, because it composes several oppositions by the same act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B03","text":"The inner mechanism of freedom under primary causality, the singular account of election, and the joint between divine abandonment and created fault are not yet sufficiently determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_14:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B04","text":"The system coheres at this scale if primary and secondary causality are understood noncompetitively, justice is not understood as a limitation of God, and contingency is retained as a provided mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_13:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_08:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement by reducing distinctions to providence and the inclusion of secondary causes; yet reduction is resisted by the terminus of simple will, where explanation of singular identities ceases.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_15:MRT9","CH_GGVC_P_15:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_08@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_08:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 22–24","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 21 · Prima pars · Quaestio 22 · Prima pars · Quaestio 23"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 25–27","order":9,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_16","CH_GGVC_P_17","CH_GGVC_P_18"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_09@R001","sha256":"cc03e2ae2d64e47bd65c0ad69ab4295a3d82c306529f0153c9ed2585e098389c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo cognitio, potentia et beatitudo divina ordinem creaturae ad finem constituant sine mutatione, limitatione aut compositione in Deo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-02","text":"Vita aeterna denuo constituitur ut gloria intellectualis cuius bonum perfectum et obiectum ultimum ipse Deus est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_18:A1","CH_GGVC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-03","text":"Thesis globalis statuit eundem actum divinum ordinem finalem cognoscere, omne possibile non contradictorium efficere posse, atque beatitudinem increatam obiective praebere actui creato participato.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A9","CH_GGVC_P_18:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-04","text":"Argumentatio metaphoram per definitionem, difficultatem modalem per distinctionem obiecti, et relationem beatificam per distinctionem obiecti atque actus reconstruendo procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-05","text":"Fundamentum est actus purus, cuius possibilitas actualitatem creatam excedit et cuius finis a creatura tantum actu finito participatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-06","text":"Probatio communis apparentem mutationem vel defectum a principio divino ad rem cognitam, obiectum non possibile aut modum creatum transfert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:D7","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_18:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-07","text":"Motus est cumulativus et spiralis: distinctiones inscriptionis simpliciter et secundum quid, potentiae absolutae et ordinatae, obiecti et actus eandem asymmetriam successive amplificant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A13","CH_GGVC_P_18:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est teleologica, non modalis: Deus est immutabilis cognoscens, causa inexhausta et finis obiectivus, dum creatura mutabilis per actum participatum ad eum ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Actus purus omnem potentiam passivam, acquisitionem perfectionis et transitum in beatitudinem a Deo excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Cognitio, potentia, voluntas, esse et intelligere in Deo realiter unum sunt, quamvis secundum rationem officia structuraliter distincta exerceant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Immutabilitas principii divini cum mutabilitate, contingentia et participatione effectuum compatitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A9","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_18:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Ordinatio transit a gratia ut medio, per voluntatem causaliter instituentem, ad distinctionem Dei ut finis cuius et actus creati ut finis quo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_17:A11","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Finis proprius ordinis supernaturalis est gloria sive bonum perfectum naturae intellectualis, non vita naturalis neque medium gratiae separatim acceptum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_18:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Ratio intellectualis ordinem finalem et consummationem eius formaliter articulat: liber importat notitiam praedestinationis, beatitudo autem intelligere perfectum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A3","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Nullus effectus, actus creatus aut status finitus principium divinum vel obiectum infinitum adaequat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A7","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Necessitas finalis praedestinationis media contingentia non tollit: ordo ad finem indefectibilis manet, quamvis gratia et causae proximae deficere possint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_16:A8","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Unus ordo supernaturalis tribus rationibus constituitur: in cognitione divina conscribitur, sub potentia divina possibilis et efficibilis est, in actu beatifico creato participatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_18:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Negatio defectus non potentiam minuit, sed obiectum et modum perfectionis purificat: deletio ad rem transfertur, contradictio non-obiectum fit, falsitas a beatitudine removetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] Relatio Dei ad creaturam est asymmetrica: electio non habet catalogum mortis symmetricum, causa non mensuratur effectu, obiectum beatificum non est actus participatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Summum bonum intellectualiter possessum est attractor qui electionem ad gloriam, causalitatem effectuum et beatitudinem creatam in unum ordinem finalem colligit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-01","text":"Notitia redit functione mutata: primo praedestinationem conscribit, deinde cum voluntate et potentia principium effectus significat, ultimo perfectionem intellectualem formaliter constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-02","text":"Finis a termino electionis supra naturam migrat ad rationem qua effectus potentiae subordinatur et tandem in finem cuius atque finem quo distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-03","text":"Immutabilitas identitatem functionis servat sed campum extendit: scientia non mutatur, potentia non recipit, beatitudo non acquiritur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-04","text":"Distinctio simpliciter et secundum quid redit ut distinctio possibilitatis absolutae et relativae, deinde in distinctionem obiecti increati et actus creati transformatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-05","text":"Actualitas mutat munus: status gratiae non probat finem, ordo actualis non exhaurit possibile, actus beatificus creatus non identificatur cum obiecto divino.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:D3","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-06","text":"Obiectum progreditur a re mutabili sub scientia, ad possibile sub potentia, ad Deum cognitum sub beatitudine; mutatio semper in termino creato, non in principio divino, locatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-07","text":"Participatio, prius implicita in gratia et effectu finito, fit explicita in actu intellectuali creato circa bonum infinitum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_17:D3","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-08","text":"Negationes locales cumulantur in propositionem positivam: defectus non est potentia, contradictio non est obiectum, falsitas non est perfectio, reprobatio non est electio inversa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-01","text":"Metaphora conscriptionis localiter originem libri vitae explicat; hoc gradu in structuram cognitionis finalis absorbetur neque imaginem libri materialis retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A1","CH_GGVC_P_16:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-02","text":"Deletio localiter duplicem inscriptionem solvit; sursum amplificata exemplum fit regulae qua mutatio effectus immutabilitatem principii non laedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_16:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-03","text":"Irrevocabilitas praeteriti et melior universitas manent determinationes modales locales, sed coniunctae demonstrant actualitatem neque contradictioni retractabili neque clausurae possibilitatis aequivalere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A14","CH_GGVC_P_17:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-04","text":"Enumeratio contemplationis, gaudii, sufficientiae et potestatis localis est; hoc gradu in regulam eminentis containmenti perfectionum reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:D7","CH_GGVC_P_18:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-05","text":"Gratia ut causa amissibilis gradui inferiori pertinet, sed eius relatio ad actum participatum pontem inter ordinationem salutis et beatitudinem creatam efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-06","text":"Distinctiones inscriptionis, potentiae et fruitionis hoc gradu non aggregantur, sed communem formam exhibent: principium divinum absolutum per ordinem determinatum effectum creatum producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A13","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-07","text":"Exemplaria libri univoce dicti, omnipotentiae ut cuiuslibet enuntiabilis et beatitudinis ut aggregati superantur, quia obiectum, modus et finis prius determinandi sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-01","text":"Systema neque librum materialem neque collectionem bonorum in Deo admittit; pluralitas signorum et perfectionum ad unitatem intellectualem reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-02","text":"Potentia passiva, mutatio scientiae et acquisitio beatitudinis a Deo excluduntur, quia perfectionem ab alio recipiendam importarent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-03","text":"Contradictio et infectio praeteriti non sunt effectus difficillimi, sed termini quibus ratio possibilis deest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-04","text":"Ordo actualis neque potentiam neque sapientiam neque bonitatem divinam exhaurit aut ad unicum cursum necessarium claudit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-05","text":"Gratia praesens, vita naturalis et bonum finitum non sunt finis ultimus, quamvis rationem medii vel similitudinem boni retineant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_16:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-06","text":"Nulla mensura univoca cognitionem divinam et rem cognitam, potentiam et effectum, beatitudinem increatam et actum creatum identificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-07","text":"Defectus non constituit contrariam perfectionem positivam: reprobatio non est liber mortis, peccabilitas non auget potentiam, falsitas non implet beatitudinem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet Deum successione rerum informari, moveri aut per effectum ad perfectionem nondum habitam perduci.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem ordinationem eandem firmitatem habere; aliter praedestinatio, gratia, causalitas proxima et actus participatus distingui non possent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_18:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet actualitatem creatam mensuram possibilitatis divinae vel effectum finitum manifestationem adaequatam causae infinitae constituere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet relationem Dei ad creaturam aut identitatem simplicem aut exterioritatem absolutam esse; systema participationem asymmetricam requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet attributa divina aut partes reales aut voces functione vacuas esse; identitas realis distinctionem rationum operativam servare debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet defectum, corporalitatem vel falsitatem aliquid positivum addere plenitudini divinae; recipitur tantum perfectio quam imperfecte significant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-01","text":"Possibilitas ontologice inadmissibilis circa quam systema ordinatur est Deus mutabilis, passibilis aut perfectionem ex tempore acquirens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-02","text":"Contradictio non manet potentiae adversarius externus, sed absentia rei quae omnino produci possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-03","text":"Beatitudo creaturae independens ab obiecto divino est impossibilis, sicut comprehensio finita quae obiectum infinitum exhauriat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-04","text":"Clausura absoluta actualitatis est exclusa: neque status praesens salutis neque cursus mundi neque actus creatus plenitudinem finis aut causae adaequat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-05","text":"Systema circa absentiam symmetriae ultimae construitur: non datur aequalitas inter electionem et reprobationem, causam et effectum, beatitudinem increatam et participatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-01","text":"Gloria, quae libri vitae obiectum proprium est, formaliter determinatur ut actus intellectualis creatus quo Deus tamquam finis cuius cognoscitur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-05","CL_GGVC_09:GA-09","CL_GGVC_09:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_18:D4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-02","text":"Potentia activa explicat quomodo ordo praedestinationis indefectibilis in actu creato participato terminetur sine passiva mutatione causae divinae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-01","CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_17:A2","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-03","text":"Inscriptio simpliciter et secundum quid, potentia absoluta et ordinata, atque causalitas necessaria vel contingens constituunt modalitatem stratificatam potius quam unam necessitatem uniformem.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-04","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A13","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-04","text":"Deletio, contradictio et beatitudo falsa eadem operatione apophatica tractantur: mutatio vel defectus ad terminum creatum refertur neque in principio divino ponitur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-05","text":"Fixitas ordinis praedestinati plenitudinem potentiae non contrahit, quia voluntas ordinem actualem determinat quin possibilitas divina ab eo exhauriatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-02","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_17:A11","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-06","text":"Triplex asymmetria electionis et reprobationis, potentiae et effectus, obiecti et actus prohibet ut ordo salutis in oppositiones binarias convertatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-07","CL_GGVC_09:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_16:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-07","text":"Potentia divina effectui ut fini non subicitur; potius effectus intellectualis ad Deum ut finem cuius ordinatur, unde causalitas in teleologiam creaturae convertitur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-04","CL_GGVC_09:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-08","text":"Tempus creatum bifariam ordinatur: status praesens salutis mutabilis est, sed veritas eventus facti irrevocabilis et terminus praedestinationis indefectibilis manent.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A8","CH_GGVC_P_17:A14","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-09","text":"Intellectualitas totum circuitum continet: ordo finalis in Deo cognoscitur, per potentiam efficitur et in creatura cognitione Dei consummatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-06","CL_GGVC_09:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_16:A3","CH_GGVC_P_17:A2","CH_GGVC_P_18:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-01","text":"Identitas realis attributorum cum distinctione rationum permittit ut cognitio, potentia et beatitudo non tres processus, sed tria officia unius actualitatis divinae sint.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-01","CL_GGVC_09:GA-02","CL_GGVC_09:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-02","text":"Necessitas distribuitur inter essentiam divinam, ordinem finalem praedestinatum, veritatem praeteriti et contingentiam mediorum creatorum; ideo necessarium et contingens non sunt opposita simplicia.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-03","text":"Tempus systematis habet fontem immutabilem, praesentia mutabilia, praeteritum irrevocabile et terminum finalem stabilem, sine successione interna in Deo.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_16:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-04","text":"Cognitio creaturae est simul realis consummatio et comprehensio inadaequata: obiectum infinitum vere attingitur, sed actu finito neque possidetur exhaustive neque in subiectum absorbetur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-05","CL_GGVC_09:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-05","text":"Agentia creata non eliminatur ab ordine divino: gratia, causae proximae et actus intellectus effectus reales sunt, quamvis eorum firmitas et plenitudo a principio divino dependeant.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-04","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A8","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-06","text":"Methodus systematis apparentem limitationem Dei in errorem classificationis convertit: aut defectus agenti falso tribuitur, aut non-obiectum pro obiecto sumitur, aut modus creatus in Deum transfertur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-01","CL_GGVC_09:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_16:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-01","text":"Finis supernaturalis → electio → conscriptio divina → gratia ut medium → possibile defectum creatum → stabilitas ordinis finalis: mutatio circuitum renovat sine mutatione principii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-02","text":"Actus purus → potentia infinita → effectus finitus → non-exhaustio causae → renovata affirmatio infinitatis constituit circuitum amplificationis modalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:D3","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-03","text":"Obiectio ex incapaci­tate apparente → distinctio defectus agentis et defectus obiecti → remotio falsae mensurae → intensificatio perfectionis divinae est circuitus dialecticus communis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-04","text":"Desiderium partiale → abstractio perfectionis → remotio corporalitatis et falsitatis → continentia eminens in Deo convertit dispersionem beatitudinum in unum attractorem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:D7","CH_GGVC_P_18:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-05","text":"Attractor centralis est Deus ut summum bonum intelligibile: cognitio eum praefinit, potentia media ad eum ordinat, actus creatus eum participat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-06","text":"Identitas realis et distinctio rationis spiraliter redeunt quoties unum principium diversa munera cognitionis, causalitatis, voluntatis et fruitionis explere debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-07","text":"Clausura distribuitur: liber claudit ordinem cognitum, voluntas ordinem actualem, veritas praeteritum et beatitudo finem; potentia tamen campum non actualium apertum servat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_18:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B01","text":"Actus purus + simplicitas divina → cognitio, potentia et beatitudo realiter una → exclusio receptionis, mutationis et acquisitionis in principio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B02","text":"Distinctio rationum → cognitio ordinis finalis / amplitudo causalitatis / possessio intellectualis boni → pluralitas officiorum sine compositione reali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A3","CH_GGVC_P_18:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B03","text":"Finis supernaturalis → electio divina → notitia electorum → inscriptio simpliciter indefectibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_16:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B04","text":"Potentia activa infinita → omne possibile absolute → voluntaria determinatio unius ordinis → contingentia causarum proximarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:D2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A9","CH_GGVC_P_17:A11","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B05","text":"Gratia et actus intellectus creati → media realia sed participata → mutabilitas status sine mutatione causae vel finis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5","CH_GGVC_P_16:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B06","text":"Deletio / contradictio / beatitudo falsa → separatio perfectionis a defectu → relocatio mutationis, exclusio non-obiecti, continentia eminens perfectionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B07","text":"Deus ut obiectum et finis cuius + actus creatus ut finis quo → beatitudo increata causaliter intima sed formaliter distincta a participatione creata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:AFM-B01","text":"Metaphora conscriptionis → cognitio ordinis finalis → determinatio gloriae → potentia activa infinita → discretio possibilis et contradictorii → actualitas voluntarie ordinata → beatitudo intellectualis participata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_18:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:AFM-B02","text":"Apparens deletio → mutatio rei cognitae → apparens impotentia → defectus obiecti → apparens compositio beatitudinis → continentia eminens → restitutio perfectionis immutabilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:AFM-B03","text":"Finis electus → ordo possibilis → ordo actualis → medium contingens → actus participatus → possessio intellectualis boni → clausura teleologica sine clausura modalitatis divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-01","text":"Liber vitae reclassificatur ex catalogo statico in rationem epistemicam qua finis creaturae immutabiliter cognoscitur, licet status medius mutetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_16:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-02","text":"Potentia reclassificatur ex capacitate indeterminata in plenitudinem causalitatis cuius ambitus ratione entis, non multitudine formularum, definitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-03","text":"Beatitudo reclassificatur ex praemio vel collectione bonorum in actum intellectualem participatum cuius obiectum increatum est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_18:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-04","text":"Ager modalitatis distinguit possibilitatem absolutam, ordinationem voluntariam, contingentiam mediorum, necessitatem finis et irrevocabilitatem praeteriti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_17:A13","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-05","text":"Oppositio immutabilis et mutabilis corruit: modi non miscentur, sed principium immutabile effectus contingentes et participationes mutabiles producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-06","text":"Finalitas fit nexus metaphysicae et salutis: gloria, causalitas et cognitio beatifica non tres fines, sed tres articulationes unius ordinis ad summum bonum sunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei librum vitae et deletionem, ambitum omnipotentiae atque attributionem beatitudinis Deo examinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis cognitionem ordinis, causalitatem activam, voluntariam actualizationem, media contingentia et participationem intellectualem distribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A2","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus quaestiones de mutatione vel impotentia Dei in quaestiones de modo cogniti, ratione possibilis et distinctione obiecti ab actu convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:D7","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_18:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis ponit unum principium immutabile, plures ordines possibiles, unum cursum actualem, praeteritum irrevocabile et effectus mutabiles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A9","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus distinctiones successive inducit, donec ipsa forma argumenti defectum a Deo removeat et ordinem positivum ex negationibus producat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_17:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-01","text":"Identitas realis potentiae, voluntatis, scientiae et beatitudinis cum diversitate ambituum earum ratione tantum sustinetur; pondus distinctionis rationis totam structuram excedit demonstrationem localem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-02","text":"Definitio libri vitae per praedestinationem tensionem patitur cum inscriptione secundum quid eorum qui gratiam habent sed gloriam non consequentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_16:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-03","text":"Fixitas ordinis praedestinati et possibilitas divina ordinum aliorum cohaerent tantum si decretum actuale potentiam non exhaurit; relatio inter alternativa et hunc ordinem non ulterius explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_17:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-04","text":"Prioritas intellectus in beatitudine nititur transitu ab operatione perfectissima ad rationem formalem totius beatitudinis, dum munus voluntatis subordinate tantum exponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:D3","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-05","text":"Participatio requirit similitudinem veram inter Deum et creaturam, sed recusatio scalae univocae mensuram huius similitudinis incompletam relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-01","text":"Liber mutatur a metaphora conscriptionis humanae in notitiam divinam quae ordinem finalem formaliter repraesentat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_16:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-02","text":"Vita aeterna mutatur a termino nondeterminato in gloriam et deinde in actum intellectualem creatum circa Deum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-03","text":"Potentia mutatur a vocabulo potentialitatis in expressionem actualitatis perfectae, ita ut non posse pati vel peccare perfectionem significet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-04","text":"Possibile mutatur ab eo quod causis creatis praesto est in id cui termini non repugnant; impossibilitas absoluta sic a difficultate causali separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-05","text":"Finis mutatur ab obiecto electionis in relationem duplicem: Deus est terminus obiectivus, actus creatus modus quo terminus participatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite apparet ut machina asymmetrica tribus campis constans: actualitas divina immutabilis, campus possibilitatis inexhaustus et ordo effectuum mutabilium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_16:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum creatum est intellectus ordinatus et participans: neque sui finis auctor est neque passive absorbetur, sed actu proprio obiectum increatum attingit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:A2","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:HSI-03","text":"Tempus systematis habet praesentem statum amissibilem, praeteritum irretractabile et terminum finalem stabilem, omnia sub cognitione sine successione comprehensa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A8","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:HSI-04","text":"Imago minima est liber non materialis qui campum possibilitatis per ordinem voluntarium ad actum beatificum dirigit, quin aut causa aut obiectum ab effectu exhauriatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de actu puro, distinctione rationum, fine intellectuali, potentia non exhausta et participatione creata ad structuram huius gregis restituendam sufficiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B02","text":"Cohaerentia firmissima est in distinctione principii divini immutabilis ab effectu creato mutabili et in subordinatione medii ad finem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B03","text":"Minus determinata manet relatio inter praedestinationem definitam et ordines absolute possibiles, quia distinctio potentiae absolutae et ordinatae tensionem continet potius quam plene dissolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B04","text":"Minus determinatae etiam manent mensura melioris universitatis et demonstratio prioritatis formalis intellectus supra voluntatem in beatitudine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B05","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat, quia a cognitione finis per amplitudinem causalitatis ad participationem consummativam progreditur, dum negationes falsa obiecta successive removent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B06","text":"Reductioni axiomaticae resistit analogia inscriptionis, quia simul ordinem finalem certum et dispositionem amissibilem nominat; haec ambiguitas tamen mutationem creatam intra stabilitatem divinam operari sinit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_16:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171232691110Z_3ac18bc6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 25–27","source_sha256":"cc03e2ae2d64e47bd65c0ad69ab4295a3d82c306529f0153c9ed2585e098389c","sha256":"0858944458dafdb7a6f4669fb23f4ddcf8920bd9cc5f9a756b4445fccdfc50b3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:12:32.693112+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how divine knowledge, power, and beatitude establish the order of the creature toward its end without change, limitation, or composition in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-02","text":"Eternal life is reconstituted as intellectual glory, whose perfect good and ultimate object is God himself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_18:A1","CH_GGVC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-03","text":"The global thesis holds that the same divine act knows the final order, can bring about every non-contradictory possible, and objectively offers uncreated beatitude to a participated created act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A9","CH_GGVC_P_18:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-04","text":"The argument proceeds by reconstructing metaphor through definition, modal difficulty through a distinction of object, and the beatific relation through a distinction of object and act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-05","text":"The foundation is pure act, whose possibility exceeds created actuality and whose end is participated by the creature only through a finite act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-06","text":"The common proof transfers apparent change or deficiency from the divine principle to the thing known, the non-possible object, or the created mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:D7","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_18:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-07","text":"The movement is cumulative and spiral: the distinctions of inscription simpliciter and secundum quid, absolute and ordained power, object and act successively amplify the same asymmetry.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A13","CH_GGVC_P_18:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BAS-08","text":"The closure is teleological, not modal: God is immutable knower, inexhausted cause, and objective end, while the mutable creature is ordered to him through a participated act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Pure act excludes from God every passive potency, acquisition of perfection, and transition into beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Knowledge, power, will, being, and understanding are really one in God, although according to reason they exercise structurally distinct offices.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] The immutability of the divine principle is compatible with the mutability, contingency, and participation of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A9","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_18:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Ordination passes from grace as a means, through the causally instituting will, to the distinction of God as finis cuius and the created act as finis quo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_17:A11","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] The proper end of the supernatural order is glory, or the perfect good of intellectual nature, not natural life nor the means of grace taken separately.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_18:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The intellectual account formally articulates the final order and its consummation: the book imports knowledge of predestination, while beatitude imports perfect understanding.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A3","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] No effect, created act, or finite state is adequate to the divine principle or infinite object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A7","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] The final necessity of predestination does not remove contingent means: the order toward the end remains indefectible, although grace and proximate causes can fail.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_16:A8","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] One supernatural order is constituted in three respects: it is inscribed in divine knowledge, possible and producible under divine power, and participated in the created beatific act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_18:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] The negation of deficiency does not diminish power, but purifies the object and mode of perfection: deletion is transferred to the thing, contradiction becomes a non-object, falsehood is removed from beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] God's relation to the creature is asymmetric: election has no symmetric catalogue of death, cause is not measured by effect, and the beatific object is not the participated act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] The highest good intellectually possessed is an attractor that gathers election unto glory, the causality of effects, and created beatitude into one final order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-01","text":"Knowledge recurs with an altered function: first it inscribes predestination, then with will and power signifies the principle of effect, and finally formally constitutes intellectual perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-02","text":"The end migrates from the term of election above nature to the account by which an effect is subordinated to power, and finally is distinguished into finis cuius and finis quo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-03","text":"Immutability preserves the identity of function but extends the field: knowledge does not change, power does not receive, beatitude is not acquired.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-04","text":"The distinction simpliciter and secundum quid recurs as the distinction of absolute and relative possibility, then is transformed into the distinction of uncreated object and created act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-05","text":"Actuality changes office: the state of grace does not prove the end, the actual order does not exhaust the possible, and the created beatific act is not identified with the divine object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:D3","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-06","text":"The object progresses from a mutable thing under knowledge, to the possible under power, to God known under beatitude; change is always located in the created term, not in the divine principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-07","text":"Participation, previously implicit in grace and finite effect, becomes explicit in the created intellectual act concerning the infinite good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_17:D3","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RMD-08","text":"Local negations accumulate into a positive proposition: deficiency is not power, contradiction is not an object, falsehood is not perfection, reprobation is not inverse election.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-01","text":"The metaphor of inscription locally explains the origin of the book of life; at this level it is absorbed into the structure of final knowledge and does not retain the image of a material book.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A1","CH_GGVC_P_16:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-02","text":"Deletion locally resolves double inscription; amplified upward, it becomes an instance of the rule by which change of effect does not injure the immutability of the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_16:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-03","text":"The irrevocability of the past and a better universe remain local modal determinations, but together they show that actuality is equivalent neither to retractable contradiction nor to the closure of possibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A14","CH_GGVC_P_17:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-04","text":"The enumeration of contemplation, joy, sufficiency, and power is local; at this level it is reduced to the rule of eminent containment of perfections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:D7","CH_GGVC_P_18:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-05","text":"Grace as a losable cause belongs to the lower level, but its relation to the participated act makes a bridge between the ordination of salvation and created beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-06","text":"The distinctions of inscription, power, and fruition are not aggregated at this level, but exhibit a common form: the absolute divine principle produces a created effect through a determined order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A13","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:CGD-07","text":"Models of a book said univocally, omnipotence as that of anything expressible, and beatitude as an aggregate are surpassed, because object, mode, and end must first be determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-01","text":"The system admits neither a material book nor a collection of goods in God; the plurality of signs and perfections is reduced to intellectual unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-02","text":"Passive potency, change of knowledge, and acquisition of beatitude are excluded from God, because they would import a perfection to be received from another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-03","text":"Contradiction and alteration of the past are not most difficult effects, but terms for which the account of the possible is lacking.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-04","text":"The actual order neither exhausts divine power, wisdom, or goodness nor confines them to a single necessary course.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-05","text":"Present grace, natural life, and finite good are not the ultimate end, although they retain the account of a means or a likeness of good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_16:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-06","text":"No univocal measure identifies divine knowledge and the thing known, power and effect, uncreated beatitude and created act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:GNX-07","text":"Deficiency does not constitute a contrary positive perfection: reprobation is not a book of death, sinfulness does not increase power, falsehood does not fulfill beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that God is informed by the succession of things, moved, or led through effect to a perfection not yet possessed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that every ordination has the same firmness; otherwise predestination, grace, proximate causality, and participated act could not be distinguished.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_18:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that created actuality constitutes the measure of divine possibility or that finite effect constitutes an adequate manifestation of infinite cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that God's relation to the creature is either simple identity or absolute exteriority; the system requires asymmetric participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that divine attributes are either real parts or expressions empty of function; real identity must preserve an operative distinction of accounts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that deficiency, corporeality, or falsehood add anything positive to divine fullness; only the perfection which they signify imperfectly is received.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-01","text":"The ontologically inadmissible possibility around which the system is ordered is a God who is mutable, passible, or acquires perfection in time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_17:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-02","text":"Contradiction does not remain an external adversary of power, but is the absence of a thing that could be produced at all.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-03","text":"The creature's beatitude independent of the divine object is impossible, as is finite comprehension that exhausts the infinite object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-04","text":"The absolute closure of actuality is excluded: neither the present state of salvation nor the course of the world nor a created act is adequate to the fullness of the end or cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSA-05","text":"The system is constructed around the absence of ultimate symmetry: there is no equality between election and reprobation, cause and effect, uncreated and participated beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-01","text":"Glory, which is the proper object of the book of life, is formally determined as a created intellectual act by which God is known as finis cuius.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-05","CL_GGVC_09:GA-09","CL_GGVC_09:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_18:D4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-02","text":"Active power explains how the indefectible order of predestination terminates in a participated created act without passive change of the divine cause.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-01","CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_17:A2","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-03","text":"Inscription simpliciter and secundum quid, absolute and ordained power, and necessary or contingent causality constitute a stratified modality rather than one uniform necessity.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-04","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A13","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-04","text":"Deletion, contradiction, and false beatitude are treated by the same apophatic operation: change or deficiency is referred to the created term and is not placed in the divine principle.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-05","text":"The fixity of the predestined order does not contract the fullness of power, because will determines the actual order without divine possibility being exhausted by it.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-02","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_17:A11","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-06","text":"The threefold asymmetry of election and reprobation, power and effect, object and act prevents the order of salvation from being converted into binary oppositions.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-07","CL_GGVC_09:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_16:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-07","text":"Divine power is not subordinated to effect as end; rather, the intellectual effect is ordered to God as finis cuius, whence causality is converted into the teleology of the creature.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-04","CL_GGVC_09:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-08","text":"Created time is ordered in two ways: the present state of salvation is mutable, but the truth of the event done remains irrevocable and the term of predestination indefectible.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A8","CH_GGVC_P_17:A14","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:XD-09","text":"Intellectuality contains the whole circuit: the final order is known in God, effected through power, and consummated in the creature by knowledge of God.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-06","CL_GGVC_09:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_16:A3","CH_GGVC_P_17:A2","CH_GGVC_P_18:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-01","text":"The real identity of attributes with a distinction of accounts permits knowledge, power, and beatitude to be not three processes but three offices of one divine actuality.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-01","CL_GGVC_09:GA-02","CL_GGVC_09:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-02","text":"Necessity is distributed among divine essence, the predestined final order, the truth of the past, and the contingency of created means; therefore necessary and contingent are not simple opposites.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-03","text":"The time of the system has an immutable source, mutable presents, an irrevocable past, and a stable final term, without internal succession in God.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_16:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-04","text":"The creature's knowledge is at once real consummation and inadequate comprehension: the infinite object is truly attained, but through a finite act it is neither possessed exhaustively nor absorbed into the subject.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-05","CL_GGVC_09:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-05","text":"Created agency is not eliminated by the divine order: grace, proximate causes, and acts of intellect are real effects, although their firmness and fullness depend on the divine principle.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-03","CL_GGVC_09:GA-04","CL_GGVC_09:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_16:A8","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:BSD-06","text":"The method of the system converts an apparent limitation of God into an error of classification: either a deficiency is falsely attributed to the agent, or a non-object is taken for an object, or a created mode is transferred to God.","refs":["CL_GGVC_09:GA-01","CL_GGVC_09:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_16:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-01","text":"Supernatural end → election → divine inscription → grace as means → possible created deficiency → stability of final order: change renews the circuit without change of the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-02","text":"Pure act → infinite power → finite effect → non-exhaustion of cause → renewed affirmation of infinity constitutes a circuit of modal amplification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:D3","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-03","text":"Objection from apparent incapacity → distinction between deficiency of agent and deficiency of object → removal of false measure → intensification of divine perfection is a common dialectical circuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-04","text":"Partial desire → abstraction of perfection → removal of corporeality and falsehood → eminent containment in God converts the dispersion of beatitudes into one attractor.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:D7","CH_GGVC_P_18:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-05","text":"The central attractor is God as the highest intelligible good: knowledge predefines him, power orders means to him, and the created act participates in him.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-06","text":"Real identity and distinction of reason return spirally whenever one principle must fulfill diverse offices of knowledge, causality, will, and fruition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:RLE-07","text":"Closure is distributed: the book closes the known order, will the actual order, truth the past, and beatitude the end; power nevertheless keeps open the field of non-actuals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_18:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B01","text":"Pure act + divine simplicity → knowledge, power, and beatitude really one → exclusion of reception, change, and acquisition in the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B02","text":"Distinction of accounts → knowledge of final order / scope of causality / intellectual possession of good → plurality of offices without real composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A3","CH_GGVC_P_18:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B03","text":"Supernatural end → divine election → knowledge of the elect → indefectible inscription simpliciter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_16:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B04","text":"Infinite active power → every possible absolutely → voluntary determination of one order → contingency of proximate causes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:D2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A9","CH_GGVC_P_17:A11","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B05","text":"Grace and acts of created intellect → real but participated means → mutability of state without change of cause or end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5","CH_GGVC_P_16:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B06","text":"Deletion / contradiction / false beatitude → separation of perfection from deficiency → relocation of change, exclusion of non-object, eminent containment of perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_18:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FGS-B07","text":"God as object and finis cuius + created act as finis quo → uncreated beatitude causally intimate but formally distinct from created participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:AFM-B01","text":"Metaphor of inscription → knowledge of final order → determination of glory → infinite active power → distinction of possible and contradictory → voluntarily ordered actuality → participated intellectual beatitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_18:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:AFM-B02","text":"Apparent deletion → change of thing known → apparent impotence → deficiency of object → apparent composition of beatitude → eminent containment → restoration of immutable perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:AFM-B03","text":"Chosen end → possible order → actual order → contingent means → participated act → intellectual possession of good → teleological closure without closure of divine modality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-01","text":"The book of life is reclassified from a static catalogue into an epistemic account by which the creature's end is immutably known, although the intermediate state changes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_16:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-02","text":"Power is reclassified from indeterminate capacity into fullness of causality, whose scope is defined by the account of being, not by a multitude of formulations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-03","text":"Beatitude is reclassified from reward or collection of goods into a participated intellectual act whose object is uncreated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_18:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-04","text":"The field of modality distinguishes absolute possibility, voluntary ordination, contingency of means, necessity of end, and irrevocability of the past.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_17:A13","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-05","text":"The opposition of immutable and mutable collapses: the modes are not mixed, but the immutable principle produces contingent effects and mutable participations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_17:A15","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MME-06","text":"Finality becomes the nexus of metaphysics and salvation: glory, causality, and beatific knowledge are not three ends but three articulations of one order toward the highest good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A5","CH_GGVC_P_17:A8","CH_GGVC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level examines the book of life and deletion, the scope of omnipotence, and the attribution of beatitude to God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_17:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_18:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level distributes knowledge of order, active causality, voluntary actualization, contingent means, and intellectual participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:A2","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level converts questions concerning God's change or impotence into questions concerning the mode of the known, the account of the possible, and the distinction of object from act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:D7","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_18:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level posits one immutable principle, several possible orders, one actual course, an irrevocable past, and mutable effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A9","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level introduces distinctions successively, until the very form of the argument removes deficiency from God and produces positive order from negations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_17:AF2","CH_GGVC_P_18:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-01","text":"The real identity of power, will, knowledge, and beatitude with the diversity of their scopes is sustained only by reason; the weight of the distinction of reason exceeds the local demonstration of the entire structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-02","text":"The definition of the book of life through predestination suffers tension with inscription secundum quid of those who have grace but will not attain glory.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_16:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-03","text":"The fixity of the predestined order and the divine possibility of other orders cohere only if the actual decree does not exhaust power; the relation between alternatives and this order is not further explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A7","CH_GGVC_P_17:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-04","text":"The priority of intellect in beatitude rests on a transition from the most perfect operation to the formal account of the whole of beatitude, while the role of will is explained only subordinately.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:D3","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:FL-05","text":"Participation requires a true likeness between God and creature, but the refusal of a univocal scale leaves the measure of this likeness incomplete.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-01","text":"The book changes from a metaphor of human inscription into divine knowledge that formally represents the final order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_16:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-02","text":"Eternal life changes from an undetermined term into glory and then into a created intellectual act concerning God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-03","text":"Power changes from a word of potentiality into an expression of perfect actuality, such that the inability to suffer or sin signifies perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A2","CH_GGVC_P_17:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-04","text":"The possible changes from what is available to created causes into that whose terms are not repugnant; absolute impossibility is thus separated from causal difficulty.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A10","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MP-05","text":"The end changes from the object of election into a double relation: God is the objective term, the created act the mode by which the term is participated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A4","CH_GGVC_P_18:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as an asymmetric machine consisting of three fields: immutable divine actuality, an inexhausted field of possibility, and an order of mutable effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_16:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:HSI-02","text":"The created subject is an ordered and participating intellect: it is neither the author of its own end nor passively absorbed, but through its own act attains the uncreated object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_18:A2","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5","CH_GGVC_P_18:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system has a losable present state, an irretractable past, and a stable final term, all comprehended under knowledge without succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:A8","CH_GGVC_P_17:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_16:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:HSI-04","text":"The minimal image is a non-material book that directs the field of possibility through voluntary order toward the beatific act, without either cause or object being exhausted by the effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_17:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_18:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms concerning pure act, distinction of accounts, intellectual end, unexhausted power, and created participation suffice to restore the structure of this whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:A1","CH_GGVC_P_17:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B02","text":"The strongest coherence lies in the distinction of immutable divine principle from mutable created effect and in the subordination of means to end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_16:A6","CH_GGVC_P_18:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B03","text":"The relation between determinate predestination and absolutely possible orders remains less determined, because the distinction of absolute and ordained power contains the tension rather than fully resolving it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_16:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B04","text":"The measure of a better universe and the demonstration of the formal priority of intellect over will in beatitude likewise remain less determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B05","text":"The restoration preserves the true movement, because it progresses from knowledge of the end through the scope of causality to consummative participation, while negations successively remove false objects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_17:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_18:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_17:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_09:MRT-B06","text":"The analogy of inscription resists axiomatic reduction, because it names at once a certain final order and a losable disposition; yet this ambiguity allows created change to operate within divine stability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_16:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_16:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_09@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_09:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 25–27","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 24 · Prima pars · Quaestio 25 · Prima pars · Quaestio 26"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 28–30","order":10,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_19","CH_GGVC_P_20","CH_GGVC_P_21"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_10@R001","sha256":"e9eff5e8ee2ec12864c8ef537495468c6c1e731f34f60eddd183c57385cf8b05","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-01","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo pluralitas personalis realis ex originibus internis constituatur, quin essentia simplex dividatur aut relationes ad rationem tantum redigantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis ponit distinctionem personalem non in divisione essentiae, sed in relationibus originis quae, cum divina essentia identificatae, subsistunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio metaphysicam originis, analysim relationis et reconstructionem semanticam personae ita coniungit ut unumquodque stadium condicionem sequentis praebeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-04","text":"Motus a processionibus ad relationes et deinde ad personas procedit, quia distinctio personalis prius originem, tum oppositionem realem, postremo subsistentiam requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_21:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-05","text":"Progressus est recursivus: ratio creaturalis cuiusque termini purgatur, perfectio eius retinetur, atque terminus ad divinam simplicitatem translatus functionem ontologicam altiorem accipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-06","text":"Processiones duae in quattuor relationes originis explicantur, quarum subsistentia campum constituit in quo persona divina definiri potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D7","CH_GGVC_P_20:D4","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-07","text":"Interiorem originem systema non contra unitatem, sed per unitatem intendit: quo processio intimior est, eo relatio minus accidentalis et magis capax subsistentiae fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est simul numerica et categorialis: operationes immanentes processionibus terminum imponunt, oppositiones relationes determinant, et relatio subsistens rationem personae complet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Origo divina realis tantum ut processio immanens intelligitur, quae intra unitatem naturae manet nec effectum extraneum producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A2","CH_GGVC_P_19:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Intelligere et velle actiones immanentes divinas exhauriunt; unitas simplicis actus earum multiplicationem indefinitam impedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A10","CH_GGVC_P_20:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Verbum procedit secundum similitudinem naturae et rationem generationis, Amor autem secundum inclinationem voluntatis, ordine quidem a Verbo dependens sed non genitus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D3","CH_GGVC_P_19:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Processio intra identitatem naturae constituit ordinem realem inter principium et procedens, unde relationes originis reales oriuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:A4","CH_GGVC_P_20:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Relatio divina retinet rationem respectus ad oppositum, sed eius esse non accidentale est: idem est cum esse essentiae divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:A6","CH_GGVC_P_20:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Oppositio relativa sufficit ad distinctionem realem relationum, quamvis nulla distinctio absoluta essentiae admittatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:A8","CH_GGVC_P_20:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Distinctio personalis in divinis non aliud fundamentum habet quam relationes originis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A1","CH_GGVC_P_21:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Relatio originis, quia in Deo est essentia et non accidens, subsistit atque rationem personae divinae recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A12","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Persona a substantia individua rationalis naturae ad subsistens intellectuale, completum et incommunicabile transfertur, remotis materia, accidentibus et discursu.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Unitas essentiae et pluralitas personalis non sunt termini eiusdem ordinis: illa esse absolutum, haec oppositiones subsistentes originis exprimit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Nomen divinum legitime transfertur quando ratio significata conservatur, modus creatus removetur et perfectio eminentius attribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-01","text":"[Amplificatio] Processio ab emanatione immanente ad fundamentum relationis realis amplificatur et tandem in constitutione relationis personalis absorbetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-02","text":"[Inversio] Simplicitas primo processionibus obicitur, deinde modum earum purgat, ac postremo efficit ut relatio non accidat sed subsistat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-03","text":"[Transformatio terminalis] Relatio a puro respectu ad ordinem realem, ab ordine reali ad oppositionem distinctivam, atque ab oppositione essentiali ad personam subsistentem transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:A1","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-04","text":"[Mutatio] Individuatio a condicionibus materialibus discedit et in incommunicabilitatem subsistentis, in se indistincti et ab aliis distincti, reponitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-05","text":"[Redditus functionalis] Substantia in definitione personae modum essendi per se significat, sed in applicatione divina locum cedit relationi quae per modum hypostasis subsistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-06","text":"[Absorptio] Verbum et Amor identitatem suarum rationum servant, sed in gradibus sequentibus non amplius ut argumenta psychologica, sed ut principia numeri et oppositionis relationalis funguntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D7","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_21:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-07","text":"[Evanescentia modi] Modus corporeus, materialis, accidentalis et discursivus evanescit postquam rationem significatam ad transferendam perfectionem praebuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-08","text":"[Identitas stabilis] Una essentia divina per omnes mutationes categoriales manet invarians, dum processio, relatio et persona diversos modos eiusdem realitatis ordinatae exprimunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A6","CH_GGVC_P_20:A5","CH_GGVC_P_21:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-01","text":"[Localis] Analysis conceptionis intellectualis et inclinationis voluntariae manet exemplar proximum ad distinguendas processiones, non autem sola constitutio personarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A4","CH_GGVC_P_19:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-02","text":"[Localis cum effectu globali] Enumeratio quattuor relationum numerum originum explicat, sed per se nondum demonstrat quomodo quaelibet relatio ad constitutionem personalem se habeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:D4","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-03","text":"[Localis instrumentalis] Distinctiones inter essentiam, subsistentiam, rem naturae et hypostasim apparatum semanticum praebent; earum vis globalis tantum in formula relationis subsistentis consummatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_21:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-04","text":"[Amplificata] Processio immanens a solutione difficultatis de origine ad fundamentum universae pluralitatis relationalis huius gregis promovetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A2","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-05","text":"[Coniungens] Identitas realis relationis cum essentia pontem constituit inter processionem internam et subsistentiam personalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-06","text":"[Transitionalis] Purgatio modi creati non est ornamentum hermeneuticum, sed operatio quae terminos processionis, relationis et personae ad eandem ontologiam simplicem traducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-07","text":"[Superata] Motus localis, receptio materialis, accidens inhaerens et individuatio corporea, postquam falsas analogias exhibuerunt, nullam functionem constitutivam in gradu praesenti retinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-01","text":"Processio divina nec productio creati nec motus in terminum exteriorem est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_19:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-02","text":"Distinctio personalis neque per eundem Deum diversis effectibus denominatum neque per comparationem mentis tantum constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_20:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-03","text":"Relationes divinae non sunt accidentia, formae absolutae superadditae aut pluralitas essentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_20:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-04","text":"Ordo Dei ad creaturam non constituit relationem personalem realem in Deo, quia dependentia exterior non reciprocatur nec essentiam determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_20:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-05","text":"Persona nec universale nec pars nec natura alteri assumptibilis est, sed suppositum completum et incommunicabile.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-06","text":"Persona divina neque individuationem materialem neque rationalitatem discursivam neque relationem accidentalem importat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-07","text":"Perfectio divina nec tertiam actionem immanentem nec seriem infinitam verborum, amorum vel relationum reflexivarum generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_20:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem originem realem alteritatem essentiae, exterioritatem causalem aut separationem termini exigere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem distinctionem realem esse distinctionem rerum absolutarum vel substantiarum divisas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet identitatem relationis cum essentia oppositionem relativam et distinctionem personalem dissolvere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet individuationem semper materiam requirere aut relationem semper dispositionem extrinsecam et accidentalem esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet vocabula creaturalia aut univoce taxonomiam divinam metiri aut, propter diversum modum essendi, omni significatione communi carere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSA-01","text":"Possibilitas inadmissibilis circa quam systema ordinatur est simplicitas absoluta quae omnem distinctionem realem absorberet; talis simplicitas unitatem non servaret, sed relationem originis evacuaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSA-02","text":"Aequaliter inadmissibilis est pluralitas quae relationes in essentias distinctas mutaret et communem naturam divideret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_20:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSA-03","text":"Persona divina ut absolutum solitarium ontologice indisponibilis est, quia incommunicabilitas personalis relatione originis, non clausura sine respectu, constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSA-04","text":"Nullum principium temporale, materiale vel extrinsecum admitti potest ad originem, relationem aut personam constituendam; omnis distinctio valida ab actu interno et ordine originis provenit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_20:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-01","text":"Processio immanens, cum intra identitatem naturae maneat, differentiam operationis in ordinem realem principii et procedentis convertit; sic origo fit fundamentum relationis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-01","CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_19:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-02","text":"Relatio originis, quia idem esse cum essentia habet, non manet praedicatum extrinsecum sed potest ut hypostasis subsistere et personam constituere.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_20:A6","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-03","text":"Communicatio unius naturae et incommunicabilitas personae non repugnant, quia natura respondet ordini essentiae, incommunicabilitas autem modo subsistendi relationali.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-03","CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","CL_GGVC_10:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_19:A6","CH_GGVC_P_21:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-04","text":"Simplicitas ex limite negativo in principium positivum convertitur: excludendo accidentia efficit ut relationes sint essentiales, atque essentialitas earum subsistentiam personalem sustinet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_19:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-05","text":"Numerus personalis non ex copia nominum deducitur, sed per seriem moderatam constituitur: operationes immanentes processiones determinant, processiones oppositiones relationales, oppositiones campum distinctionis personalis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-02","CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_19:D7","CH_GGVC_P_20:A12","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-06","text":"Eadem disciplina analogica tres mutationes gubernat: origo ab exterioritate purgatur, relatio ab accidentalitate, persona a materialitate, servata cuiusque ratione significata.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-01","CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","CL_GGVC_10:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_20:A1","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-07","text":"Ordo Verbi, Amoris, relationum et personarum est ordo originis et intellegibilitatis, non series temporalium mutationum.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-03","CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_20:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-01","text":"Realitas divina admittit distinctionem sine divisione: distinctio augetur per oppositionem respectuum, dum identitas essentiae integra manet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","CL_GGVC_10:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-02","text":"Subiectum personale divinum non est individuum prius absolutum quod relationem postea accipit, sed subsistens cuius ipsa incommunicabilitas relationaliter constituitur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-07","CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-03","text":"Causalitas interna reclassificatur ut causalitas originis sine effectu extraneo: terminus procedens ab alio est, sed in eadem natura et eodem esse manet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-01","CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_19:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-04","text":"Temporalitas successionis removetur, sed ordo non tollitur; prioritas originis sine ante et post temporali structuram divinam ordinat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-03","CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-05","text":"Cognitio theologica fit reconstructio analogica: non transfert res creatas, sed rationes earum, quarum modos limitatos removet et functiones ad simplicitatem accommodat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","CL_GGVC_10:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_21:D6","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-06","text":"Numerus in divinis non est aggregatio entium, sed effectus formaliter derivatus ex operationibus, originibus et oppositionibus ordinatis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-02","CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_19:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus analogicus procedit a termino creaturali ad separationem modi creati, inde ad retentionem perfectionis, ac demum ad usum divinum qui ipsum terminum reclassificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-02","text":"Via amplificationis est: actio immanens → processio → ordo principii et procedentis → relatio opposita → relatio subsistens → persona.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_20:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-03","text":"Interiortas est attractor amplificationis: quo minus origo exterior est, eo magis identitas naturae servatur; quo magis identitas servatur, eo minus relatio accidentalis esse potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_20:A4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-04","text":"Formula attractiva totius gregis est unitas sine confusione et distinctio sine divisione; utrumque membrum alterum recursive restringit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-05","text":"Clausura numerica progreditur ab exhaustione actionum immanentium ad duas processiones et ab unaquaque processione ad binas relationes oppositas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:FGS5","CH_GGVC_P_20:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-06","text":"Regressus infinitus clauditur quia intelligere et velle sunt unus actus perfectus, nec reflexio multiplicat nova principia, processiones aut relationes reales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A11","CH_GGVC_P_20:A13","CH_GGVC_P_20:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B01","text":"Simplicitas essentiae + necessitas distinctionis personalis → requisitio modi originis qui nec essentiam dividat nec distinctionem nominalem relinquat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D2","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B02","text":"Exclusio motus, exterioritatis, accidentis et individuationis materialis → translatio quaestionis ad operationem immanentem, respectum essentialem et incommunicabilitatem subsistentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_20:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B03","text":"Intelligere + velle, ut actiones immanentes exhaustive positae → duo principia formalia processionum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A10","CH_GGVC_P_19:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B04","text":"Intellegere → Verbum secundum similitudinem et generationem; velle → Amor secundum inclinationem et ordinem ad Verbum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D3","CH_GGVC_P_19:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B05","text":"Processio intra eandem naturam → ordo realis principii et procedentis → binae relationes oppositae pro unaquaque processione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_20:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B06","text":"Relatio realis in Deo + absentia accidentis → identitas esse relationis cum essentia → subsistentia relationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B07","text":"Subsistentia intellectualis + completudo + incommunicabilitas + relatio originis distinctiva → persona divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A4","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B08","text":"Persona relationaliter constituta → pluralitas personalis sine essentiarum pluralitate → clausura ontologica sub attractore unitatis distinctae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:AFM-B01","text":"Distinctio personalis postulata → processio exterior exclusa → actio immanens inventa → Verbum et Amor distincta → relationes originis reales → oppositio sine divisione essentiae → relatio subsistens → persona.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:AFM-B02","text":"Terminus creaturalis receptus → modus materialis vel accidentalis remotus → perfectio significata retenta → categoria ad simplicitatem translata → significatio ontologica amplificata → usus doctrinalis stabilitus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8","CH_GGVC_P_21:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-01","text":"Processio e categoria motus et productionis exterioris in structuram operationis immanentis transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-02","text":"Unitas et pluralitas non amplius tamquam contraria simplicia tractantur, sed inter essentiam absolutam et respectus oppositos distribuuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-03","text":"Relatio ab accidente ad esse essentiale et subsistens promovetur; persona vicissim ab absoluto solitario ad relationem originis reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_21:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-04","text":"Singularitas personalis a mera particularitate numerica ad incommunicabilem modum subsistendi transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-05","text":"Numerus divinus non ex vocabulario vel aggregatione, sed ex inventario operationum immanentium et oppositionum originis derivatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_20:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-06","text":"Lectio nominum divinorum fit quadripartita: originem vocabuli, rem significatam, modum significandi et congruentiam doctrinalem discernit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B01","text":"[Gradus superficiei] Examinantur duae processiones, quattuor relationes originis et persona ut substantia individua rationalis naturae ad Deum applicanda.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D7","CH_GGVC_P_20:D4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B02","text":"[Gradus structuralis] Actio immanens originem generat, origo relationem realem, oppositio distinctionem, identitas cum essentia subsistentiam, et subsistentia incommunicabilis personam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A1","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B03","text":"[Gradus metastrategicus] Certamen interpretativum reconstituitur per distinctiones inter rationem significatam et modum creatum, esse absolutum et respectum, naturam communem et suppositum incommunicabile.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B04","text":"[Gradus ontologicus / temporalis] Realitas ponitur simplex sed interne ordinata, sine potentia aut successione, capax tamen originis, oppositionis et distinctionis realis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B05","text":"[Gradus methodologicus / performativus] Forma argumenti suas theses efficit removendo successive exterioritatem, accidentalitatem et materialitatem, donec residuae rationes positivas originis, relationis et personae constituant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-01","text":"Intellectus et voluntas secundum rem in Deo non distinguuntur, sed diversae rationes eorum duas processiones reales sustinere debent; distinctio formalis hic maximum pondus fert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D5","CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-02","text":"Relatio idem esse cum essentia habet et tamen alteri relationi realiter opponitur; transitus ab oppositione significata ad distinctionem realem manet commissura metaphysica principalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:D3","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-03","text":"Definitio personae per substantiam individuam et determinatio personae divinae per relationem subsistentem non immediate coincidunt; nexus pendet ab identitate relationis cum essentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-04","text":"Transitus a duabus processionibus ad quattuor relationes clare datur, sed distributio relationum ad constitutionem personarum in materia huius gregis minus explicite determinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:D4","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-05","text":"Analogia a verbo humano non subsistente ad Verbum divinum et a persona creata ad personam divinam necessaria est, sed modus proportionis non plene demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MP-01","text":"Processio mutatur cum ab egressu causali ad emanationem intelligibilem intra agentem transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_19:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MP-02","text":"Relatio mutatur cum ab accidente inhaerente ad ipsum esse essentiae et deinde ad subsistentem hypostasim promovetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MP-03","text":"Individuum mutatur cum materia desinit esse principium individuationis et incommunicabilitas relationalis munus distinctivum suscipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:HSI-01","text":"Imago occulta est machina simplicis actus qui, sine se dividendo, per originem internam respectus oppositos producit eosque in subsistentiam personalem densat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A11","CH_GGVC_P_20:A6","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:HSI-02","text":"Ens personale intra hanc machinam non est atomus clausus, sed suppositum completum et incommunicabile cuius distinctio relatione originis constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A4","CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:HSI-03","text":"Tempus huius systematis est ordo sine successione: principium et procedens ordinantur, sed nullum fieri, ante temporale aut mutatio admittitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_20:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio systematis per subtractionem fit: falsi modi creati successive removentur, donec ratio originis, respectus et incommunicabilitatis ad simplicem realitatem applicari possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B01","text":"Restitutio huius gregis sufficit si simul retinentur processio immanens, relatio realis eadem essentiae, oppositio relativa et subsistentia personalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est catena quae originem internam in respectum realem, respectum in oppositionem et relationem essentialem in personam subsistentem convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B03","text":"Minus determinata manet exacta relatio inter inventarium quaternarium relationum et constitutionem personalem, praesertim ubi vocabula originem et relationem vicissim significant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B04","text":"Fragilitas residua consistit in duplici transitu analogico: ab actibus intellectus et voluntatis ad processiones reales, atque a substantia individua ad relationem subsistentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B05","text":"Cohaerentia praesentis restitutionis servatur quia ordinem generativum processionis, relationis et personae retinet, non ordinem mere capitularem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B06","text":"Reductioni axiomaticae resistit asymmetria residualis nominum: processio amoris minus proprie nominatur, et terminologia relationis atque originis non ubique perfecte separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171309875602Z_2d0f2013","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 28–30","source_sha256":"e9eff5e8ee2ec12864c8ef537495468c6c1e731f34f60eddd183c57385cf8b05","sha256":"cc81661d1744f9132e82963cd9c3f183d8698d176139c35bfdfdfd23ba7f6449","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:13:09.877413+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-01","text":"The central question is how real personal plurality is constituted from internal origins without the simple essence being divided or relations being reduced to reason alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis posits personal distinction not in a division of essence, but in relations of origin which, being identified with the divine essence, subsist.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-03","text":"The argument so combines a metaphysics of origin, an analysis of relation, and a semantic reconstruction of person that each stage provides the condition for the next.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-04","text":"The movement proceeds from processions to relations and then to persons, because personal distinction requires first origin, then real opposition, and finally subsistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_21:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-05","text":"The progress is recursive: the creaturely account of each term is purified, its perfection retained, and the term, transferred to divine simplicity, receives a higher ontological function.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-06","text":"Two processions are unfolded into four relations of origin, whose subsistence constitutes the field in which the divine person can be defined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D7","CH_GGVC_P_20:D4","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-07","text":"The system intends internal origin not against unity but through unity: the more intimate the procession is, the less accidental and the more capable of subsistence the relation becomes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BAS-08","text":"The closure is at once numerical and categorical: immanent operations impose a limit on processions, oppositions determine relations, and subsisting relation completes the account of person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Divine origin is understood as real only insofar as it is immanent procession, which remains within the unity of nature and produces no extraneous effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A2","CH_GGVC_P_19:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Understanding and willing exhaust the divine immanent actions; the unity of simple act prevents their indefinite multiplication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A10","CH_GGVC_P_20:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The Word proceeds according to likeness of nature and the account of generation, whereas Love proceeds according to the inclination of will, dependent in order on the Word indeed, but not begotten.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D3","CH_GGVC_P_19:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Procession within identity of nature constitutes a real order between principle and that which proceeds, whence real relations of origin arise.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:A4","CH_GGVC_P_20:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Divine relation retains the character of reference to an opposite, but its being is not accidental: it is the same as the being of the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:A6","CH_GGVC_P_20:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Relative opposition suffices for the real distinction of relations, although no absolute distinction of essence is admitted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:A8","CH_GGVC_P_20:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Personal distinction in the divine has no foundation other than relations of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A1","CH_GGVC_P_21:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] The relation of origin, because in God it is essence and not accident, subsists and receives the account of divine person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A12","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Person is transferred from individual substance of a rational nature to intellectual, complete, and incommunicable subsistent, with matter, accidents, and discursiveness removed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Unity of essence and personal plurality are not terms of the same order: the former expresses absolute being, the latter subsisting oppositions of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] A divine name is legitimately transferred when the signified account is preserved, the created mode removed, and perfection attributed more eminently.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-01","text":"[Amplification] Procession is amplified from immanent emanation to the foundation of real relation and finally absorbed into the constitution of personal relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-02","text":"[Inversion] Simplicity is first objected to processions, then purifies their mode, and finally causes relation not to inhere as an accident but to subsist.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-03","text":"[Terminal transformation] Relation passes from mere reference to real order, from real order to distinctive opposition, and from essential opposition to subsisting person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:A1","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-04","text":"[Mutation] Individuation departs from material conditions and is placed in the incommunicability of a subsistent, undivided in itself and distinct from others.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-05","text":"[Functional return] Substance in the definition of person signifies a mode of being per se, but in the divine application yields its place to relation which subsists in the mode of hypostasis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-06","text":"[Absorption] Word and Love preserve the identity of their accounts, but at subsequent levels function no longer as psychological arguments, but as principles of number and relational opposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D7","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_21:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-07","text":"[Disappearance of mode] Bodily, material, accidental, and discursive mode disappears after it has supplied the signified account for transferring perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RMD-08","text":"[Stable identity] One divine essence remains invariant through all categorical mutations, while procession, relation, and person express diverse modes of the same ordered reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A6","CH_GGVC_P_20:A5","CH_GGVC_P_21:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The analysis of intellectual conception and volitional inclination remains the proximate model for distinguishing processions, but not the sole constitution of persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A4","CH_GGVC_P_19:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-02","text":"[Local with global effect] The enumeration of four relations explains the number of origins, but does not by itself yet demonstrate how each relation bears upon personal constitution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:D4","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-03","text":"[Instrumental local] Distinctions among essence, subsistence, thing of nature, and hypostasis provide a semantic apparatus; their global force is completed only in the formula of subsisting relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_21:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-04","text":"[Amplified] Immanent procession is advanced from a solution to the difficulty concerning origin to the foundation of the entire relational plurality of this group.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A2","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-05","text":"[Connecting] The real identity of relation with essence constitutes a bridge between internal procession and personal subsistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-06","text":"[Transitional] Purification of created mode is not a hermeneutical ornament, but an operation that translates the terms of procession, relation, and person into the same simple ontology.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:CGD-07","text":"[Surpassed] Local motion, material reception, inhering accident, and bodily individuation, having displayed false analogies, retain no constitutive function at the present level.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-01","text":"Divine procession is neither the production of a creature nor motion toward an exterior term.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_19:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-02","text":"Personal distinction is constituted neither through the same God denominated by diverse effects nor through a comparison of the mind alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_20:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-03","text":"Divine relations are not accidents, superadded absolute forms, or a plurality of essences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_20:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-04","text":"God's order toward the creature does not constitute a real personal relation in God, because external dependence is not reciprocated and does not determine the essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_20:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-05","text":"Person is neither universal nor part nor a nature assumable by another, but a complete and incommunicable supposit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-06","text":"Divine person imports neither material individuation nor discursive rationality nor accidental relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:GNX-07","text":"Divine perfection generates neither a third immanent action nor an infinite series of words, loves, or reflexive relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_20:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that every real origin requires otherness of essence, causal exteriority, or separation of term.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that every real distinction is a distinction of absolute things or divided substances.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that the identity of relation with essence dissolves relative opposition and personal distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that individuation always requires matter or that relation is always an extrinsic and accidental disposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that creaturely terms either measure the divine taxonomy univocally or, on account of a different mode of being, lack every common signification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSA-01","text":"The inadmissible possibility around which the system is ordered is an absolute simplicity that would absorb every real distinction; such simplicity would not preserve unity but evacuate relation of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSA-02","text":"Equally inadmissible is a plurality that would turn relations into distinct essences and divide the common nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_20:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSA-03","text":"Divine person as a solitary absolute is ontologically unavailable, because personal incommunicability is constituted by relation of origin, not by closure without reference.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSA-04","text":"No temporal, material, or extrinsic principle can be admitted to constitute origin, relation, or person; every valid distinction proceeds from internal act and the order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_20:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-01","text":"Immanent procession, because it remains within identity of nature, converts difference of operation into a real order of principle and that which proceeds; thus origin becomes the foundation of relation.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-01","CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_19:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-02","text":"The relation of origin, because it has the same being as essence, does not remain an extrinsic predicate but can subsist as hypostasis and constitute person.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_20:A6","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-03","text":"Communication of one nature and incommunicability of person are not incompatible, because nature corresponds to the order of essence, whereas incommunicability corresponds to the relational mode of subsisting.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-03","CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","CL_GGVC_10:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_19:A6","CH_GGVC_P_21:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-04","text":"Simplicity is converted from a negative limit into a positive principle: by excluding accidents it causes relations to be essential, and their essentiality sustains personal subsistence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_19:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-05","text":"Personal number is not deduced from a multitude of names, but is constituted through a regulated series: immanent operations determine processions, processions relational oppositions, and oppositions the field of personal distinction.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-02","CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_19:D7","CH_GGVC_P_20:A12","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-06","text":"The same analogical discipline governs three mutations: origin is purified of exteriority, relation of accidentality, and person of materiality, while the signified account of each is preserved.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-01","CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","CL_GGVC_10:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_20:A1","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:XD-07","text":"The order of Word, Love, relations, and persons is an order of origin and intelligibility, not a series of temporal changes.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-03","CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_20:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-01","text":"Divine reality admits distinction without division: distinction is increased through opposition of references, while identity of essence remains intact.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","CL_GGVC_10:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-02","text":"The divine personal subject is not a prior absolute individual that subsequently receives relation, but a subsistent whose very incommunicability is relationally constituted.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-07","CL_GGVC_10:GA-08","CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-03","text":"Internal causality is reclassified as causality of origin without an extraneous effect: the proceeding term is from another, but remains in the same nature and the same being.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-01","CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_19:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-04","text":"The temporality of succession is removed, but order is not abolished; priority of origin without temporal before and after orders the divine structure.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-03","CL_GGVC_10:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-05","text":"Theological knowledge becomes analogical reconstruction: it transfers not created things but their accounts, removing their limited modes and adapting their functions to simplicity.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-09","CL_GGVC_10:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_21:D6","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:BSD-06","text":"Number in the divine is not an aggregation of beings, but an effect formally derived from ordered operations, origins, and oppositions.","refs":["CL_GGVC_10:GA-02","CL_GGVC_10:GA-04","CL_GGVC_10:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_19:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-01","text":"The analogical circuit proceeds from a creaturely term to separation of the created mode, thence to retention of perfection, and finally to a divine use that reclassifies the term itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-02","text":"The path of amplification is: immanent action → procession → order of principle and that which proceeds → opposite relation → subsisting relation → person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_20:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_21:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-03","text":"Interiority is the attractor of amplification: the less exterior origin is, the more identity of nature is preserved; the more identity is preserved, the less relation can be accidental.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_20:A4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-04","text":"The attractive formula of the whole group is unity without confusion and distinction without division; each member recursively restricts the other.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-05","text":"Numerical closure proceeds from the exhaustion of immanent actions to two processions and from each procession to two opposite relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:FGS5","CH_GGVC_P_20:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:RLE-06","text":"Infinite regress is closed because understanding and willing are one perfect act, nor does reflection multiply new principles, processions, or real relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A11","CH_GGVC_P_20:A13","CH_GGVC_P_20:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B01","text":"Simplicity of essence + necessity of personal distinction → requirement of a mode of origin that neither divides essence nor leaves distinction merely nominal.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D2","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B02","text":"Exclusion of motion, exteriority, accident, and material individuation → translation of the question to immanent operation, essential reference, and subsisting incommunicability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_20:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B03","text":"Understanding + willing, posited exhaustively as immanent actions → two formal principles of processions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A10","CH_GGVC_P_19:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B04","text":"Understanding → Word according to likeness and generation; willing → Love according to inclination and order to the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D3","CH_GGVC_P_19:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B05","text":"Procession within the same nature → real order of principle and that which proceeds → two opposite relations for each procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_20:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B06","text":"Real relation in God + absence of accident → identity of the being of relation with essence → subsistence of relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B07","text":"Intellectual subsistence + completeness + incommunicability + distinctive relation of origin → divine person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A4","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FGS-B08","text":"Relationally constituted person → personal plurality without plurality of essences → ontological closure under the attractor of distinct unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:AFM-B01","text":"Personal distinction postulated → exterior procession excluded → immanent action discovered → Word and Love distinguished → real relations of origin → opposition without division of essence → subsisting relation → person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:AFM-B02","text":"Creaturely term received → material or accidental mode removed → signified perfection retained → category transferred to simplicity → ontological signification amplified → doctrinal use stabilized.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8","CH_GGVC_P_21:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-01","text":"Procession is transferred from the category of motion and exterior production into the structure of immanent operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-02","text":"Unity and plurality are no longer treated as simple contraries, but distributed between absolute essence and opposite references.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-03","text":"Relation is advanced from accident to essential and subsisting being; person, in turn, is reclassified from solitary absolute to relation of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_21:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-04","text":"Personal singularity is transferred from mere numerical particularity to an incommunicable mode of subsisting.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-05","text":"Divine number is derived not from vocabulary or aggregation, but from the inventory of immanent operations and oppositions of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_20:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MME-06","text":"The reading of divine names becomes fourfold: it discerns the origin of the word, the thing signified, the mode of signifying, and doctrinal congruence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Two processions, four relations of origin, and person as individual substance of a rational nature to be applied to God are examined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D7","CH_GGVC_P_20:D4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Immanent action generates origin, origin real relation, opposition distinction, identity with essence subsistence, and incommunicable subsistence person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A1","CH_GGVC_P_20:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The interpretative contest is reconstituted through distinctions between signified account and created mode, absolute being and reference, common nature and incommunicable supposit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / temporal level] Reality is posited as simple but internally ordered, without potency or succession, yet capable of origin, opposition, and real distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_20:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / performative level] The form of the argument effects its theses by successively removing exteriority, accidentality, and materiality, until the remaining positive accounts constitute origin, relation, and person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-01","text":"Intellect and will are not distinguished in God according to the thing, but their diverse accounts must sustain two real processions; formal distinction here bears the greatest weight.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:D5","CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-02","text":"Relation has the same being as essence and yet is really opposed to another relation; the transition from signified opposition to real distinction remains the principal metaphysical joint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:D3","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-03","text":"The definition of person through individual substance and the determination of divine person through subsisting relation do not immediately coincide; the connection depends on the identity of relation with essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A3","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-04","text":"The transition from two processions to four relations is clearly given, but the distribution of relations with respect to the constitution of persons is less explicitly determined in the material of this group.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:D4","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:FL-05","text":"The analogy from the non-subsisting human word to the divine Word and from created person to divine person is necessary, but the mode of proportion is not fully demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MP-01","text":"Procession changes when it is transferred from causal egress to intelligible emanation within the agent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_19:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MP-02","text":"Relation changes when it is advanced from inhering accident to the very being of essence and then to subsisting hypostasis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_21:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MP-03","text":"The individual changes when matter ceases to be the principle of individuation and relational incommunicability assumes the distinctive function.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_21:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:HSI-01","text":"The hidden image is a machine of simple act which, without dividing itself, produces through internal origin opposite references and condenses them into personal subsistence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:A11","CH_GGVC_P_20:A6","CH_GGVC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:HSI-02","text":"The personal being within this machine is not a closed atom, but a complete and incommunicable supposit whose distinction is constituted by relation of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_21:A4","CH_GGVC_P_21:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:HSI-03","text":"The time of this system is order without succession: principle and that which proceeds are ordered, but no becoming, temporal before, or change is admitted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_20:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:HSI-04","text":"The system proceeds by subtraction: false created modes are successively removed until the account of origin, reference, and incommunicability can be applied to simple reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_21:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B01","text":"The reconstruction of this group suffices if immanent procession, real relation identical with essence, relative opposition, and personal subsistence are retained together.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the chain that converts internal origin into real reference, reference into opposition, and essential relation into subsisting person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B03","text":"The exact relation between the quaternary inventory of relations and personal constitution remains less determined, especially where the terms signify origin and relation reciprocally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B04","text":"The residual fragility consists in a twofold analogical transition: from the acts of intellect and will to real processions, and from individual substance to subsisting relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B05","text":"The coherence of the present reconstruction is preserved because it retains the generative order of procession, relation, and person, not a merely chapter-based order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_21:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_10:MRT-B06","text":"Axiomatic reduction is resisted by the residual asymmetry of names: the procession of Love is named less properly, and the terminology of relation and origin is not everywhere perfectly separated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_19:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_20:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_10@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_10:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 28–30","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 27 · Prima pars · Quaestio 28 · Prima pars · Quaestio 29"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 31–33","order":11,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_22","CH_GGVC_P_23","CH_GGVC_P_24"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_11@R001","sha256":"1b338cd643554e383c71697ef0eee1142918de6cf6e8eda466cbd9ecb8d0fb76","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-01","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo una essentia simplicissima tres personas vere distinctas patiatur, numeretur et nominetur, cum origines personales nec ex creaturis demonstrentur nec per categorias communes sine correctione exprimantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_23:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-02","text":"Systema unitatem essentialem, pluralitatem personalem et mediationem notionalem velut ordines formaliter distinctos sed coordinatos constituit: oppositio originis personas constituit, disciplina significationis earum enuntiationem custodit, revelatio accessum aperit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_23:A1","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio fit metaphysico-semantica et epistemica, quia distinctio in re, distinctio in signo et distinctio in modo cognoscendi nec confunduntur nec seorsum operari possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_23:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-04","text":"Motus a contradictione apparente simplicitatis et pluralitatis transit ad relationem subsistentem, inde ad sermonem typis distinctum, demum ad limitem rationis et mediationem revelationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_23:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-05","text":"Progressus est spiralis et cumulativus: quod ontologice per relationes statuitur semantice regulatur, epistemice limitatur, deinde per notiones ad ordinem relationum redit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_24:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-06","text":"Clausura non est demonstratio exhaustiva mysterii, sed stabilis regimen distinctionum, numerationum, ambituum et consequentiarum, quo unitas et pluralitas simul dicuntur sine multiplicatione aut absorptione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Una essentia communicabilis et tres personae per origines distinctae constituunt duplicem ordinem irreducibilem unitatis essentialis et pluralitatis personalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Persona divina est relatio subsistens, non essentia multiplicata neque individuum per materiam aut formam separatam constitutum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Sola oppositio relativa distinctionem realem personalem efficit; distinctio absoluta vel essentialis pluralitatem divinam generare nequit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Ordo originum cum regula oppositionis et non-oppositionis clausuram ternariam producit: relationes oppositae personas distinguunt, non oppositae in eadem persona concurrunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A5","CH_GGVC_P_24:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Numerus in divinis secundum obiectum numeratum typatur: unum ad essentiam, tres ad personas, quattuor ad relationes vel proprietates, quinque ad notiones pertinent, nullo ordine quantitatem essentiae metiente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A11","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Essentia ut quid, persona ut quis et notio ut quo tres functiones significationis ordinant, quibus natura communis, suppositum distinctum et ratio cognoscendi separantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A8","CH_GGVC_P_23:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Sermo trinitarius est apparatus operatorius typis et ambitu regulatus; grammatica structuram divinam non imitatur directe, sed eam sub distinctionibus determinatis exprimit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A7","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Cognitio naturalis ex effectibus ad essentiam et virtutem creativam communem pervenit, sed ante distinctiones originum personalium terminatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A2","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Ratio post revelationem a probatione radicis ad congruentiam internam et defensionem non-impossibilitatis transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A5","CH_GGVC_P_24:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Notiones sunt rationes cognoscendi personas quae relationes reales significant, non res additae, supposita nova aut partes divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A9","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Totum systema medium stabile quaerit inter singularitatem personalem quae personas absorbet et pluralitatem essentialem quae divinitatem multiplicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Revelata distinctio personarum reordinat non solum cognitionem internam Dei, sed etiam creationem per Verbum et amorem atque salutem per Filium et Spiritum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-01","text":"Relatio identitatem ontologicam retinet, sed functionem mutat: primo personam constituit, deinde sermonem de suppositis regit, postremo per notionem fit obiectum cognitionis abstractae sine amissione realitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-02","text":"Numerus ab oppositionibus personalibus ad nomen Trinitatis et inde ad taxonomiam notionum migrat; constantia eius non in una arithmetica, sed in congruentia inter numerationem et obiectum numeratum consistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A11","CH_GGVC_P_23:A4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-03","text":"Communitas mutatur a communitate rationis nominis personae ad communicabilitatem essentiae et communitatem operationis, neque hae formae communitatis in rem universalem unam coalescunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A15","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-04","text":"Simplicitas, initio impedimentum pluralitatis apparens, fit regula positiva qua proprietates abstractae, relationes reales et pluralitas semantica sine compositione ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-05","text":"Negatio a remota quantitate ad operatoriam exclusionem et demum ad terminum cognitionis transit; sic quod primo tantum removet paulatim structuram positivam typorum et ambituum constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_23:A8","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-06","text":"Ratio naturalis non evanescit cum potestas demonstrandi removetur, sed ad congruentiam, defensionem et disciplinam consequentiarum transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_24:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-07","text":"Oppositio Arianismi et Sabellianismi a limite lexicali ad normam inferentialem de haeresi migrat: error non iam solo vocabulo, sed consequentia intellecta et pertinacia aestimatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-01","text":"Enumeratio paternitatis, filiationis, spirationis et processionis manet apparatus localis; hoc gradu amplificatur in regulam generalem qua ordo originum simul ternarium personarum et quinarium notionum producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:D2","CH_GGVC_P_24:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-02","text":"Discrimen masculini alius et neutri aliud est instrumentum locale; sursum amplificatur in principium quod grammatica secundum genus obiecti ontologici typanda est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-03","text":"Distinctio inter solus categorematice et syncategorematice acceptum localiter locutiones exclusivas corrigit; hoc gradu fit generalis doctrina ambitus operatorum theologicorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A8","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-04","text":"Quinque notiones, quattuor relationes et tres notiones personales taxonomiae inferiores sunt; structura praesens ex eis regulam elicit quod pluralitates formales eidem rei imputatae non sunt eiusdem generis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-05","text":"Impossibilitas demonstrationis naturalis localiter ad cognitionem Trinitatis pertinet; hoc gradu ea cum disciplina significationis coniungitur, ut limites cognoscendi simul limites licitae translationis constituant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:D2","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-06","text":"Oppositio plana inter unum et multa superatur: unitas, pluralitas et cognitio non sunt gradus unius scalae, sed ordines coordinati quorum confusio contradictionem apparentem generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-01","text":"Systema excludit essentias, substantias, partes aut mensuras multiplicatas; pluralitas personalis nullum totum compositum introducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_22:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-02","text":"Excluditur tam singularitas personalis quam confusio suppositorum: essentia una non est persona sola neque solitudo divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-03","text":"Categoriae creaturarum, genera grammatica et quantitates non possunt in divinam structuram sine conversione semantica transferri.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-04","text":"Effectus creati, appropriationes essentiales et similitudines mentis non constituunt demonstrationem originum personalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-05","text":"Notiones nec personae additae nec res seorsum numerandae sunt; multiplicatio rationum cognoscendi multiplicationem rei non infert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_24:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-06","text":"Nec rationes infirmae pro demonstrationibus nec omnis dissensio notionalis pro haeresi haberi potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet distinctionem realem semper differentiam essentiae aut suppositi substantialiter separati postulare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_23:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet unitatem et pluralitatem in eodem axe formali consistere, quasi alterum alterius negatio absoluta sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet vocabula theologica veritatem retinere independenter a significatione, situ syntactico et ambitu exclusionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet causalitatem creaturarum vitam intrinsecam causae exhauste manifestare aut cognitionem essentialem continuo in cognitionem personalem produci.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet distinctionem rationis aut meram fictionem esse aut necessario compositionem realem inferre.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet statum doctrinalem propositionis ex sola forma verbali constare; nexus inferentialis, cognitio consequentiae et pertinacia ad eius aestimationem pertinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSA-01","text":"Possibilitas plenae possessionis naturalis vitae personalis divinae indisponibilis est; effectus causam communem indicant, sed origines personales occultas relinquunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSA-02","text":"Nullum genus, universale, totum aut spatium superius admittitur intra quod essentia et personae partes comparabiles fierent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSA-03","text":"Systema circa absentiam identitatis immediatae inter esse, dici et cognosci ordinatur; inter ordines semper requiritur translatio disciplinata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSA-04","text":"Inadmissibilis est electio inter Deum ut monadem solitariam et deos essentialiter separatos; attractor systematis utrumque extremum antecedit et excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-01","text":"Quia persona est relatio subsistens et lexicon secundum essentiam atque suppositum regulatur, grammatica trinitaria non est vestis extrinseca ontologiae, sed instrumentum eius differentias sine compositione conservans.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-02","CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_22:A1","CH_GGVC_P_23:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-02","text":"Coniunctio numeri transcendentis, ternarii personalis et taxonomiae notionalis efficit ut omnis numeratio divina prius obiectum suum formaliter definiat quam unitates computet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-05","CL_GGVC_11:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_22:A11","CH_GGVC_P_23:A4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-03","text":"Communitas rationis nominis personae et status notionalis rationum cognoscendi demonstrant communitatem conceptualem posse fundamentum reale habere sine re universali addita.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-06","CL_GGVC_11:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_22:A15","CH_GGVC_P_24:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-04","text":"Terminus cognitionis naturalis structuram ontologicam sequitur: quia actio creativa omnibus personis communis est, effectus essentiam communem manifestant, non origines quibus personae distinguuntur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-01","CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-05","text":"Negationes quantitatis, diversitatis essentialis et probationis infirmae simul architecturam positivam typorum ontologicorum, semanticorum et epistemicorum producunt.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-05","CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_22:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_23:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-06","text":"Auctoritas revelata regulam semanticam non suspendit, sicut ratio mysterium non constituit; utraque in expositione congrua et defensione non-impossibilitatis coordinatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CL_GGVC_11:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A6","CH_GGVC_P_24:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-07","text":"Invariantes ontologicae orthodoxiae stabiles manent, sed status haeresis historice mutari potest secundum manifestationem consequentiae et pertinaciam; stabilitas doctrinae igitur iudicium immobile non postulat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CL_GGVC_11:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_23:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-01","text":"Realitas divina admittit identitatem essentiae et differentiam personarum ut formas non competitivas: distinctio augetur sine partitione, identitas servatur sine absorptione.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-01","CL_GGVC_11:GA-03","CL_GGVC_11:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_22:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-02","text":"Sermo theologicus fit calculus typorum in quo quid, quis, quo, genus grammaticale, numerus et exclusio diversas operationes exercent neque inter se sine regula commutari possunt.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-06","CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-03","text":"Absconditas personarum origines non contingentia effectuum, sed communitas causalitatis divinae producit: quod Deus communiter agit essentialem unitatem manifestat et personalem distinctionem celat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","CL_GGVC_11:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-04","text":"Numeri theologici non participant unum campum arithmeticum simpliciter; quisque est index relationis inter rationem numerandi et ordinem rei numeratae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-04","CL_GGVC_11:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_22:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-05","text":"Ratio, potestate constitutiva mysterii privata, fit instrumentum locale validius: congruentiam examinat, impossibilitatem repellit et consequentias doctrinales ordinat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","CL_GGVC_11:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_24:D4","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-06","text":"Subiectum doctrinale non est spectator propositionum solitarum, sed agens historice responsabile cuius cognitio nexus inferentialis et pertinacia statum erroris transformant.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-09","CL_GGVC_11:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-01","text":"Simplicitas → apparentia impossibilitatis pluralitatis → relatio subsistens → pluralitas personalis → disciplina sermonis → simplicitas iterum servata: primus circuitus obstructionem in machinam convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_22:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-02","text":"Origo → relatio → oppositio → persona → numerus → notio → cognitio originis constituit circuitum quo initium ontologicum per mediationem semanticam ad se redit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A14","CH_GGVC_P_22:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-03","text":"Ternarius personarum non terminat numerationem, sed eam in quattuor relationes et quinque notiones amplificat; proliferatio tamen typis distincta ad ternarium personalem recurrit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A3","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-04","text":"Negatio quantitatis → distinctio ambitus → terminus cognitionis: exclusionum accumulatio non vacuum relinquit, sed positivam distributionem rei, signi et accessus efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-05","text":"Terminus demonstrationis fit via amplificationis: ratio a probatione removetur, sed ad congruentiam, defensionem et iudicium consequentiarum reactivatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_24:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-06","text":"Attractor totius structurae est una essentia in tribus personis non naturaliter demonstrabilis sed rationabiliter ordinabilis; circa hunc attractorem ontologia, grammatica et epistemologia convergunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B01","text":"Una essentia communicabilis + virtus creativa communis → effectus essentialem causalitatem manifestant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B02","text":"Effectus essentialem causam manifestantes + origines intrinsecae non manifestatae → terminus naturalis cognitionis ante distinctionem personalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A2","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B03","text":"Revelatio originum + modus humanus significandi → introductio notionum tamquam mediationum cognoscibilium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B04","text":"Origines generationis et processionis + subsistentia relationum → constitutio personarum non essentialiter multiplicatarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A4","CH_GGVC_P_22:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B05","text":"Oppositio relativa → distinctio personalis; non-oppositio → concursus relationum; utraque simul → clausura trium personarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A5","CH_GGVC_P_22:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B06","text":"Distinctio essentiae, personae et notionis → numeri et vocabula secundum obiecta propria typantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A8","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B07","text":"Applicatio ambitus syntactici + examinatio consequentiae fidei → locutiones reguntur et errores secundum implicationem, cognitionem atque pertinaciam discernuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A9","CH_GGVC_P_24:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B08","text":"Exitus est apparatus semanticus qui distinctionem personalem realem sine compositione, pluralitatem formalem sine multiplicatione et rationem utilem sine demonstratione mysterii retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:AFM-B01","text":"Simplicitas apparenter exclusoria → relatio subsistens → oppositio originis → tres personae → numeratio typata → disciplina nominum et exclusionis → terminus cognitionis naturalis → revelatio → notiones → iudicium consequentiarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:AFM-B02","text":"Repudiatio quantitatis et universalitatis → repudiatio grammaticae ontologice immediatae → repudiatio demonstrationis naturalis → restitutio positiva ordinum essentiae, personae, notionis, ambitus et auctoritatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-01","text":"Distinctio divina a multiplicatione substantiarum ad relationem subsistentem transfertur, ita ut differentia ontologica sine partitione cogitari possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_22:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-02","text":"Numerus a quantitate mensurante ad operationem formaliter typatam reclassificatur, quae diversas pluralitates sine confusione distribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-03","text":"Grammatica ab imagine directa rei ad apparatum ambitus et participationis praedicati reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-04","text":"Cognitio Dei in campum essentialem causaliter accessibilem et campum originum personalium revelatum dividitur; ratio vicissim in probationem, congruentiam et defensionem distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-05","text":"Revelatio Trinitatis a notitia interna separata ad principium reordinans creationem, libertatem causalitatis et salutem extenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_24:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-06","text":"Lectio theologica fit inspectio typi obiecti, modi significandi, ambitus operatoris, fontis epistemici et consequentiae doctrinalis, non mera acceptio propositionis solitariae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A9","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei personas, ternarium, nomina distinctionis, dictiones exclusivas, cognitionem naturalem, notiones et statum erroris examinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis origines, relationes, oppositiones, supposita et notiones in unam distributionem ordinat, qua realitas personalis cognoscibiliter sed non compositive exprimitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus sermonem et rationem instrumenta custodiendi medium inter multiplicationem essentialem, absorptionem personalem, fideismum inertem et rationalismum demonstrativum efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis relationes aeternas atque non successivas cum historia mutabili manifestationis errorum componit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus propriam thesim efficit: per mutationes categoriae, distinctiones grammaticales et limites argumentationis textus unitatem sine aequatione differentiarum producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-01","text":"Regula qua relationes non oppositae eidem personae conveniunt ternario necessaria est, sed fundamentum eius intra hanc structuram praesupponitur potius quam demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-02","text":"Genus grammaticale magnum pondus ontologicum fert, quamquam necessitas metaphysica correspondentiae inter masculinum, neutrum, suppositum et essentiam independenter non stabilitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-03","text":"Relationes significatae realiter in Deo sunt, notiones autem rationes cognoscendi dicuntur; identitas rei et distinctio significationis regulam conversionis incompletam relinquunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-04","text":"Locutio exclusiva secundum usum proprium falsa, secundum auctoritatem et expositionem pia vera fieri potest; exceptio contextus normam semanticam simul servat et intendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-05","text":"Veritas fidei immutabilis manet dum status haeresis historice mutatur; systema hanc tensionem per cognitionem consequentiae et pertinaciam administrat, non dissolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_24:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MP-01","text":"Punctum mutationis primum est transitus a substantia multiplicata ad relationem subsistentem, quo pluralitas ab essentia ad originem transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_22:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MP-02","text":"Punctum mutationis secundum est transitus a numero quantitativo ad numerationes typatas essentiae, personarum, relationum et notionum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MP-03","text":"Punctum mutationis tertium est conversio solus ab attributo solitudinis in operatorem ambitus qui consortium praedicati distribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A8","CH_GGVC_P_23:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MP-04","text":"Punctum mutationis quartum est remotio rationis a probatione mysterii et restitutio eius in congruentiam, defensionem et disciplinam inferentialem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-01","text":"Imago occulta est tabula coordinatarum typatarum: essentia, persona et notio axes constituunt, dum numerus, genus et exclusio velut portae ambitum propositionum regunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_23:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum intra hanc machinam fit interpres disciplinatus qui auctoritatem recipit, rationem localiter exercet et modum cognitionis suae in omni enuntiatione agnoscit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A6","CH_GGVC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-03","text":"Tempus duplex implicatur: origines divinae successionem non habent, sed cognitio consequentiarum doctrinalium et status erroris historice mutantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-04","text":"Causalitas externa communis personas non distinguit, dum causalitas originis intrinseca earum ordinem constituit; navigatio possibilis inter hos campos multiplicationem Arianam et absorptionem Sabellianam vitat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A3","CH_GGVC_P_24:A14","CH_GGVC_P_23:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-05","text":"Persona apparet non ut atomus substantialis, sed ut nodus subsistens originis et oppositionis, cuius identitas relatione constituitur et tamen unum esse divinum non dividit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de una essentia, relatione subsistente, oppositione relativa, numeratione typata, distinctione quid–quis–quo et limite cognitionis naturalis sufficiunt ad structuram huius gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi relatio subsistens et oppositio relativa cum distinctione probationis et congruentiae coniunguntur; ibi ontologia et epistemologia mutuo se determinant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B03","text":"Minus determinata manet derivatio completa quattuor relationum et duarum processionum, quia ordo earum ex doctrinis praemissis importatur et hic potius ordinatur quam generatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B04","text":"Fragilitas maxima in conversionibus inter nomen commune et rem singularem, relationem realem et notionem cognitivam, regulam semanticam et expositionem auctoritative admissam consistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B05","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat, si ab unitate apparenter exclusoria per relationem, significationem et limitem rationis ad mysterium revelatum ordinabile sed naturaliter non possidendum procedit; ipsa revelatio reductioni axiomaticae terminaliter resistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_24:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171349742225Z_065d6670","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 31–33","source_sha256":"1b338cd643554e383c71697ef0eee1142918de6cf6e8eda466cbd9ecb8d0fb76","sha256":"47de3489cf4832a333b44dc1e7fb4abf0e62b7547319214d785fb9f03125578a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:13:49.743962+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-01","text":"The central question is how one most simple essence admits, is numbered, and is named as three truly distinct persons, when the personal origins are neither demonstrated from creatures nor expressed through common categories without correction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_23:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-02","text":"The system establishes essential unity, personal plurality, and notional mediation as formally distinct but coordinated orders: opposition of origin constitutes the persons, the discipline of signification safeguards their enunciation, and revelation opens access.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_23:A1","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-03","text":"The argument proceeds metaphysically-semantically and epistemically, because distinction in reality, distinction in sign, and distinction in the mode of knowing are neither confused nor able to operate separately.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_23:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-04","text":"The movement passes from the apparent contradiction of simplicity and plurality to subsisting relation, thence to discourse distinct in its types, and finally to the limit of reason and the mediation of revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_23:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-05","text":"The progression is spiral and cumulative: what is established ontologically through relations is regulated semantically, limited epistemically, and then returns through notions to the order of relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_24:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BAS-06","text":"The closure is not an exhaustive demonstration of the mystery, but a stable governance of distinctions, enumerations, scopes, and consequences, by which unity and plurality are simultaneously asserted without multiplication or absorption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] One communicable essence and three persons distinct through origins constitute a double irreducible order of essential unity and personal plurality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] A divine person is a subsisting relation, not a multiplied essence nor an individual constituted through matter or separate form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Relative opposition alone effects real personal distinction; absolute or essential distinction cannot generate divine plurality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The order of origins, together with the rule of opposition and non-opposition, produces a ternary closure: opposed relations distinguish persons; non-opposed relations concur in the same person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A5","CH_GGVC_P_24:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Number in divine matters is typed according to the object numbered: one pertains to essence, three to persons, four to relations or properties, five to notions, with no order measuring the quantity of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A11","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Essence as what, person as who, and notion as whereby order three functions of signification, by which common nature, distinct supposit, and manner of knowing are separated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A8","CH_GGVC_P_23:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Trinitarian discourse is an operative apparatus regulated by types and scope; grammar does not directly imitate divine structure, but expresses it under determinate distinctions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A7","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Natural knowledge reaches from effects to the common essence and creative power, but terminates before the distinctions of personal origins.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A2","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] After revelation, reason is transferred from proof at the root to internal congruity and the defense of non-impossibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A5","CH_GGVC_P_24:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Notions are manners of knowing persons that signify real relations, not added things, new supposits, or divine parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A9","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] The whole system seeks a stable middle between personal singularity that absorbs the persons and essential plurality that multiplies divinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] The revealed distinction of persons reorders not only internal knowledge of God, but also creation through the Word and love, and salvation through the Son and Spirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-01","text":"Relation retains ontological identity but changes function: first it constitutes the person, then governs discourse concerning supposits, and finally through notion becomes the object of abstract knowledge without loss of reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-02","text":"Number migrates from personal oppositions to the name of the Trinity and thence to the taxonomy of notions; its constancy consists not in a single arithmetic but in congruity between enumeration and the object enumerated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A11","CH_GGVC_P_23:A4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-03","text":"Community changes from the community of the concept of the name person to the communicability of essence and community of operation, and these forms of community do not coalesce into one universal thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A15","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-04","text":"Simplicity, initially an apparent impediment to plurality, becomes the positive rule by which abstract properties, real relations, and semantic plurality are ordered without composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-05","text":"Negation passes from the removal of quantity to operative exclusion and finally to the limit of knowledge; thus what first merely removes gradually constitutes the positive structure of types and scopes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_23:A8","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-06","text":"Natural reason does not vanish when the power to demonstrate is removed, but is transferred to congruity, defense, and the discipline of consequences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_24:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RMD-07","text":"The opposition of Arianism and Sabellianism migrates from a lexical boundary to an inferential norm concerning heresy: error is assessed no longer by word alone, but by understood consequence and pertinacity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-01","text":"The enumeration of paternity, filiation, spiration, and procession remains a local apparatus; at this level it is amplified into a general rule by which the order of origins simultaneously produces the ternary of persons and the quinary of notions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:D2","CH_GGVC_P_24:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-02","text":"The distinction between masculine alius and neuter aliud is a local instrument; upwards it is amplified into the principle that grammar must be typed according to the kind of ontological object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-03","text":"The distinction between solus taken categorematically and syncategorematically locally corrects exclusive expressions; at this level it becomes a general doctrine of the scope of theological operators.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A8","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-04","text":"Five notions, four relations, and three personal notions are lower taxonomies; the present structure draws from them the rule that formal pluralities attributed to the same thing are not of the same kind.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-05","text":"The impossibility of natural demonstration locally pertains to knowledge of the Trinity; at this level it is joined to the discipline of signification, so that the limits of knowing simultaneously constitute the limits of licit translation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:D2","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:CGD-06","text":"The flat opposition between one and many is overcome: unity, plurality, and knowledge are not degrees of one scale, but coordinated orders whose confusion generates apparent contradiction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes multiplied essences, substances, parts, or measures; personal plurality introduces no composite whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_22:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-02","text":"Both personal singularity and confusion of supposits are excluded: one essence is neither a single person nor divine solitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-03","text":"Categories of creatures, grammatical genders, and quantities cannot be transferred into divine structure without semantic conversion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-04","text":"Created effects, essential appropriations, and likenesses of mind do not constitute a demonstration of personal origins.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-05","text":"Notions are neither added persons nor things to be separately numbered; multiplication of manners of knowing does not entail multiplication of the thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_24:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:GNX-06","text":"Neither weak arguments may be regarded as demonstrations nor every notional disagreement as heresy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that real distinction always requires a difference of essence or a substantially separate supposit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_23:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that unity and plurality stand on the same formal axis, as though one were the absolute negation of the other.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that theological words retain truth independently of signification, syntactic position, and scope of exclusion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that the causality of creatures exhaustively manifests the intrinsic life of the cause or that essential knowledge is continuously produced into personal knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that a distinction of reason is either mere fiction or necessarily entails real composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that the doctrinal status of a proposition consists in verbal form alone; inferential nexus, knowledge of consequence, and pertinacity pertain to its assessment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSA-01","text":"The possibility of full natural possession of divine personal life is unavailable; effects indicate the common cause, but leave personal origins hidden.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSA-02","text":"No genus, universal, whole, or higher space is admitted within which essence and persons might become comparable parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSA-03","text":"The system is ordered around the absence of immediate identity between being, being said, and being known; disciplined translation is always required between the orders.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSA-04","text":"The choice between God as a solitary monad and gods essentially separated is inadmissible; the system's attractor precedes and excludes both extremes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-01","text":"Because person is a subsisting relation and the lexicon is regulated according to essence and supposit, Trinitarian grammar is not an extrinsic garment of ontology, but its instrument for preserving differences without composition.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-02","CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_22:A1","CH_GGVC_P_23:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-02","text":"The conjunction of transcendent number, personal ternary, and notional taxonomy ensures that every divine enumeration formally defines its object before counting units.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-05","CL_GGVC_11:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_22:A11","CH_GGVC_P_23:A4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-03","text":"The community of the concept of the name person and the notional status of manners of knowing show that conceptual community can have a real foundation without an added universal thing.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-06","CL_GGVC_11:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_22:A15","CH_GGVC_P_24:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-04","text":"The limit of natural knowledge follows ontological structure: because creative action is common to all persons, effects manifest the common essence, not the origins by which the persons are distinguished.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-01","CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-05","text":"The negations of quantity, essential diversity, and weak proof jointly produce a positive architecture of ontological, semantic, and epistemic types.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-05","CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_22:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_23:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-06","text":"Revealed authority does not suspend the semantic rule, just as reason does not constitute the mystery; both are coordinated in fitting exposition and defense of non-impossibility.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CL_GGVC_11:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A6","CH_GGVC_P_24:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:XD-07","text":"The ontological invariants of orthodoxy remain stable, but the status of heresy can change historically according to the manifestation of consequence and pertinacity; doctrinal stability therefore does not require an immobile judgment.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CL_GGVC_11:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_23:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-01","text":"Divine reality admits identity of essence and difference of persons as non-competitive forms: distinction is increased without partition, identity preserved without absorption.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-01","CL_GGVC_11:GA-03","CL_GGVC_11:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_22:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-02","text":"Theological discourse becomes a calculus of types in which what, who, whereby, grammatical gender, number, and exclusion exercise diverse operations and cannot be interchanged without rule.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-06","CL_GGVC_11:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-03","text":"The hiddenness of personal origins is produced not by the contingency of effects, but by the community of divine causality: what God acts commonly manifests essential unity and conceals personal distinction.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","CL_GGVC_11:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-04","text":"Theological numbers do not simply participate in one arithmetical field; each is an index of the relation between the rationale of numbering and the order of the numbered thing.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-04","CL_GGVC_11:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_22:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-05","text":"Reason, deprived of constitutive power over the mystery, becomes a stronger local instrument: it examines congruity, repels impossibility, and orders doctrinal consequences.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-08","CL_GGVC_11:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_24:D4","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:BSD-06","text":"The doctrinal subject is not a spectator of isolated propositions, but a historically responsible agent whose knowledge of inferential nexus and pertinacity transform the status of error.","refs":["CL_GGVC_11:GA-09","CL_GGVC_11:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-01","text":"Simplicity → appearance of the impossibility of plurality → subsisting relation → personal plurality → discipline of discourse → simplicity preserved again: the first circuit converts obstruction into a machine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_22:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-02","text":"Origin → relation → opposition → person → number → notion → knowledge of origin constitutes a circuit by which the ontological beginning returns to itself through semantic mediation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A14","CH_GGVC_P_22:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-03","text":"The ternary of persons does not terminate enumeration, but amplifies it into four relations and five notions; the proliferation, however, distinct in its types, returns to the personal ternary.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A3","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-04","text":"Negation of quantity → distinction of scope → limit of knowledge: the accumulation of exclusions does not leave a void, but effects a positive distribution of thing, sign, and access.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-05","text":"The limit of demonstration becomes a way of amplification: reason is removed from proof, but reactivated for congruity, defense, and judgment of consequences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_24:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:RLE-06","text":"The attractor of the whole structure is one essence in three persons, not naturally demonstrable but rationally orderable; ontology, grammar, and epistemology converge around this attractor.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B01","text":"One communicable essence + common creative power → effects manifest essential causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A1","CH_GGVC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B02","text":"Effects manifesting the essential cause + unmanifested intrinsic origins → natural limit of knowledge before personal distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A2","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B03","text":"Revelation of origins + human mode of signifying → introduction of notions as knowable mediations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B04","text":"Origins of generation and procession + subsistence of relations → constitution of persons not essentially multiplied.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A4","CH_GGVC_P_22:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B05","text":"Relative opposition → personal distinction; non-opposition → concurrence of relations; both together → closure of three persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:A5","CH_GGVC_P_22:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B06","text":"Distinction of essence, person, and notion → numbers and terms are typed according to their proper objects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A8","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B07","text":"Application of syntactic scope + examination of consequence for faith → expressions are governed and errors are discerned according to implication, knowledge, and pertinacity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A9","CH_GGVC_P_24:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FGS-B08","text":"The outcome is a semantic apparatus that retains real personal distinction without composition, formal plurality without multiplication, and useful reason without demonstration of the mystery.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:AFM-B01","text":"Apparently exclusive simplicity → subsisting relation → opposition of origin → three persons → typed enumeration → discipline of names and exclusion → limit of natural knowledge → revelation → notions → judgment of consequences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:AFM-B02","text":"Rejection of quantity and universality → rejection of ontologically immediate grammar → rejection of natural demonstration → positive restoration of the orders of essence, person, notion, scope, and authority.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_24:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-01","text":"Divine distinction is transferred from multiplication of substances to subsisting relation, so that ontological difference can be thought without partition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_22:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-02","text":"Number is reclassified from measuring quantity into a formally typed operation that distributes diverse pluralities without confusion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-03","text":"Grammar is reclassified from a direct image of the thing into an apparatus of scope and participation in the predicate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-04","text":"Knowledge of God is divided into an essential field causally accessible and a revealed field of personal origins; reason in turn is distinguished into proof, congruity, and defense.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-05","text":"The revelation of the Trinity is extended from separate internal information into a principle reordering creation, freedom of causality, and salvation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_24:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MME-06","text":"Theological reading becomes an inspection of object type, mode of signifying, operator scope, epistemic source, and doctrinal consequence, not mere acceptance of an isolated proposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A9","CH_GGVC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level examines persons, the ternary, names of distinction, exclusive expressions, natural knowledge, notions, and the status of error.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level orders origins, relations, oppositions, supposits, and notions into one distribution, by which personal reality is expressed knowably but non-compositely.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level makes discourse and reason instruments for preserving the middle between essential multiplication, personal absorption, inert fideism, and demonstrative rationalism.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level combines eternal and non-successive relations with the mutable history of the manifestation of errors.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level enacts its own thesis: through changes of category, grammatical distinctions, and limits of argumentation, the text produces unity without equating differences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-01","text":"The rule by which non-opposed relations belong to the same person is necessary for the ternary, but its foundation is presupposed rather than demonstrated within this structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-02","text":"Grammatical gender bears great ontological weight, although the metaphysical necessity of correspondence between masculine, neuter, supposit, and essence is not independently established.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_23:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-03","text":"The relations signified are really in God, while notions are called manners of knowing; identity of thing and distinction of signification leave an incomplete rule of conversion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-04","text":"An exclusive expression false according to its proper use can become piously true according to authority and exposition; the exception of context simultaneously preserves and intensifies the semantic norm.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_23:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:FL-05","text":"The truth of faith remains immutable while the status of heresy changes historically; the system manages this tension through knowledge of consequence and pertinacity, rather than dissolving it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_24:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point is the transition from multiplied substance to subsisting relation, by which plurality is transferred from essence to origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_22:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point is the transition from quantitative number to typed enumerations of essence, persons, relations, and notions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point is the conversion of solus from an attribute of solitude into a scope operator that distributes participation in the predicate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:A8","CH_GGVC_P_23:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MP-04","text":"The fourth mutation point is the removal of reason from proof of the mystery and its restoration in congruity, defense, and inferential discipline.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_24:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-01","text":"The hidden image is a map of typed coordinates: essence, person, and notion constitute axes, while number, gender, and exclusion govern the scope of propositions as gates.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_23:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-02","text":"Within this machine, the subject becomes a disciplined interpreter who receives authority, exercises reason locally, and recognizes the mode of his knowledge in every assertion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A6","CH_GGVC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-03","text":"A double time is implied: divine origins have no succession, but knowledge of doctrinal consequences and the status of error change historically.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_24:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-04","text":"Common external causality does not distinguish the persons, while intrinsic causality of origin constitutes their order; navigation between these fields avoids Arian multiplication and Sabellian absorption.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:A3","CH_GGVC_P_24:A14","CH_GGVC_P_23:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:HSI-05","text":"The person appears not as a substantial atom, but as a subsisting node of origin and opposition, whose identity is constituted by relation and yet does not divide the one divine being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_24:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms concerning one essence, subsisting relation, relative opposition, typed enumeration, the distinction what–who–whereby, and the limit of natural knowledge suffice to reconstruct the structure of this corpus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B02","text":"The structure is firmest where subsisting relation and relative opposition are joined with the distinction of proof and congruity; there ontology and epistemology mutually determine one another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B03","text":"The complete derivation of four relations and two processions remains less determinate, because their order is imported from prior doctrines and is here ordered rather than generated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B04","text":"The greatest fragility consists in conversions between common name and singular thing, real relation and cognitive notion, semantic rule and authoritatively admitted exposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_23:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_11:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement if it proceeds from apparently exclusive unity through relation, signification, and the limit of reason to a revealed mystery that is orderable but not naturally possessable; revelation itself ultimately resists axiomatic reduction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_22:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_24:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_24:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_11@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_11:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 31–33","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 30 · Prima pars · Quaestio 31 · Prima pars · Quaestio 32"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 34–36","order":12,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_25","CH_GGVC_P_26","CH_GGVC_P_27"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_12@R001","sha256":"edd6fe212a2c6204653210438ed2087414ccce1d2b0c0990dd99991abc7c9af6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo Pater, Verbum et Imago personaliter praedicentur, dum unitas naturae, aeternitas processionum et aequalitas personarum integrae manent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis statuit nomina personalia constitui per relationes originis subsistentes, non per partitionem essentiae neque per proprietates creaturales accidentales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A17","CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio semantico-metaphysica vocabula primum purificat, deinde eorum rationes formales restringit, postremo eas secundum modos processionis personaliter distribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-04","text":"Modus creaturalis impositionis removetur, sed res significata retinetur et ad perfectionem aeternam relationis originariae restituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A2","CH_GGVC_P_26:A1","CH_GGVC_P_27:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-05","text":"Motus procedit a Patre ut principio non de principio ad Filium ut Verbum procedens, deinde ad eundem Filium ut Imaginem perfectam et ad creaturas ut similitudines participatas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A14","CH_GGVC_P_26:D4","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-06","text":"Progressio est spiralis: eadem ratio originis redit, sed successive fit principium asymmetriae, criterium personalitatis, forma generationis intellectualis et conditio imaginis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:D1","CH_GGVC_P_26:D1","CH_GGVC_P_27:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-07","text":"Probatio cumulativa excludit temporalitatem, separationem, causalitatem creaturalem et similitudinem indeterminatam, ut asymmetria realis sine hierarchia perficiatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-08","text":"Clausura constituit unum Patrem innascibilem et unum Filium naturalem qui, ut Verbum et Imago, Patrem perfecte exprimit atque creaturas sine multiplicatione verbi repraesentat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Veritas nominis divini pendet a distinctione inter rem significatam et modum creaturalem quo vocabulum imponitur vel communiter intelligitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A2","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] In divinis ratio originis distinguit personas, dum essentia communicata una et indivisa manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A17","CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Origo divina est realis et asymmetrica, sed successionem temporalem, minorationem et subiectionem non inducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_25:A5","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Relatio originis in natura divina non accidit personae iam constitutae, sed ipsa subsistit ut persona.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Pater constituitur ut principium non de principio, cui paternitas generationem completam et actum dicendi personalem attribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A14","CH_GGVC_P_25:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Processio intellectualis divina est generatio, ideo conceptus subsistens procedens est idem Filius sub ratione Verbi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Verbum et Imago non duas proprietates filiales addunt, sed eandem nativitatem exprimunt ut processionem intellectualem et similitudinem originatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Imago proprie dicta requirit non solam similitudinem specificam, sed processionem a principio cuius similitudinem exprimit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Communicatio eiusdem naturae personalia nomina non distribuit; propria ratio processionis determinat cur Verbum sit Imago, amor autem non eadem ratione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Filius naturalis est medium formale quo filiatio, expressio et imago creaturarum ordinantur ut participationes derivatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A13","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Unitas divinae intellectionis unum Verbum constituit quod Patrem et multitudinem creaturarum aeternaliter exprimit sine multiplicatione personali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Unitas naturae et distinctio per modos originis claudunt systema contra pluralitatem principiorum absolutorum et contra indiscretam communicationem nominum personalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_27:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-01","text":"Origo identitatem structuralem retinet, sed functionem mutat: primo principium definit, deinde nomen personale constituit, postremo similitudinem in imaginem convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A1","CH_GGVC_P_26:A2","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-02","text":"Relatio subsistens a fundamento personae Patris ad subsistentiam Verbi transit et in definitione Imaginis tamquam relatio originata absorbetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D3","CH_GGVC_P_27:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-03","text":"Generatio ab oppositione inter processum et terminum completum ad processionem intellectualem migrat, ubi Filius et Verbum eandem nativitatem designant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-04","text":"Similitudo ex participatione derivata in ratione Filii ad similitudinem constitutivam Verbi mutatur, deinde in originem expressivam Imaginis restringitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A13","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-05","text":"Creatura a filio adoptivo ad obiectum uno Verbo expressum et tandem ad imaginem participatam transfertur, semper sub mediatione Filii naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-06","text":"Negatio ab remotione causalitatis et temporalitatis ad determinationem positivam unici principii, aeterni Verbi et originatae Imaginis amplificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-07","text":"Spiritus Sanctus a persona procedente et aequali ad limitem distributivum notionis imaginis deslocatur: similitudo naturae manet, sed ratio Verbi deest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A18","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-01","text":"Differentia Latina inter causam et principium localis manet; hoc gradu tantum regula generalis retinetur qua modus creaturalis a relatione divinae originis separatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A3","CH_GGVC_P_25:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-02","text":"Distinctio entium a non-entibus, pluralitas idearum et extensio Graeca vocabuli imaginis sunt probationes locales, non axiomata constitutiva totius gregis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A12","CH_GGVC_P_26:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-03","text":"Relatio originis, subsistentia et exclusio successionis supra suos contextus amplificantur atque communem grammaticam trium nominum constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:D3","CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-04","text":"Verbum fit commissura praesentis gradus, quia paternitatem ut generationem intellectualem coniungit cum imagine ut similitudine ex origine procedente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:D5","CH_GGVC_P_26:D4","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-05","text":"Gradus locales filiationis, cognitionis et imaginis creaturalis absorbentur in propositionem superiorem quod omnis similitudo creaturae participatio expressionis Filii est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:D7","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-06","text":"De Spiritu Sancto hoc gradu non datur integra doctrina processionis; eius munus est ostendere naturam communem sine propria ratione processionis nomen Imaginis non determinare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A18","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-01","text":"Origo divina non est causatio creaturalis, emissio localis, separatio substantiae, successio temporalis aut gradus dominationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-02","text":"Nomen personale nec essentiam communem simpliciter significat nec accidens superveniens personae iam constitutae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-03","text":"Verbum divinum non est vox exterior, cogitatio successiva, conceptus accidentalis aut sermo multiplicatus secundum multitudinem rerum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-04","text":"Imago non constituitur per similitudinem genericam, accidentalem, non-originatam aut per solam communicationem naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-05","text":"Creatura nec mensura generationis divinae nec principium cognitionis Verbi nec imago univoce perfecta esse potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem asymmetriam originis inaequalitatem naturae, temporalem praecessionem aut dependentiam substantialem importare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet essentiam communem omnem rationem personalem absorbere, quasi modus processionis nullam differentiam nominandi inferat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet creaturas divinam intellectionem informare vel Verbum temporaliter determinare, cum ipsae ex divina auto-intellectione exprimantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet similitudinem staticam sufficere ad imaginem, quia ratio imaginis motum originis expressivae requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet vocabula divina aut univoce cum modis creaturalibus retineri aut in meras metaphoras dissolvi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSA-01","text":"Systema ontologice inadmissibilem habet pluralitatem principiorum personalium absolute innascibilium, quia talis pluralitas unitatem naturae et distinctionem relativam dissolveret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_25:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSA-02","text":"Nulla regio intelligibilium a divina essentia independens admittitur, quae auto-intellectionem Dei recipiendo compleat aut unum Verbum multiplicet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSA-03","text":"Creatura perfecta, autonoma et immediate filialis vel imaginalis est possibilitas exclusa; omnis talis habitudo per Filium naturalem derivatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSA-04","text":"Persona divina sine relatione originis est possibilitas structuraliter interdicta, quia neque essentia communis neque similitudo indeterminata personalem distinctionem sufficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-01","text":"Pater et Verbum constituunt polaritatem realem principii et expressionis procedentis, cui asymmetria originis inest sine inaequalitate perfectionis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-02","CL_GGVC_12:GA-03","CL_GGVC_12:GA-05","CL_GGVC_12:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_26:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-02","text":"Verbum et Imago eandem processionem filialem duplici ratione determinant: Verbum ut conceptum procedentem, Imago ut similitudinem specificam ex eodem principio ortam.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-06","CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","CL_GGVC_12:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-03","text":"Paternitas personalis, expressio creaturarum in Verbo et imago participata componunt ordinem quo creaturae per similitudinem Filii naturalis intelliguntur et producuntur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","CL_GGVC_12:GA-10","CL_GGVC_12:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-04","text":"Analogia divina fit processus regulatus: modus creaturalis removetur, ratio formalis vocabuli restringitur, deinde perfectio eius secundum originem personalem restituitur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-01","CL_GGVC_12:GA-02","CL_GGVC_12:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-05","text":"Multitudo creaturarum continetur in singulari expressione filiali, quia unum Verbum omnia repraesentat et perfecta Imago eiusdem naturae manet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","CL_GGVC_12:GA-10","CL_GGVC_12:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-06","text":"Similitudo Spiritus Sancti cum Patre et Filio, coniuncta exclusioni nominis Imaginis, demonstrat personalia nomina a modo processionis, non a gradu possessionis naturae, distribui.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-02","CL_GGVC_12:GA-09","CL_GGVC_12:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_27:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-07","text":"Negationes causalitatis, temporalitatis et similitudinis indeterminatae non vacuum relinquunt, sed topologiam positivam principii innascibilis, Verbi procedentis et Imaginis perfectae producunt.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-03","CL_GGVC_12:GA-05","CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","CL_GGVC_12:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-01","text":"Realitas divina concipitur ut unitas relationibus subsistentibus articulata, in qua asymmetria originis pluralitatem personalem sine compositione substantiali generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-02","text":"Tempus bifariam reordinatur: processiones personales et respectus intelligibilis ad creaturas aeterni sunt, productio effectuum autem temporalem ordinem recipere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS7","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-03","text":"Cognitio theologica neque vocabula creaturalia simpliciter reiicit neque retinet, sed per exclusionem modi imperfecti et restitutionem rationis formalis procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-04","text":"Creatio fit consequentia expressionis divinae sui, non conditio cognitionis divinae: creatura prius continetur in uno Verbo quam temporaliter producitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-05","text":"Subiectum creatum non est imago autonoma, sed ens cuius filiatio et similitudo constituuntur per participationem ac tendentiam ad perfectionem Filii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A13","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-06","text":"Apophasis hic vim constructivam acquirit: exclusionum cumulatio unicum principium, processionem intellectualem et imaginem originatam determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus semanticus procedit a vocabulo creaturali ad separationem modi impositionis, ab hac ad rationem formalem, et ab illa ad praedicationem divinam perfectam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A2","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-02","text":"Via amplificationis originem ab eo a quo aliquid procedit ad conceptum intellectualem procedentem et inde ad similitudinem ex principio ortam promovet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A1","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-03","text":"Circuitus intellectualis Patrem ut dicentem, Verbum ut expressionem Patris et creaturarum, atque Imaginem ut perfectionem eiusdem expressionis conectit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:D2","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-04","text":"Circuitus participationis a Filio naturali ad creaturas expressas descendit et per filiationem atque imaginem participatam ad exemplar filiale refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-05","text":"Attractor totius gregis est perfecta expressio filialis: ad eam paternitas, generatio, Verbum, Imago et similitudines creaturales convergunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:D5","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-06","text":"Clausura recusat utramque dissolutionem, sive pluralitatem principiorum absolutorum sive expansionem indiscretam Imaginis ad omne quod naturam divinam participat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B01","text":"Vocabulum creaturaliter impositum → distinctio rei significatae a modo impositionis → retentio perfectionis significatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A2","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B02","text":"Perfectio retenta → exclusio causalitatis, successionis et accidentis → aptitudo vocabuli ad praedicationem divinam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B03","text":"Importatio originis → relatio realis → subsistentia relationis → nomen personale.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D1","CH_GGVC_P_27:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B04","text":"Principium non de principio + generatio completa → Pater ut fons personalis et dicens Verbi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A14","CH_GGVC_P_25:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B05","text":"Processio intellectualis + subsistentia conceptus → Verbum → Filius naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B06","text":"Verbum + similitudo specifica ex origine → Imago perfecta → proprietas filialis confirmata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B07","text":"Unum Verbum exprimens omnia → creaturae cognitae et producibiles → filiatio atque imago participatae sine reciprocatione causali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:AFM-B01","text":"Ambiguitas nominum creaturalium → purgatio modorum imperfectorum → origo ut criterium personalitatis → relatio subsistens → Pater ut principium non de principio → processio intellectualis ut Verbum et Filius → similitudo originata ut Imago → creaturae ut expressiones et participationes → clausura contra temporalitatem, hierarchiam et pluralitatem principiorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-01","text":"Oppositio inter essentiale et personale reordinatur: essentia communicata unitatem praebet, ratio originis autem nomina personalia distribuit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-02","text":"Oppositio inter asymmetriam et aequalitatem corruit, quia ordo originis realis esse potest sine ordine perfectionis, temporis vel potestatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_25:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-03","text":"Cognitio et creatio non amplius ut actus paralleli ordinantur: una auto-intellectio unum Verbum constituit, cui respectus factivus ad creaturas consequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A10","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-04","text":"Similitudo et imago separantur: similitudo statum communem indicare potest, imago autem originem expressivam formaliter requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A2","CH_GGVC_P_27:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-05","text":"Ager creaturarum denuo describitur ut ordo expressus, factibilis et participativus, cui Filius naturalis simultanee exemplar intelligibile et terminus perfectionis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_26:D8","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei examinantur nomina Patris, Verbi et Imaginis atque condiciones quibus singula personaliter et proprie dicantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali relationes originis subsistentes, modi processionis et communicatio unius naturae machinam distributionis nominum constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A6","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico obiectio superatur per mutationem regulae lectionis: vocabulum non ex usu creaturali integro, sed ex ratione formali purificata iudicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas est aeterne processionalis, relationaliter distincta et substantialiter una, sine successione interna sed cum ordine ad effectus temporales.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo textus ipsam purificationem quam docet exercet: vocabula dividit, modos improprios excludit et residuum formale in structuram personalem convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FL-01","text":"Cohaerentia gregis pendet a praemissis relationis subsistentis et processionis intellectualis ut generationis, quae adhibentur potius quam hoc loco integre demonstrantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FL-02","text":"Unum nomen Verbi simul relationem personalem ad dicentem et respectum consequentem ad creaturas continet; distinctio ordinis significationis pluralitatem rei impedire debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A7","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FL-03","text":"Restrictio Imaginis ad Filium stabilis est intra rationem Latinam processionis Verbi, sed extensio Graeca ad perfectam similitudinem limitem semanticum permeabilem relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MP-01","text":"Principium mutatur ex vocabulo causalitatem et prioritatem suggerente in puram relationem originis sine tempore et dependentia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_25:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MP-02","text":"Generatio mutatur ex processu in fieri ad relationem completam, deinde ad processionem intellectualem quae Verbum et Filium identificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MP-03","text":"Similitudo mutatur ex communitate indeterminata in similitudinem specificam originatam; hoc puncto nomen essentiale in nomen personale transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite est intellectus relationalis aeternus, in quo principium se ipsum uno Verbo consubstantiali exprimit et in eo multitudinem creaturarum continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum creatum est similitudo recepta et tendens, non fons sui ipsius: filiatio et imago eius a perfectione Filii naturalis derivantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A13","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:HSI-03","text":"Tempus systematis duplicem ordinem habet: aeternam originem personalem sine ante et post, atque temporalem productionem effectuum iam aeternaliter cognitorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio conceptuum fit per alternationem exclusionis et restitutionis: modus creaturalis removetur, relatio originis detegitur, nomen personaliter reconstituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de distinctione significationis, relatione subsistente, processionibus personalibus et similitudine originata sufficiunt ad structuram principalem gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est grammatica originis, quia eodem criterio Patrem ut principium, Verbum ut Filium et Imaginem ut similitudinem procedentem ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MRT-B03","text":"Minus determinata manent fundamentum conventionis Latinae de causa et principio, modus continentiae non-entium in Verbo et extensio Graeca vocabuli Imaginis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MRT-B04","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat, si progressio non ut series nominum, sed ut purificatio recursiva originis, expressio filialis et reordinatio participationis creaturalis legitur; resistit tamen plena reductione diversitas usuum analogicorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171435576184Z_77cabc0e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 34–36","source_sha256":"edd6fe212a2c6204653210438ed2087414ccce1d2b0c0990dd99991abc7c9af6","sha256":"18fe2c095107afa0889e5f73b08d10fe21f2d5753941d63496eca7d6911ba6ff","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:14:35.577165+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how Father, Word, and Image are predicated personally, while the unity of nature, the eternity of the processions, and the equality of the persons remain intact.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis establishes that personal names are constituted by subsisting relations of origin, not by a partition of essence nor by accidental creaturely properties.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A17","CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-03","text":"The semantic-metaphysical argument first purifies terms, then restricts their formal notions, and finally distributes them personally according to modes of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-04","text":"The creaturely mode of imposition is removed, but the thing signified is retained and restored to the eternal perfection of the relation of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A2","CH_GGVC_P_26:A1","CH_GGVC_P_27:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-05","text":"The movement proceeds from the Father as principle not from a principle to the Son as proceeding Word, then to that same Son as perfect Image and to creatures as participated likenesses.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A14","CH_GGVC_P_26:D4","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-06","text":"The progression is spiral: the same notion of origin returns, but successively becomes the principle of asymmetry, the criterion of personality, the form of intellectual generation, and the condition of image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:D1","CH_GGVC_P_26:D1","CH_GGVC_P_27:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-07","text":"The cumulative proof excludes temporality, separation, creaturely causality, and indeterminate likeness, so that real asymmetry without hierarchy may be achieved.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BAS-08","text":"The closure establishes one unbegotten Father and one natural Son who, as Word and Image, perfectly expresses the Father and represents creatures without multiplication of the word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The truth of a divine name depends on the distinction between the thing signified and the creaturely mode by which the term is imposed or commonly understood.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A2","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] In divine things, the notion of origin distinguishes the persons, while the communicated essence remains one and undivided.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A17","CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Divine origin is real and asymmetrical, but does not introduce temporal succession, diminution, or subjection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_25:A5","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The relation of origin in the divine nature does not accrue to a person already constituted, but itself subsists as person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] The Father is constituted as principle not from a principle, to whom fatherhood attributes complete generation and the personal act of uttering.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A14","CH_GGVC_P_25:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Divine intellectual procession is generation; therefore the proceeding subsisting concept is the same Son under the notion of Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Word and Image do not add two filial properties, but express the same nativity as intellectual procession and originated likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Image properly so called requires not merely specific likeness, but procession from the principle whose likeness it expresses.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Communication of the same nature does not distribute personal names; the proper notion of procession determines why the Word is Image, whereas love is not so in the same respect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The natural Son is the formal medium through which filiation, expression, and the image of creatures are ordered as derived participations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A13","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] The unity of divine intellection constitutes one Word that eternally expresses the Father and the multitude of creatures without personal multiplication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Unity of nature and distinction through modes of origin close the system against a plurality of absolute principles and against indiscriminate communication of personal names.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_27:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-01","text":"Origin retains structural identity but changes function: first it defines principle, then constitutes a personal name, and finally converts likeness into image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A1","CH_GGVC_P_26:A2","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-02","text":"The subsisting relation passes from the foundation of the person of the Father to the subsistence of the Word and is absorbed in the definition of Image as an originated relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D3","CH_GGVC_P_27:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-03","text":"Generation migrates from the opposition between process and completed terminus to intellectual procession, where Son and Word designate the same nativity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-04","text":"Likeness changes from derived participation in the notion of Son to the constitutive likeness of Word, then is restricted to the expressive origin of Image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A13","CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-05","text":"The creature is transferred from adopted son to object expressed by one Word and finally to participated image, always under the mediation of the natural Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-06","text":"Negation is amplified from the removal of causality and temporality to the positive determination of the unique principle, eternal Word, and originated Image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RMD-07","text":"The Holy Spirit is displaced from a proceeding and equal person to the distributive limit of the notion of image: likeness of nature remains, but the notion of Word is absent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A18","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-01","text":"The Latin difference between cause and principle remains local; at this level only the general rule is retained by which creaturely mode is separated from the relation of divine origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A3","CH_GGVC_P_25:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-02","text":"The distinction of beings from non-beings, the plurality of ideas, and the Greek extension of the term image are local proofs, not constitutive axioms of the whole corpus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A12","CH_GGVC_P_26:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-03","text":"Relation of origin, subsistence, and exclusion of succession are amplified beyond their contexts and constitute the common grammar of the three names.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:D3","CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-04","text":"Word becomes the joint of the present level, because it connects fatherhood as intellectual generation with image as likeness proceeding from origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:D5","CH_GGVC_P_26:D4","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-05","text":"The local levels of filiation, cognition, and creaturely image are absorbed into the higher proposition that every likeness of a creature is participation in the expression of the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:D7","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:CGD-06","text":"Concerning the Holy Spirit, no complete doctrine of procession is given at this level; its role is to show that common nature without a proper notion of procession does not determine the name Image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A18","CH_GGVC_P_27:A9","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-01","text":"Divine origin is not creaturely causation, local emission, separation of substance, temporal succession, or a degree of dominion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-02","text":"A personal name neither simply signifies the common essence nor an accident supervening upon a person already constituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-03","text":"The divine Word is not an external voice, successive thought, accidental concept, or speech multiplied according to the multitude of things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-04","text":"Image is not constituted by generic, accidental, non-originated likeness, or by the mere communication of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:GNX-05","text":"A creature can be neither the measure of divine generation, nor the principle of the Word's knowledge, nor an image univocally perfect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that every asymmetry of origin entails inequality of nature, temporal precedence, or substantial dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that common essence absorbs every personal notion, as though a mode of procession introduced no difference in naming.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that creatures inform divine intellection or temporally determine the Word, since they themselves are expressed from divine self-intellection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that static likeness suffices for image, because the notion of image requires the movement of expressive origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that divine terms are either retained univocally with creaturely modes or dissolved into mere metaphors.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSA-01","text":"The system regards as ontologically inadmissible a plurality of personal principles absolutely unbegotten, because such plurality would dissolve unity of nature and relative distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_25:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSA-02","text":"No region of intelligibles independent of the divine essence is admitted, which might complete God's self-intellection by being received or multiply the one Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSA-03","text":"A perfect, autonomous, and immediately filial or imaginal creature is an excluded possibility; every such relation is derived through the natural Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSA-04","text":"A divine person without a relation of origin is a structurally forbidden possibility, because neither common essence nor indeterminate likeness suffices for personal distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-01","text":"Father and Word constitute a real polarity of principle and proceeding expression, in which asymmetry of origin inheres without inequality of perfection.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-02","CL_GGVC_12:GA-03","CL_GGVC_12:GA-05","CL_GGVC_12:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_26:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-02","text":"Word and Image determine the same filial procession under a twofold notion: Word as proceeding concept, Image as specific likeness arising from the same principle.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-06","CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","CL_GGVC_12:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-03","text":"Personal fatherhood, the expression of creatures in the Word, and participated image compose the order by which creatures are understood and produced through the likeness of the natural Son.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","CL_GGVC_12:GA-10","CL_GGVC_12:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-04","text":"Divine analogy becomes a regulated process: creaturely mode is removed, the formal notion of the term is restricted, and then its perfection is restored according to personal origin.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-01","CL_GGVC_12:GA-02","CL_GGVC_12:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-05","text":"The multitude of creatures is contained in the singular filial expression, because one Word represents all things and remains the perfect Image of the same nature.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","CL_GGVC_12:GA-10","CL_GGVC_12:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-06","text":"The likeness of the Holy Spirit with the Father and Son, joined to the exclusion of the name Image, demonstrates that personal names are distributed by mode of procession, not by degree of possession of nature.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-02","CL_GGVC_12:GA-09","CL_GGVC_12:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_27:D4","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_27:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:XD-07","text":"The negations of causality, temporality, and indeterminate likeness do not leave a void, but produce a positive topology of the unbegotten principle, proceeding Word, and perfect Image.","refs":["CL_GGVC_12:GA-03","CL_GGVC_12:GA-05","CL_GGVC_12:GA-07","CL_GGVC_12:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-01","text":"Divine reality is conceived as a unity articulated by subsisting relations, in which asymmetry of origin generates personal plurality without substantial composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-02","text":"Time is reordered in two ways: personal processions and intelligible reference to creatures are eternal, while the production of effects can receive temporal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS7","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-03","text":"Theological knowledge neither simply rejects nor retains creaturely terms, but proceeds through exclusion of the imperfect mode and restoration of the formal notion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-04","text":"Creation becomes a consequence of divine self-expression, not a condition of divine knowledge: the creature is contained first in the one Word before being temporally produced.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-05","text":"The created subject is not an autonomous image, but a being whose filiation and likeness are constituted through participation and a tendency toward the perfection of the Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A13","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:BSD-06","text":"Apophasis here acquires a constructive force: the accumulation of exclusions determines the unique principle, intellectual procession, and originated image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-01","text":"The semantic circuit proceeds from a creaturely term to separation of the mode of imposition, from this to the formal notion, and from that to perfect divine predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A2","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-02","text":"The path of amplification advances origin from that from which something proceeds to a proceeding intellectual concept and thence to likeness arising from a principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A1","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_27:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-03","text":"The intellectual circuit connects the Father as uttering, the Word as expression of the Father and creatures, and Image as the perfection of that same expression.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:D2","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-04","text":"The circuit of participation descends from the natural Son to expressed creatures and refers back through filiation and participated image to the filial exemplar.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-05","text":"The attractor of the whole corpus is perfect filial expression: toward it fatherhood, generation, Word, Image, and creaturely likenesses converge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:D5","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:RLE-06","text":"The closure rejects either dissolution, whether a plurality of absolute principles or indiscriminate expansion of Image to everything that participates in the divine nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B01","text":"A creaturely imposed term → distinction of the thing signified from the mode of imposition → retention of the signified perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A2","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B02","text":"Retained perfection → exclusion of causality, succession, and accident → fitness of the term for divine predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_26:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_27:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B03","text":"Introduction of origin → real relation → subsistence of relation → personal name.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D1","CH_GGVC_P_27:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B04","text":"Principle not from a principle + complete generation → Father as personal source and utterer of the Word.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A14","CH_GGVC_P_25:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B05","text":"Intellectual procession + subsistence of the concept → Word → natural Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A6","CH_GGVC_P_26:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B06","text":"Word + specific likeness from origin → perfect Image → filial property confirmed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A8","CH_GGVC_P_27:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FGS-B07","text":"One Word expressing all things → creatures known and producible → participated filiation and image without causal reciprocation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:AFM-B01","text":"Ambiguity of creaturely names → purification of imperfect modes → origin as criterion of personality → subsisting relation → Father as principle not from a principle → intellectual procession as Word and Son → originated likeness as Image → creatures as expressions and participations → closure against temporality, hierarchy, and plurality of principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-01","text":"The opposition between essential and personal is reordered: communicated essence provides unity, whereas the notion of origin distributes personal names.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A3","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-02","text":"The opposition between asymmetry and equality collapses, because the order of origin can be real without an order of perfection, time, or power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_25:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-03","text":"Knowledge and creation are no longer ordered as parallel acts: one self-intellection constitutes one Word, to which a productive relation to creatures follows.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:A10","CH_GGVC_P_26:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-04","text":"Likeness and image are separated: likeness can indicate a common state, whereas image formally requires expressive origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:A2","CH_GGVC_P_27:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MME-05","text":"The field of creatures is redescribed as an expressed, producible, and participatory order, for which the natural Son is simultaneously intelligible exemplar and terminus of perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_26:D8","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the names Father, Word, and Image are examined, together with the conditions under which each is said personally and properly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_26:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, subsisting relations of origin, modes of procession, and communication of one nature constitute the mechanism for distributing names.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A6","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the objection is overcome by changing the rule of reading: a term is judged not from its entire creaturely usage, but from its purified formal notion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_26:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, reality is eternally processional, relationally distinct, and substantially one, without internal succession but with an order toward temporal effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the text performs the very purification it teaches: it divides terms, excludes improper modes, and converts the formal remainder into personal structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FL-01","text":"The coherence of the corpus depends on the premises of subsisting relation and intellectual procession as generation, which are employed rather than fully demonstrated here.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FL-02","text":"The one name Word simultaneously contains a personal relation to the utterer and a consequent relation to creatures; the distinction in the order of signification must prevent plurality in reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A7","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:FL-03","text":"The restriction of Image to the Son is stable within the Latin notion of procession of the Word, but the Greek extension to perfect likeness leaves a permeable semantic boundary.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_27:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MP-01","text":"Principle changes from a term suggesting causality and priority into a pure relation of origin without time and dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_25:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MP-02","text":"Generation changes from a process of coming-to-be into a complete relation, then into intellectual procession that identifies Word and Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A9","CH_GGVC_P_26:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MP-03","text":"Likeness changes from indeterminate community into originated specific likeness; at this point an essential name passes into a personal name.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_27:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_27:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly eternal relational intellect, in which the principle expresses itself in one consubstantial Word and contains in it the multitude of creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_26:A8","CH_GGVC_P_26:D7","CH_GGVC_P_27:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:HSI-02","text":"The created subject is a received and tending likeness, not the source of itself: its filiation and image derive from the perfection of the natural Son.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A13","CH_GGVC_P_27:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system has a double order: eternal personal origin without before and after, and temporal production of effects already eternally known.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:A4","CH_GGVC_P_26:A11","CH_GGVC_P_27:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:HSI-04","text":"The navigation of concepts occurs through alternation of exclusion and restoration: the creaturely mode is removed, the relation of origin is discovered, and the name is personally reconstituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_25:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_27:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms concerning distinction of signification, subsisting relation, personal processions, and originated likeness suffice to reconstruct the principal structure of the corpus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MRT-B02","text":"The most secure structure is the grammar of origin, because by the same criterion it orders the Father as principle, the Word as Son, and Image as proceeding likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MRT-B03","text":"Less determined remain the foundation of the Latin convention concerning cause and principle, the mode of containment of non-beings in the Word, and the Greek extension of the term Image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_12:MRT-B04","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement if the progression is read not as a series of names, but as recursive purification of origin, filial expression, and reordering of creaturely participation; nevertheless, the diversity of analogical usages resists full reduction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_25:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_27:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_26:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_12@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_12:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 34–36","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 33 · Prima pars · Quaestio 34 · Prima pars · Quaestio 35"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 37–39","order":13,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_28","CH_GGVC_P_29","CH_GGVC_P_30"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_13@R001","sha256":"50ce0df0193c983a63cdc13ccd1ee094d2a563d53dc46a3401db5ebc5c984a96","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo Spiritus Sanctus personaliter nominetur, distinguatur et communicetur, salva unitate essentiae, aeternitate originis et non-possessiva relatione ad creaturam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-02","text":"Thesis centralis statuit unam processionem per modum amoris esse principium structurale ex quo nomen personale, relatio originis et ratio doni ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-03","text":"Argumentatio ab insufficientia significationis communis transit ad distinctiones modi significandi, quibus vocabula communia relationem personalem exprimere possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_29:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-04","text":"Topologia intratrinitaria stabilitur per originem Spiritus a Patre per Filium et ab utroque tamquam ab uno principio, sine multiplicatione virtutis spirativae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-05","text":"Amor ex habitudine essentiali in rem procedentem subsistentem mutatur, deinde actum notionalem denominat quo Amor producitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-06","text":"Donum originem intratrinitariam ad participationem creaturae extendit, sed relatio ad creaturam processionem aeternam manifestat potius quam constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_30:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-07","text":"Motus est spiralis: difficultas vocabuli distinctionem semanticam excitat, distinctio ad processionem redit, processio nomen reformat, nomen autem novam praedicationem et communicationem aperit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-08","text":"Clausura duplex producitur: intrinsecus Spiritus terminatur ut Amor procedens; extrinsecus idem Amor manet apertus ut primum Donum temporaliter participabile.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Unitas essentiae excludit distinctiones absolutas, dum pluralitas personarum tantum per relationes oppositas originis constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Duae processiones, Verbi per intellectum et Amoris per voluntatem, minimam structuram distinctionis personalis praebent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_29:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","text":"[Attractor] Modus processionis est principium invarians quo nomen personale proprium et distributio proprietatum determinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A11","CH_GGVC_P_29:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Vocabulum essentialiter commune potest personalem functionem accipere per accommodationem vel extensionem analogicam, dummodo relatio originis modum significationis regat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Nomen personale significat rem procedentem subsistentem, non accidens, actum transeuntem aut nudam relationem lexicalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-06","text":"[Terminal] Pater et Filius sunt unum principium Spiritus propter unam virtutem spirativam, sine instrumento, potestate secunda aut successione temporali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Amor essentialiter habitudinem communem significat, personaliter autem Amorem procedentem cum relatione ad principium spirans.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Actus notionalis personam productam determinate includit, unde principium processionis per effectum personalem denominari potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Donum primario significat aptitudinem aeternam ad dandum, non dationem temporaliter iam perfectam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Persona divina recipitur a creatura rationali per liberam cognitionem, amorem et fruitionem, non per dominium aut virtutem naturalem propriam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Amor est primum donum: originem gratuitatis constituit et ordinem oeconomicum manifestative ex processione aeterna producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-01","text":"Unitas essentiae et relatio originis identitatem stabilem servant, quamvis ab argumento distinctionis personarum ad argumentum nominationis et donationis transferantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-02","text":"Communitas vocabuli recurrit functione mutata: spiritus et sanctus accommodationem requirunt, amor bifurcationem essentialem-personalem, donum autem reclassificationem relationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","CH_GGVC_P_29:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-03","text":"Spiritus Sanctus ab nomine accommodato ad contentum processionis amorosae, deinde ad principium donationum gratuitarum amplificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","CH_GGVC_P_30:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-04","text":"Amor primum ordinem Verbi et voluntatis confirmat, deinde nomen proprium personae fit, tandem ut primum donum pluralitatem donorum generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-05","text":"Actus a spiratione originis ad diligere notionale mutatur, dum donum actum dationis deponit et aptitudinem donabilem assumit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A7","CH_GGVC_P_30:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-06","text":"Relatio ad creaturam ex extensione secundaria amoris in structuram explicitam receptionis rationalis migrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:D6","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-07","text":"Inopia vocabuli naturaliter proprii invertitur: quod initio defectus sermonis est, fit necessitas analogiae et machina distinctionis ontologicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-08","text":"Dationis temporalitas structurali opere peracto subordinatur aptitudini aeternae; eventus donationis manet effectus, non ratio primaria nominis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-01","text":"Communitas lexicalis vocum spiritus et sanctus manet difficultas localis; ad hunc gradum tantum regula generalis accommodationis personalis ascendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-02","text":"Demonstratio processionis a Filio manet machina intratrinitaria inferioris gradus, sed sursum amplificatur ut topologia invarians Amoris et Doni.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-03","text":"Solutio ablativi Spiritu Sancto localis est, sed regulam transunitariam efficit qua persona procedens actum notionalem denominat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-04","text":"Capacitas rationalis ad fruitionem est terminus localis doctrinae Doni, sed hoc gradu transitum ab origine aeterna ad communicationem temporalem constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-05","text":"Spiritus Sanctus, Amor et Donum non sunt nomina synonymice aggregata, sed sectiones distinctae eiusdem processionis secundum nominationem, subsistentiam et communicabilitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-06","text":"Ordo a Verbo ad Amorem coniungitur ordini ab Amore ad Dona, unde processio voluntatis fit machina transitus inter distinctionem personalem et gratuitam communicationem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D5","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-07","text":"Obiectiones grammaticales inferiores absorbentur in distinctionem inter rem significatam, modum significandi, relationem originis et effectum denominantem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-08","text":"Propositio propria huius gradus est identitatem personalem per seriem operatorum semanticorum cognosci, quorum invariantem mensuram processio originis praebet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-01","text":"Persona divina neque proprietate absoluta neque pluralitate essentiarum distingui potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-02","text":"Nomen personale neque ex sola vi lexicali neque ex significatione essentiali communi constitui potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-03","text":"Duae processiones immateriales ut lineae parallelae sine ordine mutuo admitti non possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-04","text":"Processio per Filium nec instrumentum nec inaequalitatem nec successionem temporalem significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-05","text":"Spiritus Sanctus nec medium originis inter Patrem et Filium nec principium formale dilectionis essentialis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-06","text":"Donum personale nec nomen essentiae, nec servitus personae datae, nec relatio dominativa recipientis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_30:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-07","text":"Missio vel datio communiter attributa non sufficit ad nomen personale proprium constituendum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet exemplar in quo essentia, relatio, origo et subsistentia personae quasi res separabiles componantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-02","text":"Falsa esse debet arithmetica unica quae numerum personarum, principiorum, virtutum et actuum eodem modo distribuat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-03","text":"Falsa esse debet symmetria perfecta actuum personalium, quia participatio essentialis non convertit personam procedentem in principium suae processionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar causale creatum in quo amor sit accidens transiens et donatio alienatio rei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar semanticum quo sola significatio nativa vocabuli veritatem personalis praedicationis metiatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-06","text":"Falsa est tam oeconomia constitutiva, qua creatura processionem aeternam causet, quam aeternitas clausa, quae communicationem personalem excludat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-01","text":"Systema circumagit absentiam vocabuli naturaliter proprii processionis voluntatis; haec indisponibilitas vim analogicam totius constructionis generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-02","text":"Possibilitas communicationis quae datum in possessionem recipientis convertat ontologice inadmissibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-03","text":"Filius et Spiritus Sanctus ut personae mutuo inordinatae, sola communi origine distinctae, intra systema cogitari non possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-04","text":"Donum quod recompensationem exigit rationem gratuitatis destruit atque ideo extra campum proprii Doni cadit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-05","text":"Altissima exclusio duplex est: neque aeternitas sine communicabilitate neque communicabilitas quae a creatura Deum constituat admittitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-01","text":"Nomen personale generatur cum vocabulum commune, relatio originis et subsistentia procedentis sub uno modo significationis componuntur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-04","CL_GGVC_13:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_30:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-02","text":"Series Spiritus–Amor–Donum eandem originem successive exprimit ut designationem personae, formam subsistentis processionis et aptitudinem communicativam.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-07","CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-03","text":"Spiritus est nexus Patris et Filii quia ab utroque procedit ut Amor mutuus, sed eadem relatio medium originis reale fieri non potest.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-06","CL_GGVC_13:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_29:A6","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-04","text":"Denominatio Patris et Filii per Amorem procedentem novam causalitatem non addit, quia actio notionalis eandem unam virtutem spirativam secundum effectum inclusum exprimit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-06","CL_GGVC_13:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_29:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-05","text":"Donum aeternum esse potest quia relatio ad dantem est origo personalis, dum habitio recipientis manet effectus temporalis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","CH_GGVC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-06","text":"Amor ut primum donum coniungit productionem notionalem et distributionem gratuitam, quin communis missio proprietatem personalem determinet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-08","CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-07","text":"Participatio rationalis constituit communicationem realem solum sub exclusione dominii, alienationis et sufficientiae naturalis recipientis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-08","text":"Defectus vocabuli proprii non relinquit processionem voluntatis indeterminatam, sed seriem nominum analogicorum sub disciplina originis generat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_29:A2","CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-01","text":"Identitas personalis divina est positio subsistens intra topologiam processionum, non differentia substantialis super essentiam communem addita.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-01","CL_GGVC_13:GA-02","CL_GGVC_13:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_29:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-02","text":"Semantica fit instrumentum epistemicum constitutivum: mutatio modi significandi detegit distinctiones ontologicas quas grammatica superficialis celat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_29:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-03","text":"Tempus bifariam ordinatur: aptitudo personalis ad donationem est aeterna, receptio autem et missio in creatura temporaliter eveniunt sine mutatione originis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_30:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-04","text":"Causalitas oeconomica est asymmetrica: processio aeterna communicationem fundat, creatura recipiendo participat, sed nec datum possidet nec originem retroactive constituit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","CL_GGVC_13:GA-10","CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-05","text":"Subiectum creatum reclassificatur ut capacitas rationalis desuper elevata, cuius actio propria est libera cognitio, amor et fruitio, non acquisitio dominativa.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-06","text":"Pneumatologia fit commissura inter ordinem immanentem et oeconomicum: Amor procedens gratuitatem constituit, Donum autem eandem gratuitatem participative distribuit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-07","CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus semanticus procedit a vocabulo communi ad relationem originis, ab origine ad nomen proprium, deinde a nomine proprio ad reinterpretationem vocabuli communis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-02","text":"Circuitus originis interpretativus transit a Patre per Filium ad Spiritum et redit per Amorem mutuum ad unitatem Patris et Filii in spiratione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_29:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-03","text":"Via amplificationis Amoris est: ordo a Verbo → nomen personale → actus notionalis → primum Donum → pluralitas donorum gratuitorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-04","text":"Circuitus Doni coniungit aptitudinem aeternam, dationem temporalem et fruitionem rationalem, sed causalitatem a recipiente ad originem redire prohibet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-05","text":"Negationes doctrinales recursivae non tantum errores removent, sed distinctiones novas efficiunt quibus implicitum nomen, origo et communicatio explicantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-06","text":"Attractor totius systematis est processio amoris: ad eam redeunt distinctio personae, denominatio actionis et ratio gratuitae communicationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A10","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B01","text":"Defectus vocabuli naturaliter proprii + communitas significationis → necessitas accommodationis et analogiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_28:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B02","text":"Unitas essentiae → exclusio distinctionum absolutarum → relatio originis opposita ut principium distinctionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B03","text":"Duae processiones immateriales → ordo Verbi et Amoris → Spiritus a Patre per Filium → unum principium spirativum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B04","text":"Processio subsistens + modus significandi relativus → Spiritus Sanctus et Amor ut nomina personalia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B05","text":"Amor procedens determinate inclusus in diligere notionale → principium spirans denominatur per personam productam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B06","text":"Gratuitum velle bonum → Amor ut primum Donum → processio Spiritus ut radix distributionis donorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B07","text":"Aptitudo personalis aeterna → datio temporalis → receptio rationalis desuper data → fruitio sine possessione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:AFM-B01","text":"Communitas nominum → distinctio modi significandi → topologia originis → Amor procedens → denominatio notionalis → Amor ut primum Donum → participatio rationalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:AFM-B02","text":"Exclusio proprietatum absolutarum → exclusio mediationis instrumentalis → exclusio accidentis transeuntis → exclusio donationis possessivae → affirmatio communicationis personalis gratuita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-01","text":"Proprietas nominis transfertur a monopolio significationis lexicalis ad relationem originis per modum significandi expressam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_29:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-02","text":"Oppositio inter essentiam communem et identitatem personalem corruit, quia persona distinguitur relationaliter sine essentiae multiplicatione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-03","text":"Oppositio inter mediationem et immediationem dissolvitur distributione earum inter ordinem suppositorum et ordinem unius virtutis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-04","text":"Amor reclassificatur ab affectu vel habitudine communi in processionem subsistentem et principium generativum gratuitae donationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-05","text":"Donum reclassificatur ab effectu creato vel translatione temporali in nomen personale fundatum in aptitudine originaria.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-06","text":"Relatio ad creaturam non amplius opponitur aeternitati, sed ut participatio temporalis processionis aeternae sine causalitate inversa describitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiali aguntur nomen Spiritus Sancti, processio eius, personalitas Amoris, praedicatio per Spiritum et proprietas Doni.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali nomina, personae, processiones et communicationes per relationes originis, modos significationis et distinctionem actuum ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico controversia ex grammatica superficiali ad quaestionem de genere relationis, origine et denominatione transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas divina est una essentia relationaliter subsistens, cuius processio aeterna effectus temporales sine mutatione producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo argumentatio ipsam doctrinam efficit per distinctiones semanticas, conversionem obiectionum et reordinationem analogicam vocabulorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FL-01","text":"Accommodationis personalis firmitas ab usu ecclesiali et sensu implicito pendet, quorum criteria intra structuram praesentem non plene derivantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FL-02","text":"Analogia Verbi et Amoris maximam vim generativam habet, sed inopia vocabulorum voluntatis eandem analogiam necessariam simul et indeterminatam reddit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FL-03","text":"Denominatio Patris et Filii per Spiritum Sanctum quasi causalitatem formalem sonat, quam systema eodem tempore a dilectione essentiali removet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:D4","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FL-04","text":"Donum ad creaturam relatum aeternum dicitur, sed stabilitas huius assertionis tota distinctione inter aptitudinem originariam et possessionem temporalem sustinetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-01","text":"Voces communiter essentiales in nomen personale mutantur cum usus eas ad relationem processionis restringit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-02","text":"Amor ab habitudine essentiali ad rem subsistentem procedentem mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-03","text":"Diligere ab actu essentiali communi ad productionem notionalem Amoris mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A7","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-04","text":"Donum ab actu dationis iam perfecto ad aptitudinem aeternam donabilem transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-05","text":"Processio amoris ab ordine intratrinitario ad ordinem oeconomicum extenditur, non mutatione originis sed manifestatione participativa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite apparet ut circulatio immaterialis Verbi et Amoris, in qua numerositas relationum unitatem essentiae non frangit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-02","text":"Spiritus est vector et terminus subsistens Amoris Patris et Filii, non tertium instrumentum aut spatium medium inter eos.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:D2","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-03","text":"Subiectum creatum est capacitas rationalis desuper aperta, quae datum recipit cognoscendo, amando et fruendo potius quam possidendo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-04","text":"Tempus habet duo strata non aemula: aeternam donabilitatem personae et temporalem receptionem effectus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-05","text":"Navigatio intra hanc machinam fit distinguendo originem, identitatem, possessionem, actum et effectum, ne imago creata causalitatis ordinem divinum capiat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de relationibus originis, duabus processionibus, modo significandi, Amore procedente et aptitudine Doni sufficiunt ad structuram huius gradus restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est invariantia processionis amoris, quae distinctionem personalem, nomen proprium et rationem donationis continenter ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B03","text":"Minus determinata manent criteria accommodationis ecclesialis et extensio analogica vocabulorum voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B04","text":"Restitutio doctrinis antecedentibus de relationibus originis et duabus processionibus pendet, quas hic gradus exercet potius quam integre demonstrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B05","text":"Cohaerentia relationis ad creaturam servatur distinctione aptitudinis a datione actuali, sed tensio inter receptionem realem et negationem dominii non penitus solvitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B06","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat ab accommodatione nominis per processionem et Amorem ad Donum participabile; usus tamen ecclesialis et elevatio rationalis reductioni mere formali resistunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171525962202Z_5cd207e2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 37–39","source_sha256":"50ce0df0193c983a63cdc13ccd1ee094d2a563d53dc46a3401db5ebc5c984a96","sha256":"1ff254ca0b7868ad736b2dfe678683cbe7345f6745a8506c9195335d06913d26","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:15:25.963121+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-01","text":"The system asks how the Holy Spirit is personally named, distinguished, and communicated, while preserving the unity of essence, the eternity of origin, and a non-possessive relation to the creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-02","text":"The central thesis holds that one procession in the mode of love is the structural principle from which the personal name, the relation of origin, and the account of gift are ordered.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-03","text":"The argument proceeds from the insufficiency of common signification to distinctions of mode of signifying, by which common terms can express personal relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_29:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-04","text":"The intratrinitarian topology is established through the origin of the Spirit from the Father through the Son and from both as from one principle, without multiplication of spirative power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-05","text":"Love is transformed from an essential relation into a subsisting proceeding reality, then denominates the notional act by which Love is produced.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-06","text":"Gift extends intratrinitarian origin to the creature's participation, but the relation to the creature manifests rather than constitutes the eternal procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_30:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-07","text":"The movement is spiral: difficulty concerning the term occasions semantic distinction, distinction returns to procession, procession refashions the name, and the name in turn opens a new predication and communication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ASP-08","text":"A twofold closure is produced: intrinsically the Spirit terminates as proceeding Love; extrinsically the same Love remains open as the first Gift capable of temporal participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Unity of essence excludes absolute distinctions, while the plurality of persons is constituted only through opposed relations of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_28:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Two processions, of the Word through intellect and of Love through will, provide the minimal structure of personal distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A5","CH_GGVC_P_29:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","text":"[Attractor] The mode of procession is the invariant principle by which the proper personal name and the distribution of properties are determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A11","CH_GGVC_P_29:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] A term essentially common can assume a personal function through accommodation or analogical extension, provided that the relation of origin governs the mode of signification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] A personal name signifies a subsisting proceeding reality, not an accident, a transient act, or a bare lexical relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-06","text":"[Terminal] The Father and the Son are one principle of the Spirit by reason of one spirative power, without instrument, secondary power, or temporal succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_28:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Love essentially signifies a common relation, but personally signifies proceeding Love with relation to the spirating principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] A notional act determinately includes the person produced, whence the principle of procession can be denominated through the personal effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Gift primarily signifies an eternal aptitude for being given, not a giving already completed temporally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] The divine person is received by the rational creature through free knowledge, love, and enjoyment, not through dominion or a proper natural power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Love is the first gift: it constitutes the origin of gratuity and manifestatively produces the economic order from eternal procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-01","text":"Unity of essence and relation of origin retain stable identity, although they are transferred from the argument concerning distinction of persons to the argument concerning naming and giving.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A2","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-02","text":"The commonality of the term recurs with altered function: spirit and holy require accommodation, love an essential-personal bifurcation, but gift a reclassification of relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","CH_GGVC_P_29:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-03","text":"The Holy Spirit is amplified from an accommodated name to the content of loving procession, then to the principle of gratuitous gifts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","CH_GGVC_P_30:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-04","text":"Love first confirms the order of Word and will, then becomes the proper name of a person, and finally, as the first gift, generates a plurality of gifts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-05","text":"Act is transformed from spiration of origin to notional loving, while gift lays aside the act of giving and assumes a donable aptitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A7","CH_GGVC_P_30:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-06","text":"The relation to the creature migrates from a secondary extension of love into an explicit structure of rational reception.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:D6","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-07","text":"The lack of a naturally proper term is inverted: what at first is a defect of speech becomes the necessity of analogy and the mechanism of ontological distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RMD-08","text":"The temporality of giving, once structural work has been completed, is subordinated to eternal aptitude; the event of giving remains an effect, not the primary account of the name.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-01","text":"The lexical commonality of the terms spirit and holy remains a local difficulty; only the general rule of personal accommodation rises to this level.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-02","text":"The demonstration of procession from the Son remains an intratrinitarian mechanism of a lower level, but is amplified upward as the invariant topology of Love and Gift.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-03","text":"The solution concerning the ablative Spiritu Sancto is local, but it effects a transunitary rule by which the proceeding person denominates the notional act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-04","text":"The rational capacity for enjoyment is a local terminus of the doctrine of Gift, but at this level it constitutes the transition from eternal origin to temporal communication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-05","text":"Holy Spirit, Love, and Gift are not synonymically aggregated names, but distinct sections of the same procession according to naming, subsistence, and communicability.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-06","text":"The order from Word to Love is joined to the order from Love to Gifts, whence the procession of will becomes the mechanism of transition between personal distinction and gratuitous communication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D5","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-07","text":"Lower grammatical objections are absorbed into the distinction among the reality signified, the mode of signifying, the relation of origin, and the denominating effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:CGD-08","text":"The proper proposition of this level is that personal identity is known through a series of semantic operators, whose invariant measure is provided by procession of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-01","text":"A divine person can be distinguished neither by an absolute property nor by a plurality of essences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-02","text":"A personal name can be constituted neither from lexical force alone nor from common essential signification.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-03","text":"Two immaterial processions cannot be admitted as parallel lines without mutual order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-04","text":"Procession through the Son signifies neither instrument, nor inequality, nor temporal succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_28:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-05","text":"The Holy Spirit is neither a medium of origin between Father and Son nor the formal principle of essential love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-06","text":"A personal Gift is neither a name of essence, nor servitude of the person given, nor a dominative relation of the recipient.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_30:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:GNX-07","text":"Mission or giving commonly attributed does not suffice to constitute a proper personal name.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-01","text":"The model must be false in which essence, relation, origin, and subsistence of person are composed as though separable realities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-02","text":"The single arithmetic must be false which distributes the number of persons, principles, powers, and acts in the same manner.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-03","text":"The perfect symmetry of personal acts must be false, because essential participation does not convert the proceeding person into the principle of its own procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-04","text":"The created causal model must be false in which love is a transient accident and giving an alienation of a thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-05","text":"The semantic model must be false by which the native signification of a term alone measures the truth of personal predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:DBN-06","text":"Both a constitutive economy, by which the creature causes eternal procession, and a closed eternity, which excludes personal communication, are false.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-01","text":"The system revolves around the absence of a naturally proper term for the procession of will; this unavailability generates the analogical force of the whole construction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-02","text":"The possibility of a communication that converts what is given into the possession of the recipient is ontologically inadmissible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-03","text":"The Son and the Holy Spirit as mutually unordered persons, distinguished solely by common origin, cannot be conceived within the system.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-04","text":"A gift that requires recompense destroys the account of gratuity and therefore falls outside the field of proper Gift.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSA-05","text":"The highest exclusion is twofold: neither eternity without communicability nor communicability by which the creature constitutes God is admitted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-01","text":"A personal name is generated when a common term, relation of origin, and subsistence of the proceeding reality are composed under one mode of signification.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-04","CL_GGVC_13:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4","CH_GGVC_P_30:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-02","text":"The series Spirit–Love–Gift successively expresses the same origin as designation of person, form of subsisting procession, and communicative aptitude.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-07","CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_28:D2","CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-03","text":"The Spirit is the nexus of Father and Son because it proceeds from both as mutual Love, but the same relation cannot become a real medium of origin.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-06","CL_GGVC_13:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11","CH_GGVC_P_29:A6","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-04","text":"The denomination of Father and Son through proceeding Love adds no new causality, because notional action expresses the same one spirative power according to the included effect.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-06","CL_GGVC_13:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_28:A15","CH_GGVC_P_29:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-05","text":"Gift can be eternal because relation to the giver is personal origin, while the indwelling of the recipient remains a temporal effect.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_30:A3","CH_GGVC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-06","text":"Love as the first gift joins notional production and gratuitous distribution, without a common mission determining personal property.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-08","CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-07","text":"Rational participation constitutes real communication only under the exclusion of dominion, alienation, and the recipient's natural sufficiency.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_30:A5","CH_GGVC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:XD-08","text":"The lack of a proper term does not leave the procession of will indeterminate, but generates a series of analogical names under the discipline of origin.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_29:A2","CH_GGVC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-01","text":"Divine personal identity is a subsisting position within the topology of processions, not a substantial difference added above the common essence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-01","CL_GGVC_13:GA-02","CL_GGVC_13:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_29:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-02","text":"Semantics becomes a constitutive epistemic instrument: a change in mode of signifying discloses ontological distinctions that superficial grammar conceals.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-03","CL_GGVC_13:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_29:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-03","text":"Time is ordered in two ways: the personal aptitude for giving is eternal, while reception and mission in the creature occur temporally without change of origin.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_30:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-04","text":"Economic causality is asymmetrical: eternal procession founds communication, the creature participates by receiving, but neither possesses what is given nor retroactively constitutes the origin.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-09","CL_GGVC_13:GA-10","CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_30:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-05","text":"The created subject is reclassified as a rational capacity elevated from above, whose proper action is free knowledge, love, and enjoyment, not dominative acquisition.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:BSD-06","text":"Pneumatology becomes the joint between the immanent and economic orders: proceeding Love constitutes gratuity, while Gift distributes that same gratuity participatively.","refs":["CL_GGVC_13:GA-07","CL_GGVC_13:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-01","text":"The semantic circuit proceeds from a common term to the relation of origin, from origin to a proper name, then from the proper name to reinterpretation of the common term.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-02","text":"The interpretative circuit of origin passes from the Father through the Son to the Spirit and returns through mutual Love to the unity of Father and Son in spiration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:D7","CH_GGVC_P_29:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-03","text":"The path of amplification of Love is: order from the Word → personal name → notional act → first Gift → plurality of gratuitous gifts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A11","CH_GGVC_P_29:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-04","text":"The circuit of Gift joins eternal aptitude, temporal giving, and rational enjoyment, but forbids causality to return from the recipient to the origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-05","text":"Recursive doctrinal negations do not merely remove errors, but also effect new distinctions by which implicit name, origin, and communication are explicated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:RLE-06","text":"The attractor of the whole system is the procession of love: to it return the distinction of person, the denomination of action, and the account of gratuitous communication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A10","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B01","text":"Lack of a naturally proper term + commonality of signification → necessity of accommodation and analogy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A6","CH_GGVC_P_28:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B02","text":"Unity of essence → exclusion of absolute distinctions → opposed relation of origin as principle of distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A1","CH_GGVC_P_28:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B03","text":"Two immaterial processions → order of Word and Love → Spirit from the Father through the Son → one spirative principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_28:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B04","text":"Subsisting procession + relative mode of signifying → Holy Spirit and Love as personal names.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B05","text":"Proceeding Love determinately included in notional loving → the spirating principle is denominated through the person produced.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A8","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B06","text":"Gratuitously willing good → Love as the first Gift → procession of the Spirit as root of the distribution of gifts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A9","CH_GGVC_P_30:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FGS-B07","text":"Eternal personal aptitude → temporal giving → rational reception given from above → enjoyment without possession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:D1","CH_GGVC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:AFM-B01","text":"Commonality of names → distinction of mode of signifying → topology of origin → proceeding Love → notional denomination → Love as first Gift → rational participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:AFM-B02","text":"Exclusion of absolute properties → exclusion of instrumental mediation → exclusion of transient accident → exclusion of possessive giving → affirmation of gratuitous personal communication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_30:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-01","text":"The propriety of the name is transferred from the monopoly of lexical signification to the relation of origin expressed through the mode of signifying.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_29:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-02","text":"The opposition between common essence and personal identity collapses, because the person is distinguished relationally without multiplication of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-03","text":"The opposition between mediation and immediacy is dissolved by distributing them between the order of supposita and the order of one power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-04","text":"Love is reclassified from affection or common relation into subsisting procession and the generative principle of gratuitous giving.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-05","text":"Gift is reclassified from a created effect or temporal transfer into a personal name founded in original aptitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MME-06","text":"The relation to the creature is no longer opposed to eternity, but is described as temporal participation in eternal procession without reverse causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B01","text":"At the superficial level, the name of the Holy Spirit, its procession, the personality of Love, predication through the Spirit, and the propriety of Gift are treated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, names, persons, processions, and communications are ordered through relations of origin, modes of signifying, and the distinction of acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the controversy is transferred from superficial grammar to the question of the kind of relation, origin, and denomination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, divine reality is one relationally subsisting essence, whose eternal procession produces temporal effects without change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the argument effects the doctrine itself through semantic distinctions, conversion of objections, and analogical reordering of terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_30:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FL-01","text":"The firmness of personal accommodation depends upon ecclesial usage and implicit sense, the criteria of which are not fully derived within the present structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FL-02","text":"The analogy of Word and Love has the greatest generative force, but the lack of terms for will renders that same analogy at once necessary and indeterminate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FL-03","text":"The denomination of Father and Son through the Holy Spirit sounds like formal causality, which the system at the same time removes from essential loving.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:D4","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:FL-04","text":"Gift referred to the creature is called eternal, but the stability of this assertion is wholly supported by the distinction between original aptitude and temporal possession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-01","text":"Terms commonly essential are transformed into a personal name when usage restricts them to the relation of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:A7","CH_GGVC_P_28:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-02","text":"Love is transformed from an essential relation into a subsisting proceeding reality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A3","CH_GGVC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-03","text":"Loving is transformed from a common essential act into the notional production of Love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:A7","CH_GGVC_P_29:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-04","text":"Gift is transferred from an act of giving already completed to an eternal donable aptitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A1","CH_GGVC_P_30:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MP-05","text":"The procession of love is extended from the intratrinitarian order to the economic order, not through a change of origin but through participative manifestation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as an immaterial circulation of Word and Love, in which the multiplicity of relations does not break the unity of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_28:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-02","text":"The Spirit is the vector and subsisting terminus of the Love of Father and Son, not a third instrument or an intermediate space between them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:D2","CH_GGVC_P_29:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-03","text":"The created subject is a rational capacity opened from above, which receives what is given by knowing, loving, and enjoying rather than by possessing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:A6","CH_GGVC_P_30:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-04","text":"Time has two non-rival strata: the eternal donability of the person and the temporal reception of the effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:HSI-05","text":"Navigation within this mechanism occurs by distinguishing origin, identity, possession, act, and effect, lest the created image of causality take hold of the divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_29:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_30:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B01","text":"Axioms concerning relations of origin, two processions, mode of signifying, proceeding Love, and the aptitude of Gift suffice to reconstruct the structure of this level.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the invariance of the procession of love, which continually orders personal distinction, proper name, and the account of giving.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B03","text":"The criteria of ecclesial accommodation and the analogical extension of terms concerning will remain less determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B04","text":"Reconstruction depends on antecedent doctrines concerning relations of origin and two processions, which this level employs rather than demonstrates in full.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_29:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B05","text":"The coherence of relation to the creature is preserved by distinguishing aptitude from actual giving, but the tension between real reception and the negation of dominion is not wholly resolved.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_13:MRT-B06","text":"Reconstruction preserves the true movement from accommodation of the name through procession and Love to participable Gift; ecclesial usage and rational elevation nevertheless resist merely formal reduction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_28:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_30:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_13@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_13:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 37–39","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 36 · Prima pars · Quaestio 37 · Prima pars · Quaestio 38"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 40–42","order":14,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_31","CH_GGVC_P_32","CH_GGVC_P_33"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_14@R001","sha256":"566fd95ccb2999ae720496f421426eb6fd64f68edad74868b168cfcd3e6a74c1","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo essentia numero una personas distinctas et actus originis sustineat sine divisione, mutatione aut compositione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis statuit essentiam, relationem personalem et personam eandem esse secundum rem, dum oppositio relationum personas distinguit et actus notionalis eundem ordinem originis exprimit sine re tertia.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio ab identitate ontologica per constitutionem relationalem ad dynamicam processionum progreditur, ita ut semantica, hypostasis et actio successive eandem structuram explicent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-04","text":"Distinctio inter rem et modum significandi fit operator recursivus quo identitas realis servatur neque tamen diversae functiones essentiales, personales et notionales confunduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-05","text":"Categoriae creatae successive purgantur: relatio desinit esse accidens, actio eventus mutabilis, potentia possibilitas ad opposita, et singulae in modos actualis ordinis divini convertuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-06","text":"Appropriatio ramum epistemicum constituit: communia essentialia personas manifestant, sed sola relatio personalis eas constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-07","text":"Motus verus est spiralis et cumulativus, quia identitas essentiae et personae per relationem, actionem, naturam et potentiam iteratur, quolibet reditu nova functione acquisita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-08","text":"Clausura numeralis unicum terminum cuique modo processionis statuit, sed demonstrationem suam doctrinis antecedentibus de simplicitate, relationibus subsistentibus et processionibus innititur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D12","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Simplicitas divina omnem compositionem realem excludit, quia quidquid realiter in Deo est divina essentia est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A1","CH_GGVC_P_32:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Essentia et persona sunt idem secundum rem, atque una eademque essentia numero in tribus personis subsistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_32:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Relatio personalis est ipsa essentia subsistens, sed oppositio relationum distinctionem realem personarum efficit sine distinctione essentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Relatio personalis non proprietati supposito praeexistenti additur, sed ipsam hypostasim divinam distinguit et constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] Identitas secundum rem compatitur differentiam rationis et modi significandi; haec differentia universam coordinationem essentiae, personae, relationis et actus gubernat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Origo, ut actus vel via, personam non primitus constituit, sed necessario designatur per actum qui secundum rem relationi personali idem est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_33:A2","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Processus ad extra actionem essentialem, processus autem personae a persona actionem notionalem requirit, quae remoto motu solum ordinem originis importat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A3","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Processiones intradivinae sunt naturales et per se necessariae; tota natura indivisa communicatur, voluntate concomitante sed non productive principiante, distinctione sola originis permanente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_33:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Potentia notionalis est principium quo actus iam actualis exercetur; essentiam directe significat et relationem personalem oblique connotat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A14","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Relationes subsistentes eiusdem rationis immaterialiter multiplicari nequeunt, et simplicitas actuum divinorum unum terminum cuique modo processionis claudit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","CH_GGVC_P_33:A18","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] Attributum essentiale potest personam manifestare, sed appropriatio neque proprietatem constituit neque communis attributi possessionem dividit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Grammatica theologica est instrumentum conservationis ontologicae, quia differentiae praedicationis eandem rem secundum irreducibiles rationes ordinant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-01","text":"Identitas essentiae et personae stabiliter redit, sed eius ambitus augetur: primo praedicationem, deinde constitutionem relationalem, postremo identitatem actus notionalis cum relatione sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-02","text":"Relatio a principio distinctionis in formam hypostasim constituentem mutatur, deinde sub forma actionis in ordinem originis operationaliter exprimitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A5","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_33:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-03","text":"Modus significandi idem munus conservativum retinet, sed a numero et suppositione nominum ad differentiam relationis, personae, essentiae et potentiae migrat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-04","text":"Origo functionem mutat: ut via non est principium primum constitutionis, sed, terminis relationaliter constitutis, per actum notionale necessario significatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_32:D6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-05","text":"Communitas ab attributo appropriabili ad proprietatem non personalem et tandem ad potentiam essentialem transit; in singulis casibus communitas personalem constitutionem non efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_32:A8","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-06","text":"Numerus a regula grammatica in clausuram ontologicam transfertur: primo formam aut supposita sequitur, postremo ex immaterialitate relationum et simplicitate actuum terminatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-07","text":"Matrices appropriationis, opere manifestativo peracto, in distinctionem superiorem inter proprietatem constituentem et communem manifestationem absorbentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_32:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-01","text":"Regulae de nominibus concretis et abstractis locales manent, sed sursum amplificant principium generale quo semantica vetat identitatem realem in substitutionem indiscretam converti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-02","text":"Quattuor ordines appropriationum manent tabula epistemica inferioris gradus; hoc gradu tantum discrimen inter manifestationem communem et constitutionem personalem structurale fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-03","text":"Experimenta abstractionis et distinctiones prioritatis constituunt commissuram inter semanticam identitatis et doctrinam actuum, quia demonstrant quid hypostasim constituat et quo sensu actus relationem praecedat aut sequatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:AS7","CH_GGVC_P_32:D7","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-04","text":"Distinctiones locales inter naturam et voluntatem, generationem et creationem, potentiam et possibilitatem doctrinam relationum in theoriam integram processionis amplificant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-05","text":"Innascibilitas ut negatio non constitutiva localiter tractatur, sed hoc gradu sub exclusione generali omnis individuationis negativae vel extrinsecae absorbatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-06","text":"Structura propria huius gradus est coordinatio distributa grammaticae, ontologiae relationis et doctrinae actus ad tres invariantes servandos: essentiae unitatem, distinctionem personalem et ordinem originis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-01","text":"Personarum distinctio neque divisionem essentiae neque pluralitatem substantiarum absolutarum neque genus commune supra individua admittit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-02","text":"Relationes, proprietates et actus notionales non sunt accidentia suppositis addita neque res tertiae inter essentiam et personas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_32:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-03","text":"Nulla persona absoluta prae-relationalis admittitur, neque principium individuationis non relationale distinctionem divinam efficere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-04","text":"Processio nullum motum, passionem, mutationem, intervallum aut successionem temporalem recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-05","text":"Generatio neque a voluntate ut principio productivo neque ex nihilo neque per materiam, partitionem aut transmutationem procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-06","text":"Identitas realis non licentiam substitutionis universalis praebet, et praedicamenta sensibilia non possunt ad divina univoce transferri.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-07","text":"Unus modus processionis plures terminos personales eiusdem rationis non admittit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet identitatem rei secum ferre identitatem rationis, modi significandi et functionis praedicativae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_32:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem distinctionem suppositorum divisionem formae, materiam individuantem aut differentiam essentialem absolutam requirere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet libertatem, potentiam et actionem ex indifferentia, carentia actus aut possibilitate nondum completa definiri.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet originem posse terminos constituere ante relationes quae ipsos terminos hypostaticos distinguunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet manifestationem analogicam ex attributis communibus aut creaturis vel proprietatem personalem constituere vel Trinitatem demonstrare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-01","text":"Nulla quarta res inter essentiam et personas neque substratum externum in communicatione naturae admittitur; tota structura intra identitatem simplicem clauditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-02","text":"Modus divinus cognoscendi et nominandi intellectui creato indisponibilis manet, unde systema analogia et negatione operari debet sine demonstratione proprietatum personalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-03","text":"Possibilitas intradivina qua persona procedens esse aut non esse posset ontologice inadmissibilis est; libertas divina contingentiam processionis non postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-04","text":"Persona addita eiusdem modi processionis impossibilis est, quia relatio immaterialis eiusdem rationis et actus divinus simplex pluralitatem terminorum non sustinent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_33:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-05","text":"Subiectum divinum absolutum quod relationes postea accipiat est absentia constitutiva systematis: persona tantum ut relatio subsistens et correlativa intelligitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-01","text":"Differentia modi significandi causalitatem argumentativam exercet: non solum verba ordinat, sed impedit ne simplicitas in confusionem personarum aut distinctio in divisionem essentiae convertatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-05","CL_GGVC_14:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-02","text":"Relatio est medius operator totius gregis: ut res est essentia, ut opposita constituit personam, ut actione significata ordinem originis exprimit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-02","CL_GGVC_14:GA-03","CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_33:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-03","text":"Apparens circulus inter relationem et actum solvitur per ordines typatos: relatio ut fundata actum praesupponit, ut persona originans actum praecedit, et origo passiva viam ad terminum constituit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-06","CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_32:D9","CH_GGVC_P_32:D10","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-04","text":"Communia essentialia personas cognoscibiliter manifestare possunt, sed distinctio personalis tantum a relatione subsistente constitutiva provenit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6","CH_GGVC_P_32:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-05","text":"Essentia communis est principium quo processionis, dum relatio connotata actum personae propriae determinat; sic vitantur et essentia tamquam suppositum generans et permutatio munerum personalium.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-02","CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CL_GGVC_14:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_33:D9","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-06","text":"Clausura numeri personarum oritur ex concursu communicationis totius naturae, immaterialitatis relationum eiusdem rationis et simplicitatis actuum intellectus atque amoris.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CL_GGVC_14:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","CH_GGVC_P_33:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-07","text":"Actio notionalis, motu et voluntate productiva remota, fit expressio necessaria ordinis relationalis iam perfecte actualis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-06","CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:A10","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-01","text":"Persona divina non est substantia absoluta relationem gerens, sed essentia ipsa relationaliter subsistens; agency personalis ex ordine originis, non ex accidente addito, emergit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-03","CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-02","text":"Grammatica theologica in calculum conservationis transformatur: locutio valida est quatenus unitatem essentiae, distinctionem relationum et proprietatem actuum simul servat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-05","CL_GGVC_14:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-03","text":"Causalitas intradivina est communicatio non temporalis eiusdem naturae sub ordine originis, non productio efficientis termini essentialiter alieni.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-04","text":"Libertas et potentia a contingentia separantur: libertas est immunitas a coactione, potentia perfectio principii actualis, et fecunditas perfecta in termino unico clauditur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CL_GGVC_14:GA-09","CL_GGVC_14:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-05","text":"Negationes materiae, accidentis, motus et possibilitatis non vacuum relinquunt, sed positive generant relationem subsistentem, actionem ut ordinem et potentiam ut actuale principium.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-01","CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CL_GGVC_14:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_32:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-06","text":"Cognitio naturalis praebet materiam manifestationis, non principium demonstrationis; ordo personalis revelatus communia essentialia retroactive in tabulam appropriativam ordinat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-11","CL_GGVC_14:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-01","text":"Simplicitas excludit distinctionem absolutam; haec exclusio relationem subsistentem postulat; relatio autem distinctionem sine divisione efficit et sic simplicitatem confirmat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A1","CH_GGVC_P_32:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_32:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-02","text":"Identitas realis postulat distinctiones semanticas; hae distinctiones praedicationem rectam efficiunt; praedicatio recta vicissim identitatem realem a confusione custodit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-03","text":"Relatio constituit terminos, termini actum originis requirunt, actus relationem sub forma processus significat, et sic reditus ad relationem statum dynamicum potius quam repetitionem simplicem producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:D6","CH_GGVC_P_32:D9","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-04","text":"Natura tota communicatur, sola origo distinguit, relatio incommunicabilis actum proprium determinat, et actus proprius eandem naturam indivisam manifestat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A13","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-05","text":"Series exclusionum ab accidente per motum et potentiam passivam ad pluralitatem processionalem ascendit atque in attractorem actualitatis simplicis relationaliter articulatae convergit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-06","text":"Attributa essentialia manifestiora proprietates personales manifestant, sed proprietates fide positae vicissim determinant quomodo ipsa attributa appropriative distribuantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B01","text":"Essentia una indivisa + pluralitas personarum data → requisitio principii distinctionis quod essentiam non dividat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_31:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B02","text":"Simplicitas → exclusio materiae, accidentis et differentiae absolutae → eliminatio omnium principiorum distinctionis non relationalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_32:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B03","text":"Relatio ut essentia + oppositio correlativa + subsistentia → constitutio hypostasis distinctae sine multiplicatione naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B04","text":"Typatio semantica rei unius → distinctio abstracti et concreti, formae et actus, recti et obliqui → distributio munerum essentialium, personalium et notionalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B05","text":"Actio − motus − passio → ordo originis; natura ut principium → communicatio totius essentiae; potentia ut principium quo → actus personaliter determinatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B06","text":"Immaterialitas relationum + simplicitas intellectionis et amoris + determinatio naturae → unus terminus cuique modo processionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","CH_GGVC_P_33:A18","CH_GGVC_P_33:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B07","text":"Structura constitutiva completa → attributa communia ad personas appropriative ordinantur → manifestatio epistemica sine nova distinctione ontologica.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:AFM-B01","text":"Unitas essentiae → exclusio divisionis absolutae → oppositio relationum → relatio subsistens constituens personas → actus originis purgatus → communicatio naturalis totius essentiae → potentia ut principium quo → unicitas terminorum processionalium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_32:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_33:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:AFM-B02","text":"Cognitio ex creaturis → modus significandi analogicus → attributa essentialia manifestiora → appropriatio ad personas → manifestatio proprietatum sine demonstratione aut constitutione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-01","text":"Oppositio inter unum et tria corruit, quia unitas ad essentiam et pluralitas ad relationes subsistentes diversis rationibus distribuuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_32:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-02","text":"Relatio, actio et potentia reclassificantur respective ab accidente, eventu mutabili et possibilitate ad opposita in subsistentiam, ordinem originis et principium actuale.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-03","text":"Semantica desinit esse ornamentum expositionis et fit disciplina formalis quae simplicitatem sine confusione atque distinctionem sine partitione tuetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-04","text":"Oppositio inter voluntarium et necessarium solvitur, quia concomitantia voluntatis, naturalitas processionis, necessitas per se et absentia coactionis separantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-05","text":"Perfectio fecunditatis non amplius multitudine productorum mensuratur, sed communicatione integra naturae in termino processionali unico.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-06","text":"Distinctio inter manifestationem et constitutionem novum campum epistemicum aperit, in quo communia personas indicant sine earum proprietates efficiendo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:D9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei formulae de essentia, personis, generatione, relationibus et actibus secundum regulas praedicationis admittuntur aut reiciuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali simplicitas omnes distinctiones absolutas removet, relatio subsistens personas constituit, et communicatio naturae cum ordine originis processiones ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico modi significandi et distinctiones formales errores divisionis essentiae, confusionis personarum, creationis Filii et contingentiae intradivinae prohibent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas est simplex, perfecte actualis et non successiva, dum prioritas tantum secundum diversas rationes relationis, actus et termini distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo textus ipsam doctrinam efficit per distinctiones iteratas: forma argumentationis identitatem servat dum munera separat, sicut ontologia ipsa unitatem servat dum personas distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-01","text":"Identitas relationis, essentiae et personae secundum rem cum differentiis praedicationis tantum per modum significandi conectitur; haec commissura necessaria est, sed magnum pondus ontologicum semanticae imponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-02","text":"Origo ut actus negatur esse principium primum constitutionis, quamvis omnis origo actu designari debeat; distinctio viae, relationis et personae tensionem ordinat, non penitus aufert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A2","CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-03","text":"Voluntas Patris generationem necessario comitatur sed non principiat; libertas igitur a contingentia separatur, quo sensu voluntarium a principio voluntario stricte distingui debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-04","text":"Potentia generandi secundum essentiam communis dicitur, sed actus generativus Patri proprius manet; rectum, obliquum et connotatio relationalis hanc asymmetriam continent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-05","text":"Clausura numeri personarum principiis de immateriali individuatione et determinatione naturae ad unum nititur, quae intra hunc gregem assumuntur potius quam plene probantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-06","text":"Matrices appropriationis similitudinibus selectivis nituntur; earum vis manifestativa stat, sed necessitas singularum distributionum minor est quam necessitas constitutionis relationalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MP-01","text":"Relatio a signo distinctionis in ipsam formam subsistentem hypostasim constituentem mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MP-02","text":"Actio ab eventu mutationem implicante in modum significandi ordinem originis convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MP-03","text":"Potentia a possibilitate nondum completa in perfectionem principii quo iam actu operantis mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MP-04","text":"Numerus a regula morphologica nominum in principium clausurae terminorum personalium transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite fingitur ut essentia simplex quae non partes continet, sed relationibus oppositis se personaliter articulat et actibus originis exprimit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum non est nucleus absolutus proprietatibus vestitus, sed terminus subsistens relationis cuius ipsa correlativitas distinctionem et identitatem personalem constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:HSI-03","text":"Tempus processionale deletur: nullum ante et post reale datur, sed tantum ordines intelligibiles secundum relationem, actionem et viam ad terminum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio intra systema fit per portas grammaticales et apophaticas: quaelibet formula probatur an unitatem, distinctionem et originem servet, dum modus divinus ipse cognitioni creatae indisponibilis manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de simplicitate, identitate reali, relatione subsistente, actu purgato, communicatione naturae et potentia actuali sufficiunt ad structuram principalem huius gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B02","text":"Non satis determinantur probationes antecedentium de simplicitate, processionibus et individuatione relationum immaterialium; hae condiciones ut fundamenta externa manent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B03","text":"Systema cohaeret si identitas rei, distinctio rationis, constitutio relationalis et pluralitas ordinum intelligibilium simul et stricte retinentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B04","text":"Firmissima structura est transitus a simplicitate ad relationem subsistentem et inde ad actionem sine motu atque generationem consubstantialem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B05","text":"Reductioni plenae resistunt necessitas singularum appropriationum et probatio ultima unicitatis terminorum, quarum rationes selectivae aut aliunde assumptae manent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B06","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat, quia quaestionem unitatis et pluralitatis per relationem solvit, solutionem in semanticam transfert, eam in actus et potentiam amplificat atque clausura numerali terminat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171605055551Z_f40383c2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 40–42","source_sha256":"566fd95ccb2999ae720496f421426eb6fd64f68edad74868b168cfcd3e6a74c1","sha256":"6c497b163797dfb856e1b5a4c7bdc3dcebe06156615f13310b9537fec5674dd5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:16:05.056500+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how an essence numerically one sustains distinct persons and acts of origin without division, change, or composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis holds that essence, personal relation, and person are the same in reality, while the opposition of relations distinguishes persons and notional act expresses the same order of origin without a third thing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-03","text":"The argument proceeds from ontological identity through relational constitution to the dynamics of processions, such that semantics, hypostasis, and action successively explain the same structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-04","text":"The distinction between thing and mode of signifying becomes a recursive operator by which real identity is preserved and yet the diverse essential, personal, and notional functions are not confused.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-05","text":"Created categories are successively purified: relation ceases to be an accident, action a mutable event, power a possibility toward opposites, and each is converted into modes of the actual divine order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-06","text":"Appropriation constitutes an epistemic branch: common essential features manifest the persons, but personal relation alone constitutes them.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-07","text":"The true movement is spiral and cumulative, because the identity of essence and person is reiterated through relation, action, nature, and power, with each return acquiring a new function.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BAS-08","text":"Numerical closure establishes a single term for each mode of procession, but grounds its demonstration in preceding doctrines concerning simplicity, subsisting relations, and processions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:D12","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Divine simplicity excludes every real composition, because whatever is really in God is the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A1","CH_GGVC_P_32:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Essence and person are the same in reality, and one and the same essence numerically subsists in three persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A2","CH_GGVC_P_32:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Personal relation is the subsisting essence itself, but the opposition of relations effects the real distinction of persons without a distinction of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A3","CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Personal relation is not added as a property to a pre-existing supposit, but distinguishes and constitutes the divine hypostasis itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_32:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] Identity in reality is compatible with a difference of reason and of mode of signifying; this difference governs the entire coordination of essence, person, relation, and act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Origin, as act or way, does not primarily constitute the person, but is necessarily designated through an act which is the same in reality as personal relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_33:A2","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Procession ad extra requires essential action, whereas the procession of person from person requires notional action, which, with motion removed, imports only an order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A3","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Intradivine processions are natural and necessary through themselves; the whole undivided nature is communicated, with will concomitant but not productively originating, while the distinction of origin alone remains.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_33:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Notional power is the principle by which an act already actual is exercised; it directly signifies essence and indirectly connotes personal relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A14","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Subsisting relations of the same ratio cannot be multiplied immaterially, and the simplicity of divine acts closes a single term for each mode of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","CH_GGVC_P_33:A18","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] An essential attribute can manifest a person, but appropriation neither constitutes a property nor divides possession of the common attribute.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Theological grammar is an instrument of ontological preservation, because differences of predication order the same thing according to irreducible ratios.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-01","text":"The identity of essence and person returns steadily, but its scope increases: first it sustains predication, then relational constitution, and finally the identity of notional act with relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A1","CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-02","text":"Relation changes from a principle of distinction into a form constituting hypostasis, then is operationally expressed under the form of action in an order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A5","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_33:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-03","text":"Mode of signifying retains the same preservative function, but migrates from the number and supposition of names to the difference of relation, person, essence, and power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-04","text":"Origin changes function: as a way it is not the first principle of constitution, but, once the terms are relationally constituted, it is necessarily signified through notional act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A10","CH_GGVC_P_32:D6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-05","text":"Communality passes from appropriable attribute to non-personal property and finally to essential power; in each case communality does not effect personal constitution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_32:A8","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-06","text":"Number is transferred from a grammatical rule into ontological closure: first it follows form or supposits, finally it is determined from the immateriality of relations and the simplicity of acts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RMD-07","text":"The matrices of appropriation, once their manifestative work is completed, are absorbed into the higher distinction between constituting property and common manifestation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_32:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-01","text":"Rules concerning concrete and abstract names remain local, but are amplified upward into the general principle by which semantics forbids real identity to be converted into indiscriminate substitution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A10","CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-02","text":"The four orders of appropriations remain an epistemic map of a lower level; only at this level does the distinction between common manifestation and personal constitution become structural.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A16","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-03","text":"Experiments of abstraction and distinctions of priority constitute the joint between the semantics of identity and the doctrine of acts, because they demonstrate what constitutes hypostasis and in what sense act precedes or follows relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:AS7","CH_GGVC_P_32:D7","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-04","text":"Local distinctions between nature and will, generation and creation, power and possibility amplify the doctrine of relations into an integral theory of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-05","text":"Unbegottenness as a non-constitutive negation is treated locally, but at this level it is absorbed under the general exclusion of every negative or extrinsic individuation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:CGD-06","text":"The proper structure of this level is the distributed coordination of grammar, the ontology of relation, and the doctrine of act in order to preserve three invariants: unity of essence, personal distinction, and order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-01","text":"The distinction of persons admits neither division of essence nor plurality of absolute substances nor a common genus above individuals.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-02","text":"Relations, properties, and notional acts are neither accidents added to supposits nor third things between essence and persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_32:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-03","text":"No absolute pre-relational person is admitted, nor can a non-relational principle of individuation effect divine distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-04","text":"Procession admits no motion, passion, change, interval, or temporal succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-05","text":"Generation proceeds neither from will as a productive principle, nor from nothing, nor through matter, partition, or transmutation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-06","text":"Real identity does not grant license for universal substitution, and sensible predicates cannot be transferred univocally to divine things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:GNX-07","text":"One mode of procession does not admit several personal terms of the same ratio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that identity of thing entails identity of reason, mode of signifying, and predicative function.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_32:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that every distinction of supposits requires division of form, individuating matter, or absolute essential difference.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that freedom, power, and action are defined from indifference, lack of act, or possibility not yet complete.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that origin can constitute terms prior to the relations that distinguish the hypostatic terms themselves.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_32:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that analogical manifestation from common attributes or creatures can either constitute personal property or demonstrate the Trinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-01","text":"No fourth thing between essence and persons, nor any external substrate in the communication of nature, is admitted; the whole structure is enclosed within simple identity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-02","text":"The divine mode of knowing and naming remains unavailable to created intellect, whence the system must operate by analogy and negation without demonstration of personal properties.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-03","text":"An intradivine possibility by which a proceeding person might be or not be is ontologically inadmissible; divine freedom does not require contingency of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-04","text":"An added person of the same mode of procession is impossible, because an immaterial relation of the same ratio and a simple divine act do not sustain a plurality of terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_33:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSA-05","text":"An absolute divine subject that subsequently receives relations is a constitutive absence of the system: person is understood only as subsisting and correlative relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-01","text":"Difference of mode of signifying exercises argumentative causality: it not only orders words, but prevents simplicity from being converted into confusion of persons or distinction into division of essence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-05","CL_GGVC_14:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-02","text":"Relation is the mediating operator of the entire group: as a thing it is essence, as opposed it constitutes person, as signified by action it expresses the order of origin.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-02","CL_GGVC_14:GA-03","CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_31:A4","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7","CH_GGVC_P_33:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-03","text":"The apparent circle between relation and act is resolved through typed orders: relation as founded presupposes act, as originating person precedes act, and passive origin constitutes the way to the term.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-06","CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_32:D9","CH_GGVC_P_32:D10","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-04","text":"Common essential features can manifest persons cognoscibly, but personal distinction derives only from constituting subsisting relation.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6","CH_GGVC_P_32:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-05","text":"The common essence is the principle by which there is procession, while the connoted relation determines the act of the proper person; thus both essence as generating supposit and interchange of personal offices are avoided.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-02","CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CL_GGVC_14:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_33:D9","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-06","text":"Closure of the number of persons arises from the concurrence of communication of the whole nature, the immateriality of relations of the same ratio, and the simplicity of the acts of intellect and love.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CL_GGVC_14:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","CH_GGVC_P_33:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:XD-07","text":"Notional action, with motion and productive will removed, becomes the necessary expression of an already perfectly actual relational order.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-06","CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:A10","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-01","text":"The divine person is not an absolute substance bearing relation, but essence itself relationally subsisting; personal agency emerges from the order of origin, not from an added accident.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-03","CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-02","text":"Theological grammar is transformed into a calculus of preservation: speech is valid insofar as it preserves simultaneously unity of essence, distinction of relations, and propriety of acts.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-05","CL_GGVC_14:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-03","text":"Intradivine causality is non-temporal communication of the same nature under an order of origin, not efficient production of an essentially alien term.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-04","text":"Freedom and power are separated from contingency: freedom is immunity from coercion, power the perfection of an actual principle, and perfect fecundity is closed in a single term.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-08","CL_GGVC_14:GA-09","CL_GGVC_14:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-05","text":"Negations of matter, accident, motion, and possibility do not leave a void, but positively generate subsisting relation, action as order, and power as actual principle.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-01","CL_GGVC_14:GA-04","CL_GGVC_14:GA-07","CL_GGVC_14:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_32:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:BSD-06","text":"Natural knowledge provides the material of manifestation, not the principle of demonstration; the revealed personal order retroactively orders common essential features into an appropriative map.","refs":["CL_GGVC_14:GA-11","CL_GGVC_14:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_31:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-01","text":"Simplicity excludes absolute distinction; this exclusion requires subsisting relation; relation, however, effects distinction without division and thus confirms simplicity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A1","CH_GGVC_P_32:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_32:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-02","text":"Real identity requires semantic distinctions; these effect correct predication; correct predication in turn guards real identity from confusion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-03","text":"Relation constitutes terms, terms require an act of origin, the act signifies relation under the form of process, and thus the return to relation produces a dynamic state rather than simple repetition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:D6","CH_GGVC_P_32:D9","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-04","text":"The whole nature is communicated, origin alone distinguishes, incommunicable relation determines proper act, and proper act manifests the same undivided nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A13","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-05","text":"The series of exclusions ascends from accident through motion and passive power to processional plurality, and converges upon the attractor of simply actual reality relationally articulated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_33:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:RLE-06","text":"More manifest essential attributes manifest personal properties, but properties posited by faith in turn determine how the attributes themselves are distributed appropriatively.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B01","text":"One undivided essence + plurality of persons given → requirement of a principle of distinction that does not divide the essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_31:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B02","text":"Simplicity → exclusion of matter, accident, and absolute difference → elimination of all non-relational principles of distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_32:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B03","text":"Relation as essence + correlative opposition + subsistence → constitution of distinct hypostasis without multiplication of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:A3","CH_GGVC_P_32:FGS4","CH_GGVC_P_31:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B04","text":"Semantic typing of the one thing → distinction of abstract and concrete, form and act, direct and indirect → distribution of essential, personal, and notional functions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A11","CH_GGVC_P_33:A4","CH_GGVC_P_33:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B05","text":"Action − motion − passion → order of origin; nature as principle → communication of the whole essence; power as principle by which → personally determined act.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A5","CH_GGVC_P_33:A12","CH_GGVC_P_33:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B06","text":"Immateriality of relations + simplicity of intellection and love + determination of nature → one term for each mode of procession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A17","CH_GGVC_P_33:A18","CH_GGVC_P_33:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FGS-B07","text":"Complete constitutive structure → common attributes are ordered appropriatively to persons → epistemic manifestation without new ontological distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A14","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:AFM-B01","text":"Unity of essence → exclusion of absolute division → opposition of relations → subsisting relation constituting persons → purified act of origin → natural communication of the whole essence → power as principle by which → uniqueness of processional terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AF1","CH_GGVC_P_32:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_33:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:AFM-B02","text":"Knowledge from creatures → analogical mode of signifying → more manifest essential attributes → appropriation to persons → manifestation of properties without demonstration or constitution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A6","CH_GGVC_P_31:A13","CH_GGVC_P_31:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-01","text":"The opposition between one and three collapses, because unity is assigned to essence and plurality to subsisting relations according to different ratios.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_32:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-02","text":"Relation, action, and power are reclassified respectively from accident, mutable event, and possibility toward opposites into subsistence, order of origin, and actual principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-03","text":"Semantics ceases to be an ornament of exposition and becomes a formal discipline that protects simplicity without confusion and distinction without partition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-04","text":"The opposition between voluntary and necessary is resolved, because concomitance of will, naturality of procession, necessity through itself, and absence of coercion are separated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-05","text":"The perfection of fecundity is no longer measured by a multitude of products, but by the integral communication of nature in a single processional term.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MME-06","text":"The distinction between manifestation and constitution opens a new epistemic field, in which common features indicate persons without effecting their properties.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:D9","CH_GGVC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B01","text":"At the level of surface, formulas concerning essence, persons, generation, relations, and acts are admitted or rejected according to rules of predication.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, simplicity removes all absolute distinctions, subsisting relation constitutes persons, and communication of nature together with order of origin orders the processions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, modes of signifying and formal distinctions prevent the errors of division of essence, confusion of persons, creation of the Son, and intradivine contingency.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, reality is simple, perfectly actual, and non-successive, while priority is distributed only according to diverse ratios of relation, act, and term.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_33:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the text effects the doctrine itself through repeated distinctions: the form of argument preserves identity while separating functions, just as ontology itself preserves unity while distinguishing persons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-01","text":"The identity of relation, essence, and person in reality is connected with differences of predication only through mode of signifying; this joint is necessary, but imposes a great ontological burden upon semantics.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-02","text":"Origin as act is denied to be the first principle of constitution, although every origin must be designated by an act; the distinction of way, relation, and person orders the tension, but does not wholly remove it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_33:A2","CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-03","text":"The Father's will necessarily accompanies generation but does not originate it; freedom is therefore separated from contingency, in which sense voluntary must be strictly distinguished from proceeding from a voluntary principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-04","text":"The power of generating is called common according to essence, but the generative act remains proper to the Father; direct, indirect, and relational connotation contain this asymmetry.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_33:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-05","text":"Closure of the number of persons rests upon principles concerning immaterial individuation and the determination of nature toward one, which are assumed rather than fully proved within this group.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:FL-06","text":"The matrices of appropriation rest upon selective similarities; their manifestative force stands, but the necessity of individual distributions is less than the necessity of relational constitution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_31:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MP-01","text":"Relation changes from a sign of distinction into the very subsisting form constituting hypostasis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_32:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MP-02","text":"Action is converted from an event implying change into a mode of signifying the order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_33:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MP-03","text":"Power changes from possibility not yet complete into the perfection of a principle by which that which is already actual operates.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_33:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_33:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MP-04","text":"Number is transferred from a morphological rule of names into a principle for the closure of personal terms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:A9","CH_GGVC_P_33:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly imagined as a simple essence that contains no parts, but articulates itself personally through opposed relations and expresses itself through acts of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_33:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:HSI-02","text":"The subject is not an absolute nucleus clothed with properties, but a subsisting term of relation whose very correlativity constitutes personal distinction and identity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_32:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:HSI-03","text":"Processional time is erased: no real before and after is given, but only intelligible orders according to relation, action, and the way to the term.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_33:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:HSI-04","text":"Navigation within the system occurs through grammatical and apophatic gates: each formula is tested as to whether it preserves unity, distinction, and origin, while the divine mode itself remains unavailable to created knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_31:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B01","text":"Axioms concerning simplicity, real identity, subsisting relation, purified act, communication of nature, and actual power suffice to reconstruct the principal structure of this group.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B02","text":"The preceding proofs concerning simplicity, processions, and individuation of immaterial relations are not sufficiently determined; these conditions remain as external foundations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B03","text":"The system coheres if identity of thing, distinction of reason, relational constitution, and plurality of intelligible orders are retained simultaneously and strictly.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_32:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B04","text":"The strongest structure is the transition from simplicity to subsisting relation and thence to action without motion and consubstantial generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B05","text":"The necessity of individual appropriations and the ultimate proof of the uniqueness of terms resist full reduction, their rationales remaining selective or assumed from elsewhere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_14:MRT-B06","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement, because it resolves the question of unity and plurality through relation, transfers the solution into semantics, amplifies it into acts and power, and terminates in numerical closure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_31:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_33:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_14@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_14:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 40–42","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 39 · Prima pars · Quaestio 40 · Prima pars · Quaestio 41"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 43–45","order":15,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_34","CH_GGVC_P_35","CH_GGVC_P_36"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_15@R001","sha256":"9692be7cd96a92277dba0090e4309475a3d7d41854d6c80b2274fe9b6b68c549","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo ab uno Deo simul constitui possint distinctio personarum aequalium, missio temporalis earum et dependentia universalis creaturarum, nulla in Deo divisione, mutatione aut indigentia inducta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis distinguit originem personalem, terminum temporalem et causalitatem participativam, eas tamen sub una plenitudine divina sine compositione ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio categorias creatas non simpliciter removet, sed in perfectionem transferibilem et defectum removendum dividit antequam ad divina applicentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-04","text":"Motus procedit a comparatione personarum ad praesentiam earum in creatura, deinde ad universalem processionem totius esse creati a primo principio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-05","text":"Progressus est recursivus et mutatione actus, quia processio redit primo ut ordo intradivinus, deinde ut missio ad terminum creatum, postremo ut emanatio universalis entis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD7","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-06","text":"Omnis defectus successionis, distantiae, indigentiae et inferioritatis ad modum creatum relegatur, dum relatio, communicatio et causalitas ut perfectiones servantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-07","text":"Probatio per distinctiones typorum operatur: essentia a relatione, origo a termino, praesentia communis ab inhabitatione, causa una a rationibus causalibus distinguitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_36:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-08","text":"Clausura systematis est plenitudo communicativa quae pluralitatem personarum, modorum praesentiae et creaturarum generat sine augmento, partitione aut acquisitione perfectionis divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A16","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Omnis perfectio absoluta personis communis est, dum distinctio personalis in relationibus originis realiter oppositis consistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Origo analogice ordinatur: ad intra asymmetriam relationis sine inferioritate constituit, in missione rationem personae mittibilis praebet, in creatione dependentiam esse participati significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Processio ab interioritate subsistente ad habitudinem temporalem missionis et inde ad emanationem universalem entis transit, quin hi tres modi in unum genus univocum contrahantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Praedicatum creatum ad divina transfertur tantum post distinctionem perfectionis significatae a dimensione, successione, motu, indigentia vel limitatione.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Aeternitas et immutabilitas divina omnem novitatem intrinsecam excludunt, sed relationem ad effectum vel receptorem temporaliter innovatum non excludunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Praesentia divina tribus modis ordinatur: ut mutua praesentia personarum, ut praesentia causalis omnibus rebus communis et ut inhabitatio fruitiva creaturae rationalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Causalitas effectuum ad extra est communis uni principio divino, sed ratio personalis missionis secundum relationes originis distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Plenitudo divina communicat sine amissione: naturam integram personis, praesentiam personalem per gratiam et esse atque bonitatem creaturis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Esse, forma et bonum creatum sunt modi participationis, quorum determinatio et perfectio a primo principio simplici dependent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Pluralitas relationum, idearum, effectuum et creaturarum compositionem in Deo non constituit neque ullam regionem ontologicam extra causalitatem primi principii relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-01","text":"Identitas stabilis est plenitudo simplicis esse divini: in personarum aequalitate et in causalitate primi entis eadem indivisio manet, quamvis munus argumentativum mutetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-02","text":"Origo redit functionaliter: primo ordinem relationum constituit, deinde missionem personae specificat, postremo in dependentiam causalem entis participati transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-03","text":"Processio mutatur ab interioritate sine distantia in relationem ad terminum temporalem, atque inde in emanationem quae non mutationem particularem sed totum esse respicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-04","text":"Praesentia amplificatur a mutua inexistentia personarum ad causalitatem communem in omnibus, deinde ad inhabitationem cognitivam et amativam in creatura rationali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-05","text":"Aequalitas intra divinitatem identitatem perfectionis exprimit, sed in ordine creato in similitudinem participatam sine aequalitate naturae transformatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_36:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-06","text":"Pluralitas functionem mutat: relationes personas distinguunt, effectus missiones appropriant, respectus ideas multiplicant, participationes autem creaturarum diversitatem constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-07","text":"Temporalitas ab ipsa origine removetur, in innovationem recipientis transfertur et tandem sub causalitate universali absorbetur quae successionem inter rationes primi principii non requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-01","text":"Comparatio localis secundum coaeternitatem, magnitudinem, praesentiam et potentiam sursum contrahitur in invariantem consubstantialitatis: omnis perfectio absoluta indivise communis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-02","text":"Distinctiones inter illuminationem, caritatem, gradus innovationis et signa visibilia missionis locales manent; ad gradum praesentem ascendit sola structura originis aeternae cum termino creato novo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A12","CH_GGVC_P_35:A14","CH_GGVC_P_35:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-03","text":"Materia prima, pluralitas idearum et appetitus naturalis sunt probationes locales; sursum amplificantur ut inclusio potentiae, formae et finis sub causalitate universali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:D2","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-04","text":"Transitus ab aequalitate personarum ad missionem efficitur cum asymmetria originis, iam ab inferioritate separata, fit ratio mittentis et missi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-05","text":"Transitus a missione ad creationem efficitur cum principium effectus temporalis commune Trinitati extenditur in causalitatem totius campi entis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A18","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-06","text":"Exemplaria creaturalia univoca, motus localis et fieri ex subiecto superantur; persistit autem regula distinguendi modum praedicationis ante applicationem ad Deum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ME8","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-01","text":"Origo personalis nec prioritatem essentiae nec imperium dominativum nec gradum minorem perfectionis constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_35:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-02","text":"Generatio et missio divina neque fieri temporale neque motum localem neque mutationem intrinsecam Dei continent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_35:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-03","text":"Nulla materia, potentia vel portio esse creati principium increatum aut causaliter autonomum a Deo constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-04","text":"Exemplaria non sunt res separatae extra Deum, nec pluralitas rationum causalium pluralitatem realium principiorum inducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-05","text":"Deus nec praesentiam prius absentem nec finem acquisitum nec perfectionem ab extrinseca mensura recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse debet unum genus univocum derivationis generationem divinam, missionem et creationem exhaurire, quia tale genus defectus processionis creatae ad omnes ordines transferret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse debet omnem distinctionem realem divisionem substantiae exigere vel omnem pluralitatem attributorum compositionem realem in Deo constituere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse debet omnem productionem aut praedicationem temporalem mutationem in producente divino inferre, quia terminus novus et emanatio universalis aliter ordinantur quam fieri particulare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse debet effectum creatum donationem divinam exhaurire vel similitudinem participatam identitatem cum fonte constituere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D5","CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSA-01","text":"Possibilitas ontologici exterioris, in quo Deus abesset aut quod extra causalitatem eius subsisteret, systemati indisponibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSA-02","text":"Systema simul excludit alteritatem independentem et unitatem absorbentem: personae distinguuntur sine essentiis diversis, creaturae autem participant sine identitate naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_36:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSA-03","text":"Inadmissibilis est Deus qui successione, mensura externa aut fine acquirendo perficiatur; tota generativitas ex plenitudine iam perfecta procedere debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-01","text":"Quia origo personalis ordinem sine gradu perfectionis constituit, missio Filii vel Spiritus originem a mittente exprimit quin imperium aut minorationem importet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-01","CL_GGVC_15:GA-02","CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-02","text":"Missio invisibilis praesentiam causalem universalem praesupponit sed eam superat, quia non novum esse Dei in loco, sed novam capacitatem cognoscendi, amandi et fruendi constituit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-06","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-03","text":"Esse ab alio bifariam typandum est: in persona divina relationem originis sine defectu, in creatura participationem esse cum dependentia causali significat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-02","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-04","text":"Unitas operationis ad extra non delet distributionem personalem missionum, quia effectus est a causa divina communi, ratio autem personae missae ab ordine originis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-07","CL_GGVC_15:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-05","text":"Gratia creata cadit sub universali participatione bonitatis, sed singulariter disponit creaturam rationalem ad donum increatum ipsius personae divinae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-08","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-06","text":"Tempus non metitur vitam aut causalitatem divinam, sed ordinem terminorum receptorum: aeternitas originis, innovatio creaturae et distinctio rationum causalium sine successione reali componuntur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-07","text":"Praedicata relationalia de Deo non unum statum ontologicum habent: relationes personales realiter subsistunt, relationes temporales ex effectu novo praedicantur, rationes exemplares secundum respectus multiplicantur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-01","CL_GGVC_15:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-08","text":"Nulla forma univoca exitus potest generationem, missionem et creationem regere; earum unitas consistit in communicatione perfectionis, non in identitate modi productionis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-03","CL_GGVC_15:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_34:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSD-01","text":"Systema duas asymmetrias non convertibiles constituit: asymmetria originis inter personas aequales et asymmetria participationis inter Deum et creaturam ontologice dependentem.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-02","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSD-02","text":"Aeternitas non est sterilitas causalis, sed exclusio successionis in fonte qui varios terminos temporales sine interna mutatione producit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSD-03","text":"Creatura rationalis fit locus ubi dependentia universalis entis in capacitatem fruitivae praesentiae elevatur; gratia creaturalitatem non tollit, sed modum participationis transformat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-06","CL_GGVC_15:GA-08","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSD-04","text":"Creatio et missio sub attractore communicationis sine indigentia conveniunt, sed terminis differunt: creatio esse et bonum participatum constituit, missio personam ut fruibilem donat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-08","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus analogicus procedit a similitudine creata ad detectionem defectus, a remotione defectus ad conservationem perfectionis, atque ab hac conservatione ad praedicationem divinam typis distinctam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-02","text":"Circuitus intradivinus procedit ab essentia indivisa ad relationes oppositas, a relationibus ad ordinem originis et ab ordine ad aequalitatem quae divisionem essentiae iterum excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-03","text":"Via missionis amplificatur ab origine aeterna ad terminum creatum novum, inde ad gratiam, inhabitationem, donationem personae et manifestationem visibilem selectivam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-04","text":"Via creationis amplificatur ab esse participato ad determinationem formarum, a formis ad bona particularia et a bonis ad ordinationem universalem in bonitatem divinam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-05","text":"Attractor totius est plenitudo simplex quae pluralitatem communicat et ad unitatem causalitatis reducit sine differentiarum personalium aut creaturalium absorptionе.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B01","text":"Praedicatum creaturale → separatio perfectionis a defectu → determinatio generis relationis → translatio analogica ad divina constituit operatorem communem argumentationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B02","text":"Essentia numerice una et plena + relationes originis subsistentes et oppositae → distinctio personarum sine divisione → ordo sine hierarchia → aequalitas absoluta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B03","text":"Processio personalis aeterna + terminus temporaliter novus in creatura + gratia sanctificans → missio sine motu divino → inhabitatio et fruitio personae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B04","text":"Esse participatum + determinatio exemplaris + ordinatio ad bonum → causalitas efficiens, exemplaris et finalis omnium creaturarum ab uno principio simplici.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A5","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B05","text":"Distinctio personalis ad intra + causalitas communis ad extra + pluralitas respectuum et participationum → multiplicatio ordinata sine multiplicatione reali primi principii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:D8","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:AFM-B01","text":"Comparatio personarum → obiectiones ex modis creatis → remotio successionis et quantitatis → distinctio essentiae et relationis → aequalitas cum ordine originis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_34:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:AFM-B02","text":"Ordo originis → habitudo ad terminum creatum → novitas in recipiente → gratia et inhabitatio → missio personaliter distincta sine mutatione divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:AFM-B03","text":"Esse participatum → emanatio universalis → inclusio potentiae et materiae → rationes exemplares → communicatio bonitatis ut finis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:AFM-B04","text":"Distinctio principii personalis et principii effectus → causalitas communis primi principii → pluralitas modorum sine pluralitate fontium → clausura in plenitudine communicativa.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-01","text":"Axis originis separatur ab axe dependentiae: esse ab alio potest intra Trinitatem ordinem sine inferioritate, extra Trinitatem autem participationem causaliter dependentem significare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-02","text":"Processio reclassificatur in ordines non univocos: processio personalis ad terminum aeternum, missio ad terminum temporalem et emanatio universalis ipsius esse creati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-03","text":"Praesentia desinit esse oppositio simplex praesentiae et absentiae atque fit tabula mutuae inexistentiae, causalitatis communis et inhabitationis fruitivae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_34:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-04","text":"Pluralitas reclassificatur secundum modum constitutionis: relativa in personis, appropriata in missionibus, intentionalis in ideis et participativa in creaturis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-05","text":"Causalitas divina non iam uno actu efficienti exhauritur, sed ut unitas realis rationum efficientis, exemplaris et finalis legitur, servata distinctione ab origine personali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A13","CH_GGVC_P_36:D8","CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei comparationem personarum, missiones visibiles et invisibiles atque causalitatem omnium entium, materia prima inclusa, tractat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis essentiam, relationem, terminum creatum et participationem coniungit ut matricem quae distinctionem personalem, praesentiam et dependentiam causaliter ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus obiectiones solvit mutando genus quaestionis: comparatio quantitativa fit relatio perfectionis, missio localis fit originis habitudo, mutatio particularis fit emanatio essendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis ponit Deum simplicem, aeternum et immutabilem, creaturas vero participantes atque temporaliter innovabiles sine successione reali in fonte.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus suam thesim efficit per repetitam purgationem vocabulorum: forma argumenti ipsa impedit ne distinctio in divisionem aut causalitas in mutationem convertatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FL-01","text":"Aequalitas personarum plenam reciprocitatem perfectionis postulat, sed origo asymmetriam non convertibilem retinet; systema hac tensione indiget ut distinctionem sine hierarchia servet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FL-02","text":"Operatio gratiae communis est Trinitati, missiones tamen personaliter distinguuntur per originem et appropriationem; nexus inter effectum communem et attributionem personalem commissura delicata manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FL-03","text":"Relatio nunc realiter subsistit, nunc ex effectu temporaliter praedicatur, nunc secundum respectum intellectualem multiplicatur; ambitus ontologicus relationis uniformiter definiri nequit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FL-04","text":"Gratia creata causatur a persona et ad personam habendam disponit; circulus vitatur distinctione causae et dispositionis, sed nexus doni creati cum dono increato ulteriorem explicationem requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MP-01","text":"Processio mutatur ubi ab interiori origine sine distantia transit ad missionem temporaliter terminatam et deinde ad emanationem universalem esse participati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MP-02","text":"Praesentia mutatur ubi identitas essentiae et correlatio personarum cedunt causalitati communi, quae iterum in inhabitationem rationalem per cognitionem et amorem intensificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MP-03","text":"Causalitas mutatur ubi causalitas originis, quae ad productionem efficientem externam reduci nequit, distinguitur a causalitate efficiente, exemplari et finali creaturarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:HSI-01","text":"Imago latens est machina simplicis actus: intra se relationes subsistentes sine partitione ordinat, extra se campum entium participantium sine multiplicatione fontis constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum rationale intra hanc machinam non est effectus clausus, sed ens causatum cui capacitas fruitionis personalis per gratiam superadditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:HSI-03","text":"Tempus non est linea per Deum transiens, sed series innovationum recipientium circa fontem aeternum; actio divina communicationem perfectionis, non acquisitionem sui, significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de perfectione absoluta communi, origine relative distinctiva, novitate in creatura et esse participato sufficiunt ad structuram huius gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est duplex distinctio inter absolutum et relativum atque inter originem aeternam et terminum creatum; teleologia communicationis boni clausuram universalem praebet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MRT-B03","text":"Minus determinatae manent identitas essentiae cum perfectione, nexus causalis doni creati et increati atque regula qua esse participatum causam essentialem postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MRT-B04","text":"Restitutio cohaeret quia verum motum servat: modos creatos purgat, originem a dependentia distinguit, novitatem ad creaturam transfert et pluralitatem sub unitate fontis ordinat; resistit tamen reductioni quae omnes relationes uno statu ontologico complecti vellet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT9","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171641939476Z_d3086929","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 43–45","source_sha256":"9692be7cd96a92277dba0090e4309475a3d7d41854d6c80b2274fe9b6b68c549","sha256":"917974b476e6f9c99c99bb41da957029d5440b41b2e9a2975248fc0a9ae4bffd","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:16:41.941708+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how the distinction of equal persons, their temporal mission, and the universal dependence of creatures can simultaneously be constituted by one God, without introducing into God any division, change, or need.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis distinguishes personal origin, temporal terminus, and participative causality, yet orders them under one divine fullness without composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-03","text":"The argument does not simply remove created categories, but divides them into perfection transferable and defect to be removed before they are applied to the divine.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-04","text":"The movement proceeds from the comparison of persons to their presence in the creature, then to the universal procession of all created being from the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-05","text":"The progression is recursive and mutation-driven, because procession returns first as an intradivine order, then as mission to a created terminus, and finally as the universal emanation of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD7","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-06","text":"Every defect of succession, distance, need, and inferiority is relegated to the created mode, while relation, communication, and causality are retained as perfections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-07","text":"The proof operates through distinctions of types: essence is distinguished from relation, origin from terminus, common presence from indwelling, and one cause from causal intelligibilities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A1","CH_GGVC_P_36:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BAS-08","text":"The system's closure is communicative fullness, which generates a plurality of persons, modes of presence, and creatures without increase, partition, or acquisition of divine perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A16","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every absolute perfection is common to the persons, while personal distinction consists in really opposed relations of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Origin is ordered analogically: ad intra it constitutes an asymmetry of relation without inferiority; in mission it provides the intelligibility of a person capable of being sent; in creation it signifies the dependence of participated being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Procession passes from subsisting interiority to the temporal relation of mission and thence to the universal emanation of being, without contracting these three modes into one univocal genus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] A created predicate is transferred to the divine only after distinguishing the perfection signified from dimension, succession, motion, need, or limitation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Divine eternity and immutability exclude every intrinsic novelty, but do not exclude relation to an effect or recipient temporally made new.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Divine presence is ordered in three modes: as the mutual presence of the persons, as causal presence common to all things, and as the enjoyable indwelling in the rational creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The causality of effects ad extra is common to the one divine principle, but the personal intelligibility of mission is distributed according to relations of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A17","CH_GGVC_P_35:A18","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Divine fullness communicates without loss: the whole nature to the persons, personal presence through grace, and being and goodness to creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Created being, form, and good are modes of participation, whose determination and perfection depend upon the simple first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] A plurality of relations, ideas, effects, and creatures neither constitutes composition in God nor leaves any ontological region outside the causality of the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-01","text":"The stable identity is the fullness of simple divine being: the same indivision remains in the equality of the persons and in the causality of the first being, although its argumentative role changes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-02","text":"Origin returns functionally: first it constitutes the order of relations, then specifies the mission of the person, and finally is transferred into the causal dependence of participated being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-03","text":"Procession changes from interiority without distance into relation to a temporal terminus, and thence into emanation, which concerns not particular change but all being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-04","text":"Presence is amplified from the mutual inherence of the persons to common causality in all things, then to cognitive and loving indwelling in the rational creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-05","text":"Equality within divinity expresses identity of perfection, but in the created order it is transformed into participated likeness without equality of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_36:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-06","text":"Plurality changes function: relations distinguish persons, effects appropriate missions, respects multiply ideas, while participations constitute the diversity of creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RMD-07","text":"Temporality is removed from origin itself, transferred into the newness of the recipient, and finally absorbed under universal causality, which does not require succession among the intelligibilities of the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-01","text":"The local comparison according to coeternity, magnitude, presence, and power is contracted upward into the invariant of consubstantiality: every absolute perfection is indivisibly common.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-02","text":"Distinctions among illumination, charity, degrees of newness, and visible signs of mission remain local; only the structure of eternal origin with a new created terminus ascends to the present level.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A12","CH_GGVC_P_35:A14","CH_GGVC_P_35:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-03","text":"Prime matter, the plurality of ideas, and natural appetite are local proofs; upward they are amplified as the inclusion of potency, form, and end under universal causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:D2","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-04","text":"The transition from equality of persons to mission occurs when asymmetry of origin, already separated from inferiority, becomes the intelligibility of sender and sent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-05","text":"The transition from mission to creation occurs when the principle of a temporal effect common to the Trinity is extended into the causality of the entire field of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A18","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:CGD-06","text":"Univocal creaturely exemplars, local motion, and coming-to-be from a subject are overcome; yet the rule of distinguishing the mode of predication before application to God persists.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ME8","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-01","text":"Personal origin constitutes neither priority of essence, nor dominative power, nor a lesser degree of perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_35:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-02","text":"Divine generation and mission contain neither temporal coming-to-be, nor local motion, nor intrinsic change of God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_35:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-03","text":"No matter, potency, or portion of created being constitutes an uncreated or causally autonomous principle apart from God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-04","text":"Exemplars are not separate things outside God, nor does a plurality of causal intelligibilities introduce a plurality of real principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:GNX-05","text":"God receives neither a presence previously absent, nor an acquired end, nor perfection from an extrinsic measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that one univocal genus of derivation exhausts divine generation, mission, and creation, because such a genus would transfer the defects of created procession to every order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that every real distinction requires a division of substance, or that every plurality of attributes constitutes real composition in God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that every temporal production or predication entails change in the divine producer, because a new terminus and universal emanation are ordered otherwise than particular coming-to-be.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that a created effect exhausts divine gift, or that participated likeness constitutes identity with the source.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D5","CH_GGVC_P_36:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSA-01","text":"The possibility of an ontological exterior in which God would be absent or which would subsist outside His causality is unavailable to the system.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSA-02","text":"The system simultaneously excludes independent otherness and absorbing unity: the persons are distinguished without diverse essences, while creatures participate without identity of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX6","CH_GGVC_P_36:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSA-03","text":"A God perfected by succession, external measure, or an acquired end is inadmissible; all generativity must proceed from already perfect fullness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_35:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-01","text":"Because personal origin constitutes order without a degree of perfection, the mission of the Son or Spirit expresses origin from the sender without importing dominion or diminution.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-01","CL_GGVC_15:GA-02","CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-02","text":"Invisible mission presupposes universal causal presence but surpasses it, because it constitutes not a new being of God in a place, but a new capacity for knowing, loving, and enjoying.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-06","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-03","text":"Being from another must be typed in two ways: in the divine person it signifies a relation of origin without defect; in the creature, participation of being with causal dependence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-02","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-04","text":"The unity of operation ad extra does not erase the personal distribution of missions, because the effect is from the common divine cause, while the intelligibility of the person sent is from the order of origin.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-07","CL_GGVC_15:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-05","text":"Created grace falls under universal participation in goodness, but singularly disposes the rational creature for the uncreated gift of the divine person itself.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-08","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-06","text":"Time does not measure divine life or causality, but the order of received termini: eternity of origin, newness of the creature, and distinction of causal intelligibilities without real succession are combined.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-07","text":"Relational predicates concerning God do not have one ontological status: personal relations really subsist, temporal relations are predicated from a new effect, and exemplary intelligibilities are multiplied according to respects.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-01","CL_GGVC_15:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:XD-08","text":"No univocal form of going forth can govern generation, mission, and creation; their unity consists in the communication of perfection, not in identity of the mode of production.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-03","CL_GGVC_15:GA-04","CH_GGVC_P_34:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_35:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSD-01","text":"The system constitutes two non-convertible asymmetries: the asymmetry of origin among equal persons and the asymmetry of participation between God and the ontologically dependent creature.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-02","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSD-02","text":"Eternity is not causal sterility, but the exclusion of succession in the source that produces diverse temporal termini without internal change.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSD-03","text":"The rational creature becomes the place where the universal dependence of being is elevated into the capacity for enjoyable presence; grace does not remove creatureliness but transforms the mode of participation.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-06","CL_GGVC_15:GA-08","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:BSD-04","text":"Creation and mission converge under the attractor of communication without need, but differ in their termini: creation constitutes participated being and goodness, while mission gives the person as enjoyable.","refs":["CL_GGVC_15:GA-08","CL_GGVC_15:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-01","text":"The analogical circuit proceeds from created likeness to the detection of defect, from the removal of defect to the preservation of perfection, and from this preservation to divine predication distinctly typed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-02","text":"The intradivine circuit proceeds from undivided essence to opposed relations, from relations to the order of origin, and from order to equality, which again excludes division of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-03","text":"The path of mission is amplified from eternal origin to a new created terminus, thence to grace, indwelling, the gift of the person, and selective visible manifestation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-04","text":"The path of creation is amplified from participated being to the determination of forms, from forms to particular goods, and from goods to universal ordering in divine goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A3","CH_GGVC_P_36:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:RLE-05","text":"The attractor of the whole is simple fullness, which communicates plurality and reduces it to unity of causality without absorption of personal or creaturely differences.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A17","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B01","text":"Created predicate → separation of perfection from defect → determination of the genus of relation → analogical transfer to the divine constitutes the common operator of the argument.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B02","text":"Numerically one and full essence + subsisting and opposed relations of origin → distinction of persons without division → order without hierarchy → absolute equality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B03","text":"Eternal personal procession + a temporally new terminus in the creature + sanctifying grace → mission without divine motion → indwelling and enjoyment of the person.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS2","CH_GGVC_P_35:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B04","text":"Participated being + exemplary determination + ordering to the good → efficient, exemplary, and final causality of all creatures from one simple principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A5","CH_GGVC_P_36:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FGS-B05","text":"Personal distinction ad intra + common causality ad extra + plurality of respects and participations → ordered multiplication without real multiplication of the first principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:D8","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_34:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:AFM-B01","text":"Comparison of persons → objections from created modes → removal of succession and quantity → distinction of essence and relation → equality with order of origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_34:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:AFM-B02","text":"Order of origin → relation to a created terminus → newness in the recipient → grace and indwelling → personally distinct mission without divine change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_35:A4","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:AFM-B03","text":"Participated being → universal emanation → inclusion of potency and matter → exemplary intelligibilities → communication of goodness as end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:AFM-B04","text":"Distinction between personal principle and principle of effect → common causality of the first principle → plurality of modes without plurality of sources → closure in communicative fullness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SD6","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-01","text":"The axis of origin is separated from the axis of dependence: being from another can signify order without inferiority within the Trinity, but causally dependent participation outside the Trinity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-02","text":"Procession is reclassified into non-univocal orders: personal procession to an eternal terminus, mission to a temporal terminus, and the universal emanation of created being itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-03","text":"Presence ceases to be the simple opposition of presence and absence and becomes a map of mutual inherence, common causality, and enjoyable indwelling.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6","CH_GGVC_P_34:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-04","text":"Plurality is reclassified according to its mode of constitution: relative in persons, appropriated in missions, intentional in ideas, and participative in creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MME-05","text":"Divine causality is no longer exhausted by one efficient act, but is read as the real unity of efficient, exemplary, and final intelligibilities, while preserving its distinction from personal origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_36:A13","CH_GGVC_P_36:D8","CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level treats the comparison of persons, visible and invisible missions, and the causality of all beings, prime matter included.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level joins essence, relation, created terminus, and participation as a matrix that causally orders personal distinction, presence, and dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level resolves objections by changing the genus of the question: quantitative comparison becomes a relation of perfection, local mission becomes a relation of origin, and particular change becomes the emanation of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level posits God as simple, eternal, and immutable, but creatures as participative and temporally capable of newness, without real succession in the source.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_36:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level effects its thesis through repeated purification of terms: the form of the argument itself prevents distinction from being converted into division or causality into change.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_36:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FL-01","text":"The equality of the persons demands full reciprocity of perfection, yet origin retains a non-convertible asymmetry; the system requires this tension in order to preserve distinction without hierarchy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FL-02","text":"The operation of grace is common to the Trinity, yet missions are personally distinguished through origin and appropriation; the nexus between common effect and personal attribution remains a delicate joint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FL-03","text":"Relation now really subsists, now is temporally predicated from an effect, now is multiplied according to an intellectual respect; the ontological scope of relation cannot be uniformly defined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A3","CH_GGVC_P_35:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_36:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:FL-04","text":"Created grace is caused by a person and disposes for possessing a person; the circle is avoided by distinguishing cause and disposition, but the nexus between created gift and uncreated gift requires further explanation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MP-01","text":"Procession changes where it passes from interior origin without distance to temporally terminated mission and then to the universal emanation of participated being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:A14","CH_GGVC_P_35:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MP-02","text":"Presence changes where identity of essence and correlation of persons yield to common causality, which is again intensified into rational indwelling through knowledge and love.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:D7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A5","CH_GGVC_P_35:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MP-03","text":"Causality changes where causality of origin, which cannot be reduced to external efficient production, is distinguished from the efficient, exemplary, and final causality of creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:HSI-01","text":"The hidden image is a machine of simple act: within itself it orders subsisting relations without partition; outside itself it constitutes the field of participating beings without multiplication of the source.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:FGS1","CH_GGVC_P_36:A13","CH_GGVC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:HSI-02","text":"The rational subject within this machine is not a closed effect, but a caused being to which the capacity for personal enjoyment is superadded through grace.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:A7","CH_GGVC_P_35:A9","CH_GGVC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:HSI-03","text":"Time is not a line passing through God, but a series of newnesses in recipients around the eternal source; divine action signifies communication of perfection, not acquisition of itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_35:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_34:A8","CH_GGVC_P_36:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms concerning common absolute perfection, relatively distinctive origin, newness in the creature, and participated being suffice to reconstruct the structure of this cluster.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the double distinction between absolute and relative, and between eternal origin and created terminus; the teleology of the communication of the good provides universal closure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MRT-B03","text":"Less determined remain the identity of essence with perfection, the causal nexus of created and uncreated gift, and the rule by which participated being requires an essential cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_15:MRT-B04","text":"The reconstruction coheres because it preserves the true movement: it purifies created modes, distinguishes origin from dependence, transfers newness to the creature, and orders plurality under unity of source; yet it resists a reduction that would seek to comprehend all relations under one ontological status.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_34:MRT9","CH_GGVC_P_35:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_36:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_15@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_15:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 43–45","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 42 · Prima pars · Quaestio 43 · Prima pars · Quaestio 44"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 46–48","order":16,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_37","CH_GGVC_P_38","CH_GGVC_P_39"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_16@R001","sha256":"ad36e4193b643cf74dcedaa983f09e1315366806218ad1ef60df08d098628f24","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo causa prima totum esse, initium durationis et universitatem distinctam producat, nulla materia, tempore vel coordinatione priore supposita.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis creationem constituit ut dependentiam totalem a Deo voluntario et sapiente, cuius effectus temporaliter incepit secundum fidem atque in pluralitatem ordinatam distribuitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_39:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio errores magnitudinis corrigit: categorias causalitatis particularis, probationes physicas et explicationes materiales vel fortuitas ab origine totius removet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-04","text":"Fundamentum metaphysicum est proportio inter amplitudinem effectus et causae: ipsum esse, quia universalissimum, neque subiectum antecedens neque causam secundam admittit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-05","text":"Demonstratio attingit dependentiam creatam et non-necessitatem aeternitatis, non autem liberam determinationem qua mundus reapse initium accepit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-06","text":"Finitudo cuiusque effectus singularis pluralitatem formarum et graduum exigit, ut bonitas divina per complementum totius perfectius repraesentetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-07","text":"Motus verus est recursivus et cumulativus: mutatio in relationem, necessitas in voluntatem, singularitas in distributionem, pluralitas denique in unitatem ordinis convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est ontologica et teleologica, quia omnia ad unum principium et finem ordinantur; non est tamen clausura demonstrativa, quia veritas initii temporalis revelationi reservatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Creatio est emanatio totius esse a causa universali, nullo ente tamquam materia vel subiecto antecedente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Creatione a motu remota, manet relatio realis qua creatura a Creatore ut principio sui esse dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Causalitas naturalis realis est, sed tantum intra ordinem iam creatum operatur neque creationi totius ordinis admiscetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] «Ex nihilo» stabiliter negat causam materialem, sed rationem temporalem «post nihilum» non ex sola notione creationis infert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Prioritas Dei transit a falsa antecedentia chronologica ad prioritatem causalem et aeternam, quia res cum tempore suo producuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Prima causa est voluntaria et sapiens; ideo duratio, distinctio et ordo effectuum ab intentione, non a necessitate naturali, procedunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A1","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Ratio naturalis cognoscit dependentiam mundi, sed liberam determinationem initii temporalis solum per revelationem accipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Quia nulla creatura bonitatem divinam adaequat, communicatio bonitatis ad pluralitatem complementariam universi tendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Diversitas, inaequalitas et unitas sunt effectus coordinati: gradatio formarum perficit totum, unitas autem ex ordine partium constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_39:D3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Omnia creata unum mundum constituunt quatenus mutuo et ad Deum ordinantur, exclusis co-principiis et totalitatibus independentibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-01","text":"Creatio identitatem fundamentalem retinet ut productio totius esse, sed ambitus eius a subsistentibus ad materiam, tempus et universitatem ordinatam extenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_39:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-02","text":"«Ex nihilo» ab exclusione causae materialis ad duplicem rationem non-de-aliquo et post-non-esse transit; prior ratio creationem definit, posterior actualem novitatem addit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-03","text":"Relatio a dependentia creaturae ad Creatorem migrat in prioritatem Dei non temporalem et tandem in unitatem mundi per ordinem relationum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-04","text":"Universalitas primum amplitudinem effectus et causae significat, deinde includit materiam ac tempus intra effectum, postremo omnia entia sub uno ordine complectitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_39:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-05","text":"Voluntas divina ex ratione productionis scientis in principium durationis contingentis mutatur atque in sapientiam distinctionem rerum ordinantem amplificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-06","text":"Insufficientia creaturae singularis non manet defectus privativus, sed fit machina positiva pluralitatis et mutuae suppletionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-07","text":"Forma, quae prius ut principium non subsistens a subiecto creationis distinguitur, postea fit principale principium distinctionis et gradationis universi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-01","text":"Distinctio subsistentis a forma et accidente manet determinatio localis subiecti creationis, sed sursum terminum constituit ne principia formalia tamquam entia separata reificentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A8","CH_GGVC_P_37:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-02","text":"Disputationes de infinito praeterito et seriebus causarum per accidens manent locales quaestioni durationis; hoc gradu tantum limites probationis naturalis sustentant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D10","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-03","text":"Enumeratio naturarum simul creatarum et appropriationes exegeticae non fiunt axiomata cosmologica universalia, sed temporalem et exemplarem clausuram primae productionis determinant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A18","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-04","text":"Negatio mutationis, localiter ad rationem creationis pertinens, sursum amplificatur in exclusionem omnis temporis, spatii vel status mundani creationi praesuppositi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-05","text":"Voluntas divina unitates coniungit: originem sine necessitate naturali, durationem contingentem et distinctionem sapienter intentam eodem principio explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-06","text":"Notiones «prius» et «unum» recodificantur: prioritas fit causalis potius quam temporalis, unitas autem ordinativa potius quam numerice simplex.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_39:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-01","text":"Nihilum neque materia neque subiectum est, nec aliquod ens productioni totius esse antecedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-02","text":"Nullum metatempus, spatium vacuum vel statum mundi priorem admittitur in quo creatio collocetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-03","text":"Nulla creatura, causa secunda vel natura spiritualis creationem totalem efficit aut primam productionem mediat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX17","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-04","text":"Aeternitas et unitas Dei neque effectum aeternum neque uniformitatem creaturarum naturali necessitate inferunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-05","text":"Mundi novitas non demonstratur ex quidditate, causalitate creativa vel scientia naturali, nec fides pseudodemonstratione eget.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-06","text":"Casus, materia et merita praecedentia neque distinctionem primam neque inaequalitatem originariam universi explicant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-07","text":"Aequalitas absoluta partium, multiplicatio mere numerica et pluralitas mundorum independentium non constituunt perfectionem finaliter intentam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-01","text":"Systema corrueret si Deus et creatura intra campum entis vel lineam durationis communem tamquam causae eiusdem ordinis continerentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-02","text":"Dependentia causalis non potest successionem temporalem inter causam primam et effectum essentialiter includere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-03","text":"Nulla creatura finita potest esse sui ipsius ratio sufficiens aut repraesentatio exhaustiva bonitatis divinae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-04","text":"Ordo universalis non potest ex concursu posteriori partium antea independentium emergere, quia mutua ordinatio ad rationem primae constitutionis pertinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-05","text":"Distinctio rationis et revelationis deleri non potest: metaphysica structuram possibilitatis tuetur, sed decretum contingens non producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSA-01","text":"Altissima exclusio est absentia omnis tertii ontologici—receptaculi, medii vel metat temporis—inter Creatorem et universitatem creatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSA-02","text":"Possibilitas inadmissibilis creaturae singularis perfecte adaequantis Deum vim distributivam systematis generat; si talis effectus daretur, pluralitas repraesentativa cessaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSA-03","text":"Nulla mensura univoca durationis vel perfectionis Deum, mundum et singulas partes continet; inde neque coaequalitas temporalis neque aequalitas partium admittitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSA-04","text":"Systema circum absentiam accessus naturalis ad decretum concretum ordinatur: ratio structuram creationis et ordinis cognoscit, non cur hic initium et hi gradus electi sint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-01","text":"Creatio manet ratio totalis dependentiae sive effectus initium temporale habeat sive aeternus dialectice ponatur; novitas temporalis est determinatio libera superaddita, non pars definitionis minimae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-01","CL_GGVC_16:GA-04","CL_GGVC_16:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_38:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-02","text":"Quia nec subiectum nec tempus praecedit, primum nunc non recipit creationem ut eventum mensuratum, sed cum rebus producitur ut limes originarius successionis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-01","CL_GGVC_16:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-03","text":"Pluralitas non imponitur primae causae extrinsecus: posito fine communicandae bonitatis, insufficientia effectus singularis fit ratio sapienter intenta distributionis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-06","CL_GGVC_16:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-04","text":"Relatio creationis et unitas mundi eandem formam diversis magnitudinibus exprimunt: creatura singularis ad principium sui esse, universitas autem per ordinem omnium ad unum refertur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-02","CL_GGVC_16:GA-09","CL_GGVC_16:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-05","text":"Causae secundae differentiationem intra materiam et formas exercent, sed neque esse absolute neque consilium totius ordinis producunt.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-03","CL_GGVC_16:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-06","text":"Ratio ad necessitatem structurae—dependentiam, contingentiam, pluralitatem ordinatam—pervenit, sed actuale initium et distributionem singularum formarum incompleta relinquit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-07","CL_GGVC_16:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-07","text":"Processiones Verbi et Amoris, exemplar in Filio et communicatio bonitatis convergunt in imaginem creationis ut actus intellectualis, voluntarii et communicativi, non ut effluxus naturaliter necessarius.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-06","CL_GGVC_16:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_37:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-01","text":"Mundus secundum fidem initium durationis habet, sed eius creaturalitas formaliter non in initio sed in relatione totalis dependentiae consistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-02","text":"Causalitas fit hierarchia inclusiva: Deus esse, tempus et ordinem dat; creaturae ex principiis receptis effectus particulares intra illum ordinem producunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-03","text":"Tempus non est continens mundi, sed modus successionis creatus; ideo primum nunc originem temporis designat, dum aeternitas divina extra successionem manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-04","text":"Epistemologia systematis asymmetrica est: ratio demonstrat ordinem dependentiae et removet contradictiones, revelatio autem determinat novitatem temporalem, sapientia divina distributionem concretam retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-05","text":"Creatura rationalis est simul imago activa et lector finitus: verbo et amore principium repraesentat, sed decretum liberum et totam rationem distributionis non comprehendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A16","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_39:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus creationis est: effectus universalissimus excludit subiectum prius; exclusio subiecti excludit mutationem; exclusio mutationis relinquit relationem; relatio universalem dependentiam confirmat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-02","text":"Circuitus repraesentationis est: finita insufficientia generat pluralitatem; pluralitas formas graduat; gradatio complementum totius auget; bonum totius partes vicissim mensurat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:D2","CH_GGVC_P_39:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-03","text":"Via voluntatis progreditur a non-necessitate creaturarum ad contingentiam durationis, inde ad limitem rationis et tandem ad revelationem decreti temporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-04","text":"Negatio amplificatur a materia praesupposita ad tempus vacuum, a causa creata ad casum cosmicum, et ab his ad exclusiónem totalitatum independentium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-05","text":"«Ordo» est attractor communis: ordinat operationem divinam et processiones, principium temporale et exemplare, formas inaequales atque omnia ad unum finem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B01","text":"Categoriae locales—materia, motus, tempus, causalitas particularis et concursus partium—primum exhibentur ut exemplaria insufficientia originis universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B02","text":"Amplitudo effectus augetur usque ad ipsum esse; hac mutatione magnitudinis materia, tempus et spatium ex condicionibus exterioribus in effectus internos transferuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B03","text":"Remotis subiecto et mutatione, productio universalis formaliter restituitur ut relatio realis dependentiae creaturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B04","text":"Causa voluntaria durationem et distinctionem non necessitate naturae sed praedefinitione sapientiae determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B05","text":"Finita repraesentatio distribuit bonitatem in formas diversas; diversitas gradus inaequales parit, quorum complementum perfectionem universi constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B06","text":"Mutua ordinatio partium claudit pluralitatem in unum mundum, intra quem causalitas naturalis operatur et ultra quem sola causa prima esse absolute producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:AFM-B01","text":"Distinctio emanationis universalis → exclusio subiecti prioris → resolutio mutationis in relationem → contingentia durationis → limes demonstrationis → determinatio revelata initii → distributio bonitatis in formas → gradatio partium → unitas ordinis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:AFM-B02","text":"Quotiens materia, tempus, necessitas, casus vel aequalitas totum explicare conantur, systema ad amplitudinem causae primae redit atque condiciones suppositas intra effectum creatum reponit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-01","text":"«Creatum» et «temporaliter inceptum» fiunt rationes distinctae: primum dependentiam, secundum liberam determinationem durationis significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_37:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-02","text":"Causae reclassificantur secundum amplitudinem effectus: causa prima dat esse et agrum causalitatis, causae secundae tantum intra agrum datum agunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-03","text":"Perfectio transfertur a maxima perfectione cuiusque partis ad proportionem et coordinationem totius graduati.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_39:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-04","text":"Unitas mundi desinit esse nudam singularitatem numericam et fit unitas relationis, ordinis et finis communis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_39:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-05","text":"Defensio doctrinalis reordinatur: ratio contradictiones removet et fines suos servat, neque contingentem veritatem revelatam in necessitatem simulatam convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei examinantur modus creationis, initium universi et ratio multitudinis, inaequalitatis atque unitatis mundi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali agunt relatio dependentiae, contingentia voluntatis et ordo partium, quae originem, durationem et formam universi connectunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico systema translationes illicitas inter causalitatem particularem et universalem detegit atque rationem, fidem et bonum totius diversis officiis assignat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas creata est nexus relationum finitarum, tempus est effectus, et pluralitas graduata modum participationis bonitatis constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo textus propriam thesim efficit removendo successive subiectum, tempus, necessitatem, casum et aequalitatem tamquam falsa principia totius.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FL-01","text":"«Ex nihilo» oscillat inter negationem materiae et ordinem ad non esse; cohaerentia requirit ne posterior sensus temporaliter in definitionem creationis simpliciter inseratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FL-02","text":"Relatio creationis creaturam iam existentem quasi subiectum requirit, quamvis ipsam dependentiam qua creatura esse accipit significet; distinctio prioritatis obiectivae et subiectivae commissuram sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D5","CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FL-03","text":"Actualis novitas mundi est centralis sed ex axiomatibus metaphysicis non sequitur; systema praemissa revelata indiget sine qua statum temporalem indeterminatum relinqueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FL-04","text":"Unitas mundi firmiter ex ordine actuali deducitur, sed transitus a potentia divina plurium mundorum ad necessitatem unius totalitatis actualis non plene resolvitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MP-01","text":"Punctum mutationis primum creationem ex genere eventus vel motus in genus relationis ontologicae transfert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MP-02","text":"«Principium» a simplici indice originis mutatur in nodum temporis, exemplaritatis in Filio et immediationis causalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MP-03","text":"Multitudo, initio quasi repugnantia unitati divinae posita, in instrumentum necessarium repraesentationis distributae convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_39:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MP-04","text":"Inaequalitas ab apparente iniustitia primae distributionis ad structuram formalem boni totius mutatur, quamvis ratio singularis allocationis in sapientia divina remaneat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_39:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite est campus ordinatus a centro causali productus, non receptaculum praeexistens: materia, tempus, formae et relationes intra eundem effectum continentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:HSI-02","text":"Creatura est nodus receptivus et activus: esse, determinationem et ordinem recipit, deinde secundum formam propriam intra totum operatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A16","CH_GGVC_P_39:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est linea ab origine simul cum mundo explicata; nullum «ante» eam continet, et aeternitas divina ei non continuatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:HSI-04","text":"Mundus est quasi distributio prismatica bonitatis simplicis: nulla pars lumen totum adaequat, sed differentiae graduatae in una figura ordinata complentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:D2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de creatione universali, voluntate contingenti, repraesentatione finita et unitate ordinis sufficiunt ad originem, durationem et structuram universi hoc gradu restituendas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MRT-B02","text":"Compages firmissima est nexus quo universalitas effectus excludit subiectum, creatio a motu separatur, et insufficientia singularis pluralitatem ordinatam generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum satis determinantur liberum decretum initii, distributio singularum formarum et necessitas unici ordinis inter omnes effectus possibiles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MRT-B04","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat si creationem, initium temporale, pluralitatem et unitatem non ut conclusiones aequales, sed ut gradus relationis, determinationis liberae et ordinationis totius distinguit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT9","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171721065844Z_bf175243","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 46–48","source_sha256":"ad36e4193b643cf74dcedaa983f09e1315366806218ad1ef60df08d098628f24","sha256":"3e5b9326ca7c89bfa8ca9184c6781ec2660d95f5fd8be341f3f89ff266566ddb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:17:21.067912+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how the first cause produces all being, the beginning of duration, and a distinct universe, with no prior matter, time, or coordination presupposed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis establishes creation as total dependence on a voluntary and wise God, whose effect began temporally according to faith and is distributed into an ordered plurality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_39:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-03","text":"The argument corrects errors of scale: it removes the categories of particular causality, physical proofs, and material or chance explanations from the origin of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-04","text":"The metaphysical foundation is the proportion between the scope of the effect and the cause: being itself, because it is most universal, admits neither an antecedent subject nor a secondary cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-05","text":"The demonstration reaches created dependence and the non-necessity of eternity, but not the free determination by which the world in fact received a beginning.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-06","text":"The finitude of each singular effect requires a plurality of forms and degrees, so that divine goodness may be represented more perfectly through the complement of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-07","text":"The true movement is recursive and cumulative: change is converted into relation, necessity into will, singularity into distribution, and finally plurality into unity of order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BAS-08","text":"The closure is ontological and teleological, because all things are ordered to one principle and end; it is not, however, demonstrative closure, because the truth of the temporal beginning is reserved to revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Creation is the emanation of all being from a universal cause, with no being antecedent as matter or subject.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A1","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Once creation is removed from motion, there remains the real relation by which the creature depends on the Creator as the principle of its being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Natural causality is real, but it operates only within the already created order and is not mixed into the creation of the whole order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] «Ex nihilo» steadily denies a material cause, but does not infer the temporal account «post nihilum» from the notion of creation alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] The priority of God shifts from false chronological antecedence to causal and eternal priority, because things are produced with their time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A8","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The first cause is voluntary and wise; therefore the duration, distinction, and order of effects proceed from intention, not from natural necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A1","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Natural reason knows the dependence of the world, but receives the free determination of the temporal beginning only through revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Because no creature equals divine goodness, the communication of goodness tends toward the complementary plurality of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Diversity, inequality, and unity are coordinated effects: the gradation of forms perfects the whole, while unity is constituted from the order of the parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_39:D3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] All created things constitute one world insofar as they are mutually ordered and ordered to God, excluding co-principles and independent totalities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-01","text":"Creation retains its fundamental identity as the production of all being, but its scope is extended from subsistent things to matter, time, and the ordered universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:A6","CH_GGVC_P_39:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-02","text":"«Ex nihilo» shifts from the exclusion of a material cause to the twofold account of not-from-something and after-non-being; the former account defines creation, the latter adds actual newness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-03","text":"Relation migrates from the creature's dependence on the Creator into the non-temporal priority of God and finally into the unity of the world through the order of relations.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-04","text":"Universality first signifies the scope of effect and cause, then includes matter and time within the effect, and finally embraces all beings under one order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_39:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-05","text":"The divine will is transformed from the account of knowing production into the principle of contingent duration and is expanded into wisdom ordering the distinction of things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-06","text":"The insufficiency of the singular creature does not remain a privative defect, but becomes a positive engine of plurality and mutual supplementation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RMD-07","text":"Form, which was earlier distinguished from the subject of creation as a non-subsistent principle, later becomes the principal principle of the distinction and gradation of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A9","CH_GGVC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-01","text":"The distinction of the subsistent from form and accident remains a local determination of the subject of creation, but above it establishes a boundary preventing formal principles from being reified as separate beings.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A8","CH_GGVC_P_37:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-02","text":"Disputations concerning the infinite past and series of causes per accidens remain local to the question of duration; at this level they support only the limits of natural proof.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:D10","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-03","text":"The enumeration of natures created simultaneously and exegetical appropriations do not become universal cosmological axioms, but determine the temporal and exemplary closure of the first production.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A18","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-04","text":"The negation of change, locally pertaining to the account of creation, is amplified above into the exclusion of every time, space, or worldly state presupposed to creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-05","text":"The divine will joins the unities: it explains by the same principle origin without natural necessity, contingent duration, and wisely intended distinction.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:CGD-06","text":"The notions of «before» and «one» are recoded: priority becomes causal rather than temporal, and unity ordering rather than numerically simple.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_39:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-01","text":"Nothing is neither matter nor subject, nor does any being antecede the production of all being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-02","text":"No meta-time, empty space, or prior state of the world is admitted in which creation may be situated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-03","text":"No creature, secondary cause, or spiritual nature effects total creation or mediates the first production.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX17","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-04","text":"The eternity and unity of God infer neither an eternal effect nor uniformity of creatures by natural necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-05","text":"The newness of the world is not demonstrated from quiddity, creative causality, or natural knowledge, nor does faith require pseudo-demonstration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-06","text":"Chance, matter, and preceding merits explain neither the first distinction nor the original inequality of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:GNX-07","text":"Absolute equality of parts, merely numerical multiplication, and a plurality of independent worlds do not constitute the finally intended perfection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-01","text":"The system would collapse if God and creature were contained within a common field of being or line of duration as causes of the same order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-02","text":"Causal dependence cannot essentially include temporal succession between the first cause and the effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-03","text":"No finite creature can be its own sufficient reason or an exhaustive representation of divine goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-04","text":"Universal order cannot emerge from the subsequent concurrence of previously independent parts, because mutual ordering pertains to the account of first constitution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:DBN-05","text":"The distinction of reason and revelation cannot be erased: metaphysics safeguards the structure of possibility, but does not produce the contingent decree.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSA-01","text":"The highest exclusion is the absence of every third ontological term—a receptacle, medium, or meta-time—between the Creator and the created universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSA-02","text":"The inadmissible possibility of a singular creature perfectly equaling God generates the distributive force of the system; if such an effect were given, representative plurality would cease.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSA-03","text":"No univocal measure of duration or perfection contains God, the world, and individual parts; hence neither temporal co-equality nor equality of parts is admitted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSA-04","text":"The system is ordered around the absence of natural access to the concrete decree: reason knows the structure of creation and order, not why this beginning and these degrees were chosen.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-01","text":"Creation remains the account of total dependence whether the effect has a temporal beginning or is dialectically posited as eternal; temporal newness is a superadded free determination, not part of the minimal definition.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-01","CL_GGVC_16:GA-04","CL_GGVC_16:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_38:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-02","text":"Because neither subject nor time precedes, the first now does not receive creation as a measured event, but is produced with things as the originating limit of succession.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-01","CL_GGVC_16:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-03","text":"Plurality is not imposed extrinsically on the first cause: once the end of communicating goodness is posited, the insufficiency of a singular effect becomes the wisely intended account of distribution.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-06","CL_GGVC_16:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-04","text":"The relation of creation and the unity of the world express the same form at different scales: the singular creature refers to the principle of its being, while the universe refers through the order of all things to one.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-02","CL_GGVC_16:GA-09","CL_GGVC_16:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-05","text":"Secondary causes exercise differentiation within matter and forms, but produce neither being absolutely nor the plan of the whole order.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-03","CL_GGVC_16:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-06","text":"Reason arrives at the necessity of structure—dependence, contingency, ordered plurality—but leaves the actual beginning and distribution of singular forms incomplete.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-07","CL_GGVC_16:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:XD-07","text":"The processions of Word and Love, the exemplar in the Son, and the communication of goodness converge in an image of creation as an intellectual, voluntary, and communicative act, not as a naturally necessary outflow.","refs":["CL_GGVC_16:GA-06","CL_GGVC_16:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_37:A14","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-01","text":"According to faith, the world has a beginning of duration, but its creatureliness formally consists not in its beginning but in the relation of total dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-02","text":"Causality becomes an inclusive hierarchy: God gives being, time, and order; creatures produce particular effects from received principles within that order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-03","text":"Time is not a container of the world, but a created mode of succession; therefore the first now designates the origin of time, while divine eternity remains outside succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-04","text":"The epistemology of the system is asymmetrical: reason demonstrates the order of dependence and removes contradictions, while revelation determines temporal newness, and divine wisdom retains concrete distribution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:BSD-05","text":"The rational creature is at once an active image and a finite reader: by word and love it represents the principle, but it does not comprehend the free decree and the whole account of distribution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A16","CH_GGVC_P_38:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_39:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-01","text":"The circuit of creation is this: the most universal effect excludes a prior subject; exclusion of the subject excludes change; exclusion of change leaves relation; relation confirms universal dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A10","CH_GGVC_P_37:A3","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-02","text":"The circuit of representation is this: finite insufficiency generates plurality; plurality grades forms; gradation increases the complement of the whole; the good of the whole in turn measures the parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:D2","CH_GGVC_P_39:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-03","text":"The path of will proceeds from the non-necessity of creatures to the contingency of duration, thence to the limit of reason, and finally to revelation of the temporal decree.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A3","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_38:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-04","text":"Negation is amplified from presupposed matter to empty time, from a created cause to cosmic chance, and from these to the exclusion of independent totalities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_39:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:RLE-05","text":"«Order» is the common attractor: it orders divine operation and processions, the temporal and exemplary principle, unequal forms, and all things toward one end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS7","CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B01","text":"Local categories—matter, motion, time, particular causality, and the concurrence of parts—are first presented as insufficient models of universal origin.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B02","text":"The scope of the effect is enlarged up to being itself; through this change of scale, matter, time, and space are transferred from external conditions into internal effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B03","text":"Once subject and change are removed, universal production is formally restored as the real relation of the creature's dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A5","CH_GGVC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B04","text":"A voluntary cause determines duration and distinction not by necessity of nature but by the predefinition of wisdom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A4","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B05","text":"Finite representation distributes goodness into diverse forms; diversity produces unequal degrees, the complement of which constitutes the perfection of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8","CH_GGVC_P_39:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FGS-B06","text":"The mutual ordering of parts closes plurality into one world, within which natural causality operates and beyond which the first cause alone produces being absolutely.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A11","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:AFM-B01","text":"Distinction of universal emanation → exclusion of prior subject → resolution of change into relation → contingency of duration → limit of demonstration → revealed determination of beginning → distribution of goodness into forms → gradation of parts → unity of order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:AFM-B02","text":"Whenever matter, time, necessity, chance, or equality attempt to explain the whole, the system returns to the scope of the first cause and places presupposed conditions within the created effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-01","text":"«Created» and «temporally begun» become distinct accounts: the former signifies dependence, the latter the free determination of duration.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_37:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-02","text":"Causes are reclassified according to the scope of their effect: the first cause gives being and the field of causality, while secondary causes act only within the given field.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-03","text":"Perfection is transferred from the greatest perfection of each part to the proportion and coordination of the graded whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_39:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-04","text":"The unity of the world ceases to be bare numerical singularity and becomes unity of relation, order, and common end.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_39:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MME-05","text":"Doctrinal defense is reordered: reason removes contradictions and preserves its own limits, and does not transform contingent revealed truth into feigned necessity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD7","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the mode of creation, the beginning of the universe, and the account of the multitude, inequality, and unity of the world are examined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, the relation of dependence, the contingency of will, and the order of parts operate, connecting the origin, duration, and form of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A6","CH_GGVC_P_38:A5","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the system detects illicit translations between particular and universal causality and assigns reason, faith, and the good of the whole to different offices.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_38:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, created reality is a nexus of finite relations, time is an effect, and graded plurality constitutes the mode of participation in goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_39:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the text enacts its own thesis by successively removing subject, time, necessity, chance, and equality as false principles of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_38:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_39:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FL-01","text":"«Ex nihilo» oscillates between the negation of matter and relation to non-being; coherence requires that the latter temporal sense not simply be inserted into the definition of creation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D1","CH_GGVC_P_38:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FL-02","text":"The relation of creation requires the creature already existing as though a subject, although it signifies the very dependence by which the creature receives being; the distinction between objective and subjective priority sustains the joint.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:D5","CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FL-03","text":"The actual newness of the world is central but does not follow from metaphysical axioms; the system requires a revealed premise, without which it would leave the temporal state indeterminate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_38:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:FL-04","text":"The unity of the world is firmly deduced from actual order, but the transition from divine power for multiple worlds to the necessity of one actual totality is not fully resolved.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_39:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MP-01","text":"The first point of mutation transfers creation from the genus of event or motion into the genus of ontological relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_37:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MP-02","text":"«Principle» changes from a simple marker of origin into a node of time, exemplarity in the Son, and causal immediacy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:A17","CH_GGVC_P_38:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MP-03","text":"Multitude, initially posited as though contrary to divine unity, is converted into a necessary instrument of distributed representation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_39:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MP-04","text":"Inequality is transformed from the apparent injustice of first distribution into the formal structure of the good of the whole, although the particular account of allocation remains in divine wisdom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_39:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly an ordered field produced from a causal center, not a preexisting receptacle: matter, time, forms, and relations are contained within the same effect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_39:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:HSI-02","text":"The creature is a receptive and active node: it receives being, determination, and order, then acts according to its proper form within the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:A16","CH_GGVC_P_39:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:HSI-03","text":"Time is a line unfolded from the origin together with the world; no «before» contains it, and divine eternity is not continued into it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_38:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:HSI-04","text":"The world is like a prismatic distribution of simple goodness: no part equals the whole light, but graded differences are completed in one ordered figure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_39:A4","CH_GGVC_P_39:D2","CH_GGVC_P_39:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms concerning universal creation, contingent will, finite representation, and unity of order suffice to reconstruct at this level the origin, duration, and structure of the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest framework is the nexus by which the universality of the effect excludes a subject, creation is separated from motion, and singular insufficiency generates ordered plurality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MRT-B03","text":"The free decree of the beginning, the distribution of singular forms, and the necessity of a unique order among all possible effects are not yet sufficiently determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_16:MRT-B04","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement if it distinguishes creation, temporal beginning, plurality, and unity not as equal conclusions, but as stages of relation, free determination, and ordering of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_37:MRT9","CH_GGVC_P_38:MRT8","CH_GGVC_P_39:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_16@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_16:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 46–48","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 45 · Prima pars · Quaestio 46 · Prima pars · Quaestio 47"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 49–51","order":17,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_40","CH_GGVC_P_41","CH_GGVC_P_42"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_17@R001","sha256":"ea79ce9839f51a3f53529c6dfd27636c9680ef19d973bad43bc34cf6cee92332","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-01","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo primatus ontologicus boni servetur, cum malum realiter occurrat et pluralitas creaturarum ultra ordinem corporeum extendatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-02","text":"Thesis globalis statuit omnem entitatem positivam secundum esse et perfectionem bonam esse, malum autem ut dependentem privationem, pluralitatem vero immaterialem ut positivam distinctionem formarum constitui.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_42:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-03","text":"Argumentatio fit metaphysico-causalis et reconstructiva, quia apparentia principia adversa per distinctiones entis, causalitatis, materiae, operationis et dependentiae resolvuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-04","text":"Motus a supposita natura mali ad privationem boni debiti transit, deinde ab operatione intellectuali ad substantiam immaterialem ascendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-05","text":"Causalitas mali per accidens et per defectum causae secundae explicatur, ne causalitas prima vel bonitas entis in principium defectus convertatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_41:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-06","text":"Perfectio universi attractor communis fit: gradus defectibiles et substantiae intellectuales requiruntur, sed malum ipsum nullam perfectionem positivam universo confert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-07","text":"Motus verus est recursivus et cumulativus: primatus boni negationes ordinat, negationes causalitatem purgant, atque causalitas purgata agrum entis ad formas immateriales amplificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-08","text":"Clausura est anti-dualistica et participativa: nec primum malum nec creatura a se existens admittitur, sed unus ordo boni formas finitas, defectus accidentales et necessitates causatas complectitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Esse, actualitas et perfectio rationem boni habent; omne positivum igitur bonitate ontologica praeditum est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Malum constituitur non ex quacumque absentia, sed ex privatione boni quod subiectum capax habere debet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Causalitas per se enti positivo convenit; malum igitur causari potest tantum per accidens vel ex defectu principii secundi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-04","text":"[Attractor] Perfectio universi consistit in ordine graduum et modorum bonitatis, non in uniformi perfectione singularum partium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Diversitas universi simul bona defectibilia et creaturas intellectuales incorporeas complectitur; defectibilitas et immaterialitas sunt modi distincti bonitatis creatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Providentia ordinem totius efficit conservando proprias naturas causarum secundarum, non omnem defectibilitatem vel consequentiam naturalem supprimendo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Causa prima entitatem, perfectionem, ordinem et conservationem praebet, dum defectus actionis secundum rationem defectus ad principium proximum deficiens reducitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:D4","CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Operatio modum substantiae sequitur et duplicem vim habet: naturam agentis manifestat atque, in ordine voluntario, bonitatem vel deordinationem eius determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Finitas creata non ex materia necessario provenit, sed ex esse recepto quod essentiae determinatae ut actus ad potentiam comparatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Materia non est condicio universalis receptionis, pluralitatis aut limitationis, quia distinctio formarum et receptio esse sine materia consistere possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_42:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Forma creata subsistens naturaliter incorruptibilis esse potest, quamvis esse eius continuo a causa conservante dependeat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] In ordine voluntario malum praecipuum est deordinatio operationis, non defectus entitatis; ideo culpa causae primae ut culpa attribui nequit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A15","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Bonum et malum causaliter non sunt symmetrica: pluralitas positiva sub uno principio bono stat, malum autem nec summum terminum nec primam radicem constituere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-01","text":"Perfectio universi redit cum mutatione functionis: prius defectibilitatem partium ordinat, postea existentiam et abundantiam creaturarum intellectualium positive postulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-02","text":"Bonum identitatem ontologicam retinet, sed functiones accumulat: est subiectum privationis, radix causalitatis accidentalis, mensura ordinis et actualitas recepta creaturae spiritualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_41:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-03","text":"Privatio stabiliter rationem mali definit, sed ab absentia simplici secernitur et ad incorporeitatem non transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-04","text":"Incorporeitas, quae superficialiter ut carentia videri posset, vim invertit: non defectus entis, sed modus positivus formae subsistentis fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-05","text":"Materia a principio generali potentiae et defectus ad condicionem regionalem rerum corporearum dislocatur; potentia, receptio et finitas sine ea permanent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-06","text":"Defectibilitas a corruptibilitate separatur: quaedam bona deficere possunt, sed creatura finita et causata naturaliter incorruptibilis esse potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-07","text":"Distinctio actus et potentiae migrat ab ordine formae et operationis ad structuram essentiae et esse, unde finitas immaterialis explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-08","text":"Operatio redit functione mutata: in moralibus mensura bonitatis agentis est, in intellectualibus indicium constitutionis substantialis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-09","text":"Ordinatio per accidens a permissione eventus mali ad attributionem corruptionum consequentium extenditur, sed numquam malum in perfectionem per se convertit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_41:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-10","text":"Divisio culpae et poenae gradu morali inferiori manet, dum distinctio causalitatis entitatis et defectus in structuram globalem absorbetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_41:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-01","text":"Comparatio qua culpa poena gravior est manet localis ordini voluntario; globaliter persistit tantum principium quod operatio deordinata gravius quam mera privatio boni possessi aestimatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-02","text":"Numerus Angelorum et unicitas specifica cuiusque sunt determinationes locales; sursum amplificatur distinctio formarum sine divisione materiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-03","text":"Definitio privativa mali et causalitas eius per accidens excedunt loca originis, quia totam asymmetriam inter positivam entitatem et defectum ordinant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-04","text":"Perfectio universi est commissura principalis inter unitates: in una defectus partium contextualizat, in altera ordinem creaturarum incorporearum requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-05","text":"Distinctio actus primi et secundi localiter taxonomiam mali voluntarii sustinet, sed distinctio actus et potentiae globaliter finitudinem omnis creaturae explicat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-06","text":"Transitus ad substantias immateriales non est thema additum, sed probatio quod privatio, limitatio et materia aequiparari nequeunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-07","text":"Exemplaria symmetriae principiorum, quantificationis omnis pluralitatis et materializationis omnis potentiae superantur atque distinctionibus causalibus et transcendentalibus substituuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-01","text":"Malum nec res positiva nec natura subsistens est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-02","text":"Malum neque causam formalem aut finalem neque efficientiam per se habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-03","text":"Nullum summum malum vel principium primum malorum contra primum bonum constitui potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-04","text":"Non omnis limitatio, dependentia vel imperfectio relativa rationem mali habet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-05","text":"Materia non est fundamentum universale substantiae, potentiae, receptionis aut pluralitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-06","text":"Immaterialitas creaturam nec actum purum nec infinitam nec a se existentem efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-07","text":"Causalitas divina culpam secundum rationem deordinationis non producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-01","text":"Systema constare non potest nisi omnis actualitas positiva antecedenter sub ratione boni cadat; aliter malum posset entitatem propriam obtinere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet perfectionem totius exigere maximam et uniformem perfectionem singularum partium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet defectum causae secundae secundum eandem rationem causae primae attribui.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_41:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-04","text":"Systema clausuram sensibilem et hylemorphismum universalem excludit, quia aliter substantia intellectualis nec cognosci nec ontologice constitui posset.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-05","text":"Esse causatum cum corruptibilitate intrinseca aequari non potest; aliter necessitas naturalis creata impossibilis fieret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-06","text":"Distinctiones intellectus humani compositionibus realibus rerum isomorphice respondere non possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSA-01","text":"Malum purum, sine subiecto bono, sine causa positiva et sine ordine ad perfectionem debitam, est possibilitas ontologice inadmissibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSA-02","text":"Creatura quae esse non recipiat vel conservatione causae primae non indigeat ex hoc ordine excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSA-03","text":"Universus ad sensibilia, corpora et pluralitatem quantitativam clausus inadmissibilis est, quia perfectionem causae intellectualis sufficienter non repraesentaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSA-04","text":"Ordo in quo causa prima naturas secundas destruat ut defectus impediat impossibilis est; exclusio mediationis creatae ipsam providentiae rationem evacuaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-01","text":"Perfectio universi simul gradus defectibiles et substantias incorporeas requirit, sed tantum hi modi positivi bonitatis perfectionem constituunt; defectus actualis accidentaliter ordinatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-04","CL_GGVC_17:GA-05","CL_GGVC_17:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-02","text":"Cum creatura immaterialis, finita et causata naturaliter incorruptibilis esse possit, defectibilitas non ex sola ratione creaturae, finitudinis vel dependentiae sequitur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-05","CL_GGVC_17:GA-09","CL_GGVC_17:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-03","text":"Bonum quod privationem sustinet non necessario est materia corporea; ratio subiecti boni latius patet quam ratio materiae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-02","CL_GGVC_17:GA-09","CL_GGVC_17:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-04","text":"Explicatio mali ad materiam universaliter reduci nequit, quia defectus voluntarius ex non-subiectione regulae oritur et potentia immaterialis sine materia consistit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-07","CL_GGVC_17:GA-10","CL_GGVC_17:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_41:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-05","text":"Eadem causalitas prima quae esse et conservationem formae spiritualis praebet entitatem actionis causare potest sine productione deordinationis culpabilis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-07","CL_GGVC_17:GA-11","CL_GGVC_17:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_41:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-06","text":"Operatio est commissura inter ontologiam et moralem aestimationem: intellectualis operatio immaterialitatem substantiae manifestat, voluntaria autem operatio bonitatem vel culpam agentis constituit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-08","CL_GGVC_17:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-07","text":"Multitudo formarum et specierum non inducit pluralitatem principiorum primorum, quia distinctio positiva sub causa universali communi ordinatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-04","CL_GGVC_17:GA-10","CL_GGVC_17:GA-13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-08","text":"Incorruptibilitas naturalis non omnem mutabilitatem tollit; exclusio dissolutionis substantialis et exclusio cuiuslibet mutationis modaliter distinguendae sunt.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-09","CL_GGVC_17:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX12","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-01","text":"Finitas, defectibilitas, privatio, corruptibilitas et dependentia non sunt gradus unius carentiae, sed modi ontologici distincti quorum confusio malum reificat vel creaturam spiritualem materializat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-02","text":"Primatus boni pluralitatem positivam non comprimit; multiplicatio formarum sub causa communi unitatem principii confirmat potius quam dualismum producit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-03","text":"Providentia fit causalitas distributa: causa prima dat esse et ordinem, causae secundae secundum proprios modos agunt, defectus autem secundum rationem defectus in limitibus earum emergit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-04","text":"Malum non est regio ontologica iuxta bona, sed modus lapsus intra operationes et perfectiones bonorum finitorum, semper ab actualitate positiva dependens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-05","text":"Structura temporalis est asymmetrica: potentia et perfectio debita defectum antecedunt, subiectum bonum privationem sustinet, et causa conservans durationem naturae sine necessitate dissolutionis continuat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-06","text":"Methodus negativa agrum non evacuat, sed falsas aequationes removendo ontologiam positivam formarum, modorum causalitatis et necessitatum creatarum generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-07","text":"Status agentis dupliciter ab operatione determinatur: operatio naturam eius ontologice manifestat et, ubi voluntaria est, ordinem eius moraliter constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-01","text":"Perfectio universi bifurcatur in conservationem graduum defectibilium et productionem graduum intellectualium, deinde ad unum ordinem bonitatis redit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-02","text":"Bonum generat circuitum dependentiae: bonum subiectum privationem sustinet, bonum causale effectum positivum producit, et bonum ordinans eventum defectivum per accidens includit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_41:D2","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-03","text":"Quaestio mali recursive ad bonum redit: quo magis mali entitas et causalitas investigantur, eo magis dependentia eius a subiecto, forma et fine positivo manifestatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-04","text":"Via amplificationis causalis procedit a defectu locali ad causam secundam, ab ea ad distinctionem entitatis et deordinationis, atque inde ad causam primam quae primum tantum positive causat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-05","text":"Via intellectualis spiraliter progreditur ab obiecto immateriali ad operationem immaterialem, ab operatione ad substantiam, a substantia ad esse receptum et ab esse recepto ad dependentiam conservativam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-06","text":"Negatio materiae universalis non ad indeterminationem ducit, sed distinctionem formarum, specierum, graduum et modorum finitudinis amplificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-07","text":"Attractor terminalis est esse receptum: eo creatura simul positive bona, finite determinata, causaliter dependens et a Deo distincta intelligitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B01","text":"Esse et perfectio sub ratione boni constituuntur, unde omnis positio positiva mensuram ontologicam accipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B02","text":"Perfectio universi → diversitas graduum bonitatis → bona defectibilia et bona intellectualia → pluralitas ordinata sine pluralitate principiorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B03","text":"Bonum debitum → defectus in subiecto capace → privatio realis → malum sine natura positiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B04","text":"Entitas causae → bonitas causae → effectus positivus → defectus consequens per accidens vel ex principio secundo deficiente.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B05","text":"Operatio intellectualis → immaterialitas operationis → forma subsistens → pluralitas formarum sine divisione materiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B06","text":"Forma creata subsistens → essentia ut potentia ad esse → finitas sine materia → dependentia conservativa sine corruptibilitate intrinseca.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B07","text":"Unum principium bonum → ordo plurium formarum → causalitas secundarum servata → defectus privativi subordinati → clausura anti-dualistica.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:D7","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AFM-B01","text":"Primatus boni → reclassificatio mali ut privationis → causalitas per accidens → distributio causalitatis primae et secundae → exclusio dualismi → extensio entis ad formas immateriales → finitas per esse receptum → necessitas creata sub conservatione divina.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_41:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AFM-B02","text":"Perfectio universi → bona defectibilia → defectus actualis accidentaliter ordinatus → creatura intellectualis incorporea → multitudo formarum → unitas causae primae sine uniformitate effectuum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-01","text":"Ager mali ab oppositione inter duas naturas ad dependentiam privativam intra bona finita transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-02","text":"Ager causalitatis a simplici attributione effectus ad causam in distinctionem entitatis, defectus, causalitatis per se et causalitatis per accidens reordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-03","text":"Materia ex nota universali finitudinis ad principium particulare individuationis et corruptionis corporalium restringitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_42:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-04","text":"Pluralitas a quantitate separatur et ut distinctio transcendens formarum ac specierum cogitatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_42:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-05","text":"Incorruptibilitas ab aseitate et absoluta immutabilitate separatur, unde necessitas naturalis causata primum stabiliter describi potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:ME7","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-06","text":"Divina causalitas ab exemplari indistinctae responsabilitatis ad structuram distributam entitatis, ordinis, conservationis, permissionis et iustitiae transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei investigantur natura et causa mali atque constitutio creaturae intellectualis incorporeae, multiplicis et incorruptibilis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali operantur privatio, causalitas per accidens, actus et potentia, materia et forma, operatio et substantia, essentia et esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico quaestiones de re mala vel de mundo necessario corporeo mutantur in quaestiones de condicionibus defectus, modis participationis et limitibus attributionis causalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas est ordo actualitatum receptarum, in quo defectus perfectionem debitam praesupponit et creatura incorruptibilis per conservationem durat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo, series negationum falsas reificationes removet, distinctiones autem remotionem in positivam descriptionem ordinis convertunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-01","text":"Perfectio universi defectibilia requirit, quamvis malum qua malum eius perfectionem non constituat; commissura pendet omnino ex distinctione naturae defectibilis et defectus actualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-02","text":"Transitus a potentia deficiendi ad assertionem quod defectibilia interdum actu deficiant assumitur potius quam plene demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-03","text":"Corruptiones Deo causaliter attribuuntur et simul privationes per se intentae negantur; stabilitas nexus pendet ex causalitate consequentis per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:D5","CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-04","text":"Operatio modum substantiae manifestat, sed modus compositivus intellectus humani non debet in compositionem realem substantiae proiectari; cognitio procedit ex effectu sine isomorphia plena.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-05","text":"Excessus multitudinis angelicae analogia, non eadem necessitate qua immaterialitas, sustinetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-06","text":"Unicitas specifica cuiusque Angeli firmius quam conversio omnium graduum intellectualium in species distinctas demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MP-01","text":"Perfectio universi functionem mutat ab ordine qui defectus partium tolerat ad principio quod formas intellectuales positive requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MP-02","text":"Defectus mutatur a privatione ontologica boni debiti ad non-subiectionem actualem voluntatis regulae, unde causalitas moralis specialem structuram acquirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MP-03","text":"Causa materialis mali significat subiectum bonum privationis, non materiam corpoream; transitus ad substantiam immaterialem hanc aequivocationem coercet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:D1","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MP-04","text":"Necessitas ab ordine universi ad stabilitatem intrinsecam formae subsistentis migrat, sed in utroque casu causaliter a Deo dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A11","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:HSI-01","text":"Imago occulta est machina participationis stratificatae: actualitas divina formas finitas producit, formae proprios modos agendi explicant, et defectus ut lacunae dependentiae intra hos modos apparent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum creatum est bonum receptivum et operativum: essentiam determinatam habet, esse recipit et secundum propriam operationem perfectionem vel defectum manifestat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:HSI-03","text":"Tempus systematis est asymmetria debiti et lapsus: perfectio possibilis prius ordinat, defectus posterius accidit, subiectum autem conservatione causae perdurat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio conceptualis fit per bifurcationes formales: per se et per accidens, entitas et defectus, materia et receptio, corruptibilitas et dependentia, immaterialitas et aseitas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de primatu boni, malo privativo, causalitate per accidens, perfectione universi, operatione substantiam manifestante et esse recepto sufficiunt ad structuram gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est in asymmetria qua omnis actualitas positiva ad bonum reducitur, malum autem a bono secundum subiectum, causam et mensuram dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum plene determinatur cur omnis potentia naturalis deficiendi aliquando actu deficiat; hic nexus ordine universi magis assumitur quam demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B04","text":"Abundantia substantiarum angelicarum et distinctio graduum earum in species manent minus necessariae quam immaterialitas et incorruptibilitas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B05","text":"Systema hac magnitudine cohaeret non ex ordine lineari quaestionum, sed ex reditu distinctionum inter positivum et privativum, per se et per accidens, receptum et subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B06","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: explicatio defectus purgat causalitatem, causalitas purgata unitatem principii tuetur, et unitas principii pluralitatem immaterialem sine dualismo sustinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171807185521Z_05dc6bf1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 49–51","source_sha256":"ea79ce9839f51a3f53529c6dfd27636c9680ef19d973bad43bc34cf6cee92332","sha256":"c4624cef605cc16dabb0dd91517a3f979355f427da316d31663570904e8390e3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:18:07.186467+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-01","text":"The central question is how the ontological primacy of the good is preserved, when evil really occurs and the plurality of creatures extends beyond the corporeal order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-02","text":"The global thesis holds that every positive entity is good according to being and perfection, whereas evil is constituted as a dependent privation, and immaterial plurality as a positive distinction of forms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_42:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-03","text":"The argument proceeds metaphysically, causally, and reconstructively, because apparently opposed principles are resolved through distinctions of being, causality, matter, operation, and dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-04","text":"The movement passes from the supposed nature of evil to the privation of due good, then rises from intellectual operation to immaterial substance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-05","text":"The causality of evil is explained through accident and through the defect of a secondary cause, lest primary causality or the goodness of being be converted into a principle of defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_41:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-06","text":"The perfection of the universe becomes the common attractor: defectible grades and intellectual substances are required, but evil itself contributes no positive perfection to the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-07","text":"The true movement is recursive and cumulative: the primacy of the good orders negations, negations purify causality, and purified causality extends the field of being to immaterial forms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AS-08","text":"The closure is anti-dualistic and participatory: neither a first evil nor a creature existing through itself is admitted, but one order of good encompasses finite forms, accidental defects, and caused necessities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Being, actuality, and perfection have the character of good; therefore every positive thing is endowed with ontological goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Evil is constituted not by any absence whatsoever, but by the privation of a good that a capable subject ought to have.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Causality per se belongs to positive being; therefore evil can be caused only per accidens or from the defect of a secondary principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-04","text":"[Attractor] The perfection of the universe consists in an order of grades and modes of goodness, not in the uniform perfection of individual parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The diversity of the universe includes both defectible goods and incorporeal intellectual creatures; defectibility and immateriality are distinct modes of created goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Providence effects the order of the whole by preserving the proper natures of secondary causes, not by suppressing every defectibility or natural consequence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The first cause provides entity, perfection, order, and preservation, while the defect of action according to the character of defect is referred to the proximate deficient principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:D4","CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Operation follows the mode of substance and has a twofold force: it manifests the nature of the agent and, in the voluntary order, determines its goodness or disorder.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Created finitude does not necessarily arise from matter, but from received being, which is related to determinate essence as act to potency.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Matter is not the universal condition of reception, plurality, or limitation, because the distinction of forms and the reception of being can subsist without matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_42:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] A created subsistent form can be naturally incorruptible, although its being continuously depends on a conserving cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D10","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] In the voluntary order, the principal evil is the disorder of operation, not the defect of entity; therefore it cannot be attributed to the first cause as fault.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A15","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Good and evil are not causally symmetrical: positive plurality stands under one good principle, whereas evil can constitute neither a supreme terminus nor a first root.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-01","text":"The perfection of the universe recurs with a change of function: first it orders the defectibility of parts, afterward it positively requires the existence and abundance of intellectual creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-02","text":"Good retains its ontological identity but accumulates functions: it is the subject of privation, the root of accidental causality, the measure of order, and the received actuality of the spiritual creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_41:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-03","text":"Privation consistently defines the character of evil, but is separated from simple absence and is not transferred to incorporeality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A2","CH_GGVC_P_40:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-04","text":"Incorporeality, which might superficially seem a lack, reverses its force: it becomes not a defect of being, but a positive mode of subsistent form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-05","text":"Matter is displaced from being a general principle of potency and defect to a regional condition of corporeal things; potency, reception, and finitude remain without it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-06","text":"Defectibility is separated from corruptibility: some goods can fail, but a finite and caused creature can be naturally incorruptible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-07","text":"The distinction of act and potency migrates from the order of form and operation to the structure of essence and being, whence immaterial finitude is explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-08","text":"Operation recurs with changed function: in moral matters it is the measure of the agent's goodness, in intellectual matters an indication of substantial constitution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A16","CH_GGVC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-09","text":"Ordination per accidens extends from the permission of an evil event to the attribution of consequent corruptions, but never converts evil into a perfection per se.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_41:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RMD-10","text":"The division of fault and punishment remains at the lower moral level, while the distinction of the causality of entity and defect is absorbed into the global structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_41:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-01","text":"The comparison by which fault is graver than punishment remains local to the voluntary order; globally, only the principle persists that disordered operation is judged graver than the mere privation of a possessed good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-02","text":"The number of Angels and the specific uniqueness of each are local determinations; upward, the distinction of forms without division of matter is amplified.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-03","text":"The privative definition of evil and its causality per accidens exceed their places of origin, because they order the entire asymmetry between positive entity and defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-04","text":"The perfection of the universe is the principal joint between the units: in one it contextualizes the defects of parts, in the other it requires the order of incorporeal creatures.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-05","text":"The distinction of first and second act locally supports a taxonomy of voluntary evil, but the distinction of act and potency globally explains the finitude of every creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A13","CH_GGVC_P_42:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-06","text":"The transition to immaterial substances is not an added theme, but proof that privation, limitation, and matter cannot be equated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:CGD-07","text":"Models of the symmetry of principles, the quantification of all plurality, and the materialization of all potency are overcome and replaced by causal and transcendental distinctions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-01","text":"Evil is neither a positive thing nor a subsistent nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-02","text":"Evil has neither formal nor final cause, nor efficient causality per se.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-03","text":"No supreme evil or first principle of evils can be constituted against the first good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_41:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-04","text":"Not every limitation, dependence, or relative imperfection has the character of evil.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-05","text":"Matter is not the universal foundation of substance, potency, reception, or plurality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-06","text":"Immateriality renders a creature neither pure act nor infinite nor self-existent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:GNX-07","text":"Divine causality does not produce fault according to the character of disorder.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-01","text":"The system cannot stand unless every positive actuality first falls under the character of good; otherwise evil could obtain an entity of its own.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that the perfection of the whole requires the maximal and uniform perfection of individual parts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that the defect of a secondary cause is attributed according to the same character as the first cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_41:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-04","text":"The system excludes sensible closure and universal hylomorphism, because otherwise intellectual substance could neither be known nor be ontologically constituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-05","text":"Caused being cannot be equated with intrinsic corruptibility; otherwise created natural necessity would be impossible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:DBN-06","text":"The distinctions of the human intellect cannot correspond isomorphically to the real compositions of things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSA-01","text":"Pure evil, without a good subject, without a positive cause, and without orientation to due perfection, is an ontologically inadmissible possibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_41:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSA-02","text":"A creature that does not receive being or does not require the preservation of the first cause is excluded from this order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSA-03","text":"A universe closed to sensible things, bodies, and quantitative plurality is inadmissible, because it would not sufficiently represent the perfection of an intellectual cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSA-04","text":"An order in which the first cause destroys secondary natures in order to prevent defects is impossible; the exclusion of created mediation would empty the very character of providence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-01","text":"The perfection of the universe requires both defectible grades and incorporeal substances, but only these positive modes of goodness constitute perfection; actual defect is ordered accidentally.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-04","CL_GGVC_17:GA-05","CL_GGVC_17:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_40:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-02","text":"Since an immaterial, finite, and caused creature can be naturally incorruptible, defectibility does not follow from the sole character of creaturehood, finitude, or dependence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-05","CL_GGVC_17:GA-09","CL_GGVC_17:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11","CH_GGVC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-03","text":"The good that sustains privation is not necessarily corporeal matter; the character of a good subject extends more broadly than the character of matter.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-02","CL_GGVC_17:GA-09","CL_GGVC_17:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-04","text":"The explanation of evil cannot be universally reduced to matter, because voluntary defect arises from non-subjection to a rule and immaterial potency subsists without matter.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-07","CL_GGVC_17:GA-10","CL_GGVC_17:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_41:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-05","text":"The same primary causality that provides the being and preservation of spiritual form can cause the entity of an action without producing culpable disorder.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-07","CL_GGVC_17:GA-11","CL_GGVC_17:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_41:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-06","text":"Operation is the joint between ontology and moral evaluation: intellectual operation manifests the immateriality of substance, whereas voluntary operation constitutes the goodness or fault of the agent.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-08","CL_GGVC_17:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-07","text":"A multitude of forms and species does not introduce a plurality of first principles, because positive distinction is ordered under a common universal cause.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-04","CL_GGVC_17:GA-10","CL_GGVC_17:GA-13","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:XD-08","text":"Natural incorruptibility does not remove all mutability; the exclusion of substantial dissolution and the exclusion of every modally distinguishable change must be distinguished.","refs":["CL_GGVC_17:GA-09","CL_GGVC_17:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX12","CH_GGVC_P_42:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-01","text":"Finitude, defectibility, privation, corruptibility, and dependence are not grades of one lack, but distinct ontological modes whose confusion reifies evil or materializes the spiritual creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-02","text":"The primacy of good does not compress positive plurality; the multiplication of forms under a common cause confirms the unity of principle rather than producing dualism.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-03","text":"Providence becomes distributed causality: the first cause gives being and order, secondary causes act according to their proper modes, while defect according to the character of defect emerges within their limits.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-04","text":"Evil is not an ontological region alongside goods, but a mode of falling within the operations and perfections of finite goods, always dependent on positive actuality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-05","text":"The temporal structure is asymmetrical: potency and due perfection precede defect, a good subject sustains privation, and a conserving cause continues the duration of nature without the necessity of dissolution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_40:A12","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-06","text":"The negative method does not empty the field, but by removing false equations generates a positive ontology of forms, modes of causality, and created necessities.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:BSD-07","text":"The status of an agent is determined in two ways by operation: operation manifests its nature ontologically and, where it is voluntary, constitutes its order morally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_40:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-01","text":"The perfection of the universe bifurcates into the preservation of defectible grades and the production of intellectual grades, then returns to one order of goodness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-02","text":"Good generates a circuit of dependence: a good subject sustains privation, causal good produces a positive effect, and ordering good includes a defective event per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:D2","CH_GGVC_P_41:D2","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-03","text":"The question of evil recursively returns to good: the more the entity and causality of evil are investigated, the more its dependence on a positive subject, form, and end is manifested.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-04","text":"The path of causal amplification proceeds from local defect to the secondary cause, from it to the distinction of entity and disorder, and thence to the first cause, which causes only positively in the first instance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-05","text":"The intellectual path advances spirally from an immaterial object to immaterial operation, from operation to substance, from substance to received being, and from received being to conserving dependence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-06","text":"The negation of universal matter does not lead to indeterminacy, but amplifies the distinction of forms, species, grades, and modes of finitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:RLE-07","text":"The terminal attractor is received being: through it the creature is understood simultaneously as positively good, finitely determined, causally dependent, and distinct from God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B01","text":"Being and perfection are constituted under the character of good, whence every positive position receives an ontological measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B02","text":"Perfection of the universe → diversity of grades of goodness → defectible goods and intellectual goods → ordered plurality without a plurality of principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B03","text":"Due good → defect in a capable subject → real privation → evil without positive nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B04","text":"Entity of cause → goodness of cause → positive effect → consequent defect per accidens or from a deficient secondary principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A2","CH_GGVC_P_41:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B05","text":"Intellectual operation → immateriality of operation → subsistent form → plurality of forms without division of matter.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B06","text":"Created subsistent form → essence as potency toward being → finitude without matter → conserving dependence without intrinsic corruptibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FGS-B07","text":"One good principle → order of multiple forms → preserved causality of secondary causes → subordinated privative defects → anti-dualistic closure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A8","CH_GGVC_P_41:D7","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AFM-B01","text":"Primacy of good → reclassification of evil as privation → causality per accidens → distribution of primary and secondary causality → exclusion of dualism → extension of being to immaterial forms → finitude through received being → created necessity under divine preservation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_41:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:AFM-B02","text":"Perfection of the universe → defectible goods → actual defect accidentally ordered → incorporeal intellectual creature → multitude of forms → unity of the first cause without uniformity of effects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:D6","CH_GGVC_P_42:D1","CH_GGVC_P_42:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-01","text":"The field of evil is transferred from opposition between two natures to privative dependence within finite goods.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-02","text":"The field of causality is reordered from simple attribution of effect to cause into the distinction of entity, defect, causality per se, and causality per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-03","text":"Matter is restricted from a universal mark of finitude to a particular principle of individuation and corruption of corporeal things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_42:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-04","text":"Plurality is separated from quantity and conceived as the transcendent distinction of forms and species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:ME3","CH_GGVC_P_42:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-05","text":"Incorruptibility is separated from aseity and absolute immutability, whence caused natural necessity can first be stably described.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:ME7","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MME-06","text":"Divine causality is transferred from a model of undifferentiated responsibility to a distributed structure of entity, order, preservation, permission, and justice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the nature and cause of evil and the constitution of the incorporeal, multiple, and incorruptible intellectual creature are investigated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, privation, causality per accidens, act and potency, matter and form, operation and substance, essence and being operate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, questions about an evil thing or a necessarily corporeal world are transformed into questions about the conditions of defect, modes of participation, and limits of causal attribution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, reality is an order of received actualities, in which defect presupposes due perfection and an incorruptible creature endures through preservation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_42:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, a series of negations removes false reifications, while distinctions convert removal into a positive description of order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-01","text":"The perfection of the universe requires defectible things, although evil as evil does not constitute its perfection; the joint depends entirely on the distinction between a defectible nature and actual defect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A6","CH_GGVC_P_40:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-02","text":"The transition from the potency to fail to the assertion that defectible things sometimes actually fail is assumed rather than fully demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-03","text":"Corruptions are causally attributed to God while privations intended per se are denied; the stability of the connection depends on causality of the consequent per accidens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:D5","CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-04","text":"Operation manifests the mode of substance, but the compositional mode of the human intellect must not be projected onto the real composition of substance; cognition proceeds from effect without full isomorphism.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-05","text":"The excess of angelic multitude is supported by analogy, not by the same necessity as immateriality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:FL-06","text":"The specific uniqueness of each Angel is demonstrated more firmly than the conversion of all intellectual grades into distinct species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MP-01","text":"The perfection of the universe changes function from an order that tolerates the defects of parts to a principle that positively requires intellectual forms.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MP-02","text":"Defect changes from the ontological privation of due good to the actual non-subjection of the will to a rule, whence moral causality acquires a special structure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MP-03","text":"The material cause of evil signifies the good subject of privation, not corporeal matter; the transition to immaterial substance restrains this equivocation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:D1","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MP-04","text":"Necessity migrates from the order of the universe to the intrinsic stability of subsistent form, but in both cases depends causally on God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A11","CH_GGVC_P_42:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:HSI-01","text":"The hidden image is a machine of stratified participation: divine actuality produces finite forms, forms unfold their proper modes of acting, and defects appear as gaps of dependence within these modes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A3","CH_GGVC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:HSI-02","text":"The created subject is a receptive and operative good: it has a determinate essence, receives being, and manifests perfection or defect according to its proper operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:A8","CH_GGVC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system is an asymmetry of what is due and lapse: possible perfection orders first, defect occurs later, while the subject endures through the preservation of the cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:A3","CH_GGVC_P_42:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:HSI-04","text":"Conceptual navigation occurs through formal bifurcations: per se and per accidens, entity and defect, matter and reception, corruptibility and dependence, immateriality and aseity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_42:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms concerning the primacy of good, privative evil, causality per accidens, the perfection of the universe, operation manifesting substance, and received being suffice to restore the structure of the whole.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:A1","CH_GGVC_P_41:A7","CH_GGVC_P_42:A5","CH_GGVC_P_42:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure lies in the asymmetry whereby every positive actuality is reduced to good, while evil depends on good with respect to subject, cause, and measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_41:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B03","text":"It is not yet fully determined why every natural potency to fail at some time actually fails; here the connection is more assumed from the order of the universe than demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_41:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B04","text":"The abundance of angelic substances and the distinction of their grades into species remain less necessary than immateriality and incorruptibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B05","text":"A system of this magnitude coheres not through a linear order of questions, but through the recurrence of distinctions between positive and privative, per se and per accidens, received and subsistent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_40:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_17:MRT-B06","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: the explanation of defect purifies causality, purified causality safeguards the unity of principle, and the unity of principle sustains immaterial plurality without dualism.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_41:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_42:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_17@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_17:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 49–51","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 48 · Prima pars · Quaestio 49 · Prima pars · Quaestio 50"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 52–54","order":18,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_43","CH_GGVC_P_44","CH_GGVC_P_45"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_18@R001","sha256":"478ec1a7bc63dc5490043bc5723eb012ca77d8827b1951a528343a485010be06","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-01","text":"Grex interrogat quomodo substantia intellectualis creata, naturaliter incorporea, possit sensibiliter apparere, definite adesse et localiter mutari sine conversione in corpus aut in omnipraesentiam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-02","text":"Thesis globalis statuit corporalem manifestationem Angelicam non esse corporis naturalis possessionem, sed effectum extrinsecum virtutis ad materiam et locum applicatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-03","text":"Argumentatio procedit per distinctiones modorum unionis, praesentiae et motus, ita ut eadem incorporeitas quae corpus essentiale excludit causalitatem localem non excludat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-04","text":"Motus systematis est spiralis: corpus assumptum primum ut signum apparitionis ponitur, deinde ut terminus applicationis virtualis, postremo ut occasio successionis localis et temporalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-05","text":"Corporalitas non evanescit, sed ab elemento naturae ad medium repraesentativum et ad terminum operationis spiritualis reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-06","text":"Finitas virtutis Angelicae convertit incorporeitatem in praesentiam definitivam, non in libertatem ab omni termino creato.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-07","text":"Motus Angelicus non est translatio magnitudinis, sed ordinata reapplicatio virtutis, quae motum continuum vel non continuum recipit et tamen prius atque posterius retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-08","text":"Clausura gregis est typologia non aequivoca: corpus circumscriptive est, Angelus definitive per virtutem, Deus ubique per causalitatem infinitam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Intellectio perfecta corpus naturale non requirit; ideo incorporeitas Angelica est principium positivum perfectionis, non mera privatio corporis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Corpus, quod animae imperfecte cognoscenti instrumentum acquisitionis est, Angelo fit medium contingens manifestationis potius quam complementum naturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Apparentia exterior communis corpus extrinsecum requirit, sed corpus assumptum Angelum non informat neque vivificat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Applicatio virtutis est nexus generativus quo corpus apparens, praesentia localis et motus localis sub una ratione causalitatis ordinantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] Virtus Angelica finita unum terminum creatum immediate determinat; hinc nec omnipraesentia nec multilocatio simultanea Angelica sequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Locus Angelicus non est situs quantitativus, sed unitas termini cui virtus immediate applicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Corpus assumptum duplicem functionem habet: est signum sensibile virtutis spiritualis et terminus corporalis operationis virtualis, quarum functionum identitas non praesumitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Motus Angelicus ex successione applicationum virtualium constat, non ex divisione substantiae Angelicae aut praesentia simultanea in pluribus locis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Effectus physici et similitudines vitae concedi possunt, dum principium vitale formale et actus vitales proprii negantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Perfectio Angelica motum ex indigentia propria excludit, sed ministerium creaturae motum voluntarie determinatum admittit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-01","text":"Incorporeitas identitatem servat, sed functio eius mutatur: a negatione corporis naturalis transit ad rationem praesentiae localis et motus non quantitativi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_45:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-02","text":"Corpus recurrit mutatum: in apparitione est instrumentum repraesentativum, in localitate est terminus virtutis, nec utraque ratio in naturam Angelicam redit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-03","text":"Determinatio localis ab motu per accidens corporis assumpti transit ad determinationem formalem per applicationem virtutis et ad successionem terminorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A14","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-04","text":"Actio quae in apparentia similitudinem vitae praebebat, in motu reclassificatur ut actus actualis virtutis sine principio vitali intrinseco.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-05","text":"Continuitas non persistit ut conditio universalis motus, sed fit variabilis modus applicationis localis: per medium in motu continuo, sine medio in motu non continuo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-06","text":"Tempus mutatur ab indice cosmologico universali ad mensuram successionis dispositionum localium Angelicarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-07","text":"Differentia Dei, Angeli et corporis persistit, sed a sola scala dignitatis ad typologiam modorum praesentiae, causalitatis et termini explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-01","text":"Condensatio aeris et coloratio materiae sunt mechanismi locales apparitionis; non portant structuram globalem, quae corpus assumptum sub ratione mediationis virtualis intelligit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-02","text":"Negationes nutritionis, generationis et vitae animalis manent locales probationes apophaticae; ad gradum gregis ascendunt tantum ut separatio inter effectum visibilem et principium vitale.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_43:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-03","text":"Exclusio plurium Angelorum ab eodem loco desinit esse quaestio singularis co-localitatis et fit regula globalis de exclusivitate causalitatis immediatae completae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-04","text":"Distinctio motus continui et non continui amplificatur ultra physicam localem, quia constituit modum quo finita causalitas tempus proprium habere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-05","text":"Corpus repraesentativum et locus virtualiter determinatus in gradu praesentis gregis coordinantur, sed non identificantur: alter significationem, alter terminum immediatae operationis designat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-06","text":"Ordinatio apparitionum ad incarnationem Verbi manet teleologica extensio localis; machina praesentis gregis sine ea ex distinctionibus naturae, virtutis, loci et motus restitui potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-01","text":"Systema excludit conversionem incorporeitatis Angelicae in naturam animalem aut in corpus Angelicum naturaliter proprium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-02","text":"Systema excludit reductionem apparitionis exterioris communis ad imaginem privatam vel ad phantasiam propheticam solitariam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-03","text":"Systema excludit locum ut receptaculum quod Angelum continet, mensurat aut quantitative circumscriptum facit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_44:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-04","text":"Systema excludit illationem qua incorporeitas creaturae infinitatem virtualem, ubiquitatem vel multilocationem immediate conferret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-05","text":"Systema excludit transitum ab effectu exteriori ad vitam formalem, sensum, nutritionem aut generationem Angelicam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-06","text":"Systema excludit tam motum instantaneum quam subiectionem omnis motus Angelici tempori caelesti universali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-07","text":"Systema excludit pluralitatem causarum immediatarum completarum circa unum eundemque terminum localem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse debet omnem intellectum perfectum ex sensibilibus, organis et corpore naturali scientiam accipere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse debet quidquid exterius videtur eo ipso vivum, animatum aut eius naturae esse quam figura sensibilis simulat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse debet spatium et tempus sub unica forma quantitativa omnem creaturam spiritualem, corporalem et divinam comprehensibilia facere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse debet relationem moventis ad mobile vel effectum externum per se unionem substantialem, vitam formalem aut naturae identitatem demonstrare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_45:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse debet causalitatem immediatam completam multiplicari posse sine divisione termini, subordinatione causarum aut mutatione rationis causalitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSA-01","text":"Possibilitas creaturae spiritualis simul sine corpore, sine termino locali et sine successione temporali ordinata systemati indisponibilis est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSA-02","text":"Identificatio omnipraesentiae divinae cum praesentia virtuali Angelica prohibetur, quia infinitas causalis non est extensio finitatis creaturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A6","CH_GGVC_P_44:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSA-03","text":"Figura sensibilis non potest spiritualem naturam exhaustive exhibere, quia signum visibile ad virtutem significatam ordinatur et eam non absorbet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSA-04","text":"Spatium et tempus ut receptacula neutra, homogenea et per se determinativa praesentiae excluduntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-01","text":"Corpus assumptum non est exceptio ab incorporeitate Angelica, sed duplex exterioritas qua virtus spiritualis simul signum sensibile producit et terminum corporalem immediate contingit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-01","CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","CL_GGVC_18:GA-04","CL_GGVC_18:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-02","text":"Finitas virtutis Angelicae non tantum ubiquitatem negat, sed unamquamque praesentiam Angelicam constituit ut electionem termini creati determinati.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-03","text":"Apparentia publica non revelat naturam Angelicam per identitatem figurativam, sed instituit campum in quo visibile signum et invisibilis causalitas coordinate leguntur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","CL_GGVC_18:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-04","text":"Motus, sonus et figura corporea possunt causaliter reales esse sine vita corporali, quia actualitas virtutis Angelicae non est actualitas formae vivificantis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-04","CL_GGVC_18:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12","CH_GGVC_P_45:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-05","text":"Exclusivitas termini immediati et negatio multilocationis efficiunt ut mutatio localis Angelica per successionem ordinetur, non per simultaneam expansionem praesentiae.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A3","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-06","text":"Absentia medii in motu non continuo non delet tempus, quia successio terminorum localium prius et posterius retinet etiam ubi continuum spatiale non percurritur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-07","text":"Motus Angelicus ministerialis describit finitam virtutem quae ex se non indiget, sed se localiter determinat secundum necessitatem creaturae cui servit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-01","text":"Grex ontologiam agentis spiritualis creati constituit ut causalitatem finitam exteriorizabilem: non est res corporalis, neque actus ab omni termino creato solutus.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-01","CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-02","text":"Spatium reordinatur ut ordo termini causalis, tempus ut ordo successionis applicationum; neutrum manet mensura ontologice univoca omnis entis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CL_GGVC_18:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-03","text":"Cognitio sensibilis humana recipit verum signum spiritualis agentiae sine eo quod figura corporalis naturam spiritualem literaliter exhibeat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-02","CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","CL_GGVC_18:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-04","text":"Hierarchia corporis, Angeli et Dei non per quantitatem distantiae, sed per modum causandi, continendi et terminari disponitur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-05","text":"Perfectio non opponitur ministerio: Angelus non movetur ut sibi desit aliquid, sed ut virtus eius ad indigentiam alterius ordinate applicetur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-06","text":"Distinctiones vitae, loci et motus prohibent ne manifestatio sensibilis, efficacia causalis et identitas ontologica in unum praedicatum confundantur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CL_GGVC_18:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-01","text":"Intellectio incorporea → negatio corporis naturalis → corpus assumptum repraesentativum → applicatio virtualis → praesentia definita → successio localis → tempus proprium: circuitus confirmat incorporeitatem per exterioritatem ordinatam, non per absentiam operationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-02","text":"Finitas virtutis → unus terminus immediatus → exclusio multilocationis et co-localitatis → necessitas successionis in motu: imminutio extensionis fit principium ordinis localis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A3","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-03","text":"Similitudo vitae → negatio principii vitalis → concessio effectuum exteriorum → reditus ad virtutem spiritualem: apparentia conservatur, biologia excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-04","text":"Mutatio modi applicationis virtutis bifurcat motum in continuum et non continuum, sed ambo rami ad attractorem successionis temporalis redeunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-05","text":"Applicatio virtutis est attractor occultus qui corpus, locum, motum, finitatem et ministerium in unam machinam causaliter ordinatam colligit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B01","text":"Intellectio incorporea → corpus non est conditio perfectionis Angelicae → corpus naturale excluditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B02","text":"Apparentia exterior communis → corpus extra videntem requiritur → corpus temporale assumptum fit medium manifestationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B03","text":"Corpus assumptum ut instrumentum repraesentativum → effectus sensibiles conceduntur → vita, sensus et nutritio formales negantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B04","text":"Applicatio virtutis ad corpus → locus Angelicus fit terminus causalitatis virtualis → finitas virtutis unum locum definitive constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B05","text":"Reapplicatio successiva virtutis ad loca diversa → motus Angelicus → transitio continua per medium vel non continua sine medio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B06","text":"Successio dispositionum localium → prius et posterius → tempus Angelicum proprium, quod a motu caeli non dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B07","text":"Voluntas Angelica → determinatio modi et velocitatis applicationis → ministerium indigentiae alterius sine indigentia moventis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A14","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B01","text":"Intellectio non corporea → recusatio corporis naturalis Angelici.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B02","text":"Recusatio corporis naturalis → admissio corporis assumpti ut signi exterioris et instrumenti mobili.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B03","text":"Corpus repraesentativum → separatio effectus exterioris a vita formali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B04","text":"Separatio naturae et corporis → reconstitutio loci per applicationem virtutis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B05","text":"Applicatio virtutis finita → unus terminus localis → exclusio ubiquitatis et co-localitatis Angelicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B06","text":"Unus terminus successivus → motus continuus vel non continuus → tempus proprium non instantaneum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B07","text":"Motus voluntarius → causalitas ministerialis → creatura perfecta localiter efficax sed finite determinata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-01","text":"Corpus reclassificatur in tres ordines distinctos: naturam substantialem, signum repraesentativum et terminum operationis virtualis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-02","text":"Locus reclassificatur ab occupando spatio ad constituendum terminum immediatae causalitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-03","text":"Motus reclassificatur ab unica translatione continua ad genus mutationis localis quod continuitatem aut discontinuationem recipere potest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-04","text":"Tempus Angelicum fit ratio successionis operativae, nec ex motu caeli nec ex continuo corporali universaliter derivata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-05","text":"Distinctio inter Deum, Angelum et corpus movetur ab oppositione simplici spiritus et materiae ad gradus infinitatis, finitatis virtualis et quantitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-06","text":"Lectio apparitionis fit methodus quae figuram sensibilem servat, sed prohibet eam in biologiam, anthropologiam aut ontologiam Angelicam converti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_43:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei decernit utrum Angelus corpus assumat, sit in loco et localiter moveatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis relationes corporis, loci et motus per modum cognitionis, applicationis virtutis et successionis causalium terminorum ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus obiectiones ex figura humana, puncto, repletione spatii, continuitate et tempore per distinctionem generis relationis dissolvit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis finitatem creaturae spiritualis describit ut praesentiam virtualem terminatam et mutationem successioni subiectam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus distinctiones operatur quas affirmat: natura, signum, effectus, vita, locus, motus et tempus separantur ut analogiae illegitimae impediantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS7","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-01","text":"Corpus assumptum simul materialiter reale, exteriori visioni publicum et vitaliter inane ponitur; criterium quo similitudo exterior a vera vita discernitur metaphysice stabilitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-02","text":"Unitas loci Angelici pendet ex termino virtutis, sed extensio termini potest variari; ratio unitatis quae variationem continet non ulterius resolvitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-03","text":"Applicatio virtutis ad terminum novum tota simul facta difficulter componitur cum pluralitate nunc successivorum requisita ad motum temporalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-04","text":"Exclusio co-localitatis fundatur in causalitate immediata completa, sed discrimina inter causalitatem cooperantem, remotam et completam non plene formalizantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-05","text":"Corpus assumptum ut instrumentum repraesentativum et corpus ut terminus praesentiae virtualis coordinantur, sed non datur regula universalis qua eorum coincidentia vel separatio definiatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MP-01","text":"Corpus mutat functionem cum ab elemento cognitionis imperfectae ad medium manifestationis Angelicae transfertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MP-02","text":"Locus mutat rationem cum commensuratio quantitativa relinquitur et terminus virtutis immediatae constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MP-03","text":"Motus mutat rationem cum transitus per medium desinit esse necessarius et fit proprietas motus continui tantum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A8","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MP-04","text":"Tempus mutat rationem cum continuitas desinit esse universalis et successio nunc mensuram motus non continui accipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A12","CH_GGVC_P_45:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite describitur ut campus stratorum relationum, in quo natura determinat quid ens sit, virtus determinat quid efficere possit, et figura sensibilis determinat quid homini manifestari possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:HSI-02","text":"Angelus emergit ut subiectum finitum sine indigentia corporali, cuius identitas non in possessione loci sed in virtute localiter applicabili consistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:HSI-03","text":"Tempus emergit ut effectus ordinationis actionum finitarum: non flumen cosmologicum omnibus idem, sed series priorum et posteriorum applicationum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio Angelica non est fuga a loco, sed gubernatio finitae applicationis virtutis per transitum continuum vel non continuum ad ministerium alterius.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de intellectu incorporeo, corpore assumpto, applicatione virtutis, finitate termini et successione locali sufficiunt ad machinam praesentis gregis restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est translatio corporis, loci et motus a praedicatis substantiae et quantitatis ad ordinem significationis, causalitatis virtualis et successionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MRT-B03","text":"Restitutio nondum plene determinat criterium unitatis termini virtualis, discrimen effectus vitalis et similitudinis vitae, neque mensurabilitatem successionis nunc discontinuorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MRT-B04","text":"Motus verus gregis servatur, quia progressio ab incorporeitate ad apparitionem, ab apparitione ad localitatem virtualem, et a localitate ad motum temporaliter ordinatum retinetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171847868600Z_960eb028","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 52–54","source_sha256":"478ec1a7bc63dc5490043bc5723eb012ca77d8827b1951a528343a485010be06","sha256":"559bfe1d39e14e29f2893b08e7d7ea6439d0900247d7e5f8d528b9e9b16f4cda","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:18:47.869543+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-01","text":"The sequence asks how a created intellectual substance, naturally incorporeal, can appear sensibly, be present definitively, and move locally without conversion into a body or into omnipresence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-02","text":"The global thesis establishes that angelic bodily manifestation is not possession of a natural body, but an extrinsic effect of a power applied to matter and place.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-03","text":"The argument proceeds through distinctions of modes of union, presence, and motion, such that the same incorporeality which excludes an essential body does not exclude local causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-04","text":"The movement of the system is spiral: the assumed body is first posited as a sign of appearance, then as the terminus of virtual application, and finally as the occasion of local and temporal succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-05","text":"Bodiliness does not vanish, but is reclassified from an element of nature into a representative medium and a terminus of spiritual operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-06","text":"The finitude of angelic power turns incorporeality into definitive presence, not into freedom from every created terminus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-07","text":"Angelic motion is not the translation of magnitude, but the ordered reapplication of power, which admits continuous or non-continuous motion and nevertheless retains before and after.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ABS-08","text":"The conclusion of the sequence is a non-equivocal typology: a body is present circumscriptively, an Angel definitively through power, God everywhere through infinite causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Perfect understanding does not require a natural body; therefore angelic incorporeality is a positive principle of perfection, not a mere privation of body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] A body, which is an instrument of acquisition for a soul that knows imperfectly, becomes for an Angel a contingent medium of manifestation rather than a complement of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] A common external appearance requires an extrinsic body, but an assumed body neither informs nor vivifies an Angel.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The application of power is the generative nexus through which an appearing body, local presence, and local motion are ordered under one account of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] Finite angelic power immediately determines one created terminus; hence neither omnipresence nor simultaneous angelic multilocation follows.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Angelic place is not a quantitative position, but the unity of the terminus to which power is immediately applied.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The assumed body has a double function: it is a sensible sign of spiritual power and the bodily terminus of virtual operation, and the identity of these functions is not presumed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Angelic motion consists in a succession of virtual applications, not in a division of angelic substance or simultaneous presence in several places.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Physical effects and likenesses of life may be granted, while a formal vital principle and proper vital acts are denied.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A10","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Angelic perfection excludes motion from a need proper to itself, but admits voluntarily determined motion in the service of a creature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-01","text":"Incorporeality preserves its identity, but its function changes: from the negation of a natural body it passes to the account of local presence and non-quantitative motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_44:A1","CH_GGVC_P_45:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-02","text":"Body recurs in a changed form: in appearance it is a representative instrument, in locality it is the terminus of power, and neither account returns to angelic nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-03","text":"Local determination passes from motion per accidens of the assumed body to formal determination through application of power and to a succession of termini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A14","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-04","text":"The action that in appearance supplied a likeness of life is reclassified in motion as the actual act of power without an intrinsic vital principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-05","text":"Continuity does not persist as a universal condition of motion, but becomes a variable mode of local application: through an intermediate in continuous motion, without an intermediate in non-continuous motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-06","text":"Time changes from a universal cosmological index into the measure of the succession of angelic local dispositions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RMD-07","text":"The difference of God, Angel, and body persists, but is explained not merely by a scale of dignity but by a typology of modes of presence, causality, and terminus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-01","text":"Condensation of air and coloration of matter are local mechanisms of appearance; they do not bear the global structure, which understands the assumed body under the account of virtual mediation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-02","text":"The negations of nutrition, generation, and animal life remain local apophatic proofs; they rise to the level of the sequence only as a separation between visible effect and vital principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_43:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-03","text":"The exclusion of several Angels from the same place ceases to be a singular question of co-locality and becomes a global rule concerning the exclusivity of complete immediate causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-04","text":"The distinction between continuous and non-continuous motion is amplified beyond local physics, because it constitutes the mode in which finite causality can have its own time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-05","text":"The representative body and the virtually determined place are coordinated at the level of the present sequence, but are not identified: the former designates signification, the latter the terminus of immediate operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:CGD-06","text":"The ordering of appearances to the incarnation of the Word remains a local teleological extension; the mechanism of the present sequence can be reconstructed without it from the distinctions of nature, power, place, and motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the conversion of angelic incorporeality into animal nature or into a naturally proper angelic body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A6","CH_GGVC_P_43:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-02","text":"The system excludes the reduction of common external appearance to a private image or to solitary prophetic phantasy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-03","text":"The system excludes place as a receptacle that contains, measures, or makes an Angel quantitatively circumscribed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_44:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-04","text":"The system excludes the inference by which the incorporeality of a creature would immediately confer virtual infinity, ubiquity, or multilocation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-05","text":"The system excludes the transition from external effect to angelic formal life, sensation, nutrition, or generation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-06","text":"The system excludes both instantaneous motion and the subjection of every angelic motion to universal celestial time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:GNX-07","text":"The system excludes a plurality of complete immediate causes concerning one and the same local terminus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that every perfect intellect receives knowledge from sensibles, organs, and a natural body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that whatever is seen externally is thereby alive, animated, or of the nature simulated by its sensible figure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX2","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that space and time under a single quantitative form render every spiritual, bodily, and divine creature comprehensible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that the relation of mover to movable thing or external effect demonstrates through itself substantial union, formal life, or identity of nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_45:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that complete immediate causality can be multiplied without division of the terminus, subordination of causes, or change in the account of causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","CH_GGVC_P_44:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSA-01","text":"The possibility of a spiritual creature simultaneously without body, without local terminus, and without ordered temporal succession is unavailable to the system.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSA-02","text":"The identification of divine omnipresence with angelic virtual presence is prohibited, because causal infinity is not an extension of creaturely finitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A6","CH_GGVC_P_44:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSA-03","text":"A sensible figure cannot exhaustively exhibit spiritual nature, because the visible sign is ordered to the signified power and does not absorb it.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSA-04","text":"Space and time as neutral, homogeneous, and through-themselves determinative receptacles of presence are excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_45:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-01","text":"The assumed body is not an exception to angelic incorporeality, but a double exteriority by which spiritual power simultaneously produces a sensible sign and immediately touches a bodily terminus.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-01","CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","CL_GGVC_18:GA-04","CL_GGVC_18:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-02","text":"The finitude of angelic power not only denies ubiquity, but constitutes every angelic presence as the choice of a determinate created terminus.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-03","text":"Public appearance does not reveal angelic nature through figurative identity, but establishes a field in which visible sign and invisible causality are read in coordination.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","CL_GGVC_18:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-04","text":"Motion, sound, and bodily figure can be causally real without bodily life, because the actuality of angelic power is not the actuality of a vivifying form.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-04","CL_GGVC_18:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12","CH_GGVC_P_45:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-05","text":"The exclusivity of the immediate terminus and the negation of multilocation entail that angelic local change is ordered through succession, not through simultaneous expansion of presence.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A3","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-06","text":"The absence of an intermediate in non-continuous motion does not eliminate time, because the succession of local termini retains before and after even where spatial continuity is not traversed.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:XD-07","text":"Ministerial angelic motion describes finite power which does not need from itself, but determines itself locally according to the need of the creature it serves.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-01","text":"The sequence constitutes the ontology of a created spiritual agent as exteriorizable finite causality: it is not a bodily thing, nor an act free from every created terminus.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-01","CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-02","text":"Space is reordered as the order of the causal terminus, time as the order of the succession of applications; neither remains an ontologically univocal measure of every being.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CL_GGVC_18:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-03","text":"Human sensible knowledge receives a true sign of spiritual agency without the bodily figure literally exhibiting spiritual nature.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-02","CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","CL_GGVC_18:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-04","text":"The hierarchy of body, Angel, and God is arranged not by quantity of distance, but by mode of causing, containing, and being terminated.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-05","CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-05","text":"Perfection is not opposed to ministry: an Angel does not move because something is lacking to itself, but so that its power may be orderly applied to the need of another.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:BSD-06","text":"The distinctions of life, place, and motion prevent sensible manifestation, causal efficacy, and ontological identity from being confused in one predicate.","refs":["CL_GGVC_18:GA-03","CL_GGVC_18:GA-06","CL_GGVC_18:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-01","text":"Incorporeal understanding → negation of natural body → representative assumed body → virtual application → definitive presence → local succession → proper time: the circuit confirms incorporeality through ordered exteriority, not through absence of operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-02","text":"Finitude of power → one immediate terminus → exclusion of multilocation and co-locality → necessity of succession in motion: diminution of extension becomes the principle of local order.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A3","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-03","text":"Likeness of life → negation of vital principle → concession of external effects → return to spiritual power: appearance is preserved, biology is excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-04","text":"Change in the mode of application of power bifurcates motion into continuous and non-continuous, but both branches return to the attractor of temporal succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:RLE-05","text":"The application of power is the hidden attractor that gathers body, place, motion, finitude, and ministry into one causally ordered mechanism.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B01","text":"Incorporeal understanding → body is not a condition of angelic perfection → natural body is excluded.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B02","text":"Common external appearance → a body outside the seer is required → a temporal assumed body becomes the medium of manifestation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B03","text":"Assumed body as representative instrument → sensible effects are granted → formal life, sensation, and nutrition are denied.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B04","text":"Application of power to body → angelic place becomes the terminus of virtual causality → finitude of power definitively constitutes one place.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B05","text":"Successive reapplication of power to diverse places → angelic motion → continuous passage through an intermediate or non-continuous passage without an intermediate.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B06","text":"Succession of local dispositions → before and after → proper angelic time, which does not depend on the motion of the heavens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FGS-B07","text":"Angelic will → determination of the mode and speed of application → ministry to another's need without need in the mover.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A14","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B01","text":"Non-bodily understanding → rejection of a natural angelic body.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B02","text":"Rejection of a natural body → admission of an assumed body as external sign and mobile instrument.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B03","text":"Representative body → separation of external effect from formal life.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A11","CH_GGVC_P_43:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B04","text":"Separation of nature and body → reconstitution of place through application of power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B05","text":"Finite application of power → one local terminus → exclusion of angelic ubiquity and co-locality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B06","text":"One successive terminus → continuous or non-continuous motion → proper non-instantaneous time.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:AFM-B07","text":"Voluntary motion → ministerial causality → a perfect creature locally efficacious yet finitely determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-01","text":"Body is reclassified into three distinct orders: substantial nature, representative sign, and terminus of virtual operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-02","text":"Place is reclassified from occupied space to the constituted terminus of immediate causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-03","text":"Motion is reclassified from a single continuous translation to a kind of local change that can admit continuity or discontinuity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-04","text":"Angelic time becomes the account of operative succession, derived universally neither from the motion of the heavens nor from bodily continuity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-05","text":"The distinction between God, Angel, and body moves from the simple opposition of spirit and matter to degrees of infinity, virtual finitude, and quantity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MME-06","text":"The reading of appearance becomes a method that preserves sensible figure, but prevents its conversion into angelic biology, anthropology, or ontology.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:SNX5","CH_GGVC_P_43:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level decides whether an Angel assumes a body, is in a place, and moves locally.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level orders the relations of body, place, and motion through the mode of cognition, application of power, and succession of causal termini.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level dissolves objections from human figure, point, filling of space, continuity, and time through distinction of the kind of relation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level describes the finitude of the spiritual creature as bounded virtual presence and change subject to succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_45:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological level performs the distinctions it affirms: nature, sign, effect, life, place, motion, and time are separated so that illegitimate analogies may be prevented.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS7","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-01","text":"The assumed body is posited as materially real, public to external vision, and vitally empty at once; the criterion by which external likeness is distinguished from true life is established metaphysically.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_43:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-02","text":"The unity of angelic place depends on the terminus of power, but the extension of the terminus can vary; the account of unity containing that variation is not further resolved.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-03","text":"The application of power to a new terminus, made all at once, is difficult to reconcile with the plurality of successive nows required for temporal motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-04","text":"The exclusion of co-locality is grounded in complete immediate causality, but the differences among cooperative, remote, and complete causality are not fully formalized.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:FL-05","text":"The assumed body as representative instrument and body as the terminus of virtual presence are coordinated, but no universal rule is given by which their coincidence or separation is defined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MP-01","text":"Body changes function when it is transferred from an element of imperfect cognition to a medium of angelic manifestation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A3","CH_GGVC_P_43:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MP-02","text":"Place changes account when quantitative commensuration is abandoned and the terminus of immediate power is constituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_44:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MP-03","text":"Motion changes account when passage through an intermediate ceases to be necessary and becomes a property of continuous motion alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A8","CH_GGVC_P_45:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MP-04","text":"Time changes account when continuity ceases to be universal and succession of nows receives the measure of non-continuous motion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A12","CH_GGVC_P_45:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly described as a field of layered relations, in which nature determines what a being is, power determines what it can effect, and sensible figure determines what can be manifested to a human being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:HSI-02","text":"An Angel emerges as a finite subject without bodily need, whose identity consists not in possession of place but in locally applicable power.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:HSI-03","text":"Time emerges as an effect of the ordering of finite actions: not a cosmological river identical for all, but a series of prior and posterior applications.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A11","CH_GGVC_P_45:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:HSI-04","text":"Angelic navigation is not flight from place, but the governance of finite application of power through continuous or non-continuous passage in the service of another.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_45:A6","CH_GGVC_P_45:A7","CH_GGVC_P_45:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MRT-B01","text":"Axioms concerning incorporeal understanding, assumed body, application of power, finitude of terminus, and local succession suffice to reconstruct the mechanism of the present sequence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_43:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_44:A4","CH_GGVC_P_45:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the translation of body, place, and motion from predicates of substance and quantity into the order of signification, virtual causality, and succession.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:A13","CH_GGVC_P_44:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction does not yet fully determine the criterion of unity of the virtual terminus, the difference between vital effect and likeness of life, nor the measurability of the succession of discontinuous nows.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_18:MRT-B04","text":"The true movement of the sequence is preserved, because the progression from incorporeality to appearance, from appearance to virtual locality, and from locality to temporally ordered motion is retained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_43:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_44:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_45:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_18@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_18:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 52–54","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 51 · Prima pars · Quaestio 52 · Prima pars · Quaestio 53"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 55–57","order":19,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_46","CH_GGVC_P_47","CH_GGVC_P_48"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_19@R001","sha256":"95f992510a33bdd4c2c0650c21598a332021ab081261be8b169e003dfd5f6192","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B01","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo substantia intellectualis separata, finita nec actus purus, cognoscere possit sine coalescentia substantiae, esse, virtutis et operationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B02","text":"Systema cognitionem angelicam constituit non ex identitate essentiae cum omnibus cognitis, sed ex distributione formarum, specierum et similitudinum proportionatarum finitae naturae intellectuali.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B03","text":"Argumentatio diagnosticam oppositionem instituit inter Deum, in quo esse, intelligere et agere identice conveniunt, et creaturam intellectualem, cuius perfectio per distinctiones internas exercetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B04","text":"Motus systematis transit ab ontologia actus et potentiae ad necessitatem specierum, deinde ad formas praesentiae quibus Angelus seipsum, alios angelos et Deum diversimode cognoscit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B05","text":"Motus non est linearis, sed recursivus: finitas essentiae redit ut distinctio operationis, ut insufficientia medii cognitivi, et ut terminus cognitionis divinae naturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B06","text":"Clausura systematis est cognitio naturalis analogica Dei, quae veram similitudinem admittit, sed visionem essentiae et comprehensionem excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B07","text":"Hierarchia intellectualis non per maiorem notitiarum congeriem, sed per pauciora media universaliora et eminentiora ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B08","text":"Methodus argumentativa nomina psychologica et traditionales divisiones potentiarum ad rationes ontologicas actus, obiecti, organi et similitudinis revocat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Omnis intellectus creatus finitus ex distinctione essentiae et esse intelligi debet; ideo eius operationes et perfectiones cognitivae non sunt ipsa essentia subsistens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Deus solus est terminus identitatis plenae inter esse, intelligere et agere; omnis cognitio angelica intra participationem creatam manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Cognitio exigit obiectum potentiae formaliter unitum, sed modus huius unionis mutatur secundum cognitionem sui, alterius vel Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A1","CH_GGVC_P_48:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Esse naturale rei et esse intelligibile eius in cognoscente distinguuntur; haec distinctio cognitionem sine identitate naturali efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Absentia corporis naturaliter uniti removet facultates sensitivas et abstractionem per phantasmata, sed eam non in cognitionem immediatam absolutam convertit; species connaturales substituuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_47:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Influxus divinus simul originem specierum, similitudinum rerum et proportionem universi ad cognitionem angelicam constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Perfectio cognitiva superior non est multiplicatio formarum, sed compressio mediorum: pauciora universalia eminentiora plures rationes proprias continent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","CH_GGVC_P_47:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Essentia angelica finita non potest esse medium exhaustivum omnium quae obiectum intellectus communis complectitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A2","CH_GGVC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Cognitio angelica distribuitur per gradus praesentiae: substantia propria formaliter adest, alius angelus intentionaliter, Deus per similitudinem creatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_48:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Infinitas divina cognitionem naturalem creatam non annihilat, sed ipsius adaequationem, comprehensionem et visionem essentiae terminat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-01","text":"Essentia angelica redit cum functione mutata: primum negatur esse ipsum intelligere, deinde negatur esse medium omnium cognitorum, postremo affirmatur esse principium cognitionis sui tantum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-02","text":"Species intelligibilis transit a medio necessario distincto ab essentia ad dotem connaturalem divinitus causatam, atque deinde ad praesentiam intentionalem alterius angeli.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D1","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-03","text":"Absentia corporis redit non ut mera privatio, sed ut mutatio mechanismi: excludit sensum, abstractionem et necessitatem propinquitatis localis ad cognoscendum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_47:D4","CH_GGVC_P_47:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-04","text":"Universalitas mutatur ex ambitu obiecti intellectus in virtutem medii eminentis, quod singularia propria cognoscere potest sine dissolutione in cognitionem vagam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","CH_GGVC_P_47:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-05","text":"Deus redit simul ut causa specierum, mensura hierarchiae et terminus negativus cognitionis creaturae; causalitas positiva et incomprehensibilitas non separantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-06","text":"Vocabula sensitiva et psychologica manent, sed ab indicatione facultatum ad designationem similitudinum, actuum et modorum praesentiae transferuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D7","CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-01","text":"Distinctio intellectus agentis et possibilis manet localis condicionibus cognitionis humanae per phantasmata et intelligibilia potentia existentia; non ordinat architecturam angelicam totam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-02","text":"Attributiones sensus, memoriae et phantasiae Angelis manent locales regulis analogiae sermonis; in gradu praesentis synthesis tantum indicant necessitatem discernendi nomen a ratione metaphysica.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-03","text":"Distinctio substantiae, esse, virtutis et operationis ex limite metaphysico locali amplificatur in regulam generalem qua cognitio angelica per principia distincta constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-04","text":"Causalitas divina specierum, localiter explicans originem cognitionis, in gradu gregis fit nexus qui dispositionem universi et apparatum cognoscitivum simul ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-05","text":"Cognitio sui per essentiam non manet exceptio isolata, sed fit primus terminus systematis relationum inter praesentiam formalem, intentionalem et analogicam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-06","text":"Motus localis, localiter remotus ab acquisitione cognitionis, absorbetur in distinctionem latiorem inter praesentiam loci et praesentiam intentionalem obiecti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D7","CH_GGVC_P_48:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-01","text":"Systema excludit creaturam quae sit ipsum intelligere subsistens, quia identitas talis distinctiones inter Deum, Angelos et gradus cognitionis destrueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-02","text":"Systema excludit essentiam creatam quae una forma simplici omnes rationes rerum perfecte et proprie continere possit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-03","text":"Systema excludit doctrinam quae experientiam sensibilem vel abstractionem statuit fontem necessarium omnis cognitionis intellectualis creatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-04","text":"Systema excludit cognitionem univocam quae seipsum, alium angelum et Deum eodem modo praesentiae attingere praesumat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-05","text":"Systema excludit propinquitatem localem tamquam condicionem essentialem cognitionis angelicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_47:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-06","text":"Systema excludit visionem naturalem divinae essentiae atque comprehensionem Dei a quolibet intellectu creato.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_48:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse debet cognitionem intellectualem semper aut ex motu exteriori aut ex identitate naturali cognoscentis et cogniti procedere; species intentionalis tertium modum instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse debet immaterialitatem creatam statim in cognitionem infinitam vel exhaustivam converti; intelligibilitas est conditio, non adaequatio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse debet universalitatem cognitionis necessario vagam esse; sed explicatio eminentiae, qua una forma plures rationes proprias continet, mensuram intrinsecam incompletam relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse debet ordinem universi ab instrumentis cognitionis angelicae separari, quia dispositio rerum et species eis proportionatae sub una causalitate divina continentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_48:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSA-01","text":"Systema circumagit impossibilitatem omnis repraesentationis creatae quae divinae essentiae coextensiva fieret aut identitatem divinam esse, intelligere et causare participaret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSA-02","text":"Systema prohibet campum cognitionis totaliter perspicuum, in quo ipsum, alterum et Deus unius modi praesentiae fierent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSA-03","text":"Systema prohibet autonomiam completam intellectus creati, quia nec species nec proportio cognoscibilitatis extra divinam dispositionem constitui possunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-01","text":"Exceptio cognitionis sui necessitatem specierum non revocat: substantia propria est intelligibilis actu pro seipsa, sed essentia finita non est medium exhaustivum omnium cognitorum.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","CL_GGVC_19:GA-08","CL_GGVC_19:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-02","text":"Remotio mediationis corporalis non producit immediationem absolutam, sed acquisitionem experimentalem substituit specie connaturali divinitus data.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-03","text":"Compressio cognitiva hierarchica cognitionem singularium auget solum si universalitas medii eminentiam realem retinet; aliter universalitas in vagam communitatem relaberetur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-07","CL_GGVC_19:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_47:D8","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-04","text":"Esse intentionale separat cognitionem ab accessu locali et contactu causali: obiectum cognitum formaliter adest, quamvis naturaliter distet.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","CL_GGVC_19:GA-04","CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_47:D6","CH_GGVC_P_48:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-05","text":"Causalitas divina cognitionem angelicam dupliciter determinat: species constituit positive, sed infinitas essentiae divinae omnem adaequationem negative claudit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","CL_GGVC_19:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-06","text":"Si universum creatum amplificaretur, amplificatio non per acquisitionem experimentalem Angelorum, sed per novam proportionem specierum ad ordinem rerum intellegenda esset.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_48:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-01","text":"Cognitio reclassificatur ut topologia praesentiarum formalium, non ut oppositio simplex inter activitatem et passivitatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_46:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-02","text":"Perfectio intellectualis creata maxime alta non per identitatem immediatam cum rebus, sed per mediationem magis compressam et eminentem definitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-03","text":"Hierarchia angelica fit mensura propinquitatis ad unitatem divinam: quo intellectus creatus simplicior est, eo plura distincte per pauciora cognoscit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-04","text":"Finitas creaturae non est ignorantia nuda, sed productio relationum cognoscitivarum diversarum inter seipsum, alium et Deum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-05","text":"Providentia divina fit principium commune quo res producuntur et simul condiciones cognoscibilitatis earum in intellectibus angelicis constituuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-01","text":"Finitas essentiae → distinctio esse et operationis → insufficientia essentiae ut medii totalis → necessitas specierum → reditus finitatis ut terminus omnis cognitionis creaturae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-02","text":"Absentia corporis → absentia sensus et abstractionis → species connaturales → absentia acquisitionis localis → confirmatio cognitionis substantiae separatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_47:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-03","text":"Deus → species et similitudines creaturae → cognitio naturalis Dei per imaginem creatam → exclusio visionis essentiae → imminutio creaturae iterum declarata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11","CH_GGVC_P_48:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-04","text":"Pauciora media → maior universalitas → cognitio plurium propriorum → maior similitudo unitatis divinae, sed non imminutio finitudinis creatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_47:D8","CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-05","text":"Nomen traditum → examen conditionis ontologicae → recodificatio nominis per analogiam vel similitudinem → imminutio valoris probativi vocabuli nudi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B01","text":"Actus purus divinus + essentia creata participans → negatio identitatis inter substantiam, esse et operationem → constitutio interioris articulationis angelicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B02","text":"Absentia corporis naturaliter uniti → exclusio sensus et phantasmatum → exclusio abstractionis materialis ut via cognitionis angelicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_47:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B03","text":"Obiectum intellectus universale + essentia angelica finita → insufficientia essentiae ut medium omnium → necessitas specierum intelligibilium distinctarum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A3","CH_GGVC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B04","text":"Species divinitus causatae + immaterialitas substantiae separatae → cognitio connaturalis rerum → praesentia intentionalis aliorum angelorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B05","text":"Diversi modi praesentiae → cognitio sui per formam propriam, alterius per speciem intentionalem, Dei per similitudinem creatam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B06","text":"Compressio hierarchica mediorum → maior universalitas eminentior → cognitio naturalis analogica → clausura per incomprehensibilitatem divinae essentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AFM-B01","text":"Actus purus divinus → finitas creaturae intellectualis → separatio essentiae, esse, virtutis et operationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AFM-B02","text":"Separatio a corpore → remotio acquisitionis sensibilis → species connaturales divinitus fundatae → hierarchia cognitionis per pauciora media universaliora.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AFM-B03","text":"Praesentia sui → praesentia intentionalis alterius → similitudo creaturalis Dei → cognitio naturalis analogica → exclusio visionis comprehensivae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_48:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-01","text":"Distinctio cognitionis intellectualis et sensitivae reordinatur ut differentia ontologica inter operationem sine organo et operationem per organum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-02","text":"Universalitas reclassificatur ut densitas et eminentia medii cognoscitivi, non ut imminutio cognitionis propriae vel singularis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-03","text":"Locus et motus ex officio epistemico removentur atque ad ordinem operationis angelicae in rebus localibus rediguntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-04","text":"Oppositio inter cognitionem directam et mediatam dissolvitur in tres praesentias: essentiam praesentem, similitudinem intentionalem et similitudinem creatam relucentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-05","text":"Providentia divina non solum causa rerum, sed etiam condicio intelligibilitatis earum intra mentem angelicam fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei, quaestio tractat utrum Angelus cognoscat per essentiam, per species et per quos modos seipsum, alios angelos atque Deum attingat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali, cognitio constituitur ex proportione potentiae, formae intelligibilis, modi essendi et modi praesentiae obiecti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico, argumentatio opponit usui vocabulorum nudorum examen rationum actus, similitudinis, esse naturalis et esse intentionalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico, ordo essendi fundat ordinem cognoscendi: rationes rerum sunt in Deo, species in Angelis, res autem secundum proprios modos in universo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo, forma quaestionum ipsa ostendit quod omnis difficultas cognitiva per structuram unionis, similitudinis et proportionis resolvenda est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FL-01","text":"Cognitio sui per essentiam tensionem gignit cum negatione essentiae angelicae tamquam medii totalis; stabilitas obtinetur tantum per restrictionem cognitionis per essentiam ad ipsum Angelum cognoscentem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FL-02","text":"Universalitas eminentis speciei cognitionem plurium propriorum promittit, sed mensura intrinseca excellentiae qua haec promissio sustinetur non formaliter explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FL-03","text":"Species connaturales simul originem divinam et absentiam acquisitionis temporalis retinent, ita ut relatio inter donum naturae et influxum divinum terminis non plene distinctis maneat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FL-04","text":"Cognitio naturalis Dei simul specie immediate accepta assimilatur et cognitioni speculari comparatur; systema hanc oscillationem per gradum similitudinis, non per genus univocum, continet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MP-01","text":"Essentia angelica mutat munus ex eo quod negatur esse ipsum intelligere in eo quod affirmatur esse forma intelligibilis actu pro cognitione sui.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_48:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MP-02","text":"Immaterialitas mutat munus ex negatione facultatum organicarum in affirmationem cognitionis non acquisitae, sed haec affirmatio ad visionem divinae essentiae non extenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_47:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite apparet ut ordo stratificatus formarum et similitudinum, in quo dispositio universi et dispositio cognoscibilitatis eius eadem causalitate divina connectuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:HSI-02","text":"Angelus apparet ut nodus intellectualis relatus, sibi formaliter praesens, alteris intentionaliter apertus, et ad Deum per imaginem finitam ordinatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:HSI-03","text":"Tempus, motus et distantia non sunt formae essentiales cognitionis angelicae, sed condiciones exteriores operationum quas Angelus in rebus localibus exercet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio intellectualis possibilis est per proportiones formarum et similitudinum, non per captationem divinae essentiae; cognitio naturalis manet vera sine dominio comprehensivo.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_48:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MRT-B01","text":"Nexus inter participationem creatam, unionem formalem obiecti, absentiam corporis, originem divinam specierum et terminum incomprehensibilitatis sufficit ad restituendam machinam praesentis gregis.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-01","CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","CL_GGVC_19:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi eadem proportio potentiae et formae simul necessitatem specierum, diversitatem praesentiarum et hierarchiam universalitatis explicat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","CL_GGVC_19:GA-07","CL_GGVC_19:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MRT-B03","text":"Restant minus determinata mensura excellentiae universalitatis et status exactus specierum connaturalium divinitus acceptarum; hae lacunae tamen limites internos, non dissolutionem systematis, constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MRT-B04","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat si ab insufficentia essentiae finitae ad species, a speciebus ad praesentias relationum, et ab his ad terminum cognitionis divinae procedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T171923822755Z_e1ea6a14","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 55–57","source_sha256":"95f992510a33bdd4c2c0650c21598a332021ab081261be8b169e003dfd5f6192","sha256":"a9886443bbca1fcb02c64e3d681980320aab41c69418da5edbf8513110921cb8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:19:23.823730+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B01","text":"The central question is how a separate intellectual substance, finite and not pure act, can know without a coalescence of substance, being, power, and operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B02","text":"The system establishes angelic cognition not from the identity of essence with all things known, but from the distribution of forms, species, and likenesses proportionate to a finite intellectual nature.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B03","text":"The argument establishes a diagnostic opposition between God, in whom being, understanding, and acting coincide identically, and the intellectual creature, whose perfection is exercised through internal distinctions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B04","text":"The movement of the system proceeds from the ontology of act and potency to the necessity of species, then to the forms of presence by which the Angel knows itself, other angels, and God in different ways.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B05","text":"The movement is not linear, but recursive: the finitude of essence returns as the distinction of operation, as the insufficiency of the cognitive medium, and as the limit of natural divine knowledge.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B06","text":"The closure of the system is analogical natural knowledge of God, which admits a true likeness, but excludes the vision of essence and comprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B07","text":"Intellectual hierarchy is ordered not through a greater accumulation of cognitions, but through fewer, more universal and more eminent media.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AS-B08","text":"The argumentative method refers psychological names and traditional divisions of powers back to ontological accounts of act, object, organ, and likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every finite created intellect must be understood from the distinction of essence and being; therefore its operations and cognitive perfections are not the subsisting essence itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] God alone is the term of full identity between being, understanding, and acting; all angelic cognition remains within created participation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Cognition requires an object formally united to a power, but the mode of this union changes according to cognition of self, another, or God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A1","CH_GGVC_P_48:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The natural being of a thing and its intelligible being in the knower are distinct; this distinction makes cognition without natural identity possible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] The absence of a naturally united body removes sensory powers and abstraction through phantasms, but does not convert it into absolute immediate cognition; connatural species are substituted.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_47:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Divine influx simultaneously establishes the origin of species, the likenesses of things, and the proportion of the universe to angelic cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Higher cognitive perfection is not a multiplication of forms, but a compression of media: fewer more universal and eminent forms contain more proper accounts.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","CH_GGVC_P_47:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] A finite angelic essence cannot be an exhaustive medium of all that the object of the common intellect embraces.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A2","CH_GGVC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Angelic cognition is distributed through degrees of presence: one's own substance is formally present, another angel intentionally, God through a created likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_48:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Divine infinity does not annihilate natural created cognition, but limits its adequation, comprehension, and vision of essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-01","text":"Angelic essence returns with a changed function: first it is denied to be understanding itself, then it is denied to be the medium of all things known, finally it is affirmed to be the principle of cognition of itself alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-02","text":"The intelligible species passes from a necessary medium distinct from essence to a connatural endowment caused by God, and then to the intentional presence of another angel.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D1","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-03","text":"The absence of a body returns not as mere privation, but as a change of mechanism: it excludes sense, abstraction, and the necessity of local proximity for knowing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_47:D4","CH_GGVC_P_47:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-04","text":"Universality changes from the scope of the object of intellect into the power of an eminent medium, which can know proper singulars without dissolving into vague cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A6","CH_GGVC_P_47:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-05","text":"God returns at once as the cause of species, the measure of hierarchy, and the negative limit of creaturely cognition; positive causality and incomprehensibility are not separated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A2","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RMD-06","text":"Sensory and psychological terms remain, but are transferred from indicating powers to designating likenesses, acts, and modes of presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D7","CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-01","text":"The distinction between agent and possible intellect remains local to the conditions of human cognition through phantasms and potentially existing intelligibles; it does not order the whole angelic architecture.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-02","text":"Attributions of sense, memory, and imagination to Angels remain local to the rules of analogy in speech; at the level of the present synthesis they indicate only the need to distinguish name from metaphysical account.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-03","text":"The distinction of substance, being, power, and operation is amplified from a local metaphysical limit into a general rule by which angelic cognition is constituted through distinct principles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-04","text":"Divine causality of species, locally explaining the origin of cognition, at the level of the group becomes the nexus that simultaneously orders the disposition of the universe and the cognitive apparatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-05","text":"Cognition of self through essence does not remain an isolated exception, but becomes the first term of the system of relations among formal, intentional, and analogical presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:CGD-06","text":"Local motion, locally removed from the acquisition of cognition, is absorbed into the broader distinction between the presence of place and the intentional presence of the object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D7","CH_GGVC_P_48:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes a creature that is subsisting understanding itself, because such identity would destroy distinctions between God, Angels, and degrees of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-02","text":"The system excludes a created essence that could perfectly and properly contain all the accounts of things in one simple form.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-03","text":"The system excludes a doctrine that establishes sensible experience or abstraction as the necessary source of all created intellectual cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-04","text":"The system excludes univocal cognition that presumes to attain itself, another angel, and God through the same mode of presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-05","text":"The system excludes local proximity as an essential condition of angelic cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_47:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:GNX-06","text":"The system excludes natural vision of the divine essence and comprehension of God by any created intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_48:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that intellectual cognition always proceeds either from external motion or from the natural identity of knower and known; the intentional species establishes a third mode.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that created immateriality is immediately converted into infinite or exhaustive cognition; intelligibility is a condition, not adequation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that universality of cognition is necessarily vague; but the explanation of eminence, by which one form contains several proper accounts, leaves an incomplete intrinsic measure.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that the order of the universe is separated from the instruments of angelic cognition, because the disposition of things and species proportioned to them are contained under one divine causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_48:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSA-01","text":"The system revolves around the impossibility of every created representation that would become coextensive with the divine essence or participate in the divine identity of being, understanding, and causing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSA-02","text":"The system forbids a totally transparent field of cognition, in which self, other, and God would become of one mode of presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSA-03","text":"The system forbids the complete autonomy of the created intellect, because neither species nor the proportion of cognoscibility can be constituted outside divine disposition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-01","text":"The exception of cognition of self does not revoke the necessity of species: one's own substance is actually intelligible to itself, but a finite essence is not an exhaustive medium of all things known.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","CL_GGVC_19:GA-08","CL_GGVC_19:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-02","text":"The removal of bodily mediation does not produce absolute immediacy, but substitutes for experimental acquisition a connatural species divinely given.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-03","text":"Hierarchical cognitive compression increases cognition of singulars only if the universality of the medium retains real eminence; otherwise universality would relapse into vague commonality.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-07","CL_GGVC_19:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_47:D8","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-04","text":"Intentional being separates cognition from local access and causal contact: the known object is formally present, although naturally distant.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","CL_GGVC_19:GA-04","CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_47:D6","CH_GGVC_P_48:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-05","text":"Divine causality determines angelic cognition in two ways: it positively constitutes species, but the infinity of the divine essence negatively closes off every adequation.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","CL_GGVC_19:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:XD-06","text":"If the created universe were enlarged, the enlargement would have to be understood not through the experimental acquisition of Angels, but through a new proportion of species to the order of things.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_48:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-01","text":"Cognition is reclassified as a topology of formal presences, not as a simple opposition between activity and passivity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_46:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-02","text":"The highest created intellectual perfection is defined not through immediate identity with things, but through more compressed and eminent mediation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-03","text":"Angelic hierarchy becomes a measure of proximity to divine unity: the simpler a created intellect is, the more it knows distinctly through fewer means.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-04","text":"The finitude of the creature is not bare ignorance, but the production of diverse cognitive relations among self, another, and God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:BSD-05","text":"Divine providence becomes the common principle by which things are produced and at the same time the conditions of their cognoscibility are constituted in angelic intellects.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-01","text":"Finitude of essence → distinction of being and operation → insufficiency of essence as a total medium → necessity of species → return of finitude as the limit of all creaturely cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A1","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-02","text":"Absence of body → absence of sense and abstraction → connatural species → absence of local acquisition → confirmation of the cognition of a separate substance.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_47:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-03","text":"God → species and likenesses of the creature → natural knowledge of God through a created image → exclusion of vision of essence → creaturely diminution again declared.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A11","CH_GGVC_P_48:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-04","text":"Fewer media → greater universality → cognition of more proper things → greater likeness to divine unity, but not diminution of created finitude.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_47:D8","CH_GGVC_P_47:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:RLE-05","text":"Traditional name → examination of ontological condition → recodification of the name through analogy or likeness → diminution of the probative value of the bare term.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B01","text":"Divine pure act + participating created essence → negation of identity between substance, being, and operation → constitution of interior angelic articulation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_46:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B02","text":"Absence of a naturally united body → exclusion of sense and phantasms → exclusion of material abstraction as the way of angelic cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_47:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B03","text":"Universal object of intellect + finite angelic essence → insufficiency of essence as the medium of all things → necessity of distinct intelligible species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A3","CH_GGVC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B04","text":"Divinely caused species + immateriality of separate substance → connatural cognition of things → intentional presence of other angels.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A9","CH_GGVC_P_48:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B05","text":"Diverse modes of presence → cognition of self through its own form, of another through an intentional species, of God through a created likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FGS-B06","text":"Hierarchical compression of media → greater and more eminent universality → analogical natural cognition → closure through the incomprehensibility of the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AFM-B01","text":"Divine pure act → finitude of the intellectual creature → separation of essence, being, power, and operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_46:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AFM-B02","text":"Separation from body → removal of sensible acquisition → divinely grounded connatural species → hierarchy of cognition through fewer more universal media.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A9","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:AFM-B03","text":"Presence of self → intentional presence of another → creaturely likeness of God → analogical natural cognition → exclusion of comprehensive vision.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_48:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-01","text":"The distinction between intellectual and sensory cognition is reordered as an ontological difference between operation without an organ and operation through an organ.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-02","text":"Universality is reclassified as the density and eminence of the cognitive medium, not as diminution of proper or singular cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-03","text":"Place and motion are removed from epistemic office and reduced to the order of angelic operation in local things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-04","text":"The opposition between direct and mediated cognition is dissolved into three presences: present essence, intentional likeness, and resplendent created likeness.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MME-05","text":"Divine providence becomes not only the cause of things, but also the condition of their intelligibility within the angelic mind.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the question treats whether an Angel knows through essence, through species, and by what modes it attains itself, other angels, and God.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, cognition is constituted from the proportion of power, intelligible form, mode of being, and mode of the object's presence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the argument opposes to the use of bare terms an examination of the accounts of act, likeness, natural being, and intentional being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_48:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological level, the order of being founds the order of knowing: the accounts of things are in God, species in Angels, and things according to their proper modes in the universe.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the form of the questions itself shows that every cognitive difficulty must be resolved through the structure of union, likeness, and proportion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:A10","CH_GGVC_P_48:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FL-01","text":"Cognition of self through essence generates tension with the denial of angelic essence as a total medium; stability is obtained only by restricting cognition through essence to the knowing Angel itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_47:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FL-02","text":"The universality of an eminent species promises cognition of more proper things, but the intrinsic measure of excellence by which this promise is sustained is not formally explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FL-03","text":"Connatural species simultaneously retain divine origin and the absence of temporal acquisition, so that the relation between the gift of nature and divine influx remains in terms not fully distinguished.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:FL-04","text":"Natural knowledge of God is simultaneously assimilated to a species immediately received and compared to mirror-like cognition; the system contains this oscillation through degree of likeness, not through a univocal genus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MP-01","text":"Angelic essence changes its role from that which is denied to be understanding itself to that which is affirmed to be an actually intelligible form for cognition of self.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_48:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MP-02","text":"Immateriality changes its role from the negation of organic powers to the affirmation of unacquired cognition, but this affirmation is not extended to vision of the divine essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_46:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_47:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as a stratified order of forms and likenesses, in which the disposition of the universe and the disposition of its cognoscibility are connected by the same divine causality.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:HSI-02","text":"The Angel appears as a related intellectual node, formally present to itself, intentionally open to others, and ordered toward God through a finite image.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:HSI-03","text":"Time, motion, and distance are not essential forms of angelic cognition, but external conditions of operations that the Angel exercises in local things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:HSI-04","text":"Intellectual navigation is possible through proportions of forms and likenesses, not through apprehension of the divine essence; natural cognition remains true without comprehensive mastery.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_48:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_48:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MRT-B01","text":"The nexus among created participation, formal union of the object, absence of body, divine origin of species, and the limit of incomprehensibility suffices to restore the mechanism of the present group.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-01","CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","CL_GGVC_19:GA-05","CL_GGVC_19:GA-06","CL_GGVC_19:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_48:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is where the same proportion of power and form simultaneously explains the necessity of species, the diversity of presences, and the hierarchy of universality.","refs":["CL_GGVC_19:GA-03","CL_GGVC_19:GA-07","CL_GGVC_19:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MRT-B03","text":"The measure of the excellence of universality and the exact status of connatural species divinely received remain less determined; these gaps nevertheless constitute internal limits, not dissolution of the system.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT5","CH_GGVC_P_47:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_19:MRT-B04","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement if it proceeds from the insufficiency of finite essence to species, from species to relational presences, and from these to the limit of divine cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_47:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_48:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_19@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_19:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 55–57","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 54 · Prima pars · Quaestio 55 · Prima pars · Quaestio 56"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 58–60","order":20,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_49","CH_GGVC_P_50","CH_GGVC_P_51"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_20@R001","sha256":"56810b6772383bea8180ec53f05aa461a284a79342c28e58b7cc7d0e926acb92","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo natura angelica cognitionem, operationem intellectualem et voluntatem habeat sine eo quod intellectus creatus cum intellectu divino confundatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-02","text":"Thesis globalis est angelum intra ambitum naturalem speciebus connaturalibus complete perfici, sed hac perfectione neque omniscientiam neque sufficientiam supernaturalem neque autonomiam adipisci.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-03","text":"Argumentatio ab ordine entium et modo recipientis transit ad formam actus intellectualis, deinde ex universalitate cogniti appetitum intellectualem et libertatem elicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-04","text":"Motus systematis est recursivus et spiralis: cognitio universalis voluntatem generat, voluntas autem limites cognitionis, possibilitatem erroris et necessitatem ordinationis divinae iterum determinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_51:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-05","text":"Multiplicitas rerum, operationum et potentiarum non per aggregationem, sed per unitatem speciei, rationem formalem obiecti et medium cognitionis ordinatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","CH_GGVC_P_50:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-06","text":"Limites cognitionis angelicae non sunt merae privationes, sed termini positivi quibus futurum contingens, interior libertas et secretum divinum a naturali intelligibilitate secernuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-07","text":"Visio Verbi perfectionem naturalem non evacuat, sed eam in cognitionem beatificam non comprehensivam, revelationem graduatam et officium hierarchicum inserit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-08","text":"Clausura huius gradus non est terminatio statica, sed forma perfectionis creatae quae naturaliter completa, supernaturaliter aperta et ad bonum se excedens ordinata manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Omnis receptio cognitiva et appetitiva determinatur secundum modum recipientis, non secundum nudam condicionem materialem obiecti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A2","CH_GGVC_P_51:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Intellectus angelicus intra ordinem naturalem speciebus intelligibilibus connaturalibus completur neque cognitionem a sensibilibus abstrahendo acquirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Universalitas progreditur ab eminentiori repraesentatione plurium, per unitatem formalem intelligibilis, ad apprehensionem universalis rationis boni.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Perfectio intellectualis angelica consequentias naturales in principiis et praedicata in quidditatibus immediate continet, ideoque discursum acquisitivum et compositionem operativam excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A11","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Unitas actus, distinctio potentiarum et diversitas cognitionum a ratione formali obiecti atque a medio cognoscendi pendent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Perfectio creata est completudo relativa ad ambitum naturae, non plenitudo quae omne intelligibile aut appetibile exhauriat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Quod nondum habet esse proprium, quod ab actu libero pendet, aut quod ex pura voluntate Dei procedit, naturali cognitioni angelicae non necessario patet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_49:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Voluntas primum terminum cognitionis naturalis constituit, deinde iudicium naturale ordinat vel deordinat, tandem ut appetitus intellectualis boni universalis explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Determinatio intellectus ad verum naturale cum libertate voluntatis compatitur, quia cognitio veri et electio particularis boni diversis rationibus formalibus mensurantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A10","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] In creatura intellectuali essentia, intellectus et voluntas realiter distinguuntur; earum identitas ad Deum solum pertinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Verbum est principium intelligibilitatis, medium unitarium cognitionis beatificae et terminus reditus cognitionis creaturae ad suam causam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Subiectum angelicum constituitur ut naturaliter perfectum, supernaturaliter receptivum et appetitive ordinatum ad bonum quod propriam essentiam excedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D1","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-01","text":"Species connaturales identitatem structuralem servant, sed ab instrumento cognitionis materialium et singularium in principium actualitatis, simultaneitatis et simplicitatis intellectualis amplificantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-02","text":"Universalitas functionem mutat: prius extensionem virtutis superioris ad plura, deinde unitatem obiecti sub specie, postremo fundamentum appetitus et libertatis significat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-03","text":"Simplicitas ab eminentiori continentia inferiorum ad actum sine successione transit, neque in identitatem potentiarum desinit, sed distinctionem intellectus et voluntatis compatitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-04","text":"Voluntas e campo obiecti clausi migrat in principium recti vel falsi iudicii, ac demum in potentiam appetitivam distinctam quae bonum universale respicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-05","text":"Motus et potentia vim imperfectivam amittunt: motus fit actus perfecti, potentia autem vel omissio considerationis vel receptivitas revelationis nondum datae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_51:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-06","text":"Distinctio matutini et vespertini, localiter expositiva, in structuram superiorem processionis a Verbo, cognitionis termini et reditus ad principium absorbetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D6","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-07","text":"Passio sensitiva ut proprietas angelica evanescit, sed vocabula affectuum redeunt functione mutata ad simplices actus voluntatis et conformitatem divinae regulae significandos.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_51:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-01","text":"Taxonomia futuri secundum causas necessarias, frequentes et fortuitas localis manet; ad gradum praesentem ascendit tantum ut exemplar dependentiae cognoscibilitatis a modo essendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A7","CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-02","text":"Expositio matutini et vespertini localiter distinctionem cognitionum interpretatur; hic autem duplicitas mediorum in circuitum processionis et reditus integratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-03","text":"Negatio irascibilis et concupiscibilis localiter psychologiam angelicam purgat; praesentis gradus structura ex ea regulam analogicae attributionis affectuum efficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A12","CH_GGVC_P_51:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-04","text":"Species innatae a mechanismo cognitionis obiecti amplificantur in architecturam quae actualitatem, pluralitatem et simultaneitatem totius cognitionis naturalis ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_50:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-05","text":"Libera voluntas unitates coniungit: ut actus interior cognitionem alterius claudit, ut inclinatio potentiam distinctam constituit, et ut regula iudicii veritatem supernaturalem ordinat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_51:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-06","text":"Transitus maior fit cum completudo intellectus naturalis per cognitionem boni universalis non in quietem, sed in productionem voluntatis et liberi arbitrii convertitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-07","text":"Oppositiones inferiores inter spiritum et materiam, actum et potentiam, determinationem et libertatem superantur per distinctiones modi praesentiae, ambitus et rationis formalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-01","text":"Cognitio angelica neque sensitiva neque imaginaria neque abstractiva est; materialia cognoscuntur per praesentiam intentionalem speciei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-02","text":"Simplicitas cognitionis angelicae discursum, acquisitionem ignoti, compositionem et divisionem tamquam vias necessarias cognitionis excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_50:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-03","text":"Excellentia intellectus creati nec omniscientiam nec situm aeternum ex quo omnia tempora simul praesentia sint constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-04","text":"Conversio veri et boni non permittit identitatem essentiae, intellectus et voluntatis in creatura, quia relationes formales potentiarum manent diversae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_51:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-05","text":"Libertas angelica neque ignorantia neque oscillatio neque deliberatio inquisitiva est, sed iudicium universale de bonis particularibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-06","text":"Vita appetitiva angelica non dividitur in irascibilem et concupiscibilem nec passionibus sensitivis constituitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A11","CH_GGVC_P_51:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-07","text":"Visio beatifica non est comprehensio exhaustiva nec possessio statica omnium secretorum, sed actualitas permanens revelationi ulteriori aperta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet perfectionem intellectualem creatam eo ipso omnem differentiam inter cognitionem naturalem, revelationem et omniscientiam abolere.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet multiplicitatem cogniti aequalem multiplicitatem vel successionem actus cognoscentis postulare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet convertibilitatem realem veri et boni rationes formales obiectivas atque distinctionem potentiarum evacuare.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:D4","CH_GGVC_P_51:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet ordinem specierum naturalium ad futura contingentia, actus liberos et secreta voluntatis divinae sine residuo extendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_49:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet creaturam intellectualem sibi ipsi principium sufficiens intelligibilitatis et bonum ultimum esse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSA-01","text":"Systema circa impossibilitatem situs creati ordinatur ex quo omnia tempora, omnes actus liberi interiores et omnia secreta divina simul pateant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSA-02","text":"Inadmissibilis est terminatio intellectus et voluntatis in creatura tamquam ultimo cognoscibili et appetibili; talis clausura noctem structuralem produceret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_50:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSA-03","text":"Abest possibilitas creaturae simul sui sufficientis et libere excentricae, quia intellectus suum lumen et voluntas suum bonum ultra essentiam propriam recipiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSA-04","text":"Ontologice inadmissibilis est visio creata quae essentiam divinam exhauriat et omne quod in sapientia divina latet necessario appropriet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-01","text":"Determinatio intellectus ad omne verum naturale et libertas voluntatis non sunt gradus unius indeterminationis: prima perficit receptionem veri, altera particularia sub bono universali eligit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-04","CL_GGVC_20:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_51:A10","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-02","text":"Opacitas actus liberi interioris non est defectus contingens cognitionis angelicae, sed effectus distinctionis inter cognoscere rem et appetitive se ad eam determinare.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-07","CL_GGVC_20:GA-08","CL_GGVC_20:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_51:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-03","text":"Error oritur cum voluntas iudicium naturale ultra ambitum specierum connaturalium ad ea extendit quae ex sola ordinatione divina determinantur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-06","CL_GGVC_20:GA-07","CL_GGVC_20:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_49:A10","CH_GGVC_P_50:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-04","text":"Una species angelica plura singularia sub uno intelligibili continere potest, sed simultaneitas omnium rerum sine distributione specierum soli cognitioni per Verbum convenit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-02","CL_GGVC_20:GA-03","CL_GGVC_20:GA-05","CL_GGVC_20:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-05","text":"Electio angelica est immediata sine esse immediata causaliter: non sequitur discursum, sed iudicium universale quo bonum particulare sub ratione boni apprehenditur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-04","CL_GGVC_20:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","CH_GGVC_P_51:A9","CH_GGVC_P_51:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-06","text":"Beatitudo angelica est actualitas stabilis sed non exhaustiva, quia visio Verbi revelationes ulteriores secundum gradus et officia recipere potest.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-06","CL_GGVC_20:GA-11","CL_GGVC_20:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-07","text":"Eadem res intellectui ut vera et voluntati ut bona adest, unde realis convertibilitas obiecti duas habitudines operativas non confundit.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-05","CL_GGVC_20:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","CH_GGVC_P_51:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-08","text":"Temporalitas angelica successionem conceptionum et novitatem revelationis admittit, quamvis successionem acquisitivam rationis et transitum ab ignoto ad notum excludat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-04","CL_GGVC_20:GA-06","CL_GGVC_20:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-01","text":"Ontologia intellectualis creata formam completudinis apertae producit: natura in proprio ambitu terminatur, sed supernaturali dono et bono infinito patet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-02","text":"Cognoscibilitas non gradu obiecti in abstracto, sed modo eius essendi et dependentiae mensuratur: actualitas, causalitas, libertas et voluntas divina diversos accessus constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-03","text":"Tempus angelicum est successio non discursiva: intellectus non ratiocinando progreditur, sed conceptiones et revelationes novas sine participatione aeternitatis recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_50:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-04","text":"Subiectum angelicum est excentricum: species eius a Deo derivantur, bonum eius essentiam excedit, et perfectio eius revelationem ulteriorem recipit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-05","text":"Defectus moralis reclassificatur ut error magnitudinis et competentiae, quo iudicium naturale a regula divina separatum in campum supernaturalem indebite extenditur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-06","text":"Hierarchia non est sola inaequalitas perfectionis, sed distributio cognitionis, revelationis et officii quae administrationem sinit sine translatione omniscientiae ad administratores creatos.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-07","text":"Methodus systematis est purgatio analogica: vocabula humana non removentur simpliciter, sed secundum obiectum, medium et modum operationis disiunguntur atque restituuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-01","text":"Circuitus principalis est: eminentior continentia inferiorum → cognitio boni universalis → voluntas → iudicium de particularibus → nova determinatio limitum cognoscitivorum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_51:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-02","text":"Via amplificationis progreditur ab unitate virtutis ad pluralitatem simpliciter contentam, inde ad iudicium universale quod sine discursu actionem elicit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_51:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-03","text":"Circuitus erroris est: perfectio naturalis → abstractio iudicii a sapientia divina → extensio ultra competentiam → falsitas supernaturalis → necessitas subordinationis voluntatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_50:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-04","text":"Revelatio spiraliter auget cognitionem: receptivitas permanet, mysterium secundum hierarchiam communicatur, officium novum cognitionem exigit, sed comprehensio divina numquam consequitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-05","text":"Circuitus processionis et reditus creaturam a cognitione rerum in Verbo ad cognitionem proprii esse ducit, deinde terminum cognitum ad Deum ut principium refert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_50:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-06","text":"Attractor dominantissimus est perfectio limitata: systema simul naturalem plenitudinem tuetur et omnem conversionem eius in autonomiam vel omniscientiam impedit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-07","text":"Ratio formalis obiecti est attractor classificatorius: ad eam redeunt unitas actus, distinctio mediorum, separatio potentiarum atque compatibilitas determinationis et libertatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B01","text":"Ordo entium + modus recipientis → inferiora eminenter et intentionaliter in intellectu angelico continentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B02","text":"Continentia eminens → species connaturales formas et principia individuationis repraesentantes → cognitio materialium et singularium.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B03","text":"Species actu praesentes + lumen perfectum → consequentiae in principiis visae → actus simplex sine acquisitione discursiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B04","text":"Cognitio universalis rationis boni → appetitus intellectualis proportionatus → voluntas distincta → liberum iudicium de particularibus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A4","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B05","text":"Nondum-esse, actus liber interior et pura voluntas divina → indisponibilitas naturali speciei → terminus cognitionis creatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_49:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B06","text":"Iudicium naturale sub regula divina → veritas intra ambitum; subtractio voluntaria ab ordine divino → extensio illegitima → error.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_50:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B07","text":"Verbum ut principium et medium → revelatio graduata → cognitio creaturae et officium → reditus termini ad principium sine comprehensione exhaustiva.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AFM-B01","text":"Continentia eminens inferiorum → impressio specierum connaturalium → cognitio singularium → actus intellectus simplex → apprehensio boni universalis → voluntas → libertas immediata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AFM-B02","text":"Perfectio naturalis → determinatio ambitus → occursus futuri contingentis, actus liberi et mysterii → clausura cognitionis naturalis → receptivitas revelationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AFM-B03","text":"Processio rei a Verbo → cognitio in medio creato → inclinatio voluntatis ad bonum excedens → subordinatio vel deordinatio iudicii → reditus ad principium vel falsitas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-01","text":"Oppositio materiae et intellectus transfertur in quaestionem de modo praesentiae intentionalis, unde materialitas obiecti per se non impedit intellectionem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-02","text":"Oppositiones universalis et singularis atque unius et multorum reformantur per distinctionem inter abstractionem humanam et unitatem formalem speciei angelicae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_50:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-03","text":"Oppositio perfectionis et limitationis dissolvitur: completudo naturalis et indigentia supernaturalis partes unius status creati fiunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-04","text":"Oppositio necessitatis cognitivae et libertatis moralis corruit, quia determinatio ad verum et apertura ad particularia bona axes formales diversos occupant.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_51:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-05","text":"Interioritas reclassificatur non ut mera invisibilitas, sed ut actus actualis cuius determinatio a voluntate libera dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-06","text":"Falsitas separatur ab ignorantia naturali et ad actum voluntatis qui competentiam iudicii transgreditur refertur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-07","text":"Simplicitas angelica non amplius identitatem omnium principiorum significat, sed operationem non discursivam quae pluralitatem realem potentiarum compatitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_51:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-08","text":"Vocabula temporalia matutini et vespertini in tabulam ontologicam principii, processionis, termini et reditus transformantur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei distribuit cognitionem angelicam secundum obiecta, modos actus et potentias: materialia, futura, secreta, simultaneitatem, veritatem, voluntatem et libertatem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis species intelligibiles, rationes formales, media cognitionis et inclinationes appetitivas tamquam mechanismos distributionis instituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus certamen interpretationis circa competentiam constituit: praedicata humana purgantur, ambitus naturales servantur, et extensiones indebitae reprimuntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis creaturam ut ens non aeternum, successionem conceptionum patiens, sed discursu carens et ad bonum extra se ordinatum constituit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus ipsam doctrinam per negationem modorum humanorum efficit: terminos non delet, sed analogice distinguit donec nova architectura intellectus et voluntatis appareat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT10","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-01","text":"Cognitio singularis a repraesentatione principiorum individuantium pendet, sed mechanismus huius repraesentationis intra materiam praesentem assertus potius quam explicatus manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-02","text":"Completudo actualis naturalis et facultas naturalia non actu considerandi distinctione potentiarum conciliantur, sed relatio inter possessionem speciei et suspensionem actus compressionem retinet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-03","text":"Libertas ex iudicio universali derivatur, sed transitus ab apprehensione immediata boni ad electionem non deliberativam mediationem causaliter incompletam relinquit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-04","text":"Voluntas falsum iudicium supernaturalem efficere dicitur, sed modus quo inclinatio appetitiva actum intellectus deordinat non plene explicatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-05","text":"Cognitio per Verbum et cognitio per species innatas simul manent, sed necessitas functionalis duplicis medii ultra distinctionem eorum non demonstratur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-06","text":"Vocabulo generali angeli utitur systema, sed visio beatifica, rectitudo et error partitionem inter beatos, bonos et daemones requirunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-07","text":"Structura processionis et reditus argumentum ordinat, sed sua forma matutina et vespertina ab exegesi Augustiniana hic assumpta dependet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MP-01","text":"Universalitas mutatur ab amplitudine repraesentativa intellectus in rationem formalem boni quae appetitum et libertatem generat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MP-02","text":"Voluntas mutatur ab obiecto alteri intellectui clauso in regulam iudicii, deinde in potentiam constitutivam ipsius subiecti angelici.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MP-03","text":"Simplicitas mutatur ab unitate actus sine successione in structuram quae pluralitatem realem intellectus et voluntatis non excludit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MP-04","text":"Perfectio mutatur ab apparentia superioritatis absolutae in completudinem localem quae ordinationem ad bonum infinitum et revelationem servat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite apparet ut machina hierarchica translationis, in qua inferiora per species continentur, potentiae per rationes formales distribuuntur, et Verbum unitatem ultimam praestat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum angelicum est nodus luminosus sed excentricus: naturaliter completus, realiter pluripotens et ad bonum extra essentiam suam inclinatus.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:HSI-03","text":"Tempus huius machinae est successio discreta conceptionum et revelationum, non fluxus ratiocinativus neque simultaneitas aeternitatis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio possibilis est custodia ambitus: intellectus terminos naturalis cognitionis servat, voluntas se regulae divinae conformans cognitionem creaturae ad principium reducit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata de modo recipientis, speciebus connaturalibus, rationibus formalibus, completudine limitata et appetitu universalis boni sufficiunt ad structuram cognitionis et voluntatis angelicae restituendam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B02","text":"Minus determinata manent repraesentatio singularitatis, causalitas voluntatis in iudicium et necessitas simultaneae operationis duplicis medii cognoscendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B03","text":"Cohaerentia firmissima est ubi distinctiones ambitus, medii, modi operationis et obiecti formalis impediunt ne superioritas angelica in omniscientiam vel libertas in indeterminationem convertatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B04","text":"Restitutio principiis antecedentibus, partitione ordinum angelorum et exegesi matutini atque vespertini partim nititur; haec dependentiae limites autonomiae huius gregis constituunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B05","text":"Motus verus servatur ut amplificatio cognitionis naturalis, restrictio per contingentiam et libertatem, generatio voluntatis, apertura revelationis et reditus analogicus ad principium; irreducibilis manet necessitas sermonis analogici.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT10","CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T172006989149Z_fb40f2c6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 58–60","source_sha256":"56810b6772383bea8180ec53f05aa461a284a79342c28e58b7cc7d0e926acb92","sha256":"5553a532418b5d34423a8d6789f2cd4ec395a949a52e815ecfb2e71f44b74010","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T17:20:06.990079+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-01","text":"The system asks how angelic nature possesses cognition, intellectual operation, and will without created intellect being confused with divine intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-02","text":"The global thesis is that an angel is completely perfected within the natural sphere by connatural species, yet by this perfection attains neither omniscience nor supernatural sufficiency nor autonomy.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-03","text":"The argument proceeds from the order of beings and the mode of the recipient to the form of the intellectual act, then derives intellectual appetite and freedom from the universality of what is known.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-04","text":"The movement of the system is recursive and spiral: universal cognition generates will, while will in turn determines the limits of cognition, the possibility of error, and the need for divine ordering.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_51:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-05","text":"The multiplicity of things, operations, and powers is ordered not through aggregation, but through the unity of the species, the formal notion of the object, and the medium of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","CH_GGVC_P_50:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-06","text":"The limits of angelic cognition are not mere privations, but positive boundaries by which the contingent future, interior freedom, and divine secrecy are separated from natural intelligibility.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-07","text":"The vision of the Word does not evacuate natural perfection, but inserts it into non-comprehensive beatific cognition, graded revelation, and hierarchical office.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AS-08","text":"The closure of this level is not a static termination, but a form of created perfection that remains naturally complete, supernaturally open, and ordered toward a good exceeding itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every cognitive and appetitive reception is determined according to the mode of the recipient, not according to the bare material condition of the object.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A2","CH_GGVC_P_51:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Angelic intellect is completed within the natural order by connatural intelligible species and does not acquire cognition by abstracting from sensibles.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Universality progresses from the more eminent representation of many things, through the formal unity of the intelligible, to the apprehension of the universal notion of the good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Angelic intellectual perfection immediately contains consequences in principles and predicates in quiddities, and therefore excludes acquisitive discourse and operative composition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A11","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] The unity of act, distinction of powers, and diversity of cognitions depend upon the formal notion of the object and the medium of knowing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Created perfection is completeness relative to the sphere of nature, not plenitude exhausting every intelligible or appetible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] What does not yet have its own being, what depends on a free act, or what proceeds from the pure will of God, is not necessarily manifest to natural angelic cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_49:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Will first constitutes a boundary of natural cognition, then orders or disorders natural judgment, and finally is unfolded as the intellectual appetite for the universal good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] The determination of intellect toward natural truth is compatible with freedom of will, because cognition of truth and choice of a particular good are measured by different formal notions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A10","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] In an intellectual creature, essence, intellect, and will are really distinct; their identity belongs to God alone.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] The Word is the principle of intelligibility, the unifying medium of beatific cognition, and the term of the return of creaturely cognition to its cause.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] The angelic subject is constituted as naturally perfect, supernaturally receptive, and appetitively ordered toward a good exceeding its own essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D1","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-01","text":"Connatural species preserve structural identity, but are amplified from an instrument for cognizing material and singular things into a principle of intellectual actuality, simultaneity, and simplicity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-02","text":"Universality changes function: first it signifies the extension of a higher power to many things, then the unity of the object under the species, and finally the foundation of appetite and freedom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-03","text":"Simplicity passes from the more eminent containment of lower things to an act without succession, and does not end in the identity of powers, but is compatible with the distinction of intellect and will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-04","text":"Will migrates from the domain of an object closed to another intellect into a principle of correct or false judgment, and finally into a distinct appetitive power directed toward the universal good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-05","text":"Motion and potency lose their imperfective force: motion becomes the act of the perfect, while potency becomes either the omission of consideration or receptivity to revelation not yet given.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_51:NX3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-06","text":"The distinction between morning and evening, locally exegetical, is absorbed into the higher structure of procession from the Word, cognition of the term, and return to the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D6","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RMD-07","text":"Sensitive passion disappears as an angelic property, but the vocabulary of affections returns with a changed function, signifying simple acts of will and conformity to the divine rule.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_51:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-01","text":"The taxonomy of the future according to necessary, frequent, and fortuitous causes remains local; it rises to the present level only as a model of the dependence of cognoscibility on the mode of being.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A7","CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-02","text":"The exposition of morning and evening locally interprets the distinction of cognitions; here, however, the duality of media is integrated into the circuit of procession and return.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-03","text":"The negation of the irascible and concupiscible locally purifies angelic psychology; the structure of the present level makes from it a rule for the analogical attribution of affections.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A12","CH_GGVC_P_51:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-04","text":"Innate species are amplified from a mechanism for cognizing the object into an architecture ordering the actuality, plurality, and simultaneity of all natural cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_50:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-05","text":"Free will joins the unities: as an interior act it closes off another's cognition, as an inclination it constitutes a distinct power, and as a rule of judgment it orders supernatural truth.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_51:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-06","text":"The major transition occurs when the completeness of natural intellect, through cognition of the universal good, is converted not into rest but into the production of will and free choice.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A2","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:CGD-07","text":"Lower oppositions between spirit and matter, act and potency, determination and freedom are overcome through distinctions of mode of presence, sphere, and formal notion.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-01","text":"Angelic cognition is neither sensitive nor imaginative nor abstractive; material things are known through the intentional presence of the species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-02","text":"The simplicity of angelic cognition excludes discourse, acquisition of the unknown, composition, and division as necessary ways of cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_50:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-03","text":"The excellence of created intellect constitutes neither omniscience nor an eternal standpoint from which all times are simultaneously present.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-04","text":"The conversion of truth and good does not permit the identity of essence, intellect, and will in a creature, because the formal relations of the powers remain diverse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_51:NX5","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-05","text":"Angelic freedom is neither ignorance nor oscillation nor deliberative inquiry, but universal judgment concerning particular goods.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:NX6","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-06","text":"Angelic appetitive life is not divided into irascible and concupiscible powers, nor is it constituted by sensitive passions.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A11","CH_GGVC_P_51:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:GNX-07","text":"Beatific vision is not exhaustive comprehension or static possession of all secrets, but a permanent actuality open to further revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that created intellectual perfection thereby abolishes every difference between natural cognition, revelation, and omniscience.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that the multiplicity of what is known requires an equal multiplicity or succession in the act of knowing.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that the real convertibility of truth and good evacuates objective formal notions and the distinction of powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:D4","CH_GGVC_P_51:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that the order of natural species extends without remainder to contingent futures, free acts, and the secrets of the divine will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_49:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that an intellectual creature is for itself the sufficient principle of intelligibility and the ultimate good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSA-01","text":"The system is ordered around the impossibility of a created standpoint from which all times, all interior free acts, and all divine secrets are simultaneously manifest.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSA-02","text":"The termination of intellect and will in the creature as the ultimate knowable and appetible is inadmissible; such closure would produce structural night.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX4","CH_GGVC_P_50:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSA-03","text":"The possibility of a creature both sufficient to itself and freely eccentric is absent, because intellect receives its light and will its good beyond its own essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSA-04","text":"A created vision that exhausts the divine essence and necessarily appropriates everything hidden in divine wisdom is ontologically inadmissible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-01","text":"The determination of intellect toward every natural truth and freedom of will are not degrees of one indetermination: the former perfects the reception of truth, the latter chooses particulars under the good universal.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-04","CL_GGVC_20:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_51:A10","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-02","text":"The opacity of an interior free act is not a contingent defect of angelic cognition, but the effect of the distinction between knowing a thing and appetitively determining oneself toward it.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-07","CL_GGVC_20:GA-08","CL_GGVC_20:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_51:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-03","text":"Error arises when will extends natural judgment beyond the scope of connatural species to things determined by divine ordering alone.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-06","CL_GGVC_20:GA-07","CL_GGVC_20:GA-08","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_49:A10","CH_GGVC_P_50:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-04","text":"One angelic species can contain several singulars under one intelligible, but the simultaneity of all things without distribution among species belongs to cognition through the Word alone.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-02","CL_GGVC_20:GA-03","CL_GGVC_20:GA-05","CL_GGVC_20:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A5","CH_GGVC_P_50:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-05","text":"Angelic choice is immediate without being causally immediate: it does not follow discourse, but the universal judgment by which a particular good is apprehended under the notion of good.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-04","CL_GGVC_20:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","CH_GGVC_P_51:A9","CH_GGVC_P_51:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-06","text":"Angelic beatitude is stable but non-exhaustive actuality, because the vision of the Word can receive further revelations according to grades and offices.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-06","CL_GGVC_20:GA-11","CL_GGVC_20:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_49:A11","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-07","text":"The same thing is present to intellect as true and to will as good, whence the real convertibility of the object does not confuse two operative relations.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-05","CL_GGVC_20:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","CH_GGVC_P_51:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:XD-08","text":"Angelic temporality admits succession of conceptions and novelty of revelation, although it excludes the acquisitive succession of reason and transition from the unknown to the known.","refs":["CL_GGVC_20:GA-04","CL_GGVC_20:GA-06","CL_GGVC_20:GA-12","CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-01","text":"Created intellectual ontology produces a form of open completeness: nature is terminated within its own sphere, but open to supernatural gift and infinite good.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-02","text":"Cognoscibility is measured not by the grade of the object in the abstract, but by its mode of being and dependence: actuality, causality, freedom, and divine will constitute diverse accesses.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-03","text":"Angelic time is non-discursive succession: intellect does not progress by reasoning, but receives new conceptions and revelations without participation in eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_50:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-04","text":"The angelic subject is eccentric: its species are derived from God, its good exceeds its essence, and its perfection receives further revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-05","text":"Moral defect is reclassified as an error of magnitude and competence, whereby natural judgment, separated from the divine rule, is improperly extended into the supernatural domain.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-06","text":"Hierarchy is not merely inequality of perfection, but a distribution of cognition, revelation, and office that permits administration without transferring omniscience to created administrators.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:BSD-07","text":"The method of the system is analogical purification: human terms are not simply removed, but are differentiated and restored according to object, medium, and mode of operation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-01","text":"The principal circuit is: more eminent containment of lower things → cognition of the universal good → will → judgment concerning particulars → new determination of cognitive limits.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_51:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-02","text":"The path of amplification proceeds from unity of power to plurality simply contained, and thence to universal judgment that elicits action without discourse.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_51:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-03","text":"The circuit of error is: natural perfection → abstraction of judgment from divine wisdom → extension beyond competence → supernatural falsity → necessity of the subordination of will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_50:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-04","text":"Revelation spirally increases cognition: receptivity remains, mystery is communicated according to hierarchy, new office requires cognition, but divine comprehension is never attained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_49:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-05","text":"The circuit of procession and return leads the creature from cognition of things in the Word to cognition of its own being, then refers the known term to God as principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_50:NX10","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-06","text":"The dominant attractor is limited perfection: the system simultaneously maintains natural plenitude and prevents every conversion of it into autonomy or omniscience.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:RLE-07","text":"The formal notion of the object is a classificatory attractor: to it return the unity of act, distinction of media, separation of powers, and compatibility of determination and freedom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A5","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7","CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B01","text":"Order of beings + mode of recipient → lower things are contained eminently and intentionally in angelic intellect.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B02","text":"Eminent containment → connatural species representing forms and principles of individuation → cognition of material and singular things.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_49:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B03","text":"Species actually present + perfect light → consequences seen in principles → simple act without discursive acquisition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B04","text":"Cognition of the universal notion of good → proportionate intellectual appetite → distinct will → free judgment concerning particulars.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:A4","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B05","text":"Not-yet-being, interior free act, and pure divine will → unavailability to natural species → boundary of created cognition.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS4","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_49:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B06","text":"Natural judgment under divine rule → truth within the sphere; voluntary withdrawal from divine order → illegitimate extension → error.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_50:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FGS-B07","text":"The Word as principle and medium → graded revelation → creaturely cognition and office → return of the term to the principle without exhaustive comprehension.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","CH_GGVC_P_49:A12","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AFM-B01","text":"Eminent containment of lower things → impression of connatural species → cognition of singulars → simple act of intellect → apprehension of the universal good → will → immediate freedom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_50:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_51:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AFM-B02","text":"Natural perfection → determination of the sphere → encounter with contingent future, free act, and mystery → closure of natural cognition → receptivity to revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_49:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:AFM-B03","text":"Procession of the thing from the Word → cognition in a created medium → inclination of will toward the exceeding good → subordination or disordering of judgment → return to the principle or falsity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:A15","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-01","text":"The opposition of matter and intellect is transferred into the question of the mode of intentional presence, whence the materiality of the object does not in itself impede intellection.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-02","text":"The oppositions of universal and singular, and of one and many, are reformed through the distinction between human abstraction and the formal unity of angelic species.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_50:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-03","text":"The opposition of perfection and limitation is dissolved: natural completeness and supernatural need become parts of one created state.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-04","text":"The opposition of cognitive necessity and moral freedom collapses, because determination toward truth and openness to particular goods occupy diverse formal axes.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_51:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-05","text":"Interiority is reclassified not as mere invisibility, but as an actual act whose determination depends upon free will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_49:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-06","text":"Falsity is separated from natural ignorance and referred to an act of will that exceeds the competence of judgment.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-07","text":"Angelic simplicity no longer signifies the identity of all principles, but non-discursive operation compatible with the real plurality of powers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_51:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MME-08","text":"The temporal terms of morning and evening are transformed into an ontological table of principle, procession, term, and return.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:ME5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level distributes angelic cognition according to objects, modes of act, and powers: material things, futures, secrets, simultaneity, truth, will, and freedom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT1","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level establishes intelligible species, formal notions, media of cognition, and appetitive inclinations as mechanisms of distribution.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level constitutes an interpretive contest concerning competence: human predicates are purified, natural spheres are preserved, and improper extensions are repressed.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level constitutes the creature as a non-eternal being, subject to succession of conceptions, yet lacking discourse and ordered toward a good outside itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_50:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level effects doctrine itself through the negation of human modes: it does not delete terms, but analogically distinguishes them until a new architecture of intellect and will appears.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT10","CH_GGVC_P_51:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-01","text":"Singular cognition depends upon the representation of individuating principles, but the mechanism of this representation in present matter remains asserted rather than explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-02","text":"Actual natural completeness and the capacity not actually to consider natural things are reconciled by the distinction of powers, but the relation between possession of the species and suspension of act retains compression.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-03","text":"Freedom is derived from universal judgment, but the transition from immediate apprehension of the good to non-deliberative choice leaves causally incomplete mediation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_51:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-04","text":"Will is said to effect false supernatural judgment, but the mode by which appetitive inclination disorders the act of intellect is not fully explained.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-05","text":"Cognition through the Word and cognition through innate species remain together, but the functional necessity of the double medium beyond their distinction is not demonstrated.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-06","text":"The system uses the general term angel, but beatific vision, rectitude, and error require a partition among the blessed, the good, and demons.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:FL-07","text":"The structure of procession and return orders the argument, but its form of morning and evening depends upon Augustinian exegesis assumed here.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MP-01","text":"Universality changes from the representative scope of intellect into the formal notion of good that generates appetite and freedom.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A6","CH_GGVC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MP-02","text":"Will changes from an object closed to another intellect into a rule of judgment, then into a power constitutive of the angelic subject itself.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A9","CH_GGVC_P_50:A14","CH_GGVC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MP-03","text":"Simplicity changes from unity of act without succession into a structure that does not exclude the real plurality of intellect and will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MP-04","text":"Perfection changes from the appearance of absolute superiority into local completeness that preserves ordering toward infinite good and revelation.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as a hierarchical machine of translation, in which lower things are contained through species, powers are distributed through formal notions, and the Word supplies ultimate unity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A1","CH_GGVC_P_50:A7","CH_GGVC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:HSI-02","text":"The angelic subject is a luminous but eccentric node: naturally complete, really endowed with multiple powers, and inclined toward a good beyond its essence.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D1","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:HSI-03","text":"The time of this machine is a discrete succession of conceptions and revelations, not a reasoning flow nor the simultaneity of eternity.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:A8","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:HSI-04","text":"Navigation is possible through safeguarding the sphere: intellect preserves the boundaries of natural cognition, while will, conforming itself to the divine rule, returns creaturely cognition to the principle.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:D5","CH_GGVC_P_50:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_51:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B01","text":"Axioms concerning the mode of the recipient, connatural species, formal notions, limited completeness, and appetite for the universal good suffice to reconstruct the structure of angelic cognition and will.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT1","CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B02","text":"The representation of singularity, the causality of will upon judgment, and the necessity of the simultaneous operation of the double cognitive medium remain less determined.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT4","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT7","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B03","text":"Coherence is strongest where distinctions of sphere, medium, mode of operation, and formal object prevent angelic superiority from being converted into omniscience or freedom into indetermination.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT3","CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B04","text":"The reconstruction partly relies on antecedent principles, the partition of orders of angels, and the exegesis of morning and evening; these dependencies constitute the limits of the autonomy of this cluster.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT2","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_20:MRT-B05","text":"The true movement is preserved as amplification of natural cognition, restriction through contingency and freedom, generation of will, openness to revelation, and analogical return to the principle; the necessity of analogical discourse remains irreducible.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_49:MRT6","CH_GGVC_P_50:MRT10","CH_GGVC_P_51:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_GGVC_20@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_GGVC_20:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","title":"Chapters 58–60","context":"Prima pars · Quaestio 57 · Prima pars · Quaestio 58 · Prima pars · Quaestio 59"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 61–63","order":21,"parents":["CH_GGVC_P_52","CH_GGVC_P_53","CH_GGVC_P_54"],"revision":"CL_GGVC_21@R001","sha256":"6a7df5a8e9de76babf04a0f6dd1505c14d9e171fd7c41decd112f5e156a96925","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo natura angelica creata simul inclinationem naturalem, libertatem electivam et transitum supernaturalem ad terminum beatificum recipiat sine confusione ordinum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_54:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis angelum constituit ut ens participatum cuius dependentia a Deo naturalem ordinem amoris fundat, gratia facultatem creatam elevat, et visio divina motum essentialem claudit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","CH_GGVC_P_54:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio per distinctiones coordinatas procedit: essentia ab esse, dilectio naturalis ab electiva, bonum universale a bono beatificante, et natura a gratia atque gloria separantur ut deinde ordinentur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_52:AS6","CH_GGVC_P_54:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BAS-04","text":"Motus a causalitate creationis ad ordinem universi, ab ordine ad dilectionem Dei, et a dilectione naturali ad conversionem meritoriam atque visionem terminalem ascendit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:D1","CH_GGVC_P_52:D7","CH_GGVC_P_54:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BAS-05","text":"Progressus est cumulativus et spiralis, quia eadem dependentia creaturae recurrit ut participatio essendi, ordinatio appetitiva et receptivitas beatifica, singulis reditibus functione amplificata.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_52:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_54:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BAS-06","text":"Elevatio numquam principium inferius delet: natura permanet in intellectu, electione, gratia et gloria tamquam capacitas receptiva successive perfecta.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BAS-07","text":"Libertas mutatur ab electione particularium sub fine naturali ad conversionem meritoriam sub gratia, deinde ad electionem indefectibilem intra finem visum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est essentialis sed non operationaliter vacua: meritum et augmentum substantiale finiuntur, dum fruitio, ministerium et augmentum accidentale permanent.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Omne angelicum esse est participatum, ideo neque immaterialitas neque subsistentia angelum a causalitate creatrice eximit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A1","CH_GGVC_P_53:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Natura manet principium receptivum et operativum per omnes amplificationes intellectus, voluntatis, gratiae et gloriae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-03","text":"[Emergent] Bonum proprium angeli continetur intra bonum totius, unde ordo cosmicus, dilectio supra seipsum et distributio perfectionum eadem structura participationis reguntur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_52:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_53:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Dilectio est radix omnis appetitus, sed ab inclinatione naturali ad Deum ut bonum universale in caritatem, meritum et fruitionem supernaturalem mutatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A1","CH_GGVC_P_52:D7","CH_GGVC_P_54:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Electio ordinat particularia sub fine recepto; ubi finis facultatem naturae excedit, gratia novam motionem praebet sine abolitione actus liberi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A7","CH_GGVC_P_54:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Actio divina naturam intellectualem secundum modum eius liberum perficit, non secundum necessitatem quae operationem recipientis evacuet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A7","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Contingentia creationis et gratuititas gloriae ab eadem libertate divina pendent, quamvis sapientia divina utrumque donum ordini naturarum congruenter distribuat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Temporalitas angelica complectitur initium creatum et successionem actuum sine corruptione naturae aut mensura motus corporei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Visio divina voluntatem non immobilitate passiva, sed electione indefectibili sub ordine finis perficit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","CH_GGVC_P_54:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Adeptio finis claudit meritum et progressum essentialem, non autem fruitionem, operationem naturalem aut diffusionem perfectionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Deus ordinat totam structuram ut causa essendi, bonum universale naturaliter dilectum et essentia supernaturaliter visa, semper tamen incomprehensibilis creaturae finitae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","CH_GGVC_P_54:A16","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] Gradus naturae, conversionis, gratiae et gloriae coordinantur hierarchice sine eo quod natura donum supernaturale efficiat vel sibi debitum reddat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:AS5","CH_GGVC_P_54:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RMD-01","text":"Natura identitatem retinet ut principium creatum, sed functionem mutat ab inclinatione voluntaria ad capacitatem incorruptibilem et demum ad subiectum in gloria servatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A2","CH_GGVC_P_53:A7","CH_GGVC_P_54:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RMD-02","text":"Deus redit functionaliter ut causa producens, bonum universale et obiectum beatificum; haec non sunt nomina parallela, sed gradus causalitatis, appetibilitatis et praesentiae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A1","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","CH_GGVC_P_54:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RMD-03","text":"Relatio partis ad totum migrat ex cosmologia originis in ordinem amoris et inde in providentiam graduum, ita ut totalitas fiat regula creationis, inclinationis et consummationis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RMD-04","text":"Dilectio naturalis non evanescit adventu caritatis: mutatur ex radice finis in actum meritorium, deinde in fruitionem et diffusionem perfectionis possessae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A15","CH_GGVC_P_54:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RMD-05","text":"Libertas redit cum variatione: primo sine discursu eligit, deinde sub gratia convertitur, postremo intra finem visum indefectibiliter operatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A8","CH_GGVC_P_54:A7","CH_GGVC_P_54:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RMD-06","text":"Tempus transit ab exclusione aeternitatis ad successionem actuum et tandem ad clausuram futuri essentialis, sine reductione ad motum corporalem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:NX4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A12","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RMD-07","text":"Locus corporeus, opere significationis peracto, ut principium ontologicum evanescit et in ordinem praesidentiae spiritus erga corpus absorbetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:CGD-01","text":"Differentia inter unitatem numericam et specificam manet mechanismus localis dilectionis inter angelos; hoc gradu tantum quatenus capacitatem et intensitatem secundum ordinem receptivum explicat persistit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:D5","CH_GGVC_P_54:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:CGD-02","text":"Caelum Empyreum manet determinatio localis et probabilis; synthesis retinet solam reclassificationem loci in signum potestatis gubernativae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:D6","CH_GGVC_P_53:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:CGD-03","text":"Simultaneitas creationis angelicae et corporeae non ascendit ad axioma necessarium, sed rationem localem praebet cur perfectio partis per ordinem totius interpretetur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:NX7","CH_GGVC_P_53:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:CGD-04","text":"Creatio angelorum in gratia manet conclusio probabilior; ad gradum praesentem amplificatur tantum ut nexus inter originem creatam et facultatem primi actus meritorii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D3","CH_GGVC_P_54:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:CGD-05","text":"Distinctio essentiae et esse transcendit quaestionem originis, quia dependentiam ontologicam in ordinem amoris et indigentiam gratiae propagat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_52:SD1","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:CGD-06","text":"Series naturae, electionis et gratiae, localiter actus voluntatis distinguens, fit hoc gradu schema coniungens inclinationem, meritum et gloriam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_54:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GNX-01","text":"Immaterialitas, subsistentia et incorruptibilitas non significant esse a se, aeternitatem aut sufficientiam ad beatitudinem.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:NX1","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GNX-02","text":"Natura neque irrationalitati opponitur neque sola finem supernaturalem producit; est principium rectum sed finite proportionatum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX1","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GNX-03","text":"Libertas non constituitur discursu necessario, indifferentia absoluta aut potestate mali eligendi.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX5","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GNX-04","text":"Gratia neque naturam substituit neque ex proportione naturali debitum vel causatum donum fit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:NX11","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GNX-05","text":"Conservatio sui non est terminus absolutus, quia dilectio creaturae ordinatur ad bonum universale cuius ipsa pars est.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:GNX-06","text":"Clausura beatifica non est evacuatio operationis naturalis neque inertia, sed exclusio novi meriti essentialis cum permanentia fruitionis et ministerii.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:NX8","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet excellentiam creatam gradatim in modum divinum transire posse, quia etiam visio vera nec esse a se nec comprehensionem Dei confert.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet universum aggregationem substantiarum separatarum esse; aliter causalitas, amor et gloria non possent per ordinem partium coordinari.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_53:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet actum creatum aut autonomum aut mere passivum esse, quia inclinatio indita et gratia movens operationem propriam recipientis exigunt.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:NX2","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet omnem successionem motu corporis mensurari aut omne incorruptibile esse sine initio.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet finem ultimum indefinite mobiliter superari posse, quia talis progressus rationem termini et fruitionis destrueret.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX8","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSA-01","text":"Systema excludit creaturam quae sibi causa, mensura boni et principium beatificationis sit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:SNX1","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSA-02","text":"Nullus status neutralis extra ordinem divinum admittitur: angelus velut pars causata, naturaliter inclinata et supernaturaliter ordinabilis semper intra totalitatem manet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:SNX2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSA-03","text":"Possibilitas tacite vetita est aequalitas creaturae cum Deo, sive per autonomiam essendi, sive per appetitum ascensus, sive per comprehensionem visionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:NX9","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSA-04","text":"In termino beatifico indisponibile fit futurum essentiale quo comprehensor ad statum viae redeat aut finem possessum transcendat.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX3","CH_GGVC_P_54:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:XD-01","text":"Primatus naturalis dilectionis Dei non est lex extrinseca voluntati imposita, sed translatio dependentiae essendi in ordinem appetitus.","refs":["CL_GGVC_21:GA-01","CL_GGVC_21:GA-04","CL_GGVC_21:GA-11","CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","CH_GGVC_P_52:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:XD-02","text":"Rectitudo inclinationis naturalis est donata simul cum natura creata; ideo neque a subjecto sibi sufficiente oritur neque culpam electionis deformis causat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_21:GA-01","CL_GGVC_21:GA-02","CL_GGVC_21:GA-05","CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_52:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:XD-03","text":"Elevatio supernaturalis intensificat structuram partis ad totum: quod naturaliter ordinatur ad bonum universale per gratiam ordinatur ad immediatam eius visionem.","refs":["CL_GGVC_21:GA-03","CL_GGVC_21:GA-04","CL_GGVC_21:GA-06","CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_52:A13","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:XD-04","text":"Libertas divina et libertas angelica non sunt symmetricae: prima constituit contingentem campum essendi et finis, secunda intra naturam et motionem receptas operatur.","refs":["CL_GGVC_21:GA-05","CL_GGVC_21:GA-06","CL_GGVC_21:GA-07","CH_GGVC_P_53:A6","CH_GGVC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:XD-05","text":"Incorruptibilitas conservat subjectum operationis, sed sola visio bonitatis per essentiam eius voluntatem indefectibiliter ordinat.","refs":["CL_GGVC_21:GA-08","CL_GGVC_21:GA-09","CH_GGVC_P_53:D4","CH_GGVC_P_54:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:XD-06","text":"Historia angelica est finita sine temporalitate corporali: initium creatum, successio minima actuum et terminus irreversibilis constituunt eius mensuram.","refs":["CL_GGVC_21:GA-08","CL_GGVC_21:GA-10","CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_54:A12","CH_GGVC_P_54:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSD-01","text":"Dependentia ontologica in agentia interna convertitur: esse receptum naturalem appetitum generat, et appetitus elevatus in praesentia causae suae consummatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","CH_GGVC_P_52:A1","CH_GGVC_P_54:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSD-02","text":"Perfectio agentiae non crescit per multiplicationem alternativarum, sed per certiorem ordinationem electionum ad finem verum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A17","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSD-03","text":"Historia creata habet formam asymmetricae trajectoriae: donum originis non est praemium, via meritoria non est terminus, et terminus non redit ad viam.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A5","CH_GGVC_P_54:SD3","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSD-04","text":"Hierarchia fit coordinatio gratuita capacitatum et donorum, non effectus autonomus naturae neque distributio ordinis expers.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:SD4","CH_GGVC_P_54:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:BSD-05","text":"Modus cognitionis statum voluntatis mutat: cognitio per rationes particulares discordiam admittit, sed praesentia essentiae bonitatis ordinem electionis terminaliter figit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:D10","CH_GGVC_P_54:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RLE-01","text":"Participatio essendi → dependentia a bono universali → dilectio Dei → motio gratiae → visio → voluntas confirmata → diffusio ordinis recepti.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RLE-02","text":"Natura → inclinatio → electio → conversio → fruitio constituit viam amplificationis in qua quod prius principium receptivum erat in quolibet gradu servatur et perficitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:SD2","CH_GGVC_P_54:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RLE-03","text":"Apparens contradictio → distinctio rationum formalium → conservatio utriusque ordinis → subordinatio in structuram ampliorem est circuitus methodologicus recurrens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RLE-04","text":"Gradus naturae → intensitas conversionis → mensura gratiae → gradus gloriae est series escalationis, sed causalitas naturae ad donum in singulis transitibus interrumpitur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D6","CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:RLE-05","text":"Attractor totius structurae est praesentia divina quae causalitatem, appetibilitatem et beatitudinem unit, dum creaturam sibi assimilando numquam in se absorbet.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A14","CH_GGVC_P_54:A8","CH_GGVC_P_54:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:FGS-B01","text":"Esse per participationem → creatio ex nihilo → natura intellectualis subsistens sed non sibi sufficiens.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A3","CH_GGVC_P_53:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:FGS-B02","text":"Natura recepta → inclinatio voluntaria → appetitus perfectionis → dilectio boni proprii et universalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:A3","CH_GGVC_P_52:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:FGS-B03","text":"Angelus ut pars → ordo universi → subordinatio boni proprii → dilectio Dei supra seipsum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_52:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:FGS-B04","text":"Finis facultatem creatam excedens → motio gratiae → conversio libera caritatis → meritum doni supernaturalis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:A4","CH_GGVC_P_54:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:FGS-B05","text":"Actus meritorius → successio intellectualis minima → visio essentiae divinae → confirmatio voluntatis in bono.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D5","CH_GGVC_P_54:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:FGS-B06","text":"Gradus gloriae adeptus → clausura meriti essentialis → permanentia naturae → fruitio, ministerium et augmentum accidentale.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:D9","CH_GGVC_P_54:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:AFM-B01","text":"Distinctio Creatoris et creaturae → participatio essendi → initium angelicum → angelus ut pars universi → inclinatio ad bonum universale → primatus naturalis dilectionis Dei.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_53:A8","CH_GGVC_P_52:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:AFM-B02","text":"Perfectio naturalis initialis → excessus finis beatifici → gratia elevans → conversio meritoria → visio immediata → libertas confirmata → clausura progressus essentialis cum diffusione perfectionis.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:AS2","CH_GGVC_P_54:AS3","CH_GGVC_P_54:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:MME-01","text":"Immateriale reclassificatur ut modus creaturae participatae, non ut tertium genus inter Deum et mundum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:ME1","CH_GGVC_P_53:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:MME-02","text":"Natura, libertas et gratia cessant esse principia competitiva et fiunt gradus causaliter distincti unius operationis elevatae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:DNX3","CH_GGVC_P_54:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:MME-03","text":"Oppositio amoris sui et amoris Dei corruit, quia bonum proprium creaturae intra bonum universale causans et perficiens collocatur.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:ME4","CH_GGVC_P_52:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:MME-04","text":"Tempus dividitur in initium essendi, successionem actuum et clausuram progressus, quorum nullum motum corporalem requirit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:ME2","CH_GGVC_P_54:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:MME-05","text":"Operatio terminalis reclassificatur: post beatitudinem actus non amplius finem meretur, sed finem possessum fruitur et diffundit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_54:SD5","CH_GGVC_P_54:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei tractat originem, dilectionem, gratiam, meritum, gloriam et statum terminalem angelorum tamquam quaestiones distinctas.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:AS1","CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis eas quaestiones ordinat per participationem essendi, relationem partis ad totum et seriem naturae, gratiae atque gloriae.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT2","CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus contradictiones dissolvit distinguendo rationes obiecti et modos causalitatis, non eliminando alterum membrum.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_52:ALT3","CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis producit creaturam finite receptivam cuius historia ab initio contingenti per successionem actuum ad terminum irreversibilem transit.","refs":["CH_GGVC_P_53:ALT4","CH_GGVC_P_54:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_GGVC_21:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus formam systematis performat: distinctiones stratificatae inferiora servant, excessum finis